alchemist class and want a laugh. It’s normal uses are in poisons, especially\nthose that work with emotions, and it represents the more destructive side of Fire. It has been added to brews on some occasions as well, perhaps to heat up the body in cold winters.\nLocation: Bushes in cold climates.\nStrong\n\nName: Crimson Vase\nRepresentation: Heat, Warmth, Love, Passion, Compassion\nDescription: In my opinion, this flower is the most beautiful that can be found in the forests. As it names suggests it has a strong red color,\ncrimson. This is the color that the large petals of the flower have, and the form of which they take is of an elegant vase. It’s beauty is also enhanced by it’s rarity, as finding one in a forest is an extreme delight. It appears at the base of young\ntrees, growing almost clinging to them. When the sun is high up, the plant starts almost glowing, as a beam of light passes through the small leaves and shines on it. Such combination of sunlight and protection can not be found on older trees. The plant\nsplendor does not end here, as my favorite trait is that the flower is warm to the touch, lovingly so. There are not many fire symbols which have representations of the ‘good’ side of fire, yet this one seems to have most of them. Warmth, Love, Passion,\nCompassion, this plant can be used for most emotion changing concoctions. Of course it’s very important to fire based potions as well, such as Alchemist’s fire, but with it poisons of envy and rage, and potions which bring focus, courage, and warmth\ncan as well.\nLocation: At the base of young trees in forests.\nName: Drake’s Tail\nRepresentations: Heat, Destruction, Chaos\nDescription: Of the herbs and plants of which I speak of in this volume, Drake’s Tail is the strongest and probably the rarest symbol of Fire. A rare sight in the deserts, almost\na legend sometimes, this plant is probably the best you may find without having to slay a beast of mythical stories. It grows in the deserts, but even in them the conditions needed for it to grow are quite scarce and hard to find. This plant’s growth is\nvery dependant on the moisture and temperature in the air, which means in the hot desert wastelands you will not find one growing. Only near Oasis, yet not too close does it grow. It needs the moisture that exists in the air because of the Oasis, and the\nhotness of the desert, so it becomes an area which one might find Drake’s Tail. It seeks shade as well, embarrassing it’s thin and long vines filled with thorns around a rock. With a red dusky color it’s easy to spot, when there is one around. To harvest\nit one has to remove the whole plant, as both the thorns and the roots are the necessary bits that are used by the alchemists in their concoctions. The harvesting is not only hard, but also dangerous. If one is struck by one of the thorns, he will gain\na strong fever and have a high chance of passing out in the middle of a hot desert, to be food to the coyote’s. It’s characteristics make Drake’s Tail one of the best in the fire eccentric representations.\nLocation: In deserts close to oasis.\nContinues in part 3\n\nWritten by Daniel Nodal\nThe Grand Harvest, 1480", ""),
        StaticBook("AlchemyGuide 2-3", "Daniel", "\\_+*+_/\n   Alchemy Guide\n\n\n\nVolume 2 – Reagents\nPart 3/4\n\n\n\n\n-By Daniel Nodal\nWater Symbols\nWeak\n\nName: Blissfoil\nRepresentation: Calmness\nDescription: Blissfoil is a plant which has more applications in healing medicine than in alchemical healing potions. While it has been found to have weak potency in\nalchemy, it’s effects are quite used in healing. I do not believe many good doctors exist which have not heard of the use of this plant, for it is one of the best numbing agents out there. The greatest problem with it, is the fact that overuse of it\ncauses permanent numbing to an area, and with the power it holds, it happening by someone who does not know of it’s effects is quite possible. The plant itself looks like a combination of many small blue flowers with a thick and flimsy stalk.\nIt’s harvesting is as easy as collecting a flower, and it is born and grows under birch trees near grassy areas.\nLocation: Under birch trees in grassy areas.\nModerate\n\nName: Serpent's Stalk\nRepresentations: Life, Rebirth, Calmness, Fluity\nDescription: This plant is one of the easiest to find in the forest of the realm. If one knows where there are small ponds and perhaps streams of\nwater, they would find the Serpent's Stalks. Long Emerald hued stalks, with stripes and ridges of a lighter green and brown along its length, almost like a serpent. Sometimes simple mistaken by normal sugar canes by those unknown of this plant, and to\ncollect it is the same as well, cutting it at the bottom. Another attribute it holds similar to a serpent’s it’s the poisonous nature it has. Specific insects that come in contact with it are normally found dead all around them, yet from all it’s use, no\nother creatures seem to die from it. It is actually used many times as a healing agent, specifically to heal and treat burn wounds. A normal oinkment from simply crushing the plant and mixing it with some water may smooth the pain and keep the wound\nsafe. It is as such a good water symbol that can be used for antidotes, oils, balms, healing potions and potions of calmness, as well as fire extinguishing potions. Those are good to have when preparing alchemist fire.\nLocation: Grows near small bodies of water in forests.\nName: Mandragora\nRepresentation: Rejuvenation, Life, Rebirth, Regrowth\nDescription: This is one of the reagents most alchemists use when creating more powerful healing potions. It’s meat rejuvenating traits makes it so that it’s very well\nsought by many alchemists. No good ingredient comes without its dangers thought, and Mandragora is one that can bring a collector to a very humiliating death. It is observed growing into the shallow waters of swamp lands, with thick green leaves flowing\nout of the water. Such leaves are quite delicious as garnish for soups and to make a quite rejuvenating tea. It is highly nutritious as well, filled with nutrients. It is not the leaves that one uses as a reagent thought, but the “meat” of the plant.\nThe part of the plant normally underwater is shaped like a parsnip. It is this “meat” that needs to be collected and prepared to use by the alchemists. Collecting it it’s not as easy as it sounds. This plant creates highly narcotic and paralyzing spores\nwhich are released quite easily when the plant is moved. Inhaling them brings the humiliating death of drowning in a foot high water level, as you simply fall on it and are unable to move any further. As such, one has to known when the spores are fully\nreleased, and only then retrieve them. Normally simply a group of at least two set out to find them, and one pulls the other from death if the spores are still with the plant.\nLocation: Low waters in wetlands.\nName: Zawabate\nRepresentations: Life, Calmness, Rebirth\nDescription: Zawabate is the only reagent I know of water representation in the desert lands. Of course it does not grow in the middle of the sand, it grows in the rare oasis one might\nfind. There is it protected from the strong heat and low humidity, in the fertile grounds around the waters. It is identified by it’s prominent colors of green and yellow, with short curvy petals in a long stalk. For those that live near them, especially\nthe orcish shamans, it is a plant which brings a higher connection with the spirits and out of body experiences. To say more simply, Zawabate is a hallucinogen, creating great comfort and sensations, which are further enhanced if made into a stong tea.\nThese flowers are certainly an amazing addition to potions designed to numb pain or heal because of their home in such a lush landscape among a wasteland of aridity. The amount to use however, should be greatly controlled, due to its hallucinogenic\nproperties. Too much, and the healing potion might cause delusions and mental problems, which means it can also be used for to create those same poison effects if wanted.\nLocation: In the fertile lands of an oasis\nName: Frost Vine\nRepresentation: Life, Calmness, Ice\nDescription: Frost vine is a blue vine which grows in very cold climates. It seems to have a need for shade, the most common of places being around trees, leaving long blue spirals in their\ntrunks and falling from their branches. The plant is a very good numbing agent, one which can easily be made into a sticky clear substance which numbs pain and loosens stiff muscles. Too much of it and it may affect the limbs, making them completely numb\nfor some time. One must always be sure to wash the area after applying the substance. It is by some considered a good alternative to a stronger but also more dangerous rubbing agent, Blissfoil, and with some other good qualities in the mix.\nThe vine is quite cold to the touch, which means it may also be further used to better the effect of numbing and treating wounds and pains. With these traits, it is no wonder that this plant represents life, calmness and cold.\nLocation: Shaded areas in cold climates.\nStrong\n\nName: Athin\nSymbol: Freezing, Ice, Life, Balance\nDescription: Athin is quite a potent Water Symbol that one finds in ice lakes and rivers of fresh water, which are normally frozen. It is a blue algae, sometimes quite hard\n{\"text\":\"\"}\nto find if the ice is too thick or the snow stops vision to the unfrozen water under the ice. One particular difficult to harvest plant, not due to the how you take it, but because of the danger associated with it. It is taught to all alchemists that it\ntakes two people to harvest Athin. This is because it grows under ice, on very cold water. The ice breaking and someone getting stuck is a high probability, but either way you will have to get into the water to collect it. Sometimes people get stuck\nunder the ice, not knowing where the hole they did was, sometimes they do not take precautions with heating before entering the water and freeze in the cold wind when out. Such dangers do come with reward, as Athin is one of the materials there are that\nare fireproof. It has a great representation of ice and freezing, and an alchemist that carries around alchemist fire, or simply makes it, always have some athin around with them as well.\nLocation: Under the ice of frozen lakes and rivers.\nContinues in part 4\n\nWritten by Daniel Nodal\nThe Grand Harvest, 1480", ""),
        StaticBook("AlchemyGuide 2-4", "Daniel", "\\_+*+_/\n   Alchemy Guide\n\n\n\nVolume 2 – Reagents\nPart 4/4\n\n\n\n\n-By Daniel Nodal\nAir Symbols\nWeak\n\nName: Jailer’s moss\nRepresentations: Travel, Movement\nDescription: Quite an annoying plant in many cases, the Jailer’s Moss seems to stick to everything it touches. It is found the caves near or in swamps,\ngrowing in water streams from the walls, and sometimes even in small currents of water. It has a very light yellow color making it easily noticeable in the dark caves. It’s main property is the stickiness it has, just a touch and it never seems to\nlet go. Of course it doesn’t hold much force, so no one but the small fishes and insects it feeds on get stuck to it, it normally breaks or the whole plant gets dragged with the animal or person. It is from this that the ingredient is considered an air\nsymbol, representing the motion of travelling with the other animals, this way spreading. A weak symbol which is great for new alchemists to use and try out.\nLocation: Caves in swamps\nModerate\n\nName: Swamp’s blossom\nRepresentations: Quickness, speed, Travel\nDescription: This is the flower that would be considered the most beautiful in the awful looking lands of swamp and wetlands. A purplish\ngreen flower that grows through the branches of the trees, with a short and thick stem. One might feel bad for removing the little beauty one might find in the swamplands, which is quite understandable. After collecting this flower, you can remove the\nnectar which has a very peculiar reaction. This nectar is a clear liquid, but one that acts like quicksilver. Extracting a bit of it and pouring it over your hand, and it will dance gracefully until finding a way to the floor between your fingers.\nIt is this nectar that is used in the concoctions of the alchemists, one that represents a clear symbol of air.\nLocation: Growing through the branches of swamp trees\nStrong\n\nlName: Crouching Feather\nRepresentations: Speed, Travel, Gracefulness\nDescription: A graceful and rare sight of the forest and plains. This quite potent reagent can be recognized by it’s\nlong three white petals that sweep in a downwards curve to the point where they touch the ground, appearing like feathers. Like the name it has, they are found “crouching” under large fauna, such as big bushes and shrubs. The harvesting of this peticular\nplant is one that is quite hard. The flower only blooms at night and a strong wind will blow the petals right off. When finding one, the alchemist or botanist must carefully remove the petals from the stalk, and keep them safe from being blown away, and\nfrom being crushed. When finally harvested, this plant is quite a strong symbol of air. The extract of the petals much be collected first, and doing so to a graceful petal is quite hard. It’s use it’s mostly for potions of celerity and when the\nrepresentation of speed is quite desired. Yet gracefulness and travel also represent these long petals.\nLocation: Under big bushes and shrubs of forests and plains.\nName: Elf’s hair vine\nRepresentations: Travel, Gracefulness, Speed, Flight\nDescription: One of the most beautiful plants of which I speak of in this volume, Elf’s Hair vine is a rare sight in the top of cold mountains. Like the elegant hair\nof the nibble elves, the plant has a extreme lightness to it, flowing softly even in the most minute of breezes. The vine is thin and white, seeming to float in the air. Normally protected from the wind, when a stronger gust of air finds it, the small\nblossoms that grow from the vines are broken off, and start flying with the wind, travelling together. They have many pure small white petals which gracefully come together to create the flower. These flowers is what an alchemist uses in his concoctions,\nwhich makes the collection quite difficult. If a simple breeze can take it away, picking it up or moving it around is an very timely task. The alchemist has to be slow and gentle, as not only would harsh movements send the graceful flower flying away, it\nmight also damage the petals of this fragile plant. With a representation of grace of the flower, it’s petals have to be in perfect condition when used, a tear or a part of it damaged, and most of the use is lost. This reagent serves with great use for\nconcoctions centered around speed and grace.\nLocation: Covered from the wind at the top of cold mountains.\nWritten by Daniel Nodal\nThe Grand Harvest, 1480", ""),
        StaticBook("Aleksandria", "Delphinus Fenfaron", "I walk into the City of Aleksandria which is the Capital of a Kingdom called Courland. The first thing i see is Mylas Co. a shop that sells many things in General offering jobs. Next to it is another stall owned by Loic de Savin. I see a plae called Riga\nCircle which holds other Shops and Stalls Selling Fresh Produce. Farther into the City isee more and more stalls. Halfway into the City there is a Mote to go into The second half of the city i suppose. This Area i suposed the Palace of Curonberg that upon\nOffical Buisness. I couldnt go anywhere beyond this point.", ""),
        StaticBook("Alloys & Metals", "Koralon Doomforged", "The Alloy Compendium\n\n===================\n\nA concise guide on the most widely used alloys for craftsmanship,\n\nby\nKoralon Doomforged\nIntroductions\n\nWhile the core metals provide an ample variety of strength, durability and flexibility for tools, construction and decorations, the more scholarly smiths realised that blending one metal with another (or creating carbon alloys) can\nhelp mend the disadvantages of metals while perfecting and fine-tuning their other qualities.\n\nCreating alloys is a must-know for any blacksmiths who seek to achieve the highest quality of tools, weapons and armour.\nThe Core Triad\n\nThe core triad refers to the three base metals widely used in smithing:\n\nAurum, Ferrum and Carbarum.\nFerrum:\n\nFerrum is revered for its versatility. It's used to craft arches, reinforce structures, make tools, weapons and armour as well. However, it's prone to rust and can easily be refined into steel. Ferrum has a relatively low melting point.\nAurum:\n\nAurum is brittle, heavy and hard to sharpen. Any equipment forged out of aurum is bound to have terrible durability. However, aurum never rusts, and as such it's the preferred metal to preserve wealth. Coins are minted from aurum, while the\nnobility drinks their wine from aurum goblets.\n\nAurum has another propety though. It's capable of interacting with the unnatural forces that keep undead and some other dark monsters anchored to our world.\nAny such creature struck by a weapon of aurum will feel peen much alike a mortal would, and a few slashes with an aurum blade can easily banish them and destroy them permanently.\n\nAurum melts easier than ferrum.\nCarbarum:\n\nCarbarum has a blue hue to it and is extremely durable. At the same time, carbarum can't be sharpened and therefore only a handful of blacksmiths in history could ever craft weapons out of pure carbarum.\nCarbarum also has an extremely high melting temperature and can only be properly worked with the help of a crucible and a decent-sized forge.\nRefined alloys:\n\nRefined alloys are produced by refining a single metal through different means. Any such methods usually takes at least twice as much base materials than what the forgemaster seeks to procure.\nLuminous Aurum:\n\nBy heating aurum scrap to an extremely high temperature within a crucible, impurities can be purged and a stronger blade can be forged. While more effective against the undead and spectral, luminous aurum is never used to craft\narmour, tools or cutlery due to the sheer amount of aurum consumed or ruined in the process of creating it.\nRefined carbarum:\n\nA high amount of carbarum can be refined a lot like aurum can, but doing so requires immense experience in geology and craftsmanship to procure the proper temperature and circumstances. It's used to craft armour.\nThere is no recorded case of refined carbarum produced outside a blast furnace.\n\nThe temperature necessary cannot be achieved through burning charcoal, coal or coke, only by feeding a blast furnace with alchemical fuel.\nCarbon Alloys\n\nCarbon alloys are the different versions of steel produced in a crucible or a blast furnace by cleansing iron with carbon.\nSteel:\n\nSteel is the most widely used alloy and metal. Low quality steel can be produced by melting ferrum scraps together with chunks of coal in an enclosed and heated crucible. Better quality can be drawn from a blast furnace.\nSteel retains the strength and durability of iron, while improving on its flexibility and slightly altering its general properties. A master blacksmith is able to choose the proper carbon:iron ratio for every piece of tool, weapon or armour they craft.\nBlack ferrum\n\nBlack ferrum is sometimes referred to as the \"champion of alloys\" because of its superiority in battle. Black ferrum is neither black nor ferrum, merely high-carbon steel that proved to be the most effective weapon\nalloy after centuries of trial & error. Due to its flexibility, black ferrum is never used to craft armour: comapred to steel, it'd just bend easier and give way to piercing weapons that a steel plate would deflect.\nSecond-degree alloys:\n\nSecond-degree here refers to two different base metals from the triad used to produce the alloy. If moulded, the qualities of the base metals mingle much like the colour and the material itself.\nSecond degree alloys are used to make metals easier to work on and more effective in combat.\nSlayer steel:\n\nSlayer steel is an alloy of ferrum and aurum with the goal to harden aurum enough to craft lasting weapons that retain aurum's undead-banishing abilities. Slayer steel is the most frequently used alloy for monster hunters\nand many adventurers prefer to keep a slayer-steel side weapon on them at all time in case they encounter an enemy they can easily maim with it.\n\nWhile slayer steel allows weapons to cause decent harm to both the undead and the living,\nthe aurum content keeps any weapon crafted brittle and lacking in durability. Therefore, slayer steel is never used for armour or cutlery.\nBluesteel:\n\nInvented during the 18 years war, bluesteel is a high-temperature alloy of carbarum and ferrum. Records exist of bluesteel produced with the crucible method, but a blast furnace is always preferred. The carbarum content leaves the\nferrum far more durable than any weapon (easily rivalling pure carbarum weapons), while it retains the sharpness and flexibility of ordinary steel blades. Bluesteel is a preferred choice for those looking forwards to a long battle.\nBluesteel is seldom used to craft armour, when it is it's mostly ceremonial purposes due to the metal's blue-ish hue. Bluesteel armour resembles steel in durability and strength.\nThird-degree alloys:\n\nThird degree alloys are produced by moulding carbarum into the most popular alloys. Because of the three base materials, third-degree alloys require purified carbarum moulded into the metal:\nin the form of a flawless diamond. Any jewelcrafted can attest to the incredibly high temperatures at which a flawless diamond would melt - only a couple craftsmen are capable of refining alloys with pure carbarum, and the only recorded precedent uses\na special dwarven blast furnace overheated with the aid of magic.\n\nThird-degree alloys can't sustain larger chunks of metal, and are only used for thin rapiers, foils or sabres.\nDaemon Steel:\n\nDaemon steel is an alloy of high-carbon steel and pure carbarum. While it doesn't gain much in durability, any blade forged from daemon steel can be sharpened far better than black ferrum.\nAengul Aurum:\n\nAengul Aurum is an alloy of slayer steel (which is an alloy of gold and ferrum) and pure carbarum. It's the most dreaded metal by undead. It possesses higher durability than slayer steel, can be sharpened far better while it still retains\nthe anti-monster properties of aurum.\nAlternate names:\n\nFerrum\n- Iron\nAurum\n- Gold\nLuminous Aurum\n- Hardened Aurum\n- Heavy Aurum\nSteel\n- Crucible steel (if produced in crucible)\n- Blasted steel (with blast furnace)\nBlack ferrum\n- Blacksteel\nSlayer steel\n- Witchhunter gold\n- Witchhunter's steel", ""),
        StaticBook("Alreis' Notebook", "Alreis Faereon", "[!] Drawings and short notes will be placed through out the book", ""),
        StaticBook("Alteration", "Lefkos Amethil", "=---=   Mana   =---=\n\nWhat is mana?\n\nIn simplicity, mana is an invisible substance that encompasses us and everything we see. Imagine seeing a rock, and lifting it up. Mana resides even so much as within a pointless object such as that. If you\nwere to look at the person next to you, even they have mana. What makes people different than objects in terms of mana is the fact that we, as Descendants, are capable of growing and hence manipulating our mana pools.\nHow come we see mana when something is transmuted?\n\nYou don't. If you saw one transmute, you likely saw their Aura. An Aura is the excess that comes off of ones mana. The color is very much depending on ones\nmental state.\nWhat is Transmutation?\n\nTransmutation itself is a rather simple concept. Simply altering an object to what you want it to be. In actuality, accomplishing this is difficult and requires immense study upon what you wish to change.\nYou must follow the law of equivelent exchange as well, being unable to create diamonds from dirt, or water from rock. You may very well change something like water into ice, or perhaps change the shape of stone.\nHow do I transmute something?\n\nWe'll use an example. Take a sphere of ferrum, able to fit in your palm and weighing five kilograms. You must first study ferrum in all its' senses. How it reacts to temperature, pressure, and everything.\nYou must as well find its mana signature. A mana signature is the way mana is 'layed out' in a specific object. You may find this able to be done easiest by meditating with the material, and sending your own mana coursing through it at times.\nYou may stop once you have familiarized yourself with it.\nAfter this, you would summon your own mana, and envelop the ferrum sphere with it. Fill it, coat it, and everything of the like. Much akin to how one 'wills' their evocations to act, you would 'will' the ferrum's properties to change. For this, we shall\ninvision a ferrum rod. If you truely know what ferrum is, and how it works, it should begin to shape how you wish it to. The first go will be immensely tiring, as well as bear a danger shared by any and all transmutation.\nWhat is the danger?\n\nYour stupidity. If one was to dare try and shape it into something that would require more of the substance then what you posses, you'd find your mana rapidly drained and yourself dead. This goes for any amount.\n=--= Enchanting =--=\n\nWhat is Enchanting?\n\nEnchanting is the act of changing the properties of an item, much akin to Transmutation in that sense. The difference here is that you are changing it to have magical ability,\nrather then to look different. This does not mean you may use the enchantment as much as you wish, however. This is due to the fact that it still requires 'equivelent exchange'. For this, we shall move onto mana gems.\nWhat is a mana gem?\n\nTake a precious material. A finely crafted diamond, emerald, or even gold. The more valuable, the better. These materials, past their own mana, have space to hold more than what they have.\nTaking advantage of this, we may go so far as to fill the empty space with our own mana, and then order it to 'fuel' an enchantment. The gem, filled with mana, is hence called a mana gem.\nHow do we actually enchant something?\n\nEasy! You are to use your mana much as you did with transmutation, and 'will' the object to cast a certain spell when supplied with mana. It should be noted one can not cast with a magic they can not cast.\nAlong with that, you 'will' the mana in the mana gem to supply the enchantment upon a certain order. This can be motion, sound, or physical contact.\nDont lie. I know transfigurationists who enchant with things they don't know!\n\nOkay, you caught me. They can, but it's a difficult act. For one, they need someone who knows the magic to help them. Second, they need to fully understand said magic.\nWe'll use a water evocationist and me for example. To do 'joint enchanting' with a water evocationist, I must first understand water evocation as though I were capable of actually casting it. After that, I'll have him cast a spell to be wrapped in my mana\nOnce I envelop their spell, I will 'break it down' into its original mana that created it, and use my own to funnel it into the object I wish enchanted. The last stage requires a certain level of trust. If the other person gets scared, it will fail.\nWhy would they be scared?\n\nBecause, you're essentially taking their mana to do joint enchanting. It gives an odd feeling to them. Such may cause them to grow scared and cease casting, which results in failure.\n=--=   Warding   =--= \n\nWhat is warding?\n\nWarding is a more difficult concept, but still one able to be grasped farely quickly. To ward a magic, one must understand it as though to the extent of joint enchanting.\nThe difference between joint enchanting and warding is the fact that such can be done on your own, without aid. After you understand the magic you intend to ward, you then create a 'web' of mana. Such takes immense concentration and energy.\nAfter some minute of forcing mana out, you have it ready to attack the mana anchor of the magic you wish to ward. As the spell would hit your ward, it should quickly have its mana anchor 'attacked' by your own.\nAssuming your ward has more mana than the spell attacking you, it should promptly vanish. If not, or if its a magic you arent familiar with or are not currently warding against, it will simply pass the ward and hit you.\n=--= Abjurgation =--= \nWhat is an Abjurgation?\n\nAn Abjurgation is simply a summoned amount of mana. It works much the same as a ward in every way, yet often takes the color of ones aura.\nIt's used to be thrown at other peoples spells either before it is finished casting, or in mid air. Abjurgations themselves are created with the purpose of attacking another spells mana anchor, and are quite easy and quick to summon.", ""),
        StaticBook("An Ancient Tome", "Thurak", "Rescribed by the Farseer Thurak, 17'th of The Deep Cold, 1486.\nThis book looks ancient, as if it predated the arrival of the Aegean Exodus to Asulon. It is filled with indecipherable texts and strange diagrams. While the text is unreadable, the pictures seem to show a method of golem creation.\nThe first stage of golem creation seems to be the creation of the core. The images show a block of gold held aloft by a being no dissimilar in appearance to a dwarf. It could possibly have been one of the race that built Karik. The picture also\ncontains what looks like a shaman of some sort, but definitely not one of dwarven descent. At the centre of the drawing is a bolt of unnatural looking lightning. It seems as if the Shaman is summoning the magical lightning to strike the core.\nIn the next diagram, the golden core and the dwarf holding it seem enveloped in some sort of field of lightning. A third diagram shows the dwarf holding the core, which is now transparent, with a mist swirling inside it. It is possible that this\nis making an impression of the dwarf’s essence and soul onto the core, rather than the crude rituals used in Aegis to transfer the soul entirely. Further on in the book, there is a diagram of a golden body being forged by the same dwarf\nthat held the core aloft. The anvil strongly resembles the anvil of Karik, albeit in better condition than the one in Karik today. The body  is far more intricate than the comparatively primitive golems of Aegis. The next diagram is a\ncross section of the golem. It seems to be made of several interlocking parts, all either forged or carved from what looks like no more than common ore or stone. In the centre of the body is a large central cavity. The final images show the craftsman\nplacing the core into the cavity, the body being enveloped in the magical lightning, and then the golem sitting up and looking at its creator. This book seems to confirm that the Ancients of Karik had the power to make golems, and used that power.\nGiven that golems have the ability to live almost indefinitely, this raises the question: Where are they all?", ""),
        StaticBook("An Anesthetic", "Aevalyn", "The Calendera\n    Illisium Clover-\n     An Anesthetic\n\n       Haelun'or,\n          Axios\n\n    Published 1592\n\nby Averroa Dewhurst\n    Transcribed by\n   Aevalyn Bethiros\nAs written in the 'Study of the Effects of the Calendera Illisium Clover', Calendera demonstrated potential in use as a painkiller--having potency in grown Elves at just 50μL.\nA fellow scientist, Lucion Sullas, suggested creating an anesthetic from the clover, and for the past year I've been trying various mixtures,\ncombining the clover infusion with everything from spider venom to pumpkin wine.\nAfter undertaking these studies, I've discovered that the painkilling properties of the clover are heightened when combined with the latex of the common poppy.\nIn addition, the combination works as an effective anesthetic, potent for an hour on average. However, I have yet to conduct studies on creatures other than mice or chickens,\nso the following should only be used in practical applications after further research.\nThe clover can be found amongst the roots of large trees near the Nawari Gypsy camp as well as in certain Elven Forests. However, at the time of writing this, the exact locations of clovers in the Isles of Axios are unknown.\nTo prepare the Calendera Illisium Clover infusion:\n\nSimmer 10mg fresh clover in 1 liter of water for 4 minutes.\nThe mixture and how to prepare it:\n\nMix 700mg poppy latex with 20ml of simmering water and simmer for 3 minutes.\nTurn off the heat and quickly add 10ml of the Calendera infusion while the solution is still hot and stir quickly until well-mixed.\n50 microliters (μL) seemed to be the optimum dosage for the mice I tested on. After scraping away some of their skin and applying salt water to increase their pain,\nthis dosage caused them to cease squirming and fall into a sleep-like state.\n\nHowever, about 0.05% of the mice became asphyxiated and nearly died at this dosage,\nleading me to believe that some creatures are more sensitive to the mixture than others. In addition, as I gradually increased the dosage,\nthe chance of asphyxiation also gradually increased until an average lethal triple dose of roughly 150μL.\nWhen I performed the same procedures on chickens, I found that a higher dose of 1.5ml was required to have the same effect. Similarly, a triple dose of 4.5ml was the average lethal dose.\nFrom these results, I hypothesize that body mass influences the amount of dosage required for the desired result.\nAs the mice weighed 20g on average and the chickens weighed roughly 3.2kg on average, the dosage may be proportionate to body weight.\nAs such, it may be practical to weigh patients before giving them their appropriate dose, if possible.\nHopefully these results will assist others in further research as well as healers in treating patients with more severe injuries or scientists hoping to prod into living organisms.\n\n-Averroa Dewhurst", ""),
        StaticBook("An Approval", "Tristin", "The Cosmos Druid Indra is hereby permitted of her external home within the Dominion of Malin, exempt from any taxes, charges, or obligations to the Dominions hierarchy.\n\nRegards,\nHigh Prince T.T", ""),
        StaticBook("An Immoral Study", "Anonymous", "-----\nSubject #001\n-----\nDate of creation\n-----\n Subject appears to be rejuvenating flesh and muscle at a rapid rate. Minor discrepancies visible in skin tone. Gashes appearing on flesh; deep red coloration.\nNo bleeding. Subject soon to have absorbed remaining draught. -----\nSubject #001\n-----\nDay 2\n-----\n Subject appears to have remastered essential functions.\n-Slow, ragged breathing.\n-Blood clot time:\nApproximately eight minutes.\n-Reflexes nominal.\n-Body temperature feverish.\n-Eye pupils undeveloped.\n-Muscles slightly\nswollen in volume.\n-Shorter length hair.\n-Consciousness: No -Articulation of speech: No\n\n*The page continues with observations of similar calibre.*\n-----\nSubject #001\n-----\nDay 3\n-----\n Functions vastly improved from previous day. Near all elements fully developed. Still no instance of consciousness.\n-----\nSubject #001\n-----\nDay 4\n-----\n Subject making unconscious motions. Occasional groaning fits noted. Restraints being applied as precaution.\n-----\nSubject #001\n-----\nDay 5\n-----\n Subject has achieved consciousness. Awareness of surroundings minimal. Subject capable of primitive communication.\nRestraints deemed insufficient. Steel door bolts to be installed.\n-----\nSubject #001\n-----\nDay 6\n-----\n Subject aware of surroundings and other presences. Sessions of consciousness spanning up to five hours. Neutral but dazed disposition.\n-----\nSubject #001\n-----\nDay 7\n-----\n Subject exhibiting full awareness of surroundings. Muscle control also appearing fully developed.\n-----\nSubject #001\n-----\nDay ...\n-----\n Subject released.", ""),
        StaticBook("An Introduction", "Peurith", "===================\n\n\n    An Introduction\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n==================\nKarin’ayla, welcome to Peurith’s Archive.\nI am our lord Forefather’s trusted scribe, whose duty is to document the goings on of our blessed Kingdom. If you are reading this, you yourself are a trusted advisor to Malin. Be warned, the punishment for exposing anything you are about to read\nis banishment.", ""),
        StaticBook("An Old Note", "Deaded", "[!] Spruce leaves and a pressed flower found in deep forest lies here. There's small water stains, perhaps from snow?\n\nAurum is a Marked Man's greatest ally. Great care was taken to hide the blade's blueprints", ""),
        StaticBook("An Orc's Life", "Goj Malog'Yar", "((This was written by an orc, but since most of the orcish language is actually just mispronounced common, I only wrote words that are actually different for orcs in the Blah. The words shared between the two languages are written in Common.))\n Mi name is\nMalog'Yar. Mi am the Goj of the War Uzg, and of mi people, the Orcs. As such, it is mi job to guide the orcs, especially the Rex, in wisdom from experience and the spirits. Mi have been alive for almost 90 years. During this time, mi have experienced just\nabout every aspect of life an orc can gruk. Mi have been blargless. Mi have led armies. Mi have been a spiritual guide to mi people. With that said, mi will start from mi cubhood. Mi was raised in a small yet old vilage in the desert by mi momo, Dura, agh\nmi popo, Gurak. Mi, as all uruks, began mi combat training as soon as I was old enough to hold a weapon. The orcish cub, unlike the cubs of other races, is hardly afforded the luxury of \"playing.\" An orc must grow up fast, or nub at all. Because of this,\nmany of us are considered adults at 8 or 10-years-old, as opposed to the other races, who are allowed to wait until they turn 18; but mi digress. Mi popo taught mi how to fight under the hot sun, agh on the blistering sands mi grew to love. He taught mi\nhonor above all, agh it was during a training session that mi witnessed the definition of dishonor. Ash day, a shara was travelling in our desert. Mi popo confronted him, agh demanded an explanation from the trespasser. The shara did nub gruk the Blah,\nbut challenged mi popo to an ash-on-ash honor klomp. He accepted, agh, to make a long story short, was almost flat'd when the shara whistled. At this, a pair of archers rose from their hiding places, agh loosed their ligs at Gurak. Mi popo won the klomp,\nbut the sharas' attempt to cheat in an honor klomp stuck in my memory for the rest of my life. Mi popo was flat'd a year later by a horde of the monsters who roam the wilderness every night. Mi eventually took mi lusk, agh went off on mi own. Mi wandered\nthe desert alone for about 20 years. On mi 34th year of life, mi stumbled upon the goi of San'Orca. Mi remained blargless for some time after that, until the Braduk clan took mi as ash of their own. They allowed mi to share the blarg of another clan\nbrother. Mi lived in that blarg until the War Uzg was temporarily disolved, agh the clans spread throughout the desert, establishing individual clan forts. Mi served as a grunt in the Braduk fort, until Grool'Gorkil'Azog founded the Trog in order to both\ncentralize our people once more, agh to keep a closer eye on the pink skins. Mi became a chicken farmer in the Trog, agh found it to be a humble agh gratifying life. Many would look down upon such a life. Those people are globs, too filled with their own\npride to see the hoshness of such simplicity. It was in the Trog that mi met a young goblin named Durah. We became close, agh she grew to trust mi in the hardest years of her life. After mi brothers conquered Kingston, agh established it as our new\ncapitol goi, Gronkkston, she became mi lifemate. Durah agh mi hab been together for around 40 years, agh she has borne mi h' cubs. Anyways, the Braduk clan was disbanded while we were in Gronkkston, agh those of us in that clan became Ugluks, as it was\nthe popo clan to the Braduks. This was a hard time, but we pressed on. While in Gronkkston, the witch doctor, Grool, took mi as his apprentice, agh mi began mi long journey as a shaman. A shaman, as it turns out, is what mi was always meant to be. Mi have\nfound little more enjoyable than serving mi people as a spiritual guide. Mi will blah more of that later. While mi was an apprentice, Pok flat'd after choosing mi as the new Wargoth of the Ugluk clan. Mi revived the Ugluk clan, agh made it a respected\nclan again. For a while, it became the bub'hoshest of the clans in Gronkkston. Mi even had to stop recruiting to give the other clans a chance to build their numbers. During this time, the Wargoths led orc government as a council. Mi learned that being a\nleader is often like being a popo. You spend more time scolding people, agh making sure they all behave than anything else. Shortly, after becoming the Wargoth, mi first cub was born. We named her Nurena. She brough mi bub'hozh joy, agh continues to honor\nmi to this day. Perhaps mi over-fed her. She got quite fat, but it didn't bother mi or her. It didn't matter that she was fat. What mattered was whether she'd grow to be strong, wise agh honorable; agh she did. She grew to be a desirable feorc, agh is now\na mate of the Rex, who wressled a scaddernak to earn her favor agh mi approval. During mi time as the Ugluk wargoth, mi was also chosen as the commander of the United Anthos Coalition, an army of sharas, albais agh uruks, klomping together against the\nBlack Scourge. We fought against the forces of Setherian, at the same time that we were fighting a war against the dwarves, who had walled off a massive portion of the continent of Anthos. There were glorious klomps in that time. After some time had\nan elder in mi clan, Nux, decided he wanted to be in charge. He challenged mi for mi position, won the klomp agh bekame mi Wargoth for a time. I was, however, forced to take mi followers from within the Ugluks, agh form a new clan. A clan war had started\nbetween the Azogs, agh a clan of Iblees worshiping whitewashes, called Kaxils. Despite the dishonorable behavior of the Kaxils, Nux sided with them, agh mi had nub choice but to take mi followers away to preserve their honor. Mi hold nub grudge against\nNux. Mi gruk why he sided with the Kaxils. The Ugluks agh the Azogs have hated each other for generations, but mi could nub side with the Kaxils miself. So, mi formed the Yar clan in honor of mi great great great grandpopo, Yar. After that, mi beloved\nDurah birthed a pair of twins named Malgroth agh Balgroth. Mi blah lat, do nub ever underestimate the value of a hosh mate. Durah has been loyal to mi for many years, agh has brought me the bub'hoshest joy mi have ever gruk'd. Mi love her more than mi can\nblah. Some time after the birth of the twins, the Wargoths re-established the Rexdom, with Urik'Azog as Rex. He chose mi as his Yazgurten, the chief builder agh economic head of orc government. Mi served as Yazgurten until we went to the Fringe. Mi people\nsettled in a canyon in the desert. Mi soon became the High Shaman, agh served faithfully for years. Mi had long-since been a well-gruk'd teacher of shamanism, agh remain a teacher to this day. Eventually, the orcs became disatisfied with Rex Urik. Mi wull\nnub pretend mi did nub take a side, but mi wull nub pretend it was nub painful to peep titles come between orcs. Orcs are all brothers agh sisters; cubs of Krug. It hurts to peep siblings klomp. Later, under Rex Boghat, we moved to our warcamp near the\nobsidian mountains. After some time, a new High Shaman came into the position, though mi still happily performed mi duties as a shaman to the Uzg. This new High Shaman led a clan, which held an illegitimate tournament to usurp the Rex, who at the time was\nGrogmar'Gorkil. It was a sickening sight. It almost led to a clan war, agh the High Shaman, along with his clan, were exiled under suspicion of burz mojo. An honorable brother named Buubztik'Lur became High Shaman, agh mi was Yazgurten again for almost 20\nyears. Soon after the rebelious clan was exiled, Durah gave mi another cub. We named him Ognir. He, like his sister, brought mi bub'hosh happiness. After the 10-year trip to Thales, mi continued to serve as Yazgurten until the flat of Buubztik. Mi built\nmany blargs. While in Thales, Durah agh mi had another cub. He was different. He was born with a rotting eye. Many feared for his health, but mi gruk'd he was touched by mi master, Orgon. Mi hab been, lat peep, a loyal servant of the disease spirit,\nOrgon, for over 20 years. He is the ruler of disease agh pestilence, agh feeds on all decay. Nub matter who lat are, remember. Lat will decay. Lat will feed mi master's power. We who worship him have a saying. Mubaramishi, gith prasogat. Mubaramishi, gith\nkul Orgonob: In the end, everything decays. In the end, everything belongs to Orgon. Many find this troubling, but Orgon is a spirit just as much as Enrohk agh Tagnir. Mi am, as all hosh orcs, a follower of Krug. Mi am an instrument of Orgon to bring\nsuffering agh failure upon all of Krug's enemies. Having said all this, mi gruk'd mi kub tu bi chosen by Orgon. We named him Vadok, agh he is a champion of Orgon. Orgon has even begun to manifest his power in my cub's hands. It troubles him at times, but\nOrgon is an orcish spirit, agh orcish spirits do not weaken their servants. They strengthen them into greater weapons. They sharpen us. After Buubztik's flat, mi became High Shaman again until we arrived in Athera. Grogmar had stepped down, agh the\nDominus Thore'Gorkil chose mi as the new Rex. Mi served for some time, but mi nub ever wanted to be Rex. It proved not to be where mi was meant to be. It brought mi only bub'hosh weariness of heart. Eventually, mi Warboss, Reksam'Kog, klomp'd mi for the\ntitle. Mi had long been tired of that word... Rex. Reksam klomp'd with strength agh honor. Mi recognized this in his klomping, agh he became the new Rex. The Azogs still do not approve, agh it is why they continue to war against our Uzg. It has been to mi\nanother painful sight, as brothers flat each other over a title again. To lat, whoever reads this, mi impart upon lat this wisdom mi have learned in my life: Do nub be quick to chase after power. Be content, agh learn to peep the hoshness of a simple\nlife. Find a loyal mate. Have cubs, agh raise them with honor. Do nub spite lats brother. Find what lat love to do, agh do it honorably. Mi found more joy as a chicken farmer than mi ever did as Rex. Finally, be a cactus. Mi will end this book with\none more brief story from my life. A shara priest was once confused that a spirit sent mi on a trial before he healed mi after mi lost mi eyes, when his god, he claimed, gave freely to him. Mi explained the hoshness of the trial as follows: The orc is\nlike the cactus. He lives in a harsh environment with little to nub nourishment, but he thrives agh grows tough because of it. The sharas... the sharas are like grass. There's a lot of it, agh it's everywhere; but if you take away its nourishment, even\nfor a short time, it withers agh flats. Sharas are like grass. Be a cactus. The trials of the spirits are to make us stronger. If they handed everything to us, we would grow complacent agh weak. Learn from life, brothers agh sisters, as mi hope to\nkeep learning for however much longer mi will live.", ""),
        StaticBook("Anc Golem Speech", "BudderBacca247", "Ark of Urguan Speech\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\nBackground: In the Mountains of Urguan, the Dwarves of Urguan were led to an Ironborn cave, which was until recently, unexplored. Deep inside the cave, in a room locked in the very back, A golem was found, alive\nintact. The golem was rare, being able to communicate fully, and being able to act without an Impera. On this day, the thousand year old golem told the Dwarves about ancient history of the Dwarves.\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-Here are the notes of what the Golem\nsaid:\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-Urguan had abandoned the Dwarves, and Grand King Barriden was elected afterwards. After Barriden, Grand King Magnus followed. Magnus was mysteriously assassinated, and soon after, an Ironborn King was elected.\nThe Ironborn continued to make a seal (No explination on to what that is, the Golem's memory has been in pieces). The used it to strongarm the themselves (Make them stronger), and to make golems who were more powerful than any other. The Ironborn used the\npower of Iblees to create a complete monarchy of the Dwarves, making their end goal to expand their control over every realm. Anyone who opposed the Ironborn would be put into soul capicators and killed. Unfortunetly, the Seal (Unkown seal) could not hold\nThe Ironborn killed so many, that they had no population to rule over. Kal'Urguan was abandoned, and golemancers and runesmiths were put into golems to preserve dwarven knowledge (The Golem himself was one of them). The Ironborn split, some going to\nAegis, Ansulon, Anthos, and Vailor, (Plus one unkown continent), Urguans tomb lays in Vailor, which means Urguan went to Vailor, not the other continents.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ancient Elves", "Archrim Elmoran", "Achient elves\n\nA long time ago, before written history, the world was inhabited by a single race known now as the achient elves and were the first ofthe Aegis, the build marvels in what is now niben bay\nThe achient elves built cities that are now considerd marvels and large statues of birds, lions, and also dragons, and it should be noted the elves learned how to befriend dragons aswell.\nthey knew the friendship between them was strong and so the dragons tought them the basics of what is know nowdays as magic, they also taught them on how to store energy within crystals and use them to power cities and give them light\nEventually a dragon by the name of Akron took power of the empire that had previously been formed by the elves and dragons. Akron hated the other newly formed races including the elves and so he started creating large crystals and using them for war\nbut there were dragons who did not agree with him and stood in the way of his plans, and so Akron called upon the forces of Iblees\nHe then used this power to slowly drain the life of the other dragons. and then the dragons seeing the inevitable end, us\ntheir remaining strength to close the gate to the nether that supplied Akrons Evil power. They died in the progress of closing the portal. The few dragons remaining turned them selves to stone waiting to one day be awoken\nWith the dragons out of the way Akron started the inslavement of the other races and with that came the great war witch lasted decades.\nFinnaly Akron was one day defeated and with that the humans took control of the crystals of power the dragon once ow\nThe human eventually became mad with power and started the genocide of the Anchient elves and burnt their cities to the ground, few managed to escape, and those few are now the ancestors of the current elven peoples\n\nAnd thus ended the Anchient elves", ""),
        StaticBook("Ancient Hist. V1", "Mage Baruk-Ghaz", "\"The Ancient History\"\n\n*The next lines are curved*\n\"These volumes contain the Origins of Aegis, written by the \"Wandering Wizard\" in the second seed of year 84 at the Cloud Temple of Aegis.\"\n\n*The book apears to be in good shape, it must be a copy*\nThere were no planes of existance. There was nothing. Just the void. And a birght shining light. It was not a light we could see, it was not really white either, but it would be the only way to explain the existance of such a Deity in contrast to the\nemptiness of the Void. None knows why, how or when this Deity existed. It is in-fact, herecy to speculate on such matters. The all knowing God was this Deity.\n\nTruly none can describe the majesty of the creator, the one and only. The Merciful Creator of\nthe Seven Skys. With his intent, and only his intent, the World of Aegis was created. All he had to do was simply want it to occur and it happened. The rolling seas, proud mountains and vast landscapes, all in a second, created by God.\nThe World was not created in play or for fun, but as a theater for the inhabitants of the World to be tested in. And tested for what? Well, that is for us to speculate. Though I believe it is to test us for purity, how hard we can fight temptation, and\nhow clean and good can our actions be.\n\nThe first mortal being to be created was a man. This man was sculptured with clay and water, but left hollow. Soulless, God's creation lay there for the other immortal beings to see. The Aengul and The Daemon, the\ntwo spirits created before the mortal beings and before the creation of Aegis. Not much is known about these two spirit races, but hopefully in the future we may know more.\n\nGod then blew his own breath of existance into the hollow shell and the Man\nlived. God then took the man and put him in the centre of all of Aegis, the same spot where The Cloud Temple now stands. God also made the Man a partner, from the exact same clay and the exact same breath, she was the first Woman. These simple beings\ncould not talk, nor did thay know much about the World. They roamed the world, enjoying its pre-historic beauty. Untouched, the fresh glades and dark thick forests were a wonder to set eyes on. Soon they had four children in the four corners of Aegis.\nMalin was the first of their sons, born in the deep forests of Aegis, he had blonde hair and sharp ears. Standing tall, he was the father of the Elves of Aegis. Krug was born in the scorching deserts of Aegis, fierce and relentless, he was\nthe father of the Orcs. In the fresh meadows of Aegis was born Horen, father of Humans. And lastly, in the deep underground caves of the World, Urguan was born, master of the Dwarves.\n\n*You quickly grab the next volume*", ""),
        StaticBook("Ancient Hist. V4", "Mage Baruk-Ghaz", "\"The Ancient History\"\n\n*The next lines are curved*\n\"These volumes contain the Origins of Aegis. written by the \"Wandering Wizard\" in the second seed of year 84 at the Could Temple of Aegis.\"\n\n*The book apears to be in good shape, it must be a copy*\nBefore they could complete the sentence, Iblees stood tall for one last time.\n\n“You believe you may simply banish me from this plane and that my taint shall not last? I have touched this world with evil and it shall forever be part of the souls that\ninhabit it.\n\nMalin, I curse you with sterility, you and your kin shall forever lack the children they need. May your forest halls forever be silent, and your hearts heavy with sadness.\n\nUrguan, your greed and lust shall overcome you, you are not worthy of\nthe height God gave you, your descendants shall be short, squalid and ugly. You will always seek to find Gold and Gems in the deep underground of the earth, your hunger never satisfied.\n\nHoren, you wish immortality? I will curse you with the opposite,\nearly death for you and your kin. You shall age quickly and die before you experience the fruits of your useless labour.\n\nAnd you Krug, the most hated of The Descendants, you shall always have the lust of war. You are strong? Well the strength shall be\nused against your brothers, used to pillage and murder! Your lust for battle shall be unsatiated and your descendants shall grow ugly and heartless.”\n\nAs soon as his words were uttered, the world grew suddenly dark. A great roar erupted from Ibleeses\nmouth and in a blast of fire he was banished from the Mortal World.\n\nThe robed figure stood before the four brothers.\n\n“There is nothing in my power that may undo what that evil did. There is one thing I may do however, and that is to bless you.\nMalin, may your forests be a sanctuary of peace and your children long lived.\n\nUrguan, may your descendants be hardy, strong hearted and strong of mind.\n\nKrug, may your people show valour and honour where none exist.\nAnd Horen, may your people one day explore the Seven Skies.\n\nI can do no more, for all my power is spent. We will go back to our master now, I believe your children may see us once more but long in the future.”\nAnd with that, the great host of Aenguls and Daemons dissapeared into thin whisps in the air. \n\n*You finished reading about The Ancient History, it feels like you understand the world a lot better*\n\nCopies mady by:\n~Baruk-Ghaz", ""),
        StaticBook("Ancient Mali", "Aedan", "The Ancient Elves\nBy Aedan\nOnce upon a time, long before the beginning of written history, the lands of the wilderness were inhabited by a single race: The Ancient Elves. This race was the first to love in the lands of Aegis.\nThey built incredible structures in the lands of the Niben bay, and its surroundings.\nThe Niben bay was a large body of water lying in the Niben Basin, largely east of the city of Hawkhaven. It lies across the Niben River, splitting it into two parts, and so is technically a lake rather than a bay.\nThe Niben was once occupied by their capital: Garlas Malathar, also known as Nirn Weye vas Cyrod: The White Gold City.\nhis city was, according to the ancient books, the biggest capital in Aegis. The city was filled with complex tunnels and districts with different ambience. They say you could feel one with the city,\nit was filled with statues of nature, exotic birds and wonderful animals… including Dragons…\nThe Ancient Elves learned how to befriend a Dragon, instead of taming them like most races did. They knew that friendship was stronger than any force in the world. These Dragons shared their knowledge with them,\nthey showed them the basics of energy manipulation that are still used now-a-days.\nThey soon found how to store energy in crystals and use them for many things. They used them to power their entire civilization, giving power and light to their cities.\nOne day, a new Dragonlord took power of the empire. His name was Akron. He was foolish and always wished to have more power. He hated other races and considered them inferior. He soon tried to power stronger crystals for war.\nThe Dragons refused and prevented him from doing so.\nAkron then called upon the forces of Iblees to drain the dragons’ power. The dragons, foreseeing their end, created the varla stone and powered it with The Dragonfires, sealing the gates to The Nether, and killing themselves…\nSome dragons remained as statues, petrified, and waiting to be awakened. They will wake up when the right time comes.\nAfter the beginning of the First Era, Akron began to damage nature and attempted to enslave other races. This marked the beginning of the Great War which lasted decades.\nAkron was finally defeated. To the fall of their Empire, humans took the power of the crystals. Their power turned them blind and foolish.\nThey began to kill all survivors of the Ancient Elves and burned their cities to the ground. Some of the managed to escape and survived.\nMany kings tried to restore their old glory but failed. Without the power of the Dragonfires, they weren’t able to do such thing\nThey say that if you look closely to the sunrise, you can still see the ruins of Garlas Malathar, waiting to be discovered, and raised once again…", ""),
        StaticBook("Ancient Scrap", "Thurak'Yar", "… -ûgh Uruk puzg’uga agh hon’uga\n agh quiil’uga az ul gakh kranklûk\n ghaash’uga. Da Lur Nar flûst, da \nDom nar gîmog- rûgh âdh’uga, baak \ntraum’uga ad da gûl ob krank’ulub \nad urrhak’ulub.", ""),
        StaticBook("Animated Armor", "Gansem", "===================== Observations of == == Animated Armor  == ===================\n                            Following a demand for assistance, a fight in the town of Metz was had between a man of the Marked, Gansem, and two townsmen.\nThe creature was immune to most forms of assault but was slowed by assaults of the magi. \n\nFi mages, as they're called, are able to completely immobilize the creatures.\nMeans of disposal:\n\nRender immobile with blunt weaponry, disassemble and dismantle.\n\nField testing required.\n\nSuggested assault numbers: 2-4.\nSuggested weaponry:\nMauls, warhammers and matters of the arcane influence.", ""),
        StaticBook("Another Joke", "Lyulen", "I have no life!", ""),
        StaticBook("Anthos life: I", "Gerald Elgan", "===================\n\n\n\nWildlife and Monsters of Anthos\nTranscribed By:\nGerald Elgan\n\n\n\n\n==================\nOrenian Wildlife\n===================Cockatrice\n---------\nDescription:\nA rather comedic looking creature, the cockatrice is found to have the body and wings of a drake, with the head and legs of the common rooster. The creature is noted\nOrenian Wildlife, cont\n===================-to stand as tall as a small hut, with the body length to match. Strangely enough, the beast maintains an uncomedic deep roar over the expected high-pitched squawk.\nFurther inspection and interaction with the-\nOrenian Wildlife cont,\n===================cockatrice has revealed a small pouch beneath the beak of the cockatrice. When enraged, the cockatrice inhales deeply, the pouch expanding and pulsating momentarily, before exhaling an ash-like smog.\nOrenian Wildlife, cont.\n===================Should the smog come in contact with an individual, he/she will be cursed with a strange spell. This curse, now referred to as, \"Stoning,\" has been noted to thoroughly turn a victim to stone, with no known method\nOrenian Wildlife, cont.\n===================of returning flesh to their cursed body. The beast has talons roughly as sharp as the common fighting blade, the strength expected of a massive beast, and the bodily scales maintain the quality of common iron.\nOrenian Wildlife, cont.\n===================Habitat:\nThe creature is found to reside within vast cave systems, and dense forests. Typically near civilization hubs, but remaining out of sight. Perhaps to feed on unsuspecting cattle, or lone travelers.\nOrenian Wildlife, cont.\n===================Typically the Den, or nest, of a cockatrice is lined with various straw-line plants, or fibers and is dotted with the bones of victims.\nOrenian Wildlife, cont.\n===================\nHarpy:\n-----\nDescription:\nA truly repulsing creature, they possess large claws protruding from their toes and fingers, as well as a sharp beak. They might be mistaken for an ugly woman if-\nOrenian Wildlife, cont.\n===================iit weren't for the two large wings sprouting from their backs and the sharp beak, harpies also have a lethal screech, which appears in the dreams of those foolish enough to stumble upon their lair. If one were-\nOrenian Wildlife, cont.\n===================to walk through the poorer back alleys of Salvus, they would hear the orphans sing a popular melody, which is very related to this beast:\nOrenian Wildlife, cont.\n==================\n\"Harpy, Harpy seem them fly, drop the children from the sky, when the younglings misbehave, escorts children to their grave. Never back-talk, never lie, or they'll drop you from the sky!\"\nOrenian Wildlife, cont.\n===================Habitat:\nHarpies prefer mountainous areas, full of rocky ledges where they can build nests and swoop down on unsuspecting travellers, the trench known as brigands pass once had a large nest of harpies, until\nOrenian Wildlife, cont.\n===================the White Rose moved in.\nCharacteristics:\nSome find zombies repulsing, others find spiders more so, but the Harpy is doubtlessly the most disgusting of the lesser demons, they have humanoid legs and arms, though\nOrenian Wildlife, cont.\n===================large raven-like wings sprout from their backs. There are different types of Harpies, which shall not be noted, a recurring trait seems to be kleptomania.\nMalinor Wildlife\n===================\"Valahii'ame\"\nLeaf Apes:\n---------\nDescription:\nStrange Wolf-like creatures that reside among Malinor's various trees. The creatures are often quite thin, have very short patchy hair and\nMalinor Wildlife, cont.\n===================communicate in a series of high-pitched chortles and howls. The creatures are seen to move in large packs, moving between trees, jumping from branch to branch, and have been noted to utilize crude tools.\nMalinor Wildlife, cont.\n===================Habitat:\nHeavily forested lands of Malinor, though they live among the uninhabited forests, simply observing the roads for lone travelers or unfortunate prey.\nMalinor Wildlife, cont.\n===================\nCharacteristics:\nThe Tiny creatures are extremely fast and aggressive. It's extremely common for the creatures to attack the necks of its prey, aiming to either bleed or strangle it's prey. Should this fail, -\nMalinor Wildlife, cont.\n===================iit's common for the creatures to bite and claw at exposed flesh. In the extremely unlikely event that the creatures find no other method to attack their opponents, they often attack with sticks and rocks in an -\nMalinor Wildlife, cont.\n===================attempt to disable prey. The teeth, claws and \"Tools\" used by these creatures are generally inefficient and are only a minor threat. Instead, their massive numbers compensate for their lackluster strength. -\nMalinor Wildlife, cont.\n===================Strangely enough, striking the creatures with common steel only causes blunted damage. For an unknown reason, common Iron and Steel do not penetrate or break the skin of these creatures. The creature is roughly-\nMalinor Wildlife, cont.\n===================the size of the standard dog, though considerably thinner, almost sickly in it's nature. These creatures build Nests, made of various hides and leaves, typically producing litters of 8 or more young.\nMalinor Wildlife, cont.\n===================\"Ihnsil Tali'ame\"\nSpear Vine:\n----------\nDescription:\nThese plants look to be the common Venus Fly-trap, though with roots clearly exposed and forming a bit of a bush around the central pod. The plant\nMalinor Wildlife, cont.\n===================seems to have a will of it's own and moves without clear motive, slowly wandering aimlessly about the forests of Malinor.\nMalinor Wildlife, cont.\n===================Habitat:\nDensely forested areas within the borders of Malinor. The creatures are nomadic in nature, seeing them outside of Malinor, or around civilization is exceptionally common.\nMalinor Wildlife, cont.\n===================Characteristics:\nThe vines of the creature are abnormally thick and though, they've been noted to impale an unarmored figure with ease. The prey fed to the central pod. When ingesting food, the creature remains-\nMalinor Wildlife, cont.\n===================entirely inactive. Generally unresponsive to the exterior world, even when clearly attacked with efforts to claim it's life. Upon closer inspection, the creature seems to be a collection of creatures, working -\nMalinor Wildlife, cont.\n===================within a hivemind environment, the central pod directing the creature entirely. The Central pod is surprisingly thin and frail, lack of effort to protect the mind of the organism is, strange to say the least.\nMalinor Wildlife, cont.\n===================Further observations would be needed to get a better understanding of the creature. The digesive acids of the central pod weaken considerably over time, suggesting the constant need to produce acid from the-\nMalinor Wildlife, cont.\n===================central pod. When left unhindered, the creature has been known to grow sizes rivaling that of the common tree.\nDwarven Wildlife\n===================Due to the harsh Climates of the Dwarven lands, Native Wildlife is scarce.\n\"Cave Leech\"\n-----------\nDescription:\nOf all the unfortunate beasts to come across, this winged beast is the most horrid, putrid-\nDwarven Wildlife, cont.\n===================and generally repulsive creature to meet within the depths of a cave. The creature looks remarkably like a naked bat with an extended neck and featureless face. Where a nose and eyes perhaps once stood,\nDwarven Wildlife, cont.\n===================a large drooling maw now consumes the face of this beast.\nDue to it's highly aggressive and repulsive nature, the creature is widely avoided and genuine investigation on a live subject is nearly impossible.-\nDwarven Wildlife, cont.\n===================The creature is seen to walk upon two legs, with wings. Suggesting the ability to fly, but there have been no confirmed instances of such.\nDwarven Wildlife, cont.\n===================Habitat:\nThe creature simply craves a massive darkspace. Due to preferences, the creature resides within the icy northern reachers, and is known to plague the cave systems of the Dwarven lands.\nDwarven Wildlife, cont.\n===================Characteristics:\nThe thick stretchy hide of the repulsive creature is a natural flame retardant. The teeth of this creature have been known to cleave Iron as if paper, and the removal of a limb when coming into-\nDwarven Wildlife, cont.\n===================contact with this creature is excessively common. The creature clings to the ceiling of vast cave systems, simply awaiting opportunity to fall onto it's prey, typically aiming to behead immediately. Due to it's -\nDwarven Wildlife, cont.\n===================nest, the high-pitched screech emitted from this creature's maw is deafening, literally. Often resulting in loss of hearing for several days. Once dead, the creature is noted to drain the carcass of its victim. -\nDwarven Wildlife, cont.\n===================The creature is noted to be roughly the size of an adult Orc, with a wingspan of roughly 5 feet.\n[!] A sketch of a cave leech sits on the bottom of the page [!]\nOrcish Wildlife\n===================\"Duhnah Skhelll\"\nSand Tortoise\n------------\nDescription:\nThe common Tortoise, though abnormally large and noted to be abnormally territorial. The Sand Tortoise, commonly referred to as the, \"Duhnah Skhell\nOrcish Wildlife, cont.\n===================, ,due to it's ability to blend and camouflage within the harsh environment that is the, \"War Uzg\", is a territorial and reclusive hunter. It's favored method of hunting is a form of ambush. The Dune Shell creates\nOrcish Wildlife, cont.\n===================a massive crater, and lays flat, only the upper portions of it's head and shell fully exposed. Even when directly next to the creature, it's shell and head are remarkably similar to that of it's surroundings, -\nOrcish Wildlife, cont.\n===================genuinely appearing to be yet another sand dune, with a small cave mouth and various assorted rocks dotting it's approach.\nWhen prey comes within reach, the creature lurches forth in a surprisingly fast motion,-\nOrcish Wildlife, cont.\n===================,typically snapping at it's prey's legs in an attempt to disable effective escape. Once the prey is disable, the Tortoise will often move to simply crush it's unfortunate victim. It's been noted for the Tortoise -\nOrcish Wildlife, cont.\n===================to simply walk over the victim, breaking bone and entirely disabling the creature. Once the prey is entirely disabled, the creature will move to swallow the victim whole, exhibiting traits of a snake, unhinging-\nOrcish Wildlife, cont.\n===================iit's jaw and swallowing the prey slowly.\n\n[!] A crude sketch of a large turtle sits on the bottom of the page, with a green figure lodged in its mouth.\n[!]\nOrcish Wildlife, cont.\n===================Habitat:\nThe Sand Tortoise is only found within the War Uzg lands of Anthos. It's found in secluded lands, typically on the outskirts of settlements, it's unclear of how the creature remains-\nOrcish Wildlife, cont.\n===================hydrated, as it is not seen consuming cacti, and prefers to avoid any bodies of water.\n\"A small tale has depicted the sand tortoise simply hydrates through the consumption of its prey.\"\nOrcish Wildlife, cont.\n===================Characteristics:\nThe Creature is a staggering size, roughly the equivalent to a small gatehouse, or nobleman's manor and it's not uncommon for the creatures to be mistaken for mobile islands. [Next Volume]", ""),
        StaticBook("Anthos Life: II", "Gerald Elgan", "===================\n\n\nWildlife and monsters of Anthos: Volume II\n\nTranscribed by:\nGerald Elgan\n\n\n\n\n==================\nOrcish Wildlife\n===================\"The last volume was midway through the depiction of Sand Tortoises\"\n[!] A small scribble of a book with the \"I\" mark on it, with an arrow pointing to the book, the number 50 on the end. [!]\nOrcish Wildlife, cont.\n===================Characteristics:\nThe shell of the Sand Tortoise is noted to have qualities surpassing that of the finest steel, and is roughly as thicker than a grown man's forearm. Preferred method of breaching remains unknown.\nOrcish Wildlife, cont.\n===================However, upon discovery of a deceased Sand Tortoise, it's noted that the shell has grown weak and brittle, making it entirely useless for combat adaption, suggesting the shell is in some form an organic -\nOrcish Wildlife, cont.\n===================,material, much like teeth. When the host dies, the shell dries out, the color diminishes and becomes weak and frail. The Jaw of the Sand Tortoise is known to bend and crack Iron, as if made of Wood. Close-\nOrcish Wildlife, cont.\n===================fighting with the creature is not advised, avoidance is strongly suggested. The bodily scales of the Sand Tortoise are noted to maintain the quality of common Iron, and are quite dense.\nOrcish Wildlife, cont.\n===================\"Straadoth\"\n----------\nDescription:\nStraadoth's are typically nocturnal in nature, they silther and slide across dunes, sometimes travelling in pairs. The beast emerges from it's sleep at night, -\nOrcish Wildlife, cont.\n===================coughing up some bile and then slinking off into the night, the beast does this to mark safe spots and also mating places. Orcish hunters often look for these beasts for the skin, which is very resistant to the -\nOrcish Wildlife, cont.\n===================elements, the teeth of the Straadoth are like needles, they are numerous but easily broken, meant for ripping prey apart instead of chewing, the Straadoth has no claws, but instead humanoid hands which it can grip\nOrcish Wildlife, cont.\n===================things with. The beast also possesses a dart-like tongue, which shoots out to impale its victims. But the Straadoth's real asset is it's tail, thick and long, which it uses to whip things with. The Straadoth\nOrcish Wildlife, cont.\n===================iis usually four feet tall, and twelve feet long, with muscular limbs, the good thing about the Straadoth, is it can only see moving things, as it has no eyes and can feel the vibrations of footsteps through the -\nOrcish Wildlife, cont.\n===================sand, it can only survive in the sand as it constantly shifts and moves, if someone where to take the Straadoth away from it's habitat, it would die.\n[!] A drawing of a Straadoth is here, crudely done [!]\nOrcish Wildlife, cont.\n===================Excerpt from an explorer's journal:\n\"I saw the dunes rise, my wagon shook and a long hiss was heard, a red spike suddenly pierced through my cavern and blood soaked the wall, I looked out of the hatch to see that-\nOrcish Wildlife, cont.\n===================\"both drivers were dead, with large holes in their chests and most of their bones picked clean.\"\n[!] A drawing of the wagon is here, with the Straadoth roams nearby, it the color of sand. [!]\nOrcish Wildlife, cont.\n===================Habitat:\nSandy biomes only, thick sandy dunes are where it functions, anything lesser would result in starvation, blindness and eventually death.\nOrcish Wildlife, cont.\n===================Characteristics:\nThe Straadoth takes whatever color of it's environment is, making it excellent at blending in, it's attack style is quick, vicious and brutal, with no care if it hurts itself in the process. It-\nOrcish Wildlife, cont.\n===================will shoot it's tongue out at the opponent, grip his horse and throw it at him, whip him with the tail or create a large cloud of sand by smacking it's tail repeatedly against the ground.\nGlobal Wildlife\n===================Vodnik\n------\nDescription:\nThe beast is humanoid in appearance, and is not to be mistaken with a zombie. Vodniks lurk around coastal towns and villages with deep lakes or rivers, they are revived bodies of\nGlobal Wildlife, cont.\n===================men and women that have met their demise by drowning. What makes a Vodnik is actually the parasites that lurk in the water, they use the body as the host and grow...\nTheir hair is slimy and green, as is the ends -\nGlobal Wildlife, cont.\n===================of their arms and legs, they leave trails similar to a snail's and make gurgled howls when it is a full moon. They possess a toxin which sedates their prey, which they then drag into the water to feast upon.\nGlobal Wildlife, cont.\n===================Excerpt from a text on Marine Creatures:\n\"These are scoundrels who ended their wicked lives in the water. Drowned alive or thrown into deep watery ravines, they turn into vengeful creatures which stalk the -\nGlobal Wildlife, cont.\n===================i\"inhabitants of fishing settlements, dragging unsuspecting bathers off into the depths.\"\n[!] A sketch of a morbid, swimming zombie is seen here, grabbing onto the foot of an harmless elf. [!]\nGlobal Wildlife, cont.\n===================Habitat:\nDeep lakes, Rivers, Coastal Sea and Ponds. Anywhere with a vast, deep amount of water for the vodnik to dwell in.\nGlobal Wildlife, cont.\n===================Characteristics:\nThe Vodnik is slow and weak, but in the water, the creature is at its best. It can swim at unbelievable speeds and hear the faintest of footsteps on the land, the beast also possesses a sedative -\nGlobal Wildlife, cont.\n===================iin its saliva, which it uses to drown the prey. The Vodnik also possesses the ability to ignore bad injuries, one could cut off all it's limbs and it would still try and attack its prey, it also doesn't weaken -\nGlobal Wildlife, cont.\n===================when it bleeds, is poisoned or tossed off cliffs. The Vodnik, as agile and aware as it may be, is completely blind, it relies completely on feeling, smell and its hearing. The Vodnik is quite scrawny, like a -\nGlobal Wildlife, cont.\n===================decomposing corpse, though it possesses abnormally large claws and teeth like knives, which it has several sets of. Upon death, the Vodnik does something very odd, it hacks up it's insides and the parasites that -\nGlobal Wildlife, cont.\n===================lived within crawl back into the water to find another host corpse, and create another Vodnik.\n[!] A picture of a Vodnik clawing it's stomach is seen here\n[!]\nGlobal Wildlife, cont.\n===================\"Winged Screamer\"\nGiant Raven\n----------\nDescription:\nA massive Raven. The reason for it's mutation is unknown. Perhaps the exposure to mana, or simple adjustment to the wildlife within Anthos.\nGlobal Wildlife, cont.\n===================Much like all ravens, the creature is a Near Black, Dark Blue. It's Beak and Talons a jet black. The creatures typically stand at 10 feet with a wing span exceeding 12 feet.\nGlobal Wildlife, cont.\n===================Habitat:\nThe creature is nomadic, typically living atop mountains for a mating cycle before moving on.\n[!] A picture of a raven compared to a human is here. [!]\nGlobal Wildlife, cont.\n===================The creatures Talons could easily render a bit of low quality Iron useless, though the creature prefers to simply scoop it's prey before allowing it to plunge to the grounds below. The Beak of the bird is capable-\nGlobal Wildlife, cont.\n===================of cracking platemail, though only with repeated efforts. The Giant Raven emits a loud scream that can easily be heard for miles around, often said to echo throughout the lands, earning it the nickname,-\nGlobal Wildlife, cont.\n===================\"Winged Screamer.\"\nThe creature typically feeds on cattle or lone adventurers, preferring to make short work of it's meals. When it's nest is approached, the raven goes into an enraged frenzy, attempting to knock\nGlobal Wildlife, cont.\n===================iit's attacker from the mountain, if not, with it's talons, the wind produced by the flap of it's massive wings.", ""),
        StaticBook("Anthos Ruins: 1", "Valmir_", "Ruins of Anthos Vol. I - Northern Anthos\n               Part two.\n                  ------\nNatural Beauty\n\nAlthough I had promised myself to keep this text on point I find myself unable to prevent myself from describing the wonders of the Spider Cave. Although not specifically a ruin, I find it to be a most profound example of a breed of\nnatural beauty not seen since the now-lost caverns of Menorcress in Asulon. It’s entrance does, however, bear the carved stones seen in other Anthosian ruins. Upon exiting Leumalin from the gate to the Western Docks if one hugs the cliff wall they will\nfind a gaping and glowing cave. Upon entering, one would be greeted by two sights; course black pebbles on the cave floor and and a thick covering of spiderweb on the cave ceiling. Despite any natural reaction of fear one might have from this evidence of\na spider infestation, none of my visits have managed to show any sign of current habitation. Past this initial cave can be seen a quite remarkable sight. The cave opens on the lip of a massive cave, covered in mushrooms and vines of all descriptions, but\nperhaps most striking are the massive luminous mushrooms, headed with sweeping translucent caps that bow towards a beautiful subterranean lake. I would urge any druid or scholar who reads this to visit this sight, as it represents an unique environment\nquite unlike anything I have seen outside the labyrinthine caverns of Menorcress.\nAMMENDMENT:\n\nDo not travel to this cave without heavy guard! A spider broodmother seriously injured a druid when I led an expedition to the cave and her brood is still in residence. Take extreme caution!\nEpilogue\n\nIn my next volumes I shall explore and describe the prolific ruins of the satellite landmass known to most as ‘The Wilds’, a lawless and dangerous region that is host to what have been said to be the most complete and extensive ruins in\nAnthos, as well as the ruins of Southern Anthos. Until that time, I offer these observations of a simple traveller to the purview of Malinor’s scholars to do as they please.\n\nPenned by Kaelin Mahariel, traveller and amateur explorer.\nMap References ~\nLumber Camp and Forest Ruins - ((X:-1176 Y:88 Z:-398))\nCave Colonnade - ((X:-936 Y:72 Z:-729))\nStatue and Stone Circles - ((X:-853 Y:72 Z:-795))\nTower Temple Ruin - ((X:-787 Y:85 Z:-136))\nIce Camp - ((X:-137 Y:121 Z:-997))\nSpider Cave - ((X:-920 Y:67 Z:-1178)\n          ---------------", ""),
        StaticBook("Anti-Contagion", "Lelien", "Anti-Contagion\n  Filtration Mask\n     Guidebook\n\n       by Mirtok\nThank you for accepting your very own anti-contagion filtration mask, through this handbook you will learn all the important functions and procedures for operating and effectively using your mask. By the order of the Hochmeister in hopes to combat the\nrising infectious ailments, every Hanseti citizen is issued their own filtration mask for safety.\nSafety Tips\n\n1) Never misplace or lose your mask, though the Hochmeister cares deeply for your safety, he will not be able to give out spare masks to careless people.\n2) Never share your mask, to prevent the spread of the illness the Hochmeister urges all mask users to stay with their own mask no matter the circumstances.\n3) Maintain your mask, keeping your mask in proper order at full upkeep will prevent incidences of breaks or breaches in your mask’s special protective filtration and sealant systems.\n4) Use filters to their fullest, each few years the Hochmeister will distribute new filters for your masks but until then you must ration off what you have, this will not only test your ability to be responsible of your life, but to prove you have what it\ntakes to survive in a hazardous world.\nPreparing your Mask\nUpon receiving your mask, it is a good idea to become acquainted with how it works and how to properly use it to fend off infective agents of death.\n\nFirstly, it is a good idea to make sure your filters are in place and secure\nalong both sides of the mask.\n\nUnder the eye sockets of the masks should be two metal containers with 3 clip secure locks located on the circumference of each capsule. Inside you can see the several layers of filters and spinning mechanism that make\nup the filtration system. Do refrain from tinkering with the delicate parts and only manipulate the filters. Once assured that the filters fit snuggly in their respective areas we can make to making sure there are no cracks in the mask. We are unsure as\nto how the infection is spread and therefore it is important to count for all possible biological entries into the body. First examine the two large eye sockets and lenses on the front of the mask. Also scan along the main folds and seams of the mask to\nmake sure no loose strings or openings are present. Finally, make sure the center piece where each tube leading from the two filter capsules is not loose or emitting a rattling noise when shook. Be sure to be extra careful when checking for breaches as\na single hole can mean the difference between life or death.\nReplacing Filters\nTo replace a filter, you must first unlatch the lid to the two filtration capsules. Once the interior is exposed, carefully turn the filter pads until a hard click is heard above the smaller clicking during turning. When heard, the\nthe pads should slightly elevate themselves into a popping motion and then should be ready for removal. Replacement works in the opposite fashion, place the new ones in the direction of the painted arrows and turn when the resistance is felt.\nSeveral clicks should be heard until a final snap indicates its in place. Close the capsule and move to the next one.\nUsing your Mask\nWhen your situation calls for you to use your mask, you must follow a few simple steps to ensure your maximum safety in the face of an infective area. First loosen all of the straps along the back and front of the mask. Then place the\nloose mask over your head and position the eye sockets for your preferred viewing.\n\nWhen ready, slowly tighten each strap until the strapped area feels tight and snug over your head. It is very important to maintain a tight fit but also to keep the mask\nfrom cutting off blood flow to your mask and face as such will prompt discomfort and compel you to adjust the mask. When all straps have been secured, turn the small dial located on the front of your mask where the capsule tubes meet until you hear a\nsmall rush of air., When all these are done, you should have achieved maximum anti-contagion safety.\nBreaching/Cracks\nIn the event of a breach or crack in your mask, it is advised by the Hochmeister to quickly remove yourself from the jeopardizing area and seek cover and solitude from any other contact with others. The Hochmeister then urges you to\nremove the filter pads from your filtration capsules and attempt to apply them over your nose and mouth if no other repair methods are successful on the damaged mask.\n\nGood luck out there and may Celestia keep this tragedy from our frozen lands.", ""),
        StaticBook("Aphidylytes", "Anonymous", "Scribed from the last words of Urangoi Ballenz, fifth descendant of Urguan’s generations-\n\nI am stuck. I ventured too deep into the coil of the Motley Ravine, and after a wrong turn in one of the\nabandoned mines I suppose I was knocked out. I’ve awoken to be affixed to a wall of some gooey, thick sludge. It binds me to the wall, but luckily I have my journal wedged beside me, and close enough to write on. Nearby I\nhear a woman, I can barely make out her lectures, but it sounds like she is preaching in a far off cavern… I fear for my life here.\n\nDeep underground, beneath the ridges of the Motley Ravine, lay a muddied labyrinth\nmarbled in stone and the hardened byproduct of ant-like construction. Riddling the maze of tunnels and crevices once scuttled swarms of uncountable hordes, writhing masses of legged, exoskeletal shells\nand tibia, clusters of wriggling bugs formed out of coxa and spinnerets. With thick armor of biomass from their antennas to their thoraxes, in the pitch abyss roamed the aphids, grand and gargantuan in both number and size.\nBut now, all have vanished. Not a single critter may be sought scuttling about in those barren halls, decrepit with time’s withering. That being due to collapse. The Deep now only consists of a chamber; the\npith. The lifeless bluff of the overworld resides without motion while all of the Aphidylytes are compacted into their own deposits and veins of sand and sediment. Except for one.\n\nIn the core of one\nmesa’s knoll, wedged down below in a sliver of openness, lies the central crux. It too lies in stillness, but not in death, but in concealed ambush. The ancient Hive Queen rests in unconscious slumber, awaiting the day for\nexcavation of a foolish kind before her automaticly reactive limbs may draw in the prey and feed upon it to revive her, and thus the Hive.", ""),
        StaticBook("Apology for Tail", "Rhova'dir", "My apologies Tailesin, I didn't want to drag you to the cave to get hurt and you shouldn't risk your life unless you're sure you're going to live.\nI beg your pardon.\n-Rhova'dir", ""),
        StaticBook("Arabella", "Vicelin", "Lucy,\n\nYou are to head into town and linger around the tavern. \n\nYou are to wear the red dress I had put in your wardrobe and, if possible, dye your hair a darker shade.\nRemember, you are a masseuse.", ""),
        StaticBook("Arcana & Oddity", "Audrey Caillot", "~Arcana & Oddities!~\nThis shop is dedicated to bringing those who value items with stories just that! Items with stories.\n  We have put forth the energy to find items from those before and those past, and we have made ourselves focused to-\ntaking the utmost of care of the artifacts and relics we have collected over the years, and now we would like to share them.\n  We have two locations currently, one permanent home in Aethermoore where we have been allowed\nto originate, and a stall in the Monk Market, where you have probably recieved this booklet.\n\nOn top of items we have collected, we carry enchantments and the like, and support the community of mages and the arts.\nIt is with the greatest of pleasures we share our collections with you, and we hope you enjoy your stay!\n\n-=-", ""),
        StaticBook("Arcane Concepts", "[Ghost] The Eternal Librarian", "Arcane Magic:\n      Concepts\n\n   by Kalenz Uradir\nIt is the arcane mage which summons their spells from the void. However, simply connecting to the void and summoning forth what a mage desires is no simple affair. Just as the novice artist finds themselves incapable of painting in as much detail as a\nmaster, a mage must learn the simple aspects of arcane magic which make said magic possible before they are capable of producing anything desired.\n\nLet us then look at the casting of a spell. It is the mage who uses their mind to\nconnect to the void. Which in turn is combined with the energy of their mana to form their desired arcane subtype. However, even if one is to know that, there are many other simple elements of magic which must be known to the apprentice mage.\nShifting to the topic of aura. Aura is quite simply is a field of mana which surrounds a mage's body while they cast their magic. Almost each and every mage is to take upon an aura, though they are often very faint and are only evident to the careful\nobserver at an almost uncomfortable range. Thus, to pick a mage out by aura alone is difficult if not impossible. It is often said that aura takes the color of a mage's personality. Each having a different color depending on their particular person.", ""),
        StaticBook("Arcane Concepts", "Eenhoornheid", "Arcane Magical Concepts \n\n          by Kalenz Uradir\nIt is the arcane mage which summons their spells from the void. However, simply connecting to the void and summoning forth what a mage desires is no simple affair.\nJust as the novice artist finds themselves incapable of painting in as much detail as a master, a mage must learn the simple aspects of arcane magic which makes said magic possible before they are capable of producing anything desired.\nLet us then look at the casting of a spell. It is the mage who uses their mind to connect to the void. Which in turn is combined with the energy of their mana to form their desired arcane subtype.\nHowever, even if one is to know that, there are many other simple elements of magic which must be known to the apprentice mage. Shifting to the topic of aura.\nAura is quite simply is a field of mana which surrounds a mage's body while they cast their magic.\nAlmost each and every mage is to take upon an aura, though they are often very faint and are only evident to the careful observer at an almost uncomfortable range. Thus, to pick a mage out by aura alone is difficult if not impossible.\nIt is often said that aura takes the color of a mage's personality. Each having a different color depending on their particular person.", ""),
        StaticBook("Arcane Evocation", "Salendys", "-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-        Arcane\n      Evocation\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\nThis book was written to help students and aspiring students of arcane evocation to better understand this magic and ease their learning.\n\nWritten by: -Salendys\nChapter 1: What is Arcane Evocation?\n                           \n\nArcane Evocation is the art of drawing pure magical energy from the void. It can then be shaped as anything the mage can think of. This is a creative form of magic\nwith mostly artistical uses. While it is possible to use this magic in combat, only a skilled arcanist can do so, and even then it is not as strong as the other types of evocation. If your intention is to acquire a means of dealing damage, then this is\nnot the magic for you.\nChaper 2:\nArcane Energy\n                           \n\nArcane energy is a rare element. In fact, it does not exist naturally in the world. It is an ethereal substance almost exclusive to the void. Because of this, Arcane Evocation is\nthe most difficult type of evocation to learn.\nAs with all other types of evocation, one must fully understand the element that is being evoked. The only way to study arcane energy is by observing an evocation of someone who already knows this magic.\nThis means it is practically impossible to learn without a teacher.\n\nNow, for those who already have a teacher and seek to complement their lessons with further knowledge, the arcane element can be described as follows.\nIn it's purest form, arcane energy is invisible, shapeless, odorless, completely inhert and very volatile. It can be compared to air or smoke, having a similiar composition than most gaseous substances.\nThose who have observed evocations may have noticed\na fine, thin mist surrounding them. This is because it isn't a single mass. It is in fact a conglomeration of countless tiny wisps of energy that together give the illusion of being a single object.\nSmoke is perhaps the thing that visually resembles\narcane energy the most in our world. Studying its shapeless and volatile nature may be of big help to understand arcane energy.\nChapter 3: Aura\n                           \n\nAura is a field of mana that surrounds living beings. More complex beings, such as descendants, have a colour associated to their aura. Each individual has their own colour for their aura.\nSome believe that the colour depends on one's personality. This isn't always the case, however, and anyone may have any colour.\nThis colour doesn't change, unless other forces somehow manage to tamper with your aura, which is usually very bad.\nAuras are very relevant to Arcane Evocation in particular.\nWhen raw arcane energy is drawn from the void, it instantly mixes with the mage's aura, making it visible and giving it colour. It is a common misconception to assume that arcane evocationists\nmanipulate aura itself. In truth, it is simply the product of mixing aura with arcane energy that is being manipulated, not the actual aura.\nAnd no, arcanists cannot see other people's aura or make it visible.\nAura is a very personal thing, like\nyour own soul.\nThis means your evocations can never mix with someone elses, or other types of evocation.\nChapter 4: Beginner steps\n                           \n\nAfter you have managed your first evocation, there is not much you can do. You will only be capable of producing a small wisp and hold it for a short time. The best thing to\ndo is to keep practicing. With each successful attempt you will be able to hold the wisp a little longer. Make sure to have rested enough to be completely recovered after each attempt.\nEventually you will be able to hold your wisp for about five minutes.\n[!] A detailed drawing of a wisp hovering over an open hand occupies most of this page.\nAt that point you'll get enough time to figure out how to get your wisp to do things. You are in control of your evocation, but must learn to control it properly.\nTry moving it around slowly. Think clearly of the movement you want it to make.\nAt first a few inches is all you can manage at a time, but with practice it'll get better. Another good excercise for beginners is to make it shrink and grow slightly in size. Adding and removing the amount of energy in an evocation is a basic\ntool that is key for the later stages of learning.\nOnce you can comfortably manipulate the size and movement of the wisp with relative freedom, you can start to attempt shaping it. Simple geometrical shapes such as cubes, spheres and cylinders\nare the easiest to achieve and you should start there.\nImagine the arcane energy taking the desired shape with as much detail as possible. Do not lose focus once the evocation has taken the desired shape or it will become amorphous again.\nThis is the end of this book. Hopefuly this will help many students to complement their learning of arcane evocation.\n\nA book dedicated to advanced students and even novice arcanists will be written in the future.\nThank you very much for reading my book and I hope you found it helpful.\n\n[!]What appears to be a drawing of a chibi dark elf in robes giving the reader a thumbs up lies in the bottom half of this page.", ""),
        StaticBook("Arcane Evocation", "Lilak Nislive", "Book\n          on\n        Arcane\n      Evocation\n\n\n\n\n\n[Link]\nhttps://www.lordofthecraft.net/forums/topic/163172-book-arcane-evocation/", ""),
        StaticBook("Arcane Evocation", "Kirrekith", "Arcane Evocation\n\nTranscribed by the Farseer Thurak, 19th of the Great Harvest, 1529.\n\nOne: What is Arcane Energy?\nTwo: Arcane Energy.\nThree: Aura.\nFour: Beginner steps.\nChapter One\nWhat is Arcane Evocation?\n-------------------\nArcane Evocation is the art of drawing pure magical energy from the void. It can be shaped as anything the mage can think of.\n\nThis is a creative form of magic with the mostly\nartistic uses. While it is possible to use this magic in combat, only a skilled arcanist can do so, and even then it is not as strong as the other types of evocation. If your intention is to aquire a means of dealing damage, then this is not the magic for\nyou.\n\nChapter Two\nArcane Energy\n\nArcane energy is a rare element. In fact, it does not exist naturally in the world. It is an ethereal substance almost exclusive to the void. Because of this, Arcane Evocation is\nthe most difficult type of evocation to learn. As with all other types of evocation one must fully understand the element that is being evoked. The only way to study arcane energy is by observing an evocation of someone who already knows this magic. This\nmeans it is practically impossible to learn without a teacher.\n\nNow for those already have a teacher and seek to complement their lessons with further knowledge, the arcane element  can be described as follows. \n\nIn its purest form,\narcane energu is invisible, shapeless, odorless, completely inert and very volatile. It can be compared to air or smoke, having similar composition to most gaseous substances. \n\nThose who have observed evocations my have noticed a fine, thin mist\nsurrounding them. This is because it isn't a single mass. It is, in fact, a conglomeration of countless tiny wisps of energy that together give the illusion of being a single object. \n\nSmoke is perhaps the thing that visually resembles arcane energy the\nmost in our world. Studying its shapeless and erratic nature may be of big help to understand arcane energy.\n\nChapter Three\nAura\n-------------------\nAura is a field of mana that surrounds living beings. More complex beings, such as\ndescendants, have a colour associated to their aura. Each individual has their own colour for their aura. \n\nSome believe that the colour depends on one's personality. This isn't always the case, however, and anyone may have any colour. This colour doesn't\nchange, unless other forces somehow manage to tamper with your aura, which is usually very bad. Auras are very relevant to Arcane Evocation in particular. \n\nWhen raw arcane energy is drawn from the void, it instantly mixes with the mages\naura, making it visible and giving it colour. It is a common misconception to assume that arcane evocations manipulate aura itself. In truth, it is simply the product of mixing aura with arcane energy that is being manipulated, not the actual aura.\nAnd no, arcanists cannot see other people's aura or make it visible. \n\nAura is a very personal thing, like your own soul.\n\nThis means your evocations can never mix with someone else's or other types of evocation.\nChapter Four\nBeginner Steps\n-------------------After you have managed your first evocation, there is not much you can do. You will only be capable of producing a small wisp and hold it for a short time. The best thing to do is to keep practicing. With\neach successful attempt you will be able to hold the wisp a little longer. Make sure to have rested enough to be completely recovered after each attempt. \n\nEventually you will be able to hold your wisp for about five minutes.\n[!] A Detailed Drawing of a wisp hovering over an open hand occuies most of this page.\n\nAt that point you'll get enough time to figure out how to get your wisp to do things. You are in control of your ecovation, but must learn to control it properly. Try\nmoving it around slowly. Think clearly of the movements you wish it to make. \n\nAt first a few inches is all you can manage at a time, but with practice it'll get better. Another good exercise for beginners is to make it shrink and grow slightly in size.\nAdding and removing the amount of energy is an evocation is a basic tool that is key for the later stages of learning.\n\nOnce you can comfortably manipulate the size and movement of the wisp with relative freedom, you can start to attempt shaping it.\nSimple geomertical shapes such as cubes, spheres and cylinders are the easiest to achieve and you should start there. Imagine that arcane energy taking the desided shape wit has much detail as possible. Do not lose focus once the evocation has taken the\ndesired shape or it will become amorphous again.\n\nThis is the end of this book. Hopefully this will help many students to complement their learning of arcane evocation. \n\nAs book dedicated to advanced students and even novice arcanists\nbe written in the future. Thank you very much for reading my book and I hope you found it helpful.\n\nWrote by Farseer, re-wrote by Kirrekith during the raid on the Orc Capital, on the 16th of The Grand Harvest, 1532. \n\nSigned Kirrekith", ""),
        StaticBook("Arcane Familiars", "Ac'Aelu Tinuvial", "An Introduction to Familiars\n\nBy Ac'Aelu Tinuvial.\nContents -\n\nI - An Overview\n\nII - The Familiar of Stone\n\nIII - The Familiar of Fire\n\nIV - The Uses of Water\n\nV - Arcanic Familiars\nI - An Overview\n\nFamiliars are, in the most basic sense, magical golems.\n\nMade of evoked material, a familiar serves its master through a verbal link not unlike the constructs of\nGolemancy. \n\nThey consist of two parts. The shell, and the substance.\n\nThe shell is a number of enchanted plates that provide a boundary for the evoked material. While it does not physically restrict\nthe material's formation, it serves as a sort of guideline to give it shape. A familiar's shell can be nearly as full or bare as the creator wishes, so long as it defines the shape of the familiar. The shells are crucial to the function of a familiar, and\nas such, those with more coverage of the body tend to create more stable beings.\n\nThe substance of a familiar is the element of which it is made. At the time of this writing, five types have been created with functional stability. Those are\nStone, Ice, Arcane, Water, and Fire.\n\nThe properties of these materials directly affect the creature's functionality, which will be elaborated on in the following chapters.\nII - The Familiar of Stone\n\nThose who've seen Golems of stone will find many similarities between them and Stone Familiars.\n\nThe most solid sort of Familiar, Stone beings share most of their uses with Golems.\nThey can hold objects, and fight using them.\n\nThey can also launch small projectiles from their bodies, usually in the form of spikes. These take a long period of time to reform on their bodies, though.\nBeing the most solid, they are the most resistant. Damage to their plates has a less immediate effect on them than on fluid forms, though a destroyed plate is still devastating.\nII - The Familiar of Fire\n\nOn the opposite end of the spectrum from stone stands the Familiar of Flame. Made of voidal fire, these creatures are as destructive as they are fragile.\nThey cannot hold weapons like a solid familiar could, but have a much superior use of their forms as projectiles.\n\nFire Familiars can project flame from their bodies in the form of orbs or a jet, but their volatile element puts extra\nstrain on their plates. As such, a damaged plate is a much greater threat to their body than it would be to a stone familiar.\nIV - The Uses of Water\n\nWater can form two types of Familiars, water and ice.\n\nThese forms are very similar to Fire and Stone, respectively, and behave the same way.\nIce is nearly as solid  as Stone, and Water is similar in use to fire.\nVI - Arcanic Familiars\n\nArcane familiars are a sort of middle ground between the 'solid' and 'fluid' constructs. They can manipulate objects as well as a stone or ice construct, as well as project itself like a water or fire familiar.\nThis middle-ground construct is more solid than a fluid sort, but not as resilient as one of stone.\nThose interested in learning more about Familiars, and other similar projects, are encouraged to seek out the Celein Institute of Magic and Technology.", ""),
        StaticBook("Arcane Magic", "Gallidron Elindrow", "An\n       Encyclopedic\n         Arcanum\n~````````````````:'''''''''''''''''~\n             ;O;\n    a guide to magic\n           `.{0},'\n\n             By\n   Gallidron  Elindrow\nWhat is magic? To undertand the intricacies of the acrane we must first understand this basic question.\nTo some magic is a miracle that cannot be explained, to others it is a science that can be disected and recorded. In fact it is somehwere in between.\nMagic can produce wonderous effects when used properly, and it can be horribly malicious when malpracticed.  It is not the belief of this author that magic has feelings or desires of its own, but the void from where it originates can be rather harsh on\nlife. Or so I have been told.\n\nMagic is inherently dangerous and should only be attempted by the well studied and practiced.\nBasic Spell Crafting\n         Theory\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~The idea behind magic is terribly simple. Formulate in detail the spell you desire in your mind and then pull the desired effect from the void using the mana that exists in all of us. This is,\nhowever, much more difficult and complicated in practice. To have the mental prowess and fortitude to formulate the spell EXACTLY as you need it is a daunting task in and of itself. This action is in fact creating the desired spell IN the void! Consider,\nif you will, your consiousness traveling into the hostillity of the void and there creating a spell, that if performed incorrectly, could kill you. It can all at once fill you with awe and terror.\nIt is also important to note that if one attempts a\nspell that is out of their respective league, the energy required could cause serious and sometimes perminant damage to the user.\nThe Schools of Magic\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~Herein I shall list the schools of known magic and offer a description of its form and function so far as I am able.\nArcane Magic\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~Arcane magic is the most wide spread magic in the world. It is the most written about, the most studied and the most practiced. It is that which is primarily drawn from the void and has several schools of use.\nTransmutation\n`````````````````````````\nThis kind of magic is the most like a science. One must study and understand to a great degree that which they wish to transmute. They must also understand that which they desire to transmute the item in\nquestion into. Further more you must be able to see the item. There are a few rules that one must follow as well. Namely that one cannot transmute that which is alive, nor can you make too great a change. For example, iron cannot be made into water as\nthey do not share an element, nor are they in the same physical state. Also there must be an equivilent exchange. A pound of stone may not become ten pounds of silver.\nEnchantment\n~~~~~~~~~~\nA usefull kind of magic, and one that must be performed at an enchantment table.\nUsing this school, one may imbue objects with spells and magical properties. \n\nTo do this, one needs a Mana Gem. These gems can be made of\nany mineral, but they need to be, at least, roughly gem shaped and polished or engraved. The larger and more highly valued the gem, the more mana that can be stored therein. You can then use the Mana Gem to fuel the enchantment. Enchanted items need to be\nrecharged or the enchantment will lose power and fail.\nWards and Abjuration\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nIn all magic, mana is used to manifest the void born spell in the physical world. This is commonly refered to as a mana anchor. The purpose of a ward or an abjuration is to disrupt the mana anchor and thus\ndestroy the spell. A ward is used more like a shield, to stop incoming spells. An abjuration is used in a more offensive way. For example and abjuration could be hurled at a spell to disrupt it, rather than to wait for it to come to you.\nBoth must be used to counter act specific kinds of magic. A ward used to deflect a fireball cannot also dispell and illusion. Each ward and abjuration must be tailored to that which it is meant to stop.\nIt is also important to note that a spell which is\nmore powerful than the ward or abjuration will be unaffected. A working knowledge of the kind of magic to be disrupted must be had in order to produce an effective counter spell.\nTelekinesis\n~~~~~~~~~\nThis is a simple form of magic. Essentially it is the use of ones mind to lift or manipulate objects without the use of hands or other physical means.\nVoid Translocation\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nNow this is an interesting form of magic. The idea is to disolve an object into the void to be recalled at a later time. However, to do this one must have a perfect memory of the object in order to reform it later and\npull it back into reality.\nHowever, an argument is to be made that the object in question is gone forever and that what ever you pull from the void is just a replica of varying quality depending of the memory of the caster.\nElemental Evocation\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nThis kind of magic is the flashy kind that everyone thinks of when talking about mages. Be it hurling a fire ball or calling down a bolt of lightning, all of this is evocation. Allow me to list the types there of.\nFire\n`'`'`'`'\nThis kind of evocation can be used to summon flame, smoke and light. It can also increase the rate at which alchemy functions. However, it is important to note that the flame evocationist is not immune to the heat of their own spells.\nWater\n~~~~~\nTo create water and control its forms is a powerful kind of evocation. Ice magic tends to be more highly sought after, but one usually learns water evocation in the process. Drinking summoned water is somewhat useless as it will vanish\nfrom the ingester's system when the spell ends.\nAir\n===)))\n\nThe most unused form of evocation because its known uses are few and the control gained is tenuous at best. There are legends of powerfull air mages who could whip up storms and the like, but these are just myths.\nElectric\n********\nThis kind of evocation is immensly powerful, but can be hard to control. The devistating attacks that are unleashed by the electric evocator are almost impossible to evade, but do take time to charge up. It is also good to note\nthat once released, magic lightning behaves as regular lightning. If there are high amounts of metal near by, the bolt may veer off in that direction.\nArcanism\n^v^v^v^v^\nThis refers to evocation of all kinds. It also includes the creation of glass like energy barriers that defend against magical and physical attack.\nThese barriers have no effect on mental or illusion magic.\nConjuration\n%%%%%%%%%%%\n\nTo conjure one must have an understanding of both biology and botany depending on that which they wish to summon.\nMorphon, is the name given to the art of summoning creatures. These magical constructs can be\ncombinations of many creatures, so long as the conjuration can function and live. \n\nPerrenial conjuration is used to summon plants, and once again, the summoned plant must make scientific sense. \nThere are historical instances of mages conjuring\nplant/creatures, though these are highly complicated to make.\nThe final and perhaps most difficult form of conjuration is Primordial. This melds the magics of evocation and conjuration into a powerful elemental. This kind of magic requires a fine\ndegree of control and much power to even attempt.\n\nConjuration is a delicate and time consuming form of magic that cannot be done on the fly. One must be prepared and have time to focus when summoning even the most simple constructs. These\nconjured entities are temporary in their nature, and only last so long as they have a supply of mana from their conjuror.\nIllusion\n-*-*-*-\nCreating false images and sounds are just the surface of the school of illusion. Indeed a talented illusionist can trick any of the five senses, even touch. If an illusion is unbelievable however, it will break.\nA branch of illusion is Cognitism. This is used to trick the mind into being more productive than usual. The applications of this kind of illusion are many, but they are delicate.\nThe third branch of illusion is mental magic. This involves entering the\nmind of another and actually influencing their thoughts. One can alter what another sees, hears, smells and touches as well as what they may think.\nOther Forms of Magic\n###################\n\nThere are, of course, more forms of magic than I have explored here. Most notably Deity Magic, Alchemy and Dark Magic. These will each be covered in later additions to my series of guides.\nConclusion\n~~~~\\,,,,,,,,,,,;,,,,,,,,,,,/~~~~\n\nIt is my hope that this guide has helped you to gain a basic understanding of what each of the Arcane Schools has to offer. To actually learn magic, one should seek out a teacher. Van'ayla my dear\nreaders and my you ever seek to gain knowledge throughout all of your days.\n\n-Gallidron Elindrow\n\nPublishing date\n9th of Amber Cold\n1514\nLook for my next book!\n\n\"The Power of Prayer\"\na guide to deity magic.", ""),
        StaticBook("Arcane Origins", "[Ghost] The Eternal Librarian", "Arcane Magic:\n       Origins\n\n   by Kalenz Uradir\nSince long into the past mages have existed. Pulling their spells and magic into reality. Different mages find themselves specializing in different forms of the arcane. However, the root of this magic throughout those who practice the arcane magic\narts is the same. Each arcane mage finds their source of magic from a realm known as the void, to which each living and sentient being is connected.\n\nThe void itself is a realm of infinite potential, yet almost paradoxically is entirely comprised of\nnothing. It is from this absolute and undetermined potential which spells and magic is pulled forth from. Connecting only with their minds a mage must take this void and change it into the form which they desire. For an evocationist this may be their\npreferred element; be it earth, wind, water or fire. For others this may be an illusion, pulling fourth light and twisting and bending the minds of their targets.\n\nHowever, it is to be noted that pulling such power from the void is no easy task. For\none to be able to control both the amount of power and the form of their desired magic is no easy feat. Indeed, many a novice find themselves rendered unconscious simply upon their first connection to the void. But, with practice over time balance is\nachieved and thus some of the most potent arcane magic is created.", ""),
        StaticBook("Arcane Origins", "Eenhoornheid", "Arcane Magic:\n       Origins\n\n   by Kalenz Uradir\nIf this book is found anywhere else than the Eternal Library of Lin’evaral, the Enclave of Haelun’or, it is stolen.\n\nBoth buyers and sellers will be punished.\n\nSigned, the Tilruir’Indor Lelien\nSince long into the past mages have existed. Pulling their spells and magic into reality. Different mages find themselves specializing in different forms of the arcane. However, the root of this magic throughout those who practice the arcane magic\narts is the same. Each arcane mage finds their source of magic from a realm known as the void, to which each living and sentient being is connected.\nThe void itself is a realm of infinite potential, yet almost paradoxically is entirely comprised of nothing. It is from this absolute and undetermined potential which spells and magic is pulled forth from. Connecting only with their minds a mage take\nthis void and change it into the form which they desire. For an evocationist this may be their preferred element: earth, wind, water or fire. For others this may be an illusion, twisting and bending the minds of their targets.\nHowever, it is to be noted that pulling such power from the void is no easy task. For one to be able to control both the amount of power and the form of their desired magic is no easy feat. Indeed, many a novice find themselves rendered unconscious\nsimply upon their first connection to the void. But, with practice over time balance is achieved and thus some of the most potent arcane magic is created.", ""),
        StaticBook("Arcane Puppetry", "Nienna Calm", "Arcane\n     Puppetry\n            \n            O\n           -|-\n            ^\n           ***\n\n\n\n\n\nBy: Nienna Calm\nA Foreword\n-------------------Dear Reader,\nMagic is an incredible thing, a wonderous art form through which the imaginary becomes real. However, there are many who would rather only use it as a tool to advance their own power. They are only-\n-Half right. Magic, especially Void magic, is indeed a tool to be used in the same way a carpenter would use a saw, but no true power will ever come of it. We live in a world where the mage is distrusted in every corner of the globe. We are Discriminated,\n-hated for our unique persepective on reality. It is a touched life we walk; Do not embark on this trek lightly.\n\n             O\n            -|-\n             ^\nWhat Is\nArcane Puppetry?\n-------------------*Everything on the topic is listed here*\n\n((Link: https://goo.gl/9qEdyA ))\n\n*You should definitely read this to learn the magic*\nCreating Your\n  Arcane Puppet\n-------------------A properly made Arcane Puppet is a complicated piece of machinery, on par with a Golem or a Obelisk in complexity. In order for a puppet to function, every piece of the Marionette's makeup\nis specially enchanted with telekinetic mechanisms that allow it to move of its own accord. This process might seem straightforward at first, but as the puppet becomes more lifelike, hundreds of small enchantments will end up overlapping and at times\nconflicting with one another just to operate simple movements. More than ten enchantments may be working in unison for an arcane puppet to simply walk on a flat plane.\n\nNaturally, because of this complex design, only a skilled Enchanter\ncan create a puppet for you. If you know the magic yourself already, well, this portion of learning just got easier for you. If not, expect to be indebted to one handsomely quite soon.\nHere is a list of what Enchantments Any Arcane puppet Should Have:\n\n@-A telekinetic Enchantment for every component of the puppet.\n\n@-A special visual enchantment that allows one to see(*)\n@-(Optional) An illusionary enchant to allow one to speak through the puppet.\n\n@- An overall Alterational modification to make the Clay puppet light enough to use.\n(*)- Creating the visual enchantment can be achieved through a cursory study of Soul Puppetry. Since the heart of Arcane puppetry is the connection of the soul to an enchanted puppet, some special enchantments like this one can be preformed, where\notherwise it would be impossible for a void mage to enchant such.\nConnecting to the\n  Arcane Puppet\n-------------------\n\nAs with all arcane magic, first, connect your mind to the void.\n\nThrough the void, connect to your Arcane puppet, and imagine yourself inside of it. Imagine that you-\nyourself /are/ the puppet, with a whole seperate mind, body, and life. Through this method, one is able to connect to a completed Arcane Puppet.", ""),
        StaticBook("Arcane Shielding", "Lilak Nislive", "Book\n         on\n       Arcane\n      Shielding\n\n\n[Link]\nhttps://www.lordofthecraft.net/forums/topic/163174-book-arcane-shielding/", ""),
        StaticBook("Arial Poem No.2", "Arnorian", "Open your eyes and watch the sky,\nto see the blue and the white,\nand view the stars that roam up above\nand watch the birds in flight.\nTo see the seasons change with time\nand the people grow and age,\nto see the kindness in their hearts\nand their dark eyes that hold their rage.\nOpen your eyes to notice the difference\nbetween the rumours and praise,\nfrom the people who honestly care\nto those that could not be more blasé.\nTo notice the change from black to grey\nfrom purple to blue, orange to red,\nand see green turn to yellow,\nthe rich comforted and the hungry get fed.\nOpen your eyes to watch the pain\nthat others hide from the rest.\nThey might be the man on the street\nor the masquerade, best dressed.\nNotice the seasons wash the air new\nto make room for their colours, \nand make the people change their clothes\nas well as watch out for others.\nOpen your eyes to their lives going by,\nto their hopes flickering and fading,\nthe things they want most leaving\nand their dreams gone from trading.\nWatch out for a puddle of tears\nnear a gravestone of the loved,\nand see those who longed to be touched\nas they keep their fingers gloved.\nOpen your eyes to see the compassion\nthat seems to flow in this realm,\nfrom the caring and the kindness\nto the comfort that can overwhelm.\nBut also take note of the depression\nthat sits at the bottoms of the lakes, \nthat rots on the tree branches\nand in the corners of the crates.\nOpen your eyes to see what I see, \nthe final realisation; \nthat with every new begining\ncomes yet another civilisation.\nBut just rest and take it all in,\nwith your eyes wide open\nand see this shattered realm like me,\nwith my heart completely broken.", ""),
        StaticBook("Arianna's Diary", "Arianna", "Upon traveling to Axios I have been more open to adventure. I come across the site of a large, white obleisk of magical power in a spring that lies between the wood and dark elf camps.\n\nSul, Kairn's brother, also found a large dragon like being.\nIt appeared like a Hydra with the ability to spit fire. Be forwarned, it is several oceans and mountain ranges away. It is of no immediate danger to our town, and I wouldn't want to walk all the way back to kill it. But I assume that's up to the others.\nAfter walking all the way out to the being and returning I doubt I will be going on many more adventures. Kairn and I are getting a home in town and I will most likely divert my engergies to domestic matters. I also need to speak to Artimec about,\nmy training, but he is often surrounded and busy in this transitional time. I'm sure he will have more free time soon and I will talk to him then, it's just there is so much still to do in our new land. Artimec also is commonly entertaining many women,\nwhich often compeates with his free time. Now he is also putting those who wish to join his seed through trials to test their worthiness. I doubt this will leave him with much free time, but I am finding myself too shy to bother him on the subject.\nI often worry about coming across as needy, and therefore am aprehnsive to ask him for any favors.\n\nElvonhir is rather rude to Kairn, I wonder why he ever asked me to join his seed. I'm glad Kairn influenced me to decline, he is an ass of a man.\nI finally spoke with Artimec about my training, unfortunately he quized me just after a small disagreement with Kairn where I was very cloudy in my thinking. It made me question a lot of things, but Kairn is supporting me and helping me stay resolved to\nstudy harder. I feel very lucky to have him as my partner.\n\nKairn punched some new Sirame recruit, I believe his name was Leo. And he almost got in a fight with Elvonhir. We got in a fight about it when we got home, but ultimately we made up. \nElv is possibly my least favorite person I have ever met. Or he is quickly earning that title. He needs to learn to be less of a dick to Kairn, just because he can be one doesn't mean he should be. Kairn was mad I didn't support him 'winning' their\nposturing contest. I think we said some things we both regret. I'm just worried because he seems distant often. I assumed he would be more open in time but I will probably have to continue coaxing it out of him.\n\nFaeinn is one of the people I went on\nSul's journey with. I've seen her a couple times now. She's nice and I see her becoming my friend, even if she's Artimec's daughter. \n\nKairn has been increasingly distant. He continues to care for me, he even cooked me a meal but, if anything that ju\ncauses to worry me more. Unfortunately the moments when I am most concerned about our relationship I feel most called by nature. I've met more and more dryads and the call to join them increases whenever Kairn and I are in conflict.\nI know it would devastate him if I left him to devote myself to that call, so I try and ignore it as much as possible. But if our relationship were to end I would certainly have no other reason to hear the call and join the sisterhood of the dryads.\nI have heard rumblings that Artimec's other student is sleeping with him. I'm not suprised, just irritated that I can not also use my own sexuality against him to get the training I want. Kairn would hate me flirting with him, and he would hate\nArtimec even more if he took things too far. Which he undoubtedly would. It's frustrating to not be able to use my former ways of getting things done, and instead worrying about Kairn's reaction to what I probably need to do.\n\nLife among the other wood\nelves once felt fresh and lively. But I'm going to need to do things to save myself from bordem it seems.\n\nIn order to save myself from ever feeling bored I've resolved to make more female friends. A new high elf moved into town today\nand I greeted her, she also lives in the upper canopy. She recomeneded I become friends with Arahaelth, she said we were similar. I belive she is Katar Aureon's wife. I should ask Kairn about her.\n\nMy life has gotten signficantly less boring, I believe\nI may be pregnant. For the past several months I have awoken for almost every morning and was ill. I have also had to fight a terrible fatigue. If I had to guess I've been with child for only a month or two, but I have yet to tell Kairn or anyone else.\nIn reflecting upon our future child and my past writing, I feel my past thoughts foolish, I think of Kairn and I seperating as ridiculous. I will follow his fathers advice and make sure our union is one that is bright and lively. Even in his moments\nwhere his temper risen he can be calmed when he thinks of me. I need to respect that we are good for each other. \n\nMy pregancy is begining to be physically obvious, and an is an unavoidable topic of conversation. I'm okay with it though, I am rather\nquite large lately. Most people are happy for me which is kind, and nice to hear.\n\nI bought Kairn a steel sword today, it's in imaculate condition. I hope he likes it when I give him his gift. It's not quite as nice as the book he gave me but, it's him.\nI named it Cerridwen's Charm. I thought it was fitting considering I was giving it to him, and I would like to have the aspects guide and protect him. Even if he doesn't believe in them.\n\nOur Son, Elenion, was born on the 5th of the Grand Harvest, 1577.\nElenion is keeping me quite busy, and I am questioning continuing my pursuit of the druidic arts. It feels like half the city are decidants, and care for it mostly for it's healing capabilities. Not because I am the most devout. Cal offered me a librarian\npostion in passing. I may take him up on that offer as I do have a fondness for books and organization. \nWho knows what I could do? I could make a library that educates our people so well it is the source of envy to the high elves. That would bring me\nsuch pride. \n\nElenion turned a year old today, he is growing rapidly into a wonderful son, I hope he makes Kairn and I proud.", ""),
        StaticBook("Armin T.", "Ol' Man Sano", "Dear Armin,\n\nI must deeply thank you for all you have provided me within the last few decades. A recreational and enriching activity to help expand my knowledge and experience.\nMost of all, however, I am deeply grateful that I had garnered such a loyal, honest friend such as yourself. Not only were you a valued instructor, but a dear ally of mine. I've left you some items that-\nI thought you may enjoy, a bag of rare herbs, four-leaved clovers, and a wooden cane, given to be back when I had been a senior seargent. Take care, for I shall forever miss you in the Seven Skies.", ""),
        StaticBook("ART OF WAR p2", "Dionysus the Akritian", "PART II OF THE ART OF WAR\n_____________________________\nIV.Siege Warfare and Its Importance\n_____________________________I.Sieges are what win wars, not battles. To meet the enemy of the field you win nothing but the enemy’s shame and reduction of troops, whereas\nduring a siege you may slowly depart him from his kingdom. If done well, this can be done with minimal loses. If done badly, sieges are the most costly part of warfare.\n\nII.Therefore, the value of siege engineers is immense. An army without them is no\narmy all,but a useless rabble, of no use at all. Therefore, a commander must make an effort to get a numerous amount of the best siege engineers, or he will fall into inability.\n\nIII.Merely throwing your heavy infantry at a castle\nwith little prior preparation is most inadvisable, for in your impatience, you will cause the enemy troops to reduce your forces, with no progress made. In sieges, you must be patient.\n\nIV.Stone-throwing artillery is most valuable during a siege.\nSome engineers will require prior assembly, but a true master of siege equipment can assemble them in the field. The trebuchet is most famous, but large ballistae may also be used. It is not necessary in all cases to storm a breach:\nsometimes, the threat of a breach will implore the enemy to surrender. In a siege, you must be patient. \n\nV.In addition, it is advisable to set up barracades and pavises and fortifacations in your own siege camp,\no that your crossbowmen may wittle down the enemy’s numbers, and so that you may fight the enemy with ease should he decide to sally forth.\n\nVI.Siege towers are also very worrying to the enemy,but take time and skill to construct. They are far preferable\nto ladders. The ancients often used to merge ram and siege tower in a single, masterful combination.\n\nVII.If no artillery can be constructed, mines are the next best option. If your mines are\ndiscovered, dig more. You must have patience. The enemy will set up countermines, and you must retreat from your current mines and block them to prevent any trouble stirring.\n\nVIII.Or alternatively,\nyou may not do this so the enemy will think you are coming from there, and then dig somewhere else. They will deploy troops in case you attack from the other mines. If the enemy sends reinforcements everywhere, he will everywhere be weak.\nIX.Remember this above all: The worst possible course of action is an unprepared attack. You will lose many of your men, and so you must be patient. \n\nX.And so you need not even take the castle, merely compel him to surrender. This is\nthe best possible course, for you will lose little men. The captured soldiers should be treated with kindness and kept, and then rulers will respect your benevolence and justice, as well as your own men and the enemy.\nXI.If the enemy surrenders, do not sack the castle or city. If he does not, and you have to take it by force, you are at liberty to plunder. Preferably, the citizens will be spared of death, but there will always be many deaths regardless. You\ncan not stop soldiers, for many are blackguards and curs.\n\nXII.However, plundering will make your men adore you, for you have given them wealth. You must not do it if the enemy surrenders\nbecause you will get a reputation for cruelty and being dishonourable. Rival princes and nobles will dislike you, and then your realm is nothing. The same goes for ordering a deliberate massacre of enemies.\nYou must not do this, but if the enemy refuses to surrender, you must sack. There will be deaths then, but you will not be held responsible. If your troops are truly disciplined and do not kill anyone during a sacking, you are a truly brilliant\ncommander and you are favoured by Saint Thomas. Your troops will then be commended and their praises sung, and you will be famed and your troops morale will be high.\n\nXIII.If you fail to take the castle, return to your own realm. The\nskillful soldier need not raise a second levy. Instead, you must merely hold your own castles, and wait for your troops to recover. Then, you may try again. If your losses are terrible, then do raise a second levy, but this will be regretful.\nV.Logistics and Maneuvering\n_____________________________I.An army is said to march on its stomach. While the men who fight in an army are often hardy men, they are carnivores. They must have ample food. It is said in one day, the\nsoldier will consume 1 flagon of wine or 2 of ale, 2 pounds of bread, 1 pound of cheese and a pound of meat.\n\nII.Knights will consume noticeably more, and in addition the cavalry of the army will need to feed their horses, of which they can have many.\nIII.Therefore, a wise general does not merely forage, nor takes pre-prepared supplies. He does both. To forage from the enemy will damage his people’s morale, for they will see their sovereign as weak. \n\nV.But in case\nthe enemy takes a policy of scorched earth, it is always advisable for your troops to be well-supplied, regardless of foraging.\n\nV.In a brief manner, bring supplies with you, but make a point of replenishing your supplies with ones foraged from the enemy.\nVI.For the quick moving of your army in the field you must ensure that the cavalry have both riding and fighting horses, and have spare ones to replace fallen horses. You cannot dither, especially with a cavalry force, with the replacement of horses. You\nmust acquire them, and do well by them.\n\nVII.To the infantry, the baggage train of wagons which is often imagined is of complete falsehood. Nay, what is carried must be done so on their backs or in donkeys. This will ensure a fast-moving\narmy. For though having a baggage train of heavy goods may be advantageous to your supplies, it will be very slow.\n\nVIII.And for the entertainment of expensive guests, this will increase prices. You must only entertain guests if they will improve morale,\nor are willing to travel in the manner of a common soldier, or at the best, a knight. They will simply slow you down if otherwise with special requirements and niceties.\nV.In Battle!\n_____________________________I.In battle, commanders divide their fources into four acies. It is preferable to dismount some knights, in order to form 3 acies of foot and 1 of horse. The acie of horse must be kept in reserve and used only\nwhen the enemy is near breaking; cavalry is useless in sustained warfare, and are useful only at the tipping point of battle, defeating the enemy in a single charge or retreating. Not stopping to fight, but charging, retreating, and charging again, until\nthe foe is broken.\n\nII.For this you must ensure the cavalry are firmly grouped together when they do charge. Therefore, give always your most trusted commander command of the cavalry, or perhaps you yourself should take it.\nIII.The infantry are usually deployed in a defensive formation, but advance into an offensive formation as the battle progresses. With an army strong in heavy infantry you must ensure the flanks are strong so that you may surround the enemy,\nrelying on the cavalry to do the finishing blow.\n\nIV.With an army of missile troops, you must deploy stakes and wait. If you are trapped, they will fight to the death and show great valour. You must stand your ground,\nand incite your enemy’s anger to cause him to charge. This is a tactic that works even outnumbered, especially with terrain that prevents enemy flanking. You must group the few men-at-arms you have on the flanks. You must have a large reserve.\nV.A force of mostly cavalry must break the enemy with the initial charge, and if they cannot, they must retreat. If they cannot retreat, they should not charge in the first place, but dismount and fight as infantry.\nVI.The same goes if the enemy's’ cavalry greatly outnumbers your own. Your own cavalry must dismount and aid your infantry. Otherwise they will be made useless.\n\nVII.In the case of a rout, if you wish to rally your men, do it on\nhigh ground. If the enemy routs, do not use mounted knights to pursue them, but light cavalry.\n\nVIII.If you fight horse archers, if they advance, as if they mean to attack, do not advance. They are merely baiting you and will destroy your infantry\nwith missiles. Withdraw, and wait for another battle where you may take them by surprise.\n\nIX.If the enemy is of infantry and you cavalry, you must feign disorder or rouse him to anger to cause him to want to attack you. If you\nthink battle may be offered under better conditions, or you do not wish to fight at all, withdraw! \n\nX.And remember this above all: the mark of a good commander is to know when to withdraw, and dare to do it. If\nyou think battle may be offered under better conditions, or you do not wish to fight at all, withdraw!\n\nXI.Remember the biggest enemy of a cavalry man is missiles at close range in unfavourable weather, for the horses will be made slow by mud\nand vulnerable. If there are many missile troops in such conditions, do not charge headlong. If he is in such a position where outmaneuvering is impossible, then do not charge at all, but withdraw and take him another day.\nXII.It is often appropriate to have men in light armour but equipped as swordsmen to run down skirmishes. These should be the fastest men.\n\nVII. Horses:Dangers, Types and Sustenance\n_____________________________\nI.Horses may be divided into three categories: War horses, riding horses and saddle horses.\n\nII.Under war horses fall horses such as destriers, who are bred for us in battle.\n\nIII.Under riding horses fall\nhorses bred to be used to travel or hunt with great speed. These include rouncies, cobs, etc.\n\nIV.Saddle horses are poorer horses which yeomen can afford.\n\nV.A good knight will have at least 1\nwarhorse and a riding horse, and will see to their sustenance. Many will have more, and those that do would require such a baggage train for feed that the army would be slowed massively. It would\nbe wise to sustain an army of largely cavalry with foraging.\n\nVI.Now your light cavalry are poorer, and often you must buy their horses, or they can only afford one. it is good for them to buy rouncies or cobs. These\nhorses are for general purposes and are essentially the compromise of riding and warhorses.\n\nVII.With saddle horses a commander should not trouble himself with, but allow the yeomen and other classes of people of your army to buy for themselves.\nVIII.Therefore, it is so advis’d that those armies who wish to travel merely on their baggage train and not commit to foraging of any sort, to take as few horses as possible. This may be done by having dismounted knights and sergeants,\nand if you require cavalry taking a small amount.\n\nIX.And it shall be noted that those who do are in territories where the enemy is implementing a scorched\nearth policy or you are in an infertile or destitute region, the same aforementioned rule applies. Take but few horses and cavalry as possible without severely crippling your forces.", ""),
        StaticBook("Artificial Eye", "Lillith Winterleaf", "((The book seems to contain page after page of concept drawings and schematics related to an artificial eye, some of the diagrams being extraordinarily complex. There are several notes in\nthe margins, as well as a list of materials beside some of the component schematics.))\nOuter Casing:\n-Pure Aurum\n-Fine Ferrum Wires\n-Redstone\nCare must be taken to form a perfect sphere, impurities of the shape can damage eye socket. Ferrum wires must be as fine as a maiden's hairs. Redstone must be free of impurities, the\nlense must be thin, no thicker than a flake of skin, and polished until translucent.\nInner Wiring and Circuits:\n-Pure Aurum Dust\n-Blessed Living Slime\n-Enchanted Ender Pearl\n-Ferrum Dust\n-Redstone Dust\n-Avanite Lense\nEnder pearl must be flawless, any impurities will cause the enchantment to become flawed. Must be enchanted with a Power rune composed from carbarum for maximum effectiveness.\nLiving slime must be carefully filtered and purified. Enhance it with druidic healing several times, use a fairy ring to enhance the effects. Focus on imbuing the slime with healing energy, do not rush the process,\ndo it carefully over several weeks, ask the slime to help the eye function and grant you vision. The slime alone will not do this, but it will guide the power from the pearl and facilitate this function.\nThe inner casing needs space for the pearl and a coating of slime. Form casing by melting down and combining the pure Aurum dust, Ferrum dust, and the Redstone dust to form a highly conductive alloy.\nThe casing must be no thicker than a millimeter, form the front to hold the avanite lense. Avanite lense is a component of light sensors, and  will enhance the quality of vision.\nOnce the inner casing is completed, close it within the outer casing, filling the interior with slime, taking diligent care to ensure all air is removed from the artificial eye before sealing the casing.\nTo prepare for insertion of the eye, I must remove the blinded eye completely, I will need someone to do this for me, I cannot imagine doing it myself safely. I will cleanse the socket, then coat the eye in living slime and carefully insert it as\nas I focus mending energy upon the socket, repairing the natural muscle and nerve connections, causing them to connect to the artificial eye as they did my natural eye, and if everything has been\ndone correctly, I should regain my sight through that eye for the first time in over 150 years.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ashton: Age 8", "[Child] Ashton", "On the top of the page, a scraggly text is written. \n\"My name is Ashton. I am 7 years old.\"\n\nBelow the text is a crudely drawn picture of a cactus.\nThe text on this page has quite a few spelling errors. However, it might be understood as the following:\n\"My grandma always told me death was inevitable. I guess that's true. A man Mr. Oliver knew died. His dad is a druid. It was sad.\"\nThe next several pages are filled with drawings of flowers, shrubs, trees, and other fauna. \n\nEach picture is labeled with a basic description.\nI'm 8 years old today. Mister Aeran (Mister Oliver called him Aeran) gave me a book. I don't think he knew it was my birthday. It was nice.\n\"There is a person in the infirmary. They were  badly burned. Mister Aeran made a salve for them. He told me I could watch, so I can learn.\"\n\nA hastily drawn picture of a person in bandages lies below the writing.\n\"Mister Muildir told Mister Aeran that a seed is a good way to stitch up a wound. Mister Aeran has to grow the seed in the wound to help it heal. He said to coat it in tipp in root salve.\"\n\"They made the seed grow! It looked weird. They used it to help the lady's leg.\"\n\nA drawing of a zig zag sproutling takes up the rest of the page.\n\"Mister Muildir said something bad has happend. That there is a disturbance in nature. \n\nHe said it's terrible, but they don't know what it is.\"\n\"Today, I was playing in the forest near Felsen. I saw a hare. It was pretty. \n\nBut a hunter killed her. He butchered her. It was really sad. \n\nI found her babies. I brought them back to the grove with me.\"\n*A drawing of three infant hares takes up this page.*\n\"Mister Oliver told me that Mister Taynuel is the Hare Druid!!! I took the babies to his office, but he wasn't there. So, I put them in a basket and left a letter. I hope he gets to them quick. \n\nI'll check on them until he comes.\"\n\"I was in Felsen today...\n\nI heard the church men yelling about Mass. I remember Mass from when I lived in Felsen. That's where I would get food.\"\n\"Today wasn't like the other times I was there, though.\n\nEverything was chaos. \n\nAn orc tried to take me! He told me to follow him, and he started saying weird words.\"\n\"Then, Mister Aeran showed up! He saved me. He told the orc I'm not a slave, and he made him go away. \n\nMister Aeran took me out of the church, and a woman accused HIM of kidnapping me!\"\n*A drawing of Aeran, bravely telling the orc to go away is on this page. Including a speech bubble of Aeran saying fuck off.*\n*On this page, a drawing of Aeran calling a mean looking woman a cunt is drawn.*\n\"After that ended, a woman almost got kidnapped outside of Felsen.\n\nFelsen is a scary place. I don't ever want to go back without someone.\"\n\"But...that means I can't see Karrow anymore. I have to go back. I miss him. He's my first friend in a long time.\"\n\n*A drawing of Ashton and Karrow playing is below the text.*\n\"I went to a moot with Mister Oliver today. It was neat. I liked listening to the people. Except when the people were arguing.\n\nMister Oliver got chosen to be a guide! I'm so excited!\"\n\"But I have to wait until I'm 16 to become a dedicant. I wish I didn't have to wait that long.\"\n\n*A picture is drawn of an older Ashton, as she imagines herself to be at 16.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Aspect Stones", "Leyun Kameki", "A Description of the Sacred Stones and Their Properties\n\nA tome written by the Song Druid\nThe Sacred Stones of the Aspects are powerful Artifacts associated with the Druids. There is believed to be three, one for each of the figurehead Aspects and a third that binds them together. They are large, rounded square-ish boulders that each are a\ndifferent colour; Blue for Cerridwen, Silver for Cernunnos, and black for the binder. They are very heavy, but one person could transport one stone on his own. The three together however have known to require at least 3 people to carry a chest with them\nin it. And once the Stones are close enough they magnetize, though this effect is only present when all three are together it seems.\n\nThe stones emit a powerful aura of Druidic Energy. Together the three stones can prevent\ncorruption of any kind from breaching the perimeter of the grove they are in. Indeed, just one has enough power to stop corruption for up to twenty feet, but together their power is much larger. The stones have been known to give visions to those who\ntouch them, and help aid Druids on paths to enlightenment through their pulsating auras.\n\nSymbolically the stones represent the completion of the Order. Each one represents an Aspect, and are thought to have been molded by the Aspects\nthemselves. To possess something touched by the Aspects is beyond blessed to the Druids. Even when broken down the stones seem to emit light Druidic energy even centuries after their crumbling.\nIt is rumored the the Order remains in possession of the Stone Dust that was once the Great Aegis Stones.", ""),
        StaticBook("Aspect Studies", "Tever Softfoot", "I was walking along the river near my home when I spotted a very nice spot to sit and take a nap. It was quiet, sunny and warm.\nI lay down and closed my eys. I felt the sun warming me. Felt the wind blowing and the life all around.\nI began to meditate. I felt a peace that I hadn't felt before. I eventually fell asleep. I dreamed I was bathed in light. The air tasted sweet. There was music in the air that sounded like an orchestra of nature. When I awoke I was reminded of my\nteachings. Of Cerridwen and the light and life she brings. I looked up into the tree, upon rising from my resting place, and saw a honey comb dripping with beautiful golden honey. Like it was a gift from Cerridwen meant for me.\n\nThe honey represents\nCerridwen because not only is it golden, it is life sustaining, warm, sweet,and the labor of creatures of life. Nothing would be living without Cerridwens blessing of bees to pollinate things.\nAs a lumberjack I find myself in search of exotic woods deep in mysterious places. I heard of a source of dark oak deep within the forests of the Mali. As I traveled through the ancient forest I felt the presence of the trees watching me.\nIt was a welcoming feeling however. I made my way to the location of the trees and made camp. Later that night a terrible storm came upon me. My camp was blown away and I lost my way. Three days I wandered the forest with no hope.\nI was hungry and cold. Hope had fled from me. I finally fell to my knees and yelled defiantly at anything that could hear me. \"I will no' die tis way!\" I thought of my love. Of the future that would never be.\nAs I kneeled there in the damp leaves, the quiet of the forest settled around me. The stillness was tangible. There was not a sound to be heard. As I stood up and looked around I saw a pure white deer looking at me. As I slowly backed away I tripped over\nwhat I thought was a fallen branch. On closer examination the branch turned out to be a moss covered bow. The string was made of vines. There were also a few moss covered arrows wrapped in a sheet of old leather.\nAs I picked up the bow the deer bolted away through the underbrush. Being on the verge of starving, I shrugged off the despair. This was my only chance to survive. I needed food. I grabbed the Bow and arrows and started after the deer.\nI tracked the deer through valleys, over hills, through fields and forests for what seemed like an eternity. As i crested a small hill I came upon the deer once more. The wind was blowing torwards me. The grass was soft and silent.\nIt was the perfect chance and my only one. I had not the strength to track this quarry any longer. I slowly nocked an arrow and raised the bow. I thought the mossy wood would creak and give as I pulled it, but it remained silent. I held my breath.\nThe only sounds were the wind and the fast beating of my heart. The thrill of the hunt running through my veins. The arrow flies true and hits it's mark. A clean kill. I went to the deer and sat by his side.\nCrying at my salvation I began to dress the deer.I built a fire and ate my fill all the while praising my luck. As I ate I was reminded of my teachings. Of Cernunnos the great huntsman. I believe the deer and the bow where gifts from him.\nI sat near the fire and began to meditate on what I had learned and thanks the Horned God for his generosity and for saving my life. \nThis moss covered bow reperesents Cernunnos. It is the tool of the true hunter.\nOf his dedication and prowess. Of the thrill of the chase and of the taking of your prey. And of the thankfulness for a life given to save another life.\nI was in the far north. Conscripted to a group of explorers as repayment of a debt. After trudging the snow for several days we came upon twin mountains. Very unusual looking with they were. We decided to make camp at the base of the second with plans to\nexplore them the next day.\nAfter a hot meal and a few tunes from a pipe we turned in for the night. As I lay there I heard someone crying out past the ring of light made by the campfire. I rose from my bed and walked the the edge of the camp.\nI could make out the shape of what looked like a small child. I paused and looked back at the others still sleeping. They would be fine, and so would I as long as I kept the fire in sight.\nAs I stepped out into the cold dark of the night, four other figures appeared. I turned to run back into the camp when a numbing coldness came over me. I couldn't move. Last thing I saw was the ground coming at me, then darkness...\nWhen I awoke I was in a lightless place bound in iron. I could hear muffled voices nearby. The ground was hard and cold. Luckily they did not take my jacket or any of my things. I fished a lockpick from my boot and began to fumble in the dark to unlock\nthe shackels around my feet. It was very difficult to pick the locks without making a sound and alerting my captors. My previous title as Borrower helped in the task of breaking free. I finally freed my feet and began trying to free my arms.\nLuckily for me being a halfling meant that the chains were far to big for my small arms and with a little effort I slipped my hands right through them.\nI crept towards the voices, grasping in the dark so as not to bump into anything.\nThe voices grew louder and louder as I crept in the dark, until finally I could understand what they were saying. It was three females talking about what to do with me. It seemed like the consensus was to toss me down a deep hole.\nI began to panic and flail around in the dark for an escape but only ended up tripping and banging my head. Bright light filled my vision as I was lifted from the ground. I was carried for some distance and then wind. Nothing but darkness and wind.\nI fell for ages it seemed then splash. I fell into an underground lake. The darkness was so thick I could not see my hands in front of my face. I picked a direction and began to swim. Eventually I found what seemed like a bank.\nI was so afraid. What was I going to do? I was miles underground with no light, no food, and no hope. I sat and cried for a while. Such was my despair that I decided that if I was going to die that it would be my way,\nNot eaten by some unknown creature of the dark. I rose from the place I was sitting and began to wander in the dark, tripping and fumbling as I went. As I was scrambling through the dark I tripped over a loose stone and fell down a hill.\nI rolled and rolled and fell off of a small cliff, breaking my leg as I hit the bottom. I screamed out in pain as I pulled my leg out from under me, bone protruding from the skin.\nAll I could do was lay there in despair.\nAs i sat there writhing in pain my heart sunk. I was not alone here in the dark. I heard small pebbles shifting in the dark. Something grabbed my broken leg and began to drag me.\nPain shot through my body as the creature sank it's teeth sank into my body. \n\nI sat up from my bedroll with a scream. The pain still wracking my body as I came to terms with what had happened. Everyone looked at me in bewilderment,\nwondering what was going on. As I sat there the pain faded and the realization that it was just a dream dawned on me. The horror and helplessness I felt was still there.\nI shudder even now as I write this. The feeling of that dream will haunt me to the end of my days. I think that dream was from Niimasae. Showing me that I I should find my own light, that, like in the caverns I am helpless without it.\nThe object I think represents Niimasae is the enchanted stone I had made so that I would never be without my own source of light. I will not be left alone in the darkness again.", ""),
        StaticBook("Aspects: Greed", "Valmir_", "Aspect Tome: Greed\nAuthor Unknown\nGreed, not even the very good can resist this emotion. Something as Evil as Greed can't even be described properly, but it can be done. The Emotion of Greed carries out in generations to come from the first evil. The Evil God, Iblees, cursed the Dwarves\nwith this evil. This Emotion, this Avarice can turn your own friends against you, and it is triggered by Temptation, which very few people can easily resist. This makes Greed a very dangerous Emotion. This emotion is never good and must not be taken\nlightly, so watch yourself, Druid, for you might be its next victim.", ""),
        StaticBook("assassinator", "Ser Laurence Baldwin de Vimont", "I'm going to kill peter sigismund\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\nhey its ser laurence aka skinnypenis coming at you with another video\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\nthe deed is done.....", ""),
        StaticBook("Asul I", "March Ash", "These pillars of shale. They remind me of the sea-traps the old druids would summon. Hidden spikes of rock, just beneath the waterline, to gouge apart the hulls of ships that wandered too close to our hidden sanctuaries. Some of the sailors would survive,\nadrift at sea. Many would drown, or die of exposure and thirst. Most would eventually drink saltwater and turn mad. Weeks later, we would go out on rafts, and capture the survivors for sacrifice. I remember their screams and curses so vividly.\nUpon the pyre, they would pray to their gods for salvation. There was never an answer.", ""),
        StaticBook("Asul II", "March Ash", "I hate the City. It is the ultimate culmination of all our sins against nature, the greatest perversion of our brain. Be they made of corpses, or cobbles, they are evil, all the same. I will break them. This sandstone rises high, but even the greatest\nconstruction by Men cannot withstand the eternity of nature.", ""),
        StaticBook("Asul III", "March Ash", "Underneath the mushroom-caps, the smell of the spores fresh in my nose, it feels easier to breathe. It reminds me so much of the Great Rot. Miles of mycelium, stretching all the way to the horizon. A ground alive with ten trillion hyphae,\nsplitting and merging like living rivers, a chaotic order. The memory is as sweet as slime mold.", ""),
        StaticBook("Asul IV", "March Ash", "It can take ten thousand years for a stream to carve a new valley. But it will still do so, it has an endless resolve. It is difficult to truly grasp the immensity of generational time, let alone geological time.\nNot even in the histories of a hundred families will the mountains grow a meter, but they will still grow.", ""),
        StaticBook("Asul IX", "March Ash", "And here lay the corpses of titans which once walked the world, and which will soon walk it again. I only pray that they are on our side in the war to come, rather than with those who oppose all life.", ""),
        StaticBook("Asul V", "March Ash", "Here, at the edge of Axios, it would be so easy to build a boat and leave. To abandon the descendants to their terrible fate, and to abandon the land to the wrath of the Aspects. To leave, and never return. But I have a mission.\nI cannot leave until it is complete.", ""),
        StaticBook("Asul VI", "March Ash", "Long ago, there were stories passed around by the bone druids. About how, one day, a great tree would be born from the breeding together of every tree throughout all ecology, in all time. An avatar of nature, who would crush the world beneath its roots.\nThis was before they were shunned from their order, after it was discovered that they murdered their Archdruid and burned his organs in the pyre to receive visions from the Aspects. Sometimes I wonder if their stories were true.", ""),
        StaticBook("Asul VIII", "March Ash", "The jungle is a wild place. There is more life -- more biodiversity here -- than most other places in Axios. Only the shrublands match it in the number of species. Survival is an art.", ""),
        StaticBook("Asulon Churches", "Valmir_", "Yearbook ~ Reformed Churches of Asulon\n\nBy Various Authors\nChurch and Information Directory\n\nReformed Churches of Asulon:\n1 Introduction\n2 Meditation\n3 Church Directory\n4 From the Curatorium\n5 Meditation\n6 About us\n7 Book Committee\n1: INTRODUCTION\nDear reader, we live in an era and are part of a culture that continues to be dazzled by new accomplishments.\nKnowledge and scientific discoveries are multiplying exponentially so that new technologies,redstone engineering feats, and\nbreakthroughs continues to emerge that would have been unthinkable merely decades ago in Aegis.\nYet all of these accomplishments pale in comparison to the most extraordinary accomplishment in history: the continued existence of religion and our church.\nOur denomination exists since the creation of Aegis.\nNo matter what race the member is, or what country he lives in, he or she can be saved.\n\n->Written by the Curatorium (The Board of Trustees of our denomination).\n2: MEDITATION “Why Do We Believe What We Believe?”\nWe believe that our God only hears people who worship him. Is that a sad situation? No, everyone could and should be obedient if they wanted.\nWe believe in a creator of Aegis and Asulon, our God.\nIt is his choice to choose who will be saved from Iblees.\n“Treat yourselves and each other with respect.” is an old adage but still actual! Every person in this world has a soul. What is a soul? Think of it as a balance.\n\nPraying and other positive things\nwill bring your balance to the good side. The opposite is also possible when someone dedicates his life to an evil spirit, or doesn't worship Asulon's creator.\n\nAs the holy God elects his children, we need to have an infallible belief which will be\nreflected in a life which is almost without sins.\n\nWe live in a sinful world, but that's not an argument to wash away your sins. Have you achieved that infallible belief already and are you as a sinful creature obedient to him?\n\nOr do you think you're\nbetter off alone?\n\n->Written by Pastor Petrus\n3: CHURCH DIRECTORY\nA church that doesn't have its own pastor has got a counselor who visits and serves the church often-\n> Kal'Alras city. Pastor: vacant, counselor: Petrus\n> Kal'Alras farms, part of City.\n> Arethor Pastor: vacant, counselor: Petrus\n> Skravia. Pastor: vacant, counselor: Kilross\n> Holm. Pastor: vacant, counselor: Petrus\n> Dwarven mission post. Pastor: Kilross\n> Somerset. Pastor: vacant, counselor: Kilross\n> Silva Insula. Pastor: Petrus\n4: FROM THE CURATORIUM\nThe Curatorium is our Board of Trustees. An important role of the curatorium is the education of new pastors. \n\nIt is well known that the denomination has more congregations than pastors. Therefore we are always looking for capable\npastors who can serve the denomination unders god's lead. A few years ago the curatorium accepted Kilross as a pastor.\n\nAfter that we got more applications but the curatorium didn't have the boldness to accept those people.\nThat means that the team exists out of two religious workers: The pastors Petrus and Kilross.\n\nMay Asulon's God bless them in this demanding job to lead our denomination!\n\n→ Written by the Curatorium.\nApplications can be sent to Pastor Petrus.\n5: MEDITATION “What Is The Meaning?”\nEverybody has a place in our world, we all try to progress and make our own life – and other lives - better, but to what end?\n\nWe are born, live and die, a seemingly endless cycle, with little meaning or purpose.\nThis however is without considering our God and his greater goals-because we all have souls our souls are created to do good, and show that we are worthy of the respect to do good, and show that we are worthy of the respect of God as we show him respect\nin return. \n\nWe have emotions in our lives: of happiness, love, care and sadness. Yet do we see those as all we live for?\nWithout God they are all we live for – yet feelings don't last forever.\n\nSo, with this in mind our lives are truly without purpose:\nwithout our God's respect- for they are without meaning for our God’s tests.\n\nWe are living because our God created us and we live for his promises. For without God: is there really any true purpose living at all?\n → Written by Pastor Kilross.\n6: ABOUT US\nThe Reformed Church denomination was established several years after the creation of Aegis. The main Human church underwent a split related to church-orderly and theological issues.\n\nWe 'reformed' the errant religion of the Humans and placed\nit into a broader perspective.\nWe are orthodox and conservative, but we also commit ourselves to serve and to tell others about our religion.\n\n In Aegis we became the major religion at the time. In Asulon we continued our work... Why?\nIn our history, we've experience God's grace upon us. Miracles happened and are happening. God is with us and will be with us.\n\nThat's what we pray for ourselves and for all the souls in Asulon.\n\nAnd that's something which is special in Asulon: we are not\nbound to kingdoms or races and we have such a big history...\n\n→ Written by the Reformed Book Committee\n7: BOOK COMMITTEE\nThe Reformed Book Committee is one of the major book publishers in Asulon.\nBooks of them are spread around Asulon The unique thing is: the books are free! Right now the following books are available:\n> Iblees' Curse, by Pastor Kilross, 4 pages\n> Yearbook Asulon, by Ref. Churches, 23 pages\n> The Infallible Belief in Asulons God, by Pastor Petrus, 6 pages\n> The Split – Historical review of the Ref. Church, by Pastor Judase and Petrus, 24 pages\n> Our Inheritance: Meditations by Pastor Judase, 10 pages\n> Our Inheritance: Meditations by Pastor Kilross, 12 pages\n> On Sin, by Pastor Subona, 10 pages\nAnd a lot more... For a book, contact the committees chairman: Pastor Petrus", ""),
        StaticBook("Atheran Uruks V1", "Temür Törs Ajedh'raq", "Betrayal of the             Uzg\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWritten and Recorded\nby\n\nTemür Törs Ajedhraq\nRider of the Subudai\nThe Uzg of the Uruks, centered in the Goi, San-Vitar, of the new world, Athera, had experienced a unity un-paralleled in recent history.  In the Goi, the clans Gorkil, Lur, Yar, Kog, Magra, and various others coexisted.  This unity is attributed to the\nRex Malog'Yar.  A wise and powerful Shaman, Malog'Yar enacted reform among Uruk culture to bring the Uzg into the forefront of the politics of Athera.  Under these reforms, stricter codes of honor were introduced, which elevated the Uruks from a looseknit\nculture of raiders to a unified culture based on code-of-law. These reforms, though, drew harsh criticism from some of the Uruks, especially from the Azog clan.  \n\nThe Azogs, already dissatisfied with the Uzg's hostility towards Raine Academy, was\npushed further from their brothers.  Tensions were heightened between the Uzg and the Azogs.\n\nAt this time, another perilous threat arose to challenge the Uzg.  An Uruk, by the name of Zogrocka, had risen to immense power through the wicked\nand vile means of Dark Shamanism (a topic I will fully explain in the Expanded History of the Uruks).  Under Zogrocka's leadership\nthe ancient and exiled clan Dom rose again.  The Doms were a clan dedicated to Dark Shamanism, that fell out of Krug's grace\ndue to their trickery and abuse of spirits and elementals.  They also offended the Uzgs and other nations through their abominable practice of cannibalism.  Justly, the Uzgs hunted down and executed the Doms in earlier times.\n\nThe rise of the Doms\ncoincided with the split of the Azogs and the Uzg.  In the Azogs, the Doms saw an army to enforce their corrupt ways.  In the Doms, the Azogs saw a means to achieve power and claim the Uzg for themselves.  \n\nDespite the Uzg offering complete\nand total amnesty to the Azogs upon their return to the Uzg, the Azogs forsook Krug and the Spirits in favor of the dreadful\nDoms.  Making a deal with the patron Spirit of the Dark Shamans, Ixli, the Azogs traded parts of their sanity for the corrupting\npower enjoyed by the Doms.\n\nNow combined, the Doms and the Azogs sacked San'Vitar, the Uruk's 'Old City'.  At first, the unholy alliance encountered little resistance and many Uruks of the Uzg were slaughtered.  A joint force of Uruks and\nHumans were unable to repel the assailants later on.  The Goi was left severely debilitated following the attack.\n\nAfter the attack, the desperate Uruks pleaded the spirits for guidance.  In an odd series of events, the Uruks were given\nassistance.  Following the shrieks of an injured scaddernack, the Uruks discovered a cave where the spirit Veist revealed itself to them.  Veist pledged its support against the Azogs and the Doms, but in return, the Uzg's High Shaman, Brunhyldir,\nwas morphed into a Goblin.\n\nIt was in this frail form that the High Shaman Brunhyldir confronted the Dark Shaman Zogrocka.  Alone, the two battled, drawing upon the Mojo that the Spirits granted them (whether that be honorably as\nin Brunhyldir's case, or dishonorable, in Zogrocka's).  The honor and the strength of the High Shaman prevailed, and the abhorrent and corrupt Zogrocka was defeated.\n\nLeft without a leader, the Doms were weakened.  The Azogs\nfollowing Zogrocka's defeat then attempted to gain power by their own means.\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nOn the 6th of the Lunar Cycle of Sun's Smile, in the year 1471, I, Temür Törs Ajedh'raq, was witness to the following events that occurred in San'Vitar.\n\nThe Azogs, unable to gain power through the corruption of Ixli and the Doms, arrived\nat the Goi armed and armored.  They approached the Rex in his Blarg and demanded the Rexdom under threat of force.\n\nIt is notable that by Uruk custom, which has been observed for generations, the Rex may be challenged to an 'honor klomp', in\nwhich the Rex and the Challenger fight for the title and position of Rex.  These fights generally occur unarmed and unarmored.  With that said, it is also of worth to note that the Azogs, in no way, shape, or form, challenged the Rex honorably to such a\nfight.\n\nThe Azogs' justification for such demands were that the current Rex was weak, and the Uzg was crumbling.  They came to the Goi claiming they could make it strong again.\n\nTo justify their for-\n-saking Krug and the Spirits, they claimed that the dark powers of Zogrocka had made them servants of the Dark Shamans.  Despite there being a lack of Azog Shamans at the confrontation, the Azog clan claimed to have made amends with the Spirits.  This\nblatant lie is further discredited by the presence of Dom Shamans accompanying the Azog party.\n\nFor two days, the Azogs and their Dom Shamans held the Rex.\nTheir terms: the Rexdom and the Uzg, or war.  For two days the Rex held out and\nattempted to reason with the Uruks made unreasonable through\nIxli's Bargain.\n\nOn the 8th of the Lunar Cycle of Sun's Smile, in the year 1471, the Azogs departed the Goi as enemies of the Uzg.  With their coup-de-tat failed, they returned to\ntheir fort without the Uzg in their command.  Both sides, immediately following the encounter, started to strike alliances with other nations and factions.  The Uruks of the Uzg appealing to those who uphold honor, and who wish to maintain orderly law\nthroughout Athera.  And the splinter Azogs, appealing to those who would rather there be the vile corruption of chaos unleashed upon the land.", ""),
        StaticBook("Atlas of Axios", "John Lyons", "World Atlas of Axios\n\n\nhttps://tinyurl.com/LOTCatlas", ""),
        StaticBook("Atlas Of Tahn", "John D'Lyons", "First Atlas of Tahn, 1578 Edition\n-------------------Dedicated to his Imperial Majesty,      John Horen III\nand to Lord Alastair Vonslichten\n\nCartograher:\n     John D'Lyons\nAuthor:\n     Illanoria Calithil\nThis Atlas was created in the year of 1578, upon the isles of Axios. It covers the Orenian Empire, Elven Nations, and Kingdom of Urguan. Presented as a guide to all travellers and Officials, it instills the hope the lights the way.\n*Each map found within the atlas would be carefully outlined, coloured, labelled, and proportioned by a careful hand.*\n\n((imgur.com/a/SIUUr))\nMappe of the Isle of Tahn\n------------------\n\nThis map depicts the entire isle of Tahn, including every nation, road, city, and settlement found upon the land in the year of 1578.\nDominion of Malin\n------------------\n\nThe Dominion of Malin is found on the Southernmost sector of Tahn, an honourable vassal to the Orenian Empire.\n\nClimate is tropical, the land covered in forestry suitable to the Wood Elves and\nDark Elves that inhabit the land.\n\nThese inhabitants appear to follow a Druidic lifestyle, following in the guidance of the Aspects Cernunnos and Cerridwen.\nArch Duchy of Lorraine\n------------------\n\nThe Arch Duchy of Lorraine is located North of the Dominion, loyal to the Orenian Empire. \n\nThe climate is temperate, suitable to the majorly Southern human inhabitants.\nThese inhabitants follow the Canon religion; the Creator.\nThe Crownlands\n------------------\n\nLocated North-West of the Arch Duchy of Lorraine, the Crownlands contains the Orenian Capital; Johannesburg.\n\nThe climate is temperate, the inhabitants being of many various races,\nmostly human, whom all follow in the Canon religion; the Creator.\nThe Kingdom of Haense\n------------------\n\nLocated North of the Crownlands, the Kingdom of Haense is loyal to the Orenian Empire, similar to the Dominion of Malin.\n\nThe temperature is colder North, suitable for the Northerners and Raevir\nthat are generally found upon the lands.\n\nThe Kingdom follows in the Canon Religion; the Creator.\nRed-Rock Canyons\n------------------\n\nLocated North-East of the Crownlands, the Red-Rock Canyons are an uninhabited zone that is effectively loyal to no nation.\n\nThe climate is hot and dry, unsuitable for most flora and fauna to thrive in.\nDry Dune Desert\n------------------\n\nLocated North-West of the Red-Rock Canyons, the Dry Dune Desert is an uninhabited zone that is effectively loyal to no nation.\n\nThe climate is hot and dry, unsuitable for most flora and fauna to thrive in.\nThe Grand Kindgom of Urguan\n------------------\n\nLocated West of the Dry Dune Desert, the Kingdom of Urguan is loyal to none but themselves. \n\nThe climate is very cold, mostly due to the amount of thanium in the mountains.\nIn being a mountainous region, the Dwarves are the main inhabitants of this region. \n\nThe religion followed is that of the Brathmordakin.\nSilver State of Haelun'or\n------------------\n\nLocated in the Westernmost sector, the Silver State of Haelun'or is loyal to none but themselves. \n\nThe climate is temperate, suitable for the inhabitants that are the high elves.\nThe high elves follow no religion aside from their belief in purity; the maehr’sae hiylun’ehya.\nThe Western Frontier\n------------------\n\nLocated North of the Silver State of Haelun'or, the Western Frontier is comprised of the Needle Fields, Frost Fever Taiga, Whisperwind Forest, and Godfrey's Peaks.\n\nThe climate is incredibly cold,\nunsuitable for settling in the year of 1578.\n\nThe land varies from tundra to mountains, forestry, and fields.\nObsidian Steppe\n------------------\n\nLocated northernmost of Tahn, the Obsidian Steppe is a location of mysterious energies and environments. \n\nThe climate is warmer than other sectors, the land comprised of plains full of tall grass with limited\nflora, and the occasional tree. The only animals to roam the plains are common insects.\n\nAt the edge of the Obsidian Steppe sits a mysterious 'Rift', awaiting further exploration.\nAll maps included are the work of Cartographer John D'Lyons.\nAll writings included are the words of John D'Lyons, interpreted and recorded by Illanoria Calithil, Librarian of Linandria", ""),
        StaticBook("Attunement", "Tristanm1", "The Attunement Ceremony\nForging the Link\n\nBy Salmon Druid Petyr\nFor a Dedicant, the attunement ceremony is the final step of initiation. This forges a link between nature, the rest of the Druidic Order, and themselves. The guide leading the ceremony must be careful to do such properly.\nI personally choose to do this\nceremony by the Birch Pond. I have them close their eyes, and I begin to coax their minds into accepting the spirits of nature around them. At first, I merely whisper to their minds, hoping to soften their natural defenses. Once their mind is unshielded,\nit is possible for enlightenment occur. It is different for everyone, but most report vivid images of the forest talking to them. In my opinion, the visions should not necessarily be told to everyone. They reveal something true about a person's inner\nbeing which should only be known to them. Of course, later, they may choose to use this information when choosing a title or totem.\nThe correct chanting must be performed and not stopped until you have internally communicated with the Dedicant\nafterwards. Be wary of pushing on the Dedicants to forcefully, for the mind is a fragile thing. Make sure that while forging the link, they do not react negatively, harming your mind as well as their own.", ""),
        StaticBook("Auvergine", "Sarrion Zytiaear", "Auvergine for\nDummys\n\nBy the Pascal's\n-------------------\nHON HON HON\nhttps://translate.google.com/", ""),
        StaticBook("Auvergne Dialect", "ski_king3", "A Guide to the\n  Auvergnian Dialect\n\n\n   -by Rose Valois\n\n\n\n       Volume One:\n       The Basics\nTable of Contents:\n\n\nThe Basics - Pg. 3\nGreetings - Pg. 5\nParting - Pg. 7\nPeople - Pg. 8\nRacial Terms - Pg. 10\nTitles - Pg. 12\n\nMessage from the Author - Pg. 16\nThe Basics\n\n\nOui - Yes\n\nNon - No\n\nS’il vous plait - please\n\nMerci - Thank You\n\nPas de problem - not a problem\nDe rien - You’re welcome\nGreetings\n\n\nBon Matin - Good Morning\n\nBon soir - Good Evening\n\nBonne nuit - Good Night\n\nBonjour - Hello [Formal]\nSalut - Hail [Informal]\n\nEnchante - Pleased to meet you\nParting\n\n\nÀ bientôt - Until Next Time\n\nAu revoir - Good-bye\n\nAdieu - Good-bye\nPeople\n\n\nMon seigneur - My lord\n\nMa dame - My lady\n\nMonsieur - Sir\n\nMadame - Misses [Married]\nMadamoiselle - Miss [Not Married]\nRacial Terms\n\n\nHumain - Human\n\nElfe - Elf\n\nNain - Dwarf\n\nVerdâtre - Orc (literally means ‘Greeny’)\nSubalterne - Underling (can be used to substitute Nain, more derogatory)\n\nSouffrant - ill, unwell (often used to make racial term derogatory)\nTitles\n\n\nDuc - Duke\n\nDuchesse - Duchess\n\nComte - Count\n\nComtesse - Countess\n\nBaron - Baron\nBaronesse - Baroness\n\nChevalier - Knight\n\nArchevêque - Archbishop\n\nDame - Lady\n\nSeigneur - Lord\n\nMaître - Master\nMaîtresse - Mistress\n\nVicomte - Viscount\n\nVicomtesse - Viscountess\n{\"text\":\"\"}\nI hope that those of you who read through this book make use of it. Auvergnian is a very unique dialect dissimilar to any other dialect of Common present in Anthos. If you have any suggestions for words which should be in the next volume, please\nfeel free to visit me in Auvergne, or another member of the Valois family, to make reccomendations.", ""),
        StaticBook("Avern'ne", "Dio Astóre", "A copy of a tome from the archaeology site of Haelun’or, Asulon.\nThe original being found underneath the Black Seat*, the short volume pertains to an iteration of the ancient Heial’thilln, its seven Okariran and the titular Avernne’an or ‘Seekers’ that carried out its will.\nFor how long this social structure prevailed remains unclear. Study of the Heial’thilln is advised prior to perusal of this text. Simplification is provided, due to much of the necessary contextual objects being no longer available for study.\nTranslation of the primary lore item along with appended notes is included, as well as text on objects of power purported to be associated with each colour. Only the Miruel variant is known to have existed, now lost.\n*The Black Seat refers to the center-most section of a large throne-like structure found within the oldest known council chambers of Haelun’or.\n\n===\nEach one of seven councillors - known as an Okarir - existed as an embodiment of a certain aspect of the maehr’sae hiylun’ehya. The Avern’ne would operate similarly to the Okarir they represented, though the Okarir had authority as a teacher and exemplar.\nThese duties were archetypal and became symbolized by certain colours, which were widely integrated in society. How an Avern’ne was selected remains uncertain. Listed below are said archetypes.\nBarbu Avern'ne [Black Seeker]: The Mirror\n\nMirror that reflects scenes in an endless pattern though never shows the beholder within them.\nShadows of the light. Where perfection exists, there the black does not. Teachers of obscure lessons. Let them guide others, that they might fly toward the radiance of wisdom. As moonlit lakes at dusk, they offer a chance for reflection.\nWhen all has been completed and the hues are unified in a pure white illumination the shade shall shrink into a fulfilled nothingness.\nLittle is known of the way this type of Avern’ne functioned or whether it existed as a coherent group with a shared ideology.\nIt could be inferred that the Maheral belonged to this archetype - regarded as a unifying figure, however this unification might not have been achieved via wholly virtuous means.\nSpeculation is that the Black represents those that have deviated from maehr’sae hiylun’ehya, acting as inverted paragons.\nVallel Avern'ne [Blue Seeker]: The Wheel\n\nGyroscope that spins in accordance with the strength of nearby emotions.\nObservers and analysts of the natural world and its workings. Perceptive minds as well as critical thinkers, the blue is seeing the frost covered lands, the depth of the seas, the tempest of the winds through the eye of logic.\nSouls that are methodical and instructive, they prescribe to forms even as they subject such forms to their machinations. Keepers of memory and knowledge, they protect what has been and what always will be.\nPrimarily involved in scholastic and scientific pursuits, this Avern’ne archetype committed most strongly to maehr’sae and were among the most able academics, usually being individuals which valued things that could be subjected to reason.\nProne to political ambivalence and internal contestation. Their contributions were a keystone of Mali’aheral society and earned them favour.\nLentos Avern'ne [Brown Seeker]: The Flute\n\nMusical instrument that has the ability to hasten plant maturation and compel lesser creatures.\nEndurant presences upon the earth, abundance becomes not only their own benefit but others. Bastions of quiet grace and strength.\nVoids become whole; the truth of self becomes realised in the sanctuary they provide. Crowned by browns life was. By its law, they live.\nA rarer multi-disciplined Avern’ne. Closely aligned with hiylun’ehya, their activities tended towards those of a creative or restorative nature.\nLeading in matters of infrastructure, community welfare and culture, they ensured daily life was stimulating and prosperous. An Avern’ne changing paradigms to the Brown after service with another was acceptable practice.\nFilental Avern'ne [Green Seeker]: The Key\n\nKey with an uncut blade and a sphere bow. Effects vary.\nKeepers of balance and vanguards of harmony. Openers of doors and cultivators of opportunity. With persistence the green will persevere; adaptive, growing; assuming a wide spectrum of forms as diverse as they are numerous.\nCapable of enduring or creating change, they find themselves at comfort amidst what others think strange.\nPossessing a heightened affinity for forethought and often of an adaptive persuasion, these Avernne’an had a greater potential for compromise and mediation, which at times put them at odds with other Mali’aheral, especially those of the Yellow.\nMany of them were involved in extra-political affairs and cases of dissent are associated with them. Whilst less orthodox they provided opportunity for development.\nValmuel Avern'ne [Purple Seeker]: The Crystal\n\nPrism which changes colour chaotically, depicting broken glimpses of memories.\nStudents and practitioners of the ancient artforms. Manipulators of force and creatures of mystery. Upon the border of reality will they pluck their threads and ply their craft.\nEsotericism is where the purple mind dwells, upon the farplanes with no names; places that thought, spirit and aspect cast their spell; dream that is never the same.\nThose Avernne’an that were highly learned in magic and had the greatest understanding of the incorporeal. Lore implies they had a propensity for secrecy and were frequently the most disconnected with Mali’aheral culture.\nThey specialized in applying their expertise to augment or supplement conventional activities and research, yet were oddly vulnerable to idiosyncratic behaviours.\nMiruel Avern'ne [Red Seeker]: The Sword\n\nWeapon with two forms. It uses flames against things dark or aggressive in nature.\nEnd-bringers and accomplishers. Through trials of fire will the true order be birthed. By the path of a sword will the way be carved and through a closure of the heart shall the passage to truth be opened.\nPurging illuminators, reds are a blazing inferno that leave ash in their wake. From ruins are their purpose born. Upon crumbled foundations will the glorious monuments be placed.\nWhether these Avernne’an were the most loyal or the furthest removed from hiylun’ehya is a matter of perspective. They tasked themselves with securing favorable conditions for the Mali’aheral and minimising circumstances that posed danger.\nTheir aversion to defeat made them formidable, suitable to the militant and strategic activities that defined them.\nAyal Avern'ne [Yellow Seeker]: The Scale\n\nGolden cloth. Any item it touches feels heavier the less worth it has to the holder.\nDiscerning spirits whose talent lies in their ability to embody the qualities of what they persue.\nThey cultivate what is valuable, in the hands of their hue a seed buds into an existence greater and more glorious than itself. In hands held to the sun, all is balanced.\nOrganized and collected, with a focus on maintaining order and performing administrative duties.\nMost Avern’ne belonging to the Yellow were seen to co-operate with the Red and had sway in the interpretation of law and oversaw the disposition of resources, which included the assets of their information network.\nThey possessed links to other Avern’ne and generally took a neutral stance in affairs that did not concern civil stability.\nEND", ""),
        StaticBook("B. Winthrop", "James Norrington I", "Issued by Steward James Norrington I of the Imperial Administration, given to Benedict Winthrop, whom is a Class C1 Citizen, on the 10th of Amber Cold, 1588. This passport is legal tender until 10th of Amber Cold, 1598.\n\n\n                       -->\nIf found, please return to the Imperial Administration in Johannesburg.\n\n\nSigned: Benedict Winthrop\n\nConfirmed by: Steward James Norrington I.", ""),
        StaticBook("B.o.T. Ch. I", "Sunder", "Book of Tales\nChapter I\nwritten by Isovar Kurben, copy by Sunder.\n------------------\nTranslation by various.\nForeword of the publisher\n\n\"Old blood runs deep and has long histories.\" - Isovar Kurben\n\nI, Novtorn Stonefire, have decided to begin releasing the chapters and stories of the \"Book of Tales\".\nWhat the book be, you may ask, so I shall answer. The \"Book of Tales\" is less of a book, but more of a compendium of past times, reaching back further and more extensive into Human history than any book I know of.\nIt tells the tale of not only my family, but the tales of many a man who lived and walked the lands before our ancestors. Written in a tongue long lost to the common man.\nTranslating it out of its original language is a difficult task, a task, on which\nthree men before me have worked on and succeeded to various amounts. These first chapters were translated by Isovar Kurben, the son of Galtor I. Stafyr.\nHe received the book originally from his grandfather Beorn Stafyr, who was an aged man at that time.\nLet his words speak for him.\n\n------------------\nI. Chapter - Myth\n\nGrandfather had become open about his past in these past two years. He was nearing his eighty-sixth birthday, he was weak and tired. I suppose that he wished to ease his mind before heading on.\nFor the stories he has told and things he had done I can understand. Yet again, it deems me that Grandfather intended to preserve something, thus he gave me this mysterious book, called \"Book of Tales\".\nIn his dying breath he told me... no, us, not to forget our roots and to preserve tales of old. \nUncle Hanethor was suspicious what it could mean, but he seemingly shrugged it off and turned his attention back to the progressing march of the undead.\nFather did not seem to care too much either, though he mourned remarkably. Aunt Sybilla wept lightly, but a kind smile was on her face... like she has forgiven him for something.\nI will try to maintain a constant series of entries as I progress with the book Grandfather gave me. Consider this the first. I have given it plenty of thoughts, though I assume it is best to start with talking about the past with the first who belongs to\nit. The stories Grandfather told me are a heavy burden on my mind, but blood and family are supposed to know some day.\n\nMy Grandfather, Beorn Stafyr, committed theft and murder.\nFor a quarrel with his father, Brimar, and being disowned by him, he had slain his very own mother, Alexandra, and stole the heirlooms of his family, leaving a mourning father with a younger brother, Gorn, behind. The heirlooms consist of following items:\nFirst and foremost, an old crown of copper with an emerald, to be worn by the head of Stafyr. Uncle Hanethor currently has it and wears it often enough.\nSecondly, our old falcon Thondor, grey feathered with a small green tabard. Father meant he had looked like that ever since he can think back, when he was but a child. He seems to be in service to Hanethor.\nThirdly, a set of armor, which deems me of incredible value. A plate armor of gold and a chainmail of silver. Nobody wears it right now, but we keep it safe, as it is... precious. There has to be something about it.\nAlso, two weapons so fine and sharp as if they were never used before, despite their high age. A foreign tongue is written on the hilts of the Longsword Hanethor and the Battleaxe (one-handed, I have to remark here) Galtor.\nFather and Uncle both wield their namesakes right now.\n\nThe last heirloom Grandfather gave me was this very book. Book of Tales. Records of times past, records of events, people and items. I wonder what I may dig up...\nIt was a dark day as we left our home two weeks ago. The undead are marching onward, nigh unstoppable. Uncle Hanethor led father and our men into a few battles, I took part with my bow.\nIn terms of heirlooms, I was able to witness the twin blades in action for the first time. As if their weapons, armors and bodies were made of paper, Hanethor and Galtor cut through the dark and dead beings with ease.\nThey were able to kill many a foe, but after losing a few men and the relentlessly assaulting undead seemed to take no end, we retreated. I can hear a horn sounding. Finishing this entry, battle calls.\nThe Verge. Father is dead.\nWe got split up. Uncle Hanethor's children are nowhere to be found. I only have Aunt Sybilla, Suldren, Sevren and his wife Aewves and Hunrad with me. Hunrad leads us, I do hope, to safety.\nThe last entry was years ago. Many a thing happened, I am an aging man now. And the last one alive it seems. I have made the decision to work on this book now, as much as I can, to preserve what can be preserved. To translate what can be translated.\n- Personal Entries seem to end here -\n\nFollowing was translated by Isovar Kurben from Old Rivachegian to the common tongue. It begins with the eldest entries.\nThus it was in old times past, that the Almannir came to meet their fate. A foe strong enough to crush an entire people, such was the test of Machr, dr Gott (God?). Fyrschlund, dr Dracha (Dragon?), came to consume the lives of many of the Almannir.\nHeroes fell in battle, one after another. Nobody could stop the beast with its insatiable hunger.\nEven Großma, the last of the Galdr, fell to Fyrschlund after three days and nights of battle.\nAs all hope seemed lost, the last chieftains of the Almannir came together and rallied their men to their side, a force numbering the thousands of thousands.\nLed by chieftain Rigfyr Stoafyer, chieftain Krashgar Rettersma, Altkönig (King?) Zubr Altbom, chieftain Haralt Stoakachl and the female chieftain Juna Wiidafrou, the five armies drew a rainbow through the lands of the Almannir,\ngreen, yellow, light-brown, red and blue.\n\nFyrschlund has been waiting and was prepared. As the bright colored army approached the wastelands of the Northern regions of Almannir,\nwhere Fyrschlund has eaten man and Tier (animal?), consumed the plants and very earth itself, he greeted the five last heroes with an army of his own. \n\nReeking and pitch-black, the Totamännr (?) crawled out of the cold and snowy wasteland,\nthousands and thousands of them, consuming the very light that shone upon them by the sun.\n\nFor a week the armies fought, dotting the white snow with tabards and armor of green, yellow, light-brown, red, blue and pitch-black.\nFyrschlund himself became impatient at the unyielding Almannir and charged into battle himself, burning hundreds of the brave with his searing fire, smashing thousands with his claws and tails.\nAnd so it was time that the five chieftains of the Almannir came to fight Fyrschlund himself. Rettersma died first, but took the dragon's tail. Stoakachl took his wings before being stomped under Fyrschlunds claws.\nAltbom crippled his legs before vanishing in fire. Stoafyer took his breath before being crushed by his jaws. But Juna Wiidafrou was not able to slay the dragon, too deep her wounds were.\nThe son of Rigfyr then approached, as the last Almannir standing amidst the field of colors and dead. Fyrschlund was enraged and tried to snap at him, to devour him, to destroy whatever he could from the people who have brought him to fall.\nJuna took her last will and power and blinded the one-eyed Fyrschlund with an arrow from one of his own Totamännr. Unseen, the son of Rigfyr, climbed on the furious, blind and maimed dragon and drove his lance deep into his skull, ending the nightmare.\n. The Almannir saved their lands at the cost of their own lives. And thus the son of Rigfyr was the last of the Almannir, left alone in the endless wastelands covered in what have been such fertile and peaceful people.\n- End of this translated section -", ""),
        StaticBook("B1 AOH", "Azuline", "Anatomy\n    Book One of The Art \n         of Healing\n\n         By Azuline\nAnatomy\n\tThe body consists of many functions that work together as one machine. The mind, or brain would be apart of one of the major functions as it is the connection to our nerves and what we feel, how we respond, how we move.\nIt is all due to the brain. Without it, we wouldn’t move or function. The next major one would be the heart. The heart pumps blood and circulates it throughout our body to function properly.Blood clots and even when the blood is rather thin\ncan be bad for a person. However, some treatments require these things for a person to live a bit longer! As a healer, doctor, physician, and medical scientist, you must quickly think and determine what is best for your patient at the time.\nSometimes failure happens, but you must move forward and take responsibility. With that being said, you must be diligent, but cautious. Remember, the body can only go through so much before it fails and ultimately dies.\nHere are some drawings of the body, what you expect to see in a person and how it functions. *There would be a detailed picture of the body of the different systems and how the body looks like from the inside out.*\nSystems and Functions\n\nBones: The skeletal structure of a body helps move the body. The largest bone in the body is the femur which helps reproduce the blood cells! Bones can break, though they can also regrow and be put back together. The bones in the\nbody doesn’t fully develop until the mature age of twenty-eight. Before then, the body would have massive amounts of collagen or ‘soft bone’ that is rather flexible. Breaking these is possible. There isn’t that much blood that can flow\nthrough collagen, though with that being said it takes a very long time on healing fully. Collagen can be found in the nose and ears even after the person fully matures! \n\nNervous System: This took me a while to figure it out. I was wondering what\nsilvery sheen that is like hair that would connect to the fascia and muscles of the body. I found out after working on a cadaver that it would be activated by salt and or redstone (this is if it is fresh). Realizing after watching a human\nbeat in an orc’s skull that it was all connected to the brain and once the brain was shut down, all systems failed. This is crucial to know! Nerves can be damaged and people can lose functions when the nerves are damaged! From\nwalking, to even using their fingers...it is crucial and highly advised that when working on someone to check and see if there are any major nerve damage. *The shoulders, elbows, knees, neck, and middle section following the whole\nspine was circled.* These are the major nerves areas. Please keep in mind of how the nerves are more exposed in some areas than most and  where they align with the muscles and bones.\nCirculatory system: The blood flows one way and comes back another way. It is constant and never stagnant and if it is, we have a problem. Blood flows through all muscles, tissue, the brain, and heart. There are ways to thicken the\nblood which can be needed for a person whose blood is too thin and to thin the blood for those who have it too thick. Pinching the fingertips to check and see the blood flow by the change of colors is one way, noticing fatigue or even a\nsmall prick to see how the blood flows is another. There is also wrapping a band tightly around their arm and until you actually feel the blood run under your finger (at the inner arm under the band) and take note of how many\npulses you would feel in a minute. There is also just checking their temperature (too cold would mean the blood is trying to keep close to the center and too hot would well, feel too hot) and feeling their pulse in a general manner. The\nblood tells us a lot of things, and possibly more!\n\nRespiratory System: Our lungs are protected by the rib cage that comes up to the clavicle down to just the diaphragm. The lungs doesn’t just cover the\nsystem, but so does the bronchial tubes that connect to the lungs which are small pockets that blood goes in and out of. From there you have the windpipe (trachea) then the voice box (larynx) which then opens to the mouth and nose.\nThe mouth and nose are closed off into two chambers to separate and prevent infections that can be caused and promote proper breathing. That small flap that separates it, is called a pallet. Breathing can be easily affected\nby drugs such as alcohol, opium, and even from caffeine. It can either slow it down or hype it up, though drugs affect the body differently for everyone as everyone is different in one way or another.\nDigestive System: This deals with the mouth again to the esophagus, stomach, liver, gallbladder, spleen, pancreas, large and small intestine, all the way to the exit. People can experience pain and discomfort with any of these parts. Diet\nis key to taking care of these parts as well as exercise. If any of these parts fail, it can cause major issues and system malfunctions!\nMuscular System: The muscles are all wrapped by a thin film called fascia and fibers. They are placed in various areas of the body to have the bones move by connection of the tendon. The muscles can be damaged which is bad! It\nmeans that nerves and blood vessels that are intertwined with the muscles can be damaged and leave that muscle to be utterly useless. The muscles would also develop extra fascia and damaged tissue build up to create pain and\nscars for the patient. As a doctor, we try to prevent scars at all cost. Though it is impossible to leave one scar behind, it is also treatable with salt rubs and friction! Muscles reply to the body when the body is at a normal temperature,\nand the higher it goes, the faster it can reply until overworked. The lower the temperature the slower the muscles can reply. The will also be overworked as the body is trying to quicken it at the same time (the muscle would shake\nwithout control). Of course these things can be treatable and reverse the effects. You can also fix muscle placement at a young age. The older, the harder and the more times you have to put them under a knife.\nTheories\n I believe that there is another system. Another system that protects the body from certain ailments, though I am not sure what it would be called. I knowthat coughing, sneezing, fevers, aches, and so on are the signs of this system\neither working or failing. This system can be treated with honey, ginger, and other herbs to help bright that system back up to protect our body! Reminder: Treatments are meant to be repeated, and not just one time thing!\nRemind your patients and visit them frequently.", ""),
        StaticBook("B2 AOH", "Azuline", "Book Two of\n   The Art of Healing\n   \n        By Azuline\nBotany\tI tell my students that they should read and absorb this books which I had carefully copied down each word and chapter for you here.\nhttps://www.lordofthecraft.net/forums/topic/141741-the-plant-index/\nhttps://wikia.lordofthecraft.net/index.php?title=Flora\nOthers would be:\nGinger Roots which would be found up in the dry parts of the mountains and in the earth. Promotes blood flow, helps the body heal from colds, coughing, and abdominal stomach issues.\nBeet Roots could be found in your local gardens with extreme weathers to even normal temperatures. They are hearty, yet hold so much potential to the body. Promotes blood flow, thickens the blood, energy, and easy on the stomach.\nLicorice Roots are also hearty and grows in various places with cool places or lakes. Easy to grow and in vast amounts! It is used for stomach discomforts, blood flow, energy, and to help the body regain back to it’s natural healing potential.\nThere are more herbs and spices that would help the body, it is up to you to go out there and learn more about it as these books are just going over the tip of the iceburg.\nHow Much is Too Much?\n\n\tGenerally speaking, you should always have your herbs and plants grounded up into fine powder or paste. This makes things easier to apply to\nthe body or into the system. Keep in note: dilute your powders and pastes with water and start out with a little and work your way up. From five grams and up. Though with the Kha, I’ve learned that tippen’s root and poppy powder\n(opium) mixed together works well on them to sedate. The heavier the person is, the heavier the dosage. Orcs are a bit tricky to sedate, they can wake up in the middle of surgery, so it is best to keep a premade sedation vial nearby to\ninject to their system. Needles are made by your local blacksmith or if you tend to travel a lot, use a snake fang and it’s tubing. Of course after cleaning it out and drying it.\nThe signs of seeing too much in their systems could be reversed if you know your herbs and how they would affect the system. Though the patient would start to shake, fevers, tremble, go cold, have a hard time of breathing,\nsweating, feeling uneasy, nausea, dizziness, pupils dilated, and many more signs. Always use a clean bowl to mix your solution to prevent this!\nWhen Treatments fail\n\n\tOwning up to your mistake and genuinely apologizing is the first step as you are trying to find the solution. Sometimes, we try to treat someone for one thing instead of the other, and the other would ultimately lead them up to\ndeath. When treating the body, we as healers must heal the body as a whole! Even if it is a cough and you just treat the fever, the cough can end up ruining their lungs which would ruin their blood and kill the brain. Or if we treated just\nthe cough and not the fevers, then your patient would die because the body was literally cooking itself. Treat the whole body, do not just rely on your magic or simple salve to treat the body as a whole. Be thorough with this.\nThat being said, work with your patient. Be clear with your questions to figure out what is truly wrong with them and keep notes that are confidential of their case so you may look over your work later and possibly come up with\nmore solutions if they come back or when you go to visit them.", ""),
        StaticBook("Back Into the...", "Monk Scribe", "Back Into the Light\n\nI remember\nOf what I said\nduring that weary, dreary, stormy night.\nThe Undead\nyou see.\nThey are here\nand there\nand well,\nalmost everywhere.\nOne for as far as I\ncan see.\n\nSkirmish here\nto Skirmish there.\nTheir magic never goes.\nFrom their Golden hoes,\nto their Undead robes,\nOf what\nthe World foretold.\nI see an opportunity\nto all.\nall who intend to join.\nFor it is\na chance.\nBack\ninto the light.\n\n- Written in Aegis by an unknown author.", ""),
        StaticBook("Back to our Root", "Regale Ba'ikana", "Scout and map out the Ker'norian settlement while remaining unseen by watchful eyes.", ""),
        StaticBook("Baldin", "Baldin Frostbeard", "Tha gret beast stud infront of mhe, gret muscular legs with sharp deadly claws. Squid hunters called it \"Zazul The Red\". It seemed that this polar bear spent its time attacking small fishing boats sinking them and and then waiting for the fishermen to\ndrag themselves to the snowy coast. Once there eyewitness claimed that Zazul devoured them. Legends of neighboring  villages say that from all the blood spilled on the creature its white fur turned red. Legends also say  Zazul is actually an undead\nspirit that seeks revenge on all hunters... I being the curious dweb decided to see this creature by mi self.\nDAY 1:\nAh decided to hire two sailor twins to take me to the area where most claim to hav seen Zazul. They resisted at first, but no being can resist the offa ef dweb gems. I had no intention on giving them any gems tho...I harddly had enough minas for\nmiself, ah just needed somun to tak me the. Ther boat was net big, the size of 6 Uruks laid stragh on tha ground. The twins we human dweb hybrids called Aleker and Jolok, not that thee fact pleased meh but again...ah needed a boat...even ef it was a\nsmall, old, craked one. Worst of all thes half dwebs drank wine and ate squid...all...the bloody...time...\nDay 2:\nWeh het a storm as expected tha ship dint hold. Tha storm crashed us into tha frozen coast. We all survived, but Jolok broke both hes arms treying to keep contrel of tha sails. Ah told them they sheld go back hum, but they beth refused,\ntheyd beth probable die if theyd left ane way. afta 5 minutes ah alrede started regreten no leaven them behind, Jolok ded no stop hes winning about hes arm pains, and Aleker being paranoid sayin: \"This is all Zazul, he summoned the storm, he truly is a\nspirit.\" Wyrvun please if you can hear meh let meh get thre this without kellin mehself...\nDay 3:\nWe had to stop the two twins wer tired an hungry. Ah went to get som wood to mak a fire, an hopefuly fend sum food. When ah came back the two brothas wer gonned, leaving onle a trail of blood into tha woods. Ah asumed et must be Zazul, I had to\nfollow the trail. Tha woods wer cold an glume... and smelled of bleed an rotten flesh. Afta an hour ah found a holein tha ground big enough to be a bear den. Ah entered tha hole, eventually leading meh to a cave. Et seemed tha the hol was tha onle\nentrance to tha cave. Az ah kept investigating tha cave a found a pond of blood and at the middle of et ah saw a boulder with Uruk carven on it. I sighted in disapointment. As I examined tha carvings ah heard som moans comming frem the top of tha boulder.\nPlacen mah  fengers ontop of tha boulder ah started tiptoen to see what was maken tha noise...et was aleker, his legs had been removed, not cut...litteraly removed, as if a boulder had squished hes lower part off. Ah was about to help when ah heard\nsomethin comming frem the hole, ah hid behin the stone. Voices speakin blah could be heard aproachen. Ah dent understand Blah, but afta so many wars against tha disgustin Uruks ah have learned som words, ah heard:\nOther, small, abomination, escape.\nThan tha steps got closa to tha boulder, et seemed like ther wer 3 of hem and one seemed te be prayen as he approached even closer...thei wer gonna sacrifice Aleker. Before ah could intervine ah heard the screams of Aleker as ah felt tha blood of the half\ndweeb drull down meh shoulder. Than jest lik that the left Aleker to bleed to death, ah especte a trap, so ah waited. After 30 minutes ah heard anotha sound commn down the whole...et was no uruks...et was tha sound of a bear...\nZAZUL:\nAh unsheashed mah rusty sword, jest as ah did this ah saw that the bear had placed itz front paws on the stone, en such a way ah could see part of its paws and its razor sharp claws. Alaker had died 10 minutes ago alreadi so he made no sound as\nZazul ate what wes left of him. When ah saw tha chance ah took mah uruk bone blade with mah free hand and  stabbed the beast lowar part of tha paw in an upward motion. Zazul roared in pain and moved back, away from the boulder. Ah moved to face him...for\ntha first time ah had a clear look at tha beast. Et was the size of two war horses, ets fur was derte white with patches of red, ets eyes wer black as the void itself. Tha beast held its left paw up cause of tha stab leavin a big weakspot in ets defense.\nWhen tha bear stood up to crush meh weth its wheight ah charged and slithed under ets rib cage. Ets intestines flowed out of tha beast and after ah couple of seconds tha bear's eyes whitened and ets bode fell to tha ground.\nAh knew Wyrvun wes with meh at thah moment. Fer tha ah skinned Zazul and now wear tha beasts pelt. Ah wear et to honor our great lord Wyrvun, and to send ah message to al otha beasts whom presence harms tha good of thes world.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ballad", "Dionysius de Savin", "In the Middle of the Earth in the Land of a shire .\n\nLives a brave little hobbit whom we all admire.\n\nWith his long wooden pipe.\n\nFuzzy, wooly toes,\n\nHe lives in a hobbit\nhole and everybody knows him.\n\nBilbo! Bilbo Baggins\n\nHe's only three feet tall.\n\nBilbo! Bilbo Baggins\n\nThe bravest little hobbit of them all.\nNow Hobbits are a peace lovin' folks you know\n\nThey don't like to hurry and they take things slow.\n\nThey don't like to travel away from home.\n\nThey just want to eat and be left alone!\nBut one day Bilbo was asked to go.\n\nOn a big adventure to the caves below.\n\nTo help some Dwarves get back their gold.\n\nThat was stolen by a dragon in the days of old.\nBilbo! Bilbo Baggins\n\nHe's only three feet tall!\n\nBilbo! Bilbo Baggins\n\nThe bravest little hobbit of them all.\nWell he fought with the goblins!\n\nHe battled a troll!\n\nHe riddled with Gollum!\n\nA magic ring he stole!\n\nHe was chased by wolfs, \n\nLost in a forest!\nEscaped in a barrel from the Elven Kings Halls\n\nBilbo! Bilbo Baggins!\n\nThe Bravest Little Hobbit of them all.\n\nNow he's back in his hole in the land of the shire.\nThat brave little hobbit whom we all admire,\n\nJust a-sittin' on a treasure of silver an' gold.\n\nA-Puffin' on his pipe in his hobbit hole.\n\nBilbo! Bilbo! Bilbo Baggins\nHe's only three feet tall\n\nBilbo! Bilbo! Bilbo Baggins!\n\nThe Bravest Little Hobbit of them all\n\n- The Ballad of Bilbo Baggins", ""),
        StaticBook("Bandit Letter I", "Bandit", "[!]The letter seems sloppily wrote, the text hurried and botched upon the crumpled paper.\n\n\"Fo'l north'rnmen, yae seek san'ktm behin dae walls. We shal' return te raz yor lan an' homes to ash...\"\n\nThe last parts of the letter seem torn off", ""),
        StaticBook("Basic Cooking", "Lillian", "<><><><><><><><><>\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n   A Guide To Basic\n         Cooking\n     \n            By\n       Lillian Hill\n\n\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~    <><><><><><><><><>\n<><><><><><><><><><>\n~~~~~~Dough~~~~~~\nIngredients:\nTwo binds of wheat.\nCooking Pot.\n\nFind the granules of wheat and remove them, before grindng them and mixing them with a small amount of water. You now have a basic dough.\n<><><><><><><><><>\n~~~~~~Bread~~~~~~Ingredients:\nOne lump of dough\n\nCut off a small amount of the dough made previously, and form it into a ball. Place it in your cooking pot over your hot water, and wait for it to cook.\n<><><><><><><><><>\n~~~~Pan-Cakes~~~~\nIngredients:\nTwo portions of dough.\nCut your dough into two portions, and then go to flatten them out, and place them in your cooking pot side by side over heated water.\n<><><><><><><><><>\n~~~~~~Fish~~~~~~~\n\nIngredients:\nRaw fish of your choice.\n\nRemove the bones of the fish, and peel off one layer of scales, placing it in the cooking pot with the small amount of seasoning.\n<><><><><><><><><>\n~~~~~~Meats~~~~~~\nIngredients: Your choice of raw meat.\n\nSeason the meat with your choice of herb or salt, and then place it in your cooking pot, with a small amount of fat, or water.", ""),
        StaticBook("Basic Cooking V2", "Lillian Hill", "<><><><><><><><><>\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n   Basic Cooking V.2\n   Soups And Stews.\n          \n            By\n       Lillian Hill\n\n\n\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~   <><><><><><><><><><>\n<><><><><><><><><><>\n\nFor each of these recipes a bowl will be needed. These can be easily brought from most stores, or if you feel skilled enough, easy to carve yourself from wood. This is the second installment of the 'Basic Cooking' books.\n<><><><><><><><><><>\n~~Sailor's delight~~~\nIngredients: A cooked fish of your choice. \n\nAdd a small amount of water to your cooking pot, and allow it to warm. Meanwhile, finely dice your fish, making sure to skin and bone it, removing the head. Place\nthe chunks of fish in the hot water, and allow it to reach boiling point. At this point, you may feel free to add herbs or salts of your choice, such as tarragon, dill weed or basil. After the broth has boiled for half an elven hour, take a ladle and pour\nit into a bowl, taking care not to spill any of the liquid, as it may burn. Fish are an easy ingredient to attain, making this the perfect recipe for an easy and cost effective meal that would satisfy the hunger of your whole family.\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n<><><><><><><><><><>\n~~~Mushroom Stew~~\nIngredients:\nOne red browncap shroom.\nOne brown browncap shroom.\n\nTo start with, add a large quantity of water to your cooking pot, lighting your fire underneath the\ncauldron of water. As the water warms, peel your mushrooms of the top layer, as this allows for flavour to soak into the water. Then continue to slice your mushrooms into a few reasonable size chunks. After the water has started to bubble, throw in the\nmushrooms, adding some salt and perhaps some butter or lard, if you have the resources to do so. Allow the mushrooms to cook, stirring the broth occasionally. Once the mushrooms have coloured slightly, and the aroma begins to fill the room, ladle the stew\ninto a bowl. An easy recipe, as this type of fungi are commonly found in the wild, or can be bought from a store. This recipe makes enough for one person, though can be easily changed to make enough for the whole family.\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n<><><><><><><><><><>\n~~~Chicken Stew~~~\nIngredients:\nOne large piece of roat chicken.\nStart by lighting your fire and pour some water into the cooking pot to halfway, allowing it to heat and boil. Take the chicken and remove the skin. Then, make sure to\ncut it into bite size chunks, making sure to carefully place them in the cooking pot to avoid the splashing of water. After doing this, allow the chicken to cook before adding any extra vegtables. Once the chicken has browned further and the aroma fills\nthe room, remove the pot of broth from the heat and pour into a dining bowl. Allow to cook slightly before eating.\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ <><><><><><><><><><><>\n<><><><><><><><><><>\n~~~~Pork Soup~~~~\n\nIngredients: \nCooked Pork\n\nStart off by lighting your fire and heating your cauldron, before placing the cooking pot over the boiling water. This creates a Bain Marie.\nAfter doing this, fill your cooking pot halfway with water. Next, slice up the pork, removing the fat. Place the slices into the cooking pot with salt and rosemary or sage. Stir the soup occasionally. After leaving it to cook for about half an elven hour,\nremove the bowl from the heat. Pour the soup into a serving bowl, though allow it to cool as the water would be boiling.\n <><><><><><><><><><>\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n<><><><><><><><><><>\n~~~Vegtable Soup~~\n\nIngredients:\nTwo baked potatoes. \nFour carrots.\n\nCreate the Bain Marie once more and add your cooking pot. Fill the cooking pot with warm water to about\na quarter of the way. While the water is warming, slice your potatoes into chunks, and add them to the water. Next, cut your carrots into thin round disks. Add these to the water. If you wish, salt and rosemary can be added to give the soup some seasoning\nand flavour. Soon after, remove the cooking pot from the heat. Pour the contents into a serving bowl. \n <><><><><><><><><><>\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~", ""),
        StaticBook("Basic First Aid", "Gwyneviere de Savoie", "Basic First Aid\n\nGwyneviere de Savoie\n\n~                        ~\n          Vol 1\nIt is important for those who commonly engage in fighting or combat that the wound is more deadly than your enemies' weapon. Even the smallest cut can kill you. Tend to your wounds as soon as you can and ensure that your wound does not become infected.\nUnder the circumstance that the patient has been inflicted with a cut or puncture injury, there will be blood. Tourniqet the wound to stop the blood flow, or apply a moss to absorb and clot the wound.\n\nForeign material, such as cloth and dirt\nfor example, will need to be removed from the wound. Particularly if the wound is a puncture. Anything inside the wound can lead to infection and then death.\n\nEven the smallest injury can kill the strongest, and it is important to be aware\nof how deadly infection is. Animal urine is an efficient way to sterylise an injury of any infection. Cauterizing the wound is a painful method, but an efficient one, to reduce chances of external infection. If perhaps you do not have ready available\nanimal urine, or a brand (or a fire), or you do not have herbs or medical plants; wrap the injury as best you can and replace bandaging often. Reach a doctor, or a field medic immediately.\n\nAfter sterylising the injury, you may chose to apply a medical\nor herbal paste to the wound if you have it on hand. Otherwise, apply a clean bandage to the wound and seek proper medical aid. Again, change the dressing regularly.\n\nIf a wound is so severe that an internal organ is punctured\nor cut by sword or knife- there isn't much first aid can do. Organ damage will most likely lead to a painful death without proffesional care. It is unlikely that the correct attention will be gained if the wound was inflicted in battle. Use tea's or herbs\nto ease your pain, or your patients' pain as best you can. It is likely that the patient will be suffering from his or hers' injury.\n\nSide note: Alcohol is good way to sterylise a wound and act as a pain killer.\nSevere Head Injury:\n\nIt is likely that in battle a person will come across a head or skull injury. This may also occur after a fall or a slip. If the injury is small, reach an area where you can sit, and check yourself for obvious\ninjury. It is likely you will be dazed or nausious. If skin has split, apply a bandage and seek help as fast as possible to ensure that no long term damage is dealt.\n\nIf the injury is severe, such as the crushing of a skull, your\npatient is most likely unconcious, or in a coma. Either way, they're in a bad state- and hopefully you're there to save their life. Check their pulse first, they may appear to be dead. Swelling of the face, nose, and eyes is a sign that the patient\nhas undergone some serious damage to their head or skull. In this case, it is unlikely that basic first aid can save their life. Do not move them, and if possible, seek proper medical attention. The brain of the patient will swell, causing brain damage\nor death. A hole will need to be drilled into the skull of the patient in order to allow the brain to swell. It is still likely that the patient will die.\n\nHead injuries can cause nausia, headaches, dizzyness and physical sickness. Resting will heal these\nBroken Bones:\n\nYou can check to see the severity of your patients injuries (or your own) by physical appearance. Your patient or yourself will most likely be in shock because of the injury. State of shock is a dangerous thing. Never\nunderestimate the severity of the situation. Broken bones often can be seen externally as lumps in the skin, particularly in limbs. Check for mishape or difference in your limbs, and the limb affected.\nYou can use sticks and straps from boots or clothes, or fabric from your clothes also, to create a splint to keep limbs straight. If your patient has a broken leg, it is likely they wont be able to walk. This is a no brainer to identifying a broken bone\nor fracture. Splinting or creating a stretcher out of sturdy sticks strapped together in a ladder shape can be used to transport the patient. A splint can be used to keep the injury straight and reduce movement to the affected area\nin the case of injuring yourself.\n\nYou can also pack mud around the limb to set the break. Seek proper medical attention as soon as possible.\n\nDislocations can be relocated with pressure to the\naffected area. It is painful. Your patient may need pain killers. If you do not feel comfortable tending to a dislocated bone, seek medical attention of another, or man up.\n\nSlings, made out of tied cloth, or a shirt is great for arm or shoulder breaks.\nA bone break can also break the skin. There may be blood. Apply a splint or use a stretcher to get the patient to proper medical attention if this is the case.\nWater Injuries:\n\nIf a person has found themselves floating face down in the water. The first thing you should do is turn them onto their back. It is important not to apply weight to their body, as you could force them under water.\nThere isnt much you can do out in the water, so bring them back to shore quickly, and remember to keep their head above the waters' surface.\n\nLay them on their back and check for a pulse. A persons pulse can be found under their neck or the under-\n-side of their wrist. Either way, there is a possibility of saving the patient. Place one hand, a fist, onto the chest of the patient above their heart. Place your second hand atop the other.\n\nPump their chest, with short breaks. Count thirty pumps before\nstopping. This can force water out of the lungs of the patient or restart the heart.\n\nOpen the airway of the patient by placing your palm on the persons forhead and gently tilting their head back. Check for normal breathing. If the patient is not breathi-\n-ng still, open the persons mouth and transfer air from your own lungs to the patients. Afterwards, continue pumping. Hopefully this will be enough to revive the patient or get the water out of their lungs.\nArrow Wounds:\n\nIf your patient has an arrow injury, first be prepared to apply a lot of force to free the person of the arrow. They are very hard to get out safely. Pulling it out without care can sever arteries or break leave splinters\nor wood inside of the body. You could die of blood loss or infection. So long as the bolt or arrow is inside of the patient, the blood loss will be lower than without it.\n\nYou can remove the arrow by propulsion, where you force the arrow\nthrough the flesh and out the exit point of the wound. Reccomended for limb injuries.\n\nSaw off the shaft, and leave it for a few days so that the wound becomes full of pus and can then be removed with ease. The pus signals infection.\nand would then need proper medical attention.\n\nStretch the wound by plugging it with probes of elder pith, soaked in honey and then using a pair of tongs, reach into the wound and slowly, carefully, tug the arrow/bolt free.\nWash the wound with wine or liquor, and apply a bandage securely or cauterize the wound. Reduce the amount of strain on the affected area and rest for a few days to prevent pains and quicken the rate of healing.", ""),
        StaticBook("Basic Math", "Benjamin Berric", "Basic Math:\nExamples and Work\nBasic counting:\n\n1 : One___2 : Two\n3 : Three_4 : Four\n5 : Five__ 6 : Six\n7 : Seven_8 : Eight\n9 : Nine_ 10 : Ten\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~A special number 0, means to have none\nex) No apples left= 0\nMath:\nExamples:\nBasic Use:\n\nHow many?\n\na) o o o o =\nb) o o o  =\nc) o o o o o o =\nd) o o o o o =\ne) o o =\nf) o o o o o o o o o =\ng) o o o o o o o =\nh) o o o o o o o o =\nMath:\nExamples:\nBasic Use:\n\nHow many?\no = 1, * = 2\n\na) ooo** =\nb) ***o =\nc) o*o*o* =\nd) ***o* =\ne) oo**oo =\nf) o**oooo=\ng) ***oooo =\nMath:\nExamples:\nBasic functions:\n\n(+) this symbol is used to ADD numbers,\nmaking them larger\n(ex) 1 + 1 = 2\n\n(-) this symbol is used to MINUS numbers,\nmaking them smaller\n(ex) 2 - 1 = 1\nMath:\nWork:\nBasic Functions:\n\na) 1 + 3 =\nb) 2 + 5 =\nc) 4 + 2 =\nd) 5 + 4 =\ne) 6 + 3 =\nf) 6 - 3 =\ng) 5 - 4 =\nh) 4 - 2 =\ni)  3 - 1 =\nj) 2 - 2 =\nMath:\nExamples\nBasic Functions:\n\nIn review you have 2 basic function to use:\n\n+ symbol also known as addition\n\n- symbol also known as subtraction\nMath:\nHomework:\nBasic Functions:\n\nTry to make some of your own functions and solve them, and bring them in next time we gather, double check your work!\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~", ""),
        StaticBook("Bastion: 1626", "Victoria Horen-Vientos", "3rd of The Grand Harvest, 1626\n\nUpon entering Bastion, I've first noticed that the blight is gone. The earth is now dry and rotten, but the undead taint in the air has somewhat receded.\n\nA bridge, likely made of what seems to be Druidic vines, has\nour entrance into the city easy, and we're within the first set of walls.\n\nRubble is scattered everywhere, and vines grow on every stone-made structure. Old, tattered flags bearing the sigil of Mordring still hang, but with a sort of pointless presence.\nThe outer structure of the former temple of Owynism is still intact, though the inside is in complete ruin. All that remains of it's former beauty are some stone bricks painted in molten gold.\n\nAt the center of the city, a pillar stands. An\ninscription reads 'Mordring's Pillar', though from my observation, it is giving off no energy.\n\nThroughtout the main square, all is in ruin. Dead trees sprout up in the old streets, and the only surviving callbacks to this great city are the occasional\nsurviving marble pillar or iron gate. Making my way up to the former Royal Palace, I find that the stairway is flooded, though the water seems fresh and pure.\n\nThe main courtyard of the Horenic Palace is in shambles, but the view still reminds me of the\ngreatness that was this stalwart kingdom. No flowers grow here anymore, where previously roses and berries might have thrived.\n\nThe throne room itself has been turnedi nto one for Mordring's servant, Ghamul. Black and dreary.\nManaging to make my way to the top of the old palace, the entire upper level has been reduce to rubble.\n\nConcluding my journey into the city, I have found that it is inhabitable, but not without an air of grief, sadness, and death looming over it for\nall time.\n\nSigned,\n\nVictoria Horen-Vientos,\nArbiter of the Ascended Order & Princess of Lotharingia", ""),
        StaticBook("Battle For CT", "Eenhoornheid", "Seth Calith's tell of the battle for the Cloud Temple of Anthos. The 29th of The Amber Cold in year 1452\nIt's early in the morning, the humans, dwarves, orcs and maybe even some elves are shouting about praising a squid, a spy bat, praising the sun, creator and many more things. Shouts of hatred towards one another is filling this small fort.\nThe forces are seemingly ready as the sun goes down once more. Wether or not this attack shall happen at night, I do not know. Many things is still shouted, speaks of herasy is heard as someone wish to dine in the Nethers while others wants in the Seven\nHavens, the must disturbing of all the shouts must be the 'Blood for coin' which is what House Flay shouted in times of old. A Disbute has started of what war-cry is the one they wish for. Instead of debating, they simply shout, someone even attempted to\nmix shouts to make this even worse. I hope this war shall soon start and close the mouth of theirs.\n\nThe war has started, the first footmen of the scourge has been sighted. They have sent few troops in advance to keep them at bay while the rest\nof the army uses crossbows and bows alike to end them. The sound of monsters is heard, most likely giving the chill to many men. A charge has started, explosions are seen on their charge, damaging the army. I will now move a bit forward to see what will\nhappen now. The battle is bloody in the ruins of an old fort. I avoided a magical spell by few inches from the 'friendly' side. This is indeed a chaos filled with blood and the screams of death. I know not whom will win yet.\nShous of retreat is heard while others seek to run head first into the battle, orders seemingly have little meaning now. \n\nThe soldiers are slowly pushing forward, many spells of death is fired to the only bridge allowing them to pass and\nattacking the enemy themself.\n\nSomeone is claiming the battle is on the losing end while others wish to scale the mountains and lastly, others give orders to kill the enemy mages on the mountains.\nI still wonder how this will end, I am without answer as this night surely will be long.\n\nA knight of Oren shouts of the retreat of the scourge, suddenly an ambush was revealed from the right flank. The fate is yet to be seen.\nIn the distance, I can see them hacking at the gate, seemlingly they managed to break it, allowing for a further attack. \n\nThe gate was a trap, attackers came from behind, some died while I managed to escape.\nThe Scourge has positioned guards at the gate, I can't enter to see the actual battle.\n\nThe ambushers was tricked into running into the allied fort, bringing them into a quick death.\n\nThe allied are\nadvancing now once more, I will follow.\n\nThe Scourge has placed mages and archers on top of a giant construct of some sort. Raining down fire on the allies, almost hitting me once more.\nSeemingly, the allies wants to enter the library, for what reason I do not know. Maybe the scourge is hiding there.\n\nI start to think that these arrows I have avoided is actualy from the allies, attempting to hit the\nmages.\nThey found a way to enter the library, now they need only to enter the floating tainted earth, chained to the earth of the Cloud Temple of Anthos.\n\nThe Library is swarmed by the monsters of the scourge and the allies of Anthos.\nLava also flows in the library, making this far too warm for comfort combined with the stench of dead.\n\nSeemingly a portal of some sort is placed on the second floor, it's frame made of ice and white shining light of some sort.\nSomeone now wants to dine in 'hell', I really wonder where they all get these names.\n\nWords are shouted of breaking the portal to the floating earth. Wether or not it will work, I do not know.\nA new plan is forged, everyone enters the portal at the same time to meet the powers of the magic at the same time. I must say one of the best plans to be heard, running head first into the fire.\nThe light of the day returns as the battle is still here. One of the red crystals from the tainted earth flew towards a warmechine on the mountain, what the result is, I do not know.\n\nI found the remains of a Billy Bob's award medal.\nLooking like a flower, on it, claiming this Billy Bob killed a dragon, most likely, it was a drake.\n\nAs I enter the library once more, the library is destroyed, sounds of cheer is heard yet the battle is now over.\nThey still need to destroy the chains to the tainted earth so it may float or crash, I do not know what will happen but hopefully one of the two options.\nWhile under attacks of the enemy, the allies managed to break the chains by hand.\n\nThe battle is almost over, they are going to finish off the rest of the Harbingers of the Setherins. Seemingly they are winning this war.\nIt's done, the war is won, Anthos won the war against the Scourge, hopefully. I shall now leave the lands which stinks of death, rot and fire.", ""),
        StaticBook("Battle of Riga", "Ser White", "The Battle of Riga: Oren's Darkest Hour\nPrelude: The Battle of Riga was one of the darkest days in recent memory for the Holy Oren Empire. A part of the Courlandic Rebellion, the Battle of Riga was a last ditch effort on the part of the Axis to best Oren and drive back their forces.\nWith the Vanirs having recently recaptured their home of Kraken's Watch, the Staunton leadership had fled, expecting Oren to capture Riga and swift end the war. All that was left to defend Riga were the proud men of the Axis.\nBattle: The Battle of Riga started on the Grand Harvest of 1563. Leading the Axis infantry was a prominent Dreadlander, and the Farfolk leader took charge of the cavalry. The Orenian leadership was more united, being commanded by the Gold Corps leader.\nThe Axis marched outside of Riga in order to meet assult attack Oren's army. Upon seeing this Oren marched onto the field from the ruins of Kraken's Watch. While Oren continued on along the main road, the Axis took to a hill north of the road.\nUpon seeing this, there was a brief exchange of arrows, but the wind was so heavy that arrows couldn't fly properly and all missed. Seeing this, the Axis charged down the hill towards Kraken's Watch while the two contingents of cavalry duked it out in a-\nwheat field along the river near Kraken's Watch. However, Oren's infantry had kept advancing on Riga, so the two armies had practically changed positions. They then rushed at each other, and met just south of the road leading to Riga.\nThe fighting was fierce. At the start, it seemed that Oren's infantry would carry the day with their superior numbers. The Axis cavalry had killed the majority of Oren' cavalry and then all rushed into the melee. As the battle carried on and men were-\ngetting worn down, however, the tides shifted. Small contingents of oreners were being caught away from the main force and cut down. Oren's wounded had fallen back towards Riga, behind the fresher infantrymen.\nHowever, the Axis's battered and bruises patched up what they could and carried on. It was this weakness that would be Oren's downfall. As freshmen sat back trying to fully recover, the Axis discovered where the weak had hidden away.\nWhat followed next can only be described as a slaughter. The battle had shifted into Oren's medical camp. The weak were slaughtered, and with so many fresh men having stayed back, the numbers quickly shifted as disarray swept through Oren's lines.\nOreners fell left and right. After the dust had settled, Orenian bodies littered the ground. All that remained were a few cavalry that galloped around and tried to do something, only to be piked off their steeds and cut down.\nWhilst that occured, the Axis proceeded to hunt down the cowards which had attempted to hide upon realize their defeat. Not a single Orenian would return from the plains outside Riga.\nConclusion: That day, Orenian high command managed to squander every advantage they could have taken. Granted, they were smart in not marching up the slope to face the Axis, but that seemed to spell the end of their tactical genious.\nThe cavalry forces were similar enough in size that the superior skill of the Axis cavalry showed. Without any infantry to support the cavalry, most of Oren's riders were doomed to die.\nThe infantry tells a different story entirely. The Axis managed to remain a cohessive force throughout the battle, where as Oren faced problems with units being isolated and cut down. Along with that, keeping men in the medical camps for too long surely-\nalso cost Oren dearly. However, it should not be forgotten or denied that the Axis was a better trained force than what Oren had. Orcish strength, the Dreadlanders legendary fighting skills, and the numbers provided by Courlanders, Krajens,\nand the former Nortruppen ultimately led to the Axis's military being more prepared than that of Oren's. On top of the fact that the Axis also had superior commanders, the Axis had taken the tiniest of advantages and maximized them, unlike Oren.\nEpilogue: Based off this telling, it would seem apparent that the Axis should have won the war. Well, scholars today cannot say why the Axis lost, other than God himself had cursed their effort. Despite their being the victorious army which had utterly-\ncrushed the Orenian at the Battle of Riga standing between Oren and Riga, an Orenian army managed to sweep into the city without a fight, capture it, and loot it. However, the Axis did still have a war against Oren in the south to fight.\nYet, even that was cursed by God, as no side was even able to muster an army to do battle until they arrived at Axios. There, enough Axis members had passed away, disappeared, or switched allegiances that the Axis no longer stood a chance.\nBy some miracle of God, Oren survived its darkest day. Despite Oren having come so close to being defeated, as the Axis would have been able to besiege the capital had God not interfered, few Oreners remember this day.\nEven fewer recognize how close Oren truly came to defeat. If anything can be taken from the Battle of Riga, it should be these two things.\n1. Oren isn't invisible. As hard as it may be to defeat Oren, it can be done with enough men, skill, supplies, and tactics.\n2. So long as God is with Oren. Oren will never fall. In order for Oren to fall, one must either have the support of God himself, or convince God to let fate decide itself.\nThe End.\n\nIn memory of all those brave men of the Eagle and their allies who gave their lives in hopes of achieving freedom.", ""),
        StaticBook("Battleground", "Varstivus", "The Divine Battleground\n\nMany recall Aegis with an air of fondness, nostalgia, reverance. However, in my centuries of abscence from that plane. I have come to realize that it contained some glaring issues that last to this day.\nThe land was not a utopia, nor was it a place of expression. After all this time, I have learned that Aegis was nothing bore than a chessboard for beings beyond our comprehension.\nThe battle between the Archaengul Aeriel and the Archdaemon Iblees was\nthe world's sole focus. The descendant races clashed, to be sure. Birthing the strange alliance between the elves and the orcs, as well as the blood oath between the dwarves and the humans. All of the war paled in comparison though, to our unified foe.\nThe Undead. Fear would strike anyone as thunder could be heard from just over the mountains. The Ascended were not much better, all callous to the smaller issues of the world. Battling the undead was their only purpose. The insignificance of our own lives\nwas palpable. All were expected to throw their lives away for the god's cosmic game.\nNothing could bring them to truely care for our lives. We won in the end, fullfilled our purpose. Then we've had none.\nThe humans in this time sought a new patron,\nand found one in their creator. The elven culture split in ways that were utterly ofensive at the time, but that are simply considered as normal today. The wood elves  resorted to very bad politics, while the High elves put barriers between themselves and\ntheir cousins.\n\nEach race coped differently. But the abandonment of the Aenguls left a fledging society that did not know what to do with themselves.\nNext you hear of Aegis being a land of peace and plenty, recall this.", ""),
        StaticBook("be a gud olog", "Gu'Gren", "how to be gud olog\n\nztep 1 nub eat goblin\n\nztep 2 nub eat uruk\n\nztep 3 eat zquealz\n\nztep 4 but nub tu many \n\nztep 5 lern tu read\n\nnow latz gud olog!", ""),
        StaticBook("Bell's Diary", "liam_barnett", "Bell's Super Duper\n      Private Diary\n-------------------\n\nThis will be my log of important events, starting with me being the victim of guard brutality.\n10th of Sun's Smile, 1563:\n\nThis is the new chapter in my life; Skyfall has fallen to the hands of Vandoria, I'm out of my old teaching job, and I now run a junkyard.\nUpon walking into the tavern, I request that I buy a whole load of drinks. Six rum, three vodka, and a glass of water. The girl behind the counter, seeming to be in her twenties,  if even that, refused. Her heavy accent\nmade it quite difficult to understand her request, but she told me to buy only one drink. As I continued to demand that I be served multiple drinks, she told me to leave the tavern. So, as any alchohol deprived\nman would do, I came back with a knife. I asked one more time to be served, and when she refused, I pulled my knife out, demanding the drinks I had asked for. I instantly met the wrath of some man, abnormally tall, wearing heavy\nmetallic armour. He turned me into the guards, and recounted what had just happened. As I sat at a table in the barracks, almost five guards stood by. When they weren't looking, I easily hopped over the wall.\nI slept in the woods for just one night, then returned the next day, only to be grabbed by the same guards again. They proceeded to hang me upside down from a tower, beat me, and the like. But then I was taken into the basement.\nThat's where I was strapped to a chair, and one guard with mis-matched eyes retrived his own knife, asking if I wanted my left or right eye removed first. Struggling, I remained strapped down as the\nman continued to drill my left eye with the knife, my sockets full of blood. Afterwars, he cut me in various places, legs to chin. But it was nothing compared to the loss of my left eye. I'm now blinded and scarred,\nunable to see through that eye. \n\nAbuse by the Felsen guard at it's finest.\n12th of Malin's Welcome, 1566:\n\nUpdate since my last entry, which was quite some time ago; My daughter, Daisy, has been born, and I'm still living in at the same junkyard. Business is fine, I'm able to\nsupport us both. I'm just thankful that we live outside the walls, I'd hate to be within the same city as all those criminals or corrupted soldiers.\n\nToday is my birthday, and I just went out for a drink, then\nsat down with Daisy at home. It's raining outside.\n\nIt was a nice birthday, to say the least.\n2nd of Sun's Smile, 1566:\n\nIronically, I've joined the guard force. The junkyard has declined in sales, and we're losing more money than we're receiving. I've decided that I'll need to take up a second\njob, just to take care of Daisy and myself. I was swiftly accepted into the force, and shown how to operate the gate, given a copy of the rules, all that good stuff.\nI'm considering selling the house and the junkyard, and moving into a cheaper apartment in the city. It may be best for Daisy to live within the walls, as Orcs and the like have started showing up more frequently.\nAnd Kha. Kha are disgusting.\n11th of Snow's Maiden, 1567:\n\nOn the watch today, Mattington brought in two orcs, assisted by some of the Goldies. They stored a larger one upstairs, and the Goblin in a cell, monitored by myself.\nI was instructed to search all of his belongings, and confiscate any arms or armour it had on it's person. There were blades and the sort, which I took away for safety precautions. Mattington then\ndemanded a fine of one hundred mina from the Goblin, for whatever crime he had commited, and the Goblin declared that it had no money. And so, I was told to confiscate all of his items, to make up for the fine.\nThis included a journal, some spare ink, and some type of buckler of sorts. I placed all of his belongings on a desk, as the rest of the guards were handling the other orc. I was hissed at by the Goblin from behind the bars,\nas he declared that a, \"Swampguth\" had given the buckler to him. After flipping through his own journal, I found nothing of interest, so I allowed him to keep that. But, long story short, the other guards ended up killing\nhis friend by accident, in some type of brawl. The Goblin became upset, attacked me and Mattington, but was quickly aprehended. They threw him into the moat, leaving him to die.\nIn my eyes, this was, of course, appropriate punishment. However, it was not the appropriate solution. If he were to wake up, he would only cause trouble again. I hauled his resting body\nback to the Uzg, leaving him in the sand outside their city, hoping that somebody would find him. What I did was not out of respect, or care for this criminal, but out of fear. I wanted him out of Oren.\nSo this was, by far, a noble act, as I was caring for the empire, and not the individual-- But does the Lord applaud my actions? Have I satisfied him?\n11th of Malin's Welcome, 1567:\n\nThis is the first major attack, directed at Felsen as a whole, and not just an individual. These fire-related incidents are n-\n[!] Suddenly, the rest of the page is torn to a shred, and the other twenty or so pages have been removed as well.", ""),
        StaticBook("Bestiary I", "Melia", "Welcome to the bestiary of the Westerlands.\n-------------------11th of Snows Maiden, 1604. \n\n   Within this book you may discover the description of various cruel beings and the given weaknesses they obtain. Furthermore I do hope you find this\ndocument useful and for any inquiries on this subject, and/or the author contact;\nMelia Finnigan\n~Table of Contents~\nIntroduction\nFrost Witches \nLiches\nGiant Crabs\nGhouls\nHomunculi\n~Ice Witches~\n\n        Better known as Ice Demons these brutal monsters are women now turned into men-devouring savages. To indentify one them you must obtain a keen eye - for their teeth with be pointed, and flesh cold. An aurum blade\nor fire will do just finely.\n~Liches~\n\n      Liches are immortal undead and are most likely aptly skilled in magical arts. They are resistant to the elements and can endure such damages brought upon them. They cannot perceive pain inflicted by physical damage, such as iron\nweapons or other forms of corporeal  trauma.  \n          Yet, Liches obtain a skeletal and frail figure - hence being able to be dispatched easily. They are weak to to gold, and divine magic.\n~Giant Crabs~\n     \n        Are beasts from a faulty experiments. Much isn't known of them, yet that they obtain a hard carapace that is difficult to get any average weapon through for spikes prod outwards from them. The best way to have\nthem slain is from the soft tissue of the under-abdomen region.\n~Ghoul~\n\n          A more typical foe these beast tend to feast upon kin of the four brothers with vile claws, and decaying flesh. The most simplistic way to have them slain is to use any weapon to depatch their limbs or use aurum ones.\n~Homunculus~\n\n         Beings forged by alchemy and brough from the dead. They can be hostile or peaceful though none the less aurum works finely.\nAll is done for now - for anymore information contact\nMelia Finnigan via bird.", ""),
        StaticBook("Bestiary V1", "Adeon of Rhoswen", "The Marked Man's Bestiary\n\nContents:\n1. Beasts of Nature\n2. Natural Monstrosities\n3. Sentient Supernaturals\n3. Supernatural Monstrosities\n4. Constructs\n-Beasts of Nature-\n\nThese creatures are the beasts commonly seen throughout the world and pose no real threat to the innocent mundane.\nCanines: Either intelligent pack hunters or less witty companion animals, the canine often possesses sharp teeth and fur- unlike their Ursidae cousins, they are not often large and do not possess significantly sharp claws. Canines are known to be tamable.\nRats: These creatures are the messengers of coming pestilence and death, they've the standard qualities expected of small rodents. Extended exposure to these creatures often leads to sickness, earning them the nickname \"Plague bearers\".\nBats: These creatures are physically quite similar to the common rat despite the fact that they have wings and do not possess a tail.\nThey're generally nocturnal and have an enhanced sense of hearing which makes up for their poor vision.\nBirds: Variations of these are seen far and wide. From the common pigeon to the barn owl. The creatures have near countless variations and are often used to carry messages over long distances. They are mostly harmless.\nSand Tortoise: These creatures are of staggering size. We've precious little information on the beasts and taking one down would require no less than a siege party. The creature grows in size rivaling a small keep. They are extremely rare.\nSand Lizard: A common sight within the Orcish deserts. These creatures are surprisingly fast and can topple a target with very little effort. Their hide is nothing worthy of note. Their bones are of decent density and genuinely sturdy.\n-Natural Monstrosities-\n\nThese are the creatures commonly found within nature but are considered perverse and diluted in purpose. They're to be hunted and their existence extinguished.\nThe Harpy: These monsters have the ability to fly and resemble ugly women- their skin is extremely oily and susceptible to fire. They're bones are quite brittle and will crack under pressure. Their feathers are fine for use in arrows and their pelts make-\n-for good middle class clothing. They've a cruel sense of humor. They are known to scoop up targets and drop them from lethal heights. If a Harpy nest is discovered it is suggested that it be burned immediately.\nKrummavisur: Resembling a Raven, though staggering in size. These beasts have awe-inspiring wing spans and considerable strength.\nThey scoop up their prey and toss them immeasurable distances. The beast is not to be fought alone. They can kick up dust-\n-with the density to block sight for yards. When effort is applied they can shove a man in full plate to his knees with the power of the air from their wings alone. It is suggested that the feet are struck, as they are quite thin and easy to amputate.\nCockatrice: An odd looking creature. Standing at the height of a small building with the width to match.\nThey are quite intimidating to fight up close and are able to fly, rendering close combat to be the inevitable result of an encounter.\nThe Cockatrice has the ability to exhale a thick gray smog that turns whoever comes in contact with it to stone. Being submerged in water will negate this effect.\nTheir skin is unholy in strength, steel will hardly damage it, an aurum blade is required.\nThe Beast's bones are strong as stone and they've the strength to topple a building with ease.\nLeaf Apes: Fundamentally illusive creatures that have flesh as hard as rock and bones like fresh timber. They possess decent strength for their size but struggle to penetrate leather. They tend to rush a target and make an effort to climb atop its face.\nOnce atop the victim's face, the Leaf Ape will tear at the flesh. Bladed steel weapons are practically useless against these creatures and will often break upon contact with their skin- blunt weapons are suggested as well as aurum swords.\nCave Leeches: A beast that drops down on it's targets and spews acid onto them, it has the strength to render armor useless. They only attack in complete darkness. \n\nNo one has survived an encounter thus far.\nDrakes: Creatures with bat-like wings, the ability to breathe flame, scaly hides, complete with muscular legs and tail-- these truly majestic beasts have captured the awe of men for centuries. Despite this, magical perversion has lead to the Drake species\nundergoing various mutations and become near extinct. It is expected that combat with a Drake be avoided and alternative methods to killing be used to neutralise the threat such a beast poses. The Drake's main weaknesses are its wings, mouth and eyes,\n-however this beast will continue fighting until the last drop of blood runs from it's wound. Decapitation and siege weaponry is suggested.\nEnlarged Arachnid:\n\nThe average spider, though colossal in size and extremely venomous- they are susceptible to fire and relatively easy to defeat compared to other beasts in this compendium.\n-Sentient Naturals-\n\nThese beings are to be reasoned with if possible and relocated away from areas where they may have negative effects on the local mundane population.\nTroll: Usually found lurking under bridges, in caves or forests. These beasts can be at times helpful and friendly-- at other times they are forces to be reckoned with. Trolls are generally quite intelligent and are capable of speech, complex emotion and-\n-co-operation. The best method of slaying a Troll is to use aurum and to disable it's method of movement, trolls are known to carry enormous amounts of weight in the form of fat around their waist and are unable to get up if any of their legs are damaged.\n-Sentient Supernaturals-\n\nThese beings are to be reasoned with and if possible relocated away from areas where they may have negative effects on the local mundane.\nSpecters: Spirits without bodies, these beings can be benevolent, neutral or malevolent, just like a living person. They can only be harmed by aurum as normal metals will pass straight through them.\nSpecters have the ability to wield enchanted weaponry\n-\n-and don enchanted armor, some have the ability to fly and cast spells, those that have this ability use it to deadly effect. It is suggested that aurum weaponry be used combined with a high-guard stance.\nSpecters are vulnerable to salt and it is-\n-suggested that the perimeter in which the spirit is manifesting be surrounded by lines of pure sea salt.\n-Constructs-\n\nThese are the result of spells or golemmancy, they are able to fit into the supernatural sentient category as well as the monstrous supernatural category depending on what they are- constructs usually have a master and a purpose to follow.\nHunters: \n\nSharing many traits with a specter, the Hunter has the ability to fly- it wears large, heavy armor but is not impeded in any way by this fact. The Hunters are apparently a sort of Golem gone rogue, they once served a holy order and sought to-\n-slay dangerous Magi. Now they slay any who wield magic, including Marked Men. Hunters explode when defeated and it is advised that those who have defeated it clear the area before it does so, as shrapnel is often projected.\nAurum seems to weaken the-\n-creature considerably, though it is probably wise to use steel in order to damage the armor before an aurum weapon is presented.\nHalf swording is suggested due to the armored nature of this foe.\nGolems: The result of powerful runes and magic, Golems can take many forms- from colossal lumbering humanoid to slithering metal snake, all Golems have an 'Impera' who dictates their every action-- Golems will attempt to protect these individuals at all-\n-costs. These constructs are often the result of a soul being bound to the magegold core, destroying this would most likely neutralise the threat. \nWays to destroy the Golem depend on a number of things including environment and the material the Golem is-\n-made of. Golems made of stronger materials may need to be cast from great heights, thrown into watery depths or toppled into a substance hot enough to melt metal.\n-Supernatural Monstrosities-\n\nThese creatures defy all reason. They serve no purpose in this world and are to be slain.\nNecrophages: These creatures come in two variations; Fleshed and Skeletal.\n\nFleshed typically maintain a slumped posture, they've considerable strength and an immunity to pain.\n\nAurum weaponry is recommended for these types of creatures.\nAlone, their presence is a joke, but when amassed it's often best to simply route.\nThe method of reanimation is unknown, however it is to be noted that they appear more frequently around areas of frequent fighting or wickedness.\nFire is a weakness.\nLich: The ultimate product of an individual's greed for power or knowledge. Liches are beings that have made a transformation into entities powered purely on arcane energies and a deep seated hatred for those that get in the way of more power.\nTypes of Liches vary broadly and improvisation is to be expected. One recurring trait seems to be the presence of a crystal known as the phylactery- it is where the Lich's soul is rumoured to be kept, destroying this crystal will kill the creature.\nBloodsuckers/Sangbriseur:\nThese creatures take the form of an obscene lump of slimey acid. Depending on their environment, the creature can absorb it's surroundings and become deadlier-- there are such things as Bloodsuckers who have absorbed fire,\nbecoming thrice as dangerous as their acidic counterparts. To dispose of the creature, it is suggested that it be cut into smaller pieces and set alight-- be sure that every chunk is burnt or else it will regenerate over time.", ""),
        StaticBook("Big journal", "'Big Green'", "Mi Big Green mi good books", ""),
        StaticBook("Bighorn Sheep", "Avonnia Akla'Vyf", "A Study of:\n\nThe Big-Horn Sheep\n\n\nThe Body and Build.\nThe bighorn sheep is a breed that is native to the north. It is best suited for mountain like and cold environments. \n\nThese horns can weigh up to 14 kg (30 lb), while the sheep themselves weigh up to 140 kg (300 lb).\nBighorn sheep are named for the large, curved horns borne by the rams (males). Ewes (females) also have horns, but they are shorter with less curvature.\n\nThey range in color from light brown to grayish\nor dark, chocolate brown, with a white rump and lining on the backs of all four legs.\n\n Males typically weigh 58–143 kg (128–315 lb), are 90–105 cm (35–41 in) tall at the shoulder, and 1.6–1.85 m (63–73 in) long from the nose to the tail.\nFemales are typically 34–91 kg (75–201 lb), 75–90 cm (30–35 in) tall, and 1.28–1.58 m (50–62 in) long.\n\nMale bighorn sheep have large horn cores, enlarged cornual and frontal sinuses, and internal bony septa.\nThese adaptations serve to protect the brain by absorbing the impact of clashes.\n\nBighorn sheep have preorbital glands on the anterior corner of each eye,  inguinal glands in the groin,\nand pedal glands on each foot. Secretions from these glands may support dominance behaviors.", ""),
        StaticBook("Bio Theories", "Leyu", "Contrary to the magic theory of life being so diverse due to magic, I have observed something quite different. The following will be my notes and observation on reality.\nThe offspring seem to have traits dirived from their parents. The calf of a piebald doe and a solid coat stag had approximately half the spots its mother had. The following is a sketch:\n*a sketch of a spotted doe, a solid color stag, and half of each calf\nI thought that maybe that if one was to build on one specific trait, it would become more pronounced. I took 50 mice from the wilderness, each of more or less the same physical appearance, and caged them in my room. I selected the most approachable of the\nmice, being the ones that did not instantly recoil from my presense. I took those mice and bred them together. After a few weeks, I selected the most approachable of the babies. These too, I bred. I continued this for five generations.\nGeneration 1: These mice did not instantly recoil when I approached them. They also accepted food I gave them. I deemed these mice, out of the original batch, to be the more approchable of the batch.\nGeneration 2: The more approachable mice out of this generation were as follows: They were less hesitant to accept food from me, they did not scurry away from my hand, and they were unphased by my presence.\nGenereation 3:\nThese mice were astoundingly strange. They seemed to be joyous when I arrived to check on them, and they did not recoil at all. They did not hesitate to accept my food.\nGeneration 4:\nThese mice were very different. They were extremely overjoyed to see me, and they were like dogs. They snuggled agaisnt my finger, and kept to me for warmth. When I touched them, they were in ecstacy. These were tame.\nGeneration 5:\nThese mice are as tame as any household pet! They scamper towards me and attempt to cuddle with my hand. They seek my presence and are saddened by my absense. I believe I have successfully produced a pet, and tamed mice.\nI decided to test if the obverse was true. Out of the original batch I captured from the forest, I bred the most unruly ones. The results are as follows.\nGeneration 1:\nThese mice were the unruly ones I selected. They ran away from my finger faster than the rest, they did not sniff the food I offered, and they seemed a bit afraid.\nGeneration 2:\nThese mice were even scarder. They took less time to run away from my finger, they did not even go near the food I offered, and they occasionally got defensive.\nGeneration 3:\nThese mice were even more defensive. When I put my finger near, they hissed and ran away. They ran away from the offered food and did not even attempt to reconcile with me.\nGeneration 4: \nThese mice were even more ferocios. When they saw me, they got defensive, and attempted to bite my finger several times. They snarled at the food I presented.\nGeneration 5:\nThese mice were as aggresive as a mother bear! They actively attacked my finger when I put it in there, and I have the scars to prove it. They hissed and snarled at the food, and they were alerted by my presence and were violent.\nThe results of the Mice experiment were very fruitful! It proved that if one were to exploit the traits and capitilize on particular traits, in this case, tameness and aggression, one could change the entire race of animal! We have proven that traits are\ndependant on parental traits and that they can be artificially manipulated and be used to make new races of animals, with different behaviors and physical descriptions.\nI have developed an extraordinary theory! The results of the mice experiment proved that traits can be artificially manipulated and selected, but could nature do this as well!? It may go against everything that we are taught, but perhaps the diversity of\nlife in the wild is a product of nature, not magic! Could nature dictate that the creatures with the better traits more suited to its environment survive to pass their traits to their kin, thus making that trait prominent in the race. Eventually, this\nwould accumulate and become a new race! This could explain the diversity of life far better than magic ever could! I dub this theory Draug's Theory of Natural Manipulation of Traits.\nDraug's Theory of Natural Manipulation:\nMany people would object to the past statement, announcing it as heresy and idiocy, but there is enough proof to atleast make an argument for it. I realize that I have not really explained the Theory of Natural Man-\n-ipulation. Basically, nature plays the role I play. The beasts with the desirable traits, ones better suited to the land they live in, will be able to reproduce, thus passing the trait that allowed them to survive to their kin. Nature weeds out the unde-\n-sirable traits through illness, predation, food accessability, and famine. The beasts that have the better traits will pass the trait to the kin, and so on. Eventually this will manifest into new beasts, with distinctly different traits than its\nancestors. Overtime, these beasts become specialized to their environment, and have developed specific traits for their lands. For example, creatures of the desert have ways to conserve fluids and keep cool, like larger extremities and needing less water\nto survive. I bet that these started out as, a beast needed slightly less water to survive, and it survived, with its water consuming peers dying of thirst. Eventually the trait would become prominent. We have not yet discovered how these changes come-\nabout, but we know they exist. Given enough time, a beast will become specially accustomed to its land, eventually thriving in its habitat. Life will prevail and overcome obstacles through Natural Manipulation.\nThe Theory of Dominance:\nWith each generation traits are passed down from parent to offspring. It seems that some traits mask other traits. The red petals of flowers are more dominant than white. Yet in the next generation,\nthe plants were red and white. It seems the trait was not destroyed, yet hidden away. Such stands the theory of specific traits being dominant over other traits.\n\n-Xanthur Altraza\nPlant Luminescense Theory:\n\nAfter planting flower cultures and observing their growth, I noticed a strange phenomenon. When I first planted the flowers, some were planted, accidentally, on a hump in the dirt, making them face more horizontally then\nverically, like the others. However, after three more days of observations I noticed that these plants has started to tilt. They eventually, throughout another week of my spectating them, aligned themselves with the original vertical plants, making now\nboth groups face vertically, albeit one group's bases are planted horizontally. I concluded from this discovery that plants require something from the Sun, (Through Artificial Manipulation they achieved this characteristic/ability, since a plant which is\nable to tilt itself towards its source of nourishment, the sun as I concluded, would be more efficient than one which could not, making it more likely to thrive and prosper, thus through nature the plant has been manipulated so as now the whole species\nshares this ability), This something required by the plants could either be the sun's warmth or the light it emits. So as to test this, I created a new experiment. I planted a few flowers under the shadow of a tree, thus making them not at all exposed to\nsun's light.  I planted a few more flowers next to the trees shadow, where it was exposed to light. After two weeks, the leaves of the plants, under the tree, began to shrivel and yellow. After about another week, the plants completely died. On the other\nhand, the plants exposed to light were green and healthy, prospering. After several retrials of this test, I can safely say that plants in fact, do require light to survive, as well, plants have developed a method of adjusting themselves so as to be\nexposed to light, this through Artificial Manipulation.\n\n- Sil Iyat\nWhales\nThis may be something different from the rest in this journal, but I believe it is necessary. I will observe the habits of whalers. I can see what can drive a beast to threatening status.", ""),
        StaticBook("Birthday Card", "The Rat Grin Raiders", "[!]A hastily signed birthday card would be held in your hands, ripped at the seams and stained with blood and urine [!]\n\"Happy Birthday Dawson! \n\nFifty years gone by in a flash and now it's time for you to say good bye. We've arranged for your retirement for a very long time and I'm afraid you have no say in the matter.\n\nCaptain \"Jack 'The Rat' Graeme\" has been chosen as-\nyour succesory and we know, you hated him for the last 3 years he's been on this ship but once you get to know him, he's not that bad of a guy! He even bought us drinks with your pension money!\n\nWell, anyways, happy birthday Dawson and have fun on the-\ndesert islands for us!\n\nP.S I've heard you'll be living with some of the tiny folk, finally home hm?\n\n\n[!]Below would be signed\nan assortment of twenty signatures in a variety of\nwriting ability.", ""),
        StaticBook("Black Cactus", "Cuyler", "Black Cactus\n\nCactus Green (Dye)\nFern\nInk Sac\nCoal", ""),
        StaticBook("Black Sun V. I", "Wretched", "-- The Black Sun -- \n --    Volume I     --\n\nThe radiance of shrouds born upon the Sunless Day, 12th of the Amber Cold, 1355. The day of the great Cataclysm, the birth of the loving Abyss.\n\nWalk among the ashes\nof the lost light and be humbled, for now it is nurtured by the dark, and in the dark it thrives as an entity of solace.\n\nKneel to the vast nothing and allow its acursed gaze into the soul, to snuff stray glimmers of a world less absolute.\nSing a song of melodies, utter a prayer of sanctity, for our souls belong to the Abyss, and the Abyss becomes all we know.\n\nRadiant is the Black Sun.", ""),
        StaticBook("Black Sun V. II", "Wretched", "-- The Black Sun --\n--    Volume II    --\n\nOur dark is tamed by a master of of the immolating flame. The known Mordring. Wings of bone shield us. Breath of dark heals us. Gaze of malice keeps us.\n\nIn his wake, our march is\neternal, our days are sleepless and our souls are renewed. We bathe in her magnificent shadow and we call it home.\n\nThe love of a father keeps this place in eldritch harmony, order amongst the unliving, peace to the tormented.\nHe brings us purpose and nourishment, a faith in the world far from the touch of the cruel Sun and its armies of damnation.\n\nRadiant is the Black Sun.", ""),
        StaticBook("Black Sun V. III", "Wretched", "--  The Black Sun  --\n--     Volume III    --\n\nThe wretched prowler, the guardian of the Abyss, it was named 'Satar'. The Drake does own a hunger that is indeed ravenous, but fear not for it is obediant to its father.\nNone bound to the Sunless Sanctum should fear its hateful wrath, for a creature of darkness knows of family, but those outside of these ethereal bonds would learn to gaze upon it and despair.\n\nThe Abyss will keep it, even after death\nSatar will find sanctuary here, to reform time and time again for as long as it dwells within the great expanse of pitch that is the Abyss.\n\nIts call is one of voice and stone, an obelisk of its homeward binding, to summon it forth\nin service and duty of protection, and the words that bind it do follow:\n\n\"Baduzg-dag hiishtstaaz. Su-burznurzum Satar.\"\n\nRadiant is the Black Sun.", ""),
        StaticBook("Black Sun V. IV", "Wretched", "--  The Black Sun  --\n--     Volume IV    --\n\nOur Sanctum is entrenched in a blanket of dark, sustained by radiant beacons of Mordring's power.\n\nHere our sanctum's power and peace is contained and\nsustained. What exists beyond these walls, we do not know, but souls claim to hear dark whispers through the mist, and distant roars. Truly a sanctuary for all manner of horror.\n\nThe Drake Satar roams it when not called upon to the Sanctuary, one can\nonly begin to picture the things those black eyes have laid gaze upon.\n\nBut in our home, they do not tread. Under our serpentine master we are protected, and we are loved.\n\nRadiant is the Black Sun.", ""),
        StaticBook("Black Sun V. V", "Wretched", "--  The Black Sun  --\n--     Volume V     --\n\nMordring's Gate, our door from sanctuary to the harsh bitterness of the world. To pass the threshold is to exist in a state of peace, none may harm another in the awe of the Abyss.\nShould the unwanted come a-lurking in masses undesired, then by the will of the Master the door will be moved, and can be moved any number of times after.\n\nAlas fear not dark-dweller, for Mordring created for us the Black Sun,\na sigil that when clasped tightly will return its holder to the embrace of the loving Sunless Sanctum.\n\nBut to enter the realm of peace, one must have peace in their heart. To escape demise and conflict, the amulet will not\nfunction. Its nature similar to soulstones of the Cloud Temple in this regard.\n\nRadiant is the Black Sun.", ""),
        StaticBook("Blackfoot Plague", "Lelien", "Blackfoot Plague\n\n    by Lyuin Avern\n22nd of Grand Havest, 1461\nSymptoms:\n- Coughing\n- Blurred vision\n- Inability to clot blood\n- Internal acid burns\n- Haemorrahage of lungs\n\nThis has been dubbed 'Blackfoot plague'.\nThe Mali of Than’siol seek a cure, these have come in several forms.\nThe latest of which are thanhium pillars which attempt to kill plague particles.\nThe masls are somewhat effective, but not plague-proof.\n1st of Amber Cold, 1461\nIt has been discovered that strands of the plague can latch on to wheat crops, infected them and making ingestion of the infected bread to cause the plague. Furthermore, it has been adivsed and tried to see if this plague can\nnfect other food-stuffs.\nIn better news, Clerics have discovered they are able to rid the plague from its host. Thus creating an efficient method to remove plague from a host. However many Clerics are not immune themselves and thus choose not to involve\nthemselves in such matters.\n\nThe plague is both transmitted through consumption and through ingestion of air and infected foodstuffs.\n20th of Snow's Maiden, 1461\nA cure has been found! Discovered by the Valah withing the Fringe. This is an odd solution made up of several components including milk, carrot, tippen's root and other materials.\nThe filter-masks have proven useful and\nwith the cure having cleansed many of the people of their ailments, it is safe once more for our people.\n‘Blackfoot’ plague cure\n- A single gound carrot\n- A ground carrot of golden complexion\n- A single unit of Tippen’s root.\n- A measure of plague blood extracted from a victim of the plague\n- A single egg (remove the shell)\n- A single bucket of milk (should be fresh)\n- Oddly, a feather plucked from a chicken.\n- Several units of fertilizer", ""),
        StaticBook("Blacksmithing V1", "Lark Steelwall", "Blacksmithing\n         Volume 1\n\n  \n\n            By\n\n      Lark\n           Steelwall\nIntroduction to\n     Blacksmithing\n\nBlacksmithing is the art of using heat and brute force to change the shape, hardness, sharpness, and occasionally the color of metal to one's will.\nThis art takes many years to master, and cannot be learned\neasily. As with other trades, one start off on the lowest rung of the metaphorical ladder of trade work and climbs their way up through hard work and dedication. One does not simply try to forge without any experience. Thankfully, you have this book.\nChapter 1-\nForging 101: Operating the forge.\n\nAssuming you have found a forge suitable to work with, you will require the following things: Gloves to prevent burns on the hands, an apron to keep sparks off your clothing, and if you\nhave long hair, something to tie back the hair to keep it from catching on fire.\nIf you have these clothing materials, next on your list should be tools for the forge, a basic set of tools for the beginner blacksmith should consist of a hammer, a\npair of tongs, a poker to stoke the fire, a chisel to clean up the metal and add engravings and such,\nand billows to get the heat of the forge up. When you have these basic tools you are ready to begin smithing.\nOperating the forge is not quite hard, a fuel source such as wood or coal will work, and the heat can be further brought up through the use of billows or poker, arousing the wood or coal to keep circulation of heat going.\nOnce the heat has reached the desired temperature you can finally begin smithing. Placing an ingot into the furnace with the tongs will allow the ingot to heat up. When the metal has become a bright yellow or red it is malleable and able to be forged into\nthe desired shape or object. When you have hammered out your metal object you should dip it in a water source to quickly cool it off. It is also advised to reheat the metal to strengthen it. This process is known as tempering.\nTo improve the metal even more, one should sharpen it on a grindstone. \n\nIf you wish to learn more about Blacksmithing, look for Volume 2 of this many volumed series.\n\n-Lark", ""),
        StaticBook("Blah Dictionary", "Shreck", "Diz buuk tranzlatez wurds in blah tew kommon, writtun bi Shreck.\n\n-Ug ¦ Hello, Hi, Hail\n-Throm'ka ¦ Formal greeting\n-Yub ¦ Yes\n-Nub ¦ No\n-Gug'ye ¦ Goodbye\n-Lat ¦ You\n-Mi ¦ Me, I\n-Wi ¦ We, Us\n-Hi ¦ He\n-Rulg ¦ Thanks\n-Blah ¦ Talk, Speak, Orchish Language\n-Blah'er ¦ Mouth\n-Peepers ¦ Eyes\n-Skah'er ¦ Male Reproductive Organ\n-Gruk ¦ Think, Know, Understand\n-Dabu ¦ Yes, My Pleasure\n-Bubhosh ¦ Great, Big\n-Nubhosh ¦ Bad, Small\n-Snaga ¦ Slave\n-Buub ¦ Pig\n-Pushdug ¦ Stinky\n-Glob ¦ Fool, Shit, Poop\n-Klomp ¦ Fight, Attack\n-Flat ¦ Dead, Kill\n-Blarg ¦ Home\n-Brudda ¦ War Uzg Orc\n-Stout ¦ Dwarf\n-Twiggeh, Treehugger ¦ elf\n-Darkie ¦ Farfolk, Dark elf\n-Squeals, Snaaks ¦ Halflings\n-Quickspawn, Breeder, Shara, Pinkii ¦ Human\n-Nuutshara ¦ Ascended\n-Nubded ¦ Undead\n-Howlur ¦ Dog, Wolf\n-Skah ¦ Fuck\n-Agh ¦ And\n-Buurz ¦ Dark\n-Mojo ¦ Magic\n-Bi ¦ By\n-Krimp ¦ Stun, Capture\n-Uzg ¦ World\n-Goi ¦ City\n-Lusk ¦ Axe\n-O'lig ¦ Bow\n-Ligz ¦ Arrow\n-Zult ¦ Sword\n-Stik ¦ Staff\n-Steemiez ¦ Redstone\nNumburz!\n\nAsh ¦ One\nDub ¦ Two\nGakh ¦ Three\nFuth ¦ Four\nH' ¦ Five\nH'ash ¦ Six\nAshety ¦ Ten\nAshty ¦ Eleven\nDubty ¦ Twelve\nDubty ¦ Twenty", ""),
        StaticBook("Blockades", "Jerry_Man", "Mental Defence\n\n\nInformation not for public consumption\nTo begin with you must recognise when an unwelcomed presence has taken residence within your mind. Those who delve in minds know well how to go undetected, so you must recognise the signs. Firstly comes the subtle feeling that you are not alone.\nSuch feelings tend to come in the night, when the candles have worked their way to snuff and the distant sounds of rustling cooperating with the dancing shadows to create ghostly apparitions within your imaginings. That sensitivity to space that rises in\nsituations most troubling in which your skin seems able to feel the open air, bringing with it the confidence that you are indeed alone, and that sleep should no longer evade you. It is such sensitivity to your physical surroundings that arises when your\nthoughts are occupied by more than yourself. Secondly is recognising thoughts that seem unfamiliar to you. One's own mind works in certain patterns that are as unique to them as a language is to a race. Familiarising yourself with the way that you\nthink can prove neccessary in determining the invasive thoughts of others. Not just in moments of cerebral invasion, but also in the morbid agreement with the doubts of others. Such concepts that are outside your own considering are a\nvirus upon your positive imaginings. But such is a digression. Thirdly is the most obvious, the experiencing of visions and the hearing of voices that are not the product of your own consciousness. If the invasive mind has gotten so far as for\nyou to witness such things, it may already be too late to resist them.\nResistance is a purposeful action. At any moment of awareness that your mind may no longer be a place of solitude, one should employ a simple avoidance technique. Preoccupy your thoughts upon one thing. Prepare this thing within your mind during\npersonal meditation so that it can be called upon at a moments notice. If a secondary presence exists within your mind, you should experience their attempts to work around this barrier. Most likely they will attempt purely to distract you so that\nyour purposeful thought slips away, if even for a moment, that they might continue unimpeded.\nYou may attempt to rehearse this simple barrier such that it become impenetrable even to emotional blackmail or physical distraction. But do not expect to keep out all intruders with a simple fence. For they are like the fox that seeks out a hole,\nthat they might have their feast upon the innocent poultry of your thoughts.\nThe Best Defence that one can have is trickery. If you are sure that your thoughts are not solitary, and the other party is indeed working to belittle your wall, you must protect that which is most sacred. Do NOT think upon the thoughts or memories\nthat you old most secretly. Keep them far from your mind, and instead, lead your mind through a series of thoughts that you beleive the other party most wanting to see. If needs be, invent the image that they seek as though you were dreaming.\nFabricate the vision, re-invent the thought. Lead your mind through patterns that are safe, and all the while fein defeat.\n\nThere are some skilled minds in our world that know well how to push the consciousness. If they remain convinced that no foul\nis in action, they may be appeased at their own ability to search through your mind, and release their attachment with your consciousness. Never knowing that your trickery has left you guarded.", "")
    )

    private fun _AXIOS_TAHN_1(): List<StaticBook> = listOf(
        StaticBook("Bloodied Book", "Aila, Druid of the Fox", "[!] The journal was hurriedly written. Almost like a confession, and blood-stained.\n\n...\nI killed them. I didn't mean to, I swear.\n\nIt was him- it. IT.\n\nTethys-.. Bruum. My love. My sweet, sweet Bruum.\n\nOwl- You never listened! I wish. I wish.\n\nIt was it though. Him. That thing. It was my-\n-fault though. All my fault.\n\nOh Aspects hear me plead. It wasn't me, I swear it.\n\nI didn't kill them. It wasn't me. They were family. It couldn't of been me.\n\nBut it was my fault. My hand. I betrayed-\nthem, and for what.\n\nNow I sit here. Cold, lifeless. No afterlife waits for me. I committed taboos. I'm not me anymore. I don't deserve even this.\n\nBut I'll listen next time. Please. I never finished our medallions. Our little-\nimbuements. It's all my fault.\n\nSmash them.\n\nI-\n\n[!] The rest is unfinished.", ""),
        StaticBook("Bloody Journal", "Akami Azara", "Another day, another drink.\nI don't know anymore... What can I do? How can I do this? I miss Krisa... I miss home... My little tent, our small camp fire... I want to return home... I want to be with Krisa again...\nI had the nightmare again... the blood... the hammer.... my mom... dead... on the floor...\n\nStop, stop, stop!\nThe is a pleasant field... \n\nA pleasant day...\n\nI wonder how Krisa is doing...\nOh god I'*blood smear*\n\nThe bea*blood drop* ripped out my *blood stain, claw marks*\n\nKrisa... for*tear drop stains the words* me...", ""),
        StaticBook("Blue", "Athe'lor", "The Kraken\n\nOne stormy sea, under midnight blue.\nSailed a ship, pirate ship,\nfull with pirate crew.\n\nA deafening roar, a sickening crunch,\nWood splinters flew.\nCaptain's face a terror, for he had a hunch.\nA large tentacle, make it's way up the side. \nYo-ho, called the pirates,\nit was the end of their ride.\n\nThen the captain: \"Yo-ho mi harties, the beast be attackin!\"\nAnd the boat began to fell, to the maw of the Kraken.\nBut the captain, wasn't lettin Ol'Bessy go down without fight.\n\"Let's gather our might lads, \nand beat this bloody fright!\"\n\nSo the pirates, gathered weapons and went a'hackin,\nsoon to be felled, by the hands of the Kraken.\nIt opened it's gaping mouth,\nthe boat snapped in two. \n\"Ah crap.\" said the captain.\n\"Ahm threw.\"\n\nThen the captain, as his vision began to blacken,\nfell like the others, to the wrath of the Kraken.\nOriginally written by Salamandra.\n\nRe-written by Athe'lor.", ""),
        StaticBook("Bokolos: A Study", "Nimne", "[!]\n\n   Here, a simple design has been etched upon the page. The image depicts a large, frail-seeming creature, similar to a bird in its avian qualities but different in its proportions.\n-------------------    Bokolos: A study\n   written by\n     Nimne Devione\n-------------------\n\n Bokolos take the shape of thin, avian creatures whom stand on two legs. As creatures of general affability and intellect, they can be the\nideal companion or mount. When faced with one you will likely notice that it does indeed possess wings, which are folded at its sides. Sadly, Bokolos are unable to fly, the only meaningful use for their wings being to express emotion.\nIt is important to consider that Bokolos are herbivores if you are looking to care for one. They uphold this diet throughout their lifespan- from Bok-Boks to adults- and are unlikely to deviate from it. Despite the lack of meat intake, an adult Bokolo\nis strong enough to withstand the weight of a fully armored, adult male, while wearing light armor themselves.\n\n   Besides the general behaviour of these creatures, they are also known for their vividness of color. A Bokolo's color is often\ndetermined by where it lives. For example, a red Bokolo is more likely to come from a hot, desert-like place than a blue Bokolo, since blue Bokolos more often than not hail from areas which are closer to large bodies of water. A Bokolo's personality and\ntemperment are also something which is dictated by their hue.\nAs it happens, Bokolo variants other than purple and magenta are fearful of magic users, and will resist if one attempts to mount them.\nIn conclusion, Bokolos are strange but fascinating creatures. They are often domesticated by members of the Warhawkian Chiefdom for their usefullness in manual labor and battle, and if neither of the latter traits are needed they make pleasant\ncompanions. \n\n [!]\n   \n   The rest of this page is taken up by an etching of what can be inferred as a Bokolo egg, a single crack forming at it's apex.", ""),
        StaticBook("Boogie Volume 2", "The Boogie Man", "The Book of the Boogie Man, written by the Boogie Man, created by the Boogie Man.\n\nCopyright to Boogie Man\n\nIf you find this book, please return. Love you.\n\nVolume 2\nVictim: Dark Elf\n\nThe Dark Elf woman continues to yell at me but I slowly start to remove her eyes to replace them with the big black buttons I made earlier, look beautiful. Spreads fear! Mysterious too.\nVictim: Druid\n\nThe Druid woman, I cursed her with a nightmare curse. She's having a bad time, I made her believe that something keeps hunting her. I think she is about to kill herself. Who knows?\nVictim: Druid 2\n\nWell, joining up with this weirdo made the work boring. He just makes that Druid drink his own blood while I try to have some fun atleast. Atleast I made his wounds worse and a little curse never hurted. Ha what a joke!\nVictim: Druid 3\n\nThat old wood elf Druid, I keep annoying him and I think he always tries to kill himself. I believe he made me his arch nemesis for his entire life. I already won by doing that, now I never leave his mind. c:\nVictim: The Entire Druid Order\n\nAt last, joining the Black Scourge was a great idea. I found that sapling and I place it under their grove and see what happens. Harbingers told me that it eats trees, perfect!\nVictim: Malinor\n\nDestroying the Druids wasn't enough for me. I have that feeling that just doing more amazing tricks like that would give me a blast. I just slam the entire nation of Malinor by destroying their town, lovely!\nWell, it turns out that destroying a forest was a bad idea. I accidentally lost my favorite wool doll and it's now lost in the corrupted mess I caused...\n\nA sad day for my amazing self, sniff sniff.\nVictim: Human\n\nTricking Humans is too easy. I mean you just walk up and they attack you! How dumb is that? This dude just tried to stab me and I somehow managed to lead his stab into himself. Badass Boogie Man is born.\nVictim: Telekinesis Mage\n\nI always wanted to know Telekiness, Nessin...that thing where you make things float and explode. I just tortured this mage until he explained everything I had to know to learn it myself. Too easy for me.\nVictim: Orc\n\nCan somebody believe this? A freaking Orc first tried to stomp me, now he bows down to me! I love it, I forced him to bow down to me and he's two times taller than me and is such a muscular mountain, byeautiful.\nVictim: Dwarf\n\nThis Dwarf is too nice to hurt. But he really trusts me and I just can't ignore this, I have to experiment on him for new curses. I probably made it too far, he's having these disgusting black blood balls on his skin.\nOh shame, the entire Cleric Order wants me dead after they found out that I can curse the mortals. First they thought I was a goof but they never realized that my stupidity is just fake. I just remove this costume for a while, won't hurt.\nI removed the costume and people flirt with me, this is weird. I don't want to flirt with anybody.\n\nAtleast that one guy has made me go interesting. He's very brutal and does disgusting things to his victims, love him already.\nVictim: Elven Mage\n\nThis Mage is so freakin' cute. He has cute glasses and trusts a Scarecrow for some reason. I forced mice with my amazing magic to dance around. He loved it, but then I replaced his eyes with two buttons, spooky.\nInviting this new dark magic was amazing. Now my possibilities are endless! I mean I can curse anybody, but of course a great inventor needs a student and the first one arrived already. Let's see how it turns out.\nFor sake, a Cleric has healed me. It still hurts like nether.\n\nHe healed my scars and, damn book I look freakin' amazing! I'm such an handsome guy! Woah! I love myself, I wish I could kiss the beauty I see in the mirror.\nVictim: Cleric\n\nOh well, he healed me but I still have to pay back because it hurted a bit so I cursed him with a new curse. His skin turns black and it starts to slowly burn from the inside, I wonder how it feels like.\nVictim: Dark Elf Child\n\nI never wanted to hurt children, but they forced me to hurt this child. I turned her into chocolate and they ate her.\n\nI had no idea I would feel this way, I feel...sorry.\nThe latest events of me cursing people made me think. Maybe I should just stop and try to have a life, have a family like all the other people I'm jealous about?\n\nBut I don't know, it's like Boogie Man became it's own being now.\nVictim: Elf\n\nI just made him sit in the chair and talked to him, forced him to tell me stories of his family and his life. I loved to listen to that, I only tested a curse where he's growing hair all over his skin.\nThe other dark spook folks don't want me in their circle. It's like they don't want me cursing them. Well looks like even the spook people are scared of the Boogie Man, that's awesome. I don't have enemies, only the normal folk of course.\nI started to switch from costume and my beautiful self from time to time, maybe living normally and meeting people without cursing or hurting them might give me advantages next time...you know book? You don't know, you are just a book.\nOkay, Okay. Somebody kissed me. That was an odd feeling, I mean what the heck?\n\nI never felt so weird before, I feel weirder than Boogie Man really is, gross.\n\nBut it was fun.\nSometimes wish you were talking back to me, I'm just writing into you. But I feel like I just want somebody to talk to. I feel so lonely, nobody ever wants to hang out with Boogie, even the spooks are scared by him. Atleast my real self has 'friends'.", ""),
        StaticBook("Book of Alchemy", "Hamilton Huntley", "The book of alchemy\n\n1) Botany and gathering \n\n2) recipes\n1) Fire symboles:\n-Crmson Vase \nfound in: woodland's and plains (( Blocks: Grass)\n\n-Drake's tail\nfound in : Savanah\n((Shrub))\n\n-Dwarf's Pumpkin\nfound in : Swamps\n(( Block: Grass))\n-Blood Lotus:\nfound in mostly desserts and sometimes savanah\n((Blocks: Grass /Shrubs))\n\nFlamtongue root\nfound in : woodland's /Plains\n((blocks : grass)\nWater Symboles\n\nMandragora\nfound in : swamps\n(blocks Lily pad's)\n\nSerpent's Stalk\nfound in : wood lands\n((blocks : sugar canes))\nFrost Vine\nfound in: Snowey regions, Mountains\n((Vines))\n\nBlissfoils\nfound in: Woodland's/Plains\n((Blue orchard))\n\nAthin\nfound in: Snowey ice lands\n((Blocks: Ice ))\nEarth Symboles\n\nTippen's Roots\nfound in: Woodlands's\n/Plains\n((Grass))\n\nAlabaster leaf\nfound in: Woodland's/plains\n((grass blocks))\nSaffvil\nfound in : Swamps\n((grass))\n\nClutcher's Straw\nfound in : Savanah /Desserts\n((Shrubs))\n\nMetzli's Tangle\nfound in : Jungles\n((Grass or leaves))\nAir Symboles\n\nLarihei's Fingers\nfound in : Spruce forests\n((Grass))\n\nElf's Hair\nfound in : Mountains/snow\n((Vines/grass))\nHalfling's grass\nfound in : Plains\n((Grass))\n\nCrouching feathers\nfound in : woodland's/Plains\n2) Recipes\n\nStoneskin\nMandragora\nSerpents stalks\nDwarf pumkin\nDrakes's tail\nFlame tongue\nCrouching feather\nAlabaster leaf\nClutcher's straw\nMetzils tangle\nalabaster leaf\nAlchemist Fire\n\nMandragora\nserpents stalk\ndwarf Pumkin\nDrake's tail\nflametongue\ncrimson vase\nGreater Healing\n\nAthin\nFrost vine\nCrouching feather\nFrost Oil\nSerpents stalk\nAthin\nFrost Vine\nCrouching feather\nElf's hair\nTippen\nMinor healing:\n-Tippen\n\nChill Blain:\n-Athin\n-Frost Vine\n\nGreater chill blain\n-Athin\nFrost Vine\ncrouching feathers\n\nWinters blood: Athin -Serpent stalks\nSmoke Wispers\n\nBlood lotus\nDrakes tail\nlaehlin fingers\ncrouching feather\nBoggy conco