        StaticBook("Butterflies.", "The Scribe.", "The Progress of the Lives of Butterflies.\n\n\nThe majority of Butterflies live their full life of four months. These four months are divided into three stages, where the most prominent and well known stage is the last one.\nStage One; Pupae to Larvae. \n\nWhen butterflies are birthed, they are not birthed as creatures of the spring air, flapping their iridescent wings. Instead, they are born as maggots, or 'pupae'. In this state\nthe butterfly has no natural defenses. It grows slowly as it consumes in small amounts the foliage around its body. As it continues to grow, the pupae slowly becomes a caterpillar. This stage lasts a month. During the caterpillar's time\nas well, a caterpillar, it consumes as much food as it can find.\nThis is in preparation for its next stage of life.\nStage Two; Caterpillar to Crysallis.\n\nThis is the beginning of the end for our friend the caterpillar. The caterpillar stocks up on food by devouring ravenously a multitude of plants and leaves. After doing so, the caterpillar changes\nroles from tree-top destroyer, to spider-like home spinner. The caterpillar secrets a thick strand of webbing, and wraps its body from tip to end.\nFrom here, the wrapping hardens, and the caterpillar prepares itself for the\njourney ahead. This stage lasts two weeks.\nStage Three; Crysallis to Butterfly, and the time after.\n\nInside the crysallis, the caterpillar's anatomy wildly changes. It becomes shortened, and wings develop. The butterfly emerges from the crysallis two weeks\nafter its formation. Here, the butterfly spends some time preparing its wings for flight. The butterfly will live on its own for up to two more months, harvesting what it can gather from flowers using an elongated probiscus.\nThe butterfly will lay its own larvae during a migration to either the north or the south. The cycle begins again, with the formation of new caterpillars marked by the death of the old butterflies.\n*a detailed description of butterfly anatomy lies here*\n\n*a drawing labels and guides the reader through the visual steps of growth*\n~penned; The Scribe.", ""),
        StaticBook("Calling", "Atheria Smallburrow", "=======Calling=======  Atheria Smallburrow\n\nThe towering great pines,\nWhistle in the wind,\nThe crys of living timber,\nAs they are gruesomely de-limbed\n\n\n===================\n===================Nature is abused,\nDoes not have a voice to use,\nIt is cut and torn,\nChopped and worn,\nYet only the druids,\nSit and mourn\n\n\n\n\n===================\n===================Tress are not re-planted,\nAnimal carcasses left rancid.\nIt is a time for change,\nand no accpetions granted.\n\n\n\n\n===================\n===================Forests will be  mended,\nAs the aspects have always intended,\nNurse it back to health,\nAnd gain our hoarded wealth.\n\n\n\n===================\n===================Although there is negative in nature there is also good,\nFrom the wintery warm woods, \nTo the colourful coastal cliffs,\nNever forget...\nas memory always insists.\n\n===================\n===================Bellowing beats of the bountiful boulder,\nattached to mountains,\nshoulder by shoulder.\n\nThey stand themselves high,\nReaching for the sky,\nAll thourgh the day when the end comes nigh.\n===================\n===================\n\nAnd as the sun makes its debut,\nFore the grass alines with dew,\nYou hear the roaring cries of the Druids..\n\nAspects Guide You.\n\n\n===================", ""),
        StaticBook("Camp Report", "Ka'Rian", "Report:\n\nMost of the trees are on fire.\n\nSmall skirmishes with Orcs fighting against Orenians happening here and there.\n\nOrenians are chasing down anyone who looks like the enemy.\nUn-warrented attacks from the Orenians make it difficult to scout deeper within the camp.\n\n            [!]\nBlood seems to smudge the lower part of the             page.\n            [!]\nInjured due to sudden surprise attack. Managed to run away from heavily armored assailant.\n\nFurther scouting is not possible.\n\n-Ka'Rian", ""),
        StaticBook("Captain's Log #1", "Finalhazard", "Captain's Log:\n\nAlas! Our galleon ran into a mighty storm that pushed us into some rocks, forcin' us t' abandon the 'Esmeralda' and take residence upon this here island. According to my first mate, we be not thee only ones here.\nMy first mate has reported that thee trees and bushes be always shufflin' about. I have reason to believe it's just thee wind. None of these islands be charted, meaning that no one else has visited them.\nDay 2: What I had previously said 'bout thee island havin' no inhabitants be false. 'tis land his home t' many tribal people. Many o' them have magical abilities.  Some o' them, be knowin' o' thee void's existence while others proclaim that\nthee gods bestow them thee abilities t' cast flames from their hands.\nDay Unknown:\n\nChapter 1:\n\nThee culture o' each tribe be extremely difference from thee next. Many o' them, if not a vast majority o' them hate each other as many o' them be at war with one another.\nSeein' as how our galleon has been completely destroyed, me men and I have decided t' try t' communicate with thee tribals in order t' figure out how t' survive here on thee isles they call 'Vailor'.\"\nTh' Ral'skas, th' Blind Bandits (who be all, actually blind one way or another), th' 'Kraskls, 'n th' Leafroots, among hundreds 'o others be all tribes within Vailor.\nSome 'o be here fer only a dozen or so years, while others have be here fer hundreds 'o years, or so they claim.\nMe First matey, Logan Proudwell, who be in his only in his early thirties has told me that th' crew be plannin' a mutiny. They feel me leadership isn't whar it be 'n that th' natives gunna murder them in their sliumber.\nUnfortunately, 'tis means that I must make a decision. As th' cap'n I decided that 'tis best if th' crew 'n I part ways. them that wish to help be rebuild th' Lusty Rose gunna stay wit' me, while th' others gunna have to find their own way,\nor join up wit' th' tribes.\nChapter 2:\n\n 'tis plan worked well, as I met wit' many 'o th' chieftains. They decided which 'o me former-crew 'n chose whom would fit in best wit' each tribe.  I then sent me own First matey, Logan to join th' Leafroots in order\nto act as a spy. ye spy wit' ye eye, th' Leafroots be currently th' strongest tribe.  They wield no magic, 'n they be also th' smallest in numbers. But they be th' eldest, which provides them wit' th' most wisdom, 'n wisdom be everythin' in their culture.\nChapter 4:\n\nConstruction on our newest ship, th' 'Lusty Rose II' has begun. 'tis be a year since th' crew split, 'n I haven't heard word from Logan, which leads me to believe that he's either in Davy Jones' treasure chest, or successful in his mission.\nChapter 5:\n\nSeven years later later 'n th' beautiful 'Lusty Rose II' can finally drop her sails. She's a fine vessel, much better than her predecessor, meanin' she'll brin' us back to th' cove in less than a a year.\nChapter 6: Departure\n\nTh' sun has just set 'n bin finally heart back from me first matey, Logan. He has befriended th' youngest Leafroot, a dark-skinned knife-eared fella' by th' moniker 'o Ri'va.\nIt hadn't be brought to me attention that 'tis whole the hour their true family-moniker was T'sagari,  'n that Leafroot was th' common-moniker given to them by other common-speakin' people that landed on Vailor.\nSo, Ri'vi T'sagari be his true title. Movin' on, at th' moment Ri'va be tied up 'n gunna be our trophy that we'll brin' home back to th' cove.  Seein' as how his family expects him to be off on a pilgrimage, they won't expect him to disappear.\nye spy wit' ye eye, every T'sagari leaves home to be off on a pilgrimage in order to discover their 'bond wit' nature', or somethin' to that notion. 'tis a comin' 'o age ceremony. They don't come back fer hundreds 'o years, if at all.\nLogan was goin' to take his sister, but th' females don't be off on pilgrimages like their male-counterparts.\nFinal Notes:\n\nIn case the hour takes me mind away, bin decided to keep a second cap'n's log in 'tis ship as a reminder that me treasure be still buried in 'tis island.\nRemember, ye don't trust ye own crew mates so ye hid it within a second journal. Chances be, th' savage animals (th' tribals) have that journal.", ""),
        StaticBook("Carver of Fate", "Leo O. Aureon", "The mighty obliterator of the soil carves out the lands of old.\nWith its rapids of destruction it fashion's new worlds.\nThe pneuma models grace, yet brutality. \nLife yet death.\nIt is a contradiction unto itself.\nIts vigor is unmatched by any other.\nIt is the creator and destroyer of Flora and Fauna.\nWhat is this vivacious forces that shows no forbearance,\nbut the one who models the beauty of annihilation?\nTis it is the great and mighty river \nthat can shape continents and fate itself.", ""),
        StaticBook("CASE #006 BAIL", "Arthur Amador IV", "-------------------JOHANNESBURG\nCAPITAL\nPOLICE.\nRECORDED BAIL.\n-------------------BOTH CRIMINALS FROM CASE FILE #006 BAILED UNDER A. AMADOR IV FOR FOUR-HUNDRED MINA TOTAL.\n-------------------", ""),
        StaticBook("Case: Garman", "Jester", "Case: Garman Assault.\n\nRecording Officer- Jester.\n\nOfficers Involved-\nJester, Talos Harkness, Caesar Kidd, Bradshaw.\n\nPerson Involved-\nKarina Gotthold, Asger II Tiberan, Lion.\nPlace of Incident-\nJohannesburg Town Square.\n\nCrime(s) Committed-\nAssault(?)\n\nNo items missing or stolen.\nDescription of Suspect-\nDark brown hair, Male, in his 30's.\n\nShort summary of Incident-\nKarina and Garman were having a heated argument in the square, after a while it escalated. An elf known as Lion interrupted by punching Garman in\nthe face. From there guards arrived on the scene and took control of the situation. Lion was cuffed and taken to the palace to be let go, and Garman was arrested but later found innocent of all charges.", ""),
        StaticBook("Case: Steven", "Jester", "Recording Officer-\nJester\n\nOfficers Involved-\nJester, Bradshaw, Brutus Norrington, Talos Harkness.\n\nPersons Involved-\nSteven, supposedly Asger II Tiberan.\nPlace of Incident-\nJohannesburg Town Square.\n\nCrime(s) Committed-\nNone, really. No offenses were broken.\n\nItems Stolen/ Missing-\nNone.\n\nSuspect Name-\nSteven.\nSuspect Description-\nWood elf, age unknown, Male, light body type and scronny, wears a green jacket and brown pants, has glasses, brown hair, roughly 6'0\".\n\nSuspect Demographics-\nHaria.\nSteven was called a Dreadlander for his Harian descent. Accusation made by Brutus Norrington. While other people joined in on this allegation Steven denied any ties to being a Dreadlander. Situation elevated when a kid (supposedly) Asger II Tiberan\nunsheathe his sword and attempt to swing at Steven. The crowd was shooed off and Steven was arrested. Though since no laws were broken I saw it fit to let him go with a warning.", ""),
        StaticBook("CAT", "Sandk1ng", "[!] A poor drawing of a fox is on the book. It's horrid and you question if it's a fox, a wolf or a dog. But in the depth, you see it's a fox. It was meant to be a cheerful drawing, but the lack of colours makes it look unintentionally macabre.\n[!] The eyes of the fox are blackened as it's legs are huge as set by the size of the coal.\n\nThe word CAT is by it's side. If you manage to inspect further, you see some sort of nail atop it's head.\n\nCAT WITH A HAT.\n[!] A second drawing of a fox. It's similiar, albeit the shades of the eye sockets differ from eachother. It has an open mouth that you can somewhat distinguish open agape with a scratch infront of it, which supposedly represents the sound of the fox.\nCAT\n\nCAT WITH A HAT.\n[!] A third drawing of a fox is now here. It seems to be fatter and more macabre as it lacks eyes and there's the thin nail.\n\nFAT CAT WITH A HAT.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ceru I", "March Ash", "It is visceral. I smell the dry earth, the rind of the roots, the bitter air of tangled moss. The shade is cool. But then I exhale, and I am pulled back. I think I would be just as happy were I born a tidal wave or a breeze.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ceru II", "March Ash", "The ashes fall like snowflakes. I taste its sludge on my tongue. Sulfur on my lips. In this wound of the world I feel more alive than in any other place. Beneath my feet beats the pounding pulse of the planet.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ceru III", "March Ash", "On the mountaintop, the stone beneath my feet, I see kilometers of frozen wastes all around me. The wind bites at my skin. The cold helps me to concentrate on my mission. To change the descendants, or destroy them utterly. It is harsh.\nBut, they have the choice to die, and that is mercy.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ceru IV", "March Ash", "The serenity of ice. The air is exceptionally clear here. The sky is very beautiful. They told me, once, that nature is the true source of beauty. All that we try to make is an imperfect clay mold. Perhaps they were right.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ceru IX", "March Ash", "In salt and ice eternal.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ceru V", "March Ash", "The smell of the sea, like brine, seaweed sex, and phytoplankton. It reminds me of salt. Soon, Axios will be washed away to nothing, like the rocks turned to sand by the ocean waves. Unfortunately, its death will not be as beautiful.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ceru VII", "March Ash", "Taken by the hunt, everything else fades away. We fail to listen. Not to other people, but to the World. Here, in the black, damp, heat -- nature's voice comes in its purest form. Nothing is hidden. It is naked. It is as easy as fucking.\nIt whispers to me so quietly: kill them all.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ceru VIII", "March Ash", "Even at the top of the world, my sight from these two eyes only goes on until the horizon. But, my sight from my thousand eyes, that seems to go on forever.", ""),
        StaticBook("cEwk", "Harrrison", "m I    n AM    e\n   i   Z \n              c EW k", ""),
        StaticBook("cEwK", "HI3_", "M i     n  aM  e\n         i  Z\n                  cE w k.", ""),
        StaticBook("CH Handbook", "Saithor", "Introduction\n-------------------The Crimson Hearts are a guild of Spellswords, Sellswords, Mages, and Scholars all alike, all seeking the same goal, knowledge, power, wealth, and fame.\nThe Hearts of this guild are brothers and sisters, bound by oath.\nPaths\n-------------------The Crimson Hearts are divided into three categories. Knights, Mages, and Mechanists. No matter what path you pick, your brothers and sisters will protect you. And no matter what they pick, you will too.\nPeople of Honor\n-------------------Sonoren Klaren: He is the Ace of Hearts, our leader\nTalimeracahe: He is The Red Joker, second in command\nEdwyn Lynderly: He is the maker of the Crimson Hearth, the guild hall of the Crimson Hearts.\nTrainers o' the Paths\n-------------------Olympus: Trainer of the sword\nLelien: Trainer of the magic\nVirgo: Trainer of the Mechanists\nSaithor: Trainer of the bow and of the Realm\nRules\n-------------------1) Ye will protect your brothers and sisters\n2) You will obey all orders\n3) Knights will remain loyal\n4) Mages will heed to heal\n5) Mechanists will procede to prosper\nPath o' Knight\n-------------------The path of the Knight consists of the noble warriors of the Heart. They are the men and women who seek to be armed with a sword, those who know how to use one, and those who wish to know. They are loyal to the Hearts\nPath o' Mage\n-------------------The path of the Mage consists of the arcanic people of the Hearts. They are the men and women of the Hearts who seek the arts of magic. They heed to heal us, and will continue to do so.\nPath o' Mechanist\n-------------------The path of the Mechanist consists of the artisans and merchants of the Hearts. They are the men and women of the Hearts who seek the most money and fame they can get. They will procede to prosper.", ""),
        StaticBook("Chapters Of Life", "Corryn Stormtaker", "~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n \n[It only gets tougher]\n\n\n\nWritten by Corryn Stormtaker,\n\n\n\n\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nChapter one, \n\nWhen you first open your eyes to your new life, you are greeted with a bright beam of light. This is the start of a story, your life story and although it may seem easy at first. It gets tougher, a whole lot tougher.\nWhen I was a boy, my siblings and i was subjected to torture from our father. Countless days of pain and suffering, but the one thing that we had to push ourselves through the pain, was each other. We each came out of the dark days differently, adapting\nif you wish. My younger brother and sister, who are twins, ended up with split personalities. At first i didnt understand, but not i realise it was to make it easier for them. I dont remember much, its all a blur really however every night i sleep. . . I\nre-live the darkest of days. In order to get by, I ended up with a drinking habit to stop myself from sleeping. During my times being alone in my room, i paint. I paint the past, the future, and anything that causes an important emotion.\nChapter two,\n\nI spend most of my days in my room, locked away from the outside world. Im scared, no, im terrified of what can happen to me. I cant speak in a loud manner without my voice straining agaisnt my throat. So I remain quiet. . . Just stay quiet.\nAs i mentioned at the start, it may seem easy at first, but it gets toughe. But what if it starts of tough? Does it get easier?\n\nThe answer to that is simple. It will only get easier by the path you choose.\nAs time progressed, I became more confident with my voice and my confidence overall. However it was still hard for me to speak to anyone I havent met. \nThrough the hundred and thirty years of my life, I always hoped for it to get better. But I guess I\njust have to wait that little bit longer.\n\nAs of a couple of months ago, I met woman who I call, my only friend. We have things in common and we love to just walk around, even if we dont speak. . . We are still in each others company.\nChapter three,\n\nThe nightmares. . . They now become consistant. Not only in my nights, but in my days. As my mind wonders, it takes me back to a time of pain and suffering. Each and every blink, is a punch to the face, each beat of my heart\nis a kick to the chest. And then suddenly, it stops. I jump in shock as the scenes from my past turn into the present. To see a worried friend and siblings stare at me in confusion. How do I tell them these tings?\n\nI dont want to hurt anyone, or make them\nworry for me. So I just have to refrain from my mind wandering. Keeping my staff spinning is a great way to keep my mind on track.\n\nAs for sleeping, thats something I still cannot do. Not until they stop, or every bad memory just fades. . .\nAs I mentioned, drinking is a great way to forget the pain and suffering. But it isnt a permenant solution, as of just a temporary one. \n\nI heard that hitting you head extremely hard can cause memory loss, however I dont wish to be put through such pain.\nChapter four,\n\nLove is a strange feeling. I have feelings for someone, but someone has feelings for me. I enjoy being with both of these people, however I understand that if it comes to it, choosing one over the other is what I must do.\n[!] The rest of the pages seem to have been ripped out of the book?\n\n\nWhere could they be?", ""),
        StaticBook("Child Crusade", "Walter Marshall", "The Tragedy Of The Childrens Crusade\n\nAn accurate account ofthe massacre at the Silver City gates.\n\nBy Walter Marshall\nUpon the frigid and barren peak of Mount Augustus, a small assemblage of noblemen, soldiers, and guardsmen sit in a circle. Their grimly-set visages dimly illuminated by the moonlight, the men mutter tersely amongst themselves.\nThe first to rise and speak is the Prince Boris Carrion..\nBoris paces back and forth in thought, his downward gaze denoting pensiveness. At last he speaks, an alarming tone in his voice. “The crowned prince, my cousin Roy - where is he?\"\nSer Lothar Horen turns to Boris in response to his frantic query. “Our last report tells us he is encamped outside of Haelun’or, the Silver City. Your cousin has amassed an entourage of boy soldiers, and he has embarked on a children’s crusade.\nSer Baron Corbett VanCleef acts as his guard.” Boris stops in his steps, his eyes narrowing as he glances out towards the glimmering spires of the distant elven holding. “Corbett? A loyal man. But in times such as these, we do not know who we can trust.\nBring me my cousin Ser, bring me my nephew, and should the Baron attempt to stop you, put a dagger through his heart.” Boris then gives a quick glance to Dederick Varodyr, who stands expectantly as he leans on his greatsword. “And you, ser?\nTake my ward with you, it’s about time he met the son of Heinrik.” Ser Lothar gives a quick nod, striding away. Dederick scrambles suit, following after Horen in his brusque pace.\nFrom the edge of the forest, Dederick perches himself on the thick branch of an ancient tree, brushing the leaves to a side to peer down at the bustling camp below. His hawk-like gaze scours the large congregation of nomads,\nglancing down at the children as they dart in and out of the rows of tents. Many of the young boys and girls heft up swords much too big for themselves, as they move to converge on a single lad under the looming shadow of Haelun’or.\nA young boy within the camp, with a bejeweled crown upon his head, swings his oversized sword wildly as he roars loudly. “In the name of the King and holy Godan! Attack!” At the rallying call of their boy leader,\nthe droves of children rush towards the gates of the Silver City with unimposing cries, attempting to lift the gate to no avail.\nDederick, with a look of relief upon his face, clambers down from the tree, joining Lothar at the massive timber base.\n“It’s him! It’s the crown prince Roy!” With an air of mirth, Varodyr begins to jog towards the group of children, Ser Lothar following with an unimpressed grunt as they near the children’s militia.\nAs the mass of youths surround and swarm the steel gate, hanging from the bars and whooping indignantly, Roy Carrion turns to the distant thundering sound of hooves against the cobbled roads. Riding in hard from Vekaro,\nthe encroaching throng of horsemen heave up the crimson banners of the Decterum. Giving a boisterous chuckle at the sight of his father’s army, Roy lifts his sword with a triumphant cry as he bellows towards the gatehouse.\n“Your city is truly in peril now, elves, for Heinrik’s legion has arrived! Fear the men of the Decterum, for your days are suddenly numbered!” As the young prince continues to hurl imprecations at the unyielding gates of the elven city,\na new and alarming sound reaches his ears - the clash of swords accompanied by shrill cries of terror. As Roy shoulders his way past the mass of armored boys at the gates, his eyes widen in despair at the treacherous and cruel sight before him.\nThe soldiers of the Decterum advance on the children in the camp, cutting down the young crusaders mercilessly and callously setting fire to the tents as they go. The youthful and inexperienced boys stand no match for the hardened and pragmatic soldiers,\nand they carve a swath through Roy’s camp as they cleave their way towards the fearfully paralysed children at the gates.\nMeanwhile, the two sent to rescue the crown prince stand similarly frozen in shock at the appalling and insidious massacre. As they watch the sacking of the camp, and the men of the Decterum redden their blades with the blood of the youths,\na deep sense of dread ran over them. Had they failed their prince?\nThe remaining children, who stood at the gates, rapped frantically on the iron bars they were moments ago attempting to pull open. Corbett VanCleef, the steadfast servant of Roy,\nsparred with many members of the Decterum, but as they surged onwards and surrounded him, he was brought to his knees with a series of blows and shackled. Roy, spinning around confusedly amidst the massacre,\nwas hoisted from the ground by a passing uruk and evacuated before the men of the Decterum could kill him.\nMeanwhile, both Lothar and Dederick watch in disarray, at the events unfold before them. Dederick began to rush forth, unsheathing his sword,\nbut Lothar stopped him with gritted teeth - to run into the folly ahead was sure and certain suicide. As the men watched helplessly, the surviving rabble of child crusaders swatted fruitlessly at the gates, begging for mercy.\nBut no mercy did come that day, and at the hands of the Decterum the gates of the Silver City were awash in red.", ""),
        StaticBook("Circuitry", "[Ghost] The Eternal Librarian", "Electrical\n     Circuitry\n\n   by Magna Grimmhall\nIf this book is found anywhere else than the Eternal Library of Lin’evaral, the Enclave of Haelun’or, it is stolen.\n\nBoth buyers and sellers will be punished.\n\nSigned, the Eternal Librarian\nA problem with redstone dust - as explained in ‘Properties of Redstone Dust’ - is the range. The signals can only travel the length of 7% humans, and then the signal becomes too weak. However, you can use a redstone torch at the end and the length\nwill be extended by another 7% human lengths. The problem with this is that the signal will be in the opposite state. To solve this you could put out yet another redstone torch. But instead of having too big torches one after another, the redstone\nrepeater was constructed. It consists of two redstone torches but in a smaller size, to make them less space.\n\nA problem in making bigger circuits was that for some projects you would need to delay the signal. This was also\nthought of, and a delayer has been built into the redstone repeater. To change the timing, the only thing needed is to change the distance between the two redstone torches. By doing so, the signal is forced to move through another line of a delayer. The\nredstone repeater has 4 modes, with the timing from 1 to 4.\n\nA problem in making bigger circuits was that for some projects you would need to delay the signal. This was also thought of, and a delayer has been built into the redstone\nrepeater. To change the timing, the only thing needed is to change the distance between the two redstone torches. By doing so, the signal is forced to move through another line of a delayer. The redstone repeater has 4 modes, with the timing from 1 to 4.\nA final thing was thought of when creating it. If you wanted to delay the signal greatly, then you would have to use several repeaters. Instead of them having to use a big area, the redstone repeater was created to be shielded off from the sides from\nthe sides from other signals. This means that the signal can only be imputed from one side, and on the opposite side the output is located. This means the redstone repeaters can be placed tightly next to each other without affecting the other “lines”\ngoing next to it.\n\n*A picture is shown on how to construct a repeater*\n\nThe redstone repeater is crucial to create circuits, and the advantage is also that you can create things in a much smaller width.", ""),
        StaticBook("Citizen Passport", "Floris de Ruyter", "=-     PASSPORT    -=\n\nIssued by FLORIS DE RUYTER of the Imperial Administration, given to GARMAN, whom is a class C1 Citizen, on the 8th of the SUN'S SMILE, 1586. \n   This passport is legal tender until the 8th of the Sun's Smile, 1596. If found,\nplease return to the\nImperial Administrative\nin Johanessberg.", ""),
        StaticBook("Cleanup Bill", "Pasquale Calabreeni", "Calabreeni Cleanup\n        Crew Bill\n===================*Removing Embers +30\n*Cleaning Ash +40\n*Repairing Wood +50\n*Company Resources +50\n*Sweeping Streets +30\n------------------\nSub Total: 200\n------------------\n*Dangerous Working Conditions +100\n*Work Crew +50\n-------------------\nDiscounts:\n*Homie Hookup -100\n-------------------\nTip:\n+50\n------------------\nTOTAL BILL: \$300\n------------------\nx Pasquale Calabreeni \nx Stephen I", ""),
        StaticBook("Clerical Healing", "[Child] Silus Hightower", "A guide to Creator Clerical healing\n\nby Lady Sarah Hightower.\n\n\nDedicated to my dutiful students.\nAssessment.\n\nThe first step in treating a patient is to assess his or her injuries. Ask yourself the following questions before you attempt to treat the injury.\n\n1 Where is the wound located?\n2 What is the severity of the wound.\n\n3 Am I able to treat this wound.\n\nStart by locating the wound, sometimes you'll have to cut away clothing to properly access it.\n\nThen classify the\nwound using the following scale\n\nI Light cuts and bruises, no severe bleeding.\n\nII Cuts with bleeding, at risk of infection, no internal damage. Burns that leave skin intact.\nIII Broken bones in the limbs. Major burns and arrow wounds in the limbs or ones that did not damage major organs.\n\nIV Broken ribs, Internal injuries, broken skulls arrow and crossbow bolt wounds that pierced major organs.\nV Loss of limb, defects in the lungs or heart.\n\n\nAttempt the find the classification that fits the scale best and then decide if Your clerical abilities are prudent to use, or perhaps the patient can be better treated with\nmundane healing. In the early stages of your clerical career you will often have to combine both Clerical and mundane healing.\nConnecting\n\nThe second step one must take to heal a patient through clerical magic is to connect to the Creator, this must be done through prayer.\n\nYou begin by clearing your mind of all woes\ntry and think of a place or memory that fills you with joy, then you will have to say or think of a prayer, asking the creator to bestow his Holy gifts upon you. for the newer clerics this is an exhausting process, but the more talented can summon\nHoly light in a matter of seconds.\n\nYou must be a devout follower of the creator to use his holy light, one who kills or injures without good cause will not be able to do so.\nGuiding the light\n\nThe next step is to bring the holy light onto the injury, staves may be used although using your hands is most likely the more practical solution. \n\nIf you concentrate enough you will find\nthat the light will obey your commands and goes where you want it, in theory you could heal a patient without using your hands, but this will be severely exhausting and even Class I wounds will prove a challenge to fix for the advanced cleric.\nHealing\n\nWhen you've guided the light to the injury, you may start the healing, this is not done automatically, you must know how the injury works before you are able to heal it. \nFor instance if you cannot set a bone\nproperly, you cannot use the holy light to do it, the results will most likely be unpleasant, so educate yourself in mundane healing before attempting to treat the more difficult wounds. \n\nTo heal the wound you simply imagine how the\nwound mends, think of the procedure and guide the light so that it does thus, you will find that the light will mend the injury you are faced with, granted it is within your abilities to heal it.\nProgressing your abilities.\n\n§ § Clerical magic differs from other schools of magic in one aspect. A cleric can draw on more power than he or she can handle this is fairly common and in light doses harmless\nhowever there are\nside effects\nI Fatigue\nII Light shaking.\nIII Headache.\nIV Light coughing.\nV Danger of falling in an unconscious state.\nVI Coughing up of blood.\nVII Long term weakness, damage to the lungs.\nVIII Death.\nYou will often have to push yourself to stage V or even VI\nto advance your abilities. this will mean you advance faster, but comes at risk of long term weakness, if you treat wounds that are at your level of experience you will also grow\nin power, but you will rarely find wounds that match your experience exactly.\nMindsoothing.\n\nA cleric also has the ability to calm the minds of others, to achieve this you must be in a calm state yourself. If you are not then you will not be able to succeed, however you can calm yourself through a quick prayer\nor a short meditation session.\n§PDistress Scale.\n\nA: Normal state of mind.\n\nB: Light panic, nervous eye movement, soft speech, cautious movement.\n\nC: Total panic, crying, heavy shaking, difficulty speaking.\nD: Catatonic state, generally inable to move or speak, will sit or remain still, as if frozen. Some patients may repeat phrases or motions until treated.\nAs with the healing of wounds, you must first assess the condition of the patient, if there is a physical injury as well you must decide which to treat first. \n\nThen you must clear your mind of woes and connect to the creator.\nThen you must guide the light to either your eyes or your hands. and look at the patient directly, or in the latter case, move your hands to touch his body, then you simply project your own calmness unto the patient.\nLimb regereneration.\n\nIn the final stages of your abilities you will be able to regrow limbs using the creator's blessing, however this is not to be taken lightly and will take a great physical cost and depending on the severity\nmay require several Clerics. However fingers and hands can be regrown over multiple sessions at a lesser physical cost.\n\nYou MUST § do the proper research before attempting this procedure, every vein, bone and muscle must be regrown\nperfectly or the limb will not be of much use, or worse the patient may suffer internal bleeding and die.\n\nIn theory one could regenerate a vital organ such as a lung or liver, but this will leave you at a severe risk of dying.\nNever attempt to regrow a heart or brain, you will most likely die of the side effects before you generate a working heart, the brain is simply impossible.\nI hope that this guide has helped you in understanding Holy magic.\n\nMay you heal many people.\n\n~Sarah Hightower\n\n10th of Sun's Smile\n                  1456", ""),
        StaticBook("Cloud Temple", "Rosso", "The cloud temple is a historical fortress that rest in peace, away from all sign of life in Aegis. It is the primary spot where the king’s of Oren would reside in time of great need, or in severe warfare conditions between an infightable\nfortress. Cloud temple also once was the home of Count Valkmore, whom disappeared several hundred years ago. It was said that Count Valkmore was the original creator of the temple, in hope that Aegis would forgive him for committing an ugly sin.\nCloud Temple\n\nRetold by Leyu’Maehr\nCoppied by Rosso\nVaerHaven", ""),
        StaticBook("Cloud Temple", "Leyu'Maehr", "Cloud Temple\nBy Leyu’Maehr\nThe Cloud Temple is a historical fortress that rest in peace, away from all sign of life in Aegis. It is the primary spot where the king’s or Oren would reside in time of great need, or in severe warfare conditions between an unfightable fortress.\nThe Cloud Temple also once was the home of Count Valkmore, who disappeared several hundred years ago. It was said that Count Valkmore was the original creator of the Temple, in hope that Aegis would forgive him for committing an ugly sin.\n        --------", ""),
        StaticBook("Clue 12", "Niera Acal'elor", "Beneath the sailors great domain. \nHave never been a clue so plain. \nYet you're in for a big surprise. \nFAR beneath the deck is your prize.", ""),
        StaticBook("CMask Guidebook", "[Ghost] The Eternal Librarian", "Anti-Contagion\n  Filtration Mask\n     Guidebook\n\n       by Mirtok\nThank you for accepting your very own anti-contagion filtration mask, through this handbook you will learn all the important functions and procedures for operating and effectively using your mask. By the order of the Hochmeister in hopes to combat the\nrising infectious ailments, every Hanseti citizen is issued their own filtration mask for safety.\nSafety Tips\n1.) Never misplace or lose your mask, though the Hochmeister cares deeply for your safety, he will not be able to give out spare masks to careless people. \n\n2.) Never share your mask, to prevent the spread of the illness\nthe Hochmeister urges all mask users to stay with their own mask no matter the circumstances.\n\n3.) Maintain your mask, keeping your mask in proper order at full upkeep will prevent incidences of break or breaches in your mask's special\nprotective filtration and sealant systems.\n\n4.) Use filters to their fullest, each few years the Hochmeister will distribute new filters for your masks but until then you must ration off what you have, this will not only test your ability to be\nresponsible for your life but to prove you have what it takes to survive in a hazardous world.\nPreparing your Mask\nUpon receiving your mask, it is a good idea to become acquainted with how it works and how to properly use it to fend off infective agents of death.\n\nFirstly, it is a good idea to make sure your filters are in place\nand secure along both sides of the mask.\n\nUnder the eye sockets of the masks should be two metal containers with 3 clip secure locks located on the circumference of each capsule. Inside you can see the several layers of filters and spinning mechanism\nthat make up the filtration system. Do refrain from tinkering with the delicate parts and only manipulate the filters. Once assured that the filters fit snuggly in their respective areas we can make to making sure there are no cracks in the mask. We are\nunsure as to how the infection is spread and therefore it is important to count for all possible biological entries into the body. First examine the two large eye sockets and lenses on the front of the mask. Also can along the main folds and seams of the\nmask to make sure no loose strings or openings are present. Finally, make sure the center piece where each tube leading from the two filter capsules is not loose or emitting a rattling noise when shook. Be sure to be extra careful when checking for\nbreaches as a single hole can mean the difference between life or death.\nReplacing Filters\nTo replace a filter, you must first unlatch the lid to the two filtration capsules. Once the interior is exposed, carefully turn the filter pads until a hard click is heard above the smaller clicking during turning. When heard, the\nthe pads should slightly elevate themselves into a popping motion and then should be ready for removal. Replacement works in the opposite fashion, place the new ones in the direction of the painted arrows and turn when the resistance is felt.\nSeveral clicks should be heard until a final snap indicates its in place. Close the capsule and move to the next one.\nUsing your Mask\nWhen your situation calls for you to use your mask, you must follow a few simple steps to ensure your maximum safety in the face of an infective area. First loosen all of the straps along the back and front of the mask. Then place the\nloose mask over your head and position the eye sockets for your preferred viewing.\n\nWhen ready, slowly tighten each strap until the strapped area feels tight and snug over your head. It is very important to maintain a tight fit but also to keep the mask\nfrom cutting off blood flow to your mask and face as such will prompt discomfort and compel you to adjust the mask. When all straps have been secured, turn the small dial located on the front of your mask where the capsule tubes meet until you hear a\nsmall rush of air., When all these are done, you should have achieved maximum anti-contagion safety.\nBreaching/Cracks\nIn the event of a breach or crack in your mask, it is advised by the Hochmeister to quickly remove yourself from the jeopardizing area and seek cover and solitude from any other contact with others. The Hochmeister then\nurges you to remove the filter pads from your filtration capsules and attempt to apply them over your nose and mouth if no other repair methods are successful on the damaged mask.\nGood luck out there and may Celestia keep this tragedy from our frozen lands.", ""),
        StaticBook("Cobbler and Crow", "Sofetios", "The Cobbler and the Crow\nBy Sofetios\nI was working in the night,\nAs I bent over a shoe,\nI was working very hard,\nTo finish before the morning dew.\n \nI was just about finished,\nWhen what was this I hear?\nA tapping, slight tapping,\nAnd it seemed to be so near.\nI turned to the window,\nAnd what did I see?\nA crow tapping at my glass,\nStaring at me.\n \n“Go away.” I said,\nSternly as I did stand.\n“Don’t you know I have work to do?”\nThough I know it didn’t understand.\nBut the crow kept tapping at the glass,\nAnd I began to get mad,\nThis crow just would not stop,\nNot even a tad.\n\nI turned to my unfinished shoe,\nTo work as long as I could bear,\nBut then I noticed something missing\nThat would stop me from completing the pair.\n \n\nThe golden lace that I needed,\nFor this order to be complete,\nI couldn’t find it anywhere,\nAs the glass the crow did beat.\nI checked my table, checked my pockets,\nAnd then to my surprise,\nThere was a hole in one,\nThat was just the right size.\n\nI would never finish this shoe,\nBy the morning light,\nNow things were dire,\nAnd my situation was quite tight.\n“I must have dropped it,\nOn my way back from the store!”\nBut it was too far I thought,\nAs my confidence tore.\n \nBut then I realized, “What’s this?”\n“Where was the tapping I couldn’t bare?”\nI looked to the window,\nAnd the crow wasn’t there.\nI went to the window,\nAnd what was in its place?\nIt was simple and divine,\nThe golden lace.\n \nI opened the window,\nAnd took it with care,\nBecause of who gave this gift,\nI was certainly aware.\nI went to my table,\nAnd finished the shoe,\nBut then thought of the crow,\nIf I only knew!\n \nI then went to bed,\nWith not much I could say,\nI only did hope,\nThe crow would come back some day.", ""),
        StaticBook("Code of Chivalry", "Jacob Chapel", "Knight's Code of Chivalry\nThe Knight's Code of Chivalry, as revised on the 7th of The Amber Cold, 1470, by Noble Ser Maric II Varodyr, the Winged Knight and scribed by Ser Akal Ipos.\n\nPrinted at 'Books of Oren', Petrus.\nA Knight shall live by honour, for glory, and guard the honour of fellow knights.\n\nHonour The Creator and maintain His Church.\n\nKeep the faith and act in righteousness.\nHe shall serve his liege lord valorously and with conviction.\n\nAnd persevere to the end in any enterprise begun and never turn his back upon an equal foe.\nA Knight shall refrain from the wanton giving of offence and despise pecuniary reward.\n\nGive succour to widows and orphans and regard the honor of women.\nHe shall offer that which is not needed, to those who are needy.\n\nAnd safeguard the helpless and uphold the weak.\nA Knight shall respect those placed in authority but fight for the welfare of all.\n\nAbstain from Injustice, cruelty and deceit.\n\nHe shall be vigilant and show courage, even in the face of evil.\nResolve not with swords what can be with words.\n\nAnd at all times speak the truth, even if faced with death.\nIn their blood the creator’s will shall be written.", ""),
        StaticBook("Cognitism", "oblivionsbane", "<>*<>*<>*<>*<>*<>*<>*<>          Cognitism\n<>*<>*<>*<>*<>*<>*<>*<>\n\nCognitism is a magic that allows one to see their own illusions. As any illusionist knows, this is normally impossible due to the nature of illusionary magics. Normally, an illusion would\nvanish if someone were to realize that it was, in fact, an illusion. Getting around this done through a technique known as the observers eye, and it is no over-estimation to say this is the key to this magic. It is done by separating the mind in two,\nwhere one views the illusion and the other manipulates it. They communicate through a subconscious connection, never truly being separate. This can cause mild to severe mental issues at first, but eventually as the mage progresses these subside or at\nlessen to the point that they aren't noteworthy.\n\nThe ability to see your own illusions through Cognitism creates many uses. I have categorized these uses into three subtypes: Tools, Virtual Representations, and Visual Assistances.\nTools are the simplest of the three. They are anything you create that allows you to perform a specific function. Examples of these would be illusionary meter-sticks, measuring squares, and protractors. These are the simple, beginners tools, however.\nExperienced Cognats are able to create their own tools which perform significantly better, but they are only possible through Cognitism. An example of this is an illusionary bar that can extend and tell you visually the exact height of a certain object.\nThis leads us into our next subtype, Virtual Representations. These are separated into two types, models and overlays. Models are detailed three-dimensional illusions. They can be as large and intricate as a cathedral, and as small and simplistic as a\ntack. One use of models is when designing something. For instance, a blacksmith would be able to plainly view the sword he wants to design and make real time alterations to said design rather than simply using the foggy picture in his head.\nThen we have overlays, which are basically flat, two-dimensional models. These are useful for scribing and creating blueprints or planning out paintings. Anything that would be have to do with work done on a flat surface could be aided using overlays.\nIt is also possible to convert one to another, which makes this particular part of the magic work well with blueprints, since an overlay of a blueprint could be made, then changed into a model.\nFinally, we have the real magical aspect of Cognitism, Visual Assistances. This is where all of the \"legendary\" aspects of Cognitism reside. The most basic use of this subtype is creating numbers and symbols to do mathematical operations visually.\nThis allows one to not have to worry about paper, and it removed the physical lag between writing the next part of an operation down. If done enough, this can get to the point moderate calculations can be done in a mere moment, and advanced ones might\nonly take half a minute or less, depending on the individual. It should be noted that Cognitism does not make one \"smarter\". The person is as smart as they will ever be, but what it does allow is it allows them to do things faster, which is why so many\npeople seem to think it can, in fact, make someone smarter. Visual Assistances also allow someone to, technically, improve their memory. This is done through the storing of Visual Assistances, which can give a Cognat highly detailed photographic memories.\nNow, we come to a part of Cognitism that is indeed considered legendary, Hyper Thought. Hyper thought is achieved through a state of meditation, where a Cognat speeds up their thinking using Cognitism in an attempt to discover a solution or revelation\nover a problem. There is not much more I can say about it, other than it can occasionally leave one mentally fried, with a severe migraine, inability to organize thoughts, and loss of some motor capabilities.\n\nIt also cannot be used in a fight. It takes a\ngood toll on your concentration to even use Cognitism due to the spectators mind, and any extreme stresses would interrupt the fragile technique. \n\nOverall, if you are a tradesman or simply someone wishing to learn a magic that will enhance your ability\nto think and work rather than destroy or manipulate, I would say Cognitism is right for you.\n\n- - - - - - - - - - - \n\nWritten by the master Cognitism mage, Mark Lander\n\n- - - - - - - - - - -", ""),
        StaticBook("Combat Manual", "Temp Thersist", "Combat     Basics\n\n         The 3 Stances\n\nHigh - Form is leaned in, Knees bent. Arms arced in pre-wind-up. Blade is to be pointed skyward. Referred to as the \"Counter,\" stance. Used to counter-act Mid-guard and stanceless men.\nMid-Guard - Form is relaxed, blade pommel parallel to the user's waistline. Knees bent and arms relax. Referred to as the \"Assaulting,\" stance. Attacks vary on situation, be it arc or thrust. Counters Low stance and untrained fodder.\nLow - Form is lowered, knees bent and body leaned in. The arms are left in a half-wind-up with the blade parallel to the flooring. Referred to as the \"Wounding,\" stance. Counters High Guard, spearsmaan and isn't typically used to kill a target.\nMovements\n\n\nWhen in combat, keep your foe in direct line of sight. Movements are circular in nature, there are to be no steps forward or backward, instead, side-step in or out.\nWhen Assaulting - Nature may say rush at the target head-on. Instead, aim to the target's left or right with movement. Aim to strike the target and take place on either flank or rear of the target. Once flanked, strike either the neck or lower back.\nWhen Countering - Side-step, parry, or retaliate. Know the range of the opponent's weapon. IF your range is superior, retaliate with a side-step and aim to cleave limb or behead the enemy. If your range is lesser, parry the blow of the enemy and close\nWhen Countering cont... \n\nthe gap, making an effort to disarm or hinder.\nCrossbow Usage\n\nThe following is a petty guide for loading and firing a crossbow.\n\nSet weapon, if required. Simply setting it grip-first onto the ground.\n\nDraw back string, with device or hand.\nMove foot from grip.\n\nLift weapon and load with bolt/munition.\n\nShoulder weapon and aim.\n\nFire.\n\nRepeat as needed.\n\nNote loading device.\nCreated for usage by the Caerngard of Kaedrin. \n\n - Temp Thersist of Kaedrin.", ""),
        StaticBook("Combustion Magic", "Kypris'dionne", "Combustion Magic!\nFire Evocation Subtype.\n\nCombustion magic is the art of expanding your flame once it is thrown, causing a sort of 'explosion' of sense. To do this it is expected you have practiced the magic to the point where you'd be ready to teach\nanother student. This is because to do this requires full control of your evoked flame at all times, specifically after it's left your hand. Now the first step obviously is to connect to the void and evoke your flame. From there you are to produce more\nand more energy and concentration into the flame, but do not increase its size. ((This usually takes about 3 emotes to connect, create the flame, and charge.)) Then you throw the flame towards your target and use that stored energy ((the charge)) to\nexpand the flame outwards, spreading out the energy you charged into your attack. This will spread the flame and heat outwards making the flame less hot over all but now increased in size. This isn't nessacarily a subtype but more or less a different\nstrategy from a Fire Evocationist, Kypris'dionne Thylsealaes and is practiced by all of her students. \n\n((This is labeled as a subtype simply because you need to be tier 5 to do it, but it isn't really? Idk.))\nTL;DR\n\nYou charge fire evocation for one emote longer and throw it, expand the flame in all directions which lowers the heat but increases radius of damage.\nRed Lines:\n\n-Takes at least 3 emotes to cast.\n-Can only be done once per fight.\n-Requires tier 5.\n-If done with blue fire you'd roll to pass out.\n-Reduces heat\n-Increases radius", ""),
        StaticBook("Comming of age", "High Consul Samsung II Irongrinder", "A comming of age story.\n-------------------------------\n\nTwas a gloomy day within the darkening halls of Dragur, a sojourn to learn with an elf, another elf, and surprisingly yet another elf. Such was uncommon company for our hero, for to converse with\nsuch sizeable beings, as one so short himself was rather intimidating, a slight on his stone-born honour. Yet nontheless they conversed, on topics taboo to those of the everyday. Untill much to his supprise, events took a turn for the worse, a lack of\nappreciation for one's particular choice of rhetoric, a face turning from joy to anger, and he was taken down. The remaining two turned to our chosen, displeased with his lack of empathy for their ways, one melded into shadow, and we saw naught but night\nfor many an unnaturally long hour. And so we walked, out of such a scholarly place, far through the woodlands, accross raging rivers and grassy plains, past sleeping elk and ignorant hunters. Stopping beside a rather naturally appealing area, a small\nspring and waterfall tucked beside a gargantuan mountain within a thick fir forest. The socially inept elf was thrown aside, and all eyes turned upon our hero, laying unaware upon the ground. The shadow walked forth, and planted life within him, delving\ninto a stygian pool, arising\nfree, reborn. Such is the sad. . . sad. . .is such a poor choice of wording, for to call something poor merely because it is commonplace within society is a farce itself, for such is subjective, always a choice! One must\nnever limit their opinion based upon what is deemed natural! For the unnatural is a learning expierence itself, indubitably so. So let us return to our tale, and resume where we have left off. . .Our hero awoke a great deal of time later, days after the\neternal darkness had left the world, within a cell much like the ones within your own home's dungeon, beside him the socially inept elf, bloodied, and asleep. Our father was present, watching over us with an ever-loving gaze, he would ensure our rebirth\nexisted without interferance, a plesant birth, unlike those of years past, we would find ourselves not tormented, but knowing of our gift, not agressive to our kin, but warm, a true family.", ""),
