        StaticBook("Crazy Notes", "Calliope_", "kjdsfal\ndfkdlasfkldsa\ncdassfad\ncxzcda\ngbvsdvfdsgsfds\ns\nvfsdvfdsvf\n\n*Blood stains are throughout the pages, but the source is unclear.*\nI feel like I've been hiding for so long. What is happening to me? Why can't I control my thoughts? The scriptures should help. Why aren't they helping?\n\ndfsafdsafd\nfdsafdsa\nfdasfdsfdasfdas\ndsafdsa\ndfsafds\nafdsfdfdsa\nfdfafdsf\nsdafdfafdsafda\ndasfdsafdaf\ndafdsfdsfdasfdas\nadfsafdsa\nafdafdsafdsfdsa\ndasfdafdasfdsa\nfdasfdasfdsafdsa\nfdfdasfd\nfdafdsafda\nadsfafasfsafdas\n*This page appears to be actually written in blood.*\n\nWhy?\n\nWhere is everyone?\n\nMy head hurts. I can't see straight. What am I looking for?\ndfdaf\ncda\ndacdsacac\ndsacd\ncdascacad\n\nWillow trees are so pretty. Didn't we make love under a willow tree the first time? I think so. In that pretty place near the old grove. I miss that place.\nThings were good there. Does he remember? He was in so much pain, but he was getting better.\n\nWe were happy there.\n\nWe are happy now.\n\n*The line above has been written multiple times and striken through each time.*\nI never wanted to come here. \n\nI didn't ask to come here.\n\nWhy am I here?\n\ndfdsagffdvdg\ndfadsavfd\nvfdabfva dvfdavfda\nvfdavfadvfadvfad\nBird are just rats with wings. \n\nA mare is a female horse. \n\nThey are happier without me. \n\ndfafdafdsafdsa\nfdsafdsafd\nfdafdsafdsafdsa\nfdsafdsafdsafda\nafdsafdsa", ""),
        StaticBook("Creature Index I", "Princess Siri Ihelia", "The Creature Index\nVolume I\n\nPhoenix\nThe Phoenix is a large bird with a wingspan of over 15ft across, it is the largest winged avian in the known world. With a plumage ranging from red to green depending on the species.\nThe phoenix wields sharp claws and a razor beak, yet posses a keen intelligent seen behind their black eyes. They watch their environment and focus on anything which could become an immediate danger to them or their master if tamed.\nThis is why Phoenixes are so difficult to capture, and why their masters are chosen by them solely out of respect.Phoenixes, while not being pack animals, will latch onto who it may deem to be an Alpha.\nWhen a Phoenix is mortally wounded or near the end of its lifespan, they will shed their feathers and dissipate into dust, leaving behind a large golden egg. The egg can be hatched to rebirth the Phoenix once more.\nOnly 12 Phoenixes are known to ever be in existence at the same time.\nIgnis -The fire Phoenix, who's plumage flutter in shades from yellow to red crimson. On the end of the feathers a little flame would continue to exist during the Phoenix's entire life.\nGetting more powerful as the Phoenix grows older of age and eventually even becoming so strong that the Phoenix burns itself.\nLigno - The forest Phoenix has a plumage ranging from a dark brown to dark green. Whoever'd look a little closer would see that the Ligno Phoenix in fact is more like a flying bush,\nit's tail also as parts of it's wings are made out of Twigs, vines, and branches.\nGlacium - The Glacium Phoenix is the Phoenix of Ice. Its plumage ranges from light to dark blue. Whoever gets close to this Phoenix would clearly feel the cold it radiates as it leaves behind a trail of snowflakes.\nDwarven legends have it that the earliest forms of hail stem from the wroth of a Glacium.\nAether - The Aether phoenix, the Phoenix of Air, is the rarest species of phoenixes in existence.\nSoaring constantly at high altitudes, only the sharpest eyes with the aid of a scope may spot one gliding by. Its plumage ranges from a pure white to a slate grey. The Aether Phoenix is known as the fastest of the Phoenixes.\nSigned, Siri Ihelia", ""),
        StaticBook("Creatures by Ork", "Eirik Ireheart", "Notice: These books are rushed copies of tomes in the library of the Orkish capital, as made during the raid of the 16th of The Grand Harvest, 1532. The following was originally written by an Ork, translated to\nview the modicum of Ork culture inside.\n\"Disclaimer: Whomever is reading this must know that this book about the various forms and types of creatures and races. Thank you for reading this book. Also, I wrote a lot of it in a sewer.\nChapter One: The Halfings.\n\nHalflings are weird. They are small. You can through them at walls. But, there is more to them than just mutalation. In this chapter, you will learn of the more sophisticated lifestyles of Halflings. The have a complex\nthat you wouldn't excpect. Firstly, it turns out that Halflings don't live in holes. Well, they kind of do, but they are called burrows. These burrows are actually quite nice and decorated. This is of course if you can even fit in it. Other than killing\nthem, Halflings are useful for trading, as I met many Halfling traders on the roads. They are usually very nice creaturs, but they're so mall that we like to make fun of them whenever we see them. Also, Halflings make for good Bartenders, that is, if they\ncan even reach the counter, yes?\n\nChapter Two: The Dwarves\n\nRecently, I learned about the Halflings- Small, ugli, and weak creatures they are. To understand a Dwarf is to understand alcohol.\nYou see, these 'Dwarves' fill their holes with beer. Lots and lots of beer. They are a merry race, much so like the Halflings. They are also short like the Halflings. Unlike the Halflings, they are fatter, and they like to fight almost as much as we Orkos\ndo. Almost. To be honest, there is much to admire about these creatures. They are a breed of warriors. Of course, the Dwarves can't compare to the strength of an Orkos, but they seem to be stronger than even the biggest human. Much like us Orkos, Dwarves\nhold their honor to a huge extent. Both Orkos and Dwarves like to use axes and hammers. To be honest, Dwarves are like tiny, ugly, smelly, dumb Orkos in a way. I think that we should still kill them, but, we need to appreciate why they're so fun to kill\nand fight. Now, we're going to shift gears here, and switch to a taller race.\n\nChapter Three: The Elves\n\nThis race is one of a disgraceful sense of honor. The Elves think they're better than us. I mean, so do the Halflings, Dwarves,\nand other stuff, but the Elves seem to hate us even more. They are a group of creatures that think they are so beautiful and smart. But, I feel that in some ways, they actually are smart. You see, they may be finer, smellier, and dumber than us, but I\nthink that they in some way, deep inside, that Elves have some degree of endulgence. Perhaps Elves can make good weapons or armor, or even good buildings. But, Elves seem to grasp the art of Magic very well. Now, we are going to dive into the specific\ntypes of Elves.\n\nChapter Four: The High Elves.\n\nIt is this clan that sucks the most, in my opinion. They're the ones that REALLY think high about themselves. Considering it's in their names and such. These ones live long, look tall, are super\npale, drink the teas, eat the cakes, write the novels, mock the other races, do their fancy magic, waste time in making stuff pretty (Even their weapons!), and take their baths, and clean their [klofz] and ears, and that's pretty much it. Basically, they\nsuck.\n\nChapter Five: The Wood Elves.\n\nNasty Tree-huggers, that's what these Wood Elves are. Believe it or not, Wood Elves don't even use swords, axes, or even thereputic lavatorial papers. They use bows. And for lavatorial papers, I\nthink they use leaves. Also, Tree Elves are much like twigs. That's why another name for Elves in Blah is 'Twiggeh'. These Wood Elves are a bunch of pansies. They hide in the shadows to hunt for their prey. But, us Orkos hunt for our prey in the open,\npartly. Although, Wood Elves are good at sneaking around. I have not studied the Wood Elves much, be cause they are usually hiding from me. So, they're is still much to learn about them. Now, we're going to take a look at the gray ones.\n\nChapter Six: The\nDark Elves.\n\nThese Elves look like the nighttime skies themselves. They are pretty much gray and kind of blue. They are pretty modest, for Elves, that is. They seem like the most humble of the Elves. Just like they're mysterious appearance, not much\nhas been recorded of the Dark Elves. Maybe they're is, but they did not share it with me. So, I am just going to tell you about their physical appearance, rather than their real culture. They have dark skin, dark eyes, but they usually dress with pretty\nbold colors. Also, I mainly noticed piercings and gray hairs. So, I don't talk about the Elves, because they're PRETTY LAME. So, now, we're going to shift gears again and learn about the Humans.\n\nChapter Seven: The Northern Humans.\nThese are smelly, diplomatic, tiny, ugly, weak, dum, and really dumb. You know what we are talking about. The Humans. But, these are the Humans in the North. I gathered this information in the city of [Ubrezchi]. They are a complicated race, so I'm going\nto break this up into different categories. First, we are going to talk about how we see them, or how they look. Humans are shorter than Elves, and fatter than Dwarves. They call themselves 'HOO-MANZ' and don't call themselves 'Sharaz', because they are\nso dumb, they don't even know what it means. They spoke with me, and said that they have something called 'Pulektikz' (TN: Politics, most likely.) I think it's like the [Krughai] Confederation, but they said it was more ugly. Also, they are greedy, like\nDwarves, but they are not greedy for gold, but Minaz in its stead. And, they NEVER admit it. So, basically, the Northern Humans are more evil than I ever thought. As you already know, the [Uhbrezchi] Humans are our allies in most wars, because they are\nsome of the only ones who don't betray us. Now, we will look into Adunia.\n\nChapter Eight: Adunians\n\nThey're neat. I obtained this information from the King of Adunia himself, Jarl [Lazchlahn Moare Ilindul]. So as you can see, this book gave\nme the honor to meet countless officials in the world. Anyway, the Adunians are said to be the oldest. Their King told me that they were the first human around, making him much older than the Adunians. Adunians also have politics like the [Uhbrezchinz],\nbut their's is much different. You see, in their culture, the youngest born is the one whose destiny is to lead, unlike more popular cultures where the Elders lead. These Adunians have many different ranks, too, like a High Thane, and High Marshall. Also,\nthese creatures are the longest lived Humans around, because apparently they have Elven blood in their history. However, they don't seem like Elves. No, Adunians are still much bigger than them, as they are pretty tall and mighty.\n[!] *A few pages appear to have been misplaced, instead replaced by notes.*\n\nMayra,\n\nHow I miss you. Our son has just arrived in Khaz'Kazak, and seems ever the firebrand. He's got your nose. I only hope he does well with young Hogan.\n[!] *What seems to be a second sheet lays here as well.*\n\nAlarik: oxoooooooxoooxoooo Hathrid: xoxxxxxxxxx\nHogan: x\nDuren: ox\nMidgor: xx\nDrynn: xxx\nNora: xxox\nThereon: xxxxxxxxx\nleft right here in [Gronkkzton], in the [kiddun] district. But, they all moved to [Mahlinoare] now, probably because we Orkos were too strong for them. There are four types of Kha, and we're going to delve into all of them right now.\n\nChapter Ten: The\n[Tygur] Kha\n\nThese are the biggest of the Cat Creatures, and some of them are as big as an Ork. They look like [Tygurz], and they fight like them too. They are usually the Warriors of the Kha, and they are pretty dumb. I don't know much about them.\nChapter Eleven: The [Zcheetuh] Kha\n\nThese ones are the smallest, but unlike a fat Dwarf, they are REALLY fast. The [Zcheetuh] Kha look like [zcheetuhs], they have spots all over their skin. And to me, they make the best carpets. (TN: Yes. They do.)\nChapter Twelve: The Dark Kha\n\nThey look like [punturz] an they are sneaky, like [Punturz], too. Always look out for Dark Kha, because they can steel heaps of things at any moment. To me, they are rather like Dark Elves, strictly speaking. Sadly, that is\nall I know about the Dark Kha, seeing as Kha are mysterious and they did not let me learn about them.\n\nChapter Thirteen: The [Lepurd] Kha\n\nThese ones obviously look like [Lepurdz], but unlike the other Kha, these ones don't exceed in any\nspecific skillset, but they are the best suited for doing anything they set their heart on. They are bigger than [Zcheetahz] and [Punturz], and they are faster than [Tygurz] and [Panturz]. You will most likely see these ones the most. Wait! We never\ntalked about the different types of Dwarves, did we? Well, we will rectify that now.\n\nChapter Fourteen: The Snow Elves\n\nI never heard of them. Their skin is white like snow. Their hair is white like clouds. They are Snow Elves. They are an endangered\nspecies. To be honest, these Snow Elves are albino, and they do not like it when we call them that. The Snow Elves aided the Dwarves win the past war, so I don't really like them. They live in a place called [Frohztfohl]. But, that's all I know, because\nthey don't really like me.\n\n\nThis is only the first volume in my series of books dwelling upon the topic of Creatures. The end.", ""),
        StaticBook("Crimson Hearts", "Ilkazar", "Crimson\nHearts\n\n\n\nThe \nGuild\nThe Crimson Hearts\nwere a late Atherian \nguild along the same lines of what the Arcan Delvers were in the past. The idea was to learn combat and magic respectivly, while exploring the land for treasure and artifacts of great worth.\nThe guild was brought into being by the Mali'Ker Sonoren\na tedious man at the best of times who always found reason to use the word Ayuh.\nHis right hand man being an Aheral by the name of 'Thor'. It also basically served as another incarnation\nof the Mages Guild.\nThe guild was based on the northern edge of Embermoor, near the town of Salvus.\nThe basic structure consisted of 'Mages'\nand 'Knights'. The guild had preformed some\nsurprising feats in its time, such as the destruction of a\nstone giant the locals of the area worshipped as a god.\nFighting along others in a skirmish against a Dragon. The guild was home to some notable people such as the earth evocationist Eliza, the electrical evocationist Lanavia\nthe skilled warrior Katari Stirling and his then wife Cheza. Along with the disreputable August/Aislinn. It also held the mages Coltaine and Artemis,\nwho had a sorcerous duel ending in one haveing heavy burns and the other acquiring crushed\nlungs. After some time though it was revealed that Sonoren, the founder of the guild was actually the Aheral known as Kalenz, former dictator of the Silver State, having enforced the notion of purity to ridiculous extremes in his time, at that point the\nguild disolved and everyone went there own ways.", ""),
        StaticBook("Crumena T.", "Ol' Man Sano", "Dear Crumena,\n\nI am humbled that you had entrusted myself to operate a facility such as the Conservatoire. As I depart to the Seven Skies, I must present to you the spare stamps-\nwhich we rewarded to all students and faculty, as a sort of token of their attendence. It is my deepest wish that you continue to educate the masses, and expand your fountain of knowledge. I thank you greatly.", ""),
        StaticBook("Crumpled Page", "Owl", "[!] The page, despite being written in perfect cursive, appears to have been ripped out from a book and unfinished.\nJournal, I'm seeing if your capabilities of writing work well.\nOh- Strange. Perhaps I'm just too archaic. Why are you still writing? Pah- I need Sister Fox to give you sentience. Though of course she's 'busy' with Lion- Journal! Stop writing. Aspects dam-\n[!] The rest has been cut off.", ""),
        StaticBook("Cult Book One", "Jekon", "Prologue:\nKiera was fleeing from the hooded figures.  She dodged trees, bushes, and animals and made it to the town known as Ivybend, the home of Halflings.  Realizing that she would easily be discovered in the streets, she rented a room at the inn.  She\nplunked her equipment on the floor, and relaxed on the bed.  After writing a quick message to her brother Sol and sending it, she fell asleep in the bed.\nIt was the last time she was heard from again.\nChapter One:\nSol woke up in his nice and comfortable bed.  After blinking the sleep from his eyes, he wandered over to his mail.  His eyes widened at what he recieved.\nA message from Kiera!  Kiera had gone missing a long time ago.  She was taking a trip\nto see the old chapel.  She had never been heard from again.  He looked at the note again, and saw that she had detailed her location.\nIvybend.\nSol bit his lip.  Ivybend, although inhabited by Halflings, was in the Dwarves territory.  Being an Elf, he\ncouldn't go strolling in there.  Elves and Dwarves have a long history of hate.  He would have to find someone to find her for him.  He thought of who he could send in his place.  Farmer Joe?  No, he was to old.  Oliver?  To inexperienced.\nThen he\nremembered Jekon.  Jekon was an Adunian adventurer, with green eyes and long hair that covered his longer ears from his Elven parent.  Jekon was currently in the employ of Farmer Joe, due to an illness that forced him to stay at home, in Vekaro, for a\ntime.\n\nSol grabbed the note, and went off to Joe's farm.\nChapter 2:\nJekon was harvesting the crops when Sol arrived.  Jekon was around 20 years old, and he was at the end of aging like a human, and would begin aging like an Elf.  Jekon was a bit distant from most people.  Something had happened to him that made\nhim dislike crowds.  But, if you were his friend, he would behave like any normal person.\nWhen Sol came up, Jekon instantly had a smile on his face.  Sol was a good friend of his, and had saved him once.  He waited while Sol walked up.\n\"Jekon,\" Sol said,\nwith worry clearly on his face.\n\"I need your help.\"\nHearing this, Jekon's smile fell.\n\"Of course Sol.  Anything.\"\nJekon said, a tad bit worried for his friend.\nSol looked around warily.\n\"Not here.  There could be people listening.\" he said, gesturing for\nJekon to follow.\nChapter 3:\n\"Jekon,\" Sol said, taking a deep breath.\n\"Jekon, my sister sent me a note.  And the news she brought wasn't good.  She's being chased by a Cult.  I need you to go find her, and bring her back safely.  If... if she's dead, bring back her\nnecklace, and her sword.  These are items passed down through the Chase family, and I couldn't bear to think that they're missing.  Jekon, will you do this for me?\"\n\nJekon sat back and thought.  This would be very dangerous.  Dwarves at this time had no\nlove for humans as well as Elves.  Imagine them seeing a mix of the two.\nBut, Sol was his friend.  He couldn't abandon him, especially now.  So, he got up and said,\n\"When do I leave?\"\nChapter 4:\nJekon took his sword, some armor, and food.  Before he left, Sol gave him a spiked ring and two bottles of a colored liquid.  Sol explained,\n\"Dip the ring in this bottle.  It is poison.  Then, jab it in your foe's neck.  It will paralyze them\nfor 5 Elven minutes.  Now, take care friend.\"\nThat would be the time they talked for months.\nBy the time Jekon set off, it was mid-morning.  He had no trouble sneaking past the Dwarvern sentries posted at the border, and managed to sneak into a forest\nbehind it.  There, he set up camp, and got a fire going.  He ate some bread and some meat, cooked by the fire.  After eating, and slept until early morning, when he packed up and left for Ivybend.\nChapter 5:\nWhile walking along the road, Jekon thought to himself that he was lucky he had not been attacked by bandits.  The area was hardly patrolled, and there were many hideouts in the area.  As it was, most of the hideouts were warring with\nthemselves, and were to busy to go out pillaging.\nJekon kept on going.  Soon he reached a small town.\nHood raised, Jekon walked in, and asked questions about where he might be, and which direction Ivybend was in.\n\nAs it was, no one knew.  They had never\nheard of the place.\n\nAfter stocking up on supplies, Jekon went back on the trail.  Soon night came, and he was forced to shelter in a small cave.  When he woke up, he was being charged by an angry Dwarf, seeing a human (As far as he could tell) resting in\nhis mine.\n\nJekon, hearing his bloodcurdling scream, jumped up and stepped aside.  The dwarf stopped and turned around.  He quickly pulled out his axe, and swung it around.  It was clear he was a master of the craft.  Jekon bit his lip, worried, because he\nwas only an average swordsman at best.\nHe didn't have much more time to think, because the Dwarf charged again.  Jekon didn't have much time to react, and the axe cut his leg.  It was clear Jekon was losing this fight.  He took out a bottle, the liquid\ninside being a potion, and drank it.\n\nInstantly his leg was healed, and he felt more powerful than before.  He dodged the next charge easily, and stabbed his sword into the Dwarf's skull.  The dwarf fell, and made no more noise.\nChapter 6:\nAfter searching the body, Jekon found a map of the surrounding area.  Opening it, he saw that Ivybend was a few more miles East.  If Jekon had looked closer, however, he would have noticed that the house representing Ivybend was in ruins.\nJekon went further East, until he came across what was Ivybend.  Few souls were living there now, and many buildings were destroyed.  When he asked survivors what had happened, all they could say was, \n\"Iblees... Iblees... Ibless...\" over and over again.\nHe soon found the building described in the note, and walked in.\nChapter 7:\nThe place was devestated.  Bodies of half-lings were everywhere, and they were all blood-splattered.  Jekon, feeling sick, closed his eyes and moved on.  He couldn't focus on the death and destruction, he had to find Kiera.  Although, with all\nthis, he doubted she was alive.  He checked each room, until he came to the last one.  Hand shivering, he opened.\nWhat he saw scarred him for the rest of his life.\n\nKiera's corpse, gutted and throat slit, lie on the floor in the middle of her guts.  Jekon\ncould barely stand, but he walked over and took her necklace, and her sword which was a few steps away.\n\nJekon went back to Sol.\nFinal Chapter:\nJekon visited Sol at the healing center near Vekaro, and it appeared he was in some sort of meeting.  AFter waiting it out, Sol approached warily and said,\n\"Well?\"\n\"I'm sorry.\" Jekon said while handing him the sword and necklace.\nSol's eyes looked downcast as he gave Jekon a just reward.  Then he went off to another room.  He was plotting.\n\nTHE END", ""),
        StaticBook("Cupcake", "Klaudia Crast", "-------------------\n\n\n\nThe Life of a Cupcake\n\nby Lady Klaudia Crast\n\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\n\n\n-------------------\nThey put me in the oven to bake.\nMe a deprived and miserable cake.\nFeeling the heat I started to bubble.\n\nWatching the others I knew I was in trouble\nThey opened the door and I started my life.\nFrosting me with a silver knife.\n\nDecorating me with candy jewels.\n\nThe rest of the batch looked like fools.\nLifting me up she took off my wrapper.\n\nFeeling the breeze I wanted to slap her.\n\nOpening her mouth the\nsight of shiny teeth inside.\n\nThis was the day this cupcake had died.", ""),
        StaticBook("Curiosity I", "Chet of Locklear", "In Felsen, the richest and most prominent city of Oren, given its position in the imperial demense, lived Anselm and Lothar, two wealthy and noble gentlemen, so strictly united in the bands of amity that every one who knew them called them by way of\nexcellence and epithet, the Two Friends. And, both being bachelors, and their age and education so much alike, it was not to be wondered at that this reciprocal affection sprung up between them. True, it is, Anselm was rather more addicted to amorous\nadventure than Lothar, whose chief delight was in hunting, but yet, upon occasion, Anselm could quit his own amusements to pursue those of his friend, and Lothar could postpone his favourite diversion in order to practice that of Anselm. In this manner,\ntheir inclinations proceeded so mutually that no clock could be set with more regularity. Anselm happened to fall desperately in love with a young lady of title and beauty, who lived in Felsen, descended from such a noble family, and of such personal\nmerit that he determined, with the approval of his friend, without which he did nothing, to demand her of her parents in marriage. And so Anselm put his resolution in practice. Lothar was entrusted with the message, and conluded this affair so much to the\nsatisfaction of his friend that in a very little time Anselmo saw himself in possession of his heart's desire, and Camilla, in turn, thought herself so happy in having obtained such a husband that she was incessant in her thanks towards God and Lothar, by\nwhose action her happiness was made. During the first two days after marriage, which are commonly spent in feasting and mirth, Lothar, as usual, frequented the house of his friend with a view of honouring ceremony, and endeavouring, as much as he could\nmuster, to promote the joy and festivity attending all such occasions. But in time, the wedding being over, he began carefully and gradually to absent himself from Anselm's house, thinking, as every prudent person would naturally conclude, that a man\nought not to frequent the house of a friend after he is married in the same manner as he had while his friend was single, for, though suspicion should never find harbour with true and virtous friendship, the honor of a married man is oft so delicate to\ninjury not only from a friend, but even a from a brother. Anselm perceived Lothar's remissness, and complained of it loudly, saying that if he had known his marriage would have impaired their former friendship, he never would have thought of marrying, and\nbegged, that as by the mutual companionship which birthed that agreeable title of the Two Friends, he would not now suffer that endearing and celebrated name to be lost by a scrupulous adherence to mere decorum. He therefore entreated Lothar, if he might\nbe allowed to use this expression, to be master of his house, and to come in and go out as before, assuring him that the inclinations of Camilla, in that respect, were exactly the same as his own, and that, knowing the perfect friendship which subsisted\nbetween them, she was extremely mortified at his shyness. To these and many other arguments used by Anselm to persuade his friend to frequent his house as usual, Lothar answered with such prudence, force, and discernment that the other was convinced of\nhis friend's careful conduct. And so it was agreed between them that Lothar should dine with him twice a week, besides holidays, but notwithstanding this agreement, he resolved to comply with it no further than he should see convenient for Anselm's honour\nwhich was dearer to him than his own. He said, and his observation was just, that a man on whom heaven has bestowed a beautiful wife should be cautious of the men he brings to his house, as careful in observing the female friends with whom his spouse\nconverses, for, that which cannot be done in a public place, where a husband cannot forbid his wife, may be easily transacted in the house of a female friend or kin in whom no suspicion lay. For this reason, Lothar observed that every married man had\nreason for some friend to apprise him of any oddities in her conduct, for, it often happens that he is too much in love with his wife to observe, or too much afraid of offending her, to prescribe limits to her behaviour in those things which may tarnish\nhis own honour, but this inconvenience may be easily amended by the advice of a friend. However, where shall Anselm find such a zealous, humble, and trusty friend as is required? He knew not, save for Lothar himself, who consulting the honour of Anselm\nwith the utmost care and circumspection, was at great pains to diminish the number of his days at his friend's house so that the idle and prying eyes of malice might not indulge their love of slander upon perceiving a genteel young man of such birth,\nfortune, and accomplishments as he knew himself possessed of, to go in to the house of such a celebrated beauty as Camilla, for, although his virtue and honour might be a sufficient check to the most malevolent tongue, he would not expose his own\ncharacter, or that of his friend's, to the smallest censure, and therefore employed the greatest part of the days on which he had agreed to visit Anselm in things he, pretended, at least, were of the utmost importance, so that when they were together,\na great deal of time was consumed by the complaints of the one, and the excuses of the other. One day, however, as they were walking through a meadow outside the city, Anselm addressed himself to Lothar in these terms:\n\"You believe, my friend Lothar, that I can never be thankful enough to God for the blessings I enjoy, not only in the most gracious parents, and in the abundance of good nature and fortune, but, also in a friend like you, and a wife like Camilla, which\nare two pledges I esteem, if not as highly as I ought, at least, as much as I can. Yet, though I possess all those benefits which usually constitute the happiness of Man, I find myself one of the most disgusted and discontented men alive. I have been for\nthese many days since my wedding, so harassed and fatigued with such an odd, unexplainable desire that I cannot help being amazed at my infatuation, for which I often blame and rebuke myself, endeavouring to suppress and conceal it from my own reflection,\nbut, I find it impossible to keep the secret, as if I hd industriously published it to the whole world, and since it must actually be disclosed to somebody, I would have it deposited in the most secret archives of your heart, in full confidence, that by\nthe diligence which you, as a trusty friend, will exert in my behalf, when you know it, I shall soon see myself delivered from that anxiety to which it has reduced me, and by your assiduity be raised to a pitch of joy equal to the degree of vexation which\nmy own folly hs entailed upon me.\"\n\nLothar was astonished at this discourse of Anselm, as he could not comprehend the meaning of such a long preface and preamble, and endeavoured, by revolving every thing in his imagination, to find out what this desire\ncould be that preyed so much upon the spirits of his friend, but, finding himself always wide of the mark, was willing to ease himself immediately of the excessive pain his suspense occasioned, and with this view, told Anselm that he did a manifest injury\nto the warmth of their friendship in going about the bush, seeking indirect methods to impart his most secret thoughts, since he was so well assured that he might entirely depend on him, either for advice to suppress, or assistance to support them.\n\"I am well convinced of the truth of what you say,\" Answered Anselm, \"and in that confidence will tell you, my friend, that the desire with which I am possessed is to be certain whether or not by wife Camilla is as virtuous and perfect as I believe her to\nbe, and this truth I shall never be fully persuaded of until the nature of her perfection appear upon trial, as pure gold is proved by fire, for, it is my opinion, that there is no woman virtuous but in proportion to the solicitations she has withstood,\nand, that she only is chaste, who has not yet yielded to the promises, presents, tears, and continual importunities of persevering lovers. And pray, where is the merit in a woman's being chaste, when nobody ever courted her to be otherwise? What wonder\nthat she should be reserved and cautious who has no opportunity of indulging loose inclinations, and who knows her husband would immediately put her to death should he once catch her tripping? For this reason, I can never entertain the same degree of\nesteem for a woman who is chaste out of fear, or want of opportunity, as I would for she who has triumphed over incessant solicitation, so that, for these and many other reasons I could urge to sanction and enforce my opinion, I desire that my wife\nCamilla may undergo the test, and be refined in the fire of importunate addresses by one possessed of sufficient accomplishments to inspire a woman with love, and, if she comes off, as I believe she will, victorious in trial, I shall think my own\nhappiness unparalleled. I shall, then, be able to say that my wishes are fulfilled, and even if the contrary of what I expect should happen, the satisfaction of seeing my opinion confirmed will help me to bear with patience that which would otherwise\nprove such a costly experiment. Supposing then, that nothing you can say in opposition to this desire of mine can avail in diverting me from my purpose, I expect and entreat that you, my dear Lothar, will condescend to be the instrument with which I\nexecute this work of my inclination. I will give you proper opportunities and supply you with everything I see necessary for soliciting a woman of virtue, honor, and reservation, and what, among other things, induces me to entrust you with this enterprise\nis the consideration, that should Camilla's scruples be overcome, you will not pursue your conquest to the last circumstance of rigour, but only suppose that done, which for good reason, ought to remain undone, so that I shall be injured by her\ninclination alone, and my wrongs lie buried in the virtue of your silence, which, I know, in whatever concerns my welfare, will be eternal as that of death. For this reason, if you would have me enjoy what deserves to be called life, you will undertake\nthis amorous contest; not with lukewarm passion and languor, but with eagerness and diligence which corresponds to my wish and the confidence in which I am secured by your friendship.\"\nSuch was the discourse of Anselm to which Lothar listened so attentively that, except what he is already said to have uttered, he did not open his lips until his friend had finished his proposal, but, finding he had nothing more to allege after having\nfor some time gazed upon him as an object unseen, filled him with astonishment and surprise. \"I cannot be persuaded, Anselm,\" said the bachelor friend, \"that what you spoke was not in jest, for, had I thought you in earnest, I should not have suffered\nyou to proceed so far, but, by refusing to listen, have prevented such a long harangue. Without doubt, you must either mistake my disposition, or I be utterly unacquainted with yours, and yet, I know you to be Anselm, and you must be sensible that I am\nLothar. The misfortune is that I no longer find you the same Anselm who was my friend; nor is what you ask a thing to be demanded of that Lothar who shared your confidence. Good men avail themselves of their friends, but dare not presume upon things\ncontrary to the law of God. Tell me then, Anselm, is this in danger before I venture to gratify your wish by complying with the detestable proposal you have made? Surely, no, for on the contrary, if I understand you correctly, you are desirous that I\nshould indefatigably endeavour to deprive you and myself also of that very life and honour, which it is my duty to preserve, for, if I rob you of honor, I rob you of life, since a man without honour is worse than dead, and I being the instrument as you\ndesire I should be entails such a curse upon you, and so I should not be dishonoured, and of consequence, dead to all enjoyment. Listen with patience, my friend Anselm, and make no answer until I shall have done with imparting the suggestions of my mind\nconcerning the strange proposal you have made, for there will be time enough for you to reply, and me to listen in my turn.\"\n\"With all my heart!\" Cried Anselm, \"You may speak as long as you please.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Curiosity II", "Chet of Locklear", "Accordingly, Lothar proceeding, saying, \"In my opinion, Anselm, your disposition is at present like that of the Qali, who will not suffer theselves to be convicted of the errors of their sect by quotations from the holy scrolls, nor with speculation, or\nthe basic tenants of faith, but must be confuted or convinced by examples that are palpable, easy, familiar, and subject to the certainty of mathematical demonstration. For instance, if from equal parts we take equal parts, those that remain are equal.\nAnd if they do not understand this proposition verbally, as is frequently the case, it must be explained and set before their eyes by manual operation, which is also insufficient to persuade them of the truth of our holy religion. The selfsame method I\nmust practice with you, whose desire deviates so far from everything that bears the least shadow of reason that I should look upon it as time misspent to endeavour to convince you of your folly, which is the only name your intention seems to deserve. Nay,\nI am even tempted to leave you in your extravagance as a punishment for your preposterous desire, but I am prevented from using such rigour by my friendship which will not permit me to desert you in such manifest danger of perdition. But, to make this\naffair still more plain, tell me, Anselm, did you not desire me to solicit one that was reserved, seduce one that was chaste, make presents to one that was disinterested, and assiduously court one that was wife? Yes, such was your demand. If you are\napprised, then, of the reserve, virtue, disinterestedness, and prudence of your wife, pray, what is your aim? If you believe she will triumph over all my assaults, as undoubtedly she will, what fairer titles can you bestow upon her than those she\npossesses already? Or how will she be more perfect after that trial than she is at present? You either do not believe she is so virtuous as you have represented her, or know not the nature of your demand. If you think she is not so chaste as you have\ndescribed her, you should not hazard the trial, but rather, according to the dictates of your own prudence, treat her as a vicious woman. If you are satisfied of her virtue, it would be altogether impertinent to make trial of that truth, which from the\nrest, can acquire no additional esteem. From whence we may reasonably conclude that for men to execute designs which are clearly productive of more hurt than benefit is the province of madness and temerity, especially when they are not incited or\ncompelled to these designs by any sort of consideration, but on the contrary, may at a greater distance perceive the manifest madness of their intention. Difficulties are undertaken either for the sake of God, of this world, or of both. The first are\nincurred by holy men who live the life of Aenguls here on earth; the second by those who traverse the boundless lands, visiting such a diversity of climates and nations with a view of acquiring what are called the goods of fortune, and such undertakings\nas equally regard God and man fall to the share of those valiant soldiers who no sooner behold in the wall of an adverse fortification a breach, though no bigger than that which is made by a single pounding of stone shot, than laying aside all fear and\noverlooking with unconcern the manifest danger that menaces them, winged with desire of signalising their valour on behalf of their emperor, nation, and God, throw themselves with the utmost intrepidity into the midst of a thousand deaths that oppose and\nawait them. These are the enterprises which are generally undertaken, and, though full of peril and inconvenience, attended with glory, honour, and advantage, but that which you have planned, and purpose to put in execution, neither tends to your\nacquiring the approbation of God, the goods of fortune, nor the applause of mankind, for, granting that the experiment to succeed to your wish, it will neither make you more happy, rich, or respected than you are, and should it turn out contrary to your\nexpectation, you will find yourself the most miserable of all descendants. It will then give you little ease to reflect that your misfortune is unknown, for the bare knowing it yourself will be sufficient to plunge you in affliction and despair. As\nconfirmation of this truth, you must give me leave to repeat the following stanza, written by the celebrated poet Soren Horen at the end of Siegmund's Lament.\n             -\nWhen Siegmund saw the approach of rosy morn,\nHis soul with sorrow and remorse was\ntorn.\nFor, though from ev'ry mortal eye conceal'd, The guilt to his own bosom stood reveal'd:\nThe candid breast will, self-accusing, own\nEach conscious fault, tho' to the world, unknown:\nNor, will th' offender 'scape internal shame, Though unimpeach'd by\njustice or by fame.\n             -\n\"Considering this, secrecy will never assuage your grief, but on the contrary, you will incessantly weep, not tears from your eyes, but drops of blood from your heart, and although this is a poetic fiction, it\nnevertheless contains a well-couched moral worthy of notice, study, and imitation especially, as what I am going to say will, I hope, bring you to a due sense of the great error you want to commit. Tell me, Anselm, if God or good fortune had made you\nmaster and lawful owner of an exquisite diamond, the brilliancy of which was admired by all the lapidaries who had seen it, and unanimously allowed to be the most perfect of its kind, an opinion which, as you knew nothing to the contrary, was exactly\nconformable to your own, would it be wise or pardonable in you to put that jewel under the hammer, and by mere dint of blows and strength of arm, try if it was as hard and perfect as it had been pronounced? For, supposing that the diamond should resist\nthe force of this foolish experiment, it would acquire no addition of value or fame, and if it should be broke to pieces, a thing that might easily happen, would not all be lost? Yes, for certain, and the owner be universally deemed a fool. Consider then,\nmy friend, that Camilla is an exquisite diamond, not only in your estimation, but in that of everyone who knows her, and it would be highly unreasonable to expose her to the least possibility of being broke, for, even should she remain entire, her\nreputation will receive no increase, but should she fail in the trial, reflect upon what you must feel, and the reason you will then have to complain of yourself for having been the fatal cause of her perdition and your own despair. Consider that no jewel\nin this world is comparable to a woman of virtue and honour, and that the honour of the sex consists in the fair characters they maintain. Since, therefore the reputation of your wife is already as high as it can possibly be, why would you bring this\ntruth into question? Remember, my friend, that woman is an imperfect creature, and that instead of laying blocks in her way over which she might stumble and fall, we ought to remove them with care, and clear her paths from all obstructions so that she\nmay, without trouble, proceed smoothly in attaining that perfection which she may still want, namely, immaculate virtue. A virtuous woman also resembles a bright, transparent mirror, which is liable to be stained and obscured by the breath of those who\napproach too near it. A virtuous woman, like relics, ought to be adorned at a distance. She ought to be preserved and esteemed as a beautfiul garden full of flowers and roses, the owner of which will suffer nobody to handle them or pass through it,\npermitting them only to enjoy its fragrance and beauty from a distance, through the iron rails that surround it. In fine, I will repeat a few verses that I just now recollect from a recent comedy because they seem to have been composed on the very subject\nof our present discourse. A sage old man advising his friend, who is blessed with a handsome daughter, to lock her up, and watch over her with the utmost vigilance and care, among other reasons, cautions him with these:\nI\nWoman is form'd of brittle ware;\nthen, wherefore rashly seek to know\nWhat force, unbroken she will bear,\nAnd strike, perhaps some fatal blow.\n              II\nThough easily to fragments tore,\n'Twere equally absurd and vain,\nTo dash in pieces on the floor,\nWhat never can be join'd again.\n             III\nThis maxim, then, by facts assur'd,\nShould henceforth be espous'd by all;\nWhere'er a Lilyana lies immur'd\nThe tempting show'r of gold will fall.\nAll that I have until now suggested, Anselm, regards yourself, and now it is but reasonable you should hear something that concerns me, and if I should be protracted in my observations, you must excuse me, because it is absolutely necessary to expatiate\non the subject in order to extricate you from the labyrinth you are involved, and from which you desire to be disengaged by my assistance. You consider me as your friend, and yet seek to deprive me of my honour, a desire opposite of all friendship or\nregard; nay, even endeavour to make me rob you of your own. That you want to destroy mine is plain, for Camilla finding herself exposed to my solicitations, as you desire, will certainly look upon me as a man void of all principle and honour, for I\nattempt to succeed in a design so contrary to the dignity of my own character and the friendship subsisting between us. That you desire I should rob you of yours is not to be doubted, because Camilla, seeing herself importuned by my addresses, will think\nI must have observed some levity in her conduct which has encouraged me to disclose my vicious inclinations, and therefore think herself dishonoured accordingly, and so you will be as much concerned in her dishonour as if it was your own. Hence springs\nthe common observation that the husband of a lewd woman, though he neither knows nor gives the least occasion for the misconduct of his wife, and, though his misfortune was neither owing to his lack of prudence or care, is in spite of this pointed\nat and distinguished by a name of scandal and reproach; being looked upon by those who know the frailty of his wife with an eye of disdain intead of compassion, which he certainly deserves, as his disgrace proceeds not from any fault of his, but from the\nloose inclinations of his worthless spouse. In the same way as the whole person is affected by the pain of the foot or any other member of the human body, and the head, though no way concerned in the cause, is a fellow-sufferer with the ankle when it\nhurts; by the same rule a husband, being part of the whole, must bear a share of his wife's dishonour, for as all the honours and disgraces of this life proceed from flesh and blood, the infamy of a vicious woman, being of the same origin, must\nbe shared by her husband who ought to be looked upon as a dishonoured person, though he be utterly ignorant of the guilt. Reflect, therefore, Anselm, on the danger into which you bring yourself by seeking to disturb the peace and tranquility of your\nvirtuous wife. Reflect upon the vanity and impertinence of that curiosity which prompts you to awaken and stir up those humours that now lie tamed and quiet in the bosom of your chaste spouse. Consider, that in this rash adventure your gain must be very\nsmall, but your loss may be so great that I leave it unmentioned, because I lack words to express its estimation. On the whole, if what I have said is insufficient to divert you from your mischevious design, I desire you will choose some other instrument\nof your misfortune and disgrace, for I will not undertake the office, though, by my refusal, I should even lose your friendship, which is dearer to me than any thing upon earth.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Daniel T.", "Ol' Man Sano", "Dear Daniel,\n\nI do believe that you had been so kind and helpful, dating back to the times we spent at Skyfall, no matter how secluded you were from the rest of the residents.\nMay it have been registering me with the rest of the folk at the Sanctuary, assisting me in finding a willing teacher, or giving me advice within my stubborn life scenarios, you were truly a grateful soul.\nFor this, please do take this aurum lion statue, one which I bought at a fair some time ago. In addition, this toy cat, which was given to me by none other than Anna Sophia of Mondstdat. Please save it for-\nyour child, who is sure to be raised well alongside yourself and Nemir. Thank you, truly.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dark Arts Vol I", "Balder Frostbeard", "---Dark Magic---\n\n--Necromancy--\n\nNecromacy a dark and powerful magic, mostly still unknown to the people of this realm.\n\nNecromancy is the practise of bring the dead back to life a novice necromancer would only be able to\nsummon a creature of darkness by using the life energy from another, however an master in the art can summon a creature by using its own life force by not killing himself it takes years for a someone to master this art but its very rare to see\nNecromancy is more commonly used on someone who is inraged by the death of a loved but this is a weeker magic user so I can reanimate the loved one with a death of another.\n\n--Ghouls--\nGhouls are a necromancers first leason to master\nIn controling one is a victory in itself for ghouls are soulless undead that roam and yearning for lifeforce it can exist forever until it is either slayed or destroyed.\nOnce summoned a ghoul can attack its master if he is unexperianced.\nThe weakness lof a ghoul like all things undead is gold, a gold or enchanted object can easily kill a ghoul also a holy object can easily do the same. Most common thing to stop any forms of the undead is a paladin a paladin is a holy warrior which protect\nthis realm from anything unholy.\n---Blood Magic---\nBlood magic is more used for rituals and not in combat, however its still useful. Blood mages can reach there full potential during a blood ritual blood mages will gather together with sacrifecs\nenchantments or an Item of magical power but depending on what ritual they use is depending on the out come.\n--Ritual Types--\nThere are three types of rituals blood magic uses which is an elemental ritual, Summoning ritual and a creation ritual\nby far a creation ritual would be the most dangerous of them all it involes different magics which is used to form a twisted an evil form of life, This takes a Master Blood Mage to do and years of pratice you would need to have a lot of knowledge in order\nto pull this off. Attempting to do this allone requires the user to weild a lot of mana from either over mages or from blood. The mages need to do the ritual correctly would be a conjuratioists, shamans, necromancers and maybe an alchemest\nalso they must all have a huge amount of power people even trying to create.\nThe one problem with blood magic is that it restricts the user for example Blood mages need blood for a living host for there magic to work however you dont have to use your self\nyou can drain from overs as well.\nThe requirments are simple though a living source of blood mana doesnt travel through vials of blood so an open wound is needed.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dark Magic", "Daeren Rorel", "Dark Magic & You \n===============\nOriginally composed by Nienna Calm.\nRevised and translated by Daeren Rorel.\nContents:\n-What is a Dark Mage?\n-Necromancy\n-Shades\n-Soul Puppeteers\n  - Soul Contractors\n-Black Dragon Parasites.\n-General Warning Signs of a dark mage.\nWhat is a Dark Mage?\n-------------------\nA dark mage is a user of magic that inherently harms others in order to function. Dark Mages can receive their powers in a variety of manners; including pacts with dark gods, rituals set forth by Iblees,\nand other similarly horrifying methods. It is for this reason that all Dark Mages must be identified and killed on site, for they would not hesitate to do the same to you.\nNecromancy\n-------------------Necromancy is the quintessential dark magic, and probably the first to ever be founded. Its age has not made it any less dangerous, however, and is directly responsible for all manners of Wraiths and Liches plaguing\nthis world. Necromancers drain the very life force of plants, animals, and indeed people around them to cast their spells. In fact, they need a constant supply of life force to even survive, and must seek it out regularly.\nHow to Identify a Necromancer:\nThe bodies of necromancers are often in a very frail, almost decayed state.  Since necromancers need life force to cast spells, be on the lookout for dead or tainted patches of plant life,\nor reports of people feeling drained after touching a specific person. These are both serious signs of a Necromancer infestation.\nShades\n-------------------Shades are the result of Iblees magic corrupting the mind and soul of an existing mage. These dark mages are ticking time bombs, for within them lies an eldritch, a second personality that desires for only chaos and destruction.\nShades are the result of Iblees magic corrupting the mind and soul of an existing mage. These dark mages are ticking time bombs, for within them lies an eldritch, a second personality that desires for only chaos and destruction.\nHow to Identify Shades: \nShade mages are hard to identify, for their true nature is only only revealed when they cast spells. The hallmark of a Shade is the ability to create black tentacles out of thin air.\nTheir ability to corrupt their own magic may cause them to cast spells that are not usually possible to create. If you suspect a mage of being a Shade, contact a cleric immediately. Shades suffer from severe aversion to holy spells and relics,\nand these can be used to verify if a mage is, in fact, a shade.\nSoul Puppeteers\n-------------------\n\nSoul puppeteers are masters of curses. Using a small fetish (a doll of some sort), and a physical part of another person (such as their hair, blood, etc.), they are able to bring sickness, pain and even death\nto a person from an extreme distance. Random, shooting pains and illnesses with supernatural symptoms are strong signs of the interference of a Soul Puppeteer.\nHow to Identify a Soul Puppeteer:\n\nIt is difficult to identify a Soul Puppeteer straight off. Be on the lookout for those who try to take blood or locks of hair from their enemies.\nIf you suspect someone of soul Puppetry, inspect them immediately for a fetish. It is not a guarantee that they will always have one on them, but it’s the only way to confirm for sure.\nSoul Contractors are similar to soul puppeteers, in that they are capable of fashioning magical legal documents that bind the signer to the very letter of their word.  This would be potentially useful,\nif not for the material they must fashion these documents on.  Soul contracts can only be written upon the flayed skin of men that was taken while they were still alive.  It is a brutal and horrifying process,\nthat speaks to the inhumanity of these casters.\nBlack-Dragon Parasites\n-------------------\n\nA more recent addition to dark magic, black-dragon parasites are a growing problem in the Caliphate. A black-dragon parasite is an insidious form of insect that infects its host and causes\nthem to literally absorb blood and the flesh of the mortal races in return for benefits. It is unknown how a parasite passes from person to person, so it is absolutely vital that you isolate a suspected carrier far from the uninfected.\nIt is currently unknown if Black Dragon Parasite victims can be cured, so it is recommended that they either be expelled from the city, or in extreme cases, purged.\nHow to Identify a Black-Dragon Parasite:\n\nBlack-Dragon Parasites are easy to identify. All carriers for the parasite bear a tattoo of a black dragon on their person, usually winding around the stomach area.\nIf you suspect someone of having this terrible disease, conduct a full body search immediately.\nGeneral Warning Signs of a Dark Mage\n-------------------\n\nDark Mages can and will follow stereotypes at times. If you keep a look out, there are many signs that indicate if a person is just a dark mage in general.\nThese are by no means deciding factors in a suspect’s ability to cast black magic, but they are definitely red flags to investigate.\n\nNext page for list.\nBe suspicious of any persons you see that:\nWear primarily black robes.\nAre hooded at all times.\nPossess bright red eyes.\nProject a magical aura that is black, gray or red in color.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dark Magic & You", "Nienna Calm", "Dark Magic\n      And You!\n-------------------  A Guard's Guide to\n  Identifying Dark \n          Mages\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBy: Nienna Calm\nForeWord\n-------------------This book was written with the intent to educate the guardmen and women of the Caliphate of Khalestine. However, should you find this book in your possession, I would suggest reading it anyways. It is a good\nguide for identifying Dark mages.\nWhat is a\n    Dark Mage?\n-------------------\nA dark mage is a user of magic that inherently harms others in order to function. Dark Mages can receive their powers in a variety of manners; including Pacts with dark gods, Rituals set forth by\nIblees, and other similarly horrifying methods. It is for this reason that all Dark Mages must be identified and killed on site, for they would not hesitate to do the same to you.\nNecromancy\n-------------------\nNecromancy is the quintessential dark magic, and probably the first to ever be founded. It's age has not made it any less dangerous, however, and is directly responsible for all manners of Wraiths and Liches plaguing\nthis world today. Necromancers drain the very life force of plants, animals, and indeed people around them to cast their spells. In fact, they need a constant supply of life force to even survive, and must seek it out regularly.\nHow to Identify:\nThe bodies of necromancers are often in a very frail, almost decayed state. Since Necromancers need life force to cast spells, be on the lookout for dead or tainted patches of plant life, or reports of people feeling drained after\ntouching a specific person. These are both serious signs of a Necromancer infestation.\nFrost Witches\n-------------------Frost Witches are monsters of Ice and Snow who disguise themselves as women and prey upon the libido of Men. The Frost Witch is an easy threat to counter in the hot weather of the Caliphate, but requires constant\nvigilance to identify. A Frost Witch's true form is bright blue, but using her curse's magic, she is able to take any form she pleases, so long as that form is female. Frost Witches use these disguises to trick men into a false sense of security,\nwhereupon they will take their true form, and devour the unsuspecting male.\n\nHow to Identify:\nThe easiest way to identify a Frost Witch is by touching their skin. A frost witch's body temperature is colder than anything one could imagine.\nThere is no way for them to disguise this. Also, because of this impairment, any disguised frost Witch will show signs of great fatigue under the Caliphate sun. Any women demonstrating a severe aversion to high temperatures and regular food should have\nthe temperature of their skin checked immediately.\nShades\n-------------------\nShades are the result of Iblees magic corrupting the mind and soul of an existing mage. These dark mages are ticking time bombs, for within them lies an eldritch, second personality that desires for only chaos and\ndestruction. Shades are capable of corrupting every form of Arcane magic, empowering their spells with the dark powers of Iblees himself.\n\nHow to Identify:\nShade mages are hard to identify, for their true nature is only\nrevealed when they cast spells. The hallmark of a Shade is the ability to create black tentacles out of thin air. Their ability to corrupt their own magic may cause them to cast spells that are not usually possible to create. If you suspect a mage of\nbeing a Shade, contact a cleric immediately. Shades suffer from severe aversion to holy spells and relics, and these can be used to verify if a mage is, in fact, a Shade.\nSoul Puppeteers\n-------------------\nSoul puppeteers are masters of curses. Using a small fetish (a doll of some sort), and a physical part of another person (such as their hair, blood, etc.), They are able to bring sickness, pain, and even death to a\nperson from an extreme distance. Random, shooting pains and illnesses with supernatural symptoms are strong signs of the interference of a Soul Puppeteer.\n\nHow to Identify:\nIt is difficult to identify a Soul Puppeteer\nstraight off. Be on the lookout for those who try to take blood or locks of hair from their enemies. If you suspect someone of Soul Puppetry, inspect them immediately for a fetish. It is not a guarantee that they will always have one on them, but it's the\nonly way to confirm for sure.\nSoul Contractors\n-------------------Soul Contractors are capable of fashioning magical legal documents that bind the signer to the very letter of their word. This would be potentially useful, if not for the material they must fashion these\ndocuments on. Soul Contracts can only be written upon the flayed skin of men that was taken whilst they were still alive. It is a brutal and horrifying process, that speaks to the inhumanity of these casters.\n\nHow to Identify:\nLike Soul Puppeteers,\nit is hard to identify a Soul Contractor. The only way to tell for sure is to either catch them in the act, or discover their flaying equipment, which may not even be on their person.\nBlack-Dragon\n     Parasites\n-------------------A more recent addition to dark magic, black-dragon parasites are a growing problem in the Caliphate. A black-dragon parasite is an insidious form of insect that infects its hosts and causes\ncauses them to literally absorb blood and the flesh of the mortal races in return for benefits. It is unknown how is parasite passes from person to person, so it is absolutely vital that you keep any suspected carrier of this foul creature far away from\none's person at all times. It is unknown at this time if Black Dragon Parasite victims can be cured, so it is recommended that they be either expelled from the city on sight, or, in extreme cases, purged.\n\nHow to Identify:\nBlack-Dragon Parasites\nare easy to identify. All carriers of the parasite bear a tattoo of a black dragon on their person, usually winding around the stomach area. If you suspect someone of having this terrible disease, conduct a full-body search immediately.\nGeneral Warning\n    Signs Of A\n    Dark Mage\n-------------------\nDark Mages can and will follow stereotypes at times. If you keep a look out, there are many signs that indicate if a person is just a dark mage in general. These are by no means\ndeciding factors in a suspect's ability to cast black magic, but they are definitely red flags to investigate.\n\nBe Suspicious Of Any Persons you see that:\n\n-Wear Primarily Black Robes.\n\n-Are Hooded at all times\n-Possess bright red eyes.\n\n-Project a magical Aura that Black, Gray, or Red in color.\nAs a guard of the Caliphate, it is up to YOU to root out these psychopathic evildoers wherever they might rise their ugly heads. For the sake of our grand city, do your duty well.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dark Passages", "Mysterious Author", "*This book's cover is entirely black. The material used to craft it seems to be leather, though it's thicker then usual. Whatever it's made out of. It's obvious it's not that of an animals hide.*\n-As you open the book. You'd take notice on how each and every page is made of a thin leather as well. The coloring of each being a light shading. The words written are thinnly laced along too. Diffrent from a regular quills.-\nGreetings ot whom ever reads these words incribed.\nYou now have the chance to learn and take in things that I've experianced on my adventures throughout the diffrent lands we've traversed.\nI've seen many things, though I'll speak of few in these pages. One competely corporal. Though, the other. Not so much.\nThe first I'll speak on is that of those whom once held breath. Once lived as you and I do.\nTasted, laughed. And possibly loved. Though, for such beings. These things matter none to their broken minds. They exist on, after death to carry out one goal. To feast on the warm flesh of the living. To taste the life that runs in\nthe blood that flows through every vein in your body. If you, who reads has such.\nThese creatures that crawl, creep and continue to come after being hit, even after losing limbs. For physical pain is nothing to them.\nThey only feel the lust to feed. To devour all life that harbors in every fiber of a living things body.  Though, I've also witnessed them gnaw on a corpse, long dead as it's dried skin cracked between it's jagged teeth.\nThey seem to be in a constant setting of pain. Though only from their shattered minds trying to cope with realities harsh lessons of how tampering with nature. Can have\nunexpected repercussions. Even in creating\nsuch a being. As few truely take to heart. That monsters do, what monsters are capible of. And that they should be feared by all the living.\n*A detailed picture is penciled in. That showing of three Ghouls. One being a human with a cut neck. The second, an Uruk who's head is half caved in. And the third, a Ghoul Kha that's missing a right arm. All three are reaching out.\nTheir faces all posed in a sorrow-filled expressoin. Though they seem to be clawing.. At the reader, as if to make a point.*\nAs for the second being of darkness I shall decribe, is one that has found a way to ascend in their own sense. Through warping the ways of a certain dart art. They're are to unbind themselves from this realm, though partially\nto say. As their spirit is in a constant struggle. Caught between both the land of the living. And that of the dead. Something anyone would. nd should dread even the thought. Though, from my seeings. I've taken note\nthat some have lost their minds partially. Forgetting and rambling on. Those they knew. Nothing stuck to this one. But others. Are as they were in their mortal shell. Calm for the most part. Though brash all the same when\nspeaking for them in anycase.  For they are in a state of undeath. Damnation that rids them of mortal needs. But a thirst for life still. As I've witnessed them suck the land dry around them. Leaving nothing of a husk of flora\nand trees. Fueling them along in whatever their twisted minds compel them with. Though, if one is wise. And hopefully fast on their feet if not. Then if running into one of these unholy creatures. You could have a talk.\nFor those whom do so. Would say that they hold many secrets. Some willing to share. Others, they keep for only the most trustworthy. Living or otherwise.\n\nRemember. Do not make enemies with a Wight. For death\nis only a setback in their burning, though hollow eyes.\n*On the next page is a penciled drawing of two Wights. Each being vastly diffrent looking. The first, being a hooded figure of a man at first. Though when squinting at the small drawing. You'd then be able to make out\nthe skeletal outline on it's facial features. It's would be hands that of a skeletal appearance as it's eyes give a faint illumnination of a red glow coloured in with some type of dye. The second figure stands to resemble that\nof a Lich. It's would be head missing any trace of flesh at all as it's hollowed out eyesockets glow with nonshaded dots of flames that seem to harbor nothing to burn to. It holds a large staff in both hands. Cradling it to one\nside as it leans towards that angle. Both skeletal figures stand to stare directly outward at the reader.*\nI leave you now to ponder on what's been taught. But remember this. The next time you hear something slam in an alleyway. Or shuffling noises permeate the darkness ahead of you. Think twice on traveling forth. For the\nshadows hold many secrets. Some harmless. Others not so much.\n((No signs of whom wrote the book are given. Only the knowledge provided is set within these pages.))", ""),
        StaticBook("Dating armor", "Tesel Silvervein", "\"Dating Armor\"\n   By Savet Yvonus\n\n\n  Inspired by Orithur\nStep one: Pick the cutest suit of armor in town.\nStep two: Get your gosh darn welly wonky shoes on, make yourself fancy as all heck.\nStep three\" Observe with caution, suits of armor are known to be shy with love.\nSteo four: Pick the right time.  Only during a blue moon will a suit of armor feel willing to take on a mate.  Observe when it's dome is the shinyest. \nStep five: Grease up, It is important for suits of armor to slide easily onto you.\nStep six: Get into position.  You must strip yourself of your earthly possetions, remove the fancy getup you've used to entice and inspire jealousy within the suit.  And once bare, one must spread their arms and legs for ease of limb-access.\nStep seven (Optional)\nOne must exclaim their love for the armor as it sensually slips onto their limbs, encompassing their body with it's cold embrace.  Once you have worn an armor, it is yours for life.\nLife with a suit of armor.\n\nDepending on the reason this suit of armor is alive, life can be either simple or harsh.  If it's sentient, simple husbanhood will do.  If it is not, one has to deal with the constant stigma of folk accusing them of being\ninsane or an armorphile.  But worry not, one's love for armor is true and real.  If it is true, you will never leave your armor.  Your armor is love, and you armor is life.\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\nBuy Grease Muffins\n\n  \"They're greasy!\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Day 1, Kevan the", "Kevan Chester", "Day 1\nTraveled through the Teuton lands, ending up in a ruin infested Jungle. Met a man named Zayden, was warned about bats and rats, Found a strange set of wooden buildings near and in trees. Found a candle lit stoneyard, with large flying creatures\nabove it. I may die, but I will cross or attempt to. Now following a blood trail in a savannah. Still no clue where I am, but perhaps that is for the best. Sins require petenance, and Sermonosi will let me repent or deal me justice as I have earned.\nPigmen on the Horizon...I might not survive this. A Hellish landscape with a tower in the distance. The Three gods have abandoned me here, or else I am outside their domain. A ruined fort lies across Rivers of lava, and a burning forest as well.\nThe sea and Storm are far away, and the sun blocked. Sermonosi protect me. I have appear to quite literally reached the end of the world, and will be turning back. Floating Islands of hell await. Found a Castle back in the Savannah, will seek refuge there\nNo one at the Castle, entering the valley with Scythes, Mills, and Lights among the grey. It appeared to be a abandoned Mine area, with pulleys and drills of crystal. Odd place to have it, perhaps an old dwarven mine? As I near a darkened pillar I can\nfeel a great aura of darkness...This area is covered with a sickness. Trees with fading crystals line the landscape ahead, and it seems the sickness is weak here. It must be centred at that mine. There lies an entrance into the hillside, I think I shall\nbrave it. I must find someone to keep this record after I fill it so much, it is far too valuable to lose, and Sermonosi would never forgive me. A strong pillar lies further on, lighting the area. I seem to be in an oasis in the valley. Lovely place.\nI have found a statue of an Orenian Aengul. Interesting thing, with a bare bookshelf. Might have a book existed here before? Was it taken? A bridge statue, says Eh' Torien Mezzenia. I stop in another grey area...to tired to carry on, my phantom fingers\ntwitching. Hopefully tomorrow I shall continue.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dear Dawn", "Idril Aureon", "Dear Dawn,\n\n  I'm sorry about what happened at your house. I'll try to keep them under control though I know it'll be hard. We're going to move to a bigger house soon so hopefully that will help.\n\n      -Idril Aureon", ""),
        StaticBook("Dear Elise", "Loren", "Dear Elise,\n\nIt occurs to me, while writing this letter, that I may have given a rather open ended invitation to see each other again. I would like to remedy this. Perhaps you would like to join me for a stroll near Johannesburg? I know you enjoy\ntravelling, and I believe this may be a good way to speak more. If you would like, send me a bird to specify the time and day. \n\nIt has also occured to me that I know not how to get this letter to you. I will drop it off at your home,\nhopefully it will reach you there. \n\nI have also included a tulip. I hope this does not seem too forward of me, but I was unsure what would be suitable. I hope you enjoy it. \n\n~Loren Allson\n{\"text\":\"\"}\nOOC:\n\nMessage me on the forums, if i'm not here. Same username, Zoslore. Lol. \n\nOh no, I just realized Elise is blind and can't even read this omg", ""),
        StaticBook("Death of Availer", "Josef Timothee", "THE DEATH OF THE\n WANDERING WIZARD\n\n\nOn Ahad, the 8th of the Deep Cold, 1336, the world of Aegis was struck by a terrible tragedy. I, Josef Timothee, record here my own experience during these events.\nI was in Al'Khazar when a voice rang out, filling all of Aegis. It identified itself as the Wandering Wizard. He said that he had three relics that needed to be taken to the Cloud Temple. If they were to fall into Undead hands, he claimed, terrible\ntrouble would result for the people of Aegis. He sent forth a cry over all the lands, asking for support on the journey from Al'Khazar to the Cloud Temple on the King's Road. A large crowd assembled with him in Al'Khazar, mostly humans but\nrepresentatives from other races there as well.\nThe procession headed down the King's Road and was immediately attacked. Lightning rained down from the skies, and monsters appeared out of thin air. But those in the crowd were ready, and struck back against Iblees minions. The monsters were defeated\nthrough sheer numbers of those opposing them, as well as the powerful magic of the Wandering Wizard. All along the journey, he kept up words of encouragement and urged the crowd onwards. The lightning and monsters were relentless, delaying\nthe journey terribly.\nBy the time the procession reached the Cloud Temple many had died trying to protect the Wizard en route. It was there that the Undead suddenly struck the most violently I have ever witnessed, not only casting lightning powerful enough\nto damage the Cloud Temple, but also changing the landscape around it to look like the Nether. Among this, explosions and lightning were striking everywhere, causing great suffering. The Wizard urged all present to take shelter in the Cloud Temple.\nI took this advice, having been clipped by lightning and set ablaze. Once inside, the extent of the damage was clear. Hundreds entered the Temple, many wounded by burns or monsters. The Temple shook as explosions rocked it from outside and pieces of it\nbroke off. Then...\n\nA new voice rang out, saying that the Wizard had been slain by the Undead. The outpouring of grief was immediate, and the attacks on the Temple ceased.\nSomeone shouted that the Undead had taken three objects from the Wizard that looked like eggs. The skies lightened, the landscape changed back, and the crowd left the Temple. But the world was altered permanently with the death of the\nWandering Wizard. It remains to be seen what the Undead will do with the stolen relics.", ""),
        StaticBook("Decapitation", "Regale Ba'ikana", "Track down the beast that attacked Dirk and bring back it's head.", ""),
        StaticBook("Decorative Book", "Septimus", "This book and quill is meant to decorate Keening's grind room, and serves no other use but that. If you're reading it, you should probably be thrown off the Krag.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dedicant notes", "Kasfer", "Dedicant stuff\nTask one and two: Make a thing, give it to Oori. Then research Aspects, then make a thing about them. Complete!\nTask three and four: Get a task from another guide. then meditate and discover.. something. Complete!\nTask Five: Raisea sapling as a friend, until Oo'ri sees fit to plant it. Complete!\n\nI IZ DROOD yey", ""),
        StaticBook("Defaced Journal", "Owl", "The Barriers.\n\nAfter Fox's fourth experiment proved successful, we have managed to manifest physical barriers capable of repelling both organic and inorganic material.\n\nUnfortunately they appear to have a fragile composition-\nat the moment, and can be broken quite easily. Though Sister Fox intends to improve upon her studies with this, Brother Lion lending his aid.\n\nI will be keeping to my own research and documentation. More information on barriers can be found in-\n... [!] The rest is missing. The ripping suggests it was purposeful.", ""),
        StaticBook("Deity Magic", "Gallidron Elindrow", "I I\n             I I\n       ___\\I I/___\n       ----I I----\n         `~/I I\\~'\n             I I\n             I I\n             \\/\n            The\n   Power  of  Prayer\na guide to deity magic\n             By\n   Gallidron Elindrow\nDeity magic, unlike arcane magic, is highly contingent upon the relationship between the \"caster\", for lack of a better term, and the source of their power. For example a cleric or an aengulic faith may recieve great power from their patron aengul. Given\nthat they are trusted enough and have gained sufficient favor with the patron. Indeed, the practitioner of deity magic must learn to rely almost wholly upon their otherworldy masters and their whims for a scrap of their might.\nIn these pages I will attempt to list and off a brief explanation as the to each of the known branches of Deity Magic.\n~ONE~\n        The Cleric\n-------------------Clerics tend to gain power through the worship of the \"Creator\" and the veneration of His Aenguls. The powers gained depend largely upon the aengul from which they come though are usually\ncentered around healing, light and protection.\nThe aenguls are listed here.\nAeriel- Arch~aengul and caretaker of souls\nEshtael-Balance and destiny\nGazardiael-curiosity and new beginings\nNemiisae- aengul queen of spiders\nTahariae- purity and patron of clerics\nWandering Wizard- An aengul who wander the seven lands.\nWyrvun- Cold and virtue\nYeu Rthulu- contentment and compassion\nXan- order\nMost clerics venerate Tahariae or Xan though worship of the others is not unheard of.\n*TWO*\n           Druids\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~Druidism is perhaps the oldest of the deity magics, but this depends on whom you speak with. The druids have, for ages taken it upon themselves to protect nature and to keep its secrets. They order of\ndruids is most definately an old one and has survived relatively unchanged. This is due to the certain level of indoctrination that take place amoung the acolytes who seek to join the order. This process is called Dedicancy and is evidently\nquite effective. After some time of being given tasks to complete and lectures to attend, the worthy new-comer is led to a pool of attunement and placed in its waters. The high concentration of druidic energies there attune the mind of the individual to\n\"The will of nature\", or so it is said. Whether or not this is the case the druid gains impressive control over nature and usually becomes wholly devoted to protecting the natural world.\nThe powers of the druid, so far as I have been able to catalog are listed here.\n\nCONTROL OF NATURE-\nA druid can coax life from even the driest ground. They can cause trees to spring immediately from tiny saplings. They can\ntie their foes in vines and mold trees into new shapes. The Druid is a master of manipulating nature in almost endless ways.\n\nBLIGHT HEALING- When necromancy is used there is often an occurance of blight. The land becomes cursed and all life in it withers\nIt is within the druids power to remedy this, though depending on the strength of the blight it may take time and more than one druid.\n\nHEALING- Druids are talented healers that seem to increase the bodies natural ability to heal itself. It is said that\nonly monks and clerics are better at it.\n\nSHAPE SHIFTING- This is perhaps the most facinating branch of their magic (no pun intended). The Druid, when powerful enough, can change their very physical and biological make-up and become a mariad of different\nthings. Not much is known about this abillity, in fact very few even know about it. Even I, who have read all I can find on the subject, am not sure if it is even a reality or just a rumor. One thing remains certain, that this is one of the most closely\nguarded secrets of the druids.\n\nCOMMUNION WITH NATURE- This is perhaps the most important of the druid's abillities. Not because it is the most powerful or awe inspiring to witness, but because this is from where all their other powers stem.\nIn truth the druid does not command nature. They speak with it and ask it to do things for them, and if nature is willing it complies.\n%Three%\n          Shamans\n-------------------It is believed that Shaman originated from the orcs. As the story goes, thinner, smaller orcs were thought to be more apt at intellectual persuits than the brutal aspects of a stronger orc's\nlife, and so the art of Shamanism was born. These orcs learned to commune with spirits of various natures and there by gain magical power of various natures as well. The entire practice of Shamanism has to do with the contact and appeasment of spirits.\nThe spirits are catagorized into three different types.\n\nELEMENTAL- These are spirits of the elements and embody the aspect that they represent.\n\nIMMORTAL- These represent various aspect of life. These spirits are not so flashy\nbut are highly sought for various reasons. For examply, one might commune with the spirit of the hunt if they wish to be \"blessed\" in their hunting efforts. There other Immortal spirits of course, each having to do with different aspects; Honor, strength,\nhusbandry, battle, wisdom, ect...\n\nANCESTRAL- These are the spirits of the dead. Those who came before and might be called upon to offer wisdom and proctection. They are often refered to as Ancestrals rather than spirits.\nGREAT SPIRITS- While not exactly one of the three base distinctions, it is wise to denote that a Great Spirit is of some import. They are the most powerful of their kind. The is a great fire elemental spirit as there is a great spirit of fertility, and so\non. These are akin to kings over their kind of spirit.\n\nShamans call upon these spirits to gain different effects though most develope an affinity for one or another.\nThese shaman subtypes are as follows.\nELEMENTALIST- A caller of elemental spirits to devistating effect.\n\nFARSEER- One who communes with Immortal spirits to gain blessings that increase strength, prowess, healing, ect...\nLATAUMAN- Uses Ancestrals to increase their combat prowess.\n\nWITCHDOCTOR- These interesting shamans use potions and brews to gain the effects and help of all types of spirits.\nCONCLUSION\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nThese are the main kinds of deity magic users. There are also The Temple Monks and the Muun'Trivazja, but these two sects are not covered in this work.\nIt is my hope that the subject of deity magic has been illuminated\nsomewhat for you and that this book has left you, if not wiser, then more educated at least.\n\n-Gallidron Elindrow\n\nPublication date\n11th of Sun's Smile 1518\nPlease look for my next book!\n\nARCANISTS AND WORSHIPERS\na comparison of magics.", ""),
        StaticBook("Delivery Birds.", "The Scribe.", "DELIVERY BIRDS.\nHow is it that birds are able to find the recipients of letters without knowledge of who they are needed to visit? My theory is that birds can be trained to detect the soulstones of those who need letters delivered to them. If this is true, can\nall animals sense soulstones?\n\nAll musings of course.", ""),
        StaticBook("Desert Bezerkers", "Durza Volkihar", "The Orcs of the desert are bezerking abominations.They crave war and fighting. the majority of fights i have been in and have witnessed have been created by orcs.They do not speak a normal tounge.Their tounge isnt as elegant as the elfs or a simple as the\nmen of oren or the dwarves.Their language is called the blah.The blah shouldnt even be considered a language at all, it is just a series of grunts and guttaral sounds.They often resort to eating people to stop there endless hunger for meat and blood.\nThere are three types of Orcs:\n\nThe Uruk: The Uruk is the most common of the orcish blood.They have a very limited volcabulary and a limted brain size.They are very skilled in combat though.\nThe Goblin: The goblin is considered the smartest of the race of orcs but the weakest and smallest. What they lack in braun they make up for in brain size and wit.\nThe Olog: The Olog is the strongest and powerful of all the orc's. They are the dumbest of all the orc's. They do not possess the ability to think. They are mindless beasts built for one pupose, war\nIt is obvious that the orcs are a race that only cares about war. The only execption for that is the goblins who would rather tinker with devices than fight every creature they come across. The word negotiate is not in their vocabulary.\nIf you share these views come find me.\n\n\n[!] A red eagle is drawn here.", ""),
        StaticBook("Desert Herbs", "Laerean", "=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=Herbs of the Desert\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=All herbs organized in alphabetical order and separated by lines to save space.\nVol. 1 in the series of herbal books.\nHerb count - 12.\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=Blood Grapes, instead of using water, for some reason, uses blood. The seeds are burried beneath the sand in a deep hibernation. After a good amount of blood is taken in, it begins to grow out of the sand.\nThe herb is rare though\nunless it is planted by someone. When it blossoms, it shows crimson red flowers, and these flowers are normally used by orcs for warpaint and rations.\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=Blood Lotus is an alchemical ingredient with a moderate fire symbol. The red vine-like bush grows on cave enterances, growing down the ceiling and acting as a curtain keeping the cave cool. The vines are easily harvested, and\ncan be used to make a nutrient-rich soup that one could theoretically live off of. But if it is fermented, it can be made into a strong red alcohol.\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=Cactus is a prickly little plant, being painful to step on. It is found normally in the harshest deserts. If you cut it just above the base, it can be heated into a furnace to become softer. This soft substance can then be rolled into\nfabric and be smoked to get high, though it is very addictive.\nOther than a drug, it can be used as a dye. No alchemical uses.\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=Clutcher's Straw is an alchemical ingredient with a moderate earth symbol. It is commonly mistaken as\ndead grass, but when uprooted it has pitch black roots, with ends as sharp as a knife.\nThe effects, if eaten locks up the person's jaw, but if used in potions it can be used to impair someone, though only weakly. Effects can be increased. \n=-=-=-=\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=The Desert Berry Bush is an alchemical ingredient with a moderate earth symbol. It looks like a withered rose bush with no leaves, but if it is cut then one would find the insides to be green, instead of dead brown like a normal\ndead bush. Every full moon this plant gives red berries, but get them quickly, because they don't last long because the animals find them quite lovely!\nThough if someone ate the stalk, they would be confronted with a lot of juice, and if drank enough\nit can kill within the day.\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=The Drake's Tail is an alchemical ingredient with a strong fire symbol. The herb has a dusky color, making it spotted easily. It has long, sharp thorns that jut from its surface and sometimes\nwraps around a rock.\nDrake's Tail is a rare herb, although it is resilient, strong, and quite sharp but it only grows in very particular conditions of moisture, dryness, and humidity. Gather with protection though, as the thorns are laden with a fever\ninducing poison. The plant's alchemical uses vary, but are mainly used in poisons.\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=Goblin's Ivy is an alchemical ingredient with a weak earth symbol. The short vine and leaves are usually seen clinging to the sides of buildings,\nmountains, ruins, or anything else that would allow it. It is commonly considered a weed though, but it is able to be used to create weak poisons. What is more interesting is that it can actually boost some resilience potions such as Stoneskin.\n=-=-=-=\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=Gijakul, also named the \"Bloodflower\" is a very rare alchemical ingredient with a moderate fire symbol.\nIt is a very rare herb found growing in deserts, especially orc lands. It is known for its crimson petals that give off an odor\nsimilar to that of rotting flesh. The flower is normally found next to Gijakul trees that have adapted to the climate by growing near the banks of river or an oasis. Another thing to note is the faint glow that it emits for a short period of time after\ndusk. The effect mostly appears during the time they bloom though, and they only bloom during a blood moon, giving them the signature name of \"Bloodflower\". The herb has healing potentials, but is mostly kept to the Shamans, as it is considered a gift\nfrom the spirits. It also represents life.\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=Javens is an alchemic ingredient with a weak water symbol. This plant is usually found in deserts, especially orcish deserts. Javens is a large sand spur with green colored going along the\ngreen plant. Other than its thorns, it is soft and easy to chew. It is commonly used by field doctors though, as when it is eaten the victim has 5 minutes before they became drowsy and fell asleep. With the right recipe, an alchemist can extend the\nperiod of unconsciousness that one would normally have if it was eaten.\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=The Murex Cactus is an alchemical ingredient with a moderate water symbol. It is an odd little cactus with a squat, spiraled cone structure.\nIt is named after the murex shell, a type of conch featuring long spines. The murex cactus is covered in small barbs, but features several larger spines positioned along the path of its spiral. The cactus is partially hollow, with walls in its interior\nthat break up its spiral into thin pods. Each of which are filled with a clear sap that causes vivid, primarily positive and fun hallucinations if drank in large enough quantities. Fumes from burning the sap can also cause hallucinations if inhaled. The\nherb represents fluidity, due to its hallucinating effects. Remember, drink the sap, don't eat the cactus itself.\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=The Wisps of Old is an alchemical ingredient with a strong air symbol. The extremely fragile flower is found growing\non cacti. The flower only grows and blooms on the cactus for 7 years, and after the night it blooms the flower will die. One requires very steady hands and a lot of care to remove it from the cactus, as if anything on the flower breaks it will die. If\nthe flower is taken before blooming though, it can remain alive indefinitely if nothing on it is harmed. When it blooms, whatever the person says in a ten second period will repeat in a low whisper, until the flower dies. No alchemical uses.\n=-=-=-=-=\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=Zawabate is an alchemical ingredient with a moderate water symbol. The blossom is as rare to find in a desert as an oasis. The green and yellow plant has a tall stalk, with short curvy petals. The blossom is found growing in the fertile\nground near the waters of the oasis it resides within. The herb, if consumed, induces strong hallucinations.\nIt is also used to increase the effects of healing potions, but use it in moderation because it can become a mind destroying poison.\n=-=-=", ""),
        StaticBook("Deserting Beggar", "Raymond Ronjon", "The Deserting Beggar\n\nOnce, there was a lad name Brenuin, Brenuin wasen't the richest fellow, quite the oppisite, he was one of the poorest fellows in Felsen. While Brenuin may have been able to steal a fishing rod or two and catch fish on the docks of\nFelsen, he still wished he could do better.\n\nSo when a recruiter stopped Brenuin, despite the rags, in the markets, he felt he was up on his luck, which he never is. He said Aye, whats that? Food a bed, and a roof to sleep under!\nSign me up! However, this recruiter was a Gold Corps recruiter, Aye it was all rainbows and sunshine the first week, wear a uniform, get a room, get some food and a little mina, it wasent like that for long.\nSoon they had Brenuin watching the tortures, of\nthe Rebel soldiers, He had to fight Rebel Soldiers, while it may have been part of the job he realized something.. These soldiers.. They were just like him.. Except.. Something was different about them.. Then it hit him, they had purpose, reason a will to\nfight for something rightous, he was just some street urchin that ain't killing for nothing but a little bit of bread. At the end of the day he thought, is that really worth it? He struggled with this for weeks, Till he came to a conclusion, he was to\nleave, the Gold Corps wouldnt let him leave of course.. They needed manpower and if they just let one person leave everyone would leave, so he bough a suit with the mina he had earned, in the middle of the night he slipped out his window, nearly breaking\nhis leg mind you, and deserted the Gold Corp. some months later when he was traveling the rodes he found himself sitting in Krakens Watch, when another man, much like the Gold Corp recruiter came up to him, Brenuin had heard this story much before, except\nthis time, this time, he would be fighting for something, to protect the people of Krakens Watch, while he couldn't live with the Gold Corps torture he could live in Krakens Watch, however, he decided for good old times he'd go fish in Felsens harbor one\nmore time. As he was making his way to the docks, he saw a Kha up on the roof's and heard the rush of horses, none other then the Gold Corp horses, clearly that Kha was in some deep shit. So he shouted at the Gold Corp's men, what was going on, when there\nhe was, the silver-tounged recruiter, he walked up with a smug smile on his face and said eh, we found you dident we Brenuin, dont mess with us, next thing Brenuin knew, he was on a chopping block in Carnatia, never knew what happened to that damnable Kha\nhe risked his damn life for.\n\nThis is a true story about a beggar in Felsen named Brenuin", ""),
        StaticBook("Desmond Report", "Desmond Thistle", "Desmond Thistle\nFootman\nThe Amber Cold\n1591\n\nIt started off as a uneventful month. Me and other men were called upon to help recruit men into the army. I failed to recruit any. I did some watch duty, nothing out of ordinary happened. A\ncouple days later, me and Dan practiced sparring. I did some more gate watching. I met a couple of the new recruits and showed them some of the ropes. Then, when watching the gate, Ljhin decided to join me. I let someone in, she slapped me, we know the re\nst of the story. She was fined, I was not. Dan was whipped for arresting me.\nSigned\nDesmond Thistle\nFootman", ""),
        StaticBook("Diary 1", "Johanna Downer", "15th of the Amber Cold, 1560\n\nI figured I should start writing, just to take up some time.My name is ███████ ██████, and I live with the ████████. I’m ten years old now. I think my adoptive dad is ████, but he’s rarely around so I live here. My favorites\nare██████████, they’re really nice to me. ██████████ was even okay with me liking other girls. She told me there was nothing wrong with me, but I know there is.\n\n███ is █████’s wife, they have a kid together. She’s too young to play with still.\nI bought a training blade today, I spent too much but it looked sturdy. It’s very well crafted, at least. My dad, birth dad, used to say that it was best to have something of quality than having to replace it. I think he was talking about me.\n17th of Snow’s Maiden, 1561\nI’m taking a break from trying rope to make fishing nets to sell. My inheritance will be here in three years next month. It’s a lot, ████ said it was around five thousand. I guess my dad's new wife didn't really like him all\nthat much after all.\n\nI met a man in dark clothing, he said he didn’t know his name but he was nice. Mia told me about him, he wants to get rid of religion but I don’t know about it.\n17th of the Grand Harvest, 1561\n\nI reported Mia. I feel so bad about it, but her friends are bad. I pray I did the right thing, and God smiles upon me.\n\n\nI’m starting to be trained to fight, I’m not very good but I’ll get stronger.\n9th of Sun’s Smile, 1562\n\nNot much interesting has happened, I started really training with Merilon. He’s an elf with white hair, he lets me call him Meri because I’m young. He’s not very nice, and I remember █████ mentioned being beaten by him.\nI need to practice more, get stronger.\n15th of Malin’s Welcome, 1565\nI’m 15 now, and it’s been a while since I wrote here. I still like girls, but the ████████ accept me for who I am. I have my dad’s inheritance, 5500 mina from interest included now.\n21st of Suns Smile, 1565\n\nI joined the Red Brothers in the dreadlands. I don’t know what to think of them, I have more of a chance to make a mark on the world here than in Oren. I don’t know if █████ will be angry, or worse disappointed.\nI just want to make him proud, he's like my dad.\n\nI watched a man die today. A spy mali’ame. I’m just realizing, I didn’t feel anything at all. I feel sick now.  Maybe all the corpses in Felsen made me colder, less feeling. One of the first ones\nwas a small boy, probably barely even walking. Cradled in his mother’s cold and lifeless arms.\n\n\nEven with that, it could be great here. I could be great.\n23rd of Amber Cold, 1565\n\nWell I fucked up. I think Millosm thinks I’m a spy, because Mia showed up at the bone fort. I need to just lay low for a while, keep to myself. Or that may make things worse. I don't know what to do, I hope things get better soon\n7th of Malin’s Welcome, 1566\n\nThings have gotten better over time, but I think Audra may be questioning my mental state. That’s alright, I may decide to milk it further. Sometimes the best way to do things is to make people question, but not know for\nsure. People fear the unknown, after all. But, I’m not sure if I want that. Right now I just need to do a good job.\n\nNobody takes me seriously, saying ‘you’re just a kid’. I murdered a man today, at least ten years older than me. It was so easy, and when\nI left I felt like I did something wrong but also excitement. My heart pounded in my ears, even as I remembered the last look in his eyes before he died. The pain on his face as the blood seeped from his skull. His last word. I wonder if the monks managed\nto save him. I hope they did.\n16th of the Grand Harvest, 1566\nHer name is Sumnia, and one eye is as green as the grass and tree’s leaves. The other is as blue as the ocean. Her hair matches the forest come autumn. She was enslaved by the beings known as orcs for three long years.\nShe’s terrified, and every word I spoke to her was another cruel mistruth hammered into my conscience. She is not safe with us, soon her former captors will return and haul her back to a life of slavery.\n\nBut I can’t let my emotions cloud my judgement. My\nloyalties lie with the brothers, and if I speak a word of warning then I’ll be sent to Iris’s mercy. Or rather her blade. My skin will be hauled up for all to see, I can’t let my emotions take control of me. I need to be strong. I will not forget her.\n\nI\nwill not forget. I pray she sleeps well, and her end is quick and painless.\n8th of The Deep Cold, 1566\nIt’s so cold here. I hate the cold.\n19th of Malin’s Welcome,1567\nAxis, or Atlas as he’s named now is mine. I had to pay Lhindir for some reason, but I can’t remember why, all I remember is blinking and being somewhere new, with Atlas and myself injured. He’s off making friends right now, I\njust hope the world is as good to him as I hope to be. He’s still learning, and probably scared about whatever happened to us.\n16th of The First Seed, 1567\nAtlas is learning fast, and I finally understand why people say their heart swells with pride. He showed a man mercy, after he had apparently tried to sell him to the ones who sought to rip him away from me. I can't help but\nwonder, is he truly safe with me? Would it be best if I gave him up?\n19th of the Amber Cold, 1567\nI met with Mia today, and we kissed. But then Lhindir showed up, and threatened us with his golem. Mia tried to stand up for us both, but I managed to appease him.\n\nMia, as sweet as she is, doesn't understand how the\ndreadlands work. It’s like a pond, big fish eat the smaller fish if they can. The small fish either die before they grow, or lay low as they slowly grow larger. The smart ones survive, and I fully intend to be a smart one.\n\nI understand now. When left to\ntheir own devices, the descendants can be little else but evil and self destructive.\n18th of Snow’s Maiden, 1568\nHaakon is going to kill himself, and Audra is ill. I’m worried, but I need to hope. I have to keep hope. My friend from when I lived on the streets always said we have to hope things will get better. Hope is the strongest thing\nyou can have, after all. I hope she was right. I hope we’ll all be okay.\n\n\nI don’t think we will.\nI remember sitting in church, looking up to Audra. She was a holy dame, and I remember the feeling. Excitement. Admiration. Hope. I wanted to do that with my life, so I asked █████ to teach me to fight. God how I wish I could go back, when the world was\nshiny and beautiful.\n\nMaybe I can keep it that way for Atlas, if I try hard enough. For now, hope may be the only thing I have going for me.\n11th of Snow’s Maiden, 1569\nNjord is dead. Audra, I don’t want to talk about. Millosm is missing. Haakon is as good as dead, even hearing his name now enrages me. The cowardly traitor defected to Oren, and I feel ill when I think of him. He should have\nkilled himself.\n\nAtlas is missing, and I think he went into the sea. I hope he’s happy there, and of course safe. I hope I was able to teach him the beautiful parts of the world before he learned of the ugly.\n\nThere are a lot of new people, and I don't\nrecognize almost all of them. But I guess that means they don’t know me, so I can make a fresh start with them. I hope I can make new friends.\n9th of Malin’s Welcome, 1670\nAll good things eventually must end. I learned this not long ago, I ended my relationship with Mia. I loved her, but I had to. I still love her.\n\nAdditionally I’m pregnant. Nobody will know, but the father is an Orener. The\ngrand mayor of Felsen.\n\n\nThe truce Lhindir was forced into may be broken, as well. I hope he doesn’t go after my child, if he decides to attack me. I need to grow stronger.\n17th of Malin’s Welcome, 1670\nMy child is dead. Bradshaw, his father, killed him. I cannot properly express my rage, my pain. I considered him a friend, but look at what he did to me. To my child, to his child. I don't know how, but I will get revenge. I\ndon't care the cost, as long as he pays.  I can’t help but think one thing.\n\n\nHappy birthday, ███████.\n8th of the Grand Harvest, 1670\nI am nothing, and that has become painfully obvious. Hakon moved on from me in under a month, to some bright eyed Qali woman. I can’t help but hate her, she looks like what I used to before my child died. I want to be\nhappy, but it seems I’m not fated to be lighthearted and joyful. I’m fated to grieve, no have my heart torn and broken and reaved. She’s fated to he happy, and I’m fated to cry myself to sleep and stare at an empty cradle. Why does she deserve happiness\nand not me?\n4th of Snow’s Maiden, 1571\nI could have had my child back, but like the poor mother I am I threw the chance away. My baby’s body burnt to ash, and he’s gone forever. My sweet Emrys is gone forever.\n17th of Snow’s Maiden, 1571\nI wish I could just die, just close my eyes and never have to open them again. Last night I could have sworn I heard a babe cry out, and I felt my heart flutter with hope. Sadly it was just my imagination playing a cruel joke.\nI could die. I sit on top of the bone fort, empty space below my feet. I have nobody to miss me, nobody to mourn. Nobody.\n\nIt’s been exactly a year since I lost my son.\n10th of The Grand Harvest, 1571\nThe world is new, and once again I find myself hopeful. I wonder if I’ll be able to find happiness here, in Axios.\n\n\nIt’s a little easier to smile.\n10th of The Amber Cold, 1571\nMy sweet Emrys will never have legitimate justice. He will never be avenged, and I will be left to mourn him alone. Sparing Bradshaw was a mistake, one I will likely never forget, nor do I want to forget. With a heavy heart, I\nwill continue on.\n\nI’ve been reading over my past entries, how I wish I could go back. ███████ ██████ is dead, she died with her son. I miss her, I miss being truly happy. I miss being able to smile.\n21st of Snows Maiden, 1572\nI died, or at least I think I did. I don’t know why I’m here or what happened, but I did somehow. I don’t know how I can move this charcoal, either. But that's beside the point.\n\n\n(Continued in Diary 2)", ""),
        StaticBook("Diary 2", "Johanna Downer", "I guess the woman I used to be is dead literally now. I took the liberty of wiping out all the sensitive names, just in case.\n\nI can feel a deep anger consuming me, swallowing me whole until nothing is left but my rage. I don't know why, but my desire for\nfor revenge is even stronger than before. I need to get revenge, not just on Bradshaw. All criminals.\n\n\nI hate my new body. I hate what I am. I hate that I still exist. I hate not being able to be with my son, and most of all I hate Oren.\n11th of Sun’s Smile, 1572\nVinoth, or Adedontus, knows who I was now. I have a feeling he will go after me, or worse my family. I know my father could easily survive if he was attacked, but I worry about the others. Additionally he is aging, and I dread\nthe day he succumbs to old age, even if he’s only in his forties. I am immortal, unchanging, while my loved ones are not.\n\nI’ve realized, in my time alone. I may be bound by my duty to punish criminals, but I am the judge, jury, executioner and lawmaker.\n17th of Malin’s Welcome, 1573\nThree years have passed like days, and today my grief grows stronger. Emrys died three years ago today, and I have found a quiet corner of the Abyss to mourn.\nI have another death to carry, Lucus Song. I don’t know what happened and I probably never will. All I can do is pray to a God that turned his back on me that my friend is resting well.\n15th of The Deep Cold, 1573\nFor the first time in a while I started crying and I couldn’t stop. I had nearly every shred of happiness ripped from me, and even now I’m a shell of the woman I used to be. I wish I could grasp the hands of time and turn\nthem back, back to the days I would play and laugh. I would do anything to be able to go back.\n\nBut I was not destined for a life of joy. I will never be a mother, I will never marry, I will never grow old with the one I love. I will spend forever in an\nagonizing limbo, unable to rest or see my son.\n\n\nJust five years ago I was smiling, joking, laughing. Hoping. Loving. But all of those things are gone, and all that remains is my sorrow.\n15th of The Deep Cold, 1574\nI have finally realized fully that the woman who I was is dead. The woman who laughed, joked, cried is gone, and I am what is left. All that I am is my animus, my rage. My hatred.\nI’m sorry, father. I wish I could have made you proud.\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\nA list is jammed here.\n\nThere are small sketches by each name of a smiling, happy face.\n\n\nWulfric Borr\nNjord Ruric\nAudra Vibren\nLucus Song", ""),
        StaticBook("Diary of Death 1", "Jistuma", ".         -   \n        /          ,\n-       .             \\\n             -             \n  /                *\n         _        -  '\n   \\           d\n     .       .     a   /\n  ,        \\     -  r\n         -            k\nthe night is long\n\n\n\n          never ending\n\n\n\nnever started\ne\n  t\n   e\n   r                     e\n  n                     m\n a                     p\nl                      t\n                      y\nMy existance the same\n\n\n              Wandering around eternaly\n\n\nNothing to feel\nNothing to\n\nSEE\n        s      l  l\n          m ee\n\n   l                 t o\n    i                    u\n     s              h c\n      t\n       e       etsat\n        n\nEmptiness\n\n\nall around\neverywhere\nthere\nomnicient\nhere\non all sides\nhere\nhere\n    here    here here\nMyself am unique\n   I exist where else\nnothing is born\n\n   I exist where else\nnothing is seen\n\n   I exist where else\nnothing is alive\n\n   I exist\n                   alone", ""),
        StaticBook("Diary of Death 2", "Jistuma", "T\n    I\n    M\n     E\n\n\n      was it over?\n\n\n  had my time came?\n\n\n \n     has time stopped?\nI can't tell\n\nOne circle.\nOne cicle\nOne line\nOne lie\nOne day?\nNo sun\n                No moon\nNo cold\n             No warmth\nNo light\n          Only the dark\nWhen does the day end\nWhen does the night\nWhen does the seed\nWhen does the year\n\n\nEnd      end\n  END               end\n         end end\n     end             END\nEND IT\n                end it\n            end this\n  end it      life\n\n     end this      end it      existance \n\nend it          end this\n     end it    darkness\nend it\n end it          end it\n    end it         end it\n\n             end it\n  end it \n            end it  end it         end it\nend it\n                end it\n       end it\n\nwhy doesn't it end\nMy solitude has damaged me\n\nAlone and broken\n\n\n         So much so\n\n\n\nThat I see dark wings\n       In a dark world", ""),
        StaticBook("Diary of Death 3", "Jistuma", "B   L   A   C   K\n\n\nW   I   N   G   S\n\n\n\n\nD   R   E   A   M   S\n\n?   ?   ?   ?   ?   ?\nWhy\n\n\nWhy after so long\n     Why now that I dream\n\n  So long I suffered\nalone  empty  broken\n\nWhy after so long\n     Why am I dreaming\nThere is nothing but darkness\n    It was dark\n\nNothing can be seen\n    It was black\n\nNothing to hear\n    I heard a roar\n\nNothing to feel\nhope\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\nhope\n{\"text\":\"\"}\nhope\nhope\nhope\n\n\n\n hope\n\n\n                   hope\n\n\n\n\nhope\nhope\n\n\n I heard it again\n                   hope\n\n\n      I saw darkness\nagain\n\n    hope\nIts roar\n\n   Its wings\n\n\n       Its magnitude\n\n\n\nIt is hope\nAnd once more in an eternity\n\n\n       I see light\n       I feel warm\n       I see the fire\n       I am not alone", ""),
        StaticBook("Diary of Death 4", "Jistuma", "Radiant is the\n     Black Sun\nShinning darkness in\nthis Abyss\n\nBringing warmth to the\ndeceased\n\n\n\n\nRadiant\nis the Black Sun\nI'm no longer alone, together with a few\n\nThe end of eternity,\nthis is something new\n\n\n\n\nRadiant is\nthe Black Sun\nWe feel, we see, we taste, smell and hear\n\nThe light so grand, we have nothing to fear\n\n\n\nRadiant\n    is the\n        Black Sun\nRadiant\n     is\n         the\n            Black\n                    Sun\nI feel alive\n\nAfter so long\n\n          After so long\n\nRadiant is the\nBlack Sun\nThe solitude I felt\n\n Gone\n              It's over\n   Finaly I'm not alone\n\n\nNot anymore\n        Not since he\n                     came\n\nRadiant is the\nBlack Sun\nLike the great sun\n      of long ago\n\n    It kept me warm,\n       I remember\n  This one is warmer\n  This one is bigger\n  This one is greater\n\n\n\nRadiant is\nthe Black Sun\nIt repaired me\n  It game me my sight\n  It is like that wish\n\n  That wish I wished long ago.\n  That wish I forgot\nlong ago.\n\nRadiant is\nthe Black Sun\nI wished for warmth\nI now remember\nI was cold\nI was blind\nI was deaf\nI was dead\n\n                Radiant\n               is the\n            Black\n          Sun\nThe Black Sun\n     brought me life\n         once more\n     brought me a life\n         once more\n     brought me a wish\n         once more\n\n\n\n         once more\nRADIANT\n\n      IS\n\n        THE\n\n           BLACK\n\n                 SUN", ""),
        StaticBook("Diary One", "Mia Noctis", "Mia's Diary\n\nDate *Scratched out*\n     Haru has given me this book to help improve my writing. I tried to tell him it was fine enough for me, but apparently writely neatly is important for later on in life. To keep up with what has happened I'll\njust write down what I've been through so far. \n     After eleven years of living off nature and only going into town for food and ask for money, I met a amazing man named Varstivus. He is a blue elf and loves alchemy. Vars was kind enough to take\ncare of me most of the time. Although I feel like I'm a burden on him. The Rothgard House in the capital to better train myself to protect myself. I love the training cause it gives me something to do rather be in Vars's buisness. I don't wanna bother him\nor anything. After I met these two men I ran into a man named Haru. Haru loves magic and likes to show off hes magic to people. He is really good at it. :)\nThere is also this other man named Sanada. He likes to read but I think he can't tell the differenc\nfrom book to real life, but he has taught me some really cool things like Sky Whales! \nSo I've been living with Vars for some time even though that Rothguard guy in the capital is now registered as my guardian. I don't really understand what this means\nbut I think he's suppose to take care of me. I don't really care either way cause I got Vars to depend on. \nSo that's how it's been for a while. I've done some stupid things like trying to use a pipe, but Vars managed to get the bamboo out of my cheek.\nAnother thing that's happened was that Haru and I went on a little trip around the land looking for a sky whale. I slept most of the time but we managed to find one. The whale was *scratched out* but also like *scratched out*. It was a pretty cool find.\nWe even walked through the desert and found this huge floating ice island. It's suppose to be some sorta of sky island for one of the gods or something, but it was really cool how it was snowing in the desert.\nWe made our way up north and visited the\nhome of the dwarfs. I think that's spelled right. There was this cave filled up with these huge mushrooms that glowed. Haru kept asking people about how he was looking for this man with glasses or something, but no one knew the guy. \nThere was also this\nweird thing in the snowy parts of the north that we found. It was this huge sorta doorway. It kinda looked like some sorta giant curtain covering a window. There was also some baby ones that were titles with the races: humans, wood elves, high elves, ect.\nHaru didn't wanna go through the thing, but I tripped and fell through it. Inside, cause of the signs, we found out the place was called the \"Sunless Sanctum\". There was a temple and marked out words and two towers. One had some sorta lab and we could see\nthe other tower from the top. When I looked over to it there was this -very bright red light- and maybe a person? I'm not sure. I'm not sure how I got home either. I don't remember.\n\nDate *scribbled inlegitably*\n\n     Vars just saved\nme from falling off a building. I don't remember going up to it or even leaving my room. I only remember getting into my bed. Vars told me i was in a \"trance\" and was doing weird things. I think I hurt him. I don't know. Why don't I know? I was to know.\nVars told me i was saying \"Sei speciale\" and the words \"fuggito\", \"demonaco\", and \"per sempre\". I recognize these words. My mom and I made these in a code for when my dad was acting weird or mean. My new mommy doesn't know about it. The only other person\nwho knows about it was Maledetto, my doctor. He left when I had been seven for 3 or so years. I don't remember much or anything about him. Why don't I remember alot of things? Is there more things wrong with me? Why can't I be normal? Why me? Why me? Why?\n*There is a drawing of a little girl and a blue elf on this page in front of a boat. It is drawn very childlike*\n\n*It is clearly a drawing of Mia and Vars in front of the boat outside Chamberry*\n*There is some more scribbles in black and red. It almost appears like multiple symbols and letters have been written over eachother over and over again*\n*At the bottom there is clearly tear spot and scribbleing of questions* \"Why? Why Maledetto? Why?\"\nDate *too poorly written*\n     I had a dream last night. It was my mother. My original mother before she committed suicide. She was saying me something to me. I couldn't understand what she said. Her words came out as muffled, as if she was full of water.\nShe looked so sad when she realized I could not understand her and walked off. I screamed for her, but she did not stop. I turned around and saw Maledetto there. He was covered in blood, MY blood. He looked like an evil had comsumed his eyes and replaced\nthe spaces with bright lights. He grasped my arms and I could not escape. I was trapped. I was frightened. He said to me,\"Che tu possa mai invecchiare. Possiate non crescerà mai. La vostra mente congelata in forma innocente. Fuggire, fuggire, non guardare\nindietro. Per tutti quelli che vedi dietro di voi, sarà andato.\" It was my mother and I's special language. He knew it all too well. It translates to,\" May you never age. May you never grow. Your mind frozen in innocent form. Escape, Escape, do not look\nback. For everyone you behind you, will be gone. \n\n\n\n\nI hope to forget this dream.\n*This portion of the diary appeared to have been stuck, or glued together*\n*There is a picture here of another boat and a green man with a brown man holding a book. It is clearly Haru and Sanada. Sanada is smileing and Haru looks annoyed*\n\n*There is a scribbled sun and clouds. It is very childlike.*\nDate: *Chicken-scratch*\n\n     I saw a pretty thing today. It was raining and the water made little circles on the window and the water made little lights! It was very pretty. I reminded me of stars.\nI wanna go starwatching tonight.\nDate *There is a drawing of a cat here instead*\n\n     Today I sat on a bench all day to see what happened. I saw so many things! I saw Sanada trip on the curb. Haru try to hit it off with the Baker that Sanda went after but then got interrupted by Vars.\nI saw a bird too! It was pretty and red.\nIt's so nice having these distractions in my life.\nI need distractions. I want distractions. Distractions hold me back, and that's what he would have wanted. I don't wanna ever drive someone else away like I\ndrove Maledetto away. I don't know why he left. He was the only other person that felt like family to me besides my mother, but she's gone now, residing at the bottom of the ocean. It's so strange how a man like the Doctor could have done so many horrible\nthings to me and still have a place in my heart. Where has he gone? Why did he leave? Was it my fault? Did i dissapoint him or make him angry? I want to find him, and I think  i know where. *There is a drawing here of a dark tower with a light shining at\nthe top. It appears more detailed and sketched out compared to the childish drawings earlier in the book.*\nDate - Summer\n     I've decided to go to the portal and meet the light. Hopefully, it'll be nice and we can be friends! But if not, then I am sorry if you find this and I haven't come back. I understand how you must feel, cause it's how I feel everyday,\nalone. \nI'm sorry Vars.\nI'm sorry Haru.\nI'm sorry Sanada.\nI'm sorry mommy.\nI'm sorry daddy.\nI'm sorry new mommy.\nI'm sorry cows.\nI'm sorry sister.\nI'm sorry Maledetto.\nI'm sorry Rothgard House.\nI'm sorry me, we shouldve made it.\n*A page or so is torn out here. On further inspection, you can tell through the indentions on the next page that is a poorly sketched out map based upon the stars. The endpoint is titled: Gateway.*\n{\"text\":\"\"}\nDiary Entry\nDate *A date*\n\nHevor is dead. He was beheaded in the Capital by the Guards for just being in the Rothgard House. I guess now I'll either be passed down the family line...\nI wanna ask Vars to be my guardian, at least now legally.\nI feel like I'm at home here, like nothing can go wrong.. But the Guards in the Capital killed Hevor, and I'm apart of the Rothgard House because he was my guardian. They chased me when I was coming home. I think they may be drunk, but i was so scared. I\ngot Vars and this girl names Azuline died my hair and gave me new clothes. I guess now I'm hidden.. \nI'll be okay here with Vars though.\nHe'll be there for me.", ""),
        StaticBook("Diary, Vol. 1", "Splen", "12 of The Amber Cold, 1590.\n\nMet Dewlox and another, older looking biggum in that one Island City nearby ... I forget the name already. Fashioned a cozy burrow today, and made a wool delivery. Met the town sherrif and a deputy of sorts.\nMy burrow is close to what the Sherrif called \"an old abandoned church for humans\" or something of the sort. It makes me nervous. I'll be planting plenty of trees to block my view of it, and I doubt I'll put any windows on that side of my den.\nDewlox (is he a dwarf? hard to tell under all the armor) showed my GIANT DUCKS in the lake around the Big City. How terrifying. The city itself was incredibly huge. Why do all biggums make their dwellings so preposterously large?\nWould love to find a way to make the village of Reedsborough more mercantile ... but how can we attract merchants when all is so barren around here? Just a handful of halflings here, and I only saw TWO biggums in the city nearby.\nThere are two storage facilities here, one \"official\" one and one by the aviary. Not having a central storage may drive me bonkers. I need to think for a while and dream up some sort of rational, halfling-level storage for us to enjoy.\n... The Sheriff seemed a bit upset with me when I told him I didn't give the wool DIRECTLY to the princess. I don't see the problem. That Dewlox fellow looked trustworthy enough. I looked for that princess for a good 2 hours.\nMet another halfling at the bar. He seemed nice. Not very good with names today. Edgar, was it? Eddie? Bah. I'll get this down eventually.", ""),
        StaticBook("Digowen Part 1", "Jallentime", "One cold winters morning, upon the breast of new fallen snow, there stood a proud spruce forest of irrefutable infamy. There is nothing immediately discernible about these woods; the trees carried the same burdens of frost and insects as any other for\nmiles around. But what this forest did have, and that was quite unheard at the time, was a name. Digowen Woods was the name given to it, or at least that was the name etched into the sign just outside. If you decided to follow this sign you would find\nyourself upon the shambles of an old frontier road, long since buried under mounds upon mounds of soil and brown pine needles, only apparent from the trees whom still could not breach the stone laid so very long ago. It was peaceful here, in inherently\nominous. On this particular day a tattered huntsman trudged his way through the thicket, scattering leaves and pine-cones at his feet as he dragged a chain of cold, metal traps behind him. He stopped only a moment at a time, his eyes gazing at the\nlandscape around him and the ghostly breaths emanating from his throat, before he would lay down his trap and pull back the jagged teeth around it. The huntsman's pattern continued well on into the day, until the sun passed well over it's perch in the sky\nand began to refract it's light upon the forest floor. Golden brown sunshine danced throughout the canopy, signaling the forest creatures that night would soon belong to the predators, of whom Nature did not count it's intruder.\nThe huntsman, sadly, realized the error he had made too late, and found himself far from home, in a world not his own. He dragged his coarse leather boots through the rotting needles, clearing a small section of the forest floor to himself as the last\nbeams of light shone through the mist above him. He laid down on this small amount of luxury, and stared skyward at the cloudless midnight above him, his mind slowly counting each star and naming them off to himself. Soon his eyelids fell, and his dreams\novertook him.", ""),
        StaticBook("Diplo. Letter", "Ser Patrek Roswell", "To his majesty, Prince Artimec of the wood elves.\n===================\nI have witnessed the beauty of your forests, the green crowns which pride the trees around the place you call your home. \n\nIt beauty goes unrivalled and-\n- I saw the beauty from the farms surrounding your great holding.\n\nYet what plagues my mind is what'll happen to this great city of the Mali'ame. What'll happen to you and your peoples after the war is over?\nI do not care for your pride, or my own. I could simply threaten you and say that we will win, to which you'll retort that you and the empire will stand true and be victorious.\n\nI wish to see past this. I wish to meet with you on neutral ground or\nin Krakow, neutral ground or on your city, for I trust in the honour of the elves.\n\nTo discuss the matters that lay at hand to the future of you, and the people of Pasnia.\nI wish you a good day.\n\n\nSigned;\n\n Lord Patrek Roswell\n  Grand Hussar of the   Peoples of Pasnia  \n  And Hetman of the       Armia.", ""),
        StaticBook("Diplomatic Writ", "Owyn Amador", "To the noble lord or lady reading this,\n\nPlease welcome unto your noble house from Mondstadt, my servant and envoy, Aylwin Blaxton. He has come upon my request to search for a potential betrothal match, to secure the noble house of Amador\nand bring prosperity to a worthy bride. I sincerely request unto thee that you would allow him safe passage through your realm and permission thereafter to talk to the members of the nobility and aristocracy of Lorraine. Whilst unto your care,\nthe aforementioned shall adhere to the laws and customs of your realm, whilst maintaining the prestige of my own household. \n\nYours sincerely,\nLord Owyn Amador, Baron of Mondstadt", ""),
        StaticBook("Directions", "Plumbus", "Wear to find da boom boom steel.\nGo east from da krag down da roads.\n\nTurn lefd at da eyes plane sine.\n\ncross da stupeed brige.\n\nturn right when you use a fork and left when you use anudder fork.\nHead towards da bass chin.\n\nRun away from da big monsta.\n\nMore monsters? Sneak around dems.\n\nFind and follow da coast to da black rocks, dems are da boom boom rocks.", ""),
        StaticBook("Directions.", "Erin Lockley", "*A map was drawn of the location of Erins home land.\n\nA map displaying the Library of Dragur, and the area surrounding. \n\nTo get to the location marked, one would walk straight along the path away from the library, through a forest. At a cross\nroads, they would then head south towards the beach. They would find the structures of Erins home to be a windmill and some few homes.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Dirk T.", "Ol' Man Sano", "Dear Dirk,\n\nAs we met in Felsen, upon when I arrested you shortly after the Felsen Dock Bombings, we soon became political allies and desperatley close friends.\nI care so deeply about our time spent together, and I cannot thank you enough for your advice and companionship. In return, please accept this iron ring, a representation of our advocacy for-\nthe working class across Axios and beyond. Stay safe, and may you be happy in your journies to come.", ""),
        StaticBook("Div'laureh", "The Bastard", "1rst of Malin's Welcome, 1632.\n\nAureons, your time is neigh, you have now been accosted for your crimes against the people of Laureh'lin.\n\nKill Leo Aureon. Or I will.\nLeo Aureon, if you refuse to kill yourself or be killed by proxy, every single one of your children will die. \n\nYour crimes are numerous, you think yourself infallible, but now true justice reaches you.\n\n- FEAR. RETRIBUTION.-\nVigilante justice is the only way by which I can achieve my aims. Your crimes against the military are just as numerous, your destruction of the sanctity of warfare, the right to honorable combat. You will die honorless and I will be unchallenged.\nYour family are innocents, but sometimes innocents get caught amidst the broiling conflict we call war, if you do not pay for your crimes they will.\n\nLike an angel of retribution I sweep down to destroy you.\nConsider this closely, the lives of your wife, family and children are deeply entwined in your actions of the next year. \n\nSuffer. Wither. The Aspects care not for you. Your ancestors would be ashamed of what you've become.\nIN THE NAME OF JACKAL.\n\nIN THE NAME OF THE ASPECTS.\n\nTHE FATHER AND THE MOTHER APPROVE.\n\nAS DO THE PEOPLE YOU'VE WRONGED.\nSO SPEAKS THE CITY.\n\nHARKEN,\n\nAND FALL.\n\nSigned, Laureh'lin", ""),
        StaticBook("Documents", "Godric var Ruthern", "I, Godric var Ruthern hereby bestow my property and surrounding land that resides by the east exit of Johannesburg onto Patrek Roswell.\n\nGodric var Ruthern", ""),
        StaticBook("Draft Procedures", "Acaele", "Draft: The Council of Wisdom\n\nRecognizing the need for legal procedure to remove a sitting Maheral who is in some capacity unfit or unable to fulfill their duties as Head of State to the Silver City and cultural\nchaperone to the\nMali'thilln, this document seeks to establish such a procedure. It seeks further to establish an assembly for the adjudication of these proceedings and to outline the composition of this assembly to best ensure that the\nintegrity of our way of life is forever maintained. \n\nThe Assembly:\n\nThe assembly is to be comprised of Maheral former who have relinquished the office and remain pure citizens in good\nstanding. Those who have committed crimes against purity or the maehr'sae hiylun'ehya have lost good standing and may not sit in the assembly. Those currently holding government office temporarily relinquish their right to sit in the\nassembly until such a time as they have resigned and their office is filled or abolished.\n\n\nThe Procedure:\n\nAny individual eligible to serve upon an assembly has the right to call one. In order\nto take effect, this motion must be seconded by at least one other individual eligible to serve. The assembly must meet within one elven week of its initial calling. The time and location of the assembly are to be determined by the calling member.\nThose who are eligible and unable to attend reserve the right to cast their votes beforehand in absentia. Those who fail to attend or to vote in absentia forfeit their vote. The sitting Maheral can be removed from office by a\nmajority vote against them. Following the removal of a sitting Maheral, any member of the assembly may nominate a replacement. Should more than one candidate be nominated, a vote will be held to determine which\ncandidate will be considered first, with a simple majority being sufficient. Candidates in consideration must be confirmed by an absolute majority of the assembly. Maheral who are unseated by vote of the assembly are considered not\nto be in good standing. Once an assembly has been called, a sitting Maheral may not resign and confer their position to another until and unless the assembly concludes and they are not found unfit to serve. If the sitting Maheral is\nbrought to assembly and found fit to serve, they may not be brought to assembly again until new evidence of their incompetence is available. Should a sitting Maheral die without naming a successor, an assembly must be held within the\nfollowing elven week, which will move immediately into replacement nomination and confirmation procedure.\n\n\n\nFrom the quill of Acaele Lazul", ""),
        StaticBook("Dragon Princess", "Niera Acal'elor", "Once upon a time, in a kingdom far far away, there was a king and queen who lived in a golden castle with their beautiful daughter. They lived in peace and prosperity, and never knew heartbreak or want.\nYet one night, an ugly orc captured the princess and carried her away, locking her up in a tall, dark tower. \n\nThe king and queen were struck with immeasurable grief and promised the princess's hand to any knight who could rescure thier child.\nSo the knights in the land assembled, wanting to bring the princess back to be their bride. \n\nThe Orc roared in anger when he saw the approaching knights. And one by one, he tore them to shreds at the foot of the tower.\nThe princess looked on in horror as her rescuers were slewn. She shrunk back into the confines of her room, weeping as she thought of her fate. \n\nYet someone heard her cries...\nhe princess was awakened by the sound of thunderous wings, flapping in the moonlit sky. A large Dragon, with obsidian scales clung to the side of the dragon, baring his large teeth at the orc.\nThe creature took a deep breath, and in one burst of flame, turned the orc to ash. \nThe dragon then turned his attention to the princess, prying apart the bars that held her in the tower\nShe carefully climbed upon the dragon’s back, and the dragon beat his wings once more, bringing her up into the clouds. \nThe dragon returned the princess to the king and queen, and they were in awe at such a marvelous creature.\nYet, how could they keep their promise? How could a dragon wed their daughter? When asked this, the dragon started to transform in a blinding light, until all that remained was a handsome prince in his place.\nThe princess looked upon her savior, and the dragon took her to be his loving wife. \n\n\n\nThey both lived happily ever after. The end.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dragur", "Orithur", "The Daemon known as Dragur is quite easily the daemon most shrouded in mystery. For you see, Dragur one day vanished from all planes and realities, he went missing, or went into hiding many years ago and has made no effort to make himself known since.\nDragur is commonly referred to as the Daemon of knowledge and the father of all dragon-kind - both greater and lesser Dragonkin are children of the Daemon Dragur. Dragur himself was known to appear as a dragon in the distant days when he apparently\nexisted. So little is known about Dragur, and in that there is a unique irony, how the Daemon of all knowledge is so shrouded from it himself. There exist several theories on the fate of Dragur, one being that Dragur has been imprisoned by another Aengul\nor Daemon for a reason unknown, perhaps as a means of leeching power, or perhaps in punishment for the creation of the Dragonkin on the world. If this were the case, it is likely that the Aengul responsible would be Xan, the Aengul of Guardianship, and\nenemy to Dragonkin. Another theory is that Dragur has seen so much of the present, past and future that he grow fearful of how easily his own knowledge of it could change the future for the worst, and instead decided to remove himself from the world as an\nact to preserve it. The final theory is that Dragur ascended behond that of a Daemon, after being so knowledgeable on the world that there was nothing left to be known. Some believe he may have reached another state of being, and transcended reality.\nBut as for what we do know: He does, or did once exist. His dragons are evidence enough, and no other Aengul or Daemon has claimed ownership of his creation. As well as this, it has been noted in the past that as libraries begin to expand and grow, blue\nwisps, wisps of Dragur, have been seen to congregate. They are reclusive, as if they do not wish to be seen. As author of this edition on Dragur, I have seen the wisps myself in a large underground library in Athera. But when the library was destroyed,\nthe wisps vanished. Perhaps they are not even related to Dragur, but the thought still remains that they are his spies, watching the congregation of knowledge from the shadows for reasons still unknown.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dragur Library", "Wretched", "The History And Tale Of The Library Of Dragur\n                 -Orithur\n-------------------\n\nThe Library of Dragur stands today as a monument to the betterment of our world, no library may ever hope to match its vast expanse of knowledge across\na variety of topics from ancient history to modern magic. The library continues to grow each day, as more and more of the world's Descendants discover the blossoming hope that is the Library of Dragur. As its size grows, so does its influence and\npopularity. More take notice, more come to its halls, more donations are left. But, this was not always the way.\n\nI am the co-founder of the Library of Dragur, my name is Orithur, and this is my account of my dearest Library's journey:\nIt was during the early days of the Descendants arrival to Athera, that I found myself particularly lost, and without purpose. As a fallen Harbinger of the now deceased Drakaar known as Setherien, I was immediately shunned by every civilised culture upon\nthe landmass. Many of my kin were driven to suicide, and those that were not either went into deep hiding, or became consumed with the hatred against them, and went on blood thirsty rampages.\n\nThis of course, did myself no aid in trying\nto find a new place to fit in, and a new purpose to have. \n\nIt should be known that I served as Setherien's keeper of tomes, and before that, I existed as the book keeper within the Order of the Golden Lance. Being a librarian, has always been\nwithin my nature. And it was this inherent nature toward the preservation, that did draw the most unlikely of friends to my path.\n\nThis friend, just so happened to be a Dragaar named Aedrex. For those unaware, Dragaar act, to the best of their abilities,\nas guardians of the Descendants. They seek to collect and preserve knowledge in order to further better the descendant races - thus this remains as our library's primary goal and focus.\n\nAedrex recruited me, and showed me his very well\nconcealed home. It was a vast empty hall with many empty shelves. He told me, he intended to fill them, and that he would be honoured if I were to assist him on this great task.\n\nI could never have anticipated what this quest would mean for not only\nmyself, but the world. Almost immediately we began to make contact with all known nations, and began to acquire copies of books scattered across the realm. We delved deep into ruins, we scavaged through cities that had fallen to war to salvage their\nlibraries. These cities had of course been looted, but none thought of the value within the library.\n\nWe began to make significant political ties, and to this day hold these ties to various nations and their leaders, which greatly assists in the\npreservation of the library. One such political tie was Tristen Tresery, who later became the Prince of Malinor.\n\nYou see as our shelves expanded, the workload became too much for Aedrex and I to manage by ourselves. We recruited\nscholars to assist our efforts, I had even tailored a unique red uniform for them to wear which, to my deep surprise they did.\n\nOur numbers expanded, and thus we became the Order Of Dragur. However, we still very much remained a secretive\norder. Very few knew of the existence of the hidden library, located behind a complex hidden door, deep underground. We did this out of fear, our order was young and there existed dangerous forces in the world that would surely tear it all apart should we\nbe naive enough to reveal our knowledge to the world. It is only now that I write this that I realise how ridiculous that sentiment was, but perhaps it did do us good.\n\nWe continued to grow. First to one hundred books, then two hundred, then three\nhundred. We ventured and explored the realm, plundering dungeons, recording events, filling in the gaps in history that had been lost or neglected, and we did this with such pride and such purpose. Never before had I felt a joy as pure as recording and\ncollecting our broken little world into books and tomes, all organised neatly upon shelves.\n\nEven in these early days of the order, we had already become the largest known library to ever exist throughout the history of the Descendant\nraces. But the title meant very little to us, and still we continued to grow and expand.\n\nEven deeper below the library in the library vault, we kept a large Dragaar's Lexicon, belonging of course to Aedrex. This, absorbed all the knowledge upon the\nshelves so that in the event that the books were lost, the library would not be. Also in this vault, we safeguarded several powerful objects. And these objects, were Dragon Eggs.\n\nAedrex, upon entering our realm did so with seven Dragon Eggs that he hoped\nto safeguard and nurture until they may hatch. So they sat in our vault, growing slowly. Dragons are some of the most powerful and intelligent creatures in the known realms, it is no surprise that they grow very slowly, and take a significant amount of\ntime to hatch. But for the longest time, they were safe.\n\nSome time into the order's existence, Aedrex and I found ourselves in council with the Aengul of Order and Guardianship, Xan. There was a new threat to the realm, and this threat\nwas the Arch-Drakaar named Azdromoth. We communicated with the Greater Entity with his clerical and paladin patrons, and this was not the first time our order found itself in contact with an Aengul. \nThe Aengul who called itself 'Wyrvun' made several\nvisits to our library for what I believe to be purely curiousity reasons. Ours was a passtime for even Gods, it would seem.\n\nAnd so it seemed that nothing could go wrong, that we could only ever continue to progress and expand. But then disaster struck.\nWe had drawn the attention of Aenguls, we should have expected the same of Daemons. A Daemon who remains unknown in name or purpose, attacked our library with peculiar spectral entities. We defended the library valiently, and were joined by\nthe paladins of Xan to fend off the invaders. Alas, Aedrex could not transform into his enormous Dragon form without destroying the library.\n\nThe battle was destructive, and took place within the library halls itself. Fires raged, pillars toppled, the\nroof began to cave in. The library was destroyed.\n\nOur biggest concerns of course, were the Dragon eggs and the Lexicon. Both were thankfully unharmed but the vault would not stand for long. Another force recognised this, and\nXan himself pulled the Dragon eggs out of the library and into his realm, where one of his patrons named Herun Athna informs me they still exist today. Aedrex also managed to safely transport the Lexicon to a nearby cave system, but this attack had...\nChanged him.\n\nWe suspended the duty of the scholars and sent them out into the world. We closed off the entrance to the secretive library for good, and Aedrex saw that the Lexicon remained in a safe, inaccessible location. After this was done, Aedrex came\nto me with a heavy heart. With the attack, the threat of unknowns and the obvious threat of the Arch-Drakaar, Aedrex told me he was leaving, likely forever. Where to, he never did specify. Another land, another realm, I could not say for certain. All I\nknew was that he left me with the Lexicon, and a duty to see the Library of Dragur not only restored, but improved.\n\nAnd it was in Vailor, that I saw to the construction of an enormous structure that would house the knowledge stored within the giant\nlexicon. I met many troubles, many groups approached me with distrust, the repuation I still held with certain key political figures was the only thing allowing me to do this.\n\nOf course, this time the library was to exist to the public. I had a theory\nthat when people saw the library's potential, the inherent good within people would allow it to flourish, and they would assist it. Much to both my relief and joy, I was correct.\n\nI began to recruit scholars once more, and very soon the old magic\nof the library returned to my hollow frame. I began to feel at home once more. It could never replace the sensation of family I felt around Aedrex, but it felt good regardless.\n\nWe began to go on expeditions, we recruited scholars as dedicated as I was to\ncollecting and documenting knowledge. We wrote much, we made a great number of friends, we formed new political ties. Our collection continued to grow on mostly donation alone from the comman man. I have now grown very close to the scholars working here\nthe longest.\n\nBut again we are not without our troubles. Hostility has arisen between myself personally and the Holy Orders that I once served under, and once aided us. To draw their attention away from the library so that their rage may not be\ntaken out upon it, for some time I left the library to go in hiding. It is only recently from writing this that I make my return, believing the dust to have now settled. However I now understand that my active presence in the public eye of the library\nwill only ever cause chaos. I have therefore left it in the very capable hands of my most trusted Scholar, and now Librarian: Aluuvia. Or, Lyeth, as she now goes by.\n\nMy role in the library exists in the background now, until such a time that\nI believe it safe for my presence on the library floor to become commonplace.\n\nBut all of this aside, the library continues to flourish and grow. We now near close to a thousand unique books upon our shelves, and our library's reputation has grown so\nsignificantly. Teachers and students alike of many paths of study flock to our halls for a taste of its knowledge - we continue the work of Aedrex most efficiently.\n\nBut I miss him dearly.\n\nThere exist unsolved mysterious of the\nlibrary, such as, what was the creature that destroyed the original library, what was its goal, and will it attack again? What will Xan do with Aedrex's Dragon Eggs? Will they be returned to me, will he destroy them, or simply guard them for all eternity?\nAnd of course, where is Aedrex now? I gave up praying for his return some years ago. His duty upon our world was concluded, he is the reason this library stands today, it would not surprise me if I were to never see him again.\n\nThe Library of Dragur will\nstand strong throughout the events, ages and realms to come. It will remain a beacon of peace and study for all for centuries more, of this I am sure. We will have further troubles ahead no doubt, but we must never forget that no matter what, it will\nsurely be worth it.\n\n- Orithur, Paladin of the Golden Lance, Harbinger of Setherien, and co-founder of the Library of Dragur.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dragur's Brood", "Thurak'Yar", "Dragur's Brood\n\nThe Dragons all descended from Dragur, an Arch-Daemon of the land named Asulon. Dragur’s true form is that of a dragon, so the appearance of his offspring is of no surprise. Dragur raised\nthe first of his brood in his volcanic lair, and taught them vast knowledge and wisdom. Like their father, the dragons are capable of morphing into a humanoid shape. The majority of the brood are wise and indifferent to mortals, sometimes posing as\nscholars or mages; spending their time distributing their knowledge of the realms with the races of this world. However, a certain sect of Dragur’s offspring exists, known as Drakes. The scales of these drakes have turned to a shade back as night.\nThese Drakes, unlike their brothers the Dragons, are heavily opposed to mortals, sometimes spending time in humanoid form purely to destroy them or to spread corruption in hopes of turning them against each other.\nAfter the creation of his brood, Dragur fell into a deep slumber within the volcano, and has yet to be awakened. In spite of this, the dragons are overseen by a Matriarch, or “Queen”.\nAs the brood grew, they began to scatter across the\nland, some going off into the mainlands, or even farther into the opposite ends of the world. Some stayed close to their birth home, such as the Matriarch as well as Velketzar. Velketzar was the first born male of the brood. While\nXandraza was born with the mind of Dragur, the yearning for knowledge and learning, Velketzar was born with the strength, pride, and sense of wanting to protect. This Dragon worked closely with the past civilizations of Asulon, ensuring\nthat peace was kepy between them and that they prospered. In his humanoid form he was known and respected greatly across the lands. Always possessing an astounding amount of patience, he thought things through for the best possible outcomes.\nHowever, as much as he wanted it to, no everything could stay in the peaceful serenity he so desperately worked for… There was just some hate in the hearts of beings that one could never come to change, for Velketzar, he felt pity upon these.\nFew of the brood saw how he aided these creature, as they were so far beneath them, and while some attempted to understand, others simply refused to care at all, and shunned him for his passion. But alas, it wasn’t simply his own\nkind that acted in such a manner. The humanoids he helped, some sought greed over all, and despite how much they already had in this world, nothing satisfied their thirst for gaining more wealth of power… Thus lead to the day of betrayal.\nThe day when some of us cast aside the trust of us and stole knowledge for their own personal gains came too soon. After that day, Xandraza and Velketzar sought out what they could together but could only find so much. Velketzar’s\npride had been dealt a heavy blow. He was born with the sense of urge to protect, and he felt he had failed to aid Xandraza in the protection of her vast collection of scrolls and books. Depression fell upon him greatly; he stopped visiting\nthe civilians, and though she tried her best to console him and tell him that, indeed, in time, together they would perhaps be able to recover that which was stolen, Xandraza’s words would not reach him. His emotions slowly began to consume him.\nOne day after Xandraza returned to the island, filled with happiness after reclaiming another book in ruins, her eyes befell Velketzar and her heart sank. Once a bright healthy ruby shade of red, his scales had begun to dull in colour, and had saturated\nnearly to a dank brow. Bringing him outside so he could see for himself in the light of the sun, Velketzar finally understood what he was becoming. His head grew clouded with his emotions, as Dragons, it is known, have the strongest\nemotions of all creatures. Sadness and rage overtook him, and blinded by this the urge to halting his protection against corruption grew. And then he stopped, and began to think. Pondering on the best possible outcome, as he always did…\nAnd so Velketzar changed into his true form, and with determined rage, he destroyed the mountain on the east side of that island that was their home. For what reason? It didn’t occur to Xandraza what he was doing before it was too late.\nHe was making a clearing for himself. Once he had enough space, he stood at the edge of the island, looking out to sea. And then it began. First, his claws, spikes and horns began to harden and turn to stone, then his wings, arms and\nlegs went next... All turning to rock. He did this to himself… But why? “Do not think ill of me.” He said to Xandraza who watched, mortified and as still as the stone he was becoming. “I do not wish to become one of them. I wish to stay in the\ngood of your heart. I will guard this island so that what has happened may never happen again, and I hope in time, my scales will return to that shin and hue you love so dearly. Goodbye.” And as the final whip of his tail slammed into\nthe side of the volcano, it too then turned to stone.", ""),
        StaticBook("Drinks", "Meriel Aureon", "Pine Whiskey\n\nStrength: 7\nFlavor: Pine, lumber\nSmell: Pine, lumber\nColor: Medium brown\n\nA pale brown liquid, with a slight green tint.\nSnow Petal Wine\n\nStrength: 2\nFlavor: Dry, hint of sweetness\nSmell: Sweet, almost floral\nColor: Very pale yellow\nDark Brew Ale\n\nStrength: 5\nFlavor: Bitter, slight sweet aftertaste.\nSmell: Wheat\nColor: Medium Brown\nMullberry Wine\n\nStrength: 2\nFlavor: Sweet, fruity\nSmell: Fruity\nColor: Dark purple\nLemon Zest Tea\n\nStrength: 0\nFlavor: Bitter, sweet after taste\nSmell: Citrus\nColor: Pale yellow\nSalted Hiney Coffee\n\nStrength: 0\nFlavor: Bitter, very sweet aftertaste\nSmell: Coffee smell\nColor: Brown with golden flecks\nJungle Juice\n\nStrength: 10\nFlavor: Incredibly strong, nausiating\nSmell: Likestraight alcohol, somewhat musty\nColor: Pale pink\nJUNGLE JUICE RULES\n\nThe drinker rolls 20\n\nUnder 15, they pass out, vomit and urinate.\n\nOver 15 they are incredibly drunk, may or may not vomit.\n\nAdjust rolls depending on the character.", ""),
        StaticBook("Drugs", "Marren", "Drugs \n\nCactus Green:\n\nCactus Green (dye)\nGrass\nDrugs\n\nBlack Cactus:\n\nCactus Green (dye)\nFern\nInk Sac\nCoal\nDrugs\n\nPure Quartz:\n\nQuartz\nGlowstone Dust\nCocoa Beans\nFern\nDrugs\n\nBlueberry Cactus:\n\nBlue Orchid\nCactus Green (dye)\nLight Blue (dye)\nFern\nDrugs\n\nEternal Leaf:\n\nGrass\nFern\nVine\nDrugs\n\nIce Kiss:\n\nSnowball\nAllium\nVine\nDrugs\n\nBaby's Brain:\n\nMushroom Stew\nCactus Green (dye)\nFern", ""),
        StaticBook("Druid Groves", "Ralnor Kelyarus", "{\"text\":\"\"}\nA Commentary on the Different Groves\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBy:\nRalnor Kelyarus\nThe druids are a group of induviduals that believe in the preservation and protection of Nature's \"balance\". They do this by training and and attuning people in their \"groves\", areas that the druids call home. There are two main groves of Axios,\nthe\nMother Grove of Sutica, on the Island of Ceru, and the Naelurir, of Linandria on the Island of Tahn. Even though these two groves both essentially believe in the same things and use the same type of magic, there are many differences that surround their\npractices and customs. For example, the Naelurir stay contained to the forests of the Elven Dominion, while the Mother Grove spreads their knowledge across Axios. Following this pattern, the Naelurir only allow Elves to join their ranks, and the\nMother Grove accepts anyone willing to work hard and serve their purpose. The Naelurir serve as the priests of the Dominion, and the Mother Grove serves as the priests and knowledge bearers of all of Axios. Even though the druids have different groves,\nthey all practice and believe in the same things.", ""),
        StaticBook("Druidic Conduct", "Taynuel", "~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~\n          The Druidic\n     Code of Conduct\n\n       As created by\n   Apollan in the wake\n    of the Age of Poor\n          Judgement\n\n Scribed by Hare Druid       Taynuel Viellsinch\n\n~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~\nSection A: Druid Conduct\n\nGeneral Conduct\n\nA) Never insult a fellow brother or sister in any way. ((ic or ooc))\n\nB) Never kill a brother or sister ((for fun, etc.))\nC) Never steal from the Order or from a brother or sister.\n\nD) Don't destroy property of the Order.\n\nE) If you are below the rank of guide, it is not your place to make decisions that affect the Order as a whole.\nF) All Druids must conduct themselves in a mature and upright manner. ((ic or ooc))\n\nG) Never criticize a brother or sister in an overly negative way. ((ic or ooc))\n\nH) Calm the heck down!\nI) Always immediately contact a higher ranking Druid if you have a problem.\n\nJ) Stay active. ((on the forum))\n\nK) Never criticize someone. ((ooc for actions done ic or vice versa.))\nL) A Druid may  use violent force if they or other Druids are in danger, it  is self defense, or if it is in defense of nature or the balance.\nConduct Around the Shunned.\n\nA) When a shunned person enters the Grove, immediately instruct them to leave. If they do not leave instruct them once that you will forcibly remove them if they do not leave. If they still stay a Druid is free to use\nany means possible to remove a shunned from the Grove and the surrounding area.\n\nB) When a shunned person with KOS designation enters the Grove, immediately instruct them that they will be killed in the next ten seconds if they do not leave. When ten\nseconds has expired a Druid is free to slay any non-obeying shunned.\n\nC) When you see a shunned person, even with a KOS designation, somewhere other than a Grove, continue on your way and do not try to make contact.\nD) If a shunned tries to make contact with you somewhere outside a Grove, simply reply with the phrase \"Much wind pours from your mouth\" and move on. If they try to speak with you again, repeat the phrase. If they try a third time inform them that if they\ntry to speak to you again you will reply with violent force.\n\nE) If a shunned with a KOS designation tries to contact you somewhere other than a Grove, inform them that they have ten seconds to move away from the present location before violent force\nused.\n\nF) If at any time a shunned becomes aggressive or violent, refer to Section A, Subsection 1, Line L of the Druidic Code.\nSection B: Initiation and Ranking Up\n\n1) Outsider to Dedicant\na) Complete an extensive interview with a Guide.\nb) Recite the Dedicant's Vow.\n\n2) Dedicant to Druid\na) Stay a member for at least two Elven weeks. If seen as unready\nby the guide or higher, shall stay until the guide deems you ready.\nb) Complete a varying amount of Druidic Trials assigned successfully.\nc) Complete a Grand Task.\nd) Choose carefully what totem you will go under. This can only be changed once\nbecoming official.\ne) Become attuned in the ceremony performed by an Archdruid or Guide.\n\n3) Druid to Guide\na) Stay a member for four Elven weeks (dedicancy not included). If seen as unready by an arch or higher, be patient and gain wisdom.\nb) Once deemed as ready, take training underneath the Head Teacher as an apprentice, and watch how they are to Dedicants, how they assign tasks, how they handle the Grove, etc.\nc) Study up on the subject, as well as how to perform an attunement ceremon\nwhat the tasks entail, what the interviews for Dedicants are meant to have, as well as other things your Head Teacher suggests you learn.\nd) Practice giving a few Dedicants tasks under the supervision of your Head Teacher.\ne) Once you and your Head\nTeacher both feel that you are ready, the teacher will discuss with an Archdruid and you shall begin your Guideship.\nSection C: Punishments\n\n1) The punishment for breaking a rule depends on the person, severity, rule broken, and previous track record.\n\n2) The punishment for breaking a rule includes but is not limited to a warning, probation, a shun, a KOS des\nand banishment from Athera. ((server ban))\nSection D: Clauses\n\n1) All rules are subject to change.\n\n2) Section B, Subsection 1, Line C is optional if the Dedicant does not plan on becoming a Druid.", ""),
        StaticBook("Druidic Healing", "Thurak'Yar", "The Nature Of\nDruidic Healing\n\nBy Lillith Winterleaf\nDruidic Healing is a topic many are curious about, but few, even amongst Druids, wholly understand the cost on the one performing it. Most Druids use living reagents to assist in the mending process, this is so that they can draw\non the living essence within the reagent and draw less from themselves, but a skilled Druidic healer can also safely mend wounds without any reagents on hand.\nDruidic healing is, quite simply, an exchange of living essence from the healer to the patient. The Druid focuses upon the living tissue around the wound and asks the patient’s body to mend itself, giving of their own living\nessence to aid in the healing.\nThis is where the cost and risk of Druidic healing is, and you should heed it well. A Druid is capable of amazing feats of healing at times, but all of our healing derives from ourselves and it is possible to\ncause lasting damage to oneself while healing the wounds of another. This is why living reagents are used, to lessen the need to draw from oneself. I have personally healed a variety of wounds, from cuts and scrapes to sword clashes\nto broken bones to some far worse. They all draw from you to some extent, even when using reagents. Simple wounds you may not even notice the drain upon yourself, it depends how strong your healing has become, and how\nfamiliar you are with the process. Practise truly makes perfect in this regard. I am of the belief an example of a mistake is the best way to pass on a lesson, so I will share how I nearly lost my life while healing the King of Skravia back on Asulon.\nHe and some of his soldiers had been lured out to the base of a rogue mage that had harassed their kingdom for a long while. When they gained the upper hand and cornered the mage, his trap was revealed, the walls of his base were lined with\nexplosives, and he detonated them. Three of the soldiers died in the blast, the others dragged a severely injured but alive King back to Skravia and to my inn, knowing I was a healer. His wounds were great, part of his skull was visible on\nthe top of his head, and he had shrapnel wounds all across his body, blood everywhere. There was nothing to do but try, I coated the wounds with a mixture of living slime and bonemeal, then began the healing process; drawing upon the living essences\nas well as myself to stabilise and mend the kind King laying before me. It took nearly two hours, but his wounds sealed and he was alive and left in a coma for a few days. However, I had given of myself far more than I should have, my skin was pale,\nalmost white, and my eyes had lost most of their colour and I could hardly breathe. I am told I lost consciousness; I awoke five weeks later, my every limb sore, my hair a shade lighter, but my skin almost back to its normal tone. A fellow Druid,\nJena, had to come out to restore some living essence to me or I would have perished within the first day or two, I was so weakened. Take my mistake with you if you seek to heal, you five of yourself, there is a limit you will reach and you\nshould not go beyond it or you risk your life. Find your balance between personal sacrifice and reagents to ease your burden, you almost always have something available to ease your personal strain, even if it is the grass around you or a planter\nof flowers outside the window, any living essence can ease your burden if the situation is a bit beyond your ability to heal safely with nothing on hand.", ""),
        StaticBook("Druidic Myths", "Wayward Druid Respiren", "* The Myth of the *           Great War\nMany moons ago a terrible war broke out between the two mighty guilds of wizards -one good and one evil- that controlled great empires. Wizards on both sides vowed to fight until  utterly triumphant\nSeeking to purge their rivals from the land. With fearsome magic and dragon armies they battled for centuries, neither side winning final victory . Through their warfare, the wizards wrought vast devastation on the world,\nForests blazed up, islands sank into the sea, entire races became extinct. Eventually, the the great goddess of Nature awakened from her sleep to witness the savage conflict.\nShocked by the destruction, the Goddess sent a vision to a single woman who would become the first Grand Druid. Through the vision, this chosen figure saw that she must found a druidic order to preserve the fragile remains of her world's ecology.\nWith the guidance of her goddess, the  Order grew in strength Until finally it had the power to intervene in the wizard war...\nThe force of young druids pooled  their powers and together vanquished the members of both battling guilds, transforming the combatants into innocent wild beasts.\nOnce the former wizards now unable to fathom the concept of good versus evil - slithered, bounded, loped and crawled off into their ruined habitats, the Order began to heal the lands.\nSince then, the druidic order  continually works to prevent such destruction from ever occurring again. Druids pledge to make sure the wars of good  and evil no longer mar the precious land.\nBut, the Order also has bitter enemies in the ancient remnants of the  guilds of warring wizards- those good and evil mages who luckily escaped the fate of their fellows.\nEach guild claims it had been on the verge of victory and would have won, had druids not interfered. \n\n-As recounted by Hierophant Pulver, Master of Dungeons", ""),
        StaticBook("Druidic Origins", "Finalhazard", "Arlen Teharissa's Compendium on:\n\nThe Druids\nThe Creator\nThe Aspects\nNature\n\nIn Loving Memory Of:\n\nMy Teacher: Salhassan\nMy Best Friend: Fawynn\nMy Father: Aphoros\nTable of Contents\n\nChapter 1: Page 5\nThe Creator\nChapter 2: Page 17\nOur Realm\nChapter 3: Page 21\nThe Druids\nAuthor's Note:\n\nThis book isn't for the ignorant. Nor is it for whom believe their God of choice is the only God in existence. This book is for the thinkers, the inventors, and those who wish to seek knowledge. Do not be afraid to interpret the-\n- teachings of your Archdruids, Paladins, Preachers, Popes, Kings, Queens, and your parents differently. You're not going against their word. You're expanding your knowledge by proceeding and thinking differently.\nChapter 1:\n\nThe Creator\n\nThe start of all lies. While I do not doubt \"The Creator\"'s existence, I doubt his ability to interfere to directly with the mortal realm. That is, if he is even still alive, or-\n\"Active.*\"\n\n[*]Active; I'm led to believe that Aenguls and Daemons can, or are forced to enter a dormant state where they are unable to directly influence the world, mortals, or their own patrons. Being 'Active', is when an Aengudaemon is-\n- whenever they are not dormant.\n\n\nThe Creator[Cont.]:\n\nThe Creator was the first to breathe life into the world. I believe that The Creator had many failed experiments in order to create-\n- some sort of Primordial being similar to himself. With this, I believe he was the first alchemist. \n\nWhile this may seem trite, I believe The Creator tried to create a wife, or a husband. I really don't know as The Creator may not even have a-\n- true gender. Perhaps The Creator was genderless. Anyways, I digress.\n\nThe Creator tried to create a companion in order to keep himself company. If his experiment succeeded or not, I do not know. Yet I believe that something tragic occured -\n- hence why we hear nothing of a second Creator-tier being.\n\nThen he created nature. By nature, I don't mean the grass, trees, and animals. I mean he invented a complex force (Similar to that of Mana, Life-Force, and Olive Oil) -\n- that cannot be governed, or maintained by any Aengul, Daemon, group, or individual.\n\nHowever, he tried to maintain it. Through this, he created The Aspects. Cerunnos, and Cerrwiden.\n\nThe two then began to maintain nature. At -\n- the time however, nature was contained within a garden, or a 'Grove' of sorts.\n\nEventually, nature grew rampant and spread to the nearby lands outside The Grove. The once dry deserts turned into a lushful oasis, and the lifeless tundra sprouted -\n- greens and turned into a dense forest.\n\nIt was beautiful.\n\nBut it all had to die.\n\nThe Creator saw all the life that had been created, and decided that there must be a counterweight in order to ensure that nature did not -\n- overprogress. \n\nSo, he allowed another being to roam the land. Yet, this woman was cursed. Everything she touched that was outside 'The Grove' would perish. The flowers would wilt and turn black and the dirt would lose its fertility faster than an elf.\nThis woman would be come to known as Nemiisae.\n\nAs time began to pass, Cerunnos, Cerridwen, and Nemiisae knew that the three of them alone could not maintain nature, so instead they passed on the art that they knew onto the ancient descendents, thus -\n- creating the 'Second Generation' Druids.\n\nThe Aspects themselves, being the 'First [or Primordial] Generation Druids.'\nChapter 2: \n\nOur Realm\n\n\nI'm led to believe that the realm we live in cannot be directly touhed by any Aengudaemonic being. The Creator was no fool, I imagine he setup a barrier that is -\n- impenetrable to specific beings. This would include the Shamanic Greater Spirits.\n\nWhy this barrier was setup, I do not know. I do have my theories, however.\n\nPerhaps The Creator forsaw himself using his powers to -\n- directly influence us. \n\nOr maybe, he realized that his future-kin would try to intervene in our mortal affairs. \n\nWhatever the case. I've come to this conclusion due to the fact that if the Gods could truly step down upon this realm they-\n- would have a long time ago, and this very land that sit on would be a warzone for the Aenguls and Daemons to fight on. \n\nInstead, they choose to have us follow beliefs, religions, and guided-mindsets in order to speak to them.\nChapter 3:\n\nThe Druids\n\n\nI say this as the son of a Druid, and as someone who has switched between the Naelurir and the Mother Circle.\nA catastrophe is a naturally occuring event that occurs whenever the balance is disrupted to the point of no-return. \n\nThe freezing over of Thales.\nThe drought in The Fringe.\nThe Bull Worm of Athera.\nAll these moments of loss is a product of our own misconduct.\n\nTo be blunt. A Catastrophe is nature's way of resetting itself from the damage that we let occur, whether it be overgrowth, or the entire destruction of nature. Do remember that nature itself-\n- is a primordial force that the Aspects do not control, but help maintain nature, and simply represent specific aspects of it.\n\nWhile I do not believe that the destruction of nature is the way to obtain 'balance', on the contrary I also do not -\n- believe in the idealogy that planting trees and having each dedicant create a grove as a Grand Task is optimal for the balance.\n\nA cruel type of irony it is that we as Druids are supposed to aid in maintaining the balance, when a large portion of\n- us refuse to change our lives in order to fit the balance we're meant to uphold. \n\nBut, I stray from my original topic. \n\nThe Druids as a collective whole are a unique group of individuals whom work both tegether and seperately in order-\nto serve the Aspects, and therefore nature in order to 'protect the balance'.\nFinal Notes:\n\n\nVol. 2 Coming Soon[TM]\n\n\n20th of The Grand Harvest, 1561.\n\nAuthor:\nArlen\nTeharissa", ""),
        StaticBook("Druidic Report", "Tennallar", "Tennallar's Druidic Grove Report\n7th of the Grand Harvest, 1620\n-------------------\n[The guide begins from the disembarking of the Tahn Docks boat.]\nFrom Boat:\nTunnel through a low hill with little to no cover. Comes out to the [Shun Board], where enemies of the druids are listed. Atop the hill is a large farm run by the druids. Continue along tunnel road to the Druidic Portal.\nEnemies of the Druids can travel through. {Portal can be raided through.}\nPortal comes out to a dock-like structure raised above the turtle's back, with a map and statues flank the area. There are little to no fortifications across the island. Marketplace is directly to the right of the portal coming out.\nThe first large tree houses the druid tavern. Within, female druids seem to constantly sit in wait. Running next to it is a small creek, cutting across the island with small bridges intermittent. The other large tree hosts the Archdruid residences.\nBehind the dock sits a large, natural stone arch within which is a small reading nook/library, along with a turtle egg and rare animal living space. To the opposite corner of the island is a short stone mountain. Within it is the Drudic Communal Storage.\nThe rest of the island is made up of druid housing.\n\nThis concludes the report.\n-------------------", ""),
        StaticBook("Druidic Studies", "Aria Lanyathir", "=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=Ariadni Lanyathir's\nDruid Studies.\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n=-=-=- Index -=-=-=\n\nCh 1: Aspects\nCh 2: Blessings\nCh 3: Balance\nCh 4: Cycle of Life\nCh 5: The Order\nCh 6: Totems\nCh 7: Powers\nCh 8: Responsibilities\nCh 9: Ranks\n=-=-=-Aspects-=-=-=\n\nCerridwen: Mother of the Harvest.\n\nCernunnos: Father of the Hunt.\nCerridwen is the Mother of the Harvest, the Green Lady and the Woman of Morn.\n\nCernunnos is the Father of the Hunt and the Great Huntsman.\n=-=-=Blessings=-=-=\n\nCerridwen's blessings cover all harvests and marriages. Newly-weds may also receive the blessing of many children.\n\nCernunnos' blessings are used upon armies and honourable fighters.\n=-=-=Balance=-=-=\n\nThe balance of nature is one in which every life that lives is fair and just. None shall perish, both plants and animals, without a natural end. If their end is not natural, then a Druid is able to interfere to save the nature and\nwildlife from their unfateful end. However, is a forest is alite due to a natural storm or weather, then a Druid musn't interfere, but rather let nature run its course. This promotes the natural life cycle of all organisms.\n=-= Cycle of Life =-=\n\nThe Cycle of Life has 4 phases. Birth, Maturity-Growth, Reproduction and Death.\n\nBirth:\nBeginning of a New Life.\nMaturity-Growth:\nGrowth Stages into Adulthood.\n\nReproduction:\nFinding a Mate to create a new life.\n\nDeath:\nLoss of life.\n\nThe Food Chain is the order in which animals eat one another; the\n'Chain'.\nDecendants don't have a place in this chain, but would be near the Top, otherwise.\n=-=- The Order -=-=\n\nThe Druids are dedicated to preserving the balance of nature. Druids undergo learning and studying in order to establish a strong link with nature; a bond.\nThe Order is open to all races.\n=-=-= Totems =-=-=\n\nA Totem is a title that defines and identifies who a Druid is, representing their history, personality and approach to life. Only one Druid may possess a specific totem at one time.\n=-=-= Powers =-=-=\n\nThe extent of a Druid's powers are unknown, though they are some of the best healers and are deeply connected with nature. They serve nature, often using their powers in the form of favours.\n=- Responsibilities -=\n\nA Druid is a keeper and protector of nature. A Druid works to maintain the balance and peace of nature, possibly allowing the removal of a tree of forest, but expect each tree to be replanted elsewhere in return; balance.\n=-=-=- Ranks -=-=-=\n\nDedicants:\nThe students and learners of Druidism, under a Druid Guide.\n\nDruids:\nThe main rank, the middle position of the Order after Dedicants and before the Inner Circle.\nDruid Guides:\nThe teachers and 'newbies' of the Inner Circle.\n\nArch-Druids:\nThe heads of the Inner Circle. They maintain all affairs and have direct contact with the Aspects themselves. This is how most orders from the Asoects are\nconveyed.\n\nGrand-Druids:\nMiddleman for if a split were to occur.\n\nHierophants:\nRetired Inner Circle members, though still extremely strong. Respectable Druids.\n\nNotable Druids:\nUsually deceased\nDruids who have made such an impact on the Order and nature that they're kept on record as High Status Druids.\n\nDemi-Aspects:\nDeceased Druids who have passed on to join the Aspects; One of the highest honours the Order can bestow.\nSeekers:\nThe first rank amongst Druidism; People that have taken an interest in the Aspects, the Druids, and their practices.\n\nAcolyte:\nOne who is learning Druidism outside of the Order.\nLost Druids:\nDruids that have disappeared without a trace of explanation. Their return may result in punishment.\n\nForgotten Druids:\nDruids that have been removed from the Order, whether it's by death or unattunement, but despite being 'Forgotten', many of\nthese Druids are unforgotten due to their accomplishments.\n\nShunned Druids:\nDruids that have been shunned by an Arch Druid, due to their actions that have threatened the protection or peace of the Order. No Druid of the Order is peritted to speak with\none, but if a Shunned approached them, they must only say:\n\"Much wind pours from your mouth\".\nIf the Shunned persists, Druids should either ignore them or warn them that defensive action may be taken. This action should be carried out if the Shunned does\nnot heed the warning. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=By:\n    Ariadni Lanyathir", ""),
        StaticBook("Druidic Tasks", "Iatrilemar Elervathar", "Dedicancy started:\nThe 22nd of Sun's Smile.\n\nDedicant:\nAnthron\n\nTeacher:\nAeras Ibar'ker\n\nPS: Suns smile 1515\nPPS: Tay gave most\nof the tasks.\nFirst task:\nThe Aspect Cycle\n\nFind three objects that each represent one of the aspects\n\n*Aeras's signature*\nSecond task:\nBardic Rite\n\nWrite a poem about nature\n\n*Taynuel's signature*e\nThird Task: \nHat task\n\nCreate a hat with things you find in nature.\n\n*Tay's signature.*\nFourth Task:\nTen Flowers\n\nFind ten different types of flowers and plant them around the Grove.\n\n*Tay's signature.*\nFifth task: \nShrooms\n\nFind a woodland creature, get its feces, smear them under your armpit and grow a shroom.\n\n*Tay's signature*\nFirst Lesson:\n\nAll things in the world are natural, trees leaves and even stones. There is but one thing in the world that's unnatural. The Void. This is why when a mage opens the passage from the Void to the realm we live in. a huge amount of\nunnatural energy is released and why Void slinging is dangerous to nature and its balance.\nSixth task:\nA Lecture on Void Slinging.\n\nGo to different cities and lecture to 10 different people about Void slinging and why it's bad.\n\n*Aeras's signature*\nSeventh Task: One With Nature\n\nPretend to be a carrot for an elven hour.\n\n*Tay's signature*\nEighth Task: Study Time\n\nRead the history of the Druidic Order\n\n*Tay's signature*\nNineth task: \nGather the wool\n\nGather wool without shaving a sheep.\n\n*Aeras' signature*\nTenth Task: The List\n\nObtain the following items:\n1) A scrap of cloth from a high elf's robes\n2) A stone from dwarven lands\n3) A cup of sand from orcish lands\n4) An apple from Oren\n\n*Tay's signature*\nEleventh Task: Grow a Tree\n\nSelect a sapling of your choice and grow it into a tree, bonding with it as you do.\n\n*Tay's signature*\nTwelfth Task: Rite of the Staff\n\nUsing a branch from the tree you grew, carve your first Druid's staff.\n\n*Tay's signature*", ""),
        StaticBook("Druidism", "Oracle", "Druidism\n\nRetold by Leyu'Maehr\n\nOracle Library\n*Strange Numbers\n((9/19/13))\nIs this what the druid college is like...? Being idnapped and forced to write books? Er, kidnapped. Not idnapped. They think I'm a druid for some reason... It's as if they're brainwashed.\nThey think I'm an elf, too! I'm a damn dwarf! They trapped Bell in here, too. She's also forced to write. He just said to write..anything. I guess this will be okay to write, maybe...? I'm just jotting down notes... And my thoughts... And why is htis\nhappening!? So, what do write now. I don't even feel like making paragraphs. Hmm. Well, since I last wrote in a journal, Many things have happened. For one, I've been indulged in a quest to find an ancient artifact... It's a magical artifact from\nWinterfall that the undead want. Now it's in the hands of one, named Hwaldar, who hid it. I rea some clues. It's from the Kar'Lani tribe, and is hidden in the \"fake father of Al'Khazaar\". It's cold there, too. I find the whole quest odd, found by books\nwritten by Hwaldar, who is actually an undead himself, yet HE hid the artifact. :: :: I've been living in Al'Khazaar and Laurelin latly. I left Al'Khazaar because the rulers were stupid and no one even realized it, causing a bad monarchy. I went\nto Laurelin, where it turns out a friend did too. Nothing much happened for a while. But then, a few days ago, I found some lvers near a pumpkin and was playing around with them, when a druid invited me in his house to give me a book. I accepted, of\ncourse. I like books. But when I came in, the druid blocked off the door, and gave me enough books to fill my backpack. He commanded me to write and hit me a few times. My friend I mentioned earlier, Bell, was there. The druid was trying to brainwash us\nor something. He kept on saying we were elves and druids, which neither of us were. Bell's human and I'm a dwarf. And I don't think either of us would want to study druidism after this.... Anyways. Thankfully, a guard found it. Er, not it. us. He tried\nto break us out, when the druid teleported Bell and I to the treetops on top of his house . We found a way back down, and I hit him a few times. He then ran away. So pretty much, I think I'll go back to Al'Khazaar... but I'll write about the next\nadventure . :: :: I went to go to Al'Khazaar with Bell after being kidnapped. On the road, we met two men who pleaded for Bell's help to heal a man named Ademas. We went to follow, but Bell dissapeared. I still don't know where she is. We continued on\nthe path, along with an orc shaman who tagged along. Once we got there, the shaman accidentally activated the demon inside him while trying to destroy it. The demon went mad. I wrote about it in a different book. He eventually jumped off a cliff and\ndied. :: :: A while later, the Oren carnival opened. It was fun at first. I won 100 minas at an archery tournament, and watched others fight in the Fight Pits . The Wizard gave me a fortune. He said I would be either a great protector of good or an evil\nbandit. It's obviously a load of crap. But then, something actually happened at the carnival. Undead attacked. A man revealed himself to be undead and lit the place on fire. The king of Al'Khazaar didn't even notice. He, along with the rest of human\nroyalty, is just STUPID. There's no other way to put it. Then everyone just continued playing games, even after a few men died. They didn't even CARE. The people of this world are fools. Maybe the undead do have a point...no. Untrue. Just untrue.\nAnyways, Brum, the first undead I ever met came. veryone thought he was a pale orc, even though he's admitted to be undead many times . The fools... the idiots, the fools... I went to watch one fight. A man that looked very similar to an earlier undead\ncame. He even used the same teqnique; He set the ground on fire wherever he walked to kill the opponets. The fools.. no one noticed, even when I said it. I am surrounded by oblivious morons. No one understands what is going on... :: :: I would write\nmore about my life, but I realize I just don't know who will get this book. I might die and good looted. I mean, get looted. Anyways, I can't let people know of my feelings or all of my thoughts. That's pretty much all of my life so far that I care to\nshare.", ""),
        StaticBook("Druidology", "Valmir_", "Druidology—What is a Druid\nby Druid Respiren\ntranscribed by Elorna Avern\nDruids are the drui, the dryw, the druwid.\nNature's sorcerer, the seer, the oak-knower.\n\nFor those that know the oak, the troew is both the tree and the truth. Mysterious guardian of a sacred grove, wise counselor to monarchs,\ncunning master of many\nshapes, friend of animals, and terrible defender, of unspoiled Nature.\n\nThe Druid revere Nature, wielding power over plants, animals, the weather, and the elements. All druids are of neutral alignment and share an ethos devoted to protecting the\nwilderness and maintaining natural cycles and a balance between good and evil.\n\nThis book was originally found in the Druid's Grove in Elandriel, in Asulon. It was brought over and transcribed by Elorna Avern.", ""),
        StaticBook("Druidology", "Respiren", "~Druidology~\n\nDruids are the druii, the dryw, the druwid.\n\nNature's sorcerer, the seer, the oak-knower.\n\nFor those that know the oak, the trēow is both the tree and the truth.\nMysterious guardian of a sacred grove, wise counselor to monarchs, cunning master of many shapes, friend of animals, and terrible defender of unspoiled Nature.\nThe Druid revere Nature, wielding power over plants, animals, the weather, and the elements.\nAll druids are of neutral alignment and share an ethos devoted to protecting the wilderness and maintaining natural cycles and a balance between good and evil.\n\n~Scribed by Wayward\nDruid Respiren", ""),
        StaticBook("Dsc. of Tapestry", "VenymNyx", "-------------------------\n\n      The Tapestry\n        of Creation\n\n-------------------------\n*This 'book' is not an actual rp book, it is a\nway to be able to\nread the signs above\nfor those that do not\nhave anything like:\n\nOptiFine\nMCPatchers\n\nThis serves as a way\nto read the desc.*\nhttps://i.gyazo.com/ec09780f36411ff5cdb5a56148fa1881.png\nhttps://i.gyazo.com/fcfc60f987a35fe28df7111ff267cbdf.png\nhttps://i.gyazo.com/f8188302ab2e1fad022eb1790cebdad6.png\nhttps://i.gyazo.com/5ae1c3eefa2578589944dcf553cb849a.png", ""),
        StaticBook("Dunstan T.", "Ol' Man Sano", "Dear Dunstan,\n\nIn my time at Skyfall, you had protected me and shielded me from many foes, dangers, and other threats upon my life, as well as assisting me on a personal level.\nAs an ally in the Skyfall Rebellion, and as we were both sitting members on Lanavia's Dragon Council, I do recall drinking quite a bit. I thought that you, of all people, would be able to appreciate this rare, strong liquor.\nTake care, and may we see eachother another day, in another time.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dusty Book", "Unknown", "[!]The entire page has been torn out.\nEntry one\nI figured I start writing this all down, help keep track of everything and to ease my thoughts.  They're alwats swirling in my mind as I feel around for something else to investigate, leading me to forgetting small\ndetails.\n\nMost names in this book are altered for the safety of the poor afflicted souls that I care for.  Not everything in this book is going to be on the same topic.\n\nSeveral years ago, a dear friend of mine that I shall call\nLudleth opened up to me that he had been cursed with a Shade.  I hadn't known very much on the magic/curse at the time, so I wasn't able to provide much help at the time.\n\nAfter a few days of digging around, I discovered that the Shade's curse can\nbe cured by a powerful cleric, but only if its found in its early stages.\n\nThe Shade supposedly grows stronger as time continues on and it turns less of an annoyance and more of a tormenter to the host.  A different newly cursed friend mentioned\nthat he heard only voices in his sleep and experienced frequent nightmares.\n\nLudleth looked awfully tired whenever I saw him, along with acting rather paranoid.  He said he kept seeing shadows on the corners of his eyes that wouldn't be there if he l\ndirectly at them.  He said he felt as if he were always being followed and often heard a voice in his head, a cruel one.\n\nI know that it is too late to save Ludleth, all I can do is make life easier for him to ease him through his suffering.  I am aw\nthat there is a chance of him exploding one day, breaking; the Shade will take over and I will need flee until he can regain control of himself again.  I understand any violent actions made won't be from him, but from the monster inside him.\nEntry Two\n[!] The entire page has been scribbled out completely.\n[!] This page has been scribbled out as well.\nreason was because Albert was \"annoying\" to him.  He was also the one to give Albert the curse, and perhaps with Ludleth as well since he recalled who he was when I described him.\n\nLudleth has said this elf kind once you know him, but I'd still prefe\nkeep my distance and remain unnoticed by him.  Another thing which I find rather unsettling and peculiar is that Ludleth refers to this unknown elf as a father-like figure along with never speaking his name. \n\nLudleth has said to me that this elf is\nto be helping him in learning how to use the dark tendrils of a Shade.  He says it's at least one upside from all of this mess and that he wishes to do good.  I still hope he manages through all of this.\nEntry Three\nI had discovered an old journal of mine from back in Vailor.  I noticed a few entries involved my discoveries of these frozen ruins north of my old tower in Carnatia, which used to be a duchy in the Old Orenian Empire.\nThese have caught my interest, the enteries and notes.  They may be of use for me in the nearing future.\n\nI came across a tomb burrowed into the mountainside north of my old home and there were engravings reading this,\n\"Herein lies Dralazar, Herald of Xion, Lord of Torment.  We are born by the dark; Made men by the dark; Undone by the Dark; We fear the Old Dark.\"\n\nAnother ominous finding was within one of the mountain peaks north-west from the tomb.\nAfter reaching the top, I discovered a gaping hole which formed into a dark stairway that swirled deeper into the hard earth.  If I hadn't carried candles with me, I would have been in pure darkness.  A ladder\nwaited for me at the bottom of the steps, and when I carefully climbed down it, I saw a source of light in that cold, dark place.\n\nFollowing it, I came into a cavern-like room with a sanguine altar.  Words were written above it, in the stone, saying,\n\"Aknu'gul, Remniscent of the Old Fire; an unbeknownst power reborn- his vessel, his will, his herald of ebon.  The abyss will endure.  We. Fear. The. Old. Dark.\"\n\nI have heard and see the phrase mentioning the Old Dark several times in my time.\nI wonder if the Old Dark is to mean anything about the Abyss or who/what may lurk within.\n\nI plan to try to learn more soon.\nEntry Four\nI have met the elf who cursed my friends.  I have not learned his name, and if I ever do, I will keep from writing in here for the safety of myself, my friends, and him.\nThe elf expressed how he didn't like giving others the curse due to how terrible it was, when I questioned him.  But had also said that he wasn't entirely a good person, and continued to give it those who seemed fit for it, and who asked him.\nI understand how he'd say that with Albert, but Ludleth?  It can't possibly be true that he'd ask for something so terrible and dark to happen to him.  I plan to bring this up to him the next time I visit him.\nI had grown worried for Ludleth, he seemed to be getting worse.  He moved out from his old home and into another. \n\nWhen I visited, everything within was destroyed.  It was as if a fight had gone on in there.  Ludleth claimed\nthat it was the shade's doing since he doesn't remember how the destruction came to be.\n\nBut the elf had given him some amulet, saying it will help him with the voices.  He had also shown him how to use this \"#/-=\" in front of me.\nI suppose it's what the tendrils are, since a thick darkness began to form around their hands when they practiced it.  And their eyes turned as dark as pitch.  I was terrified through all of this, to be truthful, but I feel a bit at ease, I guess?\nI know more on this whole deal and I'm feeling more hopeful that Ludleth will make it through this and that he won't harm anyone or himself if he can control this.\nEntry Three\nRemember \"Siegwald of Gelt\"\n6th of The Grand Harvest, 1609\nA strange altar I had discovered  hidden beneath the rather enigmatic mountains north-east of Sutica appears to have been broken.  I found a note beside it, reading -\n\"The Uzg follows you without relent. - Gijaak'Raguk\"\n\nPerhaps if things go silent for me for a bit, I can try to distract myself by investigating this.\n5th of The Sun's Smile, 1609\nI've started going on my walks again.  They help take my mind off of things and are a way for me to get out of the #[-#/,,. [!]The rest is all unreadable.\nWhile I was on a walk today, I came across a peculiar thing in the Enchanted Forest beside Haria on Asul.  A large, wooden door was discovered on the side of one of the mountains.  Past it, is a ruined cavern-like hall leading up to a curious and rather\nornate door.\n\n[!] The rest of the book appears to be unfinished.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dwarves V1", "Mi'Tha'Kaal", "The Grand Kingdom\nOf Urguan   \n              \"The Father\"\n\n\nThis is the place where dwarves live, little creaturs of the north, thay habbit in mountains and caves most of the time, but they have establesments outside too.\nDwarves are known for they'r\ngreat mining tehniqes and the way that extract precious ores vrom the caverns in witch they habbit.\n\nEvery dwarf has a beard, It's a thing for honor, they drink much too, at the dwarves feasts they invite all the races beeing greatfull and sharing all\nthey'r food and drink whit others.\n\n\nThe dwarves tend to build houses in the mountains and underground, they'r architecture beeing quite simple, building large halls for feastes, grand smelters and anvil rooms, furnances\nand other equipament to\neasy they'r job at the forge, they also build statues of themselves beeing so good stonemasons they make great work of it.\n\n\nThey have small amounts of books due they'r small amount of knowlege, but they have contraptions and mechanisms of large amount.\nThey have well forged armour, and not a very powerfull army. Due to past events.\n\n\nAlso dwarves love gold,and a good cooked steak. Eating whit no manners and speacking whit no manners too make them an unworthy race.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dynatite Study", "Elwrick Albright", "THE DYNATITE STUDY\n-by Elwrick Albright-\n\nA Magical Science Fiction Short Story\n\nWritten 1574\n{OOC: For those who don't want to murder their chat, you can also read The Dynatite Study here http://tinyurl.com/hqfwwju }\nCHAPTER ONE\n\nThe hot summer sun shone, having no alternative, down on the town and on the back of Finnegan Clark as he walked swiftly down the center of the road. He listened to the sound of the gravel crunching beneath his feet until he had progressed\nfurther into the town where the streets were paved with cobblestone. There up against the heart of the town lay the manor of the renowned mage Abraham Montey, the man who discovered Dynatite. \nFor centuries it was firmly believed that it was impossible\nfor a gem to be able to hold a truly infinite supply of mana, but that is just what Dynatite seemed to do. Like thanhium, the source of this new gem’s mana is extremely dangerous to observe, but it’s still rather simple to enchant other items to draw mana\nfrom it. It was perfect-- nothing short of a miracle and a dream come to reality for transfigurationists everywhere.\nIndirectly, Abraham was the reason no one would ever have to reset a timekeeping device manually again, the reason fountains of evoked\nwater would never run dry, the reason cooking no longer required fire, the reason telekinetic enchantments on armour became practical, and the reason candles became obsolete in favour of magelight lamps. And people waved and 'good day'ed Finnegan as\nhe paced onwards toward his destination, for to them he was none other than the stellar apprentice in transfiguration of Abraham himself, on his way to another lesson. And he waved back at them. \n\nHe crossed through the iron gate and ascended the steps\nto the sturdy wooden doors of the great stone manor, whose walls were a garden of tangled ivy and mandevilla vines. Several of its windows featured lovely geometric patterns of stained glass in vibrant greens and blues. \nMounted next to the door was a\nsimple orange gem that when tapped would command a clever mechanism to ring a bell deep inside the bowels of the house. Its crystal of Dynatite was not visible, but it did have one. \nIn an instant, Abraham was at the door, wearing his typical dark green\nand dusty robes, his entire person flecked with trinkets and pendants bearing gems. Each of his fingers sported its own unique ring, which also had gems set into them. His eyes sparkled subtly as he smiled and invited Finnegan inside.\n“At the conclusion of our last lesson you expressed interest in my timekeeping device..” he started, once they had sat down to tea. \n“Mm!” Finn nodded eagerly, his mouth stuffed with a big bite of teacake. \n“You’ll be getting to make one of your own.\nI’ve decided it’d be a valuable lesson in enchanting for you to see how a transfigurationist can work together with a mage trained in a different type of magic to create an enchantment..” he said, waiting until his apprentice was able to speak.\nFinnegan swallowed the teacake and immediately began asking questions; “How can two mages work together to create one enchantment?” “What does it have to do with the timekeeper?” “The pointers move slightly at regular intervals-- that uses telekinesis..?”\nAnd after each question, Abraham granted him an answer.\n\nOnce they had finished their tea, he took the timekeeper down off the wall where it hung like a painting and showed it to Finnegan, told him to observe it for a moment and tell him how he would go\nabout making one of his own. \n“Why, I’d fashion a disc with a peg in the middle, fasten the pointer hand to it and hold it on with a stopper. Next, add those same twelve tic-marks around the edge, all spaced apart at equal intervals. Then I'd label them\n12 midnight, 3 dawn, 6 noon, 9 dusk,” he said, glancing up at Abraham, who nodded silently in approval for him to continue. “Then I’d put its mana gem here,” he pointed to the center of the timekeeper, over the stopper. “And enchant the thing to move its\npointer around the dial real slow like it’s doing now.. And I’d have it draw a continuous stream of mana from this piece of Dynatite nearby.” \n“Very good, Finn. Care to show me?” he asked, lifting a box off the shelf and opening it before his apprentice\nto reveal all the materials he had described in his process. “I’ll aid you with the telekinesis enchantment.”\nFinnegan nodded, and eagerly got to work while his instructor ferried porcelain teacups to the automatic washbasin in the other room.\nAnd like this the afternoon continued, with Abraham offering small bits of wisdom to Finnegan as he worked. \n“Mr. Montey,” Finnegan said to get his attention after they had finished the last step in creating the timekeeper and had been left for a moment\nto think. “Does Dynatite ever run out of mana, do you think? I know it’s never happened before, but do you think one day it might? And then everything will stop?” he asked. \n“I don’t think it will.”\n“How’s that work, then? Don’t you know where it gets its\ninfinite supply of mana?” he asks, blinking curiously up at Abraham, who didn’t respond, but sat still as a marble statue as he thought. \n“Aw c’mon, you were the one who discovered it!” Finnegan chuckles. “Really don’t know?” \n“Can’t say I do.” Abraham\nshook his head, offering a thin smile. “No one really does. It’s like thanhium-- can’t really look at it like that,” he shrugged. \n“Well, I’m gonna study it, then!” Finnegan proclaimed boldly. “Why, if we knew that, imagine what else might be possible!\nWe’d be honoured all across the world! Well, you’re already honoured all across the world, but then I would be too--”\n“No!” Abraham cut him off and stood abruptly, towering and booming like a rumbling black cloud over his apprentice who was still seated\nin his chair. Finnegan froze, bewildered, and waited carefully for what was to be said next. \n“No.. Don’t ever think about studying Dynatite again,” he said firmly.\n“Yes, sir..” Finnegan spoke quietly, still dazed, and dreadfully disappointed.\n“I understand if you want to work alone… but… please, when you’ve got Dynatite figured out, do you think you can tell me..? I just want to know what makes it so great…” \nAbraham let out a long sigh and pinched the bridge of his nose to calm himself.\nFinnegan hadn’t meant any offense by it. “Yes, yes..” he grumbled, hesitantly sitting down again. “I’ll let you know.”\nCHAPTER TWO\n\nMonths passed as Finnegan waited for an answer, and each time he asked, “any news on your Dynatite study?” he was met with a dismissive “patience, Finn,” as Abraham avoided other details he might ask about. He began to realize that even\nAbraham might be unable to solve this mystery… Often when he was at home, he gazed up at his timekeeper not to determine the hour, but to puzzle over the fantastic little crystal of Dynatite that powered it. \nIt was difficult to determine the exact\nmoment Finnegan decided he would go against Abraham’s word and study Dynatite. Like filling a cup, it is hard to tell how many careful drops of water it will take before the water runs over the edge, but indeed there is a final drop that breaks that\nsurface tension, just as there must have been some last drop of temptation that caused Finnegan’s curiosity to drive him to action. \nHe was aware from what Abraham taught him that he couldn’t interact with Dynatite’s mana directly, so he would have to\ntake a different approach to his study than messing around in a lab. He figured it might be useful to gather some basic information before getting deeper into the study. On the other side of town, past Abraham’s manor, he knew of a shop that sold\nenchanting supplies, where he had visited many times as a transfigurationist-in-training. This would be the first time he had ever been there alone. \n\nHe decided to pass through the public park on his way there, simply because he liked watching the\nfountains as he passed by. The quaint, lush park contrasted greatly with the section of the town he was heading to, where the streets were narrow and the buildings loomed overhead in place of trees. He held his hands in his pockets as he walked, looking\nup at the old, creaking shop signs, hanging out over the street with peeling letters. Eventually, he spotted the one he had been looking for, which read The Velvet Box. It was only legible because the letters had been carved and not just painted. The door\nwas bordered by two marble golems standing stock-still. They didn’t move as Finnegan let himself in. The bell above the door rang out into the empty room, causing a figure behind the front desk to stir and come to life. He was a jolly, portly man with\ncreases at the corner of his eyes from his constant cheerful smile.\n“Ah, Finnegan! Good to see ya, boy!” He bellowed as he caught sight of him. \n“Good afternoon, Mr. Milo!”\n“Abraham aint with ya?”\n“No, sir.”\n“Runnin’ errands for him?”\n“No, sir. I just want to ask some questions about Dynatite if that’s alright!” \nFinnegan scurried over to Mr. Milo’s desk and hoisted himself up onto it. \n“Sure thing, lad, sure thing! Ask away,” he said. He didn't seem nearly as opposed to Finnegan's\ncuriosity on the subject as Abraham was. \n“Where does Dynatite come from? Do you know how it’s formed?” he asked professionally, unfolding a piece of paper from his pocket and snatching a quill off the desk. \nMr. Milo shrugged. “Not sure. The suppliers\naint tell me where they get it from.”\nFinnegan nodded disappointedly, scribbling this down on the paper.\n“But I do have an idea of how it’s formed,” he said, raising his pointer finger into the air to let him know he wasn’t done talking.\n“Like obsidian, Dynatite doesn’t have a crystal structure-- or at least, not one big enough that I can see it. The coloring of obsidian comes from impurities in it, usually iron, that are caught in with the silica. The reason why it doesn’t have any\ncrystals is because it cooled so fast into a solid that it didn’t have time to grow any!” Mr. Milo explained as Finnegan scribbled down everything he was saying with furious speed, nodding as he listened. \n“If it was my guess, I’d say Dynatite is a type\n‘a volcanic glass, like obsidian but not-- it’s almost completely translucent, which means that it doesn’t have any other materials in it but silica!”\n“Thanks a bunch!” Finnegan exclaimed. He knew it was a good idea to ask Mr. Milo about this.\n“Need anything else?”\n“No, sir,” he said, shaking his head. \nThe crisp ringing of a little bell rang out into the space, and the duo directed their attention to the door.\nThere stood a brown-eyed girl who looked just a bit older than Finnegan, wearing a\nhooded woolen cloak over her plain dress. She carried a leather satchel with her. \n“Welcome to The Velvet Box, how can I help ya?” Mr. Milo said automatically, not having been acquainted with the girl before. Finnegan offered her a friendly wave.\n“I’d like to purchase twenty minas worth of Dynatite,” she said, taking a small drawstring bag from her satchel. She spoke in a hushed, polite voice, and her manner seemed mild and pleasant.\n“Sure thing, miss!” Mr. Milo said, rummaging around in the\nsupply bins held behind the counter until he found two crystals of Dynatite that met his unspoken standards. He got up from his chair and waddled over to the balance scales with the two gems.\n“Oh, that reminds me!” Finnegan exclaimed. “Mr. Milo, do you\nknow any other people who could help me with my Dynatite study? Abraham didn’t want to.”\n“Hmm, I dunno any names other than other humble salesmen like meself,” the man shrugged. “They know as much as I do.”\n“Darn.. alright, but thank you anyway! You've\nbeen a huge help already!”\n“Hey, no problem, Finn.” \nAt Finnegan’s seemingly harmless question, the girl’s soft face had contorted in an expression of absolute horror that had gone unnoticed in her silence while the two talked.\n{OOC: Minecraft books can only hold up to 50 pages, so this story will have to be continued later! You can still view the live link http://tinyurl.com/hqfwwju \nfor updates. Sorry for the cut-off!}\n\nEND OF PART ONE.", ""),
        StaticBook("Economy & Merits", "Ol' Man Sano", "The Myth of\n    Meritocracy\n----------------\n\nBell Sano\n\n11th of Sun's Smile, 1613\nPrelude:\n\nThis essay is one that should expand on a subject that I've only barely touched upon in earlier works, specifically \"The Sanoist Manifesto,\" where I discussed economics.\nWe are to explore the true embracement of a so called \"Meritocracy,\" and how one can truly be created, not through a capitalistic society, but through the use of socialist policies.\nA meritocracy, in the sense of economics, at least, is defined by the procurement of material wealth through hard work. Equal work for equal pay, essentially. Those who work the hardest will generate the most wealth.\nThe true creation of a meritocracy must be the most beautiful thing for a society to accomplish. Unfortunatley, the scourage of capitalism has perverted this glorious element of economics.\nIn a civilization dominated by the industry, otherwise, the businesses themselves, you will not see a distribution of wealth dependent on the hard labor of the working class. It will be disproportionate.\nShould the businesses themselves determine what is a fair wage to pay their workers, then naturally, all workers will be underpaid. It is only human nature, those at the top of the economic ladder will allow greed to take hold.\nHowever, that does not mean that the elimination of capitalism is the solution. While that would, admittedly, destroy the income inequality among nations, it would also prevent any meritocracy at all from being formed.\nSo, what is the answer to this dichotomy? Mutualism, the belief that government involvement should regulate industry to the point where the working class is able to survive by default of simply living in their own society.\nIt is immoral and unethical to allow the working class, the backbone of a society, to go hungry, homeless, or poor, simply because their employer has refused to pay them enough to survive.\nTherefor, the government and the state should intervene, setting up a default, minimum standard of living, which no individual may fall beneath. With the introduction of methods such as a minimum wage, -\nindustry regulation, social assistance, welfare, and much more, the government can create a safety net of sorts, a level of poverty which one musn't ever fall beneath.\nThis standard is to be determined by objective, measurable statistics. For example, how much wealth does one need to posess in order to pay for housing, food, clothing, and other necessary services?\nIf those essential necessities are covered, then no extra luxuries are to be granted to those at the bottom of the economic ladder. From there on out, capitalism is to take hold, and individuals are responsible for-\nprocuring their own wealth in the free market. This isn't to say that further regulation cannot be imposed on the industry to ensure that one individual or business creates a single corporate monopoly over one industry, or -\nso that the workers are not unfairly paid, but it does mean that the private market must be the primary benefactor of the majority of citizens. You cannot create a socialist state, in which everyone is dependent on the public sector, for -\nthat would be the opposite of a meritocracy.\nTo conclude, the answer to creating an economy where workers are paid a fair amount for equal amounts of labor is not free market capitalism, but rather, the embracement of mutualism, socialism, and regulation.\n~ Bell Acaele'par Amuel R. Sano", ""),
        StaticBook("EG: Book 1", "Alifer Amice", "-=The Explorer's Guide=-\n\nBook 1-8\n\nContent:\n\nThe Isle of Tahn, Part 1\n1. Alifer's Bluff\n2.The Tahnari Desert\n3. The Rift of Cinder\n4. The Lost Isle\nDisclaimer: \n\nThe names used to name Tahn's many realms are inspired by the Island's name. The Atlas produced by the empire of Oren are \"Official\" but should be taken with a grain of salt for the sake of the explorer's out there.\n--------<Chapter 1>---------\n\n          Alifer's Bluff\n\nBetween the plains of Tahnar and the Tahnari desert is a pass I've named Alifer's bluff. The pass is a large messa of blisteringly hot clay and sand, the enviroment is inhospitable to life.\nAlifer's bluff is littered with small cacti, the juices inside the cacti can be consumed in place of water. \nWhen the sun sets, the unwelcoming touch of winter's kiss enters the Bluff, any who find themselves on the surface will require a heatsource.\nNote: \n\nWhen I ventured to Alifer's bluff, night creeped into the bluff and the chill of death forced me to huddle by my camp fire. In the darkness stirred the wild howls of something..strange, something I never heard before..\n-------<Chapter 2>----------\n\n       The Great Tahnari\n                Desert\n\nI woke up covered in minor burns, the blistering sun woke me where I slept. I packed what I could and moved north.\nI had to climb my way through the bluff and risk life and limb to reach the Tahnari desert. I managed to safely climb down a sandy slope, I couldn't help but feel as though I was being watched.\nI've seen nothing but barren sand for miles, the dunes have been disturbed somewhat but no signs of life can be seen for miles. There's quite a few cacti around the desert so water has not been an issue. How would the cacti acquire the water though?\nBreakthrough! I found a well containing water, the structure is made of intricate sandstone, could there have been a civilization dwelling in the desert long before we arrived?\nYet another breakthrough!\nI managed to find a miraculous oasis close to the well, the water here is fresh. Purer then anything I've tasted before, but that might just be my thirst.\nLarge trees have grown around the oasis, they seem quite old.\nNote: Sandstone tends to poke out of the dunes time from time, they look like structures. This may further prove the existence of a lost civilisation.\n---<The Rift of Cinders>--\nAssuming an ancient civilisation did live in this desert once, then I may have found the root of it's extinction. The Rift of Cinders is located in the north eastern centre of the Tahnari.\nThe bottom of the rift is covered in a blood red layer of cinder-like sand. To the north of the rift is a tranquil island, the rift could of been created as a result of the destruction of Aegis..but my gut tells me this is a lie.\nWhat's mysterious about the rift is the red sand, why would sand be red? Furthermore, this is a desert, why has the sand not simply covered the rift? Something has been pushing away the sand, keeping the rift from collapsing.\nWalls of sandstone can also be seen lining the rift, it leaves you to wonder, what could of created such a strong impact?\n-------<The Lost Isle>------\n\nTo the north of the rift of cinders is the Lost Isle. The isle is fertile and covered in a thick forest of birch trees. Large mushrooms seem to dot its landscape. Wildlife is also plentiful here, mayhaps they came from here?", ""),
        StaticBook("Ehier report -L", "Ljhin", "------------------\n\nReport on Ehier\n\n------------------\nEhier was found in the silver city, he seemed paranoid to the point of shivering, confused and distorted from the area. \n\nI suspect either magical means or his own sanity catching up to him? (Elven old age?). Reguardless this report is based\non his attack against the guard, Ehier. Who runs the private investagor department of information. \n\nI did inform him of the rules of doing such but he persisted. I detained him, taking his keys before removing him from the city.\nI suggest keeping him out of the city to an exile for a few elven days until it is seen for him to be 'sane' once again.\n\n~\nLjhin.", ""),
        StaticBook("Eldritch Tome", "Adorellan Sintel", "[The tome is littered in runic glyphs, stained in a scarlet hue, its contents reveals the sacred knowledge of a lost spell from the eldritch blood magi. The ability to weave rifts from blood.]\n((Upon legitimately obtaining this tome you are bequeathed the\nknowledge of blood magic rifts- albeit requires you to be a blood magi to wield it.))", ""),
        StaticBook("Electric Evo.", "Haadi Mubdee", "=--=--=--=--=--=--=            Electrical\n           Evocation\n=--=--=--=--=--=--=\n\n\n     -< ^v^v^v^v^\nThere is an old saying that humans (mortals) fear most other humans. I believe, however, that those who say that have never looked outside the confines of the human world. If anyone has come face to face with the power of nature, they will consider the\nprevious proverb a joke. If this sounds like nothing more than nonsense coming from an old fool, then answer this next question. If you can possess any form of power, what would you choose? Would you choose the power of mankind, or that of a wild beast?\nWould it be the roars of powerful men, or the sound of thunder that shakes the heavens? Is it the limited life of men, or nature's continuous cycle of life? Whichever way you look at it, the power of man is feeble compared to the grandeur of nature.\nThroughout history, all of mankind has admired nature's power and though they had feared it, they tried to deny that. This is one of man's many follies. They neglect nature's power, which does not discriminate, solely because they are a part of nature.\nIn particular, as humans learned of Mana and started seeing a glimpse of nature's other realm, they began neglecting nature's power even more. They didn't realize that their \"magic\" was actually an imitation of nature's power. This is what worries me.\nThere are many students who are Wizards and Druids in training who do not understand that every magic's starting point is a natural phenomenon. I, who also boasted in my knowledge of Electric magic , did not learn this until I saw lightning strike down at\nthe Crown Lands Plateau of Oren. In hopes that those who come after me will not make the same mistake, I decided to write this book. In other words, I hope that beginner wizards will learn the laws of nature and have a healthy fear of it as well.\nAlthough this book only deals with lightning power, which is only one of nature's awesome power, if you are wise, you will take the moral of the story to heart and apply it when training other magic as well.\nThe Principle of Electricity series Magic Skill\n                -=-\nIn order to understand the principle of Electric magic, you must first learn its natural counterpart: Lightning. If you've seen anyone use Electric-based magic, you probably noticed a close resemblance to a lightning strike. The lightning strike occurs\nwhen Mana, the energy that surrounds us, splits into two polarities of energy for reasons unknown. These split polarities each continue to accumulate energy, when, in an instant, an explosion of energy flow occurs between heaven and earth.\nThe intensity of the light and heat during this process contains tremendous power. Also, because of its unpredictability of where it strikes, it has been an object of fear to mankind. There are many opinions as to when and why Mana, splits into two\npolarities of energy. However, before anyone could come up with any concrete evidence, the debate's focus shifted because of the ‘great’ Wizard Ambrosia, who at times lacked common sense. He claimed that he was able to stabilize his Mana to split the two\npolar energies in a controlled manner, which caused all the scholars to shift their focus from the conditions in which the energy splits to the process of it. (It is a shame that scholars today are not interested in insightfully studying natural\nphenomena, and rather just want to uncover it just for the sake of using it. This is quite foolish.) Once Mana is split into two polar energies, each polarity begins accumulating energy at a rapid rate and causes an electric discharge. Then, when the\nbalance of energy between the two polarities is broken, a transfer of energy occurs from the one with more energy to the other. So imagine what would happen if one could embody either of the polarities and designate his or her target as the other\npolarity. Then, using Mana, if he or she polarizes the Mana and also raises his/her own energy level to be higher than their target, what would happen?\nExactly. This is what is known as Electrical Energy Magic.\nHow to use the Lightning Bolt\n                -=-\nThe Lightning Bolt attack is a magic that uses the mechanic of creating static electricity, which in turn utilizes the characteristics of the negative charge for a sudden electrostatic discharge. During the energy transfusion, a bright explosion\nresembling a lightning strike, rushes toward your target as Mana is depleted into replicating this phenomenon. Once all the Mana is depleted from the bolt and the surrounding elements reach equilibrium, the flow of energy ends. (Just like a lightning\nstrike in nature.) There are many questions surrounding this magic, such as \"How powerful is it?\" and \"How easy is it to use?\", which is technically asking how much energy it needs and how long it takes. To give you an answer, there is a limit to how much\nenergy you can gather, and you can only maintain the energy for about 15 seconds until later coming to a greater grasp of the art. You can charge your energy multiple times to gather more energy, but it is reported that it can become highly unstable after\nafter the third charge which is already risky enough. Also, you only have about 15 seconds to charge all your energy. This is because of several factors, such as the difficulty of maintaining the Mana's focus, and also maintaining the polarized energy at\nthe same time. (Even if you have plenty of Mana, it is difficult to charge for an extensive electrical bolt). The ‘Lightning Bolt’ attack is used to strike your enemy with electricity . Once your opponent is struck with this attack, they will be in a\nstate of shock due to the electricity surging within them as it an energy. Not a tangible object. Since this attack is based on an instant energy explosion between you and your opponent, the lesser the energy gap between you and your opponent, the great\ndamage it will inflict as the longer the distance the surge of electricity must travel, the more it discharges. Wasting precious Mana in the long run.\nSimple\n              Usage\n                -=-\nOnce you've carefully read through this book, and understood the principles behind the Lightning Bolt attack and are ready to use it, you can do so by following these simple steps. First, a connection to the Void is a must. As any form of magic. The\nsimplest manner in which to begin evoking such an element is to picture the empty black abyss that is the Void. A sleet of pure nothingness. Void of any life as the name suggests. Now one must mentally picture lightning crashing down upon the Earth. But\nstrictly the lighting. If one were to picture the scene, one could possibly border the realm of Pseudomancy (Illusionary magic) or if too much detail is placed on the Earth, soil or stone may be produced. Then you will see the static discharge enivision\nsuch an occurring unfolding before your palm you calm your mind to allow your Mana to polarize the energy and fuel it. Once the preparation is finished, lightning-like strands of light energy will flow around you. This indicated you have successfully\ncalibrated yourself with the Void and established an affinity to Electrical Evocation.\n\nThough mentioned before, I want to remind you that the intense light and heat from this attack can significantly startle your opponent.\nApplication:\n    Chain Lightning\n               -=-\nBefore we move on, I need to reiterate and explain in detail regarding multiple charges. As you know by now, the Lightning Bolt attack is very similar to the actual lightning strike that happens in nature. Does this mean that this magic is capable of\nimitating the continuous strikes that occur in a natural lightning strike?\n\nThe answer is yes. Scholars call this ‘Chain Lightning’. By charging the magic multiple times, you are able to hurl this energy to your target back to back.\nHowever, there is a limit to how many times you can strike in a row. As previously mentioned, since you can charge up to about three bolts, yet the risk increases with each charge. One interesting fact is, these bolts of energy attract to metallic\nobjects. Thus when in the vicinity of metal objects such as the bands of a barrel, swords and armor, iron grating, and other Ferrum or Arcarum apparel, the bolt will change it’s path of perjectory and curve to meet said object.\nContinuous Attack\n    Between Lightning\n         Bolt Users\n               -=-\nWe looked at the principle behind the Lightning Bolt, the Chain Lightning attack, and the application of these attacks in the previous chapter. If you think you've mastered everything through these two attacks, you still have a lot to learn from mother\nnature. If anyone has studied lightning strikes carefully, you know that lightning does not only occur in single, or multiple chain of strikes. Sometimes, lightning strikes attract other lightning and fuse together. Thus, where there are multiple\nLightning Bolt users, they can fuse each other's energy to form a collaborative attack.\n\nThis is a unique trait of Electric energy based magic that other ‘generic’ elemental based magic do not possess. When a user is charging his or her Lightning bolt\nattack, you can add on to their energy and instantly form a Chain Lightning attack. In other words, if you have charge your Lightning Bolt attack near another user that is charging, your charge will add to their charge, increasing their total number of\ncharges.\nThe Effects\n                of\n        Lightning Bolt\n               -=-\nSo, when is it a good time to use the Lightning Bolt attack? If you are wise, you should be able to figure it out yourself.\n\nFirst, the Lightning attack is good when facing multiple targets at once. Try it out yourself.\nUse skill of Electrical Evocation and attempt to fire off a bolt at a grouping of targets.. You will be amazed at how effective and convenient this property can prove to be.\nHowever, there is something you must remember: Chaining charges  inflicte damage which subsequently decreases with each hit. Beginners, unaware of this, might overuse the attack and find themselves out of Mana and getting attacked by the opponent.\nEven when you successfully use the Chain attack, the opponent might not have received as much damage as you think. Thus, the first target of the Chain Lightning Skill is very important. This is something every good wizard should be mindful.\nAuthor: Archmage Crumena V. Illwindior [HeeroZero]\n\nConsoliant: Electomancer Ceruberr Asul'Ailer [CaptainSheepy]\n\nCopier:\nGuildmaster Haadi Mubdee [Eladriendil]", ""),
        StaticBook("Electric Evo.", "Elluna Koortova", "Electric \n         Evocation\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  By Gauldrim Irongut\nChapter 1, Uses of Electromancy:\n\nElectromancy is a very volatile form of arcane evocation, is just as likely to veer off it’s course or shock the user. A source of incredible heat and force, electromancy is a formidable tool. Slow to conjure\nand is a lifelong commitment electromancy can be used in survival situations. Able to create fires when need be through the burning of wood or other flammable materials. Another property that can be found in electromancy is  the extreme attraction\nto large amounts of metal. An anvil, a suit plate of armour, or a large iron gate can cause the electricity to be attracted towards it and then channeled inside of it. If one is to touch a piece of metal charged with electricity they will be hurt or burnt\nas the electricity discharges. The most obvious use of electric evocation is the use of it in combat. A deadly force to be reckoned with once the user has achieved a high enough power to use it. Slow to conjure, though fast once released, electric\nevocation is one of the most powerful forms of arcane evocation. Able to kill a large man in full plate mail in a single bolt, if large enough this just lends perspective to the raw power. Electric evocationists also have the ability to summon forth\nlightning from the heavens in the event of a storm with very good accuracy.\nChapter 2, Properties of Electromancy:\n\nAttracted to metal, can be conducted through metal, has the force to shatter stone and the ability to travel through water. Electromancy is as versatile as it is powerful. Electric\ncurrents can be sent through water enabling one to shock someone that is in contact with the said body of water. This practice also applies to metal and if one is in contact with a suit of plate mail when the electric current is sent towards the bearer\nthey will experience not only the force of the bolt but the current of the electricity as well. The current of the electricity will also cause muscle seizure and the dulling of senses. The shattering of stone occurs when an extremely powerful bolt is sent\nhurtling towards the stone, resulting in flying rubble and scorched rock. As well as being able to scorch rock, Electromancy can set wood, paper, and any other flammable materials alight causing fire and burns.\nChapter 3, Conclusion: \n\nElectromancy is an almighty power to be reckoned with and those that perform it should be regarded with extreme caution. Slow to cast into immense power yet still dangerous even at short range.\nIt is advised that when in combat against such a mage, that large amounts of metal and or armour are unadvised to have and even steel or iron greatswords. So to wrap this short informative text up, one would be wise to heed the words of an electromancer\nand to regard the raw power and wisdom of those that wield it.\nCopied by Elluna Koortova", ""),
        StaticBook("Electricity", "Fury_Fire", "12th of the Deep Cold\n((6:30))\nLightning struck some distance away. After searching for some time, it was found to be the root of a tree that had been struck. Upon examination, it was charred, a slight stench coming from it. By all appearences, the tree\nlooked to have been burned. The only thing that told me otherwise was the static electricity still in the air for a short time around it.\n6th of Malin's Welcome\n((12:40pm))\nSanctuary\nLightning had struck only a short distance away, in the nearby forest. After searching, the path of earth that was struck had been found. Being even near the strike that had happened moments before left\nthe taste of metal in my mouth, and the smell of burning grass. The ground looked as if it had caught aflame for some time, yet the downpour had put it out. Other then that, the lightning strike itself was caught in full view. It had shot down\ndiagonally from the sky, other minor areas branching off from the strike. It had been followed by a loud clap of thunder.\n5th of the Grand Harvest\n((11:44 AM))\nSpoke to Nemir, a Telekenisis user.\nShe mentioned tha\n*The rest of the page is ripped out*\n5th of the Grand Harvest\n((11:45 AM))\nSpoke to Nemir, telekenisis user.\nStated that every time one connects to the void, they get a tad weaker as their magic grows a tad stronger. Explained that they would clear their mind, much as done in\nnormal meditation, and then one would imagine said element in their mind, along with their target. As they did this, they would envision a connection with the void. Often, one would twitch someplace when they connected, and their bodies would be put under\ngreat stress.\n5th of the grand harvest, 1554.\n((11:25 AM))\nI sat in my home, having connected with the void. The spark I summoned remained there for some second, before I would aim to brighten it, as shown before. As this happened I would grow tired almost immediatly,\nthe spark vanishing and I fell over, exhausted. I had felt something different then the normal rate of mana consumption, however. As I forced myself to use the mana required to make the spark brighter, I felt something that could only be described as a\na portion of 'life force' being withdrawn. I couldn't quite tell the amount, but I assumed this was my mana. All I could learn from this attempt was that it used up more mana then a normal spark.\nSometime in the Amber Cold, 1554\n((1-2 am-ish?))\nI allowed myself to be struck by electricity in my Augur form. Almost all feeling left me side pain, my entire body feeling as if it had become static. Side that, I could not tell much else about it.\n15th of the Amber Cold.\n((9 PM))\nI had now grown familiar with telling the amount of mana being used. As I would brighten my spark, I now fully felt the mana leave me. I had over time grown accustomed to how much Mana I had anyways, which\nis a major help as I determine the usage. I remain aware that my mana pool will end up growing eventually through meditation anyways, yet I would imagine it would be slow enough that I would grow used to it as such happened.\n11th of the First Seed, 1556.\n((5:44 PM))\n\n[!]Page has been torn out angrily!\n16th of the Deep Cold, 1557.\n((10:39 PM))\nI sat upon an altar in a forest with Nemir, preparing to shoot a bolt of electricity. It began with normal meditation, and the summoning of several sparks. I would concentrate them within the center of\nmy palm, forming a 'bolt', of sorts. After this I would hold my hand out and release it forward.\nThe bolt would hit the ground, leaving the air with a light feel of static for some moments before it would vanish and the brunt of fatigue hit me.\n9th of the Sun's Smile, 1559\n((3:30 PM))\nAt this point, not much had changed side my bolts growing steadily stronger as well as my ability to cast more. At this point I can cast three before I run out of mana, and the chance of me forgetting to\ncut the connection with the void before firing is minimal. I have finally noticed to conductive affects of metal, having cast near an iron rod once. My bolt had veered in midair, hitting the rod instead of continuing to go straight.\n12th of the Amber Cold, 1559\n((6:50 PM))\nA Kharajyr female was attacking a group of elves as I stood back and raised my hand, curious on how powerful my bolts had truely grown. Sparks began to form as well as sweat upon my brow, soon collecting\nwithin the center of my palm to form a bolt. It was obviously weak in power compared to Locke's, yet still okay in my eyes. Soon I let it fly towards the Kha, and the effects were surprising. The Kha fell over, stunned for some moments as the elves took\nthat chance to grab the Kha and bind it. Upon further inspection, the Kha bore a charred burn mark where the bolt had hit- although likely only caused due to her fur temporarily catching aflame.\n9th of the Sun's Smile, 1562\nThis hasn't been written in for some time, but it's about time to continue it. Since my last entry, my bolts have grown to full power and I'm able to cast three in a row before being unable to cast another. A full powered bolt\nwill easily leave burns on someones skin and make them paralyzed for some while. Alternatively, I can call a bolt down from the sky.. Such is done as a normal bolt is made within the hand. The difference would be that you're treating a point in the sky as\nthough it would be what you were summoning with instead of your hands. This alone would cause much more mana, and you'd also need a view of your target. It would take as much mana as though you summoned a normal bolt and shot it to that point in the sky.w\nPast that, you would pour much more mana than a normal bolt of electricity into it, soon to the point where it would be a full powered bolt of lightning ready to be launched. At first it would remain very hard to aim, and almost every  shot would miss.\nThese would not grow more powerful, and the reason you summon it in the sky is simple: Controlling that amount of mana close to you is stupid and dangerous. Even if you controlled it, the amount of electricity would harm you even if you are the creator.\nAs you continue doing such, it will become much easier to aim and not stress you as much.\nFinal words:\nThis book was originally aimed as a record of my learning, yet eventually I decided that it could be used to help any aspiring Electric Evocationists learn. It does not cover everything about the magic, although it still does with a lot of\nit. And I urge any who would use it to be cautious and find another electric evocationist to assist them in learning, be it as a teacher or mentor. This magic is dangerous to learn and at times I nearly killed myself with it.\n-Lefkos Glowsbane", ""),
        StaticBook("Electromancy", "RedBench", "Electric Evocation\n\n\nBy Gauldrim Irongut\nChapter 1: Uses of Electromancy.\n\nElectromancy is a very volatile form of arcane evocation, it is just as likely to veer off its course or shock the user. A source of incredible heat and force electromancy is a formidable tool.\nSlow to conjur and is a life long committment electromancy can be used in survival situations. Able to create fires when need be through the burning of wood or other flammable materials. Another property that can be found in electromancy is the extreme\nattraction to large amounts of metal. An anvil, a suit of plate armour or a large iron gate cause the electricty to be attractedd towards it and then channelled inside of it. If one is to touch a piece of metal charged with electricity they will be hurt\nas the electricity discharges. The most obvious use of electric evocation is the use of it in combat. A deadly force to be reckoned with once the user has achieved a high enough power to use it. Slow to conjur but fast once released electric evocation\nis one of the most powerful forms of arcane evocation. Able to kill a large man in full platemail in a single bolt if large enough this just lends persepective to the raw power. Electric evocationists also have the ability summon forth lightning from\nthe heavens in the event of a storm with verry good accuracy.\nChapter 2: Properties of Electromancy\n\nAttracted to metal, can be conducted through metal, has the force to shatter stone and the ability to travel through water. Electromancy is as versitile as it is powerful.\nElectric currents can be sent through water enabling one to shock someone that is in contact with the said body of water. This practice also applies to metal and if one is in contact with a suit of platemail when the electric current is sent towards the\nbearer they will experience not only the force of the bolt but the current of the electricty will also cause muscle seizure and the dulling of senses. The shattering of stone occurs when an extremely powerful bolt is sent hurtling towards stone resulting\nin flying rubble and scorched rock. As well as being able to scorch rock electromancy can set wood, paper and any other flammable material alight causing fire and burns.\nChapter 3: Conclusion\n\nElectromancy is an almighty power to be reckoned with and those that perform it should be regarded with extreme caution. Slow to cast into immense power yet still dangerous even at short range. It is adviesed that\nwhen in combat against such a mage that large amounts of metal armour are unadvised and even such things as steel or iron greatswords. So to wrap this short informative text up, one would be wise to heed the words of an electromancer and to regard the raw\npower and wisdom of those that weild it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Electromancy", "Crumena Ilwindior", "- The Basics of Electric Energy: Electrical Evocation - \nAuthor: Arch-Mage Crumena V. Illwindior [HeeroZero]\nConsoliant: Electomancer Ceruberr Asul'Ailer [CaptainSheepy]\nPreface\nThere is an old saying that descendants fear most other descendants. I believe, however, that those who say that have never looked outside the confines of the mortal world. If anyone has come face to face with\nthe power of nature, they will consider the previous proverb a joke. If this sounds like nothing more than nonsense coming from an old fool, then answer this next question:\nIf you can possess any form of power, what would you choose? Would\nyou choose the power of mankind, or that of a wild beast? Would it be the roars of powerful men, or the sound of thunder that shakes the heavens? Is it the limited life of men, or nature's continuous cycle of life? Whichever way you look at it, the\npower of man is feeble compared to the grandeur of nature. Throughout history, all of mankind has admired nature's power and though they had feared it, they tried to deny that. This is one of man's many follies. They neglect nature's power,\nwhich does not discriminate, solely because they are a part of nature.\nIn particular, as the descendants learned of Mana and started seeing a glimpse of nature's other realm, they began neglecting nature's power even more. They didn't realize\nthat their \"magic\" was actually an imitation of nature's power. This is what worries me. There are many students who are mages in training who do not understand that every magic's starting point is a natural phenomenon. I, who also boasted in my\nknowledge of Electric magic, did not learn this until I saw a lightning strike down at the Crown Lands Plateau of Oren.\nIn hopes that those who come after me will not make the same mistake, I decided to write this book. In other words, I hope that\nbeginner wizards will learn the laws of nature and have a healthy fear of it as well.\nAlthough this book only deals with lightning power, which is only one of nature's awesome power, if you are wise, you will take the moral of the story\nto heart and apply it when training other magic as well.\nThe Principle of Electricity series Magic Skill:\nIn order to understand the principle of Electric magic, you must first learn its natural counterpart: Lightning. If\nyou've seen anyone use Electric-based magic, you probably noticed a close resemblance to a lightning strike. The lightning strike occurs when Mana, the energy that surrounds us, splits into two polarities of energy for reasons unknown. These\nsplit polarities each continue to accumulate energy, when, in an instant, an explosion of energy flow occurs between heaven and earth. The intensity of the light and heat during this process contains tremendous power. Also, because of its\nunpredictability of where it strikes, it has been an object of fear to mankind. (So much so that people use this word 'lightning' to curse others. I.E. I hope lightning strikes you dead!)\nThere are many opinions as to when and why Mana,\nsplits into two polarities of energy. However, before anyone could come up with any concrete evidence, the debate's focus shifted because of the ‘great’ Wizard Ambrosia, who at times lacked common sense. He claimed that he was able to\nstabilize his Mana to split the two polar energies in a controlled manner, which caused all the scholars to shift their focus from the conditions in which the energy splits to the process of it. (It is a shame that scholars today are not interested in\ninsightfully studying natural phenomena, and rather just want to uncover it just for the sake of using it. This is quite foolish.)\nHow to Use the Electrical Energy\nElectrical Evocation a magic that uses the mechanic of creating static\nelectricity, which in turn utilizes the characteristics of the negative charge for a sudden electrostatic discharge. During the energy transfusion, a bright explosion resembling a lightning strike, rushes toward your target as Mana is depleted into\nreplicating this phenomenon. Once all the Mana is depleted from the bolt and the surrounding elements reach equilibrium, the flow of energy ends. (Just like a lightning strike in nature.)\nThere are many questions surrounding this\nmagic, such as \"How powerful is it?\" and \"How easy is it to use?\", which is technically asking how much energy it needs and how long it takes. To give you an answer, there is a limit to how much energy you can gather, and you can only maintain the\nenergy for about 15 seconds until later coming to a greater grasp of the art.\nYou can charge your energy multiple times to gather more energy, but it is reported that it can become highly unstable after the third charge which is already risky\nenough. Also, you only have about 15 seconds to charge all your energy. This is because of several factors, such as the difficulty of maintaining the Mana's focus, and also maintaining the polarized energy at the same time. (Even if you have plenty\nof Mana, it is difficult to charge for an extensive electrical bolt).\nElectrical Evocation has absolutely no applications other use other than being exercised as combative tool. The 'lightning bolt', your main and only real spell, is used to\nstrike your enemy with electricity . Once your opponent is struck with this attack, they will be in a state of shock due to the electricity surging within them as it an energy. Not a tangible object. Since this attack is based on an instant energy\nexplosion between you and your opponent, the lesser the energy gap between you and your opponent, the greater damage it will inflict as the longer the distance the surge of electricity must travel, the more it discharges. Wasting precious Mana in\nthe long run.\nSimple Usage\nOnce you have carefully read through this book, and understood the principles behind the fundamentals of Electrical Evocation and are ready to use it, you can do so by following these simple steps. First, a\nconnection to the Void is a must, as is the case with any form of magic. The simplest manner in which to begin evoking an element is to picture the empty black abyss that is the Void. A sleet of pure nothingness, void of any life as the name suggests.\nNow one must mentally picture lighting crashing down upon the Earth. But strictly the lighting. If one were to picture the scene, one could possibly border the realm of Pseudomancy (Illusionary magic) or if too much detail is placed on the\nEarth, soil or stone may be produced.\nThen you will see the static discharge envision such an occurring unfolding before your palm you calm your mind to allow your Mana to polarize the energy and fuel it. Once the preparation is finished,\nlightning-like strands of light energy will flow around you. This indicates that you have successfully calibrated yourself with the Void and established an affinity.\nI cannot stress enough that the intense light and heat from this attack\ncan significantly startle your opponent.\nApplication : Chain Lightning\nBefore we move on, I need to reiterate and explain in detail regarding multiple charges. As you know by now, Electrical Evocation is very similar to the\nactual lightning strike that occurs in nature. Does this mean that this magic is capable of imitating the continuous strikes that occur in a natural lightning strike? The answer is yes. Arcanists refer to this as the process of ‘Chain Lightning’. By\ncharging the magic multiple times, you are able to hurl this energy to your target back to back. However, there is a limit to how many times you can strike in a row. As previously mentioned, since you can charge up to about three bolts, yet the risk\nincreases with each charge.\nOne interesting fact is, these bolts of energy attract to metallic objects. Thus when in the vicinity of metal objects such as the bands of a barrel, swords and armor, iron grating, and other Ferrum or\nArcarum apparel, the bolt will change it’s path of trajectory and curve to meet said object.\nContinuous Attack Between Electrical Evocation Users\nWe looked at the principle behind the evocation of electricity, the chaining of it, and\nthe application of these styles in the previous chapter. If you think you have mastered everything through these two attacks, you still have a lot to learn from mother nature. If anyone has studied lightning strikes carefully, you know that lightning\ndoes not only occur in single, or multiple chain of strikes. Sometimes, lightning strikes attract other lightning and fuse together. Thus, where there are multiple Electrical Evocation users, they can fuse each other's energy to form a\ncollaborative attack.\nThis is a unique trait of Electric energy based magic that other ‘generic’ elemental based magic do not possess. When a user is charging his or her Electrical Evocation, you can add on to their energy and instantly form a\nchain effect. In other words, if you have charge your Electrical Evocation near another user that is charging, your charge will add to their charge, increasing the volume of charges.\nThe Effect of Electrical Evocation\nWhen is it a good\ntime to use Electrical Evocation? If you are wise, you should be able to figure it out yourself.\nFirst, the Electrical Evocation is good when facing multiple targets at once. Try it out yourself. Use skill of Electrical Evocation and attempt to fire\noff a bolt at a grouping of targets. You will be amazed at how effective and convenient this property can prove to be.\nHowever, there is something you must remember: Chaining charges inflicts damage which subsequently\ndecreases with each hit. Beginners, unaware of this, might overuse the attack and find themselves out of Mana and placed in a vulnerable situation. Even when you successfully chaining multiple charges of electricity, the\nopponent might not have received as much damage as you think. Thus, the first target of your 'chain' is very important. This is something every good mage should be mindful.\nLaw of Diminishing Marginal Damage\nWe must go\nthrough the Law of Decreased Damage before you can fully understand Electrical Evocation. The Law of Decreased Damage is commonly linked with Electric based magic where, when the electricity is charged multiple times, it actually\ndecreases the inflicted damage, though it uses the same amount of Mana. It is an important law that can help you better calculate the relationship between Mana and inflicted damage.\nConclusion\nIn this book, we discussed about\nthe Electric Energy based magic, specifically the art through the wisdom of nature. Electrical Evocation is a powerful and flashy magic, but it also requires a high level of discernment in order to use it effectively. Do not just rely on the\nknowledge from having read the book, but practice it until you get a better feel for it. Lastly, I hope that with excessive practice, you the reader will be guided to success in this art under this tome’s wisdom.", ""),
        StaticBook("ELECTROMANCY", "onm224", "ELECTROMANCY\n         GUIDE\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBy: Richard Tarus\nAdapted: Amras Lúinwë\nWhat is electric evocation?\nElectrical Evocation is the arcane magic form whereby a mage creates Electrical bolts for his or her purposes. Unlike other types of Evocation electrical bolts is intended to be much more difficult to control due to its\nspeed and high energy nature. Mages who specialize in electrical evocation will be able to form electrical bolts and streams of electricity to electrocute their targets.However, electrical evocation requires much more energy than for example\nfire and therefore a single electrical bolt requires much more energy than a fireball. This however is made up for by the fact the lightning bolt is somewhat equal in power to the two fireballs which could be made in the same time period.\nStrength\nAn electrical evocationist is capable of producing powerful electrical bolts\nBolts may travel from any point to point with speed and reliable accuracy.\nWeakneses\nElectrical evocation takes a greater amount of time to produce a bolt\nthan other types of evocation\nElectrical evocation is dangerous to learn and during some phases of learning the mage can be incapable of producing any spark which will not injure themselves.\nProcess\nReaching Tier 1:\nWhen you begin to learn magic, you will start a Tier 1. At that point in time, you are unable to cast any form of magic unless you have some sort of experience and have connected to the void.At this tier you will learn\nhow to connect to the void, and then research electricity as an element itself. Connecting to the void will take perhaps even years of practice, and once completed,you may still have some difficulty. Researching electricity would consist of practically\nfinding any sort of detailand then taking note of it.\nReaching Tier 2: \nAfter their advancement from tier 1, and their connection to the void, they can now create a multitude of sparks and perhaps an even minor bolt,albeit difficult to\ncontrol till towards the end of Tier 2.  Even though they can create sparks, users at this tier may have an overload in which the sparks will practically burst outwards towards the conjurer.In this tier they will need heavy loads of practice in order\nto become more proficient with a minor bolt.\nReaching Tier 3:\nIn this tier they can finally create a full powered bolt withought major troubles, and have full proficiency. At this point they can now create streams of electricity,\nthough they will simply spark and singethe target, rather then cause major damage. With this tier, they are novice mages. \nReaching Tier 4:\nNow, the electrical evocation users can create the \"call-down\"of electricity, aka a bolt from a high point\nin the sky. They can create multiple bolts in a shorter time, although a fire evocationist could create fireballs in an even shorter time.The call-down is not very proficient, and will rarely land on the user's target.  In this tier,they can create great\nstreams of electricity that will do some good damage (burns, etc.) They are very proficient with the bolts now.\nFor more information go to this link, there is the same info + RP guide:\nhttp://www.lordofthecraft.net/topic/88498-improved-electricity-guide/", ""),
        StaticBook("Electromancy", "dragonmaster0219", "So what is electromancy? Well its the art of bending electricity to your will. This involves a couple of steps that this book will explain to you.\nChapter 1: Connecting to the void. \n\nTo start you must connect to the void. To do this you must calm your mind. This is harder than it looks so think of something or someone that calms you and rest for 10 minutes. This exercise can take a week to\nmaster until you can do this within seconds. ((Once you have done this you are ready to be a t1 electromancer)) \nNow you should try connecting to the void, imagine your hand going into a plain of creation and pulling the desired thing out. I cannot\nexplain the feeling  but once you do it youll know.\nChapter 2: Making Sparks\n\nNow that you can connect to the void imagine pulling the desired thing out of it. In this case imagine pinching a spark. Do this until you've confirmed you can pinch it and then open your eyes and\nwitness your first piece of magic. Once you've done this your possibility shall be endless.\nChapter 3: Increasing your stamina (becoming a T2 & T3 electromancer) Now that you can connect to the void do many mind taxing excercises to increase your stamina. Eventually you will be able to hold stable elctricity in your palms and if yo can imagine a\nsurge of it going forward a lightning shot. I shall leave shaping and other ideas to your imagination, remember though Magic is not a tool, it is an art, use this knowledge wisely.\n\n-Damien Sezarius", ""),
        StaticBook("Elem. Alchemy", "Rosso", "The Tales of a Travelling Alchemist\n------------\nElements of Alchemy\n\nVolume I-2 of V\nThe Elements:\n--------\nFire\n--\nEarth\n--\nWater\n--\nAir\nSkeptics often approach me with a wholly ignorant conundrum, and that is “how can you trace every spell and element back to these four basic elements.” But what they do not realize is that an understanding of what is meant by these four elements is\nrequired before that question can be answered and in fact, if that understanding is acquired then this question will never be asked.\n\nThese four basic, rudimentary elements, Fire, Earth, Water, and Air, are what every potion, oil, elixir, and\nconcept, in Alchemy of course, is based upon. An ignorant outlook on this statement is that what is meant is the physical, literal meaning behind these elements but one must look into the symbolism, they must look deeper than the surface. I shall go into\neach of these elements in detail, so that you, and budding alchemist or simply a well-read individual, may understand how Air may both aid someone’s speed, as well as their perception of their surroundings.\nFire\n===\nThe Destroyer, the Unmaker, the Cleanser.\nWe will begin with one of the most rudimentary and used element, Fire. Fire can represent many a feeling, action, and state and because of this, it is often one of the most useful elements of the Alchemist’s arsenal. Fire can represent rage, anger,\nhatred, as well as bravery, courage, and gusto. Through this a brew can be crafted to make someone unquestionably and savagely furious, but it could also craft a brew to strengthen one’s will, and allow them to do what other men would shrink away in fear\nat. These feelings, these emotions can be invoked by the element of Fire within a potion, but feelings are not the only thing that fire can produce, actions are another.\nActions are often the most recognized aspect of fire, and by this I mean the action\nof burning, consuming, and destroying. Alchemist’s Fire, a handy inferno in a bottle, is an example of this aspect of Fire, for within it is the action of destruction. This action can be further expanded upon with burning oil placed upon a weapon, but if\none were to use this example they would also have to include the element of pain, another feeling that fire an invoke. State is aspect that Fire can take one within an alchemist’s potion and this is often represented as Chaos. It is true that Chaos is\noften something alchemist’s fear, for it is something athat often ruins a potion, but it is yet another aspect of Fire that must be recognized. Chaos, being the state that it is, may seem like it has little place in a potion but brilliant minds and\npowerful reason can bring it to use just the same as the first farmer realized a stone and a stick, two completely different objects, could help them till their fields by putting them together. As this is not a book on the philosophy of alchemy, or\nsolely on the element of fire, I will not go into depth on how Chaos can be used. The teacher must leave something for the student to ponder.\nEarth\n===\nThe Enduring, the Lifegiver, the Fortifying\nWith the conclusion of Fire, the other elements will not have as long as description for most of the fundamentals of the elements are covered in how they can represent different things, I will simply go over what they may represent, starting with Earth.\nEarth is a truly powerful element for it may represent metals, strength, the notion of being stalwart, solidity, firmness, flora, animals, and countless other, quite obvious, subjects. Earth is often used for potions that increase one’s endurance, or\nstrength, and it is a must in potions that toughen one’s skin. In fact, a strong series of representations of Earth are required to perfect a barksin, or stoneskin potion. Protecting oneself is not the only use for the element of Earth, for it is also\nused in antidote potions, disease-curing potions, and, of course, fertilizers. Antidotes use this element for it can represent animals, and among those elements are snakes and spiders, often associated with poison. Of course a symbol of Water is also\nrequired for a proper antidote, but this will be addressed later on. Many of the uses of the element of Earth are quite obvious, but a always, if one wishes to master the field of Alchemy they must learn creativity is their greatest friend, and using\nelements in odd and interesting ways can be useful, and quite detrimental, in numerous ways. A final note on the element of Earth is how it is associated with the fable of Transmutation. Now, as a scholarly and skeptic individual, I have doubts upon\ntransmutation, its existence, and possibility. This will be described more in depth, but know that the element of Earth is the greatly represented by metals, for metals are merely ores in their purest forms.\nWater\n===\nThe Base, the Purifier, the Healer.\nWater is the element that seems to get the most amount of use due to how it is a base for many a potion and it is true, for if someone wants a liquid spell they want to use the Element of Water. Often known as the “base” element, it truly lives up to its\nname for observations, and personal experience, lead all to believe it is necessary for life. This base element, is often associated with flowing, liquids, balance, peace, calm, order, life, and rebirth. One requires water for any potion that one plans on\ndrinking, and any oil that one plans on applying for to have a liquid, one must use the Element of Water. Now that and understanding on how Water is a base, we must go into how it is used beyond simply supporting the other elements.\nWater’s uses are varied, for it can be used both in antidote as well as poisons, showing that it is quite the versatile element. One may also use it to create a potion of calmness, or perhaps a potion of healing due to its association with life. But one\ncan also use this beautiful element in the creation of an oil to coat a weapon, or to coat and strengthen armor. This is not the same as enchanting armor or weaponry, mind you, for doing that is often permanent and requires magic. Through oils, one may\nreap similar benefits of enchantment but instead it is only temporary and anyone with basic sense can apply them. The purest base, and often representation of water, is Aqua Vitae or “Water of Life,” which is best made by distilling wine or other liquors.\nAir\n===\nThe Nimble, the Traveller, the All-Seeing.\nOur final element, the element of Air, is not the least by any stretch of imagination but is often the hardest one to put into representation and use in a potion. Now this element is often associated with agility, quickness, travel, feet, perception, and\neven flight, it can be quite difficult to embody the element of Air into a physical item due to our basic fault of lacking understanding of what we cannot see. But with reason and the opening of one’s eyes, the ways in which to represent Air are quite\nobvious in our everyday world.\nItems that can be used to represent air, and subsequently put through your tools to produce a potion, are rather easy to find during your average day but of course, as with all the elements, purer ingredients are often quite\nrarer. One representation that you may have already thought of is a mere feather, which is often the most common representation of Air. This, of course, is not the purest representation of the element but it will often due for your more basic potions\ncentered around this element. Another, more outlandish representation, are rabbits’ feet. Rabbits are often seen as quick and agile critters, and as Air takes on the aspect of agility and quickness, it becomes quite obvious how the feet of a rabbit and\nAir intermingle. With that said, it becomes rather easy to find out representations of Air through simply looking and observing the world around you. But do not fret if you are still hard-pressed to find these symbols, the next chapter will explain\nherbs that will best aid you in the process of finding symbols for all the elements.\nThe Tales of the Traveling Alchemist, Vol I-2\n\nCoppied by Rosso\nVaerHaven", ""),
