        StaticBook("escp rltionship", "Dirk", "how to escape from your relationship:\n1. try breaking up with her, if she isn't insane and manipulative, this might work!\n\n2. sneak out in the middle of the night, now, this might sound crazy, but it just might do the deal!\n3. get a friend to tell her you're leaving! this might end up with you having a dead friend.. or two!\n\n4. fake your death, now this one here is a fine one, it's worked for me once, but idk maybe she'll find you\n5. kill her, if you're really desperate, you might just have to stab her in the throat\n\n6. realise you're stuck with her. now, this one's pretty hard kids, but it just may be that your wife is an immortal demon, and then you have to realise you're stuck\nand maybe get married that might make her nicer to you.\n\n7. hang yourself, worked for laethis.", ""),
        StaticBook("Essential Oils", "Nyxxaa", "Essential Oils - A guide to theraputic uses\n\nBy Nyx\n\n\n((ooc disclaimer: this is written mostly from Modern Essentials: A Contemporary Guide to the Therapeutic use of essential oils isbn 978-1-937702-04-5))\nquick Definitions:\nEssential oils: substances created inside aromatic plants that are both volatile (they evaporate) and oil soluble (they easily mix with oils and fats).\n\nAromatic: Referring to plants that have an aroma.\nTopical Application: Placing an essential oil directly on the skin or other surface of the body.\n\nAromatic Application: Often referred to as aromatherapy, aromatic application refers to inhaling an essential oil or it's aroma.\nInternal Application:\nInternalizing an essential oil, typically through the mouth.\n\nCarrier oil: A carrier oil refers to a vegetable oil, wax, fat, or other oil that an essential oil is mixed with. The carrier oil \"carries\" the essential oil and dilutes\nit so it's effects can be spread over a larger area.\n\nNeat: refers to applying an essential oil by itself, without diluting it in a carrier oil.\n\nDilution: refers to mixing an essential oil in a carrier oil so it's effects are not as\nconcentrated in one area.\n\nVolatile: a substance that will evaporate when exposed to air is referred to as volatile. Volatile substances are typically light substances with small parts.\nSingle oil: A single oil is one type of oil by itself.\n\nOil Blend: An oil blend is a mixture of two or more single oils.\nTable of Content\n\nWhat are essential oils?--------see p.9\n\nTopical application p.13\n\nAromatic p.28\n\nOils p.\nWhat are Essential oils? Essential oils are the volatile liquids that are distilled from plants (including their respective parts such as seeds, bark, leaves, stems, roots, flowrs, fruit, etc.). One of the factors that determines the purity and\ntherapeutic value of an oil is it's constituents. These constituents can be affected by a vast number of variables: the part(s) of the plant from which the oil was produced, soil condition, fertilizer, geographic region, climate, altittude, harvest season\nand method, and distillation process. For example common thyme produces several different effects depending on the conditions of it's growth, climate, and altitude. If it is distilled during mid summer or late fall, the oil with be more caustic or\nirrritating to the skin. Low pressure and low temperature are key to maintaining the purity, the ultimate fragrance, and the therapeutic value of the oil.\nTopical Application\n\nTopical application is the process of placing an essential oil on the skin, hair, mouth, teeth, nails, or membrances of the body. Applying eddential oils directly can sometimes be harmful  so usage of a carrier oil is needed\noften carrier oils are coconut oil, almond oil, olive oil, jojoba oil, etc. Several topical application methods are outlined below.\n\nDirect application:\nTo achieve best results use 1-3 drops of oil.\ntips\n\n- The feet are the second fastest area of the body to absorb ouls because of the large pores. other quick absorbing areas include behind the ears and on the wrists.\n- When massaging a large area of the body, always dilute the oils by 15% to 30% with coconut oil.\n\n- When applying to infants or small children always dilute oils using 1-3 drops of the oil and about a spoon full of coconut oil.\n- use caution when creating blends. oil parts can be altered and cause undesirable reactions.\n\n- Layering individual oils is preferred over mixing your own blends for topical use. Layering refers to the process of applying one oil\n, rubbing it in, and then applying another oil. There is no need to wait more than a couple of seconds between each oil.\n\nMassage:\nTo create a simple massage oil that includes the benefits of oils, combine 3-10 drops of your oil\nwith a full spoon of coconut oil. apply a small amount of this mixture on the massage location and massage it into the skin using light to medium-light strokes of the hand of fingers.\nContact point:\nIs a simple method of appying oils to contact points in the feet or hands. A series of hand rotation movements at those control points create a vibrational healing energy that carries the oils along the pathways. The oils either help remove\nany bloackage along the pathways or travel the length of the pathways to benefit the particular organ. Refer to hand and foot charts on the following pages for more details.\n\nCompresses:\nBasin. Fill a wash basin with two buckets of hot or cold water, and\nadd the desired oils. stir the water viforously; then lay a towel on top of the water. Since the oils will float to the top, the towel will absorb the oils with the water. after the towel is completely saturated, wring out excess water, and place the\ntowel over the area needing the compress. for a hot compress, cover with a dry towl and a hote water bottle. For a cold compress, cover with water treated leather. finally, put another towel on top, and leave for as long as possible (1-2 hours)\nMassage. Apply a hot, wet towl and then a dry towel on top of an already massages area. The moist heat will force the oils deeper into the tissues of the body.\n\nBaths:\nbathwater. begin by adding 3-6 drops of the oil to the bathwater\nwhilst filling the tub. soak for 15 minutes.\n\nSoaps. during the creation process add 3-6 drops to 1/2 an oz of the base.\n\nCharts\nhttp://i58.photobucket.com/albums/g261/senactra/20160712_161828.jpg\nhttp://i58.photobucket.com/albums/g261/senactra/20160712_161856.jpg\n\nhttp://i58.photobucket.com/albums/g261/senactra/20160712_161847.jpg\nFor those that would wish to make blends themselves a chart for you.\n\nhttp://i58.photobucket.com/albums/g261/senactra/20160712_161948.jpg\nAromatic\n\nDirect inhalation: is the simplest way to inhale the aroma of an oil. hold bottle under nose and breath alternatively place 1-2 drops in your hands and cup over nose and mouth before breathing.\nOils:\n\nhttp://doterra.com/US/en/pl/singleoils\n\nhttp://www.sustainablebabysteps.com/uses-for-essential-oils.html", ""),
        StaticBook("Etiquette Guide", "[Ghost] The Eternal Librarian", "A Guide to\n   Proper Social\n     Etiquette\n  \n   by Lucion Sullas\nI have been asked on a number of occasions upon the \"proper\" way of acting when in the presence of fellow citizens. Not that I wish to presume my compatriots have terribly poor manners (though many could perhaps use advice) I shall regardless outline\nthe proper etiquette taught to me by my family. Should the citizenry be interested in such things, then do please read on.\n\nI shall no offer explanation for \"why\" to do such. Merely that I find it pleasant, as should anyone.\n-One's Attire-\nA Mali'aheral's outfit should be clean, devoid of creases, and be of a fine quality. Avoid garish, bright colours that would attract pointless attention. Be a beacon through your words and mind, rather than the hue of your under-shirt.\nAlways wear an outfit that is tasteful to the eye. Though there are outfits with smaller amounts of material that compliment its wearer's natural perfection, showing unnecessary skin speaks poorly of your character, and may mark you as one of ill-repute.\nWhen wearing a long-coat, always be sure to position the bottom hems carefully when sitting down upon a chair, a stool, or the ground. The material can become easily crushed, and create dreadful creases.\nWhen dressed in full robes, be sure to sit straight on your chair. The cloth located upon one's sternum is highly likely to crush when leaning forward, so take special care to smooth the material whilst sitting for long periods.\n-One's Posture-\nNever slouch under any circumstance in public. Slouching implies weariness, and looking weary around others may give them the impression that you find their presence tiring. Should I have to explain why such a thing tends to reflect\npoorly on your reputation, I feel you should simply close this book now.\n-One's Voice-\nAlways speak clearly with precise annunciation. A fiercely exaggerated \"r\" does nothing to endear yourself to you compatriots. \n\nThere is nothing more dismal than a Mali'aheral who mumbles. Worse still,\none who speaks with awful colloquialisms (Example, \"Aye,\" \"Nay,\" \"Milord,\" \"Milady,\") is similar to that of a dove braying like a donkey. \n\nRefrain from filthy languages as often as possible. The Uruk tongue, though it may have its uses in\ncommunication with those beasts, should be avoided during social gatherings. So too, should any foul words native to the common tongue (I shall no write them here, as it is a public book, after all). Speaking as a brute is but the first step to being a\nbrute.\n-One's Habits-\nDo not pick at your features when in the presence of your fellows. An itch upon ones ear may be scratched, certainly, but an irritation in the nose must wait until privacy may be found.\nAlways cough or sneeze into a handkerchief, or if one is not available, away from the table/direction of your colleagues. Illness spreads in the air, as well as the body, and others may avoid you should you not have a way of keeping your expulsions\ncontained. Should you feel the need for flatulence, excuse yourself from the vicinity.\n\nNever smoke or chew tobacco; it dirties the lungs, fouls the air, and stains the robes. Those who do such are naturally filthy, and their stench is\ndeplorable. Be mindful of your fellow citizens, and respect their nostrils.\n\nOne should always carry a handkerchief, or at least a clean length of cloth, to wipe away any grime that should get upon your clothes. Better yet, carry a second to\noffer a compatriot who is otherwise handkerchief-impaired.\n-One's Courtesy-\nShould a citizen be walking towards a gate behind you, be sure to open it for them if they intend to go forth themselves. The same idea extends to that of doorways, however, one should offer entrance to the one behind first.\nShould you observe fellow residents caught in the rain, it is polite to offer them sanctuary from the elements until they pass over. You yourself would not wish to be sodden, and thus extending that courtesy is polite.\nWhen you have a guest within your home, be sure to first offer them a refreshment of some sort. If none is to be had, then offer food. If there is a lack of both, be sure to apologise for your poor housekeeping.\nAlways ask permission to sit at another's table. As a guest in a home, you should never presume that you have any right to be seated in the presence of another. Furthermore, always request permission to leave, once conversation or purpose has been\nexhausted. Should you be seated at a public table, then consider the ones seated at it before you the \"owners\" of the space and the rules may be applied appropriately.\n-One's Pleasantries-\nWhen greeting a fellow citizen, a simple \"karin'ayla\" is sufficiently polite for strangers. However, those closer to you, or those worthy of praise, should be entitled to more elaborate forms of greetings. A short\nbow towards a respectable fellow is reasonable enough, as well as a quick arm gesture (example, touching one's chest, and extending your arm outwards) would be sufficient still. \n\nCombining all three is polite in all situations without any chance\nof insult.\n\nWhen retiring from conversation, a simple \"Van'ayla\" combined with the bow and gesture is excellent indeed.\n\nAddressing your fellow citizens by name is tasteful, and it is always best to seek\nout their name at the beginning of every conversation. Should you not recall another's name, inquire of it quickly to avoid further embarrassment. \n\nThe statement \"maehr'sae hiylun'ehya\" is in itself a blessing, and may\nbe used as both a delightful \"hello,\" or \"goodbye.\" However, to not return this blessing upon receiving it is -extremely- rude. How could you not return such a sentiment? Are you truly so devoid of eloquence that you dare not embarrass others with your\nfoul pronunciation? It is truly outrageous.\n\nKnow these words, and use their advice. The people of this city will be far better for it.\n\nMaehr'sae hiylun'ehya.", ""),
        StaticBook("Evelina's Diary", "Evelina Rovin", "20th of the Grand Harvest 1502~\n\nTonight was pretty hectic, since I was invited to a masquerade! Well, I wasn't directly invited since House Rovin wasn't visible on the guest list, but I used Klara's invitation to get in. She was unable to attend,\nseeing that she's still in this 'Lady School', which seems like absolute torture by the several letters I've recieved from her. Such a shame that she was unable to attend though. She would've loved the flamboyant masks pasted upon these people's\nfaces, and the mystery that they held. I expected for Rhosyn to attend too, but due some unfortunate reasons with her son, she was unable to arrive whilst the ball started. She came later that night, though I haven't heard much from her since, because she\nwas dancing all night with this.. baron? Hmrph, seems like she has another man courting her. I wasn't expecting for Athelstan to attend too. From what I know, I wouldn't think that Athelstan would go to these parties pure out of fun, and excitement.\nHe'd probably attend them for political reasons, which is.. smart, I guess. But really though, after our marriage, I really have to pump some more joy into his body, and maybe drag him away from his desk. He's barely around, and is always buried\ndeep down, where his office is. Well, the masquerade wasn't quite what I've expected, as people were just screaming around, as they were children playing in the garden outside. The only one keeping me company, was Ceto Kharadeen, really. She had the same\nexact thoughts I had when she stood there at the party, as my ears could've exploded if it wasn't for Lady Horen starting her first dance. To my great surprise, I saw Karl at the party. I expected Lorin to come too, but good thing she didn't. I might have\nborrowed her blue corset and dress for this masquerade, as Karl wouldn't even notice that I was wearing his sister's attire. Lorin would've been furious if she knew that I was wearing her party gown, as she's so over possessive about her clothing, like I\nam. Things went well at this masquerade, until the endless amounts of screaming occured, when there was a dragon flying above our heads. Tessa rescued both me and Ceto, as she strapped her armor on in a rather fast pace. I think Tessa would be a good\nand responsible Paladin, as she proceeded her endless amounts of quests. After the dragon flew away, everyone started dancing with their partner. You saw many men seeking for a woman to dance with, as there were only a couple. I had the chance to dance\nwith Adrian de Bar, Klara's uncle, if I'm correct. He was a charming man, and certainly did make me feel comfortable at this party, while Ceto left hours ago. The ball went great, and it was a rather pleasant relief after my horrid illness I've had, as\nI've been locked inside my room for days.\n24th of Sun's Smile 1502~\n\nI don't think that I can ever escape out of this nightmare father placed me in. It's truly horrifying to know that he's willing to push me off the Hiebenhall tower, simply because of my decisions. I'm happy, and father can\nsimply ruin my fortune pure out of despite for House Stafyr. Perhaps I see something else in House Stafyr than father, though I definitely see a whole other person in Athelstan than everyone else does. The only person I've talked to about this yet was\nTessa, who's currently staying in Al-Dirakh. The city itself is absolutely magnificent. It would probably be prettier than Ayr, if I do say so myself. Though, that's my opinion. I've packed several things with me on my journey to Al-Dirakh the night\nbefore, and left the next morning to simply have a chat with Tessa. The carriage ride that I took at the Cloud Temple must've been the most relaxing thing I've ever experienced at the time being. I had the chance to actually draw again, and create these\nsupernatural creatures. Heh, my imagination's big, I guess. Upon arrival, I felt the air immediately fall upon me, and the sand crawling between my toes in my shoes. Tessa seemed the most comfortable from us two, as she was only wearing a thin orange\ndress, with only slippers to embrace her feet. The carriage was unable to stop at the village itself, so we had to walk another part through the desert, to finally sit down, and have tea together. While Tessa would've been my greatest nemesis, she's\nthe only person, besides Rhosyn and Athelstan, that I can fully trust. You really need a friend who can purely just listen to you, and where you can tell everything to. Since Klara was this person before, I was locked with these secrets that I was unable\nto carry alone, and needed a person who I can talk to, and feel safe.\n10th of Malin's Welcome 1503~\n\nOh dear, today I've seen Athelstan again. It must've been over a year since we had our last conversation occuring, and our last sight of eachother. Though his beard may have grown longer, he hasn't changed a\nsingle hair, as for his personality. His polite, and charming voice chanting behind me, calling my name. The feeling of me seeing him again was like seeing Klara again, after she got back from her Lady boarding school. This may sound dramatic and all,\nand it certainly is, but it was absolutely a delight to see him again. He wanted to have a small chat, about our future, and such things. He gave me his permission to actually steward the new visitors, whom are in the need of housing. As I will become\n'Countess Evelina Marie Stafyr Rovin', he told me that he'd  share his titles equally with me, and that I won't become an accessory for him. Again, Athelstan is very kind, and I desire to never leave him for my father. I do wish for us to plan our wedding\ndate soon, as Athelstan's cousin, Margaery will already have her marriage occuring soon. If I see Rhosyn and Farley, I really desire to have a child one day. Having a little youngling following you around, perhaps helping you with a few things. Though\nfather may throw me off the Hiebenhall tower for this, I'm still willing to carry Athelstan's child. I cannot imagine our children to look like. A young, flamboyant redhead, with eyes so grey as Athelstan's eyes. Oh, I'm filled with joy already!", ""),
        StaticBook("Ever After", "Aevalyn", "Ever After\n\n        Haelun'or,\n           Axios\n\n     Published 1592\n\n\n\n  by Aevalyn Bethiros\nOnce upon a time,\nthere was a beautiful princess named Marine. She was the most beautiful and poised princess out of all her sisters in the grand kingdom of Springcourt; she was the shining jewel!\nPrince Faron was the most handsome prince from Springcourt's enemy kingdom, Felmoor. He was the most prized prince out of all his brothers, being the first-born and the most charming.\nFelmoor and Springcourt had been at war with each other for over a century for reasons that most later generations had forgotten entirely, it would seem.\nThey had already won their desired territory, already stabilized their economies--now it was simply a tit-for-tat revenge war that kept on going.\nOne day, Prince Faron grew tired of his castle and of Felmoor; he wished to go visit the fabled Springcourt in all its rumored wealth and beauty!\nThe only problem was that he was the Crown Prince, and he couldn't just walk into the enemy kingdom! And so he put on a disguise that fooled even his father, who was just returning from one of his hunting parties.\nThe disguised prince sneaked into the stables and rode out upon his favorite steed, a horse with the most luxurious mane and fluffy hooves out of all the horses in Felmoor. Still, no one noticed him.\nPrince Faron rode and rode until he finally reached the open gates of Springcourt. His disguise must have been great, for he managed to peacefully pass right through the gates and into the capital city.\nSpringcourt was just as awe-inspiring as he had heard! The roads were perfectly kept, the buildings looked brand new, all the food was fresh, and the people were so happy and warm and welcoming!\nSpringcourt was so joyously grand that it made Prince Faron feel like he never wanted to leave.\nWhen Prince Faron rode into the resplendent gardens, he found himself in awe once more--and when he rounded the corner, he felt like he was in a dream.\nStanding there, admiring some of the bright and colorful roses, was the most beautiful woman he had ever seen--the marvelous Princess Marine!\nPrincess Marine looked up at the sound of someone approaching from around the bend. She found herself so wonderstruck by the sight of the most majestic steed\nand its most handsome rider that she fell immediately in love with this charming stranger that she had seen the likes of only in her fantasies.\nIt was love at first sight for Prince Faron as well, who dismounted his horse and immediately expressed his desire to marry the beautiful princess Marine.\nAnd so he took the princess by the hand and helped her onto his steed, then climbed up and seated himself close behind her. They rode away in search of a priest as soon as possible so that they could be married.\nTheir marriage united the kingdoms of Felmoor and Springcourt and ended their century-long feud. Their alliance was the strongest in all the lands; they flourished and suffered no defeats!\nWhen the rulers of both kingdoms grew too old, which was not very long after the marriage, Prince Faron and Princess Marine stepped up to the throne and were crowned King Faron and Queen Marine.\nThey had many, many beautiful children over the next few years, and they were so absolutely in love that it seemed like they would never separate--and they never did!\nThey lived happily ever after, Faron and Marine.\n\n\n\n\n\n        The end.", ""),
        StaticBook("Everal History", "Leyu'Maehr", "The History of Everal, The First City of the Elves\nBy Leyu’Maehr\nA long time ago the First Race crossed one of the Great Oceans of Aegis to arrive on a beach. This beach was bestowed with a magical power from a long gone time. It let all plant grow abundantly there and in the surrounding areas. The sand there made\nglass as hard as steel and that which would never break. So when the Frist Race, later known as Elves, planted their magical seeds… Great towering trees grew in their place. Ordinary fire could not scorch these trees, spreading its seeds wherever they\nwent, creating an Empire dwarf all others previously known. The Elves lived inside the trunks of these towering trees, singing to them to help them grow.\nThen on day many centuries later, an astronomical storm swept across the land, felling the magical trees where they stood. Lightning stroke the exposed Earth, melting the ground and forming pools of lava. Great fire, fuelled by the dark energies of the\nstorm, burnt all of the remaining trees. Only a few kilometres remained. This is where the Elves sheltered during the storm. They named this area Evaral, meaning ‘protected’ in their lost language. They tried to spread the seeds of the magical trees once\nmore, but the Earth still remembered the horrors of the storm and wouldn’t let them grow. And when this area became overpopulated, the Elves started to reach for the sky! The trees grew until they touched the highest planes of the atmosphere and all was\nat peace once again. The Elves built walls of enchanted wood around Evaral, to protect the city from new predators and spirits that rose with the storm. And then a terrible thing happened.\nSome of the Elves dissented from this way of life, as wonderful as it was. They became greedy and wanted more land, ores, and resources. One by one the Dissenters left Evaral; preferring the new forests beyond its border. They spread out far across the\nland, struggling to cope with their new homes. Eventually even they settled down and formed small villages, under no ruler. Some even evolved into other races, forgetting what they left behind.\nBy this time only a few families remained in Evaral, and they did not know what to do. They missed the kinship of the other Elves, so they decided to leave too. But before they left each family took with them a seed from the first tree, which happened to\nreside in Evaral. This tree was very old and wrought with homes and its spirit was sad too, for it missed the Elves that left. It shed its bark to help the remaining Elves in their journeys, forming impenetrable armour. This armour now resides in the Tomb\nof Evaral, as the First Tree’s spirit reclaimed it. And then none were left in the Evaral. However over the centuries the seed still could grow, but the land never accepted them.\nUntil one day many centuries later, it came in the hands of a young Druid. The great city of Evaral’s location is hidden from the world, but many believe it is still out there. Perhaps one day, a great hero will stumble upon it.\nAnd bring it to power once again.\n           -------------", ""),
        StaticBook("Evidence", "Ser Walter Marshall", "[!] A message is written in all capital letters, in deep black ink.\n\nDEAR GUARDS,\n\nTHIS IS A LETTER FROM THE ONE AND ONLY DAN COOPER. IF YOU DON'T RECALL THE NAME, I'M A VERY FAMOUS WANTED CRIMINAL HERE IN OREN. NOW, I'M PERFECTLY HAPPY TO LIVE OUT\nTHE REST OF MY LIFE PEACEFULLY, BUT I THOUGHT I MIGHT SAY HELLO. YOU HAVE A NICE NEW DETENTION CENTRE, BUT THERE ARE MANY FLAWS. I WON'T ALERT YOU TO THEM, BUT BE ADVISED THERE MAY BE A PRISON BREAK. THANK YOU SO MUCH FOR YOUR HELP, AND CREATOR SAVE\nWHAT IS LEFT OF OREN.\n\nSINCERELY,\nTHE ONE AND ONLY\nDAN COOPER", ""),
        StaticBook("EWOROENLETEA", "Thurak'Yar", "Entities within our realm of Existence no Longer Existing, And Then Existing Again.\n\nOr, Void Translocation\n\nRescribed by the Farseer Thurak, 1'st of Snow's Maiden, 1488\n1. Introduction\n\n2. Study\n\n3. Sensory Overhaul\n\n4. Destruction\n\n5. Re-Creation\nIt does no take much searching within a library to gain some concepts of the Void as an alternate existence outside, winin and with no relation at all to our reality. Arcanists, Mages, Sorcerers- whatever the name- users of voidal magic pull a 'thing'\ninto this realm that did not previously exist within it, and hold it there for as long as they can wield a void connection. But no ‘thing’ pulled from the void is retained here. Such power is reserved to The Creater to pull real matter from The Void.\nBut what is a ‘thing’ –be it inanimate, plant, animal, edible- already existed? Then the connection to The Void need only be instantaneous, because the ‘thing’ is not created, but simply IS.\nStudy\n\nTake within your hands something that exists. \nAny kind of thing will suffice and for the sake of example we shall call it and any potential other thing \nan 'Entity'. Begins your examination in the simplest of interests:\nForm.\nWhat size is it?\nWhat’s it made of?\nHow heavy is it?\nHow malleable is the material?\nDoes it react to heat?\nWhat happens under great pressure?\n \nIf already you are struggling then you should return this book whence it came.\nSecondly you will need to form these observations into a mental map of the object. This is a far more complex procedure and verges on a particularly niche form of magic known as cognitism; however Telekinetics may find themselves more easily inclined\ntowards this type of thinking. You cannoy be bound by your perceptions in understanding the world. If you are purely an experiencer of your surroundings then you will never formulate any greater understandings of anything ever. So work on that.\nIf you are able to mentally comprehend the object beyond what is merely visible and physical and can mentally calculate the entity’s existence, then it is time to understand it magically.\nSensory Overhaul\n\nThere may be some slight overlapping of comprehending an entity scientifically through its calculable values and perceiving the entity’s magical value. Aside from universally shifting perspective\nwith the aid of magic, the quantity of information required to mentally re-create the entity can be better fulfilled by magically understanding it. All things are magical. All things were originally pulled from a real in which is not a single thing\nbut the potential for all things. And thereby all things that exist are still magic. Perceiving magical value is a skill that requires much practise and isn’t really teachable as you either find yourself able to perceive the presence of magic or not.\nCertainly with practise comes the strengthening of such a skill; but to attempt to explain to another how they are to ‘feel’ an apple tree from a dozen metres is (in almost all instances) utterly fruitless.\nThe complexities of such a thing all being laid\n{\"text\":\"\"}\ndown, what you do understand this entity in such a detailed way, you muse measure its mana supply and sacrifice that same amount of your around; surrounding its attachment to the void with your own so that the entity is no longer isolated in this\nworld but, in losing its own link to The Void of its origin, becomes a part of ones’ self. The sliding scale of difficulty is seen here in that the more ‘alive’ an entity is, the more rapidly it produces mana. Anything that has a soul is independently\nexisting within this realm and as a consequence produces and burns through mana with such a drastic suddenness that it would be impossible to balance that in any one instant. Soul-less entities then exist somewhere between a completely lifeless sliver of\nglass and a being with a soul. As mentioned the more ‘alive’ it is the more mana that will be present, and the briefer the instant at which one may be able to match said supply of mana before it shifts.\nNo Longer Existing\n\nEvoked magic automatically returns to The Void when a mage is no longer forcing it to exist in this realm. As it leaves this plane of existence it also ceases to exist itself on all planes. What once was tangiable\njust stops and is no more. \nSo it can be in the reverse that something that DOES exist independently of a void connection can have that original connection from the moment of its diving creation re-instated, and therefore able\nto return to the nothing from which it came. Within The Void there is potential floating around aimlessly. When it is given an aim through the use of Arcane Magics it is no more the potential of being something but becomes of itself a something\nfor that fleeting moment. But without being birthed into existence by the creator it cannot remain as that. However entities that already exist are somewhat different. Though they cease to exist entirely, there becomes a new potential within The\nVoid that is assigned to being that entity.\nSo fear not that an entity which by your hand no longer exists may not be brought back into our reality as something temporary or destructive like an arcane missile or a shield of ice. For the\npotential of that thing has some divine marking upon it that keeps it sacredly linked to once again become what the Creator made it to be (or more accurately the way that it was, as a ceramic teapot will not become a crude clay but remains a teapot).\nTo Return Again\n\nIt is a good thing that all those mental calculations were required to adequately assess the entity before it could be eradicated from reality; because that mental reconstruction of the original entity is the only\nthing that maintains it as something that ever existed. A sacrifice of identical mana to cover its original quantity so that a newly independent existence outside of The Void is made (I.e redoing the Creator’s work) will assign the potential\nwith its destined form. And the forgetting of such things means eternal damnation upon an entity that once existed in relative peace before you came along and destroyed it.\n\nGood Job,\nYou Meanie.", ""),
        StaticBook("Expedition North", "Ebonsquire", "An Expedition North, to the Root of Evil \n\n((Originally written by Respiren))\nWord had reached our ear's in the fair city of Laurelin that Winterfell had fallen. Decided and empty handed, Dwarf Foreman Holmes Dolir and I set out to inspect the town now know as 'Winterfell'.\nA detour on the road to Oren was taken, to see the gardens and grand halls of the dwarves, known as Kal'Urguan. After some talks with a guard, Win'on, hateful of elves, we were granted entry.\nUndiscouraged, we continued on, assured that nature would provide. \n\nAfter many days, we reached the kingdom of men, only to find its gates closed to travelers. Around its east wall and across its port we swam.\nThe dwarf keeping to the shallows, till we once again reached a snowy path heading north. We followed its turning east through outposts and Alstion, where the undead were driven back. These towns seemingly deserted. After long travels we reached the walls\nof Winterfell, and found it to be a prison tower, curiously intact after its inhabitants were destroyed by the undead, but empy, with only a lonely birch displaying damage. No men, but only a protected pumpkin patch remained. Disappointed and keenly\ndesiring the company pumpkins, we resolved to  continue northward, coming to a stop to build a house to take shelter from hunger and the night. Knowing we had travelled far to the northeast, we changed our heading northwest.\nOn this path we met with many caves and sighs of fallen arrows and torches - people had gne before us even in these wilds. After many, many days of travel, and hunger, my keen eyes saw a burning tree. Following these flames ever northward we found a small\ncave in which to sojourn.\n\nThere dismayed, we placed a table and dined on restorative mushroom broth, it seemd so far north there was nothing to find but hardship and the wilds. Looking over the land once more before we returned, I spied\na clearing with roses.\n\nSeeking to collect some of these herbs as a memento of our long journey, I descended into the clearing. And lo, before us towered a firey city in the sky, yet, completed, emanating evil and\nblighting the land below it. Finding a point of ascent and leaving the dwarf below in the dangerous mines, I entered what appeared to be an obsidian temple. I found myself curiously drawn by an irresistable force towards it's altar.\nLosing my footing, I fell into an unseen sacrificial pit of Aegis, body destroyed but spirit intact to wait on the healing powers of monks, resolved not to return to that foul place, and to uproot this evil from the land.\n\n-Wayward Druid Respiren", ""),
        StaticBook("Experiment #02", "Fox", "[!] A dirtied extract from a lengthy journal; a set of notes it would seem. And they are completely legible!\n\n...\nExperiment #02 -\nStatus: Deceased.\nSynopsis: Manipulation of pre-existing lifeforce within an object of nature works, but cannot sustain for longer periods.\n\nAs I delved more and more into my studies, I experimented with various parts of-\n-our magics. Or as the others would call it, our 'gifts'.\n\nThese gifts can entail disaster. Why would beings of higher power instil powers of this magnitude within creatures derived from unrelated ancestry?\n\nMy studies are in-\n-place to explore the boundaries of these powers.\n\nIncomparable to my first disastrous experiment, my second yieled higher success. The subject was placed into an intense coma, and their 'energy' extracted, then returned. Additional energies-\nwere applied to this subject; foreign powers if you will.\n\nThe results conclude that beings can only sustain a limited amount of life within them before imminent, irrepairable death.", ""),
        StaticBook("Experiment #09", "Fox", "Experiment #09\nStatus: Alive\nLocation: Unknown\nSynopsis: Reanimated sentience of a once deceased creature.\n\nI tend to keep my darker research private, though this discovery is beyond the necessity of secrecy. Life can be eternal!-\nThis discovery may allow me to further my project. Perhaps I could return it to what it once was before.\n\nFor #09, I have released the kitten back to the wilds. After days of study, its shown no odd deformities in personality or physical appearance. -\n[!] The rest of the notes seem crudely scratched at. Almost like frantic ripping.", ""),
        StaticBook("FALIÇ SANT JORDI", "Arthur Thompson", "🌻❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀    FALIÇ SANT JORDI\n❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀    FALIÇ SANT JORDI\n❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀    FALIÇ SANT JORDI\n❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀    FALIÇ SANT JORDI\n❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀    FALIÇ SANT JORDI\n❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀    FALIÇ SANT JORDI\n❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀❀", ""),
        StaticBook("Fall Bail 02", "Bell Sano", "Bail for Fall Mari'ael. Terms for release are 50 mina bail, and the suspect must still appear in court, or face maximum charges, waving her right to a fair trial, as well as being assumed guilty to the highest degree.\nPenned by:\nBell Sano\n\nPayed by:\nMarie Mari'ael\n\nSigned by:\nMarie Mari'ael\nFall Mari'ael", ""),
        StaticBook("Fall of Aegis", "Monk Scribe", "Fall of Aegis\n\nThe miasma in the north lingered ever more so. Galahar was evacuated and the cloud temple became our final stand. From the temple I shouted out into the crowds, summoning those who where chosen by the Nations as their champions.\nUpon arriving to Laurelin, I called all of the champions into Dawns Bakery, where a secret entrance lay.\n\nThe High Priestess handed out blessed armor pierced, enchanted in Aeriel's grace. To each of the champions. We then took a small passage,\ninto what was once the Laurelin Gauntlet. Entombed in a massive oak tree, lay Vardak's portal from the nether. \n\nThe champions gaze into the portal and grip the hilts of their weapons tightly. \n\nI step out of the way\nof the portal, clench my soulstone in my hand tightly and wish them good luck. As I vanish the brave few enter head first. \n\n- Spoken by Native in the Elf in the Deep Cold, 1351.", ""),
        StaticBook("FallBail", "Fall", "Bail for Kajara anim fortis & Fall. Terms of release are 75 mina bail for the pair and appearing for a court date.\n\nPenned By:\nDavius\nSigned by:\nFall\nKajara Anima Fortise", ""),
        StaticBook("Fallen Golem", "Geoboy66", "A falling boulder, yet screaming. On this blackest of days, as all days are, the peaceful nothing, the silence of the Abyss was penetrated by the tumbling of a stone creature.\n\nThe creature's origin is unknown, but the Sunless Sanctum shook as it\nimpacted the ground, its life instantly ceasing. Closer inspection of the creature revealed several sources of power fuming within its grey belly - Cores, I heard them named?\n\nA new fearsome silence befell the Sanctum\nas one of the Old Lords came forth from the shadow of a rock formation, and within a wiry grasp did pluck the cores from the golem's interior without uttering neither word nor sound. It is known to be the Old Lord of Umbrage, King of the Abyss.\nWhere the cores are now, is surely unknown. The husk of the golem sits unmoved, its lifeless eyes staring upward to the world it surely left, resting eternally by Mordring's Gate.\n\nRadiant is the Black Sun.", ""),
        StaticBook("FALUM", "Wargoth Falum'Lur", "Falum of Clan Lur\n          Vol. I\nThis story details the origin of Falum the Orc and follows his journey through his life. Through the story, there are many obstacles, challenges, and battles Falum must endure and allows one to understand his experience of those trials.\nCHAPTER ONE: THE DEPARTURE OF VAILOR\n\nDuring these times, Falum was nothing but a Cub and entered the Realm knowing nothing other than what his family had taught him. After his father had risked his life to save the Realm he ultimately cast it into\ndestruction all the same causing the Descendents of Vailor to abandon the Realm and sail towards Axios. After experience the sights through the Spirit Realm, the Descendents landed upon Vailor and had to rebuild everything from nothing. The Orcs sailed\naround the New Realm and landed upon the Jungles of Asul figuring it might be a better environment to settle in. Falum worked hard even as a Cub aspiring to one day be like his father, Dominus Vorgo’Yar.\nCHAPTER TWO: THE RISE TO REXDOM\n\nFor a time, Falum had followed his father learning the ways of the Hunt and using it as a time of concentration aside from the work that was asked of him from the nation. Upon finally returning to the War Uzg it was\nrevealed that the political state of the Orcs was in chaos after the death of Rex Kharak’Raguk. The Rightful Dominus, Vorgo’Yar returned with his cub only to find out that Kulgarok’Lak had taken his place as Rex but was quickly defeated by Malgunuz’Raguk.\nRex Malgunuz fell into a civil war between the Nation and a native Clan of Orcs called the Rams. Dominus Vorgo’Yar eventually sided with Rex Malgunuz as Orenia began marching onto their lands after wiping whatever was left of the Dreadlands.\nCHAPTER THREE: THE DEATH OF REX VORGO’YAR\n\nWhile Rex Malgunuz attempted to deal with the Civil War between the Nation and the marching of Orenia, he mysteriously disappeared leaving the peril upon his Dominus and soon Rex.\nThe few Orcs that resided in San’Kharak prepared what they could for the War to come knowing they were at great odds with the Elves assisting Orenia in the march. As they crossed onto Orcish territory incited the Battle of the Bloody Bridge\nwhere 20 Orcs battled against 150 Orenian and Elven warriors. The skirmish was lost and Oren marched upon San’Kharak preparing their siege weapons to destroy the walls. Rex Vorgo’Yar knew the land was doomed with very few supplies and sent most of the\nOrcs including his cub, Falum, to continue life elsewhere, while the Rex, the Dominus, and an Honorary held what was left of San’Kharak and succumbed to the blades of Humans and Elves.", ""),
        StaticBook("Falum'Lur VOL 3", "Wargoth Falum'Lur", "Falum of Clan Lur\n         Vol. III\nThis story details the origin of Falum the Orc and follows his journey through his life. Through the story, there are many obstacles, challenges, and battles Falum must endure and allows one to understand his experience of those trials.\nCHAPTER SEVEN: THE WARGOTH MASSACRE\n\nAs the Coalition claimed victory after victory many rejoiced in the turning of the tides. Falum attended many feasts that Drokon held in honor to whatever he wished to honor that day. Falum was honored\nto service Drokon as Targoth and helped run the thriving nation until one fateful day during a hunt against the Dungoth, Rex Drokon was fatally injured. He only survived due to Kulgarok saving him with his magic and was deemed not a whitewash,\nbut whispered things into Drokon’s ears and influenced him with the same magic. Falum walked around the newly constructed San’Torr with pride until Wargoth Lukra’Braduk met him in the sands.\nLukra spoke ill things happening in the Rex Palace that seemed all too familiar to Dark Shamanism and informed Falum that Rex Drokon and Kulgarok killed one of the other Wargoths for showing too much pride but was taken as a challenge by the Rex.\nWith this in mind, Falum returned to the early constructed Lur Den and thought upon it. After several days pass, he emerged from the Lur Den and entered the Rex Palace only to find noone around. As he walked past the Throne of the Rex, he noticed\na familiar face yet all his Spirit could feel was pity as he observed the heads of the Wargoth’s including Lukra’Braduk.\nCHAPTER EIGHT: THE DEATH OF REX DROKON’UGLUK\n\nWhile Falum never spoke of the things seen that day he continued his service to Drokon with suspicion of Kulgarok manipulating him, but made sure to keep his distance as to not end up like the others.\nWith new Wargoths to be searched for the growing War Nation became crippled until others could take their place though it only seemed it was not enough. After the few feasts and tournaments that was held Drokon vanished and no Keshig, Orc, Goblin, or Olog\ncould find him. After years of searching, Rex Drokon’s corpse was found scorched and clawed within the Dungoth lair. After witnessing the turmoil that was caused Falum begun searching for a means to make his reality more sensible so he turned towards the\nSpirits as his Father once had, left his Wargoth title behind, and set upon a nomadic journey as a servant of Ghorza the Spirit of Travel, Movement, and Fortune.\nCHAPTER NINE: SPIRIT WALKING\n\nBefore Drokon’s death, Falum met a Half Orc wandering around the Rex Palace by the name of Elphaba’Gorkil. In their discussions, Falum came to know Elphaba as his Father’s Shaman mentor as well as\nknowing Kulgarok’s misdeeds with Drokon. When it seemed the conflict would not cease Falum decided to ask Elphaba to help him train in the ways of the Shamanic Arts. Through intense training and meditation, Falum eventually became capable of speaking with\nSpirits of the Elemental Realm and bonded with a Spirit of Fire and Storm. When the Spirit of Storm demanded Falum’s trial to begin he was smited with a great bolt of lightning that ultimately killed him until Elphaba’s distress brought him back to life\nbeing reborn and renamed as, Falum, by the Spirit.", ""),
        StaticBook("Falum'Lur VOL II", "Wargoth Falum'Lur", "Falum of Clan Lur\n          Vol. II\nThis story details the origin of Falum the Orc and follows his journey through his life. Through the story, there are many obstacles, challenges, and battles Falum must endure and allows one to understand his experience of those trials.\nCHAPTER FOUR: THE REFUGEES OF AZAGHOL\n\nAfter the Siege of San’Kharak and the death of his father Vorgo’Yar, the remaining Orcs sailed across the seas to the Urguanic desert and began constructing a refugee camp\nas was provided by Grand King Torvin Grandaxe. Falum in his 20’s  humbly served as Targoth of the Orcish people and helped construct the walls and buildings although many of the Dwarves had referred to him as the Rex. Even though they pursued\na new life it was all too sudden that The Dominion of Malin had found the Orcish settlement and relayed the message to their protectorate, Orenia. As time passed by, Falum and other Wargoths had to attend the many hostile negotiations that were had\nbetween Urguan and Orenia. While Urguan kept Oren at bay, an internal controversy arose among the remaining Orcish people.\nCHAPTER FIVE: THE REXDOM OF DROKON’UGLUK\n\nWhile Oren and the Dominion once again aggressed on the Orcish people the Orc named Kulgarok sought to once again deem himself as the Rex of the lands. A council of the Wargoths was called to dispute the\nmatter where most were not in support of it and one Orc especially took a stand against it. Drokon’Ugluk faced Kulgarok’Lak and demanded they meet in combat to bring a solution to the matter. They broke into action and Drokon’Ugluk came out victorious\nand claimed the Rexdom with support of the other Wargoths. Falum eventually got inducted into Clan Lur by Eath’Lur as he was apart of the bloodline and also became Targoth serving Rex Drokon’Ugluk, but after Kulgarok’s defeat he chose to bring his\nallegiance under the Emporer of Orenia acting as his Court Mage.\nCHAPTER SIX: THE AXIONITE COALITION", ""),
        StaticBook("Fate of Hanseti", "Coltaine Wick", "The\nFate\nOf\nHanseti\n\n\n\nWritten by an eye\nwitness.\n\"I was on gate duty as usual when the first distrought citizen came to Petrus. They were screaming some lunacy about flying men and fire. after we had him calmed down, he told us the town of Hanseti was under attack by Undead.\nOur commander Prince Pual Carrion order me and the other men to suit up and get ready to march. Shortly there after we men of the Crow Regiment marched out of Petrus to meet the enemy at\nHanseti.\nNight fell as we neared the small town, even from a distance you could see the glow of flames and the distant screams. As we marched into the town proper , everything quite frankly went to shit. Shambling dead lurched out of alleyways to assault\nout regimental formations, men scattered in panic, which is when the real madness hit, there was a man, or something, flying through the air. some foul Iblees spawn hurling balls of flame, I saw too many of my brothers in arms\nbe seared to ash still in there armor, at the time I was still young and inexperianced with such things so I fled to a manor within the town that was miraculously unburned, I was not the only one there unfortunatly. Some men from the regiment made it\nthere along with other people from the druids grove I believe, as we peered out the windows to witness the flaming slaughter, the flying Iblees mage, flew to the manor we were in and started summoning hordes of undead to devour us.\nNot wanting to die, I only stayed to fight for long enough to manage an escape back outside. where I then ran full tilt into the surrounding woods to escape the remains of Hanseti. It would take several years after the fall of Hanseti\nfor Iblees to finally be cast down and those who lost there life to be put to rest.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Felsen Sky Whale", "liam_barnett", "The Sky Whale of\n          Felsen      \n-------------------\n\n9th of The First Seed, 1569\n\nBell Sano\nProem: This is simply an eye witness account of the Sky Whale which made it's way over the skies of Felsen.\nSky Whales are generally regarded as being rare, but were originally discovered in Vailor. Due to their low population, little is known about their actual biological features.\nSimply, they're often described as being tranquil, passive creatures, seen feasting on flocks of birds as they float through the sky, may it be across a desert, ocean, or in this rare case, a city.\nPhysically, their under bellies are plain and white, while their skin is either some shady brown, or a variety of blues.\nAccount: Approaching Felsen, it'd be apparent that it was night, and it was stormy. However, upon entering the city, it'd also be obvious that some large object above the crowd of people would be blocking the rain.\nOf course, above us, a Sky Whale was suspended, hoovering at least one full mile off of the ground. It was as if the beast was shielding the people below from the rain, but it's unlikely that this was intentional.\nNauzican guards requested that both the Guards force of Felsen and the Corpsmen present attack it, and kill it, so many men withdrew their crossbows. However, as they fired, the beast seemed unaffected.\nObviously fed up with the offensive assault, the majestic creature turned on it’s side, presumably heading towards the imperial palace. It exposed it’s side, facing perpendicular to the street we were currently standing on.\nI could easily see that it held a deep, dark blue color, nearly black, in that respect. As it floated off, that was the last I saw of the whale, or any Sky Whale, for that matter, but this encounter was extremely important for academic and\nscientific purposes, and was crucial that I record my experience.\nAnalysis: I really only have two notes to make about the Sky Whales that aren’t already common knowledge, two observations I made.\nFirstly, the white, plain underside I mentioned, may have stronger and reinforced skin for the exact reason displayed during the encounter. Many enemies and hostile creatures would definitely launch an offensive assault\nfrom the ground, as they wouldn’t have any real means to get close to the beast. This forces it to develop a more reinforced, strong, and generally tougher underside, to prevent small projectiles from inflicting damage.\nThe second observation made is that, the whale appeared during what may as well have been the stormiest night of the decade. Roaring thunder storms, lightning, heavy rainfall -- This may have been soggy\nand generally wet enough for a Sky Whale to traverse through a densely populated urban area.\nBell Sano\n\n9th of the First Seed, 1569\n\nFelsen", ""),
        StaticBook("Felsen Tax Plan", "Theran", "Proposed Tax Plan\n___________________\n\nCurrent Plan:\n- Class A shop\n  o Pays 200 Minas\n  o Pays every week\n- Class B Large Home\n  o Pays 100 Minas\n  o Pays every week\n- Class C Stall/Home\n  o Pays 50 Minas\n  o\nCurrent Plan:\n- 2 Weeks to pay or evicted.\n- Warned with a notice after one week of a lack of paying.\n- Taxes are paid with tax papers worth 50 minas per.\n- Stewards attempt to remind the people to pay their taxes.\nNew Plan:\n- Definitions:\n  o A public externality is defined as a benefit to society without society choosing to support said benefit. Example: Library, church, military.\n  o A shop is defined as a building that offers goods through face-to-fac\nNew Plan:\n  o A stall is defined as a building that offers goods through bidding or without face-to-face interaction.\n  o A large home is defined case-by-case depending on the population it can hold and the space taken up by said home.\no A small home is defined case-by-case depending on the population it can hold and the space taken up by said home.\n- Pricing for Taxes:\n  o A building deemed a positive externality by the Mayor or his Stewards or any other Government Official will be pardoned for their taxes. Their tax will be attributed to the positive impact that this building makes on the city.\no A shop will continue to pay 200 minas per cycle.\n  o A stall will continue to pay 50 minas per cycle.\n  o A large home continue to pay 100 minas per cycle unless the home is deemed extremely large in which it will pay more based on population.\no A small home will continue to pay 50 minas per cycle.\n- Punishments:\n  o If a positive externality does not provide its goods, services, or if it does not qualify as a *positive* externality anymore, it will be forced to undergo a fine or eviction, depending on the severity of the nonfulfillment.\no If a shop has not paid its taxes in two weeks and is still selling goods, then it will be forced to pay twice the amount it owes -- 800 minas.\n  o If a shop has not paid its taxes in two weeks and is not active, then it will be evicted and may need\n...to repay the taxes missed in the future.\n  o If a stall has not paid its taxes in two weeks and still has goods to be sold stocked, then it will be forced to pay twice the amount due -- 200 minas.\no If a stall has not paid its taxes in two weeks, yet is unstocked and inactive, it will be evicted and may need to repay the missed taxes in the future.\no If a large home has not paid its taxes in two weeks, it will be evicted, all belongings inside will now belong to Felsen, and the missed taxes may need to be repaid in the future.\no If a small home has not paid its taxes in two weeks, it will be evicted and all belongings will now belong to Felsen. The taxes will be exempt unless in the case of a crisis, in which the owner will be liable to repay the missed taxes.\no If there is a disagreement between a citizen and the punishment offered by these sets of rules, or if a government official wishes to provide a different form of punishment, it will be taken to a higher court to decide the punishment.\n- Amendment Policy:\n  o If changes are sought to the tax system or punishment system for taxing, it will be taken to a higher court to approve the change, or at the Mayor's discretion.\no If the Mayor's decision is deemed unfair by three (3) or more citizens or other government officials, then the decision will be taken to a higher court. \n  o The higher court has one week to host a hearing.", ""),
        StaticBook("Feudal intro", "Annabella", "Feudalism is a grouping of legal and military customs, prevalent in Oren, and various other human nations. The purpose behind feudalism is to decentralize an empire which can no longer handle being in a small area.\nFeudalism is typicaly broken down into 7 ranks in an empire: Emperor, King, Duke, Count, Baron, military, and common folk. The emperor is the center of all feudalism, and can create and remove titles at his will\n(Note, a Tyrant emperor is likely going to have a rebellion on his hands if he adds or  removes too many titles.) A king has a Kingdom either within an Empire or independently, should he be independant his ability is the same as an emperors.\nOtherwise, he can adjust the titles of his direct vassals. A Duke may do the same as a dependant king, but with a much smaller group of vassals. A count typically runs a town and has a vast amount of land for what he pleases.\nIt is his job to make sure he has a military to supply his liege in case of an attack on the nation or area, and he will typically pay for loyality in minas or housing or both. Common folk live in the protection of the area, and exchange must pay their\nliege in either minas, or hte product they make.\nFeudalism loyality is hereditary and only works with Vallah because other races live too long for a proper system to work.\nAnother part of Feudalism to note is Clergy, although they are not a part of the system they have a strong influence on it because of the Vallah’s obsession with the deity known as ‘The Creator’ A High Pontiff is the person who crowns\nnew emperors and even has the ability to excommunicate them, making them disrespected among the Vallah", ""),
        StaticBook("Feudal Rights v2", "Christopher d'Ibelin", "A SUGGESTION OF A FEUDAL LAW\n_____________________________By Francois d'Ibelin. \n\nSecond Edition and transcription by Christopher d'Ibelin. \n\nA document wherein a suggestive replacement for the Feudal Law of Oren is contained.\nIntroduction\n-----------------------------Greetings, fair men of the new Empire. The Feudal Law was a document detailing clergymen, burgher, peasants, yeomen and nobles, and the roles thereof. This was accepted by the good King Olivier, yet it is doubted\nthat a similar document is required for the Holy Orenian Empire of his Imperial Majesty, John I. I find this most distressing. The Feudal Law was itself an expression of traditional privaleges.\n\n-Ser Francois d'Ibelin\nI.Definitions\n\nI.A feudal vassal (otherwise known as a secular vassal) is a secular nobleman who owns a landed title within the Empire, be they directly or indirectly loyal to the crown. With these category, there are two further subcategories:\nOne:Minor nobles are those nobles who are lower than the rank of count.\n\nTwo:Senior nobles are those who are counts or higher.\n\nII.A senior clergyman (otherwise known as a Canon vassal),\nis one who holds an ecclesiastical, or non-secular title, titular or otherwise, that is a bishopric or higher.\n\nIII.Those who are under this rank are categorised as lesser clergy.\nIV. Landed gentry are those who hold a knighthood and an estate but hold no other titles. For example, a duke who is also a knightly estate-owner is considered part of the senior noble class, not the landed gentry.\nV.Those commoners who are not bound to any land, own no property and lack any sort of allegiance are called free subjects, these being the majority of our empire. \n\nVI.Those skilled commoners who work in the arts and crafts\nor any trade for a liege are known as craftsmen. \n\nVII.Those commoners bound to the land of a secular or canon vassal in agricultural labour are called serfs or villens.\n\nVIII.Those who hold council titles in a county, ducal, princely\nor imperial council are known as unlanded nobles.\n\nIX.Those who hold such titles as “Lord Mayor” and are given governance of a city are known as burgher titles.\nII.Vassalage and Obligations.\n\nI.The vassals are obligated to support their liege during a war. If the Emperor calls the realm to war, then he may be sure that the vassals give their full military strength in support of his cause; if they do not,\nthe Emperor is at will to revoke their titles or imprison them.\n\nII.The Emperor is obligated to maintain the feudal privileges of the vassals; if he rules with tyranny, and attempts to revoke feudal laws such as this,\nvassals are under no obligation to follow him. \n\nIII.Each man of the landed gentry, unlanded nobles and secular vassals is required to keep a destrier or a courser, riding horses; his own arms and armour of the highest quality.\nIV.It is the feudal duty of the commoner to be armed with the most basic of weapons.\n\nV.Burgher vassals are free from the obligation to fight or provide levies, as they provide extra financial contributions to the realm.\nVI.The clergy likewise are under no such obligation.\n\nVII.It is thus requested burgher taxes can be up to double those of the feudal vassals, however, they are under no obligation to go to war with their liege.\nVIII.The Emperor is obligated to defend his vassals and come to their aid when they are attacked. \n\nIII.In Respect of the Lexicon of Ashford and the Ducal Law.\n\n[note-henceforth the Lexicon of Ashford has been superseded\nwith a new law, yet the principle remains the same - Christopher.]\n\nI.It is said no Emperor will revoke the privalege of the dukes to create their own ducal laws, no Emperor shall ever revoke this privalege, this privalege will not be revoked!\nII.The Lexicon of Ashford takes place only in those duchies without a Ducal Law, or that are in possession of the Emperor.\n\nIII.Counties, baronies and so forth may not make their own laws.\nIV.In Respect of the Rights and Responsabilites of the Commoners.\n\nI.It is said that the commoners of any rank are only to be judged by either the Law of Ashford or their respective Ducal Law, by no other law they may be tried, and\nonly when proven guilty may they be persecuted. \n\nII.Further, the serfs can be expected to marry at the behest of their liege. This is because their children will be serfs as well.\nIII.No noble may displace a law-abiding citizen unless he has been inactive for one Saint’s week.\n\nIV.He shall not be permitted to visit a man’s court without the approval of his liege.\nV.Any man born of a free family shall not be taken as property of any foreign or local power.\n\nVI.Each peasant, whether serf, yeoman, or otherwise, has the right to own weaponry. [and, furthermore - a responsability if an adult male]\nV.In Respect of the Incarceration of the Nobles and Clergy.\n\nI.The clergy are only to be imprisoned by their liege only with the approval of the High Pontiff.\n\nII.The Emperor may only\nrevoke a man’s titles or imprison him on one or more of the following conditions: He has a legitimate claim on one of their titles, he has committed treasonous acts with ample evidence to support such a case, he has committed a crime\nof the first or second degree.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fi'hiiran'tanya", "Toodles", "Fi'hiiran'tanya\nOriginally written by\nValia'laure Faeifeth\n\nTranscribed for the Library of Dragur by\nRevion M. Tathron\n\nThe following is a transcript of a book found in the ruins of a house in Celein.\nThe Smile of Larihei Heals the Mind Like Milk Heals the Body.\nThe Lifting- Sacrifice\nThe Ritual of the Lifting is different from that of Untempered Fi, for it is the stringent conditions which make for the true, Tempered Fi's creation.\nThe ritual of the Elibar'acal follows, and yet it is sufficient but not necessary to create a Tempered soul.\nThe sacrifice is tied to the Altar, imbued with the magic of Fi. The room is lit only by the light of a Fi' orb in a specially made lamp.\nGold dust is scattered upon the sacrifice as the following is read. Each in attendance may bless themselves as they so desire.\n<Transcriber's note:\n\nBoth the Elvish and common versions of the Ritual have been removed, to deter those who seek to practice this vile art.>\n<Basically, it detailed how the Golden Owl is saving everyone from monsters. It wasn't worth reading, believe me.>\n{\"text\":\"\"}\nMilk is passed between those in attendance in a Silver Chalice. It is drunk by each in turn, symbolising they are worthy of the Milk of Larihei, and therefore her smile.\nYour body unfit for the milk, Your mind unfit for the smile of Larihei, \nYour very essence forfeit.\nThe Milk is refused to the sacrifice, symbolising they are unworthy of it. A blade imbued with Fi' energy (read: Fi'chant, just as the altar is)\nis used to cut the sacrifice's throat and as this is done droplets of blue will pool on the blade's tip.\nBlood is collected in a clay pot. The droplets will spin and form a blue light which will become stable (PK)\nor will explode in a flash of light (no PK, soul escapes). It is required an orb be present to power both the altar and the blade.\nFi'hiiran'seth\nThis subtype of the magic focuses on the negation of Arcane Magic. Whether Evocation, Conjuration, Illusion, Runes, or Alteration, if can either send a forming spell back to the void or eat away at a created spell.\nThe magic will also steal the aura needed for Shade magic, but has no affect on existing tendrils.\nFi'hiiran'acaele\nThe second subtype of the magic can stop all Deity Magic. (For example: Clerical, Druidism, Shamanism, Monk, Muun'Trivazja, and Ascended). Unlike its brother subtype, which funnels mana away into the void,\nFi'hiiran'acaele disrupts a connection, interfering with someone's ability to connect with their chosen deity. This can be small, when they cast a spell, or large, severing a connection for a time.\nStrangely, neither Fi'hiiran'acaele or Fi'hiiran'seth affect Necromancy.\nThe mage must be a first-time magic user, never having connected to anything, Deity, Void, or otherwise.\nThe mage must be of good condition. Fi'hiiran'tanya corrupts the body twice as much as a normal magic, and the mage's increased metabolism may wither them away without proper care.\nThe mage must perform the Ritual.\nThis Ritual, developed by the Elibar'acals, is the source of the mage's power. They much find a sacrifice (a character willing to be permanently killed) that they know well, and kill them on the altar.\nIt is in this moment, when the soul is leaving, that the mage will connect to the Void for the first time. The soul will be returning to The Cloud Temple,\nand the mage will grab it, trapping it in a state of Limbo. A state of half-death, forever caught in the mage's grasp. The soul will become a tool,\nand will eventually forget its old self, becoming more and more compliant. There is a small chance, in the beginning years, that the soul will attempt to wrest control, though no soul has ever gained full control.\nPhysical and mental strain\nLoss of weight and muscle mass\nIncredibly realistic lucid dreams and nightmares, leading to a confusion on what is real and what is imagined.\nEnchanted areas will leave a Fi'hiiran'tanya user fatigued if they stay in there for too long a time period.\nProblems with breathing, blood loss, internal bleeding, and the rate at which wounds heal.", ""),
        StaticBook("Field Herbs", "Andriel Elré Z'lorn", "In the field there are many ways to treat the wounded. From burns to cuts to scrapes to arrow wounds, there can be many different things that may need to be cared for. Here is a guide on Medical Uses of different Herbs during everyday life.\nBlissfoil:\nBlissfoil can be very useful for minor injuries or ailments. It can relieve pain and itchyness at the slightest of touch. The oil around it's stalks and petals can be used medically to relieve these symptoms.\nTippen's Root:\nThis herb is great for stopping the bleeding of a large wound once made into a Salve/Balm. This root is known for having an unpleasent smell, however, the medical uses outweight such factors.\nFlameTounge Root:\nThis Root is not to be used lightly, and is only to be used if out of Tippen's Root. It gives off an intense heat that can be used to seal and stop blood flow. NOTE: Make sure to wear gloves when handling this Root.\nSerpent's Stalk:\nThis herb is generally dangerous for consumption as a plant, however, once one crushes the upper stalk and mix it with water, it can be used to treat burns and minor pain.\nFrost Vine:\nIt is wise to crush this herb and mix it with water. This will produce a substance, somewhat sticky, which can be used to numb areas from pain.\nAqua Nymph:\nWARNING: Only use in extreme cases.\nThis plant can cause closing of the airway if taken orally. However, if one were to receive\na terrible burn. To use the plant correctly, boil the plant (Gently) in some water, strain the plant from the water\nAqua Nymph Cont.:\nand use the remaining oil on the affected skin.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fieldwork Notes", "Morami Casil", "The Ice_Fang Library\n  \nThis library has been formed by former espionage agent, Warhawke and Artist curatoras, Balduul Exrith while he was travelling around the Icey Mountains. The temple was selected to be a library due to its strange magic properties.\nSuch as the countless, colored, floating globes that surround the central fountain and the warm, gushing water that comes from the water system. The library is also protected by several spider guardians that have diminished over the past few monthes.\nThe current staff of the library is...\n*Balduul Exrith, Curator, Founder, Architect\n*Royce Andre, Grand Librarian, Scholar\n*Elrith Searith, Librarian\n*\nNotes\n\nWalls are high, with mountainous terrain surrounding.\n\nEasy to jump out once inside the city\n\nLots of high buildings for a good vantage point.\njumping out on the nothern side of the city leads over a ridge and back to the forest near Ker'nor.\n\nJumping out quickly may cause injury, as the walls have a sheer slope.\n\nCitizen door seems to be in the side of the city.\nHigh towers offer a good view of the street happenings.\n\nThick trees on the upper level of the city provide good cover\nand nooks to hide in.\n\nMany empty houses on the upper level for hiding spots\nLarge ballroom on upper level\n\nBallroom has empty small storeroom above for hiding\n\nalternate paths around the back of the houses.", ""),
        StaticBook("Finding Nature", "Lillith", "How did I Find Nature?\n\nBy: Lillith Winterleaf, the Sequoia Druid\nI found the Order by mistake, oddly enough. It was only about four years since Aegis had fallen and I had been married for about a year. I was five months pregnant, and stubbornly travelling to Salvus to trade some of our wools and\nleathers for food supplies, as we had not built our farms yet.\n\t\nOn the crossroads leading towards the Salvus farmlands a man drew a knife on me, and proceeded to steal my leathers and wools, and what little minas I had.\nHe then decided he was going to take me to sell as a slave, so I started struggling. He sliced my arm and side as I broke away from him and fled across the outskirts of Salvus.\n\nI did not know what was beyond Salvus,\nI fled into a dense area of oak trees and ended up stumbling upon a coastline with a long wooden bridge that almost looked grown out of the trees, spanning the waters to an island of dense trees with a huge tree in the center.\nI held my bleeding side and crossed over the bridge, pushing vines and leaves out of my way.\n\nI stepped off the bridge into a small clearing, a small shop stall on the right, ahead a root gate leading inside the great tree,\nto the left a pathway led into the trees and I could see a small wheat farm along the path. Standing in the root gateway were two robed figures, one male and one female, both elves.\nThey turned and saw me, the woman stepping towards me after a moment. She wore red and yellow robes, and her eyes were fake, made of gold, but they moved and she seemed able to see, a worried look on her face as she saw me,\nasking if I was okay. I told her I was attacked and she took me down the path toward the farm, sitting me down next to the small stream to relax while she tended to me.\nI asked what this place was, it was beautiful. She smiled and told me it was the Druid Grove, and introduced herself as Affection Druid Jena, a Guide of the Druidic Order. We spoke for a long while, my wounds taking little\ntime for her powers to heal, but finding pleasant conversation in each other. She told me of the Order and answered all my questions. When we grew hungry, she excused herself to get us a snack.\nWhile she was away, the man from the gate approached, asking if I was okay and introducing himself as Ice Druid Jameson, one of the Archdruids. We spoke for a short while, then two Orcs with staves ran by, one\nwearing a pumpkin on his head, yelling to watch out for the 'bangaloos', hitting my head grazingly with his staff as he ran by. Jameson excused himself and ran after them, yelling at them to be silent. Jena returned shortly\nwith a plate of bread slices, a cream spread on them which she told me was made of bonemeal, and sliced apples.\n\nWe talked through the night, both of us napping serenely under the canopy and stars.\nIn the morning I asked if I could return after having my child to join the Order, she smiled and said that I was welcome to return whenever I wanted and she would be happy to instruct me.\n\nI had my son four months later, Aeran,\nand I returned to the grove four months after that with him in my arms, answered Jena's questions and became a Dedicant. Jena instructed me, with advice along the way from Archdruids Jameson and Saviticus. Once I became attuned as the\nSequoia Druid by Jena, I began learning all forms of medicine and healing that I could, from Jena as well as a little from Saviticus, but mostly taking their lessons and experimenting on my own to refine the techniques.\nThe rest is a much longer story for another time, but this is how I found my calling in nature.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fire Evocation", "Evelangéline", "About Fire Evocation:\n\n-Fire Evocation, one of the six evocation arts is the utilization of fire by the evocationists. Although Fire Evocation is not very hard to learn, it is one that must be practised a lot about, because of its destructive behaviour.\nBasic Understanding:\n\n- Fire evocation, as the other types of evocation arts, is powered by the void. The evocationist who has a connection to the void calls forth the fire from the void. One aspect that is not known by many is that the fire formed is -\nnot real on this plane of existance. A thing that I tell to my students, \"The fire is fake, only the effects of the fire are real.\" is an accurate statement, considering this.\n\n-The origins of the art are unknown, although It is one of the oldest arts.\nProgress of A Fire Evocationist Student:\n\n- Fire evocation is easy to learn, yet hard to master. So, a Fire Evocationist needs to take their time and have stable observations and practises to use their potential to a maxiumum.\n- During the first five elven days, the student needs to form a stable connection to the void, through meditating. While meditating can be done in any position, it can also be done for flexible amounts of time. For example, while many evocationists -\nchoose to meditate for at least half an hour once. I meditated for five minutes six times a day. The important thing is efficiency, and focus. The student needs to clear their mind in order to form their first connections to the void.\n\n- After the evoca-\n-tionist forms a stable connection to the void, they work on conjuring low-powered flames, propably shards of embers. During this period, the evocationist must be observing how fire burns, how it spreads, and how it affects the substance it burns on.\n- After an elven week, the evocationist will get started with conjuring small flames, not exceeding the size of a regular candle's fire. During the beginning of this period the evocationist will be greatly fatigued, propably not being able to hold the -\nfire for long. The time of the evocation will increase from ten seconds to a few minutes if done correctly. The evocationist should focus on increasing the size of the flames and lenghten the duration of how long they can hold the flame.\n- After this period, the evocationist will be able to evoke bigger flames, propably not exceeding the size of an elven fist, after the two elven weeks of the period.\n\n- Next period, the evocationist will focus on shaping their flames as spheres.\nTo be able to throw fiery balls of fire at objects. The evocationist will fail to throw a ball of fire successfully the first five elven days, then will be fatigued after one small ball of fire. During the ends of this phase, the evocationist will increa-\n-se the size and range of their fire spheres, the phase lasting for nearly two more elven weeks, exactly one elven month after the evocationist had first started to learn.\n\n- From the start of the next phase, the fire evocationist will-\nbe having covered most of the parts to be known, moving to a period of practise. The evocationist will be able to evocate walls of fire and flames that are distanced from the evocationist. However, as the distance of the fire increases from the evocation-\n-ist, so does the difficulty and mana requirement. The evocationist at this point would be able to form multiple fire spheres before being fatigued, not exceeding an amount of three. While the wall of fire can be maintained for an average of thirty-\nseconds. After this period, is the mastering period.\n\n- A master of fire evocation has learned how to effectively and efficiently use their mana to cast larger flames, calling fires to this realm of existance quicker. Gaining the ability to-\nevoke large areas of vigorous, reactive fire; fire novas. Bear in mind that an evocationist should never try to evoke more than their training has given to them.\nMore Things to Know:\n\n- Although fire may be engrossing and exciting, it also is very dangerous. More than the other arts actually, at least in my point of view. You cannot, simply cannot manipulate the fire you have summoned, meaning that-\nif a fire evocationist accidentally set an object on fire, they cannot extinguish it. So try to remain calm, and don't cause accidents.\n\n- To further explain the lack of fire manipulation, I'll go into slightly more detail. A fire evocationist cannot-\nutilize already existing fire. They can only summon flames from the void into this realm of existance. Once they summon the flames and use them, they are out of control. As I say to my students: The fire is alive, it has a mind of its own. You cannot -\nforce it to do anything. You can only convince it.\n\n-Lastly, an evocationist of any type shouldn't ever push their limits too hard, to exceed their level. If an evocationist proceeds to cast magic for too long-\nthey will get extremely fatigued, then maybe even lose their life.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fire Evocation", "Dorin Irongut", "A Book On the Study and Use of Fire Evocation\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWritten by Dorin Irongut\nTable of contents\n\nChapter 1\nLearning of Fire\n\nChapter 2\nMeditation & Void Connection\n\nChapter 3\nSummon Your Spark!\nChapter 4\nPractice!\n\nChapter 5\nBecoming adept!\n\nChapter 6\nAdvance Mana Control!\n\nChapter 7\nBasic Combat!\nChapter 8\nCreativity & Mastership!\nProlouge\nId like to put this bit in here before you read this book, so you know why I write this book. I write this book because, I , just like my master before me, wish to exstend my knowledge of the art to students who wish to learn. I write this\nto teach. And to me, teaching is a great thing. I like my master before me, and his master before him, am now spreading the knowledge passed from each of us down to the next generation, in the hopes that you will do the same. Now, lets get reading!\nChapter 1, Learning of Fire.\nIn order to do elemental evocation, you must first learn of your element!\nThat means learning what your element looks like, smells like, feels like, sounds like, and yes... even tastes like, in great detail... You must\nbe able to study a single flame for hours, remembering its every aspect.. and even then you will not be finished, as you need to learn more about fire... Many, many flames, of all types must be learned of. Take time to study flame every time you see one\neven if you think it is the same as another. This concludes chapter one, and the studying of flames should be done inbetween sessions.\nChapter 2, Meditation & Void connection\n\nThe next lesson, or lesson 1.5 and 2. Is meditation to help train the mind and body to enter the void. It is also how one enters the void. Meditation, at first, should be done in the most sutible position to you.\nWether it be simply sitting, standing, laying, or the prefered lotus style. When meditating, to get things started, one should get into their desired position, and close their eyes... allowing all of the world to simply go away...  But also keeping mind\nof your surroundings.\nAfter this is done, calm your breathing, stay like this for however long you want. Eventually after hours, a day, or maybe even a little more, you should exsperince your first quick connection to the void. When this occurs, your body\nmay react in many diffrent ways. It could be from the more common of twitching and breaking out into a sweat, to getting sick and puking, however, you must do the same again, and again to last longer while connected to the void and blocking these symtoms\nout. After achieving a short connection time, and you are able to stay connected for a longer periode of time, you should move onto the next lesson.\nChapter 3, Summoning Your Spark!\nThis lesson is usualy the most exciting for all of my students, as you summon your very first flame. Weather you succeed or not depends on how you handled the prior lessons. \nInbetween your time of meditation and\nconnection, you should have studied a candle flame by now. Once you think you are ready, get into your meditation position, and face your palm up into the air... I cannot exspress how much when i say, focus on the spot ABOVE your hand, and not your hand\nitself... else you will be very sorry you did. Next, connect to the void, after doing so, remember all the aspects of a candle flame, then, using your mana as a anchor, pull the image from the void and above your hand... This can take a few trys, so fret\nnot if you fail the first time. After doing so, you should have summoned your first flame! Although you wont be able to keep it up for long, summon another after a short break and keep doing so unto tired.\nChapter 4, practice\n\nIn this lesson, we will be taking summoning you flame to the next level by doing simple movements with it. By now, your flame should be a little larger, and you should be able to keep it up and running for quite some time.\nNow, this next part is quite easy... or so it seems... After you summon your flame, keep a constant flow of mana, and image your flame moving from left to right... This will get tring but after a day or so, you should be ready to start moving it in\ncirlces around your palm. Do this, and keep doing this for a couple of times each day for about a stone week or so, practicing moving your flame and building your mana up.\nFrom here is where i exspress practice... it is the most vital thing you do now,\ndont miss a day, unless sick. Keep this in mind and you should start to increase in exsperince as each day pass's until your ready for the next lesson.\nChapter 5, Becoming Adept!\n\nIn this chapter is where you begin to become adept at evocation. If you have been practicing like ive exspressed in the past chapter, you should be ready to continue onto the next lesson... Throwing your fire!\nYour fire should now be modertaly size... that of a torch flame or so. If not, do not continue reading until so is done. Now then, if you are ready, summon your fire, whilest standing, and in a open area, as this could go wrong. Now then, after you have\nsummoned your flame, arc it over your back as you would, and simply throw it, imagin it being hurled over and keep the flow of mana to it, and as it hits the target your throwing it at, allow it to exsplode... Keep practicing this for about 2 or so elven\nweeks before moving onto the next lesson.\nChapter 6, Advance Mana Control\n\nYou should now be well into about 2 1/2 to 3 months of training now. And this is where we move into the more advance things... In this case, advance mana manipulation. In the past, you might have seen a evocationist\nevocate farther away than just a arms lenth away. With this lesson, your going to be summoning you mana in farther spots, from the left, right, and infront of you. Keep doing this only with mana, unto you are able to without to much tire, as this requires\nmuch mana. After you can do this, this time, do they same as you would to summon a normal fire, but in those locations of your focus away from you... Do this for quite the while, until you feel more comfortable with it, which should take a few days.\nAfter\nyou have done this, you are now ready for the next lesson.\nLesson 7, Basic combat\nNow, just because this chapter is in here, does not mean you should use evocation for combat only, but it is a use fire evocation is spesialized in... But not its only use! so remember that!\n\nMoving on....\nIn this chapter, you will be learning how to move about and such while connected to the void and summoning fire. You will also learn how to move about while keeping a current fire you hold in hand, further more, I will say if you are in a fight, you will\nneed to pull fast connections, and even faster summonings.\nTo start, simple try walking around while connected to the void.... this will take a high level of concentration, but once your able to, go ahead and try a slightly faster pace, and so on to a jog\nand even further onto a run. Once your able to do this, which this could take quite the while, maybe a week, move onto keeping a fire in your hand while walking. Once your done with that, follow the same prosess up to running... But this next part, could\ntake even longer, and be even harder. You must now summon your fire while walking, and so on. then move onto summoning a fire at a distance while walking and so on... This means you will have to keep a concentraion on the spot your summoning. Once your\ndone with this keep practicing for awhile... maybe take... heh, no justing kidding. No breaks!\nAfter practicing a few more days after achiving this, move onto the next, and final lesson... or so your told.\nChapter 8, Creativity & Mastership!\n\nAt this point, you should have been training atleast 4-5 months. You have learned all of which i could teach you through a book, but now, you must study more!\nYes, learn as much as you can, and use that knowledge to do\ncreative things, that others wouldnt use normaly! Make your evocation a art! perfect a certain fire! do things to make yourself diffrent! because that is what makes a true master... After you have gotten this far in the book, all i can say it keep\npracticing, and maybe, when you think you are ready, go onto have a apprentice of your own! I hope you do good with the knowledge i have givven you!\n\nWritten by one Dorin Irongut on the 15'th of the Deep Cold, 1519, in the Cloud Temple Library.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fireflies", "Evelynn Shards", "-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-  \n   Fireflies\n  \n          From\n         \n                 Above\n\n-------------------A story written by Evelynn Shards\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\nOnce upon a time, in a small town called Areguana, there was a huge storm raging above the tiny houses. Thunder and lightning was everywhere to be seen and to be heard. Suddenly the lightning stroke down into a house. A woman holding a baby ran screaming\nout of the house. Flames were sticking out of the roof, making big gaps. A huge cloud of smoke filled the sky. People ran with buckets full of water to the house, trying to put out the fire. Since the city was layed on a beach, between a forest\nand an ocean, it could be reached easily. \n\nThe next day, when the storm calmed down an d went away, people were running up and down, carrying logs and stone to build up more houses, and safer houses. After the storm, if you walked inside\nthe town you could hear people speaking of a legend. The legend said, each time there is a storm, when you walk exactly 150 steps from the center of the storm, you'll see a tree. Each time you hold your hand on it, millions of fireflies come flying down\nfrom the sky. They say their light could make you blind. This legend was popular in the small town. Everyone spoke about it. Later on they didnt believe in it anymore, until that one day...\n\nIt was a very hot summer day. Johan was\njumpin around the field playing with some friends. The mother told Johan to not go too far away from town, as he remembered. His friends said: Hey Johan, do you want to come with us to the forest? But Johan didnt want to, his mother\ndoes not agree with such thing. She is scared something will happen in the forest. But they kept asking and asking until Johan said: Okay,okay i'll come with you, but not for too long! Else my mother will be mad. After that they ran into the forest.\nThen suddenly in the middle of the forest a small place where no trees grew was there. Only one single tree, which had an orange color, Strange, Johan said, trees arent orange, right? No they arent, his friend said. Then Johan went to sit onto the tree.\nBut then suddenly the fireflies came from above. Look at that! They said. The light formed one huge firefly. Thats the most beautiful and magical thing i ever saw. Thats not normal! Johan said. After that they quickly ran home, to tell this story to their\nfamily. When Johan came home his mother asked: Where the hell were you? I thought you were dead! Then Johan said: Im sorry mom, i went into the forest with my friends, im sorry about that, but i saw something magical. What is it? His mother asked.\n\"I saw the fireflies..\" He quietly answered..\n\n\n\n------------------- \n\nTHE END OF A SHORT STORY ((May be continued))\n\n-------------------", ""),
        StaticBook("First Aid Kit", "Azuline Elverhilin", "-----------------------First Aid Kit-----\n         \n           By\n         Azuline\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n6th of The Amber Cold, 1572\nItems you need:\n\n*Cotton Cloths cut into strips.\n\n*A vial of vodka for cleaning wounds and tools as well as your hands.\n\n*Gauze.\n\n*Tippen's Root.\n* Suture needle and a spindle of thread.\n\n* Water bottle.\n\n* Honey.\n\n* Medical mask.\n\nThese items are just to perform basic first aid until real help arrives. For more information on\nhow to use these items, please ask your local healer.\n\n(Note: Honey is great for sore throat, or even for new borns to induce their hunger.)", ""),
        StaticBook("First Mage War", "Elindor", "The  First  War \n      Of   Mages   \n\n Inscribed By Elindor\n\n\n ijfeaslkklmfdslkmdall\n\n\n      Chapter I\n    Magic's Genesis\nIn an age before history Aenguls and Daemons walked upon the face of the earth amongst mortals. The four fathers of all nations lived in reverence of their similarities as brothers, for to them the celestial beings were removed in near every aspect.\nThe first children of Malin, Horen, Krug and Urguan were bringing forth a new generation that reflected the talents and aspects of their forefathers. Compared to the Aenguls and Daemons, the mortals had no power at all. But united they were a force upon\nthe face of the earth, and the descendants set about establishing for themselves townships, and eventually kingdoms. To most of the deities the activites of the mortal beasts was whimsical and entertaining, but some saw the shift in power that had already\nbegun. The mortals were new to the world, yet they quickly learned and adapted to use resources to their advantage. No daemon had need to cut down a tree, yet forests were now being flattened, and the goodness of the earth ripped up and melted.\nChapter II\n   The Earliest Days\n         Of Magic\nMagic has always been in all things. By virtue of having been created from the void, every element of the universe is within itself capable of magic, however mundane. To each newly born mortal is handed a soul to posess the vessel of flesh. Suddenly the\nbeing of the seven skies were no longer separated from the other creations. To a babe newly born is bestowed a soul. With it, the potential for greatness: independant thought, power over the elements of the created world, the choice of one's destiny, and\nmost influential of all... magic. Not just regular magic like that found in a tree or a bird, but access to the limitless expanse of void. There had barely been three generations born from the fathers before the shift in power was clear to those watching.\nNot all descendants presented this danger. Some pursued knowledge and understanding, overtime making way for wisdom. And these gifted mortals conversed with the Aenguls about the nature of existence. The celestial beings were able to learn\nsome things that their immortal forms had no need to consider. And so between them a handful of Aenguls and mortals formed a wise counsel and watched as the children of mortality spread themselves across the earth in search of kingdoms and power.\nChapter III\n       Temptations\n       In Shadows\nZalam was a mortal with an insatiable hunger for magic. His thirst for greater sources of arcane energy lead him to consort with an Aengul known as Iblees. The two delved deeper into the possibilities of dark magic, and as they did so sought seclusion.\nThe counsel of wise mortals and aenguls grew concerned that these two rejected all who queried their actions. The ever heightening need for privacy was most concerning for the deities, for selfishness and jealousy were mortal attributes.\nA handful of mortals grabbed hold of Zalam one afternoon and made demands that he share what his consorting with Iblees was purposed for. His response was one without words but with a very clear message. Those who had grabbed hold of him found their skin\ngrowing brittle, their muscles weakening, and their energy quickly exhausted. The other two received dark tendrils piercing through their shoulders. Zalam made quick work of silencing the questioners and, by sunset that day, had brought three lifeless\nbodies back to Iblees. The survivor of that short magical skirmish reported back to the counsel, sparking immediate action. Confrontation was not enough. These two would have to cease their activities if they so quickly corrupted the minds of men.\nBut the world had not witnessed dark magic before. They knew not the pull that power had over mortals. In so short a time Iblees had gained followers whose loyalties would stretch even beyond their final breath. This was no longer a matter of a rogue mage\nand a fallen aengul. Now standing opposed to the wise counsel was the beginnings of an army.\nChapter IV\n  Inevitable Warfare\nIblees was still new to battles, but his tactis were wise enough to send first the mortal minions whose will's were bent to unquestionable loyalty at his promises. With sword, spear, and bow the lines of humans rushed towards the collected magi. Steel had\nyet to taste the bitter sting of magic upon its surface, and moral lives paid the price for this lesson. Soon not a soul stood to brandish a weapon against the counsel. Zalam moved in next accompanied by a horde of reanimated corpses. These proved less\nvulnerable to magic, and the tides of battle turned against the magi. The aenguls could dispel of the tainted walking corpses, but more would continue to rise. Zalam struck down an aengul whose name has forever been lost. The other aenguls of the counsel\nfled from the battle, realising that their immortality had its limits. All except for the Wandering Wizard, who rallied the magi. With him keeping Iblees' zombies at bay the magi trapped Zalam in an arcane cage. Furiously he blasted at the cage using\nevery form of magic he had learned. In desperation he screamed out for Iblees to rescue him. But no answer came. He grappled at his cage and poured all his power into breaking it. But the walls remained in tact, and the mortal's body was left drained of\nall energy in the shell of a now wearied old man. His weakened muscles could barely keep him standing, and his brittle bones shattered with every movement. About his neck was fastened a charm that seeped any mana his body could create, magically crippling\nhim so that his mind remained alert behind the broken body of a ruined mortal man.\nChapter V\n        Epilogue\nThe cunning of Iblees was beyond the might of the Wandering Wizard. Though in their magic neither could surmount the other, Iblees was without honour, willing to grasp any opportunity for advantage. The mortal magi rejoined their friend to find the\ntwo interlocked in a furious struggle. Now Iblees saw his opportunity. Lightning rained from the heavens atop the onlooking mortals. Their tragic last screams distracted the Wandering Wizard who sped to their bodies that he might save them.\nElectricity shot from Iblees' fingertip in a concentrated beam. The Wizard's being was struck through the heart. Instantly he seized up in agony. To his side appeared the shoulder of the Arcane Mage, the last survivor of the mortal mages of the counsel.\nHe aided the Wandering Wizard to rise and protected him as another rain of lightning fell from above. The Wizard drew from his pocket a common clear crystal and held it up towards Iblees. An effervescent light shone from its sides engulfing the field of\nbattle in an impenetrable brightness. When the light had dispersed Iblees stood dazed. In his present form he could no longer see. He waited for the affect to wear off but the blindness continued. Enraged he threw fire, ripped the ground assunder,\nand tainted every living thing within miles. But the Wandering Wizard and Arcane Mage remained standing in opposition. He grew all the more furious and brought forth unspeakable horrors, the names of which should never be uttered. But they were likewise\nto no affect. The Wizard and Mage opposed him yet. In a mighty sulk Iblees exploded in a raging fireball and dissappeared from the realm of mortals.\nThe wandering Wizard's power never fully returned from that day, but the Arcane Mage grew wiser still. Knowing that Iblees would appear again, he reasoned with the Four Fathers that they give him no scrap of power. But time would tell if the discernment\nof mortals could resist Iblees' deception. And what became of Zalam? His frail remains was doomes to die the death of mortals. Though whether he did pass on to the Seven Skies has never been confirmed.", ""),
        StaticBook("First Questions", "Lillith Winterleaf", "An assortment of Aspirant Questions.\n\nWritten by:\nLillith Winterleaf, the Sequoia Grove\nAspirants, those seeking to become Dedicants of the Order, must be questioned by a Guide or Archdruid before being accepted as dedicants. This is to ensure the person joining the Order is doing so for the right reasons. You must be unbiased in your\njudgment of their answers, and not be afraid to tell them their path does not currently lie with the Order, but perhaps one day it will. These are not the only questions you may ask, just ones I prefer to ask. This is a guideline, not set in stone.\n\"Who are you? From where do you hail? What have you accomplished?\" Watch for self-righteousness and excessive pride in their accomplishments, the self absorbed are not typically Druid material, they are usually after personal glory.\n\"Why do you seek to join the Druidic Order?\" - Weigh their words. Watch for motivations of greed or seeking power. Wanting to help nature or help others is not enough, pry them for more.\n\"What brought you to the Druids for this? Why not another group? Why do you need to be a Druid?\" Press this one firmly, pick apart their answers and ask over and over why this requires them to be a Druid until you are satisfied or they run out of answers.\n\"What do you believe 'the balance' is?\" This question is more vaguely answered usually, and is just meant to make the Aspirant think philosophically, just watch for answers that are forcing change for supposed balance.\n\"If you came across an injured bird in the forest, what would you do?\" Again this is open to broad answers, and has no real wrong answer, it just tells you about the Aspirant.\n\"If you become a Druid, what would you do to bring notice and prestige to the Order?\" This is a trick question, as we do not seek these things actively. Our good deeds are rewards in themselves, and will bring us better recognition if done\nselflessly than any intentional act would bring.\n\"Are you positive this is the path you want to walk?\" This is another test of intention and character, take the answer they give as a judge of their character, and if they seem to be answering honestly, both to you as well as themselves.\n\"Are you positive this is the path you want to walk?\" This is another test of intention and character, take the answer they give as a judge of their character, and if they seem to be answering honestly, both to you as well as themselves.\nthat they are not ready to be a Dedicant, tell them so. Tell them WHY you believe so. If you believe them ready, have them recite the Dedicant's Vow and welcome them to the Order.", ""),
        StaticBook("First Report", "Leonard Frerich", "Today reportings -\n\nFirst sightnings -\nA rotten ground east of Blaxton Castle. It is small, and may be hard to catch. It seem to contain rotting disposed hands tossed around the ground.\n\n\nNext sightnings\nSecond sightnings -\nNorth east of the Castle proves a strange region where gigantic dead tree stands. The scout does not bother to investigate further as it lead to a cave. Any further endeavor may requires a party for a situation like this.\nNext page.\nThird sightning - \nFar north west across the lake of the Savannah proves a wooden fort undergoing construction. Unknown affilation is to be said, and cannot be seen at this present moment. Aside from that. Assume the fort as unidentified. Next page.\nThese sightnings can be confirmed by Leonard Frerich, Guard of House of Blaxton, and the Blacksmith. \n\nWith these honest words to Creator. By his words. These site exists.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fishidex", "Cir'dian", "The Fishidex\n\n\n\nThe #1 information book for fish and fisherpeople.\n\nBy Sen Nymphea\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n-Bonefish-\n\nThis fish has skin so thin that its bones are visible, and there are so many that I can't even count them ( I lost count at 420, couldn't be bothered to start again ). I don't think there's enough meat on the entire body of\nthis thing, other than bone, to even justify trying to eat it. Any volounteers are welcome to try, but I cannot be held responsible if they choke...\n\nTends to weigh around 1lb and 6oz and is found virtually everywhere. Doesn't\nseem to give any unusual effects after consumption, but my husband, after volounteering to try some, still managed to cough up a bone even after I spent fourty minutes making sure there were none left.\n-Ghostfish-\n\nThis fish is very odd. It's practically weightless and I can almost see straight through it. In fact, I'm not entirely convinced it's actually here. It could just be my imagination and perhaps I never even caught the fish in the\nfirst place.\n\nI can't even get an accurate measurement of its weight, but it weighs less than 1oz. I've only ( barely ) seen these swim about in swampy areas. My husband told me it tasted and felt like paper, and that for a moment, he felt dead.\n-Sunfish-\n\nThis variety of fish has very shiny, yellow scales. They're a very common sight, especially around dawn, but always swims toward shelter when night falls. It hates Mooneye fish with a passion and viciously attacks them\nwhenever they see them.\n\nThese fish tend to weigh around 4lbs 4oz and are found in literally every location. Some people actually throw these back after catching them. My husband says it tastes very nice, but is a hint too spicey for him.\n-Mooneye-\n\nThe Sunfish's nocturnal rival. These fish bare a large contrast compared to the Sunfish, donning pale blue scales that glow under moonlight. They are just as common as Sunfish, and why they fight so often I have no idea,\nbut I've heard that if the two varieties of fish are ever seen swimming together in a friendly manner, an eclipse is going to occur soon.\n\nFound everywhere, just like Sunfish, and weighs around 2lbs 5oz. Apparently lovely texture, but tastes\nbland, so my husband suggested that I find something to serve with it to give it some flavour.\n-Weaverfish-\n\nThis fish tends to bury itself on the bottom of lakes and snatch small animals as they venture past, including smaller fish. It has a sand-like colour to its scales with a fairly black tail and dorsal fins.\nI've only found these in thick jungle forests, where many other dangerous varieties of fish tend to live, and usually weighs around 5lbz 7oz. My husband nearly collapsed after I had him try eating some, and said he was almost paralyzed. I'm not sure what\nexactly caused this, but I'm considering finding other volounteers...\n-Monkfish-\n\nThese beasts are huge and very greedy, its teeth are also very sharp, which has allowed them to bite through many of my nets in the past. They're also quite difficult to cook because of its size.\nPretty difficult to weigh, but on average they size up around 14lbs 10oz. They're found in several locations, usually rivers and thick wooded areas. After convincing my husband to try some of this fish, he said that it was quite chewy, but made\nhis entire body feel like it'd spent a year on the most comfortable mattress and it definately made up for the last fish I'd made him try.\n-Cactusfish-\n\nThis prickly feller is covered head to tail in grey needles, which makes it very difficult to cook, catch and prepare. Their scales are normally dark green and the teeth are surprisingly blunt. Sometimes other fish get stuck to the\nspines along its body, which is a bonus if you're willing to try and peel them off.\n\nFound in dry, desert areas and weighs on average 6lbs 2oz. After very carefully removing all of the needles, my husband said the fish tasted similar to steamed\nvegetables and that the texture was delicate. Nevermind, he still managed to find a needle with his tongue...\n-Hagfish-\n\nThis thing is actually pretty creepy. It looks shriveled and aged like an old Human lady and it even has a bit of hair growing on it. It also smells like mouldy wood. To be honest, it probably is just a really old fish of another variety\nthat has somehow found a way to take refuge away from the rest of fish society. They hate venturing far from their homes and hate anything that ventures too close to their homes even more. \nOnly found in murky swamplands and usually weighs\naround 3lbs 9oz. It smelled disgusting, even when cooked, and my husband agreed, but after finally trying some ( and struggling not to vomit ) he told me that he could somehow see everything much better and that he could see my beauty even better than\nusual. I'm considering serving this to my husband more often.\n-Silverfish-\n\nThis fish is very interesting... Because I don't think it's a fish at all. In fact, I'm pretty sure that it's a bug, but whatever it is, I found it swimming about like any other fish. The only reason I'm making an entry for it is\nbecause I accidently squished it on to the page...\n\nI find these things swimming about near large mountains, but its too small to weigh.\n\n     \\ \\ / /\n-->]}}}}}}}}|===\n     / / \\ \\\n-Knifefish-\n\nAs the name probably suggests, this fish is notably dangerous because of its knife-like shape. The entire head is like one long blade, varying in length from 2 - 5 inches, about as hard as a rock, and so sharp it could\nprobably be used as a weapon. The body is rather light blue whereas the head blends in to a more subtle white.\n\nTends to roam around thick jungle areas with an average weight of 1lb 2oz. My husband said it tasted quite nice, and he kept the\nhead as a spare knife, but felt nothing strange.\n-Toadfish-\n\nThe round, fat body of this fish makes it difficult to distinguish from other animals that roam aqautic habitats, such as frogs. Actually, it looks so much like a frog that it might actualls just be a legless one with an\nunusually fish like tail. Whichever it actually is, it certainly likes to croak.\n\nOnly found quite occasionally in swamp and marsh regions, where other similar animals live and, on average, weighs around 2lbs 2oz. My husband had a\nsevere stomach ache that lasted several hours. I've decided that I won't be asking him to try anymore fish. I'll just have to find some volounteers instead.\n-Alefish-\n\nI despise this fish because it smells distinctly of alcohol, and the smell gets even stronger when it's cooked. I don't have any clue why it smells like this. It's mostly white with a faint hint of amber.\nmaybe this is where\nale actually comes from? I really don't know, but one thing I do know is that this is probably the fish I've never been more dissapointed to find.\n\nI found this fish swimming around Vaerhaven, which is far too cold for most fish to survive, and\nit weighs just 1lb 2oz. My husband volounteered to try this fish as soon as he could smell it coming from the kitchen, and said it had that Halfling brew taste. It took me an hour to get him to stop acting drunk.\n-Mullet-\n\nThis fish is rather dull, and doesn't seem to possess any 'unique' properties. The scales are grey and the fins wash to a colour fairly similar to cooked beef, which only puts me off even more. It can easily be distinguished because\nof its exceptionally long body and the 2 dorsal fins on both its back and belly.\n\nThese are quite commonly found around mountainous areas and weighs around 5lbs 11oz on average. A friend of mine volounteered to try this one, and\nactually quite enjoyed it, claiming it had a very unique taste that she would expect from an expensive restaurant, but said she didn't feel anything unusual after consumption.\n-Snakefish-\n\nFor some reason, I wasn't very happy with catching this fish, probably because it reminds me of my childhood obsession with snakes. Everything about this fish is remniscent of a snake, even the tail somewhat. It can be\ndistinguished by the pale pink scales across the body and the long fins that stretch by its sides. In fact, if it weren't for its fins, I'd say I really had caught a snake.\n\nFound in a river very close to a jungle and weighs around 5lbz 4oz.\napparently tastes like mutton with a much finer texture, but didn't have any unusual effects.\n-Salmon-\n\nThis fish is apparently popular among deepsea fishermen due to its high demand. It has an appearance similar to Mullet, but normally with a dark spotty texture along its back with a very subtle hint of red. The meat itself however is\nvery distinguishable because of its unmistakable salmon pink colour when raw.\n\nFound quite commonly near or in the Ocean, with an average weight of 7lbs 8oz. My friend said she loved the taste and would happily try more if I needed her to. No\nunusual effects were reported.\n-Lakefish-\n\nThese fish are slick and very oily, and also have a strong tail which they flail about madly when startled. This makes them fairly difficult to handle, especially with nets. The scales shine a variety of blues, usually lightest from\nthe back and gradually shading darker until it reaches the belly.\n\nFound very commonly in lakes and sometimes near thick wooded areas. Usually weighs around 5lbs 2oz, apparently tastes quite bland and has no unusual properties.\n-Magikarp-\n\nI really don't have much to say about this one. It's probably the most boring fish I've ever seen, despite how ridiculous it looks. The scales are very vibrant orange and the fins are equally as vibrant yellow. The eyes are very large\nand don't even look like they belong to a fish.\n\nI find these quite scarcely just about everywhere, and they weigh around 2.2lbs on average, depsite their average size. My friend told me it was the most boring thing she'd ever eaten and\nnothing even slightly unusual happened. The only thing slightly interesting about this fish is that it splashes around madly when pulled to land.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fishing Song", "Melodystar", "Katie's Fishing Song\n\nOne, Two, Three, Four, Five!\n\nOnce I caught a fish alive!\n\nSix, Seven, Eight, Nine, Ten!\n\nThen I let it go again!\nWhy did you let it go?\n\nBecause it bit my finger so!\n\nWhich finger did it bite?\n\nThis little finger on my right!", ""),
        StaticBook("Flesh Worm", "Veldryn Uuthlini", "A large, slimy, snake-like worm that hails deep from the Frozen Hearts of the North in Anthos. The Ollphéist, or more commonly known as, the Flesh Worm, is a legless, armless, eyeless cold-blooded beast. It dwells within large,\nmoist caves deep within the Earth, surviving off of underground critters, small mammals, and off of florescent fungus and minerals in the North.\nHow it survives is, of course, through eating. Whenever it finds something small dwelling its tunnels, it hunts off of reverberations in the tunnel. It forms a ribbed tunnel,\nwith grooves in it so it might squirm about between them, its skin acting like a writhing muscle in order to propel itself forward, or backward, or to turn as it needs.\nIt would proceed to hunt said creature through its movements, and with its maw (a folding, four segmented, tooth lined mouth), consume it whole.\nIts skin, is this worms most marvelous tool. It acts as, again, its primary mode of movement, but as well as a secondary way to obtain food. Occasionally said worms will find themselves in caverns,\nwhich allow for exponential growth. Caverns often held bio-luminescent fungi or luminescent quartz. The feint lighting and the space would allow the worm to both widen and to grow in length.\nThe worm's skin basically conducts photosynthesis, like plants do. It forms food from the light from the fungi and crystals.\nIn legend, these Worms were used as a Children's story to ward children the dangers of going into the Night or the Dark Forests. It was believed these worms were nocturnal, however, its more realized they rarely sleep,\nand rather hibernate until sensing disturbances in their tunnels. Additionally, it is known that in the North, a variant of Worm, not too distant to its cousin,\ndwelling under forests rather then plains. Its believed it used the tree branches to detect when larger creatures were wandering too far off and could get bigger game this way.\nNorthern Worms were, naturally, more hostile and found Humans to be easier pray than their Adunian kin. An overview goes as follows.\n'''Northern Worms'''\n\n Hostile, usually just smaller than their Adunian kin. They rely more on meat than light, and as such do not grow as large. They would kill small dogs especially, children,\nand if some could, adults. Parties would occasionally gather and hunt for caverns to slay the Worms and destroy the clutches.\n'''Adunian Worms'''\n\nHostile, but only to things that entered their tunnels such as miners, adventurers and explorers. They were commonly incredibly large, but were lesser seen, lesser heard, and not a large worry of many's life.", "")
    )

