hing over mortals, as it is both subtle and inconspicuous. There are only two Dragaar that have revealed themselves to the mortal races, and the decision to do so was not lightly concluded. Though the Dragaar seek to protect the\nmortal races, they often decide to do so by living in secrecy. Many discern that if they choose to associate themselves with mortal affairs too frequently, dire consequences would arise. The primary concern held by Dragaar, in regards to\ninvolvement in the matters of mortals, is that the races would eventually resort to relying on them to protect mortals from any form of evil. However, the greater dragons aspire to teach the mortal races self-preservation, without them\ndepending on the intervention of immortals.\nDrakaar\n-------------------\n\nTo attempt to bend the will of a Dragaar would be all for naught, and thus what can cause a Dragaar to devolve itself into a twisted abomination of hatred is unknown. The ancient ancestors\nof the four mortal races once believed that the choice for this horrendous transformation to occur was their own, though the aftermath of such a decision would contradict their entrusted duty. The greater dragon itself is a terrifying opponent,\nbut a Dragaar that feels no remorse and fears no consequence? That is the true fear of corruption; the perversion of the mind and distortion of one’s morality is a dreadful circumstance. In past times, the outcome of such an event would\noften be referred to as a “greater drake.” It is the combination of a Dragaar’s sentience and a drake’s all-comsuming hatred. The likelihood of a Dragaar devolving into a being tormented by rage is next to none, as mose would, in their right mind,\nturn themselves into stone to prevent the conversion. The only verifiable event recorded of a Dragaar turning to stone is that of Velketzar. The Guardian Velketzar, consumed by self-condemnation and despair due to his failure, dramatically transformed\ninto a stone statue to prevent the inevitable calamity. If a Dragaar were to fall under the hand of corruption, it would hold the power to politically corrupt nations with ease. Additionally, detecting and pursuing such a foe would be toilsome,\nall due to its shape shifting ability. Fortunately, deep meditation and concentration can inhibit this rare occurrence, along with immersing themselves in their aspect of knowledge.", ""),
        StaticBook("Gredge Tav.", "Bell Sano", "Tavern Dispute \nWitness Accounts\n\nAccount 1\nCarter Vacanti, Human\nMale, Age Thirteen\n\nClaims one of the disputing parties, the armored male, was watching him and his brother with malicious intent. Wouldnt stop after requested?\nCarter and Don went to the tall ear and told him about the supposed stalker. Don , according to carter, has a relationship with this man as a friend.\nThe elf then went outside to confront the man.\n\nCarter claims to not remeber what was said, then the-\n-officers arrived on scene.\n\n-Recorded: Davius", ""),
        StaticBook("Green & Sleep", "Annabella", "The healing ability of Cactus Green baked into foods.\n\nVol. 1; Sleep issues\nShould my hypothesis be correct this will become an entire series.\nThe testing will be on a number of paitents who have issues sleeping, they will be given cactus green bread after passing a series of questions deeming them fit for testing.\nUpon my interviews with the citizens of Gimblewood I was told most always smoke pipeweed, a much weaker form and sleeping issues are un heard of within the community.\nPreperation: In order to have a proper test one must keep all variables but one the exact same. For this reason the test will be done within the home of the subject. To avoid them fearing I will tamper with their body I will also pay for installation of a\ndoor lock, given the door has a window of some sort so I may view the subject's activity. The bread which has the Cactus green in it will be of a high consentrate to ensure the test works.\nSide note: Cactus green which is smoked harms more than it could possibly help. Cactus green MUST be baked for proper bennefits. Smoked cactus green might help sleep, but it hurts lung capacity.\nSubject 1:\nSubject 1 claims to stay awake for 3 hours just laying in bed before they fall asleep. After a test with no green to make sure the claims are indeed true. The next evening I fed Subject 1 the bread, they had the typical  symtoms of cactus gree\nn. After the inital laughing stage the subject went to their bed, and lied there for roughly 45 minutes rather than 3 hours. The subject woke up on the time they typically do, giving them 2 hours and 15 minutes more sleep than normal.\nSubject 2:\nSubject 2 is different, they had no problem getting to sleep, however they woke up often through the night. Upon testing their claims Subject 2 woke up 5 times for 15 minutes, leading to an hour and 15 minutes of sleep loss.\nAs they were fed the Cactus green bread they acted similar to Subject 1, and went to bed after the initial laughing stage. During the night I recorded 1 time where they woke up for roughly 15 minutes, leading to an overall more fufilling sleep.\nConclusion: The Hypothesis that Cactus green would help sleep was a sucess. Both subjects expirenced a boost in sleep, and woke up at the times they typically do.\nSide notes: Both subjects have only tried cactus green a few times in their life, and are not regular users. Regular users may have to use a higher concentrate. \n\nOne should not use this every night, but rather the nights they feel\nsleep is not an option as it is a known fact that Cactus green is a substance which you must use more of to get the same feeling. This can get quite expensive if done every night. IT is recomended that cactus green is not used more than once a week.\n------++{_}++------\n      This book is\n        Property\n          Of the\n         Eternal\n         Library\n------++{_}++------", ""),
        StaticBook("Grils adventures", "Grilthram Grandaxe", "THE STORY OF GRILTHRAM CHAPTER ONE: First hunt\n\nIt was about mid winter and I was in the legion I had just come back from the outside world and wanted to make a name for myself. I spent alot of my time watching the gate with my shirt off needless to say\nI didn't get alot of traffic through the gates when I was on watch. I was bored sitting at my post when the marshall walked up yelling and going off about some giant monsters attacked mountain caravans.\nI was 100% on board to get out the guard house so I\nwent along with him. This was before I had rune weapons so I just used a hammer. The marshall lead us up the mountain side and boy was it cold you never really know how cold until you climb a mountain in about a blizzard with no shoes or shirt to speak\nof. Good times they were good thing I had my beard grown out I might of froze to death. *A poorly drawn picture of grilthram climbing a mountain with thumbs up as if looking into the sky* We had walked for about a good couple of hours before hearing the\nscream of the giant winged screamer, Perfectly named monster... It looked like a giant raven and man did it squawk the damn thing would not shut up and I had to stuff my ears full of cotton to stop them from bleeding. It tried taking one of the dwarves\nwho I can't recall his name. I think he left the legion shortly after this but Luckily I was there and smashed my hammer right into its side from the flank. It screeched again..... It got really annoying at this point.\n*A crude drawining of grilthram holding his ears with the giant raven in the background squawking* It lifted off and then swung around the mountain side hovering there as it dodged a few fireballs from Dimlin.\nThen out of no where it just decided this was a good time to rush a bunch of angry dwed. We were all ready for it and it would seem the marshall was ready more than anyone else as he threw another dwed member at the creature. The dwarf flew right into it\nbut the giant beak of the creature attacked him off. As the creature laided there attempting to get back and finding it hard with the attack to its wing I did to it earlier when it tried to take off one of our companions. We moved in for the kill but it\nwas still alive and kicking swinging its beak around and attacking dwed. That is until I got down there in the thick of it I ran at the creature with a mighty blow to the face I smashed its head in. Leaving the creature dead within seconds it was a good\nhunt to say the least. I took out my trusty knife and removed its talon as the head was to far gone to take at that point. * a crudly drawn picture of the dwarf smashing the creatures head in with a thunderous blow would be seen here*\nI later gave these items to the arcadians and it started the kindling of a friend ship with the runesmiths that still grows bright to this day. *A crudely drawn picture of grilthram is here with two thumbs up dancing around* \nTHE END.", ""),
        StaticBook("Grizzly Legend", "Ryn Powell", "Legend of the Grizzly\n\nLong, long ago there were only creatures on the earth. There were birds, bears, deer, mice, everything but people. In this long ago time, all the animals spoke the same language.\nAnd just like some people nowadays, they played tricks on one another and made each other laugh. They also helped each other. So it was with all the animals.\nOne day in the winter when the lakes had frozen, but before the winter sleep, Bear was walking along the lakeshore. As he was walking, he came upon Otter sitting near a hole on the ice with a pile of fish.\n\"You've got a mighty big pile of fish there,\" Bear said. \"How did you get them fish?\"\n\nInstead of telling how he dove down into the water and caught the fish, Otter decided to trick Bear.\nYou see, back then Bear had a very long bushy tail. He was very proud of his tail, and all the animals knew it.\n\n\"The way I catch my fish is by putting my tail in this ice hole,\"\nOtter explained. \"I wiggle it around once in a while so the fish see it. When a fish bites onto my tail, I quickly pull it up and out of the water.\"\n\"That sure is an easy way to catch fish,\" Bear said. \"Do you mind if I use your fishing hole?\"\n\nOtter, laughing behind the Bear's back, said, \"I have enough fish. Use my fishing hole as long as you like.\"\nThen Otter picked up his fish and walked away. Bear carefully poked his tail into the ice hole and waited. He waited and waited. Once in a while he'd wiggle his tail so the fish could see it.\nBear waited until the sun began to set, but not one fish even nibbled at his tail. At last, he decided to go home, but when he tried to stand up, his tail had frozen into the ice! He couldn't move!\nHe pulled and pulled at his tail, but it was stuck tight. Finally, he pulled with all of his strength and ripped off half his tail!\n\nNow you know why the Bear has a short tail, and remember . . .\nDon't always believe what people tell you!\n\n((Adapted from a real Native American legend.))", ""),
        StaticBook("Guide to Druid", "Wendy", "Commoner’s Guide to Druidism\nBy: The Melody Druid - Wendy\n11th of Snow’s Maiden, 1583\n[!] A signature of elegant cursive is set here, scribed: The Melody Druid\nOn a side note: This book is intended for anyone of any race and any age past eighteen (Minors can also study but not attempt the magic until necessary age is reached).\nWhat is Druidism?\nDruidism at its core is to nature itself. Having no specific boundaries, no set motives, and just is. Being to nature itself, there are the Aspects, the Druids and nature that is seen as a balance in the realms.\nWho are the Aspects?\nCerridwen, the mother of harvest, the Aspect of Life. She is the Aengul that represents birth. Cernunnos, the father of hunt, the Aspect of Hunt & Death. He is the Aengul that represents life and death.\nThey work together to attune a druid’s well being, aswell as influencing them through Druidism as a whole.\nWhat are Druids?\nThe Druids are individuals who have undergone a lengthy dedicancy, proving their loyalty to the Aspects and the Druidic Order as a dedicant.\nThese individuals are given totems, alongside with the power to commune with nature, influence it through exchanging requests and healing nature along with its creatures in order to maintain what most know as the Balance of Nature.\nWhat is the Druidic Order?\nThe Druidic Order is an organization that serves the Aspects as a whole, having Archdruids as the leader of a circle along with a large number of druids that reside within each circle.\nA circle is another group of druids that have split from the main Grove in order to go about teaching of the Aspects and nature in their own ways. No matter the circle, they will always have one main purpose that they must not stray from:\n“To serve under the Aspects, and to protect and maintain the balance of nature at all costs.”\nAre there any rankings in the Order?\nAs a commoner, a person that wishes to seek the ways of the Aspects will undergo a lengthy interview with a druid guide and will be scored based on their knowledge of nature as well as the way they go about things.\nSoon after, if accepted, they will become a Dedicant. They will receive tasks in order to prove their loyalty until their guide deems they’re ready.\nTypically when they’re ready, the guide will often have the Dedicant think of a totem, as well as creating a staff of their own.\nWhen finished, a guide will bring their Dedicant to an attunement pool and begin the attunement where the Dedicant will journey through and seek their totem given by the Aspects themselves.\nAfter a Dedicant receives their totem and speaks it aloud, they are no longer a dedicant, rather they are a fully-fledged druid, capable of tuning in on the nature around them.\nThough it is overwhelming to most, they will undergo training in order to learn of how to concentrate and use their gifts with a sturdy grasp of knowledge.\nAs a druid, an individual is now learning more of themselves, continuing their path chosen by the Aspects, as well as learning more of the Gifts.\nSoon after some time, a druid can move towards a Druid Guide, where they’re able to have another interview in order to test for their knowledge so that they themselves may learn of how to teach and spread word of the Aspects and nature.\nWhen passed and trained, a druid becomes a Druid Guide. As a guide, they are now part of the Inner Circle, a circle within each circle that assists in the decisions of the Order as a whole.\nIf a guide is worthy enough, they can be vouched in order to become an Archdruid once one has stepped down, during a Moot. An Archdruid is a druid that has spent an extreme amount of time within the Order and knows the in’s and outs of the Order.\nThere are three to each circle and will often be the ones to make decisions for the Order, in regards to their guide peers and Hierophant advisors.\nA Hierophant is a druid that has been an Archdruid and stepped down in order to achieve more personal goals. These druids are a beacon of knowledge and often referred to by the Archdruid for decision making.\nAny other rankings?\nTypically if a druid has done something extremely remarkable within their time as a druid, they can eventually climb up as a Notable druid. These druids are praised for their achievements and looked to as heroes of the Order.\nOne of the highest honors the Order can bestow is: The Demi-Aspect. These are druids that have been through each and every single rank.\nThey have done remarkable feats within their time in the realm and are lead towards the realm of the Aspects where they are able to enjoy an eternal rest with the Aspects themselves.\nThey’re often referred as saints to the Order. There are also the Lost & Forgotten Druids. Lost druids are typically druids that have been gone or unseen from the Order for a short period of time.\nMost will often come back or sometimes even scolded for doing so without reason. Forgotten druids are druids that have left the Order, gone missing or have been unattuned for a variety of reasons.\nThese druids can and will receive punishment if their reasoning isn’t worthy enough for going against the path of the Aspects. Then there are the shunned. Individuals that have harmed a druid or the Order.\nShuns will be approached with a simple phrase: “Must wind pours from your mouth.” If the shun continues to harass a druid, they may warn them once more before taking action. If a shun continues their actions, they will be made to KOS, kill on sight.\nWhat are the ‘Gifts’?\nThe gifts are bestowed from the Aspects at the ending of an attunement.\nThe druid will be taught of how to commune with the nature around them, as well as learn to bless and exchange requests with it. Soon after they are able to seek out others within the Order in order to learn of healing.\nThere are two subtypes to healing: Nature’s Healing & Blight Healing. Nature’s Healing is using salves or herbal means in order to bless through and apply to either a creature or nature itself.\nThough it can heal most, it cannot heal what blight healing is able to. Blight Healing is the healing of tainted or corrupted land.\nTypically the reasoning behind taint is usually from a darker being tapping into the natural energies of nature and stealing it away for personal gain.\nThis healing requires time as a druid must concentrate onto the tainted land in order to restore what is dead back to lushful life.\nWhat is the balance of nature?\nThe balance of nature is nature as a whole. It’s literally not to tap into nature and fiddle with Cerridwen’s creations.\nAnyone or anything that goes against this through any means is considered unnatural and will be dealt with accordingly.\nVoidal and Dark arts are often considered unnatural. They add to an already full scale of nature, typically manipulating or even taking from nature as a whole.\nLast note:\n\nIf their are any potential dedicants, please do not hesitate to come to the Mother Grove. Ask around if you're not sure. I, the Melody Druid, if still around can acknowledge you as you wish. And with that, Blessed Be, reader.\n[!] There is a signature onto this page.\n\nThe\n    Melody\n            Druid\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~-------------------", ""),
        StaticBook("Guide to Reason", "Grigor Grandaxe", "A Guide to Reason. A Philisophical Bestseller by Grigor Grandaxe.\n\nHey you.\nYeah You.\nWhat do you know about Philsophy? Here in this book I will give you statements to help you to reson with yourself, to think and\nto reflect on actions based on the Philosophical premises that I will give to you.\n\nInstustions for use of this book:\n1. Open this book\n2. Follow the guidelines of each statement\n3. Keep it to one statement a day\nso that you may have the designed, 10 day reading period here, weather you read this at church, at work, in bed or at home.\n\nOn the next page your journey through Philoposphy will begin.\n---->\nDay One, Statement One.\n\"Progress just means bad things happen faster.\" - Grigor Grandax.\n\nConsider the connotations of this statement and its effect on you and your life, are bad things happening to you?\nDay Two, Statement Two.\n\"I think therefore I am.\"\n\nWHat do you want to be? HAve you tried to be this? Mabye you are all you want to be, and if so have you considered how you got there?\nDay Three, Statement Three.\n\"I can't go back to yesterday, because I was a different person then.\"\n\nHow much have you changed since yesterday? since last week? last year?\nDay 4, Statement 4.\n\"Don't bitw off more than you can chew because nobody looks attractive spitting it out\"\n\nWho has strived for something so far out of their reach they injure themselves whilst striving for it?\nDay 5, Statement 5.\n\"All is fair in love and war.\"\n\nThink on this statement for yourself and apply its Philosophy to your life. It has important conotations.\nDay 6-10\nPlease purchase Part Two of the Grigor Grandaxe Philosophy\nReading Plan for the added statements, remeber you will become a better persons if you apply the Philosophies of this book.", ""),
        StaticBook("Guide to Sorcery", "Ambros", "A Guide to Sorcery\n\n\n      By Ambros\nIn this book you will find a very simple guide on being a proper mage, this would include  your supplies you need as well as the proper training you need to become a decent mage.\nWhat is Arcane Magic?\nAll magic uses the same power source, although what varies from magical user to magical is dependent on how the user goes about manipulating his/her powers. Arcane magic is often considered to be a more modern version\nof magic compared to the ancient druids ot the gifted Ascended or Undead, although none the less Arcane magic can be considered to be the most complex of magical manipulation.\nHow To Manipulate Arcane Magic.\nArcane magic can be manipulated in a number of ways, although most scholars believe the best way to go about doing this is creating an image in your mind of what you want the final effect of your spell to be.\nSome scholars believe that the best way to use the most powerful form of magic is through emotion Of course this is quite wrong and this form of magic is hard to control and should never be done. Many mages claim that their powers are akin\nto keys-necessary to unlock the final effect of a spell-another, new theory has begun to gain ground among younger mages.  These energetic mages assert that components aren't keys, but rather locks, suggesting that even the most learned of\narcanists don't fully control their own powers, and that components are necessary intruments to keep the spells in check. Whether these locks were placed by the deities themselves or are simply such an old conention that\nno one today questions their utility is anyone's guess.\nDiffrent Types Of Magic\nMages are mostly a combat and \"trick\" type magic.  Rarely do they have access to many of the necromany and healing magic that the Undead, Ascended, or druids might have.\nAlthough they can often achieve a number of other magical feats that the other magical orders can not.  Since arcane magic is a magic of the mind its power is based off of your intelligence then more often than not you will see a mage locking a door with\na spell, shooting fire from his staff, or moving blocks of stone about.  This is due to the fact that arcane magic is not a spiritual form of magic so any form of \"spiritual\" attributes about it are gone.\nA healer mage is a very rare sight as well, healing magic is a form of \"spiritual\" magic helping the mind cleanse and wash away pain and injury. Now of course you might see an unorthodox way of healing from a mage such as sealing a wound with fire\nor easing pain with a numbing spell.  Whatever the case is arcane magic is a magic of the mind.", ""),
        StaticBook("GUY.CO INSURANCE", "Ayche Raven'kor", "ARE YOU PAYING TOO MUCH FOR CART INSURANCE?\n\nSEEK OUT GUY. CO FOR PREMIUM INSURANCE PACKAGES.\n\nYOUR CARTS ARE AN INVESTMENT. PROTECT THEM.\n\n15 MINUTES COULD SAVE YOU 15% OR MORE.", ""),
        StaticBook("Haelun'or Attack", "Amras Yavelty", "Accounts of the Attack of Haelun’or\nBy Amras Yavelty\nAs I arrive from my most recent travels I’m confronted with the destroyed gate of our blessed city in Haelun’or. The gates were pulled and bent by some colossal force which until this day is still unconfirmed. The only Mali'Aheral who witnessed such\nexplosion were Vulnir and Dyonne which encountered the recently destroyed gate after hearing, what they described to be, an explosion. To no surprise the forces who perpetrated such act headed to Malinor where both Vulnir and myself saw the great\ncreatures standing around 11 feet tall and a dreadful and horrifying appearance. As Vulnir and me hurried back to our beloved city we were relieved to see both Kalenz, a powerful master of telekinesis and our golem Aeon which wielded a mighty battle\nhammer for good measure. Kalenz quickly ordered all the adult Mali’aheral to take up weapons and march to Malinor to aid in what was left of the battle. I quickly went into my residence and blew the dust from my bow and gathered as many arrows as I could\nfind, hoping they were still sharp enough to hurt such creatures that awaited us in Malinor. \nAs the small company of Vulnir, Safrill, Aeon, Kalenz, and myself arrived at the main gates of Malinor we could only see what was left of a great struggle\nbetween the Malinor guard and the two terrible creatures. To our content no Mali’aheral blood was to be spilled as one of the creatures had been slain and the other ran its way to the North followed by what was left of the Malinor defense. As we headed\nback to our cihi and the bright of day gave way to the sacred night a strange presence was felt. As we approached the gates my mind seemed to be filled by an unfamiliar thought, a dark and soft voice crept through my head and seemed to be powered by the\ncool breeze of that night. Kalenz shouted “Get ready Mali’aheral for that being is not far.” Indeed we could see shadows lurking in the forest. Vulnir, Safrill, and myself headed to the towers while Aeon stood below and Kalenz just behind him.\nWe kept watch all night but nothing could be seen. Day arrived and we still felt uneasy. We drank and ate as Kalenz deduced this creature could come again at night. Night approached and once again we took our positions now with the help of another archer,\nCeruberr. We kept the children safe inside the walls and prepared for an imminent attack. Suddenly the voice appeared in our heads again. This time I managed to get some composure and write down its words as I heard them in fear: \"Blessed are those who\nwalk in the Light… Sanctified are those who can walk with their shadow… For their path shall not stray, their step shall not falter… Never journeying alone…… In the brightness or dark.” As these words were uttered a dark figure began approaching and\nSafrill gave the word to aim at the being. Aeon lowered his hammer and Kalenz concentrated what seemed to be some energy in his hands. I have never seen Kalenz use his abilities, I just knew he was a mage because I was told.\nThe creature approached and Kalenz began to move one of the logs that was resting on the ground probably to hurl it at the figure, yet the being was smart enough to use its dark powers to levitate to a height similar to the wall. I was first to fire, but\nthe arrow seemed to have no effect or perhaps I missed, but so did every arrow released that night. The being was dark as the night sky absent of stars and its shape was hard to decipher but as Kalenz emitted a light using his own powers the creature\nretreated. It was then that we realized its weakness was light. The night was beginning to fade and the morning light covered Haelun’or in safety.\n             -----------", ""),
        StaticBook("Haelun'or Attack", "Aevalyn", "Accounts of the\n  Attack of Haelun'or\n\n       Haelun'or,\n          Axios\n\n    Published 1593\n\n   by Amras Yavelty\n    Transcribed by\n   Aevalyn Bethiros\nAs I arrive from my most recent travels I’m confronted with the destroyed gate of our blessed city in Haelun’or.\nThe gates were pulled and bent by some colossal force which until this day is still unconfirmed.\nThe only Mali’Aheral who witnessed such explosion were Vulnir and Dyonne which encountered the recently destroyed gate after hearing, what they described to be, an explosion.\nTo no surprise the forces who perpetrated such act headed to Malinor where both Vulnir and myself saw the great creatures standing around 11 feet tall and a dreadful and horrifying appearance.\nAs Vulnir and me hurried back to our beloved city we were relieved to see both Kalenz, a powerful master of telekinesis and our golem Aeon which wielded a mighty battle hammer for good measure.\nKalenz quickly ordered all the adult Mali’aheral to take up weapons and march to Malinor to aid in what was left of the battle.\nI quickly went into my residence and blew the dust from my bow and gathered as many arrows as I could find, hoping they were still sharp enough to hurt such creatures that awaited us in Malinor.\nAs the small company of Vulnir, Safrill, Aeon, Kalenz, and myself arrived at the main gates of Malinor we could only see what was left of a great struggle between the Malinor guard and the two terrible creatures.\nTo our content no Mali’aheral blood was to be spilled as one of the creatures had been slain and the other ran its way to the North followed by what was left of the Malinor defense.\nAs we headed back to our cihi and the bright of day gave way to the sacred night a strange presence was felt.\nAs we approached the gates my mind seemed to be filled by an unfamiliar thought, a dark and soft voice crept through my head and seemed to be powered by the cool breeze of that night.\nKalenz shouted “Get ready Mali’aheral for that being is not far.” Indeed we could see shadows lurking in the forest.\nVulnir, Safrill, and myself headed to the towers while Aeon stood below and Kalenz just behind him.\nWe kept watch all night but nothing could be seen. Day arrived and we still felt uneasy. We drank and ate as Kalenz deduced this creature could come again at night.\nNight approached and once again we took our positions now with the help of another archer, Ceruberr. We kept the children safe inside the walls and prepared for an imminent attack.\nSuddenly the voice appeared in our heads again. This time I managed to get some composure and write down its words as I heard them in fear:\n“Blessed are those who walk in the Light… Sanctified are those who can walk with their shadow… For their path shall not stray, their step shall not falter… Never journeying alone…… In the brightness or dark.”\nAs these words were uttered a dark figure began approaching and Safrill gave the word to aim at the being.\nAeon lowered his hammer and Kalenz concentrated what seemed to be some energy in his hands. I have never seen Kalenz use his abilities, I just knew he was a mage because I was told.\nThe creature approached and Kalenz began to move one of the logs that was resting on the ground probably to hurl it at the figure,\nyet the being was smart enough to use its dark powers to levitate to a height similar to the wall.\nI was the first to fire, but the arrow seemed to have no effect or perhaps I missed, but so did every arrow released that night.\nThe being was dark as the night sky absent of stars and its shape was hard to decipher but as Kalenz emitted a light using his own powers the creature retreated.\nIt was then that we realized its weakness was light. The night was beginning to fade and the morning light covered Haelun’or in safety.", ""),
        StaticBook("Haelun'or Attack", "Amras_Yavelty", "Accounts of\n    the Attack\n   on Haelun'or\n\n  by Amras Yavelty\nIf this book is found anywhere else than the Eternal Library of Lin’evaral, the Enclave of Haelun’or, it is stolen.\n\nBoth buyers and sellers will be punished.\n\nSigned, the Tilruir’Indor Lelien\nAs I arrive from my most recent travels I’m confronted with the destroyed gate of our blessed city in Haelun’or. The gates were pulled and bent by some colossal force which until this day is still unconfirmed.\nThe only Mali’Aheral who witnessed such explosion were Vulnir and Dyonne which encountered the recently destroyed gate after hearing, what they described to be, an explosion. To no surprise the forces who perpetrated such act headed to Malinor where\nVulnir and myself saw the great creatures standing around 11 feet tall and a dreadful and horrifying appearance. As Vulnir and me hurried back to our beloved city we were relieved to see both Kalenz, a powerful master of telekinesis and our\ngolem Aeon which wielded a mighty battle hammer for good measure. Kalenz quickly ordered all the adult Mali’aheral to take up weapons and march to Malinor to aid in what was left of the battle.\nI quickly went into my residence and blew the dust from my bow and gathered as many arrows as I could find, hoping they were still sharp enough to hurt such creatures that awaited us in Malinor.\nAs the small company of Vulnir, Safrill, Aeon, Kalenz, and myself arrived at the main gates of Malinor we could only see what was left of a great struggle between the Malinor guard and the two terrible creatures. To our content no Mali'aheral blood\nwas to be spilled as one of the creatures had been slain and the other ran its way to the North followed by what was left of the Malinor defense.\n\nAs we headed back to our cihi and the brght of the day gave way to the sacred night a strage presence\nwas felt. As we approached the gates my mind seemed to be filled by an unfamiliar thought, a dark and soft voice crept through my head and seemed to be powered by the cool breeze of that night. Kalenz shouted, \"Get ready, Mali'aheral, for that being is\nnot far.” Indeed we could see shadows lurking in the forest. Vulnir, Safrill, and myself headed to the towers while Aeon stood below and Kalenz just behind him.\nWe kept watch all night but nothing could be seen. Day arrived and we still felt uneasy. We drank and ate as Kalenz deduced this creature could come again at night. Night approached and once again we took our positions now with the help of another\narcher, Ceruberr. We kept the children safe inside the walls and prepared for an imminent attack. Suddenly the voice appeared in our heads again. This time I managed to get some composure and write down its words as I heard them in fear: \"Blessed are\nthose who walk in the Light… Sanctified are those who can walk with their shadow… For their path shall not stray, their step shall not falter… Never journeying alone…… In the brightness or dark.” As these words were uttered, a dark figure began\napproaching and Safrill gave the word to aim at the being. Aeon lowered his hammer and Kalenz concentrated what seemed to be some energy in his hands. I have never seen Kalenz use his abilities, I just knew he was a mage because I was told.\nThe creature approached and Kalenz began to move one of the logs that was resting on the ground probably to hurl it at the figure, yet the being was smart enough to use its dark powers to levitate to a height similar to the wall. I was the first to\nfire, but the arrow seemed to have no effect or perhaps I missed, but so did every arrow released that night. The being was dark as the night sky absent of stars and its shape was hard to decipher but as Kalenz emitted a light using his own powers the\ncreature retreated. It was then that we realized its weakness was light. The night was beginning to fade and the morning light covered Haelun’or in safety.", ""),
        StaticBook("Haelun'orSchism1", "L. Sullas", "The Haelun'or\n       Schism:\n      Volume 1\n\n   by Lucion Sullas\nThe history of Asulon is known to be rich with wars, political usurpations, monstrous drakes, and the rise and fall of nations. However, one history that eludes most modern, non-mali'aheral scholars is the secret history of the elhaelun'or, and its\nmany trials and tribulations. One such excerpt (to take from a vast swathe) is the Haelun'or Schism--a short, and unusual, period of instability and disunity in the motherland. In this three volume series, one will discuss the turbulent period for the\nbenefit of future citizens.\n\nThe Haelun'or of Asulon was, in this period, ruled by the echillan'thilln--the Silver Council. Much like its Malinorian contemporary, members were chosen by those whom were deemed worthy by the\ncurrent council members--the okariran. Two of these counsellors would begin a chain of events eventually causing the one, and only, demagogic political usurpation in mali'aheral history. Their names were Ellir'siol, the Okarir'layun (Master\nof beauty), and Nelecar, the Okarir'sil (Master of the Sword).\n\nFrom the very inception of the two working together, friction between their personalities was evident. Nelecar was a soldier with a great, and admirable, dedication to the\npurity of his kin. His efficient, though admittedly extreme, methods of protection allowed for a distinctly effective military force that has yet to be seen again within the walls of the mali'aheral. Ellir'siol was an artist, and an architect. Her\nmesmerising design of the Haelun’or residential district was one of the finest examples of classical, revivalist mali'aheral architecture available, and is still emulated to this day.Touting overtures of peace, wisdom, and forethought, she strove only for\nwhat can be perceived as \"the greater good\" in regards to the motherland.\n\nDespite their own good intentions, there were many obvious faults in their actions throughout their years in the service of the cihi'thilln. Nelecar was not a\nforgiving mali. When a single, minor wrong was committed, he would often act harshly towards the perpetrator. One such case involved an insolent mali'aheral who refused the Okarir’s demands, and was summarily locked in a cell for nearly a month as\npunishment. His liberal use of banishment to punish wrongdoers was also a harshly debated affair, and was the main issue of the coming schism. Ellir'siol, however, was by contrast far too forgiving of wrongdoers. She often pressed for impure mali'aheral\nto be re-integrated to society, and those whose ideals were not congruent with Larihei's vision were protected by her delicate, and clever political machinations. Retrospectively, conflict should have been predicted.\nThis is but a tale of two mali’aheral incapable of compromise, and such shall be shown in the second volume.", ""),
        StaticBook("Haelun'orSchism2", "Eenhoornheid", "The Haelun'or\n       Schism:\n      Volume II\n\n    by Lucion Sullas\nNow that one has learned of the two figures involved in this debacle, let us discuss the event itself. Should you not ahave read the previous volume, most of what shall be written will be nothing but a confusing morass of information.\nOne suggests you perform the logical action, and return to the previous volume prior to reading this one.\n\nNelecar's afore-mentioned zest for banishment had been mostly tolerated by the council, aside from the\nconsiberable opposition from Ellir'siol. However, one event sparked a final, fatal banishment. The husband of Ellir'siol, Talias, the second-in-command of the military under Nelecar, was exposed, along with other individuals (whom shall not be identified,\ndue to a number still living and present within the nation), as attempting to subvert, and remove Belecar from his position via aggressive action. Upon learning of this, Nelecar immediately called for the banishment of all those involved.\nElli'siol, understandably, attempted to argue Nelecar out of doing so, but only managed to stall his pronouncement with the help of other council members. When the decision was made public, Elli'siol showed her true colours.\nIn a move to directly parody the acts of Nelecar, she 'banished' the entire populations of the city, and majority of the citizenry followed her out of Haelun'or-- those won over by her popular and public dislike of the Okarir'sil. Piling upon boats,\nthey left the Emerald Isle to the town of Ceru-- a cliffside village and quasi-colony that bordered the Kingdom of Renatus. Here, they settled for a time, and waited.\nHere Ellir engaed in disgraceful, demagogic, rabble-rousing, and appearled to illogical emotional thinking to further solidify and justify her actions. This went on for many months, while Nelecar and his few loyal supporters remained within Haelun'or-\n-slowly losing confidence in their actions.\n\nAfter months had passed, and her ravenous support had died down, Ellir returned to the city-- deeming her point had been made. However, it was noticeably adsent of Nelecar.\nHis supporters remained, and were thankfully not pursued by the 'victors'.\n\nThe prologue and effects of this event will be discussed in the final installment of this series.", ""),
        StaticBook("Haelun'orSchism2", "L. Sullas", "The Haelun'or\n       Schism:\n      Volume 2\n\n   by Lucion Sullas\nNow that one has learned of the two figures involved in this debacle, let us discuss the event itself. Should you not have read the previous volume, most of what shall be written will be nothing but a confusing morass of information. One suggests you\nperform the logical action, and return to the previous volume prior to reading this one.\n\nNelecar's afore-mentioned zest for banishment had been mostly tolerated by the council, aside from considerable opposition from\nEllir'siol. However, one event sparked a final, fatal banishment. The husband of Ellir'siol, Talias, the second-in-command of the military under Nelecar, was exposed, along with other individuals (Whom shall not be identified, due to a number still living\nand present within the nation), as attempting to subvert, and remove Nelecar from his position via aggressive action. Upon learning of this, Nelecar immediately called for the banishment of all those involved. Ellir'siol, understandably,\nattempted to argue Nelecar out of doing so, but only managed to stall his pronouncement with the help of other council members. When the decision was made public, Ellir'siol showed her true colours.\nIn a move to directly parody the acts of Nelecar, she \"banished\" the entire population of the city, and majority of the citizenry followed her out of Haelun'or--those won over by her popular and public dislike of the Okarir'sil. Piling upon boats,\nthey left the Emerald Isle to the town of Ceru--a cliffside village and quasi-colony that bordered the Kingdom of Renatus. Here, they settled for a time, and waited.\nHere Ellir engaged in disgraceful, demagogic, rabble-rousing, and appealed to illogical emotional thinking to further solidify and justify her actions. This went on for many months, while Nelecar and his few loyal supporters remained within Haelun'or\n--slowly losing confidence in their actions. \n\nAfter months had passed, and her ravenous support had died down, Ellir returned to the city--deeming her point had been made. However, it was noticeably absent of\nNelecar. His supporters remained, and were thankfully not pursued by the \"victors\".\n\nThe prologue and effects of this event will be discussed in the final installment of this series.", ""),
        StaticBook("Haelun'orSchism3", "L. Sullas", "The Haelun'or\n      Schism:\n     Volume 3\n\n   by Lucion Sullas\nThe importance of the events that occurred during the Schism can not be treated lightly. The after-effects, though, were seemingly mundane. With the immediate disappearance of Nelecar, the whole city simply fell to the leadership of what council was\nleft, although Ellir obviously having significant influence over proceedings.\n\nA detrimental effect of the schism was the slow dissolution of what remained of the armed forces (then referred to as the \"Legion\"). The size and ability of the\nsoldiery was slowly whittled away, until only a few diligent guardsmen remained. Further affected was the concept of violence in general--the methods of the Okarir'sil no longer popular with any citizen. The lacking of these two elements may explain why\nthe mali'aheral nation has been a haven of peace for decade upon decade.\n\nOne is sure, however, that the reader is curious of the fate these two political rivals succumbed to.\nNelecar's disappearance did not last long, as he hid in the lowest levels of the city--murdering numerous citizens over the course of multiple years. However, after nearly four decades of being hidden, the ragged Okarir'sil found his way into the\ncity, and stood in the square, confronting frightened, and confused citizenry. His madness had overtaken himself, and, as a final act, he took his own life--broken, thin, alone, and forgotten by history.\nEllir'siol, who strived all her life to keep all those whom she loved safe, lost her entire family. She herself turned bitter, and strayed away from the citizenry in her cold, lonely tower above the Eternal College. Eventually, she herself disappeared\n--almost as if fading away with the end of her political career.\n\nLet this short history be a message of the dangers that are inherent within the extremes of political rivalry, and extremist thinking. Should one desire to take a message from these\nvolumes, then allow this humble writer to give you a final, resolute statement. \n\nRashness is rewarded only with destruction, and demagoguery is rewarded only with loss.", ""),
        StaticBook("Hafling Village", "Lucy Kilwar", "How to go to the Hafling Village\n-------------------\n\nFirst you'll want to walk to Sutica. Once you have arrived there you'll make a straight line thru it until you arrive to a brige leading to a road. The road should be surounded by trees and\none or two feelds.\nYou will follow that path untill you arrive to a crosroad. You'll take the road to your left and follow it some more. You will normaly have arrived to the Hafling village. It is dotted with small huts with round entrances who are shaped\nlike tiny hills. The Haflings are farmers so you should see multiple feelds. One interesting factor of the Hafling village is that none of the dores or chests are locked because it is the Hafling tradition to say that their own property is also the other\npeople of the village's.\n\nThe hafling who helped me in this finde was called Lily Greenhill (Emamou). \nThis is the official entry of how to go to the Hafling village by Lucy Kilwar (white_angel2003).", ""),
        StaticBook("Halfling Babies", "Unknown", "Halfling Babies\nBy Unknown\nWhere do Halfling babies come from?\nHalfling birth is by far the most magical and sweet birth of all the races. I first found out about how the Halflings are born when I went to the Halfling town, which I have forgotten the name of.\nQuite hungry when I arrived, I asked permission from one of the elders to remove a few plants from the farm, permission which was granted to me.\n\nAs I walked through the farm I took a few carrots and potatoes, then I found an overly grown cabbage.\nI thought as a thank you, I would cook the great cabbage and make the Halflings a great cauldron of cabbage soup. As I was about to take the cabbage from the fertile land, a Halfling came shouting through the fields for me to stop, seeming quite stressed.\nBelieving that somehow I was in the wrong field, or that cabbage was of prized goods, I stepped away from the cabbage, and waited the Halfling. While huffing, the Halfling, still stressed, checked the cabbage for damage, before hitting me in the shin with\nhis shovel.\nIn pain I fell to while grabbing my leg, wondering what kind of prized cabbage that could be. The Halfling looked angry and even shouted, “Wha’ were y’ goin’ t’ do t’ me son?!” I was amazed, the cabbage was so important to him, he called\nit his son. I apologized and said that as a thank you I was going to cook his ‘son’ for the Halflings, but that I didn’t know it belonged to someone. I couldn’t finish explaining before I hit repeatedly by the shovel. The Halfling was shouting as he hit\nme, “Y’ disgustin’ man, how dare’ye try t’ feed us one o’ our own babies!”\n\nI was shocked, I didn’t understand. I apologized and said many times that I didn’t know, and after a while, the Halfling stopped hitting me.\nAfter he stopped I continued asking, in serious pain I might add. I asked what the cabbage meant to the Halflings, and he told me a story I will never forget.\n\nThe story he told me one of love, the love two Halflings feel for each other.\nI already knew at the time how Dwarf babies were born, and knew that Halflings are descendents of both Horen and Urguan, so I was confused how they mated and had children. I didn’t know if it was the Dwarven way of the Human way.\nAnd what I was told was nothing more than magical. \nHe told me of him and his wife, wife for many years now. They clearly loved each other quite dearly, and one day decided to have a child. They began their evening by drinking and smoking together, alone\nin their house, only the two which love each other. They do what they love most together, drinking the finest Halfling ale, and smoking the best Halfling weed. When the moon was high, they went into the fields together, carrying a single seed, a normal\nseed. After planting the cabbage in the patch, they prayed to their pumpkin god.\n\nThe seed, blessed with the love of the soon to be mother and father Halfling, and the power of the pumpkin god, started growing quite large, into what was now the cabbage\nI almost took. The baby Halfling grows within the cabbage, to be born at the time of the harvest season. It was still a few Elven days from the harvest, and as such, if I had took the cabbage, I would give birth to the baby too soon.\nI decided to stay for a while longer to witness the birth, and it was as they said.\nI helped with the harvest that day, and soon, all the Halflings gathered by the cabbage. The mother and father started carefully removing the big leaves of the cabbage.\nIt took awhile for the small Halflings to remove the leaves, but soon enough, in the middle of it, a tiny sleeping baby could be seen. The father thanked the pumpkin god once more as the mother took the baby. That night, they made a feast, for the\nharvest, and newborns.\n\nThe name for the newborns? They thought of them while drunk and high.", ""),
        StaticBook("Halfling Study", "Ralnor Kelyarus", "A Journal on Halflings\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBy: Ralnor Kelyarus\nThe halflings are a strange race. The halfling race is known for their short size and foreign speech patterns. This, along with their strange religious tendencies somewhat isolates them from the outside world. Their village, known as Reedsborough, acts as\na safe haven for these strange creatues, providing them with protection from the outside world, and a stable spot to sufficiently produce their own resources.\nThis village is very odd, however. Instead of regular houses, their living quarters are small\nrooms nestled inside of small hills. These \"burrows\" appropriately accommodate for the many needs of the halflings. However, this is not the only oddity of their village. Reedesborough also contains a massive array of pumpkins and jack o'lanterns. I am\nunsure of their purpose, but they do serve as a good decorative device. All in all, the halflings are an interesting group of people that should be studied more to understand their culture, society, and religion in deeper detail.", ""),
        StaticBook("Halflings V1", "Mi'Tha'Kaal", "The Halflings\n\n\nThe Halflings are a breed betwin gumans (Vallah) and the dwarves.\n\nThey venerate The Pumkin it's they'r only god, they love to party drink and smoke and eat.\n\nThey don't weare shoes\nlike chivilazed people, and they live in burrows, houses built in hills whit round doors. They don't use money they simply share and love rain, due to they'r racial skills in carving pumkins they are great stonemasons.\nThe halflings don't use normal weaponery thay use shovels to defend they'r village and they don't fight other nations. They like poems and good bards who sing long and beautyfull songs.\n\nThey organize a festival where all races and nations are invited,\nthey worship Knox, the god of harvest and they are lead by elected members known as elders.\n\nThey also select they'r Sherrif to keep them safe (whit a shovel) from the bad orcs or goblins that come to raid them.\n\n               -Mi'Tha", ""),
        StaticBook("Halflings Vol. 1", "Petrus Frondor", "Halflings: A History\n              Vol. I\n\n\n     A History of Halflings\n      By Petyr Brandybuck\n\n    Edited by Petrus Frondor\nPreface\nAs is common knowledge, the origins of the halfling race reside began with couples consisting of a human and a dwarf. Nowadays, the halflings have distinct traits of their own, practically unmistakable when compared  with the modern counterparts\nof their progenitors. The purpose of this book is to educate the populace about the culture and history of the halflings. The information in this book has been preserved either in ruins, in literature, or in folklore.\nChapter 1 - Beginnings\nYears 0-300\n\nThough there are many conflicting accounts regarding the creation and following years of Aegis, most records agree that the race of humans and that of dwarves most likely had contact before Year 50. And, as when any two\ncultures collide, so do their blood, and so at some point in time, humans began to mate with dwarves. We can trace some traits back to this point, such as brewing and farming talents, but as we will see, other generic halfling traits developed over time.\nIndeed, it is hard to pinpoint the first halfling. After researching animal breeding as well as magical oddities, I would propose that, intially, the children of a dwarf/human couple would not be classified as a halfling.  You see, it would make sense if\nhalflings were a height in between that of a dwarf and human, but instead, they are actually shorter! This would indicate that, some time in the past, a great outer influence caused the future children of these mixed couples to have this odd height.\nIt is reasonable to conclude that halflings as we know them today were present by Year 300, based on folklore and literary records.\nChapter 2 - Early Developments\nYears 300-600\n\nA combination of small stature and inherant greed drove some of the first halflings to thievery, a very viable profession for nimble hands in the cities. They gained a reputation for being mischievous and\ndevious, and thus gained little respect for their brewing or farming prowess. There was some prejudice against them, no doubt; never once in history or literature does one hear of a heroic or powerful halfling. To say they were suppressed would be\nincorrect, but people did find them a thing to be \"tolerated\".\n\nOver time, of course, most halflings developed a sort of fear of violence and arguments, reducing the number of thieves. As well, most halflings moved to Oren to escape the war-mongering\nattitude of the dwarves. This is estimated to have taken place over the time span of Years 400-600 The humans were little better, though. And, over time, halflings began to move to more rural areas, escaping those that would persecute them. Small\ncommunities on the very border of human cities were formed, and there halflings began to develop customs to cheer them up. Indeed, good food and good times seemed to become the goal of every halfling.\nChapter 3 - Later Developments Years 600-1200\n\nHalflings continued migrating farther and farther out of the city.  It came to be that small communities of halflings were spread out in the vast plains surrounding Oren, with the halflings only revealing\nthemselves occasionally to trade goods. Over time, the negative connotation towards halflings mostly disappated, but the halflings enjoyed their semi-solitary lifestyles.\n\nThe countryside is where the art of halfling brew and cooking truly matured into\nthe art form that it is today. Indeed, the herbs and spices that could be found in the countryside of Oren had never been truely used to their full potential, and so halflings were the first to utilize them. Some of these herbs include the yellow\nwildflower, spice of apple, and fern dust. The ale, while very potent, began to develop more of a focus on flavor and aftertaste. This also was the case with halfling bread and cider.\nIt is important to note that there were still some halflings living in cities at this point (~Year 800). Most halflings were born of halfling/halfling, but some were still born of a human/dwarf couple. These halflings enjoyed a much easier life than their\nancestors.\nAround this time in history, the number of halflings had indeed grown to a point where surnames were required to identify with, as previously, only single names were used. Names, both first and last, were usually one or two syllables.\nNotable surnames and houses that began at this time were the houses of Took and Brandybuck, founded by Tulkan and Grombadook, respectively. The Tooks had the traits of what might be called the quintessential halfling- friendly, yet shy, of average height\nand demeanor. The Brandybucks, however, were a tad more adventurous, with darker hair than most halflings. Each family lived in a single burrow hill, most of them in the general vicinity of another. These family hills were the closest thing to a town as\nhad truely ever existed yet in halfling culture.\nHowever, in around Year 1010, some families started to break apart from population pressures. Families like the Brandybucks eventually spread all througout the lands.\nBy around this time, halflings had been isolated enough that, not only did this unique culture of peace and merriment develop, but the halflings actually forgot or disbelieved in the creation stories and of Aenguls, Daemons, and God. Indeed, the halflings\ndidn't really develop a totally obscure faith, but instead took on a quasi-religious outlook that revolved around the things they held dear: harvest and food, companionship, nature, and peace. No \"gods\" were ever named, nor was worship very common,\nbut there was a common belief that, if a halfling betrayed his tight-knit community, that the harvest and the tranquility of life would be lost.\nChapter 4 - The Rise and Decline of the Village Era\nYears 1200-1304\n\nAround the year 1200, a small group of halflings, from both Took, Brandybuck, Goodbody, and other families, decided to form a self-sufficient community apart from the family burrows.\nThey had decided to make it a collection of hills, hidden from society by the waters and hills surrounding it. This community eventually came to be named \"Dunwood\", and it remains the most notable halfling town to date. There are massive wheat fields and\na beautiful, clean lake. This town was always notable for being quite territorial, for as the humans began to urbanize more and more, family burrows were abandoned, and Dunwood was one of the last retreats for the country-loving halflings. As word of the\ntown's existence came to be, spread by the word of the Wandering Wizard, halflings from both cities and family hills came to try and gain a burrow here. The founders of Dunwood were initially very welcome, but soon, the onrush of want-to-be residents came\nto such a high number that it was impossible to distinguish which would be beneficial to the community. The aspect of companionship was always very emphasized, and as a later resident of the town, I can vouch for this fact. By the time I moved to Dunwood,\nit was impossible to walk through the streets of Al'Khazar without being pestered for the town's semi-secret location.\nEnvious of the town, many halflings and non-halflings alike began making similar towns in the surrounding hills, a more known one by the name of Thistledown.\nI am now qualified, at this point, to tell the history from a first-person perspective. Yes, for I arrived in Dunwood during a small population boom, when the town was thriving and more inhabitants came every day. The Elders of the town were Kip Took,\nLen, and Gimblo. I was first escorted to the town by Gimblo, who took Bell and I for a visit. And, as I mentioned earlier, we were pursued through the streets of Al'Khazar by nosy people! Gimblo turned a corner, snapped his finger, and suddenly Bell and I\nwere in Dunwood (a trick I have yet to emulate perfectly). The smell of hot bread and ale wafted from the ale garden, and I could hear a halfling singing with a lyre in the distance.  Indeed, it was truly the ideal place for a halfling. Soon, the whole\ntown took a trip to Al'Khazar to pledge allegiance to the newly-kinged Edmund.\nAfter many a year of drinking, story-telling, and visitor-shoveling, the town seemed to go into a cultural decline. The Elders grew a tad sickly, and so they appointed Owen Sturdyfoot II as the Mayor to help govern. However, even his efforts did not\nmaintain the vitality of the town, as Brian left to become an Ascended, Biodoc passed away, Rusty moved to Al'Khazar, and Lilly was kidnapped. This decline occured in other towns, too, leaving an area surrounding Dunwood filled with empty hill-homes and\nthe likes. I, too, left after a call from the Druids, though the years of countryside living would have a profound influence on me for my entire life.\nChapter 5 - Up to Modern Day\nYears 1304-Present Day (approx. 1351)\n\nAfter many years, around 1340, I decided along with a few relatives to restore the popularity and culture of Dunwood, and so we hosted DunFest, a large festival with much merriment.\nThere was drinking, dancing, singing, and the likes, of course. However, afterwards, it did not have the profound influence on the town population that I would have liked. And so, I went back to Malinor, only to try another festival later. Indeed, it\nappeared that our selective ways way long ago had a profound influence on the interest in the town, and so many gave up their hopes of moving and settled in the city. Many halflings have forgotten the joy of the simple and clean life, to my surprise.\nWhile I certainly traveled and was no typical halfling, the air off of Lake Dunwood in the early morn still stirs my soul like very little else does.\nAt the most recent DunFest, I did meet some fellows quite interested in culture, but none were halflings.\nI have tried to embrace the city-dwelling halflings with open arms, but very few have answered the call.\nWith the division of Oren, I as one of the only remaining Elders of the town decided to not immediately pledge our allegiance to either faction,\ninstead remaining independent for some time. I did, however, set up a trade caravan of goods between Dunwood and Galahar, trying to make use of our overstocked wheat.\nAt the time of writing this, the state of the world grows dim as the Undead continue to win victory after victory. The future will surely deserve another tome of halfling history, perhaps more in depth,as this was merely a general overview.\nHopefully this has been an informative and enjoyable read. \n\nPetyr Brandybuck", ""),
        StaticBook("Hallowed Umbrage", "Geoboy66", "I write the following epitaph with dire haste so much so that the winds part ways my words.\n\nMy account of these events may not be entirely accurate,§  something completely acceptable under the maddening, fear stricken haze that I have been left in.\nI sit here now quill in hand, wounded with a gash so dreadfully dark that I'm not sure if it really is a wound at all.  I have become a well of life, bountiful as the succulent navy mists ooze out of this growth, this... anchor; ever so dark and dreadful.\nMy pilgrimmage to this place hath cost me the trust and faith of my only friends as despite every loud, nagging warning against venturing here, my back was turned and my hands covered my ears.\nIt is the weakness of Man to succumb to the allure of power, riches and knowledge that of which the Abyss is said to contain. Trust me when I say that the power hidden away here is done so for a reason and should never belong to any mortal man.\nFor were the corrupting mind of Man ever to wrap their greedy fingers around such incomprehensible things, it would mean our doom.  The Trolls Harpies and Gryphons of our world pale in comparison to the horror of the deep, dark beyond.\nLegends tell of the Abyss as the ruins of Aegis, a land from which Man's forefathers hailed.\nI would hesitate to call the state in which the Gods left the motherland in a ruin, for truly there remains little left here at all.\nFor this Abyss, this endless chasm to which there seems no end is both the catastrophic ashes of a world once living and breathing as well as a prison for every lost soul that the world sunk with it. North, South, East, West - it all leads to despair.\nI hath deviated from the guiding compass to venture in a new direction; downward.\nFor I suspected that within the bowels of this crushing nightmare there must be both a ceiling and a floor.  I, a pawn controlled by adventurous urges, took a fatal dive.\nMy sense of time has long since fled, abandoning me like many other luxuries that once made me whole.  After a measurement of time far longer than any measurement of time I've ever thought to measure, I reached the feared and fabled end of this void.\nI dare not write about the countless demons that scour the ebon plane despite the insanity they so passively inflict.  They do not deserve the honour of being referenced alongside the Lord of the deep, dark below.  Darkness Incarnate.\nAs my wailing, shedding flesh forced itself through the dense acidic atmosphere, my feet began to fail me.  Time hath come to truly give up, and turn back I thought.  Yet my thoughts were ruptured by a presence so overwhelming that I could not think.\nAs I fought with myself to open my eyes I stared upon what could only be described as a living shadow, embodying umbral hellfire frigid enough to lock my very bones in place.\nRadiating in darkness so hollow that the Abyss stood brightly aflame beside him.\nHe worse armour, the first sign that this impossible creation was indeed Man.  Ancient was his armour, charred and blackened from what I cannot begin to imagine.  Yet his armour, heavy as it appeared did not hinder him.\nHis form suddenly shifted all at once, phasing out at one place and in again at another.  The realm was at his whim, as he did not simply move through it, but had become it.  Now, the Dark Lord towered above me, reeking of ash and death.\nAll past experiences seem like a petty joke when compared to the awesome perspective I had been blessed with. This Man, whose blood red eyes pierced through the very veil of the Abyss had drawn forth his weapon.  A terrible greatsword, massive in size.\nDripping with the howling souls of the damned.  This blade, serrated like the peak of Mount Ire was shoved into my heart, slotting into my flesh like a key within a door.  In the seconds before my consciousness faded I heard something.  I heard a voice.\nA voice that would rival a Dragon.  It was then that I knew for certain - This was the Old Lord of Umbrage, King of the Abyss.  One whose name does not touch the lips of the living, and whose sight is known only to the dead and the mad.\nHis perverted shriek defiled every corner of the Abyss, his siren call summoning the dark to his side.  As the black visage of the Old Lord faded from my sight, I heard his words.\n\n      R A D I A N T\n I S  T H E  B L A C K\n         S  U  N", ""),
        StaticBook("Harbingers", "Veldryn Uuthlini", "These elusive creatures were quite certainly some of the most dangerous things in Anthos, a part of the Black Scourge, the beings were of a kind to glass cannons in combat, able to rend dark rifts into mortal ground to draw out the overly corrupted,\nand zealotus servants of Setherien. Along with this, these beings had been bestowed with the ability to disguise their semi-flud forms with a special form of light illusion, and unforgettably, Setherien's Boon; -\nholding within it the ability to create freezing corruptive smog from the very air about them, and condense it into frigid black flames, most would agree that these are much more dangerous than your everyday mage.\nThey were beings seeming to be made of Black smoke, only able to interract with the mortal world through their armor and robes. The standard ways of defeating a creature did not appear to work on them,\nthought holy magic seems to affect them, attacking them with normal weapons at most seemed to send them back to the North in their smoke way.\nThe title of 'Harbinger' was also a senior rank in the Destruction Cult of the Undead. Whether there is a link between the servants of Setherien and the servants of Iblees remains to be seen.\nWith Setherien defeated all the Harbingers seem to have disapeared. If they are trully gone,or are simply hiding with their master defeated is still to be seen. Some of the former known Harbingers are stated at the next pages.\nThe leader of the Harbingers, only under rule of Setherien himself. His armor was of a firery orange.\n-Vak'Thuul\nKnown Harbingers of the first age, they carried blue armor.\n\n-Nihil\n-Shae'Tan\n-Dumamis\n-Daink\n-Mortum'Vherzix\n-Khrell’os\n-Kav'Zoras\n-Orithur\nFallen mortals to the will of Setherien, they were chosen to be granted the power of their master. They carried red armor.\n-Orakana\n-Eudihr\n-Absolution\n-Xort\n-Oblitus\n-Skelvyas\n-Kaernk", ""),
        StaticBook("Harian Beast II", "Glacio", "The Harian Beast\nVolume II\n\nSince the beast was last removed from Haria, it has relocated its home, seeming to be unkillable by even the most powerful of Haria and a collosal stone giant. Now nesting by the capital of the Wood Elves, the Harian Beast\nis the source of nightmares for a whole new populace. A man named Roland and myself were led there by a group of three, a blond elf, a redhead human, and an armored Kharajyr. The three forced us into the hellish ring of fire, towards the blue and white\nfamiliar wisp, none of them aside from myself knowing what it was. Swords to our backs, we were forced to stay as the Harian Beast took its form once more, the icy looking flames raising and coalescing about the wisp as it had done in the forests near\nHaria not all that long ago. The others were bewildered, having never seen such a being before with their own eyes, possibly being the reason I survived. As the brutish captors were staring at the beast in awe, I began to make a break for the safehaven\njust outside of the fiery ring's circumference. The redheaded man charged after me, his weapon drawn as his two allies turned to flee the area as well, only to be met by Roland's crossbow delivering a bolt to his left knee from behind.\nI did not turn, but it was all too obvious as the plume of searing flames scorched the air behind me, and his screams and yelps of pain were cut off rather shortly by his gruesome death. Roland proceeded to pursue the two assailants, and I accompanied\nhim and got ahead of the group using voidal shifting, my sword drawn. The Beast turned about face towards the lot of us, the familiar sight of it preparing to strike worrying me most of all, as the men sent their arms forth at Roland, clashing blade\nagainst blade, destroying his crossbow in the process. I swiftly met one of the assailants with a strike to the hip, before resuming my escape as the being's unholy fire blasted down to the earth once more, killing the other wounded kidnapper. The beast\nseemed to have gotten stronger and more durable in its time outside of the lands of Haria, rendering it nigh unkillable to those surviving present, even if it were not the case where one were to cease assaulting Roland. Finally, with none remaining in the\ncircle, and Roland's brawl shifting out past the area with his foe, the beast subsided, as opposed to the time in Haria where even staying within its sight for long enough rendered the beast to continue its slaughter. I deduce that due to its previous\ndefeat, the Harian Beast's strength is proportional to how close it is to its source, the glowing wisp, where the further it gets, the less durable and steady it is. This would explain its reluctance to continue its chase beyond its realm\nas it had before, while allowing it to still achieve its horrendous goal of murdering and scorching all that entered the fiery ring of death. Ultimately, my hypothesis due to the events leading up to now is that the beast can be defeated with large\namounts of physical force, and each time it has to reform elsewhere, the weaker and weaker it gets, rendering the Beast's days numbered.", ""),
        StaticBook("Harvesters", "Falyen Darylus", "Analysis of the Harvester Construct\nThe constructs used in the attack on Rivel appear to be based off of the golem servants favoured by the Forgotten Dwarves and now being rediscovered by the Aegean dwarves.\nHowever, they are clearly different: they possess a killer instinct unheard of in servant golems, lack individual intelligence and possess an apparatus built into the hand capable of killing a mortal being and trapping their soul, no doubt for\ncontainment in the Soul Capacitors of The Seal. Countless Harvester Constructs were destroyed in their assault on Rivel, indicating a lack of quality in their construction: it seems the dwarves built them in a time of desperation.\nHowever, such a time now befalls us: the majority of Rivel’s Lesser Caste were killed by Harvester Constructs in the assault, and I fear this propaganda we are distributing to the Lesser Caste attributing this assault to deceptive attacks by the\nForgotten Dwarves will not placate them. We may downplay their intelligence, but even they must realise the Forgotten Dwarves have been extinct for over a millenium.\n- Senior Researcher Falyen Darylus", ""),
        StaticBook("Hawks Need You", "Regale Ba'ikana", "Attempt to recruit one person into the warhawkes and bring them to Rei or Ray for a trial.", ""),
        StaticBook("Headgehogs", "Andria Barbu", "Headgehogs\nA poem by\nAdria Barbu\n*******************\nHeadgehogs are great\nHeadgehogs are neat\nThey are cute when they want sometihng to eat.\nHeadgehogs a fun\nHeadgehogs are small\nHeadgehogs come when you give them a call.\nHeadgehogs are the best\nHeadgehogs are better tha all the rest\nHeagehogs look cute hiding in a chest.", ""),
        StaticBook("Healing", "The March Ash", "I have entered this new place called the Far Glade for the first time. It is said to be a strange place, abandoned by everything but time and nature.\nIt will heal me, the High Druids have said. I do not know if I want to be healed. Still, I will see what I can learn here, and then return as swiftly as I can.", ""),
        StaticBook("Healing Paste", "Anthron", "Druidic Healing Paste\n-------------------Bonemeal\nMandragora\nFaerie Truffles\nGislocinovi\nGrobsnopper\nTippen's Root\nBlissfoil\nUse as little of the Mandragora, Faerie Truffles, and Gislocinovi as possible due to the side effect\nthat each herb has.\n-------------------", ""),
        StaticBook("Heirarchy", "Nemir", "[!] The book you've picked up has got a thick, hard cover.  It looks slightly worn, but well managed.[!]\n[!]The pages within have got a hint of yellow to them, showing their age.  Each page seems to be littered with old, faded stains. Upon reading the ink writing, you occasionally get a whiff of worn book's musty scent.[!]\n[!]The entries of this journal have delicately been written with ink and a quil.[!]\n\nHierarchies.  They're just about everywhere, be it large or small.  Important or not, life follows it.  Some may believe it creates order, others\ncould think that it's a strict and unfair chain of power.  But if you think about it, life is unfair.  We grow up knowing this.  The strongest rise to the top in this chain of the living.  Heirarchies, in a way, are created by animals.\nWolves make a lovely example, just perfect.  Each pack has got an alpha and each pack has an omega.  Each pack is lead by the most dominate one of them all, just as it is for everyone else.  A heirarchy is a part of life, and in life, the strongest live.\nIt's that simple, not really worth going more in depth.  It's a waste of time, paper, and ink.", ""),
        StaticBook("Her Moonlit Eyes", "Kili Al-Deen", "In moon Lit Gaze I saw Her Eyes,in which made my heart fill with crys, if i would fall for you it would be my demise!\nbut can I live my life with out your eyes?\nin the nights i Lie adrift in thoughts of your silky hair,and in the days i have the\nstrangth to kill a bear! and when I see you my heart races like a hare. Yet I wish you can see me amongst the croud,I shall say hi,I shall not now,days go by i see her smile, if i say hi its like a mile! oh such agony if a day goes by it will feel like\napart of me will die.\nAlas Alas it canot be more i will do it tonight!\nwhere i saw her and her eyes i will walk that mile and spare the bear for this night! the moon lit glaze fills her eyes by the tree she stands on that night i make my walk up\nslowly feeling more and more alive,what will i say what will i do for years now and i have not thought it thruo. i stand with her face to face struck by her dazziling eyes and beautiful silky hair until she made a warm smile like none ive ever seen on her\nface,and to my amaze,\nher cheeks looked ablazed.she came closer,i didnt know what do to.then i told her\"I Love You.\"with a second of silence she smiles and turns around.I walk back home in the moon light with my head down until i hear a sound\nso I turn around as i hear a gentil voice say \"I Love you too.\"\n\n\n        By:Kili Al-Deen\n       (ibraheemc2000)\n-------------------\nI made this because I was bord,i hope you injoy it and one day say it to your love i also planed this\nto be a poem but toward the end of it i couldnt find ways i could make it rhyme Hehe.\n___________________", ""),
        StaticBook("Her Story Vol. 1", "Nemir", "Chronicles of\n           Nemir\n-------------------\n\n        The Orcish\n          Deserts\nWay back in my youth, I had spent a year of my life living within the golden deserts of the orcs.  I was around the age of fifteen and had just fled from the high walls of the Silver City of Haelun'or.  I didn't agree with their ways of purity and was\nstill sepparated from my Father at the time, so had no connection with anyone from the city.\n\nI had met an impure high elf named Kelian Dawnstrider who offered me to go to the deserts and became his apprentice in smithing after I\nhad told him of my troubles with the Silver City.\n\nIt may seemed foolish of me accept his offer so quickly, but I felt as if I had no where else to go and no way to support myself.  I was lucky that his words were true, and my new home became\na shabby wooden shack in the back of the Raguk's camp on the edge of the Orcish Desert.  There is where my journey began.\nThe work was harder than how I anticipated it to be, and the scorching sun was of no help with the heat of the forge.  All of the orcs seemed to respect Kelian, he was apparently a friend of the clan's leader.  I wish I could remember his name, but time\nhas blurred it from my memory.\n\nNot all of the orcs seemed pleased with my arrival to the clan, but most of them were welcoming.  It had taken me a few months to get used to their tongue, and I eventually didn't need Kelian or one of the\nslaves to help me with translating.  My clothes had also becomed stained with sweat and dirtied with dust, my hair was a little more tangled, and I noticed how tan I was becoming due to almost constant exposure to the sun's rays.  I truly looked out of\nplace when I visited some of the major cities, or maybe I just began to look like an average peasant; however, there were the occasional few who questioned why a young high elven girl was running about in dirty and tattered clothing.\nTo be truthful, I looked more like a sun elf than a high elf, but just shorter and thinner.\n\nKelian had been teaching me how to make chainmail armor since I was too scrawny to use the hammer or other heavy equipment.  Over time, I was getting\nbetter with my work and began to feel more at home and at peace.\n\nAfter spending a few months with the Raguks, I was woken one night by Kelian saying that we needed to pack our things quickly and leave.  I was in a stupor and took a moment before\nasking what was going on.  He said that the clan leader had lost a honor klomp [klomp = fight in Blah] and thus lost his position.  His opponent turned out to be one of the orcs who disliked Kelian and I's presence in the camp and was rumored to be a\ntyrant leader by a few other orcs who were leaving with us.\n\nWe left under the cover of night, unnoticed, as we trekked out into the wastes, our footsteps being drunken by the drifting sands.  All night we walked, lugging all that we had taken from t\ncamp.  It wasn't until dawn that we came across a gargantuan rock that loomed over the sands and a cacti forest.  We had discovered our destination: The Lur Clan.\n\nThey accepted us, all of us, agreeing with our opinions of the new Raguk leader.\nKelian and I were out of work since the orcs in the Lur clan already had a smith, but we were still allowed a tent to sleep in.  We didn't plan to rest there for long and began seeking out new work.\nLuck was with us and we met a human family named the Malinovs.  They were lovely people, and over time of me knowing them, I felt as if I was a part of them.\n\nKelian and I moved out of the deserts and into dwarven lands.  A human who owned a manor\nallowed us to live in a smaller building by his home, the Malinovs included, and together we planned to  create The Blackwood Company.\n\nMy time with the orcs ended there, and I began my next beautiful journey with the dwed.", ""),
        StaticBook("Herb Symbols", "Llywellyn Oakleaf", "*&*\n      Fire symbols\n\n-Strong\nBlistering toad\nDrakes tail\n\n-Moderate-\nFlame tongue root\nDwarfs pumpkin\nSinged kha\nElrow Berries\nBlood Lotus\n-Normal-\nBlazing fern\nFire flower\nNight sap\n\n-Weak-\nDessert Berry bush (Berries)\n\nOrc's Braid\n*&*\n    Earth Symbols\n\n-Moderate-\nAlabaster leaf\nFairie truffle\nTippens root \nSaffvil\nDrilltongue\nDesert berry bush (stem)\nBronze dust\n-Weak-\nGoblin's Ivy \nMiner's helmet\n*&*\n     Water Symbols\n\n-Strong-\nAqua Nymph\nAthin\nSpirit of Magnolis\n\n-Moderate-\nSerpents stalk\nMandragora\nFrost vine\nZawabate\nJoker's Scum\n*&*\n       Air symbols\n\n-Strong-\nCrouching Feather\nElf's Hair vine \nWisp's Breath\n\n-Moderate-\nSwamp blossom\n\n-Weak-\nJailer's Moss\n*&*\n         Unknown\n\n-King's Ivy\n-Shade leaf\n-Biteit\n-Atheros (Possible Water symbol)\n-Gijaklul\n-Javens", ""),
        StaticBook("Herbalism vol.01", "Elder Elf", "~*~*~A GUIDE~*~*~*\n~*~*~*~TO~*~*~*~*\n~*~*HERBALISM*~*~\n~*~*~*vol. 01*~*~*~\n~*~ALOE   PLANTS~*~\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*\n~*~*~*~*A*~*~*~*~*\n~*~*~DRUIDIC~*~*~*\n~*~*~*ORDER*~*~*~\n~*~*~*TOME*~*~*~*~\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*\n.-. .-.\n         (_ | _)\n          (_|_)\n             |\n             |\n             \\\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~#########################Written By####\n##The Druid of Song#\n###########################♫#################♫♫♫#########\n✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿FOR BELERAN✿✿\n✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿✿\n♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪The aloe plant is an age old plant that is famous for its healing abilities.  It can be prepared a number of ways.  This tome will explain those ways.\nAloe can be ingested,\napplied to the skin, or ground and combined\n♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪with other herbs to create an even more potent healing salve.\n♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪\n♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪\n1: INGESTION\nIt is very potent to\ndirectly ingest, so cut out the flesh and brew it into a tea.  It can be used to treat...\n✿Constipation\n✿Hard of breathing\n✿Colds\n✿Partial blindness\n♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ ♪\n♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ ♪ 2:DIRECT APPLICATION\nThe cut plant can be applied directly to the skin for...\n✿Sunburn\n✿Frostbite\n✿Open Wounds\n✿Burns\n✿Sores\n✿...and flaky skin!\n♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪\n♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪3: Combination\nThe plant can be combined with other herbs.\n\n✿Goldenrod\n✿Blissfoil\n✿Cactus Green\n✿Kolagotu\n✿And many more!\n♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪\n♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪♪Please be sure to read our other volumes for more information on creating salves and poltices.\n♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣THANK♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣YOU♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣FOR♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣SUPPORTING♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣♣THE DRUIDS♣♣♣♣♣♣", ""),
        StaticBook("Herbert & Stacy", "Braelynn Copper", "Once upon a time..\nin the land of oren.\nthere was a lost little sheep who went by Herbert. Herbert was a friendly little sheep, and all he ever wanted was to have some friends to play with, and thats how he got lost.\nOne day Herbert was in the pasture with all the other sheep, but the other sheep were playing together, all of them except Herbert.\nHerbert was sad that he got left out, so he decided to wander off and try to find a friend. He searched cloud temple,\nno one wanted to be his friend. He searched around the high elf lands, and yet no friends to be found. Next was oren, he still haven't found any friends, but he did find himself lost. He was in such a worry he forgot his task of finding a friend and\nstarted asking people to help him get home. After hours of asking and being declined he lost hope. That was all until he heard a little voice calling his name.\n\"Who's there?\" Herbert asked. \"It's me! Down Here!\" called the little voice. Herbert\nimmediately looked down to find a little grass hopper below him. \"Who are you?\" Herbert asked. \"Well I'm stacy! I heard you were lost? How'd that happen, fella?\" She said \"Well, I was looking for a friend and I got lost\" Explained Herbert. \"Aww poor guy\"\nsaid Stacy. \"Will you help me get home?\" asked Herbert. \"I'm not just going to help you get home, I want to be your friend too!\"\nExclaimed Stacy.\n\"Really? You want to be my friend? Oh joy oh joy!\" Rejoiced Herbert. \"What are we waiting for? Lets go home!\"\nSaid Stacy. They made their travels back to Herbert's homeland that will soon become Stacy's home too. Stacy and Herbert were the best of friends and lived happily ever after.\n\n\n\n       The End", ""),
        StaticBook("Herbs 1", "Leyun Kameki", "A Druid's Book of Herbs\nVolume 1\n\nHerbs from Solstice Druid Callax\n\nScribed with additions by Apple Druid Leyun Kameki\nLeyun's Forward\nWhen I learned to use the gifts of nature to heal, Callax gave me his list of herbs. It is time to write this information down in a form that can be widely shared. Hopefully it'll be of use to anyone who heals using herbs.\nAthin\nAn herb with a blue visage. It grows at the bottom of almost frozen lakes.\nEffects: Athin works as a cooling balm, making an excellent lotion. It also can cause blue hued skin.\nOverdose: Mild Frostbite\nAlchemical Properties:\nAthin is a strong water symbol, good for use in colder potions.\nNotes: Generally requires at least two people to harvest due to freezing conditions.\nAlabaster Leaf\nAn herb of Alabaster hue. It grows in drier areas in forests, typcally near fallen trees.\nEffects: As a mild poison, Alabaster Leaf causes dizziness and nausea.\nOverdose: Extreme fatigue.\nAlchemical Properties: Alabaster Leaf is a moderate earth symbol.\nNotes: Often used as a dye/paint. Harvest by carefully cutting the leaves.\nAqua Nymph\nA small chain of fragile blue baubbles that grow underwater. It is often mistaken for frog or toad spawn.\nEffects: Severe hallucinations when ingested as an herb. Powerful burn remedy when boiled. Causes the throat to close up when\ningested in oil form.\nOverdose: Stronger Effects\nAlchemical Properties: Aqua Nymph is a strong water symbol.\nNotes: Aqua Nymph is extremely delicate and must not be touched by hands. A correct way to harvest the herb is to take the thin layer\nof sediment that it grows in and the whole plant, scooping it into a jar so that it doesn't touch the edges and it's roots remain intact. If done any other way, it will likely ruin the plant.\n\nThe plant can be made into a powerful burn remedy by pouring\nthe whole plant into into a cauldron and small pot. When boiled, the plant's buds will release a liquid that will make a thick oil that can be easily spread over burns.\nBeard Weed\nA shaggy green moss that grows hanging from rare trees in caves. A rare herb, but grows in plentiful groups.\nEffects: With water and blissfoil, it can aid in the healing of internal organ damage and ease pain. Beard weed famously\ncauses significant hair growth. Can be poisonous if not prepared properly.\nWhen toxic, it can cause bloating, nausea, diarrhea, internal bleeding, and even death.\nOverdose: Stiffness. Possible hairgrowth across the entire body, creating a\nbeast-like appearance. Alchemical Properties:\nBeard Weed is a moderate earth symbol. It works well in hair tonics.\nBlissfoil\nAn oily blue flower that grows in clumps under birch trees.\nEffects: Numbness where the oil is applied. It has been known to cause headaches.\nOverdose: Permanent loss of touch in the affected area.\nNotes: Oils are found near the petals and stalk.\nBread Mold\nA blue or green mold that grows on bread, cheese, and other food items.\nEffects: This particular mold only affects some individuals negatively. In these individuals, exposure can cause a rash or the throat to close up. The mold\nhas disease fighting properties that can be brought out by a skilled druid.\nOverdose: Too much can caue confusion, odd behavior, a severe rash, reduced urination, or seizures.\nNotes: A druid is required to bring out the disease fighting\nproperties, and care must be taken to reduce the effect of other types of mold growing with it.\nBlood Lotus\nA rust colored herb, found growing near entrances to caves in hot climates.\nEffects: Extremely nutritious, but extended use can turn the skin orange.\nOverdose: Kidney stones.\nAlchemical Properties: Moderate Fire Symbol\nNotes: Can be made into a strong, deep red alcohol.\nCrimson Vase\nA vase shaped plant with deep red petals that is commonly found in places with a mild amount of light. The herb grows on trees parasitically.\nEffects: Slight burning sensation if it's liquid is spilt. It'll cause rashes.\nOverdose: Will burn even more.\nAlchemical Properties: Crimson Vase is a strong fire symbol, typically used in love, rage, and envy potions, as well as Alchemist Fire.\nNotes: The petals are warm to the touch.\nCrouching Feather\nAn herb with three white, drooping petals. It only blooms at night under large bushes.\nEffects: Calming and clears the mind. Can cause light-headedness. With proper druidic preparation, it can be used as a sedative.\nOverdose: Coma\nAlchemical Properties: Strong air symbol. It is typically used in clarity potions.\nNotes: Crouching Feather is highly fragile. Wind can damage the plant.\nDiddyfunkle\nA bright, purple flowered herb that tends to grow in jungles and plains.\nEffects: The purple stems cause extremely itchy rashes. The center ball's jucies can be used as a sedative or to clear the mind. Can cause unconciousness\nor death if not prepared correctly.\nOverdose: Death\nNotes: Tiny amounts can be a delicacy.\nDraugr Tongue\nAn aloe like, orange flowered plant that grows in grassy plains.\nEffects: The liquid in the plant makes for a good disinfectant, but stings.\nNotes: The stem is not useful.\nDwarf's Pumpkin\nA stinky, orange leafed shrub that grows by water, usually in swamps.\nEffects: Burning taste similar to ginger.\nOverdose: Burns!\nAlchemical Properties: Strong fire symbol, commonly used in Alchemist Fire.\nNotes: Easy to pick. Smells bad. It's named for it's use in dwarven brews. The brightest leaves are the most potent.\nElf's Hair Vine\nAn white blossomed herb with an icy white visage. It grows on high cliffs in frozen lands.\nEffects: It has a calming effect and can result in more fluid movements, but may cause someone to move too fast, in which case physical\nexhaustion could be an issue.\nOverdose: Rapid heart beat, burst blood vessels ad the like.\nAlchemical Properties: Strong air symbol. It's used in grace and speed potions.\nNotes: The vine is extremely fragile, and the petals contain nectar.\nFlame Tongue Root\nA bright rust colored root with a rose-like flower. It can be found in heavily forested areas, burnt out forests, and areas with a lot of sun and water.\nEffects: The root can be used as a coagulant, though it can burn.\nBe warned that the spores can cause sensitivity to touch.\nOverdose: Too much blood cloting, strokes, etc.\nAlchemical Properties: Moderate fire symbol\nNotes: Fairly hot to the touch. Watch out for those spores.\nFrost Vine\nA small, brittle blue vine that grows in frosty areas, usually on trees.\nEffects: Soothes pain and and numbs/relaxes muscles where applied. Full numbness of limbs can occur on prolonged exposure.\nOverdose: Frostbite\nAlchemical Properties: Moderate water symbol.\nGoblin's Ivy\nA short brown or green vine that can be found clinging to buildings and rocks.\nEffects: Scentless, mild, nausea inducing poison that can also cause mild dehydration.\nOverdose: More nausea, vomiting, and diarrhea.\nAlchemical Properties: Weak to moderate earth symbol commonly used in resilience potions.\nNotes: Goblin's Ivy can survive in nearly moistureless areas.\nGrobsnopper\nA pink or yellow buld-like flower that grows on trees, typically found in moist forests.\nEffects: Potent healing effects. \"Soaks up\" disease.\nOverdose: Stomach aches.\nHabgobsnit\nA tall, pale-shaded grass that grows in forests and plains.\nEffects: Juices good for numbing. It can provide a sense of clarity... or just get you high.\nOverdose: Paralysis\nKing's Ivy\nAn ivy with golden flowers and a dark green stalk that grows on rocks, tree trunks, and old ruins.\nEffects: Can be taken as a stimulent, but can cause agitation.\nOverdose: Heart attacks, and in general too much energy.", ""),
        StaticBook("Herbs 2", "Pine Druid Gi'Garun", "A Druid's Book of Herbs\nVolume 2\n\nHerbs from Solstice Druid Callax\n\nScribed with additions by Apple Druid Leyun\nMalin's Heart\nA white flower that grows in plains and forests.\nEffects: Chewing numbs the whole body for a few minutes.\nOverdose: Prolonged numbness.\nNotes: A bit harder to find than blissfoil.\nMandragora\nA parsnip shaped herb that grows in swamps and wetlands.\nEffects: Revitalization and regenerative properties make the plant valuable, but the spores it releases in season cause hallucinations.\nOverdoes: Can cause growths. The hallucinogenic spores often cause choking and can be fatal.\nAlchemical Properties:\nModerate water symbol, often used in healing potions.\nNotes: Harvest 2 weeks after maturity to avoid spores.\nNight Sap\nA golden sap that drips from deformed oak trees.\nEffects: Causes a sense of calm, safety, and happiness, along with tiredness. It usually makes for about 5 hours of sleep. After waking, though, it brings splitting headaches\nand paralysis for as much time as the sleep.\nOverdoes: Longer lasting effects.\nNotes: Highly addictive.\nSaffvil\nA sickly green grass that grows in swamps near dead things.\nEffects: Nausea and blood clotting\nOverdoes: Death\nAlchemical Properties: Moderate fire symbol\nSagedust\nPollen from the Alabaster plant.\nEffects: Increased metabolism and speed, along with heightened senses and a rapid heart rate.\nOverdose: Possible heart attack.\nNotes: Incredibly difficult to harvest.\nSerpent's Stalk\nA long, reed like emerald stalk that grows in forests near or in water.\nEffects: Cooling effect when applied with water, may cause rashes.\nOverdose: Mild hypothermia.\nAlchemical Properties: Moderate water symbol. Typically used in antidotes, calming, and healing potions.\nNotes: Poisonous to bugs.\nShade Leaf\nA short, small plant with plain leaves, yellow flowers, and silvery veins that is commonly found anywhere there is grass and shade.\nEffects: Calming, stress releaving, bloodshot eyes, increased appetite.\nOverdose: Hallucinations\nNotes: Grows in large quantities, similar to normal weeds. Makes a popping noise when exposed to rain.\nSwamp Blossom\nA purple green flower with a short, thick stem found in the branches of swamp trees.\nEffects: Nectar is like honey, and the flower is nutritious, though consuming raw can gump up the throat.\nOverdose: Smelly breath and diarrhoea.\nAlchemical Properties: Moderate air symbol, usually used in speed potions.\nTippen's Root\nPurple flowers with a dark yellow speckled root that grow near fallen trees in dense forests.\nEffects: Stops bleeding almost instantly, but stinks to the seven hells.\nOverdose: Blood clots, and the dangers of blood clots.\nAlchemical Properties:\nModerate earth symbol, commonly used in strength and healing potions.\nNotes: Really, seriously stinks. Really. Make sure you're prepared for the stink.\nYarrow\nA white to pink flowered plant that grows in grasslands and forests.\nEffects: Can reduce inflammation and blood pressure, as well as intensify the medicinal effects of other herbs.\nOverdose: Dizziness and fainting due to\nlow blood pressure.\nZawabate\nA plant with a tall stalk and yellow-green curled petals that grows in desert oasis in water.\nEffects: Out of body experiences, hallucinations, pain numbing.\nOverdose: Can destroy a person's mind.\nAlchemical Properties: Moderate water symbol, used in numbing and healing potions.\nNotes: Nectar is the medicinal part of the plant.", ""),
        StaticBook("High Elf Culture", "Gallidron Elindrow", "The Maehr'sae Hiylun'ehya for Beginners.\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~      ~~~~~~~~~~~\nKarin'ayla to you. This book is intended as a guide through the noble culture of the High Elven people. Be you a youth of the Mali'aheral or a foreign diplomat who\ndesires to familiarize yourself with our ways, or even an older elf who has lapsed in their etiquette, this book can help you.\n\nPlease read on through the various lessons in these pages. Also see the guide to elven phrases in the back.\nLesson One\n    Avoid All Impurity\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nImpurity can exsist in two ways, Physical and mental. Both are to be treated with paramount seriousness, as they threaten the delicate balance of our civilized society.\nPhysical impurity is found when an individual is only partly High Elf, thus they are not \"pure\" in their lineage. Through out our long lives and our history we have seen, time and agian, that relations between a High Elf and others not of our kin end in\nmisery and failure. The impure products of these thoughtless and perverse relations are prone to lives of dissapointment and loneliness, as they do not truely belong anywhere. To any of the Mali'aheral, the formation of a \"romantic\" relationship with any\noutside of our people is forbidden, and will only serve to make yourself physically impure as well. The creation of children from such a bond is viewed with equal displeasure. This may sound harsh to those who are not of our people, but it is not. it is\nsimply the truth that wisdom and experience have taught us.\n\nWays to determine if one is of impure lineage include but are not limited to the following. Eyes of any color save blues, greens or purples. Ears that are rounded and short. Also a smallnes\nstature can indicate impurity. Hair amoung the Mali'aheral is normally fair, though it is not unheard of to have a brunette born amoung us. Dark hair, however, will certainly raise flags of warning to any who do not know the elf in question.\nMental impurity is a bit more difficult to detect as it can be hidden by the devious or the liar.\nIn truth, any who do not follow the Maehr'sae Hiylun'ehya are considered mentally impure to some degree or another. Small degrees of impurity can be treat\nand corrected. Large ones however can, have and will result in banishment and even death. Physical Impurity usually will end with the individual being \"cleansed\" by being tossed into an acid bath. Thus removing their taint from our society.\nLesson Two\nProper Conduct in the\n            City\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nHigh Elves place etiquette on a high pedistal. We enjoy conversation, and we enjoy debate, but we insist it is done right. Emotion should not cloud one's judgment\nor reasoning, neither should it color one's argument. Logic and reason should rule the mind as it rules in the city of Haelun'or.\n\nFor those of you who are not of the people, you should consider before speaking to a High Elf, or trying to enter the c\nthat there are a few key differences between you and us.\n\nWe are old, very old. Many of us have lived long enough to have met your great, great grand parents when they were children. As such our perspective is different than yours. High Elves are\nseen as cold or harsh in their demeanor or critisisms. In answer to this I invite you to consider these things. How would you feel if you saw an endless parade of children making the same mistakes, time and again, even though you yourself have warned them\nof the pitfalls of their poor behavoir many times over the past centuries? We grow frustrated when we see the same problems and mistakes being repeated and not fixed as logic would dictate that they must. You must also consider that a High Elf reckons\nthings in a longer time frame than you likely do. There for, one should not take our comments or critisisms personally, for they are intended to help you and your children and your children's children to be better. After all, why should one be upset by\nthe truth?\n\nWhen attempting to enter the city, if one is not of the Mali'aheral, one should not think to do so lightly or easily. Our city is precious to us, and we do not seek to sunder its purity by letting any and all who knock to enter.\nIf one seeks to enter they should do so with the right frame of mind. With patience and with humility one will go further. Also it is customary to bring a gift, that they may offer something in return for the honor of entering the gates.\nFor those of you who are of the people. I suggest looking the part. Dress appropriately for your lineage as a High Elf. Keep your hair seemly, and preferably un-dyed. Our flesh should be free of tattoos or piercings as these things only mar our natural\nbeauty. Makeup or accesories that accent our features may be worn however.\nLesson Three\n       Be Educated\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~Whether you attend the Eternal College or you take it upon yourself to read and learn, all good High Elves smile upon the persuit of knowledge. Learn of art, science or even the arcane lore of\nmagic, but be knowledgable of something. One should spend their whole life aquiring new learning that they may be useful.\n\nOh be wise, what more can I say?\nLesson Four\n        Courtship\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~The art of courtship is something that all young Mali'aheral should know. For one day, you may wish to impress someone of the opposite gender and unite with them in marriage. Follow this guide and\nwill hopefully avoid becoming a social pariah.\n\nDo NOT engage in sappy, lovey dovey actions or grandiose acclamations of your love. This will not end well and is unseemly for one of our people. Rather, create works of art or music or literature that\nyou can devote to the object of your adoration. Doing so will not only let that person know that someone is interested in them, but will show that you are capable in these areas. These things should, however, be done anonymously, so as not to put any\nundue social strain on you or them. When this courtship has gone on for a while and you feel reasonably sure that they will respond in kind to your affections, then you may reveal your identity to them as their admirer. If you do not feel that things will\ngo well, or you lose interest, you may simply stop courting the individual and no one should be any the wiser who it was.\n\nAlas, these things do indeed happen.\nLesson Five\n         Marriage\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~Once your courtship has gone its course and you and your beloved are together, it is expected that you will be married.\nHigh Elven marriages are usually held in large public venues or centers\nknowledge such as a library. We do not have churches and therefore do not hold weddings in them.\n\nThe ceremony is attended by all the pure citizenry, as well as invited outsiders. An individual is given the honor to speak at the wedding and officiate\nceremony. After they speak, a moment of silence is given for any to speak out against the union, should they choose. This is almost never done, as to speak out publically against the couple is considered rude in the extreme.\nThe two are then wed and ma\nrecieve gifts, congradualtions, etcetera.\n\nIt is within the bonds of matrimony and ONLY within these bonds that the creation of High Elven children may take place. Assuming you are fertile, to have a child is an honor and a joy to be planned and\ntaken with all seriousness.\nLesson Six\n         Religion\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~This will be a rather short section. The High Elves practice no religion. We would rather devote our time to logical and, for lack of a better term, provable persuits than to sit in a church and\npray to a God that we can neither see nor hear. Rather than try to guess at the whims of deity, We will continue to unravel the mysteries of the world as we can prove it exsists.\n\nFor my High Elven readers, you would do well to devote yourself to the\npractice of our culture, rather than some faith from a distant land.\nLesson Seven\n    To Offer Insult\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~The highest insult one can offer is to call another impure. This however has some stipulations. For example, if one of the leaders of the people, We'll say the El'sohaer were to call another elf\nthis offense could be taken with much gravity. However, if a half elf were to refer to a High elf as impure, the insult has no barb, as the half elf is impure to begin with. One way to offer such an insult is to give a High Elf gold. This should almost\nnever be done, as one High Elf to another, as the action can indicate that the reciever cares more for gold than they do for their people. Of course were a human to give an elf a bar of gold, it would have no such meaning, as a human could not be expected\nto know this. Gold jewlery or items can be given between High Elves, so long as the intent is clear. Unless you really do want to insult them.\nConclusion\n```````````````````'''''''''''''''''''   ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nI hope that you have enjoyed this book, but more so I hope that you are better prepared to navigate the pitfalls of High Elven etiquette. We are a strict people, but we are\ndelightsome when you know how to behave.\n\nPlease look for my next book\n\n\"An Encyclopedic Arcanum\"\na guide to magic\n\n~Gallidron Elindrow~\n\nPublication year 1514\nA Guide to\n      Elvish Phrases\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~````````````````````''''''''''''''''''Karin'ayla- Good day\nKer'ayla- Good night\nVan'ayla- Farewell\nMali- Elf\nBortu- Dwarf\nUruk- Ork\nValah- Human\nTali'bortu- Halfli\nMali'aheral-High Elf\nAcalin- Shop\nAiler- Wizard\nIler- Dark wizard\n\nHopefully these few phrases and words will be of use to any who learn them.", ""),
        StaticBook("High Elves.", "Garsto Leaf", "Those of the High Elf bloodline can usually be pointed out for their very long ears, platinum hair, and the golden tint to their fair skin. This tint is complemented by their hair, which is usually \nblonde, though silver and light brown hair is not\nunheard of. Their eyes range from hues of green to blue, occasionally even purple. It is also not uncommon for an High Elve's eye color to become darker as they age, revealing the accumulation of wisdom. They are the tallest of elves, and are usually\nquite thin, making them the sub-race worst suited for physical combat.\n\nDespite this they often excel at the use of arcane magic. They often have a strict code which governs their lives, and have a distinct hate for impurity and half-breeds.", ""),
        StaticBook("His Fungi", "Motsham Malog'Yar", "((This book was written by an orc, but since most of the Blah is mispronounced common, I only wrote the words that are actually different for orcs in the Blah. The words shared between the two languages are written in Common. Sorry for the clunky OOC\npreface, but I just wanted to give the reader a heads-up.))    Many of those who gruk mi, gruk that mi have long been a devout worshiper of Orgon. Those who have visited the shrine of Orgon atop the plateau in San'Vitar, may have noticed the fungus which\npopulates the mound on which the shrine is erected. Very few people gruk the nature agh significance of the fungus, agh would ignorantly dismiss it as nub-thing more than a bunch of ugly mushrooms. These mushrooms, however, are actually a\nsupernatural phenomenon. The fungus which grows upon Orgon's mound is not of the natural world. It is a physical manifestation of Orgon's will agh influence spreading in the mortal plane. This is why lat will nub ever find any growing on their own in a\nnormal environment. Very few also gruk that the fungus is, in fact, carnivorous, but feeds almost exclusively during the feeding rituals of Orgon worship. Now, when mi blah the word \"carnivorous\", mi mean it very strongly. During the feeding ritual, the\nfungus almost instantly takes root in the flesh of the sacrifice, and begins literally consuming its prey. The process causes the victim to be rapidly digested alive within a matter of minutes. The fungus devours every last piece of its prey, leaving\nbehind neither flesh, blood, bones or organs. This is how Orgon has revealed to his followers that his sacrifices must be offered. Outside of the feeding ritual, the fungus feeds very rarely, occassionally digesting any insects that find themselves\ntrapped in the liquid secretions of the mushrooms. Now, onto the specifics. There are dub varieties of mushrooms which grow upon Orgon's sacrificial mounds: Orgon's bile and Orgon's gall. Both of these mushrooms have some similar qualities. Namely,\nneither should be taken without asking permission of Orgon and rulging him for his generosity; agh they should both be handled with care. \n Orgon's bile: These short, squat mushrooms are a bluish-purple color with white spots. On each spot grow many\ntiny black spores. The spores are easily broken, agh contain a foul-smelling black substance. It smells very much like decomposing flesh, and tastes like rotten eggs. Contact stains the skin. A slight taste of the mushroom or the oily, black substance\ncauses nausea (agh mi mean a VERY slight taste). Mi tested the effects of full consumption of the mushroom on a willing burz-albai named Mithras. Upon immediately eating the whole thing, he was beset by extreme nausea and vomiting, a cold sweat and\nsevere shaking. This was from only ash mushroom. Mi would strongly advise against eating more than ash or a particularly large specimen, as such could very possibly result in flattening. ((Note: these are the red mushrooms growing near Orgon's\nshrine))\n Orgon's gall: These somewhat taller mushrooms are related to Orgon's bile, agh are brown in color. The cap of the Orgon's gall mushroom is bowl shaped, agh constantly secretes a very bitter yellowish-brown fluid. This fluid pools in\nthe aforementioned bowl-shaped cap, and emits musty fumes which irritate the eyes upon exposure. Physical contact with the mushroom causes a slight burning sensation in the skin, as the fungus coats itself in its own digestive fluids. In small amounts,\nthe digestive fluids seem harmless, however mi have witnessed in mi own worship of Orgon how quickly these fungi digest their prey in large enough groups; agh mi gruk it safe to assume that a single mushroom could eventually cause significant damage\ngiven enough time. Mi tested the effects of Orgon's gall on a shara named Hagan, who exhibited an extremely dry mouth, blurred vision and hallucinations. As with Orgon's bile, mi would strongly recommend against eating dub or more of these mushrooms, as\noverconsumption could have dangerous effects, including flattening. Mi would also theorise that such could possibly lead to lasting impacts on mental health. \n Further discoveries concerning Orgon's bile or Orgon's gall will be recorded agh published i\nfuture books if needed.\n -Malog'Yar, witch doctor agh loyal servant of Orgon.", ""),
        StaticBook("Historiography", "Dauth Sundavar", "A Historical Evaluation of Mage Baruk'Ghaz's \"Ancient History\" Tomes \n\n\n  By Dauth Sundavar\nA critical exegesis into the narrative conventions of Mage Baruk'Ghaz's \"Ancient History\" tomes, and the Holy Scrolls; the fundamental sacred texts of Canonism, facilitate for the development of the understanding that the aformentioned historical source\nis a blatant tool for religious propaganda. This is evident through the repetition of phrases within the two two respective texts, and a comparative analysis of the two given texts alongside \"Navitas\", by one Silius Hightower, reinforces the notion that\nthe \"Ancient History\" tomes are nothing but instruments into the establishment of the strict regimen and widespread institutionalisation of Canonism within all racial factions.\n\n\"There were no planes of existence. There was nothing. Just the Void. And\na bright shining light.\" Any faithful adherent to the tenets of Canonism would immediately recognise this passage to be the opening to the Holy Scrolls. Similarly, any well-read historian would know that this is the opening passage to Mage Baruk-Ghaz's\n\"Ancient History\" tomes. Furthermore, in my studies, I have come to find this passage imbued within a great multitude of philosophical texts, \"Navitas\" being one that particularly demanded my attention.\n\nThis evident plagarism that has been noted makes me\nquestion the legitimacy and the historicity of the Mage's text. Through rigorous study and perserverance, I have come to acknowledge that both \"Ancient History\" and the Holy Scrolls are mere reflections of each other. Later phrases such as \"He [Iblees]\ngrew large wings and began to breathe terrible fire... Only Malin, Urguan, Horen, and Krug stood in front of the terror\" have been noted in both texts.\n\nNow one could argue that the Holy Scrolls recall the histories that are outlined in the Mage's text.\nI would argue in return that they are blinded by their faith, and plea that they turn their attention to the evident plagarism that has seeped into the very fabric of history.\n\nNote how I mentioned that \"Navitas\", written by Silius Hightower, too copied\nmany phrases found within the Holy Scrolls. Upon further investigation, I began to realise many phrases have been copied, with either tenses or small words being changed to create an illusion of originality. \n\nFrom what I have gathered, Silius at the\ntime of publication was a child. Now I call into question whether a child, even in their adolescence, had the patience to both transcribe the text of their faith and then provide what is regarded as \"profound philosophical wisdom\" on the writings.\nI have come to the conclusion that an elder member of House Hightower wrote \"Navitas\", and then proceeded to place Silius' name on the binding and opening cover of the text.\n\nSimilarly, the prestigious position that House Hightower has within the\nheirarchy of the Church, as noted by Theoren in his text, \"House Hightower\", I do not believe it presumptious of me to state that House Hightower, who become reflective of the Church of the Faith, to  be ecclesiatical in their approach to the history of\nMan. Theoren states that \"The House of Hightower begins its origins far and further back through the pages of the history of Man to the first High Pontiff of the Church of the Faith, Everrard Hightower\", and therefore provides proof to my claim that it is\nnot beyond those of the Church to insert their own religious motivations within their accounts of History. \n\nIt is therefore axiomatic, within my own individual contextual framework, that Mage Baruk-Ghaz's \"Ancient History\" tomes are nothing but mere\nCanonist propaganda, and provide only a historical account of Man rather than the Descendents. \n\nIf any budding or adept historian wishes to challenges my claims and provide evidence into how the Mage has provided an accurate portrayal of the origins of\nAegis, then I highly encourage them to do so, for that is the nature of history and scholarship; to develop understanding where there is none, and to search for the one Truth amidst all the falsities.", ""),
        StaticBook("History - Slayer", "Athe'lor", "History of the Void, as Written by Arcane Mage Slayer, Aegis.\n\nBefore the beginning of time there was nothing, no planes of existence, only the Void. But within the Void was a light, we know of this light as god, the one deity.\nBut this is not the lore we are interested in. This deity created in the Void the world of Aegis, wherefore you live out your lives. It came to pass that the deity moulded on the world of Aegis Man, whom he blew his breath of existence into; giving life.\nAfter breathing his existence into man, he entwined some of his divine power, raw and unformed, into the world of Aegis itself. This power was to be called magic by man, and just as man was placed in the world to be tested, the power was to be utilised-\nby man to be a test, a test of greed and power.\n\nThe power was entwined into the very fabric of both worlds; it ensured the worlds were linked, ever connected. So it was that all the races of Aegis could access this power, but none were the same.\nAs the power was channelled through the individual it scanned their soul, and was therefore manifested as an extension of their natural environment. So it was that the Humans had a diverse spread of magic, as they were the most versatile.\nThe Elves came from their woodland homes, of nature and healing. Dwarves from their mighty halls, of stone, hardened and sturdy. Then the Orcs from their harsh deserts, strong and vicious. The power of the Nobel races came from their allegiance:\nthe Ascended from their hallowed halls, pure and righteous. The Undead from their fiery fields, tainted and evil.\n\nThe first of the Mages quickly discovered its usefulness, its power... they noticed how dangerous it was.\nThey had the power to kill in an instant, or create in an instant... They had power over all. In their wisdom the saw that something would have to be done... The power was to be controlled, learned properly.\nBut the magic was not forever present in the world of Aegis. It was lost in times long past, forgotten to all but a few, when the evil Iblees was to be banished from this world. In his banishment he was sent to void by the ancients.\nThis sent his minions back whence they came, and a barrier was erected between the worlds to stop their return. So it was that the worlds were no longer entwined, in separation the power no longer held, and magic all but disappeared from the world...\nBut it was not to last. The power of Iblees was great, even in void, and he worked at unravelling the barrier between the worlds... Soon the barrier began to break down, the Undead taint spread once more across the face of Aegis.\nAlthough this time there was little hope for salvation...\n\nWith the failing of the barrier protecting the world of the living from the dead the magic lost to the Descendants, all those years ago, once again seeped into the fabric of the world.\nThe people of Aegis once more felt a somewhat unfamiliar tingle in their blood, unfamiliar but as though it was always there.\n\nSo it came to pass that the ancient power of magic was awakened in Man.\nThose with the power of foresight could see ahead a fork in the path; one to light, the other darkness... They could only hope that with this new found power that the right decision would be made...\nSo it was that the first Mage Ram'Ir, first in the line of the great mages, gathered to him a group of the most trusted and powerful Mages in the lands, and gave them a duty, a life quest.\nA duty, to protect the land of Aegis and the Decendants from themselves, from what lies within, so that the Magic which remained through the ages would not destroy all, but be contained and conserved.\nSo it was that the Guild of mages was forged into existence, accepting those with great magical power, or great skill in other areas of their interest.\nThey will not interfere in the day-to-day lives of the people of Aegis, however would intervene at the mistreat of magic.\nAnd now it comes to pass that the mages guild is headed by the arcane mage Slayer, who reconstructed the ancient mages tower in the snowy north’s to be the head of the great guild, the centre piece of the smaller guilds-\nscattered around the world of Aegis. The tower acts as a meeting place, a place of learning and teaching to all those in the guild who make the perilous journey...\nAlthough there is just as much to be done in the city guilds who accept those of like race. \n\n\n\n\nOriginally written by Arcane Mage Slayer, rewritten by Athe'lor for Andria Ith'ael.", ""),
        StaticBook("History I", "Clan Father Vidar Frostbeard", "Frostbeard\n  History - Aegis\n    By Clan Father\n   Vidar Frostbeard\nAccording to Frostbeard legend, the clan has its origins with the fourth son of Urguan, Kaz’Ulrah. Kaz’Ulrah preferred the more solitary lifestyle of the cold mountains and journeyed there with his followers. From there, he and his descendants would make\na home there that would eventually be called Jornheim. Over time, the name Frostbeards became akin to them for whenever they would descend from the mountains, frost and snow would be in their beards from the snowy mountains.\nThe Frostbeards were a group of Dwarves who lived deep within the mountains of Aegis. They were not very well known nor did they want to be; they admired their culture and traditions and how they lived. Soon, however, a group of travellers came into their\nvillage seeking refuge and shelter from the unforgiving snow storm. Generously, the Frostbeards opened their doors and sheltered the cold and hungry travellers, but these travellers were soon to cause a lot of havoc. The travellers thanked them for their\ngenerosity and asked if they could purchase a house in the village for their goods that they were selling. The Frostbeards gave them the house without hesitation, but the Dwarves could not have known the travellers true intentions.\nAfter the travellers settled in Jornheim, the townspeople slowly grew more hostile towards each other. They began to fight over prices of food and minerals, which ultimately led to a rift forming between the inhabitants. Soon, without the knowledge of the\nJarl, the town was to become divided into two sides, one being the Domnu’s and one being the Dechtire’s. Both sides were evenly matched and had around the same number of supporters, but what it was they supported was the question that was never asked.\nWithout notice the travellers had corrupted the minds of the innocent civilians of the town of Jornheim, causing a civil war to take place inside its mighty walls. It was to be a massacre that was never forgotten.\nThe Jarl grew anxiously worried of the actions of his people towards each other; he drew his attention towards his mercenaries, who were to go and restore order within the town and bring all this chaos to a halt. However, the mercenaries, who were to go\nand restore order within the town and bring all this chaos to a halt. However, the mercenaries misinterpreted the orders of the Jarl and instead caused even more havoc by threatening the civilians with severe consequences for their actions.\nThis only further stirred the tension, as the Jarl was now being targeted by his own people. Meanwhile, the travellers watched as the town grew angrier and angrier with one another, and without notice the travellers slipped away as if they were never\nthere. Finally, a meeting was called in the centre of the town by the Jarl, where they were to negotiate on terms the Jarl did not approve of.\nThe Domnus wanted to be separated from the Dechtire’s and wanted a wall between the town separating it in half, the Dechtire’s, however, wanted to take a more aggressive approach towards the situation and said they wanted to burn down all the Dechtire's\nhouses, but then the Jarl shouted at the top of his lungs, \"Silence!\" Responding, the town quickly comprehended and grew quiet. The Jarl then asked his people \"Why, Why dae ye want tae fite each otherr! Why!\" No one had an answer to that as the crowd\nslowly started mumbling and talking between each other, but suddenly, an arrow was fired from a far flung watch tower hitting the Jarl in the heart. He tumbled down from the platform, then landing in the middle of his people. His blood poured down from\nthe back of his head forming a ruby puddle in the street. The people watched in horror before a loud voice shouted, \"The Domnu's did it!\" This caused the Domnu’s to take out their swords and stand defensively as the Dechtire's gathered around them\nshouting \"Death!\" While others agreed, \"Aye death tae tha wee bastardsh!\" The voices echoed as a dark shadow stood in the watch tower overseeing all this with a slight grin on his face. With that, a civil war had been started.\nThe Domnu's hurried to their side of the town where they had stayed and armed themselves in a defensive manner. The Dechtire's did the same; however, they were charging towards the Domnu's with everything they had. Blood stained the streets as the Jarl's\nbody was hidden within the Tower of the Dead. The sun slowly began to rise as the result of the Domnu's and Dechtire's skirmish was revealed. The stone had turned from grey to red, and only three people were left alive from the bloodshed; however, the\nthe handful of survivors soon left the empty, blood-stained town behind.", ""),
        StaticBook("History II", "Clan Father Vidar Frostbeard", "Frostbeard\n History - Asulon\n    By Clan Father\n   Vidar Frostbeard\nIn the lands of Asulon, the Frostbeards plunged to their lowest point in terms of honor and strength, and later on their highest point in honor, strength, and power. Right after the arrival to the sanctuary of Asulon, many of the Frostbeards split apart.\nKarl Frostbeard, the clan father at the time, did everything in his power to reunite the scattered Frostbeards but to no avail. Soon after, Karl the Orcbane vanished, and not a single Dwarf knew what had become of him. Years later, several Frostbeards\nbanded together and returned to Karik, reuniting under the clan name and with the leadership of Clan Father Liam Frostbeard. This was truly a new era for the Frostbeards, for better and for worse. Many years had passed and the Frostbeards, who had ended\nup taking up residence in Alras, had decided to mend the tensions between the clan and the Dwarven Nation by returning to their roots. The Frostbeards did not return to the Nation empty handed, however, they returned with an entire Kingdom in their grasp\nand granted ownership of it towards the Nation of Karik. During this time the Frostbeards had created a marriage bond with the Goldhands, living under their wing in the times in which they struggled. It was around this time when Goruk \"The Great\"\nFrostbeard, son of Karl \"The Orcbane\" Frostbeard, had returned to join the remaining Frostbeards and lead them to greater glory. That he did, leading them into many battles and returning the Frostbeards to their former glory in terms of power and\nstrength. It was around this time when the Frostbeards took a plot of land in the Nation of Karik, and upon it they built a stronghold that will be spoken of in old tavern tales for many years to come. The Frostbeards had the money; the power, and the\nthe strength to stop living under the Goldhands wing, so they did exactly that and took up their rightful birth name once more, while living under their own traditions and teachings.\nthe strength to stop living under the Goldhands wing, so they did exactly that and took up their rightful birth name once more, while living under their own traditions and teachings.\nYears later, after the three holds had mended under one Kings rule once more, the Frostbeards had risen to take up council positions within the Kingdom and restore the glory of the Dwarves. Chief Goruk the Great had become Lord Marshal of the Dwarves, and\nGorum Frostbeard had become the High Ambassador of the Dwarves. Goruk was known as the Dwarf who restored the Legion from the shards it was left in by the previous Lord Marshal, Grimloth Irongut. The Legion was restored to its former glory entirley,\nleading the Dwarves into a new era of power, wealth, and ever expanding land conquered by the power of the Legion all under the leadership of Goruk. As time passed by, tensions began to rise between Lord Marshal Goruk and King Hiebe Irongut.\nGoruk and the Frostbeards had tensions with Hiebe and the Ironguts, tensions that had been contained until one day Goruk and Gorum fully attempted to overthrow Hiebe; however, not in a dishonourable way. They wished to go about it while still\nentirely following the Dwarven constitution by using a re-election of some sort. The Frostbeards had the full backing of the council members, but when it came time to vote the council backed away and betrayed the Frostbeards trust.\nAfterwards, both Gorum and Goruk Frostbeard stepped down from their military and diplomatic positions before taking a leave from the Dwarves for quite some time.", ""),
        StaticBook("History of Vsenk", "Nathan", "3rd of The Grand Harvest, 1571.\n\nI notice now that our men live in a constant state of fear from the likes of the Gold Corps. Such a shame that their anger towards few leads to hate towards many.\nIn other news, a mighty storm struck us in the night.\n17th of Grand Harvest, 1571\n\nToday I met the emperor, and I must say I was not dissappointed in the stature of the man. I must say also, that I was in fact suprised by how much he seemed to care about the common man. I have him in high esteem.\n10th of Sun's Smile, 1571.\n\nThe Emperor has given himself more time for consideration over the plot of land we were seeking. This does not bode well for us, and I fear that we may be, as the saying goes, schlonged.\n15th of Sun's Smile, 1571.\n\nThe Emperor bides his time with this decision, I know not whether he will give us providence or damnation with his will.... I pray lord Fyodor will give him good reason to trust us.\n16th of the Sun's Smile, 1571.\n\nHis Majesty has allowed us a fief to the west of the capital, towards Mount Augustine. We are very pleased, however unsure of the land we were promised. We now go to scout it out, myself, the band, and our noble lord.\n17th of grand Harvest, 1571.\n\nWe've found our fertile land. The air is warm, its location friendly, and the distance from both the capital and the docks from the Cloud Temple perfect. I think teh emperor for his graciousness, and look to the future.\n4th of the Amber Cold, 1571.\n\nConstruction has been difficult... Most of the oaken logs the serfs have brough have been erected, yet we still lack the pure earth and refined wood to construct suitable homes. I send workers out today to fetch us these.\n11th of the Deep Cold, 1571\n\nThe Construction has slowed considerably, however the log frames of houses and the animal pen has been created. Our pigs now roll in mud, and our people see the fruits of their labor, however arduous it may be.\n14th of the Deep Cold, 1571\n\nA storm shakes our men to the very core today. The air, just warm enough to be rain and yet cold enough to chill, bites at us as we huddle in a single, half built keep, praying for warmth. I will survive, however.\n16th of the Deep Cold, 1571\n\nThe Storm has ended, finally, however now our drenched clothes freeze over with the coming winds. We have built fires in the half finished keep, sacrificing wood to keep ourselves warm.\n15th of the First Seed, 1572.\n\nThe roofs have been made, and the walls erected as our town begins to take shape. We lack merely windows and a few other oddities. I feel utter pride for my men, however one has left our company on, less than friendly terms.\n15th of The First Seed, 1573.\n\nThe town has been fully constructed now, after three long, hard years. Our walls stand erect, our rooms furnished with people and furniture. It has been a long, hard journey. I am proud to have partaken on it.\n12th of the Amber Cold, 1573.\n\nToday Lord Fyodor was married to the lady, now baroness, Theresa. The ceremony held many a man and woman in the cathedral, so many that the pews were overpacked! I feel nothing but happy for our Baron.\n15th of the First Seed, 1591\n\nFirst Entry in many years... lost the Journal for quite a while.... I have settled in a new barony, known as Ponce, after the collapse of Vsenk. The barony of Ponce is lively, and the Lord fair. I shall see how I fair.", ""),
        StaticBook("Hollowed Umbrage", "UnBaed", "[!] The pages in this book are filled with neat, ink writing.\n\n\n\n\n                 Hallowed\n                 Umbrage\n[A copy from the original]\nI write the following epitaph with dire haste so much that the winds part my words.  My account of these events may not be entirely accurate, something completely acceptable under the maddening, fear stricken haze that I have left in.\nI sit here now quill in hand, wounded wit a gash so dreadfully dark that I'm not sure if it really is a wound at all.  I have become a well of life, bountiful as the succulent navy mists ooze out of this growth, this... anchor; ever so dark and dreadful.\nMy pilgrimmage to this place hath cost me the trust and faith of my only friends as despite  every loud, nagging warning against venturing here, my back was turned and my hands covered my ears.\nIt is the weakness of Man to succum to the allure of power, riches, and knowledge that of which the Abyss is said to contain.  Trust me when I say that the power hidden away here is done for a reason and should never belong to any mortal man.\nFor the corrupting mind of Men ever to wrap their greedy fingers around such incomprehensible things, it would mean our doom.  The Trolls, Harpies, and Gryphons of our world pale in comparison to the horror of the deep, dark beyond.\nLegends tell of the Abyss ruins of Aegis, a land from which Man's forefathers hailed.  I would hesitate to call the state in which the Gods left the motherland in a ruin, for truly there remains little left here at all.\nFor this Abyss, this endless chasm to which there seems no end is both the catastrophic ashes of a world once living and breathing as well as a prison for every lost soul that the world sunk with it.  North, South, East, West - it all leads to despair.\nI hath deviated from the guiding compass to venture in a new direction; downward.  For I suspected that within the bowels of this crushing nightmare there must be both a ceiling and a floor.  I, a pawn controlled by adventurous urges, took a fatal dive.\nMy sense of time has long since fled, abandoning me like many other luxuries that once made me whole.  After a measurement of time far longer than any measurement of time I've evered thought to measure.  I reached the feared and fabled end of this void.\nI dare not write about the countless demonds that scour the ebon plane despite the insanity they so passively inflict.  They do not deserve the honour of being referenced alongside the Lord of the deep, dark below.  Darkness Incarnate.\nAs my wailing, shedding flesh forced itself through the dense acidic atmosphere, my feet began to fail me.  Time hath come to truly give up, and turn my back I thought.  Yet my thoughts were ruptured by a presence so overwhelming that I could not think.\nAs I fought with myself to open my eyes I stared upon what could only be described as a living shadow, embodying umbral hellfire frigid enough to lock my very bones in place.Radiated in darkness so hollow that the Abyss stood brightly aflamed beside him.\nHe worse armor, the first sign that this impossible creation was indeed Man.  Ancient was his armor, charred and blackened from what I cannot begin to imagine.  Yet his armor, heavy as it appeard did not hinder him.\nHis form suddenly shifted all at once, phasing out at one place and in again at another.  The realm was his whim, as he did not simply move through it, but had become it.  Now, the Dark Lord towered above me, reeking of ash and death.\nAll past experiences seem like a petty joke when compared to the awesome perspective I had been blessed with.  This Man, whose blood red eyes pierced through the very veil of the Abyss had drawn forth his weapon.  A terrible greatsword, massive in size.\nDripping with the hollowing souls of the damned.  This blade, serrated like the peak of Mount Ire was shoved into my heart, slotting into my flesh like a key within a door.  In the seconds before my consciousness faded I heard something.  I heard a voice.\nA voice that would rival a Dragon.  It was then that I knew for certain - This was the Old Lord of Umbrage.  King of the Abyss.  One whose name does not touch the lips of the living, and whose sight is known only to the dead and the mad.\nHis perverted shriek defiled every corner of the Abyss, his siren call summoning the dark to his side.  As the black visage of the Old Lord faded from my sight, I heard his words.\nR A D I A N T\nI S  T H E  B L A C K\nS U N", ""),
        StaticBook("Holy Reemergence", "Unmarked Author", "Reemergence \n of the Holy League\n\n\n   Sun's Smile, 1620\nWith recent news, I was present at the keep of the Clerics, the name of such is known as Lucerna Temple, The gathering was actually quite large. Most were Ascended, one Cleric by the name of Elvira. Who is also the leader as far as I know.\nAnd another, single Paladin who goes by the name Izier, a Dark Elf. Many things were discussed, which I will lay out in order within these pages The first was discussed on the current role of the Edict, who wished to further their alignment within the\nHoly Orders, serving mainly now as a vessel to Aerial and the other's will. This of course allowing their ranks to carry out what those bound to the deities cannot. Which I am guessing torture, capturing and slaying anyone they deem having dark purposes.\nA written agreement with Naffog and Heial was undertaken. Naffog is the leader of the Crimson Edict currently. And had given the idea first off with the conversation started. They had struck an agreement with the Paladins, Clerics and\nthose attuned to Aerial's will. Which will allow them to be a. Backup force if needed. I have stated what they are directly already in the near previous pages listed. Another group was also present, which the name of the leader was Arik.\nThey, as I heard are a small group of Witch Hunters. Who actively target dark arts users and frost witches, as it was implied. Secretly attempting to root out any corruption embedded within political figures across the lands.\nAs of hearing currently, they will be focusing on the Human lands mainly as the ties with the Dwarves and Elves, mainly the Wood are very tightly held together. This being on Ascended. The clerics have a written agreement with Veris and the Dominion to\ntarget and slay any dark beings and rogue mages as they see fit. The Paladins for some reason are banished from Veris. Which I am certain it had something to do with the brash ideals of their late, deceased leader, Ian.\nAs with the forth branch. The dragon people known as Aldrazi are currently missing in their league. Which is a good thing. They are attempting to seek them out to gain any guidance on whether they want to remain within the league. Or go about their\nown path across the lands. They have been missing for a few Elven months to the dating of this book's beginning. That is all to report on them at this time.\nHaelun'or is greatly suspected of harboring masses of Frost Witches too. So I'm sure the Holy League will be targeting this location to try and purge and burn out any who attempt to walk secretly in their streets.\nThe Ascended recently also have come across direct information regarding an individual by the name of Llindir. Who is known to be a powerful Blood Mage. This was found out by a person who had a blood rune upon the back of his neck.\nIt was transferred over to an Ascended by the name of Sophia. From what I gathered from the conversation. It compelled the victim to servitude. The rune was then purged from her afterwards. It was said he resides within Veris. Though where I was unable to\ngather the specific details upon listening.\nElvira will be visiting to speak on this to the High Prince of the Elven Dominion.\nThe last topic held within this meeting was that of a person name Gareth, a powerful shade andone who supposedly formed a group named the Dark Congress. An extremely unstable individual, especially when emotionally pushed.\nNo information was given on where he hides and moves about at. Though from what was heard. I am guessing he is like a nomad, often keeping his feet moving to avoid detection from those with holy affiliations.\nMay this recording shed understanding where it is needed most.", ""),
        StaticBook("Holy Scrolls - I", "Jacob Chapel", "The Holy Scrolls\n\n     The Book of\n     Nativities\n\nTransscribed by Jacob Chapel during the Deep Cold, 1470.\n\nUse these words to keep true to your faith and to find strength and knowledge.\nThere were no planes of existence. There was nothing. Just the Void. And a bright shining light. It was not a light we could see, it was not really white either, but it would be the only way to explain the existence of such a Deity in contrast to the\nemptiness of the Void. None knows why, how or when this Deity existed. It is, in-fact, heresy to speculate on such matters. The all knowing God was this Deity.\n\nTruly none can describe the majesty of the Creator, the one and only. The Merciful Creator of\nthe Seven Skys. With his intent, and only his intent, the World of Aegis was created. All he had to do was simply want it to occur and it happened. The rolling seas, proud mountains and vast landscapes, all in a second, created by God.\nThe World was not created in play or for fun, but as a theater for the inhabitants of the World to be tested in. And tested for what? That is for us to speculate. Though I believe it is to test us for purity, how hard we can fight temptation, and how\nclean and good can our actions be.\n\nThe first mortal being to be created was a man. This man was sculptured with clay and water, but left hollow. Soulless, God's creation lay there for the other immortal beings to see. The Aengul and the Daemon,\nthe two spirits created before the mortal beings and before the creation of Aegis. Not much is known about these two spirit races, but hopefully in the future we may know more.\n\nGod then blew his own breath of existance into the hollow shell and\nthe Man lived. God then took the man and put him in the centre of all of Aegis, the same spot where The Cloud Temple now stands. God also made the Man a partner, from the exact same clay\nand the exact same breath, she was the first Woman. These simple beings could not talk, nor did they know much about the World. They roamed the world, enjoying its pre-historic beauty. Untouched, the fresh glades and dark thick forests were a wonder to\nset eyes on. Soon they had four children in the four corners of Aegis.\n\nMalin was the first of their sons, born in the deep forests of Aegis, he had blonde hair and sharp ears. Standing tall, he was the father of the Elves of Aegis. Krug was born in the\nscorching deserts of Aegis, fierce and relentless, he was the father of the Orcs. In the fresh meadows of Aegis was born Horen, father of Humans. And lastly, in the deep underground caves of the World, Urguan was born, master of the Dwarves.\nSoon the first Man and Woman created by God departed Aegis and climbed the seven skies to meet with God their creator, for they had achieved their goal. The Sons began to explore the World of Aegis and each was stricken with grief at the loss of their\nparents, seeking to fill the chasm of emotion inside them they began to create civilisation.\n\nAlthough none of the descendants of each Son had neither their long lives or splendour, they did carry their forefathers looks and traits. The Elves with Malin\nat their head travelled the lands and began naming all the inhabitants of this world, they were the first to create a tongue and began to name the trees and grass, the mountains and valleys across all of Aegis.\n\nAt this time, Malin, Urguan, Krug and\nHoren were not far apart in looks. Horen and Krug had darker hair than the other two and Krug was a bit larger in build. Malin had blonde hair and Urguan red. They were all close companions, friends and had much love for each other and each others people.\nUrguan travelled into the deep underground of the earth, naming the beautiful ores and gems, sharing it with his brethren. Krug travelled the harsh deserts, testing his stamina and strength against the environment of Aegis, and Horen began building the\nfirst squalid huts and villages in the valleys. The people lived for hundreds of years, in harmony and peace. Until the day where one of the great Daemons, great worshipers and squalid protectors of the Void, kin spirits to the Aengul, defected.\nIblees, who was once the greatest of all of God’s worshippers, was cast down into the mortal world, and so he was about to destroy the tranquility of Aegis forever. He came in the shape of a man. A gentle being who loved things delicate, he was quickly\nbefriended by Malin, Urguan and Horen. Krug had a great distrust of him but after many years of being convinced by his brothers, he finally accepted his company.\n\nLittle did Iblees know that this was all part of the Great God's plan to test the\ndescendants of Man and Woman. Iblees wanted to destroy everything that God had designed and created, still not in a powerful physical form he began sowing seeds of evil in the minds of the Descendants. Prying on their needs and lusts.\nTo Malin, lover of nature, he promised him many children. He promised him that their laughter would resonate across their forest homes and that he would be content. Malin did not want anything more in this world than a bountiful amount of young to\noccupy the barren forests.\n\nTo Urguan, he promised infinite wealth of Gems and Ores, colours and crystals he could never imagine. To this, Urguan’s greed failed him.\nHoren, was anxious he would not live long enough to see his city completed and his lands increased. He needed more time, and Iblees struck the chord and promised immortality.\n\nKrug was the last to be tricked, Iblees tempted him with wealth, with food,\nwith power. None interested Krug. Iblees was furious, he then challenged Krug in open combat in fury.\n\nThe whole world witnessed Ibleeses transformation into a hideous beast of the void. His skin turned into scales, fangs erupted and dark horns exploded\nfrom his head. He grew large wings and began to breath terrible fire. All stood in shock and horror. The beast terrified all inhabitants of Aegis, animals fled and the Sons of the Descendants were too weak of blood to stand in front of such evil fury.\nOnly Malin, Urguan, Horen and Krug stood in front of the terror.\n\nIn Iblees’ right hand, a sword wrought in flame. Krug, naked and unarmed charged at The Daemon, throwing himself against the scalding scales of Iblees. He screamed in agony as his skin\nburned and decayed, becoming green and molten. Iblees was knocked off his feet, for the last time. He stood up, heaving in rage and fury, flames exploded from the pores of his skin, he roared in anger and where he struck his sword the land collapsed and\nthe ground erupted. And Lo, great was the Valour of Urguan and the Strength of Krug as they fought the beast. Powerful were the arms that carried Krug’s Axe and strong was Horens’ heart as they fought in open combat upon the plains of Aegis. Malin’s sword\nwas fast and swift, smiting Iblees upon his breast and sides.\n\nFor the thirty years the Descendants fought Iblees, the world became a war torn mess. The dead were defiled, summoned from their graves to follow Iblees’ mastery. The more mortal descendants\ndied, the greater Iblees’ armys grew. It was a sad chapter in the World of Aegis, the brothers threw up their hands to God in prayer and in agony. Their creations destroyed, their children massacred. Woe to the Sons of Man and Woman. Krug grew bitter,\nhis resentment of his brothers increased for befriending such a beast. Urguan grew greedy, he fought valourously but began to hide his treasures underground. Malin feared for the lives of his children and did not leave his forest sanctuary. It seemed the\nworld was destined for ruin. Iblees grew in strength and the Descendants weakened. Until one day.\n\nOne day where the sound of horns could be heard from the far east. Beautiful horns echoing all across the skies of Aegis. God had heard their prayers.\nAn army of Aengul and Daemons from the seven skies had appeared on the grand shores of Aegis. Their majesty and beauty so strong that all The Descendants could see was a flash of power white light erupt from the east. Only Malin with his strong sight\ncould see the figures of light as they sped across the skies towards the armies of Iblees.\n\nIblees’ soldiers burned where they stood, The thousands of skeletons and cadavers burst aflame and his living servants fled. There in the right middle of the\nworld, he was cast down and chained by the Aengul and Daemon. A robed figure with brown hair and a black wreathed apparation stood before him. They were a terrible image to look at, all shyed down and bowed in their majesty and glory. They stood before\nIblees, knowing he was immortal and could not be killed, sentencing him to banishment to the void where his dark soul would be forever trapped in torment.\nBut before they could complete the sentence, Iblees stood tall for one last time.\n\n“You believe you may simply banish me from this plane and that my taint shall not last? I have touched this world with evil and it shall forever be part of the souls that\ninhabit it.\n\nMalin, I find no need to curse you, for so many of your kind have already willingly submitted to me now and will on my return in the distant future. The curse you will bear, is not of my doing, but of your own. Even you have done my work,\nif you realize it or not.\n\nUrguan, your greed and lust shall overcome you, you are not worthy of the height God gave you, your descendants shall be short, squalid and ugly. You will always seek to find Gold and Gems in the deep underground of the earth,\nyour hunger never satisfied.\n\nHoren, the immortality you hope for will never arrive. Your longevity has already been stripped away thanks to the labors of the twisted heart of your brother Malin. You will age quickly and die before you ever taste the\nfruits of your pointless labors.\n\nAnd you Krug, the most hated of the Descendants, you shall always have the lust of war. You are strong? Well the strength shall be used against your brothers, used to pillage and murder! Your lust for battle shall be\nunsatiated and your descendants shall grow ugly and heartless.”\n\nAs soon as his words were uttered, the world grew suddenly dark. A great roar erupted from Iblees’ mouth and in a blast of fire he was banished from the Mortal World. The Descendants stood\nstill for several moments, pondering over the words of Iblees. Malin, Krug, Urguan and Horen all knew naught of what the great Devil had spoken of when concerning Malin’s betrayal. Dismissing it as the lies of a demon propagated to corrupt their souls,\nthe brothers thought nothing further of Malin’s supposed treason.\n\nThe robed figure stood before the four brothers.\n\n“There is nothing in my power that may undo what that evil did. There is one thing I may do however, and that is to bless you.\nMalin, may your forests be a sanctuary of peace and your children long lived.\n\nUrguan, may your descendants be hardy, strong hearted and strong of mind.\n\nKrug, may your people show valour and honour where none exist.\nAnd Horen, may your people one day explore the Seven Skies.\n\nI can do no more, for all my power is spent. We will go back to our master now, I believe your children may see us once more but long in the future.”\nAnd with that, the great host of Aenguls and Daemons disappeared into thin wisps in the air.", ""),
        StaticBook("Holy Scrolls -II", "Jacob Chapel", "The Holy Scrolls\n\n     The Book of\n     Horen\n\nTransscribed by Jacob Chapel during the Amber Cold, 1471.\n\nUse these words as a source of strength and widom.\nThe years passed and went on and on, as time is wont to do. The Decendant, after being cursed by the Great Devil, adapted their lives to suit their new roles. There was, for some time, peace and prosperity amongst the original realms created by the\nCreator. One day, upon the cusp of which a red sun rose from the east, King Horen of humanity was approached by an Aengul, a divine messenger of God. This Aengul shone magnificently, illuminated by the light of God, its shades and colours twisting\naround one another as it addressed Horen. Its wings swathed in blinding white, it opened its mouth and through it the Creator spoke.\n“Horen of Man. God has chosen you as his divine prophet, as his mouthpiece on this world, until the day of\nyour ascent into the Seven Skies at his order. You are the almighty king, the Creator’s chiefmost servant on this hallowed earth. Be jubilant, for you are second to none but me! Humanity is the holy divine being of God, the human body remaining the most\nunadulterated, original form of the Creator’s design, not possessing of neither corruption nor mutation. You are the chosen people, and you shall carry out my commands, and your people alone, not your brothers and their kin, shall swear to my commandments\nThey are as follows!\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Creator, Blessed be His Name, is the Creator and Guide of everything that has been created; He alone has made, does make, and will make all things.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Divine\nare the Creator’s regents in this realm and that their obedience is worship to the Creator.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Aenguls and Daemons are the Creator’s servants.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Creator\nBlessed be His Name, is One, and that there is no unity in any manner like His, and that He alone is our God, who was, and is, and will be.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Creator, Blessed be His Name, has no body, and that He is free from all\nproperties of matter, and that there can be no comparison to Him whatsoever.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Creator, Blessed be His Name, is the first and the last.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Creator, Blessed be His Name,\nand to Him alone, it is right to pray, and that it is not right to pray to any being besides Him.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that all the words of the Divines are true.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the\nprophecy of Horen I our teacher, blessings be upon him, was true, and that he was the chief of the Divines, both those who preceded him and those who followed him.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the entire scrolls that is now in our possession is the\nsame that was given to our Divines, blessings be upon them.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Holy Scrolls can not be corrupted\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Creator, Blessed be His Name, knows all the deeds\nof beings and all their thoughts.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Creator, Blessed be His Name, rewards those who keep His commandments and punishes those that transgress them.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that there will\nbe a revival of the dead at the time when it shall please the Creator, Blessed be His Name, and His mentions shall be exalted for ever and ever.”\n\nAnd so Horen listened, and he repeated the Creator’s words, and he carried the word\nof the Creator to his people, who listened as he did. They kneeled before Horen, first of the Divine, and pledged the commandments and supremacy of humanity over all but God. The realmn of man rallied underneath the Regent of Heven, arming themselves and\nerecting great fortresses, beginning the golden age of the Horen dynasty. For truly, it was decreed that humanity was second to none but the Creator, and the chose people would carry out his command until the end of time.", ""),
        StaticBook("Horse Purchase", "Aldor", "Pass to door on the right - 6672\n\nChest inside with saddle n training stick inside.", ""),
        StaticBook("House Barbanov", "Walter Marshall", "History of House Barbanov\n\n\n\nBy Walter Marshall\nHOUSE OF BARBOVIC, called BARBANOV in the normal speak, claims lineage from Saint Joren Horenson himself, the first of the High Kings of the North. Further down, the house claims descent or kinship from Barbov the Black, its nominal description,\nRovyk the Stern, Saint Julia of Paradisius, Saint Lothar of Balian, Saint Adrian of Leuvaarden, Blessed Jan Jeremi, Blessed Francis the Martyr, Blessed Otto of Vanderfell,\nand most importantly, coming from the loins of Exalted Sigismund himself, Prophet of Revelations.\nThe House stands as a ducal family in the Holy Kingdom of Oren, with Lord Karl III. holding the duchy of Haense, inherited from his Rovin uncle. Once, however, the family stood as Imperial Princes, the Lord and Lady Barbanov’s father,\nAlexander I being Emperor of Oren. Even so, from the Lord and Lady Barbanov’s maternal side, they were once Princes of the Hansetians, being of the now destroyed and defunct Kingdom of Aesterwald.\nHOUSE BARBANOV OF HAENSE has no long lineage, that be accustomed to its parent houses of Karovic and Rovin, or its cousins of House de Sarkozy, House of Kovac, or even House of Vladovic.\nThe House comes from the loins of EMPEROR ALEXANDER I CARRION and his wife, PRINCESS ARABELLA ROVIN, married per a peace contract between the Empire of Oren and the newly vassalized Kingdom of Aesterwald.\nThe union, however, was nay a happy one.\nAfter the start of the infamous RENATUS REBELLION, sparked by protests of the arrest of the Grand Knight, the Princess stole the two babes born of her and Alexander’s coupling; the twins Karl and Lorin.\nIt is unsure how the Princess transferred the babes unnoticed, but eventually the twins found their way under the tutelage of PRINCE OTTO ROVIN, with their father deposed and presumed dead and their mother dying of a hunting accident.\nUnder the guise that they were his bastards, the two babes eventually grew from sucking on the teat, to toddlers, and eventual kids, roaming the Waldenian Royal keep aimlessly, as children do.\nChange appeared, however, when KING VORON I ROVIN died, replaced by his Raevir-hating son, KING ARN III ROVIN. It is under King Arn’s reign that the Raevir minority of Aesterwald was pushed out, killed, or worse.\nHis hate went so far, eventually to curse HIGH PONTIFF DANIEL I, a known Carrion bastard, and declare a schism, putting his own kinsman Hubert as anti-Pontiff. Despite propaganda within the Northern kingdom,  it did not bode well to the populace.\nDefeat after defeat, and the SCHISM WAR, as it came to called after the Duchy of Savoy came to aid of the Kingdom of Akovia, rolled on. Desertion from the Waldenian ranks became more frequent, with even the King’s own kin abandoning his unjust cause.\nOTTO ROVIN, taking along the child Karl and Lorin, left the Kingdom (before, of course, posting the Condemnation of Arn’s Reign). Otto and the children fled to CYRIAUM, where he took work as the Papal Guard of HIGH PONTIFF DANIEL I.\n. It is here where Otto finally told Karl and his sister of his true heretige, where the High Pontiff confirmed as true.\nFor the next ten years, Karl trained underneath not only his Uncle, but of the numerous heroes of the SCHISM WAR. As his uncle dealt with the political nature of the Waldenian Realm, Karl fought with the likes of BLESSED EMMA VLADOVIC,\nthe woman-warrior with a thirst of heretic blood, the unifier of humanity himself, KING ANDREW I VYRDA, and the current king, KING OLIVER I ASHFORD. From the teachings of King Andrew and King Oliver,\nKarl grew to understand the affairs of state and nobility, eventually growing out from the child of a drunken uncle to a successful and witty statesman. It is also during the SCHISM WAR that Karl took up his name BARBANOV,\nafter urging of his cousin and High Pontiff Daniel I, in honor of BARBOV THE BLACK.\nAfter KING ARN III ROVIN died from burning down his precious Vanderfell and Eagle’s Perch, Karl joined his guardian Otto to pick up the pieces. Forming the unsuccessful NORTHERN COMMONWEALTH,\nKarl help fight against the Dwarves in the FOURTH DWARF-HUMAN WAR, taking a penchant to the killing of midgets and eventually,\nthe High Elves who killed the fair KING ANDREW I VYDRA. It is then when Karl, with Vladov allies and the small retinue of the Commonwealth, took the HOLD OF HIEBENHALL, eventually to be named SIEGRAD,\nthe new capital of the Northern Realm. Karl established himself as the COUNT OF SIEGRAD thereafter, holding the title to this day.\nOnce his guardian and uncle, OTTO ROVIN, left to go chase down rumors of Arn living within the secluded land of AELDIN, Karl took up the reigns of the Commonwealth, disbanding its entirety and eventually to name himself the DUKE OF HAENSE.\nAs of now, the DUKE KARL III BARBOVIC stewards his capital of SIEGRAD, one of the most populous cities within the Kingdom, as well as working where his uncle left off: rebuilding the Northern Realm.", ""),
        StaticBook("How to Survive", "Daxx Vorhees", "How to survive V1\n\nBy Daxx Vorhees\n1591\nHere are some methods of how to survive if you get lost and dont know where to go or what to do\n\nFirst look for water, water is allways important, look for something to store the water like a bottle or even your boots are useful look for something\nonce you find the water you have to boil it and clean it, you might be thirst buy you can't drink all the water at once, you have to be aware of the amount of water you are going to drink because you might need more later.\nFood: To get food you need to look for animals or plants, some plants and animals might poisonous so be careful when you try to eat something, if it has a weird color or smells weird dont eat it, it could be poisonous so look for something else to eat\nif you found a big animal like a boar, be careful because if you are too close they might attack you so kill them while they aren't looking at you or when they are asleep, to kill the animal if you dont have any weapon try to knock it out using a rock or\nsomething heavy and throw it at his head  or just hit him with it while he isn't looking at you, now to cook it you will have to make a fire, use anything flamable for it like wood or grass and then look for a sharp rock like a flint,and another rock and\nstrike it against another rock and sparks will come out and if they fall on the wood and grass you will have your fire ready now grab the meat of the animal and if you dont have any where to cook it just\nclaw a stick on it and put it  above the fire and\nit will cook and you will be able to eat it.", ""),
        StaticBook("How2KillMonsters", "[Ghost] The Eternal Librarian", "Monsters\n        and\n   How to Defeat\n        Them\n\n    by Seth Calith\nMonsters roam our lands, and a good fighter has to know how to repel them as well as their strengths and weaknesses. In this book, the reader will find a guide on how to defeat each beast using either a bow or a sword.\nZombies\nZombies are creatures that, wanting to attack, follow you around. With that knowledge, a bow is a useful tool to defeat these monsters. The key to this fight is charging a shot in your bow while running. Once it is charged, shoot the arrow to\nhit it while still charging another arrow.\nIf it is of your preference to use a sword, you can take advantage of the Zombie’s low terrain-calculation properties. Try to stand higher than its head so that it is unable to strike you.\nSkeletons\nThe average skeleton is not as strong as the zombie, yet deadlier because of his fine use of the art of archery and bowmastery. It is recommended to use a sword against such creatures since they are bad in close combat and can only\nshoot at a determined rate.\nTo do such, circle around it fast enough so you can avoid its arrows, which is not recommended unless you are wearing good armor. When it fires, sprint towards it and slash him as hard as you can. With an average iron sword\nand a good reaction, you can defeat it while only taking one arrow, probably to the knee, due to its position upon death. If you can’t dispose of these requirements, you will have to study its rapidness of shot or withstand some more arrows, which is not\nrecommended unless you are wearing good armor.\nFor profficient bow-wielders, a duel can be had against one of these creatures. One should find a place to cover oneself and do so. When it shoots, wait for the sound of the arrow to crash against your\nhiding place and leave it. Shoot it once with a good aim and hide again. It will surrender sooner or later.\nBlazes\nThe blazes’s combat is not very different of the skeleton's, and with the blaze shooting fireballs instead of arrows, three at a time. If using a sword, follow the steps for the skeleton with a slight change. Wait for three shots to be fired,\nnot one, and make sure you don’t step on the fires set ablaze by the blaze itself. Do a similar thing with the bow. You can know when he is about to shoot because it fires up.\nSlimes\nSlimes come in various sizes, and upon death they divide into smaller ones. Use a bow to defeat all but the smallest, that are inoffensive and can be easily defeated with a sword.\nEnderbeings\nThese are strange beasts. They can move from a place to another in a blink, known as teleporting. When fighting one, the only tip I can give you is to jump in some water. Oddly, these beasts are hurt by it, so it will die in its chase.", ""),
        StaticBook("Huangdi Notes:", "Casaga Ranhold", "Casaga's Recollections:\n\nDay 1: \n\nArrived off the boat to Asul. Stepping off was certainly a relief. I'm no sailor. Judging from the map, I reckon I can make it to the ruins of Huangdi in two, maybe three days. So far, I'm optimistic about the journey. I\ncan only hope that they have faith in me too. \n\nDay 2: After a good day's trek, I've settled in a fair alcove in the mountains. Starting to get bleedin' cold though, I'll tell you. Good thing I packed extra provisions, and the old man told me to wrap up.\nDay 3:\n\nFinally! From the map, and the grand, arching pillars of ice that greet me, I can only assume I've reached Huangdi. Nestled within the valley is a small stoney structure, of which I investigated further. In the center lies a stoney column, upon\nwhich are various strange writings. After a momentary series of pacing around, I have established the words:\n\n\"Rest Shou Zhu Huangdi.\"\n\nOf course, I've not a clue what they mean, but\nnonetheless, I figured it to be of some importance. \n                       -\nAs I write this, deep within the ice-clad caverns, I can only describe the beast upon which I was forced to gaze upon. \n\nEven calling it such a thing is debateable: for\nit bore no legs, and had no arms to speak of, nor anything else of the sort. It lay before me, almost resembling that of a repulsive mouth, with horrific seemingly neverending teeth within it.\nI don't know how I'll ever explain what I saw within it.\nAs I peered tentatively into the beast's maw, not only did a most foul stench greet me, sickening me to my stomach, but so did the sight of...well- Nothing. \nNothing lay within that beast, save the pitch black of a bottomless pit.\n\nMaker above, I can\nonly pray that those who lay slain to it are at peace now, and those who created this vile beast have got what they deserve.\nDay 4: \n\nMaker, these caverns are a labyrinth! I feel as though I've spent a week down here, wandering aimlessly. Perhaps I'm\ngoing round in circles, or perhaps I'm just wandering deeper into trouble.\nI pray that I'll at least see daylight before I meet my demise.\n                       -\nWho knows what day it is? Does it even matter any more? \nAfter more aimless wandering,\nI came across this...well, altar I suppose. A skull hung suspended above it, this kind of otherworldy light illuminating the 'room' in the cavern.\nBehind the altar, a crack in the wall of ice allowed me to catch a glimpse into an even deeper cave.\nBones. Huge, huge bones littered the floor of this grand room, as did a central pillar of thick ice. Skulls and skeletons, bones and more were scattered at my feet. \nI do not know what happened in this place.\nBut I can only pray it doesn't happen again.", ""),
        StaticBook("Hugh & Humbert", "Beelzebub", "There once lived two boys within the great streets and slums of Felsen, one named Hugh and the other named Humbert. One boy lived in the south west of the city, while the other lived in the north east. The two boys were remarkably similar.\nThey shared facial features and physical traits, they lived in identical homes, with identical families, with identical pets and identical living circumstances. While identical in all forms, there was one key difference: one boy enjoyed his Scriptures, -\n- and the other did not. \n\nIt was Sunday, and both the boy's parents had great meals laid out upon the tables of their homes, to celebrate as any other Orenian families would a successful week. Remarkably, both meals were the same -\na big pot pie full with vegetables and meats of all assortments. Hugh sat and had his entree laid before him, and waited for his family to sit as well. He recited Grace, and when his family was ready, he enjoyed his meal with them. He finished his meal -\n- and did not pester his mother for dessert. On the other side of the city, Humbert sat and had his entree laid before him. Before his family was sat, Humbert, without Grace, dug into his entree, and feasted like a pig on slop, making a big mess of -\n- himself. He sucked down his pot pie, and immediately thereafter demanded dessert from his poor mother. \"Gluttony today, temperance tomorrow,\" Humbert muttered as he licked his fingers.\n\nAfter their meals, each boy was given free time to do what as -\n- they will. Both journeyed, as usual, to the market square before the Imperial Palace. There, Hugh in the south west and Humbert in the north east, the boys encountered similar situations. Beggars often did their works in the market, and both boys met -\n- an individual beggar. An old lady, clearly sickened with age, pleaded to each boy for a nickel to purchase some bread. Hugh, while only having just earned the nickel yesterday, was quick to hand over his change - Hugh knew, after all, that he could -\n- easily make his nickel back. Humbert, however, refused. Humbert had as well only just earned his nickel, and felt that he had a right to it, a right that the old lady did not have. Humbert told the lady that, once he makes for himself more change, he -\n- will come back and give her a nickel, and kept his nickel for himself. \"Greed today, charity tomorrow,\" Humbert muttered as he walked away from the old lady.\n\nAfter encountering an old lady each, each boy set out to buy a toy from the local toymaker.\nDibley's Den was situated on the south west of the market square, and Bungo's Bunk was situated in the north east. As it was a little later in the day, the lines at each shop were quite long, filled with eager children to buy something to play with.\nHugh entered the line to Dibley's Den and waited his turn like a good boy, understanding that the others got there first, and that waiting in line was not the biggest problem Hugh faced. He waited politely, until he could finally get his toy from Dibley.\nHumbert entered the line to Bungo's Bunk, and immediately became upset with how long the line was. He stomped and stomped, whining like an upset girl, and sniffled and snarled impolitely. Finally, Humbert smacked the boy in front of him in line in the -\n- head, knocking the boy out of line and taking his spot. Humbert finally bought his toy from Bungo. \"Wrath today, patience tomorrow,\" Humbert muttered as he exited Bungo's Bunk with a new teddy.\n\nAfter leaving each respective toy shoppe, each boy -\n- encountered another similar situation. Waiting outside both shops were two boys: one with a very nice and expensive toy, and the other with no toy at all, sniffling due to his inability to buy one. Hugh looked upon the boy without a toy, and sighed, -\n- for he knew down-below the misfortune of the child. Hugh approached the child, and offered him his teddybear, which the child eagerly accepted. Hugh smiled to the boy and waved him off, knowing that some day he could buy the teddybear again.\nHumbert, however, looked upon the boy with an expensive toy, and grew jealous. He desired the other boy's toy, because he knew it was more valuable than his own. He approached the boy, and smacked him upside the head. He took from the boy his expensive -\n- toy, a wooden knight, and walked away. \"Envy today, kindness tomorrow,\" Humbert muttered as he played with the wooden knight.\n\nFinally, it was time to return home. Each boy made his way back, Hugh in the south west and Humbert in the north east. They -\n- entered their homes, did as they would, and finally slipped into their beds. They both reflected upon their day. Hugh ate his meal modestly, and Humbert like a pig. Hugh gave to the old lady a Nickel, Humbert a nasty glare. Hugh waited in line -\n- patiently, while Humbert cut. Hugh gave away his toy, while Humbert stole a more valuable one. You see - Hugh lives each day like it is his last, and takes each action like the Lord is with him. Humbert tells himself every night that he would make up -\n- for his sins the next day. Humbert is a procrastinator when it comes to virtue, and always thinks that he will have a chance to redeem himself. \"Sin today, virtue tomorrow,\" Humbert muttered as he fell to sleep.\n\nNeither boy knew that this night would -\n- be their last. Each boy mysteriously passed away in their sleep, and both were sent before the Lord to recieve judgement. The Lord reviewed Hugh. A good boy Hugh was, diligent when it came to virtue, and a Boy of the Scripture. Of course, Hugh was -\n- granted eternal paradise in the Seven Skies above. The Lord reviewed Humbert. A bad boy Humbert was, lazy when it came to virtue, a boy who did not listen to his Scriptures. Because of Humbert's procrastination, his constant vows of \"...tomorrow,\" -\n- Humbert was cast down to the pits of Hell, to spend the rest of eternity sitting alone, muttering the following words:\n\n \"Heaven today, or              Hell tomorrow!\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Human Babies", "Aerxuis", "Human Babies\nBy Unknown\nCopied By Aerx\nWhere do human babies come from?\nThe mother and father or the soon to be parents, shag a lot until the woman is pregnant. Human shag so much, sometimes the father is not even the\nhusband of the mother. They ‘shag’ everywhere they can, in a bar, on their home, in another's home, in a brothel, outside and so forth.\nWhen a woman gets pregnant, it takes 9 seeds for the baby to be born in the most VILE of experiences for the woman,\nwhere it seems like the nether has been opened in their wombs, and rivers of blood and slime from it, until a bloody crying newborn comes out.\nEven those men that have been in the nether itself, get disgusted by the sight that is the\nhuman birth.", ""),
        StaticBook("Human Babies", "Valmir", "Human Babies\nBy Unknown\nWhere do human babies come from?\n The mother and father or the soon to be parents, shag a lot until the woman is pregnant. Human shag so much, sometimes the father is not even the husband of the mother.\nThey ‘shag’ everywhere they can, in a bar, on their home, in another's home, in a brothel, outside and so forth.\nWhen a woman gets pregnant, it takes 9 seeds for the baby to be born in the most VILE of experiences for the woman, where it seems\nlike the nether has been opened in their wombs, and rivers of blood and slime from it, until a bloody crying newborn comes out.\n\nEven those men that have been in the nether itself, get disgusted by the sight that is the human birth.", ""),
        StaticBook("Human History v1", "Bishop Cordal", "A History of Humanity, From Aegis to Athera\nBy Lord Edward Winter II\nVolume I: Introduction and The First Age of Kings\n\nAuthor's Note: The states of the modern realm were formed in a time of civic unrest caused by militarized cultural differe\nwithin the Fourth Empire. However, while these nations differ in culture, they retain a simple heritage of governing states, so that the modern man may understand the liegestate to which he pays homage. While my cousin Cordal Winter sought to chronicle\nthe timeline of humanity and my fellow writer Procopius sought to color them with his heart, I seek to establish a coherent and continuous history connecting the modern nations to those of the past, and documenting the states through which humanity\nprogressed, to allow the modern man to draw parallels between this time and the times before.\n\n-Edward Winter II\nThe First Age of Kings\n600s-mid 1300s\nOn the Continent of Aegis and Asulon\nKings from the houses of Perea, Sheffield, Tarus, Horen, Marius, de Nurem\nAlso known as: Aegisian Ages, the First Unrest\n\nIn the first years of recorded histor\nformed by the conquering lords of the House Horen, who united many smaller sovereign feudatories into one nation. The last reigning king from the first regnal dynasty was King Daniel Horen, whose seneschal took the crown in a coup, and styled himself King\nPampo Perea. Upon his death, his own seneschal, King Edmund Sheffield, took power. King Edmund was then corrupted by the Undead and tried to eat the flesh of his wife and himself died. He was succeeded by his son, King Enor Sheffield.\n\nThe Sheffield\nDynasty was fraught with inaction and sloth, and in a coup known as the Phoenix Rebellion, Zibaen Vivayean and Eze'kiel Tarus split from the kingdom and formed their own, called Renatus, with Eze'kiel as king. King Enor Sheffield granted the remainder of\nOren to the Hochmeister of the Teutonic Order, Gaius Marius, who named it Hanseti.\n\nHochmeister Gaius Marius died, and he was succeeded by Hochmeister Samuel Bealcrest. The King Eze'kiel Tarus, fearing the military threat of the Teutons,\ndemanded their disbandment. The resolution of the ensuing war occurred when King Eze'kiel met a sariant, a soldier of the Teutonic Order, in a duel and was defeated.\n\nThe Kingdom of Salvus was formed on a nearby island by the dethroned Enor\nSheffield, alongside his wife Dawn Perea. They lived apart from the warfare of the human realm for a short while. On the mainland, King Eze'kiel left his governance to his regent, Reynard Lycian.\n\nThe kingdoms' citizens moved to a new continent when\nundead plague threatened their survival on Aegis, and were joined by the newly founded Kingdom of Seventis. This new kingdom joined Renatus in defending against an assault by the Realm of Hanseti, the dwarven Kingdom of Urguan, the Kingdom of Salvus, the\nmulti-racial Kingdom of Alras, and the Orcish war-state.\n\nUrguan, Salvus, and Hanseti then aligned themselves against Renatus, Seventis, Alras, the Orcs, and a dissident faction within Salvus led by Lorethos Basileus called the Twilight Army. Salvus\ndefeated, and was absorbed into Renatus. The noble House of Hightower was given control of the Salvian realm. Seventis was shortly after stricken with plague and devastated, and its lands too were absorbed into Renatus. The then-Hochmeister Mirtok de\nNurem, following a conflict with Renatus and an internal dissident faction called the Wolverines, surrendered his lands too to Godfrey Horen, a politician who had been handed control of Renatus and later was crowned Emperor of Oren.", ""),
        StaticBook("Humans raid elfs", "Tshilda", "My name is Tshilda. I am a witness of a riad on the wod elven city.\nThe soldiers are wearing iron armor, mostly unenchanted. They were in horses. SOme of them with diamond armor.\nSorry if I misspell some things I was in quite a stresful situation. I think the soldier were human. I was walking to write my book in the beauiful nature when I saw soldiers on the path. They mistook me for a civilian and let me go.\nI walked up the path and met a dark elf. We attempted to diffuse the situation but failed. It was then when a pillar of magic blasted me in the air, with no injuries i ran back to the docks with the dark elf.\nOut of curiosity I went back to record this. I was hidden in the bushes when a human helf a blade to my throat. I headbutted him and ran away. this was all I was able to document as I was too scared to go back.\nIm back, I decied I need to see how it ends. The humans seem to be gone. I barely got into the city. The people are mostly calm. Luckily very few people died. But some lives were lost. The soldiers appeared to be human.\nBut luckily I managed to get out alive.\n\n-Tshilda", ""),
        StaticBook("Hunting Season", "Regale Ba'ikana", "Set up a series of traps in the forest inorder to try and fight the beasts.", ""),
        StaticBook("Hydromancy", "Rosso", "Water: seemingly the simplest of elements, and yet incredibly complex. Water is a necessity of live, needed by all living things, plants and beasts alike. Just as it is the patron of life, water can also pose as the harbinger of eradication.\nDespite our best attempts; we are mortal. A single wave can take everything we own. A flood can contaminate food. A particularly harsh winter can be inescapable. Water contains raw power, a power that a hydromance yearns to wield.\nA hydromancer's training stems from the evocation and control of water itself but not the water that we know. This water can only be found in the void and some say it is not water at all. As all evocationists know, their power comes from the ability\nto control \"mana,\" but I'll leave that topic for others to discuss. After much dedication and training, a hydromancer is able to pull mana directly from the void, shaping it into a water-like substance in our world. This connection to the void is\ndifficult to put into words, as connecting to the void is more of a sensation than something that can be explained. As a mage's training progresses, connecting to the void and evoking the mana within it become more simpler tasks.\nMany mages use a staff when evoking the elements, but the truth is that the staff is not necessary. I, for instance, use a staff topped in mage-gold and carved from elderly jungle wood. This staff is fitting for me because of some of the properties\nthat is possesses, and also because it has been personalized for me. The purpose of my use of a staff is to create a simple, close point for me to concentrate on and evoke water from. When the water is pulled forth, it forms a stream from the end of my\nstaff that maintains itself midair. From here, I can move it, project is somewhere, or allow it to dissipate.\n\nOne thing about water evocation that differs from the other branches of evocation is that water can change states in our world. Novice\nwater evocationists begin with controlling pure water in its liquid form. As a hydromancer becomes more skilled ((approximately late tier 3)), he is able to change the water into ice. Ice is much more suited for battle and defence than liquid water is,\nas it can be used to create walls, freeze doors shut, block oncoming projectiles, as a form of short-distance defense, and as a method of harming others. I have personally mastered a technique of blasting an enemy with water, and then freezing\nthem in their tracks should they be hit. Magical ice is not like that which can be found in our world; void ice does not melt from the heat of the sun or a torch. To break void ice, the hydromance must either completely lose concentration, or another\nmage must do something to break the ice (i.e. a pyromancer melts the ice with magical flames). Water is not often formed into the vapor state, as the wisps of steam are too difficult for even the most trained evocationists to control.\nWater, being able to form any conceivable shape, is only limited by the caster's imagination and fatigue. With proper training, water can be suited for nearly any purpose.\nIntroduction to Hydromancy\n\nWritten by Ev Ar'ahern\nCopied by Rosso\nVaerHaven\n*Strange Numbers\n((15/6/13))", ""),
        StaticBook("Hydromancy", "Thurak'Yar", "Hydromancy\n\nWater appears of one of the simplest elements that inhabit our world, but it is in fact incomprehensively more complex that most people think it is. To fully understand it, one must practice large amounts of time meditating,\nand indeed spending their time around said element- be it by lounging around by a pond, or studying its properties profusely in laboratories. Water is a necessity of life, needed by all living and sentient things, for example Humans, Orcs, Dwarves,\nKharajyr, Elves and also various other animals or plants. Water, also appearing as such a calm element, is also one of the more dangerous; out in the seas, a storm can take out a fleet of ships within moments. One can never fully control\nwater that isn’t evocated, unless of course one is a shaman- In which case the Spirits control the element, and in-avertedly the shaman controls the water too. Despite out best attempts, we are all mortal; we do not live forever, nor do we have amazing\npower like the ascended or the undead back in Aegis. As said before, water can be a very dangerous element; a single flood can wipe out a village just as easily as it might cause it to flourish. The element water contains raw power; a power\nthat all Hydromancers would wish to wield. A Hydromancer’s training consists of learning about the Void, being able to evocate from it, and learning about their element so they can properly evocate it. It takes years on end to learn about evocating a\nsingle element. Water which has been evocated may appear to be the same as the water we have around us, however it is completely different. The water that us Hydromancers evocate can only be created in the void and can brought forth into\nthis world by ourselves. Mana, or life-force, is the power we use to create and transport water from the void, and is vital in most, if not every known magic. If one uses too much of this mana, then they would simply fall unconscious or even die before\nthey complete their task due to overuse or too much exerted force after large amounts of dedication and training; such as learning about the void and Hydromancy, and shaping and creating their mana into an interpretation of water.\nThe connection to the void is rather difficult to explain, however; though once one has learnt about Hydromancy itself then they should be able to understand where we are coming from. One’s connection to the void is more of a sensation than something\nthat can be explained- Like feeling happy, or in love. As a mage’s training progresses, connecting to the void and evocating elements becomes a simpler task. As one would possibly notice, many mages use a staff when they’re casting their magic-\nThis however, is not necessary at all, and only aids the magician by giving them something to focus on while evocating. Water can be evocated in various forms, such as a jet of water, an orb of water, an orb of ice, and other things I have not\ngenerally experimented on yet. Hydromancers which have been learning for a long time will be able to use more things and will be able to explore completely different aspects of the element. Ice is more suitable for offence in a battle, rather\nthan defence, however, generally water evocation itself is more useful to protect the caster, as walls of water or ice can be willed to block a projectile or a strike, or simply to intercept and deflect one,though such must be done at short distance.\nIce that we evoke isn’t the same that we find in our world naturally; it cannot be melted by the heat of the sun or a torch, but it can be melted with the use of Pyromancy. To break the ice, the Hydromancy must both lose connection to the void and have\ntheir creation dissipate, or have a Pyromancer melt it with their fire, or, in the later stages of their training, with steam. \nWater, being able to form any conceivable shape, is only limited to the caster’s imagination and fatigue, and with\nProper training it can be suited for any purpose.\n\n~The Mage Adorellan", ""),
        StaticBook("Hymms of Canon", "Carleton Cassius", "Sanctus\n \n \nSanctus, Sanctus, Sanctus, Dominus Deus Sabaoth.\n \nPleni sunt caeli et terra gloria tua.\n \nHosanna in excelsis.\nBenedictus, qui venit in nomine Domini.\n \nHosanna in excelsis.\n \nAmen.\nLuceat Eis Lux Invicta, Luceat Eis,\nCum tui gratia, Sancte Domine\nLux vestra.\nac ostende eis via tua.\nSanctum sanctorum viam\nAmen\nPater Noster,\n \nBenedictum sit nomen tuum.\nR.Amen\n \nBenedictum sit nomen tuum\nR.Amen\nEt dabit, nobis Messiarum\n \nHoren, Owyn, Godfrey, Seigmund.\nR.Benedicatur nomen eorum\nVenerunt omnes in nomine tuo,\nR.Amen, Amen, Amen.\n \nEt expanderunt verbum tuum et pro illo rogamus, ut pro nobis orent.\nR.Ita faciemus.\nAtque ponant omnes beatos et angelos nostre pietatis testimonium.\nR.Nos permanebunt pio modis.\n \nAmen.\nR.Amen\nAttende Domine, et miserere, quia peccavimus tibi.\nAttende Domine, et miserere, quia peccavimus tibi.\n \nAd te Rex summe,\noculos nostros\nsublevamus flentes:\nexaudi et exaltabitur,\nsupplicantum preces.\nAttende Domine, et miserere, quia peccavimus tibi.\n \nDextera Patris,\nlapis angularis,\nvia salutis,\nianua caelestis,\nablue nostri\nmaculas delicti.\nAttende Domine, et miserere, quia peccavimus tibi.\n \nRogamus, Deus,\ntuam maiestatem:\nauribus sacris\ngemitus exaudi:\ncrimina nostra\nplacidus indulge.\nAttende Domine, et miserere, quia peccavimus tibi.\n \nTibi fatemur\ncrimina admissa:\ncontrito corde\npandimus occulta:\ntua, Redemptor,\npietas ignoscat.\nAttende Domine, et miserere, quia peccavimus tibi.\n \nAttende Domine, et miserere, quia peccavimus tibi.\nDa pacem, Domine, in diebus nostris\nQuia non est alius\nQui pugnet pro nobis\nNisi tu Deus noster.\n \nFiat pax in virtute tua: et abundantia in turribus tuis.\nDa pacem, Domine, in diebus nostris\nQuia non est alius\nQui pugnet pro nobis\nNisi tu Deus noster.\n \nPropter fratres meos et proximos meos loquebar pacem de te:\nDa pacem, Domine, in diebus nostris\nQuia non est alius\nQui pugnet pro nobis\nNisi tu Deus noster.\n \nPropter domum Domini Dei nostri quaesivi bona tibi\nDa pacem, Domine, in diebus nostris\nQuia non est alius\nQui pugnet pro nobis\nNisi tu Deus noster.\nRogate quae ad pacem sunt Palatinus:et abundantia diligentibus te.\n \nDa pacem, Domine, in diebus nostris\nQuia non est alius\nQui pugnet pro nobis\nNisi tu Deus noster.\nGloria Deus, sicut erat in principio et nunc et semper, et in saecula saeculorum. Amen\nDominus regnavit,\ndecorem indutus est:\nIndutus est Dominus fortitudinem,\net praecinxit se.\nEtenim firmavit orbem terrae,\nqui non commovebitur.\nParata sedes tua ex tunc;\nA saeculo tu es.\nElevaverunt flumina, Domine,\nElevaverunt flumina vocem suam,\nElevaverunt flumina fluctus suos,\nA vocibus aquarum multarum.\nMirabiles elationes maris;\nMirabilis in altis Dominus.\nTestimonia tua\ncredibilia facta sunt nimis;\nDomum tuam decet sanctitudo,\nDomine, in longitudinem dierum\nGloria Deus,\net Spiritui Sancto.\nSicut erat in principio,\net nunc, et semper,\net in saecula saeculorum, Amen.\nHosanna Filio Horen,\nBenedictus qui venit\nIn nomine Domini\nRex Oren\nHosanna in excelsis.", ""),
        StaticBook("I Will Be There", "Phaedrus'Yar", "When mountains turn to sand, oceans into canyons, I will be there to take your hand, forever your companion, \n\nSavoring every moment we share, every tender word and touch, petting your golden hair, with you never having too much,\nI am a string without its kite, a coal without its kindling, moonless skies and starless nights, my need for you never dwindling, \n\nWith you I feel whole, as pure as your skin, the tangible essence of my soul, the perfect height to rest my chin,\nYou are forged from the sun itself, a gift just as soft and warm, my definition of a perfect Elf, the eye of my storm, \n\n   To my sundrop,\n             Phaedrus", ""),
        StaticBook("I'm Sorry", "Adira Ba'ikana", "Dear Erwin, \n\nI can't bear to tell you this. But I can't be with you, I don't want to keep lying to myself. Erwin I don't love you, I'm sorry. For this I must break up with you. I love you as a friend and want to stay that way.\nYou are just, not for me. I know you will find an amazing person who is perfect for you, but I'm not it. I do hope you understand.\n\n\n\n               -Adira\n*Other items in the chest includes her key*", ""),
        StaticBook("I. Laying Plans", "Casimir Tide", "I. Laying Plans\n\n1. Sun Tzu said: The art of war is of vital importance to the State.\n\n2. It is a matter of life and death, a road either to safety or to ruin.  Hence it is a subject of inquiry which can on no account be neglected.\n3. The art of war, then, is governed by five constant factors, to be taken into account in one's deliberations, when seeking to determine the conditions obtaining in the field.\n\n4. These are:\n(1): The Moral Law\n(2): Heaven\n(3): Earth\n(4): The Commander\n(5): Method and discipline.\n\n5-6. The Moral Law causes the people to be in complete accord with their ruler, so that they will follow him regardless of their lives, undismayed by any danger.\n7. Heaven signifies night and day, cold and heat, times and seasons.\n\n8. Earth comprises distances, great and small; danger and security; open ground and narrow passes; the chances of life and death.\n9. The Commander stands for the virtues of wisdom, sincerely, benevolence, courage, and strictness.\n\n10. By method and discipline are to be understood the marshaling of the army in its proper subdivisions, the graduations of rank amongst its officers,-\n-the maintenance of roads by which supplies may reach the army, and the control of military expenditure.\n\n10. These five heads should be familiar to every general: he who knows them will be victorious; he who knows them not will fail.\n12. Therefore, in your deliberations, when seeking to determine the military conditions, let them be made the basis of a comparison, in this wise:--\n\n13.\n(1): Which of the two sovereigns is imbued with the Moral Law?\n(2) Which of the two generals has-\n-most ability?\n(3) With whom lie the advantages derived from Heaven and Earth?\n(4) On which side is discipline most rigorously enforced?\n(5) Which army is stronger?\n(6) On which side are officers and men highly trained?\n(7) In which army is there the greater constancy both in reward and punishment?\n\n14. By means of these seven considerations I can forecast victory or defeat.\n\n15. The general that hearkens to my counsel and acts-\n-upon it, will conquer: let such a one be retained in command.  The general that hearkens not to my counsel nor acts upon it, will suffer defeat: let such a one be dismissed.\n\n16. While heading the profit of my counsel, avail yourself also of any helpful-\n-circumstances over and beyond the ordinary rules.\n\n17. According as circumstances are favorable, one should modify one's plans.\n\n18. All warfare is based indeception.\n19. Hence, when able to attack, we must seem unsable; when using our forces, we must seem inactive; when we are near, we must make the enemy believe we are far away; when far away, we must make him believe we are near.\n20. Hold out baits to entice the enemy.  Feign disorder, and crush him.\n\n21. If he is secure at all points, be prepared for him.  If he is in superior strength, evade him.\n\n22. If your opponent is of choleric temper, seek to irritate him.-\nPretend to be weak, that he may grow arrogant.\n\n23. If he is taking his ease, give him no rest.  If his forces are united, separate them.\n\n24. Attack him where he is unprepared, appear where you are not expected.\n25. These military devices, leading to victory, must not be divulged beforehand.\n\n26. Now the general who wins a battle makes many calculations in his temple ere the battle is fought.  The general who loses a battle makes but few calculations beforehand.-\nThus do many calculations lead to victory, and few calculations lead to defeat: and grievously if no calculations at all.  It is by attention to this point that I can foresee who is likely to win or lose.", ""),
        StaticBook("I: Iron Door", "Vicelin", "Contents:\n1. The Iron Door (Full)\n2. Iron Door (Middle)\n1. Whole Iron Door Guard\n\nThe form is leant forward, with the rear leg straightened and the front legs knee bent. The left arm is bent, with the hand firmly holding the pommel with an overarm grasp. The right arm is straight with the hand loosely\ngrasping the top of the hilt just under the crossguard. The grip for the right hand is underhand, with the thumb resting along the edge of the crossguard. The posture is straight with the chest out and the shoulders tense, ready to strike.\nYou can use this guard against any other hand-held weapon, as long as your have a good blade which is not excessively long. A regular 40 inch bladed longsword will do the trick. A good blade in this case would be one that is hard to break and must not\nbe too long due to the fact your defence relies on bringing your blade quickly to the center. Like a slamming door.\n\n[A diagram is sketched here, showing a man using the full iron door stance viewed from the side and front.]\nOnce your opponent has attacked, cover by bringing your sword across through the centre, keeping your pommel close to your body as you swing the flat of the sword from right to left or vice versa. You may also thrust once the blade reaches the point at\nwhich the tip is directed at your opponent.\n\nYou can defend against many blows which are not overhead or underhand by covering and passing forwards.\n2. Middle Iron Door Guard\n\nThe sword is grasped with the hands in a similar fashion to the full Iron Door, but the sword is pointed directly forwards, with the tip nearly touching the floor. The leading leg is also bent more intensely than the\nfull iron door, with the back of the hand which holds the hilt near the crossguard touching the inner knee of the leading leg. Only use this guard when your sword is longer than that of your opponent. If your opponent is using this guard, seek to use one\nof the counter stances, as if one tries to assault the middle iron door which is already prepared they will surely be killed or wounded in the process. The middle guard is perfect for powerful thrusting. If attacked, beat the sword upwards\nwith the flat of the blade and come back down to cleave into the head or arms of your opponent.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ice Golem Report", "Dougstalicious", "Lucienists were attacked by a frost golem 5th of the Grand Harvest. The monster made quick work of our gates and the boiling oil had little to no effect, it seemed to let out a shockwave-like scream every few seconds, injuring us.\nThe beast is rather slow, but capable of large bursts of speed.\n\nIt is made out of some kind of grey/blue stone, almost like an obelisk of some sorts. In it's center is has some kind of runic markings that glow occasionally. It could be perma ice.\nBrother Quinlan says the injury he received from the beast felt like a wall of ice hitting him.\n\nBrother Cendrus managed\nto trick the beast and lead it into the scourge prison, locking it in.", ""),
        StaticBook("Idle Hands", "Aluuvia", "=======================            Idle Hands\n      A fictional tale\n=======================\nThere once lived a young boy by the name of Sergio. Sergio had been born to peasantry, as many often are. His mother a milkmaid and his father a lumberjack, Sergio's life seemed doomed to toil. Though born into a life of labor, Sergio was a lazy boy,\nand more often than not would refuse to do nigh anything. \n\n   \"Sergio, fetch me a milk pail.\" His mother would plead whilst sat upon her stool, trying to keep their milk cow calm. But Sergio made no motion to move, his idle hands sat\nstill in his lap. He would only be brought to move when his father delivered a quick smack to the back of his head, and at this he would groan and rise, albeit slowly, to the task at hand.\n\n   \"Bring some wood for the fire, son.\" His father would ask,\nwhilst sat upon his rocking chair, relaxing inside after a long day's work. But Sergio made no motion to move, his idle hands sat still in his lap. He would only be brought to move when his mother delivered a quick pinch to his arm, and at this he would\ngroan and rise, albeit slowly, to the task at hand.\n\n   Eventually Sergio's parents grew sick of his slothfulness, having suffered through it many years, and sent him away to serve the Lord of the land with his sword arm.\nThough they did not see fit to warn the Lord of their son's idle hands.\n\n   Sergio was, as is to be expected, useless to the other men at arms. They sat him into the gatehouse, to raise and lower it for visitors, though even that\nhe only did after a long while, grasping the lever with his idle hands, and turning it with a groan and a roll of his eyes.\n\n   There came a time that the Lord of the land was required to call upon all his men at arms, even those useless.\nFor weeks going on months there had been disappearances along the main road. Whole caravans found toppled and torn through, yet not a thing missing from them. The only thing they lacked were the men who had manned them.\nSergio was set on patrol with other men from the town, and so travelled north along the road into colder lands, in search of a caravan that there had been no sign of. It was deep into their journey they caught the first sign of it; Splintered wood and\nscattered baubles, half-buried in the powedery snow. Yet once again there was not a soul in sight, corpse or otherwise. Yet through the thickening woods they spotted a trail of broken branches, snapped twigs and a rushing divet in the snow, leading deeper\nstill into the woods.\n\n   Hesitantly the men followed the newly-made path.\n\n  A fog rolled into the woods, seeping through the spaces between the trees, thick and grey. It seemed to surround the men, ushering them\nforwards, further into the deep dark of the woods.\n\n   The Captain of the guard caught sight of it first, looming as they entered a clearing. Here the fog was thickest, and the grey of it stained the freshly-fallen snow a sickly dark.\nIt was then they realized the fog was not of mist, but of ash, as the substance burned their eyes and throats. And there in the center of the clearing loomed the source; an ashen wraith, three times the size of the average man.\nAs it laid it's eyes, orbs of burning fire, upon the men a hissing sound arose, which escalated in pitch and tone to a deafening screech, unlike anything any of the men had heard before. The Captain rushed forth first, in effort to dispatch the beast\nwith haste. But as he tread through the ash-stained snow, wisps of the stuff thickened within the fog and clenched about his limbs. As the screech grew, so too did the black at the heart of the beast's figure; it's gaping maw opened wide, and in but a\nmoment the Captain was drawn forth and made to vanish into that inky black. \n\n   There was only a short pause before the other men rallied, charging at the beast with either rage or fright burning in their bellies.\nAll of the men save Sergio, whose idle hands had not yet even reached for his blade.\n\n   The wraith made short work of the men, all of them vanishing into the thick of the ash and smog that now permeated the forest clearing.\nThen the thing shifted its form, now larger than before, as it shifted across the clearing to tower over the last, Sergio. It seemed to give a tilt of it's head, the flame in it's eyes angling to one side. Sergio had not bothered to place his hand on\nthe hilt of his blade, nor make any other motion, though he was not frozen from fear. The wraith and the man faced one another in an eerie silence, the screeching having long since faded.\nAnd there came a crackling from the wraith's maw, as the corners of it lifted upwards, creating the macabre visage of a man's cheeks slit through to create an unnatural and bloody smile.\nAnd Sergio's hands were idle no more.", ""),
        StaticBook("IECS Report ASUL", "Atlas", "Mission report for the Imperial Exploration and Cartography Society.\n\nAsul, South of Alexandria. Coordinations; 1078 1724.\n\nExplore and document ruins.\nExcitement burns in the stomach at first glance of these marvelous wonders of stone.\n\nThe first ruin, laying flat on the ground with a seemingly decapitated/disformed head represents a body of a large reptilian. Possibly a dragon.\nThe nearest ruin, sticking out of a large tree is recognizable and thus unidentified. It seems the platform has polluted the area it sticks out of of the tree.\n\nThe largest ruin likely represents a fallen warrior, holding a large sword tipped to the\nground by a large stone figure laying on the mountain side. The warrior's face is that of a supposed bird. A wonder to be found only on the Isles of Axios.\n\nThe furthest ruin in the valley represents a beheaded snake.\nIn the corner of the mountain, a large ruin of a short humanoid-like creature. A rat seems to lead before it.\n\nUpon further exploration, no more ruins could be found.\nIn summary, the ruins seem to have depicted a fight between a humanoid bird-like\nwarrior and two reptilian creatures, with a short giant/creature watching overhead.\n\nThe journey to the location wasn't long, yet locating it was rather difficult, judging by the unspecific directions of south of Alexandria.\nThe ruins must tell a tale behind them, and further investigation shall be taken in place to learn more of the wondrous site.\n\nAtlas Delevoye in report to John Lyons.", ""),
        StaticBook("IHBH:SA", "Ser Paul Ryan", "- - - - - - - - - - - -         It's Hard\n    Being Handsome:\n\n  How to survive in \n  Athera, and other\n        life tips\n- - - - - - - - - - - - \n   By: Ser Pavl Ryan\nWith special foreword         by Emperor \n   Tuvya Carrion I\nTABLE OF CONTENTS: \n\n- Foreword\n- Authors Note\n- Chapters I-V\n- About the Author\nFOREWORD\n-------------------\n\nMeeting Ser Paul Ryan, much less becoming good personal friends with him, will most certainly be one of the most defining moments of my life. I've seen much in my time as the Emperor of Athera's greatest nation, but\nnever have I seen such strict dedication to greatness as I have in Paul. Whether it was making him part of my privy council, calling upon him to lead a heroic charge in times of war, or simply asking the favor of his attendance to my young daughters\nnameday party, I knew I could count on a man as loyal and reliable as Paul. Reading his first book, as well as getting a sneak peak at his upcoming biography, granted me a different outlook on life, and how I live it. Never before have I experienced such\na thrilling page turner as I have when reading \"It's Hard Being Handsome\". I recommend this fantastic encyclopedia of majesty to all men and women, regardless of age, race or gender, who one day wish to become sucessful.\nAUTHORS NOTE\n-------------------In my times of travel around the land of Athera, I've come to learn a great deal of things, both through speaking to some of the oldest and wisest masters of \nmany skills, and trial and error as I blundered\nmy way through city after city, town after town. I've learnt how to fight great mythical beast, how to drink a \ndwarf under the table, how to hide from halflings, sell my legitimate wares to all kinds of illigitimate folk, and a great deal of other skills\n. But if there's \none thing I've learned above all else, it's this; \nIt's hard \nbeing handsome. \n\nHi, I'm Ser Paul Ryan, and this is my book.\nMany times through the years, I've been approached by great kings and lowly merchants, all desperate for my advice. I've been the honored guest in many foriegn \ncourts, and handed out justice in my own lands.\nI recieved many great awards, both for my continued service to House Carrion and Oren as a whole, and for helping\nout the distressed through all kinds of situations. Yet I soon found out that, no matter how great I was (and trust me, I was great),\nmy life always seemed....\nempty. By the time I had done all of these great things and achieved knighthood and gentry status, all at the ripe old age of 18, I decided to write down my \nadventures, and, more importantly,\nthe rules with which I've come to live life. In the following pages, you too will learn to live by these rules. Good luck, friend,\nand I hope you enjoy it!\nCHAPTER ONE (I)\n-------------------Find friends:\nOne of the earliest lessons I learned in life was this; EVERYTHING'S better with friends, friend. Becoming close acquaintance to esteemed men and women like the \nruling class of Oren,\nor simply the pal of the local drunk and homeless, friends help you through all sorts of trouble. Need a place to stay? Fine a friend. Need\na loan? Find a friend. Need help breaking Goldsteins' stinking knees, because he still hasn't paid you back\nfor that time in the brothel? Find a friend. No matter\nwhere I go in all of Athera, I can always count on finding room and board, courtesy of my good pals. If you really think you're a step above the rest, you can even\ntry to become one of MY friends,\nand join Paul's Pals™, my adventuring group of heroes. For better or for worse, helping out someone in need of a hand can result \nin some good luck coming your way down the road. Remember my original and trademarked saying:\nA friend in need is a friend indeed, who, in the future, will owe you™. \n\nCHAPTER TWO (II)\n-------------------Find fortune\n\nOne of the greatest assets any man has in lifes' adventure is his coin purse.\nMany a schlub can be bribed, and it never hurts to have the pocket coinage to buy that\nfancy new automatic crossbow, or perhaps donate to your favorite local political party. But how does one obtain such vast, impressive wealth like that owned by\nthe plutocrats of our age, such as Emperor Tuvya, or Ser Paul Ryan? Well, friend, let me tell you; hard work, creativity, and a good bit of honest borrowing can go far. I myself made my first fortune when I founded CapCo™, Oren's premier\nentreprenuerial company, which now is valued at roughly 500,000 minas. By working hard to achieve\nyour dream, and marketing your products correctly, you'll soon build the capital needed to further your endeavors, like\nperhaps launching a new, better company. Good\nbusiness partners are a must have, and I myself continue to hold close correspondance with my good friend and investor, Jacob Goldstein, of Goldstein & Company. After I safely handed over CapCo™\nto the care of my board of directors, my next startup companies, Paul's Pawn & Picking™, Paul's Tonics & Powders™, Paul's Ghost Hunting™, \nand Paul's Travelling Stall™all quickly flourished under my careful experience. Need some help starting down the\npath to vast wealth? Try finding a local investor\nto give you a startup fee, and bleed that sucker dry! If you need some immediate cash, perhaps to pay back the loan shark who threatened to break your fabulous \ncheekbones, consider\nborrwing someone\nsomeone elses valuables and using those to pay. Remember, friends: It's not illegal if you're not caught. \n\nCHAPTER THREE (III)\n-------------------Find your talents\n\nIt never helps to have good qualities, friend.\nI myself am incredibly handsome and creative, and possess a myriad of skills that would make a jack of all trades cry\nuncle. But how can you exploit the talents you have? Simple; by deceptively manipulating others. Are you a heavy hitter? Consider\nstrong arming your way into the \nlocal tavern, and borrowing some of his ale to sell later at a profit. Small and sneaky? Deceptively sneak into a store after hours, and help yourself to the register. \nOr perhaps you're like me,\na reknown inventor throughout the lands, sought after for his political savviness and charm. Remember that in this life, NOTHINGS free. Make\nsure you charge the right amount to give that little girl the location you saw her lost dog in, or to hide that\nhalfling running from some hungry orcs. If you don't \ncapitalize on all of your chances to make yourself more marketable, you'll never make it in our dog-eat-dog world.\nCHAPTER FOUR (IV)\n-------------------Find adventure\n\nSure, friend, you may be able to talk the talk, but can you walk the walk? It doesn't matter if you've accomplished all of these other steps to becoming great, if you don't USE them! Go out on the\nroad, and venture into lands previously uncharted. Have a drink at that edgy tavern, or consider stopping by your good dwarf friends\nto see what they've been up to lately. Seeing the world is its own lesson, one that anyone can take, and for free.\nLearn how to fight or talk your way out of \nany situation by haggling with the Vanirs over the price of a fish, or wrestling with Orcs in their sand pits. Awe the local milkmaid with tales of your completely\nlegitimate exploits, or spend a night sweeping\nat a tavern to cover your room and board. Life in our world is uncertain, friend, but it's always worth checking around the \ncorner to see what kind of trouble you can get into. Fall down and break a leg, or wake up without memory in the temple of those\nmonks who definitly enchanted this\nholy water I can sell you at a discount price? Get back up, and try again. If you're ever torn between relative safety, or a possible adventure, ask yourself one \nthing: What would Paul do?\nCHAPTER FIVE (V)\n-------------------Putting it all together, and surviving the process\n\nYes, friend, it's challening to learn how to be as great as me, and even more challenging to try, but the results will always pay off. By combining\nmy advice with\na little salt-of-experience you gain on your own, you'll quickly find yourself developing into the man or woman you only dreamed of becoming. Go out there, learn\nyour good qualities, get rid of your bad ones, and make\nsome good memories while you're at it. Work your way from the gutter to a palace, and go from using that\nrusty dagger to defend yourself to summoning the most powerful of magics. You will fail at first, friend. After all, no one is perfect.\n(well, actually, speak for yourself, bub)\nbut the lessons you learn in your failure will help you in years to come. Inevtiably, the great success you'll achieve will make the lesser peons\nof this great realm jealous of you. They'll wish they had your\ncreativity, your work ethic, and above all, your dashing good looks. There's a great deal I've learned\nmyself in my many adventures, most of all I've found that, yes, it really IS hard, being handsome. But would I ever give it up?\nNot for anything in this world, friend. \n\n- Ser Paul Ryan\nSome Quick Tips! \n\nWant to get better at those strange moments of your life, when everyone suddenly has magical symbols above their heads, and people start hitting each other? Try \npracticing in your free time with some pals and a wooden\nsparring sword, or, if worse comes to worse, learn how to flee effectively! To fight another day, of course.\nDon't try so hard to win all of the time, friend! In gambling, tussling, or even a friendly debate, losing can often yield more than winning.\nIf you see Paul or one of his many friends throughout the land, consider stopping for a chat or challenge with them, rather than strangely running and jumping by.\nPick a skill or service, become talented in it, and learn how to make a living through it. Sell your paintings or swords in a stall, or on the road, like me! Get a job as a petty laborer to garner experience, before ultimately starting a rival\ncompany up with stolen secrets, and crush your former boss!\nGo outside every once in a while, friend. And I don't just mean leaving your hovel in Athera.\nHave fun, friend. What else are we here for?\n- About the Author - -------------------Ser Paul Ryan is a successful warrior, statesman, and inventor of great reknown. Founder and CEO of CapCo™, and a number of other popular brands, such as \nPaul's Pawn & Picking™,\nPaul's Travelling Stall™, Paul's Pals™, and Paul's World Fair™, he was born in the small village of Wesconsen, before squiring under Boris Carrion III. \nKnighted by the late Emperor Peter Chivay for valor extraordinare in the field of battle.", ""),
        StaticBook("II: The Lady", "Vicelin", "1. Lady's Guard\nThis is the first stance which will feature a back stance. It is similar to the regular footwork except in reverse. The reason for this is to allow for the wind-up of powerful blows. It is also helpful when fighting multiple opponents who surround you.\nThe leading foot is pushed out to the back and side in the direction of the opponent, but not completely aimed at them. The other leg is bent at the knee slightly, with the foot flat on the ground, pointing to the side.\nThe back is straight and the left arm is raised and gripping the hilt just above the pommel firmly. The other arm is bent and gripping the hilt near the crossguard, which sits just over the right shoulder, with the blade being across the back and the tip\npointing in the same direction as the leading foot and downwards. To simplify, it looks like one is about to strike a ball as hard as possible with a bat.\nThe stance is good for both defence and offence as well as the threat of power. You can use these assets to force the defender to leave his guard because if he remains in the same place he will surely be struck by your full-tilt swing or thrust.\nThis stance can also be used with a poleax.\n\nIf you are left handed you may do this exact stance but mirrored to your liking. Keep in mind, however, that in a fight it is obviously necessary to frequently swap the side on which you hold\nthe blade and point your feet due to the fact the target will move and if you make a swing the momentum will carry you off balance, forcing you to find a different guard.", ""),
        StaticBook("III: The Window", "Vicelin", "1. The Window Guard\nAnother back stance guard. The leading foot is bent at the knee with the toes pointing away from the opponent. The rear leg is straightened and tense, with the toes lifting the heel off the ground, the outer side of the foot pointed at the opponent.\nOne should be leaned in only slightly, and the forearms should be crossed at the middle, with the arm closest to the opponent grasping the hilt near the pommel, which points away from the opponent and the other arm reaching over to hold the hilt near the\ncrossguard. The blade is leveled, with the tip pointed at the upper body of the opponent.\n\nThe hands should be grasping the hilt from different sides.\n\nThe window can counter any upper body guard.\nThe window, I find, is most useful for testing the guard of your opponent to check how well versed he is and if you do not know the guard he uses, the nature of its operation. It is a perfect guard for feinting.\nThe best strike using the Window would be thrust and you can riposte and break guards easily from here as well as shift into half-swording with great ease.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ikail Bail", "Bell Sano", "Bail for Ikail. Terms of release are fifty mina bail, and appearing for a court date.\n\nPenned by:\nBell Sano\n\nSigned by:\nIkail", ""),
        StaticBook("Ikuras", "Thurak'Yar", "“And so it was that (Ikuras) was imprisoned, entomed by his rothers in fire and earth.” -Diary of Grigory Adeveci\nThere are few things in Ancient History more mysterious, more dark, than the tale of Ikuras, the Daemon of Fear.\nWhat little we know is written in the Diary of Grigory Adeveci, a monk who was by all accounts insane. However, it is the belief of some that Ikuras is very real, and that his story is true.\nThe following is an analysis of Grigory’s Writing.\nThe journal begins fairly orginarily.\n“Greetings, my name is Grigory Adeveci. I am writing this in my little room in the abbey. All is quiet now here at night and I believe it is safe to bring the artefact out. Allow me to describe this artefact to you; it is a small key, appearing as\na dagger. It looks to be forged of a crystal material, and shimmers darkly when I turn it towards the light. Tomorrow I will study it more.”\nRecords suggest that Grigory was a part of the abbey’s archaeological studies, and collected\nthis artefact, this key, on a dig. The next passage is where Grigory begins experiencing odd dreams.\n“Last night I had a vision. The world was drenched in a shadow. It looked like a damp, heavy shadow. I could no see through it, only hear the mad laughter from underneath. I do not think the artefact is safe to show anyone else. I will have to see\nwhat happens upon my sleep tonight.”\nThe next day the journal goes on.\n“My nightmares last night were nothing short of disturbing. I was the land, and I could not see. But I felt things, crawling on my back. Hairy, gaunt, rotting. I must destroy the artefact or I will be unable to sleep.”\nThere are varying arguments addressing why Grigory did not simply remove the artefact from his presence. The most prevalent belief is that he was already turning mad. This is Grigory’s last sane entry.\n“My dreams were good, heavenly last night. I dreampt that a thousand lights came down from the heavens and sucked away the darkness. I do not know where they imprisoned it, but the darkness was locked away somewhere. The fear was locked away.\nHere Grigory appears to have gone completely mad. This is several weeks after his sane entry. His writings get longer and longer periods of time between them.\n“I don’t know why I tried to break myself. He told me it was bad but I did it anyway. I had to try and escape from myself. I should have known I should have known I should have known I would shatter. The fear is eating me now.\nI see my blood on its teeth teeth teeth.”\nThe repeating of phrases is very present in the insanity writings. Always he repeats something three times.\nThe second line in this next entry is oddly out of place, it is assumed that this obscure prophecy came to him in a bout of sanity.\n“The fear fear fear is eating me and I don’t know where the lights made it gone the light made him gone gone gone. And so it was that he was imprisoned, entombed by his brothers in fire and earth. Ikuras. From the same divine spark\nas Iblees and Aeriel. Creator preserve me it said the name is said the name name name it must never say the name.”\nAt this point Grigory constantly refers to himself as “It.” This next entry is the final one, written one month after the last.\n“They crawl all over it. The wolf, the spider, the corpse. It is the First Continent, and it feels them on its back back back. Now it is the Second Land, and it is free free free of the fear fear fear. But now it is the Third Place, and it is\nback back back. It is feeling the wolf the spider the corpse again again again. The key is the prison. The key is the prison. The key is the prison.”\nDisturbingly, the last three sentences, the repeating of “The key is the prison” is written in Grigory’s own blood. Records show that he committed suicide after this last entry.", ""),
        StaticBook("Illusion Magic", "Sorairogyoku", "The Art of Illusion Magic\n\nAlong with the sub sections of it.\n\n-Sensory Magic\n-Mental Magic\n-Cognatism\nSensory Illusion\n\nAs of today it's not very understandble in it ways, as all magics have the under Illusion magic has the ability to create a illusion of some type, this one is the best at making them. As they last longer and tend\nto be more detailed.\nThey can sway the 5 senses of any human, elf, of what ever creature it might be. Making them hear, touch, small, see, or taste something the not really there. Or replace the item with another. A person who is master at this skill can get any men to drink\nmercury. It requires hard work, and back ground information on the magic, really magic itself to use this magic. So it's not a type that begginers should start on.\nMental Magic\n\nHave a unique ability to connet other mines, or to invade them. They also have the power to create illusions, but they're not as powerful as a sensory illusion mage's. This too is not a magic for noobs.\nThis also requires background information before a student can even think of using it. A mental mage can break into a person mine and listen to their thoughts by enter thought into the person's head (normally in the person's own voice) to sway them to a\nideal.\nCognatism\n\nLast of the three sub types. Here the mage can split their mines into smaller one to preform a purpose. It's a complaccated magic, hard to discribe. And user that uses cognatism magic cannot use mental magic since they do not mix.\nOne must understand the magic before seeking a teacher. This is no easy task. Most time the magic is used to collect information across an area. Where revelation happen for the user.\nMisunderstanding of Illusion Magic\n\n-Users cannot do mine control, only put thoughts into people heads.\n-This magic cannot effect the pshical plane of the land, they are only illusions\n-Normally illusion come from the person's\nown experience. So you can make a illusion of somebody dying since, well you didn't die.", ""),
        StaticBook("Immortal Spirits", "Thurak'Yar", "Immortal Spirits\n\nA list of the Greater Spirits inhabiting the Immortal Realm and what they represent. This may change, given time, and will be updated as new spirits come to power.\nVotar- The spirit of the hunt, commonly shown as a giant, bloodied wolf. Praised by the Phrase Glougaz Votar.\n\n      /\\_==_/\\\n      | /o   o\\ |\n      \\         /\n       \\       /\n        \\ *.* /\n          \\ /\nEnrohk- The spirit of bloodlust, savagery and war, often shown as a bastard sword covered in blood. \n        \n         /\\\n         |  |\n         |  | \n         |....|\n         |. .|\n      `==8=='\n          ||\nShezept- The spirit of revenge, plots and stealth, depicted as a woman with a lower body of a snake. \n      \n        O\n       -|-\n   ^\\_\\\\_\n   \\____/\nJevex- Spirit of order, hard work and self sacrifice, shown as a giant hammer. He's a deadly enemy to the spirit Shezept.\n \n     [======]\n     [==|  |==]\n         ==\n         ==\n        |.--.|\n         ==\nIxli- The spirit of forbidden knowledge, truth and judgement. Depicted as an eye, he provides knowledge as the cost of sanity. \n\n       |/  \\|\n      |  (.)  |\n       |\\  /|\nOgrol- Spirit of despair, sapped strength and entrapement, shown as a cage full of writhing bodies. He tries to lock up all who summon him.\n\n       ______\n       | | |  | | |\n       =<< >>=\n       | | |  | | |\n      ========\nKor- The spirit of the dead, depicted as a cloaked man with an open hand.\n          _\n          |O\\\n           |-''\n          /\\\nAnkrus- Spirit of the sea, fishermen and safe travels, often shown as an aquatic woman wielding a spear. \n\n           () |\n           oo/\n           \\/\n           /\\\n           \\/\nArwa- Spirit of fertility, harvest and farming, commonly shown as a plump female with over seven hundred breasts.\n \n           ()\n         /.oo.\\\n        /o.oo.o\\\n        |o.o.o.o.o|\n        \\_____/\n         [|]    [|]\nAnyhuluz- Spirit of destruction, malicious intent and internal strife, shown as a warrior covered in open wounds.\n\n         O   ^\n       /(`)-`|\n         [|]\n         /\\\nAkezo- Spirit of health, vitality and healing, depicted as a winged whale surrounded by a blue aura.\n\n   (\\./)\n     \\\\_/--^--.\n      =.    \"~\"   )\n        \\______/\nPaxahru- Spirit of arrogance and stupidity, depicted as a boasting fool.\n\n        /**\\\n       ( ^^ ) \n        /--\\ \n        |`~~'|\n        ====\n        \\/\\/\n         |   |\nUblulhar- Spirit of hope an new beginnings, shown as a tree sapling bursting from the ground. \n\n       _____\n      {~~~~}\n     {~~~~~}\n      {~~~~}\n       {~| |~}\n          | |\n       ~~~~~\nGhorza- Spirit of travel, depicted as an ever turning wheel.\n\n       /----\\\n      / /--\\ \\\n      |  |<:::::)|  |\n      \\ \\--/ /\n       \\----/\nRolfizh- Spirit of assassinations and poison, depicted as a dagger with poison dripping from it.\n\n        /\\\n        |  | \n        |  |\n       =||||=\n         ||\nTrokorl- The spirit of engineering, machinery and building. Depicted as a goblin with a goblin with goggles and a hammer.\n\n       {o o}\n        \\-/P\n         |. |/\n         |. |\n         ==\n        /  \\\nLuara- The spirit of the moon, often shown by the symbol of a pale, white wolf.\n\n        \\___(>\n         |===/\n         |    |\nRamakhet- Spirit of the desert, barren lands and sand. He is never seen, and therefore is rarely ever depicted as something other than his name. He has sworn to scour the earth of all life for all time.\n       ~~~~~\n      Ramakhet\n       ~~~~~\nKrathol- The spirit of pain, suffering and starvation. Depicted as a pile of dry bones.\n   \n      (------)\n      (------)\nVeist- Spirit of illusion, tricks and thievery, depicted as a goblin with four eyes.\n\n      (:_:)\n      \\| |/\n       /\\\n       |  |\nFreygoth- Spirit of the wind and wild animals. He takes