        StaticBook("Messages of Ice", "Baldin Frostbeard", "He told meh ah could\nshape tha world\nweth mi mind.\nThat ah could create\na whol new life.\nHe taught meh how\nto move tha stars,\none at ha time until\nnew constellations\nformed in tha sky\nund thoght ef\nendless possibilites\nshone en ma eyes.\n------------------\nWhen Wyrvun\nes in tha midst,\ndefeat\ndoesn't exist.\n-------------------When tha dark clouds cover the sun, and whn ye serch fer hope, yet find non. Place all yer trust in Wyrvun, yell neva go wrong. He will help ye sail roight through tha storm.\n-------------------Ova mah years meditaten an conectin weth Wyrvun he taught meh maneh thengs. One ef these thengs is tha when someting bad happens ye hav three choices. Ye can eithe let et define ye, let et destroy ye, or ye can let et strengthen ye.\n-------------------Mah lord Wyrvun came to meh and said:\nTruth can neva be sacrificed in tha name of peace, fer ther can be no peace without rightiousness.\n\nMay tha rightiousness of Wyrvun guide us.\n-------------------\nTha will of Wyrvun es not always easy but et es always roight.\n-------------------Ye called meh out into the blizzard,\nan ah followed out ef devotion.\n\nNeva knowing you wer testing mah service, Still ye told me it's neva too late.\n-------------------May tha righteousness of Wyrvun guide ye...", ""),
        StaticBook("Mice Are Nice!", "Dooble_Brick", "A Dedicants Poem On Mice\nBy Milly Turner\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~MICE\nI think mice are rather nice;\nTheir tails are long, their faces small;\nThey haven't any chins at all.\nTheir ears are pink, their teeth are white,\nThey run about the house at night;\nThey nibble things they shouldn't touch,\nand no one seems to like them much,\nbut I think mice are nice!", ""),
        StaticBook("Midget's Journal", "Berilac Goldworthy", "\"Tichal Dore\". What a strange name. Last thing you would expect to come out of a Halfling mind. But the ones who came before us, still had a long way to becoming what we are now. If only I could get a hold on a few more pages that day. Bloody Variela.\nToday I searched through the Sky Temple's archives, hopeful that the Wizard's writtings would induce any understanding on the strange language. Genesis is clear, but I'm not an Aengul to know each and every tongue our kind has ever flapped. Cerulin it is.\nAnd yet again I found poetry. Poetry! The forest folk may be gifted in these scribbles of theirs, but by the Creator's grace, they're more fond of rhymes then a Tooke past kissin' a fanny. Looks like it's not them that will answer my questions. Uruk will.\nThe caravan master was obviously concerned for the safety of his passengers and more so, the safety of his goods, meaning we didn't get too close to the Krug's descendants homeland. It's still close enough for me to get there. These weary two shoes know\nwhat to do. They did for quite a long time. Still on a run, huh? Running from punishment to duty. Hardly a common thing to be done by the likes of me. If... if I don't find the translation I am looking for, I might aswell try and seek out the Gimblewood.\nStatue of Chivay. The races of Men truly enjoy their ancestors. They hold them in praise, in cult even. Their heroes achieve immortality through their deeds, service to their people. We merely remember everybody's aunt and stepfamily, we take to\ngenealogy to prove who we are, and who we want to be. But even our own ways have proven wrong and were replaced. And they were, several times in our history. How can we look into the future without having any ground to stand at? Anything inwards?\nGimblewood. Not exactly as homely as Akovia, not exactly as outlandish as Laurelin. Filled with prime scent of ale and feverishly loud laughters, the place would be macroscale tavern was it not for the good manners of the folks. Half-mind I was expecting\nsomething different, something completely... dreamy. Isaias never taught me much about my real people. Is it a surprise the only idea of the wee folk was the one a child, and then one of a travel-weary dreamer?\nIt will take some time getting used to. But at least it is calm, and it is well outside of the Imperium's tumultous ambitions. It'll be a good place to stay for a moment and to work. But I know that it will never be a home I dreamed of.\nA passing of greed. That's how he called it. A trouble to be overcome Curious little fellow. Guess I have a bad habit of getting along with vagrants like me. Still didn't get a word with the sheriff - or the mayor. Not that I'm in a rush to do that.\nDaemons. A name that springs an innate fear to minds of many of us, descendants. For beings of Light, it was their ranks that still sired the Bane of Skies, and that shame did not come to be easily forgotten. It's surprising how eagerly do we forget our\nown history, but that accursed sentence of shame and dishonour may last for as long as the Descendants live on. Thoughts aside, I'd still fancy meeting one of these, even with how bloody close dwarves are to praying to them.\nSnowy peaks and a snow-white blonde ma'am. T'was a close call today. Wouldn't want to scare the wee lass with my creeping round her manor. Wintervine does it's work at keeping me warm, but I'll be damned if I can feel the tip of me nose ever again.\nSecond visit to Laurelin was mildly more eventful. Morning was wonderful with sunny weather and pleasant breeze from over the shores. I still have failed to find a way to explore the knowledge Deathsbanes hold, but I doubt they may know anything about us.\nHaelinor seems to be pretty much closed off, and an assortment of gates speaks loudly about a lack of unexpected guests. Mayhaps I should still try to reason with them. As much as it is possible with ilk as warlike.\nSuccess! After so long, I've managed to discover the place. It seems to be almost clustering a number of reliquary from the lands the Descendants once inhabited - a peculiar collection. I took my time to prepare a place in my hidden library. Now to act.\nMust you torture me so, oh so blessed, merciful Creator? I needn't yet another whip on my back, I've treated my mind as a tanning rack for nearly eight years by now. Spare me a moment of relief. And... and her. Blimey nightmares. I'll better hurry...\nAnd... failure. I can't get any closer, and what few attempts I made have only provided me with a new list of scars to add to the others. Maybe I'll need someone's help. If I dare to speak out after so long a time of solitude.\nPlentiful of passerby on the elven roads. The looks of some of that lot make me skin crawl and shudder. I'll best hurry to the Rose.\nAnd this is the moment I was nearly praying for. A guide, a plan, and a deal of places to discover. If only Maggie was here to see all this.\n\nOther then that I bumped into some new bunch o lunatics. Doing surprisingly well for now.\nJust grand. Sodding. Grand. Motherhumping mess is what all this is. Nobleman getting shot on middle of a tract, ologs wandering in Laurelin, and my bloody guide getting knocked out. I did my best to see to his wounds, but he trudged back into the woods.\nWhat a bloody month. First, the journey to the Isles of Serenity. Secondly, meeting up with Krug again... and lastly an introduction to the arrow-lubbing young noble. The fellow seems kind, and... his story did bloody remind me of something much different\nThey say, that only regret can truly change the nature of man. What would change the nature of a halfling in turn? I guess the same rule applies to all us sapients, but. I have a home, as unlikely as it seems. And I'm willing to fight for it. And for a\nfew new compatriots that don't mind a hermit among them. Quirky bunch they may be, but it's been a while since I saw so much kindness and happiness in a single place. I'll best end this note before I'm off tae choke on sugary rivers down me throat.\nIt's nearly two months since I've been brought in these parts for the first time, and in all due honesty, I never came to regret my brash decision. Even after a hulking mountain of an elf tossed me out of the kitchen for all the mess I made. Guess that's\njust a way o' sayin' hello erry now-a-then, considering I'm damn glad to have met him. Messere Sylver took quite some effort finding his settlers - and dare I say, that he didn't just grab anyone. With such foundation, maybe there's a fair reason for the\nking to bestow such favour over the little colony. Oren's always been a colossus, but the bigger one is, the harder he falls, and it's faith in those that may carry it's legacy along that ought to keep their machinery running like a dream.\n*a somewhat crude drawing depicting some being of centauric form - right below the illustration one can notice words \"Cervitaur?\"*\nAs days of work and joys pass, I grow confident in the colony. All the jest of previous days appears almost akin to crude arguments upholding the pillars of st. Amyas. I'm not the one most eager to, but I'm still one able to admit to a mistake.\n*one can see a slightly clumsy drawing of a Kharajyr enjoying warmth amidst the Crimson Lotus*\n\"A curious individual, this Kha'Panterra. Mayhaps I should still talk to him about the Truth.\" *as noted below*\nPoe Praedium. Who would have thought. I knew I would be able to find some use for the man, but... he's unconvinced. Mayhaps there's yet still room for some horseshit to feed the human, considering that Hunter didn't bother showing up.\n*carefully drafted map of Leuvaarden with several storages, landmarks and important houses marked on it*\nFascinating, how little do we know about all this. We live from day to day, and pay so much heedance to our flesh, but, almost not a penny of our attention lands atop of our souls. Not even the grand\nTwo years. Two years of blood, sweat and tears, and yet, so few fruits to be harvested. I' guess there's a good reason why I'm not paid for me job. I'd still wish the network started to operate without me babysitting their lot.\nSo much time has passed, and I have long forsaken my journal. Mayhaps... later, I will take up the effort. For now - goodbye, lil' pages. \n4th of the Grand Harvest\n1512th Seed.", ""),
        StaticBook("Miner's Journal", "Wight", "Damn frogs ate the key! Now how are we going to get through?", ""),
        StaticBook("Mint", "Gwiwen Ahverren", "Mint, household plant and helper.\n\n Mint is something widely used in teas and drinks in general for no real reason, one would think. It tastes nice, it helps with headaches, etc.\n\n The key word here is /helps/. Mint assists with headaches.\nAnd that, is just one example as to the beneficial properties of mint!\n\n Chapter 1, Mint, and how it helps you.\n\n Mint, as I mentioned before, can assist with headaches. This is a remarkable effect of the plant, as this includes migraines,\nhangovers, weather-related headaches, and what-have-you.\n\n Yet this is a single part of the many benefits that come with mint.\n Here are some, as follows:\n-Mint can assist with headaches if consumed through tea, or through any other drink. It alleviates the pain associated, and can (at times) help put-off any oncoming migraines.\n -Mint can assist with nausea, which can be of no small amount of assistance\nto expectant mothers, or those suffering from food poisoning.\n -Furthermore on nausea, it can assist with digestion, and to that extent, it can cleanse your palete. Why do you think many teeth-cleaners have mint as a part of the ingredients?\n-Mint, luckily, can assist with coughs and respiratory issues. Those who find that their breath is oft berift from them, or that breathing can sometimes be a chore under certain weather or environments, mint can (quite literally) be a lifesaver.\n-Mint can assist with depression. I cannot rightly explain it, but it gives you a boost of energy, per se. Mental energy, that is.\n -Most importantly, it can assist with /oral care/. Your teeth, gums, and tongue can be cleaned rather well by this miracle\nherb, and give your teeth a longer lifespan.\n \n Chapter 2, How to make mint tooth-cleaner.\n\n An important part of your daily hygene, this part of the book will show you how to make proper tooth-cleaner.\nRequirements:\n -1/4 cup of water.\n -Mint leaves, chopped.\n -1/2 tablespoon of corn starch.\n -1/2 tablespoon of grapseed oil.\n -A pan.\n\n -Step 1, ready a fire, and pour water into the pan. After this is done, place the mint leaves into the pan\nand bring it to a boil. Remove the pan from the heat and steep for 20 minutes.\n -Step 2, mix together the cornstarch and grapeseed oil and stir until smooth.\n -Step 3, strain the cooled mint tea, and then add the liquid to the mixture. Bring it to a boil\nuntil it is slightly thickened and smoothed.\n -Step 4, make sure that the mixture is cooled completely, and move to a jar. Make sure to seal it properly to the point that it is air-tight.\n\n Now you can use this toothpaste as needed.\nChapter 3, mint tea, to be or not to be?\n\n Mint tea, of course, is beneficial. However, one often ignores that you can gain it's benefits through the vapors coming from the liquid as much as the liquid itself.\n For one with sinus problems, I recommend\nthat one breathes in the vapors from the mint tea prior to drinking, as it will assist with the clogging.\n\n Chapter 4, mint oil?\n\n If you are unaware, I have made two other tomes that include a guide on how to make oils. However, mint oil,\nto me, seems a waste of time. First off, mint's benefits can often be gained through the drinking of tea, and as such, I would highly suggest /not/ to make oil from it.\nWritten by Gwiwen Ahverren", ""),
        StaticBook("Misconceptions", "Aewion Acaele’ellir", "Misconceptions\n------------------\nOOC NOTE: Written in Common for convenience and the fact that orcs would only use their blah words to write, not their accent.\n------------------\nHello! I've written this short informative novel to explore some\nideas. These ideas pertain to the fact that other races dislike us, I seek to find out why so we can either shore up our flaws or laugh our asses off. \n\nFirst, through various conversations with Oreners on and off their soil\nI will chronicle just why they decided it was a good idea to destroy our home.\n\nSection 1: Oren\n\nChapter 1: Fear\n\nAfter a short conversation with an Orenian knight, I learned\nsomething. Oren FEAR us. They find us to be terrifying brutes, though we certainly aren't. They find us scary because of our height and our tough demeanor. Honestly, I took it as a compliment. This knight, Ser Roland, told me how Oren found the\ndifference between our two races to be unsettling. I find this hilarious.\n\nChapter 2: Ignorance\n\nOren doesn't understand us, at all. Every single soldier has been taught to think of us as cruel, sadistic\nmonsters with an unsatiable lust for war. We can help our bloodlust just as much as they can help their puny lifespan. However, the disturbing part is the blatantly false evidence they presented me. They claimed that we picked a fight with them\nwhen they destroyed our capitol. That couldn't have been more wrong. As I recall it, they saw that we were at a time of transition and weakness and they blackmailed us. We refused the blackmail, so they thought they'd annihilate us. Not only did they\nthink that, but they thought our plan with Orgon's Plague was a project to destroy Vailor. The total destruction was accidental. We just needed an edge in the war. Plus, that was a good generation or two ago- why should this generation suffer for the\nprevious misdeeds of our people. \n\n\nChapter 3: Why They're Trapped In Ignorance.\n\nOne of the worst parts of this, is that we can't teach them about our complicated people.\nThey shut us out due to complete xenophobia. Once I was shot with a crossbow at the gates. \n\nChapter 4: Blind Loyalty\n\n*This chapter is stained with blood.*\n\nToday I made my second journey\nonto orenian soil. This time, a man tried to cut me down before I even drew a weapon. All I did was ask about the war. What is my curiosity returned by? An axe to the chest. I asked him why, and he said because I was an enemy. I asked him why again and he\nresponded with an incoherent answer before fleeing the scene. My conclusion? Half of these soldiers don't know what they're fighting for.", ""),
        StaticBook("Misery", "Sarya", "Thy misery grows deep\n\nHow can this be and nothing great\n\nThe hatred of thy soul is wider than believed\n\nNo coming out nor coming close\n\nHurt thy and thou shall die\nDie within thy heart and mind\n\nHate thy and thou shall be hated\n\nKill thy confidence and thy'll kill thou heart\n\nDestruction is bliss\n\nThy destruction is greater than thou hate\nSpite thy and thou shall depart from life", ""),
        StaticBook("Mission", "Lei", "THe Amber Cold\n           1682\n\nThe trip was rather quick on my stead -- I left behind that sellsword as he was taking too long to keep up. After a long ride I finally managed to get to the temple. I munched through around half of my\nprovisions so I knew that I'd have enough to get back. I surveyed the location around the temple, yet I did not find anything of value or anything at all -- It was quite empty. Over all, it was a big waste of time and effort.", ""),
        StaticBook("Monk Resurrerect", "Thurak'Yar", ">|<Monk>:<\n -=~Resurrection~=-\n\nIt is the salvaition of many lives, but I wonder why I have seen nothing written on it. The monks, as it is very well known, are able to save those that have passed away. While managing my stall\nat the sanctuary grounds I have been able to see for myself some of the happenings, or so I believe.\nThis magic, unlike many others, is one I know very little about. Like all holy magics it seems to\nbe manifested as a bright light, mostly used to heal those wounded. Besides the bright light, the monk performing it is praying the the Triumvirate. It appears to be like clerical healing, but has many other properties. Sometimes a monk arrives\nappears bandits and the like do not care that they are mugging what could be their savior. What I have to say about those monks, is that unlike normal folk, their wounds heal faster. This is of course, is due to their magic, and in turn the small\nflecks of light which I’ve seen surrounding and healing their wounds. Then the monks are able to bring back the once deceased to become fully mortal once more.\nThis is not to say they are necromancers. Those simply raise the dead, and they remain in a limbo state; living and being deceased. The monks are able to bring the body and soul exactly like it was before the death in near perfect condition.\nFrom those I have talked to over the years in the Sanctuary, there is an always present sensation of salvation. Present in all of those that I have seen, none have memories of their death or even of the events leading up to it. Other\ncommon effects are scars, sometimes showing how the poor soul met their end before, or of the tortures it passed. The ones that worry me the most are those that change after being saved. I have talked to some before after saving, and the\nchanges can be quite extreme. Some go crazy, others start to live in constant fear, some remain with pains in parts of their bodies. The changes they can go through are incredibly varied. I could conjure up reasons as to why this happens, all\nof them without means of proving so. I just believe death to be a terrible experience, that part of it continues on even after salvation.\nAnother interesting fact I have gathered, somehow by luck, is that the saved do not want to return to the location that they had perished. This particular thought came to me when one of the saved was hugged dearly by what I assumed was his lover.\nBefore that, his body had been carried by another, a friend perhaps, and he and I had a chat about what happened. I knew of the exact location of his demise, and as him and the woman were moving away, he asked if they were passing through\nthe area when they were returning home. With the confirmation of the woman, he started giving out other ways to reach their house. A big argument had begun when the woman just wanted to return home as fast as she could with him, and he plainly refused to\ngo through that area, which was the only road to their house. He didn’t know himself why he didn’t want to. Alas, he returned to normal about half a day later. Since then I started noticing other strange behaviours such as people staying\nin the sanctuary for longer times, not using their normal routes out of the sanctuary and returning shortly after, then leaving with a friend. I believe, once more, that the experience of death was so horrible that those saved gain a\nsubconscious fear of their death place. Besides, what would happen if they saw their own body?\nOn the mention of bodies, I do have to state as well, it is not necessary for the body to be brought back to the monks for the resurrection.\nI have seen many monks bring bodies to the sanctuary, so I believe it might be quite easier with them. This is facorable, as in the lands of Anthos there are many evils. You can be decapitated, eaten, thrown into lava, cut into little bits\nand drowned in the deepest of oceans. Your body may disappear and never be found, and you may this way still be saved. How they restore the body I do not know, and the monks seem not to answer when queried. They do answer a few questions,\nhowever. I learnt, for instance, that the monks are neutral; never taking sides in political views or wars. They also take this neutrality to those they save. I have seen those of evil whose purpose is to kill being saved together with the\nchildren that never made any harm. This has brought problems to the monks. Many was others to remain dead, some for good cause. \nMost of the stories of the savesd start simply with them explaining how they woke up in the\nmonk’s care. It would seem to always be the same as this. Some come back quite soon after their demise, already back before their friends and family run to the sanctuary to check, and others can take elven days. Yet this magic is not all powerful.\nAs the monks mention, they cannot save all. If the deceased does not walk out of the monk’s rooms an Elven week after their death, they are forever lost. The same happens to those that take their own life. I believe that if they think that they\ndon’t want to live anymore, then they wouldn’t return to the land of the living. The monks are a blessing to the mortals; they are those that save so many from their shortened lives.\n~Written by Rosso, 15’th of Malin’s Welcome, 1452\nRescribed by the Farseer Thurak, 1’st of The Grand Harvest, 1513.", ""),
        StaticBook("Monks of Charity", "Guru Pinya", "~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~\n    \n The Book of Peace\n\n    By: Guru Pinya\nThrough experimentation of the arcane, I have become enlightened. Through days of meditation at a time, I have become able to let go of my earthly tether, and enter the void. I have become one with the wind. If you do not understand of what I speak of,\nI shall explain in the simpler of speech. Through meditation my soul has left it's body and enter the void through which the spirits have given me ancient knowledge. In the book I shall write down what I have been taught so that it may be passed on to the\nworld for all the nations to hear.\n   \n         -Guru Pinya\n~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~\n\n Concerning the Soul\n\nEverytime we die, our souls leave our body and wander aimlessly around. The Monks of the Cloud Temple then collect our souls and our bodys and take them to be healed back together. However,\nI must say that when one has become a light into the dark world, and their duty has been fulfilled, their spirit will be given a new body and they will be reincarnated. This is called the Natural Order.\n~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~\n\n   Concerning the \n   Spiritual Powers\n\nEverything has a life-force inside of it. Some call it energy, some call it life, but I call it Magic. This magic is not from the void, or from a deity, but from onesel! Through\ndiscipline, and patience, one is able to harness their energy an extent, and use it for the wellbeings of others. Some examples of harnessing bodily Magic is using it do increase strength, speed, become unfamished, survive during a thirst,\nset things alight, preserve dying bodies, levitating small things, healing minor wounds, increasing senses, and entering the spirit world.\n~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~\n \n   Concerning the\n     Spirit World\n\nThe spirit world is like nothing the mortal eye has seen before. In it lies the Divine Hosts, the angels, the demons, the spirits, the gods, dead spiritual people, and some of the greatest people\nof all time. You might ask how these great people have gotten there. The answer is the Natural Order. When someone has made a great change in the world, their souls do not reincarnate themselves, but they enter into the spiritual world in the peace they\nhad so desired. To enter into peace is to live and die in peace.\n~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~\n\n    The Great Path\n\nTo enter into the realm of peace, one must live and die in peace. There are eight rules to peace, and they are:\n\nRight view, viewing reality as it is, and not how it is to be.\nRight intention, intention of renunciation, freedom and harmlessness.\n\nRight speech, speaking in a truthful, and non-hurtful way.\n\nRight action, acting in a non-harmful way.\nRight livelihood, living a non-harmful livelihood.\n\nRight effort, making an effort to improve.\n\nRight mindfulness, awareness to see things for what they are with a clear consciousness.\nRight concentration, correct meditation or concentration.\nWith the eight ways to peace said, I will now explain the four ideals. One must always hope that:\n\nAll sentient beings have happiness and it's causes.\n\nAll sentient beings be free of suffering and it's causes.\nAll sentient beings never be separated from bliss without suffering.\n\nAll sentient beings be in equanimity, free of bias, attachment and anger.\nIn the spirit world, for which I have named Tashe, meaning both the spiritual realm and the state of enlightenment, Tashe may be acquired by following the teachings of myself. If you wish to leave the cycle of reincarnation and suffering, please search\nfor me, Guru Pinya.\n((AntoniusLXIV))", ""),
        StaticBook("Monster Manual 1", "Diane Farsight", "=+-+=\n    The Monster\n       Manual\n       =+-+=\n        \n\n        Volume 1\n\n\n\n\n\nBy: Diane Farsight\nForeword\nThe world is a dark place, and it's filled with dark things. This book, and others like it, will hopefully inform you of what is out there, and how to deal with them. After all, Ignorance is a most insidious killer.\nThe Blob\n================\nDanger: Low\nDescription: Blobs are generally docile animals shaped like big piles of goo. Their size can vary greatly, but they tend not to surpass 6 feet in height. Their color varies, but will usually be\nbe the color of the enviornment they live in. Furthermore, they are covered in an outer layer of dry skin that protects them from extreme heat. Because of this, they are often found in hot climates. If enveloped by a blob, suffocation is the only way it\nkill you, as their bodies have no acidic properties.\nWeaknesses: Blobs are quite susceptable to cold, making Thanium a perfect weapon against them.\nCreation: Blobs can create more blobs by splitting themselves apart, creating two, smaller blobs.\nThe Ooze\n===================\nDanger: Moderate\nDescription: Oozes are the volitile cousin of blobs. They have the same shape and color, but can be much larger and territorial than their counterpart. Their size can become a staggering 5\nmeters in height, and their body produces a potent acid capable of dissolving flesh and metal alike. Also unlike blobs, Oozes prefer the cold, and lack the outer skin that blobs possess. If you ever need to tell an Ooze apart from a blob quickly, use your\nnose. Oozes will smell much more acrid.\nWeaknesses: Oozes are slow and notably flammable. The best way to deal with one is to set them alight, then run while they burn.\nCreation: Oozes can split themselves into more oozes, just like blobs.\nThe Giant Ooze\n===================\nDanger: EXTREME!\nDescription: On occasion, there will be a sighting of a Gargantuan Ooze. Often they come from forgotten cave systems opened by earthquakes, or humanoids digging too deep. They are like\nOozes, but much larger- usually over 10 meters in size and capable of dissolving massive castle gates in a matter of minutes. Weaknesses: Fire will still kill gargantuan Oozes, but it is imperitave that you do not attempt to hide from them- there is\nalmost no stopping one if it begins chasing you.\nCreation: Unknown. Normal Oozes should split into smaller Oozes before reaching this size. It is hypothesized that extended time in cramped conditions underground allows an ooze to grow to this size.\nThe Flesh Worm\n===================\nDanger: EXTREME!\nDescription: The tunnel worm is a subterranian monster of epic proportions. It's full length is unknown, but it is easily several meters in diameter. Most of it's life is spent boring\nholes in the earth for it to travel in, often straight through stone. A cave created by a Tunnel worm recently will always be perfectly circular, and ribbed to allow the tunnel worm to maneuver within it easily. It is hypothesized that the Underdark\nbeneath the dwarven lands of Anthos was sculpted by the errant burrowing of tunnel worms.\nWeaknesses: Any place that isn't perfectly fitted for it's body, such as large caverns or the surface.\nCreation: Unknown.\nThe Drake\n===================\nDanger: EXTREME!\nDescription: A Drake is, in essence, a corrupted dragon, like those spoken of in legend. Unlike their bretheren, Drakes are much smaller in size and easier to defeat. Despite this, they\nare still capable of flying and breathing fire, and as a result require a large body of able men to be killed safely. When killed, a drake's body will dissolve entirely, but if one can manage to retrieve some of its scales without killing the beast, they\ncan be used to great effect in alchemy.\nWeaknesses: None.\nCreation: Legend has it that drakes are born when a dragon is overcome with taint. This, however, has never been witnessed.\nThe Alchemical\n       Chimera\n===================\nDanger: Moderate\nDescription: An alchemical chimera is a fusion of two animals. It is truely an unnatural beast, created by a devious use of alchemy. Chimera come in all shapes and sizes,\nbut all will resemble the combination of two  natural beasts. They are mindless beasts, virtually untamable, and gluttonous for flesh.\nWeaknesses: : Time. A well created Chimera will last, at max, for 2 to 3 years.\nCreation: Alchemy.\nThe Dark Chimera ===================\nDanger: Moderate\nDescription: Through the use of drakkarian magic, the normal conditions for a chimera can be subverted, allowing for fully adult humans to be partially fused with parts hewn from\nanimals. The result is a fully intelligent, remarkably stable chimera. Many dark chimera are no more than victims of dark mages, but this is not always the case. Great care should be taken when dealing with one.\nWeaknesses: None\nCreation: Alchemy\nMixed with Drakkar Magic.\nThe Vodnik\n===================\nDanger: Moderate\nDescription: Vodnik are tiny, fish-like creatures that inhabit rivers and lakes. When vodnik encounter a corpse of any sort, they will begin filling and infesting it. The corpse will begin\nmoving of it's own accord, and begin dragging anything so foolish as to disturb it's water under with it, to become infested as well. Eventually, this process will crescendo until a small army of shambling corpses inhabit an area. This makes clearing\ndifficult.\nWeaknesses: Attacking the arms and legs of a vodnik-infested corpse is your best bet. Cutting off the head should have no effect.\nCreation: The Vodnik reproduce by laying eggs in the corpses they inhabit.\nThe Giant Crab\n===================Danger: High\nDescription: An enormous crab, about 15 meters across, 5 meters high, and chitin thicker than plate armor. If they see you, they will try to kill you. . They attack anything that moves,\nmembers of their own species included.\nWeaknesses: Their eyes are vulnerable, but should you lack for arrows you should try attacking their underbelly, or failing that, playing dead.\nCreation: Unknown. They certainly do not reproduce.\nThe Ghost\n===================\nDanger: Low\nDescription: A corporeal entity that is not yet ready to leave this world. Specters have several stages of 'unlife'. Stage one specters are always gray, and flit in and out of existance constantly.\nWhat seperates this stage from the others is the fact that, without fail, the spirit will not be able to come to terms with the fact that they are already dead. They usually need a large amount of persuasion and occaisonally hard evidence to make them\nrealize this. Stage two specters already realize that they are dead, and are able to begin learning to control their abilities more effectively. One of two things happen to stage three specters. They will either turn blue and become good, or turn red and\nbecome pure evil. This is usually in response to how well they were treated in their unlife, or how evil they were when they still lived. Powerful specters are capable of invisibility, minor manipulation of physical objects, and ejecting ectoplasm.\nWeaknesses: Spectres can be banished with a single swing of a weapon, especially holy and gold instruments. They can and will come back to life later, however. They are also unable to cross even the thinnest of gold lines.\nCreation: Spectres are\ncreated when someone dies, but cannot come to terms with their own passing. They become stuck betwixt.\nThe Graven\n===================\nDanger: High\nDescription: Graven are evil spirits who died carrying a great obsession in their hearts. As it drove them in life, so to  does it drive them in death.These spirits will wander the lands,\nendlessly pursuing their unattainable goal, and the pursuit of that goal itself becomes the very fuel that keeps them alive. Above all else, do not look a Graven in the eye. Their eyes are portals into their maddened soul, and will instill a lasting\nmadness into the hearts of those who see it.\nWeaknesses: A graven can be banished easily with any weapon, but is particularly susceptable to gold, and holy objects. Likewise, they are unable to cross any line made of gold. In special\ncircumstances, is also possible to banish them forever by completing the task that drives their madness.\nCreation: Gravens are created when a truely obsessed person meets an untimely demise.\nThe Apparition\n===================\nDanger: EXTREME!\nDescription: An apparition is an amalgation of many, many lost spirits combined for one purpose, and that purpose is pure evil. Apparitions are malicious, and very dangerous to fight.\nThey are capable of incredible acts of telekinesis and illusion, beyond what any living mage could ever accomplish. Normally, apparitions are bound to a central pillar, marked by many skulls and skeletons littering the area around it. If you come across\none such pillar, is vitally important that you DO NOT DAMAGE THE PILLAR IN ANY WAY, SHAPE, OR FORM. Destroying the pillar will weaken the beast temporarily, but afterwards it will be able to roam the world at large, bringing great chaos in it's wake.\nWeaknesses: An apparition is significantly more powerful than a spirit. The use of gold weaponry can keep it at bay, but the banishment itself lasts only mere moments. Only a very thick ring of gold can contain it. The only way to kill them\npermanently is through the aid of a team of Clerics or Shamen\nCreation: The exact origin of Apparitions is murky. From what can be gathered, they are formed from the death of many individuals in one place, at the same time.\nThe Boogeyman\n===================\nDanger: Moderate\nDescription: Yes, the boogeyman is real. Well, was real. The only known boogieman is currently dead. Boogeyman are sentient collections of bugs that swarm around a central corpse. Based on\non the only known boogeyman's example, boogiemen are intelligent, and extremely murderous, taking pleasure in killing innocents. When endangered, the bugs inside the boogieman will scatter in all directions. Because of this, when hunting the Boogiemen it\nis imperative that you take him by suprise.\nWeaknesses: Boogeymen are weak to fire, and crushing implements. Gold hurts it, but a sword will not have much effect on the swarm.\nCreation: Unknown.\nThe Oolog\n===================\nDanger: Moderate\nDescription: The Olog  is roughly twice the size of an orc, and  nearly three times as stupid. A product of large amounts of orcish inbreeding, Ologs were raised for having muscle and size,\nand their bodies show it. Still descendant of Orcs, they also are capable of bloodraging, making them twice as dangerous.\nWeaknesses: Ologs are stupid. I mean, really stupid. Use that to your advantage.\nCreation: These creatures are\n(loosely) considered Natural' beasts, and reproduce normally.\nConclusion\n\nThis book has merely scratched the surface of what lurks in the night. Expect more books in the furture.\nStay Alive, Atheria.", ""),
        StaticBook("Moonlight Dance", "Klaudia Crast", "[!] The story was given by a anonymous man. Though if one must know- he roams the streets of Oren daily.\n-------------------\n\n    Moonlight Dance\n\nby Lady Klaudia Crast\n\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\n------------------\n~ 1.\n\nThe sun submerged itself beneath the dimming salmon mountaintop to the sight of a harmonic moonlight beginning its climb from the darkened Earth.\n\nThe air was amongst a thinning moisture that\n~ 2\n\ntingled the aromatic smell of lingering fern.\nPerfectly placed fingers were present among the warmth of the grass pressed palm. \n\nHer teal eyes pierced the skin to which she glanced, lustfully.\n~ 3\n\nEnticing my very being.\nThe charming aura surrounding such a woman pulled me closer to her ever so slightly.\n\nReturning the gaze I then pulled my lips closer to hers, watching the dimming sight of her illuminated -\n~ 4\n\nlips under the moonlight.\n\nI found my eyes closing, furthering my body towards hers. The warming sensation of her lips became that of a snug hearth\nbeneath a wood burning stove top.\n~ 5\n\nHis mind soon became detained in cadence of her soft lips against his. A joyful ache overtook me as her arms found home upon my shoulders.\n\nNow they were wrapped around my neck.\n~ 6\n\nThe slight tug of her arms took me onto the ground alongside her torso. The swing of her affection brought me amongst a trance of cherishment.\n\nThe trance, this trance was soon broken by the inevitable. Pulling my\n~ 7\n\nfrom my lips. My adoring eyes opened in a graceful haste to look upon a warming smile within her eyes.\n\nAlmost as if it was a pleasant virus; I too felt a smile manifesting at my mouth.\n~ 8\n\nThe beating of our breath was only so slightly shadowed by the delicate rushing water of the creek.\n\nI could only take a moment of admiration towards her before I felt the forward pulling of her weakend hands against my -\n~ 9\n\nshirt. The scene fading into an aengulic light as I was pulled down against her chest.\n-------------------\n\nThis story hides the identity of the pair. Although there is more and more descretion upon us.", ""),
        StaticBook("Moot suggestions", "Tailesin", "Moot ideas:\n\n1: Next festival.\n\n2: Guide nominations?\n\n3: Ideas/plan making to draw in more dedicants.\n\n4: Empty house clearing.\n\n5: New headscribe to be voted in? As\nthe current one seems to be inactive and the library could use one.\n\n6: New scribes to help head in the library.", ""),
        StaticBook("Morals", "Furbola", "Acts of Valor Pt. 1\n=======================\nA man long ago, was well known. His name was Alexander. Long ago, you see, there were many battles. Bloody Battles.\nAlexander fought in every battle, until he lost a life.\nThis life was his own.\nCh.1 Pg.1\n=======================A man named Alex, fought in a battle. This was the first battle of The Great War. The Great War, only lasted 1 season. Winter. Alex, in his first battle, had nothing. He ran with the savages. A small clan called Neimr.\nCh.1 Pg.2\n=======================Neimr and another rival clan, Warhawkes, hated eachother. One day, Alexander, and his best friend, Doech, were taking a stroll down the War camp. They saw Warhawkes! The Warhawkes captured them before they could speak.\nCh.1 Pg.3\n=======================They took Alex and Doech, to their War Camp. They tried to get information out of them. In the end, one of them had to die. Doech, was a bad man. He never did anything right. He never deserved to live.\nCh.1 Pg.4\n=======================Alex, so per se, was the best. Great Husband. Great father. Great Warrior. Alex, showed his true greatness, when he pleaded to die. He would rather, his friend Doech, live. And this happened.\nCh.1 Pg.5\n=======================Doech lived. He decided to become a better man than he was before. This happened. You see, the moral of the story, is to believe in anyone!\n[!] The rest of the book is tattered away.\n\n\n\n\n[!] There is very bad hand writing just below.\n\ntHER3 Are Mu1tip13 copiz of diz b00c. F1d d3m!\nNovel Written By: \nStephen Mal", ""),
        StaticBook("Mother Nature", "Zyvia Ba'ikana", "She ran, the world under her feet. Her feet were bare, and she could feel everything. The rotation of the earth and the sun’s movements into darkness were all known to her. She smiled knowingly to the sky, the wind running its hands through her hair.\nShe felt the bees nursing flowers, seeds digging themselves deep into the earth. Above all, she felt the blades of grass beneath her, tearing up the soles of her feet. She paused before her next step, tears flowing from her eyes.\nThe steady streams of water flooded the valleys and plains around her, creating lakes, streams and waterfalls. Pieces of her hair drifted to the ground, each taking root. These roots blossomed into trees, surrounding her and comforting her.\nAs if on cue, vines encircled her ankles, pulling her into the dirt’s warm embrace. It created a home for her, coddling her like a small child. She became one with nature. Some say she even became nature itself.\nThese were the ages before the taint destroyed our mother. These were the wonderful years of innocence.", ""),
        StaticBook("Mountain Kings", "Durza Volkihar", "The Dwarves are a small but strong race capable of carving great cities into mountains. Most dwarves are miners or blacksmith. Their skills at forging are legendary usually creating amazing jewelery or weapons.\nDwarves have a great love of war, food and ale. They are quick to anger but have a great love for their friends and kin. They value honor over everything, It is said a dwarf will always keep his word and will never betray a oath.\nMost Dwarves live underground, prefering to mine eternaly for treasures beneath the earth, always wanting to expand their wealth. Dwarfs live much longer than humans but tend to die in battle before they can die of old age.\nDwarves are small but very muscular. Most of them prefer to grow their beards extremely long. Apart from having incredible beards, they are extremely hairy. Female dwarves are extremely rare but it is hypothesised that the are to hairy to be\nnoticed.\nThe Dwarves speak the simple tounge of men but have added their own touch to the way they speak, usually prefering to shorten words rather than speaking the full length of normal words. The dwarves have a ancient language but the elders use it more.\nIf you share these views, come seek my symbol to find me.\n\n\n\n[!] A red eagle is drawn here.", ""),
        StaticBook("Mountain Rose", "Ambrose", "-=- Rose of the -=-\n        Mountain\n\nPenned 17th Sun's Smile, 1625 by the hand of Ambrose De Montem\n\n[!] a detailed sketch of a rose decorates the cover.\nThe meaning of the name was Rose of the Mountain. I was told I was born on the slopes of a northern mountain, beside a patch of frozen flowers. The bitter cold wind of that night followed most of my childhood.\nMy parents were John and Renne of the Mountain. They each owned a knife instead of a wedding ring- they killed for their marriage and honeymoon. \n\nOur family haunted those mountains for a long time. The north\nwas my cradle. \n\nI remember the cold more than the faces I lured into the woods. Papa always gave me their coin. \"Go buy a toy, Mos.\" he would say. \"You were so helpfull today.\"\n\nAround the time my sister was born,\nmy parents had taken 4 victims. It was enough to warrant a proper bounty. \n\nWhen Lilan was four, and I was 12, they were caught. Found in the open by a mage who weilded fire like a weapon. Lilan died in my mother's arms.\nI remember how the snow around them melted with the heat of their remains. \n\nI remember how my lungs burned from the smoke and the freezing air. \n\nHe might have killed me, too, if I hadn't ran.\n[!] a watercolor of a snowy town, banners with Haense colors flying from the towers. \n\"The Town Below the Mountain.\"\n-Ambrose\n[!] several flowers are pressed between the pages, carefully labelled. \n\n\"Daisy\"   \"Poppy\"\n\n  \"?\"\n\n\n             \"Rose\"\n[!] this page has been torn from the book- but there appears to have been a rough sketch once.\n[!] a painting of a child's face, her hair curly. Freckles cover her face. \n\n\"Lilac of the Mountain\"\n-Ambrose\nI was always a sickly boy. Plauged by a nagging cough and almost daily headaches, the most I could ever do was use a pencil. Most of my education came after my family was gone. \n\nI took up painting as a child. Learned to\ndraw on the road. We were always moving. Always running.\n\n[!] a crude map is drawn here. Karlsburg is marked with a small star.\n[!] several sketches of northern buildings are drawn here. \n\n\"Another Home\"\n-Ambrose\n\nSometimes I wanted to understand why they enjoyed killing- but I suppose it's good that I don't.\n[!] a sketch of a bearded man, his eyes piercing. \n\n\"Temptation\"\n\n-Ambrose\n[!] an aged drawing of a family is tucked between the pages.\n\n\"Before the Flames\"\n\n-Ambrose, 1607\n[!] a watercolor painting of a rose.\n\n\"Rose of the Ashes\"\n-Ambrose\n[!] another aged piece of paper is held here, the ink faded. \n\n\"Once upon a time, there lived a princess in a grand castle. She had a lovely garden, and all the things she could dream to want. One day, a dragon came and scorched the land.\"\n[!] a collection of sketches cover this page, mostly of flowers and the occasional portrait.\nEvery now and then, I'd meet another child. My name was a constant source of shame- what sort of boy had a name like that?\n\nThey called me Flower Boy.\n\nLilan called me Rosie.\n[!] a detailed sketch of a lilac is drawn here, some of the lines smudged. \n\n\"Ash Fed Lilac\"\n-Ambrose\nI was always a sickly child. Plauged by a nagging cough and daily headaches- the smell of smoke is still fresh on the air for me. \n\nBurnt flesh is a smell not easily forgotten.\n[!] a hooded man, hands aflame, is painted here. \n\n\"March\"\n-Ambrose\n-=-=-=Fears=-=-=-\n\n@. Fire\n\n@. Magic\n\n@. Pain\n\n@. Alone\n\n[!] something has been scratched out here.\n[!] a wrinkled page is held here. \n\n\"Promises: \n\n@ never forgive\n\n@ stay on my toes\n\n@ no magic \"\n\n-1611\nI knew my preferences. There was no shame- no more than usual.\n\n[!] a drawing of a tavern, several young men sitting around a large table. \n\n\"Revelations\"\n-Ambrose\nI always have prefered the cold. Sitting in front of a fire with a mug of tea has always been one of my greatest pleasures. There are types of fire that help. There are types that harm.\n[!] a painting of a road, a river running alongside it. \n\n\"The Path Forward\"\n-Ambrose\n\"When in doubt, go forward.\"\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-", ""),
        StaticBook("MRGHL", "Renn", "Tori is cute.", ""),
        StaticBook("Mundane Healing", "hex37", "__Mundane Healing: The treatment of minor wounds with common herbs.__\n\nMatron’s Foreword: When I was studying medicine in Oren, a strange dwarf brought me with a book of medical recipes that used very common ingredients\nfor the treatment of various medical casualties, by an Aleya Darolien. One or two of them sounded interesting, though a large amount of them were, largely ridiculous, like one that claimed it possible to heal a major burst of an artery\nor internal organs with nothing but rose thorns and petals. In the interest of not wasting precious paper, I’ve recorded some of the more practical recipes in the book, and added one or two of my own, to make up for lost space.\n-Minor Cut (Matron)\nSimply apply a dose of  deceased Sentient-Slime to the affected area, and wrap a light bandage around it.  The slime helps stop the bleeding, and the mildly acidic nature of it is known to remove the taint from a body.\n-Headache (Aleya)\nBoil milk. Add honey while the milk boils. Take Dandelion stems and Rose thorns and put them in a thin satchel. Dip the satchel in the milk and let it infuse with the mixture for about 2 minutes. Slowly drink the milk.\n-Stomach Ache (Matron)\n\nBoil water. Once it hits a full broil, add honey until the liquid turns an amber color. Add tea leaves to a small bag, and let it soak in the mixture for about five minutes. Drink the tea slowly.\n-Soreness (Aleya)\n\nSimply apply rags with hot water to relax the muscles, and rest a lot.\n-Burns (Matron)\nSet your hands on some vinegar, and drench a clean bandage with it. Apply this bandage to the affected area, and wrap a dry bandage around this to keep the vinegar from getting absolutely everywhere.\nThe important thing about burns is to keep the affected area moist while it mends, as burned areas do not produce sweat properly. Vinegar is ideal for this, as it will keep the area moist, and not evaporate as water would. Be sure to check the burn wound\ndaily until the skin can finally reform.\n-Fever (Aleya)\nKeep the victim’s body cool using cold water. Give him hot milk steeped with brown mushroom stems and ground rose thorns. It will fight off the disease. Keep the victim rested and feed him mushroom soup.", ""),
        StaticBook("Musical Golem", "Yden", "The musical golem\nBy Yden\n\nJames was once a noble golem, he served a king and his heir and his heir until the kingdom fell. He was once again alone in this world, without purpose. James needed to find his talents.\nJames tried sport, he tried running but of course he weighed as much as a ten men combined so he wasn't going very far and he wasn't going very fast either, he accepted his failure and moved on to his next activity, next James tried body building but\nJames was built... out of stone actually but this made logical sense to James at the time. By now James was starting to feel down, he thought he was good at everything but he picked himself back up and lumbered off to the lake, he tried fishing, he tried\nalchemy but burnt the place down in the end while attempting to make a brew of invisibility. Obviously at this point James felt pretty useless so he lumbered off with a sad look on his face. He came across a small child, she was playing the most beautiful\npiece of music on her hand crafted flute, it had her name in a golden lettering 'Emily' this girl could play beautiful, if James could cry i'm certain he would be. This gave James a grand idea, James was obviously never going to be able to play the flute\nbut he was certain he would excel at playing the drums and sure enough he was, in fact he was so good the girl who has inspired him to try this hired him so they could play together, she was the daughter of a very wealthy lord after all so this was no\nproblem. Emily and James became great friends and James was finally happy again with his life now that he was not alone, he had a friend and she was the best friend he could ever ask for.\n\nThe End\nBy Yden\nAlso see; The golem who learnt to love \n\nAlso see; The little golem that could", ""),
        StaticBook("My Confession", "Ser Uther Grimlee", "Dear Malia, I am writing this message to you to tell you my feelings. Everytime I am with you I can't help but have these feelings. I get these feelings that I can have never felt before. I am writing this letter cause it is hard for me to confess my...\nfeelings to you in person. I am always weak when im around you. That is why I am confessing my love to you in this letter. I Ser Uther Grimlee Love You. -Ser Uther Grimlee. (There would be a beautifull painting of Malia attached)", ""),
        StaticBook("My Free Baguette", "Tajo S. Torto", "A man named Uther helped me make the wild grain bread.\n\nShort Red Gobbo, she told me this is her name\nTyroth\nElizabete\nUther\nPointy Hat Oldie AKA WindRaker\nBryant Allard\nAngus\nThe dwarf named Steven, though I personally think he looks more like a halfling\nCirimo P. Torto, my brother A swell guy that happens to really like baguettes\nGray Kellian III\nFredrick", ""),
        StaticBook("My Heart: Divide", "Vas Umbra-Vincrute", "The cave: I hate it\nI like the trees and the sun\nCaves are dark, no trees\nI hate living in this cave\nBut it's what my loved ones want\nWhy don't I listen\nI make my mother worry\nShe'll give me advice\nTell me what I need to do\nBut I just will not listen\nI love her deeply\nBut She doesn't love me back\nWhy do I love her\nIs it her smile? Laugh? Her hair? \nI don't know, but I love her\nThere She is, reading\nDoes She know I'm here, writing?\nDid She see me look?\nShe moved closer to me, why?\nShould I speak? Tell her to leave?\nEmotions are dumb\nI wish I didn't have them\nMy mind starts to race\nWhat if this, what if that. Stop.\nThese thoughts are useless. Just Stop.\nWe are talking now\nShe asked if I want her gone\nI told her I don't\nWas that the wrong thing to say?\nWe just continue to talk\nShe has left, I'm sad\nI shouldn't be, it's just wrong\n§\\My Love has appeared\nI wrap an arm around her\nThis one loves me. I love her.\nShe has returned. Why?\nMaking my thoughts run wild. Why?\nMy Love is sleeping\nMy Love, she is beautiful\nYet, so is She. Dammit all.\nMy Love on one side\nShe is on the other side\nShe corrupts my thoughts\nI love them both, that's a fact\nI have chosen My Lover\nHave I really though?\nIf I really have chosen\nWhy do these thoughts stay?\nCould I be unsatisfied?\nMy heart: divided. We'll see.", ""),
        StaticBook("My Return", "Wargoth Malog'Yar", "These past several years mi have been on pilgrimage. It was nub a pilgrimage to any particular holy place or shrine, but was rather a sacred wandering of sorts. Mi explored wild and uninhabited places, and further hardened mi already thick hide.\n Mi\nhave meditated atop the highest peaks of frozen mountains. Mi have trod the scorched earth of volcanic regions where the air is clouded with smoke agh ash. Mi have stalked through the underbrush of mi people's jungles, braving the dangers of the many\npredators thereof.\n In mi travels, mi have observed the skies by morning, listened to the voice of the wind by day, gazed into fires by evening, agh dreamed both wonderous agh terrible dreams by night. All of existence, both waking agh sleepeing, blah to\nmi. The spirits guide mi through the stars agh moon, agh drive mi on through the sun. They whisper in the grass of the fields agh murmur in the caves. The waves of the sea shout to they who listen.\n Mi return this day from mi pilgrimage to find mi people\nscattered, agh their blargs empty. The streets are silent. The walls have been thrown down. Just as well though. I hated that goi. The orcs have done far hosher. San'Orca; San'Vitar; Kodar'goi; San'Thraka. These were gois worthy of Krug!\n Still though, mi\nbrothers agh sisters are left without a land. The sharas mouth boastful things in their perpetual arrogance, agh their wood albai whores have spat on the shadow of Enrohk  by stretching their hands out against his shrines. Darûkûrz bûbri, afar angathfark\nagh vadokanuk, ashdautus vrasubatlat! All who read this, heed those words. Let them be the words of all the Orcish people. Gruk them agh lock them in lats spirit.\n Meanwhile, the spirit realm screams, agh the bub'hosh powers of the universe shift. Mi\nhear the moaning agh creaking of all reality in mi sleep. The h'ash arms have fallen. Such is the price of betrayal, though mi blah it with a heavy soul. Those arms could have upheld us for all eternity, had carelessness nub taken hold of our Rex. Kharak\nwas a fine Rex, but his ambition outgrew his wisdom. Now, that which brought us such power has been layed low, agh we suffer for it. The powers with which he played are not toys, agh Orgon is nub a howler on a leesh. Had he gruk'd that sooner, things\nwould still be as they ought to be. Let all living shamans learn from his error, agh excercize due caution when wielding such power.\n Now, Kinul stands where mi old master agh the giver of mi sight once stood. These days weigh heavily on mi bones. Now,\nhowever, is nub a time to mourn. Now is the time to steel ourselves. We are nub as the sharas, who live on through their gois agh land. Wi are nub as the albai, who grow fat at the trough of comfort agh luxury. We are nub as the gazat, who hole up in\ncaves, agh find their security in riches. We are the orcs, the cubs of Krug. Our strength is to be found in hardship agh trial. \n Since the days of the Ancients, our kind has fought for every morsel of food; every cup of water; every inch of land;\nevery breath of air; agh every second of existence. These days are nub to be lamented, but rather let us stand tall as ever. Let us remember who we are. These days are not a grave to lie down in. They are a crucible to purify us. They are a fire to harden\nour skins.\n We are the uruk, the goblins, agh the ologs. We are the cubs of Krug. We are the orcs. Look upon lats ancestors, brothers agh sisters, agh shout proudly. Raise lats lusks, lats zults, lats o'ligs, agh lats fists. Bare lats tusks, stand atop\nthe bloody agh broken heaps of lats enemies, agh roar. For the spirits. For the Ancestors. For Krug!\n -Malog, Wargoth of the Yar Clan.\n 7th of The Grand Harvest, 1583.", ""),
        StaticBook("My Spirit Walk", "Elder Gukdan'Raguk", "Spirit walks... An experience no man or woman would ever forget. A time to commune with the Spirit and ask for guidance or perhaps knowledge.\nI awoke, a thick fog surrounded me, my visage blinded. I felt beneath my frame, my hands wincing at the touch of cold mud.\nSlowly I stood, before stumbling forward, weary from the sudden awakening.\nAs I looked around, I saw a vast plain of mud and coarse dirt, with pointed rocks of large stature piercing the fog above: their jagged tips dissapearing into the sky above.\nTo my left was the sound of rushing water: a small river was flowing from a cluster of dark rocks. \nThrough the fog, a bright light managed to shine it's way through, hitting the surface of my eyes.\nA sudden pain pierced my head, the river flashing a crimson red in my eyes. My stomach felt as if it twisted and pulled, eating at its self, before an abrupt sound of rocks falling took me back to the reality around me.\nAn icy chill ran down my spine, like a steel blade pressed upon my skin. I felt as if I was being watched; prey to whatever may become my predator in that wasteland.\n\nAs I began to see, touch and hear the land around me... Something clicked in my mind.\nThis place felt familiar to me: as if a memory had been plucked from the depths of my mind, now displayed infront of me...\n\nMy eyes closed, my frame enwrapped with a surge of warmth, and yet I felt so cold.\nAwake again, I found myself within the comforting walls of my home, breathing heavily, I fell back laughing.", ""),
        StaticBook("My Struggle", "Kaiser Decimus Rovin, Vandalore", "====Heil Valdoria==== \n\n\n\n     The Rise of the\n     Colored Kingdoms\n\n\n    \n        Approved by\n   The Reich Ministry\n          Of Truth\nForeward\n\nThe treatise of which follows this breif forward has been legislated upon the direct mandate of the Kaiser and his white sons. It is all very scientific, you see. Praise the Kaiser and hail the White Flame.\nSince his inception, the race of man has proved his superiority over the lesser kindred time and time again, and thus, it is undoubtedly proven by science that man is Kaiser's chosen race. There is no question in the matter, for man and only man possesses\nthe conviction and blessing to mold a mighty empire, forged from the frisson of today, and supported on all facets by our pure ancestors. The dubious assertion against our one and true God and his honor guards is that of defeatist and Serenist dogmatic\npestilence, inseminated from the vile gasses of hell and popagated by the black worms and Kharadeen sympathizers. Man is true. Man is Kaiser's chosen disciple, and let his superior and engorged-gargantuan loins deluge the slime of elgenism and defeatism\nfrom our seed. All hail Kaiser's seed and immaculate fluids.\n\nAs of thus far, the intent of our father is rather opague, but within the contents of this binding of which follows, all his glory and prowess will be clear. For one to question the prowess\nor glory of our Lordi s blasphemy. Which despite punishment by which of means which shall be shined upon in further detail in at a further period, blasphemy is a sin. Thus, if one were to follow with utmost punctuality, he would find that the treatise\nof which I have been bestowed the pious and ethereal act of concieving is in fact the unwavering voice of Kaiser. It is all very scientific, and though I doubt one may absorb his excellence with ease, for his excellence is that of an infinite well of\ngolden wine, I advise one suckle at my knowledge with great heed. One must not tug nor bite when contracting the teat of Kaiser, one must priase him with a sublt pursuing, for only then will his grace seep at a rate conceivable by his sons.\nThe Sprouting of Man\n\n   The history of man is that of great piety and virtue. In practically all corners of our realm, man's raw exuberance is sown deep within the heart of the Kaiser's Seed, and his mighty, booming prowess can be felt in each and\nevery heart of all who inhabit it. Man has fought with many breeds in his legacy, and man still remains, but not as a refugee or vagabond. Man has survived in a fashion comparable to a seed of iron-wood oak, for his blessing lay deep within the soil,\ndormant but with pride, and when time comes and the Kaiser commands the man to grow, to build, to conquer, then and only then is mans' pride as palpable as the Kaiser's own. \n   Our race emerges from the remains of lesser breeds, fueled by the purity of\nhis white pride and the blessings of our Lord and Savior. All the way he spourts, man takes most attentiveness to his every direction, constantly and diligently enforcing his prowess, his muscles of pure force bulge and pulsate under the immense pressure\nof his pride. It appears that no force could ever discourse his destined and premeditated path, for man will ascend until his most superior of faculties scrapes the heavens and is once again reunited with his benevolent father. \n   His roots at which\npoint cleave deep into the blackened earth, for the front of darkness ever will seep into our fluids. Thus we must fight, we must never, as a hope, as a dream, we must never be diluted by the inferior vestigial corpses of the damned races. And as man's\ngreat limbs spread with unmeasurable force and national pride, the worms of the black sludge will begine to fester. They cross into our realm illegally, without the blessing of the Kaiser, and they burrow deep within our cavities. The very seeds of our\npride have been sabotaged! They feast upon our flesh and excrete tar from their pores. They fester and slosh in such ooze and amass great pits of darkness. They brred with no grace or consent, they feed with glutionous intent, and they spread the foul\nlies of their filthy heathen, sub-humanist Ebolinism.\n   As the sludge of the black worms collects deep within our bowels and extremities, the flame of our brethren begins to fade. The skin of a once pure race will blacken under the tremendous, bloated\nweight of the pestilent bog, and our great minds which once yielded the venerated sciences and arts will rot and drain through our facial cavities. Soon, if we continue on our path so grossly discourse from the Kaiser's will our own beautiful race will no\nlonger be even remotely recognizeable. We will be diluted to a state so impoverished and emaciated of all pride that we will have not even the conviction to cognate the most primal of tasks. We will at this point be that of which we have fought, we will\nbe all which we have feared. We will be the elfen. \n   But alas, this is not the course of man. Man will never be so easily dissolved by such spurious doctrine, for man is the direct fluid of the Holy One, the Creator, The one true hope for the salvation\nfor nationalism and pride. So my dear white brothers, we must show the Kaiser that we are worthy. We must prove to him that we as a hope, as a dream for all that is pure in this realm, the man has not and never will forget his divine quest! Let us\nimpale the rotten flesh with scolding-bladed tapes and drain the fetis wastes from our cavities! Let us carve out the filthy conspirators and blackened worm colonies, from each and every facet of our impenetrable bark of hardened iron!\nLet us Fight, my brothers! Let us fight for the salvation of the Kaiser and his seeds!\nThe Salvation of the Kaiser\n\nPraise He, the one and only, the true voice of good in a realm so corroded by the acrid sins of the lesser races. Praise he whose might and sheer dauntlessness shall cleanse the arachnids of pit and moss, he who\nshall save our white souls from the vile feces of Ebolnism and the Serenist web. Praise he who shall and forever will be the one and the only true God, praise our Lord and our grandest of Kings. All Praise the Kaiser!\n   Praise our blessed hearth, for in\nhis glorious egg lay a seed, a hope, a dream for a world of white fire. All hail the flame of God and King, praise the fervent inferno of cleansing, and let it smolder in the hearts of each and every white man, for now and ever. For us, let the flame\nguide us, let it illuminate the blackened path into oblivion, the shady death march speckled with infected warts of flesh and pus and other such fecal jellies, that of which spawn the prickly seeds of the Degenerate race and the Serenist arachnids.\nBut alas, have not fear my fellow white brothers. Praiser the Kaiser, for through his wisdom may we purge the septic grubs with flame and gas. Let our nationalism and tenacious pride obliterate their weak and feeble and highly demonic colonies. Let our\nwhite flame raze each and every festering cesspit from which they spawn, and let us forcefully enter their diseased posterior cavities in the name of the glorious Kaiser.\n======================================\n\n\n  The Struggle of Our\n    Nation and Great\n         Charter Of\n        Vanderkind\n\n\n\n\n=====================================\nFor the glory of a great nation is to kinder the white flame of our ancestors, the divine right of our Kings, and the holy grace of our one true God. \n\nIn the wake of war and the feckless sheeding of national pride through the unrelenting plot of\nSerenist Ebliontologists in coalition with Communist doctrine, only the few, so the Kaiser wills it, only the most true and pure will survive the coming fire of the primal apocalypses. So when we, as a people, as a hope, must ask why it is that the\nof the black worms in our governments and in the highest and most divine of positions in the high counsel have become so, we must ask ourselves instead why it is that the inferior races have rejected the pious might of the one true Lord and Savior.\nThis is why we must act, for the sake of all that is holy and for the propsperity of culture and civilization, and only through the social rec-construction of our deprived filth of elfen lies and slime can we regain the trust of the Kaiser and pray for\nhis forgiveness.\n\n===The Grace Of===\n====The Kaiser====\n\nAll haill thee who flows water into our rivers, plants seeds, into our soil, delivers bread to our bellies and children to our kindred. Blessed thee, our one true Lord, who in the grace of love\nand pious does he who impregnates the seed of life to our loins and the fires of national pride into our hearts. The Kaiser, in all his glory, is the one and true God, for he and only he is divine and pure. \n\nHowever the Kaiser is displeased with\nour existence. For ages, the Serenists, the enemy of all that is good and beautiful, has festered at the hearts of our brothers. They have plagued the grace and purity of the ethereal and pure Vanders, the one true race, and they have spilled their seeds\namongst the black and sodomite flesh of the negarious degenerate race. Our Savior is furious. He holds our fate in that of which is a thread over the boiling pits of Iblees' grasp. Only his will remains as our salvation, and we have allowed it to be\nspilled out of the crucible of the one, the pure race of men. We have enabled the impure to breed for far too long.\n====The Love====\n===Of the Rector===\n\nIt is the will of the divine right of the RTector and his unfathomable purity to protect the soverignty and pride of our nation, and so it be, the glory of our nation is now buckling under the weight of the\nglutenous elfen conspiracy. Only through the love of Priorism, the one true ideology, can the love and passion of the Kaiser be felt deep within our cavities. heil the Grandmaster, for through his divine right shall we drink the blood of all who oppose\nthe might and prowess of Saradomin and his belssings upon the grace of our nation and the love of our fathers.\n===The Blessings===\n==Of Our Fathers==\n\nLoveth thee who drained the swamps, chiseled the stone, impregnated the woman and filled the Kaiser's realm with the seed of the pure men and his Birthright to Gielinor. Only through the love of our fathers\nmay our seeds be spread into the wombs of the Kaiser's purity, and therefore, the mothers of our race shall be pure. May we suckle from his teat, and love his divine will until the time of departure to the realm of the Kaiser. All hail the Kaiser and the\nfathers of our seed.\n\nIf not for the will of the Kaiser, in all of his blessed glory, shall we dictate his grace amonst the scum races of our plagued realm. Let us Educate the feeble and lost in the glory of national pride and save them from the repugnant\nsludge of Serenism. Let us feed the bellies of the poor with the love fluids of god's seed. Let us forge from the ashes of the quarreling micronations a golden utopia of the pure and strong, and let us sow the seeds of the New World Order.", ""),
        StaticBook("My thoughts", "Mosue", "The people helping us are disgusting. Raising people back to life? What a waste of time. They’re only in it for the bodies we give, and in return they help Kenneth with his research. Honestly, it’s just a waste of time.\nKenneth’s dream of creating that is insanity.But whatever, I’m in it just for the ride, to see where this all goes. Whether I get sacrificed next or not doesn’t matter. -A", ""),
        StaticBook("My Will", "Donn Guthrie", "My Will\n\nIncase something ill should befall me, I will leave the company to my firstborn, if I will at some point have one. And if fate will not have it I will grant the company and all that comes with it to the only person I would trust-\nwith the safety and well-being of The Worshipful Company of Agriculture, my trusted friend Evalien. I hope you will do well with this, and if not, that will be fine aswell. I know you never really were much for responsibilities. \nSigned, Donn Guthrie", ""),
        StaticBook("Mysterious Badge", "Tyrell Blavier", "*A large and decorated \"V\" lies in the center of the page. Around it lies repetition of the phrase \"Pax et Gloria. Safe.\"*\n\n       Agent One\n         P-APP\n          -Q\n          -TB", ""),
        StaticBook("Mysterious Lette", "Wandering Dwarf", "We now hold no stance with what used to be beloved allies,\n\nConquered fearlessly with stories of propaganda and lies,\n\nA mark of our khorvadic ideas, would've proven true as well.\nA tall construct that killed flaster than Dungrimm could know and tell,\n\nMarching on the army of the Dwarves that resided in the bowel,\n\nAfter glancing at our mighty weapon, could they call a foul,\nWith it, we destroyed the city, and perhaps killed them all of,\n\nOur weapon was a sickness, while Dharok was a small and weak Cough,\n\nWe single handedly managed to wipe out the deep dwed, he could not,\nAnd then it turned against us, it was an unlucky mistake we got.", ""),
        StaticBook("Mystery Unsolved", "Samuel de Saltpans", "Perhaps it's due to my inability to choose, but this felt needed to happen. I simply couldn't take it anymore. Join my criminal Saltpan family, or stay as a loyal felsenite in my new home here.\nEdgar says blood runs thicker than water, but I think water runs deep. This is why I simply don't join my brother's ambitions to create some anarchist revolution. What he thinks is justice I think is evil. But then again, he is family. I miss them so much\nMylas hates me for supposedly conspiring with Edgar instead of turning him in. But my intention was to visit him to simply talk, I haven't seen him in years. I didn't plan on joining him, nor did I plan on turning him in. I resent Mylas for nearly-\n-killing Edgar in front of me. Edgar has committed atrocious acts, but I can not let my brother die. Does this make me bad? Does this contribute to the fact perhaps I deserve death for not wanting moral justice towards Edgar.\nHerod has vanished, so does my business ventures I guess. Mylas detests me, the Saltpans ignore me, Balthazar will probably execute me, and Brutalist is too blinded by a constant rage to feel sympathy towards me. Not that I need it anyways.\nI do this because I can't choose a side. In chess, it's called Zugzwang... when the only viable move... is not to move.", ""),
        StaticBook("Nature Healing", "Kirrekith", "Nature Healing\nBy The Sequoia Druid\nPages 17\n\nThe Nature of Druidic Healing\nBy Lilith Winterleaf, the Sequoia Druid.\n\nDruid Healing is a topic many are curious about. Few, even amongst the druids know the true cost\non the person performing the action. Most of the druids use live catalysts to assist in the process of healing. This enables them to draw on this catalysts living energy, this in turn means less energy is draw from the provider to the recipient. However a\nskilled user of this magic type, can find themselves performing the action without a live catalyst without any danger to themselves. \n\nDruidic healing for the most part is basic. It is the recieving and giving of living essence from a provider to a\nrecipient. The druid focuses on the living tissue of the recipients wounds, and asks the body to mend itself, drawing on the catalyst and the druid. Giving their life essence in exchange for the healing aid.\n\nThis is where the costs and risk of a\nDruids healing is, and any would be druid healer should heed this warning well. A druid is capable of amazing feats of healing at times, however it all comes from ones self. In turn, causing possible lasting effects on the provider, and why living\ncatalysts are used to lessen the strain on ones self.\n\nI have personally healed a variety of wounds, from cuts and scrapes to sword clashed to broken bones to some far worse than that. They all draw from you to an extent, even when using a catalyst.\nSimple wounds may show no strain on you, it depends on the severity of the healing needed, and ones personal ability at healing. Practice being key in safeguarding ones self to the harmful effects. \n\nI am in the belief an example of an mistake\nis the most successful way to pass on this lesson to another, I myself, nearly lost my life while healing the King of Skravia back in Asulon. The story had them lured out to a base of mages, that had harassed their kingdom for a while. When they'd\ncornered the mage a trap was sprung, explosives unleased upon the King and Guards. Three died in the blast, others dragged the King back to Skravia (severely wounded) and to my Inn, as they knew I was a healer. His body a mess beyond words to describe, as\nanyone could imagine from an explosion of the magnitude. However one needed to try, coating his wounds in bonemeal and living slime I began my work drawing on the catalyst as well as myself to save the King. It took close to two hours of healing, and left\nhim in a coma for several days. Though I had overstretched myself, my skin a sickly colour, my eyes drained of colour, my lungs not drawing me enough air. I collapsed, and when I woke five weeks had passed, my limbs all sore and my hair a shade lighter,\nthough my skin bore a closer to normal tone. A druid, had come to restore the living essence unto me, otherwise I myself would have perished within the first days of unconsciousness, I was that weakened from the healing.\n\nUnderstand this tale to be a\nof physical limits of ones abilities to perform healing on a mortally wounded individual without assistance or true grasp of your strength in healing. If you step to far you may risk your life as I did. Find yourself a guide in which to walk between your\npersonal sacrificing and also of the catalysts you use to strengthen your abilities, find yourself always something to ease the act of healing, be that grass around you, flowers or trees. Any living catalyst to help carry the burden.\nAs wrote by Lilith Winterleaf, the final page missing as missed during the quick jotting down of information in the raid, however it still bares wise words for anyone believing themselves a druid of power. Always know ones limits, and be sure to use all\nat your disposal.\n\nBy Lilith Winterleaf, re-wrote by Kirrekith Reffahc of the 16th of the Grand Harvest, 1532, during raid on the Orks Capital. \n\nBy Kirrekith Reffahc.", ""),
        StaticBook("Nature Healing", "The Sequoia Druid", "The Nature of Druidic Healing\n\n\nBy: Lillith Winterleaf, the Sequoia Druid\nDruidic Healing is a topic many are curious about, but few, even among Druids, wholly understand the cost on the one performing it.  Most Druids use living reagents to assist in the mending process, this is so that they can draw on the living essense\nwithin the reagent and draw less from themselves, but a skilled Druidic healer can also safely mend wounds without any reagents onhand.\n\nDruidic healing is, quite simply, an exchange of living essence from the healer to the patient.\nThe Druid focuses upon the living tissue around the wound and asks the patient's body to mend itself, giving of their own living essence to aid in the healing.\n\nThis is where the cost and risk of Druidic healing is, and you should heed it well.\nA druid is capable of amazing feats of healing at times, but all of our healing derives from ourselves and it is possible to cause lasting damage to oneself while healing the wounds of another. This is why living reagents are used, to lessen the need to\ndraw from oneself.\nI have personally healed a variety of wounds, from cuts and scrapes to sword clashes to broken bones to some far worse. They all draw from you to some extent, even when using reagents.\nSimple wounds you may not even notice the drain upon yourself, it depends how strong your healing has become, and how familiar you are with the process. Practice truly makes perfect in this regard.\nI am of the belief an example of a mistake is the best way to pass on a lesson, so I will share how I nearly lost my life while healing the King of Skravia back on Asulon. He and some of his soldiers had been lured out to the base\nof a rogue mage that had harassed their kingdom for a long while. When they gained the upper hand and cornered the mage, his trap was revealed, the walls of his base were lined with explosives, and he detonated them.\nThree of the soldiers died in the blast, the others dragged a severely injured but alive King back to Skravia and to my inn, knowing I was a healer. His wounds were great, part of his skull was visible on the top of his head,\nand he had shrapnel wounds all across his body, blood everywhere. There was nothing to do but try, I coated the wounds with a mixture of living slime and bonemeal, then began the healing process,\ndrawing upon the living essences as well as myself to stabilize and mend the kind King laying before me. It took nearly two hours, but his wounds sealed and he was alive and left in a coma for a few days.\nHowever, I had given of myself far more that I should have, my skin was pale, almost white, and my eyes had lost most of their color and I could hardly breathe. I am told I lost consciousness, I awoke five weeks later, my every limb sore,\nmy hair a shade lighter, but my skin almost back to its normal tone. A fellow Druid, Jena, had to come out to restore some living essence to me or I would have perished within the first day or two, I was so weakened.\nTake my mistake with you if you seek to heal, you give of yourself, there is a limit you will reach and you should not go beyond it or you risk your life.  Find your balance between personal sacrifice and reagents to ease your burden,\nyou almost always have something available to ease your personal strain, even if it is the grass around you or a planter of flowers outside the window, any living essence can ease your burden\nif the situation is a bit beyond your ability to heal safely with nothing on hand.\n\n\n~Lillith Winterleaf, the Sequoia Druid", ""),
        StaticBook("Necromancers V I", "Freyr Mantisuku", "Investigations into Necromancers Volume I\nA picture of a man in dark robes standing over dying man a stream of dark green is slowing from the dying man into the robed man hand, two decaying zombies stand behind the dark robed man awaiting his orders*\nArthur: Freyr Mantisuku\nCo-Author: Crineas Acosta\n[Forewarning: Do not confront Necromancers unprepared]\n[Always Bring a Paladin or war cleric with you during hunts]\nA Short Introduction\nNecromancy is the defined pragmatically as the utilisation of Life-Force. Necromancers usually have tell-tale signs of their necromancy,\nIt is like poking a hole in a bucket they can take others life force with the imbalance but their own life force is slowly drained.\n Necromancy is the draining of life-force for nefarious purposes commonly, it’s an art shunned by many.\nAppearance\nThey look like us, For all you know one could be next to you they are very hard to find the only true tell is that many will have a very pale look and are extremely sensitive\nand weak but this does not go for all necromancers. Basically, signs of decay on their bodies would be a significant give-away.\nBehavior\nDue to the extreme difficulty of actually picking one out in a crowded this second cant be added in details.\nStrengths\nThey have the power to resurrect the dead and use them as Minions.\nThey can drain the life force of living things leading to a quick death.\nWeakness.\nLike all mages they are physically weak and can be killed easily..\nSome instances, holy magic can effect them but it's not always the case. \nThey also have the ability to curse other by modifying life force.\nOrigins and Additional details\nHow mortals found this magic is unknown, but it's safe to conclude that the undead under Iblees was instrumental to the art during Aegis\nIt’s likely that they drain life-force whilst using their own bodies to draw it, whether through physical means or through other ways such as mists.\nA note of warning. \nLearning Necromancy is a taboo and would lead to severe repercussions on one’s own wellbeing and health.\nNotes:\nAny extra, Corrections or confirmations on information can be\nSent to Either Freyr, or Crineas (( samsan99, Sharkali ))Further Volumes will be compiled as more information is made available.", ""),
        StaticBook("Necromancy", "Ebonsquire", "Necromancy\n\n((Originally written by Castellano))\nNecromancy - Black Magic; The art of communicating with the dead; Witchcraft; There are many forms of Necromancy, but in this day, there is only secret Necromancy.\n\nA group that people call the \"Undead\" have been known to use Necromancy\nto their full extent. The Necromancers in their organization have been using Necromancy against the people of Aegis. The powers that the dead give them through Necromancy, gives them the ability to summon the dead, use the weather, as in lightning, and\nuse magic that comes from Hell, or also known as \"Nether\".\n\nThe people of Aegis have started to follow the \"Undead\" and Necromancers and have been studying their ways, giving them the ability to use this form of Black Magic. The Ascended(Good Guys) have\nbeen known to be against this magic. Ascended does not patrol the open roads like hte Necromancers and Undead do. Rumors around say that they stay at a heavenly place near the Cloud temple. \n\nThe attacks of the Necromancers have been deadly, and\nusually have won the battle and took the victory back to the Nether and celebrated with the spirits. The only known places that have been attacked are Snowy Fields, Winterfell, Alstion town, and Kal'Bryst. Now, if you haven't noticed already, it has been\ngoing from north to south. In that case, the conditions that have been gathered threw predictions that the next attacks could be at the following cities: Al'Khazar, Stone Leaf, Whispering Isle, and Kal'Alras. They are just slight predictions, the Undead\nprobably won't even attack them. It's just prediction.\n\nThe Undead are growing in numbers, the last known report of them travelling in a pack was the number count of fice. But the last report was long ago. The numbers could have been\ndoubled, no one knows. So, from what you have been reading, the Necromancers are deadly, and you should avoid them at all times. If not, you could lose your life, or loved ones around you.\n\nI, the Author, am leaving the book un-signed, so that\nif an Undead member finds this,  won't be slain. A second book could be created if any more records or information is released. \n\n*Book is un-signed and has blank pages in the back of the book.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Necromancy", "Aeran Winterleaf", "Necromancy\n\nM: Mithras\nA: Aeran Winterleaf\nLich: A lich\nU: Unknown dark elf woman.\n\nThis is a conversation that I (Aeran) had, learning about necromancy.\nTranscript\nM: From what I saw and gathered, necromancy was fueled by draining another person's mana pool.\nA: Mhm, not void magic.\nM: And reusing that energy to lengthen your own life, and add to a bank of life force.\"\nM:Life force is another form of\nmana you see- it's more lively.\nM: But it's not meant to be drawn upon.\nM: By yanking other people's energies their body grows unnnatural to the aiua {soul} they are born with, and begins to decay.\nA: Sounds not fun.\nM: But their life span is\nheightened, and they get stronger and stronger.\nM: Until they descent into wraith-hood once such is decided by the other Grave Lords.\nA: Grave Lords\nA: Can I write this down?\n\nINTERLUDE\nA: Wait, what are Grave Lords?\nLich: Masters of Necromancy.\nA: Are Necromancers still around?\nLich: And yes, necromancers are still around, I wouldn't be around if they weren't.\nM: They are, I impaled one in the shoulder.\nU: Necromancers aren't the type you should feel\nsorry for. Usually.\nM: Never.\nLich: Usually.\nM: I pity their wish for power.\nLich: Not all are senseless killers.\nM: They are, they are bound to eternal service through contracts.\nM: They are forced to be an army of the Gravel-Lords.\nLich: Then you apparently haven't been around them for too long!\nM: Ah?\nLich: Necromancers have all gone loose!\nM: Good, that makes them easier to capture.\nLich: Not really...\nLich: Now they have a council.\nM: It does, not for the clerics-- But for a magi it's no issue.\nM: Irfan still gives me Her blessing\nA: Are you still a necromancer, Mithras?\nM: I never was.\nA: Just knew about em?\nM: I attempted it, yes.\nM: But the second soul issue turned me off", ""),
        StaticBook("Nemir", "Unknown", "She walked onwards, onwards through the darkness. She had walked for so long, so far. The shadows around her seemed like hands, hands that wanted to grab her and drag her into the abyss below. She was unable to recall when she began her trek.\nHer memories were a blur. No matter how hard she tried to remember, she only found that she couldn't. The empty shadows devoured her name and soul. Who was I, why am I walking? Questions plagued her mind everyday.\nThough. she couldn't tell if it was day or not. She couldn't remember what sunlight was like. What the warm essence of day was like on her skin had left her mind long ago. The shadows had drained her life away many centuries, at least she assumed she...\nhad been there for that long. Time was irrelevant in the darkness. All of the pain, all of the loneliness, and all of the despair beat her down every second that passed by. Yet, there was one thing that kept her mind intact...\nOne simple thought that kept the infernal darkness at bay...\n\n\"I must keep going...\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Nemir T.", "Ol' Man Sano", "Dear Nemir,\n\nDating back to the early days of Felsen, when I had been a fresh recruit, I do remember the horrible man who took my eye had attempted to do the same to you.\nThat occassion where we had met, I was desperatley concerned for your life; However, I am grateful to see that you've found yourself in a community of scholars who deeply care about you, as well, in-\naddition to a wonderful husband. Please, do take this hankerchief, as well as this pearl jewelry. I wish you nothing but luck, and may we see eachother once again some other day.", ""),
        StaticBook("Nemir's Notes", "Nemir", "Entry one, 9th of Malin's Welcome, 1569.\nIt's another cool day here in Kovagrad, there's a nip in the air.  The cold won't be good for the crops.  Never is.  But I hardly need to worry about that.  I'm no farmer, just a simple herbalist.\nNotes of lesser accuity potions.\n-----------\nI've prepared a couple of bottles of aqua vitae, just had to soak this red root in warm water for a few hours.  It's pure alcohol, perfect for greater potions.  Along with the aqua vitae, I've prepared a couple\nof bottles of distilled water.  These are for lesser potions.  Gonna need some more coal or perhaps some charcoal soon if I want more of these lesser bases.\n\n\nAlright.  Now that I've got my bases all set up, I'm gonna put some larihei's fingers\ninto the aqua vitae.  I ended up getting a salve of larihei.  Upon using it I've noticed my movements were more... delicate for a short amount of time.  Perhaps an agility potion could come out of this.\nI added halflings grass and got something I like to\ncall a soft relxant.  It pretty much soothes muscle pain for a short amount of time.  Perfect for sore muscles!  I believe this should be enough notes for the day.  I shall continue tomorrow or perhaps sometime later on this week.\nEntry two, 12th of Malin's Welcome, 1569.\nToday I've decided to mess around with the distilled water as the base.  I will do as I did the other day, use larihei's fingers.  The outcome of this was a potion that, when drunken, I felt like my mind was\nclearer.  I was more aware of my movements, could be useful.  Upon adding halfings grass to the potion I got a liquid that was thinner than water, and it swirled nonstop within the bottle.  Upon testing it, my vision was blurred greatly, though I felt\nmore agile.  I guess it'd be helpful.\n\nEntry three, 11th of The Deep Cold, 1569.\nSimple poisons.\nRed Mushroom Poison, makes the user have an upset stomach and feel nauseated.  Good for telling someone to fuck off when they ask for wine.\nPotion of Alabaster Leaf, about the same effects as the last poison, but looks more like tea than wine.  Plus it doesn't have white particles floating around in it.  Potion could also be used as an antidote to other poisons.  If used as one, it'd still\nmake the user's stomach upset.\nPotion of Saffvil, if this is consumed in large amounts the user will die due to its poison.  If consumed in smaller amounts the user will just vomit.\nPotion of Clutcher's Straw, if this potion is taken in large amounts\nthe user's muscles will lock up, paralyzing them.  They will remain conscious.\nParalyzing Toxin, this seems to be one of the most deadly poisons I've ever made.  Any amount taken makes the user paralyzed, keeping them from seeking out an antidote.\nAnother effect is that the user will struggle to breath, eventually suffocating them.\nParalyzing Tonic, another helpful poison.  If the user takes any amount of this poison they will become paralyzed and blind for a short amount of time.", ""),
        StaticBook("Nephilim", "Unknown", "Azdrazi ou Nephilim are followers of dragons, specificly azdromoth from the sightings seen by the writter. These beings have some sort of fire magic, through it seems to be created a lot faster then voidal based pyromancy. Notable location:\nThe giant castle near haria, that contains a sword in a stone, said to be an artifact for these people.\n\nDragonkin are also associated with these beings. Notably Anethera, a elf looking being with horns comming out of her head.\nThey are capable of invoking Azdromoth through prayer, but he normally does not travel with them.\n\nTheir goal is to kill unholy beings, such as the same type the Aengulic Cult Groups Hunt.\nThey claim to be followers of GOD.\n\nThey seem able to heal themselves through their magic.\n\nNot much else is known about these creatures, but more is discovered every day.", ""),
        StaticBook("New Elven III", "Valmir_", "New Elven Lessons: Volume 3 \nby Kalenz Uradir (SupremacyOps)\nTo conjugate verbs in elven one must note precisely what person is being referred to in the sentence. Then the verb is conjugated:\n-e - First person singular \n-a - Second person singular \n-e - Third person singular \n-ae - First person plural \n-an - Second person plural\n-eyae: Third person plural\nTo create past and future tenses is quite simple in elven. However, it takes specific forms depending on the time of day. For these two tenses the following four words are used:\nKarin'ento - Next sunrise \nKarin'ante - Last sunrise \nKer'ento - Next sunset \nKer'ante - Last sunset\nIf it is night at the time the elf refers to the past or present the two forms with the 'Ker' are used. If it is day at the time the elf refers to the past or present the two forms with 'Karin' are used. These endings are simply added on to the end of\nsentences to designate the tense. \n\nFor example: Kalenz iyathe (Kalenz thinks) becomes Kalenz iyathe ker'ante (Kalenz thought). Assuming the time in which it is spoken is the night. \n\nIn spoken elven, particularly more casual speech these endin\noften shortened into the slang of karinto, karinte, keno and kente.", ""),
        StaticBook("New Elven Vol I", "Kalenz Uradir", "New Elven Lessons: Volume 1\nby Kalenz Uradir\nIn elven grammatical structure is often different to that of common. For one instead of placing an adjective before a noun it is placed after said noun. This becomes particularly important for the most basic of greetings.\nKarin'ayla - Goodmorning\nKer'ayla - Goodnight\nVan'ayla - Goodbye\n\nEach places the time of day before the adjective describing it. Noun and adjective are separated by an apostrophe.\nOther important words for the beginner in elven include race names:\n\nMali - Elf\nUruk - Orc\nValah - Human\nBortu - Dwarf\nIn order to form sub-races of elves, adjectives are taken to add more detail to the word Mali.\n\nMali'ame - Wood Elf\nMali'aheral - High Elf\nMali'ker - Dark Elf\nIn order to form sub-races of other cultures the suffix tali- may be used. This word most directly means 'part of'.\n\nTali'uruk - Goblin (Lit. Part Orc)\nTali'valah - Halfling (Lit. Part Human)\nOther basic phrases include exclamations including:\n\nAyla - Good\nSul'leyun - Brilliant (Lit. Beautiful Light)", ""),
        StaticBook("New Elven Vol II", "Kalenz Uradir", "New Elven Lessons: Volume 2\n by Kalenz Uradir\nJust as in common, pronouns may be used to replace nouns. The pronouns in elven are as follows: \n\nKae - Me \nLae - Him/He \nNae - You \nLye - We - Used to speak of elves, people or the world. \nHae - Her/She\nFor example the sentence 'elvulnir van ayla' (The trickster fared well) may be transformed into 'Lae van ayla' (He fared well). \n\nIn addition to this, other good language supplements to anyone learning elven include basic affixes. These affixes may be\nadded to create further detail or form critical grammatical structures in a sentence.\nThe dash denotes location of seed word. Affixes and seed words are separated by an apostrophe. \n\nac- (aca-) - Honorific for accursedness. \nah- (ahe-) - Honorific for reverence. Often used as a prefix for scholars. For example: Ah'Lucion.\nfi- - New or anew.\ncer- (Slang from Ceru) - Honorific for strength. Often used as a prefix for those of high military rank. For example: Cer'Silir.\n-ante (-nte) - Last \n-ento (-nto) - Next \n-onn - From or born. \nu- - Or\nvul- (cule) - Clever or deceptive. \n-ir - Designates purpose of someone or something. \n-sae - The spreading, development or management. \n-ii - Diminutive form. For example: Malii, meaning little elf.\nAs always, a full list of affixes may be found in the Elven Dictionary.", ""),
        StaticBook("New Elven Vol IV", "Valmir_", "New Elven Lessons: Volume 4\nby Kalenz Uradir (SupremacyOps)\nIn elven, numbers are formed by the composition of multiple words. Each word representing the magnitude of the number. To note a number between one to ten the simple word in elven to use. To express a multiple of ten, an elven number is placed before a\nmultiple of ten. \n\nFor example: nuit'matelu means 200.\n1 - oem \n2 - nuit \n3 - hael \n4 - vailu \n5 - kulin \n6 - banih \n7 - laier \n8 - esun \n9 - moiel \n10 - telu \n100 - matelu \n1000 - marmatelu\nAnother particularly useful prefix not mentioned before is 'fer'. Fer is used in combination with seed words to form the names of handheld tools. Some such examples include those below. However, to those more advanced in elven others may be thought up.\nFer'ame - Axe \nFer'thuln - Pickaxe \nFer'nor - Shovel \nFer'sul - Torch \nFer'bilok - Hammer \nFer'norsae - Hoe", ""),
        StaticBook("New Elven Vol V", "Valmir_", "New Elven Lessons: Volume 5\n by Kalenz Uradir (SupremacyOps)\nIn elven in order to denote affiliation the suffix -leh is used. It is placed after the object and designates the possession of said object by the subject of the sentence. However, it also has a use when no object in the sentence can be found and means in\nsuch a case 'spirit'. This also contributes to the common farewell blessing \"kaean'leh evareh\" which means \"may it protect us\". \n\nIt is also worth learning the 'operative' which is also seen in the sentence above on in word 'evareh' .\nIn elven it serves the purpose of turning a verb into a wish. It is conjugated as below:\n\n-eh - Operative singular \n-erih - Operative plural (-arih if the verb ends in -ar)", ""),
        StaticBook("New Pumpkin Lord", "Carver Le Prevost", "The Halflings Adventure to find the Pumpkin lord.\n\nWritten by Carver Le Prevost\nThis trip, or adventure started out with me yelling about Humans, then it ended up with me keeping a young halfling safe. This young halfling is now the owner of the Pumpkin lord. Or so I persume\nIt started out with an army of Halflings coming into the library. I showed them the Pumpkin mask and they were about to go on their way. I asked to join these men and they agreed. We went through an orc battlefield. We then crossed over a Giant's home.\nAfter that we went through a dark land and then into a castle. The Castle was obviously evil you could feel it. But the hobbits showed no fear. They were on a mission and I had no idea what this mission was. The leader was named Ol Willow, the rest\nI have no idea. They had to Biguns with them me and a girl. When we reached the giants they said, \"Now thats a bigun.\" We reached the castle and went to some wierd space where it was like the cloud temple but wasn't. It was dark. It was evil.\nThey were on their mission and we reached the top of a large building. Underneath it was an auctioneer and at the foot of the building sat a lone pumpkin. A lone solitary pumpkin. The kid tried to grab it and was pushed away. He praiesed it.\nAnother halfing touched it and was zapped. I tried to touch it and I was pushed away. The lady tried to touch it and she was greeted with a terrible scream. The kid touched it and grabbed it. He yelled in joy. A loud yell was greeted along with it. The\nexit was blocked by both a Knight who was wondering why we were they before he tried to kill us and then a giant pumpkin head in the distance the great pumpkin lord. We ran all escaped execpt for Ol Willow who fought off the dread knight while I took\ncharge and brought everyone home. We have an artifact. We need the artifact. The Halflings are strong. We need to get them to give the Pumpkin over. \nAll praise the pumpkin lord. \nAll praise Ol willow for saving us.", ""),
        StaticBook("Niut", "Zaniil Tinuvriel", "Niut\nBy Zaniil Tinuvriel\nIn all the world the self same of any race are considered rare: more so for those as infertile as we.\nPerhaps we can delve further into this most interesting of facts. I should like to give rise to deep thought in this book, to ponderings regarding the\noddity of twins among our kin.\n\nJust as hair of thilln is considered most pure, perhaps two can duplicates of our species be seen in much the same light?\nThese obvious and unusual traits lead to much speculation.\nCould it be that only Mali’aheral of the most pure lineage can be blessed with such striking aspects? Let us consider what is one of the most important of times for our kind:\nthe birth of a Mali’aheral.\nGenesis within the cihi is without doubt, a momentous event. One would suggest that the spawning of two Mali’aheral on one occasion reveals to us the workings of the maehr’sae hiylun’ehya. Progress through strict breeding of\nonly the most pure of kin, resulting in health of procreation.\nI shall leave it to other Mali’aheral to think on this subject.\nThose that wish to debate with the author can do so by locating him at his home: linvallei’kulin.\n           ---------------", ""),
        StaticBook("Norland Paragons", "Sven", "1. Eirik the Great\n2. Edvard the Terrible\n3. Thoromir the Father\n4. Snow the Magus\n5. Myro the wordsmith\n6. Vykk the Founder\n7. Bjorn the Gruff\n8. Beo the Betrayer\n9. Sven the Bard\n§\nEirik the Great\n-Eirik is well known for his legendary feats of diplomacy and leadership. This Norlander is the ultimate example of a great man.\nEdvard the Terrible\n-Edvard was a cruel and wicked man who continously backstabbed and betrayed all other nations until eventually he alienated Norland from any potential allies, allowing Norland to be set upon by the nations of the world.\nEdvard the Terrible is a reminder of the importance of loyalty. Edvard the Terrible is the Paragon of Evil and Sloth.\nThoromir 'The Father' Ruric\n-Thoromir was known for his grand and towering castles and sturdy walls, but most of all for founding house Ruric. Thoromir Ruric was the first king of Norland yet many details have been forgotten about him over the years.\nIt is commonly know however that Thoromir was a kind man and a fierce enemy. He is considered the Paragon on Paternity, Strength, and Architecture.\nSnow 'The Magus' Volaren\n-Snow was well known for his abilities to wield the arcane art of Fire Evocation. Snow has been the only mage to ever hold any spot of nobility in Norland, he was considered to be cold, snappy, and powerful. Snow is the Paragon\nof Magic.\nMyro the Wordsmith\n-Myro was known for his way with the art of writing. One of the original Thalian founders of Norland he preferred the power of the quill over the sword. Myro is considered to be the Paragon of study and learning.\nVykk 'The Founder' Volaren\n-Vykk founded Norland and is the only paragon known to be currently still alive, Vykk has become a secluded elf who rarely interacts with Norland anymore, however, he is considered a man of great influence and\nPower to the Norlandic people. He is considered the Paragon of Creation and Survival.\nBjorn 'The Gruff' Rayeckson Ashtyr\n-Bjorn, the son of Rayeck was the first Champion of the red brothers, and the strongest fighter of his time. Bjorn was a learned commander in battle and was able to beat back the enemies of Norland with ease. Bjorn is\nconsidered the Paragon of Fighting and Strategy.\nBeo the Betrayer\n-Beo led a rebellion which lasted less than two weeks, attempting to steal Norland which he had been charged with protecting while his cousin, the king, presided in the south ruling over Nyrhold. Beo is the Paragon of Failure and\ntreachery.\nSven 'The Bard' Ruric\nSven took after his father, Eirik the Great' Promoting the study of arts and literature, and even learned the arts of the Bard. When his family called upon him he Sven became the King of Norland, when his older brother was able,\nSven stepped down graciously allowing his elder to lead, resuming his work as a bard, inspiring the Norlandic people with his many works of poems, songs, stories and tales. Sven is the Paragon of the arts.", ""),
        StaticBook("Norsenth'onn ...", "oppay", "*The title is partially cover with blood.\nAt Norsenth'onn the gate are all time open to welcome the visitor in the city, but some day it should have be close. A armor creature come into the manor where Ac'Aelu and Titania were speaking.\nWithout advise the creature get on the platform and try to break the throne. For the safety of the other city member, they close the manor gate to trap the monster inside. They slipped away into a back room to grab her weapon and call the Silan'Sul guard.\nThe Sil'Taynei, Gathain Telvhanim, was the first to response. When he reach the gate the princess open the gate for let him enter and side with them agains the armor thing.\n*Blood cover the rest of the text.", ""),
        StaticBook("Northal, Hanseti", "Aetosion", "The Lands of Northal in Anthos, A Compendium of Environmental and Historical Information\n~~~~~~~+~~~~~~~\nby The Rt. Hon. Edward, second of his name, of the noble House Winter of the lands herein writ.\nNorthal --- A History\n~~~~~~~+~~~~~~~\n       Chapter I\nNorthal, previously within the demesne of the Kingdom of Hanseti, was never properly settled. In fact, the past human habitation of Northal is so entirely unremarkable that the writer isn't even sure the purpose of this passage. Previously unsettled, and\nonly recognized as arctic wasteland \"Wall-Adjacent\", it was unused by its lords, left as ice and stone. It was not until the modern lords and ladies of House Winter, and their hardy bannermen and vassals approached the steep and snowy cliffs, and said,\n\"Yes, this is land. It can be tamed like any other,\" and so it was. The tundras remained just as glacial, but the indomitable human spirit prevailed against the elements. The County of Northal was chartered by his grace, the Duke Codrik Green, for his new\nfound vassal, the Rt. Hon. Lord Robert Winter, son of Harold.\nNorthal --- A Land\n~~~~~~~+~~~~~~~\n       Chapter II\nThe lands of Northal stretch from the old Teuton bridge due east of the Castle Greywyn, to the open seas of Valence off the eastern coast of the Kingdom of Oren. Defining the Southward border is the sharp shift in flora and fauna notable where snow begins\nto fall south of the wall. The northern border is, of course, the North Icewall. Built by whatever force for whatever reason, no human who has dared summit it has come back entirely intact. These borders, effective by edict of his grace, the Duke Codrik\nGreen, determine the bounds of the land.\nNorthal --- A Climate\n~~~~~~~+~~~~~~~\n      Chapter III\nThe climate of Northal is the most entirely inhospitable south of the Wall. Any man, elf, or dwarf idiotic enough to build their home within these lands comes out a member of a hardened folk. The lands are infertile and barren, a layer of permafrost rests\njust beneath the soil, requiring intensive labour to render what sparse deposits of nutrient poor soil there are in Northal, usable for planting. However, it is still somehow managed, but what magics of a massed peasantry it cannot be fathomed. The\navailable land to be built upon is rocky and irregular. To traverse it is difficult, and to establish is even moreso. Excluding the pockets of flatland within Northal (namely, Ice Lake, Snowy Pass, and Bridge Gully), all other locales must be mined into\nwith a strong iron pick to break through the frozen stone and ice. It is postulated that these rare pockets are the result of glacial movements centuries past, which carved out basins into the terrain, and later melted to water the fields of Ager. The\nhigh temperatures of the land are rivaled only by the peaks of the Silver Mountains of Furnestock, and at only at one month during the year in the height of summer does the temperature rise above freezing, enough so for the ice of Northal to sweat and run\nthin streams down the cliffs into Ager, the Greymarsh, the Raev, and Norfolk. Lower down the mountains these streams gather into stillwater pools, which will continue to provide irrigation for southward farmlands, even when the water in the high up lands\nof Northal remains frozen. It is said that if you piss towards the Castle Greywyn in the dead of night, from any peak in Northal, that the ghost of the Hochmeister Mirtok will freeze your piss into a spear and the winds will blow it back into you, running\nyou through with your own piss. A nastier death a man could never fathom. The mountains of Northal are home to the frozen corpses of hermits, and the bundled men of the Winter, and none other.\nAn Author's Note.\n~~~~~~~+~~~~~~~~Father, why didn't you move us to Salvus. There is a complete lack of immoral Southeron noblewomen. Send help.\n-The Rt. Hon. Edward Winter II\n\n*The Snowflake Sigil\nof House Winter*", ""),
        StaticBook("Note", "Ceto", "~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~It is with a broken heart that I write this. I have made the decision to leave for good. I will not interfere with anyone of you no more. Sahar won as in defeat I will simply cease to be. Do not look for me as you will never find me..\n..where I am going. Allah guides me now, I love you Father..Mother..Brothers..but my time is at an end. I tried to stop her from making mistakes but I failed. May allah punish her for this. I am no longer a Kharadeen as I disown myself..\n..of my name. I am sorry that it had to come to this but I wish that you enjoy your lives and that you may find a happy ending in this storm. \nBeloved daughter and sister..\n\n-Ceto", ""),
        StaticBook("Note", "Jester", "*A small piece of paper quite obviously ripped from a full page is splattered and scribbled on with purple-ish ink*\nSince I know you collect shit like this I decided it would be better off gathering dust with you rather than gathering dust in a warehouse. I hope you don't mind but I donated some books and important notes you gave me a while back.\nIf you don't want any of it, throw it away.\n\nJester.", ""),
        StaticBook("Note 2.", "Hiylu Oronar", "[!] A second note, in Hiylu's typical messy handwriting! This one would have a small doodle of a cat on it.\n\"Dear maln again! You won't believe it, haelun's back! We're living in Devirad until you're back, with the magic people.\n\nWe miss you! ~Hiylu.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Note to Arabella", "Orileth", "First and foremost, I should apologize for writing what I am to say within the contents of a letter rather then facing you myself. Recent circumstances have prevented me from such. Nonetheless, I wish to keep this simple and to the point, Ara. I am to be\nleaving for quite some time, and do not wish to cause you grief by making you wait for me. It would be in both of our best interests to see others. This isn't to say I wish to be your enemy, as you are indeed a wonderful woman. With this letter, I hope to\nat least remain your friend for years to come.\n\n\n-Orileth", ""),
        StaticBook("Note-Block Organ", "The Musician", "How To Tune A\n  Note-Block Organ\n\nA note-block organ is a simple instrument, actually composed of several complex boxes which produce a single note each. These boxes can be tuned to produce most any note on the scale.\nIn order to tune each box, one must turn a crank once to the right for each step up the octave.\n\nFor simplicity's sake, this book only records the C major scale, but their range begins at F# below C, and can be turned 24 times before returning to F#.\nIt is interesting to note that the box's tone changes depending on what material they sit upon. Wood produced a deep, resonating sound, while simple dirt and most other materials creates a sound that is the closest to an actual organ or harp.\nC MAJOR SCALE\n\nC: 6 turns\nD: 8 turns\nE: 10 turns\nF: 11 turns\nG: 13 turns\nA: 15 turns\nB 17 turns\nC: 18 turns", ""),
        StaticBook("Note.", "Stefjan Kovachev", "You look so beautiful.", ""),
        StaticBook("Note.", "Erin Lockley", "Note:\n\n\"So far I have come home to a good selection of crops. I am impressed and pleased. \n\nI currently have a high demand for leather, so please do not mind the cows in the field. You are free to avoid that field\nentirely, if you are not comfortable around them. I simply need more space for them to roam.\n\n-Erin.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Notes", "Renn", "*A majority of the notes were written in haste.*\n\nNecromancy, mysticism, shade curse, and blood magic.\n\nMysticism involves mystics using an odd mist to blind people, among other things.\n\nMysticism, as well as-\nnecromancy is believed to involve a large stone. Called a 'menhir'. This binds souls to create things and enchantments; such as dreadknights. It can only be assumed it can be used in other ways.\n\nShade magic utilizes dangerous black tendrils as a combat-\nmechanism.\n\nEvark Evocress is also known as Ljhin.\n\nThe Frost Mother is known as Sif, Yule, or Taliyu.\n\nRenowned shade known as Corvo, or Adniel. Often accompanied by a pale white-haired student, who often-\nwill call himself 'only a simple telekinetic mage'. Though he may have wind evocation.\n\nCorvo, or Adniel, also knows about mysticism.\n\nSome of these are 'believed to be another being or entity entirely'.\n\nAnother frost witch-\nis Luxly, 'Mints', or Ituri.", ""),
        StaticBook("Notes on Orcs", "Kalvo Delevoye", "- Skulls.. lots of them..\n- Temple (Lots of books) ontop of the hill.\n-- cozy tavern looks like they have good ale here\n-weapons and armour + iron cheap\n- Clan halls ontop of big hill good advantage point for arrows\n- Also Kharajyr Village\n-Large deep pit for pushing victims in ontop of clan hill\n- Huge Orc flag ontop of hill main centre spot of city\n-Can't explore clan houses lc permit\n-sandstone after sandstone builds..\n-Fort on hill side, high sandstone walls\n-Smoking tent\n-Totem of Akezo Spirit of health\n- Large farm area, aquaduct supplies water to farm from hill side\n- Cages hang everywhere here but all empty?\n-Got a free cookie didn't I boii\n--Animal pens by front of city\n- Underground arena\n-The arena is a ice floored arena..?\n-Mines\n-Palace of the rex ~ Big hall with big tables, big ass throne for big ass orcs", ""),
        StaticBook("November", "The March Ash", "The bones weigh heavy on me, they break my body and my spirit. November. The name still stings. The memories are wasps in my mind. The pain brings tears to my eyes.", ""),
        StaticBook("Nutshell: Dwarve", "Garoll", "Dwarvern Capital. A guide to this magnificent town and it sorroundings!\nHome to all of Urugans children. (The dwed.) It is ruled by the high king who is elected by Merits or Senates.\n\n\n(Primary Source being Thond Doomforged- Commander)\nThey have a few vassals. Such as the mountain town of Yolwin and a port town.\nUnder the cities. There are the clans. Which are basically Noble Familes- But dwarvern. They trace their heritage from the very roots of this kingdom! Formed from perhaps the oldest of ancestors!\nThe obsidian throne. The person I asked seemed slightly... Hesitant about answering but this is what I learned.\nThe oldest known throne! Knobody knows how it was made, some says the gods and others say dwarvern magic! The grandest throne in Axios!\nI noticed the ceiling formed with odd crystals. They are all perfectly natural says the man. Truly beautiful!\nArcadia. This is an odd city- Near the dwarvern capital... Truly Freezing cold may I add!  Home of the engineers. The ironguy clan. Arcadia holds many dwarvern secrets- I want to learn more...\nThe Ironguts. Clan that rule Arcadia. These are the ones who make runes- Being mostly connected to the void which allows them to access the arcane arts which runes are used for.\nThe person I am asking is not allowed to tell me much about runes...\nPolitics. Dwarves are currently at war with the Norlanders. This seems to be a grudge from wrongly crossing (Norlanders to Dwarves) in a bad way. During the oren empire days.\n(Side note: Arcadia is near a large pool of thaumium- I was told anyway)\nDwarf and Dwarvern. This is associated with the Dwed (obiously) I ask what he associates with Dwed. This is the given answer.\nProud people, Stubborn as stone. They suffer dangers other races would tremble at. The best\nWarriors and craftsmen that he knows. (Somewhat Bias I assume)", ""),
        StaticBook("NV-02", "liam_barnett", "10th of the Amber Cold, 1567\n\nNemir Valnelis\n\nThe following is the account of what took place on the night of the 15th of Sun's Smile, 1567\nThis will be a transcript of Miss Valnelis' own testimony, word for word.\nSection I:\n\nVictim claims that she arrived at the gates, alone, hoping to enter in order to purchase a drink. She found two guards arguing, presumably Corporal Crider and Lieutenant Smyth.\nAs the woman was arrested, on the grounds of being an 'Aheral, she was taken to the cells beneath Ancelcourt, strapped into the chair by Smyth, accompanied by Sano, Zenik, and Crider.\nAs the victim was trapped in the chair, Crider and Sano protested, protecting the woman. Crider lunged towards Smyth, fed up with his, quote, \"Abnormal acts of violence,\" and Zenik knocked him out cold, using\na glass bottle, breaking it against his head. They proceeded to hang Crider up on the wall, and Sano departed.\nSection II:\n\nAfter the departure, Smyth took out his knife, gliding it across the victim's cheek. He began asking the woman questions, such as the following:\n\"What's your name?\"\n\n\"How badly do you want to live?\"\n\n\"Who would miss you if you were to die?\"\nAfter answering these questions, Crider came to, starting to look around the room. As he was already pinned to the wall, unable to move, Smyth ordered Zenik to hit his head with a rock.\nAfter Zenik had done so, Smyth ordered him to do it again, but harder this time, and that is where Crider's head was removed. Zenik then took Valnelis' own dagger, and returned it by darting it at her feet.\nSection III:\n\nAfter being released, Valnelis ran outside, greeted by Sano, Crawley, accompanied by Zenik, and met with a man named Vargen, a concerned friend.\nThis is a compiled report of the actions of Lieutenant Smyth on the night of the 15th of Sun's Smile, 1567. Recorded by Bell Sano, and accompanied by Michael Raher and Erren Crawley.", ""),
        StaticBook("O. Studies I", "Orithur", "~:;: The Voidal Egg :;:~\n\n- Orithur's Studies-\n------------------- Entry 1: \nI was recently approached by a resident of Hualthal known as 'Archembalt'. He claimed to have been approached by a mysterious and seemingly powerful\nstranger known as 'Errant'. Archembalt revealed to me that this Errant had given him some sort of orb covered with intricate yet unknown markings. Together we studied the object for some time before it was decided we should attempt to open it. Upon\nseveral strikes to the orb, it split open perfectly down the middle, causing a gooey creature resembling that of a large leech to fall out. The creature for some time remained motionless. Archembalt then remarked that the orb in question seemed to warm to\nthe touch of a magic-user, but remain cold to the touch of a non-magic user. Then, when going to touch the 'leech', it sprang up and attached itself to his arm. I had seen such a creature documented before in the library of Dragur, seen on several\noccasions to be feeding off objects and people of significant mana. As such, I am naming the creature, the Mana Leech.\n\nThe Mana Leech could not be pulled from the man's arm due to its toughness and slipper hide, but\nstrangely, but a matter of chance we inflicted pain upon Archembalt, and as a reaction the creature somewhat evolved, growing small legs and expanding in size. We continued to beat the man and watch as the evolution process continued to work, assumedly as\nan act of self-defence for its host.\n\nHowever, when the creature reached the size of a large dog, it sprang from Archembalt's arm and fled. We were unable to find it.\nEntry 2:\nSeveral days have passed and the creature has been sighted outside Hualthal. It was chased and followed across the snow plane until it suddenly stopped, and dug straight downwards. After digging up the earth in pursuit, we\nencountered something so bizarre and extraordinary, that words can barely describe. We encountered a massive, large black orb the size of a small house, hiding all this time beneath the earth. The creature was then never seen,  it either entered the orb\nor became one with its mass.\n\nThe egg, and an egg I assume it to be due to the similar marking as the previous smaller orb, was excavated and a small fortification was constructed around it so that it may be studied. There is a runic symbol\natop the egg, red in colour. The pattern is detailed below:\n\n             +\n      +     +     +\n             +\n             +\n             +\n        +       +\nI have seen no pattern or symbol like it. I will study further.\nEntry 3:\nI have concluded that the larger egg and the leech from before are both Voidal in nature, as much like other noted voidal creatures they are resiliant to physical attack and magical attack only fuels them. However, the markings and the rune\nappear to suggest that an intelligent force is at work here - these creatures are unlike any other voidal beings encountered in the past.\n\nThe leech has not been sighted again and the egg shows no change.\nEntry 4:\nAmazingly, the egg has changed and altered. Four large tentacle-like chitinous growths have extended at equal distances apart around its edge, extending about 3 meters into the air. As well as this, the rune in the centre has now\nchanged from the previous design, to this:\n\n             +\n      ++          ++\n      +             +\n             +\n         +      +\n         ++++++\n\nI have also noticed that when in proximity\nto the egg, I could hear a faint sound, similar to a whisper on a gust of wind. At first I believed it to be interference on my telepathic field that connects me to my brother, but alas the mortals about me confirmed to hear the whispering.\nEntry 5: The 'egg' has transformed once more. It now stands as a large obelisk, breaking the structure it was contained within.\n\nIt has remained in this state for a very long peroid of change. No further change has occured.", ""),
        StaticBook("Observations I", "Lorar Minskin", "Observations and Their Benefits\n-------------------Written by Lorar Min.\n-------------------  As you look around do you notice the fate of the people around you? The tick tock of the clockwork and the innerworkings of the life they live is set in stone.\nIt is to the point of which it seems that even the biggest actions seem to have no effect in pulling people out of this loop. Now, It'd be safe for me to say that you are probably one of those people who dilly-dally around and are stuck in one preset path\nin which you feel that you have no control over. Infact It'd also be safe for me to say that you, yourself, the person that is reading this is so clueless that they don't even realize that they're stuck in this loop. You need help, fast.\n Unlike others\nbefore you, these events don't need to happen. They don't need to be one event piling on another and another to the point of no return. You, yes you have a chance to stop this. At this point I'd say you're quite confused on what I'm talking about. I'm\ntalking about your old friend who is predetermined every single, every single day I tell you to do the same exact thing in which he does the same exact tasks until the point of no return. That no returning point being death. I'm talking about changing\nwhat you're doing. For better or worse, for the danger, for the fun, for the neverending amazement of not knowing what is going to happen next. Unlike your ancestors you can change what your future may hold. Perhaps your grandfather was a carpenter and\nyour father was also a carpenter and by golly-gee you better be a carpenter. That, that itself is what I'm talking about. Do not follow what is preset for you, stand out.\n You've got one life and you better make it worth living because who knows what\ntommorrow may hold. Take that last step, eat that extra roll, ask to court that special lady, do whatever you feel like you may never have another chance to do. Because who knows, you might not be there the next day to do it.\n\n-My First Book, Lorar", ""),
        StaticBook("Obsidian Planes", "Gabriel", "We have reached the Obsidian Planes. The ground lets your foot sink in slightly. With bits of obsidian and netherack scattered about.\n\nThe climate here is hot and dry. I had to remove some clothing to stay at a nice temperature.\nWe found weird creatures called 'Pigman.' They seem to be carry swords of Gold and are passive agressive. They seem to stick to packs and hunt in them.\n\nWe found a temple or something with beams of light shooting out. We might investigate\nWe have decided not to investigate at this time. Eyvind has written the area down in his map ((-761 -3216))\n\nWe have found the edge of the world. All that is down is a drop. Nothing but a drop. Just, empty open nothing.", ""),
        StaticBook("Obsidian Planes", "Sighard An'Halstaig", "Mission Log: Obsidian Planes Temple\n\nI:\nTook the cart from the Blood Baron's keep. Horse couldn't trot from the beggining of the Planes. Time to continue on foot.\n\nII:\nTraversing the Planes isn't hard for some prepared fellows. Avoiding the\nblobs is not a hard job, and the Pigmen are docile if not hungry.\n\nIII:\nFound the temple. A portal leads within it, and there's an annatural feeling going about the place.\n\n>Inside area is warded off. Pigmen trot about the place. Further\nexpeditions with more numbers might be required to search throughout the temple's confines.\n\n\nIV:\nThe outside isn't much, though some sort of beam goes up, and leads to some sort of starry contraption. What if this is some sort of center hub for the\nObsidian Planes?\n\n\n\nOVERALL:\n\nResults have not been as fruitful as I thought. A big expedition should be formed. This isn't something to be branded as a mere cartography mission. The burning star in the sky leads me to believe that this\ntemple has an active role in the mystery that is the Obsidian Plane itself. As said, a prepared expedition of good, able men should be formed, in order to actively search for the temple's secrets.\n\n\n--END--", ""),
        StaticBook("Obtain Intel", "Regale Ba'ikana", "Gather information on two elves, not affiliated with the Warhawke group.", ""),
        StaticBook("Official Writ", "Lilyana", "17th of the Deep Cold, 1588\n\nTo the citizens and vassals of the Federation of Sutica,\n\nIt is decreed by the Crown of Sutica that this man, and the search party that accompanies\nhim, is given permission and rights to search the City of Suitca, its vassals, and lodgings for the treasonous High Pontiff Theodosius II.\n\nAny citizen or vassal is instructed to turn over this man immediately to the\nEmpire and their men.\n\nShould any citizen or vassal be found assisting the accused from escaping justice, they will be turned over to the Empire as well for their part in harboring a fugitive.\nIn Solidarity and Commitment to our Alliance with the Empire-\n\nSigned,\n\nTrade Princess Lilyana Carrington", ""),
        StaticBook("Old Elven Part 2", "Anthron", "Continuation of Seed words from part 1\n1 - 27\n-------------------\nCurious Words 28- and on to part 3\n-------------------The credit for this dictionary goes to the maker, Sporadic whom made the post to make this book possible on the forums.\nnae: you\n-------------------naeri: devout one, cleric\n-------------------narn: to walk, travel through\n-------------------nealu: to teach\n-------------------nor: land - nor'sae: farming\n-------------------\no: why\n-------------------ohn: like - Either a prefix or stand-alone\n-------------------oment: to meet\n-------------------okar: to safeguard\n-------------------okarn: oasis\n-------------------orrar: to hunt\n-------------------\nothelu: sharp\n-------------------parir: harbinger\n-------------------pern: potato\n-------------------parsaer: to conceive, to kindle. \"to have an idea\". \n-------------------perith: to remember\n-------------------puer: to write, to draw, to scribble.\n-------------------puerith: to write down (of books), to memorize. to record (more formal than 'puer')\n-------------------riv: claw \n-------------------riurn: swamp\n-------------------\nraell: carrot, root, herb. (refers to subterranean parts of plants possessing healing or nourishing properties)\n-------------------san: word, news - saner: to speak\n-------------------saneyr: to debate, discuss. - saneyir: debater, public speaker, orator.\n-------------------salum: to feel, to sense\n-------------------seth: void\n-------------------sew: soup, stew\n-------------------siimah: tower\n-------------------sil: sword\n-------------------siol: lone, lonely\n-------------------\nsirame: Honor; connection to the forest. - Has no plural\n-------------------siru: mushroom -siruonn: bitter\n-------------------siyuer: to play\n-------------------\nsohae: devout one, cleric - In a militant or executive sense. sohaer: ruler (through teachings, more positive than uthir.)\n-------------------suika: sugar -\n-------------------sul: light - strictly a noun.\n-------------------sulier: to see\n-------\nsulii: eye\n-------------------sulirrin: glowstone\n-------------------taeleh: mind\n-------------------taelu: to learn\n-------------------tahorran: hawk\n-------------------tahu: high\n-------------------tahn: peak, height\n------------------\ntalar: horizon - considered a place between the heavens and earth;\n-------------------talareh: stone - evolved from the words tali and lareh.\n-------------------\ntaliyna: body, living being, aspect -'taliiyna' can be used to denoted the physical parts that allow the body to live, i.e. organ, heart, mind and blood\n-------------------taliiyh: to bleed\n-------------------taliyu: secret\n-------------------\nTalonnii: family, blood(line) - always capped\n-------------------tarem: Elven week -Equivalent to 7 'karim'\n-------------------tayna: life, energy of living\n-------------------taynei: green\n-------------------\ntaynuel: vitality, energetic, alive (noun or adverb dependent on positioning)\n-------------------tenna: until\n-------------------tennallar: ocean\n-------------------\nterh: to grind, process, churn - wehn'tehral: bread; valein'tehral: cheese; raell'tehral: salve, potion), luci'terhal: wine\n-------------------\ntiuth: triangle - the triangular shape is found as a symbol for oppression, unlike the circle, which is used to describe (just) councils; - taliuth: oppressor\n-------------------thruer: to explode\n-------------------thrur: explosive, volatile\n------------\nthrurn: explosive, dynamite\n-------------------thill: pure, refined, delicate\n-------------------thilln: silver\n-------------------thul: raw, unrefined, brusque\n-------------------thulith: metal\n-------------------thuln: ore, raw material\n-------------------tilru: serving, submissive\n-------------------tir: law\n-------------------tos: desert, wasteland, barren ground - tos'sae: razing\n-------------------tufer: to construct, to prop\n-------------------\ntur: bone\n-------------------turr: sheep\n-------------------tuva: everything, all\n-------------------\ntuveh: wool, something soft\n-------------------ueth: nether\n-------------------uhier: to seek\n-------------------\nulln: rot, withering - strictly a noun.\n-------------------ullr: rot, decay, wither - Often of dead flora.\n-------------------ullral: monster, undead -lit: decayed. Used for living beings that have severed themselves from the natural way.\n----------------\nuradh: to scowl.\n-------------------uradir: naysayer\n-------------------uriar: to shout\n-------------------urth: to rule - negative connotation to this word.\n-------------------urthir: ruler\n-------------------maruthir: tyrant\n------------------\nUruk: Orc\n-------------------ut: because\n-------------------uvul: powder\n-------------------Valah: human\n-------------------vallei: water\n-------------------valein: milk\n-------------------vallel: blue\n------------------\nvallum: crying, griefing\n-------------------valmir: artist - from purple, the color of art.\n-------------------valmuel: purple\n-------------------van: to fare\n-------------------Velulaei: moon - Named after the moon goddess worshiped by the dark elves.\n-------------------vihai: whisper\n-------------------vilut: cow\n-------------------vira: vigilant, mournful - Traditionally used for attending the wake of vigil for a deceased Elf.\n-------------------vularale: bat\n-------------------\nvull: to deceive, to trick\n-------------------vuln: fox\n-------------------waleh: to heal\n-------------------wehn:  grass, grain.\n-------------------welier: to listen, to hear - rewelier: to repeat, to echo\n-------------------\nwy: appendage - more useful are the words that can be formed in combination with 'an*h': anah'wy: head; anoh'wy: foot, anih'wy: left hand, aneh'wy: right hand; anuh'wy: hand (either)\n-------------------wyl: while\n-------------------wyn: happy\n------------\ny: upon\n-------------------yallr: to live.\n-------------------yuln: gemstone - Used as the seed for many words, including maleyuln: diamond\n-------------------\nCURIOUS WORDS\nNo doubt you are left with many questions as you skim through the Elven wordlist. Indeed, their mystique and unique language has many intricacies which are not readily understood by those who did not take ample time studying them.\nFor perusal at your leniency, I have taken apart the words with most reason to spark confusion, and gave them the special attention they require in this section.\n-------------------\nito:\nThis particle is a means to denote location. However, it has many different meanings, depending on its location and accompanying words in a sentence.\nThe simplest case:\nito narne: I/he walk(s) here / I/he walk(s) within.\nNo ambiguity arises here. However, when we add a noun to this:\name ito narne: The forests walks here\nito ame narne: I/he walk(s) to the forest.\name'ito narne: I/He walk(s) within the forest\nameto'eyha narne: And I/he walk(s) within the forest\name'eyha ito narne: And the forest walks here.\nNote that the location of ito becomes crucial here. Putting it on the place of a subject aligns it to the meaning 'to'. On the object's location\n(to understand this, educate yourself on the elven sentence order), the noun 'ame' becomes the subject instead, and ito regains the meaning 'within' or 'here'.\nIto can also be used as a suffix, which is demonstrated by the last examples. In this case, the\naddition of ito restricts the noun to an object.\nThis word is also used to create the elvish equivalent to the words 'to be' and 'to have'. This particularly might confuse a novice to the language. to read upon this, I refer you to the grammar section of\nthis tome.\n-------------------tali-:\nThis word can do two very different things to the word it is connected to. In the simplest case, it adds the modifier 'part of' to the linked noun. But sometimes, the addition of this prefix creates a whole new word:\ntalibortu: Part dwarf -> Halfling\ntalivalah: Part human -> Halfling\ntal'uruk: Part Orc -> Goblin.\n\nHowever, sometimes ambiguity can abound from this word. For example:\ntaliame: Tree\ntal'ame: Part of the forest.\n\nIt would seem that in confusing cases, elves add an apostrophe between to denote they mean multiple words rather than a single noun. However, this is not always a safe rule,\nas it may clash with other rules for using apostrophes. Caution is urged, and ambiguity may indeed arise.\n--------------------sae:\nThis word, meaning the development, spreading or management of something, can be used to create many new words in elvish\nSome of these may not seem obvious. Examples include:\n\nnor'sae: development of land -> farming\ntos'sae: spreading of desert -> pillaging\nThe combinations grow even more numerous when we consider that sae can be combined with\nir to create sair, lending a word for, exemplum gratia, 'farmer' and 'pillager'. It can also be turned to saean to create a \nplural (where applicable) and saer, turning the word into the stem of a verb, effectively giving us the words 'to farm' and\n'to pillage'.\nThese further combinations exist almost always wherever a word was created from the suffix sae. Knowledge of this fact will allow the reader much more affluency in this language.\n-------------------\nma-:\nApart from being an intensifier, used at your leisure, the prefix ma- often finds its home in places where the intense use of affix would cause the same affix to start. An example of this is found in the word 'log': The elves would consider a log\n'part of tree' thus 'part of a part of the forest'. However, talitaliame is NOT a correct word to use in Elven.\nInstead, the second tali is implied by the use of the intesifier. Thus:\nmataliame: Log\nIf used in an event where a repeated suffix is used, ma- is placed after the seed word, but before the suffix one wishes to repeat.\nInterestingly enough, ma- is one of the rare affixes that does stack on certain occasions, as seen in the word marmatelu.\n-------------------onn:\n\nThis word is much like tali, in that it can be used to further define a certain word, as well as be used to create a noun of it's own. Also like tali, he inclusion of an apostrophe in a confusing case will imply the speaker is\nmeaning to talk of multiple words\nAn example:\n\name'onn: Born of the Forest, from the forest.\namonn: wood\nThe suffix will create a myriad of new words for the advanced speaker. Study of its usage will surely be beneficial.\n-------------------fer:\n\ngrammatically, nothing is strange about this word. However, its uses in combinations are so numerous that a separate section may be devoted to it.\nfer'ame: Axe\nfer'thuln: Pickaxe\nfer'nor: shovel\nfer'sul: torch\nfer'bilok: hammer\nfer'norsae: hoe\nfer'puer: quill. Pen. A tool for writing.\nOther uses can be thought up by the cunning mind. However, bear in mind that the word fer is mostly used to speak of handheld tools, not of crafting tables, anvils or furnaces.\n--", ""),
        StaticBook("Old Journal", "???", "[!] The book appears in quite good condition. Other than a few ripped out pages and some tearing.\n\n[!] The first dozen pages appear missing.\n... Day 14\n\nWe have begun to work on digging out the final areas.\n\nOur absence has not gone unnoticed however. Letters have been sent out regarding our ...\nDay 29\n\nAfter being capable of successfully manifesting ...\n\n... The first barrier we have made uses a phrase code. In the event Lion forgets as he always does, the code is hidden behind the growing tree above.\nDay ..\n\nWe- [!] The rest of the page is indecipherable. Blood smeared across it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Olo's Riddles", "Olo Smials", "~-~    Olo Smial   ~-~\n~-~-~   The   ~-~-~\n~-~    Big Book   ~-~\n~-~   Of Riddles  ~-~\n~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~            12th of\n     Malin's Welcome\nThis thing all things devours:\nBirds, beasts, trees, flowers;\nGnaws iron, bites steel;\nGrinds hard stones to meal;\nSlays king, ruins town,\nAnd beats high mountain down.\nWhat has roots as nobody sees,\nIs taller than trees\nUp, up it goes,\nAnd yet never grows?\nNo-legs lay on one-leg, two legs sat near on three legs, four legs got some.\nAn eye in a blue face\nSaw an eye in a green face.\n'That eye is like to this eye'\nSaid the first eye,\n'But in low place\nNot in high place.'\nAlive without breath,\nAs cold as death;\nNever thirsty, ever drinking,\nAll in mail never clinking\nIt cannot be seen, cannot be felt,\nCannot be heard, cannot be smelt.\nIt lies behind stars and under hills,\nAnd empty holes it fills.\nIt comes first and follows after, \nEnds life, kills laughter.\nThirty white horses on a red hill,\nFirst they champ,\nThen they stamp, \nThen they stand still.\nA box without hinges, key or lid,\nYet golden treasure inside is hid.\nVoiceless it cries,\nWingless flutters,\nToothless bites,\nMouthless mutters.\nI am taken from a mine, and shut up in a wooden case, from which I am never released, and yet I am used by almost all children.\nWhat goes round the house and in the house but never touches the house?\nWhat is it that you can keep after giving it to someone else?\nWhat walks all day on its head?\nWhat gets wet when it's drying?\nWhat appears once in a minute, twice in a moment, but never in a thousand years?\nWhat is round as a frying pan, deep as a bathtub, and still all the oceans in the world couldn't fill it up?\nThere were five men going to church and it started to rain. The four men who ran got wet and the one that remained still stayed dry.\nhe more you take, the more you leave behind. What are they?\nHe who has it doesn't tell about it. He who takes it doesn't know about it. He who knows about it doesn't want it. What is it?\nBrothers and sisters have I none but that man's father is my father's son.\nWho spends the day at the window, goes to the table for meals and hides at night?\nI fasten it and it walks. I unfasten it and it stops.\nWhat goes round and round the wood but never goes into the wood?\nI have a little house in which I live all alone. It has no doors or windows, and if I want to go out I must break through the wall.\nAlmost immediately after the father came into this world, the son was seen dancing on the roof.\nThere are four brothers in this world that were all born together. The first runs and never gets tired. The second eats and is never full. The third drinks and is always thirsty. The fourth sings a song that is never finished.\nA cloud was my mother, the wind is my father, my son is the cool stream, and my daughter is the fruit of the land. A rainbow is my bed, the earth my final resting place, and I can be a nuisance to people.\nPoke your fingers in my eyes and I will open wide my jaws. Cloth, leather, cardboard or paper, I greedily devour them all.\nAnswers\n1. Time\n2. Mountain\n3. Fish on one-legged table, man sits on three-legged stool, cat gets the bones.\n4. Sun shining on daises which are growing in a field.\n5. Fish\n6. Dark\n7. Teeth\n8. Egg\n9. Wind\n10. Lead in a pencil\n11. The sun\n12. Your word\n13. A nail in a horseshoe\n14. Towel\n15. The letter M\n16. A sieve\n17. Dead man and 4 Bearers\n18. Footsteps\n19. Coffin\n20. My son\n21. Fly\n22. Sandal\n23. The bark of a tree\n24. A chick in an egg\n25. Fire and Smoke\n26. Water, Fire, Earth\n27. Rain\n28. Shears\nWritten by Olo Smials\n(( and these guys \n\nhttp://www.berghuis.co.nz/abiator/unit/hobbit/ch/riddles.html\n\nhttp://www.berghuis.co.nz/abiator/humour/riddles1.html#oneb\n\n                        ))", ""),
        StaticBook("On Armin", "Maaz", "On Armin \n\nby Maaz\n===================\n\n  Armin Ambertoe is a middle-aged halfling who works at the Library of Dragur, alongside the other scholars who reside within those stone walls. He took on the role of a scholar\nsome time back in Vailor, if I remember correctly. His history is not well-known to me, but given his current demeanor, I would have to say that he's been around other races for a longer time than he has been around his own people. He is a race traitor.\nA whitewashed half-man. I'm not sure if he has any family, but if he does, I can't imagine what they'd look like. Perhaps he has told me, but I've simply forgotten.\n\n  Armin is a nuisance to me, and I've come very close to impulsively killing him. He\ntakes after Lyeth, the previous librarian, who I would much prefer dead. She is a mentally ill wood elven woman who acts like every one else's mother. But this book is not about her. This is about Armin. \n\n  Armin has shown a p roficiency in\ntransfiguration, arcanism, and telekinesis. He is also an Archon, or a being composed of mana who can float and is hard to strike. I've learned that while he looks like a halfling, he may be killed very easily. I struck his nose and it began to bleed.\nArmin tries to act like a father figure, and I suppose he does succeed somewhat in imposing his will over others (excluding myself, as I am capable of dominating his flimsy body). This halfling tries his best to protect his friends. He enjoys peace and\nhates war, just like his people. It's just as they say. \n\nYou can take the x out of the y, but you can't take the y out of the x.\n\nHaha.\nArmin Ambertoe has unkempt brown hair and wears brown pants. He used to wear overalls, but now he wears a comfortable-looking light brown sweater. He has green eyes. Pale skin.\nIf one spots Armin Ambertoe, go up to him and say 'hi', and that Maaz told you to do this. \n\nHowever, I would much rather you killed him on sight.\n\nHaha.\nWritten on the 8th of Sun's Smile, 1594", ""),
        StaticBook("On Darkstalkers", "Revion Tathron", "Darkstalkers\nBy Revion Tathron\n\nA NOTICE BEFORE READING: Darkstalkers are /incredibly dangerous/ and should NOT be approached without adequate preparation.\nDarkstalkers, at first, appear to be merely a man in a suit of armor; however, nothing could be farther from the truth. They are Necrotic Undead; or beings raised by Necromancers. They are also capable of draining life-force, presumably to fuel\nthemselves; this may manifest as black miasma. They are fast and incredibly agile, despite all of their armor. And, akin to other undead creatures, if struck down they will rise again. In addition to this, they do not /show/ pain; whether they feel it\nor not is unknown to this author. However, Darkstalkers are capable of speech and reason, and are weak to holy magic. They are also supposedly weak to Aurum weaponry, due to its lifeforce-conduction properties, but this was not tested. But as they are\ncorporeal, they can also be slain with more mundane weaponry, such as Ferrum.\nIn conclusion, Darkstalkers are fast, use swords and a lifeforce-draining ability to attack, and when slain leave behind empty armor. They should not be approached without due caution and preparation.\n\nEND.\nThe information in this tome was acquired through observing Darkstalkers kill people, observing Darkstalkers being killed, and talking with a Paladin who seemed knowledgeable on the subject of Darkstalkers.", ""),
        StaticBook("On Death, & Life", "Elindor", "Introduction\n\nSection 1:\nMental Scarring\n\nSection 2:\nAccepting Death\n\nSection 3:\nGenerational Cycles\nIt would be beneficial to begin with by outlining common knowledge before traversing any further. We mortals have been granted a most precious gift since the first Iblees war in that the Temple Monks are capable of cheating mortality.\nRegardless of the fatal nature of our injuries we are able to be revived and restored as though such a thing had never happenned. And thus the actuality of our mortal beings comes only at a time when our soul no longer grasps on to whatever fate it was\nthat kept our body here. Either by admitting defeat or realising success. These are the only two options for a soul that no longer returns to this realm for its body. And the dream of all mortal beings is that we can discover the latter, and in doing so,\nfind our eternal peace. But for many, it is the former that defeats us; a wounded soul desiring to escape the cage of this mortal flesh.\nSection 1:\nPsychological Scarring\n\nIt would be only a fool who attributes physical scarring to a lack of skill on the part of our Temple Monks. Capable of re-grafting burnt flesh and attaching severed limbs (or growing new ones)\nthere is really no place upon these bodies for scarring. For a Monk is able to heal with the divine Triumvirates powers to restore a body to the juvenile untouched form of a babe. In those experiences where ressurrection is not required and a fleshwound\nis the result, would not their hands be able to rejuvenate such an imperfection of the skin?\nSurely it is only by acceptance of the wound that our soul attributes it as an integral part of self.\nIf the one soul were able to be bound to two identical bodies (if it were the same soul one would assume the bodies to be the same as it is a common belief that our physical appearance is manifest from our central 'being') that then lived independant,\nif after the lifetime of a human they were brought back together to be compared, would they not be considered so very different from eachother? Forgetting the earlier talk of physical scars, their personalities would have taken shape under the outcome\nof their personal experience. One may be a romantic fool while the other is defensively paranoid. And this because their experiences have shaped them more than the soul from which they came. So then, any scarring that may further differentiate them is not\nmerely a defect, but a signet. That darkened patch of skin or red line of flesh serves as a reminder of the lessons that this individual has endured. Thus for all of us, the scars that are upon our body are only those that our soul has developed an\ninseparable attachment to, in the knowledge that what came with that scarring is an alteration upon the individualism of that being.\nThe result: countless visits to the Temple Monks will still bring back the bruises of a past life. Long after\nthe physical effect would have reason to remain. It is only when the psychological association with a scar is lifted (or fades with time) thatthe body can be observed as healing.\nUnless one can avoid trips to the Monks altogether.\nSection 2\nRealising Mortality\nAs was alluded to in the preface: fatality does not come (with rare exception) when brutality of wounds overcomes the skill of the Monks. Instead the soul chooses not to return for another month or another day. There is\nsome unnaccounted for resignation to the final rest that research has never successfully concluded why the circumstances of which are wholly individual to each case. As was also alluded in the preface; realisation of mortality is clearly connected\nto a soul's concept of fate.\nWhen time's expanse is objectively viewed outside of the portion of a lifetime, what becomes of the existence of one individual is not the occupation of their years, but the accomplishment of their fate.\nEach individual soul is tasked with a thing that it is their duty to discover and accomplish. And the eternal rest that comes to a soul that has aligned itself within the universe's jigsaw is a reward so much greater than a gardener's sense of\naccomplishment over the blooming of magnolias.\nYet we are surrounded by brokenness, failed purposes and vengeful cycles of hurt. Not all souls can accomplish their purpose. Many souls would not even have uncovered what that\n'thing' it is that is required of them before their time expires.\nThe observation, then, is that the soul is a more delicate entity than perhaps we credit it. When our innermost being (whose connection to the divine/spiritual we've no comprehension of)\nabandons this vessel before its purpose is actualised, there must have been a monumental resignation. The continual numbing of repeated defeats, or the mindless wandering of undiscovered purpose, or the accepting of a rival too great to overcome.\nWhen a soul permanently abandons its vessel, it too abandons the purpose for which it needed that body in the first instance.\nWhat unbearable sadness did forsake the fallen.\nSection 3:\nCyclical Beings\nHas not it been observed that the attributes of a known figure in history can personify another whose purpose is the same? Was not High Prince Native considered the reincarnation of Malin himself? even\namongst Elves old enough to have known both within their lifetime. The of presence of Xan, an Aengul of ol', joined these mortals to fulfil an action set in motion millennia previous. And lesser examples too of the reappearance of the Arcane Mage,\nas well as others whose striking semblance of another from the past (not so in physicality but in characteristics and drivenness towards a same purpose) is haunting yet undeniably required.\nHow many times has this entity previously existed? How many other vessels has this soul occupied? And does it return because the purpose has not been fulfilled, or because it /has/ yet similar cirumstances arise in which the same purpose repeats?\nFate is a tricky thing to pinpoint. Undeiniably there are important figures who shape the way the world functions. But what of the smaller ones who, over their lifetime, have made a mark that is (at least for a time) irreversible?\nAre we all cycling\nendlessly? Or is it only the few who do? Perhaps the soul has some interaction with the Aenguls who no longer walk amongst us. They have always been so desirous of interacting with the mortals, and mayhaps it is these cyclical beings through which\nthey can. Perhaps (at more of a stretch) these /are/ the Aenguls incarnate with the mortals.\nThere are many questions that yet remain, and perhaps I, the author, should have answered more of them before writing this.\nNext time.", ""),
        StaticBook("On Dragonkin", "Aruzond, Warden of the North", "On Dragonkin\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWritten and recorded by Aruzond, Warden of the North\nThere are two species of dragonkin known to have descended from Dragur, though corrupted and defiled forms of both have formerly existed. Dragur, the Daemon of Knowledge, oftentimes appears as a dragon in his true form.\nDragur’s chief descendants, the Dragaar, are sentient “greater dragons” that seek to collect and share knowledge with mortals. They can conceal themselves under the guise of mortals and other creatures, though it is a rare occasion to meet a Dragaar in\nperson. Dragons, on the other hand, are more common -- though proportionately rare compared to other living beings -- than greater dragons. They are generally referred to as dragons, though the proper classification\nis “lesser dragon.” They are non sentient, and are commonly viewed as natural predators that roam our world. However, like all living beings, they are susceptible to taint and corruption. Though a rare occasion, dragons have been known to alter their\nvery nature into a twisted, foul portrayal consumed by hatred and rage for the mortal races. The outcome of this calamity is referred to as a drake. Little is known about the purpose of the dragonkin as a whole, except that each species' intentions vary\ngreatly. \n\nDragon\n \n    The dragon (or lesser dragon) species is beastlike in nature, and generally accepted to be non sentient. Though they cannot process thought or comprehend concepts, they are highly\nintelligent in regards to instinct. The lesser dragon was once a rare sight to mortals, but they have appeared to exist in greater numbers in Anthos. Particularly, dragons roam the frozen wastelands of the North. Though they live in other regions\nof Anthos, the frigid North is home to many deep caves and caverns, which they prefer for nesting purposes. The region is cold, secluded, and tribesmen allow the food supply to remain steady. Dragons may roam the land of Anthos in search of cattle\nor mortals if they grow tired of pork flesh, and they continue to hunt until they are satisfied. Although lesser dragons have been frequently encountered in recent times, their numbers are slowly dwindling as they have begun to retreat to the deep,\ncold North.\n\nDrake\n \n    “Do not underestimate the allure of darkness, mortal. Your kind has yet to discover that even the purest of souls are drawn to it.” -Aruzond.\nThrough the malevolent desires of twisted corruption, the dragon has the potential to unwillingly alter its very existence. When a dragon degrades into a drake, its body decays into a shadowy skeleton of its former self.\nThe scales of a drake turn black as midnight, and their fangs cloak themselves in putrefying poison. While a drake does not develop sentience, its desires can be manipulated to follow any malignant alignment. Drakes forfeit any connection to their\nformer selves, and their lust for eternal damnation of life causes them to instill fear into those who would oppose it. The drake is slightly smaller in size compared to a dragon, but what it lacks in size and physical strength is compensated\nby maneuverability and lethality. It is rare to encounter an evil powerful enough to twist and taint the mind of the mighty dragon, but these influences communicate through our world more readily than we may often realize.\nDragaar\n \n    Bestowed with the gift of immortality and sentience, the Dragaar exist chiefly to seek and gather knowledge. Each Dragaar is assigned the role of gathering a distinct aspect of knowledge, and this role defines their characteristics\nand demeanor. However, they do not solely desire knowledge and wisdom. The greater dragons, or Dragaar, act as ever watching wardens over the mortal races. However, most prefer to live in seclusion  in deep thought and meditation, only to emerge when\nthe races call upon them in their time of need. The Dragaar can and often disguise themselves under the guise of a mortal or creature. This is their preferred method of watching over mortals, as it is both subtle and inconspicuous. There are only\ntwo Dragaar that have revealed themselves to the mortal races, and the decision to do so was not lightly concluded. Though the Dragaar seek to protect the mortal races, they often decide to do so by living in secrecy. Many discern that if they\nchose to associate themselves with mortal affairs too frequently, dire consequences would arise. The primary concern held by Dragaar, in regards to involvement in the matters of mortals, is that the races would eventually resort to\nrelying on them to protect mortals from any form of evil. However, the greater dragons aspire to teach the mortal races self-preservation, without them depending on the intervention of immortals.\nDrakaar\n\nTo attempt to bend the will of a Dragaar would be all for naught, and thus what can cause a Dragaar to devolve itself into a twisted abomination of hatred is unknown. The ancient ancestors of the four mortal races once believed that\nthe choice for this horrendous transformation to occur was their own, though the aftermath of such a decision would contradict their entrusted duty. The greater dragon itself is a terrifying opponent, but a Dragaar that feels no remorse and fears\nno consequence? That is the true fear of corruption; the perversion of the mind and distortion of one’s morality is a dreadful circumstance. In past times, the outcome of such an event would often be referred to as a “greater drake.”\nIt is the combination of a Dragaar’s sentience and a drake’s all-consuming hatred. The likelihood of a Dragaar devolving into a being tormented by rage is next to none, as most would, in their right mind, turn themselves into stone to prevent the\nconversion. The only verifiable event recorded of a Dragaar turning to stone is that of Velketzar. The Guardian Velketzar, consumed by self-condemnation and despair due to his failure, dramatically transformed into a stone statue\nto prevent the inevitable calamity. If a Dragaar were to fall under the hand of corruption, it would hold the power to politically corrupt nations with ease. Additionally, detecting and pursuing such a foe would be toilsome, all due to its shape shifting\nability. Fortunately, deep meditation and concentration can inhibit this rare occurrence, along with immersing themselves in their aspect of knowledge.", ""),
        StaticBook("On Dreadknights", "Cir'dian", "Dreadknights origin and creation\n\nBy \nCir'dian Nymphea\nGenesis\n\nThe dreadknights are beings comprised of suits of armor bound together through the engraving of specific runes unique to the blood mages, of whom draw their magic from a deity presently unknown to me.\nThey originated in the land of Asulon, as did the enigmatic blood mages. As it stands however, it is somewhat of a mystery as to where their creators came from, and how their magic came to be. However it is known that the dreadknights are the tools of the\nblood mages. They are the strength behind them.\nCreation\n\nThe dreadknights are created over the process of several months, through a long and arduous ritual involving the removal of all that makes them free, stripping them of both flesh and free will. The process\nbegins with the abduction of a specific choice being. The selection is not bound to physical aspects, but rather decided by the quality of those taken. Usually of whom are stubborn and loyal to whom they serve. In post of their abduction, the patron is\ntaken to which ever strong hold the dreadknights would presently occupy. From there they would  be bound. The dreadlord then begins the process with the destruction of both kneecaps, as to prevent escape and standing. No sedatives are used in this\nprocess. The patron is then fitted with a suit of armor usually comprised of a metal known as black iron (Known for being particularly dense, and durable). The leader then engraves several runic symbols into the armor of the victim, these runes\nbind the soul of said victim to the suit of armor. Once finished, the subject is thrown into a cell, and left for several days before further work is done. For the next weeks, the victim is tortured, their wounds left to rot, until nothing remains but a\nskeleton within, and their will is broken. Dreadknights because of this process, are taught to love pain. By the time two months pass, the new dreadknight is completely finished, and left to do the work of their dreadlord.", ""),
        StaticBook("On Dreadknights", "The Eternal Librarian", "On Dreadknights\n\n by Cir'dian Nymphea\nIf this book is found anywhere else than the Eternal Library of Annil’sul, the Enclave of Haelun’or, it is stolen.\n\nBoth buyers and sellers will be punished.\n\nSigned, the Eternal Librarian\nGenesis\nThe dreadknights are beings comprised of suits of armor bound together through the engraving of specific runes unique to the blood mages, of whom draw their magic from a deity presently unknown to me. They originated in the land of Asulon,\nas did their constructs (The dreadknights). As it stands however, it is somewhat of a mystery as to where the blood mages came from, and how their magic came to be. However it is known that the dreadknights are the tools of the blood mages. They are the\nstrength behind them.\n\nCreation\nThe dreadknights are created over the process of several months through a long and arduous ritual involving the removal of freedom and physical flesh. The process begins with the abduction of a\nspecific choice being. The selection is not bound to physical aspects (Which would be removed in the end anyway) but rather decided by the quality of those taken. Usually of whom are stubborn and loyal to whom they serve. In post of their abduction- the\npatron is taken to which ever stronghold the dreadknights would presently occupy. From there they would be bound. The dreadlord then begins the process with the destruction of both knee caps, as to prevent escape and standing. No sedatives are used in\nthis process. The patron is then fitted with a suit of armor usually comprised of a metal known as black iron (Known for being particularly dense, and durable). The leader then engraves several runic symbols into the armor of the victim. This can be done\nby both dreadlord, and blood mage. These runes bind the soul of said victim to the suit of armor. Once finished, the subject is cast into a cell, and left for several days before further work is done. For the next few weeks the victim is tortured, their\nrunes left open to rot. Flesh eventually gives way, leaving nothing but the victim’s skeletal form beneath. Alongside this, the will of the victim is broken, and they are taught to love pain. By two months, the process is complete, and the new dreadknight\nmay now set out to do the will of their dreadlord or blood mage.", ""),
        StaticBook("On Enchanting", "Sarrion", "On Arcane Enchanting\n--------------->\nBy Sarrion Zytiaear\n\nThe following are my own personal notes taken from my research from interviews with other Transfigurationists and my lessons from Avenel.\nIn Transfiguration there is a sub-classed spell base called Enchanting. Enchanting is the simple art of transmuting either a command for an object or a spell  to bind to an object with a medium\nground  that powers the spell. This medium ground is almost always a mana crystal, which is any gem though the rarer the gem the more mana it can hold. The transfigurationist is to first channel his/her mana into this gem and fill it entirely\nwith his mana, then transmute the spell or command into the gem and bind it to the object arcanely. This whole progress burns /a lot/ of mana in the mage's mana pool, and it a dangerous art that can either kill the mage\nor cause a mana fluctuation. This is why that sometimes a mage may set up an enchanting lab with a “Mana Obelisk”, for those who are ignorant in the topic a Mana Obelisk is a large gem pillar that has\nbeen enchanted to contain a large mass of mana, that way when it comes time to enchant the enchanter can pull the mana from the crystal to the gem, not having to use their own mana.\nDo note the creation of a Mana Obelisk is very intricate and will need to be activated by two or more Transfigurationists.", ""),
        StaticBook("On Eternal Laws", "Lorolith Iira", "On Eternal Laws\n\n-----=====+=====-----\n\nAeternum Iuris\n\n-By Lorolith Iira\nJust as the reasonable mortals of this universe have confined their societies to the order of rule of law. This is moral and legislative law. Similarly, it would appear that the universe itself has (at least in the past, leading up to now) confined itself\nto working 'eternal laws'. These laws, like moral and legislative laws, regulate behaviour. But instead of regulating the behaviour of conscious agents, they regulate the bahviour of nature itself.\n\nWithin this book I aim to dicuss why I think these laws\nprove to be persistant as well as my own understanding of existing laws of the physical universe. This piece is an essential companion to anyone wishing to delve into the field of natural philosophical study.\nContents:\n\n1) Persistence.\n2) The law of equivalent exchange. \n3) Laws of interaction.\n4) How we may hope to understand these laws in the future.\nChapter 1\n-----==========-----\n\nPersistence\nAs it would seem, at the very moment I write these words, the world is 'ordered'. Meaning, it seems to continue to be stable (upon reflection of past events) and similar causes produce similar effects. Thing I drop fall down. When my skin is cut, I draw\nblood. When a moving object interacts with another stationary object, the stationary object recieves some part of the first object's speed. I could go on. However, it follows that these results have only been observed in controlled circumstances. Outside\ninfluences can always alter observation. As is a pain in formal study. But still, these rules persist. I would also argue that these laws have *always* persisted. There would not have been any time after the birth of the material world that these rules\nwould not have existed. \n\nI say I know this because it would seem that the order of the present is contingent on the order of the past. I.e. if things didn't always fall down, we would observe strange chaos in the world around us as some part of our world\nbe absent, sent off into the abyss of the heavens. There are also rules of existence that our very lives are contingent on. If the rules of nature did not persist in our past, little is to stop nature itself destroying the lives of all descendants through\napocolyptic storms and quakes. Yet, most likely due to the natural restrictions on these powers, we are still here to discuss. This is the simple reason that I beleive it is necessary that these laws exist.\nChapter 2\n-----==========-----\n\nThe Law of Equivalent Exchange.\nThe law of 'equivalent' exchange is, I would argue, the longest known physical law. Not only is it extremely intuitive but it has become clear within the practice of alchemy since the ancients first tried their luck within the art. Simply, the law is a\nprinciple that states that you can never get more 'out' than you put 'in'. Most alchemists (however effective in their trade) who haven't done extensive study will know this law to mean that you cannot recieve more from the properties of any final\nproduct than from the properties of composit parts. A potion created for healing will only be able to do so because their composing parts had properties that, once taken together, allow for this to happen. Essentially, there are set properties allowed to\ncome from certain types of ingredients. However, this law, as far as I can see, applies universally. Eternally. For example, when we alchemists create these new substances, we can weigh them and find that the final weight is equal to the total weight of\ncomposit parts. Nothing extra has been 'created' and nothing has been 'destroyed'. \n\nThis concept also exists within magic, it would seem. It's well known to all mages that, once something is 'evoked' from the void, it will *always* return. This is\nessentially a 'magical' embodyment of the law of equivalent exchange. You cannot *end* with more than you started with. No matter how long it sticks around. \n\nHowever, one problem I found myself with when considering this was the idea that although the\nphysically evoked substance of any spell cannot stick around, its effects on our physical universe *does*. \nI will explain this problem after first defining the term 'energy'.\n\n'Energy' as it is commonly used, is vauge in its definition. I have only\never heard it comprehensively a few times. However, here is my own: \n\n'Energy' is the property or state of being able to impose physical change. \n\nFor example, a vibrating ball would have a high energy. This is because, when another object comes\ninto contact with it, it would impose motion on that other object. Most (if not all) of the physical 'change' I will be referring to will be to do with the idea of physical motion. \n\nNow, the idea that a fire can be evoked and have it's physical\nchanges remain, seems to involve having physical change come from nothing. \nAllow me to illustrate:\n\nWhen a normal fire is lit, the energy from the fire (heat could indeed be considered energy since it has the capacity to burn and break down matter as\nfuel, hence imposing change) comes from originally striking the flame. An evoked flame essentially comes from nothing and, once it has done its work, goes back into nothing. If the results of this burning fire remain, the universe is in a state equivalent\nto having a fire burn without a starting flame. \n\nMuch like the existence of physical material, 'energy' (as previously defined) cannot come from nothing or simply disappear, it would seem. All motion and change in the universe appears to come from\npreceding motion and change. Set up a line of balls. Roll one towards them and watch the chain reaction of transfer of motion. The energy of each ball comes from the energy of the last.\n\nNow, if magic itself were to follow the principle of equivalent\nexchange, as I am to argue, it takes the mana of the 'evoker' to actually keep this change in existence. This makes sense because, unlike the material substance of a spell (such as earth evoking), energy transfered from this material into the physical\nworld *does* exist before the spell is cast. In the form of mana. This is what mana truley is. It is pure energy, as I have defined. Having mana is identical to having the potential to cause physical change in the universe *through* access to the void.\nSo, if I am right, we can conclude that the mana used in evoking some kind of magical substance from the void is in some way equal to the mana/energy required to actually drag this substance into the material world and the energy 'created' by this magical\nsubstance.\n\nThis would explain why maintaining a spell without properly casting would cost the caster much less mana. It would still cost some as this magical substance would interact with the physical world by emitting heat or interacting with the airs\nand materials around it whilst being maintained. Most of the mana would have to come from the real interactions between that magical substance and its target. Then, once that substance has returned to the void, the energy it has 'created' remains. This\nenergy is acutally sapped from the caster's mana. \n\nThis rational definition of 'mana', to my knowledge, has never existed before. We can think of it as essentially equivalent to the actual heat of a fire, or the motion of the winds. It is just as much an\nimposing force of nature as anything else.\n\nThere are some ways I can test these assertions soon enough. I plan on seeing the relationship between consumed mana and imposed motion at some point in the future with the help of a telekenetic mage in a\ncontrolled environment.\n\nI plan on releasing one or several volumes titled 'Science of Magic' that explore how would consider the laws of magic and the various mana to energy transfers that happen in different areas of the magic arts.\nIf anyone has found the contents of this chapter of this tome particularly confounding, yet they wish to inquire further, you may feel free to contact me directly to ask questions or even help with this area of research.\nChapter 3\n-----==========-----\n\nLaws of Interaction\nThere are, similar to the law of 'equivalent exchange', laws that govern the interactions between physical things, it would seem. Not only their existence. \n\nI wish to briefly discuss these along with what has been discussed in the previous chapter.\nThese come as a mixture of my own findings in research and my further reading.\n\n----------\n\nIt is clear, as I have explained previously that energy can be transfered between physical bodies. Although I have no way to quantify\n'energy' at this time, we can observe the transfer of motion upon collision of physical objects.\n\nNot only this, but we can observe that, once an object has recieved a forceful impulse, it begins to slow down. I beleive (although I cannot at this time,\ndescribe mathematically) that what truley slows this object down is the influence of surroundings like air and wind. Really, if you were to set an object in motion and nothing were to collide with it or slow it down, this motion may continue constantly\nforever. Simply put, if you try to move your hand through water (a thicker fluid), you experience more resistance than through air (a thinner fluid). It's harder to do so. You can therefore imagine that, if these mediums were to be removed *all together*,\nnothing would stop motion as nothing resists it. \n\nIt would follow, actually, that imposing motion on an object actually causes an increase in its speed, rather than giving it a set speed, as many may believe. Especially since, without this imposition,\nspeed can still be maintained.\nChapter 4\n-----==========-----\n\nHow we May Hope to Understand These Laws in the Future\nI hope that, upon further reflection on the details and observtaions I have discussed in this book, I cand find ways in greater detail to describe the course of motions in our universe. I have yet, as I have said, to collect detailed observations to test\nmy theories about energy transfer from mana. Which itself may be difficult to do without detailed mathametical basis. \n\nSoon I wish to be able to calculate the motions of all objects in our universe. If not in great detail, at least enough to have be\nable to truley watch the work of whatever gods lay beyond the heavens.", ""),
        StaticBook("On Liches", "Ilkazar", "On\nLiches\n\n\nVolume One\nBe warned reader,\nthis is not a guide on how to combat a lich, such is very dangerous and should be avoided if at all possible.\nA Lich is, in the simplest term, a skeletal mage. They are a form of undead, skeletal beings who use the arcane powers to destroy any who may stand in there path. Being undead they have much the same weakness's as other undead creatures have,\nsuch as an aversion to gold, it may not kill them outright but it does cause great pain. Clerical magic also being there weakness, the holy magic has the potential to destroy them and make them reform elsewhere. There skeletal frame is also very fragile.\nIt is very easy for one to smash a liches bones apart though such would not cause the lich pain or distress. Besides those cases, a lich feels no pain, you can immolate the creature in flames yet it will still stand, stab at it at your own peril\nfor that also does not cause it pain. They do not sleep they do not eat they do not get tired. Liches are created in a secretive necromantic ritual, the people who are made into liches are widely regarded to be skillful mages if not masters of there\nchosen art. The difference between a mortal mage an a lich is vast, a mortal mage will get tired and fatigued while casting\nA lich has no such limitation, they can continue to cast till there mana runs out completely. Liches learn how to\nhandle there mana vastly better, they tend to outpreform most any mortal mage in combat and otherwise. Liches also get the added ability to drain the life of a target to fuel them, leaving behind a blackened husk.\nThere is but one way to truly kill a lich, and that is destroying there phylactery. A phylactery is an object that has the liches soul bound to it. They are always very well hidden, thus making liches a terrible foe to fight.", ""),
        StaticBook("On Magnetus", "Eliza", "This volume chronicles the studies of Magnetus, headed by Professor Eliza of Galdorcreft College.\nDays in the field show that this grey to black mineral is found predominantly near to mountain ranges. Galdorcreft is built in the shadow of a large mountain so that gives me the opportunity to examine this mineral in earnest.\nMagnetus extracted from a geode undeniably exhibits an octahedral crystal formation, having easily observable crystal faces. It has been found to have a massive form in deposits that have grown in tight spaces in the earth. Either form shows that it is\nopaque; Light does not pass through. Furthermore, the mineral has a metallic luster meaning that it is semi-reflective. Magnetus in massive form appears to break with uneven fracture, leaving a irregular and jagged face. Otherwise the fracture of the fine\ncrystal is subconchoidal- smooth with irregularly rounded edges. While on the topic of fracture, it should be noted that the mineral is exceptionally dense and resistant to breaking.\nNow it is a miracle that I didn’t melt my skin off haphazardly fooling with Galdorcreft’s furnaces, as I am not qualified. Alas, my studies into geology put me in danger regularly. It has been surmised that Magnetus’ melting point exceeds that of iron by\nperhaps fifty or sixty degrees celsius. From that point, it may be poured into molds and so forth.\n\nIn both unrefined and refined forms, we see the most interesting feature of Magnetus. It has a strong attraction to metals such as ferrum and steel.\nPresumably any metal with traces of ferrum.. This excludes Aurum, obviously. Active redstone signals remove this entirely, and light dusting of redstone on certain parts removes the magnetism partially for that area; Perhaps the presence of condensed mana\naffects the Magnetus in this way, or perhaps it is the transferral of electrical energies. There are unperceivable reactions there nonetheless. This lead me to theorize that there may be deeply ingrained connection to magic, such as what is seen with\nThanhium and Redstone. Thus I decided to perform further tests using Transfiguration. Now, it has been shown that in larger blocks of Magnetus, the area of magnetic pull or the magnetic ‘field’ extends about three cubic meters. In this state it harbors a\nSurprisingly, when in contact with my mana, the field spread to about five cubic meters wherein all of the metal tools in the room flung themselves towards myself and the Magnetus.\nThe avenues for craftsmanship are expansive and it is my hope that this discovery and this journal will foster that. -E", ""),
        StaticBook("On Mali'Aheral", "Domainoft", "The Mali'Aheral, the blessed elves. Or as others call them: High Elves.\nThese Elven people are one of the most hated by their own race. People see them\nas racists and don't think they'll do any good. They kill members of thier own\nrace, for they are\n'impure'. However is this true?\nI say not.\nThe culture of the Mali'Aheral goes back to a specific elf known as Larihei\nLomahnih. She was one of Elven kind who bathed in water that contained enchanted\ngolden particles, which had\nchanged their appearance. Her Elven kind had a paler\nskin and longer ears than the other elven kinds. They were also taller and their\nhair had become fairer.\nThe change that these particles had made to them also was psycological.\nThese\nearly Mali'Aheral had shifted away from their original beliefs and thought more\nlogical.\nThey became scholars, one of which was Larihei.\nAs a child of her kin she learned their traditions and ideals. And soon she\nappeared to be a master in all subjects a Mali'Aheral was expected to learn. She\ngrew up to become the leader of the council of Princes in Malinor.\nHowever she prmoted the Mali'Aheral's belif in the council: That Elves were the\nsuperior race of Aegis and that they should also rule the other races.\nHowever the other Princes and Princesses said that she was only promoting war\nand was a danger to the Elves. Larihei was banished from Malinor. Half of\nthe Mali'Aheral followed Larihei when she went to find a new home for their race.\nThe other half remained with Malinor, slowly losing their culture.\nHowever when those High Elves found the ruins of their kin in Asulon, the old\nculture was revived.\nMaehr'sae Hiylun'ehya That is the core of the Mali'Aheral culture. It can be\ntranslated as \"Progress and Health\".\nBreaking that sentence down, you can split it up two parts: Maehr'sae, or\nProgress and\nHiylun'ehya, or Health. Maehr'sae refers to the development of\nknowledge and the value of it. It is the base of the position of science in\ntheir society, as scientist stand in a high position due to their ability to\nrecover truth and\nknowledge. Hiylun'ehya stands for the health and purity of the Mali'Aheral race. They wish\nto keep their race from mixing blood, because they believe that their body is\nthe perfect design. A Mali'Aheral is not to ruin his body, he\nshall not damage it in any way. This means that he or she will not tatoo nor scar their body out\nof free will. They are also not to mix blood with other races, because they\nproduce children who are not 'perfect' anymore. This includes intimate\ncontact with other races, because they woudl risk creating a 'failure' a child of mixed\nblood.\nAnother important part of their culture is that they believe to be superior to\nother races, due to them able to think\nclear because they do not follow any god.\nThey frown down upon the religions of other races, however they respect those\nwho show to be wise and able to think logical.\ncombat is another thing that is frowned down upon. as it is\nan action that does not require thinking and will only cause the loss of people that last one is\nvery important: The mali'Aheral are, of course also subject to the curse of\nMalin's children, therefor all lives are valued high and loss of one is\nthe waste. It is therefore also expected of all Mali'Aheral to create children at\nsome point in their life.\nThe Mali'Aheral frown down upon those of mixed blood, they might discriminate\nthem, they are not violent however.\nTheir only violent people are sillumir, the Mourning Blades, they are the Mali\nwho give their sacrifice to the race by taking up the sword. Thier name comes\nfrom the need for them to fight, a sad thing to do in their society, They are\nrespected for their sacrifice and remain few in number, due to the morals of\ntheir race.\nA Mali'Aheral does not fight unless necessary.\nI hope this has enlighted you about the Mali'Aheral.\nThink about this next time you see them.\nand try to understand their actions.\nMaerh'sae Hiylun'eyha\n-Vallel'Yuln Aeleyelsa\n\nScribed by Leyu'Maehr\nVaerhaven\n((Strange Numbers))\n((8/27/13))", ""),
        StaticBook("On Mali'fenn", "Ila Galanthus", "A Theory on the Relationship of Thanhium and Mali'fenn Physical and Mental Mutations\n\nWritten by: Ila Galanthus\nSnow elves, Mali'fenn, snelves, whatever we may be called we are among the most hated and reviled cultures. An offshoot of the mali'aheral, or high elves, we have several distinctive qualities such as our incredibly pale skin and hair, and cold skin.\nUnfortunately we are also known for our tendancies to lean on the less sane side of the spectrum. While members of other groups can be insane and unstable, it seems to come in higher, more consistant numbers with the Mali'fenn.\n\nI suspect a single culprit\nin all of these mostly passive mutations: thanhium. After hours of thought and study on the once rare ore, I realized the effects of it's poisoning are remarkably similar to my kin's mutations.\n\nI do not believe this is curable, however. Perhaps a group\nof impure high elves were cast out of the silver city, and ended up settling near a vein. Unknown to them they ate tainted food, drank tainted water, breathed tainted air. Many likely died, but I doubt the onset of insanity allowed them to realize this.\nBut, of course, some survived. They multiplied, their children born with trace amounts of ore in their blood. They grew resistant to the toxin, but it still chilled and paled our flesh.\n\nThe worst effect was it's icy grip on their minds, driving them\nmad ever so slowly. Other races determined it as a parasite among our people, and anyone who joined them would begin to feel the same effects of the toxic ore all around them.\n\nOf course, this is speculation. However it is firm in my mind this is indeed\nthe origin and cause of my people.", ""),
        StaticBook("On Mana Anchors", "Sarrion", "Notes on Mana Anchors\n--------------->\nBy Sarrion Zytiaear\n\nThese notes are taken entirely from my experience with magic and entirely from my years of learning from other mages.\nEverything that pulls power outside of our realm is very generally called a “Spell”, and these Spells can draw from different “wells” such as the Void, or an Aungledaemon entity. Everything that’s a spell works the same progress.\nThe person uses their mana to connect to this well, and from the well a “Mana Anchor” is created between that realm and our realm to bring forth the power of the spell that’s being casted. Now Mana anchors are a physical thing, it’s been reported that\nsometimes when a mage fluctuates too much mana the air between their spell and them have been distorted. This distortion is the mana anchor that binds the spell to the mortal realms.\nDo note that because it’s physical thing that an Transfigurationist can cast an “Abjuration” which is a burst of mana that destroys the mana anchor, nullifying the spell.", ""),
        StaticBook("On Orcs", "Lelien", "On Orcs\n\n    by Leyu'Maehr\nNo race is more adapted to the harsh deserts than the muscular Orcs. Masters of combat and wrestling these 7ft high Goliaths can destroy most prey with their bare hands. To an Orc the most important thing is the hunt and the protection of his\ntribe and clan. For that reason, they do not intermix with other races much. They have a mutual hatred and respect for the Dwarves of Kal’Urguan because of their ferocity and strength. However they disdain other races simply because they’re not big\nenough. Where other races establish cities and build monuments to their predecessors, Orcs establish tribes and build strong clans around the mythic figures of their ancestors. Orcs tend toward nomadic life, but what villages they do choose to establish\nare usually built from the ruins of other cities, swallowed and spat forth again by the drifting dunes of the desert.\n\nAlthough Orcs can naturally live longer than humans, this rarely becomes a point of debate. The oldest Orc to ever live was Karguk\nof Caln Pyrathon, who died in glourious battle on the turning of his two hundredth year (Eight hundred Orcish seasons). Orcs are just as prolific as Dwarves and Humans, but their children have the shortest period of puberty, sometimes reaching full\nadulthood in only fifteen years. Orcs are also the race in Aegis most likely to cull their own, whether purposefully leaving the incapable behind in the desert, or removing the weak through ritual trials. However, the strength of the clan is paramount in\nan Orc’s eyes, and they will defend their young and wise to their very last breath – even if it is only to give enough time for the wise to show the young how to best attack after their elder clansmen have fallen.\nOrcs are usually brown skinned with green tints, varying from sandy to dark green and rarely black, and their hair is usually very dark, with brown and black the most common. Most Orcs follow the practice of coloring their hair with the blood of their\nenemies. Because their hair is so dark, this coloring rarely shows until many dousings, and it is considered a sign of a great warrior for your hair to glow red with the blood of your enemies: Orcs of the Shaman bloodline tend more toward green skin and\nblack hair, usually distinguished from other Orcs by size.\n\nSize and musculature set them apart from all other races on Aegis, sometimes considered giants at two and a half meters tall. Orcs of the goblin bloodline, are most notably smaller than\nother Orcs, usually only reaching a meter and a half. Goblins are the most likely of all Orcs to have black skin and fairer hair. Orc eyes are usually brown or black, with a rare few blessed with blood-red.", ""),
        StaticBook("On Pure Truth", "Lorolith Iira", "On Pure Truth\n\n-----=====+=====-----\n\nBy Lorolith Iira\nMany scholars and philosophers (and laymen) alike are rather flippant in their disregard for theories of knowledge beyond or outside of pure empiricism. For example, Farley III Stafyr boldly states in his writing 'Knowledge and Experience', \"The origin of\nknowledge is clearly, through the experiment and therefore experience\". Although I don't contest this conclusion, it's painful to see such a complex matter taken as lightly as to assert that it is 'common sense'. In this work I hope to analyse the process\nof forming beliefs from experience of the universe and I hope to demonstrate that, truley, only experience can ever be considered the arbiter of 'knowledge'.\nContents:\n\n1) Meaning of 'Knowledge' and 'Truth'.\n\n2) The Nature of Experience.\n\n3) Quirks of the Universe.\nWhen we talk about 'knowledge', what exactly do we mean? This is an important question to answer before we move forward. I would define it as \"am affirmed claim which is 'true'\". This definiton comes with a set of criteria, however. There are some\ncases in which a 'true' assertion could not be considered by that definition. If I were to claim \"on that hill, there is a small, white Dog\", we could evaluate this claim by moving closer to the hill to see. If we move closer and it turns out that this\napparent small, white dog is actually a lamb, I was wrong. However, if we move further and *also* find a small, white dog on the other side of the hill, am I still wrong? I would argue that, although I was not wrong, I did not *know* that this dog\nwas on this hill. It was but a lucky guess. This is most likely uncontraversial. Perhaps a better definition for knowledge would be 'an affirmed concept that, which reason for affirmation, is 'true' '. \n\nThough, we must also now define the word 'true'.\nI must now define base on how I think people most value these terms. It would certainly seem that a 'true' assertion is valued to mean 'an assertion that correlates with the reality of the world'. I.e. a true assertion is one that describes the world\naccuratley. \n\nSo, how is it that we can achieve 'true' knowledge? Or 'pure' truth? One might be tempted to argue that experience is *not* the way to do this. If we accept our previous definitions, it would become apparent that experience is subject to\nextreme change or fault. For example, in dreams or vivid hallucinations we see things that contradict everyday experience. And, if we were to ever accept experience as the arbiter of pure truth, we would never have grounds to choose between these\nexperiences.\n\nHowever, this is not an accurate assessment of the situation. When we go about our daily lives, we find ourselves only ever subject to two mind-states. Impressions (information we feel is coming to us through observation from an\napparently external world) or imagination (ideas created by the mind itself). I would ask the reader to note that the imagination can never be as vivid as impressions. When you read a compelling novel or tale of battle, the words themselves are never\nenough to pierce through your imagination to create an experience. You can never feel the true rush of charging into battle or taking a wound just from a story. It may tickle these impression somewhat but it has never reached the same level as actually\ndoing it. But we should also note that our imaginations are subject to our impressions. By this I mean, our imagination can only ever conjure that which we are familiar with through impressions. Yes, we can imagine fantastical new creatures and universes\nfor the sake of story telling but these things are essentially re-allignments of things we have previously experienced. For example, one cannot imagine a new colour. Try to do this. It is simply not a part of our faculty. We *can*, however,\nimagine a brand new shade of a colour. But this is only because we recognize the difference between darker or lighter shades of other colours from previous impressions of them. These examples illustrate this point very well. \n\nIt would appear, therefore\nthat we are actually slaves\nto the experience all together. Our passions are dictated by interactions between ourselves and what we experience. As are our thoughts in general. Simlarly, when those effected by the likes of opium, mental deficiency or\ninsanity claim to see a universe beyond *our* experience, we can see the cause related to their difference in opinion (though, I will discuss the nature and problems with causal links soon enough). \n\nHaving accepted this, it is only one step to accept\nappealing to knowledge beyond our experience is meaningless. At this very moment I may be dreaming. But this claim is meaningless because this dream-state that is external to my experience may never effect the experience itself. Therefore, I would have no\nway of knowing this. It is an empty claim all together. The uncertainty still remains. I may very well be dreaming. But we must essentially ignore claims like this, even if we do have to accept them as possibilities. Even the laws of reason seem to come\nfrom a mixture of developed intuition and direct experience (noting that even our intuition is likely governed by past experiences, as I will also discuss in detail soon). We see a universe in which things rarely contradict one another (unless, like I\nmentioned previously, we're effected by substances or madness. In which case, we have a non-contradictory understanding of these apparent contradictions). We also see a universe where the past always seems to resemble the future. We can use maxims like\nthese to make accute deductions. Many of which turn out to be right. \n\nFinally, I wish to discuss several problems with our often taken for granted experiences. Although it may appear to be reasonable to make deductions about the future by\nremembering the past, this actually makes little sense. Nothing assures us that the apparent order in nature will continue. This is the problem with 'causal' links that I described previously. \nThe proper way to understand causality (or so it would seem)\nis to realize that if one thing truley is the result of another, they will *always* correlate. For example, forceful contact with a ball will always set it in motion. This is because there is some mechanistic link between them. We can therefore, you would\nthink, deduce that strong correlation is evidence for causation (even if it is not conclusive evidence). We can see that the pregnancy of a woman will undoubtedly follow the fertalization of a man. Therefore, we can deduce that these things are very\nlikely causally linked. Even if we don't understand underlying mechanisms. \n\nBut this is a product of our intuitions and intuitions alone. Infact, beliefs based on these intuitions aren't neccessarily that reasonable. But they are neccessary and\npractical. They have always worked. We can never know if they will work the next time. But may judge it as worth trying. \n\nPerhaps the only way to posit absolute continuity in the order of the physical world is to posit the existence of a creator. Though,\neven the nature and being of that deity is subject to the same problems. We cannot reasonable deduce continuity in the existence of that being, even if we have once found reason to believe it exists. \n\nWe must just plow forward, continuing to make these\ndeductions, trying to at least acknowledge this discrepancy. \n\nTo conclude, we can only really know how the world 'seems' to behave, moment-to-moment. But anything else is meaningless, due to our reliance on our sensible faculties. And there is little\nreason to believe that the universe is any more ordered than the void. Although it has continued to be for all of its previous existence. And I would place a bet on this order remaining forever onwards, even though I am in no place to make such a claim.\nIt is a task for myself and future scholars to attempt to find a reasonable explaination from our reliance and past experience to deduce that of the future. And if anyone can really find this explaination, feel free to contact me. I would gladly help you\npublish such a work in writing.", ""),
        StaticBook("On Shamanism V1", "Thurak'Yar", "Scribed by the Farseer Thurak,\n14'th of SUn's Smile, 1487.\n1. Those Who Practise\n\n2. The Connection\n\n3. Traversal\n\n4. Utilisation\nThose Who Practise\n\nA magic almost strictly wielded by those of Krug’s descent, Shamanism is to the Orcs as Muuntrivazja is to the priests of the Kha’s; narrowly practised and highly revered. Those that fully understand the ways\nof the magic, divided into the sects of Elementalists, Lataumans, Witchdocters and Farseers, each have their own role in the Uruks’ society and all put the needs of their race above their own or any singular individual. Dark Shamanism,\na forbidden topic, shall not be discussed in this tome, as it holds no relevance to the topic being held. The first, and debatably most simple form of Shamanism, Elementalism, is based on making a connection to the Elemental Plane and the Spirits that\nreside there. A Shaman of this type, with the aid of his or her ‘bonded’ spirit(s), may control an element such as Earth or Fire that is present nearby in their own realm. It should be noted that this differs from Arcane Magic as it requires no\nconnection to the void and, rather than creating matter, simply manipulates that already existing. The next form of Shamanism, the practitioners of which are dubbed ‘Lataumans’, is much more complex. By moving their consciousness into\nthe realm of Ancestral Spirits, these shamans can contact the forms of those who were chosen as ‘honourable’ in life, and reside in a place more connected to ours than any other. The long dead such as Lur or even Krug himself (Although it has never\nbeen done) could be contacted for advice or information, and stronger Lataumans can gain blessings from these spirits; their strength or courage being ‘boosted’ for a short, albeit valuable, time, although this can’t be reproduced on\nothers by these Shamans.\nWitchdocters, the more ritualistic group of the subtypes, choose to meddle with the Immortal Spirits- those that live in a plane dedicated to the aspects of the mortal races.\nEvery emotion, every ideal and every thought can be categorised to a spirit, there, and the power of such spirits is used by Witchdocters to curse and plague those who are seen as a threat to the Shamans’ beliefs. They can do this on anything\nliving- including animals and plants, and as such these shamans are held in wary consideration by the Druids. They may also do the same with the Elementals, surprisingly- being able to call upon the lesser of such spirits to curse whomever\nthey wish. Another important part of Witchdoctery is the production of potions, which, although similar to alchemy, instead focuses on using ingredients that represent a certain spirit to call upon its power, and requires more thought on\nthe individual pieces than the brew as a whole.\nLastly, there are the Farseers. Sometimes called the Elders of the Uruks, these shamans spend their days traversing the Immortal Plane in search of enlightenment in cultural and\nhistorical matters. They bring their council to the Rex or their race as a whole, and act as the balancing force between the two planes. In much the same way as Witchdocters can curse, Farseers have the ability to bless\nplants or animals; being able to increase favourable attributes such as strength and resilience, but also those more intangible, such as hope. It is this reason why Farseers are so widely valued, as these blessings before battles or klomps prove to be\ninvaluable assets.\nThe Connection\n\nFor the following section, we’ll be referring to the connection of the Farseers to the Spirit Realm, as it is held as the both the most complex and developed form of the art among those who practise it; being one\nthat these Shamans use to constantly and fully transport their consciousness to another plane. This forced passage between realms begins when a Farseer cuts off the link between his consciousness and his body, and ends when he, or in turn\na Spirit controlling him, returns the stream to his mortal person. Unlike any other magic, the beginning of Shamanism actually requires the limitation of Mana being spent, rather than an increase in such. The regulation of mana use is vital in both\nentering and departing the spirit realm, and as such is vigorously practised by all Farseers. To let their mind wander to the place of spirits, they must almost entirely cut off the connection between their mind and their body-\nleaving only a trickle of mana as an anchor to return. When they wish to come back, they increase the mana flow to their mortal person, and their thoughts will begin to travel back to their body. Now, that being said, although controlling mana plays\na massive part in connection to the Spirit Realms, it isn’t so that anyone that can do such may actually make this connection. When an aspiring shaman is first taken on as a student, they will be put through several trials and tests, dictated\nby their teacher. Although they are sometimes seen as a filter to weed out the dedicated from the short-sighted, they are indeed much more; as a pupil’s action in these tests decide whether or not the spirits themselves will allow him or\nher to move their consciousness into their realm. An intangible filter of sorts is present, at which a group of minor spirits regulate the influx of those entering and leaving the Spirit Realm. Those that have been seen bearing positive\nattributes during these tests may be, for the first time, allowed to enter this new realm. It should be noted that the longer a Shaman has been connecting to the Spirit Realms for, the easier it will be for them to pass through the filter without\nthe spirits scrutinising over them- and as such it’s important for these Elder Shamans to do their best to regulate their own actions as honourable or otherwise.\nTraversal\n\nOnce a Shaman has connected to the Spirit Realm, an incomprehensible variety of circumstances may occur. For the first few times, chances are their senses will be dulled or non-existent as their\nmind struggles with the lack of bodily connection. Their vision may remain pitch black, and the only ‘input’ they receive may be a soft, niggling feeling of being watched. As time progresses, aspiring Shamans learn to deal with what\ninformation they’re given, and soon the senses return, albeit in situations that differ massively from those of the Mortal Realm. Their vision may be hued; the world they seen filtered as if through coloured glass. Hearing may\nbe non-existent, or they may hear cries far away as close as if whispered in their ears. The sense of feel usually comes last for those that travel the spirit realm, and it can be the most confusing of all to deal with. Sometimes, should they come\nacross a vision of a man being slaughtered, they would feel a phantom sense of pain- like a slash across their neck as they’re decapitated. It’s important for a Shaman to differentiate these Empathetic feelings to others from their\nown, especially in the Spirit Realm, as it’s been known to drive some blindly mad. Now, on to what actually occurs in this realm. When a Farseer, presumably with full use of his senses first enters the Spirit Realm, they'll find themselves, most likely,\nin an environment they haven’t yet seen. It might be a dense forest or a dank swamp; either way, a Shaman learns quickly to adapt when they traverse the spirit realm. With them is usually their Spirit Guide; a creature in a form important\nto them or their heritage which will lead them through this realm away from, or into danger, depending on the situation. A member of the Ugluk clan, for example, might have a Spirit Guide in the form of a bull, as it is Ugluk Bulls that their clan\nis so famous for- and the same can be said for Lur Wolves or Braduk Rhinos. So, led, or not, by their respective guides, a Shaman will eventually come across what they will refer to as a vision. It may be an event of the long past, the distant\nfuture, or the twisted present- usually representing something that has or will play a major part in the development of either the Uruks or the Shamans. These won’t be straightforward events, however; one may see only the form of a crying Uruk\nmother and her child, and from there they must learn to decipher its potential meaning. And it is from that that a Farseer’s real skill is discovered; the ability to learn from these small snippets of information and then advise their leaders or people\nfor or against certain actions that could, potentially, bring massive consequences for their race. \nAnother form of visions, much rarer in comparison to these odd events, are those brought forth by a spirit himself. These are no tricks to\nbe deciphered; if a spirit goes to enough effort to force a Shaman into a vision, their vision will be straightforward and commending. Usually, these occur when the Spirit feels as if their influence in the Mortal Realm could be\nincreased, and they are to call upon the aid of a Shaman to spread their influence. The Shaman, of course, has no real choice in the matter, but those stronger in the way of words may be able to convince a nagging Spirit to change their\nmind on a matter which might be otherwise impossible, or at least very consequential, to perform.\nUtilisation\n\nLast but very much not least, we come to a Shaman’s real use in Orcish culture- their ability to manipulate the Mortal Realm around them. As said earlier, each sect of Shamanism has their own ways of doing\nthis: Elementalists by meddling with nearby elemental, Lutaumans by blessing themselves, Witchdocters by cursing others or creating tribal elixers, and Farseer by blessing Orcs or others around them who are in need.\nUsually, they go about these things in similar ways. Elementalists must bind themselves to an Elemental by first impressing them by going on certain quests to draw their attention. Then, they promise the Spirit something that it seeks that they can\ngive, and then a bond will be made. As more Elemental Spirits are bonded to, sometimes a Elementalist’s proficiency in the control of a certain element may be hindered; like if one Shaman has bonded to a spirit of water as well fire, or earth\nas well as lightning. It’s up to the Shaman himself to decide what they’ll sacrifice, or if they’ll instead focus only on one element to become utmost proficient at it over all others.\nLutaumans go about creating their influence similarly. They first must call upon an Ancestral Spirit to meet with, and then they will try and gain their favour by promises of impressive feats or proof of their past honour. Once a Spirit\nagrees, they will temporarily bind their essence to the Shaman; giving them massively increased attributes such as strength or bravery for a short amount of time, which may just turn the tide of battle in their favour.\n*the book cuts off- seeming to have run out of space. Down the bottom a small entry has been scribbled in*\n\n\n\n\"See Volume Two for the remaining information of this Tome.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("On Shamanism V2", "Thurak'Yar", "Volume Two of \nOn Shamanism, Scribed by the Farseer Thurak, 14'th of Sun's Smile, 1487.\n... The more they do this, the more word of their feats will spread among the Ancestral Plane and the more likely it is for these Spirits to accept their deals.\nWitchdocters go about things a bit differently than others. During the rituals,\nthey’ll present certain objects which hold relevance to the Spirit they are trying to evoke. For example, should they be trying to create a potion which causes the drinker to have insatiable hunger, they would perhaps need something\nsuch as the stomach of a large animal, such as a bull, or they may burn and char excessive amounts of savouries in hopes of gaining the attention of the spirit of Greed and Gluttony. Should they do so, they’ll begin to call to their desired\nspirit in the tongue of Old Blah, asking for their aid and promising that the attributes that they represent will somehow be more prominent after the use of said potion. Should the spirit agree, the mixture will be cursed, and the Witchdoctor can use\nuse it as he will on his unfortunate victims. However, these Shamans must be careful, as it’s sometimes not apparent how a spirit has cursed the potion, and unintended effects are rampant in the brews of unexperienced Witchdocters.\nFinally, the Farseers’ blessings are actually quite similar to that of the Lataumans’, in the way that it requires sharp tongue and wit to convince the spirits to give them their boon. When a Farseer decides he wishes to bless something, he must travel\nto the Spirit Realm and begin calling the name of the spirit that hold the attribute he needs for the blessing. Should the spirit answer, then the Farseer must try and convince it that the blessing will, in some way, benefit the spirit.\nIf this outright fails, and the Spirit refuses, a Farseer may do something else that no other Shaman may do; that being fight the spirit for his blessing. This is very dangerous, and is usually done only in times of desperation, as when a Shaman\ndies or is injured in the Spirit Realm, he dies or is injured back in the mortal realm. Once he’s either convinced the Spirit of the need of the blessing or beaten him in battle, it will then begin to take over a Shaman’s body. Back in the Mortal Realm\na Farseer’s limbs may start to move under its will, and words in Old Blah will be said to give the blessing direction. A mist, usually hued the colour that best represents the spirit doing the blessing, will pour from the Shaman's orifices\nand encompass the person, animal or plant he wishes to bless. When its finished, the Shaman need only to return his connection to his body and admire his handywork; the fabric of the mortal world being shifted in his favour, albeit in only a small front.", ""),
        StaticBook("On the Arsended", "Vicelin", "22nd of The Deep Cold, 1612.\n\nThe Ascended we have long suspeced of being charlatans and monster lovers have finally shown their true colours in the Fenn lands, where they threatened to kill a little girl if a seemingly innocent man named Azoth did not\ncome peacefully. I am not one to judge this tactic, but what came next was the death of Azoth and the subsequent hostage negotiation between a druid who had taken a girl to negotiate for a Frost Witch. In classic druid fashion, the one known as 'Jackal'\nthreatened to kill his hostage if the Frost Witch was not turned over. She was not, and Jackal was shot by an Ascended, releasing a sort of beast to devour the little girl. It is unknown what the extent of her injuries are.  It is clear that the ascended\nvalue the lives of Frost Witches above the mundane and are thus enemies of the Manticore Initiative. We should begin by finding this 'Blundermore'.", ""),
        StaticBook("On The Old Ways", "Owl", "On The Old Ways\n\nTraditions are important to religious fortitude. Especially when involving oneself in the studies of druidism.\n\nNature is center and our ward, with the Aspects second, then all other such attributes of our-\n-life third. Without this order of servitude, there is no value in our sacrifices.\n\nWe are merely pawns with sentience, bound to guardianship, oaths, and eternal sacrifice even beyond death.\n\n- The Druid of the Owl, 1411.", ""),
        StaticBook("On Vodniks", "Siegmeyer of Cepa", "8th of Malin's Welcome\n\nSiegmeyer of Cepa\n\nThe vodnik itself is a parasite, said to be created by some foul sorcery. This parasite can invade a corpse that’s been left in water. The parasite then mutates the corpse - vodniks can be identified by\ntheir slimy green appearance, they wield sharp claws and teeth, however most dangerous of all… They are capable of paralyzing even the strongest men with their venom, which can be transmitted through its claws and teeth. This is what makes a vodnik-\ndangerous, but their greatest weakness is that the corpse is incredibly fragile, so a strong willed swordsman may cleave several of these creatures in two with ease, a simple aurum sword may lessen the work even more. Vodniks often tend to fight in groups\nIt was previously mentioned that the vodnik carries a venom inside them. This venom works fast and will eventually kill anyone who does not receive an antivenom quickly, the end result will be paralysis and total organ failure. The antivenom may be-\ncreated by using the parasite itself, the exact ingredients are unknown to me at the moment.", ""),
        StaticBook("On Wights", "Revion Tathron", "On Wights\nBy Revion Tathron\nWights, first and foremost, are the creations of a Dark Art known as Mysticism, on which a book shall be written at a later date. They are, as it was put to me, \"Transcendent spectral entities\". They boast a wealth of powers from their state; these\ninclude:\n-Telepathy\n-Telekinesis\n-Manifestation Control\n-Better prowess in Mysticism\n-The ability to \"Haunt\" husks.\nWhat is haunting, you may ask?\nHaunting is the ability of Wights to 'possess' empty bodies. These can range from empty suits of armor to corpses. In this state, their magic is weaker depending on how heavy their 'body' is. However, it does provide\nsome protection against that enemy of all undead, Gold.\nAs Wights have the ability to control what they look like when they manifest, and they can possess husks, there are no common defining features, if you're merely looking at them. Wights are mostly made of 'Ectoplasm', which is a mixture of mana and\nlife-force that all spectral beings consist of.\nAs stated in the beginning of this tome, Wights are created through Mysticism. Only a few details are known about this ritual; firstly, that the to-be Wight is a master over Mysticism and ectoplasm, whereupon the 'sacrifice' themselves to\ntranscend to their spectral state from their bodies. However; their bodies turn as hard as rock, and if their former body is destroyed, the Wight perishes.\nThe odds are, you will never see a Wight; this is not due to the fact that they have so much control over their forms; rather, that there is only one currently in existence. This may change, however.\nThe Wight I talked with was perfectly reasonable, and did not attempt to kill me at all (as other things I've studied had.) It seemed relatively free from the instability that other undead are known to possess (See: Ghouls). \n\n\nEND.", ""),
        StaticBook("On Wisdom", "Whimsycal", "On Wisdom\n             by Shanka\nWub is wisdom? It is a mixture of things. Gruk'n, experience agh wits all come together to define wub wisdom is.\n\nAnyash may gruk that to catch a fish, latz must use bait. But only the wise ash gruks wub kind of bait will catch wub kind of fish in\nwub river or lake.\n\nAnyash gruks that scaddernaks are bub'hozh agh dangerous beasts.\nBut only ash who has faced the beast will gruk wub it is that makes it so dangerous agh fearsome. Agh only the wise will gruk how to defeat agh tame the beast.\nTo be wise is to have experienced, to have learned, to have dared.\n\nThat is wub wisdom is.", ""),
        StaticBook("On Wraiths", "Toodles", "On Wraiths\n\nBy: Someone who isn't stupid enough to reveal their true name.\nNot much is known about the actual physical characteristics of Wraiths by the author, but what they do know shall be written down. Wraiths (also known as Harbingers) are shadowy undead beings with a proclivity for killing.\nThe most recent incarnation of Wraiths are produced by the machinations of the Drakaar Mordring, through the utilization of certain altars, one of which is in the Sunless Sanctum. (The process of becoming a Wraith is described in another book.)\nThe Wraith, once created, is bound to Mordring's Will; basically, to bring about a resurgence of the Dragonkin. Wraiths have the ability to summon some form of Vessel, which fill with lifeforce when a mortal dies in the vicinity of it. It takes fifteen\ndeaths for the Vessel to be full, upon which a Dragon or Drake will spawn. If the Vessel is destroyed before the amount of lifeforce is acquired, all the accumulated lifeforce will vanish, but the Vessel can still be summoned. If the Wraith attempts to\nharm the newly-made Dragon or Drake, the Wraith will perish. After thirty years, Wraiths are released from Mordring's service, but they retain the ability to summon Vessels. Wraiths have the ability to husk\nempty bodies, much like Wights; but there are unknown complications regarding the eyes of such a body.", ""),
        StaticBook("Operation GAP", "Operative KFB", "-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------=====OPERATION===========GAP==========------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n10th of Grand Harvest\nOperation GAP\nGather Animal Products\n\nOperatives\nKerwyr Frostbeard\nAgent KFB\n\nRonnie Frostbeard\nAgent RFB\nObjective:\nInfiltration of Goldhand Fields and gathering of various animal products ranging from leather to raw beef. \n\nSecurity Level:\nMedium (||||)", ""),
        StaticBook("Operation HALL", "Kerwyr Frostbeard", "OPERATION H.A.L.L\n\nOPERATIVE: GFB\n\nOVERSEER: KFB\n\nMISSION:\nUTTER DESTRUCTION AND REMOVAL OF ALL EVIDENCE THAT POINTS TO FROSTBEARD INVOLVMENT IN RECENT CLAN HALL ATTACKS.\nASSIGNED 15TH OF THE AMBER COLD 1602\n\nSigned ~GFB\nOverser KFB", ""),
        StaticBook("Orc Attack (rep)", "Edward Poesroe", "2nd of The Amber Cold, 1572\n\nReport regarding an assault by Orcs in the Imperial District\n\nWritten by Edward Poesroe\n\nThose Present\n\nAn elf named Thain, with fair hair and\nwielding a sword and a black cape.\n\nSer Leopold, armed with his cane and sword.\n\nAdeon of Rhoswen, with a scar on his upper eye\n\nVargen Vallberg\nwielding a shield\nMany others who I could not get the chance to ask for their names. They were armoed and armed.\n\nAs I was patrolling, Thalin approached me in the city square, telling me that two orcs were attacking a human. I rushed to action to help survey the\nscene and to see if my participation was nessecary. As I was not yet issued my armor and weapon, I would have been ineffective. Additionally, about 4-5 other people helped the man out. \n\nTwo orcs were fighting with Vargen Vallberg\n. Upon an interview with Vargen he said that these two orcs fought with hiim for no reason at all. Although the two attackers were orcs, one had a staff commonly used by Shamans. According to witnesses, the shaman was controlling the other orc.\nWith Thain's cry, many others from the square started to congregte at the scene of the scuffle. About 10 people of various sorts were assembled to fight. There were a couple onlookers as well, one of which was the owner of the bookstore.\nUltimately, the orcs defended themselves against those assembled. They died quickly, and everyone dispered shortly thereafter. \n\nUpon interviewing vallen, I realized he was injured. I took him to the clinic and dressed his wounds.\nThe two Orcs did not return and everything turned back to normal after the scuffle. No people aside from Vallen were injured. \n\nThis concludes the end of my report.", ""),
        StaticBook("Orc Babies", "Rosso", "Where do orc babies come from?\nYou imagine orc babies and you imagine a green thing being born from the hot sands of the war nation, somewhat like a plant. Well, that is just not true. Believe it or not, orc woman exist and actually get pregnant like humans and elves.\nThe great aspect of orc baby creation lies in the special mating ritual that is performed before the orc woman is impregnated. I had the misfortune of being made a slave to the orcs, but it did let me witness this unusual event.\nFirst of all, Klomps are made between all of the orc women, as the strongest will have the first choice on the males. Then came to men, and this is where it gets weird. In the normal Klomps, the orcs just hit each other until one is on the ground almost\ndying. The mating Klomp is quite different.\n\nIt was to my surprise that instead of punching and kicking, the male orc came dressed in what I assume was dwarven beard, and started doing other things. One chanted poetry in blah, I still do not know how\nthat is possible but it did happen. Another one started dancing, another brought a warthog, already dead, and started cooking it, using a variety of herbs and spices. I was stunt in my chains.\n\nIt appears that orc women fight only for first choice, while\nthe orc men fight to impress the women. One would think it would be by fighting each other in terms of combat, but the orc women know that their men are strong, so they chose the orc which seems to have other skills. As such, the orc man will try his best\nto impress the women, yet of course they do not like doing such.\n\nAfter the women chose their man, the orc males will have one night before they gather with their mating partners. On this night they smoke the biggest amount of cactus green that they can,\nand then trade blows, taking each punch to the face with honor. An orc which I saw that danced like a fairy, stood still while he received blows from another for more than half the night.\n\nThey do this ritual as to recover their honor after the greatly\nunhonorable performance. None laugh of others, they respect themselves for doing so, but I will never forget the orc singing in broken common, it still to this day makes me laugh. I was to be executed after the next day’s mating, which was done inside a\ntent of course, but luckily was saved by an attack of the dwarves which happened shortly after. This has changed my view on all orcs, as I never knew they could clean so many bowls in such a small amount of time, as the first chosen orc male had done.\nWhere do Orc babies come from\n\nOriginal author unknown\nCoppied by Rosso\nVaerHaven", ""),
        StaticBook("Orc Cell", "Corvo Attano", "My name is Corvo Attono I have had this voice into my head ever since 7th of July.\nWhen I was 11 I use to sneak out passed my bedtime and go to the woods. I would hide under a log and wait for the Wood Elves to come, They would sing and dance and drink\nale all night long.I went back there one day and it seemed abandoned. The cold mist covered the area I looked around out of curiosity and stumbled over a dead Wood Elf, he had 3 arrows pierced into his pale green skin.\nI ripped it out and saw that it was forged by Orcs. I had no fear nor was I shocked at the sight. I was startled as a low Mumble appeared into the distance, it soon got so loud I had to cover my ears.\nBut it was no use, the shouting got too loud, I dived onto the ground rolling trying to make it stop. Then I realised it was coming through my head. The voice was saying: “Kill him Corvo, finish the scum off!”,\nSuddenly a powerful possession took over my body, the Wood Elf awoke. “H..h..help me p..p..please!”. I couldn't move any part of my body as if it were paralysed, I could only blink and roll my eyes. I glared at the Elf, he had terror in his eye's.\nBefore realising it, my hand had gripped a rock tightly, I picked it up and lifted it above my head.\n“Oh dear lord!” the elf whispered. My hand rammed the rock down into his face repeatedly until I could no longer swing.\nI dropped the rock and collapsed sideways onto the ground.\n“What have I done” I cried. he voice came back and whispered to me: “Well done Corvo!”. As I got up I started to run back to my house, I could see glimpses of a little girl staring at me.\ncould also hear the giggles of a little girl running after me.\n“You can run Corvo he he he” The voice turned into a deep demon like voice “BUT YOU CAN'T HIDE!!!!!!”.\nI collapsed onto the ground and fainted. I woke up in a cell on a yellow stained mattress, a candle was lighting up the cell. I looked at myself realising I was pure naked.\nI checked my sides to see if I had a stolen kidney. I couldn't see or feel any stitches or scars, “HELP ME!” I shouted knowing it was useless I still done it.I could hear loud grunts in the hallways and shadows of something eating human flesh.\nI looked into the right corner of the cell and saw a Halfling skeleton, with some kind of book in his or hers and shadows of something eating human flesh, I looked into the right corner of the cell and saw a Halfling skeleton.\nwith some kind of book in his or hers hand. I pried the dusty old book from it's hands the pages were yellow, and the writing was in Elven. “Why was a Hobbit carrying an Elven book I wonder?\" I whispered.\nI saw a shadow come closer to my cell, “Roigh' yer maggot, come wit' me”\nIt was an Orc! I had no choice but to follow him. As I walked down the halls, other Orcs were staring at me, showing their rotten teeth and snarling at me.\nI was looking around as I was walking and saw a window I would probably be able to fit through and escape, the bars were wide apart.\nI stepped aside and ran up to the window using an Orcs head as a launch pad up, I got my shoulders through when they grabbed my feet and nearly pulled me back down. Luckily I kicked them and jumped down into the lake at the bottom and swam away.\nWritten by Corvo Attono\n((mrdigdug118))", ""),
        StaticBook("Orc Romance", "Eath'Lur", "Orc Romance\n\n      One of\n    Eath'Lur's\n   best books\n\n\n\n    10/10 - Guy by his side after reading it\n\n    7/10 - An illatian's comment; \"could use more pasta.\"\nShakilaya approached Shonboku with fire in her eyes. The green orc, stunned by Shakilaya's beauty asked her\n\n\"Ug, wubz lat name\"\n\n\"I'm Shakilaya, lat muzt be Shonboku. We iz duh eazterner orkz. I see u have big katana\"\n\"Oh yub, idz big katana. Lat want to touch it?\"\n\n\"Yub, me wantz to touch lat katana\"\n\nshonboku unsheates his katana. It was wet.\n\n\"Zorry, mi wuz zwimming ad dah thermal fountain\"\n\"Oh yez, me peepz itz very hard agh zweaty rite now. Mi peep dah fumes... Hmmm...\"\n\nShakilaya rubs the edge of the katana with her lips and tells to him;\n\n\"Thiz iz zuch ah nice katana, we need to put it in dizplay.\"\n\"Dizplay? Where?\"\n\n\"In dah feztival ob dah Klompakiri, dat happenz once evereh two monthz.\"\n\n\"It haz been two monthz zince dah lazt Klompakiri, we muzt hurry NOWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWW.\"\n\"ok\"\n\nThey went quickly outside, the Klompakiri was happening. sHONBOKU approached a display and put his big dark large katana there for display; unsheated and wet with hot thermal water fountain wet transparent substance.\n\"Your big katana is dirty, we need to clean it\" said Shakilaya\n\n\"How do we klean it?\"\n\nShakilaya did a movement with her armpit and produced a sound. Suddenly, cloth came out from it! She uses it to rub the katana all the way up\nand all the way down, then back through the whole blade up then sliding it down like its a ramp so the katana shines bright and blacker than ever.\n\n\"Ok, now my cloth is dirty, we must clean my cloth\" says shakilaya\n\n\"there is river nearby\"\n\"We muzt go now agh klear dah cloth then!\"\n\n\"Ok\"\n\nthey reach the river and clean the cloth. Moments later, they return to the Klompakiri festival and they find out that shonboku won the Klompakiri big katana display festival.\nEveryone was happy and later in the day, shakilaya gave birth to eight babies. the father, Shonboku, jealous, got his way around to have babies with himself and later on the same day gave birth to two babies. Then they had 10 babies in total.\n3 years later\na baby eating elf breaks in shakilaya and shonboku house and eat all their ten babies and then the \nor cish couple gets very sad and shonboku cries\n\n\"pizzapizzapizzapizzapizzapizzapizza...\"\nafraid, shakilaya looks to him after the baby eating elven monster leaves their house. shakilaya asks him\n\n\"i never knew you were an illatian, not an orc.\"\n\n\"yeah\"\n\n\"i love u anyways\"\nthen they had 7 more babies later that day and they all lived for sixty five years because they died after sixy five years passed.\n\nthe end\nthis book is very good, do not copye\n\n\n\n\ncopye is evil, if this book has this text, its because its original", ""),
        StaticBook("Orcish Language", "Saendir Aureon", "Wordbook Common language - Orcish\n\nA Dictionary for translation of common speak.\n\nBy Saendir Aureon.\nUg = Hello, Hi, Hail\n\nTrom'ka = Formal greeting\n\nGug'ye = Goodbye\n\nSkah/ Saahkah = Curse words\n\nRulg = Thank you\nYub = Yes\n\nNub = No \n\nDabu = Yes (obedient)\n\nAgh = and\n\nHosh = good\n\nNubhosh = bad\n\nBubhosh = very good\nLat = you\n\nMi = Me / I\n\nRex = King\n\nGoth = Lord\n\nKub = Child\n\nUruk = Orc\n\nBrudda = War Uzg Orc\nStowts/ Gazat = Dwarf\n\nTwigies/ Albai = Elf\n\nTreeuggers = Woodelf\n\nSqueals = Halflings\n\nShara = Human(s)\n\nSnaga = Slave\n\nHowler = Wolf\nKlomp = fight\n\nFlat = dead\n\nVotar = hunt\n\n! Strigz = war !\n\nNubded = Undead\n\nKrimp = Stun/ Capture\nLusk = Axe\n\nZult = Sword\n\nO'lig = Bow\n\nLigz = Arrow\n\nStik = Staff\n\nMojo = Magic\nBlarg = House\n\nSan = Home\n\nGoi = City\n\nBlah = Orcish language\n\nBlah = Talk/ Speak\nAsh = One\n\nDub = Two\n\nGakh = Three\n\nFuth = Four\n\nH' = Five\n\nH'ash = Six\n\nH'dub = Seven\nH'gakh = Eight\n\nH'futh = Nine\n\nAshty = Ten\n\nDubty = Twenty\n\nNote: Translations may vary per sentence.\nAlso Translations may not be 100 % accurate.", ""),
        StaticBook("Orcish Plague", "riverfyre", "The Orcish Plague has become a serious and debilitating disease that can kill those infected. With several having perished from the disease, new information has been given. While the information is not complete nor fully understood, what can be pieced\ntogether is ways to prevent further spread of this infectious disease. As such it is important to know how the disease is spread, what the symptoms are, and how to be treated. If this plague continues to spread at its\npace, entire cities could be wiped away within days of initial contact.\nHow it is Spread\n\nThe Orcish Plague has been know to spread in many various ways. How one becomes infected can be done through contact. Any contact with an infected person, creature, food, or area are at high risk of infection.\nThose with weaker immunities, children, and elderly are more prone to the disease. With just vicinity being an issue, the spread is far more concerning. The disease seems to be spread through air, consumption,\nand contact with poisoned areas. The disease seems to enter through the mouth and nose when exposed to the spores or infected air expelled from an infected individual.\nThe disease then spreads in the body from the lungs into the kidneys and other organs. When consumed, it starts with the stomach, spreading into the lungs and other organs. It is unknown what the plague does to the epidermal\nwhen touched, but the disease does pose serious health concerns. Bodies that have been infected risk infecting those that touch them. Avoid burying the dead as it can spread through the ground\nand can lead to infection of the water supply. Cremation seems to be the best solution for the dead, but take precautions with the smoke.\nSymptoms\n\nThe plague slowly devours the body internally. The organs fall one by one until the body can no longer sustain itself. As the body slowly decomposes inside, the pain becomes unbearable and the infected dies slowly and painfully.\n- Coughing within the first day\n- Lungs begin to inflame and fill with fluid\n- Lethargy\n- Eyes and flesh begin to turn yellow\n- Kidneys fail\n- Stomach rots\n- Internal organs slowly eaten away by the acid and rot\n- Death\nEven after treatment, the infected is left weak and in pain. If you see any sign of a cough or lethargy in children, immediately seek help.\nTreatment\n\nThere seems to be no normal way of treatment to spare one from this plague. However, it does appear that holy magic can be used to remove the taint from the bodies. While the plague can do severe damage, only powerful healers can\naccomplish the task on the more severe cases. Once healed, the infected can return to their normal duties after they have rested. The infection takes much of their strength and energy, leaving them exhausted\nfor several days. It appears even after treatment, one can become infected again.", ""),
        StaticBook("Order 120", "Lord Walter Francesco Visconti", "Order for Farddak of five protection glyphs a week in return for a tome of the enchanter for one evlen month", ""),
        StaticBook("Oren has Fallen?", "Knwell Quill", "Oren Has Fallen\n\nOren hasn't been the same for decades now. Though the facade of what people believe Oren still remains the world's superpower, it is not. Theres too many faults in Oren currently.\nOne of them that sticks out like a sore thumb is; the weak power of the fedual government. Oren ideals have changed from speaking softly and carrying a big stick to, talking loudly and having nothing to back it up. Luckly for it's past monarchs it has\nsufficied for them.\n\nMy second problem with Oren is the constant infighting within Oren in order to maintain a growing power as a equal. Every nobleman feels threaten as a new power arises within Oren. With someone always looking to put them down.", ""),
        StaticBook("Oren History: I", "Jacob Chapel", "History of Oren\n       Part I\n\n\nThis history has been collected by me, Jacob Chapel. Sources are various scrolls and texts and the museum of Petrus, beside common knowledge and tales. Enjoy.\n\n((Written by Pepernoot))\nIf you're interested in the history before Al'Khazar, I suggest you pick up the first part of the Holy Scrolls, the Nativities. If you're interested in the history past Siegmund Carrion's election, then you need to find part two of The History of Oren.\nThe days of Aegis\nThe history of Oren begins in Aegis, the land of the Descendants. To the west of the Cloud Temple laid its lands. The capital of Al’Khazar was surrounded by pastures, farmlands and forests, and to the north laid the snowy lands,\ncontaining cities and towns such as Alstion and Snowy Fields. In the south were the islands known as the Whisper Isles, surrounded by the calm waters of the Whisper Lake, and filled with fishermen and craftsmen such as glassblowers.\nThe first king was Horen himself. Many Kings ruled the Kingdom wisely after him, Kings such as Saint Daniel. The Kingdom’s grand city was built by this King Daniel in 1300. Eventually King Pampo Perea, Saint Daniel’s seneschal, took power, with Edmund\nSheffield as his seneschal.\nAs time passed the Undead became stronger and bolder in their attacks on the Kingdom. Snowy Fields fell and was razed, but soldiers from Alstion retook it and the town was rebuilt. This turned out to be futile eventually as\nthe northern towns fell one by one. Even King Perea himself was killed by the Undead, within the tall walls of Al’Khazar. Edmund Sheffield took his place, but was corrupted by the dark forces and turned to the Nether. His “abduction” was accompanied by a\ngreat siege of Al’Khazar, in which a portal to the Nether opened in the city square. After a great battle the City of Man was sacked. Human refugees poured across the Kingdom and the city of Galahar, built on the ruins of the old town of Kramoroe, was\nnamed capital.\n\nEdmund’s son Enor Sheffield took his place, but under his rule the situation worsened drastically, the corruption of his father and his own weakness led to great dissent in the Kingdom.\nMeanwhile Gaius Marius, Hochmeister of the Teutons had carved out a realm for himself to the east of the Kingdom, and had even participated in wars against Oren, allying with its enemies. It is important to note that even though the Undead threatened\nOren, and although Oren was the strong defence between the Undead and the rest of the races, this didn’t deter them to wage wars against the Kingdom. Infighting between the nations of Malinor, Krug, Urguan and Oren was common.\nRebellion brew in the\nKingdom, and in Galahar the Phoenix Rebellion formed. As the weak King Enor saw his position wasn’t tenable anymore he named Gaius Marius as King of Oren. This treason lead to the rise of the rebellion and a war between the part of Oren controlled by\nthe Teutons and the Phoenix Rebellion, led by Eze’kiel Tarus as the Phoenix King. Eventually the two sides reach an agreement, splitting the realm into two parts. The Kingdom of Renatus, ruled by King Tarus, and the Realm of Hanseti, ruled by Gaius.\nAfter giving up his crown the mad King Enor and his followers settled on an island, and together with Queen Dawn Perea, wife of the old King Perea he created the nation of Salvus.\nHumanity could not rest though, as the Undead continued their march\nrelentlessly. In 1349 Galahar was attacked by the forces of evil, but even though the attack was repelled, the city was evacuated for fears of Miasma. Eventually Aegis fell in 1351, and the humans fled through the portal to the verge,\nalong with the other Descendants. \n\nA new dawn in Asulon\nAfter a brief stay in The Verge, the Descendants settled in the new lands of Asulon. Oren was still divided into the three Kingdoms, and Renatus settled around their new capital of Arethor.\nIn these turbulent times a new human nation sprung up, the Kingdom of Seventis.\n\nWhen King Eze’kiel resigned from the throne, Renatus was ruled by the Regent King Reynard Lycian until Godfrey Horen appeared. Godfrey claimed direct decent from King Horen\nand quickly received support from the Dukes and other nobles of the realm. He consolidated power and strengthened the Kingdom, which was plagued by instability and attacks from the other nations.\n\nSoon after Godfrey started his reign a coalition against\nSalvus formed by The Kingdom of Seventis, Alras, the Orcs and most importantly what was called the Twilight Army. This coalition did not have official support from Renatus, but most of its nobles supported it. Opposing the coalition were Salvus itself,\nthe Dwarves of Urguan and the Realm of Hanseti. After the humiliating defeat, and the betrayal of Queen Dawn’s guards, which murdered her, Salvus was absorbed into Renatus.\n\nAs the great plague hit Asulon, the Kingdom of Seventis was hit most severely,\npresumably due to its location close to the Cloud Temple. Most of its inhabitants died, allowing for an absorption into the Kingdom of Renatus to protect the weakened towns.\n\nThe Teutons could not stand by idly as Renatus grew, and went to war against\nthe Kingdom. Swiftly the war turned against their favour, and it became clear that they were losing the war. To avoid destruction of his nation, Hochmeister Mirtok surrendered it to King Godfrey, saying the words “I will die for this nation, but I will\nnot let it die for me”.\n\nThe annexation of Hanseti meant the unification of humanity, and the Holy Oren Empire was formed. In the Empire the Crownlands, Salvus and Hanseti were ruled as separate kingdoms, with the Emperor presiding over the individual\nkings, while also being king of the crownlands.\n\nAfter a rebellion against the crown, House Tarus, House Elendil and House Norsem were shunned and fell out of favour in the Empire. Soon though, the lands of Asulon were submerged by floods,\nand a second flight was needed.\n\nAnthos, a land plagued by war\nJust as the flight from Aegis, the new land was not reached in one trip. There were stops at the isles of Elysium and Kalos. One notable thing in Kalos was the formation of the\nPhoenix Kingdom, by Eze’kiel Tarus. The kingdom was quickly destroyed, even before leaving for Anthos.\n\nIn Asulon the Teutonic Order was nigh destroyed by the Flays, and the Hochmeister killed. A few remnants of the Order made it to Anthos, albeit\nwithout a Hochmeister to guide them. The Teutons settled on the southern side of the ice wall of the North. Meanwhile the Empire of Oren settled a bit further south, with Abresi as their capital.\n\nSoon after arriving it turned out this land was not as\nsafe as the Descendants had hoped. North of the wall the Teutons discovered a savage race of boarmen and a land filled with dragons.\n\nThis was not the most pressing issue to Oren though, as the Empress of Oren was kidnapped by the Orcs, and a joint\nHuman and Dwarf force invaded their capital and massacred nearly every orc present.\n\nEver present Elven aggression led to a crusade against the Princedom of Malinor. The Order of the White Rose quickly destroyed their forces and burned the Malenorian\nfarms. The elves eventually surrendered to the siege, proving the enormous strength of a united Oren.\n\nUnited it would not be for long, as the Teutons rebelled. In the first battle, at Kralta, the Teutons were crushed. At the second battle the\nBlackmonts stood alone against the Teutons on the Iron Fields, outnumbered two to one. The Teutonic Order was victorious.\n\nThe civil war was decided at the Siege of the Dreadfort, where the Chivays, and the Carrions (then bannermen of the Blackmonts)\ndistinguished themselves. The defeat at the Battle of Iron fields had led to close cooperation between the White Roses and the Blackmonts, which turned out to be more than the Teutons could handle. Although the Dreadfort was severely damaged the siege\nwas broken and the Teutonic Order defeated. Soon afterwards the Teutonic Order was disbanded by Emperor Godfrey.\n\nThe Scourge, the name of the goatmen and the dragons from the north made their first move south beyond the wall, destroying the old\nTeutonic castle of Greywyn with flames, and taking it for their own.\n\nThen, in a huge shock to the empire, Emperor Godfrey died. He was succeeded by his son, Horen.\n\nAs the princedom of Malinor was absorbed into the Empire as\nprotectorate, the expansion of Oren led to great concern with the other races. They formed a coalition and in the War of Anthos they attacked Oren, putting a halt to the expansion. Most prominent in the coalition were the Dwarves, angered by the\nexecution of one of their Dwarven lords by nobles of Oren. In the Battle of the Crossroads the coalition was defeated though, by a brilliant Orenian flanking manoeuvre.\n\nIn 1415 the Empire was left in disarray as Emperor Horen left, along with his\nmost loyal houses. The dwarves used this weakness to form their Grand Kingdom of Urguan in the War of Asulon. They dissolved the Empire of Oren and many parts, including Salvus and Adunia swear loyalty to the dwarves as vassal states. What remains of the\nEmpire was renamed to the Holy Kingdom of Oren and ruled by William Horen. After more chaos and disarray many more little human states sprung up or seceded from the Kingdom, leading to the current prominent Houses, states and cultures. \n \nEventually the\nGrand King of Urguan, Thorin Grandaxe dies. This caused the human vassal states to be released from their oaths to the dwarves. This made way for a renewed unification. As King William was pushing his powers and support from his nobles to the limit,\nHouse Winter made a secret pact with Ruska. This forced King William to step down, giving control of Oren to his cousin Silus. This was only temporary, as the states of Salvus, Oren, Ruska and the new state of Herendul were confederated into an empire,\nwith an elective monarchy. At the election Siegmund Carrion was voted in as Emperor of Oren.\n\nThis concludes part one of Oren's history. The events after Siegmund Carrion's election, up to the first years in Athera will be discussed in part two.\n((So you made it to the end. I hope you liked it. You can leave a message to me on the forums, username: Pepernoot))", ""),
        StaticBook("Oren Inspection", "Joneal Brandt", "NOTICE OF INSPECTION\nfor the Orenian Jurisdiction of JOHANNESBURG\n\nInspection provided by Mr. Joneal Brandt\n\n(For all questions and comments concerning the inspection of this jurisdiction, please seek out Mr. Brandt directly.) ->\nINSPECTION DETAILS:\nHerein, find the notes of inspection for the Orenian Jurisdiction of Johannesburg; including but not limited to:\n• structural, environmental, safety & hazard, and pest inspection of jurisdiction buildings;\n• placement and enforcement -\nof jurisdiction laws and mandates;\n• and other miscellaneous notes concerning the overall health of this jurisdiction.\n\nThe inspection begins on the next page.\nINSPECTION NOTE #1:\nConcerning the standards of . . . 3 GARDEN ST.\n\n• Multiple unlocked and broken storage chests, which contain personal valuables and city construction materials.\nThe lack of locks on doors and chests throughout the premises of\n3 Garden St. offers great opportunity for theft in this building.\n\n• On the 2nd FLOOR of this premises, in the second unmarked room closest to the stairs, are two broken and/or unplaced windows, providing access to the rooftop of the\nadjacent building. \n       - said rooftop has no guardrails installed, which could easily allow adolescents or the mentally impaired to succumb to injury due to a high fall.\n\n• On the 2nd FLOOR of this premises, in the third unmarked room closest to the\nstairs, are two rabbits. They offer no indication of domestication, and may have been left here by some previous owner of this residence. Both of these creatures are emaciated and filthy, and inspection indicates they have resided in this particular room\non 3 Garden St. for quite some time. Said rabbits were left in this unmarked room at the time of inspection.\nAs an added note, this unmarked room will also require sanitation service, as the waste of these creatures litters much of the limited space on\nthe floor. The smell hits you like an angry orc as soon as you step foot on the second floor, I don't think you'll miss it.\n\n• On the 3rd FLOOR of the premises, in the unmarked room on the right-hand side of the stairs, is yet another rabbit. As\nwith the third unmarked room on the 2nd floor, this room is filthy and will require additional sanitation after the creature is removed. \n\n*this page reeks of animal urine, and the bottom corner is torn*\nThat one is particularly... feral. Consider precaution when approaching this room, unless you want to be bitten or peed on.\n\n(Forgive the condition of the previous page in this notice; perhaps it offers some indication of the status of this\npremises.)\n\nEND OF INSPECTION NOTE #1\n\n-- . -- . -- .\n\nINSPECTION NOTE #2:\nConcerning the standards of . . . 2 GARDEN ST.\n\n• On the second floor of this premises\nis a broken window, providing access to all floors of the building.\n\n• Overgrowth on the west side of the building provides access to the inner courtyard and roof of this premises.\n\n• There is a locked door leading to the 3rd FLOOR of this\npremises, but the door has been hinged incorrectly and access to this floor is not changed by the presence of the lock.\nAdditionally, there are two unlocked chests on this floor with several personal valuables. \nThis premises, like the previous\ninspection, is especially susceptible to burglary and theft, and should be seen for repair immediately.\n\nEND OF INSPECTION NOTE #2\n\n-- . -- . -- .\nINSPECTION NOTE #3:\nConcerning the standards of . . . DOMESTICATED ANIMALS in this jurisdiction.\n\n• NOTED: Oddly enough, the jurisdiction of Johannesburg does have a running stable for horses, but multiple streets overflow with\nunmonitored and unkept steeds.\nThese congested streets are also in need of sanitation, from animal waste. Streets including (but not limited to)\n- Garden Street\n- John Frederick Avenue\n- Baston Lane\n- Burning Place\nare in particular\nneed of animal removal and general sanitation.\n\nEND OF INSPECTION NOTE #3\n\n-- . -- . -- .\n\nINSPECTION NOTE #4:\nConcerning the standards of . . . NORRINGTON MANOR.\n• All chests on the second floor of this premises are unlocked.\n\n• The front door of this premises will not close properly due to incorrect pressure plate placement.\n\nEND OF INSPECTION NOTE #4\n\n-- . -- . -- .\nINSPECTION NOTE #5:\nConcerning the standards of . . . 7 GLOVER ST.\n\n• In the BASEMENT of this premises, there is a high drop into a chamber, with no ladder or rope offering transportation. In the sake of good inspection, I jumped down into this\nchamber, and found it to be the parlor of (what seems to be) the city barracks. The ladder that leads to the surface is blocked by a locked trapdoor, so it seems I'm trapped down here.\n\nThis is perhaps the most ridiculous of my inspection notes, and\nshould be mended immediately.\n\n*the rest of the page is clean*\nI just realized that I have no food.\nThese barracks are unfinished; there are several rooms that have been built but unused and unlit.\nI've been shouting for about half an hour now. I don't think anyone can hear me.\nThere's a hole in the roof in the hallway out of the parlor. But what use is it now, this inspection.\nI'm trapped down here. No one is here. No one can hear me. I have no food, there is no food.\nI hate this. The waiting. Waiting to starve, waiting for someone to find me, waiting for something... ANYTHING to happen.\n\nThis will surely contribute to my inspection of this jurisdiction; in particular, building safety seems to be a major problem here\nin Johannesburg.\nI can't believe it, but I'm starting to see things. I could have sworn I saw a figure standing in the office over there. He was wearing a plain white buttoned shirt, and dark pants. A beard.\nI looked in that direction and he wasn't there. \nAm I going mad?\nThat's it. I used my Soulstone. Forgot about the damned thing.\n\nThis should suffice for my inspection. After that ordeal...\n\nEND OF INSPECTION NOTE #5\n\n-- . -- . -- .\nINSPECTION SUMMATION\n\nIn my inspection of the Orenian Jurisdiction of Johannesburg, I find several breaches in common safety, sanitary, and structural standards, and recommend highly that the city re-evaluate itself to maintain a higher quality\nof life. There are several threats to everyday living within this city – a place where people are expected to live. If it's not the disease spread from unswept animal waste, or the broken glass and debris on the streets and rooftops, it'll be the\nlack of structural safety within the buildings, resulting in entrapment or a nasty fall that could surely kill you.\n\nThis city needs some work; it nearly killed me.\n\nEND OF INSPECTION\n\n-- . -- . -- .\nInspection provided by Mr. Joneal Brandt, free of charge. Further inspections offered for compensation.\n\nFor more information, contact Inspector Brandt directly through bird.\n\nThus concludes this notice.        \n                          -||", ""),
        StaticBook("Orenian Profile", "Balduul Exrith", "*Rune Cannons\n*Horses\n*Cannons\n*soldiers(many)\n*Houses\n*Outposts(Outside Vsenk and Northern Mts.)\n*Dwarves(Allies)\n*Mage Mercenaries\n*Control over Wood Elves\n*45% of Public Op.\n~Known Haters~\n*Warhawkes\n*Orcs\n*Snow Elves\n*Dreadlanders\n*Enchantry(most likely)\n*43% of Oren pop.\n*Undead\n*Possibly Cat-Peoples\n~Weaknesses~\n*Magic\n*Stealth\n*Intelligence\n*Power\n*bombs\n*Quick attacks\n*earthquakes\n*religion\n~Military Bodies~\n*JCP(some left)\n*NOP(current)\n*OM (current army)\n*Houses\n*Families", ""),
        StaticBook("Orichalcum", "Rosso", "__Orichalcum__\n\nNienna’s Foreword: I found this little gem off of a dead spy named Devin Ryder. Yes, he was a bard and a spy, and he had quite a few things in-between. I’m pretty sure he stole this book. Actually, I’m sure of it.\nOrichalcum is a precious metal that is made out of white gold and silver. It can hold powerful and magical energies and is a great material for Magical items such as staves, swords, and magical Tiaras.\nIt is used by mages to store spells so that they can release those at the right moment. When using Orichalcum, be aware of its powerful magical properties. Don’t mess around with it - it can become dangerous at the wrong moments.\n==How to make==\n\n==Orichalcum==\n\n1- Melt the white gold and silver.\n\n2- Let flow energies of white magic into the metal while forcing it together.\n3-Make one metal bar of the combined metals\n\n4- Bend the bar to the shape of the power-rune\n\n5- Power the rune\n\n6- Reshape the rune to the symbol of resistance\n-repeat step 5-\n\n7- Reshape the rune to the symbol of capacity\n\n-repeat step 5-\n\n8- Now create the object you want to make\n9-Bury your Orichalcum at a place where it can absorb energies of nature, such as a forest or grove\n\n10- After 5 days your  metal is ready and you can recover it.\nThe process is complete now, but don’t expect it to go perfectly smooth the first time. This is a process that needs experience.\n\n-Contact Aurea in Haelun’or if you have questions-\nOrichalcum\n\nWritten by Nienna\nCoppied by Rosso\nVaerHaven", ""),
        StaticBook("Orlanden's Vis.", "[Ghost] The Eternal Librarian", "Orlanden's\n   Three Visions\n\n      by Orlanden\nIt all started our first night on Elysium as I was sleeping by a cosy little campfire where the Dwarves had begun mining out their Hold. I have many theories of what might have triggered these visions; it may have been the burning of the Elder Tree in\nAsulon before we left. For the first of the three visions thus far, I found myself seemingly flying through a large, very high canopy, high above the thick forest's floor. There was a bright light directly over what I would think would be the Mother Tree\nof the forest. I was drawn to it, but just before I could reach it, I woke up. This dream, along with the other two I've yet to speak of, I see nearly every night. It's as if they're developing into a story.\nThe second one, which happened on the second night here in Elysium, began with me standing at the tree line of this tall, tall forest. The outline of the forest was made up of very large trees the likes of which I've never seen before. I know not what\nthey are called, but they towered over everything else. As I wandered inward, there was a smaller forest of normal looking oaken trees that greeted me. Through their canopy you could see the canopy of the large trees, barely allowing any light through\nexcept for one opening in the centre. As I walked amongst these giants I saw flora that is completely foreign to Asulon and even Aegis. There were streams that ran throughout the forest, crystal clear spring water, perhaps runoff from a nearby mountain.\nIt was a sight so many will wish to behold, I am sure of that.\nThe third dream began, sure enough, on the third night. In this one I found myself in an enclosed space, but to my rear was a triangular opening with bright, natural light shining through. In front of my seemed to be what I can only think of as a\npillar or beacon. It was removable, so me with my curious nature, removed it from its resting place. It felt so... wrong. So wrong that I had removed it, the feelings it gave me were dark and grim. Immediately I replaced it, and just as quickly the\nfeelings of warmth and love rushed back to me. As I let go of the pillar and stepped back, I awoke, concluding the third vision. It must mean something.", ""),
        StaticBook("Orvarian Guard", "Morvan Bloodborne", "*The text below is written in a bold and clean form, it's lettering written in charcoal.*\n\n\n       The March of the   \n         Orvarian Guard\n\n*There appears to be no signature below, the song remaining authorless.*\nThe sun rose over the wasteland\n\nAs far as the eye can see\n \nSand fills the vast plains of Eruthos\n\nIt's vultures jeering at me\n\nBut they can circle until they drop dead\nI have not come this far\n\nTo end, but to pursue my own thread\n\nTo join The Orvarian Guard\n\nGuards of glory and of might\nRed as blood and black as night\nFlies our banner as we march\nIn the North, for the king of the Rovin\n\nThere's men of the cross and Creator\n\nA few of the Elvish moon\n\nMen simply searching for glamour\n\nSome concealing their royal descent\nThe axe-bearing foreigners they have aptly named us\n\nAll we've come from afar\n\nDiversity is what unites us\n\nWe are The Orvarian Guard\nGuards of glory and of might\nRed as blood and black as night\nFlies our banner as we march\nIn the North, for the king of the Rovin\n\nTo Northhaven and beyond\n\nThis is where the winds have us guided\nFor fame and for gold\n\nWe once set sails for these lands unknown\n\nGuards of glory and of might\nRed as blood and black as night\nFlies our banner as we march\nIn the North, for the king of the Rovin\n*On the page sits a drawing of a large shield, coloured gold, orange, and green. At its front it has a design of interlocking celtic links.*\n\n\n       Sigil of Clan Orvar\n       \"Fly High, Fly Far\"\n\n   May the Gorundyr live\n    long lives. For Glory!", ""),
        StaticBook("Our Night Sky", "Arabella Rosalie Delevoye", "As my eyes look upon the stars, a breath of air escaped my lungs.\n\nThe beauty of the constellations, the darkness of the night sky.\n\nOh how it reminded me of us, our love, our dance of life.\n\nPerhaps it was up there, our story, in the stars.\nThe times we laughed, the times we cried, the times we fought and sought comfort.\n\nIt was all there, right in front of my eyes there was our story, a world of others unknown.\n\nAs i look upon the stars, a breath of air filled my lungs.", ""),
        StaticBook("Our Purity", "Iaria Elervathar", "The Prominence\n         Of Purity\n\nA special thanks to:\n\nMy maln and haelun,\n\nIatrilemar and Ariana\nElervathar\n\nMy tutors and lliran,\n\nAcaele Lazul, Lelien Synalli & Nyna Noroval\nIntroduction:\n\nKarin’ayla everyone. Although you are probably moreso interested in the topic regarding purity, I cannot let you escape this brief introduction.  My name is Iaria Elervathar, malii’lari ito Iatrilemar eyha Ariana Elervathar.\nI was both raised and lectured in The Silver City of Axios, eager to learn more about our desire for purity and the maehr’sae hiylun’ehya. Albeit I have yet much to learn, I consider myself quite adept in the ways of our culture.\nSpecifically regarding our most prized possession, our purity. I wish to lecture you further upon the matter, or merely give more knowledge for you to enjoy.\nChapter 1:\n§PPurity\n\nPurity comes in many different ways. You have physical purity, but also mental purity. Both are priced possessions that us, the Mali’thill, would not want to trade for anything in the world\nOur purity is defined by how closely we follow the maehr'sae hiylun'ehya, an ancient phrase that the Mali’thill have carried for centuries from the old books originally left in the College of Haelun’or.\nIt roughly translates to \"The pursuit of wisdom and health\". \n\nNow let me explain to you, dearest reader, what mental and physical purity actually means..\nPhysical Purity:\nThis is a matter regarding your lineage and appearance. We cannot quite take you seriously if you’re a mixed breed.  Your maln and haelun had the (odd) idea of pursuing a romance.\nThis iniative spits onto the work that us, the Mali’thill, have protected and worked on for centuries.\nMental Purity:\nThis involves moreso your determination to the maehr’sae hiylun’ehya. You may look pure and come from a Mali’thill lineage, yet that does not necessarily mean that you’re the face of purity. It’s about your personal demeanour.\nIf anything of the maehr’sae hiylun’ehya is violated by you, we consider you as mentally impure.\nChapter 2:\nMaehr'sae Hiylun'ehya\n\nNow that I’ve explained the matter of purity to you, dear reader, I must certainly inform you about the maehr’sae hiylun’ehya I’ve been writing about.\nAs I’ve mentioned before, this ancient phrase in the Elven tongue is roughly translated to \"Wisdom and health\". Wisdom, and health. Both factors we value dearly. Let me thoroughly explain to you these two factors...\nMaehr'sae\n(Progress/Wisdom)\n\nThis refers to our expanded development of our knowledge and wisdom that we gain throughout our years in life.\nThe life of a Mali’thill must be commonly filled with the eager to learn and gain more knowledge and wisdom. This revolves around the topics of science, arts or magic.\nHiylun\n(Health)\n\nThis regards our purity, both physically and mentally. It is important for us to hold dignity in our lineage and physical appearance, as we are blessed with this glorious race that stands above all.\nChapter 3:\nPurity, why is it so important?\n\nAs my last chapter, I’d like to explain why we value the maehr’sae hiylun’ehya and our purity so much. That our life can be determined from these two factors may seem absurd to you.\nWe are proud of what we are. Yes- again, absurd to you perhaps. We do not wish to taint this work we’ve been providing for over centuries now. We presumably have more knowledge than any other race existant.\nWhy? - I hear you think. - It’s due to our years of experience and the information we are granted from our unique Eternal library. \n\nAlbeit sadly, not everyone has access to this blessed library. Sorry to disappoint you with this news.", ""),
        StaticBook("Outposts", "Ser Berengar Helvets", "The goal of this journal is to catelog the scouting trip of the Westerlandic outposts.  Three such outposts exist, one at the crossroads of the northern pass with the main road, another at the fork of Bastions road with the main road, and the final\nat Mordrings Bridge.\n\nX: -1198, Y: 93, Z: -1757.\n\nNorth-Eastern Outpost:  \nUsed as a garrison by the fallen Kingdom of the Westerlands, it was the sight of multiple battles in the war against Mordring.\nIt is seperated into two, small parts, guarding each side of the road.  It acheived fame for Westerlandic folk for a portal that opened underneath the outpost, which was destroyed after severe losses, following a major horde attack occuring simultaneously\nThe second camp is located at\nX: -1378, Y: 98, Z: -1529.\n\nCentral Outpost:\nLocated at the fork of Bastion Road with the main Westerlandic road, Central outpost was used as a staging point for scouts in the fallen Westerlands.\nSoldiers and scouts would use the outpost to restock, rearm, and ship out to hot-spots in the war, or patrol zones based on the need.  The outpost has been re-fortified since HalStaigs formation, and would be very valuable in consolidating the West.\nThe third camp is located at\nX: -1482, Y: 107, Z: -1203.\n\nSouthern Outpost:\nLocated at the eastern end of Mordrings Bridge, the Southern outpost was one of the most contested zones in the war.\nNo less than five major battles occurred at Mordrings bridge, turning the once fine keep into a ruin of stone and wood.  Plans were made in the past to fortify the position, but were rebuffed by concentrated undead resistance.\nThe Southern outpost is the furthest outpost from Halstaig, but it's strategic position cannot be denied, it can solidify both the southern flank of the Westerlands, making the bridges from the south and west impassable to enemies.\nConclusion:  The outposts of the Westerlands are of paramount concern, if they are not garrisoned outright, they should be at least re-fortified, and re-constituted into the patrol routes of all Westerlandic folk in the future.", ""),
        StaticBook("P. Revolution", "daelaris", "A History of the Phoenix Revolution based on several personal accounts by witnesses.\n\nAt the time, the stability of Oren was considered dubious at best. With the death of King Pampo Perea, his seneschal, -\n- Edmund Sheffield took to the throne. His rule rule was highly opposed by many, which only aided to feed the flames that let to the revolution. The basis of this uprising began in the minds of two men, Eze'kiel Tarus and Zibaen Vivyaen.\nThroughout the reign of Edmund, they only seemed to gain power and support as Undead attacks became more frequent, and in the end, even the king succumbed. Taken by corruption, he killed his wife and dissapeared leaving his son, Enor, to take the throne.\nEnor's reign was marred with troubles, and the fall of Al'kHazar in 1338 served only to sent the realm into a downward spiral of chaos. Enor was kidnapped and held in the Nether for nearly a year whilst the diaspora of-\n- humanity attempted to pick themselves back up and start anew.  When Enor returned, many thought him to be corrupted as his father, and so the Phoenix Revolution was born.\nThe uprising managed to quickly attract hundreds of supporters, many of which were high-ranking officials in the Kingdom of Oren. Propaganda and occassional skirmishes marked the height of the revolution. Some weeks later, -\n- King Enor caught wind of the rebellion and abdicated to Gaius Marius, Hochmeister of the Teutonic Order.\nWhat was decided there would shape the fate of Oren, The Teutons and Marius were to be granted the northern lands of Hanseti, from which he would rule in Konigsberg, and Eze'kiel granted Galahar and the lands surrounding it.\nThe Kingdoms of Hanseti and Renatus were born, and so the great human nation was split for the first time in it's history.\nThe aftermath of this travesty was the gradual fall of what remained of civilization in Aegis as the undead continued to flood south. Even in Asulon, the nations of Hanseti and Renatus remained on uncertain grounds, -\nviewing eachother with great distrust and hatred. Only during the time of Godfrey I would the two kingdoms ever be united once again.", ""),
        StaticBook("Path of Mina", "'Kommid'", "Here in my new cave, just bought this new mule here. It’s fun to ride up here in the orinian hills. But you know what I like more than materialistic things? Knowledge. In fact, I’m a lotmore proud of these seven new bookshelves that I had to get installed\nto hold fourteen new books that I stole. It’s like the billionaire Shrek’lak says, “the more lat learn, the more yub earn.” Now maybe you’ve seen my Bladex talk where I talk about how I read a book a day. You know, I read a book a day not to show off it’s\nagain about the knowledge. In fact, the real reason I keep this Mule here is that it’s a reminder. A reminder that dreams are still possible, because it wasn’t that long ago that I was in a little Cart across the country sleeping on a un-tanned leather\nbed in a mobile cart home with only forty seven mina in my bank account. I didn’t have any friends as my parents were killed by orcs But you know what? Something happened that changed my life. I bumped into a mentor. And another mentor.\nAnd a few more mentors. I found five mentors. And they showed me what they did to become Bandits. Again, it’s not just about Mina, it’s about the good life; health, wealth, love and happiness. And so I bandited a few oreners, it’s actually on my\nwanted poster, There is a copy of it on the back of this book and you can look at my three best crimes. Three things that you can do today no matter where you are.Now, this isn’t a “get rich quick” scheme. You know, like they say if things sound too good\nto be true they are too good to be true. I’m not promising you that tomorrow you’re gonna be able to go out and buy a Mule. But what I am telling you is that it can happen faster than you think if you know the proven steps. So, I\nbandited two little bandit’s and wrote another book as a guide. Like I said, now it’s not the most professional I just shot them here with my crossbow, but it’s real. Nobody can argue, this is my true story. And I’m going to giveyou the three\nmost important things you can do today. So look at the poster, go there it’s completely free to look at it it’s just a couple words. Invest in yourself. Always be curious. Don’t be a cynic. Okay, people see posters like this and they say\n“Ah that’s not real that’s for somebody else.”\nDon’t listen, don’t listen. Be an optimist. Like, Uldar Irongut, the Dwarf who started the 18 year wars,\nhe said that he was only fifteen years old when he read a book by Helen Keller, and that book changed his life. Books can change your life. And in that book, Helen Keller said “optimism” so if you’re a cynic, if you’re a pessimist\nyou don’t need to read this. Don’t worry about it, I don’t need to talk to everybody. But if you’re somebody who knows that there’s something better, cause the dream is possible, you know, for some of you watching it’s not necessarily a Mule,\n, maybe it’s a new job, a new opportunity, starting your own Nation.\nMaybe it’s a new lifestyle without so much stress, traveling Axios, doing those things you know you’re destined to do. You can do those unless you understand finances. mina,\nI don’t call it mina anymore, I call it Oil Money. You must have enough Oil Money to live out your dream and to live out your destiny. So, I’ll see you as i ride by in my mule, it’s a quick story and you’ll see there absolutely free.", ""),
        StaticBook("Penance", "Freya", "Penance\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nFreya\nIn the far away, Verdantly swathed lands of Alamere, there was once a Knight. The Stories say he was honourable, brave, and a stalwart companion. But Stories only tell you the truth the writer believes...\nSo, Intrepid Readers, here is a full truth, not a paled half-truth or thinly veiled lie.  The Knight’s name was Kramble Albermott. He was a vile man, a hero only in his own heart, which itself was black from corruption and indulgence.\nHe hurt everyone around him, whether meaning to or not. Everywhere he treads, misery and pestilence would follow in his shadow.  But do not think this man deserves your pity. He deserves his Penance.\nThis is why.  One day in the Kingdom of Alamere, a great shadow covered the land.  But it was a proudly displayed shadow, by a enemy which was willing to fight fairly. Not a selfish backstabbing deviant like Kramble.\nThe King called for Kramble, the much-despised Commander of the Royal Armies, to gather an Army capable of stopping the Evil Threat.  So Kramble, who very much liked the deadly sin of Sloth, decided he would do as the King asked.  He would gather an Army.\nBut this Army would not be composed of Honourable Knights and Devout Followers. This would be a Army of Scoundrels, Beggars, Mercenaries and Thieves. For he has access to the King's Coffers, and what he did not use for his own selfish deviances,\nhe used to bribe and buy as many soldiers as possible.  Finally, Kramble had assembled the Army, and marched upon the fields of Amok'shan, where generations of courageous men had fought and bled for Alamere. He cared not for the Desecration\nhe was about to commit. He only thought of how richly the King would reward him for his imminent victory.  Two Armies stood to attention, facing each other. One composed of Proud Undead and Evil-doers. The other a motley band of the scum of the Kingdom.\nThe Undead Overlord stood, upon his ebon throne.  He laughed.  \"Is this the BEST the King of this proud Kingdom can send against me?\" \"You DO NOT DESERVE to be killed by my followers!\"  He laughed again. Kramble's army collectively shuddered,\nthe idea of all the gold they could carry shaken from their minds - replaced with only one thing - primal fear of Death. The army turned tail, and ran for their lives.  The Overlord, stood from his throne. He held up a hand, and the world seemed to stop.\nKramble stood, suddenly, without seeming to have moved, a sword-length from the Overlord.  The Two men stood facing each other, so alike, yet also so very different.  Finally, the Overlord spoke.  \"Now, Kramble.\"  \"I am a fair man,\ndespite my heinous intentions.\"  \"I shall give you a chance, one which you do not deserve.\"  \"A Quick Death.\"  Kramble stood, petrified, with a look of despair on his face.  He tried to move, but he seemed to be rooted in place by a immovable force.\nHe cried out in fear and anguish, as the Overlord raised his sword high above his Head. The sword came down, reflecting the last rays of the day's sunlight.  As the sword fell, Kramble did something he had never done, or even thought of doing before.\nHe Prayed. Not to a God, or a Idol. But to Death himself.  \"Spare me\"  He heard his heart hammering in his ears. One beat.  Then Another. And another after that.  He took a breath, the air entering his starved lungs.\nThen, he looked up.  The Overlord stood above him, outlined with the Scarlet rays of the dieing sun. His hand was outstretched. Then, he spoke.  \"I offer you a Quick Death.\"  \"To all those who oppose us.\"\n\"Join me, Brother. Join me, and crush all who oppose us.\"  \"You Prayed to my Master, and he has Answered!\"  Kramble took the Overlords hand, and hauled himself to his feet.  The Overlord pointed at the fleeing Army, and intoned;\n\"It is time to finish what you started, Brother.\"  The two men, stood upon the shattered hill, and raised their swords, which glistened as if wet with blood, although Kramble's blade was now clean.  Quietly, the Overlord whispered to himself;\n\"Two men, so different, yet so alike. We will be worthy of our Master now, for sure.\"  The two brothers charged, towards the roaring slaughter of the unclean evil.", ""),
        StaticBook("Peppermint", "Gwiwen Ahverren", "Peppermint, and how to use it\n\n Peppermint, for many ages, has been used in food and drink for it's flavor and for the benefits that come from consuming it. This marvellous herb can assist with colds, coughs, inflamation, nausea, and morning sickness to\nname a few.\n\n However, a disappointing fact is that this plant has, by some strange circumstance, been relegated to be used singularly for it's taste in sweets and tea.\n\n Through this, I hope to help cast aside\nsuch ignorance and give you, the reader, some knowledge on how to properly use this marvellous plant.\n\n Chapter 1, Peppermint and it's properties.\n\n Peppermint is a miracle-herb, to be certain. It can single-handedly help fend off the worst\nparts of the dreaded common cold through the sinus-clearing and deflammatory properties it innately holds.\n\n It can assist with a harshness of the throat, the inflamation of the mouth (if one has eaten something suspect), unsettled bowels, and something\nthat I find remarkable, morning sickness.\n\n All these effects are often gained through consumption of the leaves or something that has it as an ingredient.\n\n Tea, of course, is an obvious way to help recieve these effects\nalthough to varying degrees.\n\n So, here is a guide on how to make peppermint oil (which is in my experience, the easiest way to help with any of the issues I've mentioned).\n\n Chapter 2, Oil and You\nOil is /not/ necessarily something flamable. It is simply a substance that lies on the top of water, and can be consumable.\n\n As such, this is a step-by-step guide on how to make consumable peppermint oil.\nIngredients required:\n -A jar, sealable and unsealable.\n -Water.\n -Enough peppermint to fill said jar.\n -Olive oil.\n\n -Step 1, gather enough peppermint to fit into a small jar of which you can seal. Run the herbs under water until clean,\nand then chop the peppermint. The smaller the pieces, easier it'll dry. Leave the peppermint out on a plate, in the sun, so it may dry.\n -Step 3, once the peppermint is dry, move the herb into the jar. When this is done, pour olive oil until it covers\nthe herbs. With this done, leave for one month.\n -Step 4, after the month has passed, strain the peppermint leaves from the oil, and toss the leaves out. Taking the oil, put it into a jar, or into vials to be used at your digression.\nChapter 3, Tea\n\n Peppermint tea is another, faster way of getting the same effects as you would've gotten from the oil, although diluted.\n\n Simply have a tea kettle, water, and some peppermint leaves.\nPut leaves in the tea kettle, pour in the water, and heat up. After what SHOULD be thirty minutes, the tea will be done. Drink however you'd like--though, I would suggest honey.\n\n Chapter 4, Peppermint in Food\nNow, food.\n Peppermint is widely known for it's use in sweets for it's flavor, however--it can be used just as well in soups or stews (and to varying degrees, bread).\n\n For one, I love to add peppermint into stew or soups, to give it that extra flavor\nalthough, that could just be me.\n\n Regardless, peppermint is a magnificent plant, and deserves our respect.\nWritten by Gwiwen Ahverren", ""),
        StaticBook("Personal menu", "Dras Lowsen", "Snacks:\nBaguettes- 1 mina\nCaramel cookie- 2 mina\nMaple Pancake- 2 mina\nTriple chocolate cookie- 3 mina\nLunch/Dinner:\nFish sticks- 4 mina\nGrilled fish- 7 mina\nLemon Fish steaks- 8 mina\nBeetroot stew- 9 mina\nSailor’s delight-10 mina\nMeatloaf- 10 mina\nDessert:\nPumpkin pie- 10 mina\nChoco pie- 16 mina\nChocolate cake- 24 mina\nCream pie- 15 mina\nMelon pie- 10 mina", ""),
        StaticBook("Phere Oath's", "Phantom", "The Phantom's Oath \n\nThe dark is my cloak, The shadows are my blade, When light is gone and silence is taken over, The difilers cease to exist,\nThe Black Oath\n\nWhen dark is right, and black as night, we find the light, and blacken the sight.\nThe Gray Oath\n\nWhen Dawn breaks, or light comes, we save thee weak, and destroy the unworthy\nThe red oath\n\nVan vul ag ar,", ""),
        StaticBook("Philip IronS T.", "Ol' Man Sano", "Dear Philip,\n\nYou may not remember me personally, as you and I have only met on a few very restricted occassions. However, as you may be aware, I was one of your father's closest colleagues.\nAs an ally back in the days of the Johannesburg Crown Police, he and I shared many memorable battles together. Under the assumption that you are to follow in his footsteps, I'd like for you to accept-\nthis golden sword, glistening with the aurum it's smelted with, as well as this necklace that I've kept close to me. Take care, and may the Ironswords prosper.", ""),
        StaticBook("Philosophorum", "Lanavia Zytiaear", "An Introduction to the\nPhilosophorum Society\n------------------------------\n\nThe information provided within these pages are to simply help you understand what the Society is and what exactly we stand for.\n\nIf you still have questions contanct\nSarrion (Toxzero), Elric (Jacey) or Lanavia (Creete).\n\n\nEnjoy~\n\n-\nLanavia\nWhat is the Society? \n\nThis has to be the most asked question we get here in the Society - at the same time it is the easiest to answer.\n\nThe Society is more a community than a guild.\nWe are a gathering of like-minded individuals that have a thirst for knowledge.\nIt is this thirst for knowledge that has pulled us all together and has led to the creation of the Society, and is the thing that still keeps us together.\nAre there any fees?\n\nNo. We have never charged new members any type of mina fee to join our ranks.\n\nThe only thing we ask is that if you stumble upon a book we might be interested in that you would donate it to the Society.\nWhat does it mean to be a member of the Society?\n\nThis one is also easy to answer. To be a member of the Society simply means you are a part of something more – you are trying to better yourself and the world around you.\nYou are not wasting the most precious thing you own: your mind.\n\nBeing a member of the Society means you are searching to answer the unknown and learn from others who have already started their personal quests to do just that.\nWhat’s with the jackets?\n\nThis is one thing we share with a lot of guilds or schools, we have a matching uniform of sorts. The navy colored jackets are a symbol of your ties to the Society – and thus your eagerness to learn and spread knowledge.\nA fact about the jackets that you need to know is that the colored trimmings do mean something. A student with gold trims on his jacket with a student of magic, whereas a student with a jacket that has a silver trim is a student of science.\nMany students study both science and magic – the jacket they decide to wear is up to them but should be trimmed with the colors associated with whichever of the two they focus more heavily on.\n\nThe best way to know what a student studies is to ask them.\nWhat is the purpose of the Society?\n\n\nThe Society’s purpose is simple. We are here to gather, document, and share knowledge – that is it.\nDo you need to be an Elf to be a member?\n\nNo. We do not care what race you are, so long as you are like-minded you are welcome here.\nThis is the basis of the Society put into the simplest terms I could. If you have any other questions about it feel free to ask any member you see – if they can’t answer your questions they can point you in the right direction. \n\nBe well~!", ""),
        StaticBook("Pigmen History", "Sunshine Druid Verden", "A Brief History of Pigmen: Aegis – Kalos\nBy Sunshine Druid Verden\nThe appearance of Zombie Pigmen was first documented during the Second Iblees Invasion, several hundred years ago. These unnatural monsters were used by the Fallen Daemon as powerful soldiers during his war of conquest against the mortal races of Aegis,\nwhere their group mentality and shear ferocity was crippling to the defenders. Unlike other lesser Undead, the Zombie Pigmen possessed an intellect far superior to any common Zombie or Skeleton. They would always be seen in possession of jagged, golden\nswords and very rarely were encountered alone.\n\nTheir speed was almost on par with that of the living, a trait that allowed few the luxury of escaping. After the invasion was ended and the Dark One had been sealed away for good, many strange things were\nobserved by the population of Aegis. While the mindless Zombies and Skeletons continued to attack anyone on sight, the Pigmen did not. They had become passive, almost completely indifferent to the world around them.\n\nInstead of mindlessly killing, they\nbegan to aimlessly roam the world, staring blindly at the things around them as if they weren’t truly there. After Aegis had crumbled and sank into the sea, many thought they would never see the creatures again. And, indeed, they didn’t. For a time. But,\nagain, the Pigmen emerged from the unknown, and they were furious. For many years the Pigmen were found roaming the darkest corners of Asulon and attached anyone foolish enough to get close. The reason for this is not clear, and many theories have arisen\nto explain. However none have been proven. Yet another strange event was observed on the island of Elysium.\n\nA large volcano near the temporary Elven settlement erupted and spewed lava over the Malinor farms; and the Pigmen rode it down the slope. They\nwere, thankfully, peaceful this time; but they appeared in numbers never seen before. Hundreds of them began to blindly wander from their lair, spilling over the border into the Orcish deserts. They were destroyed not by men, nor by beast, but by cacti.\nThe creatures tore themselves to shreds over the next few months as they walked through the cacti farms, and they would still if it wasn’t for the piles of their dead brethren impeding their movement.\n\nSince arriving in Anthos there has only been one\nreported case of Pigmen. This was a very small issue, where only three or four Pigmen would wander around a border wall in the Wilds. A logical fountain was placed at this site, and all has been quiet since then.\n\nIf the Pigmen are here on Anthos, they\nare hiding very well.", ""),
        StaticBook("Play Orc", "BuubHozh Hefner", "PlayOrc\n\n\n*The cover page features a caricature of a bunny with rows and rows of teeth*\nZlutz Uv De Munth\n\n*The following ten pages feature women with disfiguring scars in extremely high quality armor.*\nPruper Tuzk Care\n\n*Listed here is a long and suprisingly informed article about polishing tusks to shine. According to the article, \"Bitchez Luv Shinee Tuzkz\" *\nBuubHozh Hefner\n\n*This article, accompanied by a drawing of an old uruk wrestling two female uruk and a Lur Wolf at once, depicts the life of a fictitious Uruk mating tychoon named BuubHozh Hefner.*\nMojo ztrength, Real ur Fayke?\n\n*Depected in a picture for the article is a battle-scarred, armored elven woman lifting an entire boulder above her head.*\n*The rest of the article is about telekinetics.*\nDe Bear Flattin\n     Ztandurd\n*Below is a drawing of a scarred, scantily clad orc woman snapping a bear's neck with her bare hands. It folds out into 4 pages.*\n\"If Zhe can nub flat a bear wid hur bare handz, zhe iz nub Hozh Mayte!\"\nFlat - Ztickz\n      Agh Lat!\n*The featured weapon this issue seems to be the famous White Rose Arbelest, accompanied by a picture of a scarred human woman firing it.*\n*To one side of it is a column comparing serrated and normal battleaxes.*\nLettur Frum De           Zlutz\n *There's a long (and likely fictional) letter below from a (presumably) female author about how she cant stand an uruk who doesn't smell like the blood of their enemies.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Playin with Mana", "Regale Ba'ikana", "Obtain a Manablade", ""),
