        StaticBook("Pnty jw Aegxs", "Aevalyn", "Pnty jw Aegxs\n\n       Haelun'or,\n          Axios\n\n    Published 1593\n\n   \n  by Unknown Author\n    Transcribed by\n   Aevalyn Bethiros\nHad we not foretold how man would war, for clearings and meadows were few and far. It was pleaded with amnesty to the Wizard wizened, he greeted us at the portal of lands also risened.\nFor we could not bear the burden of our dead, as man fought with greed for their own homestead.\nThe Wizard spaketh with us that we are of mercy, with open palm outstretched to the new land, he said 'search these'.\nFor what we would find suitable of land, we found continents laid out and grand. The Five Families separated and pledged no war, and so we spilled no blood nor gore.\nAnd thus we began our journey, one of Pnty jw Aegxs.", ""),
        StaticBook("Poem for Taynuel", "Zelak", "I can't rhyme.", ""),
        StaticBook("Poem Long Lived.", "Amras Yavelty", "Poem of the Long Lived\nBy Amras Yavelty\nPassing like water swiftly down the river\nWithout trace\nWithout shiver\nThe soil grows thin\nThe lights go dim\nMountains are born\nNew flowers adorn\nYet you must know\nLong ears hear them\nHear them at birth\nHear them at death\nHear all in sorrow\nHear all in joy\nHear them in pain\nTime is just a toy\nLet the human’s grief\nOrcs play in the sand\nDwarves get rich\nLet’s hear them be\nHear them at war\nHear them at peace\nHear them be young\nHear them get old\nLet them have beards\nLet them feel\nHow time passes by\nYet not for long ears", ""),
        StaticBook("Poem to Kalenz", "Ikur Seregon", "*A letter is delivered, sealed with wax.*\nDearest Kalenz Uradir,\nI do think it is time to tell you that you are dear\n\nCertain am I of your purity,\n\nYet of your love for me, there is an insecurity\nWe could progess as fortold in the maehr'sae hiylun'ehya\n\nEnding at a butterfly, and beginning as gastraea.\n\nI do hope your love will be reciprocated\nYour response is anticipated\n\n\n(Do so by planting a poppy in front of the entrance of the clinic)", ""),
        StaticBook("Poems", "The Donkey Man", "A Collection of Poems\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nby the donkey\nSunshine\n\n\nFlowery birth\nRebirth of sunshine\nRise above the mountaintops\nThe night is not fine\nCruel darkness fails\nSuccumbed to good like wine\nHorses neigh and donkeys bray\nWith sunshine rebirth\nLove\n\n\nRestricted with chain\nBleeding with pain\nBroken heart\nA failed start\nA love without hope\nMen sit around to mope\nLove is but a joke\nAnd marriage a cruel elope\nSodomy\n\n\nBanished love\nBanished hearts\nFailure lips\nFailure minds\nLaw-alienated\nNever reinstated\nExecution\nLynching\nAnd love\nBuilt to die\nDye\n\n\nDye the world\nThe sky is blue\nThe earth is green\nThe hearts are red\nThe world is colored\nThe ocean is blue\nThe dirt is brown\nThe tears are colorless\nDonkey\n\n\nA donkey understands\nAn outcast\nLabeled an ass\nCalled a fool\nA donkey understands\nWorking for others\nA slave to his master\nA heart and mind like ours\nA donkey understands\nFlowers\n\n\nAre flowers happy?\nPretty in all shades\nPretty in spring and in fall\nBut they are not always happy\nSome lay at churches\nAnd we think of flowers at weddings\nBut they lie more at graves\nCrazy\n\n\nCrazy\nAre we all crazy?\nAre you crazy?\nAm I crazy?\nAre bad people crazy?\nAre good people crazy?\nOr is crazy what we just call those\nWhom aren't lazy?\nBook\n\n\nWhen I was six\nMy father said he'd teach me to read\nWhen I was seven\nHe said it again\nWhen I was eight\nHe repeated his claim\nWhen I was nine\nIt was off with his head", ""),
        StaticBook("Poems by Arahael", "Aevalyn", "A Collection of Poems\n  by Arahael Eloem\n\n       Haelun'or,\n          Axios\n\n    Published 1592\n\n   by Arahael Eloem\n    Transcribed by\n   Aevalyn Bethiros\nA New Day\n\nThe warmth is returning,\nAs the sky blushed and flushed.\nThe evil are smoldering,\nReceiving the justice of good.\nThe flowers are swaying,\nAs the branches wave at me.\nPearls of moisture stuck to petals,\nAs they bloom of renewal.\nThe wind crisp and clean,\nWith an air of importance.\nI swept the scene with a single gaze,\nIt was a new day.\nNight\n\nThe moon shines\nThe stars twinkle\nSilence fills the night.\n\nIts dark\nIts mysterious\nMy fingers tingle with sensations\nEach step is suspense\nEach step is anticipation\nThe night never satisfies of my wonders\nThe night, the mask of secrets\nThe night, the cover for horrors\nThe night, the guise for the treacherous\n\nFull of suspicion\nFull of wariness\nFull of dangers\nYet the pull\nThe tug\nThe urge to see the night\nThe urge to uncover the mask\nThe urge to know the night\n\nIt is the beauty of the night.\nMaln\n\nThe eyes\nThe twinkling eyes\nEver so serious\nYet ever so humorous\nThe pools of blue\nAs if it contained the ocean\nThe ever so sincere eye\nLooked through my heart\nIt stared with its endless depths\nThe golden hair\nShining under the light\nLustrous and wavy\nSashaying as if they had a life of his own\nThose pair of hands\nSmooth yet worn at the same time\nFluent with a sword\nYet as delicate and precise with experiments and books\nAlways covering mine\nSo small compared to yours\nI shall never forget\nYour ever welcome presence\nThat tinkling laugh of yours\nAlways overprotective concern\nThat charming smile\nThat luring overwhelming heat\nThe smell of you\nWith a tinge of musty books\nThe metallic scent if metal\nSmokiness from an unsuccessful experiment\nThe sweetness of the flowers from haelun\nYou are forever\nMy maln", ""),
        StaticBook("Pointless Poem", "Leki Song", "Roses are Red\n\nViolets are blue\n\nIm gonna jump to say Huruu", ""),
