        StaticBook("Portal Encounter", "Ol' Man Sano", "12th of Sun's Smile, 1613\n\nBell Sano\n\nInvestigative notes\n\n\"Portal\"\n\n---\nFirst Entry:\n\nAlexandra Bradshawe, Awylan Wistari, and myself, had all agreed to set off on a scientific adventure, in search of some mystical discoveries, and later publish our findings.\nWe decided to head off to the Krugmar, home of the Uruk, to view their remarkable geography and landscape. Upon arrival, we met a group of rather friendly Uruk, and a Wood Elf, who pointed us in the direction -\nof a cave -- not in Krugmar, no, but in the Dominion of Malin, the lands of the Wood Elves. The trio led us to some cave, then warned us that it was a broken portal, no longer functional. We thanked them for the discovery, and as of now, we are -\nstanding at the enterance of the cavern. The wood elf just told us that, \"The password is apple.\" We know not what he meant, but they have all departed as of now, and we prepare to enter the cave.\nSecond Entry:\n\nWe're now exploring the cavern. There appears to be a series of organized stairs leading into the cavern, covered in overgrown vines and such.\nAt the foot of the staircase, an open door remains, leading to a tiny, bright room, filled with gold and bookshelves. There's an odd device, but we can't seem to do anything with it.\nOn the other side of the cavern lays a rose plant encased in some translucent container. We've no idea how or why it's here. Upon further investigation, there seems to be tombs resting behind the flower, three to be precise.\nAfter standing in the room for a while, the three of us hear some odd whispering. Wistari has gone up to investigate. I will record more notes within the next hour.\nEntry Three:\n\nSo as Wistari went up onto the surface, he found a sword, some pebbles, and sharpened stones. He picked up the sword, and the pebbls began to levitate. Thus, he swung the sword, and the pebbles combusted.\nAs the pebbles flew everywhere, some ghost, some apparation appeared before us. Wistari's initial response was to swing the sword towards the beast, where it then phased through it's body.\nThe spectre, in response, phased inside of Wistari's body, and it's bones fell to the ground. Wistari's veins in his hands around the sword instantly turned black, and he let out a scrill shreak of pain.\nHis eyes turned green, and he began to mutter, \"Reset the clock,\" in a voice which was not his. After some time, he appeared to return to normal, but then stabbed himself in the throat with the blade. Alexandra then went-\nto retrive the blade, where the same process overtook her -- however, she was not overcome with a painful experience, but rather, the entity lead her over to a nearby pillar surrounded by skulls. We then found a pocket watch on the ground.\nThe watch was cracked, and we could now hear intense, incoherant whispers. Alexandra reset the clock to twelve-o'clock, and all of a sudden, everything stopped. No more whispers, no more posession.\nThe blade was no longer tainted, but Wistari was still bleeding, and had a cut in his throat. We lugged him to the nearest town, where the citizens fixed him up, and a cleric cleared him of any dark energy.\nWe retrieved four pebbles, the sword itself, and the bones from the beast. An odd encounter, but valuable experience none the less. I shall be reporting back to the library, and informing the Dominion's authorities of this cavern.", ""),
        StaticBook("Potion count", "Dean Osborn", "List of Potions given to the Mournstones per contract-\nGreater flame spitter- 5 \nBoggy concoction- 5\nPotions of Alabaster's leaf- 2\nLarhiel's fingers- 3", ""),
        StaticBook("Pounce", "Balor", "Pounce-Main Gate\nOak logs form the walls with no guard towers seems very crude mainly its only purpose to keep out undead witch seem to plague the land outside the gate, the gate is rather low its tallest point being around 8 metres and its lowest is 4\nFirst View on Entry\nThere is a table set up nearly as a public bench with decorations set up along it. 3 houses line the path one being much larger and most likely forms a suito lookout to see past the walls. This is also where the carragie in arrives.\nThe Bear and Rat\nThis is the local in, ver narror building going much up wards more then side ways\nThere are 8 seats in total in the public area and the cooking station is out for anyone to use. Behind the bar are chest that contain the drinks\nDaeland and King's Road Crossing\nThere is another public bench and a sign post to direct people. The wall has also faded not appear on the other side of a house\nRoad to Scared Building\nThere 5 house all only having one floor. The bank and Autions are also here, along with a donations chest\nThe Chapel of St. Everard\nPossible the second largest building in the town with a two metre wide door and two tourchs\nInside there are 3 chest and bookshelfs and alter and 10 seats. There is also a guardain to the right\nFortress entrance\nSmall gate with no way to close only to bottle neck an enimy through one spot, it is two metres wide\nInside the fortress outer walls there are large house lightly nobles or friends of rulers and a small breeding pen\nThe Fortress itself is large and is most deffinitly the tallest building decorated in the Green and Yellow which are Pounces' colours\nPeople of note\nRaibert- Blacksmith\nLukas Eselach- commener\nClinton Northbroeks-Commener\nBraehn Elendil-Commener\nOther Notes\n\nColours\nYelllow and Green\nPeople\nWear a cloth over there self as there main clothing or uniform\nLand around Pounce is plague with undead which could be used as a deffense\nConclusion\nPounce is a simple and peaceful town.\nThey fouce less on deffense and more on there own lifes\nThey do have an army but its small and if it were attack I feel Pounce would loss due to its lack luster walls and easily burned homes", ""),
        StaticBook("Progress-Health", "Athedil Haler'thilln", "----------------Maehr’sae Hiylun’ehya\n----------------Chapter 2\nAs interpreted by Lucion Sullas, former Okarir, Tilruir, Sohaer, and Maheral of Haelun’or.\nTo follow the tenets of the Maehr’sea hiylun’ehya one must first know the meaning behind the ancient elven that masks it. Its most accurate common translation is “The pursuit of wisdom and health” or simply\n‘wisdom and health.’ So revered is this term that is akin to a blessing given between adherents.\nThe Maehr’sae pertains to the acquisition and sharing of knowledge amongst fellow Mali’aheral. Our race is known for many things, but poor academics are not included. After being changed by the magics of the\nGolden Pools, we were blessed with studious minds, and gifted great talent with magic of any form. Thusly, it is imperative that we embroil ourselves utterly within tasks that further our people’s knowledge.\nThe Hiylun’ehya pertains to the bloodlines and fortitude of the people. Pure bloodlines are the ones that best retain the blessings of the ancient pools. To sully them with poorly-reasoned mixed breeding thins the\nblessings that we gained, and therefore makes the maehr’sae hiylun’ehya more difficult to complete--if not impossible. In guarding our bloodlines we must show discipline and fortitude. Things that detract the health\nof the people; violence against the pure, mixed-breeding, and being too lenient and accepting towards the other races. One must always be diligent when regarding impurities. The small concessions of today always\nlead to the vilest impurities tomorrow beings. It has been observed, and thus it is known.\nThe ultimate goal of the Maehr’sae hiylun’ehya is its completion. To reach true enlightment , the Mali’aheral strive to understand all through constant learning, and a pure people. When all is understood,\nwe will be beyond the simple meanderings of the mundane world. It is unknown what will occur when this day of total enlightenment occurs, but one suspects the Mali’aheral will know precisely what to do.\n“Maehr’sae hiylun’ehya.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Prophecy Cracked", "Ellir'siol", "Setherien will rise above his voi[sic] dominion, with the remains of those he burnt waking from the rifts. And amongst his army, there will be four of his dark lieutenants. Not the Harbingers but the ones before them.\nTanreez the Dhadow[sic],\n\nSkidrow the Dreaded,\n\nMalghourn the Drake,\n\nBalrog the Demon.\n\nThey will break into the Fringe, and they will force the obsidian portal to open.\nSetherian has always wanted to conquer a[sic] ancient land, and with the moon rising the time is nigh. \n\nOnly when his Dark Lieutenants are killed, will the golden lance be able to kill the Black Wyrm.\nStop him, before he opens a path to the world where a Daemon holds hostage.", ""),
        StaticBook("Prophecy I", "Natayshi", "Moongazer Prophecy\n-------------------\n\nThe Black Prochecy\n\nThis particular prophecy has already come to pass, and was one of the most accurate and chilling prophecies ever to be gazed upon by the Kharajyr Moongazers. Metztli bestowed\nupon them a sight unlike any other, the world ablaze in fire and brimstone, corrupt minions of an unknown origin roaming the earth wielding an ancient magic.\n\nThe Moongazers interpreted this vision of the future as the coming of Absyyl, the\nenemy of Metztli, who is the Goddess of the Kharajyr faith.\n\nAbsyyl's image is one of the sun, the sun being the symbol of all evil and wrong doing in the world. In this image, the Moongazers believed they saw this image floating above a world ablaze.\nThese events did occur, although temporary and not entirely in the way the Moongazers predicated. For the symbol was not the sun, but an eye. The wretched Eye of Iblees. \n\nThe prophecy foretold of an old enemy, and that it would once\nagain sack the world, corrupting its good and tainting its sanctity. It is for this reason that the Kharajyr mistook the visions as the returning of Absyyl.\n\nHad they have known it was Iblees, perhaps more could have been done to prepare for his second\ncoming. Alas, let it be proof of a Moongazer's worth. A prophecy from a Moongazer is never to be ignored.", ""),
        StaticBook("Prophecy II", "Natayshi", "Moongazer Prophecy\n-------------------\n\n    The Squird Lord\n\nThis prophecy already come to pass, and foretold of a collosal squid destroying an entire island, and so it did. It was named 'The Devourer' by the common descendant, and it seems to occur\nin a variety of Moongazer visions, and thus has become an omen of ill-will. The Squid Lord was predicted to devour an entire island, consuming buildings and Kharajyr in its path. And, it did. The isle the Kha' settled upon in Athera was entirely lost to\nthe creature. This prophecy thankfully was not ignored, and the island was quickly abandoned just days before the attack.\n\nThe casualties were minimal, thanks to the predictions of the Moongazers.", ""),
        StaticBook("Prophecy III", "Natayshi", "Moongazer Prophecy\n-------------------\n\n    The Snow Tide\n\nThis prophecy was made during the early days of Anthos. The Sage Natayshi accurately predicted the fleeing of the now supposedly extinct species known as the 'Bohra' fleeing from\nthe Frozen North, being carried by a great tidal wave of snow, pursued by a collosal dragon with wings as black as the night. This dragon turned out to be the wretched beast known as Setherien, who was defeated at the ending days of Anthos.\nAlthough the Moongazers made great efforts to inform the world of the coming threat, their warnings fell on deaf ears, and the inevitable occured.\n\nThe turmoil of Setherien and his Harbingers was devastating, but perhaps the damage\ncould have been lessened if the Moongazer's warning had been treated with urgency, instead of pushed to one side.", ""),
        StaticBook("Pumpkin Letter", "Aerxuis", "Dear Archdruid Danic,\n\n I request you decompose this book in the nearest compost bin as soon as you are finished reading it.\n\nThe one known as 'Aphoros' or 'The Pumpkin Druid' is dead. However in his place-\n-I Aerxuis have arisen. Aphoros' memories have long since faded thanks to the Aurem Apple he devoured. He left me a note that I had meant to deliver to you a long time ago.\nStart of the note:\n\n\"Danic, I'm leaving The Druidic Order.\n(All puns intended.)\n\nThe Order has brought me many friends and rivals, however I believe my current anf future actions contradict that of one\n-that should serve within The Druidic Order. I request that you move me to the Lost Druids List and shun me for whatever reason you feel appropriate. If this is oak with yew I would also like to stay attuned. With the return of Iblees I feel my-\n-connection with The Aspects is needed more now than ever. \n\nWhy? Is that what you're asking?\n\nTo phrase it simply:\n\nI do not want my actions to reflect upon The Order and bring-\ntrouble to you through such actions.", ""),
        StaticBook("Puppetry", "Evark Evocress", "~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~             Puppetry\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n        \n\n\n\n\n\n\n§\nContents:\n\n- Understanding the           magic.\n\n- It's title in dark arts.\n\n- What the magic can           do.\n\n- How to counter the          magic.\n\n- Is the magic bad.\n~~~\nUnderstanding the magic\n\n~~~\nPuppetry is a magic that has limited knowledge about it even to the mage that uses it himself.\nIt’s very unfamiliar how it works in conjunction to other magics.\n                              --->\nThe way to understand the magic is through a link. This link is connected by two people through a catalyst which in the case of puppetry is through a puppet. The mage connects themselves through the puppet prior to connecting the other person.\n~~~\nIt's title in dark arts\n\n~~~\nThe dark arts is a term in itself, death magic, forbidden magic. Though my understanding of puppetry in dark arts as with other magics within this group are misunderstood by people. \n                               --->\nPuppetry is set in this class due to it’s nature of needing to create a link between a person which you can perform malicious acts on.\n Though puppetry in itself can be used for both evil and good.  \n\n\n\n                              --->\nWhich is more consistent of a gray art where many people do not see.\n\nPuppetry can be used for investigative purposes with a simple truth curse or make the pain go away in people that are being hurt or raise good emotions in people.\n--->\nOf course this can all have the opposite effect if the mage wills it. \nIt all depends on the person who practices the art.\n~~~\nWhat can the magic do\n\n~~~\nThe art of puppetry can have various and many uses in itself rather than the use for malicious nature. In explanation once a link is created it is like a bond between both parties through this \n                          --->\npuppet, what the mage puts on the puppet will affect the both of you. \n\n So if the mage puts a curse of disease on the puppet, the mage themselves will suffer the same as the other person bound to it by the link.\n\n                               --->\nThis can also be used in various other ways such as a curse of truth or a curse of happiness not everything has to be used for the cause of evil as people are believed to see by people practicing the art and it’s place within the dark arts.\n\n        --->\nThat being said when the link is created both people will feel the presence inside of them and that is an indication that they’re under the influence of the magic. This can be a way to get out of the area or find someone to aid in removing the link.\n~~~\nHow to counter the magic\n\n~~~\nThe most easiest way to counter the magic is to destroy the puppet. People are believed that if they kill the mage the connection is broken and the link.\n\n                              --->\nWhich isn’t the case, if the puppet is not destroyed the link remains and anyone who practices the art can perform it.\n\nOther ways to fully break the link are to go towards the holy order, paladins and clerics have been known to seperate\n           --->\nthe link between you and the puppet. This’ll will be a painless experience.\n~~~\nIs the magic bad?\n\n~~~\nNo, depending on the person the magic can be used for good as with bad. The magic in itself being classed under dark arts gives the impression that it is housed for the scum of the realm\n                              --->\nto perform malicious intent on people. Where the magic can be used to create good and happiness in various people and aid them in many ways without harm. It varies on person to person and the mage themselves needs to be judged not the magic.\n~~~\nConclusion\n\n~~~\n\n- The magic of puppetry creates a link bond between both the mage and the person if they get a piece of you and bind it to the catalyst being the puppet. \n\n                              --->\n- It counts as a dark art though depending on the person can be used as a gray magic.\n\n- The magic can do many things, despite distance created happiness or be used in malicious intent.\n\n\n                               --->\n- To counter, go to the holy order and seek someone to help you or destroy the puppet.\n\n- The magic in itself isn’t bad, it’s dependent on the mage themselves and how they use it.\nBy Evark Evocress", ""),
        StaticBook("Purity", "Lucion Sullas", "Returning to Purity\n\n\n\n\n\n\nby L. Sullas\nThere is to be a new number of standardised regulations regarding those who have fraternized/taken on disingenuous traits that any and all impure mali’ata of pure birth may undertake. As the mali’ata has wronged the venerated race,\nthus they must seek\nredemption in the eyes of all who would call themselves mali’thill. As such, they must gain the forgiveness of all who dwell within the pure lands.\n\nThe “purifying” shall be conducted in stages.\n1. The Drawing of the Curtain--\n\nThe mali’ata must be sincere in their desire to become a part of the glorious nation, and be willing to perform all the tasks asked of them. They must be willing to shed all childish egalitarian\nbeleifs pushed upon\nthem by the hedonists of the outer-world.\nShould they not conform to this ideal, they shall not be allowed to return.\n2. Righteous Revulsion--\n\nShould the mali’ata be sincere, and willing, they will be allowed to enter the city. Here, they must seek out every citizen within its walls, and tell them individually of the crimes they have committed towards\nmali’aheral. They will then, after informing each individual of the crimes, ask for forgiveness from each citizen. The citizen may ask the mali’ata of anything, and the mali’ata will do as they ask with great vigour and a calm disposition in a manner\nbefitting any true mali’aheral. The labours the mali’ata provided are but a pittance in exchange for the attacks on purity they have performed.\n\nAs a citizen, standards of good judgement are expected and a request which calls\nto question the logic of itself will reflect negatively upon themselves if inadequately explained. Should a pure citizen request a task that clashes with the laws of the city, the citizen shall be punished according to the crimes they\nrequested to be committed.\n\nThe mali’ata may not advance to the next stage unless every citizen gives their forgiveness.\n3. Learning the Way--\n\nAll mali’ata must understand and revere the maehr’sae hiylun’ehya, as it is the very phrase that defines our people, our culture, and our civilisation. Those that lack an understanding, an interpretation, or true, unbridled zest\nfor the maehr’sae hiylun’ehya will find themselves shortly more unwelcome than they had been previously.\n\nThe mali’ata shall be assigned a teacher from the ranks of citizens, the duty of whom it will be to teach the mali'ata\nthe maehr’sae hiylun’ehya. During this stage, any citizen may approach the mali’ata with a task, and as before, they must complete it.  \n\nAt the end of this process, they will be tested by a select group of citizens of their knowledge\nregarding the blessed phrase.\n4. Meagre Acceptance-- \n\nThe mali’ata, after gaining the forgiveness of the others, and understanding the apex of our culture, will be called to an assembly of all pure citizens. Here it will be decided by the\nmajority whether the mali’ata may become a part of the exalted society and resume their title of mali’aheral. However, they will not be considered a full citizen unless they undertake the final responsibility of their race.\n5. True Acceptance--\n\nThe reformed mali’aheral may now look to the city, and consider it their home. But they will not be known as “citizen” until they find a citizen of pure blood to be bonded with, and propagate the mali’aheral race.\nAt the birth of the first child, they shall be entirely forgiven of their crimes in any fashion, as they have returned all that they have stolen from the mali’aheral people.\n\nWith this act, they should rejoice--as they have obtained citizenship.\nby L. Sullas\n\nCopied from the Law of the Mali'aheral\n*a pile of paper has been stacked neatly*", ""),
        StaticBook("Purity", "Zeus Ith'ael", "Series One of Three\n          PURITY\n--------------------------------------\n\n     Scribed on the\nSeventh of the Grand Harvest. The year, 1496\n\n       Second Revision\n          First Edition\n\n      Printed by Lazul\n          Literature\nPurity. Progression. Superiority. These are the qualities of a tried and true high elf. Through impeccable purity we gain progression. Through progression we gain superiority over the lesser, the impures and the mongrel dogs that call themselves men.\nPurity. Symbolized by silver and white. It is our most important quality. Without purity we are no more than mutated savages. Purity runs not only in the blood of our people, but the attitude they possess.\nAcceptance of lessers and impures will damn those who hold our qualities. Those that sympathize with any cause but our own are to be considered stark raving mad like a dwarf and condemned to the brand.\nThose without silver hair should make you wary, but blonde counterparts can be tolerated upon showing worth. Most notably Kalenz Uradir, our most illustrious leader.\nThose that stray into the dirty colours of blonde are NOT to be trusted, tolerated or accepted in anyway. Their mere existence is a farce of high elven culture. This brings us to the tone of skin.\nIt is well known that blacks, browns, ashes and reds are an irrefutable sign of impurity, but that is not to say that purebloods can’t gain a tan. There are those among us that do diligent work inside dark rooms surrounded by tomes and inventions.\nWe respect them. However, there are those among us that prefer to spend their time training their minds and bodies in the light of the sun. They are our protectors and the unavoidable tanning of their skin is to be respected\nat the same level as their scholarly compatriots. We do not tolerate anything more than a simple tan. Those touched by night are thieving rats. Most often greedy and violent. Simple dogs that are only to be used and abused for the progression of our\npeople. The simple notion that we allow them into our city in this day and age is revolting. The blood that creates our appearance is not the only sign of purity.\n\n\n           \n\n            =O=\nThe toleration, acceptance and communication with the lessers, the impures and the mutants shocks me. Communication is the only form of interaction that can be somewhat acceptable as we live in a diplomatic era.\nAt its current state we cannot simply liquify the muts outside our walls, but a day will come. Those that are found outside of the Silver City without a diplomatic reason for interacting with the abominations outside of our pristine zone of control\nare to be reported immediately. At that point they have shown clear signs of an impure mindset. Rehabilitation is an option, but the only real solution is liquefying their bodies and hoping their souls do not re-manifest\nin an even more disgusting form of life. By allowing co-mingling among our people and the lessers we are damning our progression as one. The chaotic ways of the others will twist and contort our brothers and sisters\ninto hideous beasts unfit to walk among our gardens, halls and places of knowledge. They shan’t speak the beautiful tongue of our ancestors.\nI hope you hold the words written to heart. Impurity is not only measured in skin tone, hair colour and irises, but in the mindset and attitude of a true elf. There are those among us that we should impose an inherent distrust\nof such as those that mix elven and common. Those that sympathize with the ideals of the chaotic savages. Through only purity can we find progression.\n\n\n\n             =O=\n          THE END\nLook for the the next book in the series, Progression.\n\nThank you for reading and I can only hope you take these words to heart. For only the people of today can shape the future of tomorrow.\nViligance is diligence.\n\n\n                Zeus Ith'ael\nOther works worth reading:\n\n*Racism by Sullas\n*Perfection and Purity by Vellulaie'thillin Vul'athri", ""),
        StaticBook("Purity and Order", "Icarus Adil", "Purity and Order\n\n        Haelun'or,\n           Axios\n\n     Published 1589\n\n\n\n     by Icarus Adil\nChapter 1: Introduction\n-------------------     There have been a great many works written about purity and the importance of the maehr’sae hiylun’ehya, each of which provides a compelling account on the importance of purity to the mali’aheral of\nHaelun’or. Yet to my knowledge, there is no literature on the importance of purity and the maehr’sae hiylun’ehya in their preservation of order within Haelun’or and among the mali’aheral.\n     If all the reader seeks is knowledge about the nature of\npurity and its appointment or attainment, then I encourage them to pursue other pieces of writing. “On Racism” and “Purity,” both by Lucion Sullas, prove valuably informative, or alternatively the more contemporary work of Iaria Elervathar, “Our Purity.”\nEach makes an invaluable case for purity and its importance, and will undoubtedly aid the reader in understanding the ways of the mali’aheral. Yet if the reader remains unconvinced, or otherwise seeks a prescriptive understanding on how the maehr'sae\nhiylun’ehya maintains order wtihin Haelun’or, I implore the reader to read further. This may prove a particularly valuable tome for those not of mali’aheral birth who have chosen Haelun’or as their home, so they can understand why they too must pursue the\ncourse of the pure.\nChapter 2:\nSystems of Order\n-------------------     Before we consider purity as a means of maintaining order within Haelun’or, one must consider how systems for promoting order work within a society. Though I expect most readers to be pure mali'aheral of\nHaelun’or, perhaps some reading have earned the right to live within Haelun’or in spite of their birth, and originate from beyond these walls. Regardless, systems of order in other societies will serve as adequate allegories for our purposes.\nFirst, let us consider the Holy Oren Empire. Ignoring their frequently shifting regional variance, there are many consistencies which promote order within their society. For example, the Empire maintains a system of nobility, informing each person\nwithin the Empire of their place in society at their birth. This position determines each individual’s rights and responsibilities, how they must conduct themselves publicly, who it is appropriate to marry and produce offspring with, and this is only the\nstart. Likewise, through the relationship of vassal and liege, every individual can trace the line of authority from themselves to the Emperor, a central figure from whom all authority comes.\n     There is no question that this system has its faults, yet\nthat is only when this system of order is ignored. At times, vassals will believe themselves capable of ousting their liege and forcing themselves into power, or liege lords will provoke rebellion through ill-treatment of a vassal, and in short order we\nfind a system of chaos. Yet it is almost always certain that, had these individuals opted for maintaining the existing system, they would have found themselves better off. No matter its issues, the Holy Oren Empire maintains a fairly effective system of\norder.\n     Next, we shall consider the Dominion of Malin, more specifically the Principality of Laureh’lin. The mali’ame have a far newer system of order, existing in earnest for less than a century, yet it has proven exceptionally effective in\nestablishing order through dogma. In a strategic move, a single individual managed to establish a false history for the mali’ame, reframing the already familiar and respected Aspects as  gods of the mali’ame. Through effective proselytizing, many were\nindoctrinated into this faith at a time when the mali’ame faced unprecedented strength and security.\n     The results of this have proven particularly exceptional. With the authority granted by these newly established gods, the Prince of the mali'ame can\njustify his every action and force order upon his people. Whether it be intrusive internal measures to maintain security or gross external violence, in the name of these Aspects he can do as he pleases. Not even the Holy Oren Empire has based its society\nso heavily on zeal and dogma, differentiating it as a thoroughly different yet similarly effective system despite seeming political equivalences.\nChapter 3:\nPurity and Order\n-------------------     It is my hope that these two examinations, though cursory in nature, have proven helpful in understanding what is meant by the term ‘system of order.’ Now it is time to consider purity through a\nsimilar lens.\n     Purity is particularly prescriptive through the maehr’sae hiylun’ehya, for it demands a great deal of those seeking to be pure. Most simply, it demands physical purity, the fervent refusal to muddle mali'aheral blood with that of other\nraces, even fellow mali. Those who ascribe to purity recognize superior traits found more consistently among mali’aheral bloodlines, and as such each must do their part to ensure they go unsullied.\n     Equally important are the components of\nmaehr'sae hiylun'ehya, more contemporarily considered ‘progress and health.’ The first gives each pure mali’aheral purpose, for each mali’aheral must actively pursue progress. Each must provide some work, typically of the mind, to add to their society.\nThe goal of this imperative is to constantly improve upon itself, to add more and in turn encourage others to add more. Through progress, we provide each mali’aheral with purpose.\n     Yet on its own, progress could be pursued recklessly. This can mean an\nofficial believing he knows best and resorting to progress at the tip of a sword, a scientist deciding progress comes through sacrifice and garnering it through deathly experiments, or a madman bastardizing progress as justification for other atrocities.\nThis is the importance of the imperative of health, for it requires that all pursuit of progress must not come at the expense of our fellow mali’aheral. Each is equally important if Haelun’or is to exist as a society rife only with order, and thus the two\nmust be pursued strictly.\n     Of course, purity requires all to behave in accordance with a series of intricate rules. There are rules of how one can and cannot treat their body, how courtship is to be performed, specific manners through which disputes\ncan be adjudicated, among countless others. Though some who decry the mali'aheral way treat them as needlessly restrictive, in fact they are no different from the rules of any other society. Each and every society has rules for socialization and\nappropriate behavior, yet Haelun’or has chosen to codify them and enforce them strictly. This is merely a means of removing ambiguity, and thusly is not strict, but instead merely ordered.\nChapter 4: Systematic\nFailing and Change\n-------------------     Despite the fact that purity and the maehr’sae hiylun’ehya are clearly exceptionally ordered, none but the most stubborn would assert Haelun’or has not faced a great many failings over the\npast century. This is not due to some failure of purity as a system, but instead the decisions of citizens and leaders alike ignoring it.\n     We have seen periods of leadership where needless aggression and warfare have given strength to the wielders of\nblades rather than pens. We have seen periods where citizens care little for the collection of knowledge and pursuit of progress, but instead their mere existence with brief recital of maehr’sae hiylun’ehya. We have seen those who pursue twisted progress\nat the sacrifice of health. When we find disorder in Haelun’or, it is not due to a failure of this system, but instead a decision, conscious or inadvertent, to ignore it for some other end.\n     Each system of order has means to create change; for\nHaelun’or, the means of change is open discussion and decision by the consensus of mali’aheral. Yet too frequently, change has been pursued by open rejection of purity or the implicit bypassing of it. For purity and maehr'sae hiylun'ehya to prove a\nsuccessful system of order, the principal aspects of purity, progress and health must always be pursued, and change must be considered within these boundaries and through the systems for change we deem legitimate.\n     Though this has been meant primarily\nas an informative account of how purity promotes order within Haelun’or, it is also a cautionary one. To maintain our system of order and to protect purity, we must maintain a society with open discussion rather than censure, and commit Haelun'or to\nholding its purity with the utmost reverence.", ""),
        StaticBook("Pursuing Purity", "Ashanaak", "------=+=------\nFor Those Who Pursue Purity...\n------=+=------\n\n\n\nA Guide for Those Who Pursue Knowledge of Tahariaean Clericism\n------=+=------\nMasjid al Nur al-Haqq\n------=+=------\n\nThe Masjid al Nur al-Haqq is the building before you, serving as a gathering place for the clerics of the Aengul of Purity, Tahariae. Tahariae has given us the abilities to establish Purity in this\nrealm, which comes in two forms. The first is the eradication of injuries, blemishes, and sickness from the mortal races. The second is the eradication of the servants of darkness throughout the realm, such as dark mages, tainted beings, and those with\nfraternal relations with such beings.\n------=+=------\nThe Five Tenets of Tahariae\n------=+=------\n\nWhen one becomes a cleric, they must follow a set of five tenets, or five main rules, told to the Prophet Braxis in Anthos by Tahariae Himself. The rules are to ensure the cleric knows what he\nor she must do for Tahariae and His duty. Breaking even one of these rules will mean forceful disconnection from Our Lord:\n[*] Shelter and protect thy brothers and sisters in Tahariae. [*]\n\nThe other clerics are much like your brothers and sisters, a family. You must always be ready to come to their aid, and to allow them to die intentionally is impure.\n[*] Do not stray in thy dedication to Tahariae. [*]\n\nNever stray from your duty, your duty is to heal those in need and to purge the darkness that roam around Vailor. To allow a simple matter to draw you away from such duty is impure.\n[*] Guide and protect the Descendants of the Four against the Impure. [*]\n\nNo matter their race or personal prejudice, cast all hatred aside, as we aid all. Help guide them onto the right path and ensure they are healed and protected from Impurity.\n[*] Do not spill the blood of the innocent. [*]\n\nDo not attack or kill an innocent person, even if they have insulted you or another. We clerics are the healers of the innocent, not slaughterers of the innocent. Such is impure.\n[*] Do not use Tahariae's blessing for anything other than His will. [*]\n\nTahariae’s power is only for His Mission. To use it to harm those innocent of crimes or for your own selfish needs is impure.\n------=+=------\nWalking the Path of Purity\n------=+=------\n\nWe are willing to take in those willing to become a cleric, although becoming one is not a simple matter of gaining His power and using it of your own free will. One must be willing to undergo\ntrials and be prepared to put Tahariae’s duty before all, including what is most precious to you personally. Most of all, you must follow the Tenets without hesitation; failing to do so will mean permanent disconnection.\n\nIf you truly have desire to bring\nLight and Purity into this realm, you shall meet with one of our masters and put through a series of trials that the master decides. These trials will help demonstrate to us your devotion and dedication, as well as help you understand the roles of the\nclerics. Once your trials are complete and the master deems you ready, you will be brought before Tahariae Himself. If He deems you ready, He will grant you His blessing of Light, and your duty as a cleric shall begin under the guidance of the master who\nconnected you to Tahariae.\n\nIf you wish to walk the Path of Purity, leave a letter explaining who you are, why you wish to serve Tahariae, what skills you have, and if you have any questions regarding us. Simply leave the letter in the chest at the\nMasjid al Nur al-Haqq, in the Caliphate of Khalestine, and await our response.\n\nIf you require healings, protection, or blessings, do not hesitate to send a bird to one of the Four Archons of the Masjid al Nur al-Haqq.\n------=+=------\nThe Four Archons\n------=+=------\n\n-[ The Mind ]-\nRamza Mantisuku\n((Zeeer0))\n\n-[ The Mouth ]-\nAshanaak\n((Ventusyr))\n-[ The Heart ]-\nAndriel Z'lorn\n((jlyoko))\n\n-[ The Arm ]-\nElvira Mantisuku\n((Farryn))\n[!] This page is dedicated to a map of the Caliphate, with a small, simply-drawn temple symbol in one of the corners of the city. [!]\n\n((-2197, 1061))", ""),
        StaticBook("Pyromancy,AGuide", "[In Costume] Archibald Cyrion", "Pyromancy, A Guide.\n\nFire Evocation, otherwise known as pyromancy, is the art of creating flames from the  very essence of the Void itself.\nGetting Started:\n\nKnow you may ask\"How do I even get to the Void?!\"\n\nWell ask no further.\n\nA simple week or two of meditation will hopefull get you along the lines of connecting to the void.\n\nImagine the void as a\nwindow within your mind, and through that window is energy (of sorts). To keep that window open there needs to be something holding it open, in other words: your energy, call it mana if you will.\nAfter connecting to the Void:\n\nAfter managing to connect to the void, a mage simply has to get better, through the means of meditation and practice. \n\nOnce a mage has formed a sort of \"bond\" with the void, they may now begin to summon flames.\n\nHow do you\nask? Well all you need to do is know how a flame is, how it is made, how it not only destroys but purify, how it burns, basically BE THE FLAME.\nOkay, I Managed With the Void and How Fire Works, Now What?\n\nNow you get to the fun part.\nWith the connection of the void and the knowing of how fire works, you probably know how to do it, somehow.\n\nAt first a mage in there first week or two will barely\nmanage to get a spark going, much less a ball of fire. However after continues effort and meditation, a mage can achieve their goal of mastering fire evocation over the course of around five elven months.\nFire:\n\nNow you may be asking how are you going to actually use it in the terms of combat. Well obviously you, with some practice, mold the flame into that of a sphere and condense it. The stronger larger the flame, the greater the energy. \n\nAs of this,\nyou can also cause an explosion of the fire as it contact with a surface, the size of the explosion depending on the strength of the mage.\nNow after reading this, you may or may not want to be a mage. But good luck!\n\n- Archibald Cyrion, Head of the Cyrion Bloodline", ""),
        StaticBook("Queen of Virtue", "Balder Frostbeard", "Wyrvun, \"Queen of Virtue\"\n-------------------Wyrvun is the wife of Yemekar and mother of the lesser gods. She first was placed upon the world along side her husband to bring an equal balance to his power.\nAfter the world was born she was charged with\nkeeping The Deep Cold under control. Trying to limit Khorvads ambition by teaching him from right to wrong, She let her guard down and was imprisoned. Khorvad wanted to corrupt Wyrvun but did not have enough power to do so, and only manage to send a\ncorrupted piece of Wyrvun to the mortal Realm.\n\nThe Shard would take the form of Ondnarch, the Terror of the North. It pained her so to be used for evil, even in this slight way. As Khorvad was busy in doing of the mortals she would of managed\nto free herself and returned to Brathermordakin. she oursued purity, virtue and righteousness zealously.\n\nWyrvun is a shape shifter and in her basic form apperas as a blizzard but to mortals she more often takes a form of\na dragon or a Wyvern. Those dwarves who choose to follow her teachings value a pure and righteous heart above all else", ""),
        StaticBook("Quintesscence", "Eskel", "-------------------\n\nQuintessence and You\n\nA brief explaination of life-force and it's importance in necromancy. \n\n( https://tinyurl.com/y8soqe47 )\n\n------------------", ""),
        StaticBook("Ranks of Clergy", "Theran", "High Pontiff\nThe High Pontiff is the absolute, autocratic leader of the Church who fills the papal throne, and fulfills the role of the previous position of High Pontiff. He is considered the Vicar of God and infallible in regards to matters of\ntheology. He wears a fresh white robe made in their honor as the head of the Church and wear a gilded laurel in honor of Horen I. High Pontiffs must be celibate as decreed by High Pontiff Lucien II. The High Pontiff is to be addressed as 'Your\nHoliness'.\n¬†\nBishop\nBishops are the administrators of the Church. They manage their entire diocese, typically an immense tract of land, and are responsible for picking acolytes and naming priests within the diocese. They\nalso are a member of the Ecclesiastical Synod. They can only be ordained by High Pontiff. Bishops must be celibate. Bishops wear the aged robes of High Pontiffs past to symbolize their role in the Synod and are to be addressed as 'Your Eminence'.\n¬†\nAbbot\nThe Abbot is considered peer to the Bishops of the clergy; however, their role is more specialized to reflect their monastic vows. Abbots often are master\ntheologians who train both priests and monks in ways of secular and clerical intellectual traditions. They administer abbeys, houses of learning and monastic life, and wear the aged robes of High Pontiffs past to symbolize their role in the Synod.\nAbbots must be celibate. They are to be addressed as 'Your Eminence'.\n¬†\nPriests\nAlso known as clerics, priests are the backbone of the Church and represent the majority of the Clergy. They\npreach in settlements, perform all sacraments, morally guide communities as leaders of their parish, and may take on other professions as long as their loyalty remains chiefly to the Church. They also must serve the\nparish they were assigned to by the bishop. Serving as holy men, they may be mobilized by their superiors or sent on a variety of different clerical missions by them. A priest can be ordained by any bishop, provided they swear the Oath of\nOrdination. They may not wed once assuming the priesthood, but may wed prior and ascend to the priesthood. They are required to wear their uniform at all times, and they wear black. They are to be addressed as 'Father'.\n¬†\nMonks\nWhen many of the priesthood are aged and no longer able to administer their duties as actively as they wish, they often retire to the monastery and undergo monastic vows. Others chose the monastic life based on their\npassions towards theology and study, relieved of their duty to preach but still permitted to access church resources. Monks are the backbone of the learned institutions of the Church and focus largely on writing, prayer, alms giving, farming and\ndonation gathering over active adminstration. They are required to wear their uniform at all times, and they wear brown. They are to be addressed as 'Brother'.\n¬†\nDeacon\nDeacons are portrayed as\nnovice clergyman. They act as the servants of the parish priests and help the parish priest with the parish. They are permitted to hold mass, but they may not perform any other sacrament, such as matrimony or baptism. They are\nrequired to wear their uniform at all times, and they wear brown. They are addressed as 'Deacon'.\n¬†\nAcolytes\nAcolytes are the fresh-faced recruits to the clergy, wholly unskilled and\nuntrained in the ways of the Canon. They undergo rigorous study in an attempt to prove their literacy and knowledge in order to ascend to become Deacons. Given they have taken no vows, they do not wear any particular uniform and are addressed by\ntheir given name.", ""),
        StaticBook("Rasputin", "Abram Votyakov", "There lived a certain man, in Oren long ago.\n\nHe was big and strong, in his eyes a flaming glow.\n\nMost people looked at him, with terror and with fear.\nBut to Petrus chicks, he was such a lovely dear.\n\nHe could preach the canon like a preacher, full of ecstacy and fire.\n\nBut, he also was the kind of teacher\nWomen would desire\nRA RA RASPUTIN!\nLover of the Oren Queen!\n\nThere was a cat that really was gone.\n\nRA RA RASPUTIN!\nOren's greatest love machine!\n\nIt was a shame how he carried on.\nHe ruled the Oren land, and never mind the king.\n\nBut the kasochok he danced really wunderbar.\n\nIn all affairs of state, he was the man to please.\nBut he was real great when he had a girl to squeeze.\n\nFor the queen, he was no wheeler dealer\n\nThough she'd heard the things he'd done\n\nShe believed he was a hole healer,\nWho would heal her son.\n\nRA RA RASPUTIN!\nLover of the Oren Queen!\n\nThere was a cat that really was gone.\n\nRA RA RASPUTIN! Oren's greatest love machine.\nIt was a shame how he carried on.\n\nBut when his drinking, and lusting, and his hunger for power became known to more and more people, the demands to do something about this outrageous man became louder and louder.\n\"This man's just got to go!\"\nDeclared his enemies.\n\nBut the ladies begged,\n\"Don't you try to do it, please.\"\n\nNo doubt this Rasputin, had lots of hidden charms.\nThough he was a brute, they just fell into his arms.\n\nThen, one night some men of higher standing set a trap, they're not to blame.\n\n\"Come to visit us\" they kept demanding, and he really came.\nRA RA RASPUTIN!\nLover of the Oren Queen!\n\nThey put some poison into his wine.\n\nRA RA RASPUTIN! \nOren's greatest love machine!\nHe drank it all and he said \"I feel fine!\"\n\nRA RA RASPUTIN!\nLover of the Oren Queen!\n\nThey didn't quit, they wanted his head.\n\nRA RA RASPUTIN!\nOren's Greatest love machine!\nAnd so they shot him 'till he was dead!\n\nOh, those Oreners...", ""),
        StaticBook("Rat and Mouse", "Esperanza Siol'Sulii", "This Book is by Esp.\nFor the terrible 'ker guard who should think his life over.\n\n-------------------Once upon a time there a blue mouse. The blue mouse was named Alakagh. Alakagh was a mean soul, he hated the rats, because the rats were perfect\nand he wasn't perfect. He wished he was as perfect as the one precious rat named Esp. Esp wished the mouse could see that he was being quite rude, but the mouse said no, mouse no like rats because rats are different. That made the rat Esp fairly upset. So\nshe wrote a child fairytail about this in a form that she could express her feelings.\nBe nice mouse.\nI know I am better.", ""),
        StaticBook("Reagent Index", "Eddard Wolfe", "Alchemical\nReagent\nIndex\n-------------\n\nA basic guide to identifying and collecting alchemical goods for beginners and the unleanred.\n\n            -1629 Edition                   1.0.0\n                     Wolfe\nThe Following will be discussed in this book:\n\nMandragora\nSerpent Stalk\nFrost Vine\nAthin\nCrimson Vase\nDrake Tail\nDwarf Pumpkin\nBlood Lotus\nFlametongue Root\nLarihei Fingers\nElf Hair Vine\nCrouch Feather\nHalfling Grass\nTippen Root\nAlabaster Leaf\nSaffvil\nClutcher's Straw\nMetzli's Tangle\nGoblin's Ivy\n------------\nGetting \nStarted\n---------\n\nBefore any alchemist may begin their journey, and a journey it shall be, an alchemist must acquire a collective of basic tools, gain an eye for identifying plants among plants and\nacquire the patience of an aged saint. \n\nTools\n------\nAlchemical Shears\nVials of varying sizes\nSlotted Satchel\nMortar and Pestle\nDistilling Kit\nSource of water\nThe Dangers and Demands of exploration\n------------\n\nNow, as a word of warning, any alchemist worth their weight will acquire their materials on their own to ensure quality. Plants are, all too often, region specific. As such, exploration and\nadventure are standard parts of work. An alchemist should always be armed or escorted to deter hostility from regional locals, be they descendants or beasts.\nMandragora\n------------\n\nRoot of an aquatic plant native to wetlands. \n     Luckily the plant's roots are typically just beneath the surface of the water and collection is a simple matter. Either remove the plant, entirely, from the\nwater or simply trim the desired section of knotted root from the remainder or the plant.\n\nDwarven Pumpkin\n---------------\n\nA rather stocky bright orange flower native to wetlands. \n        Best to harvest when the plants have not yet bloomed.\nSimply cut the bud and store. The rest of the plant is essentially worthless.\n\nSaffvil\n-------\n\nA dark green grass-like herb resembling that of small blades. Rather common in wetlands, the sickly grass is best\nharvested just before any bodies of water. Simply cut the greenery at the base and leave the root in the earth.\n\nDrake's Tail\n------------\n\nAn off-green crooked bit of grass native to drylands and deserts.       As the herb is\nquite resilient, careful handling isn't too essential. Simply cut the desired blades and collect as needed.\n\nClutcher's Straw\n----------------\n\nA stick-like grass native to drylands and deserts.\n    The grass is easily cut and gathered. The\nroot is entirely worthless.\n\nGoblin's Ivy\n-----------\n\nThe only known ivy native to drylands and deserts.\n      Simply clip the leaves free and store as needed.\nSerpent Stalk\n--------------\n\nNative to Plains and Hills, the reed-like plant is commonly found on the water's edge.\n    Simply cut a segment free. It should be noted, however, off-colored near yellow segments are worthless.\nCrimson Vase\n-------------\n\nA bright red-bulbed flower found among the grasses of plains and hills.\n     The only truly distinguishing feature that sets this flower from the rest is a small series of black dots just near the stem.  Simply\ncollect the buds.\n\nFlametongue Root\n----------------\n\nThe flametongue, much like the crimson vase, is a red flower native to plains and hills. Unlike the crimson vase, however, these plants are marked by a thing streak of orange on each petal.\nSimply uproot the plant and cut the roots free. The rest of the plant has no known uses, decorative function aside.\n\nCrouching Feather\n-----------------\n\nA plant with a rather unique set of layered leaves closely resembling a\nsimple feather. Native to plains and hills.\n   Simply Cut the leaves free of the stem.\n\nHalfling Grass\n--------------\n\nA common dark green plant native to plains and hills. Near black in appearance, the blades of grass are circular in shape.\nSimply trim the desired amounts.\n\nTippen Root\n------------\n\nThe Tippen Flower is a blue and yellow spotted flower native to hills and plains. \n    Simply cut the roots free of the flower. The rest of the plant has no real use.\nAlabaster Leaf\n--------------\n\nA large green leafed vine. The large leaves are easily spotted and look rather close to the ear of an elephant. The vine typically lays upon the ground among the grasses in hills or plains.\nSimply cut the leaves free of the stem and store as needed.\n\nFrost Vine\n----------\n\nA blue flowered vine native to the frozen wastes. \n    The plant, strangely enough, is best used as a whole.\nAthin\n-----\n\nA blue algae commonly found clinging to underside of iced over lakes and ponds.      Simply break the portion of ice (exercise caution) and scrape the algae into a container.\nLarihei's Fingers\n---------------\n\nA small stick-like plant common in the frozen patches of grass about the frozen wastes.\n    Among the only surviving plants in the wastes, they're extremely common, resilient and easy to collect. Simply cut\nthe desired sections.\n\nElf's Hair Vine\n--------------\n\nUnlike the Frost Vine, Elf's Hair is a flowerless vine native to the frozen wastes.       Simply pry the desired segment free of its surface and store.\nBlood Lotus\n-----------\n\nA red flowered shrub native to dylands and desert.\n   Simply trim the buds and store as needed.\n\n\nMetzli's Tangle\n-------------\n\nA bush native to\njungles, marked by yellow striped leaves.\n   A rather difficult root to gather, it is common to simply collect the plant whilst it's still quite young and ungrown. \n\n                   ------ Reagent uses, recipes and studies are to be printed in\nother works by Eddard Wolfe.\n\n          - In memory of those who have lost their lives fighting the anomalous, sickly and evil. \n\n§iMay the men of the marked find their place in the seven skies above.", ""),
        StaticBook("Rebirth of Evil", "Lilyana", "The Rebirth of Evil\n\n          By\n\n        Lilyana\nShe awoke in dire pain and confusion as the livelihood of the Crimson Fist’s purpose and existence, literally, weighed heavily upon her. The Champion’s mind sporadically showed images of a battle that just collapsed the temple containing most, if not all,\nof the Sanguine Hand, sending them to an early demise. Shouts meant to be full of victory turned into blood curdling screams of pain and death as they were overrun by their attackers. As she clawed at the gravel and dirt that trapped her, she tried\nlistening to her surroundings for other survivors calling out to her. But all her ears could hear were the memories of the stone walls around her cracking, sliding, grinding against one another, as they began to collapse inward on her and the others, and\ntheir screams. Oh how the memory of the screams tortured her mind, forcing her bloody and gashed hands to sift quicker. Her hands digging and sifting faster, trying to escape the memory,  but the images and sounds only seemed to come faster as she tried\nto flee, keeping in tempo with her movement. \n\nWith a heavy grunt and thrust, she thrusts her arm through a small lit-opening, finally feeling the cool air touch her skin.  This bolstered her will, giving her the strength to push herself through the\nsmall opening and back into the outside world. The elven woman lay there in the cool morning fog for what seemed like an eternity,  time completely lost to her, breathing in deeply the fresh air.  Slowly, from the dense fog a shadowy figure approaches her\nexhausted self and shoves a bow and arrow into her face. Panting, the woman looks up at the figure as he pulls back his hood, revealing the rugged features of a hunter. The man pulled back the weapon slightly from her face and asked her for her name.\n“M-my name…”, the elven woman spoke between her labored breaths, “ My name is Cora.”\n\nSeeing Cora’s condition and state, the hunter took pity on her that fateful morning and led her to his dwelling in the forest.  There, he fed and dressed her wounds\nnursing her back to health. Cora slowly came around to the man, knowing all too well how easily it is to lower ones guard when they begin to trust someone, but never spoke about the Crimson Fist. When he did question her about her past, she simply said\nthat she was a servant to the people that owned the, now, pile of rubble that he found her at. The man nodded, knowing it rude to question a person’s past, and went about his business. However, no matter how hard he tried to focus on cleaning his\nmorning’s kill or divert his gaze, he was mesmerized by Cora’s beauty and soon felt for her. Cora, knowing that the Crimson Hand’s was either utterly destroyed or scattered to the winds and that her previous life was too dangerous to try to start again\non her own, accepted the hunter’s affection with open arms and soon gave birth to a child of a rare complexion. The child’s skin was pale like snow, his hair like fine straws of white gold, and his eyes….crimson like blood. Because of his defining eyes,\nCora named him, Haemon, the Blood Child. \n\nHaemon’s features were the most exciting thing of his life as he lived a dull life in the forest. His father taught him how to string a bow, to catch a fish, to chop wood, and skin a kill. He promised to tak\nhim hunting when he was rightfully a man and left Haemon in charge of keeping order at home when he left on his numerous hunting trips. Cora took to motherhood surprisingly well. Her swift and accurate hands that once sliced a man’s throat before they\ncould blink now directed a needle and thread through cloth; her strength and determination that kept herself alive during fights with armed guards now carried in loads of firewood or cleaned the wash. She watched over Haemon throughout the years grow into\na fine young man, but also watched herself age. She knew that with her death, the Crimson Fist died as well, as did its unfinished work. So, as her husband left on one of his hunting trips, Cora brought Haemon into the cellar of their small home.\nThere, she had him swear to keep this information from his father, and showed him the history of her people, of his people. Haemon was fascinated by the information, rituals, chants, and stories his mother knew and begged to know all of it.\nSo, every time her husband would venture out into the woods, Cora would teach Haemon the ways of the Crimson Fist.\n\nThis continued for many years until the night before Haemon’s eighteenth birthday, when everything changed.\nThe hunter returned home earlier than expected, bringing with him a new bow to give to Haemon as a gift to use on their first hunt together. However, when he approached the home, all he could see was darkness through the windows. He quickly entered\nthe home, noticing that the fire and candles had been empty and snuffed for quite some time. The darkness however, did allow the light from the under the cellar door to draw his attention. He opened the door quietly, filling the room with light,\nand was met by the voices of his family, however could not make out what they were saying. Descending the staircase he saw his wife and son, dancing while around an open fire. An animal’s carcass and bloodied knife lay next to the flame and\nits blood was painted on their naked skin in weird designs and letters that he could not understand. Haemon was the first to notice his father’s presence, quickly dropping his hands arms, breaking the dance, and backing away from the cellar door.\nCora noticed the Haemon’s fear and quickly turned, meeting the horrified gaze of her husband. He, softly, began to question Cora and Haemon, but neither responded, both afraid to unveil the lies they have been keeping from him. The hunter became angry,\nhis voice raising as he stepped down the stairs, approaching his wife. Cora remained speechless, not knowing what to say or do, she simply looked at the floor. In a fit of tears and rage the man grabbed Cora’s arms and forced her against the wall,\nshouting at her, begging to her, for answers. Haemon watched in horror and fear as his father slammed his mother against the wall across the room, shouting at her, asking her questions, spewing lines of secrets, lies, and betrayal. But it was only Haemon\nthat noticed the fire in the center of the room grow larger and only Haemon that heard the flame telling him to stop his father. Haemon tried to cover his ears to escape the raspy voice but the flame’s voiceresonated inside of him, demanding Haemon to\ntake action.\n\nHaemon closed his eyes and screamed out, trying to smother the flame’s voice with his own, but when he stopped screaming, all was quiet. Haemon opened his eyes to see his hand firmly around the bloodied knife that had sat in the\ncenter of the room, and the knife he held was deeply embedded into his father’s back. His father twisted around to look at Haemon’s eyes as he desperately tried to reach for the knife in his back. Blood began to leak from his mouth as he tried mouthing\nwords, words that Haemon would never hear. His father fell towards the center of the room, his head cracking on the hard stone floor, blood leaking out of his body towards the fire. Haemon backed away from his mother who now shriveled into herself against\nthe wall, staring at her dead husband, at the pool of blood forming around his body.\n\nThe blood of the innocent man pooled and grew, eventually reaching the fiery claws of the flame. With an immense heat and power, the flame jumped high and turned\ncrimson, sparks flew from it in all directions. Haemon now stared at the fire, mesmerized by the dancing of its flames and heard the voice that spoke to him earlier, this time much clearer. He could not disobey it if he tried, the pull it had on his very\nbeing was too strong, so he walked into the flame. Cora tried to reach out to her son, but her body was frozen, whether in fear or by the flames own power she did not know, but when she called to him nothing escaped her throat. Haemon did not feel\nthe flame burn his skin, but felt it burn his insides, as if it had reached into his heart and soul and burnt them to ash. He could not scream out nor did his body react to the pain that his mind was feeling. His vision slowly became dark and blurred, his\nsense of feeling seemed to numb away, and his mind began to close in on itself.\n\nWhen Cora woke the next morning in her bed she quickly wretched onto the floor. The nightmare was so real to her, the heat of the fire, the smell\nof her husband’s blood, the image of her son walking into the fire, all shook her deeply.  She struggled out of bed and walked down to the kitchen, finding it cold and dark as it was every morning. She started a fire and hung a pot of water to boil while\nshe called out to Haemon to wake. However, he did not return her call. When she checked his bed, he found it vacant and undisturbed from the previous morning’s making. Fear struck at her as she turned to look at the closed cellar door. Slowly approaching\nit and wrapping her hand around the latch, she closed her eyes as she opened it and was greeted by nothing but the smell of burnt flesh. At the bottom of the staircase she could see her husband’s burnt skeleton in the same spot it was\nleft in her nightmare. She cried out and slammed the cellar shut and turned to run from the house, only to see a figure standing in the doorway, shadowed from the sun coming in around the figure. Its glowing, deep crimson eyes\nwere its only distinguishable characteristic.\n \nThe figure spoke to her with two voices, both familiar but from different lives.\n \n“Hello, Mother”", ""),
        StaticBook("Recipies", "Vlad Shade", "Alchemist Fire\nMandragora\nSerpents stalk\ndwarf pumpkin\nDrakes tail\nflame tngue\ncrimson vase\ncrouching feather\nStone skin\nMandragora\nSerpents\nDwarf pumpkin\nDrakes tail\nFlame tongue\nCrouching feather\nalabaster leaf\nclutchers straw\nmetzils tangle\nalabaster leaf\nGreater healing\nAthin\nFrost vine\ncrouching feather\nElfs hair\nTippens\nVirulent Slime\nMandragora\nSerpents stalk\ndwarf pumpkin\ncrimson vase\nPoisoned inferno\nMandragora\nserpents stalk\ndwarf\nflamtongue\ncrimson vase\nBoggy concoction\nMandragora serpents\n\nHermits concoction\nMandragora \ntippen\n\nTaste of sewers\nMandragora\nserpents \ndwarf pumpkin\nAll greaters require\nAqua vitae base\n\nlessers distilled water\n\nRegenerative are blood based\nFrost oil\nSerpents stalk\nAthin \nFrost vine\nCrouching feather\nElfs hair vine\nTippen\nMinor healing\nTippen\nSmoke wispers\nBlood lotus\ndrakes tail \nFingers\nCrouching feather\nChill blain\nAthing \nFrost vine\n\nGreater chill blain\nAthin \nFrost vine\nCrouching feather\n\nWinters blod\nAthin\nFrost vine\nSerpents stalk\nParalising venom\nClutchers straw-potent\n\nOr mandragora-Weak", ""),
        StaticBook("Red Priest", "Brutus Norrington", "Protect us. O Lord of Light.\n\n\nFor the Night is Dark and Full of Terrors.", ""),
        StaticBook("Red Velvet Cake", "Samantha Ashby", "Red Velvet Cake\n----Required Ingredients----\nHalf a cup of butter\nTwo cups of sugar\nThree eggs\nTwo tablespoons of salt\nFour tablespoons of refined cocoa\nOne teaspoon rose red dye\nOne cup cultured buttermilk\nOne tablespoon vinegar\n----Ingredients Continued----\nThree cups of flour\nOne teaspoon vanilla extract\n\n-----Frosting Ingredients-----\nTwo cups of creamed cheese\nTwo cups of powdered sugar\nOne stick of butter\n-----------------------------\n1. Gather all ingredients and prepare your oven. Your worksite should house two bowls, a wooden spoon, a whisk, a cylindrical baking pan, and a pastry knife.\n2. After gathering the required ingredients and tools, set the half-cup of butter into the bowl. Begin mashing and pressing the butter with your wooden spoon until it reaches a cream-like state. Gradually add the sugar as you cream the butter.\n3. Crack the eggs against the side of the bowl, and deposit the yolks into the mix you created in step two. Mix well.\n\n4. Take the cocoa powder and the rose red dye, and pour them both into a seperate bowl. Mix well. Pour into main bowl after mixing.\n5. Add the salt, flour, buttermilk, and vanilla. Beat well with the whisk after adding each item.\n\n6. Add the vinegar last, and stir mix the batter until the surface is smooth and free of bumps caused by dry ingredients.\n7. Pour the batter into your baking sheet, and set the sheet onto the highest rack in your oven. Check back often, and ensure the fire never licks the bottom of the sheet.\n\n8. Clean any tools that need to be re-used, as well as your mixing area.\n9. In a clean bowl, add the butter and cream cheese you set aside for the frosting. Once again, mix until creamy.\n\n10. Add in the powdered sugar, while continuing to mix all the ingredients together. When it's a full smooth cream, add in the vanilla.\n11. Make sure the frosting is  smooth and creamy, suitable to taste. Wait for the cake to finish baking.\n\n12. When the cake is finished, extinguish your oven's fire. Use a set of leather gloves to remove the baking sheet, as it will be quite hot.\n13. Remove the cake from the sheet. If this is difficult, take a knife and slide it around the edge of the sheet to seperate the cake, then take up your gloves once again and turn the sheet over. Don't worry too much if any sticks to the sides of the pan.\n14. Cut the cylindrical cake into three even sections.\n\n15. Use your pasty knife to spread the frosting over the top of one of the sections. Afterwards, take one of the non-frosted sections of the cake, and set it upon the frosting. Repeat.\n16. If done right, your cake should have three layers, with frosting between each layer. Spread more frosting around the sides and top of the cake, so it seems as if it's a single, solid mass.\n17. Should any cake remain stuck to the inside of the pan, which is highly likely, scrape it from the pan. Sprinkle the cake shavings over the top of the cake, as it will make the cake more aesthetically pleasing.\n\n18. Cut, and enjoy.\n------Red Velvet Cake------\nA somewhat exotic and uncommon confection, it's known for it's unique colouring.\nIt's somewhat acidic taste is highly acquirable, though the vinegar can be excluded if one simply wishes for a colourful chocolate cake.", ""),
        StaticBook("Redstone Applied", "Ogdan Frostbeard", "Redstone Ideas\n           & Applications\n\n\n               Volume 1\n\n\nby:\n\n    - Ogdan Frostbeard\n\"Minecart system\"\n\nApplications:\n\n-Transfer of goods\n-Quicker transportation\n- Traps\n\nDesc: A series of rails that power minecarts without momentum.\n\"Repeater\"\n\nApplications:\n\n- Arrow Shooter\n- Potion Bombard\n- Flickering Lights\n- Music\n\nDesc: A mechanism designed to flicker a signal ON and OFF rapidly or slowly.\n\"Combination Lock\"\n\nApplications:\n- Secrecy\n- Security\n- Password Entry using digit code\n\nDesc: A series of buttons or levers that must be hit in an order or set in a certain position to open a door. Very Advanced.\n\"Pitfall Traps\"\n\nApplications:\n\n- Suprise\n- Thwarting Enemy\n- Capture\n- Kill\n\nDesc: Removable ground in a tight area. Very advanced.\n\"Waterfalls\"\n\nApplications:\n\n- Obstacle to slow enemy\n- Able to retreat with ease\n- Confusion\n- Easy targets for archers\n\nDesc: A 'floodgate' of sorts. Unleashes a torrent of water down a hill to slow enemy movement.\n\"Alarms\"\n\n\nApplications:\n\n- Motion sensed alarms to alert when a place has been entered.\n- Noise & Flashing lights\n\nDesc: A sensor that alerts the party of an intruder. Lights & sound available.\n\"Automated Archers\"\n\nApplications:\n\n- One man can operate a number of arrow shooters.\n- One man can operate a bombardment of potions\n\nDesc: A row of arrow propellers that can all be fired at once with a single click of a button.\n\"Instant armory\"\n\nApplications:\n\n- Gear Soldiers instantly\n- Be prepared all the time for an invasion\n\nDesc: One motion could release a minecart filled with gear to thwart a raid in an instant. Can be turned on/off from a master command.\nDisclaimer:\n\nEach mechanism has different requirements and cannot be used anywhere. The atmosphere must be able to cooperate with the redstone properly or catastrophic failure could occur. (Fires, Exoplosions, ect.)\n\nThese must be maintained\nand built by a professional. \n\nSome of these designs are unproven- although believed to be possible. \n\nThis is not claiming to be ALL applications of redstone entirely.\nAll questions reguarding the building of these machines should be directed to Ogdan Frostbeard.\n\n((Benben582))", ""),
        StaticBook("Redstone Terms", "Ogdan Frostbeard", "Redstone\n      Terminology\n\n\n        \n\n\n       Written by:\n  Ogdan Frostbeard\n    \n\n\n    ((Benben582))\nTerminology:\n\n- Sequential\n- Wire\n- Current\n- Input\n- Output\n- True\n- Positve/Negative\n- Power source\n- Inverter\n- Converter\n- Drop\n- Interference\n- Shorting out\n- Gate\n- Latch\n- Pulser\nThis is a book used to educate those who wish to learn about, speak about, and perhaps teach about, redstone. \n\nThis is a must have if you want to be tink-savvy. Not all terms are listed here, but this book has many of the common terms listed.\nSequential: Forming or following a logical order. \n===================\n\nAll tinkerers must know how to think logically. It is vital to their arsenal.\n\nA great tinkerer knows whatever can go wrong, will go wrong.\nWire: Redstone wire able to conduct a electric current.\n\nCurrent: A wave of electricity, usually ran through a conductor\n\nConductor: Any material that conducts electricity\n\nInput: The place where\nthe signal enters the mechanism.\n\nOutput: The part of the mechanism that the signal exits or a device that the mechanism is trying to power.\n\nTrue/False: A way to describe if a redstone wire is 'on' or 'off'\nPostive / Negative:\nA way to describe if a signal is 'on' or 'off'. Used when speaking about a mechanism or about how it should work.\n\nPower Source: An object that is capable of sending a signal through the mechanism.\nRepeater: A device used to extend a redstone current further without a power source.\n\nInverter: A mechanism used to convert a positive signal to a negative one.\n\nConverter: Turn a negative signal into a positive signal.\nDrop: A technique used to send a signal of redstone downwards.\n\nInterference: When two redstone wires cross that cause an error in the mechanism.\n\nShorting Out: Dangerous occurance when a surge of\nelectrical currents course through the mechanism too quickly for it to handle.\n\nGate: A type of mechanism that usually has 2 or more inputs and a single output.\n\nLatch: A type of mechanism that holds a signal when sent.\nPulser: A mechanism that constantly is sending a signal throught itself. Generating a 'pulsing' effect. Can be delayed and timed for a 'clock' of sorts. Can be switched on or off.\nIf you have any questions, please send a bird to:\n\nOgdan Frostbeard\n\n((Benben582))", ""),
        StaticBook("Redstone Wiring", "Sarrion Zytiaear", "\"The Marvels of \"Redstone.\"\n\n___________________\n\nWritten by an Unknown Tinker\n\nRe-Written by:\nSarrion Zytiaear\nRed-stone, a common substance utilized to power appliances and machines, is a dusty mineral found within the deeper depths of the earth in the form of compacted, ore-like chunks. Once broken from it's stone prison, the shattered pieces of the\nred-stone ore are able to be collected and then later smashed up into a fine dust to properly utilize it's capabilities. Dwarves commonly use the substance for their in-numerous creations and the mineral has proven useful in\nAlchemy and the progression of Science in the realms of Aegis and beyond.\nWhile the mineral is common, knowledge of why it holds it's properties is not. There has been little to no explanation on why it is capable of conducting energy, once shaped into stable wire; and this\nis purely because of the fact that the wrong people have been studying it's intricacies for the time it's existed as one of man's many useful tools.\nContrary to popular belief, Red-stone and it's mineralistic structure are purely based on arcane origins. Much like the 'Golden Pools' that had been created by collections of Mages' Gold around subterranean pools of water,\nRed-stones are minerals that have been warped by the effects of magical energy over a large period of time. Being so close to the \"floor\" of the earth, the Void had expelled energy up and into the softer stone above the Bedrock,\ntainting the lower-layers of the earth with pockets of sporadic mana, which, overtime, had developed into the peculiar crimson-hued substance that is commonly found to this very day.\nBecause of the diverse nature of Red-stone, it is able to be shifted into several forms and still retain it's conductive properties. Many examples include Red-stone wiring, blocks of hardened Red-stone (which acts as a continuous power-source\nonce properly \"fueled\") and appliances and extensions to the Red-stone \"tool-set\" that allow the capabilities of the mineral to expand even moreso; a prime example being devices called \"retrievers.\"\n- - - - - - - - >\n\"Uses of Redstone and it's Capabilities\"\n\nThere is a wide array of things that Red-stone, in it's base form or not, can achieve. There have been advances in Alchemy with it's powdered, raw form,\ninnovations in technology involving energy-based lighting and piston-control and many other things that a common technician would recall upon a whim.\nFirst of all, it's prime utilization is the ability to conduct electricity via wired form. Once properly compressed and adjusted into metal wiring, there is a large variety of things able to be created; things like lamps to darker\ninventions such as electric-chairs. Pistons are powered by Red-stone, and even a dim light-source can be made with Red-stone. There are many things to create with this substance, but like everything else that is useful, it also has it's dangers.\n- - - ->\n\" The Dangers of Redstone \"\n\nBeing a substance wrought from decades of mana compressing into mineral form, Red-stone is prone to being unstable if handled incorrectly. One of worst things to encounter is water-tainted wiring which bunches\nup and clots the crimson powder within the poorly-assembled wires, and if energy is conducted through this faulty wiring, the clot is prone to burn up, explode, and possibly start hazardous\nfires should such unfortunate events transpire within structures made of wood.\nMiners, in the event of extracting the mineral from the earth, are prone to be blinded by the oft-dusty expel of the crimson substance upon cracking it open. Red-stone is able to easily damage a man's eyes on behalf of it's unstable properties.\nOther obvious dangers such as heating Red-stone and over-conducting Red-stone are also things to take note of, as the outcome of either is similar to the outcome of the first example above.\n\n- - - - - - ->", ""),
        StaticBook("Redstone: I&A v1", "Ogdan Frostbeard", "Redstone Ideas\n     & Applications\n\n        Volume 1\n\n\n       Written by:\n  Ogdan Frostbeard\n    \n\n\n    ((Benben582))\nTable of Contents:\n\npg. 4: Minecart System\npg. 5: Vaults\npg. 7: Alarms\npg. 9: Pitfalls\npg. 10: 'Arm and Fire'\npg. 13: Final Note\n-------------------\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n===================\n1. Minecart System\n\nA network of minecarts that power themselves with redstone instead of momentum.\n\n- Transfer of goods\n- Quick travel\n- Extend mining trips\n2. Combination Lock or     Vault\n\nA mechanism used to lock away goods or keep a room private. A series of buttons or levers must be hit in a certain order for a designated door to open. Requires a highly skilled engineer to produce.\n- Highly Secure\n- Sequence-sensitive\n- Storage for Valuables\n\nDisclaimer: These take a lot of space, time, and expertise to complete. There are many different designs for such a mechanism.\n3. Alarms\n\nA mechanism that is triggered by entry into a restricted area. Alarms can include light and noise. If made right, the alarm will run until 'reset' by the user.\n- Can provide general location of unwanted guests.\n- Alerts guards and residents of potential unwated guests.\n\nThese can be made to flicker or send a constant signal, making a single noise instead of a constant 'dinging'\n4. Pitfall\n\nA triggered event that removes flooring or walls when activated. Can be used to reveal rooms or trap enemies.\n\n- Trap enemies\n- Disguise entrances\n- Cause disruptions in enemy movement\n5. 'Arm and Fire'\n\nThis mechanism is used to add a 'safety' to an arrow-shooter, potion\nbomber, or even a doorway. It makes the person(s) switch an 'arm' switch which would activate the 'fire' button. While it is unarmed the 'fire' button would be -\nrendered useless. This type of mechanism can be applied to many things, including doorways. Making it so it can be locked from the inside but not the outside. \n\n- Safety switch\n- Can be used to lock doors from inside\n- One commanding person can arm or\ndisarm all dispensing mechanisms.\n- Safety of disarmed machines, can be armed at the flick of a switch.\nFinal Note:\n\nThese designs are all proven and are possible with the power of redstone.\n\nFor any questions, inquiries, or perhaps orders, contact Ogdan Frostbeard. \n\nKeep tinkerin' tinkers!\nAuthor: \n\nOgdan Frostbeard\n((Benben582))", ""),
        StaticBook("Reformed Church", "Ebonsquire", "Reformed Church Yearbook\n\n((Originally written by whoppering))\nThis is the information and yearbook of the \"Reformed Church of Aegis and nearby districts\". This book exists of out 3 parts: Information/History/Beliefs\n\nInformation: The church consists of 5 parts\nThe big Reformed Church nearby the Aegis temple. \n\n5 smaller congregations/churches in Kal'Uruguan, Kingsroad, WhisperIsle, Oren-market, Kramaroe\n\nOne headquarter, which is in the big Reformed Church.\nPastor(s) who preach and make sermons to the sinful world. The head of the church is Pastor Judas.\n\nHistory: The history of the church begins when two races met each other. The Daemon and Aengul. They were both servants of the holy God.\nWhere they met each other they planted a birch sapling in the ground. God forgave all sins of all people who prayed under this tree. After a while, a church was built with the wood from this old tree. That's why God's ghost is still in the church, and\nwhen you listen carefully, you can hear him whisper!\n\nBeliefs: Our religious organization believes in the God, our Lord. He can forgive our sins. Without forgiveness, you won't be able to be born again in the crypt of the temple.\nyou can't come in heaven. Our organization is separated from the central religion in the world. However, we believe in the same God. That's why we are called 'reformed'. We are not a separate religion, we are just an organization. We don't use symbols, we\nonly pray. Our mission is to connect people with the word of God. So that God can forgive their and our sins. \n\nThis is for now the end of the book. In the future, we will complete the story and this book.\nFor donating or information, contact Whoppering (RP: Pastor Judas). God be with you. Amen.", ""),
        StaticBook("Regarding Boots", "Emanaf Delsaran", "The pair of leather boots in this chest were confiscated from one Gilondir Oronar by El'Haler Emanaf Delsaran on the 6th of The Amber Cold, 1600.\n\nDo not wear, remove, or touch.  They are a grave hazard.", ""),
        StaticBook("report", "Arthur Amador IV", "REPORT:\n-------------------Ser Avenel and many others whom wish to remain unnamed witnessed druids cast magic threatening the structural integrity of a building. I tried to arrest the druids but Locke stopped me before attacking an innocent\ncivilian. It is to be believed that he was trying to save the criminals and heavily hurt Ser Avenel, but was sudbued by the nearby citizens/heros.", ""),
        StaticBook("Report", "Fitonor of Pompourelia", "Corporal, Leopold Baldassare was seen fleeing from a fight in the Felsen Park this saints day, the 15th of The First Seed, in the year of 1623. Many others saw him flee from this scene. Personally, I would say that this was an act of desertion.", ""),
        StaticBook("Report (Vandals)", "Edward Poesroe", "Report regarding the church tombs and vandalism.\n\nWritten on 21st of Sun's smile, 1572\n\nUpon exploring the town and its premises, I walked toward the church and its graveyard. I saw the tomb open and I decided to pay my\nrespects to the various pontiffs and kings in the area. While expoloring the catacombs, I discovered that part of the iron bars guarding the tomb has been broken away, leaving the entrance to a tomb wide open. \n\nThis was one of two paths in the catacomb\nThere was no tampering with the tomb upon further inspection, and I decided to follow the other path. \n\nIt led to a section of the catacombs that housed previous pontiffs. I took it upon myself to look around for other signs of vandalism.\nSure enough, I saw a sign signed by a person named JD which stated thusly\n\n\"Days decrease and Autumn grows, Autumn in everything\"\n\nThis sign was located next to a pontiff's resting place. There were no other signs\nmuch like it in the other pontiff's tombs. Upon reading the sign, I headed deeper into the last part of the catacombs. There were empty tombs with no names within this section\n\nAlthough some tombs were marked by stained glass, other\ntombs were not. In particular, there were three tombs that were not decorated with stained glass. I inspected these sections further and found that one tomb had a section past the wall that was larger than the others. If the wall were broken down,\nthere would be an opening and passageway just large enough for a person to fit through. To test if it was a passage, I threw some stones from my pouch. It echoed far past the other side of the wall. \n\nThere were no other passageways\nbehind the other tombs. \n\nI exited the catacombs shortly thereafter.\n\nThis may be no cause to concern, but efforts should be placed to fix the iron railings, remove the sign, and to possibly fix/complete\ncertain sections of the catacombs.\n\nAdditionally, the presence of a possible passageway may prove to be dangerous for the citizens, or for the clergy within the church. The presence of a sign may mean that this passageway\nopens at the completion of a puzzle or the opening of a switch. \n\nHerein concludes my report. Please do not hesitate to contact me if details are unclear\n\nWritten by Edward Poesroe", ""),
        StaticBook("Report 001", "Darid", "Report 001:\nTo Operatives\nGrand King\nArch-Rune Lord\n\nTerms: In these reports we shall use the term W.M.D. Weapon Of Mass Destruction.\n\nReport: The Project has gone greater then expected.\nThe first WMD, has been made. It is currently in the 'Runic Stage.' We shall add runes to the WMD, so we can safely either prepare test fires, or save it in case of emergency. \n\nProject Status: Green", ""),
        StaticBook("Report The secon", "Leonard Frerich", "Wind-raker told us that the corrupted stone with hands tied up on the stone is... very worrying. It's a necromancer's stone.  Very close to the border of Mardon's territory.  We know it's east.  It's east of Brabant Castle. The ascended, Wind-raker\nbelieved that the Necromancer's stone could pose a threat. Summoning undead, it can potentially corrupt the area surrounding it depending on the purpose - It might expand. I believe that's it for the first location. . .  And for the second -\nWind-Raker told me it is the Ashen Grove.  There was a black drake that was summoned by - he said Mordring - that burned the grove down, and invaded the place with his undead horde. He said he already knew the place. So we decided to investigate in a\ncave that was underneath the tree.\nWe found a locked door that got chains crossed over it. We broke in after a while - And find an engraving on the ground.  The ascendeds decided it is not our business.  The moss-lady decided to speak to a - I think\na man named Toren. She said that we found a symbol --------------------------------------------------------- -->>> Next page]]\n* A drawing of a happy looking temple with smiley face on it. Four people that is crudely draw in such a fashion with smiley face. One got badly drawn robe. One have long hair looking so messy and having some kind of coat with giant ass bird behind it.\nThirdly, a man with thick beard flailing all over the place with helmet on his head. He got big ass war-hammer as well. The fourth is stick-figured. Behind them is a giant gate that seem to have cross icon all over the place. Definitely hinting some form\nof clerical example. Another figure with armored vest standing behind window with big smiley face, and giant bee in the background. \n\nApparently  the first several pages were wrote by a professional handicraft easily not\nof Leonard's.", ""),
        StaticBook("Report. Klem.", "Klementim S.", "Klementim Sevchuv\nMan-At-Arms\nThe First Seed, 1591\n\nIt was a quiet month. Went for inspection on a HQ outside the Capital, turned out to be of the Army. No arrest to report here besides the burning of a heathen. Besides that, the only thing that was more\nactive on this month was that we went to the Warzone to fight the dweds.\n\nKlementim Sevchuv\nMan-At-Arms", ""),
        StaticBook("Report: Frostie", "Sighard", "~Hunt Report~\n\n-Frost Witch nearby Adelburg, 13th of the First Seedm 1625-\n\nCame upon a dry tail of blood on the road from the docks to Adelburg. Lead towards the beach. There, I found a wounded man, Fighting against what could only be  branded as a\nFrost Witch. Used Aurum to cut her down, a clean slash to her carotid artery. She stumbled to the ground, but remained alive upon Decapitation. Saved the man, lead him to Adelburg. Ice shard grazed my shoulder. -Examination of the head to be done later.\n-Eyes of an icy color. Pigment changed upon ritual?\n-Red Hair. Whether Dyed or natural is unknown. Frost Witches are all said to have hair white as snow.\n-Elven heritage\n-No blood. Instead, an icy, cold, gushy blue fluid litters her stream.\n-Easily lured a man to the beach in order to eat him. Either had the ability to mask her form, or the man was just daft.\n\n\nNo further information extracted from the dissection.", ""),
        StaticBook("ReportofOstiwick", "Daugon", "Lack of animals on the eastern (right side) farm except a few chickens.\nThe moat has been drained is mostly dry.\nThe farms have no been recently harvested.\nThere is a lack of personal within the castle as of now due to the war.\nBruce sends his\nregards to Erolas.\nThe entrance to the castle is a mess of storage.\nThe walls are rundown and seem to have not been repaired for some time.\nMany soldiers have departed for the warfront.\nDECOR!!!\nMany dangerous holes among the moat wall\nthing.\nThe outisde of the castle is a mess of stroage.", ""),
        StaticBook("Request", "Gaius", "Request: A blade of bluesteel and aurum, capable of cutting down any foe. Be they man or spook. Able to withstand even the most intense stress.\n\nMaterials:\n1x Elongated Bluesteel Blade\n9x Bars of Aurum\n3x Bars of Bluesteel\n3x Diamond Studs\n3x Diamond Spuds\n\nSidenote: Threw in my Token to Freygoth when I considered your earlier reaction to Carellith's own trinket. Mayhaps you could do me the favor of including bloodsteel in the forging process? I'll let you be the decider of that llir.\nAhernan.\n\n-Guyden Aureon.\n(That guy with the one eye).", ""),
        StaticBook("Request to James", "Alex Norrington", "To James Norrington:\nJohn Pasquier ((Bubby_64)) wishes to get a house here. Please give him one\n\nAlex Norrington", "")
    )

    private fun _AXIOS_TAHN_4(): List<StaticBook> = listOf(
        StaticBook("requiem for a g", "Slots", "white women\ndrugs in my truck\ngunning down afros", ""),
        StaticBook("Requiem of Ponce", "Myles", "Unto the Prince of Ponce, rightful heir of Salvia and all the benefits that entails;\n\nWarm regards. Your letter has found welcome ears, I bid this return letter as sign of my good health and good will. \n\nPlease see the courier is duly paid,\nEternally Your Loyal Companion And Financial Manager,\n\nMylas, Prince of Fenn and Sutica", ""),
        StaticBook("Resignation", "Archdruid Garun", "Herein lies my resignation as Archdruid. It has been a long road, one I have enjoyed through every second. I returned to the position to rebuild the mess that the Druidic Order had become, and now that quest is near enough at it's end. I have seen decades\npass, countless Druids and Guides rise and fall, and I have taught more Dedicants than I care to remember. The new Inner Circle will preserve the order as it travels into a brighter future. All I ask, is that my efforts, as well as those of\nthose before me, Callax, Verden, Milo and Thudrin, are not squandered or forgotten. We devoted our lives to getting the order to where it is today, and I would not wish to have our work be in vain. I will continue to visit the grove, to teach and offer\nadvice to the younger generation, and to retain the bond I share with my oldest friends. Bright blessings to you all, and may the Aspects guide and protect you.\n\n-Pine Druid Gi'Garun", ""),
        StaticBook("Resignation", "Edward Poeroes", "To Captain Ironsword\nand to whoever else\nwho gives a fock.\n\nI've been working here for an elven week. In that time, I've seen 10 bandit attacks, 15 assassination attempts, 12 counts of robbery, and 2 buidings being burnt down. I've seen elven assassins\nwith knives up their bumhole, lords and ladies who don't give one flying fock about us, and knights who treat us like arse. I am quite tired of all the shit that has happened with us guards, and I am tired of the constant shortcomings of those that\nwho take us for granted.\n\nTo be fair, I enjoy the company of you Captain, and the Chief. You are just people. You are kind people. I am sure that you have deeply and carefully thought about our city and what can be done to improve it.\nI do not blame you. Rather, I blame those that have constantly brought us more work, and more effort to extinguish the threat of Dreadlanders and assassins to our city. \n\nFor example, the citizen gate has not been updated and people that should\nhave keys do not have keys for over 4 elven days. Others guards and me do not have access to the eastern gate, where Dreadlanders come from. I have not heard of any money coming to me pockets, and I fear that this pension system is not worth it\nfor the shit I have to deal with. We do not have the numbers to deal with mobs, nor do we have the equipment to deal with Dreadlanders and assassins. It is not a mark upon those in the force, but for those that should provide us the equipment and funds to\ndo our duty. As I write this, there is a mob inside the square. THe crows dealt with them. Fockin Crows. We have not the resources to help them. I am ashamed that I myself did not stop the riot, but what good can I do against 20 to 30 men and women\ninsenced and angry. I feel as if I do not matter to anyone, not even the citizen, nor the lords and ladies who hold our pursestrings. I saw these Crows round the rioters and later left, a satisfied look on their face. It is disgusting.\nI am writing this in the hopes that whoever comes after me, they hopefully receive more than what I have gotten and put in to the force. I have done patrols. I have helped quell dissenters. I have brought those who are guilty to court. I have beaten\nand administered injuries on those who would disturb the peace. Quite frankly, it seems as if the people are content to enjoy violence and murder. I do not know if it was my failing as a person, as a guard. I do not know if it was the failing of the guard\nas a whole. But I feel as if I can not control the tide of violence without help. I feel hopeless as good citizens are disiillusioned and go against us as if we can change things. Because we cannot change this.\n\nI have been to Sutica\nand it seems more peaceful there. Is it our people that are broken and michievous?\n\nAs I write this, I am looking to other places for work. It has been an honor to work with you, to meet you, and to see the good that you have\ndone. To the Captain, that has always supported me and helped me work my way through reports. To me chaps and fellow privates who has patrolled with me. To the chief, who has been steadfast and firm to the code of the law.\nWith this, I will resign and work for work elsewhere. It has been a pleasure working with you all.\n\nI hope to see all of you again soon. Maybe not in Oren perhaps.\n\nSigned\nEdward Poesroe", ""),
        StaticBook("Resignation.", "Rykov Tanet", "I, Rykov Tanet, hereby resign rank and uniform. I find myself unfit to deal with the ideology of Oren.", ""),
        StaticBook("Responsible Magi", "Archembalt", "Being a Responsible Mage\nby\nArchibald Vallero \n===================\n\n      -----------\n     lIl     /\\     lIl\n     lIl    /  \\    lIl\n     lIl   /\\ /\\   lIl \n     lIl  /\\\\//\\  lIl\n     lIl  \\/\\/\\/  lIl\nContents\n-------\n\nI. Casting with Care\nII. Moral Aptitude \nIII. Keen Intellect\nIV. Dark Arts  \nV. Author's Note\n\n    /\\        /\\\n    \\/        \\/\n         /\\        /\\\n         \\/        \\/\n. - / . - = / . _ ._ =/-\nCasting with Care\n===================\n\n   Magic can be dangerous. Magic /is/ dangerous if not wielded by a competent and intellectually inclined individual. You must realize how to cast a spell without harming yourself and others. The first\nthing you must do is /study/ your art in depth. If you are learning fire evocation, realize that those flames can burn down entire homes. You can't dispel the fire that has caught onto wood. If you are learning electrical evocation, be sure that you\nand any nearby friend is not wearing an abundance of metal, else you will be in for a disaster. By understanding what the properties of these elements are, you can better prepare yourself for situations which will emphasize the need for your magical art.\nOverall, realize when your magic is actually needed and when it will be most effective. In addition, ensure that it will do what you hope, so that it will not go out of control and cause unprecedented damage to the environment or to others. If you can\nshow this level of conscienceness supports your reputation and garners trust from others.\nMoral Aptitude\n===================\n\n   Unfortunately, many use magic to commit their own raucous, chaotic and criminal deeds. While it is understandable that there will always be bad apples, understand that even some who mean well\ncan end up causing chaos for everyone.  \n\n   For this reason, it is good to know /when/ it is socially acceptable to cast magic. If a city does not allow you to cast magic, then abide by the rules and respect the law. Laureh'lin, for example, is a\ncity which currently does not allow for their citizens to practice any type of Voidal magic (c. 1540). Therefore, if one wanted to become a citizen of Laureh'lin, then you should not practice any magic within the walls. By disregarding laws on magic, you\nrisk diminishing the trust the officials and law enforcement have in magic users. \n\n   Also, be able to read the situation! If you feel as if you are surrounded by people who do not particularly appreciate the use of magic in an\nenvironment where magic is perfectly allowed, be wary. Even though magic is allowed in said area, the anti-magic sympathizers might try to aggressively halt you from casting magic, perhaps even attempt to take your life for such an action. Realize\nwhen you are at risk, for many have been negatively touched by magic and its ways,and will see you as an enemy as soon as they find out that you are a magic user.\n\n   Mages who do not respect these rules are simply criminals.\nNow, you might be asking this question: 'What if I'm in a dire situation where even though magic usage is outlawed, it might definitely help defuse or potentially save multiple lives?'\n\n   My answer for you is to restrain yourself. Let whatever\ncatastrophe might happen occur, even if the death toll is significant. You might be dissatisfied by this answer, but it is the unfortunate action that you must take in order to uphold the reputation of mages in the realm.\nKeen Intellect\n===================\n\n   As a mage, one would hope you are fairly intelligent and skilled. Unfortunately, not every mage is intelligent or wise whatsoever. So, how does a true, intellectual magic user differentiate\nthemselves from some jackass who can fire flames? \n\n   Well, quite easily, actually.\n\nWrite books, do research, and find ways to apply your magic to different aspects of contemporary life.\nIntelligent mages ponder upon the existence of their magic, the mechanisms (and studied terminology) that allow us to bring a spell into the Void. Develop theories. In fact, broaden the view of the question and begin to seek out answers.\nAdditionally, find certain objects and contraptions that your magic can be applied to which can result in increased efficiency, or develop a new tool altogether which can assist the whole of the realm, or even a portion of its citizens.\nEvery mage has their own personality traits and dogmatic views, but it is to my belief that there should be a desire to spread an understanding of how magic functions, its dangers, its uses, et cetera. Spreading knowledge should be something all mages\nshould do in order to create a realm which is more savvy with the works of the Void and conceptual knowledge.\nDark Arts\n===================\n\n   Dark arts users are an entirely different matter altogether in regards to both intellect and morality. Some practitioners of dark arts are considered to be wholly evil and selfish in their desires, but\nmany have argued that dark mages are actually heavily misunderstood. From my experience, I can come to the conclusion that both outlooks are quite foolish. It will never be so simple, all dark mages being absolutely criminal in psyche or purely misunder--\n--stood. There are most definitely dark mages who are absolutely dangerous and carry themselves like scum, but there are also dark mages who are far more benevolent in their existence. Due to the unknown nature and readability of dark mages, I advise\nyou, reader, to be wary around known dark magic users but to not entirely fear for your life, as most dark mages have ulterior motives that do not always involve going on mass murder sprees or the torture of innocents, but there are most definitely dark\nmages who do involve themselves with suh acts. \n\n   However, you must realize that there are plenty more cruel, sadistic non-dark mages overall in this realm than dark mages.\nAuthor's Note\n===================\n\n   I write with much bias, but I have tried to remain as objective as possible in this book. \n\n   I implore any mages and non-mages reading this tome to adhere to the\nrules and restrictions established in order to create a less hostile environment overall.", ""),
        StaticBook("Revenge", "Regale Ba'ikana", "Gather information on the creature that attacked Dirk and compile enough inorder to help us combat it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Revion T.", "Ol' Man Sano", "Dear Revion,\n\nAlthough not the closest of friends, you did assist me on multiple occasions. You've also served the library, and everyone who participates in managing this-\nvast collection of books. For this, I'd like you to make use of my old shoe polishing kit, as it can be used to any boots, or even armour, for that matter. Please, do take care.", ""),
        StaticBook("Rich and Poor", "Siegfried Vallberg", "The darkness is my cradle, from here I can preserve my skin, hoard my riches. In this chamber, this crypt, I feel power surging through my claws to my yellow eyes. \n\nTomorrow is a another day to be the ruler of The Nether.\nAnother day to watch hundreds perish in hunger while my silos are full of grain.\nTomorrow is another day to make record profits, buy more gold, sell more weapons and potions.\nSome say I am a beast. I say it's natural. Doesn't a snake care for themselves alone, aren't they natural too? My job, my only job is to preserve myself and I do it very well.\nPeasant-\n\nThe garment horse is finest mahogany, bespoke and carved by a master.\nThere is nothing accidental about the Vallbergs manor.\nFrom the hue of flowers to the pattern of the oriental rugs, everything makes a statement.\nMy eyes keep going back to the garments that are almost certainly dry.\nThe fabrics are finer than I can afford, even lying over the wooden frame they are beautiful.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ripped Journal", "Mosue", "Fools, all of them! I warned them. I warned them about what would happen! Kenneth isn’t a Lord. He’s an imposter of a man, spreading lies to ensnare victims in this spider web of a Keep.  [!] The page would be torn, the remaining seemingly gone.\nDoes his wife know? Does Charlotte know who he really is? They are husband and wife. How could she not know? Did she know? No. She’s too innocent of a person. She HAS to know about his secret spot up on the mountain, right? No nononononn\n           nonono\nNONO NO NO NO NO ONONONONONO\n[!] The remainder of the journal would be scribbles and incoherent babble.", ""),
        StaticBook("Riv", "Rylag Megal", "The signs still point to Riv'vallel.\n\nThe Bridge is destroyed!\n\nThe only thing that seems to stand is the stones in the front.\n\nThe Warhawken cave still stands.\n\nNo people around.\nAll of the caves are gone, my mead is gone, why is my mead gone?\n\nAll the trees are shit\n\nAll of our shit is gone, and I am pissed.", ""),
        StaticBook("Robrik notes", "Marcus Hotchen", "Robrik administration\n\nlost : 150 minas\nBank : 50 minas\nMined 46 iron and 3 dia\n\nRelationships :\nGodric var Ruthern bos , bos and friend\n\nTristan friend and unoffical boss\n\nAlijah unkown has a\nsecret I need to look into\n\ndiamonds 4 iron 66\n\nPrions diary :\nyear 1\nI got put into prison after I attempted to assisnate someone on the orders of my boss I am sorry that I wasn't loyal enough to refuse his commands\nto protect him and as such I wil hapilly accept any sentence they have for me even if it is death I can only hope that I get the chance to kill some orks and clear my soul before I go to god may I be forgiven for my sins so I can go to heaven please\nPrison song,\nday and night there is no diffence.\nNo one by my side I only have my life\nAll alone, look where I have gotten to.\nI pay for my sins I will most likely stay here for a long time.\nAnd if my days are numbered I still need to try to get my\nforgivness to god even if I live a lie.\n\nGodric if you may read it I wish that if you get my supplies , money and items and not the government that you give it to the next miner so he can get my legacy.\nGodric remember that from now on listen to advic\neven if you don't like it if it is smart.\nDon't let your sense of nationalism cloud your sense of reason.\nRemember that it was a honor to serve you but that you should listen to more advise,\n\nRobrik\nhappy song\nI am in prison but I am alive so I am good and alright.\nI can still sing and I can still write so I am good and alright.\nEven though my bed is of straw and the ground here is of dirt.\nBut still I am alive so I am good and alright.\nAnd if I will\nfall and my head goes of eyy I am still alright.\nIf the rat's will come and eat my toes I am still alright.\nBut when the demons come and I have fallen then I will not be alright.\nThis is the end of my diary.\n\nI will go and do just things however I can.\n\nI will leave the guild\n\nSigned,\nRobrik", ""),
        StaticBook("Rodion of Kralta", "JavaWizard", "The Story of Rodion\n  Karitsky of Krlata\n\n\n\n\n\nCompiled on the 20th\nof the Deep Cold, 1569\nRodion was born in the lands of Anthos many moons ago in the year 1413. He grew up in a rather stable environment with a wealthy family to back him. At the age of 25 he moved out from his family home and joined the village of Kralta.\nWhile there he encountered all forms of the destitute, this moved him deeply and after staying four nights in a home he had purchased there he gave up all of his wealth and property. Rodion accepted a small free home on the backside of the village and\nspent most of his time fishing, farming, and with the supplies he gathered cooking. While spending time in the village helping beggars and common folk alike he contracted a sickness which left him with permanent nausea and muscle weakness.\nSome say he contracted the sickness after receiving an infection caused by fishing the bordering river. This did not faze Rodion and despite his physical weakness he continued to help those around him and outside of the village,\nproviding them with large quantities of food. While sick, Rodion began to dabble in healing, he became somewhat of an expert on herbs and combined them with both his food and his profession. He would spend a great deal of time reading on herbs\nand praying for those he would meet. Despite all of his work his sickness still prevailed. Rodion would not accept treatment from anything besides what Godan had placed on this earth, and from the saints above. As Setherien was defeated in the north\nit became time for the descendants to move on and eventually at middle age Rodion still continued on with life being all the more painful. This transition only made him more infirm, while in the Fringe he had journeyed about in search of herbs and had\nslipped inside of a swamp bordering the Dwarven lands, there Rodion broke his leg and damaged his lower back. After Rodion’s fall he walked with a permanent limp. Rodion lived with his fellow Raevir in a wooded village where he opened a small herb shop\non the land of Athera. While there he took in those without work and gave them room and pay while spending time learning about herbs from his instruction. Testimony by Rodion’s employees state that he can always be remembered with a cheerful smile on his\nface. When Rodion knew he could go on no more  on the 4th of Malin’s Welcome 1500, he ascended a snowy mountain… and was never seen again. Rumors say that on his ascent he met with Aenguls who greeted him before he departed. Rodion is often depicted\nholding bread and chicken bones. Those who knew Rodion are known to tell a story about how he chose sickness in a deal he made with Godan. They say that he offered up his sickness so that those he served and fed might know Godan fully in death.\nEvidence of this is kept within the back pages of  a recipe book he wrote for himself.", ""),
        StaticBook("Rodrik and Bear", "Rodrik Vernick", "Rodrik and the bear\n\nWritten by Rodrik\nOne day a boy named Rodrik went out on a adventure. Rodrik went through the woods for days untill he found a cave. Rodrik thought about entering the cave for some time until he thought that there might be some cool treasure. Inside the cave was\nalmost empty but in the corner of the cave he could see a bear almost the size a dwarf. \"human\" the bear said \"can you help me with a problem i have?\". \"What is your problem bear\" said Rodrik. \"I need you to go to a small village not to far from here and\nbuy me some Honey to put onto my toast\" said the bear. \"Yes I can help you bear I will go and get you some honey\". On his way out the bear gave him a bag of coins to buy the honey with then he made his way to the exit waveing bye to the bear.\ntwo days later Rodrik made it to the village and went to the market *half of the books pages are missing*", ""),
        StaticBook("Rosemary", "Gwiwen Ahverren", "Uses of Rosemary,\n\n Rosemary, as you may (or may not) know, is a common garden herb used in a myriad of dishes and tinctures since we, the Descendants, have been smart enough to use it.\n\n A major boon of this little herb is the fact\nthat it can help with healing wounds and bruises when used externally in an ointment.\n\n However, the plant is not singularly medicinal (though anything using it can benefit from these properties), as it is used in cooking, baking, the making of scented\noils, and who knows what else!\n\n Now, this tome will be broken down into segments, which are the following:\n -Oil\n -Food\n\n Please follow along as you'd like, reader.\nChapter One, Rosemary Oils\n\n Rosemary oil is the main medicinal feature of the plant, as it can bring out those effects that can be absorbed through the skin, or injested with honey or the like.\n\n Rosemary is an anti-inflamatory, and\ncan assist with bruises, as mentioned previously.\n\n To make rosemary oil, you will need the following.\n -A sealable jar of which can be easily opened.\n -Water\n -Olive oil\nStep 1, gather enough rosemary to fill a sealable jar, and chop it up. The smaller the pieces, the easier it'll be to dry out. Once this is done, clean the rosemary, and leave out on a plate to dry.\n \n Step 2, once dry, move the rosemary from the plate\ninto the jar. It is important that the rosemary is /dry/, as any sort of moisture can instill rot.\n With the jar now filled, pour olive oil into it until the rosemary is completely covered. When this is done, leave in a window for a month.\nStep 3, once the month has passed, strain the oil, and toss out any rosemary you manage to catch in the process. Now that this is complete, fill a jar with the oil, or distribute the stuff into one-ounce vials.\n\n Notes: Remember to lable the container\nthe oil is in!\n\n The medicinal effects of rosemary are as followed:\n -Rosemary, as I have mentioned repeatedly, can assist with the healing of bruises and wounds if applied externally in an oil or a salve. Rub in lightly, though not completely, into the\narea that needs it.\n -For older men out there, rosemary can assist with hair loss, and can help deal with dandriff.\n -If used externally, rosemary can sooth the stomach and help with menstrual cramps.\n -Rosemary should /not/ be used by pregnant women in\nlarge amounts, as it can harm the infant.\n\n Chapter 2, Rosemary, Food, and You\n\n Rosemary has for many ages been used in soups, stews, bread, and food in general. In this age, this is no different.\nThe peasantry gather rosemary, get it wet, then hang it up to dry for months at a time. When this process is done, it is not uncommon for them to gather up the leaves of the plant, and put it into stews, or use it to ward off mice during the winter.\nSadly, I am unable to give out definite recipes to use the herb in, but I can give you some ideas.\n\n In baking, rosemary can be used in a myriad of breads--although it is uncommon for it to be used in any sort of sugary breads--that are commonly eaten\nalongside a large meal, such as stew, soup, anything with meat, or perhaps even breakfast!\n\n Rosemary can be added to a stew to help with consumption, or to give it a distinct flavor (although I prefer basil).\nRosemary can be a part in a roast's spice(s), rubbed into the meat before cooking.\n\n I've even seen it used as a garnish by some nobles, although I find it likely they knew not what they were doing.\nWritten by Gwiwen Ahverren", ""),
        StaticBook("Rugged Notes", "Unknown Scholar", "[!] Along the page you see many strange markings and drawings. They look to be rough copies, at best. There appears to be some sort of archway built of stone;  below it, several odd, circular schematics, or perhaps a map.\nNext to the map, the phases of the moon trail along.\n\n[OOC]- View in browser:\nhttp://tinyurl.com/slatrop\n-----------------------------\nAn odd name, indeed. Though, the actual device is far more mysterious and eldritch in nature. Translocators, Lori Oathcast refers to them as. Crumena took to calling them closets, as per their birthplace, the closets within Rasmot’s magical porta-potty.\nRegardless, the process for creating these translocators is a fairly complex and ritualistic one that involves both a skilled translocationist with knowledge of the subject,\nand a powerful enchanter capable of binding the spell to the locations in question.\nCreation\nAn enchanter holds the knowledge to spot. One who knows how to send matter to the void and back again must have learnt to create what is like a ‘gateway’ into the void. More than just the item itself, but anything that touches it,\neven air. Then again you do it on the other end and the mage attempts to pull the block back through the Void and the enchanter binds that to a doorway or pillar or somesuch. In short, one must reach into the Void and pull out an open space.\nMaintenance\nAfter time, it will need a mana supply, or one end will fizzle out before the other and create an endless hole. It’s advised then to have the enchanter available fairly often to refill whatever large mana gem\nor crystal you wish to power the translocators’ magic with. As far as I’m aware, this would be the only option, unless one would be able to get ahold of Kalameet’s notes on the mana obelisk. For the ignorant,\nFor the ignorant, this is a large pillar in which sums of mana are stored for use. The mana cannot be pulled out by any means by a magi to fuel their own spellcasting, but instead it exerts energy needed to power enchantments in the area.\nI’d elaborate further, though I’m only going off of what I’ve seen myself.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ruins in Tahn", "John Lyons", "\"Ancient Ruin\"    \n\nHaving spent several days and nights on this journey, I finally found it. There in the middle of a mountain range stood this God like structure!            Its outer walls stood at attention as I approached. These historic\nstoned pieces of art were severely worn down. Even chipped in many places. Moss had become a close friend of this ruin. As the centuries past had allowed them to mingle as one. This moss acompanied by the vines, covered large portions of the outer walls.\nThere were many indentations into it too. Pillars and hollows, undoubtedly made by their pre inhabitants long ago. In the middle was an open entrance. It towered over me as though it was a door built just for ologs. Like the outside the entrance was worn\ndown, and had been invaded by nature. Yes this entrance! The architecture, the deatil of it all was empowering. Enough to marvel the dwarves of the 'Grand Kingdom of Urguan'. On the inside was a rectangular garden. The exterior walls\nnow engulfed me completely. From first view trees sprung up from mother earths soil. A waterfall fell graciously into a plunge pool, which had given birth to flora around it. Though in overstock lay tons of miniature ruins. So old and fallen apart I can\nonly guess what they once were. Upon closer inspection Many parts are missing. Perhaps due to nature or perhaps it had seen some violence. Tunneling ever deeper into this piece of history, I came to the heart. A new entrance lay before me, in the shape of\nthe glass upon any chapel! Two vertical sides rose left and right of me, before joining over my head as one. Though smaller than the previous grand entrance in the outer wall. It none the less towered over me, as though judging if I was worthy to enter\nit. Now through the outer wall and passed the naturally rown garden. I stand inside. The first to meet my eye was what appeared to be a long table. Stretching from left to right. Though I may be misinformed, the ages have made any features here hard\nto recognise! This 'platform' we'll call it. Was one large block. With a slice missing halfway down all around it. Odd juts stared out at me. With countless cracks ingraved into it. Overhead this platform was an almost domed roof. The pillars on all sides\nslithered up the mountain high wall to converge in the middle of the almost domed roof. A roof, that leaves had started to grow through on their trusted branches. Which came thorugh a small hole located in the centre. I mentioned this tree briefly\nearlier. In more description this tree is enormous! It hugged u aginsat the outer shell of the ruin. This entance hall takes up most the ruin, in which I stand. Either by design or because other parts have fallen off and now lay as rubble. I\ncan't say. The only way to go was a long corridor to my left. This imitated the hall like a twin. Pillars stood opposite each other rising into the sky until it reached the roof. The corridor was much narrower than what you'd expect. Big enough for no\nmore than four at a time. Sticking out tlike sore thumb, half way down the corridor was a large area of the left wall. which had given way and now divided the corridor in two. The wall, now no more than a mound of out dated stone, was further evidence of\nhow long ago this place was built. The collapsed wall now gave a nice way into the rectangular garden. I have no doubt in time this corridor will be just another part of this beautiful, natural garden. On the other side of\nthe mound lay nothing, but the rest of the corridor. Which managed to maintain some of its former beauty, which its architects had given it. With less moss, vine and other flora, it was possible to see the end of the corridor. This was the most\nsurprising part of this ruin. As at the end stood a huge dark oak wall. How it still stands while the stone wall collapsed is unknown to me. This wood had vertical lined going down it. Obviously given to it as a way of making it more admiring to visitors\nat that time. Despite the size of the exterior walls, this ruin is mostly land covered with vegetation. The ruin itself, though having ancient beauty and unique architectural designs was less than half the area. In fear of missing something I rounded the\nruin. Climbing up the great tree, which now had been forged into the ruin. I came to the back seeing nothing but the mountain range, in which I climbed up to get here. The back of the ruin had nothing, which was most disappointing to me. Its\nouter design of up right pillars and hollows between each pillar persisted. This was what brought my exploration of this ruin to an end. Its uniqueness is like no other. Its land would make the wood elves jealous. Though not too sure what its purpose was,\nor how it came to be in this state. I can say one thing that it is a gift for anyone who finds this mysterious ruin, and gazes upon with there own eyes...                                 -Dolus.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ruins of Athera", "Layla Le'Cai", "I walk alone. \nBarefoot, over scattered stone. \n\nThe Ruins of the past towering, \nThe future around me, Flowering.", ""),
        StaticBook("S.O. Contract", "Pasquale Calabreeni", "CALABREENI CLEANING\n    CREW CONTRACT\n -----------------\nThis contract is made between the Lord Chamberlain of St. Owyn's Palace, (hereafter known as the Client) and the Calabreeni Cleaning Crew (hereafter known as the contractor. The Client desires to\nhave certain cleaning, housekeeping, and/or janitorial services, as described below, performed upon the Client's premises located in Alderburg. Therefore, the parties hereby agree as follows:\n\n1. Client shall grant Contractor access to the courtyard and\nits surroundings during regular business hours and other mutually agreeable times.\n\n2. Client shall grant Contractor access to the throne room and its surroundings during regular business hours and other mutually agreeable times.\n3. Client shall provide for the Contractor's use in performance of this contract the following equipment and supplies:\n*Keys\n*Storage\n\n4. Client shall pay Contractor a bulk sum of \$100 minas on the first day of each year for services to be\nperformed during the rest of the duration of that year.\n\n4. Services to be performed by Contractor include trimming of bushes; dusting and polishing of furniture and decorations; fixing of paintings; cleaning of bare floors; waxing of the throne; mopping;\nsweeping; and removal of trash from interior trash containers to outdoor Dumpsters or other disposal containers (otherwise known as lakes.)\n\n5. Should violence occur and the conclusion results in crimson and corpses, the Contractor will\ndiligently work to\nremove them.\n\n6. Contractor shall begin performing services on the 20th of Malin's Welcome, 1623. Thereafter, services shall be performed on a schedule to which the parties agree.\n\n7. Either party may terminate this\nagreement with written notice to the other party. Any payment for services for services rendered owed by Client shall be due and payable at the time this agreement is terminated. Failure to do this will result in total deletion.\nIn witness to their agreement to these terms,\nthe Client and Contractor affix their signatures below:\n\nX Pasquale Calabreeni, 8th of Malin's Welcome, 1623\n\nX Pepin de Bar\n8th of Malin's Welcome, 1623\nPepin de Bar\n\nCalabreeni Cleaning Crew\n\nSt. Owyn's Palace, Alderburg, The Isle of Tahn\n\n\nCalabreeni Cleaning Crew Office, Alderburg, The Isle of Tahn", ""),
        StaticBook("S.Z Res. Request", "liam_barnett", "Sarrion Zytiaear\n Resignation Request \n-------------------\n\nDrafted by the people of Skyfall\n\nRecorded by Lanavia Dreathen and Bell Sano\nThe citizens of Skyfall have conjoined, compromised, and declared that Skyfall itself, under proper and fresh authority, should indeed be reformed into a more formal, and, active local government.\nThere was a time when the leadership of this walled city had been idolized and praised, but those days have long since passed, and now the people of our mountain home fear what tomorrow brings.\nWhen one finds their Lord not only staying back and distant but also going against the very laws penned to protect these lands, there is most certainly a complication, and thus, the united people of Skyfall have banned\ntogether in hopes to push for change in the only way they see fit; a shift in absolute authority. And here, let it be stated, that the Black Dragon Reform now demands a more equivalent, fair, and representative government.\ni) Personal Leadership\ni A.\n\nAs we investigate into the legal status and unofficial criminal record of his Lord of Skyfall, Sarrion Zytiaear, it is evident that he is indeed not fit to\nserve as the leader of a large settlement, the dean of an educational facility, nor does he deserve to converse with the Kingdom of Vandoria as a whole.\nHe has directly broken laws O1, O2, and O7, and has simply not been punished by the national government.\ni B.\n\nThe general inactivity and lack of care for the physical building of Skyfall, the Society, and it’s people, raises concern for that of Lord Sarrion, as well as his administration.\nWe wish that he would be more attentive to our needs, and would filter our opinions, which our Lord has so far failed to accomplish. It can be assumed that the Society guild budget includes that of the surplus\nmade on taxes, given the decent sized population. This mina could indeed be used to fund new government sponsored social programs.\nii) Transfership\nii A.\n\nUnder the beliefs mentioned prior, the peoples of Skyfall are now convinced that someone more suited and motivated is far more deserving of the title, as opposed to\nthe current individual in power. The one that has been unofficially elected to represent the majority opinion is Lanavia Zytitear, as we are certain that her values are representative of the Society’s true values, advocating\nfor education reform, as well as a state government that encourages the free voice of it’s people.\nii B.\n\nIf, in the unlikely event that a new, carefully chosen form of leadership is not adequate for the Society or Skyfall, then it will be the duty of the people to once again overthrow\nthe then-current Lord, and replace them with another fresh, new, and competent leader.\niii) Request\n\nAnd it is with this document, this request, that we have submitted to the Scholar’s Rest, the Student’s Administration, the Skyfall tax office, or wherever else it\nmay or may not be applicable, that we the united citizens, scholars, students, administrators, Redcoats, and whoever else may support this petition, ask that Sarrion Zytiaear kindly passes the torch over to our new\nrepresentative, Lanavia Zytiaear, as we are under the belief that she may lead our Lordship and school to what the Society aims to truly achieve.\nThus, on this day of the 13th of the Sun’s Smile, 1533, the following citizenry under the names of GOD, Krug, Horen, Malin, Yemekar, the Lordship of Skyfall, the Society, the Kingdom of Vandoria, as well\nas the people of Vailor, support the resignation of Sarrion Zytiaear;\n[!] The following page is complete with multiple signatures, all done in their own style.\n- Dunstan Zytiaear\n- Bell Cranel Acaele'par R. Sano\n- Lilja Steinson Acosta Zytiaear\n- Steven Vega\n- Roy D'Avre\n- Ariselle Vega\nx. Lanavia Amakaaer Dreathen Zytiaear\n[!] The seal of a dragon is on this page, pressed onto the document, and under it, a similar illustration of a dragon.\nUpon acceptance of your resignation, please sign below:\n\n\n\nx_________________\n[!] The signing area is left blank.", ""),
        StaticBook("Salvus: Part 1", "[Ghost] The Eternal Librarian", "The History\n     of Salvus:\n       Part 1\n\n      by N. Evitan\nThe history of Salvus starts with the Oren town of Winterfell. It was the most northern, recognized settlement of man and always had the reputation of being somewhat indepent. The reign over Winterfell was in the hands of the Perea Family, after the\nSheffields had control over all of Oren from them. Since Lord Pampo was mostly absent, his wife Lady Dawn Perea was solely in charge most of the time. She redefined Winterfell from an almost stronghold like town to a welcoming and careful community.\nLife was good there, but one fateful day the undead chowed cruelty and strength like never before and tained the capital of Oren, Al’Khazar. Winterfell was now separated from the rest of Oren, not only by state of mind, but also by a belt of death.\nSince the Undead claimed the north for themselves, it was only a matter of time until they would reach for winterfell. The citizens of Winterfell lived in this Solitude for nearly half a year. Then they came... Lead by the Undead called Vardak, who\nbrought pain and suffering to the many people in the Realm of Aegis, the undead hordes attacked. The citizens fought for their home, but there was nothing to gain, but death. Just as it seemed like every last soul was to be consumed by the evil beings the\nAscended Eruza appeared and managed to hold off the undead just long enough for the survivors to escape.\n\nThe loyal subjects, not willing to leave the side of Lady Dawn, were taken in by Dawn and found shelter in her youth home.\nThis place was later to be known as the Isle of Salvus.", ""),
        StaticBook("Salvus: Part 2", "[Ghost] The Eternal Librarian", "The History\n     of Salvus:\n       Part 2\n\n      by N. Evitan\nThe survivors of Winterfell lived in relative peace for a while on the Isle of Salvus, unnoticed by the rest of Oren, which was in the process of getting ripped in half. It was around that time, when former Oren King Enor Sheffield joined forces with\nDawn Perea in hope of creating an idyll for everybody, who wanted a peaceful life. But this easygoing days would not last forever, as the Undead continued to spread their reign of terror further south with every passing day.\nThe Isle seemed not inflected, as the rest of the world started to perish in the flames, but it was soon clear that Aegis as a whole was lost. The nations started evacuating into the Verge and prepared boats for the departure of everything they ever\nknew and likewise did the citizens of Salvus.\n\nAlongside the other nations they waited for the final day and set sail into uncertainty, when Iblees raged in fury over what was once called Aegis. The boat of Salvus was not the biggest by any means,\nbut it was certainly one of the fastest and so it was one of the first to wash ashore Asulon.\n\nAfter a torturing long time on the boat, nothing could hold the people on it, once they saw the new land. Thus they set out into the night, following their\nQueen Dawn Perea and their King Enor Sheffield in the search for food and shelter. What they found was two stone structures, sitting on top of a wooded hill hinting mysterious stories from long forgotten kingdoms.\nThus the people of Salvus seeked shelter in the building, which is known today as the Palace of Solace. Day by Day, Month by Month, the citizens started the first rebuild the palace and the Keep, then building up homes for themselves and the new\npeople joining them with the wish to share a peaceful life.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sam B.", "Sam", "- Kharajyr Culture and Beliefs -\n\nBy, Samuel Beadoin\nThe Government of Kharajyr\n\n  Kharajyr, or Kha for short, have one main leader, as many societies do. They are known as Tlatlanni. The Tlatlanni selects four Kha to represent their people. The Aelkos of Faith, the Aelkos of War,\nthe Aelkos of society, and the Aelkos of wealth. Each represents and governs their particular category. For example, the Aelkos of wealth is equivalent to a human's treasurer. The Tlatlanni is chosen by Metztli, as is the Tla's heir.\nHeir to the position of Tlatlanni is the Ti'. Upon the Ti's birth, they are blessed with white fur, signifying Metztli's choice in them.\nThe Religion of Kharajyr\n\n  The Kha worship Metztli. She is who the Kha hunt for, search for, and survive for. Kha believe that they were Metztli's first and most superior creation. Later, \"apes\" were created, for the sole purpose of\ngiving the Kha something to hunt. Metztli takes the form of the moon, and fallen Kha shine as stars. Tlatlanni shine even brighter than others. Despite other races having been created for Kha to hunt, the Kha still make friends with some apes. Some apes\neven exist as Soul Kha's. The Kha believe that these Soul Kha's are Kharajyr who have been trapped in the body of an ape by Absyyl, the God of the Sun. Absyyl, in the common tongue, is reffered to as Iblees.\nSpecial Thanks to,\n\nMukar ((Adam_Barnett))\n- Upon the final page, a rather detailed and impressive sketch of a Kha is drawn. They do not truly exist, but they are impressive looking and sit atop a hill. -", ""),
        StaticBook("Sannleikurinn", "Heshakomeu", "The Sannleikurinn\n\n\nHere lies the Truth, the Way, and the Path.\n\nMay Yahweh watch over you.\nBOOK OF MALIV\n\nI. There was never a Dawn of the world. Before the Earth was Void, and in this Void lay Yahweh. Yahweh Dreamed, and so the world existed.\nII. This Vision came upon the eyes of Maliv, the First Prophet, so that he would Understand and\nspread the Truth among the Mortals.\nIII. Maliv did not Understand, however, and so, frightened by the Vision, fled his home with his wife and children.\nIV. Yahweh’s eye had not left him. As Maliv slept, the Second Vision appeared before him: Creation is\na Dream. From the subconscious of Yahweh came the Aenguls and the Daemons; the Mortal Races of the Earth; the Sun and Moon and Stars; the trees and the rocks; the seas and the mountains.\nV. Still Maliv was filled with fear. He fled to the mountains,\nin the hopes he would find peace.\nVI. Yahweh then bestowed the Third Vision: There is no end to the soul. The soul wanders from body to body after each body dies, assuming new forms and making new journeys, but it is eternal.\nVII. Once Maliv awoke from\nthe Third Vision, he stood and spoke the First Words to Yahweh: “Bugger off, ya daemon.”\nVIII. The Greatness and Glory of Yahweh then descended upon Maliv. The mountains on which his home stood upon shook, the wind pushed down the forests that\nsurrounded him, and the sky was filled with fire and lightning and rain. For Six Days, the storm tormented Maliv, destroying his home, his animals, and the very clothes on his back.\nIX. On the Seventh Day, Maliv cried out to Yahweh in fear and anguish\nthe Second Words: “What do you want from me?” Immediately, the mountains ceased to shake, the wind disappeared, and the fire and lightning and rain vanished from the sky.\nX. The Voice of Yahweh was not heard. It was not in any Mortal tongue. It appeared\nin the very Heart of Maliv. The Utterance is best understood as: “To make you Understand.”\nXI. Yahweh then bestowed upon Maliv the Mission. Maliv embarked from the mountain to fulfill his Mission and tell the Races of Aegis the Truth of Yahweh,\nknown as\nthe Sannleikurinn.\nXII. So endeth the Truth of the First Prophet.\nBOOK OF SHUL’TAK\n\n\nI. Maliv began his journey in the sands of the Uruk. He was soon captured and enslaved by a roving band of Uruks. The Uruk warriors forced him to build, mine, dig, and toil in the smithy. At the end of each day of labor, Maliv would\ncall out to Yahweh to free him.\nII. After one year, Yahweh heard his cry. The apprentice witchdoctor Shul’Tak heard Maliv’s nightly prayer for rescue while passing by the slave tent, and, intrigued, entered the tent to question Maliv about his faith.\nMaliv shared the Truth of Yahweh to Shul’Tak, and they Discussed for many hours this Truth.\nIII. Shul’Tak became tired from the talking, and hit Maliv over the head with his club, knocking Maliv unconscious. Shul’Tak then went to rest, and a Vision of\nYahweh came upon him in his sleep:\nIV. Creation is the Endless Dream of Yahweh. The Imagination of Yahweh creates and destroys mountains, forests, oceans, villages, and life. It has been Said by the First Prophet, and is True.\nV. Shul’Tak awoke and\nimmediately went to see Maliv. Shul’Tak shared with him his vision, and asked Maliv what he must do to serve Yahweh. Maliv told Shul’Tak to go into the wilderness alone and Pray to Yahweh for Divine Revelation.\nVI. The next day, Shul’Tak took bread and\nwater with him deep into the desert. He walked until the sun disappeared behind the horizon. Shul’Tak then lay upon a sandstone rock and began to call up to the stars for Yahweh to receive him. He did this for many hours until he was struck by\nexhaustion and fell asleep.\nVII. That night, the Second Vision came upon him: Receive the Path of Yahweh and share it with the Peoples of Aegis.\nVIII. When Shul’Tak awoke,a stone tablet lay in the sands beside him. Here is what was written:\ni. Thou shalt acknowledge the Truth of Yahweh as the One and Only Truth. When in times of Great Strife, call out to Yahweh so you may been Seen and rescued.\nii. Thou shalt follow the Path of Yahweh, as written here, so as to not be distracted from the\nTruth and focus on Creation, which is not Real, rather than Yahweh, who is Real.\niii. Do not concern thyself with Material Wealth, for it shall not go with the Soul to the next Form in Its Existence. Instead, pursue Peace within thyself and Knowledge\nof Creation, so as to teach thy Soul Patience and Dedication.\niv. While you walk in this World, surround thyself with the Natural Beauty of Creation, and take part in the Natural Pleasures Yahweh has Created you to have.\nv. When the sun sets every\nSeventh Elven Day, go to a place of Natural Beauty and Meditate on the Truth of Yahweh. Remember who hath given thee this Beauty and take pleasure in Yahweh’s Creation.\nvi. Show Kindness, Humbleness, and Compassion to others, but remember their Forms\nwill disappear. Do not bind thyself to these temporary Hosts, for they shall return to dust but Yahweh shall always exist.\nIX. Shul’Tak thanked Yahweh, and bowed down to praise the Glory. Half-buried in the sand, he found a slate, upon which was carved the symbol of Yahweh: an infinity symbol.\nX. Shul’Tak had one last question for Yahweh. That night, he lay upon the rock\nand begged Yahweh to explain how he could give up the Spirits of the Uruk.\nXI. After many hours, Shul’Tak fell asleep, and the Third Vision was bestowed upon Shul’Tak: If presented with a Higher Power, be it king, ancestor, or Divine, pay homage to it.\nDivine or mortal beings were set above you for a reason; you are right to follow them, so long as you recognize Yahweh as the Highest Power.\nXII. Shul’Tak awoke reassured and returned to his village. He told his master he must travel, and took Maliv\nwith him as his servant. Together, they traveled Aegis, exploring Creation and deepening their Understanding of the Truth.\nXIII. So endeth the Path of the Second Prophet.\nBOOK OF VISKA\n\nI. The Path of Yahweh, although clear, did not detail the Conduct a Follower should have when certain Occasions Arise. I, Maliv, and Shul’Tak have seen fit to prepare a Guide for the Follower in a world of those who know not the Truth.\nII. On the subject of killing: Do not kill. This violates the Sixth Commandment of Yahweh calling for Kindness. The only time it is Forgivable is when it is done in the Defense of your Life or that of Others.\nIII. On stealing: Do not steal. This too\nviolates the Sixth Commandment of Yahweh by depriving the victim of the Property they earned. The only time it is Forgivable is when the object is needed to protect your Life or that of Others.\nIV. On lying: Do not lie. It distorts the Truth and\ncompromises the Integrity and Reliability of your character, so that when you share the Truth of Yahweh, the Truth is not Accepted. The only time it is Forgivable is when the Lie protects your Life or that of Others.\nV. On sexual relations: As a\nNatural Pleasure Yahweh has given us, it is Allowable. Do not, however, place your Partner above Yahweh and the Truth in Importance, or Bind thyself to them so you could not Live without their presence. This is in violation of the Sixth Commandment of\nYahweh.\nVI. On marriage: It is advised not to if it will Distort your view of Cosmic Truth, but is Permissible should both members of the marriage be Followers. The Two have accepted they are Dust, but they wish to enjoy Creation together.\nVII. On\nbusiness, trade, and all things economic: Do not invest in Creation and its Money, which would be in violation of the Third Commandment of Yahweh. It is Permissible if the Wealth acquired is given to those who need it, not Hoarded and kept for its\nowner’s Pleasure and Satisfaction.\nVIII. On destruction of nature: Treat Creation with Respect. Cut down trees, not forests; dig tunnels, not mountains; hunt animals, not herds. Reserve areas for Nature to Survive and Flourish. To do otherwise \nviolates\nthe Fifth Commandment of Yahweh.\nIX. On relations with those who do not Know the Truth: Treat them with Respect and Kindness. It is not their fault they are Ignorant, for the World is Ignorant, and they are of the World.\nX. In conclusion: The Follower\nshould not anchor themselves to one part of Creation. Rather, they should travel throughout the World, experiencing and witnessing all they can of the growth and passing of History.\nXI. May Yahweh watch over and bless you, Follower.\nBOOK OF NEZNAKOMETZ\n\nI. I, Heshakomeu de Campari Shidari, a mali’aheral Follower, have seen fit to record the unwritten teachings of the Second Prophet Shul’Tak that he spoke of in the years before his passing:\nII. The First Vision of Yahweh bestowed\non the First Prophet, Tilur, revealed that our world never truly began, in the same way there is never truly a beginning to a dream.\nIII. Nothing can truly destroy the soul. There are magics that can trap and control souls, but never can one destroy the\nsoul. The soul is, therefore, eternal.\nIV. The Third Vision of the First Prophet and the Third and Sixth Commandments of Yahweh speak of souls as temporary guests of the Mortal body. When our bodies are finally spent, the soul moves on to occupy a new\nbody. We shall be reincarnated for eternity, until Yahweh finally awakes and our world ends.\nV. The soul cannot escape this world. Copies of a soul may find their way to realms beyond Mortal perception by performing great deeds or through deities, such\nas the legendary Hall of Heroes or the ancestral plane. However, this is not the soul; it is merely a memory of the Mortal that shall be remembered by Yahweh and in the lore of our world.\nVI. Divine beings, such as the Aenguls, the Spirits, and the\nAspects, were set above you for a reason. To serve them is permissible, if not encouraged, so long as their commandments do not violate Yahweh’s commandments.\nVII. Orange and red represent the dawn that shall come when Yahweh awakes and true creation\nbegins. Followers should wear something of these colors. It is to remind us that we are temporary beings in a temporary world.\nVIII. Yahweh is not omnipresent. It is impossible for a being to be omnipresent. His Eye wanders the world, working in events\nhe happens to see. When one prays to Yahweh, go deep into nature, lay down upon rocks or tree or grass, and chant your prayer. Weeks must be spent in this way, so that if Yahweh’s gaze falls upon you, Yahweh may hear and answer your prayer.\nIX. Shul'Tak\nonce said this to me: “You are Utterly Insignificant in the Universe.”\nX. When Yahweh touches you, you will receive visions. Yahweh does not speak in mortal tongues. Yahweh uses images, emotions, and memories to communicate. They last only for a moment;\nthe being of Yahweh is so great and so wondrous that the mortal mind cannot comprehend it.\nXI. Meditation is key to achieving inner peace, contentedness, and self-awareness so one can fully experience Yahweh’s glorious creation.\nXI. May Yahweh watch\nover you and may you walk in the Light of the Truth.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sano Burial", "Ol' Man Sano", "Armin,\n\nIf you are reading this, then you've followed my instructions thus far. This box contains the items I wish to be buried with. If you may, some sort of statue or memorial dedicated-\nin my honor within the Dragur facilities would be appreciated, but I am not greedy. I shall accept whatever burial you offer me, but please, do bury these items along with my lifeless vessel. In addition, hang the flag upon my grave.\nIt is the Felsen guard's flag, representing the freedom that the DeRolle rebellion fought for. It is in dedication to my service. Thank you deeply.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sano Testament", "Ol' Man Sano", "Bell Sano's\n      Testament\n----------------\n\nPenned on the night of 13th of Snow's Maiden, 1606\n\nBell R. Sano\nAs I grow older, frailer, and generally closer to my existential departure, I've now come to terms that I must pen my will, relinquishing my treashures to my friends and family. This document will do exactly that.\nThe following text shall be legally binding in whatever nation it falls within, as I currently sit within the Dragur Library, and internationally recognized independent structure.\nAs I continue, a series of objects shall be listed, and then whom those objects shall be offered to, may it be an individual or an organization.\n~~~~~~~++~~~~~~~\n        Testament\n           ----\n           1606\n~~~~~~~++~~~~~~~\nTo the Dragur Library, I leave the following:\n- The Fool's Sword, a blade snapped in half when it's user accidentally stabbed himself. I've written files on it's history, they're stored in the library somewhere.\n- A meteorite fragment, a rock given to me decades ago.\n- A skaddernak eye and exoskeleton.\n- The Exodus Skull, a black, deformed skull.\n- Sul'Vallel, a black dagger crafted for me by Sarrion.\n- Bokkanym's Pride, a powerful blade crafted by Doomforged.\n- A Skyfall pocketwatch, which used to belong to the long forgotten scholar, Hileia'elr.\n- A series of four pocketwatches.\n- Any and all literature written by me, to be displayed in the library publically.\nTo Armin Ambertoe, I leave the following:\n- A bag of preserved, rare, four leaved clovers.\n- A carved wooden cane.\nTo Crumena, I leave the following:\n- A set of Conservatoire stamps.\n\nTo Lefkos, I leave the following:\n- Dagor's Rock\nTo Ennulia, I leave the following:\n- The golden, lewd skull (Caution when handling it, when touched, it begins to speak on it's own.)\nTo Lilja, I leave the following:\n- A wheelchair wheel\n- A hankerchief with a golden, laced design.\n\nTo Philip Ironsword, I leave the following:\n- Golden sword\n- Aurum necklace\nTo Dunstan Zytiaear, I leave the following:\n- Chene Cognac, a fancy brand of liquor.\n\nTo Revion, I leave the following:\n- A shoe shining kit.\nTo Daniel Ward, I leave the following:\n- Aurum lion figurine\n- Toy cat\n\nTo Steven Vega, I leave the following:\n- Flute\n- Baton\nTo Nemir Valnelis, I leave the following:\n- Hankerchief with a ship design\n- Pearl\n\nTo Dirk Novokain, I leave the following:\n- Iron ring\nTo Sarrion Zytiaear, I leave the following:\n- An ebony cube.\nAll of my possessions listed here can be found stored away in my room, located on the highest floor of the Dragur Library. I entrust the duty of distributing my belongings to Armin.\nAny of my other belongings found may be dealt with accordingly, seeming however you all see fit.\n[!] A signature lays beyond on the next page, scribbled very messily.\nBell Acaele'par Rider Amuel Sano", ""),
        StaticBook("Sanoist Clarif.", "Bell Sano", "The Sanoist\n     Manifesto\n----------------\n\nAn update and clarification.\n\nBell R. Sano\nThe year is 1583, the 16th of Snow's Maiden, to be precise. I sit in my quaint, yet rather compact abode, penning this rather brief and abrupt piece of literary work.\nWithin the last two years, the Sanoist movement has exploded within the Orenian empire, concentrated mainly within Johannesburg's working class and military, in addition to a small audience within Haelun'or.\nWhile these results excite me, I fear the tyranny of the absolute monarchist rule-- It is not the concept I despise, for it is one I overwhelmingly favor, but it is rather those individuals in power that threaten my existence.\nWith Sanoism now being a relevant political philosophy, naturally, the establishment has expressed oppositon. For not only my sake, but for those who have adopted my beliefs, I can only hope that His Imperial Majesty is\nfar more tolerant in the citizenry's expression of political disagreement than proven prior. Though, for someone like myself, or the supporters I have within the Legion, would he really wish for his own\nmilitary to be executed, or treated as political prisoners? What nation imprisons their own defense force? Regardless, it is still a likely possibility, so I wish to write this while I still breath.\nThis is not an addition to the Sanoist Manifesto, as much as it is a casual rebuttal to common counter arguments to our philosophy.\nFirstly, to whine and complain about the democratic element within Sanoism is rather silly. With veto rights and balance from the Emperor himself, why should one government fear any sort of popular voting system, as\nwe've had one before, already. It is simply used as a filtration system, to align the people's values along with those of the government's. If the people vote wrong, the government is there to ensure that the correct\nindividuals are given power.\nIn addition, the outlandish argument against lack of state regulation over the church is not only childish, but arguably, heretical. To say, \"Regulation\" over the church, it is implied that the state mandates their\nmorality and fundamental duties. In this sense, it is to be sure that the clergymen of the nation do not misbehave, for what type of church is a corrupted one? We do not strive for religious tolerence\nof the politically or morally hijacked, but the purity of the Lord's children. This is not to say that we shouldn't expand the political reach of the church, or cease instituting laws based on Canonism. In fact, quite the opposite\nis true. We should absolutely impliment more laws revolving about the concept of a nationalized religion, and give clergymen more power over the law, to ensure a moral statehood. However, it is no different from when\nthe justice department of Johannesburg became corrupted, than if the church were to decline morally, as well. The national government must see to it that both, and all, departments function normally.\nFinally, one of the final points I'd like to re-establish within this short excerpt-- How can one be against funding the services which aim to protect you? Truly, only a selfish individual would be in favor of cutting aid to the\narmed forces. There is barely anything to mention in this portion of my parchment, but only children are in favor of these traditional policies.\nTruly, this is not 'Communism,' as some have reffered to it as such; Rather, this is a progressive and theocratically traditionalist movement, which should aim to please all pure and healthy children of GOD.\nI do not wish to eliminate my home city, so much as I wish for it to reach it's full potential.\nBell Sano, 16th of Snow's Maiden, 1583\n\nVolume -- of --\nUt filii Dei", ""),
        StaticBook("Sanoist M. Vol 1", "Bell Sano", "The Sanoist\n     Manifesto\n----------------\n\nVolume one:\nInstitution \n\nBell R. Sano\nSanoism;\nnoun\n\nThe political ideology of Bell R. Sano, borrowing core tenets from theocratic rule, socially liberal tendencies, and economically social policies.\nSanoist;\nnoun\n\nOf or relating to Sanoism.\nSano Law;\nnoun\n\nOfficial law enforced by the principles detailed in the Sanoist ideology.\nSano Law, or more commonly known as Sanoism, is a political ideology formally established on the 12th of the Amber Cold, 1580, though the term was more loosely used around the early 1570’s. It’s named after its primary\nfounder, Bell R. Sano, a lawyer and political scientist from Johannesburg.\nThe main focus of this book is to simply elaborate on the concept of Sanoism as a whole, in the most neutral fashion possible, and hopefully, to popularize the term. Dividing this thesis into about\nfive portions, and three volumes, Sanoism can easily be conveyed as the most efficient ideology ever devised, preparing the perfect balance between one’s socially moral core, as well as\nthe positive impact from an increased government role in a citizen’s daily life.\nThe core tenets of Sanoism aren't at all complicated, but can appear to establish contradictions every so often. Though, rest assured, should any critic tell you this, it is nonsense. Sanoism is simply\nthe belief that a nation’s government may act extremely liberal in regards to social policy and economics, yet can also remain theocratic. In this sense, it's not to fully dictate law off of any religion, but\nsimply to enforce its core beliefs, to construct a morally capable population. In addition, to keep true to the Sanoist movement’s roots, a government must also enforce democratic and liberal values, at least to some extent.\nThis would include features such as expanding social programs and the military through the use of taxpayer Mina, and returning the favor in benefits.\nFinally, a civilization and population must be, at the very least, socially tolerant, if not accepting.\nThe Sanoist philosophy worships the prospect of national regulation and order, in exchange for massive growth in government funding, economic development, technological progress, and just a general\nhub in the advancement of society. For this reason, domestic conflicts and concerns should almost always take priority over foreign ones, lest an external tension\nshould threaten the livelihood of the domestic population.\nAs opposed to developing culture, a society's traditions should remain intact for as long as they prove convenient, while simultaneously promoting diversity.\nThough, while Sanoism encourages the retainment of old traditions within the given culture, it also heavily stresses the need for education.\nAcademic education, in whatever form it may be, is the foundation for a modern and enlightened civilization. Without an educated populous, it is impossible to uphold\nthe core tenets of Sanoism, revolving around the concept of economic and social expansion.\nAs a final note, Sanoism doesn’t necessarily subscribe itself to the systemic roots of any variety of a governing process or body. While Sanoism, by it’s very nature, encourages\nsome sort of democratic or republican voting structure at the local level, when it comes to the federal and national government, any system may be installed, so\nlong as it is either for the good of the common individual, or is regulated by the theocratic moral code in place.\nFor should a total republican regulate the regime, or an absolute monarchy, so long as the will of the people are represented, it is an acceptable system.\nTruly, Sanoism is a concept which represents a dormant and untapped ideology, for those who truly take the word of the Lord as fact, as well as those wishing to embrace a new, unprecedented system of governance.\nBell Sano, 15th of Snow's Maiden, 1581\n\nVolume 1 of 5", ""),
        StaticBook("Sanoist M. Vol 2", "Bell Sano", "The Sanoist\n      Manifesto\n----------------\n\nVolume two:\nTheocracy\n\nBell R. Sano\nTo quote the scholar Baruk-Ghaz, “It is, in fact, heresy to speculate on such matters. The all knowing God was this Deity.”\nSanoism is a generally modernized, enlightened, liberal stance within the political spectrum, albeit the conservative aspect of a theocratic legislative institution. This, being the first major core\ncomponent within the philosophy, is absolutely the most conservative trait confined into the mindset of the movement. For any moral citizenry and society, they shall worship\na single, unifying Creator or Lord, whatever that may be. As Sanoism isn’t designed specifically for a single nation, the theocratic element can be interchangeable between religious faiths.\nMay it be Canonism, Druidism, or the Gorundyr, any faith may be implemented within the hands of Sanoism.\nIn this sense, a light theme of theocracy should be taken into consideration when formulating or reforming the legislative body and law system within a given society, to ensure\nthat one is not to drift apart from their concrete, moral origin. A basic set of the most prevalent and crucial religious guidelines should be installed within the law, for the primary purpose of\nsustaining the natural order of moral conduct. For this reason, the theocratic aspect of the law should apply only to those native to the given society where those rules are applicable, and\na standard shall be set for all foreigners. Regardless of who, or what, is to enter one’s homeland, they must abide by the primary religions installations, if not subscribe to the sect as a whole.\nHowever, while every civilization must stay true to some moral root, and must not stray towards the heretic and unholy path of secularism, for all three major, core values of Sanoism to coincide, there must be some\nlevel of tolerance for diversity in religion and deism. Simply persecuting or punishing those within your empire because they hold different beliefs and values from your own, or the state religion, does not exempt those individuals\nfrom the right of life. Though it may be extremely heretic to not worship whatever state sponsored faith has been installed, it is still not your primary goal to eliminate all opposing religions, but simply to preserve your own in full.\nWhile it is completely acceptable to enforce the standard set of laws protecting the currently enforced faith, it may also be true that eliminating the opposition is certainly not an option, either.\nThough, that does not excuse the fact that they are, after all, a heretical entity. To keep such in check, as mentioned prior, a standard set of moral guidelines may be imposed on all citizens, not only those\nwho are blessed to have been born within such a sacred kingdom. It is encouraged that, when creating a legislative body within a state, create regulations which are sure to preserve and continue\nto promote the faith, but only the bare minimum of such. Any more enforcement of a state religion than what is required in order to preserve it will easily oppress the minority, thus with social and economic consequences.\nThough, while it is encouraged to follow these basic outlines of the theocratic element of Sanoism, it is also advised that a nation must simply stay true to their religious roots.\nWhatever the people may have to do in order to maintain the moral order within their nation, must be performed. While faith is extremely high on the list of priorities, national security and domestic order shall presume\na higher level of importance within a governing body. Shall the drastic tensions or situation of an empire descend to such a level, it would be their immediate duty to restore the balance afterwards.\nAfter all, while Sanoism is founded on the belief that national peace and prosperity must be the end goal, security of faith and of the citizenry is a must, taking priority over all else.\nFaith prioritizes itself next, being one of the most essential values in a Sanoist civilization.\nIn terms of the church, should the state’s faith be organized enough to have such, those individuals part of the church holding power, be it religious or political, must be kept in check by\nthe state itself. Religious authorities, such as priests and the like, are to be regulated by the state, only to ensure that they remain wholesome, and spread the good word of the nation’s valued\nreligious beliefs. Should they commit a moral or physical crime, they are to be punished in some manner. The governing body does not turn a blind eye in favor of a corrupted church.\nPart of preserving the state’s faith is regulating who represents such, almost a purification process, if you will.\nAs a final note, it is important to keep to the primary beliefs of your religious philosophy. Without enforcing the major, necessary tenets of the state imposed faith, then Sanoism may not\ntruly function as intended to, and society shall crumble or degrade to the level of many other fallen empires. Though, at the same time, simply allow the flow of thought and the free market\nof ideas to operate between peoples, and various different cultures, so that the domestic nation may expand in technological and political advancements. With this in mind, simply remember\nthat whatever a government must do to protect the faith, allow them to do, so long as they stay true to the people.\nBell Sano, 3rd of Malin's Welcome, 1581\n\nVolume 2 of 5", ""),
        StaticBook("Sanoist M. Vol 3", "Bell Sano", "The Sanoist\n      Manifesto\n----------------\n\nVolume three:\nLiberalism\n\nBell R. Sano\nThe second core tenet of Sanoism, is to have a nation that is tolerant of diversity and embracing of liberal viewpoints. The primary motive behind this is to promote peaceful development,\ngiving the domestic nation a positive outcome. For example, there is an extreme economic benefit through trade that can be potentially ousted, as a direct result to conservative bigotry and\nxenophobia. Being socially liberal, or at least tolerant, is far less damaging to a society’s culture and society than some may presume.\nIn fact, the exact opposite is true, as becoming a socially liberal society could redefined and enforce the traditional attitude under a domestic nation’s banner.\nThis includes treating all four of the descendents equally; May they be Dwarves, humans, Elves, or Orcs, all have initially equal value as an individual-- Though, not as a collective.\nIn a given society, the dominant race may reserve privileges over the other, less populous races, though that doesn’t exempt them from having the same rights as the primary race in a true Sanoist society.\nThe end point is, all descendents should have the ability to coexist, there should be no racial conflict involved within the political spectrum, when discussing the four primary races.\nIt is simply tribal, barbaric, and outdated to do such, and a civilized society is capable of adapting in order to be far more accepting, not only for the benefit of others, but\nin addition, our own. Racial tension is childish.\nWith this said, it is also important to note that, while coexistence is a liberal stance encouraged by Sanoism, crossbreeding is not.\nBreeding between races is very much not encouraged, as most religious ideologies directly prohibit the practice.  Should any individual not be subscribed to\na certain faith, and uses such as an immoral, wicked excuse to continue the process of interracial copulation, that person is, by definition, breaking the first primary belief\nof Sanoism, and is a heretic, regardless of the state religion in place.\nNot only is this immoral, but for the sake of the child, it would be an eternally cruel punishment to bear an offspring who suffers from the trauma of potentially experiencing two separate, yet equally as devastating, racial curses.\nFor this reason, should the unfortunate scenario where two parents of a different, primary race produce a child, that child should not be punished or executed, but simply segregated\nfrom the rest of society peacefully, and be barred from reproducing.\nAlso contained within the liberal concept of Sanoism is education, practically being the foundation and base for an elevated culture, at the pinnacle of a higher, wealthier, and generally\nmore fulfilled populous. As a conservative government encourages the opposite, sticking only to the necessary values or skills required to operate as\na collective, Sanoism tends to lean towards the path of higher education, advocating for more academic research and specialization among individuals, so that research and scholarly work\nmay benefit the remaining less educated, yet valued none the less, working class. These developments could prove useful to all, yet we cannot\nreach this idealistic, almost fictional utopian paradise, unless the governing body of a nation is to fund these various programs.\nIn addition, a Sanoist government would allow the voice of the people to be heard. Some form of a republic, or even a direct democracy, would be preferable, only so that their will is manifested\ninto a reality. Though, in certain scenarios, allowing the people to choose is harmful. Not every common man is informed of the current world affairs, and most are uneducated in today’s day\nand age, though most can read and write. For this reason, a democracy on a local level might be the most preferable, though a people may want a higher authority to keep such a leader in check.\nThough, as mentioned in volume one, any form of government is completely acceptable, should it represent the people. However, do keep in mind, it’s the duty of the people to seize the\ngovernment should their interest not remain with the common citizen, and recreate it on more representative grounds.\nWhilst social liberalism is a good trait to have in a society, many know how the saying goes, unfortunately. Too much of a good thing is, after all, not such a good thing.\nWhile avoiding straying away from sheer authoritarianism, a civilized people can also regulate what policies are productive to a nation, and what policies are detrimental.\nSome narcotics may be allowed for recreational use, while more immoral acts, such as unwed intercourse, could remain illegal.\nIt is truly up to the will of the people to decipher, what positions are to be useful, and which others are going to corrupt a society from within.\nBell Sano, 6th of Malin's Welcome, 1581\n\nVolume 3 of 5", ""),
        StaticBook("Sanoist M. Vol 4", "Bell Sano", "The Sanoist\n       Manifesto\n----------------\n\nVolume four:\nEconomics\n\nBell R. Sano\nThe final underlying concept of Sanoism is the social, collective, community orientated concept of economics. Mina is, as we know it, the lifeblood of the universal economy.\nFew societies use anything other than physical mina as a national currency, save maybe the Halfling civilizations throughout history.\nMost strive to obtain a copious amount of mina in their lifetime, though, why is this necessary? It seems almost counterproductive to simply want to own mina, as mina\nis used only as a way to measure income and wealth, as well as an individual’s worth. While it’s a useful creation when discussing trade, or the free market, all currencies would prove to be far more useful if used\nas a collective, in a shared society.\nThe taxes taken either weekly or annually from most citizens is put towards certain programs, all sponsored by the government, or towards high profiled government officials’ paychecks.\nThe only actual issue with this process, is that the ratio between what percentage of the taxpayer money goes towards social programs or benefits, and how much is invested\ninto the personal lives of those who run the nation. It is this income inequality that a people must aim to repair, giving the common man the majority of a nation’s wealth, as\nopposed to the leaders taking up most of society’s mina for personal gain, as opposed to investing in the government itself.\nAs all these facts remain to be the undeniable truth, the free market within most economies is still extremely valued. It is moral to freely trade with other civilians, and even those from outside\none’s own society, through the use of unregulated trade. That aspect is not only acceptable, but encouraged, as the government heavily regulating the freedom of trade is oppression.\nEvery nation should make an attempt to preserve this value, albeit the issue still remains relevant; How does one fix income inequality within society, as well as fund numerous\nsocial programs to benefit the populace?\nThe answer is far more relaxed and, in all honesty, can be fixed overnight with the cooperation of the national governing body. Simply increase the taxes on the common man.\nWhile this is a concept that many dislike, and is met with disdain, it can actually have a net increase on the quality of life for many citizens.\nTaking more tax money from the people will correlate with the creation of more social programs to benefit the common citizen, provided that the government invests it wisely.\nFirst, increasing taxes, or even just redistributing them into different departments of the government, will provide enough raw mina to afford new social programs.\nThis is nearly crucial, as in an anarchist-capitalist system, those at the bottom have to way to secure wealth to make a decent living for themselves, and those at the top of the income ladder\nare able to manipulate the government as a whole, effectively creating a corporatocracy. This brand of puppetry must cease, and to do so, those at the top must be taxed at a higher rate.\nIt makes absolutely no rational sense as to why the average citizen is required to pay a larger percentage in taxes, while those that have a much wider net income continue to pay an amount of mina\nakin to that of the dirt beneath our feet. Fixing the inequality within the economy is the first step to achieving an economic Sanoist state.\nSecondly, the government must be in favor of creating beneficial programs, using this surplus in taxpayer mina. While Sanoism is in favor of offering increased funding to the military for\nnational security operations, it’s also important to note the value of other socially funded public programs. As discussed in previous volumes, an education system could prove extremely\nproductive, especially if it were free to all citizens. In addition, a healthcare program, hiring state sponsored doctors to care for injured citizens for free, not attempting to bankrupt our own population.\nWhile these are only abstract ideas, the message remains clear; Using public funding, the creation of government programs will have a benefit on a nation, as opposed to harming it.\nWhile we value the free market, not only of goods, but also of ideas, the government which represents its people must have some form of public funding. Without some national safety net,\nany given nation will collapse, and fall into a state of economic depression, which is a very real fear that we all face as a collective. Through these radical, yet very effective means, it seems\nvery unlikely that any sort of drastic economically depriving event is to take place within a civilization under Sano Law.\nBell Sano, 7th of Malin's Welcome, 1581\n\nVolume 4 of 5", ""),
        StaticBook("Sanoist M. Vol 5", "Bell Sano", "The Sanoist\n       Manifesto\n----------------\n\nVolume five:\nLiability\n\nBell R. Sano\nIf one were to read the first four volumes of this grand series, then they’d know that all three tenets of Sanoism have already been covered and accounted for. However, for this final book, it\nis crucial that one more value of Sanoism is not overlooked-- The fiscal, social, legislative, judicial, foreign and executive responsibilities of a true government under Sano Law.\nTo simply reiterate a few points that were mentioned prior, the government has quite a large responsibility. The government of a certain people should never abandon their citizenry, either\nphilosophically or literally, as such would leave them without leadership, and create a dangerous power vacuum. That is, in essence, the first and most pressing responsibility of the government,\nto never abandon its loyal citizenry, and to adapt alongside their needs.\nSo long as this is true, the question must be presented; To what extent should the government provide for the people? Instead of allowing the free market to work itself out, the government\nhas a role of accommodating for all their people, ensuring every individual is in good health, not simply the collective average. This is to say, the government must, at the very least, provide the\nminimum requirement for the people to survive, directly to those people. After every civilian is in good health, and has a stable, consistent way of life, it is then the government’s obligation to\nuse whatever surplus materials or supplies they own within public funding to support the public, may it be through new reforms, social programs, or whatever the case.\nThe next political liability the government holds to its people is mandating national security. Even if a utopia is created within a civilization, that perfection is prone to corruption, should\nexternal threats tease society’s livelihood. If a government refuses to protect the public, that is indeed, a violation of their own fundamental duties.\nThe government also has a pressing obligation to regulate the economy, only to ensure that it remains stable. This fiscal responsibility is that of the most fundamental, as without a stable\neconomy, a nation is already doomed to a nationwide appointment with Iblees. Though it is preferable for an economy to be open and unregulated, in order to allow the citizenry to trade in\nthe most moral and efficient way possible, government intervention is, more or less, required in certain depressing scenarios. To maintain the economy is, again, one of the government’s many\nresponsibilities. Should a nation enter a financial crisis, then it is that nation’s leaders’ responsibilities to temporarily prop up that failing infrastructure.\nFinally, in a Sanoist society, the government is absolutely in charge of foreign affairs. The people do not have a necessary obligation to handle the official relations with external governments, the\ncurrent leaders in place do. It would be an unimaginable disgrace to see any head of state place the responsibility of  formulating a formal relation with another larger, and presumably more\nexperienced government, in the hands of the common man.\nShould a nation’s governing body break any of these rules under Sanoism, then it is the duty of the people to, for lack of a better term, completely overthrow that government, and replace it\nwith something more suitable to that people’s needs. A government that refuses to assume responsibility for its people is no government at all, but rather an overpowered authoritarian\ndictatorship with weapons. If this is to occur, then the people have free reign to break any of the tenets of Sanoism when installing a new government, for the sake of restoring those same values\nin the long term. Though, that is not to say that if the government carries out an action the people simply dislike, it does not give them the freedom to abolish the currently standing government.\nOnly when it corrodes, and becomes abusive, does one call for revolutionary action.\nAnd with that, Sanoism is clearly the most enlightened path for any educated and responsible society. No other philosophy is superior, for it is either unrealistically promising, or contains\nfundamental flaws that have been corrupted by the mentally flawed. Wherever a nation has the opportunity to install Sanoism, it shall be done, if a civilized population wants their standard of living to improve drastically.\nBell Sano, 10th of Malin's Welcome, 1581\n\nVolume 5 of 5\n--\n        Ut filii Dei\n            --", ""),
        StaticBook("Sarrion T.", "Ol' Man Sano", "Dear Sarrion,\n\nYou may have been one of my most important, impactful mentors of my life. Guiding me from a young age when I had just lost my father, all the way up until recent times,-\nyou had taught me so many skills that I had used throughout my life. May it seem short in comparison to yours, I've felt so fulfilled with you in my life, as well as my experiences at Skyfall.\nI believe I owe you this ebony cube in return. Please, do take care of whomever it is your hold dear to you at this time. Also, good luck at your new bartending job.\nDo take care.", ""),
        StaticBook("Savoy Abdication", "Jon Renault Ashes", "I, Duke Jon Renault of the House of Ashford, loyal vassal of the Holy Orenian Empire, do abdicate all of my titles to the rightful duke, Billofrick Ashes of the House of Ashford de Bar, and afford him all of our relics, honors, and titles. May he reign\nlong and with a strong hand. Too long has he been denied his Throne by me.", ""),
        StaticBook("Scaddernack", "Dominus Eath'Lur", "Scaddernack\n-=-=-=-=-=-\nI have hunted many scaddernacks during my life, and I am to hunt more of them.\n\nGiant scorpions that used to walk amongst us normally now are rarely seen on the desert, the oldest one being Lurgoi, of the\nLur clan.\n\nIt's poison doesn't seens to be lethal, but it paralyses you. The most painful part is the sting itself, you can die because of it's great pain.\n\nIt's carapace is extremely resistant and strong, resisting to carbarum\nweapons, still, It's bottom is soft, being the scaddernack's weakest spot.", ""),
        StaticBook("Scourge, a Story", "Ebonsquire", "Scourge, a fictional tale of an Undead.\n\n((Originally written by IlumTarus))\nAbout the Author\n-------------------\nEze'kiel Tarus is a blacksmith and architect by trade, recently made Templar. He lives with his Grandfather and has fought some undead before. He does not have the best understanding of\ntheir ways, this should not be considered an accurate guide to the workings of the undead, but for enjoyment. \n\nDISCLAIMER:! I am not an Undead, or affiliate myself to them. This is merely a work for enjoyment of something\nsinister, keep in mind, is a Mature book for Mature people.\nTHE SCOURGE \n------------------\n\n\"NO! PLEASE! DON'T!\" \n\nThese final words echoed in the forest as a wicked crack was heard, for Kel'ieon this was almost his sound of merriment. For this poor farmer, this was simply the last sounds\nof his life fading to nothing. Kel'ieon dropped the corpse on the ground, next to a pile of two others . . . his family, a woman, two children. They'd sustain him with their flesh tonight. Kel'ieon grudingly sent his hand to a dismembered limb,\ndevouring flesh off dripping red muscle. Grudgingly, his mouth sank and chewed into it. Anger within each gnaw. \"The world made me this way, so this world will pay.\"\n\nKel'ieon tensed his arm to the sound of snapped branches, turning quickly\nto it. He dismissed the thoughts after a while, a sneaking predator . . . much like he was.\n\nIt had to have been six years ago, with Kel'ieon in Al'khazar. He was a cutpurse, a thief, a common-crook with an uncommon end. Kel'ieon found himself\nvaulting over roofs and shingles sloppily. \"JUST LEAVE ME BE!\" He shouted to his pursuer, whom was cloaked, head to toe, yet nimble as an arrow. Kel'ieon darted over one last roof and felt himself spinning, with no ground beneath. He flew for a few\nmoments until the sounds of crunching bones were heard. Moments after, the soft patter of footsteps fell from the sky, next to him. A hand cast over Kel'ieon's face and pulled him up. This hand was like a bear-lock.\n\"You are a foolish child to not know who you're dealing with.\" \nThe man's hood flew up and down momentarily, the words seemed to echo out, as though these words came from the depths of hell itself. \"Don't...kil me,\" these words choked out, muffly by blood\nfilling his mouth like a hot iron. \"Kill you?\" There is an idea . . . No, boy. Your life is mine now, you will suffer more.\" \n\nKel'ieon tried to recall his old name. He could not. Much of whom he was seemed to be overlapped by screams of the\ndead and damned. He heard the same crack this time, turning to face it once more. Two arrows flew out, one following another like two bees with stingers of steel. Kel'ieon reacted and lifted his staff, deflecting one to the side and letting the other go\nthrough his hand, letting the blood drip down his arm. After that, he waited and stared to the direction, a sudden roar emerged, \"You murderous, bloodlusting fiend!\" As a man iron-clad rushed at him. Kel'ieon jerked his staff forward and fire\nwashed over the man like a bath from hell. He jumped back just in time to his surprise as a sword, swung through this. He then slid back as another strike came, spinning to the side once more after. He sent out his hand to the warrior's head, the arrow\nstill pierced through. It went directly through his eye, the sword dripped to the sid as Kel'ieon leaned him back. He then slid his hand off the arrow, still lodged in the nearly-dead man's eye. He lifted his staff and looked down, but hesitated. In that\nmoment, he found himself in the weakness by his own memories. He pictured himself at his feet and bit his lip hard, letting it too bleed. He then leapt back and ran through the brush with the vigour of nature itself.", ""),
        StaticBook("Scrap Book", "Arabella Rosalie Delevoye", "* The pages are filled with drawings of Luna with friends and family. The pictures of her from all ages, from when she was just a newborn being held in Arabella's arms to playing in the snow as a 5 year old. Stories are neatly written beside each picture.\nThe book goes on for about 50 pages, a page for each year of her life. At the very last page, its a picture of Luna on the deck of the ship, she has a carefree grin on her face and is surrounded by all of the Delevoyes, there isn't a story to go along\nwith it, but instead, a note* \n\n\"My dear Luna, you may not know this but when you were born you were the only ounce of happiness i knew and had, so in that moment i named you after the moon for you were my moon, my sun and my stars. A day does\nnot go by when i do not smile because of you, and nor does not go on where i am so proud of the strong woman you are today. When the Ancestors saw me struggling, they gave me you, the best gift i've ever received. I hope one day you know what this love\nand devotion feels like, for its a blessing i cherish. I hope you know i am always here for you, no matter the time or topic you need to discuss. I will always protect you and i will always help you seek whatever you wish for. I hope this day is exactly\nwhat you wanted and if not, i'll work harder to make your 100th birthday even better. Love, Mrs. Sparkles\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Scribe's Journal", "Grand Master Lion", "The Barony of Mordskov.\n\nWritten by: Chancellor Marcus Hotchen\nLocation:\nMordskov is a barony close to Haense.\nA person can get to Mordskov when  person travels to Haense through the tunnel that eventually goes past Alrazican keep.\nYet a person needs to stop at the first \ntunnel and climb the left clif\nThen once you climb the cliff and go through the forest then you will see Mordskov.\nCurrently Mordskov is set inside a mountain valley and inside the valley is a city and keep.\nGovernment and influencial people:\nMordskov is a direct vassal of the king of Courland but at the moment is mostly left to its own devices.\nThe leader of Mordskov is Alexander Rothgard son of Luminous Rothgard.\nAt the moment Mordskov\nby Alexander Rothgard but most domestic affairs are left to a small number of people including Marcus Hotchen and Elrith Searith.\nThe building of Mordskov is mostly led by Elrith Searith and Cecila Narn'wynn though Marcus Hotchen also has a small part\nin the construction.\n\nDepartments:\nAt the moment there are not a lot of people at Mordskov but there are a number of areas that are part of Mordskov.\nDiplomacy and the military is handled by the lord Alexander Rothgard.\nThe administration and domestic affairs are mostly handled by Marcus Hotchen.\nAt the moment this is all the pfields of influence of Mordskov.\n\nYear 1611.", ""),
        StaticBook("Seal of Revion", "Siri", "This seal proves the legitimacy of The Honourable Revion Tathron, as the Ambassador of the Dominion of Malin. \n\n\n\n[!] A small wax seal bearing the symbol of the Dominion is stamped upon the bottom [!]\nSigned, \n\nSecretary of the State, Siri Ihelia.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sealed Letter", "Amelia Miles", "Sealed Letter\n\nThe following coordinates are for the eyes of the office of His Imperial Majesty regarding what we discussed.\n\n-2098/71/476\n\nHis Aide\nArion", ""),
        StaticBook("Seebo the Large", "Franswaar Kellian", "This is the Legend of Seebo the Large\n\n\n\n\n\n         Written By:\n            Franswaar\nThe raggedy old man known as Galendal the pink was in possesion of an evil artifact. Galendal knew an item such as this must be destroyed, but he alone could not do it alone. Galendal sought help from the person best suited for the task at hand, Seebo\nGalendal entered the young the halfings house, amazed that such a small creature could have so much clutter. Seebo was found at his desk reading poetry written by famous writer. As Galendal unfolded his tale of the artifact it filled Seebo wonder and\nadventure. He thought 'How dangerous could the artifact be.' 'I surely must destroy this so no harm could come to the world.' But during supper Seebo thought he could sell the artifact for quite a fortune. So in the night while Galendal slept peacefully,\nSeebo smuthered him whilst grining with his idea in mind. Unfortunatly Seebo made no profit from selling the ring and threw it in a now covered well. Seebo in his annoyance, proceeded to join the Orenian military, where had killed many dwarfs and orcs.\nThrough sheer luck and willpower (and the occasional ankle biting) Seebo vanquished his foes and earned the self imposed title of Seebo the Large, not for his size (he was quite the small halfing), but for the size of the piles of burning, rotting,\ncorspes in his wake. On the battlefield on brisk morning, Seebo found the small portrait of a dwarven family. Grief overcame the small halfing as he realized he had slain a member of a loving and happy family... and had not slain the rest of the family\nSeebo then dedicated the rest of his life to hunting the family. He deserted the Orenian military and massacre anyone that steped in his way. One such group was a tribe of Ologs. Seebo the Large came during the darkest of the blackest night and poured\nalchemist's fire down the throat of all the Ologs, except the young prince, Char'Goth, who had been fabled amoung the tribe as the strongest warrior they had ever seen. But with his home destroyed, his family burnt to a crisp, and his titled striped from\nhim, Seebo beat the Olog into eternal submission, even death shall not free him of Seebo's wraith. The 9ft Olog, Char' Goth, was taken away by Seebo to be his eternal slave.  With his new found ally, it is said that Seebo still searches for the dwarven\nfamily that had escaped Seebo's grasp, for now.\nIf you ever happen to pass the fabled Seebo the Large, be very wary, and keep your ankles covered.", ""),
        StaticBook("Self Defence", "Gerald", "-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-How to defend yourself, By Gerald, the Elder of Mellsburry.\n\n\n\nThis book has been writen to help us Mellsburrians defend themselves against biggun attack, a unfortunetely common\nthings nowadays.\nWhat to Use\n\nIf you ever want to have a chance at defending yourself, your going to need a weapon you can use to attack and parry. Most of the time a shovel or a hoe will do fine, but if you want to do much other than block your opponents attacks,\nyour going to want something that isn't designed for the farm. \n\n\nThe Heavy Shovel\n\nHeavy shovels are just like normal ones, except they are a lot heavier and can cause more damage and successfully block more attacks.\nI haven't used heavy shovels all that much, but I assume that the best way to use them is to aim for a biggun's abdomen in attempt to cripple them. Crippling your oponent usually means an easy escape and a successful self-defense.\nThe Sword\n\nI have used a sword on multiple occasions, but never really received any training in how to properly use one. I assume that its a stabbing weapon, but I could be wrong. Swords are not a weapon us halflings usually have lying around, but if you\nare stuck using one, the best way to use it, as far as I can tell, is to stab at your opponent in hope that the blow will cripple them and allow you to escape. Aiming for the head is hard to do for us halflings, so I'd advise that you aim for the stomach\narea or the legs if you are attacking a biggun.\nThe Axe\n\nI have almost no experience using an axe, so I won't be putting much information in this section. Like the sword, Axes are not usually used by us short folk. If you are ever stuck using this weapon, just attack your opponent with overhead attacks\nuntill they give up or are hit and cannot continue fighting. Make sure you do not swing so hard that you lose your balance, if you do you will be at a disadvantage while you regain your balance.\nThe Pike\n\nPikes are like shovels, except they are longer and pointier. I have never used one of these, so I don't really know how to use it. I assume that your supposed to stand back and poke at your assailent, but I could be wrong.\nThe Lance\n\nIf you are using a lance, then you are probably mounted, If you are mounted, simply ride away from your attacker. In the event that you have a lance but no mount, try using the lance like a short and clumsy pike.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ser Uhtred", "Ser Uhtred Vallberg", "A History of Ser Uhtred the Merciless of House Vallberg, Count of Lewes, right hand to the Iron-Arch Duke, the butcher of Adrimas.\nLittle young Uhtred was born in the harsh wastelands of the North in 1530. Being of a strong family, it was his duty to be a warrior for his family. He died when he was two. However it is known that his father would live for he was a strong man. Little\nUhtred was known to be of a heartless nature from a young age, commonly, he would kill the children when they stole his little bread-cakes. With this in mind, Uhtred became a strong little boy, known for his prowess in battle. He would become a war hero,\nfor Oren, killing many men in battle, he is now known for his cavalry skills, commonly seen riding a horse within his green armour. He is a friendly man, killing many in his stead, many like him, many loath him, however it is of course a great concern to\nthe elves, as many have faced his giant sword, known as a Zweihander. He would commonly cut them down and butcher their families also. This is a common trait for the good Knight. However, being a Knight it is duty to help, however he is said to only help\nthose of Human-blood. Many do not know his past, however. It is known. He was big fucking sword.", ""),
        StaticBook("Seregon Grimoire", "booklight12", "[!]\nThe book of the illustrious elf Beranabus Seregon.. It'd seem despite your best attempts the knowledge teeming inside could not be accessed through normal means as it was locked by a magically imbued iron binding.", ""),
        StaticBook("Serene Wayfare", "Berilac Goldworthy", "This will be the journal of my travel to the East. Not exactly what I would do when still being pissed at erry five hours by a bunch o' aengul choirs (weather these days) but I still should document the travel for whatever posterity it is we'll have. B.G\nAfter taking a barge to Leuvardeen, I've paid the local cathedral a brief visit, drawn by a dim chance of searching through the religious archives. While the chance has proven obvious, Fortune wasn't my lady again, and I didn't find anything of use.\nI'll take a look at the supplies I've prepped and then get going, one foot after the other, through the Amyasites' hills 'till I see the red rock over the shore and I'll be forced to find new means for sailing southwards from that point. 1st of Deep Cold.\nI've passed the Garden of Edale and the majestic fortifications beside the mighty rivers, eking ahead east. Had to get wet to get through, but at least it's not as difficult as arguing with Heartlander nobility. \n2nd of Deep Cold.\nCrossing the mt. Aeriel has proven to be the worst ordeal of this travel - at least, as of current - but the sights were well damn worth it. Coulda sworn I can see the old Akovia from here... 3rd of Deep Cold,\nNow that I have reached Ostiredge, do I truly understand that my journey - a preparation for a better tomorrow... (mayhaps a one tad less rainy) ... is at it's very craddle and as I step onto the fishing boat, thankful to Creator for the humans' kindness,\nI can't help but miss the home left way behind the cloudy mountainside.\nLate 3rd of Deep Cold. \nAboard \"Sunstride\".\n\"Sunstride\" passed the very tower of Rasmot today, or, whatever it is these lunatics galore seem to call it. Made me skin crawl, and the fishermen alltogether anxious. Can't say I wasn't glad when we finally left it out of our sight. 4th of Deep Cold.\nAfter nearly crashing the boat into a Farfolker war galley, fishermen captain ordered the crew - and his one passenger - to drop the anchor, knowing we're nearing the Isles and the foggy weather has already endangered us enough. 5th of Deep Cold\nAnd here they finally are. Isles of Serenity. Never did I think, not even as a child listening to aulder stories, that I would actually have a chance to see them with my own eyes. A place of peace, a place of beauty, and perhaps, a home for our people,\nthat is, if I am still in any way correct. \"Sunstride\" will be departing soon, so I will do my utmost to memorize - and draw - some of the things I've discovered or experienced. Creator's blessings be upon them fisher lot. \n6th of Deep Cold\nMy journey back begins, and as sorrowed as I am to leave these outlandish wonders, I still come back a richer man - richer in knowledge, and mayhaps, happiness. Who would have thought that of all things in Athera, it would be nature to poke that feeling\nback into me sorry head. 8th of Deep Cold, returning on \"Sunstride\"\nRather then keep the spot for meself at \"Sunstride\", I offered to leave closer, nearefore the de Oryden holding, so as to ensure I still have a chance to map the shores on the travel. Here, to ensure these stay more secret then the little journal, I will\nsee to it's end. I thank the captain Alabaster and his crewmates, and all the kind folks that didn't bother killing a lonely Halfling on the roads of me wayfare. God bless Gimblewood and wee folk. 9th of Deep Cold, de Oryden.\n\"O but loud they shout\nLighting out all the crowd\nThrashing onto the thatch\nWashing away every kind of grass\nRed and white all have bloom\nThere we’ve nothing to gloom.\"(In honour o' Ben Haze)", ""),
        StaticBook("Sex Deficiency", "Athelstan Aetheling", "-= The Moral, Ethical and Biological Standpoints on Homosexuality =-\n\nAn informative essay written by Athelstan the Aethling.\n\nc 1631, 12th of the Sun's Smile, year of our Lord.\nHomosexuality. A wide spread affliction amongst the denizens of Axios, though particularly common amongst those of Malin's children. First off, we must begin by asking ourselves, what is homosexuality, and who does it affect?\nHomosexuality is a 'sexual preference', although I argue it's a mental deficiency, that causes one to prefer someone of the same gender! Rather ridiculous, isn't it? Though for some reason, it seems to favour the Children of Malin!\nWhat can we exactly observe in differences to humanity, and elven kind? First and foremost, are clearly the physique. Elves posess a more feminine, slender figure. Taking after the woman more than the man. So it might point to an imbalance in what is-\nfemale and male in their bodies, causing them to stray from the default human dimorphant status of male and female. Thus entering into a femalemale and female gender diversity. This would infact, explain why so many of their men favour men. Because their-\nmen take a likeness to women more than men. Through this, we can hypothesize that the cause for homosexuality is infact, an imbalance in male and female traits. This is what would make one 'queer', if you will. Though, reader, you might still tell your-\n-selves that it's merely a condition caused by imbalance, a preference caused by a change of mind, nothing particularly worthy of the status of 'mental deficiency'. I disagree. To observe what can be classified as a 'deficiency', let's first look at the-\nReino Animalia. The Animal Kingdom, of course. Homosexuality can be found there too, surprisingly! Dogs, horses and a few other animals can sometimes don the queer's banner, just like the races of sentient folk. Still nothing particularly worthy of a-\ndeficiency, yet. The definition of 'deficiency', is a lack or shortcoming of something. In beings, this could refer to the lack of shortcoming of an ability. For example, deficient runners in predators do not survive, because they cannot perform the-\nfunction of hunting! Though, what could homosexuality prevent, you might ask? Breeding. Removing the context of civilization, the purpose of animals is to further their species, which is why they can always be seen, eating, reproducing, surviving and-\n-furthering their species existance. Homosexuality, however, caused by the afore established 'Gender Disbalance', stops you from performing a very vital function! Passing down your family, pack, murder, flock, group, etc. Disallowing you to have children.\nTo put in simpler terms. To have children is a needed function. To be unable to have children, is infact a lack of said function, thus, a deficiency. Though the lack of firmness in your gender is a mental state, which finally allows us to conclude our-\n-final point. Homosexuality is a mental deficiency. Now you might ask, how can this be treated? Unfortunately, we know of no current cure for a bad case of the queers. Though some priests claim severe conditioning, prayer and strict dieting can solve the\nplague that is homosexuality. Myself? I advocate for the re affirmation of gender identity and presence. If being queer is caused by the inbalance of a gender status, then re-affirming said status would clearly fix it. This can be done by rigorous-\nsports, training, dieting, sex with the opposite gender, albeit most likely disgusting at first to the experiencing queer, and the growing of facial hair. This would cause a femalemale to stand out far more firmly as a male, thus re-establishing his-\n-interest in women. In conclusion, homosexuality can be defined as a mental deficiency, and can be fixed by a change in lifestyle. \n\n- Athelstan the Aethling.", ""),
        StaticBook("Shades", "Triplewing", "------Shades--------------------------  I     I         I    I\n II   II    I   II    II\n  III III  II  II   III\n   II  II II    II II\n    III III  III III  II\n   IIIIIII  III  IIIIII\n     IIIIII I I IIIIII\n     IIIIIIIIIIIIIIII\n   IIII  IIII   III II\nIn the time of Aegis, a\npale and apparently evil man lived by the name of Lucas Black,\nhe acted as the leading figure of the Shades. Capable of such feats as corrupting apprentice\nof the archmage into the state known as shade. He is not where the shades\nbegan from, but he is one of the most notable people to be a shade.\n\nThese people known as shades are often deemed evil, but is that\ntruly the case? Many seem to think that the\nshades have vanished,\nand that they have.. but rumours spread.\nShades are capable\nof performing an apparent former form\nof Arcane Magicks; the      Shade Magic\n-------------------Shade Magic is magic\nthat seemingly draws it's power from a gem.\nIt's often simply called 'tendrils' since that's what really describes the\nmagic. The Shade Gem, where the shades would draw their power to perform the magic from, is very powerful, but rumours say that the gem was broken. Actually.. when it was found, it wasn't active, but it was re-activated by an Archmage.. but somehow it's\nstill broken. The shades can't use the\nmagic unless it's activated, apparently.\nChances are that it's\njust made up though.\nThe magic in action looks like black tendrils, a bit like squids tentacles. Their\nmagic is destructive, and corrupting. Not really\nsomething to seek for.\n    Some say the Shade Magic is blessed by Iblees, and therefore truly unholy. Known shades are very few though; \nIn Aegis, Lucas Black\nwas known to be one.\nIn Asulon, Salamandra\nwas known to be one.\nThey have kept themselves hidden\nor very subtle in their actions in Anthos thus far, but I've heard that a man named Adorellan is one.\n  If the Gem is currently broken, this\nman I mentioned can somehow still use the tendrils.. or maybe it's\nnot broken. The Shade\nGem on the other hand\nlooks like this:\n-------------------             [!]\nThe page has a detailed but quite\nsmall illustration of\nthe gem. Depicted\nfrom an upwards\nperspective.\n-------------------\nThe Shades are truly\na faction shrouded in mystery, but atleast I could reveal some of them.\n-------------------        Ein Sarard\n       ¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨\n   1st of Deep Cold\n   ¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨\n  Schattenburg, 1453\n-------------------", ""),
        StaticBook("Shades", "The Eternal Library", "Shades\n      ---------\n     By: Ein Sarad\nShade, the lowest point of magic, and the pinnacle of forbidden arts, is known as a curse and a gift. A Shade is not a person, or a type of magic, but a parasitic being born from Iblees, which in turn grants its host a\npeculiar skill of conjuring tendrils Shades have been documented through times, ever since Aegis. According to stories and rumours, the first caster to appear was Rilath - with unrivaled prowess. It is said that Iblees himself bound the shade\nupon him, and so the story of Shades began. A guild for dabblers in the voidal arts, The Mages Guild in the times of Aegis, got a new apprentice by the name of Rilath. The young caster became an apprentice before anyone knew of\nhis true intention, and more importantly, what he had inside him. He began learning about the arcane, but he couldn't handle the mental pressure the Shade put on him through its endless pestering of his very mind. So it wasn't long before chaos ensued,\nfor where shades go, so does disorder and turmoil. What was curious, is that the Guildmaster at the time, didn't kick Rilath out of the guild as word reached his ears. Mithas, the Guildmaster saw it as an opportunity, and soon was succumbed into what\nthe shade had to offer. One after another, masters of the guild gave in for the thirst of power, without knowing the consequences. Thus, as early as it was, the guild of magi gained its reputation for having problems with people dabbling into black\nmagic. But the balance in the guild wasn't completely ruined, since every tree has a few spoiled fruit too. The Archmage of the guild, now a man of legends, Ambros, didn't take well the unnatural occurrence of dark arts in his guild, and set out to\npunish the young apprentice. Without further notice, so he did. Ambros caught Rilath, and a heated battle took place, which ended up in the Shade getting defeated. The archmage sealed the shade in a pure, clean crystal - removing its influence from\nRilath, essentially creating the Shade Gem. A gem that held the power. Rilath, having had a taste of the power, did not simply give up but in fact stole the gem to regain his prowess. After that, shades kept popping up time after time, but the gem\ndisappeared. Famous figureheads were Lucas Black and Salamandra, who made sure that chaos was ever present in this world. Then, a time of silence and secrecy began, and the Mages Guild became more like a secret organization. Highly exclusive, and\nshrouded in mystery. Little did the commonfolk know, a lot of changes took place in the guild of magi. It was a coup of sorts, and many were essentially kicked out. Wyvernym Hold, circa 1440, hundred years later of foretold, the new guildmasters had\nsomehow gained posession of the Shade Gem.\n\n[!] A detailed sketch of the gem was on the page. [!]\n\nhttp://i.imgur.com/IhP3mFP.png\nThe guild was in shambles, and it could only be guessed what happened to it, as new shades no one had ever heard of popped up. After a small uproar, the magical community fell silent again, until word of the gem from which all shades were drawing power\nfrom had gotten broken. The shades became nothing but a rumour. What a shade is capable of, is largely of off rumours, but it is said that one shade can conjure around a dozen of pitch black tendrils. Tentacles of darkness to strangle, cut and\ntear apart nearly anything in their way. To a person unknown of this, it would appear as if they were controlling shadows. Holy magic, as per usual, clashes with the tainted being. Another effective counter for a shade isn't known. How Ambros\nmanaged to seal the first shade remains a mystery too. A person cursed with a shade has many problems however. Their grasp on reality begins slipping, as the being constantly attempts to gain a foothold of the body. Being the parasite it is, the\nshade tries to control its host, until their will finally gives in. Thus, it is a curse.The shade never sleeps, and that is why the cursed often suffer intense insomnia. The lack of sleep slowly drives them mad, and then the daemon within takes\ncontrol - with no going back. Not to mention them not being fully in control even the whole time they spend awake. If you find out that someone carries the curse, it is wise to not make them your enemy, and simply disappear from their sight.\nHowever, for several decades, shades haven't been sighted and shall remain mostly alive in the stories and rumours of old. Perhaps one day, they will return.\nCopied and edited for the Eternal Library, Snow's Maiden, 1548.\n\nIf this book is found anywhere but the Eternal Library without express permission of the Silver State of Haelun'or, it is stolen.", ""),
        StaticBook("Shades V. 1", "Lil'Khorr", "During the time of Aegis, in an age lost in many a historian's mind, a man known as Lucas Black lived. During his time, the acting leader of the Shade Clique within those lands. He was known to be capable of such feats as corrupting the apprentice of the\nland's archmage, twisting him with dark magics. The shades themselves are often deemed evil creatures, but one may wonder if such is truly the case? It is commonplace to find these creatures pop in and out of known existance, being snuffed out, or simply\ngoing into hiding. Their reappearence often copuled with rumors, dissappearences, and outright death. Shade magic is described as the manipulation of stygian tendrils that jet out from the caster, used as extra limbs to hold weapons, or\nthe tendrils themselves used as the weapons. An artifact known only as the \"shade gem\" is what is said to grant these creatures their power, if this gem is broken or destroyed, the shades will lose their ability to use the magics they internally posess.\nLegend would have it that the source of these magics comes from Iblees, however such is merely a rumor itself. During the time of Aegis, Lucas Black was said to be one of the only existing shades, their kind often kept in small, tightly-knit groups.", ""),
        StaticBook("Shady Thesaurus", "Auberon de Clare", "This tattered, handwritten book performs countless crimes against synonymisation, among them: Nasty: 1. distrafolic, respinacious, aggravatising2. sprockless, embitterious, spitoonful. Surprising: mindplosive, betwazzling, shakeastickful.\nThere are also a small number of antonyms, such as: Hand: foot, other hand, extremiosity. Hungry: bananas, pie, donkey.", ""),
        StaticBook("She Sits...", "Franswaar Kellian", "She sits elegant, gazing, whimsical as the fire sings his song\nBeautiful overcomes me with the strength of a tidal wave\nHer voice, harmonious, sweet, welcoming, softly speaks to me a fog of words\nListening, Barely. Just enough to follow along. Distracted by her features\nI look into her eyes and I am dazed\nI watch her talk and I am speechless\nI hear her breath as she takes mine\nShe strokes her hair\nI think I am falling in love", ""),
        StaticBook("Shifting.", "Helio", "Take note that I have frail information about this, the source from where I've learned being rather demented. By all means, may this book find itself to the worthy owner.\nVoidal shifting is the art of teleporting one from a place to another by the aid of the void. The process of voidal shifting is a simplistic one as it is complicated in practice. We'll start with mana-anchors. Mana-anchors is the connection from the void-\n-to the spell, this anchor's literally made of the mana that fuels the spell. Although, if the cast is not fueled with mana it will disperse, or by other means. This, isn't the case with alterationists, as they use their ability of manipulating what is --\n--already there with the connection of the void, and thus, mana-anchors. Frankly, when you project mana in a solid chunk further away is known as a mana-anchor. Now, how I understand a shifter uses their anchors to shift from a place to another, you --\n--project your mana to a space of area. Take note that this area must be on the same level as you, neither could  one shift oneself higher in the air or lower in the ground. In order to shift the anchor must be placed a distance away, with the most range-\n-of 30 feet. Here comes the uncomfortable part, if you wish to shift from the location you posess to another, you simply let your body pass through the Void and stop at the mana-anchor. Imagine the body being metal whilst the mana-anchor is a magnet, --\n--and the Void as an ocean, you simply drop the metal into the ocean and let it be attracted to the magnet. Take note that I've never tried this, and this is probably extremly dangerous to do without guidance, as you can be lost into the void. Sadly, this\n-\n-is about all the knowledge I contain of the subject, perhaps I will continue this work later on, farewell for now.", ""),
        StaticBook("Shimmering Caves", "Eyvind Darinwalder", "10th of Sun's Smile, 1626\n\nThe entrance to Ceru's Shimmering Caves are ladden with a torquoise rock, akin to that which one might find beneath the sea.\n\nThroughout the vast cave system, there are a multitude of glowing crystalin formations.\nThese crystals illuminate the cave, and, as one may have guessed, the source of the cave's name.\n\nIn the depths of some parts of the cavern, one can find a vast amount of water.  The water is likely the remains of that which carved this cave out, eons ago\nAddendum By John Lyons:\n\nAt the center of the caverns, in a like lie the ruins of what is possibly an old temple, the altar has been smashed by orcs, it's true purpose now lost.", ""),
        StaticBook("Shit and Stuff", "LilJoker90", "If you are reading this, fight me mate.\nI fuckin' dare you.\nNo balls.\n\nThis is a book made by Joker.\n\nFite me m8\n\nHue hue hue\n\nYou fuckin' pleb\nAleesia:\n\nThis bitch needs to calm the fuck down with her emotions. Goes ape-shit when she fights and shit.\n\nWhat the fuck is wrong with her.\n\nBaked beans lookin' ass bitch.\nAzariah:\n\nHe's missing some chromosomes.\n\nHe's sexually deprived.\n\n\nPesky bee.\nChirr:\n\nSome pregnant lady who needs to get her emotions in check.\n\nUPDATE:\nSHe's running for the next Mrs.Potato Head\nCole:\n\nThis grumpy ol' raisin needs to calm his damn tits.\n\nWho the fuck does he think he is?\n\nFuckin' face looks like a horse's ass.\nDakath:\n\nHe's chill. Barely spoke with him.\n\n\nShould grow some balls\nIsabelle:\n\nOh ho ho ho....\n\nThis bitch... She thinks all high and mighty, but she lowkey a peasant.\n\nNeeds to take it down a notch - or ten.\n\n*bad drawing of Isabelle with a stick\nLeilatha:\n\nShe has how many lesbian lovers?\n\nPfft only one. Me. \n*troll face\n\nBut her head is a pebble that's been through some sketchy shit.\nLeona: \n\nNeeds to get he emotions in check.\n\n.\n.\n.\npregnant ladies these days.\nMawloc:\n\nHe belongs under a bridge with all the hobos with his nasty, drug-addicted ass.\n\nHis toes are fried peas.\nRay:\n\nSome deressed guy who needs to get laid for once in his life.\n\n\nLooks like a piece of licorice that's melted on the sidewalk\nRegale:\n\nI don't fuckin' know him.\n\nRan away when I first me him.\n\nScrub.\nRei:\n\nSome lowlife who stays at the keep.\n\n\nLooks the same as Ray, but has Skittles in his hair\nTahiti:\n\nSingle father?\n\nI don't fuckin' know him.\n\nPleb.\nTalar:\n\nSome scholar who sucks nasty hairy ass.\n\nFuckin' head reminds me of a rotten pineapple\nDon't get butthurt of this shiet.\n\nFuck you.", ""),
        StaticBook("Short stories", "Aywen Morin", "The Wolf in Sheep's Clothing \n\nA Wolf was having trouble getting at a herd of sheep because of how well the shepherd and his dogs watched them.\nBut one day the Wolf found the skin of a sheep that had already been killed. He put it on over its own pelt and strolled down among the sheep.\nLeading the Lamb away, he soon made a meal of her, and for quite some time he succeeded in deceiving the other sheep too and making hearty meals of them.\n\n       The End\nThe Glow Worm and the Daw \n\nA jackdaw (a crow-like bird) once ran up to a glow-worm (a glowing beetle) and was about to seize him. \"Wait a moment, good friend,\" said the worm; \"and you shall hear something to your advantage.\"\nAh! what is it?\" said the daw. \"I am but one of the many glow-worms that live in this forest. If you wish to have them all, follow me,\" said the glowworm.\n\n\"Certainly!\" said the daw.\nThen the glow-worm led him to a place in the wood where a fire had been kindled by some woodmen, and pointing to the sparks flying about, said, \"There you'll find the glow-worms warming themselves round a fire.\nWhen you have done with them, I shall show you some more, at a distance from this place.\" The daw darted at the sparks, and tried to swallow some of them;\nbut his mouth being burnt by the attempt, he ran away exclaiming, \"Ah, the glow-worm is a dangerous little creature!\"\n\nSaid the glow-worm with pride, \"Wickedness yields to wisdom!\"\n\n       The End\nThe Ass and His Purchaser\n\nA man wished to purchase an Ass (a Donkey), and decided to give the animal a test before buying him. He took the Ass home and put him in the field with his other Asses.\nThe new Ass strayed from the others to join the one that was the laziest and the biggest eater of them all. Seeing this, the man led him back to his owner.\nWhen the owner asked how he could have tested the Ass in such a short time, the man answered, \"I didn't even need to see how he worked. I knew he would be just like the one he chose to be his friend.\"\nThe Hawk and the Nightingale\n\nA Nightingale, perched on an oak, was spotted by a Hawk, who swooped down and snatched him.\nThe Nightingale begged the Hawk to let him go, insisting he wasn't big enough to satisfy the hunger of a Hawk, who ought to pursue bigger birds.\nThe Hawk said, \"I'd be crazy to release a bird I've already caught in favor of birds I don't even yet see.\"\n\n       The End\nThe Lion and the Mouse\n\nA Lion was awakened by a Mouse running over his face. Rising up angrily, the Lion caught the Mouse and was about to kill him, when the Mouse begged, \"If you would only spare my life, I would be sure to repay your kindness.\"\nThe Lion laughed at the idea of the Mouse being able to repay a favor but let him go. Later, the Lion was caught by some hunters, who bound him with strong ropes to the ground.\nThe Mouse, recognizing the Lion's roar, came and gnawed the rope with his teeth and set him free, exclaiming: \"You ridiculed the idea of my ever being able to help you; now you know that it is possible for even a tiny Mouse to do something for a Lion.\"\nThe Crow and the Pitcher  \nA Crow was dying of thirst when he saw a pitcher. Hoping to find water, he flew to it with delight. When he reached it, he discovered to his grief that it was only one-quarter full.\nThe level of the water was so low that he could not possibly get at it. The spout was too narrow, and he too big.\n\nAnd he knew that if he tipped the pitcher over, the water would spill out before he could drink it.\nHe thought and thought. Finally, he had an idea. He collected as many stones as he could carry and dropped them one by one with his beak into the pitcher.\nWith each stone, the level of the water rose higher and higher until it came within his reach. Thus he saved his life.\n\n       The End\nThe Shepherd's Boy and the Wolf\n\nA Shepherd-boy, who watched over a flock of sheep near a village, amused himself three or four times by crying out, “Help! Wolf!”\nWhen his neighbors came to help him, he laughed at them for being so gullible. However, one day the wolf did come.\nThe Shepherd-boy, now terrified, shouted: “Please come and help! The Wolf is killing the sheep.” But no one came to help or even paid attention to his cries. The Wolf, having nothing to fear, took his time destroying the whole flock.\n         The End\nThe Fox and The Leopard\n\nThe Fox and the Leopard argued about who was the more beautiful of the two. The Leopard showed off the beautiful spots that decorated his coat.\nthe Fox, interrupting him, said: \"No, I'm the more beautiful, because my beauty is of the mind.\"\n\n\n       The End", ""),
        StaticBook("Short Story 1", "Regenald", "\"The Wizard Who Stole My Name\" By Regenald\nThe Highlander\n\nI knew a wizard, a strong one at that, truly a man of magic.\nThe magic he would focus on was mental magic I would find out years later.\nI started by telling him stories at a fire he had made.\nThere was Ale' and food that filled me quickly, I loved it all truly I did, so I decided to tell him a story of my first battle, and all of it's funny attributes.\nHe laughed and groaned, he clenched his heart and choked up food. He absolutely loved it!\nBut I was the fool, telling a fools tale, thinking that I was the high and mighty one that night, oh I was wrong, yes I was.\nHe took my name and my memories, saying he didn't want my tales to be told to anyone else. He said if someone guesses my name -\nThen I would have my memories back, who am I, I pondered to myself, and what is this wizard speaking of?\nI knew he was telling the truth, so I went off to tell the tale of the time I lost my name, asking, no begging, for people to guess just 1 name.\nI went to Felson where I spent most of my days at a bar, telling my story, and drinking my days away. \nBut one day I met a man by the name of Jester, a great man indeed.\nI told him my story and asked one thing\n\"Who am I?\"\nand he replied\nRegenald, and I be the wizard that you seeked!\nImpossible I thought he looks nothing like him, could this truly be the man?\n\n....\nI knew this story, yes I did, for it wasn't about me but it was a childrens tale\nThe man in the story was named Regenald, it was read to me when I was a small child.\nHe remembered the book for his parents read it to him, that damned wizard gave me a story of children.\n\n\n    Next page for\n         Information\nHello, I am the author of this small story or book, what ever you want to call it, I am Regenald, a highlander,  it was completely made up but I quite enjoyed it, I've really gone from Bar to Bar telling people this story but instead acting like it was -\nreal and it really draws people into it\n\n\nThank you so much for taking the time and reading my short story, even if it was complete shit,\nIf you see me around buy me a drink!", ""),
        StaticBook("Shreck's Swamp", "Daniel Ward", "A Boy Who Wandered into Shreck's Swamp\n\nThere once was a little boy named Guy DeBar who lusted for adventure. One day he stumbled across a majestic swamp, Shreck's swamp. That was a /very/ shitty decision as Shreck is very territorial\nand strong.\n\nAnyways, Shreck stomped up to the boy with his mighty orkish feet and bellowed, \"Geht outta mah swump!\" The boy stood there, his legs trembling in fear as he gazed upon the glorious ork.\nAs he did not move the fuck out of the way Shreck fucking ate the shit out of him. This is why you never go into Shreck's Swamp.\n\nTHE END", ""),
        StaticBook("Siege Weapons", "timzuiderveld", "* A fairly accurate drawing of two catapults in a forest fills this page, there is a road going between them the inscription below reads: \"Two catapults on road to Urguan, near Barbek Hold \" *\n* A detailed sketch of the Blackmaul crossing wall fills this page the inscription below reads \"Blackmaul crossing, ~1 or two guards\" *\n* A rough sketch of the Vaerhaven gate fills this page, the inscription below reads \"Vaerhaven gates, features internal drawbridge, Vaerhaven bought materials for ~4 ballistae\" *\n* A fairly detailed sketch of a dwarven steam ship fills this page the inscription below reads \"Soggy beard: No siege weapons on board\" *\n* A detailed sketch of a dwarven steam ship with a ballista on its deck fills this page, the inscription below reads: \"Frosty Axe, one ballista on top deck\" *\n* A detailed sketch of yet another dwarven steam ship fills this page, it has a big ballista on the front, and a smaller one on the right the inscription below reads \"Thorins wrath: Two Ballistae on top deck\"\n* A sketch of a sailing ship with dark sails fills this page, it has a ballista mounted on its top deck the inscription below reads \"Unknown: One Ballista top deck\" *\n* a vage sketch of a dwarven steam ship off in the distance fills this page, it has barely any details, the inscription below reads \"Unknown: Arnaments unknown\"*\n* A sketch of a ballista on the dwarven docks fills this page, the inscription below reads \"Ballista, dwarven docks\"\n* A sketch of a multiple decked sailing ship fills this page, it has one ballista barely visible on its top decks, and many ballista holes on its sides *\n\"Unknown ship, Ballista, 1\"\n* a sketch of three catapults standing neatly in a line in the snow fills this page*\n\"Kal azgoth Catapuls   One two and three\"\n* A sketch of 4 ballistae standing neatly in a line fills this page, the one on the right is far bigger* \n\"Kal Azgoth Ballistae one two three and four.\"\nSiege weapons Tally\nCatapults: 5\nBallistae: 14\nShip tally\nSoggy beard -0\nFrosty Aexe - 1\nThorins wrath -2\nunknown       -1\nUnknown       -?\nUnknown       -1", ""),
        StaticBook("Sillumir Conduct", "Andria Ith'ael", "Sillumiran Conduct and Regulations\n\n\n              \nBy the Maheral\nAndria Ith'ael\nIndex\nPage hael (3)\n  Preface\nPage kulin (5)\n  Cooperation\nPage esun (8)\n  Valah \nPage telu'oem (11)\n  Mali'aheral\nPage telu'esun (18)\n  Kharajyr\nPage niut'telu (20)\n  Avernan\nPreface\n  Our situation within the new citadel is very different from the times of Annil'sul. We are now within a new land with our allies. Due to this, the Sillumiran are in need of new regulatons to allow us to continue to\nprogress. The children of Larihei shall be safe.\n\n  These regulations shall take affect on the 1st day (oem) of the Deep Cold, in the year 1475. \n\n \n ~Maheral\nCooperation\n  As per our new agreement with House Savoie of Aldersberg, who are the owners of the land we currently reside on. We are to provide milltary assistance if they request it.\n\n  If there is trouble\nwithin their town or land, it is your duty to assist them in the removal of the trouble maker - or threat. \n  You are to cooperate with the guards of the town if required, if you do not trust them, then consider the fact that they gave us\na home.\n\n  However unlikely, in the event of a war, we be obliged to provide to help House Savoie (and House Carrion) in their battles. The Maheral is of the opinion that assistance will not be required often.\nValah\n  As we now live within the lands of the Holy Oren Empire, more specifically the land known as Aldersberg, it is going to be a common occurence to see a Valah approach the gate. Members of both House Savoie and Carrion are to be\ngranted entry if requested.  This also applies to any other member of governence within Aldersberg or Oren.\n\n  The typical proceedure for allowing a Valah entry to the citadel is simple. Simply inquire as to what their\nname is, what their business and/or reason for entering the city, and what weaponry they are carrying. If they seem suspicous or a resident of another nation other than the Holy Oren Empire, further questioning may be needed.\nMali'aheral\n  The Maheral wishes that only the uttermost pure Mali'aheral enter the citadel. The proceedure to allow them entry is similar to that for the Valah, however additonal questions are required.\nUpon the new arrival approaching the gate, one should examine them for strange eye or hair colours, excessive jewelry, or tatoos.\n\n  Examples of 'impure' traits or signs of Mali'ata include dark coloured hair, red or black coloured\neyes, golden jewlery or a severe amount of tatoos. \n\n  It is recommened you do not kill such beings, for we are not on our own land. Instead, let them be unless they continue to approach the gate after being denied.\nIf they are indeed physically pure, you may begin the mental purity test on them. The first question to ask is simply 'Thill ito kae'leh?' or 'Are you pure?' You may provide a translation of the question in Common if they are not influent in the\nElven language. \n\n  After they have sucessfully answered the afforementioned question, you may begin to ask about our society, questions such as 'Who is Larihei Lohmanih?' or 'What does the\nmaehr'sae hiylun'ehya mean to you?' are adquate questions to provide to the new comer.  \n\n   You may also ask them of their skills or occupation to allow for easier intergration into the citadel.\nIf they sucessfully pass, you may grant them entry. Though let it be known that the Maheral may overturn your judegement at their will.\nKharajyr\n  Kharajyr, much like our allies in the Holy Oren Empire, have not betrayed us. Therefore, as they once lived with us, they are to be granted entry as the Valah are.\n\n  They shall be\nsubject to the same regulations as Valah, though they may need to be protected better due to potential dislike of Kharajyr displayed by the Valah.\nAvernan\n  Avernan - simply meaning 'wanderer' or 'confused person' in our language, refers to those who are not permitted the citadel without the permission of the Maheral or are banished from our blessed society.\nAvernan include Mali'ame, Mali'ker, Bortu and Uruk. All of which, with the exception of some of the Mali'ker and Mali'ame, are to not be granted at any time. Not even the Maheral may grant an Uruk entry.\n\n  If one of the\nafforementioned beings requests entry, you may contact the Maheral for judgement of the situation or check if their name is the list of permitted Avernan, for there are few who are not associated with the nation of Laureh'lin.\nay'Haelun'or Larihei'ehya\nay'maehr'sae hiylun'ehya\n  Sillumiran, always remember your sacifice and your vows. Protect the children of Larihei.\n\n~Andria Ith'ael, Maheral of the Mali'thill", ""),
        StaticBook("Silver Tongue", "Regale Ba'ikana", "Obtain keys to the Upper District of Haelun'or.", ""),
        StaticBook("Site Report", "Sylus Reddington", "Reconnaissance Report: Beckoning Altar\n9th of The Deep Cold, 1610.\nAgent Sylus Reddington.\n\nThe following is a list of findings and anomalies within a two-hundred meter radius of the Altar, unrecorded on the briefing.\n#1, Approximately 200m North-East of the Altar, there is what appears to be an old escavation site that seems to have been collapsed, though an operational crane still remains.\n\n#2, Approximately 70 m South-East of the Altar, there is a fresh-\nimpact site. This seems to have been relatively new, as at the time of discovery flames were still burning. Impact depth was not recorded due to heat, estimated diameter is six meters.\n\n#3 Approximately 100 m South of the Atlar, there appears to be-\na campsite set up. No inhabitants were inside upon investigation.\n\n#4, Approximately 80 m South, South-West of the Impact site, located between two massive roots lies an un-named grave. Fairly poor quality, and hidden from site. Inscription reads,\n\"Here lies a woman's one and only beloved\" Author is unknown. \n\nThe Altar site itself seems to have changed durastically from the reference sketches provided in the briefing. The site seems to have deteriorated, and is mostly underground, with\nlittle to no above ground exterior remaining. The beams of light described are no longer present, though some odd particles seem to remain lingering in the air.\n\nRevisit is recommended, as it looks like things have changed from the reference sketches\nInvestigation into site changes is recommended.\n\nS.R.", ""),
        StaticBook("Skyfall Anthem", "Bell Sano", "The\n      Skyfall Rebel\n          Anthem\n-------------------\n\nWritten by Bell Sano\n\n14th of the Amber Cold, 1532, less than a year before the Skyfall Rebellion\n((To the tune of \"I'm a Good ol' Rebel.\"))\nOh, I'm a smart ol' scholar, now that's just what I am, and for the Aulic Council, I do not give a dam'n. I was proud to be a Blackcoat, I only wish we won, we won't forgive Godfrey for anything he's done.\nI hates the Vandorian nation, and everything they do.\nI hates the Lexicon of Nafis, and the Frederick Code, too.\nI hates the Royal Marshal, his sword dripping with our blood.\nI hates the winged banner, n' trashed it all I could.\n\nI rebelled with L. A. Dreathen, for six weeks, that's for sure. Was wounded by an eyepatch during the Skyfall Massacre.\nWe were safe inside our walls, and knee deep in the snow, but the Redcoats fought the Vanders, and that sure goes to show.\nBut back in '34, they left us in the dust. We retreated to Courland, before they conquered us. They died of mountain frostbite, but not our golden cross, I wish we had gotten freedom, instead of Sarrion's loss.\nWe can't raise our iron, n' chop 'em down no more. But none of us gonna love 'em, now that's for certain, sure. Yet stand up tall and strong, sir, be proud of who you are, now only a pile of rubbish, leaving the land a scar.\nI'm a smart ol' scholar, that's just what I am. And for the Aulic Council, I do not give a dam'n. I was proud to be a Blackcoat, I only wish we won, we won't forgive Godfrey for anything we've done.", ""),
        StaticBook("Small Beginnings", "Solo", "[ -- JOURNEL -- ]\n§s\nSecond month exploring the world and I have come across a castle called Johannesburg.  Its 9th of Malin's Welcome, 1587 and its a beautiful city.\n\n11th of Malin's Welcome and I have decided to become a citizen of Johannesburg.\nI am also in need of a job _ After talking to a few people I heard that Hamilton Hantley and __S__K__Y might be offering work.  I will have to talk to them.\n\nIts the 12th of Malin's Welcome and I just rented out my very first apartment!\nNote: Pay Xarkly 25 Minas every Tuesday.", ""),
        StaticBook("Smithing Guide", "Ian", "Blacksmithing for Dummies, by a (Sort of) Dummie\nThe art of shaping metal is one that many do but most are not entirely sure how they do such things almost coming as second nature to some. However, to get the most out of what you work with and what you shape in order to make extremly deadly and in some\ncases beautiful works with metal you must give it the attention like an artist to a canvas.\n\nTools: First and foremost you will need the requirements to begin working without it you will not get far\n\n*An anvil\n*Tongs\n*Bellows\n*A variety of hammers varying in size for shaping and finishing\n*Swages - Tools, variously shaped or grooved on the end or face, used by smiths to aid in the shaping process\n*Fullers - A half-round set hammer, used by a blacksmith for\ngrooves and spreading iron.\n*Punches - Tools for making usually circular holes\n*Drifts - Slightly tapered tools of steel for enlarging or shaping a hole in metal, by being forced or driven into\n*Chisels\nOnce you have that you'd obviously need an area to store it in usually a well mantained and circular in interior area for keeping the air from escaping and your fire from dying down which leads to the next topic of beginning to work.\nBlacksmithing is usually a two or in some cases three man job. A man on the bellows to keep the fire burning at decent enough tempeture. And obviously someone that works the anvil, hammer, and tongs heating the metal in the forge and shaping it.\nI have found to work metal efficently requires only two things. Heat, and Precison. For the first if your fire does not burn hot enough you end up pounding a peice of metal making no progress and wasting time. As for the second, Precison of strikes like a\nwell trained swordsman finding weak points in an enemies armor so does a smith as he works. A well trained eye and precise strikes with a hammer to find the weak spots of the metal and pound it out.\nWithout getting to in depth of how to shape metal into blades, axes, armor, trinkets, etc. They are all diffrent each artist has a style and none of them are wrong. Experiment, find what works best for you with this basic guide.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sofia Amador", "Eandyil Ihelia", "This is the tale of:\n     Sofia Amador\n      var Ruthern\n\n    as told by:\n\n      Eandyil Ihelia\nI met young Sofia some years ago and it changed my life for the better.\n\nImagine, if you will, High Prince Artimec returning to Linandria with a retinue of Sirame.\n\nHe walked past the fountain and stopped, his mouth dropping open as he saw a little\nhuman girl trying to sell something. I don't remember what it was, but the Prince wasn't buying!\n\nHer tent had been set up right in front of the Linandrian throne room. As Art began to order them to leave, a fire evocationist tried to burn them alive in\nthe tent! Her guards murdered the voidal mage, sure enough, but her guards themselves had been banished from Linandria. Myself and Aelthus Aureon were ordered to kill the guards.\n\nWhile we worked, little Sofia ran away. We buried their corpses in the\nAspectist fashion, returning them to earth in the lake.\n\nWe finished the rite just as Dorm Amador returned with his niece, a representative of the Emperor, and a small army. I was so angry that we paid them for that mess, but I owe them so much more\nthan mere minas. That's the day I met little Sofia Amador.\nIt was a few years later when I next met the young, human noble. Eleven now, the young human had come back to Linandria.\n\nWe spoke at length, talking about horses, which she loved, as well as her last visit. She didn't quite recognize me, a thing I thank\nthe Aspects for to this day. \nNot a year later she was back, again, seeking me out. Her friend needed help with horse breeding and she remembered I'd had a fondness for them.\n\nIf you think you've been embarrassed, try having a twelve year old explain\nthe wonders of breeding. I blush to think of it to this day!\n\nThe following several pages are filled with the finer art of horsemanship, breeding, knowing when a horse should be put out to pasture and so on.\nToday is the day it all went sideways. It started with a collar, almost a joke honestly. A fine, blue affair with a simple tag:\nEandyil Aureon, Apprentice Horse Breeder. If found please return to Sofia Amador at Mondstadt.\n\nThat collar led to so many\nrumors and accusations... To set the record straight, our relationship began as friendship, yes, but she adopted me as a surrogate father.\n\nYou will note that all of her children were full blooded humans. I did not then, nor have I ever, had a romantic\ninterest in the child.\n\nShe found me again, today. How did she know? I had been whipped, demoted, and forbidden to see my Meriel. I cried, I must confess, and she comforted me. I don't remember all that was said, but she promised she'd make it\nbetter again.\n\nIt's so hard to write of these events, but... I find I must do it now before my courage fails me. \n\nSofia was helping me move from Kal'Nikaer to Mondstadt when a Sirame found me. Oh, Saendir, you stupid fool. You should have let\nme just be gone. So many things would be different if you had. \n\nOn our third trip, we ran across Saendir in Kal'Nikaer. In those days, the Grand King of all Dwedmar was Torvin Grandaxe, a friend of mine. Giving my name, he was granted safe passage for\nthat journey.\n\nThat was the day he shot my little girl. \n\nI left him in the square with the king, but apparently he followed me. I entered my room, picked up a few boxes, and took the secret exit. One way in, one way out. In the time it took for me\nto load the gear on the donkeys and return, they had been arguing.\n\nSofia ordered Sae to leave me alone. He refused, so she punched him in the face. To his mind, this was enough to draw a deadly weapon.\n\nShe ordered him to leave, again, and he refused.\nThen he shot her in the leg... I lost it. I don't remember exactly what happened, only that I was standing above him, his bow was broken, and I had a sword to his throat. Sofia was somehow holding me back.\n\nIt's amusing that a sixteen year old child could\nso command me with but a quickly snapped order and a touch on my elbow.\n\nSaendir fled.\n\nWe returned to Mondstadt, where Dorm rallied his guard. We rode to Linandria to see Justice. We were met by Prince Caerme'onn.\nSaendir was to be lashed, a sentence not carried out as of the signing of this book. \n\nSofia refused all magical aid, as her people tend to do, but she survived.\n\nArtimec spoke with me and, with his blessing, I resumed my duties and was granted permission\nto marry Meriel. As promised, Sofia managed to find a way to fix every single problem with my life at that time. She was always so selfless, that way.\n\nAt eighteen years old, I was invited to the wedding of Sofia Amador and Dmitri var Ruthern. I don't\nrecall ever seeing her look so happy as she did that day.\n\nWell... that's not entirely true. There was the day her son, Boris, was born. Then Viktor, the twins Adelaide and Aleksandra, and their youngest Tuvya. At her insistance, I helped to raise her\nchildren at Metterden castle.\n\nI saw less and less of her as time went on, something that saddens me to this day. Had I been there more often, perhaps she'd have lived.\n\nOn the final day of her life, a single man survived to tell of her end. A friend,\nLefkos, told of how he had come upon her and her guard beset by bandits. The battle was fierce, but he was too late.\n\nAs she lay there, dying, she had something clasped in her hand... A blue collar with the words: Eandyil Aureon, Proud Master Breeder. If\nfound, please return to Sofia Amador var Ruthern.\n\nI went to secure her body but, of all the corpses, hers was not there. Though I have sought all of Axios, I have had no success. It is to my shame that I could not give her children the honor of a proper\nburiel.\n\nI miss you, Sofia, and wish you all the joy and happiness in the next life that you should have had in this one. I love you child, thirty-five is far too young.", ""),
        StaticBook("Son's Journey", "[Dedicant] Oo'ri Oathcast", "Forever wandering amoung the world\nTo find a place to call home\nWalking amoung his kind\nNever feeling like his home\n\nA elven maiden appears and speaks of a place that sounds of home\nHe follows the maiden to this place\nA place she calls home\n\nA grove stands tall amoung the hills\nShowing signs of peace and love\nThe dwarf follows the maiden in\nInto this place he now calls home\n\nAmoung the grove, people come and go\nThere be ones who guide others to be druids\nAnd watch them grow\n\nPatiently waiting, the dwarf stays within the grove\nMonths and seasons passing by\nA elven maiden speaks to him\nAnd wishes to be his guide\nThe test once failed, the dwarf seeks help\nLearning all he can about the tasks ahead\nThe test once passed, the dwarf is filled with joy\nCloser he can once become to the earth\nAnd make his father proud of his boy", ""),
