        StaticBook("St Amyas' Story", "Jacob Chapel", "Saint Amyas\n\nThis is the old story of St. Amyas, transscribed by Jacob Chapel from a copy on the 6th of the Deep Cold, 1470.\nAmyas, as he was known then, received no blessing from on high or cosmic message to bid him forth. This is known. A wanderer and vagabond, his travels were many, beginning alongside a trade caravan in the city-state of Solace, from whence he came,\nto which he would later return.\n\nHe appeared in many settlements, joining many a caravan as a traveling apothecary, warding against the ailments of lengthy travel and giving succor to the sick and ill at each of his destinations.\nHe demanded nary a coin or material things, but only food and drink enough to sustain himself, and the supplies with which to work.\n\nFor 5 years, Amyas traveled, on a path that many would call aimless,\nuntil the storm of battle loomed dark and thunderous on the horizon.\n\nWhen war unfurled across the realm of Salvus, \nAmyas joined with one of the few caravans that would dare travel to Solace.\nThere, the medical tents were pitched high and red, awaiting his presence. He gave his skills over to the neutral parties whose minds could not quit the welfare of their fellow man, regardless of their allegiances. There, restless for the week's toils,\nAmyas sleeplessly cared for the wounded and weary, delivering many from death, and keeping vigil as vanguard to the dying, whose chances have perished. When the battles traveled, he traveled with it,\neven venturing into the battlefield to pluck away the felled.\n\nWhen the wartime tempers cooled, Amyas quit his wandering for to watch over the city, his home of yore, and once more join with his people.\nIt was not long before the languorous agonies of Rotbrain burgeoned its affliction. A quarantine was swiftly established on the foundation of two ailing men, who were kept in a large, unattended home yet given over to trade.\nUpon hearing word of the disease and its spread, Amyas entered the quarantine with food and medicine and confronted the guards who were posted there. He was met with some resistance, as nary a man was free to see the sick, so as to curb the contagion.\nWhen held back from the ailing men, Amyas shook their grasp and forced his way inside, where the guards would not follow. There, for ten days, Amyas cared for the two, but upon the eleventh day, when he made to leave to set out for more supplies,\nthe guards would not release him, pressing the door shut. They, in their ignorance of charity and goodness, believed that Amyas had contracted the disease himself. That night, the guards set out to bind the door under boards of wood and nail.\nFor five days, Amyas and the two men slaked their thirsts on what little remained of Amyas' supply, until naught was left. On the sixth day, they went without, and in the night, when the two men rested, Amyas asked himself if his boldness was vain,\nif his mind were misplaced, and if all of this was a mistake. It was then that an immaculate light, brighter than the flames of a torch and cleaner than the spark of a passing lantern,\nshone through the boards of a nearby window and he felt its warmth upon his dried skin. Before the sun could cast its resplendence over the nighted world, Amyas endured in wakefulness to pray.\nOn the morning of the seventh day, a doctor arrived from Renatus and chastised the guards for keeping sundries from the sick, before imploring them to remove the boards from the door.\nThe doctor entered, his voice a smooth resonance from beneath a plague-mask, found and inspected Amyas and the two men. Of the two, the doctor found that the disease was passing, tapering away as Rotbrain is want to do,\ndeclaring it a wonder that they have not already expired. Of Amyas, the doctor found no disease to be passing, at all, curious as to why no tapering symptoms yet clutched at his body or mind.\nThe doctor bid the guards to leave for food and water, and inspected Amyas thrice more.\nWhen the quarantine was lifted, Amyas searched for the Clergy, aspiring to devote his life and efforts to piety and faith, in His name.\n\nDuring his lengthy service to the Faith, Amyas built a life of charity and goodwill, without want or desire,\nbut with the spark of pure intention. Never staying put, Amyas was characterized by his many travels, seeking to apply his efforts wherever they were needed, always taking note of a light that shone through distant windows in the eventide.", ""),
        StaticBook("Stars Guide You", "Erolas Ba'ikana", "Dear Zyvia,\n\nif this should find you, i hope you and our daughter are well. I'm sorry for my sudden absence. my brothers\ndragged me far north\nto the kingdom of Urguan. Where we fought along side the\nDwed, Mali'fenn, and Uruks. I fought\ncountless days and\nnights helping our \nallies before i was\nfinally able to pull\nback and return home.\nI understand i've been\ngone for almost 7 years but i returned\nhome expecting to see\nmy wife and child. i looked\neverywhere for you\nbut i found nothing. I\nprayed to the ancestors in the skies and hoped the stars\nwould lead you back to me, or to safety at least. whether you left me or decided to go\nelsewhere i do not know. I only hope that\nyou and -\nEnara are safe. The\nthought of not having\nmy family has driven me to do the only think i know. to use my axe\nand shield to help others. I will return to our home from time to\ntime. Hoping that i might\ncome home and see your beautiful\nface once more and\nwatch our daughter grow.\n\nIf you wish to find me i'll be in Ker'nor with\nthe rest of the Warhawkes. Don't know\nhow long i'll be there\nfor but it is where i'll\nbe\n\n        With love xoxo,\n     Erolas Ba'ikana", ""),
        StaticBook("Staves", "Gallidron Elindrow", "The\n          Wizard\n             &\n        The  Staff\n```~~~~~`\\I/'~~~~~'''\n\n\n            By\n Gallidron   Elindrow\nThe staff. This iconic piece of equipment is placed firmly in the minds of individuals everywhere as the tool of every wizard and mage. We all can imagine an elderly and bearded wizard, swathed in robes and leaning upon a gnarled staff.\nMost of us tend to think that the staff or even the rod and wand are an indispensable part of the mage’s arsenal. while it is in fact useful to a mage and can help to focus their arcane might, staves are, in fact, ultimately unnecessary.\nThe staff is a crutch in a literal and figurative sense. They help the often frail, physically weak, or aged mage to stand or to walk long distances. In this way they are of basic utility.\nIn the figurative sense these implements are useful in helping a mage focus their powers on a physical point in the world, the end of their staff. This simply makes it easier for a mage’s mind to form the spell\nand choose a place to bring it into the world. Magic after all is developed wholly in the mind before it becomes a reality. A veteran mage may have no need whatsoever for such a focus or aid.\nAnother use for the staff is to store a spell or spells within it to be cast when certain criteria are met. For example, an evocationist stores the spell, that summons a fireball, within their staff. The spell is set to go off when the mage\npoints the staff forward and says the command word or words. This can be incredibly useful, though also potentially dangerous. Make the command word to obvious or likely to be said, and a bystander could accidently set off your stored\nspell while you're having afternoon tea. Of course, make the criteria too complicated and you might not be able to get the spell to work when you really need it.\nThis of course, doesn’t even go into the possibility of a misfire. At this point you are not casting the spell with the same level of control you would have, had you drawn it straight from the void. The fireball could be set offin any given direction,\neven back at you.It is for this reason that a many mages will use a focusing crystal which has the ability to funnel your spell in the right direction.\nI, myself, am practiced in the trade of carpentry. As such I have made a few staves in my time. The experienced woodworker or the astute buyer of such things will note that some staves are of better make than others.\nThis, to my knowledge, affects nothing that the staff does magically. This is merely a statement of finery and fashion. A finer carved staff is simply nicer to look at and perhaps more comfortable to hold.\nOnce again, it is my hope that this book has been both interesting and informative. It is my sincere desire that you are left the better for having read it.\n\n-Gallidron Elindrow\npublishing date  10th of Deep Cold, 1519\nPlease read my guide to arcane magic!\n\n\"An Encylopedic Arcanum\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Steel Lane Death", "Edmund", "Case Name: 10 Steel Lane Dead Body\n\nSuspects: Any previous owner of the home on 10 Steel Lane\n\nCrimes: Murder..\n\nDetails: Crime scened home on 10 Steel Lane . Home found vacant and empty. --->\nBed is done nicely with blood and bile on it, presumed a dead body was once on it. But no body is there. Plates on the counter are clean, so most likely a recent owner. Cauldron dusty. I also think the suspect is a professional and organized man, since -\n-the bed was made nicely despite the grime on it... Got to speak to the Head Steward for a list of previous owners. \n- Inspector Samuel\n\nUpdate: After breaking down a wall in the basement's closet, a tunnel leading to the sewers was found.\nIn the tunnel, there were many chests. Mostly weaponry and armor of the culrpit. Inside was also various alchemist books and alchemist related items, including poison. This indicates poison was used for the murder. The stewards have no registed owners of\nthe home. Trail goes dark.\n\nInspector Nicole was led into a home of an unhinged killer, where Edmund showed up to aid her. Killer escaped. House was 11 Steel lane, right across from 10.\nThe killer was later arrested by Edmund, but after returning to the prison cell, the prisoner escaped and attacked. Edmund managed to get the upperhand with the aid of the guard, where the killed realized he was cornered.\nThe killer then revealed a vial of poison, killing himself. It's concluded he was the culrpit behind 10 Steel Lane murder due to his murderer personality and proficiency with vials.\n\nCase closed.\n-Inspector Edmund", ""),
        StaticBook("Steven T.", "Ol' Man Sano", "Dear Steven,\n\nThrough thick and thin, you may have been one of my closest allies at Skyfall and onwards. Although we didn't quite get along in the days of Johannesburg, I still valued you.\nTake my druidic flute, which I had played in that startup band we started in Skyfall, if you remember -- it was quite the ambitious goal. In addition, this riot baton, which I had used on you several times when arresting you in Johannesburg.\nTake care, friend.", ""),
        StaticBook("Stone of Metztli", "Tli'Mukar", "The Stone of Metztli.\n\n\n\n              [!]\n A crude drawing of the holy relic, suspended in the air, sits here.\n\n\nThe stone of Metztli is that of pure power. It provides every kharajyr\ntheir connection to Metztli herself. Without it such would falter, the magic she had gifted render null as they would no longer be able to access the power gained from the ancient relic.\n\nThe stone is a pure crystal of empowered lapis. Pure energy swirls\nwithin the stone, the energy the priesthood/Fylax use to master the art of\nMuun'trivazja.\n\nThoughout history everybody but the kharajyr who stood infront of the stone was forced to their knees infront of the stone. The voice of Metztli filling their\nears, turning them insane. It would be a fools errand to try to damage or touch it.\n\nBut throughout history there has been doccumented incidents where, for unknown reasons, they were able to get close enough to cause damage or even explode the holy\nrelic. The outburst of the explosion being catastrophic. In one incident the blast was so large it consumed a whole island. Though such was forseen and evacuation was already complete before the relic exploded.\n\nThe stone is also, though there has\nnever actually been any incidents so far, employable to corruption and taint. Such is prevented by the many barriers and defences that lay in wait for unsuspecting vandals or dark art users.\n\nThe crystal is also able to be damaged by\nmana\nleeches. The mana leech was able to absorb all of the energy residing within the empowered stone. Killing the leech only made it near impossible to gain the power of the energy again. A searing pain engulfed those attuned to the stone.\n\nThough while the\nstone is able to be destroyed. They may also be re-created. The majority of the time Metztli creates new ones in underground tombs.\n\nIt is the icon of power and a direct connection to the goddess Metztli.", ""),
        StaticBook("Stories", "Siegfried Vallberg", "Campfire\n_______________________\n\nA fire crackled in the corner of the campsite, projecting long shadows on the surrounding area. The light cast by flames danced across the dark trunks of trees, twisting and curling in obscure shapes and providing a\nsmall radius of light. \nThe fire itself was pulsating, the glowing embers seemed to move in rythm with the flames, matching every dip and sweep. \nIt was mesmerizing to watch, colours of orange and red gave way to yellow and white near the centre.\nWhere the emanating heat was the greatest.\nThe hills that lie friendly in the day - like the pillows of the land are darkly omnious by night. The paths that were illuminated just hours before became lost in a blackness that even moonlight cannot help. The trees that are magnificent in sunshine\ntower over me. As I step across the borderline between seen and unseen. \nChoosing not to go in is not a choice at all. \nI steel myself to keep\nmoving, my hair on end as if the forest was on the enemy side.\nThe air several degrees cooler and soon I begin\nto shiver. On my frequent stops, I listen for signs of life around me.\nBack in my home such a silence would be tranquil, here it is more quiet than a graveyard.\nThere is a castle over the way, beyond the river that divides the land of Axios. Before you clear the woodland the fortress dogs will bay to announce your coming.\nShould you be foolish enough to travel by night they will send huntsmen to ensure your quest\nends before dawn.\n Delay until you are blessed by the rays of the morning, and the guards will atleast grant you in the right to speak. \n After that, my traveling friend, your guess is as good as mine.\nWe keep to ourselves in these parts and them folk over there are no our kin. These are suspicious times and you my dear are stranger than most.\nDeath is a transition, we've known that for sometime. The individual, the personality and the memories die but the soul moves on to The Seven Kingdoms.\n It seems so strange that humanity didn't understand the soul for so long that like any other form of\nenergy it cannot be created or destroyed.\n\nOur souls come from GOD and they return to him, ready to be reborn.", ""),
        StaticBook("Storm Evocation", "Heruza", "The following is a compilation of the following books made by Heruza to save bookshelf space.\n\n1. Hydromancy\n2. Tome: Air Evoc\nBOOK ONE: HYDROMANCY\nWater: Seemingly the simplest of elements, and yet incredibly complex. Water is a necessity of life, needed by all living things, plants and beasts alike. Just as it is the patron of life, water can also pose as the harbringer of\neradication. Despite our best attempts; we are mortal. A single wave can take everything we own. A flood can contaminate food. A particularly harsh winter can be inescapable. Water contains raw power, a power that a hydromancer yearns to wield.\nA hydromancer's training stems from the evocation and control of water itself but not the water that we know. This water can only be found in the void and some say it is not water at all. As all evocationists know, their power comes from their ability to\ncontrol \"mana\", but I'll leave that topic for others to discuss. After much dedication and training, a hydromancer is able to pull mana directly from the void, shaping it into a water-like substance in our world. This connection to the void is difficult\nto put into words, as connecting to the void is more of a sensation than something that can be explained. As a mage's training progresses, connecting to the void and evoking the mana within it becomes a much simpler task. Many mages use a staff when\nevoking the elements, but the truth is that the staff is not necessary. I, for example, use a staff topped in mage-gold and carved from elderly jungle wood. This staff is fitting for me because of some of the properties that it posesses, and also because\nit has been personalized for me. The purpose of my use of a staff is to create a simple, close point for me to concentrate on and evoke water from. When the water is pulled forth, it creates a stream at the end of my staff that maintains itself midair.\nFrom here, I can move it, project it somewhere, or allow it to dissipate. One thing about water evocation that differs from other branches of evocation is that water can change states in our world. Novice hydromancers start by controlling water in its\npure liquid form. As a hydromancer becomes more skilled, they can transform the water into ice. Ice is much more suited for battle and defense than liquid water is, as it can be used to create walls, freeze doors shut, and block projectiles. I have\npersonally mastered a technique involving blasting an opponent with water, and then freezing them in their tracks should they be hit. Magical ice is not like that which can be found in our world; void ice does not melt from heat. To break the ice, the\nhydromancer must either completely lose concentration, or another mage must do something to break the ice. Water is not often formed into the vapor state, as water vapor is difficult for even the most trained evocationist to control. Water, being able to\nbe formed into almost any conceivable shape, is only limited by the caster's imagination and fatigue. Water can be suited for almost any purpose with proper training.\nBOOK TWO: TOME: AIR EVOC\nAccording to research and study, the void is a place of infinite plane of pure thought and energy surrounded by complete darkness. Since complete darkness is rather hard to imagine, think about a blank canvass.\nHypothetically, anything can be drawn out of the void if it does not contradict nature. The first steps of becoming a mage is learning to understand the void and its 'blank' concept. Meditation is the most efficient and common way, as I have found. Learn\nto blanket yourself in a blank state of mind and prepare to create your canvas. Wind and Air are essences to life from all around the realm of existance. You breathe it into your very self. With the art of air evocation, you manipulate it. Wind is\nunpredictable and one of the best studied branches of arcane magic. You must experience the element in its true form before you can even think about summoning it. In order to achieve this, I suggest moving to a place of high altitude and feeling the wind\nrush over your very body. Experience how pressure seeps through the cracks of every substance. Taste it. Feel it. Smell it. Another useful experiment is placing something in the air which can float. Watch how the wind cradles the item and gently lowers it\nback to the earth or carries it away. After you have learned all there is to know about your element, and your meditation is firm; You may begin your best attempts at summoning your element from the void. Firstly, you must find a place of peace.\nNext, use your blank canvas to imagine air, allow the thought to fill you and the energy of yourself to course through your very blood. Through combining all of this, a small amount of wind may be conjured. You may pass out a few times upon first\nconnection. After you have mastered basic connection, you can move onto some of the key spells in an air evocationist's arsenal. The first and most obvious is the force push. Essentialy, a novice air evocationist musters all of his strength for one\nforceful push at his or her enemy. Secondly, and slightly more defensive, is the air tornado. A skilled air evocationist could create a spiraling current of wind that could keep most objects out of your sphere.", ""),
        StaticBook("Strange Journal", "Septimus", "Day 1: Found a knight close to the docks. He invited me to look aroud his town and maybe join them. But The Grank wasnt my spot, seem more like a ghost town to me.\n\nThen a traveler came by and I offered me a job and a place to live. So I joined the\nSvenheld. I meet the town watch, the Lord,...\n\nNow I am working as a farmer, Alfred is my boss. The farm work is nice, leaves me a lot of time to go around the town, meet new people,...\n\nI recently got a new pet, Its called Peggy and lives in my house.\nDay 3: I talked to Alfred about making more money, he told me to try mining. I have worked hard and it paying off. Have some iron for myself, and money to spend.\n\nDren has given me some leasons. Think Im getting better at fighting.\nI meet gorgeous lady  today. Her name is Anastasia, lives in the town. She is the most beautiful creatuve I have ever seen. Her blue eyes make me feel the sky inside me.\n\nGot a deal with Alfred, he sold me a horse! Dont know much about horses...\nDay 6: I have been sick for a couple of days, winter hasnt helped...\nIm back to work, but the farm is freeze. Nothing grows anymore. Hope everything comes back to normal when spring comes.\n\nHave been doing good work as a miner in the mean time.\nDay 7:", ""),
        StaticBook("Street Fighting", "Edolin", "This is a guide for the weak and puny, and certainly not the honorable warrior. When facing an opponent stronger than yourself, there are several tricks that will even the playing field.\nIf a fight is inevitable, the first thing you should do is close the distance between you and your foe. They won't be able to generate much force when attacking.\nAim for vulnerable spots. Ears are easily ripped off and eyes can be ravaged by a simple poke. \nThroats are obviously important. Collarbones are easy to break. Groins… you understand.\nIf your hands somehow end up in someone's mouth, you can rip their jaw off.\nGravel, dirt, and sand are useful for blinding an opponent. Thanhium dust is dangerous, but provided you have means of protecting yourself, you can throw that too.", ""),
        StaticBook("Striqaephoth Rep", "Ebonsquire", "Undead Keep Scout Report \n\n((Originally written by Tyber1231))\nThis is writing of Aren Wayworn, Recruit of Followers O' Ariel (FoA), written on 28th Malins Welcome, 1214.\n\nThis report includes reconnaissance of Undead Keep, with help of FoA Recruit Glow and Elven Royal Guard Alastor.\nSurrounding Terrain. Surrounding of so called Floating City of Striqaephoth is terrifying. Large area of land around the city seems like taken straight from the Nether. Terrain consists mainly of Netherrack, with large patches of Soulsand\n, which makes movement very hard. What makes movement even more dangerous are scattered around lava pools, overflowing and causing fire hazard to anyone who is not Undead. Those pools take source from the Sky platforms above. Whole terrain is very\ndemoralizing, hard and dangerous to move about. I suggest not staying in that surrounding for too long. \n\nWays of getting in. From what I've seen, getting in is nearly impossible. There is no staircase, hidden entrance or any\nother way of getting in from the ground level. Although, during my search, I've spotted a small terrain outcropping being relatively close to what seems to be some sort of a church. Unfortunately, the gap between the ground and the platform at this point\nconsists of over 15 blocks, what seems quite impossible for me. Although, good use of magic might allow transport several people through the gap. A more extreme method of getting in would be by going up by one of the lava flows, taking source\nof the sky platforms. Someone with high enough supply of food or protection against fire could make it up the lava flow. It's an extremely dangerous method and I suggest using it as a last resort of getting in.\nDefence Capabilities. Striqaephoth is relatively easy to defend. As it would be hard and slow as it is nearly impossible to get in, several Undead could halt the entiry army. As they base their attacks on range and summonings, they can protect the city\ndealing heavy casualties to the attackers. I do not advise front attack.\n\nWays of attack. Based on my eariler statements, I suggest either using Commandos, who might clear the gap of about 10-15 blocks.\nOther, more reliable way would be using spies or double-agents. They could attempt to take over the city or eiliminate the Undead, who would be focused in fighting off the attackers. In case of that scenario, frontal attact would be a distraction.\nOf course, it might happen that spies will join the enemy or they will be tortured and forced to tell the plan of attack. All ways of attack I stated are dangerous and would have a high risk of failing.\nConclusion. Concluding my report, I strongy suggest using small group of people, who would attempt to take over the city. I strongly disapprove a frontal attack.\n\nThis is a work of an amateur, who based his work on visial recognition\nand his suggestions and predictions. It might vary from the official reports (if there are any), but I believe it is correct, as I wrote what seemed reasonable and real.\n\nThis report is recommended for\nfuture use, in case of assault on the Floating City.", ""),
        StaticBook("Study of Magic", "Toxzero", "Foreword:\nIt’s really no question that our world was forged in the ways of a greater ancient magic through voidal influence as we’re so tightly tethered to the void in which those who dedicate their lives to the study of the arcane draw their powers\nfrom can even feel any massive differences in the void. It is in my studies of recent times that everything was created and shaped by will, which brings life to the world with such an influx of mana,\nallowing people who study the arts of transfiguration to be able to shift the world as they please so long it follows equivalent exchange of course.\n“Voidal Tethering”\nOur world is so heavily influenced by the void that a lot of people don’t realize it, every action leaves a shift in the void. Our realm is tethered closely to the voidal realm, everything having dormant mana and the\ndescendants having the scar which acts as our gateway to the voidal influence goes to show such. Mana is simply our bridges to influence the void and summon forth powers that don’t even come close to match the ancient magic before our time,\nand all of this sums up to a fact of voidal tethering.\nMana’s Influence:\nEvery action from walking, to cooking, sword play and especially casting spells let them be voidal or deity, mana is consumed. Once we discovered how much influence we have over our mana we were able to create bridges\nto the void with them, and summon forth anything we could imagine, so long it followed equivalent exchange of course. Deity subjects summon the powers of the gods through a bridge created through the soul using mana,\nallowing them to summon forth the spell so long their bridge is held. Voidal users are able to summon forth arcane spells through the tear in their soul into the void rift, the bridge created and sustained by mana as they draw forth\nthe endless powers of nothingness. This goes to show that anything and everything has mana that influences us, infact without such there would be no life.\nOn Deity Users:\nDeity users are people who devote their lives to the gods, or as many call them aungles or daemons. It is proven fact that these gods have direct influence on our realm, with powers unbelievable to very thought,\nand as every god is they are greedy for more. Subjects under these gods are considered Deity users, who summon forth the ability of their deity through a bond created by being synced to your deity,\nthis bond is embedded into the soul and becomes your gateway for summoning those powers. Like all spells there is a bridge formed through mana in which allows them to draw forth the powers to our realm, so long that bridge is held.\nOn Voidal Users:\nEvery descendant has a scar inside of their soul that tethers us to the void, once tapped into and synced with the void they gain the ability to see aura and the like. Voidal users are actually little to no different to those\nwho worship gods, only they summon forth power through self will and imagination, knowledge purely and it’s not handed down to them. They create a bridge from themselves to the voidal realm,\nin which they influence the power in that realm to create the spell they so wish to desire to summon dependent on the school of magic they study, and bring forth the spell to our realm to cast such spell.\nWritten by Sarrion Di'Pascali.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sub-Lightning E.", "[Ghost] The Eternal Librarian", "The Practicality\n    of Applied\n   Sub-Lightning\n      Energies\n\n   by Lucion Sullas\nThis dissertation is primarily to argue the theoretical uses for applied sub-lightning energy (electricity) in comparison with conventional redstone devices. I use this comparison mainly due to the stark similarities in behaviour of these two\nenergies, and as redstone is the incumbent method of energy-transference, anything less beneficial has no practical purpose.\nFirstly, we shall consider the application of light. Redstone lanterns are highly efficient in their ability to dim and light glowstone clumps. These \"lanterns\" appear to contain limitless energy, despite not being connected with a redstone \"torch\"\n(strengthening the theory of redstone being a magical material, which will be discussed in a further volume). Lightning does not have this ability, as currently the only light that may be generated are sourced from electrical discharges (sparks). Were\nthese discharges made to be consistent in both intensity and length, then perhaps they could be applicable. Though, the energy requirements would still be far too difficult to gather to make such an idea viable.\nSecondly, we shall consider the application of it being a source of power. Redstone (due to its hypothetical magical capabilities) is able to activate mechanisms from afar, simply by connecting it to a \"torch.\" An electrical surge is not capable of\ndoing such a thing--it requires proper guidance across various metals to have its energies travel. And even so, one cannot fathom how sub-lightning would be capable of moving objects in the same manner as redstone.\nLastly, we shall consider the possible weaponization of the energy. Redstone, for all its uses, has a charge that is inherently harmless to any and all who would dig about in its varying dusts. However, lightning is far, far more dangerous to the\ncasual user, with even relatively small charges causing intense pain, spasms, and burns. Were there a method of containment for this resource, then further study could be performed. Until then, general observations in storms are our only option.\nMaehr'sae hiylun'ehya.", ""),
        StaticBook("Submission", "Salamandra", "I had known of the existence of the Mori’Quessir in Asulon, yet it was not until after the fact that I was informed of the language they had spoken, unlike any other. As one who delves into Lexicology on a regular basis and prides-\nhimself in being able to speak many languages, I sought the want to learn their language as well. I found it necessary to learn what I could about the race as a whole, aside from only studying the language.\nUpon scouring libraries and shops for tomes on the subject, I managed to find very few, but enough to sate my hunger nonetheless. I learned of a Deity they worshipped called Nemiisae from a poem I had bought, and of the Mori’s affinity-\nor closeness with spiders. I am not sure if it is correct for me to use the past tense when speaking of the Mori for they may still be alive, but for the sake of this minor introduction I hope the reader will condone it.\nThe Mori’s society was matriarchal, in the way that women had power over men and were allowed to have multiple slaves. After managing to track down a man who was once a slave to the Mori’Quessir, we came to the agreement that he-\nwould teach the language to me. I will include very basic words on the following pages, accompanied by three full sentences. If all words are memorized and an individual wishes to learn more, they are welcome to confront the author on the subject.\nUsstan = I/myself :  ussta = my\n\nL' = the\n\nKaas = name\n\nZhah = is\n\nXanalress = language\n\nTlun = am\nAglla = trying\n\nUlu = to\n\nScrea = learn\n\nY'sik = rather\n\nXull = difficult\n\nXal = may\n\nNaut = not\nTelanth = say\n\nWiles = words\n\nListrane = properly\n\nJhal = but\n\nShlu'ta = can\n\nInbau = get\n\nWun = in\nOl = it\n\nSevir = leave\n\nXuz = end\n\nElgg = kill\n\nSample sentences will follow.\nVendui ussta kaas zhah Izier. - Hello my name is Izier.\n\nL'xanalress Usstan tlun aglla ulu screa zhah y'sik xull.  - The language I am trying to learn is rather difficult.\nUsstan xal naut telanth l'wiles listrane jhal UssItan shlu'ta inbau ol wun l'xuz. - \n I may not say the words properly but I can get it in the end.", ""),
        StaticBook("Suffer", "Gurak'Yar", "Suffer , suffer is  pain , pain is suffer\nAll afflictions come from Krug himzelf ..\nThe pain I'm feeling now is harsh but it's slowly passing as i'm not thinking about it .. Meditation helps as pain is temporary .. It may last for a moment , day or\na week but adventually it will pass .. There is no such thing as pain , pain is just an diversion from everything as it's not real", ""),
        StaticBook("Sul'Vallel", "Bell Sano", "1549\n\nSul'Vallel\n\nDonated and created by Sarrion Zytiaear\nThe Sul'Vallel is a short, black dagger, hand crafted by Sarrion Zytiaear. The hilt is made from the finest of windswept wood, and the blade is black ferrum, designed for swiftly killing another being.\nThe dagger has it's own special ability. Upon the user rubbing the hilt with his thumb, the dagger will emmit a strong, blue light. Markings will inscribe itself on the metal of the blade, and magelight will activate.\nThe light would be more than enough to fill a dark room with a bright light, or an open area of any sort. It's useful for a makeshift torch, but it's mana drains rather quickly.\nTo deactivate it, simply rub the hilt again, and the dagger will stop glowing, returning to it's black ferrum state. After about three uses, the mana gem will need to be re-imbued.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sullasian S", "Lucion Sullas", "The Sullasian Stack\nby Lucion Sullas\nWriter's note: Should this book be found anywhere but the Eternal Library of Lin'evaral, then it is stolen. Perpetrators purchasing or selling this volume without the express permission of a Medi'ir of Haelun'or will be caught and punished severely.\nOne of many old technological marvels I have created in my century of habitation with the exalted Mali'aheral is the device by which one can create small amounts of artificial lighting (or \"sub-lightning\" as is the proper term).\nOne would usually go on to explain the methods by which he created such a device, but this tome is but a guide for its creation, and not so much its uses. Let us end, then, this frivolous banter, and begin the instruction.\n-Ingredients-\n\nFirst, one advises you to retrieve the items required for the stack's creation prior to reading the instructions (the reader may appreciate the logic in such a decision). Firstly, you will need a smith to smelt and shape\nmetallic \"discs\" or \"plates\" of a flat variety. The size of said plates is not especially important, but they must be uniform in their appearance and diameter. The plates themselves are made of two metals often mixed together for use in brass implements--\ncopper, and spelter (One would suggest inquiring about the material at your local smithery). There must be equal numbers of said plates for use in the device. Note that the more plates that are available, the more powerful the device's effect will be.\nSecondly, a number of other metallic parts will be required for the device's construction--namely two strips of copper (no thicker than the width of a finger) and two iron prongs roughly of the same width. The prongs will need to be joined at the end of\neach copper strip. One suggests leather strips to be best for binding the two. Thirdly, one will require lengths of cloth (preferably wool or cotton) as well as a bottle of brine water. The cloth must be ripped into smaller lengths approximately the size\nof the copper and spelter plates. Optionally, one may create an upright \"stand\" for these plates to be housed in. It is not necessary, but it makes moving the device and holding it in place far more simple.\nMethod\n\nFirstly (provided you have built the stand), place the (non-pronged) end of a copper strip upon the bottom of the stand. After this, place the first of your copper plates upon it, and then place a spelter plate atop the copper one.\nYou shall then take one of your pre-organised lengths of cloth, and douse it liberally with the brine-water. Once it is thoroughly drenched, place this upon the spelter plate. This copper-spelter-brine rag is referred to by mysekf as a \"unit.\"\nThe effect of the stack increases as you add further units. One suggests at least ten before performing the final step. After you have placed the appropriate number of units, place the second copper-prong between the final copper and spelter plates.\nThis is out of practicality rather than garnering the best effect, as you would doubtlessly desire to keep the strip from moving around. The stack is now ready for use.\nOperation\n\nNever, under any circumstances, touch both prongs with your bare hands, nor should you attempt to hold the stack with more than one bare hand. The stack is a facinating device, but the pain of accidentally shocking oneself is not\nparticularly pleasant. Always wear proper protection at all times while operating it. This includes: clamps to hold the prongs, thick leather gloves for your hands, and at least a leather apron to protect yourself from any other accidents.\nAlways apply the two prongs directly to your target, or there will be no effect.\n              ---------", ""),
        StaticBook("Sullasian Stack", "[Ghost] The Eternal Librarian", "The Sullasian Stack\n\n   by Lucion Sullas\nOne of many old technological marvels I have created in my century of habitation with the exalted mali'aheral is the device by which one can create small amounts of artificial lighting (or \"sub-lightning\" as is the proper term). One would usually go\non to explain the methods by which he created such a device, but this tome is but a guide for its creation, and not so much its uses. Let us end, then, this frivolous banter, and begin the instruction.\nIngredients\nFirst, one advises you to retrieve the items required for the stack's creation prior to reading the instructions (the reader may appreciate the logic in such a decision). Firstly, you will need a smith to smelt and shape metallic \"discs\"\nor \"plates\" of a flat variety. The size of said plates is not especially important, but they must be uniform in their appearance and diameter. The plates themselves are made of two metals often mixed together for use in brass implements - copper, and\nspelter (One would suggest inquiring about the material at your local smithery). There must be equal numbers of said plates for use in the device. Note that the more plates that are available, the more powerful the device's effect will be.\nSecondly, a number of other metallic parts will be required for the device's construction--namely two strips of copper (no thicker than the width of a finger) and two iron prongs roughly of the same width. The prongs will need to be joined at the end of\neach copper strip. One suggests leather strips to be best for binding the two. Thirdly, one will require lengths of cloth (preferably wool or cotton) as well as a bottle of brine water. The cloth must be ripped into smaller lengths approximately the size\nof the copper and spelter plates. Optionally, one may create an upright \"stand\" for these plates to be housed in. It is not necessary, but it makes moving the device and holding it in place far more simple.\nMethod\nFirstly (provided you have built the stand), place the (non-pronged) end of a copper strip upon the bottom of the stand. After this, place the first of your copper plates upon it, and then place a spelter plate atop the copper one. You shall\nthen take one of your pre-organised lengths of cloth, and douse it liberally with the brine-water. Once it is thoroughly drenched, place this upon the spelter plate. This copper-spelter-brine rag is referred to by myself as a \"unit.\" The effect of the\nstack increases as you add further units. One suggests at least ten before performing the final step. After you have placed the appropriate number of units, place the second copper-prong between the final copper and spelter plates. This is out of\npracticality rather than garnering the best effect, as you would doubtlessly desire to keep the strip from moving around. The stack is now ready for use.\nOperation\nNever, under any circumstances, touch both prongs with your bare hands, nor should you attempt to hold the stack with more than one bare hand. The stack is a fascinating device, but the pain of accidentally shocking oneself is not\nparticularly pleasant. Always wear proper protection at all times while operating it. This includes: clamps to hold the prongs, thick leather gloves for your hands, and at least a leather apron to protect yourself from any other accidents. Always apply\nthe two prongs directly to your target, or there will be no effect.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sunshine Letter", "Grand Druid Verden", "Dear Arch Druid Leyun,\n\n   Judging by the large knot on the side of my head and the missing leg of my traveling companion; the Black Hand has returned. They're stalking the roads within Human borders and I have reason to believe they may be getting near\nRespiren's grove. Be wary along the roads and spread awareness among the Malinor grove so that our brothers might remain safe.\n\n\n\n        Aspects be with you all,\n                                        Verden", ""),
        StaticBook("Surviving travel", "Ilbryn", "Snow's Maiden, 1595\nA traveller's guide to\nsurvival by Ilbryn\n\nSo, you find yourself on the road. You've plenty of food, and know where you are going. You may think you are safe, however you aren't. When I travel, I follow several rules religiously. At\nnight time, I climb a large tree to rest. Many aren't as skilled at climbing as I, so if you can't easily climb a tree, you should find a place off-road and secluded to rest. If someone tries to lure you from the tree, do not come down. They may be\nscreaming for help, however that's easily pulled off, and nearly got me killed. When travelling, you should not stop for anyone asking you to, or to come with them, no matter how nice or convincing. They're likely muggers, or worse, as a man on the road\nwith no place to go should not be trusted. I've only had one experience with coming along was a bortu inviting me to the grand opening of a blackjack hall, I only went with because he was with a group of humans. Also, the same can apply to entering a new\ntown. Whilst in Johannesburg, I was invited to a house for tea. Instead, I was mugged under threat of battle-axe, and lost several tens of mina, as well as my weapon, and several magic apples.\n\n-Ilbryn", ""),
        StaticBook("Suspect Report", "Sylus Reddington", "Suspect Report: Luxly\nLocation: Druid's Grove (Bertha)\nAgent Sylus Reddington, 13th of The Deep Cold, 1610.\n\nLuxly is the wife of Eletha, a dedicant at the Druid's Grove. She is a suspect that fits the description of the Mali'aheral Frost-\nWitches, as she is a Mali'aheral woman with a sympathy towards abominations who \"simply kill their victims.\" She holds a resentment towards the Ascended for \"seeing one burn a young girl to death.\" among a discussion about various abominations, her wife-\nmade the comment, \"I'd much rather a Witch than a ghoul.\" hinting the wife may be aware if Luxly is truely a witch. A thorough investigation is recommended in the matter, but be warned both the suspect and wife are familiar and friendly with me,Reddington\nso discretion and anonymity is advised. Be aware, suspect holds resentment towards Ascended and both the wife and suspect are aware of my affiliation to the Ascended.\n\nPlease do not throw me into the fire on this one. \n-S.R.\n((Player was made aware that this report was made, reasoning was made known so that metagaming wasn't brought into question.))", ""),
        StaticBook("Suspects!", "Kiveck Irelia", "Possible Frost Witch, deadly mages, spooks, etc that assaulted Cinh on the 19th of The First Seed, 1596.\n\n-Forestyne\n-'Sif', wears a disguise and has been seen within the elcihi often.\n-Mali'ame, unknown intentions but they dragged off his body.\n-Mali'ker, unknown identity, though they are an arcanist, purple eyes, white hair", ""),
        StaticBook("Sutica", "Aerodel", "Day 1 : Travels are slow but i've reached the docks.\nDay 2 : I've taken the cart to Sutica. Upon approaching Sutica I am greeted by a stranger.\nDay 3 : Sutica gates are open... streets are quiet. I've wandered near the shop and purchased some item\nDay 3 (continued) : I've come upon the Guards Barracks. It is STRICTLY guarded. They must really not want anyone in there. Night is falling so I set out, not wanting to be here during the night..\nDay 4 : I reached the boat to go pack to Tahn.\nDay 4 (continued) : I will now rest on the boat until we've arrived. \nDay 5 : I've reached Tahn. From here I know my way back home. My travel book ends here. \n\n(Other notes)\n1 - Sutica was selling many axes. They also sold strange blocks..\n1 (continued) - they also sold bows but many were out of stock.\n2 - Habitants were very plentyful although none of them were around. Every house seemed to be occupied.\n3 - Many roads were under construction.. I wonder what they're up to..", ""),
        StaticBook("Sutican Warriors", "Saendir Aureon", "A Poem/Song By:\n\nSaendir Aureon\nSutican Warriors\nFar over... the stormy sea cold....\n\nTo forest deep... and cavern old....\n\nWe must away... ere break of day....\n\nTo slay a long... forgotten Ghoul....\nThe trees were roaring... in the woods....\n\nElves needed help... to protect their goods...\n\nWe came to kill... it was our will....\n\nTo help a friend... who'd been attacked....\nThrough snow and cold... they came to fight....\n\nThey crossed the sea... with all their might....\n\nBut when they came... No beast to blame...\n\nFor the Ghoul was not to be seen, or slain....", ""),
        StaticBook("Sword Invictus", "Eandyil Torena", "The Sword Invictus\nWe who fought.\n\nThis is the oldest journal of the mali'ame known as Eandyil\nMy adventures with the Sword Invictus began for the same reason most of my adventures begin. I grew weary of wandering. In other words, I was bored.\n\nI was travelling the roads when I came across an odd band. The man I would one day know as Helvetius\nhailed me. Having grown up among humans, and cursed with boredom, I stopped to hear the man out.\n\nAs he caught up to me, the man laughed, not even breathing heavily. I stood before him with a stone sword, and he laughed at me. The man struck an odd pose,\nhis hands on his hips, arms akimbo, and he said, \"You look like an elf that knows how to fight. What say you, lad? Join my company and fight evil for a nice profit?\"\n\n\"I don't know,\" I replied hesitantly. \"I have yet to explore this island. Money\nis nice, but it isn't everything.\"\n\n\"The Minas are an excuse, lad, to do something your eyes tell me you desperately desire. It's companionship that you're looking for, is it not?\"\n\nMy eyes must have hinted at my response, because he grinned at me before\nI had barely said three words. \"Come with me,\" he interrupted me kindly. \"Meet the man who will be commanding you, your Dux. Do well and you might attain the rank yourself, some day.\"\n\nTo this day, I'm not entirely sure why I was  so ready to trust the\nhuman. Perhaps he was right, maybe I really did miss companions in my life. I signed the contract that day, beginning my work for the Sword Invictus.\nThe Keep\n\nIt was a week's journey to what would become Invictus Keep. While the gate was barred and shut, the walls were breached in several places.\n\nFrom just inside the keep, we heard the telltale sound of the undead. Skeletal archers and former\nsoldiers of the prior owners, somehow brought back from death itself to guard this ancient keep.\n\n\"The first thing we will do after we clear this place is repair the walls,\" our leader said, all confidence.\n\n\"I have some small experience at repairs, sir,\"\nI said diffidently. The other recruits gave me a variety of looks, but our leader clapped me on the shoulder.\n\n\"Good lad,\" he said simply. \"Alright men, work in pairs. I want this keep cleared by sundown.\"\n\n\"Yes sir!\" we shouted.\n\nI was only average with\na bow back then, so I drew my short sword.\n\n\"That won't do,\" my Lietenant, or Dux, said to me. \"Here, try this Xiphos. It's a sturdy blade and will be good for you. Come, your training begins now.\"\n\nSo we began, clearing the keep of the clumsy\nresidents while learning to use the blade in the way the Sword Invictus preferred. It was to be a long day, but we cleared it from top to bottom. We beat our deadline with minutes to spare.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sylverwood Law", "Fjordin Sylver", "- Sylverwood Law -\n\nBy : Fjordin Sylver, Dictator of Sylverwood\n\nInfo : This book provides a basic understanding of how a Sylverwood citizen functions in society and the guidelines one must follow.\n- Chapter 1 -\nSylverwood Law and Order can be looked at as a number of different things. Some may call it primitive and brutal, simply for the fact it is catagorized as a Dictatorship. The reality is, however, not like that at all.\nFor the sake of slander against his form of government, Fjordin Sylver likes to catagorize his Dictatorship in the sub-catagory (which he has created) referred to as  Benevolent Dictatorship. Benevolent of course meaning good.\nA \"Benevolent\" Dictatorship centers itself somewhere between good and evil. While a lot of Fjordin's actions may seem unnecessarily harsh and rushed, his sole intent is to protect his citizens and fufill their needs and wants.\nThis does not mean all of his decisions are based soley on his personal opinion and knowledge. He has a private counsel known as the Sylver Shields. These Shields are his most trusted advisors, who live as everyday citizens but feed him intrigue.\nThis should now, however, make every citizen paranoid of one another. So long as nobody plots against Fjordin's life, there is no need to worry. The truth is that despite his sometimes callous and sarcastic attitude, he dislikes violence.\nThe fact of the matter is that Fjordin's word is law. While his word may not be agreed upon by the majority it is there to protect them. So long as people obey him, they will find themselves looking forward into a brighter future.\n- Chapter 2 -\nThere is obviously a limit to how much power every citizen wields. Power in Sylverwood, however, does not come from ones control over the legal system. Instead, it comes in the form of how necessary you are to the towns functionality.\nEverybody is vital in some way, shape and form. Farmers form the basis of breeding and cooking. Miners form the foundations of stonemasonry, blacksmithing, tinkering and enchanting. Life is a constant chain of supply and demand.\nAnother way to put this is that everyone is the link of a chain. If one link breaks off so does everything after it. Laborers, such as Lumberjacks, Miners and Farmers, are the most essential and tiresome jobs one can have.\nManufactured goods, however, are what make the most of those professions. Sometimes these professions work in sync to produce even finer wares, such as studded armor made by a learned leatherworker with the help of a blacksmith.\nShould one person drop from this link it could cause havoc. However, this does not mean one should stop working just to make a point. By abandoning the practice of your designated profession, you are endangering the lives of everyone. Not just Fjordin.\nTypically in Sylverwood society, every race is forced to pick at least one profession they are most fit for. Humans, as a popular example, will most often be forced to take up a laboring role. This could include Mining, Lumberjacking and/or Farming.\n- Chapter 3 -\nIncase you have not read the notice board (somehow) before openning this book, I will now state the rules and regulations in Sylverwood as of 1486.\nNote : Finding \"loopholes\" will result in an even harsher punishment than before!\nRule #1 - No Killing/Assault of Citizens\nUnless the person in question explicitly robs you of your valuables, you may NOT slaughter one another like animals. As explained previously, everyone is important to the functionality of Sylverwood. Don't be dumb.\nRule #2 - No Theft of Citizens\nAnother common-sense rule. In all honesty, I have stolen once before. However, I stole because I was in dire need of food during the winter. If you're going to take something, do so in small quantities within reason.\nRule #3 - No Livestock Murder\nYes, I refer to the unnecessary slaughter of livestock as murder. Livestock are just as important to the function of society as humans are. Without them, lots of industry and food production will stop. (Also Server Rule)\nRule #4 - No Building (Outside Home)\nI can not stress this enough. Building outside of your designated home is prohibited by all means. Fjordin Sylver is the sole architect and engineer of everything in Sylverwood unless otherwise said so.\nRule #5 - Stay active.\nUnless you have a legitimate reason for inactivity in LOTC (this is a bit OOC but must be addressed), do not waste a perfectly good home by being on an hour every couple days. You are here to contribute, not take up space.\nRule #6 - No Granting Citizenship\nI don't care if somebody is your brother, sister, mother or father. If you want someone to move in with you or otherwise, have them contact me directly (christian2142). Otherwise keep them out of Sylverwood.\nRule #7 - No Necromancy\nSylverwood has a strict policy against the practice of the Dark Arts or anything related to it. No blood/animal/human sacrifices nor Black Magic will be allowed. This is a security threat to Athera and will be dealt with directly.", ""),
        StaticBook("t", "Nin Taliame", "{\"text\":\"\"}", ""),
        StaticBook("Tahn I", "March Ash", "The Forest is strong, here. In few other places is the land as untouched, by magic or by Men. A better weapon there is rarely ever forged. The yolk of the world will yield to us the end of civilization.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tahn II", "March Ash", "The valleys are beautiful. The soil is rich, game is plenty. It is an oasis among a world defiled by the city. I think I will rest here, for a while, and commune with the land. My journey has been harsh, and my wounds still need to heal.\nI will tend to them.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tahn III", "March Ash", "Here, this small isle is largely untouched. The canopy grows across the sky, the few cracks of sunlight spilling down like a golden rain. I have seen few other places this isolated since I came upon the grove of the Bramble druid,\nwho had an army of ents to fight the cities. The memory of his corpse, broken on the wheel, I will not forget.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tahn IV", "March Ash", "Mesa is dry. Not far from here are the salt flats of Dangier. Will reach them by nightfall. Nature is loving, but is also cruel.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tahn IX", "March Ash", "Sitting here, watching the sunrise, it would be nice to lay back and let the light wash over me. To rest until nature comes to consume me. To die peacefully. To pass my mission onto another. And then I stand up, and turn away from the sun,\nbecause my resolve is not dead, yet. I must kill the City, and all those who would ever support it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tahn V", "March Ash", "It is difficult to see, but these arid planes are some of the most diverse places in the world. Life thrives on adversity. In the jungle, the rain washes much away, making the soil nutrient-poor. Here, the sun beats harsh, making water scarce.\nMultiple survival strategies are thus made possible, not just those which seek to absorb as many nutrients as possible. This is what makes these places biodiverse.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tahn VI", "March Ash", "The swamps have always been a place for reclusive druids to go and meditate. The muck holds thousands of years within it, an ancient story of the land. Corpses of ancient men and women, who will tell me more about the history of this place\nthan books ever could.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tahn VII", "March Ash", "Not far from here, the Holy Orenian Empire's death throes tore apart the world. One of the greatest acts of sacrilege of all time. It cannot go unpunished. I will not stop until every shred of the old empire is turned to ash,\nuntil every person who was a part of this atrocity is dead. I will restore balance where it has been taken.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tahn VIII", "March Ash", "The canyon is wild. The fossils tell a story. A history. When I trace my palms down the rocks I can feel what remains of so many creatures. So many lives, now embedded in rock. Their lives give me will. Their passions are my power.\nI feed on them. Their hungers, and loves, and hates.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tahn X", "March Ash", "It is amazing that not a kilometer from here the world has been consumed by the void, yet in this place nature has recovered. Despite all of Iblees' machinations, the resilience of nature is more powerful.\nSo long as a single glade survives, the world might recover. I hope the Aspects are patient enough.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tahn XI", "March Ash", "The void has touched the world, drenched it in its poison. I will suck it from the earth as a man sucks snake-venom from the bite. Despite all his power, Iblees and his legions are nothing compared to nature, and all that it consists of.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tahn XII", "March Ash", "The air is cool, but even this deep in the wood I smell on the air the scent of burning coals, and the acrid smoke of furnaces. Even the far north is not free of colonization. Axios has suffered so much, in such little time.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tahn XIII", "March Ash", "This forest is sequestered, protected on all four sides by the mountains. It is a hidden place, for a hidden time. The undead rise in the west, and if they come to this place, I will lay a trap for them. In thorns, and blood, and light.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tahn XIV", "March Ash", "I am closer to the sky here than in any other place. I can feel the wind on my skin, through my hair. Its cold bites at me. I summon my strength, and I send it spilling out across all of Tahn, to bite at my foes.\nThe wind is but another natural thing, it only requires a gentle hand and a powerful set of lungs to guide it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tahn XV", "March Ash", "The winds converge in this place, splitting and merging between the stone like rivers. I hear on it a thousand conversations, from a thousand places all across Axios. It speaks to me.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tahn XVI", "March Ash", "I feel the undead, they are close. I can sense their clamor, the hunger, the egress of the masses. I will have to do something about this.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tahn XVII", "March Ash", "And in the sand, respite.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tahn XVIII", "March Ash", "Soon, the cities shall crumble. Either by the hand of mine, or by the claw of nature. I can only hope that if it is the claw, then that its bearer will be kind enough to spare those who have served it faithfully.", ""),
        StaticBook("Talvin", "Talvin", "Password Claw\n\nEreinion", ""),
        StaticBook("Task 2: Thesis", "Melethrë Torena", "Aspectism is a faith based on the protection and lifestyle of the World we live on.\n\nMuch of this revolves around the reverence of the two chief dieties of nature, Cernunnos and Cerridwen, Also known as the aspects.\nModern Aspectism is born of the disire to revive acient traditions of the wood elven people, To make a new version of their ways and culture its its own unique way. Most of this is the way of life wich reperestend the roots of the wood elven people.\nThe Aspects:\nCernunnos is the aspect of the hunt, Whisle Cernunnos dipicts death, this is not seen as bad, For all things must die at a Certain stage, and it is simply a part of natures Circle of life.\nCerridewn is the aspect of growth, life and fe\n. She gives us food, and the trees around us. Life. Some poeple pray to her in order to give birth to a healty child.", ""),
        StaticBook("Task for 'Hawke", "Karu", "*large moat filled with spires around castle\n*castle is on little land island \n*only entrace is gate that stretches over ravine\n*smaller castle surround area with tons of farm land\n*oceans leaks into ravine-valley\n*peninsula\n*three sections, guard/gate section/barracks,\nmarket/square, royal are\n*not many locks, open access\n*many arches and gates that section off areas, usually manned by guards\n*many holy people there\n*I saw Leyu there\n*tops of buildings have wood, fire travel easy\n*fire and pyres everywhere\n*government buildings locked off, they are main pillars", ""),
        StaticBook("Task From Verden", "Jallentime", "((X-1162 / Z-427))\n\nHead to Darkhaven and question the population about any strange occurances or sightings in the nearby forest.\n\nBring back your findings to me directly.", ""),
        StaticBook("Task One", "Morvan Bloodborne", "*The thick scrawl below appears to be written in a trained hand, its letters simple and clean. It would appear as if written with charcoal, with numerous smudges and blotches scattered throughout the book.\n\nDedicant Task One \nObservations by Morvan\nObservation One\n   The 'Mushmush Tower'\n20th of The Deep Cold, 1472\n \nMy Observations begin at a strange tower in the Northern Mountains, one which me dear Uncle has come to call the 'Mushmush Tower'. The tower itself is full of strange devices and\nand mechanisms, though it is the large variety of towering Mushrooms that have drawn us to it. \n\nWithin the tower itself a handful of massive Mushrooms have sprouted and broken through the floors, their towering bodies snaking upwards, some even pushing\noutwards through its roofs. The tower, once grand, now lies in a state of ruin as nature has chosen to reclaim the area for its own once again.\n\nThese Mushrooms vary in colour and size, though each seem to secrete a thick cloud of spores that are earthy\nin taste and smell. Because of this, dozens upon dozens of Mushrooms have grown in the area surrounding the lake and tower, their presence slowly growing outward with time. I can only imagine that one day these Mushrooms will take over a large swath of\nof land, unless other plantlife or outside intervention decides to stop them.\n\nAdditionally, there appears to be a thick vegetative fungus that smells thick and acrid, though only in the vacinity of the Mushrooms. It is of a pale pink colour, and it\nmakes a distinct squish under the feet.\n\nMy final thoughts rest on the simple fact that these mushrooms prove that above all else, nature will do as it pleases. Manmade or no, in time all things will wear down and be replaced with new growth once again.\nObservation Two\n      'The Sacred Grove'\n21st of The Deep Cold, 1472\n\nThis grove.. I find myself awestruck and enthralled by the beauty within. It feels as if I am a young man going through my Coming of Age once again. Seeing the world for the\nthe first time, revelling in its beauty and wonder. This place, this Grove, steals my breath away.\n\nBy far the most wonderful aspect would be the absolutely massive tree that hangs over the small pond below. It may even rival the size of the one back at\nDruid grove. Within its massive canopy there is a dull droning of wasps, numerous nests dotting its lowest branches. \n\nIt is a place of beauty, but also one of hostility. The aforementioned wasps, a nest of giant spiders in its roots. There is a primal\nferocity in the very air around the grove. It is one of the reasons Ketiley and I decided to bind ourselves here, under the gods, so long ago. \n\nOddly enough, there seems to float a collection of large crystals  at the center of the pond sitting at the\ntrees base. I am certain a full-fledged druid would be able to tell more of its power, but even with my innate knowledge.. I sense a great power within the crystals, their energy radiating outwards.\n\n*A few words are scribbled and blotted, a few drops of\nblood dotting at the parchment below*\n\nSpiders. Undead. As dawn broke and the sun reared its head, so did a horde of beasts. We were driven from the grove after slaying dozens of the foul creatures, now I sit upon a hill and look onwards, my eyes resting\nupon the massive tree before me. As I wrote earlier, it seems to be the focal point for the grove, its roots clawing deep into the earth below. I can see the bustle of life within, it is probably best to head home before another swarm of beasts attacks.\n*A small, detailed map is drawn on the page, marking the grove off.*\n\n((x-437 z-407))\n\nShould you be curious enough to visit the grove, take caution in the words written in these pages. It is both wonderful and dangerous.\nObservation Three\n              'Fiandria'\n11th of Snow's Maiden, 1473\n       ((x-668 z-897))\n\nI have chosen to do my last observation on a plant that I learned of long ago called an 'Allium'. I find myself surrounded by them in a land that I have\nnever before laid eyes on, one which I have decided bears mention. Fiandria.\n\nSitting here, in this field, I find it hard to even tear my gaze away from the land surrounding me. It's beauty is like none I have ever seen. By far the most noticeable aspect\nwould be the towering, bleach-white trees that dot the landscape. While not as big as the one at the Grove, these trees are many, their branches home to an assortment of large bats. Unlike the beasts that littered the grove, the ones here in Fiandra all\nseem to be relatively peaceful. A sense of complete and total calm comes over me as I watch beasts, large and small, frolick about under the canopies. A soft wind is ever present, nipping at the gaps in my armour. \n\nMoving on. Allium. They sprout from the\nground in simple stalks, tipped by an orb comprised of hundreds of small, purple star-like flowers. They have a pleasant smell, with a slight hint of familiarity.. Garlic? I believe it is. The small flowers all seem to shift in tandem with each breeze.\nIt would appear that I am not the only one drawn to them, I often spot a small moth or two hanging about, landing upon the flower to take a bite out of one of its many petals. It appears to be a favourite for these small insects to dine on, for the other\nplants remain untouched by them. \n\nI find myself brought back to memories of my homeland in Anthos, of my mother. She always had a flower much like this one entwined in her hair, it's purple flowers never seeming to wilt.", ""),
        StaticBook("Task.", "Sora", "There's a shit ton of lava here.\n\nThe people that live here are short and have long beards.\n\nThey also talk funny.\n\nThere are a couple of placsmifts and a throne made of Green Gems\nand Gold.\n\nAgain a shit ton of lava.\n\nDifferent flags, some have axes other have hammers.\n\nNo cute women to be seen. ;(\nAgain, no ladies... ;(\n\n-Sora", ""),
        StaticBook("Tasks: Lesson", "Lillith Winterleaf", "I endeavor in a series of tomes to give examples of tasks I gave as a Guide on Asulon, or that I have observed or had given to me in my time as a Dedicant. These are to help both current and future Guides, but are not the only options. Be creative and\nassign tasks to a Dedicant that are tailored to who they are, and what you feel they still need to learn. \n\n~ The Sequoia Druid, Lillith Wintereaf\nVerbal Lesson on Natural Resources: This should directly follow a gathering of a variety of natural resources. Take the Dedicant aside to a quiet place so you will avoid interruption. Take each item the Dedicant has brought you and explain,\nin your own words and opinion, the purpose of the item, its uses, its place in nature, and anything else you feel worth mentioning about it. Return each item afterwards for the Dedicant to study further on their own if they so desire.\nAsk them questions about what you have told them to ensure they have paid attention and learned from you.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tasks: Wilds", "Lillith Winterleaf", "I endeavor in a series of tomes to give examples of tasks I gave as a Guide on Asulon, or that I have observed or had given to me in my time as a Dedicant. These are to help both current and future Guides, but are not the only options. Be creative and\nassign tasks to a Dedicant that are tailored to who they are, and what you feel they still need to learn. \n\n~ The Sequoia Druid, Lillith Wintereaf\nInto the Wilds: This Task is meant to teach a Dedicant about a druid's responsibility to seek out places where nature needs a helping hand to flourish once more. Most often this involves providing them with a small quantity\nof bonemeal and saplings, and perhaps a tent kit as well if there are some to spare, and tasking them to venture out beyond the lands of the races and nations, to the wild lands beyond to seek out a place they can plant the saplings\nand use the bonemeal to make the ground fertile for grasses and flowers. They are to tend to the area until all the saplings grow, for no less than one elven day. They need to keep a journal of their stay and their thoughts and activities,\nthe Guide should provide a blank book for this, and once the Task is complete, they can return to the Guide and hand in their journal and report on their Task and what they learned from it.\n((they should RP the entire thing once finding a location and take screenshots of performing the task, tending to it, meditation, etc, and upload them either via Skype directly to their Guide,\n, or preferably uploading to a gallery like imgur as a single gallery.))", ""),
        StaticBook("Tea", "Genevieve", "Tea's and their Benefits\n\nBy Unknown\n\n*Words are etched here*  \n\nTea is meant to be served warm, with friends!\nIndex:\n\nHow To Brew\nEquipment\nTea's and their effects\nAuthor's note\nHOW TO BREW\n\nFirst one must take their kettle, usually a black one and fill it with water.  Do not fill this with anything besides water, as it will skew the taste.\n\nSecondly you set the kettle above the fire, you must wait for it to boil.  It shall\nscream at you when it is ready.  Take it off the fire.\n\nThirdly you must then get the leaves and fill the pot.\n\nFourth let it steep for a while until the flavor has taken ahold of the water.\n\nServe in cups while warm!\nEquipment\n\nTeapot\nCups\nTeabags\nSugar\nHoney\nSpoon\nTypes of Tea\nLemon Grass\nThis helps digest food, serve shortly after dinner.\n\nGreen Tea\nThe wonder tea!  Helps with immune systems, tooth decay, and sickness.\n\nGinger Tea\nHelps with nausea, and arthritis.\nPeppermint Tea\nHelps sooth, as well as helps control nausea, vomiting, and motion sickness.  Helps also with mild coughs, asthma, congestion, and aches.\n\nChamomile Tea\nThe tea to help one sleep, take before bed for best results.\nRose Hip Tea\nHelps with complexion, adrenaline, and your immune system.\n\nLavander Tea\nHelps respiratory issues, cough, asthma, and body temperature from fever.  Helps heal ulcers, sores, cuts, and wounds.\nHibiscus Flower Tea\nHelps with hypertension, and high blood pressure.  Drink when you have a stressful job.\n\nMilk Thistle Tea\nHelps clean ones liver, and improve liver function.  Drink this you drunkards!\n\nBlackberry Leaf Tea\nGood for the immune system!\nDandelion Tea\nHelps with arthristis, liver function, fluid retention, and soothing pain.\n\nHawthorn Tea\nHelps with blood circulation, and reduce stress.\n\nCinnamon Tea\nEnhances body strength, fights viruses, and is effective with honey.\nRed Clover Tea\nHelps with stress, and gives a peaceful sleep.  Strengthens bones as well as improves memory.\n\nNettle Tea\nHelps with high blood pressure, rheumatism, arthritis, immune systems, coughs and colds.  Also helps with congestion and kidneys.\nAuthors Note\n\nTea is meant to be enjoyed, drink often as I have and you will enjoy a nice quiet life.  There are plenty of plants I have forgotten so feel free to make your own tea books as well.\n*A picture of an old elven woman is sketched here, in her hand is a cup of tea*", ""),
        StaticBook("Teeth of Hell", "Domainoft", "Through The Teeth of Hell\n-Retold by Leyu'Maehr\nVaehaven\n*Strange Numbers\n((3/3/13))\nHarold Fergensun, and Orc, was walking down a stone road. Pretending he was innocent. You see, Harold was a robber, rapist, murderer, just to name a few. Then...... he was shot by gaurds. Arrow in his back, Harold dropped to his knees, and died.\nSwirling shapes and figures rushed around him. He landed, in the stone of Hell. Crying, yelling, death, all 'round. He saw above him the teeth of hell. He started climbing, and saw his friend Lucas, burning , pleading for him to help. But he said \"I\ncannot help\". He climbed further. He then saw his father, begging for salvation. Harold again says, I cannot help. He climbs almost to the top. ALMOST THERE AND- his wife. His dead wife. \"Help me Harold, I love you!\" Harold couldnt resis t. \"I love you\ntoo but.....\" he looked down. \"I must help you all\" He drags all the earlier mentioned friends through the teeth of hell. He asks them, \"Why were you there?\" They said \"Because of you....\". He told them he was sorry, and knew what to do. He jumped back\nin. He saved his friends from hell, and sacrificed himself. He the heard the voice of God calling him up while he was grinding in the teeth of Hell. God said \"You have sacrificed yourself for others. You are redeemed\" He was saved from the Nether and\nbrought up to heaven. There he saw the people he just rescued, and many more. The Cathaldus family the Harronis family, and many more. He was at peace with God, and Aegis. THE END.", ""),
        StaticBook("TeethOfHell", "Tristanm1", "Through the Teeth of Hell\nAuthor Unknown\nHarold Fergensun, an Orc, was walking down a stone road, pretending he was innocent. You see, Harold was a robber, rapist, and murderer, just to name a few. Then he was shot by guards. Arrow in his back, Harold dropped to his knees, and died.\nSwirling Shapes and figures rushed around him. He landed in the stone of Hell. Crying, yelling, death, all 'round. He saw above him the teeth of hell. He started climbing, and saw his friend Lucas, burning, pleading for him to help, but he said, \"I cannot\nhelp.\" He climbed further. He then saw his father, begging for salvation. Harold again says, \"I cannot help.\" He climbs almost to the top. Almost there, and... his wife. His dead wife. \"Help me Harold, I love you!\" Harold couldn't resist. \"I love you too,\nbut...\" he looked down. \"I must help you all.\" He drags all the earlier mentioned friends through the teeth of hell. He asks them, \"Why were you there?\" They replied, \"Because of you...\" He told them he was sorry, and he knew what to do.\nHe jumped back in He saved his friends from hell, and sacrificed himself. He heard the voice of God calling him up while he was grinding in the teeth of Hell. God said, \"You have sacrificed yourself for others. You are redeemed.\"\nHe was saved from the Nether and brought up to heaven. There he saw the people he just rescued, and many more. The Cathaldus family, the Harronis family, and many more. He was at peace with God and Aegis.\nThe End", ""),
        StaticBook("Telekinesis", "Sanguine", "~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~       Telekinesis\nA guide to learning\n\nWritten by Magister\n      Sanguine\n~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~\nFirst off Telekinesis is a form of Alteration magic, Alteration magic impacts the world around it unlike its void counterparts.\nTelekinesis works by altering the force of gravity pushing down on an object. The process of telekinesis is rather simple Focus on an object then with the help of the void alter its gravity allowing it to float.\nAlthough at higher progression you will have a better grasp of the object being able to redirect, push and stop different objects.\nStarting out you should only be able to lift a few small objects such as a Pebble, but with time you will be able to lift more and heavier objects and that pebble you started with will now be a boulder.\nKnow you must have learned a thing or two but here are some Practical uses of Telekinesis: \n~Throwing knifes: They are light allowing you to throw them at your enemies with ease\n~Doors: No problem for any telekinetics just apply force against it.\n~People: Now the living are a bit tricky to manipulate so you must indirectly using clothing is a good bypass for it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Test", "Alex H. Aureon", "Hsdasdadsadsadsdsaadsadsdasdsadsadsadsads", ""),
        StaticBook("Teuton & Wizards", "Isa", "A man of the magical type enter the hall. He would look up to the Hochmiester and question why he allows Orcs into his ranks. There seems to be a disruption in the room as the Hochmiester's daughter, Camille is upset about a Sariant calling her a spoiled\nlittle shit.\nAs the Hochmiester Sergei calms his daughter, the Wizard appears baffled as he is witnessing the Third Teutonic Order before his very eyes. He stated \"It is as if the dead souls of my kin rise from your vessles.\"\nIgnoring his daughter's cries, the Hochmiester looks down from his dias towards the Wizard, unsure of what a strange \"entity\" has to do before him.\nThe Wizard would look towards the Hochmiester with a relentless gaze, staff in hand.\nLooking apprehensive, the Hochmiester would push himself up from his seat, making his way down the few steps of his throne. He would question what the meaning of his unexpected meeting is.\nThe Wizard would say that time has brought him before the\nHochmiester. He noted that the followers behind him were simply wandering souls.\nFinally the Wizard said \"I come here to judge you.\"\nConfused, Hochmiester Sergei asks what right the Wizard had to judge him.\nThe Wizard said \"By the right of\ncreation.\"\nThe old man behind the wizard would begin to wisper to himself as the Wizard and Sergei speak.\nThe Wizard told Sergei he believed that the Teutonic has one end goal and that goal was to end creatures such as the undead.\nThe Hochmiester answered Yes to the Wizard's question and that the order protects his fellow kin, the Hansetians.\nThe Wizard asks if the people of this court are well looked after and they all agreed.\nHe then asks how far the Hochmiester may go to\nto protect thoses from Hanseti.\nSergei replied, \"As far as the oath allows us to go.\"\nThe Wizard asks to hear the Oath.\nSariant Knight Volten read out the oath to the Wizard.\nThe Wizard would speak some stange words, \"Beliae\nSergei would go on to explain how the people of this order are the last of the dying breed of the Tuetonic Order. The Wizard would go on to test the Hochmiester's legitimacy for he has seen flase Hochmiesters in the past. In particular, he named one to be\nJonathan black and the rest of the post Dreadfort leaders.\nThough he noted that the Hochmiester Sergei resembled the sway of the former Hochmiester M. Denurem. He stated \"You seem a Hochmiester to me.\" Then he requested to meet with the\nHochmiester Sergei Vladov again in the near future when he calls upon Humanity.\nHe asks Sergei if he can trust him to come forth to this meeting under the eyes of Celestia and Hanseti.\nThe Wizard notes all the order are welcome to attend.\nThe Hochmiester appeared to be confused before replying \"Ja beliae asere eru bruddaz\".\nThe Wizard would then try to depart before Sergei stopped him and questioned him on why the Wizard seems to know more on the Order than the Order knows of these\nentities. The Wizard would state that he studied the Hochmiester and the Order, for he spent his life honing the mind, body and soul.\nThe Hochmiester unsure of the Wizard, question how he should believe what the Wizard has told him.\nThe Order has been in isolation since their reformation. \nThe Wizard assured that he did not wish to lead Sergei or the order anywhere.\nHe noted that during the late 14 Century the Teutonic Order discovered the knowledge of the\nAncient Hansetia\nthat they left behind.\nIn time he will reveal the knowledge to the Hochmiester but today will not be the day.\nThe Wizard he must be off for he is in search of the Mountain's Crown.\nFinally, Sergei asked one last question and that was for the na\nof this unknown Wizard.\nThe Wizard replied, \"Know not a name, but my aura. You can see my name. Feel it as you gaze.\" The Old man behind the Wizard spoke out, saying the Wizard should give a more direct answer.\nThe Wizard replied, that in this\npoint in his existance, his name should not be remembered. \nThe Hochmiester would ask when he would appear next, for he wished to hear the knowledge of his ancestors.\nThe Wizard replied that he would come after he had climbs this mysterious mountai\nand sit upon its crown.\nSergei would then go on to say how the king of the Westerlands spoke of the Wizaed once. The Wizard identified the King to be Ciaus. He said how Caius was a good man and carried the weight of the late Hochmiester G. Marius.\nSergei said how Caius noted that \"there will be a time when he'll be need to serve his purpose. He believed supporting our reformation was his purpose.\"\nThe Wizard said that he adviced the king to stay a King and not seek an Empiral title.\nJust as he wishes to see Sergei never rely on anyone but his Order.\nThe Hochmiester said that he will wait the wizards reappears, if the wizard if not just leading them in circles.\nThe Wizard said, \"When I reach the Mountain's Crown. I'll be able\nto answer with more clarity. For now, I'm unbound.\" And with that being said the entity departed from the keep.\n\n-14th of the Grand Harvest. 1608\n\nAuthor: Isa", ""),
        StaticBook("Thanhium", "Orithur", "-- == Thanhium == --\n\nWhat is Thanhium?\n\nThanhium in its most natural form is an ore burried beneath the earth, bearing a similarity to the commonly decorative ore known commonly as 'Lapis'. However, the traits of Thanhium\nare quite different, and easy to spot. For once, Thanhium is often located in incredibly large veins of ore close to the surface, and are consistently found in areas covered in both snow and frost, but as I will explain later, this is no coincidence.\nThanhium in its ore form is significantly more brittle than Lapis, but it is most noticible by its freezing aura. Thanhium is incredibly cold to the touch, and when in a large amount, like a vein of ore, it is capable of changing the very nature of the\nbiome it resides in to one of a deep cold, ridden with frost and snow. One example of this would be the Frozen North of Anthos, that was only frozen due to the masses of Thanhium ore burried beneath its surface.\nIs it dangerous?\n\nThanhium is one of the most destructive, and toxic substances known to our world, particularly when ingested. Thanhium is quite poisonous to all mortal men, however its affects vary between mages and non-mages.\nWhile it is known to have the victim struck with intense headaches, in mages it interferes with their personal supply of manner, and from here the effects may vary. Some mages report having a massive rush of uncontrollable mana, others, more commonly,\nclaim that the Thanhium negates their magical power entirely. Non-mages would find themselves arush with a newfound power they can't possibly hope to understand. They would become quite surged and overwhelmed with mana, likely rendering them uncouncious,\nor even killing them outright. Death is possible with both mages and non-mages alike, and it has been recorded that close proximity to Thanhium for an extended period of time, causes severe cases of madness.\nWhat do I do with it?\n\nThanhium must be processed and purified for its usefulness to be extracted. A variety of methods exist and many scholars of Thanhium's nature will give you a different example on how to bring the ore\nto its purest form, creating that of a 'shard' or 'crystal. It is important to note that the Thanhium does not generate cold, it instead draws in heat and leaves cold in its wake, transforming this heat into mana. It is for this reason that Thanhium in\nits purest form is commonly used to empower enchantments, and keep them sustained. Enchantments can tap into their supply of mana and feed off it indefinately while it continues to drain heat from the air to fuel itself. The ore\nas a rule is more useful when in purified form, and from here it has a variety of uses, ranging from a powerful explosive, to a deadly poison, to a useful attachment to an enchantment, allowing for enchantments to be sustained with mana, and a great deal\nmore. I have personally found ways to forge unique armours fashioned from Thanhic alloys, and have studied into the effects of harnessing the power of Thanhium to change the very weather.\nWhat more is there to Thanhium?\n\nThe short answer, is that we do not know. Constantly new discoveries are made surrounding Thanhium and its many properties. The study of Thanhium is a particularly rewarding field to any\naspiring scholar. Its potential is almost limitless, but it is to be noted that while great things may be achieved through Thanhium, it is in its nature a destructive element. While it is capable of achieving great good, it is admittedly easier to achieve\ngreat evil. Responsibility is a necessity when handling Thanhium, for in its study I know from experience that its dangers become quite apparent, its potential as a weapon is often stumbled upon.", ""),
        StaticBook("Thank you", "Cristen Irl", "I am writing to you to say thankful!\n\nAlthough you only spent little time with me, it felt like hours. \n\nI saw that your fishing rod broke and thats why you had to leave. So i took the time and effort to craft you a new one...\nPlease take this as a thank you gift for at least talking to me....\n\nI been through some rough things and you made my day.....Thank you\n\n-Cristen Irl", ""),
        StaticBook("Thank You.", "Ker Maln", "Thanks to the man man who got me here, prince something or other... this meat makes a fine addition to my collection. Still dont know why you didnt accept my offering.... human meat is rather brilliant raw.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Abyss", "Kass Ouroborus", "=================== A few observations of the great Abyss\n=================== By Kass Ouroborus\nDisclaimer: The Abyss is not a safe place for a normal being to occupy, I advise against looking for, or even entering it.\nThe Abyss is indeed the Cloud Temple of Aegis. The entire place has a desolate look to it as you will most likely feel a weight upon your soul. On most occurances, various dark creatures (if not just one) will appear. I can personally tell you that the\ndescriptions of each creature inside the books of the Library of Dragur. A ghoul hides it's face, if not wearing armor. A graven does indeed protect itself inside armor. But when I went to the library-like area, there will be a bookshelf here or there\nwith a book title inscribed into it, but there is no book. The arrangement of the 'named shelves' is chaotically, a shade may have been the librarian at one point. then there is always the way that you seem to be inside the void itself when you look up\nor anywhere you'd expect to see the sky in the regular dimension you're most likely reading this from. It seems to be in a word, nothing. the temple seems to be the only thing around. There is also the weird, nightmarish for some, what appear to be\nplants. I encourage you, the reader, to stay curious and adventurous. But do not EVER venture to the Sunless Sanctum like I have. I am no regular person, I will never be. Almost any experience in that place is undesireable. You will most likely not\nsurvive if you do not listen to this warning. But that doesn't mean you can't continue to question why exactly something is how it is.\nThere are also large twisted, warped pillars, that's atleast how they look. There is also this pit that's called the \"scorched pit\" I believe it's where the ghouls live, if it wasn't in a past Cloud Temple, I'd already be dead.\nA grave yard (atleast how it looks) is located on the path next to the library. On the opposite path from the one to the library and graveyard, across the middle of the sanctum, there are ruins of a castle, and more book shelves with titles, but no books.\nI haven't the slightest idea where they have all gone. I only know that the Black Sun Volumes are inscribed into most of the empty shelves. That is all I can say about this place.\nI have decided to place this book of observations into the hands of the people at the Library of Dragur. I do hope you all take care of this. It's the first of any kind of documentation like this, atleast I think it is. If there is any questions about\nthis book, send me a bird. My name is Kass (KazTheDuelist). Do not send me a bird with only mediocre knowledge available of normal research. Make it a passion to know all that is already possible, and to search for the creator of this book.\n* A symbol is drawn in what seems to be crimson ink, or blood. A dragon eating it's tail in the pupal of a sinister looking eye.*", ""),
        StaticBook("The Age of Time", "Locke Lamora", "As we delve into the depths of our mind realize we to are a facet of the earth which surrounds us. We are but one little slice of a larger whole, appreciation is not often granted to the lands which provide us sustinance, and joyous harvests. From the\nHalflings to the mighty Uruks we are all but apart of a greater thing. Though we may see wars tear us apart, and love bring us together this life is not one we must choose to walk alone. A wise man may ask a younger man to carry on his task for he has\ngrown to old, and must pass the torch; such is the rythme of life it flows, and goes on just as the mighty Ice caps of the Dwarven lands melt giving way to the heaving flow of the rushing rivers pulling down the banks of sediment, and tumbling trees as\nthough they were sticks. Do not forget that blood is thicker than water both may flow, and both may coat the hands of a man; but a man with blood upon his hands is a murderer and a man with water upon his hands is but a ghost among the thousands of others\n. My words are dauntingly flitted with age, and I misconstrue the times with my own ideals and thoughts; to be presumptious I'm but a speculator of the past, present, and future. This day you are a boy innocence praises you for you are the envy of its\njuvenile prosperity, the next day you're a man wielding the blade of a warrior your body marked with the scars of one who has given, and taken what life gives to those who try to sieze it with steel opposed to the words of a politic; such still hold the\npower of daggers with precise proper meanings spewn about courts to determine the fate of the gods kin. Tread lightly upon the paths that lead to power; serpents stalk the grass, and false turns are but a harmony compared to what awaits your journey into\nthe den of the lion. Lift me up, and praise me men say for their deeds reflect honor, and vitality; do you not see the death of another man as but a morose crime, but you've no empathy for a man whos claims rival your own he is but a body among the\nhundreds you will slay to achieve your darkest desires. Let dread fill your days for all men rot, and one day to you will taunted by the shouts, and screams of blithering souls aghast at your crimes; victims to your genocide. Your fingers scrape the edge\nof a blade, a thorn pricks your finger a drop of blood to appease the gravens of death. Is it that man fears death, or the thought of not being remembered as a man noble enough to be written upon pages of parchment, and stuffed high away within the\nshelves of a vaulted study or library their tales told once a day, week, year, or even decade so long as it is spoken their memory lives on in those pages. Is this what men strive for? Is life the leaves of a tree waneing and woeing to the seasons bidding\ntill one day they dry up basking within the sun that granted them what others may call eternal life just to be swept away in the lonesome breeze collapsing into dust to be spread once more amongst the soil so life could spring its fingers of life just one\nmore time from your decayed remains. Truth lies not in words, but in the actions of these words it is the doing not the saying that is valued. We forget the luxuries of a simple yes or no; when I'm to not know your yes from your no then I'm but a stranger\nlooking into your fantasy that seems to slowly flip pages, each new page describing what has graced your greedy hands filling your desires, and sating your thirst for vengeance; and bloodlust against your foes. Life is a circle in which we all must live.\nA younger me would know these words to hold no meaning, an older me sees them as a golden relic to be treasured and safe kept for all to read; and glance but a piece of what lay within the expanse of centuries walking the lands of this world. So be it I\ndream of the skies, and drifting away. Dreams fuel us they are the embodiment of our hope, they are our ambition and the force that compels us to do the things we do for others. Dark times come, and go but do not stand, and proclaim you are afraid to bare\nwitness when you've brought such a darkness down from the heavens, and now the clouds are glinted with the tinge of power for which you asked for soon it will course through your blood; and turn your soul sour and corrupt its tendrils soaking up your\nessence and tainting you to the core of your being. \n\n\nThe Philosophies of:\nLocke Lamora", ""),
