        StaticBook("The Apple of Ice", "Irish Delfina", "Apples. Apples of various shapes, colours and shapes grew on a tree made entirely of ice.\n\nI picked the apple, knowing not of the curse that would ensue. But how could I have not endulged my desires?! \n\nThey were so beautiful! Perfect, even. It\nI shall return later.\nIt has been two weeks, and the tree deep within the depths of the library of Tahn has revealed to me it's most beautiful of gifts.\n\nAn apple made entirely of gold.\n\nPerhaps this is what the password was. The key to all knowledge. I shall take a\nAͩ͊ͬͧ̔ͤ͏̼̦̱͔ľ̞͆̽͜l̖̙ͨ͋͡ ̺͎͓k̢͈̠͈̪ͣͮͮͬͨ̅͑n̊ͧ͐͊͂̚ǫ͎̯ͤ͋w̲̺̘̹̗̞ͬ̎̾l̓̊̋͛͋ͭͮ͝ḙ͚̉͛̓̄̀d̲̳ͫg͇͇̼ͨͣ͠e̲̥̬͚̗̹͌̒ͯͩ ̴͙̻̯̻̗̝̥̄̀ͭi͔̲̼͕̬̗͚ͤ͆͋̽̄s͍̫̤̺͉ͥͦͭ͒ ̜̯̄ľ͉o̗̰͌̓ͩ́s̺̭̪͕t̎̀͏̝̰̥͉͈̟.̮̬̊̉̃\nB͕̝̝̺̘̓͡u̥͕͎̙̹͈ͬtͦ ̱̺͔̬̥̋̽̂̍ͅeͧ̒̄̽v̥͋͗ͨ̐e̖̗̣̯̼̫͙͛̎͑͐ͬ͋ͫṙ҉̖̝̞͔ȳ͙̺̘̙̭ͮͨ̄ͨt̼̥̟̮ͣ̇̒ͯ͂h̸͎̱̬̲͔̗͇͐͆ͨ̉͒͛̀i̻̘̖̗̤̞͂̎̐ͪ̍ͩ͆n͕͎̊ͮ̉̄̈̇͢ͅġ͓̙̲ͅ\nh͉̜̓ͥ͑̃̓ͩa̢͕̠ͧ̓͋̈́̍̓͌s̸͉ͥͮͭͣͩ̋̾ ̑̅҉̬̦̘̤͍b̰̖͙e̘͠e͚͈̐̌͜n͚̠̪͔͛͗̂̑͐͑ ̑̐g̙̫̰ͮ̏̊ͣͬ͟a̱̠̙̤̣͖̿ͥ̊ĭ̤͓̒̌̉̅ͥn̉͐̓ͨͨ͊̃͏̲̳̪̰̥̯ͅe̪͔̺̟͆̂̾́͊̑̈́ḍ͖̩̯͍̦̍.̅͘ͅ\n̐͛ͯ͏̘T͙̹̖͔̽h͓ͯͧ́͆̚͞ȩ̞̣͉͕̀ ̬̗͙̥͓ͣͩ͊D͔͓̫o̞͖̯̩ͯ́o͉̲̞̥͔͢r̸̤̜ͫͮͭ̄ͫ ͕̩͍̣̦͖͆͒̉͒ͥͅh̟̣̥̠͍͓ͨͬͨͭ̂͝á̴͇̰̭̻̮ͦ̄̊̔ͅs̵̲̳̙̩̯̝ ͧ͂͗̽̀̿̔ŏ̍͌̓̋̾p͚̬͒͌̚e̲̺̯͎̘ͦ̿̑̊͛ͥͬ͢n̯̰̎̈́̄͂̂e̴̿ͦ̾̓͂̃d̰̜̫̑͑̓ͪ̈ͭ\n\na͎͕̦̦͇ͤ̓͗̓ͪn͉̂̌̓͑̇̚ͅd̙͙̄͐̚ ̦͇̝̥͓̽̎ͥ̿͟I͒̄̓ͫ̊'̬͔̰̍ͣ̓ͨv̳̼̹̦͎͒͛̐̇e̺̾̑̈́̓͠ ̥͖̦̇\ṅ̥͖̦s͔ͭ́ͨ͆͑͒t̡̜̺ͭ͋e̐̑́̂̓͑̂p͏̤͎p͖̦̗͖̗ͮͥ̾̂ͅȅ͓̗͙̗͓̣͖ͯ̂͒̇̇d̼̜́͠ ̝̖̺̗̤́̇͛ͨ͟i̜̿́ͮ͘n̮͙̟͇̞ͭ̽ͅţ͉̪͔̭̭̜̐͌͛͂o͕̞̤̚ ̙̗̲̤̹̟͙̐ͩ́ͯ̔̄̋t͕̪͓̞̔̈̌h̲ͭe͛҉͇̮̻͚̣͔ ̶̭̤̠̤̾͐d̹̥ͩ͢r̈́͞e̩̜̯̞̞̅̐a̶͔͍̲̝̫̲̓̀̽̆m͇̤̖͔̲ͩ̆͌̈.̞̦͎́ͨ̈ͅ\n̖̙͉̮̳͕̳-̤̺̟̦̺̋ͨI̼̲͆̂ͅr͉͓i̤̫̫̺͆́s͔͎̥̄̄́ḩ̺̪̤̹̫͒̽ͫ̃ ̟̉ͨ͒D̤̯̼ͤ͒ͬa̺̪͕̥̱̘͑ͦ͟ḻ͔̭̠͚̔ͥͯ̈ͭ̅͝f͇ͯͤ̉̀̄̄i̙̪͈͔̪͍͇͐ͤ͂͗ͮ̐ñ̲͙͍̭͙̈̅ͯͧ͠a͚͛̒ͭ̔̈ͭ͂", ""),
        StaticBook("The Arcane Arts", "Shariana", "-------------------The Arcane Arts\n    By Shariana TWW\n-------------------\nIntroduction.\n\nIn this book, you will get an understanding of the different areas around arcane void magic. This can be useful, if you practice these arts, or fight against an Evocationist, Thaumaturge or Conjurationist.\nChapter 1.\n\n     - Evocation -\n     The Sorcerer\n\nPerhaps the most well known of the four arch-types of magic.  Evocation involves evoking the elements of air, fire, earth, water, and lightning from the void.\n-Sorcerers cannot manipulate pre-existing elements, only summon them.\n\n-Each element is considered one arch-type of magic on its own.\n\n-The elements must follow the same laws as they do in nature.\n-Sorcerers must be ‘attuned’ to their element, spend time around their element, understand its scientific properties, how it feels etc…\n\n-Sorcerer’s must see the area they wish to summon their element in.\n-Sorcerers can only summon their element in its rawest form.\n\n-Hydromancers can also be Cryomancer (Ice Mage).\n\n-Sorcerers must imagine the element in their mind and bend it in their mind before evoking it.\nChapter 2.\n\n      - Alteration -\n    The Thaumaturge\n\nA true science of magic, Alteration involves altering the physical world around the mage.\n* Enchanting *\n-------------------The art of imbuing magical effects upon an object.\n-------------------\n\n-Changes what the item does rather than what it is.\n-Thaumaturge must be touching the item to enchant it.\n\n-The enchantment cannot alter the object physically.\n\n-Enchantments only last as long as they have a mana source.\n-Thaumaturges must imagine the object they see, in great detail, with the enchantment on it in their mind.\n* Transfiguration *\n-------------------The art of changing an object’s appearance.\n-------------------\n\n-Objects must keep their original mass.\n-Objects can only change their state, not their chemical makeup. (Ie. Ice to water, not water to wine.)\n\n-Thaumaturge must be touching and see  the object to transfigure it.\n-Thaumaturges must imagine the object altering,exactly how they want it, in their mind and the steps it would need to go through for the transfiguration to be possible.\n* Abjuration *\n-------------------The art of protection.\n-------------------\n\n-Wards are barriers of mana which cancel out other, aggressive mana.\n-Wards only block spells which have less mana than the ward was made with.\n\n-Wards only last so long as they have a mana source.\n-The Thaumaturge must imagine their mana being released from their body and forming a barrier around them, in the shape they desire.\nChapter 3.\n\n   - Conjuration -\n    The Conjurer\n\nA highly complicated form of magic, Conjuration involves summoning organic beings from the Void.\n-Beings can only remain in existence so long as they have a mana source which would keep them alive in reality.\n-Conjurer’s need to understand the insides and outs, literally, of the creature they wish to summon lest they get something terribly wrong.\n-Primordial Conjurers can summon elemental beings, though they must have an understand of at least one evocation element.\n-Primordial Conjurers do not need to understand the biological structure of their being, only use their mana,  and an understanding of basic motor skills in creatures.\n-Conjurers must see where they wish to summon their creature.\nChapter 4.\n\n       - Illusion -\n      The Magician\n\nA dark form of magic which involves using mana to alter one’s senses.\n-Magicians can only alter the senses\n\n-Anything a magician does is not actually there, no matter how real it feels, looks, smells etc…\n\n-Magicians cannot read minds….or directly change one’s emotion.\n-This is often known as glamour magic.\n\n-A Magician must have experience with their illusion in real life. (ie. To make someone feel as if they are giving birth, the magician would have to understand what giving birth feels like)\n-Illusions only remain in existence so long as they have a source of mana.\n\n-Magician must be able to see where they wish to produce their illusion.\n-The Magician must (smell, taste, hear, touch etc…) the object before they can produce it, with accuracy.  This is why the Magician must have experienced the sense they wish to alter in reality.\nThe End\n         ~ ~ ~ ~", ""),
        StaticBook("The Arcane Gift", "First Enchanter Sarrion Zytiaear", "The Arcane Gift\n  <------------->\nFrom the desk of the       First Enchanter\n///////////////////\n\nThis thesis was written for those who are looking to become mages, to give the insight of how magic truely is.\nThe Arcane Gift,\nA scar in which is embedded in all descendants with true potential. Willpower is the key to unlock this potential, and with it comes the plethora of power that is embedded within us. This power is not one to surpass GOD\nand does not surpass the powers of those who serve him, the arcane gift is simply one of true potential simple, as man may tap into with the true potential of a skill that comes with practicing with a blade or hammer.\nThis true potential,\nIt is one that comes with a lifestyle embedded in so many lives, From the Mage to the Sorcerer and Wizard ways we find ourselves so drastically distant from those who do not have such an arcane gift,\nyet we are truly indifferent. We are simply those who take up book and wand, rather than a sword and hammer.\nThis lifestyle,\nIt is one not of chains and oath, loyalty to serve, It is one in which the arcane gift allows us to fully embrace our art in which we paint upon the canvas that this gift allows us to access.\nWe implement it into our very lives as not by choice, but because it is the path we chose to follow and with such as any man should we take responsibility for his choices.\nThe arcane gift will make man weak, for the laws of equivalent exchange dictates that for one, you must give another. For our potential, we give our potential to do these other crafts and skills away, our strength.\nBut as always there are the lost,\nThose who throw away their potential and arcane gift to use it for naught the discovery of knowledge or the power and potential of a faction or nation but simply to hurt.\nThis blindfold of power engulfs the mage in ways that many might follow without magic, and use their power to hurt with incoherent and distorted reasons, or to torture for fun. We dub these of our kin ‘Rogue Magi’,\nones who refuse the lifestyle of the arcane and embrace one known for cruel and personal gain. They are naught lost as hope may be brought to them, but in the end of they refuse such it is our duty together to amend this,\nand ensure the safety of not only other magi by the viewpoint of those without the arcane gift, but the safety of our ways and how all who gaze upon it see it.\nIn the end,\nWe all have different reasons from among our selves on why we choose to embrace our arcane gift. Some do such for power, in their minds linger the thought that perhaps a potential fireball holds high ground\nover the pull of a bow or swing of a blade. Some do such for knowledge, they delve into the unknown to bring the known back to descendants, allowing us to embrace a new found knowledge that we had once lost. Some of us were born into it,\nour parents embedded into the ways of the arcane for their own reason we grow up to look upon the arcane as something we must do, to follow in the steps of our parents as if one may become a knight like their father, or a smith.\nIn the end, this is our life and we embrace this with passion regardless of why we took this path.\n\n\n-First Enchanter\n   Sarrion Zytiaear", ""),
        StaticBook("The Arcane, V1", "Meldur the Blue", "______\n\n     Understanding\n       the Arcane\n          ______\n\n     Published 1472\n         Volume I\n\n\n\n\n  By Meldur the Blue\nChapter 1\n\n    Like in all fields of study, for one to adequately learn and retain knowledge of the Arcane arts, he or she must first understand the origin of what is widely known as magic. If a student were to attempt to do so without proper\nfoundation, there is a high chance that he or she would be unsuccessful, and, even if he or she was successful, there is a great risk that the knowledge gained would be used to inappropriate ends. Just as a politician would study history so as not to make\nthe same mistake twice, so must an Arcanist. \n    And so this is what the earliest parts of this book will aim to cover, namely where different forms of magic come from, how it has evolved over the many years, and important figures of study whos works and\ndiscoveries will prove beneficial to the process of understanding the Arcane.\nChapter 2\n\n    All forms of \"magic\" can be divided into two main categories, the first being Void Magic, and the second being Diety Magic, each named after their respective sources. The first of these two categories is the one which we will focus\non at the moment.\n    As mentioned previously, all Void Magic comes from the Void. The Void is the term for an endless expanse of nothingness, not physically of this world, that contains everything that has ever existed or been sensed in the material\nworld. In other words, nothing exists in the Void except for endless potential. At times, a being may attempt to make contact with the Void. If the attempt is successful, he or she may draw potential from the Void and use it in the material world. This\npotential can come in nearly any form. However, the being who attempts to draw it must first be very familiar with the form they wish to it to take. This difference in forms of potential gives us the different fields and sub-sections of Void Magic.\nNow because technically, any being has the ability to draw potential from the Void, any being also has the ability to practice Void Magic. This makes Void Magic the easier of the two main categories to learn. However, it can be difficult to establish\n╔══════════╗\n║\n║\n║   **************      ║  A diagram of the\n║    five elements\n║ is depicted on this\n║          page\n║   **************\n║\n║\n║\n╚══════════╝\n╔══════════╗\n║\n║\n║   **************\n║   A table of tips\n║ for connecting to\n║     the Void is\n║ shown on the page\n║   **************\n║\n║\n║\n╚══════════╝\na connection the the Void, and even more difficult to maintain that connection while drawing potential from it. First, the user must abandon his or her mental perception of reality, and instead open it up to the endless possibility of a limitless nothing.\nAs our minds are finite, it is impossible to grasp something infinite. Because of this, it is only possible to access certain parts of the Void, and not its entirety.\n    Connecting to the void is an exhausting and daunting task, and can take many\nattempts, especially on one's first experience. In order to establish and maintain contact with the Void, one must use the mystical energy which fills our bodies and world known as Mana. Just as performing physical tasks costs physical energy, so does\nperforming magical tasks cost magical energy. When Mana is depleted, or when the user is distracted, the connection to the Void is broken and any potential taken from the Void returns to it.\n    This brings us to the two governing laws of all Void Magic.\nThe first is called the Law of Conservation of Reality. It states that anything performed by magical means takes up the same amount of energy as if it were performed by non-magical means. In other words, there is no endless supply of energy for magic. The\nsecond law is called the Law of Creation, and states that something cannot be created from nothing. This is to say that all magical feats require an equal sacrifice to perform, usually in the form of Mana. It also states that all Void Magic comes from the\nVoid and must return to it. Now this second law is governed by what is called the Evaglno Effect, which says that just as seemingly super-physical feats can be performed at times through the help of adrenaline, so can super-magical feats be performed, but\nat an equally taxing and detimental cost.\n    Now there are four main Archetypes of Void Magic, used to more easily classify the fields themselves. They are Alteration, Mental Manipulation, Evocation, and the Dark Arts. This book will not go in depth on\neach individual field of Void Magic, but it will provide a brief description of each Archetype.\n    Alteration is the most difficult of the four Archetypes to learn. It involves using the Void to shape and alter objects that already exist in the physical\nworld. Subtypes include Transfiguration, Telekenesis, Translocation, Household Magic, and the Whimsical Magics.\n    Mental Manipulation involves using thoughts, experiences, feelings, and images from the Void in order to affect the user's\nmind or the mind of another. It is a very dangerous form of magic, although it cannot physically injure someone directly. The subtypes are Illusion, Mental Magic, and Cognitism.\n    Evocation is the broadest of all Void Magics, as well as the easiest to\nlearn. Through Evocation, a magic user can \"evoke\" potential from the Void and manifest it in a physical way as elements, objects, or living things. Subtypes of Evocation are the Five Elements, Arcane Evocation, Arcane Shielding, and Conjuration.\nThe last Archetype of Void Magic is without a doubt the most evil and dangerous. The Dark Arts are manifestations of pure evil, and serve no purpose other than the corruption of the world and the harm of others. They are outlawed by most Nations, and\ntheir use will yield dire consequences. Subtypes of the Dark Arts include Contract Magic and Okar, Necromancy, Shade Magic, Soul Puppetry, and Fi'hiiran'tanya, also known as Magic Blocking.\nChapter 3\n\n    As even the simplest of creatures is aware, our world is governed by beings of higher power known as Aenguls and Daemons. They are still ruled by the mightiest of all beings, the Creator, who brought everything into\nfruition out of nothing, including magic and the Void.\n    These Aenguls and Daemons are constantly seeking to interact with the physical world in some way, and because of this, many of them offer supernatural powers to otherwise mortal beings. We call\nthese powers Diety Magic. Diety Magic is more difficult to obtain than Void Magic, because one must be granted it by the Spiritual Entity itself, though control can be taught by other mortals with the same blessing. \n    All dieties expect something of\ntheir followers, and so not fulfilling these obligations results in what is known as an unattunement from the diety. This is known as the Law of Servitude, and states that a diety may at any time grant or take away magical abilities at a whim. This is not\nto say that it happens often though, and usually requires some sort of grave act of disobedience.\n    Now because of the first two laws of magic, we must assume that even Diety Magic requires some form of energy or sacrifice to perform. However, in this\nspecific instance, it does not only tax the user but the spirit as well. The magic used feeds off of the connection that the user has made with his or her mystical patron, and so when that connection is used up, no more magic can be performed for a period\nof time.\n    Due to their shared belief in the same or similar Dieties, many users of Diety Magic band together to form Guilds, Orders, and even Cults dedicated to the study and responsible use of their respective field of magic. Popular examples of such\ngroups include the Druidic Order, followers of the Aspects Ceridwen and Cernunos, the Ascended, servants of the Aengul Ariel, and those who practice Muun'Trivazja, Kharajyr Priests of the Daemon Metztli.\n    Now those Dieties which grant magical\nabilities often wish to establish a strong sense of contingency when it comes to their followers. As a result, Aenguls and Daemons alike have been known to strip magical abilities from their followers who attempt to practice other forms of magic. A common\nexample of this would be the Aspects \"unattuning\" a Druid if he or she were to establish a connection with the void. It is because of this nurtured sense of contingency that many practicioners of Diety Magic have harbored a mistrust and dislike of\npractitioners of Void Magic, and vice versa.      Now because there are a great deal of Aenguls and Daemons willing to bestow power upon mortal servants, the number of Archtypes used to categorize the many different fields of Diety Magic is far higher\nthan that of Void Magic. They include Druidism, Shamanism, Rune Smithing, Clerical magic, Monk magic, Ascended magic, Undead magic, Scourge magic, and Muun'Trivazja. Although there are more Archtypes, the Archtypes themselves are less internally diverse,\nin other words, they each hold far fewer fields.\nChapter 4\n\n    Now as we learned earlier, the use of magic still requires the expenditure of energy, whether it be through Mana or the connection with a Diety. However, most mortal bodies are not at all used to using these particular forms of\nenergy, and as such it can take a more costly toll on the user's physical body. This phenomenon is known as Corruption. The fourth law of magic, the Law of Corruption, therefore states that the more energy one puts into developing Arcane ability, the less\nis available for non-magical tasks. Therefore, in theory, an entirely magical being such as a spirit could not take on a real, physical form, except for through magical means.\nChapter 5\n\n    Just as with all things, magic was brought into existence by the Creator at the beginning of time. At first, magic was a very, very rare phenomenon. Not many people had access to it, and even fewer understood it. Only\na fraction of the currently known fields of magic were know during the first hundred or so years of recorded history, but great efforts were made to discover more.\n    Now as time progressed, mortals began to further explore this expanse of nothingness\nknown as the Void. Great wizards arose, and new fields of magic were found. The Arcane Arts were born as an object of study, and more and more people began to understand, study, and practice.\n    It was not at any specific time that the Aenguls and\nDaemons began to meddle with the affairs of Men, they did. As their involvement grew, so did the power and number of their followers, thus leading to the earliest Diety Magic Guilds being formed. These Guilds and their Void Magic counterparts yielded some\nof the mightiest, wisest, and maddest wizards the world has ever come to know.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Art of Love", "Ava Enlar", "-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n'The Art of Love'\n\nby David Wycombe,      'A connoisseur in the art of making love'.\n\n\n*a barely                 discernable, crude drawing of two stick figures atop of each other is here*\nDear readers, unto you shall I bestow the fruits of my labour and experiences\nwithin the art of love.\n\nWithin these leatherbound page shall you unlock the key to your partner's heart and more importantly- their genitalia: as\nillustrated by I, the\n- of all things\nsex-related, David Wycombe.\n\nIn 3 easy steps shall you learn the secret of the refined art that is intercourse,\nwhich has been tinkered with and experimented for years by me, thereby maximizing the pleasure between\nStep 1) Find a\npartner, (woman, man, dog, cat, tree...)\n\nStep 2) Stick it in the hole.\n\nStep 3) Repeat Step 2.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Art of Warp1", "Dionysus the Akritian", "THE ART OF WAR\n_____________________________\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBy Adolf von Manstein\nI.Raising An Army\n_____________________________I.In the art of war, the matter of, to say with no exageration of any kind, the most import is levying a force large enough to carry out your campaigns.\n\nII.And so the forces of the realm\nmay be divided into these categories: Sergeants, Knights and Squires, Levied Peasantry, Bugher Watches or Militias; Specialised Mercenaries.\n\nIII.When levying knights to your cause, it is not uncommon for a soveriegn king or prince to offer financial\nincentives to gentry to take up arms. These may come under movable property of any sort, be it minas, cattle, or otherwise. It must be said this may be financially straining, so it is good for a sovereign, be he in a time where his knights\nand squires are needed badly, to offer riches in the form of the possessions in his house. In the practical art of war, where the profit of the sovereign is of importance, we must see this as a last resort. \nIV.For it is well known to be\nnot very prestigious. If a king gives his household personal goods such as gold objects, jewelry and weapons, riding horses and destriers, rival princes, dukes, kings and caliphs will see your realm as poor, and you as weak, for you are giving the\nhonoured goods of your family.\n\nV.The use of giving enemy riches, which would usually go the sovereign, to knights and squires as a financial reward and incentive is much less of a poor course, however. For you have taken it from the enemy,\nat no cost to the prestige of your own house.\n\nVI.Therefore, it may be summarised as this: Financial incentives (and punishments) must be observed to get the best service, and these are preferably\nand these are preferably done from minas and loot, rather than your own possessions. For though the knights have an obligation to fight for you, they will do so best with incentive.\nVII.A final note is that horses are the most expensive part of a knight’s equipment, and they are prone to disease, death on the battlefield and other losses. Therefore, to the men who have more horses, there must be more pay. It must be added that\nthose who are use riding horses such as  palfreys on the march, and then ride destriers and coursers into battle. To these people it must be said, that they have gone out of their way to have more horses, and must be given more wealth. It is also frequent\nto replace lost horses out of the commander's purse.\n\nIX.Sergeants are another important force on the battlefield. It is these spearmen and light horsemen who have ensured Oren’s victories for the last few decades.\nAny who comes under this category is a man who is not gentry or noble, a mere common man, but one who is a professional soldier, always at the call in the manner of a retinue. For example, most of the Order of Saint Amyas’ footmen count as sergeants.\nIX.The sustenance of sergeants is of some, but not of great cost. They only expect low wages, and in some cases can afford their own equipment. Many of them are craftsmen themselves, able to repair and maintain their own spears,\nkettle helms, shields and arming swords without interruption.\n\nXI.Their training is well too, but can they match the wealth and training of a knight? Nay, but they may be relied upon well to hold the line well.\nIs it little wonder their use is so common in the realm?\n\nX.It may be necessary for the nobility of the realm to pay for the arming and training of these troops, as it has become something of a convention. That is what is expected,\nand the expectancy to pay for one’s own equipment will be greeted with hostility. The wise commander and lord sees his own sergeants equipped with his own wealth, which will be greeted with elation.\nXII.t is rare to get good sergeants out of a feudal obligation, as is common with levies and knights. Instead, one must ensure the critical task of sending out recruiting parties often and gaining the affection of the people so that they may volunteer.\nXIII.These two aforementioned groups form most of the best men besides from mercenaries, and throughout the course of our history the proportion of knights to sergeants has changed. In modern times, it is often 1 knight for every 24 sergeants.\nXIV.It is much quicker and easier to raise sergeants, for they are ready and may be called upon. It does well to have a large force of these fellows in case a desperate situation ensues, or to dispute a man of his land without expecting actual fighting.\nXV.The city militias and watches are to be rarely called onto the field, mostly used to garrison the various cities of the realm. However, if they are levied, it may be customary to offer rudimentary pay, even of a low sort.\nXVI.These men are the quickest to call upon in a levy, for they already have basic training and arms, and merely require calling into arms. It may be said that they can be used to merely boost the number of soldiers on the field, used in a siege,\nor to act as auxiliaries of sorts to their more well-equipped and trained counterparts. Many are equipped with crossbows, which are quite simple to use, and used to attack the enemy with missiles.\nXVII.It must be said that though the Codes of Saint Edmond (Chivalry) prohibit a mean sacking of cities, the militiamen and sergeants must have their regards. You must forage from the enemy, and loot from civilians.\nThese men are not knights, and are not bound by this code. This will be ample payment, and there is little need for additional incentive, should you use them in the field.\n\nXVIII.Levymen form the bulk of your missile troops\nand garrisons. Levies must buy their own equipment, and usually are unarmoured and untrained. This is why they are only useful for missile troops. Again, these men need no additional incentive but that which they forage from the enemy.\nXIX.Mercenaries allow a sovereign or a marshal to gain troops that are specialised, such as horse archers, light cavalry, missile troops such as crossbowmen, as well as high quality infantry.These men require payment to such a degree\nthat they will be a heavy financial burden on the realm. They will be covered in greater detail in the next part.\n“O, wealth of burghers! Your money of Petrus is most needed in times of war, and you are surely richer than those of the country, yet you feel you pay enough? Nay, damndest burghers, you mock poor fellows thus!”-Harald Von Manstein, 1499\nII.Mercenaries and Their Uses\n_____________________________I.There are two times when the use of mercenaries may be considered good or necessary. \nOne:-When your own subjects are disloyal or unwilling to fight, or dislike the marshal. You must ensure they\nwill not defect or run, for they care not for loyalty when the man who they are loyal to is unpopular.\n\nTwo:-When your realm is approaching a war that is critical or important. Mercenaries are a true financial burden on the realm,\nfor they expect pay at a specific time, and a specific amount and their sustenance is very costly. If you do not pay them, they will desert. They also require huge financial incentives, so do not use mercenaries\nin wars which are small and minor, or which your standard army can win without. \n\nII.The general who makes but few calculations on whether his troops are of good enough quality and quantity to defeat the enemy\nwill waste his wealth away, or watch his troops die. It is well to form a council before a war with all the great men of the realm, to discover if mercenaries are necessary.\n\nIII.Therefore we can see mercenaries\ncan be used badly or well. Sometimes, if the marshal is inexperienced, the mercenaries must be left to their own commands. For he is not versed in their speciality, merely in standard warfare. Saint Theodosius’ blessings, horsemen of Adria!\nFor he is the man of heralds and messengers and horses and all good and honest horsemen, and you will fight with valour. But be damned to your pay, for you cost your realm too much!\nIII.The Acquisition of Ships\n_____________________________I.The cheapest and quickest way of acquiring ships is requisitioning merchant vessels. If you do not wish for the merchant class to hate you, you may buy them,\nbut then it will be cheaper to build your own war galleys. Therefore, if you are using merchant ships, take them by force. Then they are are cheap, can be modified and are excellent for transporting troops.\nII.The second cheapest way of acquiring ships is to take them from the enemy or cause them to defect. This may be done by seizing enemy ports,or in naval engagements. This can be done from previous wars,\nand you should never attempt to sink the enemy for their ships will prove useful later. Rather, board them and kill them, or compel them to surrender using heavy missile fire. Then, you can use the conquered foe to augment one’s own strength.\nIII.Of course, the third cheapest way is to build your own ships. This takes time and wealth, but you may use the latest naval technology and have specialised galleys and other vessels.\n\nIV.And the final course which is completely inadvisable\nin any way is to hire mercenary fleets. Because ships are of such high sustenance, you will find yourself not only paying for the expensive cost of mercenaries but for their ships. They will expect monstrous pay, to the\npoint where your fleet will cost hundreds of ounces of silver each month, until, after a few years, one third of your income will be dissipated. And sometimes, they will be less effective than your own ships too.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Artificer I", "Belestram Sylvaeri", "The Tragedy of\n      The Artificer\n       In Two Parts\n\n         Part I\n\n\nBy Belestram of the Venerable House Sylvaeri,\n\nWritten this Sixteenth of the Deep Cold, 1609, for Aislin Maar.\nIn Princedom fair, in days of old,\nThere toiled craftsmen, wise and bold,\n\nWho by their labour did abide,\nTo pierce the veil which doth divide\nThis mortal world, and one beyond,\nAnd crossing there, could thus abscond\n\nWith truths forgotten, learned anew,\nFrom Elder Gods both false and true.\n\nOne such there lived, of  manner stern,\nAnd of his kin did most discern,\nFor strove he, always, for ideal,\nAnd grinding failures 'neath his heel,\n\nDisdained of Elves, and hid his skill,\nAmong far wooded, forest hills.\n\nUntil one day, by fate's decree,\nHe found an eldritch, ancient tree.\nWith leaves of gold, and boughs of white,\nWhich shone like silver in the night.\n\nA relic of the past, it stood,\nThe first among that sacred wood,\n\nWhose roots drank deep of mighty spells,\nWhich Elves of yore spun on the dells.\nThe elf was stunned, his soul was bound,\nAnd in that place a purpose found,\n\nTo carve in wood a likeness keen,\nA sculpture, as had never been.\n\nHe toiled long, and slaved away,\nCompelled by force beyond his sway,\nUntil at last, his labour done,\nHe stood and wept beneath the sun,\n\nFor there before him, pale as death,\nStood woman lifelike, lacking breath.\n\nHer eyes did gaze unto his own,\nAnd stirred a feeling, never known\nTo him- a pressing, urgent love,\nAnd he beseeched the gods above,\n\nTo grant her life, and make her whole,\nTo soothe his own beguiled soul.\n\nBut here, my friends, we must take note,\nOf passion's plea is often wrote,\nAnd ne'er a wise thing is it, for\nThe outcome one might oft abhor.\n\nThe elf-lord's love did seal his fate,\nFor gods of old are scarce innate,\n\nAnd love to know the hearts of men,\nTo bless, and curse, (and curse again.)\nThe Elder Ones made swift reply,\nThese gods of sound, and stone, and sky,\n\nA wind there was, a clamor brash,\nAnd from that tumult, lightning lashed.\n\nIt struck the figure, gave it life,\nAnd beauty there was born from strife\nLike none which ever had been seen,\nAnd none which ever since has been.\n\nAnd feeling, seeing, knowing so,\nHer wooden eyes did find a glow,\n\nAnd cheeks like apples flushed with red,\nJust as the smitten elf had pled.\n___________________      \n    End of Part  I\n\n-------------------", ""),
        StaticBook("The Aspect Tomes", "Dedicant Elizabeth", "Aspect Tome:\nCompassion\nCompassion, what is it? A mysterious feeling that cannot be understood, but can be felt at the most dire moments. An example would be when a child is getting hit right before your eyes. Be honest with yourself, would you feel anything when you lay your\neyes upon that child? That is called Compassion. It cannot easily be described but I will try my best to decipher its purpose in the living emotion spectrum. It is true that this feeling, this emotion, is what makes people act, makes them want to do\nsomething, makes them want to fight back. That is true, but why is this you ask?\nIt is because when one person feels another person's pain, it is followed by another piece of the Emotion chain link, which is \"Rage\". When a man has been hurt there is an urge inside of him saying, \"get him back\" or \"destroy him\",\nbut as a Druid or a Dedicant you must resist this urge no matter what.\nCompassion is one of the reasons why we Druids strive to help people, we can see how they are lowly on the streets, how they are helpless,\nand how that can be changed if the Druids can help them.\nThis has been an Aspect description on the Emotion of Compassion. There are other races that think otherwise, but we have our own beliefs, and we choose to stand by it. This is the Tome of Compassion.\nCredited to Tamsin for the work, copied by Dedicant Elizabeth.\nAspect Tome:\nFear\nFear, another emotion that drives the Will of a man. This Book will describe all it can, for fear can not be a good thing for the Druids, not at all... The emotion of Fear is susceptible but can be very deceitful,\nit can drive people to do things they have no choice of doing, an example would be like this:\nImagine a man with the perfect life and perfect family, then a stranger says that all of it will be taken away in the blink of an eye if he does not kill someone. Unless his Will is strong, this man can and will murder someone for the sake of his family,\nand the emotion that is currently driving him is the power of fear... It is the easiest emotion to spot within yourself and another man, and too much fear can lead to insanity.\nThe Druid should try not to be seduced to the madness of fear. Everybody gets scared all the time, it is part of the nature of Life, but the dark side is that it can control you if you do not fight back.\nIn order to overcome fear, you must have Confidence and Willpower; then this darkness that lies within you shall disappear. But Fear can never die, it is like a disease that can never be cured and a fire that will never be put out, remember this,\nmy friends, and do not give in to it...\nCredited to Tamsin for the work, copied by the Dedicant Elizabeth.\nAspect Tome:\nGreed\nGreed, not even the best can resist this emotion. Something as Evil as Greed can't even be described properly, but an attempt will be made. The Emotion of Greed carries out in generations to come from the first evil.\nThe Evil God, Iblees, cursed the Dwarves with this evil. This Emotion, this Avarice can turn your own friends again you, and it is triggered by Temptation, which very few people can easily resist.\nThis makes Greed a very dangerous Emotion. This emotion is never good and must not be taken lightly, so watch yourself, for you might be its next victim.\nCredited to Tamsin for the work, copied by Dedicant Elizabeth.\nAspect Tome:\nHope\nHope, the very true innocence in a place where all is lost. No matter what happens, a person will always have hope, but how does it affect us? It is very simple, Hope is a very difficult emotion anybody can do with right now.\nA hope for a miracle or healing is most likely a very common hope, usually targeted at Aerial or any of the Arch-Aenguls, but there is also a secret within this emotion that not many people know.\nHope is the emotion that supported the birth of Life. It cannot be explained easily, but it is true.\nBut for us Druids, our trigger on Hope is very similar, but different. We have our hopes on the Aspects, which are Cerridwen and Cernunnos, we are their conduits and we expect them to assisst us in our times of need...\nHope can trigger within us at any moment, when War is happening, when you're being held hostage, when a family member or a friend is dying. It can happen as much as it can, but you cannot assume to ignore it.\nIt is often described as, \"The smallest light in a room full of darkness,\" even the very evil have it, but their use for it is on their own accord.\nThis also causes many things, rebellions and such, for some take Hope too seriously, and it often turns them into power-hungry people. This has been an account of this Emotion, may your new found Knowledge flourish.\nCredited to Tamsin for the work, copied by Dedicant Elizabeth.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Awakening", "Rosie Nym Vainglorious", "*´¨)\n¸.•´¸.•*´¨) ¸.•*¨)\n(¸.•´ (¸.•` ¤ The Awakening\n\nby Rosie Vainglorious\nI had a dream the world was ending\n\nShadows bleeding white noise\n\nThe walls in their unbecoming\n\nWere confused hazy forms\nBut when I awoke alone outside\n\nThe breeze breathed into this ear of mine:\n\nTravel free and mark your stride\n\nFor this new world awaits for you to find", ""),
        StaticBook("The Azdrazi", "Icarus Adil", "The Azdrazi\n\n        Haelun'or,\n           Axios\n\n     Published 1592\n\n\n\n     by Icarus Adil\nThe Azdrazi\n===================   The Azdrazi are an odd creature, draconic in nature, which have recently returned to some prominence in the land of Axios. Upon their head are long, brown horns, and their skin is unmistakably scaly. Their eyes are orange\nand serpentine, their pupils slitted, long and thin. They can retract these fearsome features to a certain extent, though not all choose to. At a glance, the Azdrazi are monsters, and will likely strike fear in the hearts of those who see them.\nFortunately, this is false.\n   In this work, it is my hope to spread understanding regarding the Azdrazi, for these misgivings not only pose undue risks to their well-being, yet also hamper them in pursuit of their noble task. The Azdrazi should not be\nregarded as monstrosities of evil, or as ne'er do wells of any sort. Instead, they should be treated as neutral creatures pursuant of a righteous task, as I shall explain below.\n   To begin, one must look to the history of the Azdrazi, for their existence\npredates most of our own. The creatures first emerged during the Great War, borne with the sole intent of stopping the darkness of the Betrayer Iblees. Much of their history has been lost to time or otherwise destroyed, but it is known that the current\niteration of Azdrazi stem from the line formed by Azdromoth, prior to his present affliction.\n   The current brood of Azdrazi began with the stirring of one known as Alistair, the child of Azdromoth, and father of the remaining Azdrazi, at least as far\nas is currently known. He returned and began to create other Azdrazi, though the method of doing so is still unknown. Unfortunately, it was not until after this began that they learnt of Azdromoth’s descent to existence as a Drakaar, a fate most Dragaar\nescape by confining themselves to stone.\n   With this knowledge, the Azdrazi have severed ties with their progenitor, instead pursuing the goals their very existence is predicated upon. They exist to protect man against the forces of darkness, and\nhope to one day find a cure for the blight which affects their father and grandfather, Azdromoth the Arch-Drakaar.\n   Though these creatures have found conflict against the Paladins of Xan, as is natural giving their order's aversion to the dragonkin, it\nwould seem a truce may be found. The disciples in the Cult of Azdromoth also combat the Azdrazi, as is natural for those who worship the Arch-Drakaar in its present form. Yet beyond this, the Azdrazi hold no conflict with man, and should indeed be treated\nin accordance to their intentions: to protect man against the dark.\n   In conclusion, I encourage all who find themselves in the presence of Azdrazi not only to stay any hostility based on assumptions of their aesthetic, yet also to thank them for their\nservice to the realm of mortality. It seems that we all owe them our appreciation, and they are yet to find it.\nNotes\n===================\n\nThe information for this piece was gathered through the author's interview of Mister Suldaeroth and Mister Favnir, two Azdrazi who freely gave information regarding their existence. Their support of\nintellectual pursuit will not go unforgotten, so long as the information they have offered does not prove false. If you see them, thank them for their service both through this tome, yet also against those who promote darkness in our realm.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Bardic Rite", "Oliver", "The tasks we set out before our charges are not tests of their character or dedication, they are lessons, first and foremost. The test doesn't come until they have breathed their first breath as a Druid, --\n-- and felt the touch of the world as they realize their new role. Druidism is the test, not the reward, and Dedicancy is the lesson, not the trial.\n\nAnd the first lesson is to open their eyes.\nFor if they are blind, they will trudge along through all the lessons you could give without being able to see what they truly mean. \n\nFor this reason, the bardic rite is no simple talent show. It is not a test. It is no pointless tradition.\nIt may seem like a fun excersize to draw your Dedicant in, but it is an important lesson nonetheless. It is a way to open the Dedicant's mind to the path that lays out before them.\nA way of initiating them into the mindset that will be natural for them when they finally bloom.\n\nPoetry has come to be the staple, yes, but the rite makes no such requiremt. At least, not by my interpretation.\nA poem is simply what most people assume they need to do, and the presumption has infiltrated even the Guides. Creativity is a Druid's greatest asset, and this line of thought inhibits it, both for those who teach it and those they teach.\nA bard is no simple poet. A bard is an artist of many muses. A spoken word, a poem, a melodious tune. Harmony by any means is not the sole medium by which they express themselves. Songs without words, stories without structure.\nBrush, chisel, knife or even fire. Bards are storytellers, keepers of one's culture, and weavers of feeling, not through poetry, or even just tales. At the heart of every bard is art, not simply song and dance, or even a pen.\nPoetry is just one avenue they pursue. Claiming to know unwaveringly that the only true path is down that avenue.\nClaiming that the 'Bardic Rite' itself requires it, limits the Dedicant's ability to truly show their colors, to truly inscribe their personal dedication to nature into their work.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Beastiary I", "Adeon of Rhoswen", "The Marked Man's\nCompendium of Beasts\n\n\n        Volume II\n\n\n\n\n\n\n          Book I\nI. Animals\nII. Natural Monsters\nIII. Sentient Naturals\nIV. Sentient S.\nV. Monstrous S. 1/2\nSection I\n\n\n\n\n\n         Animals\n-Mammals-\n\nMammals are the group of vertebrae animals which form the class Mammalia. They have fur and the females bear live young, and produce milk for the young. Parental care of the young is universal among mammals and is crucial.\n-Birds-\n\nBirds are a class of vertebrates, the Aves. They are warm blooded and lay eggs. Their bodies are covered in feathers and they are winged. Birds are bipedal. Birds eat a lot of food compared to their weight due to their high energy use.\n-Fish-\n\nFish are gill-bearing aquatic vertebrates which lack limbs with digits. Fish are covered with scales, and have two sets of paired fins, and several unpaired fins. They are usually cold-blooded.\n-Reptile-\n\nReptile species are cold blooded, have scaly skin, and lay cleidoic eggs. They excrete uric acid, and have a cloaca. Reptiles are said to be the oldest of all animals and the closest to monstrosity.\n-Amphibians-\n\nIncluding frogs, salamanders and caecillians. These are 4 limbed vertebrates who are cold blooded. They lay their eggs in water. After hatching, they are tadpoles, which have gills. Once adult, they have lungs to breathe instead.\nSection II\n\n\n\n\n    \n\n    Natural Monsters\n-The Harpy-\n\nThese beasts prefer mountainous areas full of rocky patches where they may build nests and ambush their prey. \n\nHarpies posess large claws protruding from their toes and fingers, as well as a sharp beak.\nThey are humanoid in shape and from their spine sprouts two large, raven-like wings which are made up of large feathers of darker colours.  \n\nA trait shared by most Harpies is kleptomania, which can be taken advantage of in order to lure the beast.\nBeneath their beaks are glands which secrete oil when their body goes into combat-mode. The oil makes it very difficult for the Harpies to be grasped. Despite the advantages that may come with this ability, there is also a significant downside.\nThe oil is extremely flammable, almost on par with vodka. There is no way for the Harpies to put out the fire due to the oil soaking deep into their flesh and wings. Once alight, the Harpy is utterly doomed.\n-Krummavisur-\n\nEssentially giant ravens with powerful wings and claws. The primary method of killing their prey is by snatching them into the air and tossing them long distances.\nThey can kick up dust with the flap of their wings dense enough to block vision for yards. When more effort is applied, they can shove a fully armored figure onto his back with the strength of the air alone.\nThey have four weak spots. Both eyes and both feet. The only parts of their body not covered in dense feather. Strike in these areas to kill the beast.\n-Blodzuiger-\n\nThe Blodzuiger resembles a hairless bat with an extended neck and no face, just a massive, gaping mouth with rows of razor sharp teeth within. The beast's flesh is a natural flame retardant.\nYoung Blodzuigers resemble bloated leeches. They are without limbs and simply writhe around like a landbased tadpole. They are able to climb, however, using their powerful jaws and often drop down onto their prey from above.\nAdult Blodzuigers posess  pair of sharp wings, which they use to attack their prey with blinding accuracy and speed. The use of elixirs is suggested when fighting Blodzuigers. Particularily the kind that improve reflexes and vision in darkness.\n-Slaton-\n\nBloated creatures of the sea of humanoid appearance. They have sharp teeth with wide jaws capable of swallowing a man's head whole. They seem to enjoy feeding on livestock. Highly aggressive towards all humans.\nDespite the aggressive nature of the Slaton, it is possible to intimidate the beast with a show of force and equal amount of aggression. The Slaton's other method of combat is its ability to generate electricity through some natural process.\nDirect contact with a Slaton will cause an electric shock that will paralyse a man and send him to the floor. A dangerous problem when facing a Slaton is its many layers of blubber- which are very hard to pierce using any handheld weapon melee weapon.\nIt is for this reason a crossbow or a longbow should be used. Another weakness is fire. But most of all, if the beast is struck with a metal bolt in the right place in its spine, the electricity will backfire on the Slaton, causing it to explode.\n-Magnus Araneae-\n\nArachnids are lone hunters- they patiently wait for their prey to kill it with one swift strike when it appears. The same is true for their enlarged counterparts, Magnus Araneae.\nThese are huge creatures that took a liking to caves and big trees, becoming their undisputed kings. Rulers who do not tolerate other hunters in their territory, including Marked Men. Aranea are large, slow and protected by a durable armor.\nThe carapace, as Marked Men call this armor, is especially tough from the front, so it is much easier to wound the creature from the side or the back. The Araneae's charges its prey often. One has to evade the charge at all costs.\nAs soon as the beast has charged, one must then make their blow count. Without doubt its the best to use High-Guard along with half-pirouettes. The araneae has no fear of poison and not much fear of fire. Its nervous system barely reacts to pain.\nThe beast will heal its wounds after the fight. All said and done, the Aranea is a bug, so one's blade should be coated with pesticide oil before fighting it. The monster's susceptibility to this blade coating is probably its sole weakness.\nThe beast can easily shrug off other Marked tricks, so common poisons and spells are of little use, not to mention attempts to knock the colossus down.\nSection III\n\n\n\n\n   Sentient Naturals\n-The Troll-\n\nUsually found lurking in caves, forests or more commonly under bridges, these beasts can be helpful and friendly-- at other times they are a force to be reckoned with.\nTrolls are generally rather intelligent creatures capable of speech, emotion and co-operation. The best method of slaying a Troll is to disable its method of movement. \nThis method of movement being its legs. Aim for knees or the ankle tendon.\n-The Sylvan-\n\nSylvans often inhabit farmlands due to their diet of crops. If they can't find any caves, crevices, pits or chasms they will dig out their own little trench-like nests to live in.\nTheir nests are used to store their balls and left over crops, which they steal from nearby farmland. Sylvans combine the traits of both goats and men. They have blunt horns sticking out of their heads and often carry sacks of iron balls.\nA Sylvan's favourite passtime is playing tricks on people. These tricks can vaery from simply hiding farming tools to the more serious arsony. Sylvans can use their ability to mimick voices perfectly to devise elaborate ruses.\nSylvans are mostly harmless tricksters, their main form of defence being pelting people with iron balls. As sentient creatures, they are able to see reason. Several farmers have been able to convince the Sylvan to stop tricking people by offering food.\nIf it absolutely comes to it, a Sylvan is easily killed with a regular steel sword to any vital area including the heart, brain or spine.\nSection IV\n\n\n\n\n\n Sentient Supernatural\n-Specter/Spirit-\n\nSpirits without bodies, these creatures can be benevolent, neutral or malevolant just like in their previous lives. They can only be harmed by aurum, salt and clerical magic.\nThe easiest way to deal with a sentient spirit is to find the reason for its undeath and get rid of whatever is linking them to a place. Alternatively, clerical magic can be used or an aurum sword for temporary dispatchment.\n-Red Riders-\n\nInter-dimensional invaders. They scour the lands for the unsuspecting and abduct them to turn them into one of their own. They are omens of war and misfortune. They are extremely strong.\nTheir physical strength is matched by their magical ability, with the power to teleport both themselves and others as well as to summon strong winds that freeze all in its path. They are living beneath the armor and bleed- Hangman's oil may be effective.\nSection V\n\n\n\n\n\n       Monstrous\n     Supernatural\n-Necrophages-\n\nThe most common of beasts that a Marked Man will come across. These beings are re-animated dead, often due to necromancy or other darker magic. In the case of the Vodnik, it is due to a parasite in the water.\nAurum weaponry is recommended, though ferrum can also be used. Alone, they are easily dispatched but when amassed they can become the most dangerous of foes.\n-Zyme-\n\nHuge, featureless sacks of acid. They absorb parts of their environment, giving them different abilities. For example, a Zyme in a volcanic area may absorb sulphur and magma, becoming thrice as dangerous.\nTo destroy this beast, use an aurum sword and emphasise cutting over thrusting. This will allow the Marked Man to chop the Zyme down into pieces small enough for it to be rendered unable to clone itself. Burn the remains to ensure total death.\n-Kataphraktus-\n\nA creature of odd humanoid proportions, its hide ismade up of a black plate material. Its claws are large and it focuses on tearing its prey to pieces, which it then drags off to consume through unknown means.\nDue to the heavily armored nature of the Kataphrakt, the use of half-swording is an absolute must. Use aurum and aim for the areas beneath its arms or its joints, where the plating is weakest.\n-Wraith-\n\nWraiths are semi-spectral beings that are known for haunting areas where people have died. The wraiths are always connected to the sites of their demise, they may protect their homes, or seek vengeance.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Black Melody", "Wretched", "Where light casts;\na shadow trails in wake.\n\nWhere lives passed;\nborders there do break.\n\nWhere death lasts;\nthe fury of a drake.\n\nWhere souls fast;\nattone for our mistake.\nWhere dead sing;\nashen will be done.\n\nWhere birth brings;\nthe dark is to none.\n\nWhere spiders sting;\nwebs will be spun.\n\nWhere smog rings;\nradiant, the Black Sun.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Blah", "Heshakomeu", "THE BLAH\n\n\n\nTongue of the Orc\n\n\n\n\n\n~ Compiled by Heshakomeu de Campari Shidari, the Wandering Cleric ~\nFOREWORD\n\nThe Blah is arguably the most important language a traveler can have in their repertoire. In the event of an orc raid, understanding the bandits’ orders and demands can save your life. If you are in the presence of a shaman, or any other\nprominent member of orc society, comprehension of what is being said is crucial if one is to engage in dialogue and properly convey respect.\n\nThe current Blah (distinguishing it from Old Blah, wherein some of its roots lie) is a modified form of Common.\nGrammar is essentially identical, with some words replacing the need for multiple words (Blah ‘Mi’ replaces Common ‘I’ and ‘Me’). Most basic nouns are replaced entirely. The reason for these modifications is quite simple: the presence of tusks in orc\nmouths, which hinders the lip movement necessary to properly pronounce Common words.\n\nAlthough the speech may sound guttural and primitive, it is a poor indication of orc culture and wisdom, both of which are rich, admirable, and built on honor and glory.\nThose who meet and speak with orcs would do well to remember that.\n\nWithout further ado, a compilation of common phrases in the Blah, chosen to ensure the life and intactness of the limbs of the reader when in orcish company.\n\n~ H\nPHRASES\n\nAgh - And\nAlbai, Twiggie, Treeugger - Elf\nBlah - Talk, Speak, Orc language\nBlarg - Home\nBubhosh - Great, Big\nBuub - Pig\nBuurz - Dark\nDabu - Respectful yes (“Yes, my pleasure”)\nFlat - Dead\nGazat, Stowt - Dwarf\nGlob - Fool\nGobo - Goblin, a smaller and smarter breed of orc compared to the uruk and olog\nGoi - City\nGruk - Understand\nGug’ye - Goodbye\nHowlur - Wolf\nKlomp - Attack\nKrimp - Control somebody, Stun, Snare, Capture\nLat - You\nLigz - Arrow\nLusk - Axe\nMi - Me, I\nMojo - Magic\nNub - No\nNubded - Undead\nNubhosh- Bad, Small\nNuutshara - Ascended\nO’lig - Bow\nOlog - Largest and dumbest breed of orc, also known as ogres\nPushdug - Stinky\nRulg - Thanks\nShara, Quickspawn, Breeder - Human\nSkah, Saahkah - Orcish curse words\nSnaga - Slave\nSqueal - Halfling\nSteemiez - Redstone technology\nStik - Staff\nThrom’ka - Formal greeting\nUg - Hi, Hello, Hail\nUruk - Most common breed of orc\nUzg - World\nYub - Yes\nZult - Sword\nNUMERICAL SYSTEM\n\nThe majority of the races use a decimal system for counting (that is, counting with a base of ten). However, orcs use a quinary system (base five). The first five numbers have unique identifiers, and the numbers six through nine possess\nthe prefix “H’-”. Numbers greater than nine possess the suffix “-ty”, with the exception of ten, whose suffix is “-ety”.\n\nHere is a chart of orcish numbers:\nAsh - One\nDub - Two\nGakh - Three\nFuth - Four\nH’ - Five\nH’ash - Six\nH’dub - Seven\nH’gakh - Eight\nH’futh - Nine\nAshety - Ten\nDubty - Twenty\nMay your life be blessed and your travels safe.\n\nVan’ayla.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Brass Teapot", "Isengar Brockfall", "Our story begins with two very unwealthy people that were known as John and Alice.\n\n\"If I were rich honey, I would stay in bed with you all day\"\nhe smiled with a glistening look on his face.\n\"But! I have to get to work.\"\nHis smile faded into a depressed saddened expression.\n\nJohn got out of the bed that was originally made for one, it squeaked when they got up as one of the springs were broke.\nJohn tucked Alice in nice and warm and gave her a quick kiss before he got dressed into his coffee stained suit.\n\nJohn reached for the wooden handle and opened his wardrobe pulling out the grey suit.\nHe smelt it and made a *it's okay to wear again* look.\n\nJohn took his bucket of dirty water with flies floating around in it, and poured it over his head.\nIt drenched his suit but atleast he was clean! He thought.\nJohn got a small rag with yellow stains glued onto it and wiped himself down, although it didn't do much to get him dry.\n\"Hmph\" he grumbled, as he grasped for his silver inn key for work.\nAs he kicked open his stiff door it swung open and a heavy breeze hit johns face.\nHe slammed the door shut and headed to work.\n\n\"Good Morning Mr. Caulfield\" he waved as he left Petrus.\nJohn ran out onto the graveled path in a hurry to get to work.\n\nAs john arrived he was shouted at by his boss Vinnie! ((Read his lines in an Italian accent))\n\"Ey Johnny what do you think your doin' turnin' up this late?\"\nJohn put a fake smile and apologised, he started to mumble curse words about Vinnie as he hung his suit jacket up on the hook.\nAlice groaned as she got out of bed and reached for glass of water.\nShe chugged it down and stumbled out of her bed.\nShe grabbed her pink robe and put it on. She ran her fingers down the silk and smiled whilst doing so.\nA knock at the the hollow wooden door startled her.\nShe shuffled to the door and opened it wide, shivering at the coldness from outside.\n\"A'hm 'ere fer te'h rent!\" Their landlord (Albert) asked impaitently.\nAlice had a slight worried look on her face.\n\"I'm sorry Albert we can't afford this months rent!\"\nAlbert laughed with a sense of angryness in it.\n\"Wel' t'en what yer goin' ter do 'bout et?\" he snapped!\n\n\"I...\" before she could answer Albert pushed passed her knocking her into the door.\n\"What's te'h mos' Valuable t'ing yer go'?\" he examined the living room suspicously.\n\nAlice cried \"Pleas' Albert!\"\nHe looked at her with an imtimidating expression.\nShe pointed in the kitchen and told him.\n\"My mums Jewerly, but the gold is fake\" she cried.\n\nAlbert grabbed the jewerly and shoved it into his pocket a penny fell out and rolled under the cupboard.\nHe huffed in anger and stomped out.\nAlice slammed the door shut and screamed into a handmade cotton pillow that was rough when you touched it.\n\nShe glanced to the cupboard and dived onto the ground, she rummaged her hand into the narrow space\ntrying to find the 1 mina that rolled under.\nShe grabbed something circular and pulled it out.\nShe opened her palm and a nickel was covered in dust.\nHer eyes widened in amazement.\nShe put it in her and John's jar of savings.\nWhich contained\nA long piece of string, 4 minas including the one she found, and some screwed up denied job applications for the local barbers.\n\nJohn opened the door smiling.\n\"Why are YOU smiling\" she groaned.\n\nJohn reached into his pockets pulling out a free drink coupon at the deathbanes inn.\nAlice giggled and kissed him on the lips she whispered \"I love it when you spoil me!\"\nThe next day John woke up to his normal routine.\nHe used his quarter in his pocket to get a carriage to the inn.\n\n\"Ey Johnny you're late!\"\n\"Err sorry Vinnie I was...\"\nVinnie had interuppted him.\n\"You're fired!!!\"\n\"What?! are yer talking about Vinnie\" he smiled worrying.\n\"We have another Inn keeper who wants the job, and you always fuck up so...\" He snapped.\n\"You...You're firing me\" John felt a tear coming down his eye.\n\"But I have a wife!\"\n\"Find another job, and err oh I need the key back.\"\nJohn was full of rage, anger and despair.\nHe threw the key outside and stomped outside crying.\n\"WHY!!!, HAVEN'T YOU HAD ENOUGH FUN?\" he shouted to the sky.\nHe scraped a pebble up and thew it into the bushes.\nHe slowly strolled back to Petrus!\nAs he turned the key into his front door he saw that there was fresh blood on the floor and a bloody hammer.\n\"ALICE!\" he shouted in the living room.\nHe ran towards the bed, She was covered in thick red blood as if it were a murder.\nHe grasped his hands on her arms and shook her with a tear rolling down his cheek.\nShe slowly opened her eyes and blinked, \"Alice!\" he smiled.\n\"What the heck happened?\"\nShe laughed and told him the story!", ""),
        StaticBook("The Brotherhood", "Garman Bigge, the Traitor", "THE BROTHERHOOD OF\nDREAKVIR.\n\n\nWe do not sow.\n\nWe reap.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Caterpillar", "Annette", "The Hungry\n       Caterpillar\n          =-+-=\n\n            By\n    Annette Elendil\n\n\n \\_/-.--.--.--.--.--.   (๑′ᴗ‵๑)_)_)_)_)_)_)_)o\nIn the light of the moon, a little egg lay on a leaf...\n\nUntil one sunny morning, the leaf grew warm and.. \n\nPOP!\n\nOut of the egg came a tiny, and hungry, caterpillar..\nHe started to look for some food..\n\nOn the first day, he ate through one red apple...\n\nBut.. He was still hungry..\nOn the second day, the little caterpillar ate through two juicy green pears..\n\nBut..\n\nThe little Caterpillar was still hungry...\n\n\n...(,(,(, \")\nOn the third day..\n\nHe ate through three pretty purple plums.\n\nBut.. the little caterpillar was still so very hungry...\n\n\n...(,(,(,(, \")\nThen, on the fourth day.. The little caterpillar ate up four yummy red strawberries!\n\nBut.. he was still hungry...\n\n\n\n...(,(,(,(,(, \")\nOn the fifth day, he found a snack of five bright oranges.\n\nBut..\n\nThe poor little caterpillar was still hungry...\n\n...(,(,(,(,(,(, \")\nOn the sixth day.. the little caterpillar had a feast!\n\nHe at through one ice cream cone, one pickle, one slice of cheese, one slice of salami, one lolipop, one slice of pie, one cupcake, and one big slice of watermelon!\nThat night..\n\nThe little caterpillar had a terrible ache in his little buggy belly..\n\n\n\n\n...(,(,(,(,(,( ;~;)\nThen.. on the seventh day..\n\nThe caterpillar ate through one nice, green leaf.\n\n\n....(,(,(,(,(,(,(,(,( -u-)\n\nAfter that he felt much, much better!\nBut now, he wasnt hungry anymore..\n\nAnd he wasn't a LITTLE caterpillar anymore..\n\n\n\n    ......(,(,(,(,(,(,(,(,(,(,(,(\nHe was a big, fuzzy, FAT caterpillar!\n\n\n\n\n\n\n(,(,(,(,(,(, \")!\nHe build a special small house around himself, called a cocoon.\n\nHe stayed in his little house for more than two whole weeks!\n\nThen.. \n\nOne morning..\nHe nibbled a hole in his cocoon.\n\nAnd pushed, pushed, PUSHED his way out!\n\nAnd...\nHe had become a beautiful, colorful butterfly!\n\n\n       __ \\/ __\n      /o \\{}/ o\\\n      \\    ()    /\n       `>  / \\  <'\n       (o/\\/\\o)\n\n          The\n          End", ""),
        StaticBook("The Cave", "Lenniel Divhelia", "The last of my life has been spent here, in this aweful cave. In search of a treasure that has completely eluded me. The man who sent me here seemed quite mad but very sure that they were here. All I have found is a slight cold spot by the lava.\nIt beffudles me as the lave is very hot. I have burned away a pair of eyebrows trying to figure out this riddle. \n'Plunge quick but not too deep for the treasure that you seek. It's very hot but not in one spot, if the gloves are what you seek.'\n((Originally by: Irene42))", ""),
        StaticBook("The Challenge", "Leyun Kameki", "The Challenge\n\nScribed by Hierophant Callax, the Solstice Druid\nAn Archdruid cannot be removed from position by a vote or by force. Only if he retires or dies may his position be claimed as empty. However, when an Archdruid becomes exceedingly inactive or loses sight in what's right for the Orderand refuses to retire,\nhis position may be challenged. The Challenge is and only ever should be issued in the most extreme and rare of cases.\n\nWhen all hope is lost and the Order is suffering because of an Archdruid, the Challenge may be instituted and may\nonly be instituted by a Druid Hierophant. The Hierophant who issues the Challenge shall create a difficult, and unbiased, trial that requires the challengers and the challenged to put many skills to the test such as exploration, investigation, wisdom, and\npiety. Furthermore, the existing Archdruids must all agree to the terms of the Challenge. This event could take anywhere from a few Seeds to a Year, and whoever returns to the Hierophant, first, with the required information, items, or knowledge will be\ndeemed the victor and shall take the seat of the challenged Archdruid.\n\nIf anyone is realized to have cheated or wronged the Challenge in some way, they will be disqualified. In the case that only two individuals, a challenger and the\nchallenged, take part in this vigorous trial and one cheats or wrongs it in some way, the other will be granted the victor even if he is the individual being challenged.\n\nAs aforementioned, the Challenge shall only ever happen as a\nlast resort. The Inner Circle, all except for the Archdruid being challenged, must deem it necessary as must a Hierophant to organize and oversee it. This rite should never and cannot be abused.  Those who try to see to its usage in improper context shall\nfeel not only the wrath of the Aspects, but that of the Order as well. Blessed be he who takes any and all proper precautions with a troubled Archdruid before seeing the institution of a Challenge.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Change", "The Old Man", "I found myself sitting there, staring into the dark pit, my heart racing and my brow covered in sweat due to the extreme conditions within the nether. I was encased in some sort of atmospheric bubble which allowed me to maneuver through the nether,\nunharmed by its toxic effects. As I looked around, ichor and lava encompassed the surrounding region. It was one of the most beautiful and terrifying places I have ever laid my eyes upon.\nThe mere presence of the area itself was breathtaking, yet belittling due to the fact that the sheer power that Iblees’ realm possessed would make any mortal feel inferior. The fortress itself was incredible and the first time\nI walked through it with the Undead Overlord Sprat, he showed me around its various rooms and corridors but was obviously focused on the task at hand. He led me to the spot of the pit that would soon change my life forever.\nWhen looked into it, I could feel myself having a doubt here and there as to what I was about to give up, life. After conversing with Sprat, I finally made my decision to serve Iblees and become a conduit of which he would use to complete his mission.\nI looked into the pit one last time then back to Sprat who had a stern look on his visage before nodding once, so I took a deep breath, and began my first steps forward into a new life. I took upon the name Seraphim the Damned\nwhich I would become known as among my fellow ‘brothers’ and mortals of the realm. This domain of Iblees was to be my new home, a safe haven for those who were beyond death… Then my chance to unleash terror on the realm of Athera began… As I look back\nupon that experience that occurred so long ago, I can’t help but think that if I could do it all over again, I wouldn’t change a thing.\n\n~Signed \nSeraphim the Damned, Undead of the Chaos Sect.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Clerics", "Karyssmov Faroe", "The concept of holiness. The grasp of Purity.\nThe Light.\nThe Flame.\nThe Fire.\nThe Stag.\nThe Vehement Lord.\n\nWhat does it mean?\nWhat are these things? How does one better themselves via these?\nThere are many paths of purity, seeker.\nThere are methods and concepts beyond our own grasp, set in forth by the Aengul, Tahariae.\n\nBut who is Tahariae?\nTahariae is the Aengul of Purity. He represents the Light that is both a concept, and a literal thing. Perhaps you have been healed by a Cleric before. Have you felt the warmth and calmness flow through you? That is the Light, made manifest.\nThe Light has many properties to it, but it always comes from the Lord of Light. The Light can heal, purge taint, remove poisons, even remove curses...\n\nBut at the same time, that is not always enough.\nThe comes the Clerics of War, myself being one. War Light is slightly different from the Light used to heal. It is manifested from emotion, thus the more passionate a Cleric becomes, the stronger their spells are as well.\nHatred. Zeal. Vengeance. This can fuel the Light of a War Cleric. But at the same time, some choose not to call upon the more primal of emotions. Instead, they focus upon anger. Sorrow. The thoughts of what would happen, should they fail.\nRegardless of it all, the War Light is still Light in its stature. One may notice it is 'hard' compared to the 'liquid' state of regular Light. This is due to the Cleric, who wills it into this shape to better combat the forces of darkness.\nAll Clerics may be both a 'Priest' Cleric and a 'War' Cleric. There is no need to choose merely one. I am trained in both, using them to their extent to render the Lord's will upon this plane.\n\"But,\" I hear you say.\n\"What is the Lord's will?\"\nWell, my friend, it is simple. It is to eradicate 'impurity'. What is impurity? It is taint. Look towards a ghoul or lich. They are different from you and I. They are not \"Descendants' anymore.\nThey have given their soul for the ruinous powers. How unjust, how folly their decision. They are wrong, and as such, the Lord of Light sends us to right these wrongs. We are the instruments of the Lord's will. And by His will, you are protected.\nClerics have a duty to purge undead and impurity, wherever they should find it. They do it to keep you safe. Not out of desire for violence, not out of desire to subjugate, but simply to keep us safe, and because the Lord demands.\nIt is why Clerics will always heal you. They will preserve you, return you to your normal form. For injury is Impurity, for is it not who you were. It is wrong, and thus the Light grants us the strength necessary to save both your life...and soul.\nWe are bound by what are known as 'Tenants'. These five rules dictate the lives of a Cleric, and they must follow them closely, lest their soul be torn apart and expelled. Yes, big stakes.\n\nWhat are the Tenants?\nLet's find out.\nThe First Tenant\n\n'Shelter and Protect thy Brethren'\n\nTranslated, meaning...\nTo protect fellow Clerics in their time of need.\nThe Second Tenant\n\n'Cannot Stray from thy Faith'\n\nTranslated, meaning...\nDo not strayin dedication to the Lord. Be diligent in prayers and thanks to Him for His Gift to us.\nThe Third Tenant\n\n'Shall Guide the Lost'\n\nTranslated, meaning...\nTo guide the Descendants of the Four, and protect them from the forces of Impurity. (IE: Undeath)\nThe Fourth Tenant\n\n'Shall not Kill, Harm, Nor Spill the Blood of an Innocent'\n\nTranslated, meaning...\nClerics cannot harm a Descendant for no reason.\nThe Fifth and Final Tenant\n\n'Abuse of Thine Gift and Punishment Shall Fall to You'\n\nTranslated, meaning...\nWe cannot avoid healing a Descendant. We must, for the Lord commands.\nThat's a lot of rules!\nIt's true, but they guide the path of the Clerics as they go forth fo fulfill His Holy Mission.\n\n'But, what is that?!'\nWell...let me tell you.\nTahariae's mission upon these realms is to preserve Purity, and the Descendants of the Four. The thing standing in his way of that, is Impurity. The Undead, for instance, are one such Impurity. They are to be expunged, unless they serve the Light.\nAn interesting path of being a Cleric is their Gift. Now, you may not know much about followers of Aenguls, but oftentimes those who follow one do not experience voidal poisoning, therefore we keep our muscle mass. This is because our aengul blesses us.\nI thank you for spending some time reading through this instructional book. Should you have any questions, feel free to ask any nearby Cleric. They'd appreciate any thanks you could give, for our job is  oftentimes a thankless one.\n-Karyssmov Faroe\n8th of Snow's Maiden\n1637", ""),
        StaticBook("The Commandments", "Schreck'Lak", "The\nCommandments ᛋᛋ\n\n\nA comprehensive list of how to avoid degeneracy and please the spirits\n\n\nWritten by Schreck'Lak\n*Written in Blah*\n1. It is the avowed duty and responsibility of all orks to secure and assure the existence of the orkish race upon the mortal plane. To do elsewise is a direct insult to Krug and his blood which you bear.\n2. Be fruitful and multiply. Do your part in increasing the proportion of Krug's sons among the mortal plane.\n3. The guiding principle of all your actions shall be: \"What is best for the orkish race? What is best for Laklul? For Krug?\"\n4. Remember that the inferior inferior races are our enemies, and that the most dangerous of all is the human race. It is our immediate objective to relentlessly expand the orkish race, and keep shrinking our enemies.\n5. Show preferential treatment in business dealings with members of our race, the orkish race. Phase out all dealings with the kin of Malin, Horen, Urguan and those cat things.\n6. The offspring of interracial mates are infertile, pathetic creatures. While recieving all the curses of their lineage they recieve nothing. Do not mix your blood.\n7. Might makes right. Orks are to strive consistently towards physical, mental and martial excellence. Weakness is a disgrace to your racial comrades and ancestors: avoid it.\n8. Remain loyal to the spirits, and the spirits shall remain loyal to you.\n\n\n\nPraise Krug", ""),
        StaticBook("The Creed", "The Hochmeister", "“You are the future of the Order...\n\nYou, and those like you, hold the Orders soul in your hands. We wear the black mark, and we are the beating heart of a reborn brotherhood. It is our duty to remember. We are charged to recall the traditions that came\nbefore the moment when our Order stood on the edge of extinction. Remember those who stood against the enemies of the past, those who carried the old Order on their backs and bled for its success. Give penance for the fallen brothers of a defeated age and\nlearn from what came before.\n\nYou, and those like you, are the Order. We serve those who call upon us to do so, a Nation of our own people, a land that is our home. The traditions and codes of the old Order guide us but this new age leads us into the\nunknown. Be loyal to your comrades and the Order for they are the same and we are your salvation in an existence brimming with darkness. Give yourself to the Order and the Order will give itself for you. Fight for the Order and the Order will fight for\nyou. Die for the Order and the Order will die for you. You, and those like you, carry the Order. We wear the armor forged in a time when the first Imperium was born- repaired, amended and maintained in the decades since by generations of warriors,\nsoldiers and loyal men. Your blades have tasted the blood of every foe the old Order has ever fought slain beast and man alike in the most righteous fervor and service. The names of each man before you etched onto its hilt and the battle that claimed them\ndating to its very forging on the first motherland.\n\nYou, and those like you are the victorious leer of the legends who founded us. But why are you charged with these responsibilities? Why do you wear the black mark?...\nBecause you hate. You hate more than any other man, and your hatred runs blacker, deeper, purer than theirs. A hate that stands above all otehrs. One hate that burns in our blood annd roars from the mouths of each Sariant when we stand togther in war.\nIt is a hatred with many names, those who sought to exterminate us, those who seek to destroy us, those who offer only darkness and suffering.\n\n\n\n\nBut to us, they are simply the Enemy...\"\nThe Sariant\n           Creed", ""),
        StaticBook("The Crown-Prince", "Jacob Chapel", "\"The Basis of the Perfect State\" was written by Edward Winter II as gift to Ostromir Sarkozic Carrion upon the conquest of Renatus.\n\nThis book has been transcribed and copied by and under guidance of Jacob Chapel.\n\n((Original by AiiM))\nThe Basis of the Perfect State\nTo the Crown-Prince,\n\nThe governance of a state must be just. To be a just state, the governing body must execute their duties and powers efficiently with the will of the people and the good of the state held\nas supreme.\n\nThe judicious and firm-handed monarch can in his own right control the state. A monarchy is far more efficient, effective, and has a lesser potential for corruption than the republican system of councils, voting, and election. The downfall\nof the just monarch is his heir. The spoiled child corrupts the state, the weak-willed monarch relinquishes the power of the royal family. The royal heir must be established as the supremely noble and knowledgeable steward of the state, whose governance\nis just and his decisions well-made.\n\nThe ill-fit heir has, in the past, been rectified by extensive counsel, where the royal extends to his advisors the powers of the state. The function of the government in this state does deteriorate, as the\nabsolutism of the monarch is sullied by the extended powers and corruptions of the monarch's counselors, whose motives and intellects are unknown and unverified.\n\nSo one must establish the basis by which a just monarch can be ensured by the generations.\nElection of the most just by the common people is a flawed system, as the uneducated and ignoble masses know not of justice nor righteousness. The thieves and beggars in the charity of the state should not be tasked with the selection of a\nrepublican heir. The whims of the people to favour a man do not establish him as the most effective steward and leader to his people.\n\nElection by the masses of nobility is too a flawed system, as the nobles delight in their pleasures without properly\nknowing of management or governance. Their corruptions of sin diminish their efficacy as a just constituency.\n\nThe solution then, is to look for the most just of a collective of just monarchs in a collective of states, and to choose from them a supreme\nmonarch, who should steward the constituent monarchs in his wisdom and with a firm-hand.\n\nWere the Kingdoms of humanity to with each other combine, and the monarchs together of varying levels of aptitude to their position were to choose from amongst\nthemselves the most well fit to the supreme crown over the constituent monarchs, then a just monarch could be established. The unity of the Kingdoms should  strengthen the military and economic state of function, and further serve to demilitarize and\nfocus supplies on economic pursuits, by allowing for the each of the states to contribute to a military to a lesser degree, which shall together equal a force unrivaled by any modern monarch.\n\nThe human Kingdoms of Salvus, Ruska, Herendul, and Oren,\nwere they to unite, could each contribute but 25,000 men to a combined force, and still manage to afford their borders greater protection than if they alone attempted to muster 90,000 each for their own interests, an impossible feat regardless.\nThe unified states would be able to pass and enforce legislation and regulation, and efficiently and effectively steward their states with the guidance of an emperor-steward and his leadership in their governance.\n\nFurthermore, the borders and futures\nof the human states would be secured by the stabilizing force of the constitutional empire and her emperor-steward, who would be elected by the constituent Kings to be the most just of all men to govern humanity. The states would together validate their\nclaims and legislature, and their combined military force would both strengthen the defense of their borders and allow for each of the constituent Kingdoms to turn focus upon their domestic affairs.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Deep Below", "Wretched", "The beating, the great fading pulses of a heart most dark. I hear it, and it is stronger than my will. It churns deep below. Deep below? There is something deeper than the great deep of the Abyss?\n\nThere are few that hear it, but I am not the only\nwanderer of the loving desolate Abyss to catch the quiet ringing of something so unable to die, as if pained.\n\nThere is an ungodly warmth to this sensation, the thing in The Deep Below is not of dark, but of accursed light and burning.\nThere is little sense in these ravings of a traveler most weary, but these deep power brings worry to the crooked soul. In this place of such natural fear, still I find new things of which to be afraid. I pray that this remain a mystery I never solve.\nThere is something alive in The Deep Below. And the more I notice it, the more I feel it notices me.\n\nRadiant is the Black Sun.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Digester", "Vicelin", "-Corrupted Digester in northern mountains.-\n\nDuring a scouting mission to seek out and destroy monsters nest we picked up a terrible smell in the high mountains, carried by the wind right to us. After a brief search we found the enrance to a decrepit\ncatacomb from which the rancid stench emanated.\n\nWe took our time in case of traps, both magical and mundane. It is not uncommon for these remote places to be housing cultists and other weirdos. Thus, we were cautious from the get go.\nUpon making our way down its crumbling stone spiral staircase, we heard noises one would associate with a digester. Alfred first spotted it and noted that it was red in colour and giving off heat.\n\nThe blob was able to change shapes and it transforme\nitself into a humanoid to seek us out.\n\nWe receded up the staircase where I then consumed a Thunderbolt. Alfred and Tugev stood their ground as I dropped through a hole in the wall to flank the creature.\nAlfred used his gauntlets to cause a kinetic blast which disturbed the creature's form and caused it to halt its advance. I was able to chase it from the rear, but it had already surged past both men and receded back into its cavern, which appeared to be\na summoning chamber. Once inside it began to expand and change its form, gaining energy from the nodes within. Alfred struck the bricks with his kinetic blast and caused the room to collapse in, crushing the monster.\nA sample was gathered. The beast is likely dead or at least immobilised.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Dream", "parion_", "I, Parion Than’thill, have undertaken the duty of recording the experiences of an informed llir and Mali’aheral who has recently been stirred from a persistent rest; and might I state this has not been a rest of weariness or idle mind, yet that of\ninnovation and pensive intellect.\n\nI assure all, who might take a moment of perusal over this text, that not a mere single element of detail has been altered or contradicts the foundation of the original account.\n===================Some will say that it was nothing; that it was only a dream and nothing more.  Some will likely call me a liar outright, claiming I write this for my own greedy and selfish machinations.\n\nBut then there will be those who know that\nthe story I tell is so much more than a simple dream.  There are those who know that I speak the truth.  I write this account to all denizens of this fair land, but to those of you who know the truth I ask this: Stand with us.  Stand up to the oppression\nand the darkness of this world.  Change this world for the better!  I beg you!  Do not allow this dark vision to come to fruition.  \n\nThis tale that I tell does not begin in Lin’sulan.  It does not begin in any land or city of Haelun’or, nor does it begin\nin the vast lands of Oren or the mines of Urguan.  It does not begin in the deserts of The War Uzg or the mountains of Vandoria.  This tale begins not in the land of Vailor.  This tale begins in the lands of Anthos at the deathbed of my friend and mentor,\nGoliath.\n\nThe events leading up to this moment are irrelevant.  All that you must know is that Goliath wished to give me some departing gift; a gift that came in the form of a ritual, with me as the focus.  I have no doubt that Goliath could have\nperformed this spell, whatever it was, without the use of such a ritualistic method in his prime, but he was old now and burdened with the coming of mortality.  \nI sat in the middle of a large stone chamber, containing naught but Goliath’s large bed. He\nresided in the ornate support of draped sheets, sitting up painfully, directing all his efforts to the task at hand.  His son stood on the opposite end of the room, his face graven yet focused.  All around the floor there were strange runic carvings, that\nI was not familiar with.  However I could tell - no, tell is not the right word, I could feel that the etchings were guiding the magiks of Goliath and his son towards the centre of the room, towards the axis of this strange spell, towards me.  I could\nsense it; the touch of this spell inside of my head.  It was as if it was unlocking doors contained by my memory; yet, they were not doors that I wished released. I did not know what was behind them, whether they were there to keep something secured\nwithin the dark corners of my mind, or to keep me out.  All I knew was that whatever was behind them frightened me immensely.  Suddenly there was a great snap and a tremendous strain upon my being.  With that I found the stone chamber to no longer be\nempty and cold, in fact I do believe I was no longer within the chamber at all.  There was nothing around me but darkness, only the void existed in this place.  It was then that I knew where I was.  I can’t explain how I knew really, only that some part\nof my being just knew.  I was at the beginning.  At the beginning of Aegis, of existence, of time itself.  I saw the Creator, I saw it all come into existence!  I have been told the story of the creation of Aegis and the four races time and time again...\nBut to actually experience it... To actually see it with my own eyes; it was the most beautiful thing I have seen or shall ever hope to see again...\n\nJust as suddenly as it had appeared, it was gone again.  In a flash I was no longer\nwatching the beginning of time unfold, instead I saw... everything; I was witness to existence itself.  Before mine eyes flashed the rise of kingdoms and the fall of nations, the sowing of great forests and the burning of even greater ones, the terrors\nthat hide in the darkness, the divinities that reside in the light.  I bore witness to the birth and the death of kings, peasants, soldiers, merchants, and wizards alike.  And suddenly it was all gone; awash in darkness. It wasn’t simply that there was no\nlight; it was that there was only darkness.  Suddenly I knew what this was.  This aphotic place was the end.  It was the end of everything.  Just as I knew this, I also knew there was something else within the darkness.  It was He, The Fallen One, Iblees.\nI know not how it was that he was there, at the end, for He has been defeated; however, He was there.  He was the end.  \n\nIt was then that He looked upon me.  I do not know if this was simply a vision or if I had truly seen Him at the end of time,\nbut as he looked upon me I suddenly awoke in a strange new place.  I soon learned that this new land was called Vailor.  How I came to awaken here and now is still a mystery, for if I slept I do not know who must have cared for my body all this time.\nEven as I write this the memory of what occurred in that strange dream-state is quickly fading, while trying to remember specific details brings nothing but an agonizing headache.  \n\nNothing do I fear more than the end of this strange dream-state\ncoming into reality.  But just what is it that may become reality?  I know Iblees to have been defeated long ago, never to return.  But if this is the case, just what did I witness at the end of time?  \n\nAfter much thought and discussion about this with\ndear friend Parion, I have come to believe that this end result is not literal, but metaphorical.  I believe it to be that this ending darkness which I was witness to was a darkness that we ourselves have created.  A darkness that we ourselves have\nbrought into this world; by the means of imposed suffering and cultural recession.  And so it is that I once again ask, no, I implore that you stand with us against this condition of our state.  \n\n===================\nIf you have read this far I do so applaud you, for you are the founding minority; with dynamic minds that pursue contemporary idea and experience. Reflect upon this content with your own interpretations – whether that be the literal impression that I have\nattained or that of a more metaphorical nature (as acquired by the pivotal figure of this experience). Just allow yourselves to apply your own efforts to shift the stagnation of our progress and dedicate your capacities to enlightenment once more.\nI will conclude these writings with my own words:\n\nDo not neglect Maehr'sae Hiylun'ehya for it is to surely escort us from this period of darkness.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Dreamer", "Sofetios", "The Dreamer\nBy Sofetios\n\nThe Dreamer,\nThe one who dares not to be the same,\nFor in dreams mysteries unravel,\nAnd endless space you do travel,\nAs you r dreams you try to tame.\nAs the Dreamer,\nDreams above the sky,\nAnd looks down below,\nTo the people that show,\nWho know not what lies that high.\nUnwakened,\nThe Dreamer,\nIn a maze of thoughts,\nWandering the mists,\nWith endless twists,\nAs the path on minds papers he jots.\nThough be wary dreamer,\nAs thoughts tend to run away,\nOnly the ones you really need,\nAnd the ones you often feed,\nAre the ones that often stay.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Druids Grove", "Leyun Kameki", "The Druid's Grove\n\nScribed by Hierophant Callax, The Solstice Druid\nThe Druids’ Grove is a place of Aspectial worship and peaceful congregation. It is a place where natural Druidic energies run deep and life flourishes in the glory and light of Cerridwen and Cernunnos. The Mother Grove, usually the most grand of all\ngroves on a given land mass, houses the Druidic Order and serves as their place of spreading the Druidic way through ancient teachings.\n\nNever should violence or anti-natural forces be issued within the grove; when these things are wrought on\nsuch sacred grounds, a Druid may do what he must to see the sanctity and peaceful aura restored. Furthermore, never should armor or weapon be donned in a grove for it is an area of peace and harmony with nature. When an individual holds armor and/or\nweapon, he anticipates violence and the need for said materials which only brings violent thought and meaning to the grove, thus disrupting the peaceful and harmonic aura.\n\nDruids’ groves have served throughout history as an\nimportant aspect of Druidic culture and Druid congregation. They’ve also served as elegant gardens, floral and faunal reserves, and places of knowledge. Drui’inder, take into account the purpose and sanctity of the Druids’ grove to better your\nunderstanding of Druidic culture and spread your wisdom to the generations to come so that they, too, may be enlightened by this cultural tradition. Blessed be.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Elven Curse", "Asul'athri Parir'taliyu", "Conjectures On the Subject of the Aged Elven Mind\n-----------------\nI write this now to you, dear elven reader, to forewarn you of the curses bestowed upon our elven race.\n\nFor it is as the Bronze say, that the elves were not cursed once,\nbut by twice. The second elven curse is that of inevitable insanity, stemming from our long lives.\n\nThis insanity is common to all elves and every elf whom lives with pure blood - I say not in the fashion that we high elves have made it, but I say it in\nthe looser terms of the wood and dark elves below us, whom distinguish not between silver, bronze, and onyx - only between the children of Malin and those whom are not.\n\nAll whom live too long ages and bearing pure elven blood shall be\nsubject to the weight of thought and experience, and their minds shall fold like a piece of parchment in the water.\n\nNow, if a life is lived twice as fast, twice as strong, it shall be lived like a flame, which burns twice as bright but dies twice as\nquick. And so the mind folds.\n\nMany of us display this insanity even now, in violence, irrationality, psychopathy, and all sorts.\n\nIn most elves, the signs begin to display themselves in the ages of 500 to the thousandth year,\nwherein it should first manifest as incredible stubbornness, rigidity, and volatility and/or depression, or other neuroses.\n\nIn time, these symptoms shall continue to the point that the individual can no longer take active part in society, either due to\nbeing highly dangerous or just incapable of actively providing to the community. \n\nRegardless, the insanity besets itself on any elf, and can beset itself at the age of 100 and all the way until the thousandth year, depending on the given elf's lifestyle\nand personal experiences. The elf should thus take great care to live life slowly, rationally, and emotionally full, without neglecting either mind or emotional response. When life is lived in balance, then balance shall be in the elf, and this is what\nall elves should strive for and is encompassed in every philosophy - in the Bronze Codes of the Wood Elves, the Druidic Laws of the Druian, the ancestral ways of elmali'ker, and elmaehr'sae hiylun'ehya of my own people.\nBy Asul'athri Parir'taliyu\n\nWritten on the 12th of Malin's Welcome, 1506", ""),
        StaticBook("The Enchantry", "First Enchanter, Sarrion Zytiaear", "The Enchantry\n    --------------\n   \"Seek, Understand,\n           Adapt.\"\n\n///////////////////\n             [!]\nThe Sigel of the Enchantry sits in the middle of the page.\n\n(https://goo.gl/v6uatL))\nThe Enchantry is a circle of mages who work together and unite in their studies to further themselves and magical development privately. They follow a simple code with a straight set of ambitions, to further their own knowledge of the arcane whilst\nproviding a positive outlook on magic to the world, allowing themselves to assist nations that call for help from those attuned to arcane, and extremely knowledgeable in the art.\nSuch calls may be from a simple enchanted blade one had wished to make, to helping solve a long line of voidal phenomenons and help keep the decedent's safe from such odd threats.\nThe Enchantry also finds themselves seeking powerful artifacts of the arcane, taking interest to not only keep them out of the wrong hands but study them internally themselves.\nLastly, in a great time of need in which the fate of the realm may be at stake, the Enchantry will rise up and assist all against this united threat.\n===================\nThe Enchanters Code\n<-------<>------->\n“Let there be no monarch of the void, for it is a source of power for those with the willpower to seek, and understand, not to control and dictate power away from those with the arcane gift.”\n-1st Code\nOpen a hand to the lost, and provide guidance to those who need to see the ways of the arcane. This does not mean to spoon feed others, as potential is built, and the arcane gift of the decedent will be lost to the sins of slothfulness,\nexpecting magic to be handed to them, not sought.” \n-2nd Code\n“Provide insight to the proper ways of the arcane, do not let those blind to greed or foolery mock our ways as they throw away their arcane gift, using it for incoherent murder and torture\nor misguiding others, blinding them as well, let these fools be dubbed ‘Rogue Magi’. The Rogue Magi brings not but shame to our kin, and are to be re-educated,\nlest they wish to ignore the open hand of a fellow mage. If they so wish to continue to be blinded, then it is our duty to amend such.”\n-3rd Code\n“Respect your arcane gift, and show your true understandment to the art you spend years perfecting, use it to it’s fullest potential and allow it to embrace your ways. Being one of the arcane gift is not a hobby, but a lifestyle.”\n-4th Code\n“Along with respecting your art, comes with the duty to not spread this art thin. Allow yourself to embrace this art fully, and respect those who have interest in learning, but make sure those who are truly interested are also going to\nembrace this art as full and true as yourself.”\n-5th Code\n“Guide one's self to your journey to master your arcane gift, allowing yourself to be spoon fed will falter your growth, and blind your ways with slothfulness. Alas, pathe one’s own road, and take responsibility for your actions on the way.”\n-6th Code\n“In the act of building your road to success in the way of the arcane, one may come across the realm of dark and light, these two forces interlocked in an endless struggle. As a mage, stand between dark and light as a symbol of neutrality,\nand embrace your teaching.”\n-7th Code\n“In times of great need in which the sanctuary of our realm is threatened, stand up and fight united against this inevitable foe, this is our duty to the realm and to those who reside in it, no matter the ground they stand.”\n-8th, and Final Code.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Eye", "[Ghost] The Eternal Librarian", "The Eye:\n  Observations\n   and Biology\n \n   by Lucion Sullas\nWhen I first began to delve into dissection, my interest seemed to mostly revolve around the eyeball-- those marvelous fleshy orbs that allow us to observe the world. Their fascinating nature, coupled with their mysterious biological uniqueness, made\nthem a tempting target for my studies. Over several months, one performed numerous dissections upon eyeballs of varying species, and observed many curious things within them. My observations are recorded here, as well as my process.\nUsing a set of specially designed knives (My thanks to master blacksmith Octavius for their creation) I performed a primary incision upon the eye's pupil; cutting down vertically from the iris. Here is where I made my first discovery.\nI had always presumed the pupil (the black spot in the centre of one's eye) was a solid section of the eye's outer layer. The pupil itself is, in fact, hollow with a thin watery layer covering its outer. After making note of this, I enlarged the\ninitial incision and peeled back the outer white layer carefully, using a small pair of tweezers. It was then I noticed a translucid circular \"lens\" slightly beneath where the pupil was. Carefully removing this watery tumor, I noticed its naturally\nmalleable state. When held between my thumb and index finger, I could easily squash it, and have it return to its original shape without any sign of damage. Furthermore, when peering through it, I noticed it was almost possible to see through it. Where I\nremoved the \"lens\" there were the remnants of what looked like very small muscles. Much like those I had seen in other animals I had explored.\nOne can make rational conclusions with this information. Keep in mind, though, that I have no conceivable way of proving this as of yet. These are merely theories that I hope to test in later experiments.\nFirstly, I find it suspiciously coincidental that the \"lens\" is situated in the center of the eye, just behind the pupil. It reminds me of a \"spectacle\" that a Mr Jon Evalgno told me about; that at certain thicknesses, glass can be used to focus on\nobjects at distance or close proximity. I believe, therefore, that the muscles I found that surround the lens manipulate it in the manner that I did with my index finger and thumb; focusing and defocusing one's vision to match the depth required.\nProcedures to fix poor eyesight could become possible with only a few preliminary tests. I salivate at the future opportunities.\n\nMaehr'sae hiylun'ehya.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Farmer", "Wilhelm von Bran", "The Farmer\n            &\n              The Witch\n            OR\nThe Defeat of\n            The \n         Conjurer\n\nBy, \n   \n   Wilhem von Bran\nIndeed at once, a long time ago, there stood a village. Indeed, this village would be ordinary had it not been for the events that took place there, and for the people that witnessed.\nThis village was a small hamlet located deep and surrounded by the Waldenian forest in northern Athera.\nIn the bitter cold, the people survived on the food that they harvested, occasionally sending out parties to fish and trade, but in all, this hamlet was sleepy and still.\nUnaffected by the corrupting notions of dwarven industry, or manly battles. Truly, this town only had a handful of peasantry, a few houses a church, and it’s square.\nThough this tale concerns itself with none of that. For this tale is one of the forests, and the corrupting force that it brings.\nIn the village – named Ansbluch – lived a family named Vurteger. Though, this family was broken. The mother having died years prior from pneumonia, and the father set to rise their only daughter alone.\nThe father was a good friend of the Churchman; Father Alphonse was a finely educated man who was ordained in the short reign of Pius II and spent a number of months at the Monastery of Saint Tobias during the plague.\nReverend Alphonse and Herr Vurteger were good friends, and were crutches for each other at many times.\nAfter the death of Frau Vurteger, Erika Vurteger, the young daughter became slothful to her chores, spending her time in the forests. Rumored to be cursed, she reveled in the adventure.\nHer father tended the chickens and the potatoes of his farm, while carrying the burden of not knowing where his daughter had been.\nOne day, Erika did not return for supper, indeed this was most peculiar as Erika had just turned sixteen the day before. Her father had made a potato stew: her favorite.\nHerr Vurteger was worried, but as he prepared to go out and search, a terrible storm released itself upon the forest, and the hamlet. Unable to make his bearings, the farmer trudged to the church rectory and called upon Father Alphonse.\nSurprised to see his friend in such distress, the priest welcomed him in and sat him by the fire. In a short while, Herr Vurteger awoke, the sun was in the sky, and the storm subsided.\nHe had awoken by several knocks on the rectory door, and opened it to Frau Heiden; Frau Heiden had become worried when Father was absent from mass and had not seen him all morning.\nSeeing that his cloak and staff were absent from the vestibule, Herr Vurteger had come to the horrific conclusion that Father Alphonse had gone out to search for Erika.\nAlarmed by this, Frau Heiden rang the bells and the men of the town prepared a party to search the forest.\n\nFor the whole day and the whole night they searched, but alas, found neither priest nor girl.\nBut the morning after, a sick scene was found. Father Alphonse; slumped against the trunk of an elder spruce tree, dead. He was found nearly a whole nights travel from the village and at the foot of a hill.\nAs the posse prayed over the corpse, they heard the sound of foreign music and vain cheering. Herr Vurteger ran to the top of the hill at once and saw a small caravan of gypsy. The small wagon chain was camping by the river, it seemed.\nFilled with rage, Herr Vurteger ordered the men to abandon the body of his friend and to investigate the gypsy.\nAs the armed band of town folk approached the camp, a jolly brown skinned man emerged from a wagon.\n“A hello there my friends!” bellowed the man, a long pipe in his hand, smoke billowing from its stem and bowl. The man stood quite tall with a black goatee. A domineering figure to the farmers of Ansbluch.\n“Guten tag, herr gypsy! Ve come to qvestion you on your vhereabouts zese passed few days und your actions. Vhat is your name so zat I may know who I interrogate?” responded Herr Vurteger\n“Well I am-a Faiz Kharadeen-a! And who-a might you-a be? Why must I-a be interrogated?” retorted the gypsy, as his fellows began to gather at his side.\n“Herr Kharadeen, we found our priest, Fazher Alphonse, a gut und holy man, dead und murdered in ze vood over yonder hill. Vhile ve vould not vish to be so bold, ve feel ve must!”\nUpon hearing of death, the gypsy band gasped and dropped to their knees, facing east, and began speaking a foreign tongue. Alarmed by this, the farmers braced their pitchforks and farm weapons. The gypsy continued,\n“We certainly-a never killed any-a man! We are a peaceful people, you see? We are the gypsy’s who dance under the-a crescent moon! The ones who travel-a to bring cheer-a not death!”\nConvinced, Herr Vertuger turned “But did you see a girl, herr Kharadeen? Around 16? Blue eyed und blonde?”\nThe gypsy shook his head and returned to his camp as the farmers returned, to bring their priest home.\nUpon closer inspection, the priest’s body was branded with a fresh crescent, and died from what seemed to be pneumonia. The branded crescent was most odd, and led the townfolk to suspect foul play.\nA few days after, the funeral was held. Erika had yet to be found, and Herr Vurteger was feared to have gotten the same fate as Father Alphonse.\nDepressed and overcome with grief, Herr Vurteger made the night’s journey back to the gypsy camp to question them again. Fearing they might have gone, he was relieved to hear the same songs and joyful dancing he had heard prior.\nUpon seeing the approaching farmer, the same gypsy went out again to greet him \n“Welcome-a back my friend! I hope we-a meet under better-a cir-“\nThe gypsy was swiftly interrupted as Herr Vurteger grabbed the collar of his tunic and backed him up against the outside of a wagon, dropping his pipe in the process.\n“Vhere ist mein daughter und vhat did you do to mein freund, Fazher Alphonse!” He cried out, pressing the dark man roughly against the wagon.\n“My friend! Aha. I assure you, We did not know anything, it was not us!” The gypsy felt pained, and was shocked when he felt a sharp jab against his stomach.\nThe farmer had procured a butchers knife and pressed it against his torso before raising it to the man’s chin. “Speak! Or I vill cut off your precious beard vith zis dagger und open your skin so ze air can taste your blood!”\n“It…It was the queen! The Lady of the forest! She came to us months ago beckoning us to be her subjects! She branded us with her banner-a symbol! The crescent! Alas, that horrid figure!”\nThe gypsy lifted his tunic to reveal the same marking as was found on the priest, only older. At this confession, the farmer released the gypsy and sheathed his knife.\n\n“Explain zis qveen or lady.”\n“In truth my friend, she is no lady she is a phantom. Perhaps a queen from some by gone age, but now just a terror. She comes to us with tasks, like delivering dirt and rock, and water. We were too scared to refuse!\"\nThe gypsy wagon tread slowly, though it was morning, it might as well have been night, and the horses were easily spooked.\nHerr Vertuger and several armed gypsies sat in the back and continued to plan.\n“So she resides in a tower, ja? Und it is never her zat comes down but vone of us goes up? Vell zis is easy! I vill go in to carry ze bundles, surprise her und you come in vhile I keep her busy und support me!”\nThe gypsy nodded “This-a sounds like it may work. We can only-a pray.” When the time came, the wagon grinded to a halt and the farmer adorned a thick hooded cloak and descended from the wagon with a few bundles.\nUnbeknownst to the Lady, the farmer had two scimitars belonging to the gypsy in his bundles. As he peered out from under his hood, he saw a crumbling tower, darkened and aged with time.\nNo one greeting him, the gypsy beckoned him forward and the farmer went up the ancient stairs and into the tower.\nHaving seen cracks of light at the top of the tower, the farmer trudged up the spiral staircase until he finally arrived at the door of the hall.\nAfter he had stood there for a short while, the thick oaken door swung open to reveal a brightly lit chamber, and an avanite throne on the far side.\n“Ah, so you have arrived, set se bun-“ the phantom voice spoke from the throne, but was interrupted by the farmer removing his cloak and brandishing his swords.\nHowever, when he looked up, he was shocked to see his daughter standing with not a phantom, but her mother, and his wife, Frau Vertuger.\nThe lady, dressed all in white, and looking much younger than she ought to stood from the throne and watched as the small band of gypsies scrambled through the doorway with arms of their own. Herr Vertuger, however, was too shocked for words.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Fear", "The Inquisitor", "The September Prince was a druid blessed with unfathomable power. He hated us and our cities with a clarity and depth that he could never explain, and, I suppose, that we would never understand.\nThe old orders tried building relics to contain and ruin him, but as far as I am aware, none of them ever succeeded. He murdered countless, crushing whole cities with a hundred years of trunks.\nHe was ravenous; he could will the gentlest creatures to commit atrocities. I know only that, after a time, he fell out of favor with the glade, and with Lyes.\nSome records suggest that he was growing too strong to control. Aureus himself could not face September directly, he was forced to ask Lyes to intercede -- which, of course, she did.\nLyes cut out a piece of September's brain, banished him from the glade, and scattered him to be lost in the world forever. I have heard stories that he has only grown more powerful and unstable since.", ""),
        StaticBook("The First's Word", "Unknown", "It is on this day, lliran, we were declared no longer Mali. Some may gasp and scorn me for writing in the tongue we had for so long cast of as part of our duty to guard the talareh'sirame-- But no longer is it just the Okarir'ame who have cast off our\nancient tongue. No, it is the will of the council that all elves within Malinor, if it can even be called that at this point, forget the mother tongue which was once spoken by all of the noble descendants of Malin. I seek not to speak these words aloud\nnot for shyness, but for practicality. It is clear we may not allow our greatest cultural artefact to be simply destroyed by the now mad council. It is clear that those who lead us must not know of our impending betrayal for the sake of Malin.\nWe must prevent what is to come. We must preserve the Word Altar.\n\n- Eloem", ""),
        StaticBook("The Fjarriauga", "The Veiled Scribe", "Legends of the Volsung - The Fjarriauga\n\nOf all the tales and legends of the Volsungs, the Fjarriauga are the darkest. In Skjoldier, homeland of the Volsung family, stories of the Fjarriauga are told to scare misbehaving children into submission at night.\nThey are said to be wicked ice spirits, taking on the guise of fair and innocent maidens to draw their prey to them. Young boys and girls alike are warned against venturing into the forests where they dwell, lest they are never to be seen again.\nIt is said that Kriemhild, the first Fjarriauga, was a woman abandoned at the altar by her betrothed. Broken-hearted she stumbled out into a snowstorm, collapsing amidst the swirling snow and frozen drifts. As she waited for death, Old Father Winter, one\nof the Volsung gods, discovered and took pity upon her. He leaned in and gave her the wedding kiss she longed for, transforming her into a vengeful - and powerful - ice spirit.\nWhile Fjarriauga are malicious creatures, they are also cunning, powerful and ageless. Many of the greatest seers and fortune-tellers in Skjoldier were Fjarriauga, and were both feared and respected by all. Brave or foolhardy men would often seek them\nout, seeking to make use of their talents, powers or insight; although rarely without cost.\nHowever, those with a sharp eye who identify a Fjarriauga even through her maiden disguise may secure her aid. Although fickle and cunning creatures, a Fjarriauga is bound to aid those who discover her with a single favour - no more and no less. Such a\ntoken should not be squandered nor taken lightly, as although she may be bound to fulfil the favour, it is unwise to earn the ire or wrath of a Fjarriauga.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Flagship", "St. Thomas Denims III", "----The Flagship---\nAXIOS WAR BULLETIN I\nThe Amber Cold, 1583\n\n--Contents--\n~Grand King Executed\n~Oren Suffers Loss at THE GORGE\n~Allies Stand Firm Behind Emperor Philip Frederick\n~Religious Roundup: Reforms and Schism\n~Debate in Haelun'or Over Security\n~Haria Reigns in Military\nGRAND KING ALGODA EXECUTED BY ORENIAN -------FOES-------\n\nAlgoda, Grand King of Urguan, was executed by Orenian officials after being seized in the Orenian town of Ostermark. This has hardened opinions in Kal'Omith in favor of the the war and the\nSenate of the Grand Kingdom of Urguan will be convening this Saint's Day to select a new King.\nOREN SUFFERS HUMILIATING LOSS AT THE GORGE, ATTEMPTS TO CONSOLIDATE CONTROL IN LORRAINE\n\nThe forces loyal to the Holy Oren \nEmperor Philip I Frederick were decimated and roted from the field of battle in the opening classh of the\nStaunton rebellion. The Stauntons and their allies held firm against a numerically superior and more advanced foe. This marks a rare loss for the Holy Oren Empire and promises to prolong the current conflict.\nTHE DUCAL CITY OF\n~~~~~~METZ~~~~~~\n\nMetz, located in the Archduchy of Lorraine, has experienced heavy fighting between rebels from the Staunton family and loyalists led by Sir Otto. Forces loyal to the emperor currently control the city,\nwhile rebels control much of the rest of the Archduchy of Lorraine, setting up what is sure to be a pivotal battle in the current war.\nALLIES STAND FIRM BESIDE PHILIP I \n---FREDERICK---\n\nThe Dominion of Malin and the Kingdom of Haense have reaffirmed their loyalty to the throne of the HOE despite the recent loss. However, public opinion in the Dominion of Malin appear divided,\nas many wonder why elvish blood should (and indeed was) spilled in the internal affairs of the valah. Old debates about th true independence of the Dominion and the true allegiances of it's leadership have also resurfaced. The Kindom of Haense, however,\nhas moved to actively supress any rebel activity within its border in addition to aiding the war effort.\nRELGION ROUNDUP: REFORMS AND SCHISM\n\nThe Church of Lorraine, also known as the Lotharic Communion, has announced a schism from the Church of the One True Faith. The rebels of Lorraine and Savoy have often raised\nallegation of interference against the Emperor in regards to reforms of the Church, and this appears to be the logical course now that the rebellion is being waged.\n\nAdditionally, the Accords of Johannesburg were\nadvanced by the Emperor and High Pontiff Adrian I, further cementing the state control over the Church of the One True Faith. Only time will tell whether the schism will be sealed and if the reforms will stand.\nDEBATE IN HAELUN'OR OVER SECUIRTY\n\nCahir aep Ophael, Braxus Ni'leya, and Icarus are vying for an appointment as the elokarir'tir. Cahir appears to have the most support among the citizenry, but it is up to the Silver Council to decide who\nget the post. There is pressure on the Silver Council to act swiflty, as recent events have revealed that lax security can lead to needless bloodshed within the Silver City.\nHARIA REIGNS IN \n---MILITARY---\n\nThe Lord Regeant of Haria, Fakhri Kharadeen, has established a court system to prevent the military from harassing citizens and visitors with little to no oversight. This will hopefully make Haria\na more pleasant place to visit, having removed the threat of state violence against individuals without any due process.\n\n\n~Ebs Telrunya\nEDITOR IN CHIEF\n~St. Thomas Denims\nPRINTER OF PONCE", ""),
        StaticBook("The Flagship v2", "Thomas Denims III", "THE FLAGSHIP VOL II\nSnow's Maiden, 1594.\n\nContents:\n-John d'Amaury Captured, Escapes\n-A New Grand King\n-Kingdom of Lorraine\n-Uproar in Haelun'or\n-Criticism of Dominion\n-Market Journal\nJOHN D'AMAURY\n--Captured--\n--Escapes--\n\nThe newly minted King of Lorraine, John d'Amaury, was taken into custody by Orenian forces under unclear circumstances. Imperial officials attempted to move him\nto the Dominion of Malin, but the King was liberated by rebel cavalry numbering about 15 following a shorty clash with numerically superior (estimated 50) Orenian and Dominion escorts.\nA NEW GRAND KING!\n\nFollowing Emperor Philip I Frederick's execution of Grand King Algoda, the Senate, composed of each of the dwarven clans, convened to elect a new Grand King. Three candidates were nominated: Bastion Ireheart by\nGrandaxe and Doomforged, Wulfstag Ireheart by Frostbeard, and Kilgrim Irongut by the Ironguts. After speeches by the three candidates, Bastion Ireheart was elected with the support from Grandaxe, Doomforged, and Starbreaker clans.\nThe new Grand King provided the following comment to The Flagship: \"Without the dwed of Urguan, the crown means nothing, and the dwed who wears the crown, means nothing. I wish to thank all those who supported my campaign for the Grand Kingship, and\npromise, that upon my coronation, I will, with the help of the very dwed who make up this stoic nation, bring back the glory of the past. I will, through dedication, passion, and perseveranc, make the Grand Kingdom of Urguan truly grand once more.\nDUCHY OF LORRAINE            DECLARES          ---INDEPENDECE---\n\nThe Archduchy of Lorraine, formerly a realm of the Holy Oren Empire, has declared independence, citing the tyranny and incompetence of the current Emperor. This comes following an\nattempted coup of the Duchy instigated by the current Imperial administration that places Ser Otto in charge of the ducal city of Metz. However, the rest of Lorraine has pledged to the rebellion, including the Despotate of Nicea and other holdings.\nThis has greatly boosted the Stauntons with both territory and men.\nSTAUNTON REBELS SCORE VICTORIES IN\n----SKIRMISHES----\n\nThere have not been any major confrontations since the now famous (or infamous) Battle of the Gorge, but there have been numerous small to mid sized skirmishes in this war, and the\nrebels have prevailed more often then not. This is a remarkable reversal of the norm, as Orenian forces typically prove victorious in the brutally savage and quick fighting and raiding that makes up most modern wars. It remains to be seen how this will\nimpact Orenian morale or if it will translate to further losses in the coming days, when large open field battles and seiges will predominate.\nAXIOT COLATION \n--ANNOUNCED--\n\nThose rebelling against the Holy Oren Emperor as well as their allies have announced a treaty that adopts a structure for their joint effots to remove Philip I Frederick from power. Along with the\nStauntons of Courland, the d'Amaurys of Lorraine, the Grand Kingdom of Urguan, Krugmar, and several other form Orenian realms are signatories. This treaty likely represents one of the largest coalitions of men and material ever arrayed against the\nHoly Oren Empire since the Great War during Anthos, which ultimately ended in the collapse of the HOE and the rise of a handful of independent Kingdoms (Ruska, Savoy, Renatus, Salvus, and Hanseti), from where we can find the roots of the political\nsituation that caused the Duke's War as well as the current conflict.\n\nMARKET JOURNAL:\nIron: 2 mina Kal'Omith\nGold: 1 mina Kal'Omith\nDiamond: 4 mina Kal'O\nLogs: .02 mina Sutica\nHay Bale: .01 Sutica\nJohannesburg\nUPROAR IN HAELUN'OR\n\nThere has been much confusion and consternation in Haeluno'or as competing groups claim to be leading the city and maintain that they have the authority to enter into treaties. Much of the conflict appears to be rooted\nin the vigil affair. It seems as if one side has taken decisive action regarding the current rebellion while the other has claimed that said action is illegitimate, though one wonders what they hope to accomplish with lengthy missives few take the time to\nread. Updates on the situation will be provided, hopefully after details become clearer.\nCRITICISM OVER DOMINION INVOLVEMENT -----MOUNTS-----\n\nThe government of the Dominion of Malin is facing mounting criticism over its involvement on behalf of the HOE in its internal conflict as citizens question why elven blood must be\nspilled on what could potentially be the losing side, resulting in a catastrophe for the mali. The government has attempted to assuage fears, but one does not see an easy resolution on the horizon. War is coming to the Dominion, and judging how forces\nacquitted themselves poorly under the current leadership, it remains to be seen if the correct choice has been made.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Flaming Bird", "Jarrod Melton", "A bird flies, building it's nest. Four legs lay atop it.\n\nEverything is peaceful, until the nest burst\ninto fire! The egss are burned, the twigs slowly becoming ashes\n\nEven more horrible, the bird flies into the fire! Out comes a -\nflaming bird, not in pain, but in rejoice\nand happines!\n\nThe fire burns away all it's sorrows. The flaming bird flies into the sky, looking like a star until it is out of view, not a trace of it in sight.\n\nAnd there you sleep,-\ndreaming of the bird, how it's fire created and deystroyed. As you dream of it, you become as joyful as the bird you saw.\n\nYou tell your friends and family of the wonderful sight you saw, and as you do, they too, become joyful.\nWritten by: Jarrod Melton", ""),
        StaticBook("The Forest", "Mayilu", "Come, take my hand\nFollow me into the forest.\nThe fallen leaves, drenched with rain, will guide our path\nThrough the shaded glade and up the moss covered hill\nDon’t be afraid to step in the mud\nListen, hear the crisp snap of twigs echo in the distance\nThe soft lull of trickling water, flowing in the creek\nWatch, catch a glimpse of the timid deer\nHiding in the thicket and the little squirrel\nLilting across the treetops, acorns in cheek\nTouch, stroke the rough bark beneath your fingertips\nCaress the summer leaves, immerse your hands\nIn the tranquility of soothing waters\nFeel, accept the dawn’s gentle kisses upon your face\nThe pure spirits that inhabit the trees\nFeel nature pulsing through your body with renewed vitality\nBreathe deeply; \nInfuse your lungs with the richness of life", ""),
        StaticBook("The Fountain Pen", "Cinh'llytn", "The\n            Fountain\n                Pen\n\n           Published\n    17th of First Seed\n               1592\n\n\n         By Cinh'llytn\nThe fountain pen is a device I have recently created to help with writing. It is similar to a quill or metal-nibbed dip pen, however it does not use an inkwell, and instead stores ink in a reservoir inside the pen itself. When one writes with it, the ink\nis drawn from the reservoir through a thin feed with three tiny channels to the nib via capillary action, similarly to how a plant draws water through its system. To prevent ink leakage, the feed has been made small enough that air cannot get in by itself\nand thusly, ink cannot get out. One might think this prevents writing, but I have found a work-around. To counter-act this anti-leakage measure, I have put a small slit into the nib, so that, when one pushes against their writing surface, it spreads the\ntines of the nib and draws ink down, as well as allowing air up into the reservoir. In the feed, I have also made small ridges, a collector of sorts to prevent over-inkage and spillage, and to allow you to always have ink near the nib for writing.\nI constructed the first prototype from various metals and finished and polished wood. The body was made from a fine elven dark oak, while the feed was constructed of steel, to prevent rusting. The reservoir is made of glass, and is detachable for easy\nrefilling. The nib is constructed from platinum, but I have found that gold, and even steel can work, but must be treated differently. I also also made the whole thing easily disassembleable for cleaning and repair purposes.\n\n(This book was written\nin its entirety with a fountain pen)\n\n*Below are several drawing of the fountain pen and its inner workings.*", ""),
        StaticBook("The Frost Witch", "Gallidron Elindrow", "An Encounter with Frost Witches\n\nby Gallidron Elindrow\n\n\nRevised edition\nI first learned about the dreaded creatures, known as frost witches, from one of the tomes in the libraries of old Haelunor. I remember the fear that gripped me as a child when I learned of their macabre ways.\nThough as an adult of more mature understanding and greater constitution, I revisited the subject of “monsters” and relearned the available details of the frost witch. They are exclusively women so far as any adventurer who has survived an encounter\nwith them can tell.\n\nThey are horrid to look upon in their natural state. Grey skinned with eyes like ice, but it is not so easy to spot one of these slippery creatures for an ice witch is a master of disguise.\nThey employ illusion to mask their true selves, that they may, with more subtlety, intrude upon our societies and seek out their prey.\n\nIn fact, as the story goes, a frost witch will adopt the guise of a young woman and sit, crying, in the midst of\nsnowy glade. This is done to attract young and hapless men. The clever frost witch will then transform into her hideous self and dispatch the unwitting male then and there, or she will lure him back to her coven to become a grisly meal for her sisters.\nThey are, without exception, powerful magic users, though the older ones are more dangerous and adept. In fact, every frost witch draws her power from a “Witch Mother” who is the head of her particular coven. Like unto a queen bee, she will build her nest\nand gather workers who rely upon her, and she them to some extent.\n\nWhen another frost witch is of sufficient power and experience, she may set out to create her own coven. They begin by searching for women who are depressed or saddened.\nThe frost witch will then “mark” the woman with a curse. Should she succumb to her sorrow she will become a frost witch herself, and thus do their numbers swell.\nIt is reportedly a favorite tactic of the frost witches to seek out a married man\nand devour him, then they will curse his grieving widow. In this fashion do they gain both a meal and a prospective member of their coven.\nNot much is known about the curse, and there is no known way to remove it. It has been said, however,\nthat if the woman resists her sadness and sorrow that she may endure the curse and not become on of these fiends. Though she will likely live with the curse for the rest of her days.\nIn order to destroy a frost witch coven one must seek out and destroy the witch mother. In some cases this is enough to cause the coven to wither and die. In others, however, if a witch who is powerful enough survives, she may assume the role\nof witch mother and allow the coven to limp on. In any case, the most foolproof method of destroying a coven is just that, destroy the coven. All of it.\nIf one seeks to harm a frost witch I would give them this advice. Strike fast and strike true for you shall not likely receive a second chance. Also, a sellsword of types once told me that gold is good for killing all kinds of unnatural monsters,\nperhaps it applies here as well, though I do not know for certain.\nIt is important to note that  a frost witch is not a rabid animal, and they can be reasoned with. They are also possessed of terrible cunning and one should not expect the blind fury of mindless monster when dealing with them.\nIt is possible to treat with them and in fact they could exist within your own city, your very neighborhood and most would be unaware. They humor of a frost witch is quite changeable and every moment you stand in their presence you are in grave danger.\nThe truth is that they are fickle creatures, and there is no telling what a frost witch might do.\nIt is said that if one finds a frost witch in disguise and calls them on it that the witch will be bound by her curse to do the clever mortal one favor. Though this is only rumor and would prove both difficult and dangerous to study.\nIn closing, frost witches are a dangerous fascination and one should not seek them lightly. They are elusive and hide among the peoples of the world, it is for this reason that we must be ever watchful lest we become their next meal.\nI hope that this book has been useful to you, the reader. And that this information will help you, should you ever have….\n\nAn encounter, with frost witches.\nBy Gallidron Elindrow\n\nPublishing date 8th of Deep Cold, 1516\n\nRevised 18th of Amber Cold, 1520", ""),
        StaticBook("The Fury", "The Inquisitor", "I know only that in this helm is the first champion of the glade, as we have on record. There is not an enormous amount of information on his rule, only on his fall. He was slave to his desires. It is what made him such a perfect champion,\nthat closeness to the id. He eventually found love in a peasant-woman. Aureus was not pleased with this. He found it disgusting, that the purity of the glade could be tainted so easily.\nI suppose it is hubris to think one can be in touch with their base desires and not fall for a pretty face so easily! I am satisfied to be free of such frivolous notions. Aureus stripped this champion of his powers,\nleaving him to be mortal once again. Eventually, his soul was itself stolen, and place into this helm. Based on a few experiments, whomever wears it longs to return to the glade, finding the mortal world dull, and at times, revolting.\nIts bearer is prone to fits of fasting and strange visions (though, they do not seem aware that the visions are themselves unusual).", ""),
        StaticBook("The Golden Crow", "Walter Marshall", "History Of The Brotherhood\n\nA comprehensive history of The Brotherhood Of The Golden Crow.\n\nBy \nWalter Marshall\nNear the close of the infamous Third Human-Dwarf War, the Urguani quickly crumbled, with numerous dwarven holdings falling to the hands of King Andrew of Oren. Most important of these newly conquered fiefs was the Hold of Hiebenhall,\nthe last Dwarven Hold in both Northern Athera and on the River Picataris, decimating the Grand Kingdom of Urguan’s vital supply line of timber and coal to the war effort. The victorious capitulation was lead by the one named Karl Aleksandrovic Tuvic,\nleading Oren-aligned levies of the County of Ayr and was joined by his Vladovic kinsman of Woldzmir.\necause of his role in its capture, Karl Aleksandrovic was aptly named Count of Siegrad by the King of Oren, beginning to slow process in subjugating the neighboring tribes which enjoyed extensive autonomy under both the Urguani yoke and the past Kingdom\nWith his new office, Karl Aleksandrovic took new arms under the urging of his fellow peers and guardians, upholding the newly christened House Barbanov,\nnamed for one of the numerous Raev Princes of yore, and wielding the standard of the gold crow upon a black field, in honor of his grandfather.\nWhat came with his appointment was Count Karl’s creation of a primed levy force, attempting to reorganize the previous wild militia from the ruins of Waldenia and be akin to those like the noble houses of mainland Oren.\nIt equated into the Brotherhood of the Golden Crow, which became Count Karl’s personal retinue and staging force, joining him in the ending days of the Third Human-Dwarf War, his elevation to Duke after the death of his uncle in 1505,\nand his later death by the hand of the Adunian Flesh Worm Mordangai (ironically the spawn of the previous Adunian Flesh Worm Wundergar which was slain by his uncle nearly two decades before).\nHis son, Siguine Karovic, inherited with his demise, the Brotherhood of the Golden Crow swearing their loyalty and resuming their original post. With Duke Siguine’s unmatured age,\nCount Tarcell of Valles took charge as regent and wardfather for the young ducal figure, becoming de facto ruler of Haense and sole leader of the Golden Crow. Compared to Duke Karl’s constant involvement and participation in Oren’s affairs,\nCount Tarcell of Valles took an isolationist approach, and the Duchy of Haense and the Golden Crow remained mostly within their borders.\n\nDespite the rising tensions and conflicts between Duke Hughes of Adria and King Olivier of Oren,\nit came to great surprise when Count Tarcell of Valles led the Haensic levy in pillaging Dour Watch under the guise of peace, nearly killing the brothers Clement and Augustus de Sola. The Duchy of Haense informally begins to help the Adrian dissenters,\nand begins a full coalition against the King of Oren in 1518, for which Count Tarcell of Valles formally signed in Duke Siguine of Haense’s name.\nIn the spring of 1518, the Coalition forces of the Duchy of Adria, Vanaheim, and Haense scored numerous victories over the Royalist forces, with Duke Hughes of Adria marching the Adrian footman deep into the Druscan Marshes,\nwith Count Tarcell of Valles flanking north and the Vanaheimic forces under command of Lord Britannus Vanir marching deep into the crownlands. However, the offensive began to crumble.\nNumerous northern lords under the Vanirs of Vanaheim launched a revolt, angered in the Vanir’s choice in supporting Duke Hughes of Adria against the King of Oren, but more importantly was the early death of Count Tarcell of Valles.\nThe assaulting Haensic forces were intercepted by the Kaedreni loyalists of Grand Duke Cantonus, where despite the Golden Crow’s ability to beat back the ambush, Count Tarcell was captured. He was tried for treason and found guilty,\nbeing executed in Castle Praha in the autumn of 1518.\n\nDuke Hughes of Adria retreats back to his namesake duchy, where the Golden Crow under the young command of Duke Siguine of Haense, now of majority age, meet with him.\nHowever, before the next assault can occur, Duke Hughes is assassinated and the coalition enters into turmoil. The Golden Crow voice their loyal and loud voice to Duke Siguine,\nfor which he wins the election amongst the lords to become the newly titled Lord Paramount. In the spring of 1520, Duke Siguine leads the forces into the Druscan Marshes once more.\nHowever, with Duke Siguine’s inexperience at such a young age, the lack of guardianship with Count Tarcell’s execution, paired with the late frost which decimated Adrian crops and the land blockade on the Duchy of Vanaheim,\nthe Coalition is defeated at the Battle of the Blackwald in late 1520, forcing the combined forces to retreat into the fortress of Barrowyk.\nDuke Siguine, with the remaining forces within northern Adria, sends a token force of Golden Crow, led by the priest Enoch of Haense and Ser Sarus Mallister, to defend Haense from incursion. The pair successfully raid Royalist supply lines,\nhowever does not stop the Royalist capture of Barrowyk in 1521 and the later Sack of Brelus, which led to the fall of both the Duchy of Adria and Vanaheim.\nThe remaining force of Golden Crow, however, did not surrender and it would take until 1524 that Haense falls to the force of Jan Kovachev in the name of King Guy II of Oren. The Golden Crow is officially disbanded,\nand many flee with other Adrian rebels from capture.\n\nBut, after the succession crisis that occurred with Duke Stefan of Carnatia and later Duke Jan of Carnatia, the House of Barbanov once again finds itself in a ducal coronet,\ninheriting the title as Duke of Carnatia which is formally renamed to the previous title of Haense. Duke Petyr takes the leading role, the posthumous son of Duke Siguine of Haense to Kamilla of Woldzmir,\nwhere he officially refounds the Golden Crow to once again stand as the protectors of the Barbanov line.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Good Stuff", "Thurak", "It should be noted that the concoctions recorded here were all tested on the Charley Chickens and Heshakomeu himself and deemed safe for mortal usage.\nDreki\nDreki is the pinnacle of my work with hallucinogenic substances and is meant for recreational usage. When consumed, the user will experience vivid hallucinations for two to three hours, then fall asleep, upon which they will fall\ninto an incredibly vivid dream that lasts for six to eight hours. It is important to note nothing can be expected in these dreams other than they will appear as real as the reality you live in while sober, no matter how exotic, bizarre, or\nunnatural they become. When on awakes, the next day will be filled with periodic migraines, light blindness, constant hunger, fatigue, uncontrollable shaking, and a strong desire for sugar.\nTo make, follow these instructions:\n\nPut a few ladles of water to boil.\nSprinkle ground-up dust of a gram of cactus green into water.\nAdd a few drops of Zawabate nectar.\nAdd a few drops of Drilltongue sap.\nGrind several dried shadeleaf leaves- no more than four – And add them to the mixture.\nStir until thick, sludgy texture is achieved and concoction is deep green.\nPour mixture onto a pan and leave in warm, dry place until all moisture is gone. \nGrind up mixture into dust.\nWith Dreki dust, one can inhale it directly through the nostril for the soonest start of effects. One can also mix it into a drink for easier consumption, though the effects will be delayed. If comfortable, one can smoke it, resulting\nin a faster arrival of effects when drunk but slower than when inhaled.\nReykja\nReykja is intended for recreational usage, specifically for group smoking. It induces light hallucinations, usually no more than flashing colours, sounds that aren’t there, synaesthesia, and distorted depth perception.\n. It also puts the user into an energetic state, giving them an almost obsessive fascination with almost anything they focus on for more than a few seconds. These effects will last for around four hours. After the effects wear off, the user will\nexperience extreme fatigue, hunger, and a dryness in the mouth that lasts for around half a day.\nTo make, follow these instructions:\n\nChop head of dried speckled crimson mushroom into tiny bits and put in a bowl.\nGrind a gram of cactus green into dust and add to bowl.\nPour a few spoon-fulls of water onto the dust and mushrooms and mix until the mixture is sticky and stuck together.\nFlatten pipeweed leaf and dab crimson-green mixture along the central stem of the leaf. Wrap leaf\naround the mixture.\nWrap pipeweed wrap in thin paper and keep it closed using pipeweed sap.\nSet in warm-dry place until consumption.\nThese cigar wraps can be smoked directly, or they can be cut into pieces and put into the bowl of a pipe. The cigars can alternatively be mounted on candles, filling the room with smoke. The cigars, prior to being wrapped in paper, can\nbe cut into pieces and put into the dough or bread of pastry and consumed through the food, resulting in a slower but just as potent high.\nSprunga\nSprunga is still rather confusing to me. I have done it a few times, for the experience is not nearly as pleasant as with Dreki or Reykja; or rather, not pleasant in the same ways. Sprunga induces an intense euphoric sensation,\ncoupled with an unnatural feeling of lightness, as though one would float away at a gust of wind. The user will also experience extreme energy and excitement, which cannot be quelled until the five to seven hour inducement is over. Depth\nperception is virtually gone, and the ear more sensitive to noise; an effect that continues to plague the user for another day. Dryness of mouth, jitters and numbness of fingers and toes also accompany the pleasant effects.\nTo make, follow these instructions:\n\nExtract juice of King’s Ivy flower into a glass bottle.\nExtract juice of Mershin fungus into glass bottle.\nClose bottle and shake until contents are mixed.\nLight fire beneath bottle and cook until brown crystals accumulate at the bottom of bottle.\nDrain bottle and remove crystals.\nGrind in mortar and pestle into fine dust.\nThe dust can be inhaled through nostrils, delivering a quick high. Lighting it afire to smoke or diluting it into a drink will severely dim or completely eradicate the positive effects.\nSpeckled Crimson Mushroom\n\nThis mushroom I first discovered growing in the storage cavern underneath Ac’Talarah. Overwhelmed with curiosity after being locked inside, I ate a mushroom, experiencing a remarkably\nvivid hallucination as well as a nearly-obsessive fascination with whatever held my attention for more than a few moments. Any potions it is used in will have the same effects. It grows in damp, dark places on\nstone, and can be recognised by its brilliant red colouration dotted with white splotches.\nMershin Fungus\n\nOriginally, I thought this mushroom to be an appendage of the Speckled Crimson, but it is in fact its own fungus. If consumed, it gives the eater a feeling of extreme lightness and happiness, coupled\nwith an unquenchable energy. However, one can hardly concentrate on anything, and the side effects are mentioned in the description of Sprunga. It has a tan head with thick ruffles underneath, and covers cave floor with a squishy, vine like growth.\nZawabate\n\nMy experiments with this flower’s nectar have been a wonderful experience. It puts users in a hallucinogenic state that detaches perception from the body, if that makes sense. The shaman who introduced\nit to me called it an ‘out of body’ experience. The nectar can be put in tea, which makes taking it quite simple and pleasant. The user must be warned, however; overdosing on this can result in permanent damage to the mind, addling the senses\nand perception of what is real even when not having recently consumed the herb. Zawabate can be recognised by its short, curved flowers and tall stalk, both in hues of yellow and green, and grows primarily beside desert oases.\nDrilltongue\n\nI have determined this to be a lovely addition to my array of recreational dosages. The sap gives the user light hallucinations and dulls the senses, leaving one disorientated and surrounded by visions.\nDrilltongue resembles a thick tangle of green roots that grip the stone it grows on tightly. It can be found in mountains and tundras.\nShadeleaf\n\nShadeleaf gives users hallucinations, which is accompanied with heightened emotional sensitivity and a deep sense of calm. The leaves can be smoked, eaten and boiled into tea, all of which grants users a\npsychedelic adventure this herb provides. Shadeleaf resembles a common weed, with short leaves and yellow flowers that grow during springtime, and grows primarily in forests. They can be distinguished from other\nweeds by the popping noise their leaves make that can be heard after rainstorms, which is caused by an overabundance of water being sent through their thin veins.\nRescribed by the Farseer Thurak, 18th of the First Seed, 1484.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Gorge, 1593", "Shaman Zlash'Lur", "Battle of the Gorge\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nscribed and translated to common by Zlash'Lur\nIn the 1590's after the desolation of San'Kharak and the murder of Rex Vorgo'Yar, the Orcs had taken salvation in the desert as refugees of Urguan. They took up and constructed a settlement named Azaghol in hiding but quickly enough they were discovered\nby a Wood Elf scout and was relayed to the Empire. As relations quickly plummeted, war eventually broke out causing a Coalition to be formed against the Orenian Empire. A time where the hunt was to be directed to the battlefield was most necessary.\nThe Imperials battled their way through the mountains eventually coming upon a valley as they planned to siege a whitewash settlement. The Coalition awaited them and when their bodies drew through the gorge the Coalition made their charge. They battled a\nlong and hard fight as the gorge quickly caused the warriors to begin wading through the mounds of bodies that littered the floor. The Commanders of the Coalition did what they could on cavalry through the piles of bodies but when the Imperials attack\nwas delayed each Commander did not hesitate to shout a key phrase amidst the battle. At the speed of sound, the word was relayed and from a hill top an explosion was made from under the land causing a major landslipe to obstruct the Imperial Legion.\nThis was a major turning point for the Coalition war and left the Empire greatly bruised by the mass of deceased caused by the landslide. The Coalition forces continued to their attack and succeeded in defeating the Imperials where they stood. A grand\ncelebration and feast was held in Urguan when the Legion finally returned home.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Great Hunt", "The Eternal Library", "The Great Hunt\nBy Unknown\nDuring the Feast of Spring, hunters from all corners of Anthos gather together to take part in the spot of hunting beasts of the wild. During spring, the animal population is at its highest.\nOther crops such as carrots, potatoes and wheat are also consumed along with the meat. Kharajyr and Orcs are most likely to pick up their weapons for the hunt, while Halflings usually plant crops instead.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Halfling Pt1", "Felix Stoutfoot", "The Halfling: The Quest for the Ocafluta\n\nBy Felix Stoutfoot\n\n~A True Story~\nDay 1\n\nToday, I set off with a few measly supplies, alongside this journal, and a wooden axe and this very rare Yew Sapling to find a nice spot.\nDay 2\n\nYesterday I made some nice progress outwards, until I hit the ocean. I travelled around the coast, and made it to a town, I decided to stay at the stables in town. In the dead of night, I swore I could hear the sound of hay being moved.\nDay 2 Night\n\nDuring tonight, I had a small flashes of dreams. Some of them were nightmares of people I loved. And then there was one in particular, a powerful warrior went up to me in a blinding light, and whispered a name to me, but I couldn't catch it.\nDay 3\n\nToday I move from the town and again into the wilderness, I plan to head to a forest full of beautiful soil. In the farthest lands, near Mastah Veren's Grove, I hear that is perfect soil for a rare Yew plant like this fella.\nDay 3 Night\n\nTonight, I stayed in a small grotto. Again, I slept and I had more nightmares of me failing challenges due to my size. The big warrior that I see sometimes seems to know my name....but its not my name...I still can't make it out.\nDay 4\n\nToday I left the quaint Grotto to head down and outwards into the valley. When I reached the Valley, I saw a large foresty area at the top of the cliffside. Tonight, I will rest up for my strength to climb the cliffside.\nDay 4 Night\n\nTonight, I slept up, and then I had a terrible, yet wonderful dream of Mira. I dunno what got into me. But when I woke up, I felt a breathing on me, and it was actually the licking of a Red Weasel. When I pet it though, it was prickly.\nDay 5\n\nToday, I climb up the mountain. I told my new friend (Who I called Samuel) to climb on my shoulder. I climbed up the first few rocks, but the stuff was too steep for my little body to handle. I decided to rest up, and fish up some food for us.\nDay 5 Night\n\nTonight was very quaint with Sam and I. I told him a lot about how I felt, and he seemed to nod as if he understood me. We then snuggled up and rested up our strength for tomorrow.\nDay 5 Night continued\n\nThe dreams kept getting worse and worse, but today. I could swear I could see the great warrior had spiky hair as he slew mighty, flying beasts. With a claymore and shield in hand, he rescued me and overcame expansive challenges.\nDay 6\n\nAs dawn broke, Sam purred like a fox on my body. And I got up, planning my next way of attack. Today, I would try going horizontally.\nDay 6 Night\n\nTonight, I write this halfway up the cliffside, in a small grotto. I am resting while making a small fire in this cool cavern. Sam kept watch for any suspicious enemies.\nDay 6 Dreams\n\nI sleep today, and I see Mira at a lakeside with me, when all the sudden, I collapse down into the lake. As I fall into the deepest reaches of darkness....I can hear the jolly laughter of some devil, I dunno. And I hear the squealling of her\nDay 7\n\nToday I broke out in a sweat. I dunno what was causing anything last night. I am going to reach the top today, and set up a small camp up above.\nDay 8\n\nI climbed up nonstop today, and through the night. The coolness of the night made it difficult. But I have made it up there to watch the dawn of Day 8. I am totally pooped as I suddenly collapse into a nap.\nDay 8 Dreams\n\nAs I collapse, I feel the same falling feeling as if I was letting go of her. And I can't reach out for my Uncle. The darkness is just....blank. I sometimes make out large, fiery foes in the dark.\nDay 8 Dreams\n\nAs I rest, I can hear a light saying \"S....Stou...\" but I can't hear. It is saying something. Before I can figure it out, a small figure appears and says \"Awaken.\"\nDay 14\n\nIt appears that winter has finally ended (I left during Winter). I dunno how long I was in that trance, but Surprisingly, Sam has been around, keeping watch and bringing all these flowers somehow. At least I think so.\nDay 15\n\nToday, I am going to plant this Yew plant. Surprisingly, it has kept its shape since I've left it. I dig a small hole, and plant it. I give a small prayer to the Yew, to become strong and hardy.\nDay 60\n\nThe past two months has been tedious and long. Fun times with the tree during the day, but nightmares during the night.\nDay 60 Night\n\nTonight, I plan to explore the darkness. I hug Sam goodnight and rest my poor eyes.\nDay 60 Dreams\n\nI explored the darkness today, the past few times, I have been seeing pictures of Her being tortured and a man cackling from doing things....I dunno what...but I just hear squeals of pain that hurt my heart.\nDay 60 Dreams\n\nI travel farther and farther through the depths, until I reach a giant red castle. I sneak into it with all my strength. The castle reeks of necromancy, and blight but the darkness already did anyways.\nDay 60 Dreams\n\nI slowly sneak through the forces to try and find any source of actual life. I stumble upon a cell soon with a Knight in a helmet, chained up and bloodied. I decide to open up the cell.\nDay 60 Dreams\n\nTo my surprise, he wakes up in an instant and I can hear a smile within the helmet. \"Well, if it isn't Stoutfoot, Son of Salmon?\" I then point at myself as he nods inside his helmet, he then removes it to show prickly, spiky hair as if it-\nDay 60 Dreams\n\n-it were quills on a porcupine. \"My name is Samuel. And I am chosen to be your guardian.\" he then kneels as if I was some sorta king. Outta sort of impulse I just say, \"Rise Samuel.\" He then rises as if some sorta knight out of a book.\nDay 60 Dreams\n\n\"I was sent out by the Three in search of Relic, it is known as a Core. Used to create a powerful, and rare instrument, barely known by Men.\" I slightly nod and just say I am searching for a friend I love.\nDay 60 Dreams\n\nWith a swift nod he just says, \"I guess our paths have crossed by the Three's Decision. Let's go now.\" He goes out of the cell, suddenly having a claymore and tower shield to match his tabard torn armor. He then slices through the nearest-\nDay 60 Dreams\n\nThe nearest Skeleton, jumping back and forth as swift and cunning as a Fox. After a couple of foes down, we head downstairs as I ask where did he learn that? \"Anything is feasible, ya just gotta set yer mind to it.\" he says.\nDay 60 Dreams\n\nWe then arrive deep in a ritual room, full of Daemon magic, and a hooded man cackling with a crack of a whip as squeals are heard from behind. \"Let's finish this.\" I say. The man cackles while swinging a Druidic marked stone in the air.\nDay 60 Dreams\n\n\"The Core!\" Samuel says, as he charges head first into the battle. I then think of what I can do to help. And suddenly I just grapple onto the back of the man, so he can't control any of his magic. So, I suddenly felt a sharp pain in my-\nDay 60 Dreams\n\n-pain in my chest, as I see a sword coming through the Hooded man as he dissipates. I then collapse on the ground as I see the girl being taken away.\n\n\"Stoutfoot, Son of Salmon.\" is the last four words I hear.\nDay ???\n\nI wake up to feel water splashing on me. it is raining, and Where I see the once sapling I was planting, I see a great tall Yew plant. I then awake to see Sam at my side, nudging me to be awake and towards the Yew plant.\nDay ???\n\nI nod to the loyal pal, as I slowly chop down the tree with a soft respect and gaze. When the tree lands with a loud thump, I can see a Wooden Core, where it is thickest. I carve out a certain section of it. I then pray and thank the Aspects for-\nDay ???\n\nFor this wonderful gift. I then sit there, wondering what I am supposed to craft. I think hard about this, and I hear the whispers of grass as if it was saying \"Stoutfoot.\" but it wasn't.\nDay ???\n\nI then come up with the idea of a larger Ocarina, but with as many holes as a standard flute. As I begin to craft this, Sam nudges me and I carve in multiple Druidic symbols, like one meaning 'Courage'.\nDay ???\n\nI soon finish within a few days of work and toil. I painted it with light green. As I sat there I wondered what my life will be like with this new instrument. I then pack up my stuff, and start heading back a changed man.\nDay ???\n\nAs Stoutfoot........Son of Salmon.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Harian Beast", "Crumena Izalith", "The Harian Elemental\n-----------------\n§y Crumena Izalith.\n\nMagical Beasts. Ever changing, every developing, the creatures of the Realm have long since fascinated those both magically inclined, and inept. How these beings work is quite often far\nbeyond our comprehension, and is often a topic of debate. The reasons behind their appearances are even further lost in thought, and while we face these creatures despite the adversity, this tome will recollect the experience of my own party when facing\na Magical Creature of devastating proportions.\n\nPart One.\nDeep in the heart of the Harian forest, a large flame erupted upon a darkened eve. Called upon by nefarious individuals, a group, accompanied by myself, trekked into the forest to find\nourselves face to face with a roaring flame. Admist the smolder and smoke, was a dainty wisp which flickered and dance around. Contained within a circle of pure flame, the wisp was quaint, quiet and peaceful. Nothing would stir this beautiful light\nas the party approached closer and closer, though the wisp simply appeared to gently float and sway in the wind. \n\nPart Two.\nStepping over the boundary which circled the wisp was never going to be a smart move, but it was the action which was made.\nFinding a position inside of the crackling circle, the wisp retreated back, it's movements becoming stiff, rigid and aggressive. As a single moment passed by, the once beautiful wisp transformed into a ferocious and gigantic representation of a Tiger,\nencased in purely blue flame, raging against the wind. Immediately arms were taken against the beast, though to no avail. Arcane blasts, a Thanic filled Lich, abjurations and wards acosted nothing from the beast. Evocations were swept away, and any and\nall attempts made to battle the Creature simply allowed it to grow further and further in power. Much to ones assumption, a retreat was necessary and soon enough, the party and I found our way far away from the Creature in the forest.\nPart Three.\nAfter acquiring the resources and greater powers in the Arcane, we returned to the scene a few elven days later, and went in for round two. This time, we started to push harder and further than we've ever done before. Punching a giant and\nfully charged Arcane beam right through the centre of the Beasts chest, we found the Creature to be severely weakened. Unfortunately, each of us had depleted our Mana Pools and we found ourselves up a dangerous path without an exit in sight. When hope\nseemed lost, and the Beast to appeared to recovering it's strength. As we recounted our lives and the decisions we'd made, the earth around the base of the Beast began to crumble, crack and tear apart from the ground. A large, pale rock became visible\nthrough the cracks, and as time progressed, a giant hand appeared to surface. Once the hand had surfaced, an elbow followed. Then a shoulder, and then a head. Piece by piece, laden horizontally under the earth, this Giant Stone Titan rose from beneath\ndirt and stone. In one swoop, the stone fist came hurtling down into the Beasts jaw. As a deep release came from the creature upon impact, a whirlwind of flame spread out in a circle for a mile around. Burning all in it's vicinity to smoke and ash, the\nonce terrifying monster was reduced to nothing more tinder and smoke. Standing in it's place, a Titan out of time. Voiceless, lifeless, the saviour of the Forest simply stood motionless. As moments drew on, and the breeze swept the flames away, the\nTitan rocked, shifted, and began to trek towards the shoreline. As the Titan disappeared through the trees, one can only assume where it ended up.\nThe Appearance\nStanding narrowly beneath the treeline, the Giant Beast took on various forms. One being the aforementioned territorial beast, another being a flaming sphere which encompassed all it came across. The final form, of course, being\nthe dormant and peaceful wisp which danced against the wind. \n\nThe Beast\nLike a Giant Tiger, the Beast from was by far  the most common and clearly the most powerful in direct attacks. Covered and comprised of blue\nflame, the Beast Form would make it's attacks through a 'breath' of pure and boiling Arcane beams. Boiling? Quite so, the force and heat from the blast was enough to tear flesh from bone, and melt stone.\nThe Sphere\nTaking on the form of a flaming sphere, the attack seemed to be an 'Area of Effect, otherwise known as an AoE' to quickly thin out those around. While not particularly powerful, the heat from the sphere was enough to make a groan man sweat\nand drop to his knees. Once again, no particular attacks appeared to damage the Beast outside of brute damage. \n\nThe Wisp\nDormant, yet so alive, the Wisp danced against the wind and teetered to and fro. Peaceful, absent from\nall negative motion, this peaceful form simply drifted along the breeze and only seemed to grow irritated when someone stepped over the boundary it had so carefully laid around it.\nExtra Details\nPossibly landing from a fallen stone, fire surrounded the area of impact. Trees fell apart, and the ground smoldered, though one very distinct circle was laden around the Wisp. Placed by the force itself, or by another, it seemed to\nactivate and provoke a hostile force from the beast. \n\nPersonal Account\nWatching people melt before me, fighting a creature beyond measure in a state of disarray, I found myself entirely clueless on how to respond. I continue my research\non creatures like this, monitoring movement and activation, I aim to understand the true meanings behind this circumstance. As research would have it, it would seem the being I faced was what is known as an 'Elemental', a being of extraordinary power.\nNot all Elementals are as powerful, some are more tame, and some are more ferocios. My study continues.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Holy Grail", "Lord Hassan of Gundabad", "This offends me as a vegan transgender atheist who vapes and crossfits four times a week, I'm also a male feminist as I identify myself as a pastafarian apache helicopter dog mega multi combo of hyper death and if you don't agree with me - you're a bigot\nignorant arrogant homophobic sexist lesbian. \n\n-signed Lev\naka 'the jawline'", ""),
        StaticBook("The Holy Soldier", "Kili Al-Deen", "in the distance a man with a white turban and patted clothing with a stand of his turban waveing in the air,his arm raised high,with a curved sabre in hand his face is of a light tan and his eyes are dark brown with a light beard he towers over his grey\nhorse. he is know to be a hero, a warrior, a scholer.he hopes onto his steed and charges tword the claded enemy out numbered 1 to 8 as he charges his sword shimmers with a writing on it that says \"Soldier Of Allah\" to the enemys who robed thousands of\npeople they are known to rob kings and burn kindoms. Empores surrenders kingdoms to these men...but not this man. this man knows truth,the armored men laugh at this young man only in cloth charging to kill these 8 powerful warlords. slashing begins\nmen fall and shouts of pain can be heard from around the world untill there was one left but silence...until someone broke that silence..\"GOD IS GREAT!\"...the carvaners stood in shock  as they watched the turbaned man ride away until one called\n\"Who are you!\"  the turbaned warrior stops and turns and says \"I Am a Soldier Of Allah\"after saying that he smiles and says\"ma'a salama rafiqi\" and rides of into the sun set. the world knows him as a hero,a warrior,a scholer, i know him as\nA Soldier Of Allah.\n\n\n\n      by: Kili Al-Deen\n-------------------Thank you for reading I hope you enjoyed this book!", ""),
        StaticBook("The Homunculi", "Belegar", "The Homunculi\nBy Belegar Tunnelsmasher\n\nMalin’s Welcome, 1551\nPreface\nI, Belegar Tunnelsmasher, brother of Beros Oathcast whose body was made into a homunculi, am writing this to serve as a warning against dangers the homunculi pose and how to take on out if the situation comes to it.\nHomunculi 101\n\nThere are currently four tiers of homunculi being: fiend, deviant, aberrant and doppleganger. \n\nFiends\n- looks like a fiend\n- weak, very short lvied\n- not sentient\nDeviants \n- look similar to the race of the descendant whose body they are created from\n- slight disfigurements\n- odd skin colours\n- short lived\nAberrants\n- very similar look to descendants\n- unnatural skin colour\n- very small disfigurements\n- greater strength than descendants\n- average lifespan\nDopplegangers\n- extremely intellignet\n- very strong, to the point of being able to lift items such as entire iron gates\n- bodies are almost perfect\n- cannot be killed by natural means (will be explained later)\n- does not have blood, instead has a\nsubstance related to the element they were created with\n- look identical to the descendant they are made from\nHomunculi have no morals or regard for life. They only look to extend their own lives and further their own goal to achieve ‘ascendancy’. In other words, they seek to become a god. This is the fifth tier of homunculi, and the tier that has yet to be\nachieved. It is imperative that they do not achieve this.\n\nAdditionally, most homunculi do not have souls. \n\nThe process to create a homunculi will not be detailed in this book, but let it be known that in order to make one a corpse is required,\nand the homunculi will not hesitate to murder to get their hands on one.\nHow to Kill a Doppleganger\n\nIn order to kill a Doppleganger, one cannot use normal means. Simply cutting off their heads will not end their existence, as if their body is left alone, it will slowly regenerate until fully formed once again.\nThe only way to completely kill a Doppleganger is to inject their bodies with a ‘Potion of Unmaking’. \n\nThe process to create this potion requires an experienced alchemist. The reagents needed are: Metzil’s Tangle, Flame Tongue Root, Serpent's Stalk,\nLarihei’s Fingers and two lodestones. A lodestone is a rock that exhibits magnetic properties. Once this potion is made, the Doppleganger must be incapacitated and every piece of their body injected with this potion. The potion will then tear the\nhomunculi apart and end their existence.\nKnown Dopplegangers\n\nAt the time of writing, there are two know Dopplegangers. They are Prohan and Lotho. They are extremely dangerous, do NOT approach them voluntarily. \n\nBoth have air as their element of creation.\nProhan:\n\n- human\n- tan skin\n- black hair\n- looks like Daniel Nodal\n- Member of the Dawn Strider Voyagers, often seen wearing the uniform\nLotho:\n\n- dwarf\n- white skin\n- blonde hair\n- looks like Beros Oathcast\n- no accent\n- usually seen dressed in white robes with a set of goggles atop his head\nWeaknesses of Homunculi\n\nHomunculi are damaged by aurum and Holy Magic much like the undead are. If confronting a homunculi, especially a Doppleganger, it is highly recommended to wield an aurum blade and wear aurum armor.\nAlso, if possible, assistance of one versed in the arts of Holy Magic is highly recommended.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Inner Circle", "Leyun Kameki", "The Inner Circle\n\nScribed by Hierophant Callax, the Solstice Druid\nExisting within the structure of the Druidic Order Circle of Malinor, which is the primary and mother Circle of Druids, is an Inner Circle. The Inner Circle is rather different than a Druidic Circle, however. It is part of an existing Circle, composed of\nthree Archdruids and no set number of Druid Guides who all take responsibility for the inner working of the Order.\n\nThe Druids of the Inner Circle are those who are permitted to guide and attune Dedicants as well as train Druids in the\nways of teaching or in harnessing the Gifts of Nature. During a Moot, the Druids of the Inner Circle cast their votes, with only the best interests of the Order in mind, to make a particular decision for the Order.\n\nThe Inner Circle doesn't dictate the\nOrder, nor does it dictate or manipulate individual Druids. Rather, the Inner Circle has, for countless centuries, only served to maintain order by making larger decisions for the Order and effectively upbringing new generations of Druids.\nThe Archdruids and Druid Guides of the Inner Circle are crucial to the function and future of a Druidic Order. This ancient and important aspect of Orderly structure should never be forgotten. Blessed be.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Joy", "The Inquisitor", "A rare champion of the glade, Thickethand was a halfling. They were remarkably amiable. It bordered on the supernatural. A few suggest it was a powerful psionic or memetic event.\nRegardless, Thickethand was a halfling who was able to make friends with near any other sapient creature they encountered. They became personal friends with Aureus, and most of the other denizens in the glade.\nThey were kind, reserved. Thickethand maintained the glade, brought it great lushness and bounty. Their rule was otherwise unremarkable. Though it is likely apocryphal, records hold that they ultimately perished when they tried to befriend an avalanche.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Kaedreni", "The Bloody Baron", "22nd of Malin's Welcome,\n                              1519\n\n\n         THE STATE\n             OF THE\n           KAEDRENI\n\n\n       by Titus de Sola\nDust scatters on the horizon.  Hooves on valley upon valley thunder to a halt, beasts glaring across to the other, obeying their rider's whims.  Carrion birds dare defy the scorching heat and incandescence of the regal\nWhite Sun.  A scene is painted for\nyou that will set the stage for generations to come. But no matter the turmoil nor the degeneracy of either side I find my conscience bothered greatly by the fact that the blood of Kaedrin and Rhoswen turns against eachother under both banners of the war.\nThe Kaedreni have opted to let their luster become a finely honed weapon, a greatsword, to be used at the whims of Savoie and Sarkozic alike, though disrespected moreso on behalf of the latter.\n\nBut only the Kaedreni allowance of such be at fault.\nAnd it is a weapon, forged inside the lungs of hell, wrought by tens of thousands of the strongest men of our Kaedreni race, that we do now let the others, who have forgotten their place as our vassals, use freely and improperly against eachother,\nlike children who can scarcely pick up a fork.  That weapon is our martial mastery and sheer superiority in waging conflicts, gained by our diligence in carrying out the will of God and His first, the line of Horen, and then of Chivay.  No other Race\namongst Men can maintain aggression nor offensive nor conviction in the way that the Kaedreni man can; it is simply impossible.  They cry as they attempt to emulate our finest military traditions that they have inherited our place as the finest amongst\nmankind, but like all others their walls crumble, their people degenerate, they turn to banditry and villainy, and they destroy themselves from the inside.\n\nThey frequently seek our service as their officers, but they will never be heirs to Kaedrin.\nThe free men of the Rose have turned on eachother, instead of their proper enemies: those who envy all we Kaedreni have done.\nPeter must weep, if the dead weep, at the state of our people, our Kaedreni race.\n\nI would weep in his place, but I\nwould also hope.\n\nI would not see the blood of Kaedrin wither into nothing in the same way that the Horens did.  Even the common Kaedreni man, at this stage, is more bloodworthy than your mainstay Orenian lord, and no doubt far more\nthan those savages of color out of the Duchy of Adria whom want to eat us alive. I would not see our people fall to that fate. I would endeavor to stop it.\n\nI, De Sola, would fight to the death if need be for our people, so long as it granted my\ncountrymen victory.\n\nAnd though when fighting we are naturally greater, fight, we must not always.\n\nWe need consolidation.  Ties of marriage between our Kaedreni Houses.  Living space, territories, slaves.  We cannot forget what it means to bear\nour name.  We were made to militarily administrate the world, and everyone else living in it are either ourselves, our allies, or they are rebels.  There is no other alternative.\n\nWhich of the three are you, friendo?\nMy love and my strongest wishes to those whom this letter concerns.  May it find you in good health, and in the mind for a change of the course of our history.  Hear out this message, brothers, hear out this message and bring Creeping Death to them all.\nBy Owyn's guidance, we will prevail.\n\nAve, true to Kaedrin!\n\n                         T.d.S", ""),
        StaticBook("The Karin", "Genevieve", "The Karin's New Collar\nThere once was  a small Karin, he was prideful, his horns glimmered the brightest, and his two tails were twice his size.  Everyone was astounded by his grace and beauty, however he lacked one thing a fitting collar.\nTwo mice ran through the forest, and he pounced upon them.  \"Do not eat us!\" They begged.  \n\n\"Why should I not eat you?\"  He asked them.\n\n\"We will make you a new collar of the finest silks!\"  They said, however little did he know, these mice, were indeed\ntricky.  For he allowed them up.  \"What materials do you need?\"  He asked them.\n\n\"We require needles and thread, and gold!\"  They pleaded to him, however when he gave them the items, they stashed them away.  \n\nA few days later he returned to find them\nhard at work, or so he thought, yet it looked like they sewed thin air.\n\n\"What are you doing?\"  He asked.\n\n\"We are making your collar good sir, but it's a material that only you can see if you have faith.\"\nHowever, not being able to see anything the Karin was embarressed, looking away for a moment.  \"Oh yes, the finest.\"  He responded.\n\n\"Do you see the gold and the jewels?\"  \n\n\"Of course!\"  He lied.  And they put it on him.\nHe walked through the jungle, bragging about it and the other animals, afraid to be eaten all agreed it was lovely.\n\nUntil a small bird from up high said.  \"But...mother.  I can see nothing around his neck.\"  And that's when the Karin realized.\nIf a bird, expecially a baby could not see the collar, and they had faith far and wide, then the collar was false.  His pride had gotten the better of him.  \n\nSo he chased after the mice and ate them right up, before going to sleep with a full stomach.\nHe had learned his lesson, his pride never got the best of him again.\nThe End", "")
    )

    private fun _AXIOS_TAHN_5(): List<StaticBook> = listOf(
        StaticBook("The Knight", "The Inquisitor", "This breastplate beats with the pulse of one of the glade's old champions, the Knight. He was unusual in that he was a practical man, in touch with the physical world, and not much else.\nHe did not rely on gods, nor demons -- not the creator of the canonist, not Cerridwen or Cernunnos, not even Iblees. Perhaps this is why Aureus took such a liking to him -- his mind was focused on the world around him.\nHe entered the glade with his cohort of soldiers. They were called the Lion's Paw, a small group of mercenaries who would fight in wars for pay. None of them took to the glade, except for the Knight.\nPerhaps it was relaxing to a mind made weary by so much conflict. In the end, Aureus chose to make the Knight his new champion, and has him to slay every single member of his mercenary company.\nThe records say that, on the following morn, the Knight slit the throats of every one of his brothers. Some say that he did it stoicly. Some say that it weighed on him until his death. It is uncertain.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Lake", "Sofetios", "The Lake\nBy Sofetios\n\nI wander upon a path by a lake,\nWondering where it’s all gone.\nEvery day I used to come here,\nFrom the morning to the evening’s yawn.\nEvery now and again I wonder,\nWhy the days have passed,\nAnd think very deeply,\nWhy they don’t seem to last.\n \nDay by day, night by night,\nThe Lake becomes small still.\nThe thoughts of it become thinner,\nEven to my strongest will.\n \nIt has become ten smaller and ten times shallower,\nEven though it has not changed\nTo other people it might be normal,\nBut to me it is considered strange.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Lava Claw", "John Lyons", "1st of Snow's Maiden\n1627\n\nI have decided to celebrate the year of our lord 1627 by going on an adventure.\n\nafter setting out I immediatly feel fourty years longer, my target lies to the south of the Westerlands\nThe Lava Claw is a ruin that has perplexed me for a large part of my life, east of Haelun'or there's nothing but grass and the occassional tree, but then there's a massive crater, filled with lava and at the center there's a massive ruin of a stone\nclaw-like structure.\n\nThus I named it the claw. Due to it's unique shape and boring surroundings i was able to make a map of it in rather a short time.\n\nAccessing the claw itself shouldn't prove too difficult for a younger man\nbut I myself shan't do it!\n\nThe deep crater tells us a lot a bout the rock layers of this part of Tahn, it mostly consists of smoothstone with occassional patches of dirt, I spotted what i'm sure are bricks in the ground layers\nPerhaps this was once a site of the ancient Kingdom of Malin?\n\nAbout thirty meters below the surface the lava comes pouring out into a basin that surrounds the claw.\n\nThe structure appears to resist the lava easily, which is curious.\nAfter sticking around for a few hours night fell, this did not seem to affect the structure.\n\nThe Claw has not changed in decades, nor has there been evidence that it's linked to the forces of evil.\nTherefore I'm delighted to conclude that it is merely one of the many curiosities of Axios and not a threat to it's inhabitants.\n\n\nWritten for the Lyons institute by it's owner.\n\nJohn Lyons", ""),
        StaticBook("The Lusty Hou-zi", "Door", "*The material is so graphic in explanation that not even the wandering wizard would dare to speak the word.*\n\nYou feel as if you can suddenly wield a sword in one-hand better.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Mali'ker", "Dak'ir Des'Nox", "Birth of the Mali'ker\n------------------\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  By Dak'ir Des'Nox\nBefore I begin this tale, I'd like to state that the origin of the Mali'ker is still unknown to us. This is simply an\nold tale passed down \nthrough my clan.\nIt begins with the \nHearth Father, Malin.\nHe looked upon the Mali'ame, his first children. Their image molded after the forests they reside in. In them he saw devotion. A will to protect the trees and animals without rival.\nHe then looked to the high elves, his second children. Their display was ever the epitome of purity. In them he saw knowledge. Their desire to learn and expand in all things was unparalelled. \n\nBut he saw something they lacked. Passion.\nHe racked his mind of many days. It was not until he looked skyward as dusk fell that he saw what would design us. \n   Before him lay the night tide, a vast sea of stars and anomalies. He raises a hand to the night sky and began to collect what would\nmake us seperate from out fair colored kin. He took the dark hues from the empyrean and shaped our bodies. He took the tails of comets and darkened stone of meteorites. Giving us the blacks, whites, and faint blues of our hair.\nHe took a step back from his creation, observing the from of what would become the dark elves. Folding his arms, he thought.\n\n   What else could set these beings apart from the Mali'ame and\nthe Mali'aheral?\nNext, he looked down. His eyes falling upon the ground. Kneeling, he reached an arm into the depths of the earth and began to pull precious gems from the deep recesses. He carried the jewels back to the grey froms placing them into their eyes.\nHe favored the rubies and garnets most of all, but occasional sapphires, emeralds, and topazes glinted in their vigils.\n\n Before him stood us.\n     The Dark Elves.\nBut there was still something... What could give us the passion we lacked?\n\n   He looked above one final time and raised a careful hand. Plucking single stars from the sky and placing one within each of us. Giving us our bright and burning souls.\nHis mind lingered to the Wood Elves and High elves again.\nNature and dedication. Knowledge and Purity.\nBut what could give the Dark Elves their drive?\n\nHe pondered again. Before long, he smiled softly.\nHow could he forget? \n\n   He spoke to the still forms and uttered three words.\n\n\"Family, honor, love.\"\n\n            ...\nAnd with that, we awoke. With stars burning brightly in our chests, fueling these three things, we have become the fiercely passionate beings we are today...", ""),
        StaticBook("The Mariner", "Belestram Sylvaeri", "The Fate of the Mariner\n\n\nBy Belestram of the House Sylvaeri\n\n\nWritten this Twelfth of Grand Harvest, 1609, for the enrichment of a certain Lady.\nThe constellation known as \"The Mariner\" is among the brightest in the night sky, and eldest in the memory of the Descendants. Taking the form of a man with arm outstretched, this conglomeration of stars is beloved of the seafaring peoples of the world-\nfor no matter the location of the viewer, his hand will always point northward. He is known as Narnir'vallei in the Elder Tongue, and is personified by many true figures throughout Elven history. His companion is known as \"The Grieving Maiden\", and plays\nan integral part in the tales which surround these stars.\n\nThe following is an excerpt from the \"Lays of the Old Princedom\", a translated and abridged compendium of the oldest verses in all Elvendom. While lacking the beauty of the original text, it\nconveys in simple verse the tragic \"Fate of the Mariner\" and to this day remains the only version of the Elven story in the Common language.\n\n\n     ~~~~~~~~\nIn ancient days, before the fall,\n'Neath eldritch bough, in silver halls,\n\nThere trod an elf whose heart was true,\nA Prince, a mariner, and who\n\nWrought ships to sail the sapphire plain,\nIn calm, and in torrential rain.\nHe loved the sea, and knew her charms,\nAnd bore the fury of her storms.\n\nThis noble seafarer of old, of silver locks and manner bold,\n\nWas loved in turn by fairest maid,\nFor whom his noble heart had sway'd.\n\"I will return upon the dawn,\" \nHe sweetly vowed to her, \"and yon,\"\n\n\"Together we will ply the shore,\nAnd venture seaward, nevermore.\"\n\nThe sea is fickle, grudging, vain,\nAnd in dark passion did disdain\nThe sailor's word, and took his life,\nTo spite his earnest, loving wife.\n\nHer heart thus rent, with love unmade,\nShe leapt from highest promenade,\n\nAnd broke upon the crags of stone,\nHer mortal coil of flesh and bone.\nAnd so it is, lliran, and so,\nUnto the stars they did bestow,\n\nThe image of their tragic love.\nTheir form can oft be seen above,\n\nThe Mariner, and very near,\nThe Maiden, lantern raised austere,\nTo guide all sailors, as he swore,\nTo return home forevermore.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Marked Code", "Sighard of Bastion", "~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n                The                          Marked Code\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n[!] https://goo.gl/ky4mUb", ""),
        StaticBook("The Matriarch", "Thurak'Yar", "The Matriarch\n\nFirst born of the brood of Dragur, a female, molded in his image, and adopting his unquenchable thirst of sheer knowledge. “The Sun will awaken each new day, followed by the rise of the moon, that will light\nthe seemingly endless nights, and during these nights it will be the Stars which will guide you. This land in which you were born in will teach you many things. And as you come to learn, you will share the knowledge which you have come to acquire in the\nhopes that the ones you have come to share with learn from it. This is my dream.”\nAnd so the Daemon fell into a seemingly eternal slumber. Many centuries have come to pass since that day, and he collection continued to grow.\nUnfortunately, some had used bits of knowledge she had shared with them for their own greedy purposes. They didn’t believe in her ways of “Shared knowledge for knowledge”, and wanted it without giving anything in return.\nThey found the place in which she kept all her books, scrolls and scrawlings, and began to steal whatever they thought would bring them wealth and power. Upon returning, she felt a sense of violation and mistrust, but knew and understood that\ntime itself would heal those feelings. She began to scrawl everything she could remember from what was stolen from her, but they were merely tattered fragments compared to what she once had. Hope had reached her a few years\nlater when she found one of her books amongst some ruins and rubble. She began to hope that the others will come to reveal themselves once more.\nThus, the Matriarch wanders the land, in search of the items that were taken from her, but also\nstill learning what she can from her travels and from the land. By merely observing and keeping scrawls of what she has come to witness, to finding books, novels and scrolls from past and present civilizations of the land.\nThis is her passion… And her only purpose.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Mighty Uruks", "Vallel", "~*~ I met a wise and strong uruk. Her name was Nurena of the Yar clan. She provided all this information to me and I tried my best to organize the information properly and be as accurate as possible with it. Thank you, Nurena! ~*~\n-=- Book dedicated to people who want to learn about this interesting race. Also to clarify and provide as much knowledge as possible about orcs.-=- [!] From this point on, the book looks like it was written by a child! Still legible.\nUruks, or orcs, are massive and large beings of these lands. They are tough, strong, and honorable. Uruks are usually seen as one of the largest race, but there are Ologs! Ologs are bigger and perhaps stronger than a regular orc.\nWith great strength of an Olog, comes a deep curse upon them. These giants are unwise and lack knowledge out of all their brothers. Goblins, however, are clever and smart, but are smaller than the average orc. All of them come in different size and color.\nThe entire race all speak a language called Blah. Most words are the common tongue, yet they are uniqely said due to their accents. Uruks greet each other with a headbutt followed by \"Ug.\" It is the most honorable and respectful greeting.\nUruks belong into a clan. Clans are a big group of orcs, ologs, or goblins who are like a family, but better! They are a matter of honor to defend their brothers and sisters. Uruks are usually born into a clan, though some may take a clanless uruk in.\nEach clan have their own traditions. Every clan comes from a great ancestor related to Krug in some way. Examples of a few clans: Yar, Gorkil, Lak, Radukz, Baduks, Lur, and Ugluks. There are still a lot more!\nWithin the uruk city, they have a leader called the Rex. I mey a past Rex called Eath'Lur who is a great orc. I am not sure how an uruk becomes a Rex, though.\nIt must take strength and honor to become a Rex. To achieve that, an uruk should make it to adulthood. Only the strongest make it to adulthood. To make a strong child to allow it to be make it to adulthood, there is a tradition uruks do.\nThey make cozy and warm dens for the moommy uruk. They call it \"nesting dens.\" The comfy caves can range from a large one to a small one, but they all make baby orcs big and strong!\nOrcs do not trust other people other than their own race, especially on thier land. Orcs are fearsome and territorial to non-orc races. Although they could kill and attack outsiders, they would not harm a child. There is no honor to kill children.\nOther non-orc races pay something called tribute. Tribute is not just giving to an orc. Tribute is giving to an orc in exchange for peace between them. Food can be used as tribute to the orcs.\nOnto their worships! Uruks praise the spirits. Spirits are powerful beings that live in the Void and can take physical form. There are three types of spirits: Immortal, Ancestor, and Lesser. All spirits are free beings to an extent.\nShamans are people who can talk to and summon spirits. They usually only call to spirits when they need help or guidance. Shamans make totems for the spirits and the spirits like their totem. A shaman can call to a spirit whenever they need to.\nThese wise people have their own staffs that they have which seem very important to them. Sadly, there are bad shamans in this place. The bad shamans are called dark shamans. They use a spirit to their own will and for other evil stuff!\nLuckily, a powerful shaman can purge the evil shaman and cut off their powers to talk and use spirits.\nIt is important to note that totems are for spiits. Every spirit have their own likes, dislikes, and gifts. The totem and area around the totem are made of things that symbolize the spirit and what they like.\nDon't be a whitewash orc and not worship spirits! Whitehwash orcs are orcs who have no honor and have disrespected the race. An uruk can become whitewash if they live with non-orcs or betray their own race. Be a good and strong orc!\n~*~ Uruks are so cool! Their culture and traditions are unique and perhaps one of the only interesting one's I've seen.\nThank you to Nurena for making all this possible! ~*~", ""),
        StaticBook("The Moot", "Leyun Kameki", "The Moot\n\nScribed by Hierophant Callax, the Solstice Druid\nThe Moot is an assembly held for all Druids of a particular Circle to come together for discussion, debate, and decision making. It is a time to worship the Aspects, to make notice of the events of the world, to commit to projects, and much more.\nMany times a Moot might serve the sole purpose of voting for a new Archdruid or Druid Guide or to cast votes on shunning a particular individual who has wronged a Druid, Druids, or the Order. Seldomly, a Moot might be held to throw a party, host a\nwedding, or perform a funeral.\n\nOnly by the word of an Archdruid may a Moot be called. Druids, Dedicants, Druid Guides, and Hierophants all can, and should, present information of importance to the Archdruids, and anyone can request\na Moot be called. However, it is up to an Archdruid to decide if and when a Moot shall be held and for what topics it shall be held to discuss. Only shall the Inner Circle, the Archdruids and Druid Guides, make a definite decision, based on a vote count,\nfor the Order. No other Druids or Hierophants are permitted to make decisions for the Order, but their opinions and advice are taken seriously and with much consideration. When serving as a meeting, a Moot is held in the Moot Room of the\nhosting Grove. While a Moot is in session, often times the Archdruid who called it will take the floor to present topics. Out of respect, all who wish to speak should wait for a pause or go-ahead. Druids should request or stand to take the floor or\npresent a topic. Dedicants aren’t permitted to attend Moots, but accepts are often made. In the case that a Dedicant is permitted at a Moot, he or she shall not speak unless asked to.\n\nThe Moot is an ancient tradition of Druidic culture. Sometimes\nnon-Druids are even invited to Moots, such as when relations are being discussed between the Order and a Nation or other group. A Moot is versatile, able to serve the purpose for many different occasions. It is one of the most formal, serious, and\nimportant aspects of Druidic culture. When in attendance of a Moot, remember to respect the speaker and follow proper etiquette. Blessed be.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Mori", "Thurak'Yar", "The End of the Mori\n\nWhen the murders and attacks on the city occurred, many speculations arose within the city itself of whom was to blame and who should be slaughtered for such acts against their kind – many claimed it was the work of the\nsurfacers, others believed that such things were only possible by those living within the city.\nIt was declared and enforced that all living Mori were to return to the bosom of Nemiisae and remain within the sanctum of Menocress; behind\nthese stragglers to return the horror unfolded, each path and passage that journeyed through only hours before could be heard crumbling under the weight of explosives. The people were brought each in turn to the Temple of the\nMother to be cleansed of their taint, the sickness of the surface that had infested them. The final act of the Valsharess and her Yathrins before the war broke out.\nMany that had broken loose from such rigid traditions fought against this cleansing\nand became quickly enraged, spitting in the faces of the priestess’ whom dared demand their obedience and silence. It was not long before two factions emerged; the devout and the rebels. Beneath the surface of the world, sealed off from\nthe blinding damnation of the sun’s light, the Caverns of Menocress’ streets were littered with crude barricades, strewn with the deceased and wounded – The once marvelled city now rots with death and destruction… crumbling under the civil war.\nBathed in life blood of their kith and kin, the rebellion breached the Yathrins’ sacred enclave; banners raised in revolt, their armour and bodies marked by their treason. Once considered mere common rabble; these denizens now slaughter\nblessed noble born and their ilk standing guard at the doors of the Temple. From behind the sealed doors both rothe and Mori alike stand in the un-ease union against the threat of tait to its own city – this seeded by those turned to the\nhubris of their Ilharn Zanunder.\n\nRescribed by the Farseer Thurak’Braduk, 14th of the First Seed 1484.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Obelisks", "Leyu Ward", "The Obelisk Theory:\n\nThis is simple, a very simple theory. we're floating in a void, if you've traveled far enough you'll understand what I mean, and everything on each isle looks like it's been pieced together, a Mesa runs straight into a plain,\na desert straight into a mountaineous snow region. The areas look pieced together, my theory is that someoen got a little trigger-happy with their magic, or possibly some Daemon or Aengul, but the Obelisks seem to be sparsely placed but most often found\nin habited areas, or corners, there's some in corners of the realm, and others in the middle of the land. My theory is that these obelisks are what keep us suspended in this voidal abyss. I'm not sure why I think this, but I do. I know a few people want\nto destroy the obelisks, but if they do I'm afraid it may just make the land drop into the void and kill us all. We did get here through some kind of portal, or so I've heard.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Obvious Laws", "Lucion Sullas", "The Obvious Laws\n\n\n\n\n\n\nby L. Sullas\n-The blessed residents of mali’aheral land will not tolerate the ineffable natures of violent beasts. \n\nThis extends into any and all acts of physical aggression upon another citizen of pure blood, or, in fact any non\nmali’aheral who are allowed within the territory. Violence is the tool of the worthless animals outside elven lands, and its evils should only be put into use by those who have sacrificed themselves for the good of the race the Sillumiran.\nViolence in the name of self-defence is obviously legal, should a citizen be in immediate danger.\n-The blessed residents of mali’aheral land will not tolerate the loathsome fingers of uncontrolled greed.\n\nTheft of any conceivable nature is frowned upon greatly by any and all who deem to perform it. There is no exception\nto this rule. A society that disregards the call of the petty coin has little patience for those whose greed is akin to the Bortu.\n-The blessed residents of mali’aheral land will not tolerate the meanderings of unscrupulous and alien wanderers.\n\nThose who are deemed unworthy will not be allowed entrance. Those who are allowed within will be on a\nvery short leash.  Should they irritate enough of the citizenry, foreign beings will be ejected--by force if necessary.\n-The blessed residents of mali’aheral land will not tolerate the purity of their citizens purposely tarnished out of hedonistic glee.\n\nPurity is not in the eyes of the beholder. It is in the venerated manners of our mali'thill ancestors\nwhen we find guidance in purity. It is not enough that one’s heart is pure--for only when one’s mind and blood remains unmuddied can true purity be gained.\n-The blessed residents of mali’aheral land will not tolerate the disgraceful and irrational destruction of written thought.\n\nKnowledge is of great value to the mali’aheral as it promotes the maehr’sae which is vital to the progress\nof our venerated people. The destruction of tomes of any value within the great library is to be treated as a crime akin to both violence, and theft.\n-The blessed residents of mali'aheral land will not tolerate the presence of unscrupulous alien wanderers within the Eternal Libary\n\nThe knowledge held within the Eternal Library is not for the perusal of any of the lesser peoples upon\na whim. Only those who are deemed worthy of it by the exaulted citizenry may be permitted into the library, and only on very select occasions are they to wander the great, expanding labyrinth. All found without proper cause to be within will be met with\nimmeadiate ejection.\n-The revered Okarir’tir will be the epitome of authority in matters pertaining the laws of the mali’aheral civilisation--for they are the guardians and keepers of the peace.\n\nThe words of the Okarir'tir shall follow and upkeep on the letter of the law\n--no more no less. The Okarir'tir shall be chosen by referendum, and, should the citizenry be dissatisfied with their actions, can be removed by the same process.\n-The revered Sillumiran have the right to uphold the ways of the mali’aheral people, and guard the culture of Larehei from those whom would disrupt it.\n\nThe sillumiran obey the orders of the Okarir’tir and will follow them to the letter.\nThey are allowed, however, to perform any punishment they deem fit for breaking these listed offences, under the sole condition that the punishment they inflict does not conflict with any other current law, or the traditions of mali’aheral culture.\nby L. Sullas\n\nCopied from the Referendum on Mali'aheral Law\n*a pile of paper has been neatly stacked*", ""),
        StaticBook("The Pain", "The Inquisitor", "I do not know the name of the god to who Irri'aye pledged herself. Only that this sword has been pledged in its service, and that whoever wields it, must also wield that black voice. Just as the blade rends flesh, so too must it scar the spirit.\nWhoever that god was, they had the strength to hold onto Irri'aye, even despite the strongest efforts on part of Aureus.\nIt is not recorded whether she first became a champion of the glade, and then was taken by the temptations of this distant god, or whether she was allowed to become the glade's champion despite her prior commitments.\nShe served the glade and her god together, for a time. Times were peaceful, and the world was calm. She was one of the few champions whose ferocity matched that of the glade itself, sharp-witted and with a fiery spirit.\nShe pushed the boundaries of the glade, expanding its domain.  This made her well-respected and feared. It was wise to stay in her good graces. Unfortunately, it was not to last.\nA time came when there was conflict, and she was forced to choose between the glade, and her dark god. She chose her god, and so Aureus cast her out of the glade for all time.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Paver", "Geoboy66", "I am the Paver. I am one of the many nameless Remnant Dead, shells of our former selves. The skeletons of men you see about you are fallen citizens of Aegis, consumed to the blackness of the Abyss. Now the flock to the Sanctum and take nourishment in\nits warm dark.\n\nMy name is lost to the many cycles of the moon, but my work exists all about you. The Remnant dead have restored fallen ruins into working order in service of our great serpentine Master, Mordring.\nWhile time has been cruel to the minds of many of the dead, there exists some of us capable of writing and speech. I am one such creature, and thus I take upon the name of the Paver, for I have lead the more submissive of my brethren in the dark light of\nMordring.\n\nIt is I that writes the books you find scattered about the Sunless Sanctum, but with each passing day I feel my mind wilting. Soon enough, I too will join the dark as a soldier of the Abyss. I shall write what I can before this time\ncomes, and hopefully allow others to learn of the significance of the Sunless Sanctum.\n\nRadiant is the Black Sun.", ""),
        StaticBook("The People", "Baldin Frostbeard", "Beware\nthere is enough treachery, hatred violence absurdity in the average\nhuman being to supply any given army on any given day\n\nand the best at murder are those who preach against itand the best at hate are those who preach love\nand the best at war finally are those who preach peace\nthose who preach god, need god\nthose who preach peace do not have peace\nthose who preach peace do not have love\nbeware the preachers\nbeware the knowers\nbeware those who are always reading books\nbeware those who either detest poverty\nor are proud of it\nbeware those quick to praisefor they need praise in return\nbeware those who are quick to censor\nthey are afraid of what they do not know\nbeware those who seek constant crowds for\nthey are nothing alone beware the average man the average woman\nbeware their love, their love is average\nseeks average\nbut there is genius in their hatred\nthere is enough genius in their hatred to kill you\nto kill anybody \nnot wanting solitude not understanding solitude they will attempt to destroy anything\nthat differs from their own\nnot being able to create art\nthey will not understand art\nthey will consider their failure as creators\nonly as a failure of the world not being able to love fully\nthey will believe your love incomplete\nand then they will hate you\nand their hatred will be perfect\n\nlike a shining diamond\nlike a knife\nlike a mountain\nlike a tiger\nlike hemlock\ntheir finest art", ""),
        StaticBook("The Princes Tale", "Unknown", "0nce, lonq, lvng aqo, thcre vvas a k|nq vvhc had tvvo scns. Tne clder scn vvas cnarminq of v|saqe, bvt hc hcd a b|aok hcart. Thc ycvnqer scn, hcvvevcr, vvas tc h|s brcther cs svmmcr |s tc vv|nter, |n bcth lccks anc| tcmpercment, cnd fcr th|s h|s brcther\nc|esp|scd h|m, cnd vv|shcd ncth|nq mcre thcn tc 6e r|d cf h|m. 4nd sc vvhen |t ccme tc 6e kncvvn thct thcre vvas a fecrscme drcgon cttack|ng c smcll v|llagc bv thc edqe cf thc k|ngdcm, thc elc|er brcther volvntecred thc ycunqer tc c|efeat |t. Anc| sc thc\nycvng nnan sct cff. Hc camc upcn t|ne becst vcry qvick|y, anc| sccn dcalt a deac|ly blcw tc |t w|th h|s miqhty swcrd. Thc mcnster shcck, thcn fe|| cnd wcs decd. Hcvvcver, vnbeknovv- \n            [!]\nThe rest of the book is too water-damaged to read.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Princess and", "Alexandria of Rothesay", "Once upon a time, in a kingdom far far away, there was a king and queen who lived in a golden castle with their beautiful daughter. They lived in peace and prosperity, and never knew heartbreak or want.\nYet one night, an ugly orc captured the princess and carried her away, locking her up in a tall, dark tower.\nThe king and queen were struck with immeasurable grief, and promised the princess’s hand to any knight who could rescue their daughter. So the knights in the land assembled, wanting to bring the princess back to be their bride.\nThe Orc roared in anger when he saw the approaching knights. And one by one, he tore them to shreds at the foot of the tower. The princess looked on in horror as her rescuers were slewn.\nShe shrunk back into the confines of her room, weeping as she thought of her fate. \n\nYet.. somone heard her cries, carried \nthrough the dark of \nthe night.\nThe princess was awakened by the sound of thunderous wings, flapping in the moonlit sky. A large Dragon, with obsidian scales clung to the side of the dragon, baring his large teeth at the orc.  The creature took a deep breath-\nand in a burst of great flame, he reduced the orc to a pile of ash and bones. \n\nHe then turned his attention to the princess. She sunk back in fear as to what was to come. Yet, the flame did not come for her.\nThe dragon pryed apart the bars that held her captive, lifting her gently upon his back. She clung onto his dark scales, and he spread his wings once more, lifting her up into the clouds.\nThe dragon returned the princess to the king and queen, and they were in awe at such a marvelous creature. Yet, how could they keep their promise? How could a dragon wed their daughter?\nWhen asked this, the dragon started to transform in a blinding light, until all that remained was a handsome prince in his place. \n\nThe princess looked upon her savior, and the dragon took her to be his loving wife.\nThey both lived happily ever after. \n\nThe end.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Red Assassin", "Phantom Thatch", "Want someone dead? \n\nWell boy have you picked up the right book. The Red Assassins can hook you up for a small price with a clean kill. \n\n\nYou will not find out any of our aliases, and we will never reveal your name.\nKeep this book and we will follow you until you stop, where you will be given a Book. Furthur instructions will come.\n\n\nIf you drop this book, we know you do not require our services and we wish you a good day.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Red North", "Nazorean", "Record by Nazorean on the Eigth of The Grand Harvest, 1598. \n\nI was sailing, I had just passed the snow Urugan and entered the coast of the way northern Savana, I was riding leisurely until I saw a floating red area, it seemed dead and rotting, I went to\ncome closer, and nearly road myself off the edge of the world. Peering down it, there was nothing but the pure world itself, no land, no nothing... As if who ever created these lands had given up here, or had gotten up to go do something else, not\nconnecting our lively land with his second land. So it died and the void stuck. This is a warning to any of those who dare to go way north, be weary of the waters and look down.\n\nWandering further, I discovered what seems to be a house or ancient library\nof some sort, it had book cases with books in it, though I could not read their titles or their words beyond the dust and ancient scribbles. I also see a way to cross into the red north. So it seems, that life had connected here. For beyond the snow, the\nstone, and the Savanna. What lie north was red.\n\nWhite thing - hell spawn I see, chasing me through the red north... I had stopped to look at the ground and feel it, but fire sprung upon my back and I felt it and heard its ghostly cries and shriek.\nI do not know what witchery or type of evil spawn this was, but I know it was nothing good. Hellspawn I say, it shot fire straight at me and I had to run through that terrible sand.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Redeemed", "Ithrun", "The Redeemed\n-------------------The Redeemed a Order founded by Baldin Frostbeard-Grandaxeafter talking to Wyrvun.\n\nDuring their Lords absence the order focuses on destruction of servants of Iblees\nthat curse the domains of Wyrvun. As well as spreading their beliefsaround the nations of the descendants.\n\nThe order also offers support to those nations that have accepted worship of Wyrvun into their cultire", ""),
        StaticBook("The Rekindled", "Owl", "Stronghold of the Rekindled.\n\nFor far too long our kin had neglected us, and our studies. Sister Fox is beyond their expertise and knowledge in our gifts, and she may very well save this realm from the chaos that its doomed to fall. Visions of an-\notherwordly plague claiming all life.\n\nOur gifts could save this land. Prevent this disaster. Though they won't listen.\n\nWe are now the Rekindled. No Order, no kin. We are on our own.\n\n... [!] The rest is missing; discarded.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Riders", "Balduul Exrith", "The Riders of W.M\n\nThe Riders of the Winged Mark is a group of Warhawkian warriors that focus upon the art of cavalry in fighting. The Riders are solely composed of the most fit and loyal Warhawkes in the tribe. Currently, the Riders of the Winged\nMark use steeds, bears, bokolos and turtles as their cavalry. The Riders supply themselves with their own unique armors, weapons and saddles made for combat. The dark elf breeder and blacksmith, Erolas, prepares the steeds and the iron and leather armors\nfor the horses. Curator Balduul, myself, is the one who provides a portion of the leather used for armors and saddles. Also, Erolas the blacksmith, provides all metal weapons that are commonly associated with the art of cavalry. Usually, the Warhawkes use\nthe powerful, two-legged avians, known as the bokolos. Unfortunately, after the migration to a settlement provided by the High-Elven peoples, a good portion of the bokolos have had to stay in the previous herd area in the Dreadlands.\nMarshalls Erolas and\nBalduul have organized some missions with other Warhawkes to bring back the bokolos to the current village. A recent boost in economic standards for the Warhawkes has allowed them to purchase bears, a new military power. The Riders of the Winged Mark was\nspecifically created to help spread the art of cavalry throughout the Warhawke tribe and to counter the Orenian army and their own riders. The Riders are based upon democratic values and swear to protect the Warhawkes at all cost.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Sages entry.", "Sage Ju'Mukar", "----------------------------------------\nThe diary of Mukar\n---------------------------\nFor Mukars eyes only, should non-mukar eyes lay upon this book, close your eyes and return to Mukar or may Metztlis wrath be upon you.\n========================\n=======\n- 22nd of The deep cold, 1530.\n----------------------------------------This was a strange day that Metztli provided for Mukar. For rumours spread of a sky-rock falling onto the druidic grove many years ago. But the foolish druids never informed the Fylax.\nThey hidden it from us, for this could be the event we forsaw. \n\nMukar sent Ja'Ketzawl to investigate these rumours. Though they were true the druids refused to give any detailed explanations of the event that transpired there on that moon. The Fylax will\ncontinue to investigate these events, for they could be the bringer of something gravely evil.\n\nSa'vi Metztli.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Serpent", "Anonymous", "The Great Serpent of Earth and Stone\n\nAn unquenchable thirst for earth and stone,\nIt sits down low beneath the soil,\nFar beyond the mortal’s reach,\nWide it may open its vicious maw,\nWide it may open its vicious maw,\nShaking the mountains as it moves,\nIt slithers far off and devours many,\nBeware the Vermianae, children of mine,\nFor it asks not even a name before it turns dwarven\nflesh to gore.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Shadows", "Aislin Maar", "The Shadows,\n   They Grow Dark\n\n\n       Written By\n       Aislin Maar\n          1612\n\n      \"For my love,\n        Karyssmov.\"\nThe nights were so long and so dark, and how terribly alone I was. Yet, I was not alone. No one is ever truly alone. Trailed by our shadows all our lives, yet thinking nothing of them. How mistaken we were, to think it a simple thing, cast by the light of\nday and nothing more. I could feel them creeping in, drawing ever closer as the winds howled and whipped and clawed at the fragile panes. They were coming for me, those shadows in the night. The things that go bump and jump out and get you, how terribly\nreal they were. I could see them moving out in the white snows, the moonlight giving them away in the tiny hours of the morning. Between flurries and branches they shifted, their eyes staring at me, hungry. They craved me, and I them, for they were death\nand I was life. And it was the stars which grew brighter by the night, and the shadows which grew darker. As I slipped into the late night and the early mornings, the sun came later and the moon stayed longer. The ravens called to me and through the scope\nI saw the stars which circled my world and taunted me with their mystery. And I looked, and saw, the shadows staring back. The shapes and forms and beings in the night with eyes like stars piercing the veil of the night sky, seeking to pierce only me.\nDaemons in my mind, haunting me perhaps. The nightmares of my past and the emptiness of my soul filled me with the dread of the shadows. They hungered for me, and I for them, for they were death and I was life. It wasn’t enough, though, to hunger.\nThey needed to feast, and I was ripe with sorrow, with pain, with the hurt enough to feed them all. The death of the only love I knew, the years of life without it and the loss so soon after finding it filled me with the kind of sadness that killed.\nThe ghosts of my past ate at my mind, faces and names and places filling it with bloody memories. How had I ever thought I could handle such guilt, such sorrow? I had been a fool to seek the soul that now plagued me. I could not endure on like this\nforever, and I had no choice. And so I went to meet them, into the snow and the wind and the freezing cold which to any other would bite and claw and ravage flesh to blackened death. Onto me it did none but grasp and grope, begging for me as the shadows\ndid. Only they would feast, though, for I was ready to leave this world. Though it would not be so, no, it would not end tonight. This was only the beginning. The shadows had a soul, a life, a seed from which to grow within me. They took to me like moth\nto flame, and struck me through the heart with an arrow blacker than the night. Clawing, tearing, biting at flesh with shadowy teeth and talons. Like ravens to carrion, they took to my despair. They wrapped around my soul so tightly that I felt for the\nfirst time the feeling of suffocation. Drowning in their depths, I sank further than I ever thought I could go. For what felt like centuries this went on, falling endlessly through the black mooned night, surrounded only by the pinholed stars and my\ndaemons, my haunting friends. They cooed to me, soothed my aching lungs, filled them with their inky ichor. They drowned one who could not drown, clinging to my soul and fueling from it. Growing, manifesting.\nAnd when I woke, laid out in the snows of the nameless peaks, I was not alone. It was there, it was with me. It had always been there, unseen, forgotten, ignored. No longer, though, would it be so. No longer would it be content to cling to walls and the\nfloors. I rose, and so did it. I walked, and it strode as well. Manifest, it was there, beside me: my shadow. I turned a gaze to it, and it met mine in unison. White eyes piercing jet black, like the stars on a clear night. I looked into them and saw\nmyself; my shadow was me. It was my mind, and my soul, for it had not stolen it, but instead reflected it. I was she, and she was me. I reached out for her, and she held to me, embraced me, comforted me. The pit in my chest, the pain in my heart, it eased\nitself to solace for just a moment. In that embrace, I was warm among the snows and winds. The blackness did not fade, it enveloped. I embraced death and the shadow embraced life, for we were one in the same, joined forever.\nMy shadow never leaves me. She lurks, yes, but she waits. She hides until she is needed, and I tell no one of her. They would think me tainted, they would try to kill her. She cannot be killed though, for those who cast light only cause the shadow to\ngrow. She reaches where I cannot. She lends me her power, and I fuel hers. I give my life to her, and to me she gives the power of death.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Shreckening", "Unknown", "Once upon a time there was a sprawling dwarven slum ran by Hogarth Irongut! Though something drab lingered in the air, fear. For this slum fringed upon a glorious swamp, Shreck's Swamp! And you damn know it this bid an ill fate for all the filthy peasants\nwho dwelled there. That is why Hogarth constructed a mighty dwarven wall to keep out Shreck, emporer of swamps. Fortunately though, Shreck is stronk and with a mighty uruk roar he slapped it rather lightly and let out a swampy chuckle as it\ntoppled over!\nWith little effort he slaughtered all of them, turning their beards into warm socks. He slaughtered all but Hogarth though, let's just say he kept him around his swamp for a happy ending when he got bored of his donkey.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Simple Poppy", "Illidar", "=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\n\n   The Lowly Poppy\n           By:\n         Illidar\n\n\n\n\n\n\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\nWhile it is common knowledge that many plants have uses in the field of medicine, it is often the case that many plants with high potential go overlooked. This is the case of the source of one of the most powerful depressant drugs in existance, the poppy.\nThe poppy plant before blooming is made up of a stem and a bulb. Before the bulb opens, a one to two millimeter deep laceration to the pod should be made for the poppy's \"milk\" to seep from the pod. Generally speaking a single pod can have up to sixteen\nof these lacerations. After leaving the cuts for about one day, the milk will have bled enough to be scraped off with a flat tool, this can be done two to three times before the bulb dies. After collecting between three to five grams of this sap, mix it\ninto warm water until it is dissolved. After this, pour it into a shallow pan and place it in the sun to dry, then scrape the residue from the pan and press it back into shape. This will leave you with about 40% of the mass of what you started with. This\nproduct can be smoked, and is one of the most powerful depressant drugs currently in existence. The lesson to be learned is to leave no stone unturned in your experimentation with herbs, as this advance was only thanks to one person's (That would be me)\nfailure to overlook even innocuous seeming specimens in one's research.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Sky Madness", "Nari Colaer", "-------------------The Day The Sky Gods Got Mad\n___________________\nBy Nari Colaer!\nOne day the sky got stormy and sad,\nTwas the day that those sky gods got mad!\nThe Gods of the Sky came to earth,\nTo wreck havoc and destruction!\nThey called up a magic\nThat animated a statue, So tragic,\nThe Statue of the dragon flew around,\nDestroying Puny humans running around,\nThe sky gods were not done yet you see! \nthey called down some unknown technology!\nIt blew up the houses and carved chunks in the land!\nThe world burned in death and dispair,\nHowever suddenly the gods retreated,\nNo one know what happened or how they got beaten!\nThe earth started to magically repair the damage!\nSoon it was all fixed and the people soon started to forget!\nThe events that happened that fateful day!\nWill forever be commerated in this poem I say!", ""),
        StaticBook("The Sorrow", "The Inquisitor", "The breastplate of another champion. His exact 'placing' in the Glade's timeline is unknown, but it's obvious that he cared about the place deeply. While not being a religious man by any-means, he had his morals.\nHe entered The Glade with a group of soldiers, although he was the only one to stay. He found peace within the Glade, and quietly becme it's guardian under the watchful eye of Aureus.\nThe sorrow he feels comes from having to kill the very fellow soldiers he entered the Glade with, in order to protect it.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Spear", "The Forgotten Scribe", "\"Brev was the first man ever to strike down an Aengul, and when it’s patron of Age screamed from the heavens, ‘what have you done’, Brev could not hide his discrepancy, for the proof of the Aengul of Youth’s death blazed bright from the height of the\nsky.”\n~-~\nThe legend of Godslayer Brev is one not often noticed amongst the archives of the Temple Monks, whom covet the knowledge of the known planes upon their sandstone shelves. It is a tale of regret, of fury\nand sadness, and within it’s weathered text lies a lesson for both man and goldblooded -- to never pass the boundaries that the Creator set for them.\nBut the legend it not mere falsehoods; it is truth, bound upon layers and\nleather and scribed from men of ancient origin; from the time when holy fire raged in the sky, and from the time the same fire scorched Krug’s pure kin to the bone. The time of such event dates back even before the known times of Iblees’\nwarmongering, when the four races established themselves in their four corners uncorrupted but sparse. They prospered and they settled brief peace; it was a time known not for wars, but for curiosity and expansion, and\nknowing that their four fathers already took claim to the whole of the Aegisian plane, they sought what was beyond it -- what they could reach, but could not grasp. The sky.\nTheir attempts at claiming the heavens often fell to dust; enacted by\nover-ambitious humans and haughty Elves with towers that either did not reach high enough or simply toppled because of their reach. Ironically, it was not the mortals that reached the immortals first, but the otherway around; for the\nraces held no means of reaching their godly masters whereas the masters could reach them -- and reach them they did, in those old times, when all were naive and thought nothing of conceit and budding violence.\nAll mortal men were jealous of the\nbirds of the sky, whom could sail the wind and reach the borders of the heavens with but draws of their wings, and the shadow these creatures cast were like salt upon the wounds that were carved into the early history of red-blooded\nfailures. Shadows were a sign of irritation, and the sun’s rays were favored over the darkness of physical mass-- thus, understandable emotions derived from these mocking shadows. Human men spat upon the shade of flighted\ncreatures, Elves scoffed at them and Dwarves grumbled and retreated into their mines, seeking comfort amongst earth’s treasures. The Old Orcs, smooth of skin and monstrous naught, however, saw the shadows of winged beasts as\nchallenges and insults, and sought to snuff them from the sky in which they were projected. One such example would be of the Legend of Brev, whom mistook an Aengul for a bird in the face of the glaring sun.\nWandering the planes of Krug’s\nbirthplace, the descendant Brev, who was famed for his great strength and fortitude, was in the process of a grand hunt with the intent to return to Krug’s children with enough game to feed them all for weeks -- a feat that would surely be remembered\neven when worn from the passage of time. However, prey was sparse, and Brev’s effort in the chase was languish in the face of demanded speed. What he had caught was drawn from his impressive ability to throw spears of iron that cut through the\nair like a giant’s arrows.\nThe sun’s smile was bright and it’s rays were harsh on this day of the hunt, and it was only into the late afternoon that the towering, tan-skinned son of Krug found himself at a loss; unwilling to trek further into the\nexpanse of his homeland in search of prey that refused to challenge him. But lo’ and behold -- a great shadow was cast upon the earth from a creature of mighty size, far larger than a bird, that circled Brev upon the waves of the sky. Staggered by\nhis findings, Brev drew his eyes to the sky -- and beheld but silhouette of an assumed bird of great size alone; unable to make shape of it’s features on behalf of the sun’s blinding light. Knowing his spears were not enough to fell this creature, Brev\nsought a nearby mountainous range, and from the side of the mountain he grafted a massive spear of sturdy stone; unable to be hefted by none but himself and his kin in the manner which he planned for it.\nSo he returned to the circling\ncreature, which was unbeknownst to his plots, and with squinting aim and the tense of muscles, he flung the great spear forth -- into the sky and into the heavens which the beast lingered; an arrow, a lightning bolt of earth that shot from the\nground instead of the clouds, and in a spectacle and show of godly skill, the spear impaled the creature; but it did not draw blood.\nCuriousity was a scourge to those of heavenly blood -- it was a sign of degeneracy and ignorance, for all\nAenguls and Daemons knew most of the inner-workings of the world thus far - with the exception of their own experiences - and the trivialities of exploration and - Creator forbid it - the interaction of the mortal and the immortal. But some\ndisregarded this ideal of isolation and sought to bless the four races with their presence. One such individual was the unnamed Aengul of Youth, whom favored sailing the vast skies of Aegis, much to his patron’s displeasure and concern -- the Aengul of\nAge, whose name is also unknown.\nThe Aengul of Youth was naive and sought to explore all there was to see, and his journey led him to Krug’s birthplace, whence Brev roamed in feverous hunt. But his search for glorious knowledge led to Brev’s\ninescapable fury; a decimation carved from the very earth. Flighted in the sky with wings not unlike a hawk’s the Aengul of Youth bathed in the gross incandescence of sunlight-- blind to the one that mistakenly targeted him. In one fatal\nswoop, however, the Aengul’s heavenly being was collided against and impaled with Brev’s Stone Spear; and the event of the Aengul’s violent death was so great, that gold blood was not drawn, but fire -- the spear scorched by golden flame, plummeting\ndownward, as the very sky ignited in destructive reaction to the Aengul of Youth’s cataclysmic demise.\nThe seven heavens felt this death, this disparity -- and it’s Aengul of Age, who fathered the Aengul of Youth since it’s creation, cried\nout in horror; he cried out and his voice was so furious and abask in agony that it cracked through the sky and shook it’s very foundations -- “What have you done?!”\nAnd Brev, who stood awed and horrified by his own mistake, his worst sin, could\nnot move from the place that he threw the spear which lingered steps from him, buried point-first in the sand - he could not close his eyes despite the bright volumes of the plummeting golden fire. Without even the notion to raise his\narms to protect himself from the charging storm, Brev the Strong was engulfed in the fire of heavenly demise; roasted to the bone and decimated by it’s otherworldly power almost immediately.\nThe Monks of the Old Cloud Temple were the first to take\nnotice to this tragedy, and with hurried pace they sought the scene now riddled with ash and golden fire that still cracked and burned upon the ground; the black scorch-marks focused upon the still-standing skeleton of Brev and his spear - coined\nthe Stone Transgression - to form a most unusual display. The kin of God expressed his horror and his dejection from the skies, and thus, these old Monks sought to honor him by damning Brev’s soul to a limbo, and his spear to a grave.\nSealing his soul to a single large rib, Brev’s skeleton was buried with his godslaying spear within the depths of Krug’s homeland with his soul, trapped within the severed, surprisingly heavy bone locked within a jailed chamber of steel and earth;\ndamning Brev’s soul to a fate of ungained peace, trapped in a limbo and locked within but a peace of his own scorched structure.\n~-~", ""),
        StaticBook("The Spirit of Ma", "Mysterious Oldman", "*Strange Runes seem to Dot the\nFirst section of this page*\n\nFrom death, life.\n\nFrom dDarkness Light. \nWhen all seems hopeless.\n\nand the realm stands on the brink of destruction.\n\nOne final sacrifice shall be made. \nFor the good of the realm.\n\"An excerpt of the Tome of Blundermore. The Second Wizard Of Aegis\". \n\nMagic, according to the mages is merely a tool to be used to further one's own goals and drives. There are no true moral or immoral implications of magic. Only Magic itself.\nThis is not truly the case. For we know that magic does indeed have a light and dark side, however small or large it may be. \n\nMagic is driven by impulse and imagination. By the will and tenacity of the user but it is not the will of Mages alone whom-\ndefine what magic is alone. No, for the world itself is indeed magic. Everything and everyone within it is a magical entity of some description from the most insignificant to the mighty. \n\nI subscribe to the idea that magic is a force that connects all.\nIt is emotion, it is sanity, it is insanity, it's spirituality, it's the notion of thought and imagination and perhaps life itself. \n\nTo call it a mere tool is to insult its true nature. And to pervert it with such notions that you truly understand and\ncontrol it to its fullest extent is merely being foolish. Magic is a force to be respected and revered, not as a power or force of destruction. But as a companion almost. It is with you where ever you truly go. And should be treated with respect.\nA means perhaps of attaining a greater enlightenment of the world that exists around you.\n\nIt is the will of evil men that twists magic towards evil ends. But unfortunately for all of their lust and drive for power they will forget that the secrets of\nmagic will never truly be revealed to them through such disrespect. \n\nI've seen the extent magic can provide, and it reaches far beyond our petty notions of power.\n\nWe must- adfafmkfa\n*The page seems to end with magical symbols once more, their meaning unknown before a large tear.*", ""),
        StaticBook("The Spirit Realm", "Shel'Yar", "The Spirit Realm, spoken as Frum’Stroh by Shamans, was created by the Daemon Apohet. Within the realm are three planes. The Ancestral Plane, the Elemental Plane, and the Immortal Plane. The Three planes in order of creation go EIA. Elemental, Immortal,\nthen Ancestral.\n\nThe First Plane is the Elemental plane, spoken as Voga’Stroh. It was created by Apohet to suit himself.  The Realm itself is difficult if not impossible for Shamans to map out. This is due to the fact that elementals are able to mold the\nrealm to their liking. Meaning that they can live anywhere, within any structure.\n\nThe next plane being the Immortal Plane, was created whenever powerful elementals requested a plane of their own. The Immortal Plane is at constant war bewteen the\nimmortals. This is mostly because each immortal represents an aspect of culture, emotion, and society. The Shamans said it is no place for rest, and is always difficult to carve a path through. It usually takes multiple Shamans working together.\nThe Ancestral Plane, spoken Stargush’Stroh by the Shamans. The Ancestral Plane is a resting place for the most powerful and honorable Uruks. Shamans say that the Ancestral Plan is heavily based on the mortal world. More experienced Shamans explained that\nwhen visiting, the sound is very much like a quiet constant noise. However, as you grow more experience as a Shaman, you can extrapolate from the noise to filter perceptions of senses. Thus allowing the Shaman to hear and see.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Suicide Peom", "Carver Le Prevost", "The poem of Rose.\nIn honor of Rose Divine, my dead lover.\nThe sky is blue.\nMy life is sad.\nWe used to be true.\nBut now the thought of you gets me mad.\n\nMy life needs meaning.\nBut I find none without you.\nThe thought of us is demeening.\nI need this us I need you.\nWhy is it that I am so sad?\nIs it the thoughts of us that get me mad?\nOr is it because it is over. \nI shall never find someone who will wove her.\nway into my heart?\nI need a goal.\nI need the sea. \nI need a boat.\nI need to dr\nLife for you might be over love. \nBut for me it is just the begining. \nSoon I will sail for your name.\nEach breath I take is for you.\nEach breath I take is you.\nEach breath I take.\nEach breath.\nI am done.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Sulierdionne", "Vellulaei'thill Vul'athri", "The Sulierdionne\n   by Vellulaei'thill\n             Vul'athri\nPreface\n\nDiseases and sickness are a part of our world, it is an undeniable truth. While they certainly have no place in the blessed city of the Mali’Aheral, these pests are rampant in inferior race society.\nMany are affected by them and countless inferiors die every year.\n\nOf course, at this point the reader might wonder why we must take an interest in such things. As the reader is most certainly pure and of a respectable\nbloodline I do not doubt that they will quickly understand. The reason of course is to weaponize these diseases, to use them against our enemies and weaken them before they are even able to strike.\n\nHowever, it is at this moment that we\nrun into a severely incapacitating obstacle. The inability to truly study these disease further than their symptoms. While the Mali'Aheral have analyzed many of these sicknesses and studied their effects, we know little of their true composition,\nwhat they look like and how they react to different stimuli.\n\nHowever, I believe this will change soon. For an idea struck me in the night while I stood at my window gazing at the stars. So far away, so distant. Yet that does not stop us from\nstudying them with  telescopes, as the inferiors label this tool. What is stopping us, the most intelligent race upon the continent, from studying the infinitely small?\nTo that I respond only this; Absolutely nothing.\nThe Creation Process\n\nLest this book fall into the filthy hands of an impure or otherwise inferior creature, I shall remain vague. This tool will be a most important one in the technological and scientific advances of our race and must be kept within\nour walls, secure and hidden.\n\nThe Sulierdionne was created through a trial and error process as well as the analysis of a telescope. §\nOnce I had acquired one of these, much time was spent expirementing with the lenses, attempting to change the inflection  of these to achieve a more precise magnification.\n\nIt was a time taking enteprise, but I finally suceeded.\nThe proper lenses were created and the experimentation began.\nModel Oem:\n\nBasic telescope aiming downards upon a small piece of bark. Magnification was blurry with few details. While inspecting the element I could see very little, only a large brown blurr.\nI concluded that I needed a more precise magnification and the lenses required greater inflection. There was little difference between the backdrop and the element as well. Further thought was necessary.\nModel Nuit:\n\nInflexion of the lenses changed, image sharper yet I was still unable to distinguish the element from the backdrop. Even when replacing the basic grey piece of stone by white quartz.\nModel Hael:\n\nFound a solution to distinguish the backdrop from the element. A small redstone powered lamp now lies beneath the glass backdrop. Testing however, proved that it put unwanted strain on the eye\nand that damage to the ocular globe was a possibility. However, I was able to distinguish the object with clarity. To truly analyze the structure, I believe it is necessary to use very thing slices of material, so the light may shine through.\nModel Vailu:\n\nMain objective of this model was to reduce the blinding effect of the light. Minor experiments were led before the final model. A solution was discovered, quite simple in reality.\nThe lamp was moved away, no more is it directly beneath the backdrop. Instead, a small angled mirror reflects it upwards through grey tinted glass. This protective measure reduces the lamps effects and allows the researcher to use the Sullierdionne\nfor extended periods of time with minor eyestrain.\nModel Kulin:\n\nBy this time, I believed that I had almost reached the perfect model. This was not far from the truth. \nHowever, the magnification was still rather deplorable. In a fit of most shameful frustration I decided to simply\npile lenses up and see if that increased the effectiveness. Much to my surprise, it did. Yet too many close together seems to lower the quality of the magnification, blurring it.\nModel Banih:\n\nTo facilitate work and include as many lenses as possible, I have angled the first set. Following this grouping is an angled mirror with the second stack of lenses right after. With this, I was able to study a thin slice of pork in detai\nI believe that this will be a most excellent tool for the Mali'Aheral!\n\nI shall conclude by saying this; with the proper amount of time spent studying a disease, I believe we will be able to truly understand them. Perhaps one\nday we shall change them to a desired form. These goals are far away and surely there will be many years between their accomplishement and now. But time has little meaning for those who live lives as long as ours.\nI will live to see this next step forward, perhaps I shall be remembered as the precursor.\n\nVellulaei'thill Vul'athri\n\nMaehr'sae Hiylun'ehya, Mali'aheral.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Tales Test", "Walter Frankfert", "Hello, this is the story of a man. This man is no diplomat he is a psychopath. A man that has killed and tasted blood and destroyed bodies past the point of recognition. He is not a simple man by any means actually this is one of the most complicated man\ni have ever met. Yes i have met him in fact i survived him not without a few wounds and Scars. My name is Rick and i’m a bard a traveling bard at that and for what it's worth i’m pretty damn good at it. I got lured into his trap from the beginning he\nhe booked me for a party at his house you know the usual job. But, when i got there it didn’t look like any party i've ever seen unless you count a party as being one man with meat platters and fruit punch. So walked up to the man and he explained that\nhe was just too embarrassed  to ask me for a personal show (which i was ok with parties are 100 mina while personal shows are 50 mina). So i started to play some songs on my lute on my 5th song he told me to stop and eat some food and have some fruit\npunch i wasn't going to argue who can deny, Free Food! But, as i know now the meat platter was not beef, chicken, or lamb it was human and the fruit punch probably had some fruit  in it but the main ingredient was blood and judging by the human meat it\nwas probably human blood as well. So the next part is where i got super scared and also knew my suspicious were correct. I asked him if he had a bathroom he said yes it was inside and to the right. So i went inside there was this really weird smell in his\nwhole house it smacked you right nose as soon as you walked in. i went right and went to the bathroom that's when i noticed the lock was on the outside of the door but dummy me didn't think anything of it because you know when you gotta go you gotta go.\nAlmost as soon as i started going to the bathroom i heard a noise that i knew couldn't be anything other then the lock on the door. So i was kinda like he might just be a jokester and the other half of me knew that i am going to die and not quick either.\nI jiggled the doorknob i yelled but there was no response. I yelled again nothing. I did this for what felt like forever until i passed out of exhaustion. I woke up and jumped up and looked around remembering the situation i was in. So i walked over to\nthe doorknob and jiggled it but this time it opened i was alittle skeptical at first but then i thought now is my chance to escape so i ran right to the front door put my hand on the doorknob and then i heard a “Woosh” noise then a snap. It was a bear\ntrap right on my right ankle i screamed then i heard some footsteps and then he stuck me with a hot cow brander right on my back i screamed in pain even louder then he hit me on the back of my head head with the end of the cow brander and knocked me out.\nWhen i woke up i was hanging upside down in his kitchen with his weapon rack behind me and assorted surgery tools on the counter across from me and above that a window. From the window i could tell it was night time. He was over at the table to the left\nof me and he said “ You're one tall man aren’t ya” i didn’t respond. Then, he said “Fine, no talk, no food” and yawned and went to go to sleep but not before kicking me a good night sleep i mean that as a joke because he thought he just knocked me out\nwith that kick but no it stunned me for a little but other then that it helped me. See it gave me momentum to start cutting away at the weak ties he put around my wrists see he may have adjusted the feet hanger thing to fit my height but he forgot i had\nlong arms as well i could reach his weapons with the momentum i had. So not to long later i cut my hands loose and then grabbed the weapon and cut my one foot loose. But, i didn't think about what to do next because i cut my last tied foot loose when i\nand made a loud crashing noise. But, i popped back up and hobbled out the back door. See my leg hurt but it seem as though he was healing it i guess he didn't want to eat infected meat but i could still walk at a pretty brisk pace i walked till i found a\npath then i headed to the nearest town and seeked medical help now i tell this story and i even wrote a song about it.\n\n______THE END_______", ""),
        StaticBook("The Three Poems", "Fabien Eloy de Bosco", "The Women in the Shop\n\n There once was a women\nA women in a shop\nShe smelled of a lemon\nShe sat on the rooftop\nHer hair flowing\nStaring down the coast\nRelaxed and outgoing\nnext to a lamppost.\nThe Man in the Manor\n\nThere was a man\nHe lived in a manor\nAll alone he ran\nTo the Felsen Banner\nHe met a girl named, Theran\nHe spoke with much manner\nDidn't know how to stand\n'Cause he was nervous and tanner.\nThe lonely Farm\n\nThere was a Farm in Norland\nThere it sat, out-of-hand\nToo far away from everyone\nLaying there out in the sun\nThe farm had much crop\nAll sent into one shop\nA farmer once came\nAnd the farm gained fame.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Tortured", "Sam", "Case name: The Confession!\n\nSuspect(s): Falkenrath family\n\nCrime: Torture, fraud\n\nCase details: Philip Footman found a confession note in the evicted shop of the Courland Company, the note\nspeaks of a confession from a man who said a Falkenrath man forced and tortured him to spread rumors and lies of Count Roswell to his eventual arrest. He was also told to speak on behalf of Roswells to Dunamis. After inspector Gilbert and Sam went to\nIstria and talked to the son, it was concluded that this case took place years back, and the conflict between the two families allegedly solved.\n\n C A S E   C L O S E D\n\n-Inspector Samuel de Saltpans", ""),
        StaticBook("The Traitor", "Isa", "9th of The Snow’s Maiden, 1610\nThe main hall of Grimhaven filled as the Plebeians and Sariants took their positions before OrdenMarschall Tarkus and their Hochmiester, Sergei Vladov.\nTarkus began to inform the order about the most recent events. \nA couple of nights ago the Newest Plebeian to the order was making his way back from the mines. As he walked, he ran into three men, two of which were citizens of the town.\ns Magni asked what the three were up to, they attacked him by the means of magic. The Sariant Knight William was the first to approach the group of ‘spooks’ and attempted diplomacy even when the three men had weapons drawn\nand had severely injured the Plebeian. \nTarkus went on to know that he had allowed this “terrible attempt to play”. He watched the three criminals continue to make movements and stall for time as they exchanged vials of liquid.\nImmediately after they dove into the water and split up deep in the bottom of the ocean.\nTarkus and WIlliam unable to capture the men, took the two citizens by the names of Marion and Evander to the keep for questioning.\nTarkus had questioned Marion about her knowledge of the men and she replied with a simple “no.” Tarkus has believed her words to be false due to the information of Kae and Marion being in some sort of relationship.\nCamille Vladov, the daughter of Sergei, spoke out from being Tarkus. She claimed Marion to be a whore. As well as Sariant Knight Volten, confirming that Marion and Kae were in fact in a relationship.\nFrom the line, Dax inquired if Marion had three different relations.\nThe Orden Marschall Tarkus called for Dax and Volten to step forward. Again from behind, Camille ridiculed the woman, calling her a “harlot”.\nIn Camille’s defense, Sariant Knight Leofric stated “Either she’s a wedded woman or a whore, the lady has a point”. Directly after, Tarkus lifted a hand to quiet the Sariant Knight.  He continued on to address Dax\nand Volten about them speaking out of turn. He punished them with physical exercise. \nTarkus then began to proceed with his report. He went on to say how both Evander and Marion confessed that Kae leads an undead troop and has actively fought in Bastio\nTarkus finds this to be an alias for Marion seems to be in love with a “tainted being”. Marion is now being held in the keep and is not allowed to leave. He ordered that a Sariant guard the woman at all times.\nBase of the information given by their new Plebeian, Evander will return. Tarkus ordered the Sariants to report to him if Kae comes to this keep.\nFrom the line of men, Augustus Reinhardt Von Schlichten shouts\n“Huzzah, Death by my shiny saber,” in response to Tarkus. Surprised, he continued to say that the order will purge Kae from the realm entirely. Some of the members praised Tarkus, in agreement with his orders.\n“You should burn him alive,” Camille calls out from behind. \n“We should probably interrogate him with some mort erotica,” said Dax.\nUnimpressed, Tarkus told the two to silence their ridiculous ideals.\nHe instructed the order to have patrols done along the coast in teams of three or four. The groups shall report the findings to himself or the Hochmeister. He went on to instruct them on how to deal with a ‘spook’ with haste and efficiency.\nTarkus then hands the floor over to the Hochmeister as he proceed to sit down.\nAs the Hochmiester came forth, the room grew very serious as the men straightened their posture.\n“You heard OrdenMarschall Tarkus, there was traitors in our midst.” he stressed. \n“Such man held the Order to no high standard such as you all do. He thinks he can leave without answering for his crimes against our men. \"\n\"Defiling our Sariant Code and as well as our Sariant Creed altogether in one day. Sariants are we going to let this man take us for fools, or are we going to do something about it?”he asked, with a hardened gaze.\nThe men shouted out responses of assurance towards the Hochmiester. The seemed moved by the Sergei’s words. Some shouted out “Purge the corrupt!” Others shouted Beliae doe Orden! Death to the Traitors”\nThe Hochmiester continued on to instruct Volten, Maxim Vladov, and Dax to head to the nation of Courland to hang posters and offer a bounty for this traitorous man. He then went on to order that Sariant Crowley,\nDauros and Leofric head to the nation of Mardon to search for the man to see if the man still resides within the kingdom. \nLastly, he told Grand Sariant Titania to lead the remaining men to search the house of Lady Alwain.\nWith that he ended the meeting with an “Oorah!”.\n\n\nAuthor: Isa", ""),
        StaticBook("The Tree", "Henry Winterleaf", "The Tree\n--------\n\nA children's book by Henry Winterleaf.\nMany years ago, there was a little acorn. The acorn was so tired with being small.\n\"I want to be tall!\" the acorn would say.\n\"Everyone else looks so big!\" he would moan. He would always moan until one day, a large oak tree said to him:\n\"Just sit still for a bit and have a bit of patience.\"\nAnd so, the acorn waited. Never moving.\nNever moaning. He just sat there, waiting for this magical growth that was promised to him. Days passed and the acorn still didn't feel any taller.\n\"I'm just a small as before!\" Moaned the acorn.\n\"Oh, really?\" said the oak tree, smiling.\n\"Yes! I'm just the same!\" proclaimed the acorn once more.\n\"Perhaps you should wait longer then.\" \nAnd so he did. Waiting once more.\nA couple days later, the acorn awoke in his usual spot. \n\"Huh? What's this?\" asked the acorn.\n\"I feel different.\"\n\"An acorn does not grow into a tree over-night, child.\" said the oak tree, chuckling.\n\"But with enough patience, you will\ngrow to an incredible size. Good things come to those who wait. Just be patience.\"\nThe acorn was more determined than ever.\n\"I can be patient! I'm going to be the tallest!\"\nAnd so he waited some more. Days, months, even years passed and\nsoon the acorn had grown into a large oak tree, towering over many others. One day he would hear a sapling below him complaining:\n\"I wish I was as tall as you!\"\nThe little acorn, who was not so little any more, just smiled and said\n\"Be patient. That is all you can do.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("The Trib. of War", "Andria Ith'ael", "The Tribulation of War\n\n      Authored by\n     Andria Ith'ael\n\n      Dedicated to\n      Luna Ith'ael\n  Who did not live to\n  see the end of this\n       tribulation.\nPrologue\n This account tells the tale of the two major events which occurred within the time of author’s service as the Maheral of the Mali’aheral. Such events were known as the following: the securing of the Aldersberg Refuge and the Oren\nCivil War which granted independence to Renatus (and Aesterwald.) It is not just for the sake of recording that the author writes such, as it is hoped that this account will prevent further incidents from occurring again.\nChapter I\n  The betrayal of the Mali’aheral by the Mali’ame, more specifically: Phaedrus and Elrona Lle’hileia, was the final event of the steadily growing discontent of the lesser Elves in Annil’sul. All but one of the nations in the world\nsupported Phaedrus Lle'hielia - the rebelion leader. \n\n  It was on the mountains aside of the town of Aldersberg where a meeting that conceived the plans for shelter in such a dreadful time took place. It consisted of approximately five\nMali'aheral - alongside a Valah by the name of Ser Gawain Briarwood. One Mali’aheral by the name of Thurdan Orathon, who had served previously as Okarir’tir, and his persistence in such was both amusing and counter-productive. \n\n  In the next Elven\nday, I found myself alongside the same Mali'aheral in the court of Emperor Tuvya Carrion. Knowing of Thurdan’s plans, I tried to convince him via a polite and quiet conversation hat we should ask for shelter in these dark days. My offer was refused quite\nobstinately by the former Okarir'tir, who foolishly went ahead and asked the Emperor regarding his own plan. \n Alas, Thurdan’s efforts were in vain; the Emperor rejected his offer, citing prior crimes against House Carrion by the Mali’aheral,\nwhich essentially was the Mali’aheral support for the Chivay take over in the Fringe. Disappointed, Thurdan stormed from the palace without another word, which was a rather a rude gesture.\n Due to this, I stepped forward, and proceeded to ask for what I\nbelieved was ayla for the Mali'aheral: a refuge. The response I received was much better than those earlier, and the Emperor Tuvya offered us shelter in Petrus and the option to ask Duke Olivier de Savoie of the town of Aldersberg. However, I do not\nrecall if such an offer was made by the town of Karovia. \n It was a half or day or so walk from Petrus to Aldersberg, and there I met with Delonna Aeléyèlsa. He directed me to the Duke Olivier de Savoie and the three of us proceeded to have a meeting in\nthe Aldersberg Library. There I offered assistance in war (I had previously said that I would die for Oren in war if it meant my people were well) and many crafts and labours. In exchange I asked for a citadel. In response, I received a chuckle as he saw\nmy desperation and proclaimed that those terms were acceptable.\n Foolishly I told him we would not live within Aldersberg and said we would remain on his land, to which he questioned my knowledge of the feudal system, however this comment had no lasting\neffects and work soon began once more. The Citadel was soon constructed at a pace not seen before.  For my efforts, Delonna Aeléyèlsa bestowed the title of Maheral upon me. Despite our kind’s new found peace, one event would linger in my mind for many\nyears to come. My spouse, Janos Ith’ael soon arrived in Aldersberg and came to speak with me. He displayed his intentions to join the Marked Men, to which I refused on the grounds of him already having a child and a wife. Reluctantly he agreed and I soon\ntold him to ask the leaders of the Marked Men about it. However I heard no word from Janos again until long after the events of this book, I had almost thought he died up until very recently.\nChapter II\n In the year of 1480, my daughter, Luna Ith’ael went to live a few miles walk from Aldersberg in the fortress of Kaer Angren with a family friend of mine, Kalameet Izalith. The fortress was used by the Order of the Red Dragon,\nand before them, the Order of the Flaming Rose. I had overheard her talking with one by the name of Martial Solatius about the book of Creation and when I arrived in the fortress, I spoke to her regarding such. I warned her of the dangers of believing in\na deity and how it prevents enlightenment. She protested though soon listened to my guidance. I did not speak with Martial regarding such (though I did with Kalameet) as he gave me a tour of the fortress.\nI also gave him advice on leadership, and he told me about how Great Ser Maric Varodyr (the commander of the Order) would later receive what he deserved. I took little note of such a hint. \n Alas, it all soon became clear within the next month as the\nOrder of the Red Dragon soon declared itself independent of the Carrion dominated Holy Oren Empire. It became my objective to try and remove my daughter from the fortress as Aldersberg took no side in the conflict. My efforts proved useless as I came\nacross the broken bridge which lead to the gate of Kaer Angren.\n\n    Chapter III\n As the nations were choosing their sides; it soon became known that I would have to choose one as well. The State of Laureh'lin changed sides thrice\nthroughout the war, though as I went to a meeting with the now King Maric Varodyr, they were with Renatus and Kaer Angren. Delonna Aeléyèlsa accompanied myself, for he was more literate in ways of Valah politics.\n The meeting was a sucess and the two\nof us pledged to support him; an exception remained with the bringing of soldiers, we did not do such due to the neutrality of Aldersberg.\n King Maric also promised to sign another concordat, however with a different name, for\nthe Crimson-Silver Concordat has long passed.\n Raids and skirmishes soon were fought outside Kaer Angren, and I was caught in at least one. I remember seeing one of my own kind, named Braxus Ni’leya fight with the Carrions; I was rather disappointed in\nand proceeded to speak with the Tilruir’tir, Asul’athri Parir’taliyu regarding such. From then on the war seemed to be closer to home.\n  House Carrion and its supporters then moved forth from Petrus to try and take Kaer Angren by force. As the day of the\nbattle approached, I was steadfast that none of my kin would fight in such a battle. This was to the dismay of two of my kind: Kalameet Izalith, who worked closely with Maric and Martial during the war, and Braxus Ne’leya, who asked for soldiers to\nreinforce the House Carrion supporters. I also told my daughter to not remain in the fortress, and return to the Citadel.\n  Braxus then told me that House Carrion wished to speak with me and I agreed to come to such. I left a note in my inn room which\nstated that if I did not return from such an endeavour, I had been executed by the Carrions and the Sillumir were to fight with Renatus and their allies. Hence forth I made the trek to Petrus, and met with Braxus and Viktor Carrion. The lattter guided me\ninto the palace in Petrus, where the two of us held a meeting.\n  Viktor tried to convince me that the Carrions had done ayla by my people, and to such I agreed. Though I adamantly said that I would remain neutral - which deceived them of my true plans.\nThe one clad in Carbarum and Iron armour was also steadfast that Olivier de Savoie had supported the Carrion regime, which was rather untrue.\nChapter IV\n The battle ended with a victory for King Maric and it soon resulted in the collapse of the the Holy Oren Empire. No Sillumrian fought in the battle from my memory,  though in hindsight, such would have been better to have supported\nRenatus. However an opportunity to make a formal alliance with the new born nation was soon permitted after a lengthy discussion between Olivier de Savoie, Kalameet Izalith, Kalenz Uradir and myself. \n   Coincidently, Gawain Briarwood (whose alias was\nMartial Solatius) soon arrived at the gate of the Citadel asking if we wished to ally with them. Without hesitation I agreed, though no Concordat was signed. I consider such to be my greatest decision in my service as Maheral.\n Months later, after peace\nhad once again befallen the lands of a now divided Oren, I made another trek to the fortress of Kaer Angren with one by the name of Avern’dionne Adriane. The beginnings of the conquest of Laureh’lin soon approached. The tribulation of the Mali'aheral was\ndestined to end soon.\n\n     Chapter V\n It is known that a story has no merit without a moral; however, there is not one of such in this story, for there is multiple concepts presented in it.  It can simply be described as the following: the one\nwho takes initiative is the one who succeeds; progress and health can also involve sacrificing one’s plans for the betterment of our kind; and two societies cannot exist with one ruling the other, they must be equal or integrated - both of which are\nimpossible. \n If one remembers such, then they will be able to prosper in an age of constant war unlike any other. The world is far more turbulent, and alliances change fast. No treaty stands forever and our kind must be weary of such for only two peoples\nhave kept their treaties like tradition: the Heartlander Valah and the Kharajyr. At any moment, another tribulation may begin and our kind must be weary.\n\naymaehr'sae hiylun'ehya\n~Andria Ith'ael", ""),
        StaticBook("The URUK experim", "Baldin Grandaxe", "Can we save Uruks from their evil ways?\nI have asked myself that question many times. Despite the fact that my son was killed by their kind, I can only feel sorry for them. They did not choose the path of darkness it was choosen for them.\nNot too long ago I thougth of an experiment. If I was able to collect an Uruk baby and teach it on the ways of our people, would that Uruk become evil with time? or will we create a new breed. A breed that is kind and benebolent.\nThis is why I ask for a team of experts in certain fields for this experiment.\n\nNeeded:\nA Chemist\nA Motherly figure\nA Hunter\n\nIf you are interested or know some one that would please aply.\nAn aplication box is placed next to my home in the Grandaxe residences.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Void", "Laureh'thill", "The Void\n\nBy Kalameet Izalith\n\n-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-\n-The Void: Arcane magic is the archetype or magic which is fueled by the Void, or more specifically mana. The void is an empty plane of existence where things may be created with the use of ones\nimagination and willpower. Many teachers of the Arcane often teach students with the following proverb: \"The Void is nothing, yet everything. Like our imagination, it may be dull and empty; or it can be full and colorful.\". The Void as a whole is simply a\nplane where nothing exists, unless the mage makes it exist.\n\n-The Anchor and Connection: Before you can make anything in the Void, you must first connect to it. This obviously means a basic line of communication must be established, generally gained\nthrough meditation and practice. This connection reaches into the Void and through this connection, you manipulate the Void in a very specific way. This manipulation is when you imagine something in the Void. For example, one may create/imagine a fireball\nin the Void, you'd then attempt to pull this fireball from the void into the real world. When you pull on this fireball you are inherently using mana from your own mana pool, and you create something called an Anchor. This mana anchor is what holds your\nspell, or fireball in this case, in the real world.\n\n-Mana: Mana is sightless and is as invisible as the air in our world. It flows through our world like streams, and is in every living thing, whether it is plants or animals. Although mana comes at a\ncost, since it flows through people, Void users have gained the ability to use this mana to draw from the Void. Void users often get fatigued when over using mana, and have in rare cases died to the use of large amounts of mana.\n\nAnother drawback with the\nuse of mana is the effect (or lack thereof) on our mortal plane, when you draw on the Void for magicks such as Evocations, this element which has been evoked must eventually return to the Void. However this can become complicated with such magicks as\nAlteration, as it has the ability to prolong the existence of Void based elements in our world. Mana comes in three states; passive, active/used, and aura.\n\n-States of Mana:\n*The first is a state of passive mana. This is the mana which is already stored\nwithin all beings and plants alike. It cannot be manipulated by anyone aside from its owner.\n\n*The second is a state of active/used mana. This mana has been given a purpose (a spell), or has been stored inside a mana gem, and thus cannot be used like\npassive mana ever again. This is exactly why the famous \"Mana Bettery\" is impossible, and cannot be done. Once mana has been expelled from ones being forcefully, it cannot be regained. But it can be redirected, this is known by any competent Alterationist\n*The third and final is the well known state of aura. An aura directly reflects a mages personality through its color, which will be listed below this section. Auras are generally harmless and are simply a way of self expression. Aura is indeed harmless,\nand is expelled naturally by a mage, and all living things to some degree, but more so by those who are using their mana. The more mana you use to cast a spell, the more aura which is expelled from the user (Very much like a fire. The more wood you burn,\nthe bigger the smoke cloud is). There are only two beings which are capable of using aura, the first being an Arcane Evocationist to some degree, and a Shade. Although a shade literally consumes aura, in which case can become very dangerous when one uses\na large portion of their mana whilst combating such a creature.\n\n-Aura Colors:\nBlue: Calculatedness and logicallity (Sometimes emotional coldness)\nPurple: Mysteriousness\nWhite: Benevolence, order and innocence\nBrown: Nurturing and caring\nYellow: Greed\n(sometimes optimism)\nRed: Dominance, power and control (Sometimes tyrannical natures)\nGreen: Harmony and balance (Sometimes vanity)\nBlack: Chaos and malevolence\n\n-Mana Pools: Mana pools are how much mana we have in our person, and this determines how\ngrand our spells can be, along with the duration a spell can be held in our world. Mana pools are governed by two things; skill level and Magic type. Skill level is simply how skilled you are at manipulating mana for your specific Sub-type. For example;\nthe longer you train in the use of Evocations, the better and more efficient you are at manipulating mana for that sub-type. Magic type is a little more complicated, different magic Sub-types are naturally more mana consuming than others, a few examples\nof very draining subtypes are as followed: Alteration, Arcane Evocation, and Conjuration. Although far more difficult to learn if one of these are your first Sub-type, you will naturally get a bigger mana pool than someone whose first Sub-type was\nIllusion, or perhaps an Evocation.\n\n-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-", ""),
        StaticBook("The Void", "Nienna Calm", "The Void\nBy Nienna Calm\n\nForword:\n\n§YYou see, I’ve actually had the pleasure of gazing into the void myself back in Anthos, at the very bottom of the Hallows: a void node the mages guild had gone\nand destroyed by accident, or on purpose. Still not sure which. It is indeed endless, and the pathway to the hole defied all common logic. Frogs swam in the air, stairways upwards led downwards,\nbooks existed in languages that did not exist, from times that have yet come to pass. But I digress\n\n-Nienna Calm\nNow, this world is quite vast, to be sure. But it has its boundaries. It’s upper limits. Beyond that, is the void. A plane of existence unto itself, spanning into infinity forever. The Void gets its name because it contains nothing.\nThe nothingness nothing to ever exist, leading into a pitch black world of nothing in all directions. However, this plot-hole level amount of nothing has a very paradoxical element to it. It has the potential to become literally anything.\nA phrase you are going to hear me say often is this: “The Void is nothing, with the potential to become anything.” It’s the fundamental phrase you need to remember when considering the void itself. Now, one may ask, “How do we know for sure?”.\nNow, all mortals contain within them a small tear that leads into the void. To the best of my knowledge, this tear is a scar that was created when iblees was thrown from our world, through the void, and into the nether.\nIt’s not a… physical scar, but an ephemeral one. It’s contained within our very souls. Without it, all void magic would be impossible. But, of course this prompts the question. If we have a hole in our souls that leads to the void,\nHow do we make use of it? Through trial and error, the mages of old found that they could connect to the void, by attuning their minds to it. The mind is an organ of great potential. With it, the mortal races have accomplished great feats.\nAnd by using that mind to focus on nothing, and perhaps nothingness itself, we are able to finally connect to the void. Now, connecting to the void, is merely the first step in becoming a mage, and it is likely one of the most painful.\nYou see, when a mage connects to the void, the void will instantly begin draining your mana-An aspect of ourselves that we would die without.-All at once. For untrained mages, this would happen in but mere moment,\nand feels quite like having your soul sucked through a straw, ten times in an instant. Usually it results in them passing out, occasionally vomiting from sheer surprise, and waking up with the mother of all hangovers.\nAnnnnnd this will likely happen to you at least a hundred times. Before I’d even go into how to cast magic, I’d have you practice connecting, and learning to resist the pull of the void upon your mana.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Young Girl", "Eylianna D'iryth", "The young girl,  she looks up to the sky\nHer lips repeating\nand asking \"Why?\"\nKneeling on the ground\nWhere her mother lies.\nThe young girl, now that she is alone\nDoes her house remain a home?\nThe young girl, she walks alone\non the path to her fallen home\nHer arms are weak and weary\nHer face is sad and dreary\nbut her legs, they walk with fury\nNot ever holding back, to kick a nearby stone\nShe stumbles across a door\nOne that she's seen before\nOne that she once adored\nbut will now only bring her sadness\nand with that, nothing more.\n'The Young Girl'\nWritten by Eylianna D'iryth", ""),
        StaticBook("TheManInTheMoon", "Saendir Aureon", "The Man In The Moon\n\nA bar song written down by:\nSaendir Aureon\nThere's an...\nInn, there's an inn, \na merry old inn\nbeneath an old grey hill.\nAnd there they brew a beer so brown,\nthat the man in the moon himself came down one night to drink his fill.\nThe ostler has a tipsy cat that plays a five-stringed fiddle;\nAnd up and down he saws his bow\nNow squeaking high..,\nNow purring low..\nNow sawing in the middle.\nSo.. the cat on the fiddle played hey-diddle-diddle,\na jig that would wake the dead; He squeaked and sawed and quickened the tune.\nWhile the landlord shook the man in the moon: \n\"It's after three!\"\nhe said.", ""),
        StaticBook("Themba Zuberzuri", "Kijani Zuberzuri", "Table of Contents\n                ~*<>*~\nPg. 2 - Who was Themba \n            Zuberzuri?\nPg. 7 - What did Themba\n            do for Sylverport?\nPg. 10 - Conclusion\nThemba was most likely remembered for his immense height and brolic stature, standing at 8ft 2in and weighing a whopping 612 lbs. He often wore minimal clothing, but when he did, it was made of materials he crafted himself as a hunter for Sylverport.\nDuring the Atheran Age, Themba was young, strong, and growing for what seemed ages. He carried a huge, aurrum and bejewelled spear on his back for defense, which just made him look more intimidating than ever before.\nThemba was very kind and gentle and was also very protective and loyal. At times, he could have be seen to some as overly respectful, as he held others above himself due to his ideals\nand culture. ((Themba had the slightest of accents of one similar to Swahili)). He always defended himself and others with his wise knowledge before his brute strength. He loved all of the members of his village above all else, tending to every need\nbrought to him by friends or family.\nAside from providing love to all those who deserved the bodacious amount Themba radiated, he gave much more to Sylverport. In short, Themba was an overall wines and spirits producer, helmsman, hunter, herbalist, apothecary, doctor, and amateur architect.\nThemba stocked the “Drowning Sorrows Bar and Grill” with his hunted and cooked food and crafted alcohols. He aided in seafaring commerce and provided medical care to all patrons of the village. Skilled in structured aesthetics, Themba\nalso helped beautify the wonderful city that he provided much for, Sylverport.\nIn short, Themba fed and cared for the village as if he were a great loving and nurturing force that Sylverport could not live without. Themba could nothave provided without the aid of his other demigods that he held so closely to his heart.", ""),
        StaticBook("Themba's Log - I", "Themba Zuberzuri", "Amber's Cold - 17 - 1513\n--------------------------------  Today, our encampment for the new Sylverport had reached a stable level. I am now fully able to sit down and relax while I write in this log with accompaniment of Sylver and the animals\nwhich I had helped gather. Today, I've gotten a rabbit which seemed to like me through the journey to our storage cache outside the new Oren. He's at my feet now as I write. The next time I went out I found a pig and another sheep to breed with.\nWe have two of every animal, save the pig and/or steeds we need.\n\n It is bitterly cold in this new land - being the cold season and no longer being in the mesa of my old home. I think Im going to hunt soon. I'll try and make pelts\nfrom the game here for those at our cache, but Im no good with a needle and thread.\nThe Deep Cold - 8 -1513\n-------------------------------- In the past few weeks, I have gathered materials from hunting to make more clothes for us to keep warm in the harsh climate.  It is so unbearingly cold here that I’ve developed frostbite on my\nleg. Luckily, the pelt of local wild life keeps me, and the rest of our camp warm.\n  We’ve been gathering more and more animals - breeding and cooking enough to have a stable food supply.  Berliac and I have been cooking non stop, but\nAlyssia hasn’t even been around. Her husband, Sir Nightgrove, is always around though. He provides me with fish to cook for the camp. This camp is almost becoming as independent as Sylverport was in my mind.\nSpeaking of this camp, more and more word of finding land is springing up. Sylver has a flag design for the new village, Aesculus, but he invites others to try and make some as well. I have\nonly come up with one idea, and it varies in colors of blue, red, black, white, and orange. The black and white is for Oren, which we are under, and the blue and orange is for Old Sylverport.\n\n*Drawing of the flag cover this part of the page.*\nThe Deep Cold - 16- 1513\n--------------------------------The last week was uneventful. I’ve only picked herbs for the upcoming village which has yet to be erected. I’ve also been cooking and breeding, but one should already know that.\nToday however, was one full of joy. I met one of my friends from working at the Scarlet Lotus - Kale. She is very kind and pretty, and she has offered her abilities in fishing, medicine, bartending, and some farming.\nShe is wary of her place in our “village,” but I assure you, the reader, she will be of great use to the village as a whole. I was only showing her the camp when we came across Sylver.Words were spoken and Kale offered her helping hand within moments.\nI wouldnt mind her living with me in the new village, if I dont have anyone else yet.\n  Speaking of Old Sylverport, I ask myself, where is Aifric or Alyssia - Zelak or Krug’har? Everyone rode on the ship I piloted, but Zelak\nrode on his castle he said. I cant remember correctly. Aifirc worries me because of his physical state, and Alyssia worries me because of her state with her child.Zelak worries me because he is my friend, as well as Krug’har.\nWorry, worry, worry. “Its too cold, where are my friends? Why are we waiting here so long? Its been about two months now…” These thoughts run my head constantly as I shiver.I hope the weather warms up like Kale said because these times have been rough...\nSnow’s Maiden - 4 -1513\n--------------------------------The last weeks were too, uneventful and full of shivering, cooking, and breeding. But this week was the most fun. An official camp has been erected, complete with tents, a fire pit, the storage\ncache, and areas for training in sparring or archery. Sylver has been helping me train.The crossbows arent too bad because Ive had some progress with throwing spears and knives when hunting.\nI just barely missed the target, but I got a chunk of hay off. The swordplay was alright, and Sylver called me impressive because I found a chink in the dummies’ armor. I got a larger bit of hay out of that one, so I could have some luck with swords.\nSylver and I even fought hand to hand with sparring sticks. That was fun, but I lost. I’d like to think I only lost because I didn’t fight with full strength or I could hurt him, but honestly,I lost because Sylver is an amazing warrior. Im\nglad I have him as a teacher.\n  The tents here provide more warmth from this cold, as well as the new pelt I’ve fashioned to wear to bare it.  I also share a tent with Kale, my total informal friend. I don’t have to call her\n“miss” or “madame” anymore because she isnt my superior. I enjoy speaking to her about anything I can because I dont have to watch what I say as much. \n\n  *The next paragraph has been erased.*\nSnow’s Maiden - 9 - 1513\n--------------------------------In the past 5 days, I have seen Alyssia safely with her child, and Mason, who I have forgotten about. I had also forgotten about Miss Caswell… I hope she and Zelak are alright. They constantly cross\nmy mind in this bitter, everlasting season of cold. Cooking, breeding, and shivering persist, but now I do it alongside Kale, my tent mate and friend. Until a later time, it will be all we do.\nMason has just informed me that Driscoll, Aifric, is alright  and well. In fact, I didnt realize he was Sylver’s tent mate. That relieved me, but I still worry of Zelak, Mira, and Krug’har. If I see those three again, I will be enlightened.\nSnow’s Maiden - 13 - 1513\n--------------------------------Berliac was hurt today and I had to care for him. It was quite the wound because of the amount of blood flowing from his arm. I had to fashion a tourniquet for his arm to stop the blood so I could\nwork on him. The bleeding stopped after so long and I was relieved. Berliac could’ve lost his arm. With the recent events of medical needs, Sylver has offered to erect a temporary infirmary for\nme. I will invite Kale to help because of her experience. I’ll also need all the help I can get because of the amount of people around here. Our camp is under a few minutes walk from Oren\nand trouble seems to brew there often; trouble that will call for a medical hand.\nAmber’s Cold - 7- 1514\n--------------------------------Nothing much has happened over the elven year. I still haven't seen Zelak. Everyone else I have. All I’ve been doing is breeding, cooking, shivering at points, hunting,\nhelping in the infirmary, and practicing with the sword and crossbow. Nothing eventful has been happening. We’re in the same camp. Its like nothing has changed.\nMalin’s Welcome - 9 -1515\n--------------------------------We’re still in this small camp that Im growing to dislike. Its so cramped and I see so many people a day, its just odd and overwhelming. It is ironic too, because\nback in Sylverport, I used to seek out socialization. Now I have too much and it always feels like someone is right in front of, next to, or behind me, yapping away about wanting\nto have land or about the bitter cold. The whole camp seems to be feeling this way too, because everyone is restless or irritable. We need to\nfind land soon, or I think we’re all bound to go mad. I just want something to myself, whether it be as a doctor, barkeep, chef, or anything!\nNo word on Zelak worries me at night. The only thing to keep me from worrying are my two jobs - a barkeep in Oren and the doctor in the camp.\nThe infirmary in the camp has been sparking a bit, but only for our people. Ive helped Goldworthy with his arm wound, and today I helped Nightingale with a sword wound to the stomach.  Other than those two and a few others from outside the camp, the\ninfirmary is still as quiet as ever, except people around the infirmary arent quiet enough for my liking.", ""),
        StaticBook("Theorem: Wisdom", "Valmir", "Theorem of Wisdom\nby Godwein Stafyr\nWhat is wisdom?\n\nWisdom is not easy to define, likely similar to eternity. Every person has its own views of wisdom. To elaborate this further, a row of examples.\nIs knowledge wisdom? Perhaps.\nIs knowing the right thing to do wisdom? Perhaps.\nIs doing something good wisdom? Perhaps.\nIs learning wisdom? Perhaps.\nAs aforementioned you cannot simply define wisdom. Wisdom is a multitude, colorful, differently shaped. Wisdom can and does exist in many of us. To different degrees, in different shapes. A forester can have the wisdom of knowing how to treat his plants\nand trees properly, when to grow what to reach the best result. As can the farmer. A sorcerer or wizard can know a lot about the divine art of magic and has through this his very own wisdom.\nStill, one would say, that in these example wisdom turns out to be rather knowledge, which is only partially right, if it’s right at all.\n\nWisdom requires more than simply having knowledge. Wisdom requires understanding the spirit, the being, the living\nand many things more. The inner peace and silence may bring wisdom. On the other side, a warrior may achieve a new level of combat by finding his inner stability in combat. To be calm in the face of the storm and evil.\nAs we now scratch the evil, the darkness, I wish to bring in a small part of my very own opinion. Wisdom doesn’t exist in people who are simply evil and work for their very own profit. Wisdom requires selflessness as well.\nYou may now think I am taking the side of the good here, solely. It is right. I do align myself to the good and the light, but must say, that I may be completely wrong with my statement about wisdom and the evilness here. Perhaps the other side may have\ntheir own kind of wisdom, being evil as it is.\n\nIs it wisdom to write a book about wisdom? No.\nIs it wisdom to explain what wisdom can be? Perhaps.\n\nWhy perhaps? Because wisdom is wisdom. Colorful and different. Not definable. That is wisdom.", ""),
        StaticBook("Theory on Herbs", "Esgaron", "I have a theory of electrical evocation being possible. It would take many years, maybe even centuries. Since plants can be different, and putting two plants together that are the same and having them make seeds together, would create a plant that is like\nthem both. I theory that if you had a herb that was /very/ powerful, and you put it at a location where plant life can still live but can easily die, with a place that has a lot of lightning. The plants that can stand lightning with many of this herb.\nThere could be a very very very VERY slim chance that it could create a new species since it is gone from its home, and it must adapt to its enviroment. The herb would be more violent/strong. It'd be dangrous and could kill people harvesting the herb.\nOf course, this is a mad theory and only something I thought that could happen. I do believe that electrical flora could be a thing. And if someone did something like this it'd take many years to see the results.", ""),
        StaticBook("Thomas Tantrum", "Beelzebub", "There was once a boy, he was named Thomas.\n\nThomas had a hot temper.\n\nThomas' mother warned him.\n\n\"Thomas, if you continue to be so wrathful, your head will pop like a balloon!\"\nThomas yelled at his mother.\n\n\"I do not need your advice! I do not have the patience for it!\"\n\nThomas stomped and yelled and walked away.\n\nHe was one angry boy.\nThe next day, Thomas came upon a boy playing with a toy.\n\nHe grew naughty.\n\n\"Your toy is dumb! And so are you!\"\n\nThomas knocked the toy out of the young boy's hand, breaking it.\n\nHe was one bad boy.\nThomas' head grew rounder.\n\nIt became a shade of red.\n\nHis voice became squeakier.\nThomas' mother warned him once again.\n\n\"Your head will pop, Thomas!\"\n\n\"That is what happens to mean boys!\"\n\nBut Thomas did not listen.\n\nHe ctomped and yelled and walked away.\nThe next day, Thomas came upon a boy waiting in line for something to eat.\n\nHe grew naughty.\n\n\"Give me your money!\"\n\nThe boy gave Thomas all he had.\n\nThomas was one big bully.\nThomas went home.\n\nHe looked in the mirror.\n\nHis head was a balloon!\n\"Help! My head, my head is a balloon!\"\n\nThomas called out. But his voice was too squeaky.\n\nHe stomped and yelled and stomped and yelled.\n\nUntil his head went 'pop'!", ""),
        StaticBook("Three Covenants", "Quinton Gael", "The Three Covenants\n\nA warm hearth blazed the light filled whispers and glances of heat across a shelter stuck in the grasps of a deep and cold downfall. Upon a seat of furs and velvet sat a well-filled and plump man, his cane bedecked in nearly enough\njewels to distract the view from the weary bags that had accumulated under his eyes. Although his beard covered several of his chins and ample food for an orphanage, albeit rotted by this point, rested between the hairs he was never without company.\nIt would not be beyond the commonality of the host to throw such an unkempt patron from the establishment, yet, the inn maintained him not only for his coin but for the greatest gift he bestowed to the frequenters: a story. In times when the food grew\nstale and scarce or when the ale deliveries ran short the people of the town, one which went by the name of Lindecombe, sought out their substance in a tale.\n\nFor many of years this pacing maintained, with some variance of course, until the night\nwe come to, one which begins with a young lad by the name of Arthur Burnesbee. Arthur was not known to be a bright child, or a dim child for that fact. He was average in almost every way. His eyes were brown like all the villagers, his teeth were yellow\nlike all the villagers, but his hair was unlike all the villagers'. A bright yellow crest adorned the head of Arthur and made him quite the persecuted boy in the fields. To his parents he was affectionately called their golden boy, but the same affection\nlacked when his peers picked up on the epithet.\n\nThe gloomy night where our story takes place saw Arthur approach the man in the chair of velvet and furs and ask for a story, as many had done. However, unlike the normal matter of this occasion the\nman leaned forward, squinting at the boy with the intensity of a hawk. After a while of this peculiar gawking the man returned to his traditional state of rest and relaxation.\n\nAfter a hum and a hiss the old man's mouth cracked open, its dryness nearly\nleading Arthur to believe the man was crumbling like dry cake, that is if Arthur had ever seen a cake before. \"Three deeds I say. Hmmm, yes, for you, this shall do.\"\n\nArthur sat before the man, his legs folded over each other as his tush settled into the\nwarmed skins of an animal that had been laid astray on the floor of the tavern. \"A boy, you see, once lived around this very part of the world,\" said the old man in his grumbling and archaic manner. \"There came a day when he was through with his luck here\nand decided, upon his own thought, to bring about an end to his life, through one means or another. The child had plenty of time to consider what he would do, and the energy to complete what he wanted, yet he only wished for death. It was a dry night\nwhen he went into the woods, a stable rope tied in a noose accompanying him. After a few moments of dredging through the piles of colored and decaying leaves he came across a tree, tall and strong that stood the size of a giant. It only took the lad a\nbit of time to string up the rope and prepare himself for the jump from the branch he had struggled up to. As he looked down he saw a man, robed in red staring up at him. 'It is a long fall,' the man said to the boy. With the robed man's sharp wits and\ntongue he talked the boy down onto solid ground, but it was truly not for the sake of the boy's life. Once the youngling had found his feeting upon the dirt the robed man introduced himself, 'I am Krict and before you go and defeat your purpose here in\nthis world let me propose to you a simple deal. I will grant you a wish here every five and thirty years of anything your heart desires or your mind commands. The only stipulation I would bind to such an agreement is that you, upon your death, shall have\nto show to myself, and my companions how you have achieved happiness in this world. If you cannot I will claim all of your worldy pocessions and confine you to a token of my choosing.' The boy, in a odd situation to begin with, called upon his senses and\ntook note that his death was a long way off and that his life could be greatly improved by such magical manipulation. The words were exchanged and the deal signed with the blood of both men. It was merely a glimpse after the scroll had been slid into the\nsleeve of the magician that the youth ordered the robed man to make him a king of lands so wealthy that the world would know him as the richest man alive. And so it was. With a nod, a wink, and a slight gesture of the hands the boy awoke the next morning\nto the glistening of palace walls, decorated in the purest gold and silver, and even a privy made of solid amber. His estatic cries woke even his counciler, who quickly ushered him into another room to start his day. As the newly appointed king the boy\nhad many responsibilities to manage and the counciler would not let him slack in that regard. At first it seemed the work would slow, and that is what the boy dreamed of, but as weeks drew to months and years the boy grew older and his time scarcer.\nYet, he was moneyed and still teaming with the fruit of life granted to him by nature. When time arrived for the second wish to follow the first the king rode off from his castle to his hometown and made his way to the tree that had granted him such\nfortunes. Upon arriving the robed man asked his wish and the king delivered his blunt reply, he wished for time to spend on his own crafts and not the state of his kingdom. From the next day forward the king was never asked for anything other than the\nrare preparations for another one of his lavish festivals or feasts. And so it seemed as if the world had smiled upon the king. With his wishes he had gained the wealth of a kingdom, the time he needed to do as he pleased, and the energy afforded to him\nby youth itself. Little did the king know or prepare for the fading of such a natural gift. With his life came mortality and with mortality comes aging. He slowly lost his strength and vitality. The gold stashes and coffers of the kingdom overran with\nbooty from his years before, and his days were completely void of any duties, yet he was sickly, greyed, and reaching the end of his course here in this world. Long ago the king had forgotten his promise, so, when the day came of his last breath he was\nwisked to an unknown dimension to be judged by the clerics in red. There he could not explain to them how happiness was found in his youth; where he had no money, in his middle-ages; where he had no time, or in his later years; where he had not the\nstamina to enjoy any of his life's achievements. So, the clerics conferred upon him a harsh reality. Since he failed to find time without their interference they would grant him immortality. Since he failed to find vigor without their interference they\nwould grant him immobility. And since he failed to find material wealth without their interference he would be given only the illusion of wealth, with none of its benefits.\"\n\nThe boy sat sadly on the floor, his eyes drifting to the boards that neatly\nlined the deck. It wasn't until the words, \"And that is how I came to be here,\" left the old man's voice that Arthur looked up, shocked at the sight of the man who's story he had just heard. And it was then, in that instant, that the outside of the tavern\nlit up with light from a bolt cast down from the heavens. Silence fell and remained for some time between the boy, the man, and all of those who clung to the edges of the one-room building. There was no words to speak... until.\n\nEnd of Volume I", ""),
        StaticBook("Time Keeps Going", "Ambros", "The Sense That Time Keeps Going Faster\n\nBy Unknown\nTranscribed by Ambros\nIt's actually just after you're born that life flashes before your eyes.  Entire aeons are lived in those first few months when you feel inseparable from the world itself, with nothing to do but watch it passing by.\nAt first, time is only felt vicariously, as something that happens to other people.  You get used to living in the moment, because there's nowhere else to go.  But soon enough, life begins to move, and you learn to move with it.\nAnd you take it for granted that you're a different person every year.  Upgraded with a different body... a different future.  You run around so fast, the world around you seems to stand still.  Until a summer can stretch for an eternity.\nYou start to feel time moving forward, learning its rhythm, but now and then it skips a beat, as if your birthday arrives one day earlier every year.\nWe should consider the idea that you is not wasted on the young.  That their dramas are not more grand than they should be.  That their emotions make perfect sense, once you adjust for inflation.  For someone going through adolescence, life feels\nepic and tragic simply because it is: every kink in your day could easily warp the arc of your story.  Because each year is worth a little less than the last.  And with each birthday we circle back, and cross the same point around the sun.  We wish each\neachother many happy returns.\nBut soon you feel the circle begin to tighten, and you realize it's a spiral, and you're already halfway through.  As more of your day repeats itself, you begin to cast off deadweight, and you feel the study pull toward your center of gravity, the ballast\nof memories you hold onto, until it all seems to move under its own intertia.  So even when you sit still, it feels like you're running somewhere.  And even if tomorrow you will run a little faster, and stretch your arms a little farther, you'll still\nfeel the seconds slipping away as you drift around the bend.\nLife is short.  And life is long.  But not in that order.", ""),
        StaticBook("Time Warping", "Minuscule_Evil", "Time Warping\n\n      by, Tahjeet\n   Asul'mira Mubdee\nIf this book is found anywhere else than the Eternal Library of Lin’evaral, the Enclave of Haelun’or, it is stolen.\n\nBoth buyers and sellers will be punished.\n\nSigned, the Tilruir’Indor Lelien\nIf the theory of time as an illusion is correct then it is possible that time itself can be warped, molded or shaped, by the will of a person.\n\nTime, although a perception, an illusion is viewed as reality anymoment where the perception of time\nis changed, it is in the eyes of all, truly changed as a reality.\n\nBut to be able to learn to warp the perception of time, an illusion, a person must know how to create and mold illusions.This can be done with, perhaps, one’s mana alike how\nevocationists can create and change the arcane through the casting of mana.\n\nTo make a comparison, time is like a piece of iron and the one who can mold this piece of iron is the blacksmith, in this case an illusionist.\nTo shape and mold the iron, it requires the iron to be heated., the casting of ones mana, then to shape the piece of iron it requires a hammer, this will be the illusionist’s ability to mold and shape the illusion or perception.\nFor example, if the blacksmith hammers the iron flat it become elongated- lengthening time-if the blacksmith hammers the iron into a smaller length it becomes shorter – shortening time– if the blacksmith hammers the iron from a different angle,\nbecomes bent - perhaps stopping time.\n\nWhat may be that separates simple illusions and the warping of the time illusion, which may be the reason no illusionist, is that time is an illusion seen by all and perceived as a reality.\nThis changes what that iron is. The piece of iron the blacksmith had been shaping was just a small piece of a large statue.\nThe illusion of time surrounds us, we are immersed in it, fragments of the illusion can be shaped, changing what we see and feel. It is impossible for anyone to truly see time as an illusion even though it is known to be so.\nLiving beings are designed to perceive time as a reality, to see old and new, growth and withering, life and death.\nTo understand time is to not see through its illusion.\n\nTo warp time is left in the hands of the curious.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tinkers I", "Kalvo Delevoye", "-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-\n          -*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-\n\n      /~~~@@@@@@@~~~\\\n      \n            Learning The\n\n        Basics Of Tinkers\n\n      ~By Kalvo Delevoye\n\n      \\~~~@@@@@@@~~~/\n\n -*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-\n*----------------------------*\n            Introduction\n     *----------------------------*\n\nMy name is Kalvo Delevoye I am a Maliker or Dark Elf known by the common tongue. I have been a Tinker\nfor 336 years.\nI've had many successful creations and many creations gone wrong such as blowing up, catching fire and stinking out the room.\n\nIn these books that you read I will be teaching you many different subjects on Tinkering and explaining how you can tell-\nif something is going to go good or something that is going to go bad such as explosions, electric shocks and rashes or illnesses caught by tinkering. \n\nNow that the introduction is over lets get right to it!\n*--------------------------*\n       Redstone & Where\n            To Find It\n     *--------------------------*\n\nRedstone is the centre of all modern tinkering so you'll need a good supply of it. Redstone is a dusty type of mineral-\nit's found in the depths of the world commonly found within the Andesite layers. At first the mineral isn't pure dust, it's trapped between rock in a ore type state. Separating it from the stone is fairly simple and can take up to a day making good-\nquality dust. A Stone Pickaxe won't be able to break it up into chunks so you'll have to use a Iron Pickaxe or Diamond Pickaxe.\n*---------------------------*\n       The Process From\n        Chunk To Powder\n     *---------------------------*\n\nWhen the Redstone chunks are extracted from the mine they are hit with either a pickaxe or hammer. A hammer would be more efficent as-\nthe flat face of it would make a better impact on the chunk.\n\nWhen breaking up the chunks make sure you have a flat, stable and dry surface as when hitting the chunks it'll stop them from jumping around. The dryness of the surface will stop any small-\nreactions making the powder combust/fizzle. Once the chunks have been broken down you can now start to remove the chunks of stone until you have just the redstone bits left over. This is not the end of the process as it hasn't been made fully into powder.\nNow you need to collect small samples of the bits and place them into a mortar and pestle, this is used by tinkers like myself who have a small area to work in unlike others where they have big machines to grind it for them.\nBut now you want to fill it half way up and carefully start to grind down the bits into powder, the slower you go the better the dust as the slowness of the break down will make it finer and better quality. When you are satisfied with the quality of dust-\nplace it into a container that is dry and has a lid to keep moisture out as you don't want damp dust as this will cause explosions if the dust is crafted into wires.\n*------------------------*\n             Dangers Of\n               Redstone\n       *------------------------*\n\n~ If not stored correctly the Redstone dust can get damp meaning when used in projects it could lead to fatal failure.\n~Keep away from children and animals! It is not a type of sweet and could have bery bad effects on them!\n\n~Redstone is not a drug so don't sniff it or lick it, you'll only get bad effects from it.\n~Don't wear white when handling redstone as it's a hard substance to get out of clothes.\n\n~Using gloves is advised when handling Redstone.", ""),
        StaticBook("Titus Northbroek", "Lord Titus Northbroek", "___________________\n\nThe Diary of\n\nLord Titus Northbroek\n___________________\n\nWritten: \n4th of The Deep Cold, 1613\n\nIn loving memory of Titus Northbroek\n1584-1614\nDear,\n\nWhomst ever may read this.\n\nPerhaps this journal may reach the Great Library of Dragur before it is engulfed in flames...Much like I will be within a few Saints Days.\n\nMy entire land will burn in a sea of red and\nyellow.\n\nIt is perhaps mere cruelty to lead people to believe that we may have hope in winning against this siege.\n\nI will watch in fear and devastation as Dunamis set alight my home and flames rip their way through buildings and it's\nsurroundings.\n\nTendrils of smoke will swirl up into the air symbolising my defeat...and meaning my demise.\n\nHow quaint and curious war is, ey? \n\nYou slaughter a fellow, that you'd treat with an ale if met in a tavern.\nI can not tell you how terrified I am.\n\nThe acrid stench of burning corpse envelops my naval cavities. Pure shite, bloody tresspassers caught upon my land. Did they not read the warning sign?!\n\nI found in one of the pits; two creatures.\nTheir hair was scattered into multiple places, their mouths hung open and seemed to be melted together.\n\nThey were barely recognisable as a Human...until I noticed the uniform of a poor Lorrainian Soldier slowly melting away underneath the pres\nof the fire.\n6th of The First Seed 1614.\n\nIt has been too long since I have wrote in this Diary, which I have fortunately kept safe from evil.\n\nThe hooded vale of death has hung over me for a long time....I didn't think it'd be this soon.\nI have been scoffed at the last few Saints Days when I inform people whom I am defending my fort against.\n\n\"You won't stand a chance!\"\n\nMaybe so...but I will not stand here and let them take it without a fight!\nSo, as I am sat here overlooking the grounds that I am to be killed in. \n\nI would like to write a few private passages to my friends.\n\nSer Elias de Castro\n\nIf you are found reading this I would like to thank you for being a helpin\nhand in this Siege. You are my comrade, and an even better friend.\n\nFarewell, brother...I hope you did not perish during the battle.\nEdmund Northbroek,\nmy loving cousin, my best-friend. I would like to sincerely thankyou for assisting upon building our land to what it had become.\n\nWe shared many great adventures together, and for that I am truly thankful. I know you did\nparticipate in the siege.\n\nAnd I would have stopped you if you had attempted to fight...I love you Edmund.\n\nGoodbye, Cousin.\nClint Northbroek, my cousin and ludicrous best friend. We had a strong companionship, we shared similar feelings and ambitions...now it is something we must die for. \n\nYou aren't a warrior or a dexterous swordsman, but you are loyal...\nand you swore to protect your family.\n\nYou have helped me on many occasions.\n\nIf you happen to survive this siege, I want you to live life to it's fullest. You have a lot of potential kid, don't waste it.\n\nKind Regards, Brother.\nTristan Northbroek, my brother, my true best friend, and I'm forever greatful of your existence.\n\nYou have helped me in battle, you have helped me fight, but now you must help yourself.\n\nI want you to flee, I do not want you fighting brot\nour cousins, the Grimlees and you will meet a man called Uther. He will take care of you from there.\n\nAnd lastly...\n\nSer Nicolas Ruben, you were a respectful gentlemen when I had first had the pleasure of meeting you.\nI insisted upon leaving together, perhaps gathering enough mina to set up a small homestead. \nBut those are faded dreams and lost ambitions. \n\nFor now we focus upon slaughtering many foes.\n\nGoodbye, Nicolas!\nAve Lorraine!!!\n\n\nA blessing to everyone!\n\nAnd may we honour those who fought in the siege of 1614.\n\nSincerely, Lord Titus' Northbroek last entry.", ""),
        StaticBook("To Aebek ~ Nemir", "Nemir", "To lay a kiss on your lips,\nso gentle and delicate\nis like picking the drops of dew\noff the petals of a rose.\n\nI hold you close and feel safe,\nsheltered in from the rain,\nfrom the storms that grow and surround me.\nI take your hand and look into your -\n- eyes and see a heart made of gold and soul so pure.\n\nYou see you are an angel, an angel to me.\nI could not help but fall madly in love with you,\nthe one who stole my heart.\n\nI'm glad you did \nbecause I could never find one such as you...\nSome one who -\n- makes each day the best,\neach laugh the longest, each tear the saddest,\nand a life, my life, worthwhile.\n\nI love you.", ""),
        StaticBook("To Arganos", "Maladem Uuthlini", "To Arganos\nBy Maladem Uuthlini\n\nProud Uuthlini, raise the flagon!\nSet the table for the feast!\nGather all by boat and wagon,\nAll your kin from west to east!\nCall your fellow ker together!\nLet no beast nor Undead thrall,\nNor any sort of fearsome weather,\nKeep them from the banquet hall!", ""),
        StaticBook("To Be a Wraith", "Toodles", "Becoming a Wraith\n\nBy: Someone who's not stupid enough to reveal their name.\nPrerequisites:\n-Must be a practitioner of the dark arts or undead.\n-Must have a 'catalyst'; some sort of bone that the Drake, Satar, gives to certain people.\nThe hopeful Wraith must acquire such a catalyst, and then place it on a certain type of Altar, one example of which is located in the Sunless Sanctum. Upon doing this, they must find, kill, and take a bone from three mortals.\nThey then must take these bones to the altar... But the author is not quite sure what happens to them. But once they've been used, the Wraith-to-be must stab themself with an Aurum sword. After much immolation and probably pain, they\nwill become a Wraith. Huzzah!", ""),
        StaticBook("To my Beloved", "Zaaryth", "-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\nTo my very tan,\nCaramel,\nSucculant,\nCharming,\nEnthusiastic,\nSelf-Centered, \nHazel-Eyed, \nLight-Shaved,\nElven Beloved.\n\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\nYour words are like that of the flowing wind riding on a gentle breeze.\n\nThe light ripples along the beautiful ocean surface on a lovely summer beach.\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\nI wish to see you.\n\n[!] A small signature had been written within the right corner of the scroll. Though most of it has been scribbled out, leaving an incomprehensible two letters.\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-", ""),
        StaticBook("To My Blood", "Demagol Doomforged", "I've never wrote a book before, however with Archimedes deciding his time was to come I realized how soon my passing was. This book will go to my other son, Marring. Hopefully, he will do right by the Doomforged and make Dormmar and I proud.\nUrir Ireheart, False Paragon\n\nMy grandfather, Urir, is revered for being the savior of the descedents in Aegis. He ran into the portal to Iblees' realm wearing the armor of Urguan and sacrificed himself to lock Iblees away and give the descendents time to\nescape Aegis and rebuild. This was a lie. All of it. Urir did not sacrifice himself for the descedents, his kin, or his children. He did it for Iblees. Centuries later in Athera, when Hodir and my father Iban called the Doomforged to gather only three of\nus answered. Dorgrim, Virak, and me. Hodir, Iban, and Dorgrim all disappeared shortly after, leaving Virak and I to tend to relations in Urguan. This, during one of our lowest points, was when Urir showed up. He wanted me to hunt down the legendary\nweapons of the four brothers. I could not, naturally. Urir then had us meet with a hooded dwedmar with blue eyes similar to ours, only they did not glow with our fire yet pierced us just the same. The dwed claimed to be Velkan II Ironborn and asked\nus to join him. I, stupidly and blindly, accepted. I thought it was what our grandfather wanted us to do. By the time I realized we were in the middle of an Undead invasion force, it was too late. If we tried to leave, we would be killed. After\nentering their undeground invasion grounds, we laid siege to Kal'Agnar. The dwedmar of the city stood no chance against the undead armies, and I still see their faces in my dreams. To the Doomforged that read this: Do not trust the past nor the future.\nThey both have their own agendas, and our kind are always a cog in their plans.\nOur inherent Madness\n\nI've found, from personal experience and from reading of clan records, that we are inherently insane. Now, we have some control over ourselves. We can still think as any sane man or woman would, only we have a strange\nbloodlust that can only be compared to that of the Uruk. This bloodlust makes us prone to ferocious bursts of rage, and in some Doomforged, gives a berserker mentality to simply kill without care for our own safety or that of others. I have tried to find\na way to rid ourselves of the bloodlust and rage, but have only found ways to temporarily settle it down. I now must have daily sessions of 'Anger Removal' to keep those around me safe. This consists of taking a woodchopping axe and letting loose on a\nspecificed tree (First ensure there are no Druids in the area). Or you can simply work in the forge and create what I've taken to calling 'Rage-forged' equipment. Arms and armor made during a bout of anger. There are other ways to control our anger, but\nthese are my methods of choice.\nThe rest I have already taught you, my sons and daughters. Our methods of smithing, the Doom Forge, Dormmar, all this you already know. Throughout your life, you will be hated, used, and ridiculed. Do not let these bring you down, for you are Doomforged.\n======================================Anart Nir Dorkadrel\nNarvak Oz Dormmar\nGilthok Iblees\n========================================================================================================================================================", ""),
        StaticBook("To Petrus", "Erin Lockley", "*Within the crate sat a slip of paper addressed to Petrus. It read:\n\nOne Hundred Mina Total.\n\nTo the Account of Petrus. \n*\n\n\"I thought it would only be fair to send\nforward some mina for your first half saints week or so of employment. To keep you going.\n\nI have paid tax on the house, and did request that you be added to the ledger (I asked for them to add you to the region. Unsure if they did.)\nFrom this sunday following, I will start paying consistent amounts.\n\n-Erin Lockley.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("To Speak To One", "A.N.C.", "To Speak To One\nby A.N.C.\n\"Bespeaketh,\" they say. \"Bespeaketh to we.\"\n\"No speaketh,\" says I. \"I speaketh, I die.\"\n\"Why ceaseth?\" asks they. \"Why ceaseth to we?\"\n\"No trusteth,\" I ply. I trusteth no fly.\n\"Do trusteth,\" says they. \"Do ceaseth no speaketh.\"\n\"No do,\" I reply, for \"trusteth be badeth.\"\n\"Cease trusteth be badeth,\" says they, me thinks sly.\nTo they I shake nay, \"For badeth be speaketh.\"\nBut when gone I comply, for badeth no speaketh.\nDo pain do we part, for this speaketh be goodeth.\nFor no speaketh be killeth, and alath, I died.", ""),
        StaticBook("To Starter Mages", "Nemir", "Advised books to read for beginner mages\n-------------------         Nemir Valnelis\n             Ward of\n        The Library of\n              Dragur\n\n\n7th of the Snow's Maiden, 1616\nI first suggest that the book titled, \"On the Void\" which is located in the \"Magic\" section, is read first.  You will get a good understanding of the void, which every aspiring mage needs in order to make their first connection to it.\nAnother good book that would help one get a better grasp at what mana is, is the book titled, \"The Study of Magic\" by Sarrion.\nAfter reading these, I then suggest reading /every/ single book on evocations, and to re-read the book(s) on the magic you wish\nto start practicing.  They will do good in helping you understand how one pictures their element in the void, then uses their mana to pull it out into our reality.\nSome other helpful books are: On Mana Anchors, The Arcane Arts, Magic: The Basics, The Void, Aura, Mana Pools, and just about any other book that can be found.  Really, read any book on magic.  They help.\nAfter note:  Magic should /not/ be learned purely for violent means.  It is an art meant for great things, not death.", ""),
        StaticBook("To Sylvestre.", "Achard", "Dear Ser Sylvestre,\n\nTo start, I wish to offer my greetings. I trust and pray that you fair well, that the the current changes within the Empire have not put you out of your way. \n\nTo jump to the point, I wish to hold a meeting with you. Be such here\nwithin the Capital, or somewhere more secluded, I require your assistance. You may ignore this letter, or simply decline my request, though I truly am in need of help. Due to the shift of changes and the target placed upon our backs, I am stuck and fear\nnot only for my family, but that of the School and otherwise. By now, I trust you have worked out that it is I, Crumena Izalith, who write this letter to you, the proprieter of the Academy, and servant of the Empire. \n\nForemost, I wish to assure that I\nplayed no involvement with the recent occurences, so much so that I was not aware of the events until I was captured and beaten by the Legion. Fortunately, the good Prince Philip allowed my life to be spared, though I am now stuck at a crossroad. I am\nafraid I do not know how to continue. I wish to continue to serve the Empire, and as the pupil and previous protege of Ser Avenel, I wish to follow in the footsteps of indebted aid to Orenia. I do not oppose, and I never have nor will. \n\nWith this in mind\nI hope I am able to commune with you. The moment I step foot into the city outside of disguise, I will find my life taken from me, which unfortuantely goes against the aid I wish to offer. If there is some way for us to work out a way for me to continue\nto assist without the dagger over my head, I will gladly appreciate it. \nPlease, a bird will be greatly appreciated, even if it's simply to deny my request. \n\nSincerely,\nCrumena A. Izalith.", ""),
        StaticBook("To Vex a HighElf", "Matrim Macdunn", "How to vex a High Elf\n\n\n\n           For\n My Adunian Brothers\nThe High elf is a species of being that is usually associated with class, elegance, magic and of course power.\nHence, such qualities accumulate to a grand disgruntled vexation by the common man. As a usual high elf will look down upon 'inferior' races or\ncultures.\n\nHeaven forbid you hail from 'impurity' such as being a half elf or Adunian. Such is seen as a grand faux par, as it reminds them how they themselves were impure as to mingle with Harrenites.\n\nAs of such they often tend to haul\nthemselves up in their cities, denying access to all those whom don't hail from their mighty ancestory.\n\nOn the other hand, when these timid and commonly, rude creatures scurry from their lairs they are often condesending and harsh to all those\nnot of their kin.\n\nThis, my friends, is why I have personally taken it upon myself in to muse possible ways to disarm, vex and scare off this beast.\nMethod 1:\n\nBe from a mixed heritage, Adunian or half elf. Either will surfice.\n\nThe mere concept of love across races is dead with the high elf, so be spawned from such love is the ultimate vexation as proof that love\nconquer's order.\n\nHowever, be wary of mix-ed one. For a high elf may turn hostile. If that is the case be sure to play the racism card. If this fails, arm yourself and be sure to attack before the beast can charge a magical attack!\nMethod 2:\n\nIf they commit any actions, mutter 'Typical high elf'. Simple as that, it boils their blood good and proper.\nMethod 3:\n\nRemind them of how their past kin have been manipulative, crooked and evil to all whom are not their own. To remind them of their past brings them great tragedy. They may become snide however and claim that it was true and proper. If this is\nthe case, be sure to verbally put them down and destroy their argument.\n\nMethod 4:\n\nDistribute this guide.\n\nMethod 5:\n\nA good old punch.", ""),
        StaticBook("To Zyvia", "Erolas Ba'ikana", "Dear Zyvia,\n\nI hope you are doing well. I've come to miss\nyour touch, your beautiful face, just being around you. I also miss holding our daughter, playing with her. I miss my family, things have been difficult, even more without you around.\nI write this to you because me and my kin have found land to settle on, we will rebuild our home and\nlive peacefully. I wish\nfor you to come live\nwith us, i want to unite\nour family once more.\nMaybe you could even become a den mother.\nmany of my family have been asking for you and your whereabouts. I feel ashamed to not even be able to answer it. I will return in a few nights and hopefully you'll have an answer. I want to \nhave you and Enara in my arms once more.\nto live happily like we've always wanted.\n\n      ___      ___\n    /     \\   /     \\\n    l       \\/        l\n     \\   E  +  Z   /\n       \\           /\n         \\       /\n           \\   /\n             \\/\n[!] A heart with initials would be drawn onto the letter\n\n\n\n\n\n\n        Forever Yours,\n                Erolas", ""),
        StaticBook("To: JGLW", "Sasha Silverthorn", "Hello,\nI am interested in becoming an intern. If you are interested in taking me please send a bird my way.\nThank you,\nSasha Silverthorn(Bookwyrm2003),", ""),
        StaticBook("To: Ruin'nir T.", "Gilondir Oronar Sagehand", "Hello Ruin'nir Terin,\n\nI see your nice alchemy store and I was thinking we could perhaps meet up some time to share some knowledge, I might have a few things you'd like to buy or recipes you'd like to know!\nSend me a bird if interested!\n-Gilondir Oronar Amarthelon Sagehand Frostbeard of Faroe and de Savin.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tobias' Log - 1", "Tobias Millerson", "Entry 1\n\nIt occurs to me, as I sit on a roof in St. Karlsburg, that writing a journal is not something to be done while in a place you aren't supposed to be. Ah well, I'll do it anyway. I am Tobias\nMillerson, squire (Though not for much longer) of Ser Brynden Tosali. At the time of my writing this, I am 17 years of age. My adventure of a life truly began when I was 8, though I hardly wish to recap my past at the moment.\nI've been visiting the great library in the west regularly, and I stumbled across a whole shelf of journals and diaries. I figure that I might as well write one myself. Perhaps my life will be of some interest to the passive reader.\nI admit that I am not the best writer, but hopefully the story will pull you through.\nEntry 2\n\nEver since the destruction of Johannesburg, I've taken to causing trouble in St. Karlsburg. It isn't as though I try to be childish; I simply can't pass up the oppertunity\nto press my luck. For instance, there's a way onto the rooftops of the city. From there, it's a simple matter to enter the gatehouse and, well, close the gates. I've only been spotted once so far and the guard never came close\nto catching me. Alls well that ends well, I suppose. I doubt Ser Brynden would appericiate my antics, though. They should be glad that an enemy hasn't found this security flaw. I write this, of course, from the gatehouse itself.\nEntry 3\n\nMy time on the roof has doomed me. A man waits below as I write, bow and arrow at the ready to shoot me! He wants me to tell him the way up.\n\nI gave in. He kept sending arrows near\nmy head, he could have killed me! I showed him the way up. I'm not proud of it, but whatever it takes, I suppose. He said his name was Zaor.\nEntry 4\n\nI've decided to fill in some of my... backstory. At the age of 8 I travelled to Johannesburg. It's a miracle that I didn't die along the way, but I feel that the roads were safer back then. I have vauge\nrecollections of my plan at the time, which was to go to the city and find a mage to fix my family. It wasn't a good plan, or even one that I was able to start. I was a begger, no roof or money to my name. Granted, this is expected of a child. A\nsemi-orphan, if you will. \n\nI quickly realized that I was going to die if I didn't get food. After several hours of fruitless begging, I encountered Ser Brynden. I remember being very suspicious of him; I thought he\nplanned to kiddnap me! He didn't, of course. He asked me a few questions, and upon learning of my situation, offered to take me in as a page. I accepted with little thankfulness. It still sounded like some sort of plot, and I could not see what he got\nout of our little deal. \n\nI was not a very thankfull child in general. To be completely honest, the knight scared me speechless. I figured it was only a matter of time before he put me back on the street. How cynical, for a young child.\nAnyhow, the next few months passed with little incident. \n\nDuring the height of the Empire/Dwarven war, I decided to go outside the gates of Johannesburg and see who was about. I had vauge plans to go to the library (even though\nI couldn't read at the time, I enjoyed sitting in the building). I was around 9 or 10 at the time. \n\nAs I stood on the road, studying one of the signposts and trying to divine its meaning, a pair of dwarves ran past,\na frightened looking woman in toe. I was rather ignorant of the war and thought little of it. One of the dwarves, however, spotted me and decided that I was going along for the ride. He clubbed me over the head and must have dragged\nme behind them. I recall waking up in the woods not far from Johannesburg and seeing the woman staring at me in horror, then another blow to my head knocked me out cold. I did not awaken again until one of the dwarves was tying me\nand the woman to a stout birch tree. They gave us food and blankets, and were surprisingly kind. I do not know what they planned to do to us. Merely that they spoke of bringing us to a ship. Their plans never came to pass.\nJust as I thought all hope was lost, a mage appeared. He was not good or just, however. One of the dwarves grabbed the woman. The mage attacked him, caring not for her fate. He seemed familiar to me, but I still cannot place where I'd seen him before.\nI was still tied to the tree. The dwarf, (who's companion had gone to check on the boat and had presumably been murdered by the mage's friends) pushed the woman aside and yelled for her to untie me and flee. He battled the mage while we ran.\nTo this day, I know not his fate. \n\nWe made it to Johannesburg, where the woman roused the guards and led them to the woods. By the time we arrived, there was no sign of our captors. The situation was left unremarked upon and I returned\nto the city, scared and alone. It was during one of Ser Brynden's outings, where he was off slaying God knows what. \n\nThat was one of the larger events of my childhood. The other was my encounter with slavers on the road\nfrom Johannesburg. They were trying to capture a woman, and I, in my young foolishness, attacked them. They beat me and took my blade, but the woman escaped. It was the first time I realized that I could be a knight; that I could defend hundreds more\nlike her. I truly believe these events shaped me into who I am now. Perhaps I will write of my other adventures at a later date, as well.\nEntry 5\n\nI met a man named Coltaine today. He was sitting alone on a roof in Karlsburg. I'll admit that I was rather surprised to see anyone up there, other than myself. I sat down and had a long talk with him,\nbut found that I learned very little about him. He authored a book on the Burning of Hanseti, which seemed like quite an acomplishment to me. He also reccomended that I read up on the undead. Perhaps I will. He was rude, but I rather\nenjoyed annoying him. Not mature or knight-worthy, I know. \n\nHe has a keep somewhere, as well and seems to be a mage of some sorts. He told me little of himself and most of what I know was revealed when one\nof his companions arrived in town and began speaking to him. I must speak with him more, to annoy him if nothing else. \n\nIn other news, Jeynie and I are the best of friends. Even Ser Brynden has remarked on how attached she\nis to her \"brother\". I'll admit that she reminds me of Belle, she was that young when I last saw her. \n\nI suppose that brings me to my next topic, though I am not sure it is a happy one. Ser Brynden apperantly sent men to search\nfor my family. What possessed him to do this I will never know, but there are records of them in Sutica. \n\nIt is bittersweet. Even if I found them, they would not know me. I would not know them, either. There is nothing but heartache\nhere, and I'm afraid to see them once again. Ser Brynden seems to be under the impression that I do not want to be part of the Tosali family, but that isn't true. I simply want to keep my name, my history; it's what makes me who I am. Besides, they would\nthrow me out onto the streets if they knew my personal choices. I know journals are the place that you are supposed to reveal your deepest secrets, but I don't think this is one I can reveal. \n\nI almost told Ser Brynden, a few days ago.\nHe was going on about how I needed to find a girl, and I wanted to shout that I did not want anyone. But alas, he does not give up. I'll play along, for now. \nWhy is it that love and attraction must cost someone their life? I've thought about this a lot,\nlately. I'm not sure if who I am is wrong or not. It is simply my life now. Ah, what the hell, I'll say it. I am impartial to women. They've never... caught my eye. And I know that people will think that is because I am young, but I am not sure. I pray it\nisn't so. Life would be easier if I were normal.\n\nI suppose this means that I cannot publish this journal until I'm dead, lest some reader takes it upon themselves to knife me in my sleep. It feels right to say it, though.\nI've hidden for so long; not a soul other than these pages knows. \n\nThat might be why I'm so afraid to find the Millersons. If they saw me, would they be proud of what I'd become? How could they love a son like me?\nI would be cast out, only this time they would choose to do so. \nWould my father even speak to me? Would they let me see my sister? Little Belle is probably near 14 years of age now. Daniel, too. Who would a be to them, other than\na stranger? \n\nThis is why I am afraid. It is only a matter of time before my nature is revealed to the Tosalis... how could I lose my other family as well? \n\nIt is the worst situation to be in. I cannot meet Ser\nBrynden's eyes without being overcome with guilt. He would be so disapointed, if he knew. Do I even deserve a knighthood? My only tresspass is the person I love. Oh, the irony. \n\nAh, I should not pour my self-doubts\nonto this page. I'll fullfill my duties as well as I can.\nEntry 6\n\nI spoke to Coltaine once again, and learned quite a bit this time. He was not pleased to see me, but didn't threaten to throw me off the roof this time. We sat in the Karlsburg Tavern.\nHe seemed rather impressed that I read his account of the Burning of Hanseti. He told me of other books he had written; the most interesting by far was his life story. I wasn't able to find it at the library, however.\nHe mentioned trying to seduce an elven woman, but apperantly his actions have done nothing to win her over. To be honest, I'm not surprised. They insult each other whenever they open their mouths. Plus, Coltaine has made no\neffort to get to know her. I offered the best advice I was able to, given my situation. \n\nIn return for my help (I think I started to grow on him, a bit), he showed me his \"hidden\" keep. I would have found it eventually, but it made things\neasier. He told me that he is of House Wick, which serves House Kovachev. It was interesting to listen to. Apperantly, the keep was granted to the family after the Dwarven-Empire war several years ago. \n\nHe is a mage, of some sorts.\nHe specializes in earth evocation, and claims to be one of the best four in his field. \n\nHis name is Coltaine Wick, and he was once a lord himself. He's got to be over a hundred years old, since he lives in the keep with his\ngreat, great, great grandson. He even mentioned something that he'd seen \"a century ago.\"\n\nHe works on thanium weapons for House Kovachev. Coltaine told me that he isn't affected by the stuff, but explained the\nawful things it does to people who ingest it. \n\nNote to self: Research Thanium.\n\nHe spoke about immortality for quite some time, too. I don't know if he was trying to tempt me into it, but I know\nthere are dire consequences for those who try to live forever. He told me to do some research. I'm currently on my way to the library to do just that. \n\nI also need a new journal, since I seem to have filled this one.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tobias' Log 2", "Tobias Millerson", "Tobias' Logs\n\nBefore the fall of Johannesburg - Living with the dwarves\nEntry 5,\n\nHad a looooot to drink last night. Lot's of regrets, had to sneak back into the house. Tosali didn't mention it so he must have been asleep when I got back. Thank the Gods.\nEntry 6,\n\nFound a weird rock on the shore of the ocean near Serpentstone. Might give it to Jeyne, she likes stuff like that.\nEntry 7,\n\nNote to self: Find some hangover cures- non magical though.\nEntry 8,\n\nCan't remember what happened. Some of the townsfolk gave me strange looks so it must have been quite the night. Best not to think about it, I guess.\nEntry 9,\n\nNote: Don't call people out on cheating on their wives, you will be yelled at for hours. Even if the guy in question can hardly form complete sentences.\nEntry 10,\n\nI need to do some reading on field medicine. Jeyne keeps falling off rocks and carts and scraping her knees. Evil child.\nEntry 11,\n\nRooftopping is not a good idea when drunk. \n\nCould improve with practice?\nEntry 12,\n\nIf another bandit attacks me on the road to Karlsburg I'm going to start stabbing anyone who gets too close.\nEntry 13,\n\nGetting real tired of the pointless things Tosali wants me to do. I never want to attend another awkward family dinner at house Amador ever again.\nEntry 14,\n\nVodka is super strong. Do not reccomend for future usage. \n\nTastes horrible, too.\nEntry 20,\n\nNot a lot of money for pointless stuff any more. Need to pay this weeks rent on the house. Might have to move on soon, find a cheaper place. \n\nNote: Buy new clothes for Jeyne, old dress\nripped during the trip.\nEntry 21,\n\nDwarven drinks aren't half bad. Got a bit of coin to spare today; can't spend much though. \n\nBesides, I need to stay alert for Tosali to come calling.\nEntry 22,\n\nAscended might help out. Not sure what they'd want in return, but right now I'm desperate. Can't pay next week's rent. Jeyne doesn't know. \n\nMight have to take a last resort. Steal, or\nsomething. \n\nI can't believe it's come to this.\nEntry 23,\n\nNo need to break the law, the priest is helping out. Should be able to survive another month, even.\nEntry 25,\n\nTrial ended. Tosali won't be following us any more. I can breathe again.\n\nReturning to our home for a time. We'll need to find a new house though, things have been tense\naround here.\nEntry 26,\n\nStill no options for places to stay. Elves won't even consider us, Tosali is in Karlsburg, perhaps the halflings will house Jeyne in exchange for work from me?\n\nAsk around.\nEntry 30,\n\nBeen rough around here. We're on the road again, sleeping at inns and such. Managing to get odd jobs here and there but it's not enough to last. Its time to seriously consider sending\nJeyne to live with someone else. Not Coltaine, God forbid. Zaor? Vanir? No, they've done enough for us. This is up to me.\nEntry 31,\n\nHave to find work. Which means not being \"myself\" as a friend put it. \n\nOh well. I can be quiet. I can act, if it gets us what we need.\nEntry 32,\n\nLast entry, I think. Not much ink left. Can't buy more.\n\nCurrently hiding in Karlsburg. No sign of Tosali, yet. I don't trust the man not to kill me on sight. \n\nI need to get new\nclothes, something to hide the scar on my neck. Makes me look shady.\n\nWill write again once able.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tome: Air Evo", "Uradriethiel", "Air Evocation\nThis book was created by Master Air Evocatonist Alatar of the Mage Academy\n\nRecopied By\nUradriethiel\nTable of Conents\n\nChapter 1: The Void\n\nChapter 2: All About Wind\n\nChapter 3: Summoning\n\nChapter 4: Basic Spells\nChapter 1: \nAccording to legend and study, the void is an infinite plane of potential thought and energy surrounded by absolute darkness. Since complete darkness is rather hard to imagine, think about a blank canvas.\nHypothetically, anything can be drawn out of the void if it does not contradict nature. The first steps of becoming a mage is learning to understand the void and it's 'blank' \nconcept. Meditation is the most efficient and common way, as I have found.\nLearn how to blanket yourself in a blank state of mind and prepare to paint your canvas.\n\nChapter 2:\nWind and air are essences to all life around the realm of existance. You breathe it into your very self.\nWith the art of air evoction, you manipulate it. Wind is unpredictable and one\nof the best studied branches of arcane magics, You must experience the element in it's true form before you can even think about summoning it.\nIn order to achieve this, I suggest moving to a  region of high altitude and feel the wind rush over your very body. Experience how pressure seeps through the cracks of all substance. Taste it, feel it, smell it.\nAnother useful experiment is placing something in the air that can float. Watch how the wind carries the item and gently cradles it back down to the earth or\ncarries\nit away\nChapter 3:\nAfter you have learned all there is to know about your element, and your meditation is firm; you may begin your attempts in summoning your element from the void. Firstly, you must find a place of peace.\nNext, use your blank canvas to imagine air, allow the thought to fill you and the energy of yourself to course through your very blood. Through combining all of this. A small amount of wind may be conjured.\nWarning: You may pass out a few times uponfirst connection.\n\nChapter 4: After you have mastered basic connection, you can move onto some of the key spells in an air evocationist's arsenal.\nThe first and most obvious, is the force push. Essentially, a novice air evocationist musters all of his strength for one large\nand forceful push at the enemy. Secondly, and slightly more defensive, is the protective tornado.\nA skilled air evocationist can create a spiraling current of wind that could potentially keep most objects out of your sphere. That concludes this tome.", ""),
        StaticBook("Torn Page", "Ancient Dwarf", "[!] This page has been torn out from it's respective  tome.\nThe Magi have begun dissapearing. I pray to Khorvad that we find them, else we may be stuck in this accursed place. Their leader, Dwov, is still about. I fear for him, though. His mind has begun to deteriorate for reasons unkown. We've enough supplies to\nlast another three weeks.", ""),
        StaticBook("Torture Devices", "The Eternal Library", "Torture Devices\n\nBy Sha Greyhammer\nJudas Cradle\nThe victim would be place on top of a pyramid-like seat. Where they would be slowly impaled.\n\nCoffin Torture\nThe victim was placed inside the ‘coffin’. Torturers were well-known for forcing overweight victims into the device, or\nthe ‘coffin’ slightly larger than normal to make the victims more uncomfortable.\n\nThe Brazen Bull\nWhen a victim is placed inside the brazen bull, he or she is slowly burned to death. It has a complex system of tubes in order to make the victim's\nsound like an infuriated ox.\n\nThe Rack\nThe rack is commonly considered the most painful form of torture. The torturer turned the handle causing the ropes to pull the victim’s arms. \nEventually the victim's bones were dislocated with a loud\ncrack. This method was mostly used to extract confessions, as not confessing meant that the torturer could stretch more. \nometimes, torturers forced their victim to watch other people be tortured with this device to implant psychological fear.\nThey often had spikes that penetrated the victim’s back  - as the limbs were pulled apart, so was his spinal cord increasing not only the physical pain, but the psychological one of being handicapped at best, too.\n\nDunking\nThe victim was tied to\nwhich was elevated or lowered by the torturer. If he noticed that the victim was going to pass out, he elevated the chair. If they didn’t reveal information the chair was lowered. This could take hours.\n\nDrops of Water\nA very painful method of to\nconsisted of fixing a victim’s head under a small tube that constantly filtered drops of water. These fell on the same spot of the victim’s head leading to, in prolonged periods of time, death.\n\nFreezing With Water\nPouring water on someone in col\nEventually causing them to freeze to death.\n\nForce Drinking\nThe effect is this: the victim is forced to drink much water until his confession or death.\n\nExposure\nAs its name implies, this method consists of exposing a victim to the elem\ncould be buried up to his neck, letting any animals, insects or other people kill him slowly.\n\nChair of Torture\nThere are many variants of the chair. They all have one thing in common: spikes cover the back, arm-rests, seat, leg-rests and foot-re\nThe number of spikes in one of these chairs ranges from 500 to 1,500. To avoid movement, the victim’s wrists were tied to the chair or, in one version, two bars pushed the arms against arm-rests for the spikes to penetrate the flesh even further.\nIn some versions a hole under the seat.\n\nThe Tickler\nIt’s a very simple instrument that was used to tear a victim’s skin apart. Due to its shape, neither bones nor muscles were spared. The tool had claws on it sharp enough to tear anything.\nThe Maiden\nIt stands 7 feet tall and is able to accommodate a man. The victim was tied inside the Maiden and one of the two doors was shut, penetrating the victim’s flesh with the strategically-placed spikes that didn’t penetrate any vital organs.\nWhen completely closed, the screams from the victim could not be heard outside, nor could the victim see any light or hear anything.\n\nThe Head Crusher\nWith the chin placed over the bottom bar and the head under the upper cap, the torturer slowly\nthe screw pressing the bar against the cap. This resulted in the head being slowly compressed.\n\nRats\nThe victim was completely restrained and tied to the ground or any horizontal surface. A rat was then placed on his stomach covered by a metallic\ncontainer. As the container was gradually heated, the rat began to look for a way out through the victim’s body. Digging a hole usually took a few hours of \nagonizing pain for the victim. The almost invariantly resulted in death.\nThe Wheel Torture\nThe device consists of a large wooden wheel with many spokes. The victim’s limbs were tied to the spokes and the wheel itself was slowly revolved. Through the openings between the spokes, the torturer usually hit the victim’s hones. §\nOnce his bones were broken he was left on the wheel to die, sometimes placed on a tall pole so the birds could feed from the still-living human.\n\nFoot Roasting\nThe victim’s feet were imprisoned in the stocks and then red-hot coal was placed right\nthem. When the subject was interrogated a screen was put between the heat and his feet acting as relief. If he refused to confess, his bare feet were exposed to the flames. The torture progressed until the victim’s feet were charred to the bone.\nThumbscrew Torture\nThe victim’s fingers were placed inside the instrument and slowly crushed as the torturer turned the handle on top. This method was primarily used to extract confessions as it was both painful and very lasting.\nThe Heretic’s Fork\nThe instrument consists of two forks set against each other that penetrated the flesh under the chin in one end and the upper chest in the other. As usual, this instrument didn’t harm any vital points; thus avoiding death.\nLead Sprinkler\nAt first sight, it looks like a holy water sprinkler, but in reality it’s a bit more complex. The torturer poured molten metals in one end and its contents slowly rushed to the other side where they fell on any part of the victim’s body.\nFlaying\nThe victim’s arms were tied to a pole above his head while his feet were feet were tied below. His body now completely exposed and the torturer, with the help of a small knife, peeled off the victim’s skin slowly.\nKnee Splitter\nAs the torturer turned the handle, the claws slowly slammed against each other mutilating any skin in between. The number of spikes the knee splitter contained varied from three to more than twenty.\n\nCrocodile Tube\nThe victim wa\ninside a tube just big enough for the victim’s entrance. The tube, having crocodile teeth-like spikes, was slowly compressed leaving the victim totally immobilized. The torturer could only see his face and feet. With the help of carbon and fire\nunderneath the tube until he extracted a confession or killed the victim.\n\nThe Brank\nThe device was a metal cage or mask that enclosed the head, often with ridiculous adornments designed to humiliate its victim. Commonly attached with bell to war\nof their approach.\n\nCrocodile Shears\nThe interior design closely resembles a tube containing numerous spikes on both ends. Although it was sometimes used to mutilate the fingers, its most common purpose was to cut arteries.\nThe Copper Boot\nFirst, the torturer placed the victim’s feet inside the boot and secured them with chains inside the device. Depending on the crime, the victim could be tortured in many different ways: Molten metals, boiling water, beating it.\nThe Pendulum\nWith the help of a rope, the victim’s wrists were tied behind his back. As the torturer turned the handle, the rope slowly elevated eventually dislocating the victim’s shoulders.", ""),
        StaticBook("Torvin's Crown", "Richord Bearboot", "--------=-=--------The crowning of Torvin Grandaxe\n\nBy Richord Bearboot\n\n1. Omen\n2. Blow of the Horn\n3. Speech\n4. Gifts\n5. Thoughts\n\n--------=-=--------\nThe hours before the beginning of the event were...problematic, to say the list. Long story short, this giant obsidian sphere of varying size would phase in and out of existence, some thought it was the immortal spirit Orgon, others an omen from the\nBrathmordakin, the mistery endured until half of the event, when a man named Alex Silverberg suddenly shouted \"Why is there a giant black ball in the sky?\" then no other recordings seem to exist.\n--------=-=--------\nBack to the topic.\nThe throne room would start to be filled before the actual blow of the horn, because this Lenya Asterya brought food and everyone for some reason was hungry. \nThe tables and benches would start to be filled by people of all race and\nkind: several kinds of Mali, both royals or travellers, a confirmed Enchantry sorcerer, members from many or all dwarven clans (my ears still ring for the Frostbeards' howling), Sutican and Kharajyr merchants, travellers, mercenaries, even the Holy\nEmperor of Oren himself appeared. Some fights erupted, for the tables were supposed to be divided among nations, but all seemed friendly. Then the Grand Marshall, Svardin Grandaxe, called for silence: the Prophet was speaking.\n--------=-=--------\nThis Prophet seemed important, for he was no other than Kardel Irongut, a previous Grand King of Urguan. In the silence, he began waving a stick of burning sage, singing a loud praise in Dwarvish, here roughly translated:\n\"Glory to the Brathmordakin.\" He stops and takes one step forward \"Glory to Dungrimm.\" He steps again, discarding the sage and taking out a phial of water \"Glory to Armakak!\" He steps again, dips his hand in the phial and sprinks the water on the throne's\nsteps \"Glory to Belka and Grimdugan! And glory to Yemekar!\" He steps forward, facing Torvin, the soon-to-be crowned. He lifts the crown over Torvin's head, lifting his chin and enunciating \"Glory to King Torvin!\" And a brief moment of screams, cheering,\nhowling from the Frostbeards erupted, until the prophet stated: \"By the Divine Grace of Yemekarr and his Brathmordakin, forever may they reign, the Brathmordakin's guided will of the people has steered our Kingdom to elect its Divine Kings. For over\nthe years, the sons of Urguan, the chosen among Yemekar's creations have walked the long road towards peace and prosperity. Guided by the Brathmordakin, we have emerged into days of enlightement. Our Grand King, Torvin, inherits a kingdom at the end of a\ntroublesome era. Guided wrongly for many years, only now it's on the right path.\nTorvin Grandaxe, first of his name and chosen of the Urguani people, will continue this legacy. He will value peace and uphold justice, and will lead the people under the\nguidance of Anbella and Dungrimm, to maintain this peace. \nMay we prosper under his reign.\nGlory to Yemekarr! Greet High King Torvin!\" and the room falls again into shouting, howling and cheering. Yet silence is found again, for Torvin has the word:\n\"I will keep this short. Long I've served the nation, as my father before me. I shall bring forth prosperity and maintain the current peace. We shall continue with making the kingdom greater and greater again. After a long time we are finally back on the\nright track.\" But then, the King says the fateful words: \"Let us now celebrate this day with a feast. Get out the ale and meat!\" And the room finally falls into an endless cheering and shouting.\n--------=-=--------\nI sure hope you spend at least one (why not more, tho?) dwarven feast: nothing can describe the scent of ale and meat, the cheering and shouting, the bumps and friendly brawls that these events include. Everything could happen: this time, the same Alex\nfrom before managed to get a boat in the middle of the room, which was confiscated quickly and sold for a thousand Minas. In the middle of the gambling-less party, the Great King starts recieving gifts and meeting friendly faces, a Doomforged lady, the\nHoly Emperor of Oren John Owyn with his legionaries who gifted a symbolic block of ferrum from Johannesburg \"to help in repelling the uncouth Orcish tribes that remain\", a maiden with a cake, a tiny brawl I was yet to understand that luckily didn't fall\ninto axe dueling, a stick from Crevin Grandaxe, a friend of the King seeking help for this Ilthilien, an elf with a banner, another elf, a Frostbeard with a \"polar bear egg\" (someone must research the fauna of this land further), a shield from the\n\"Wardwarves\", his father Fimlin who greets him with an axe from his uncle Morgrim, and in the end a Starbreaker with the \"Hammer of Ograd'ad\", which nearly fell in the decorative molten rock under the throne.\n--------=-=--------\nThe Throne room would now be empty, except for the sorcerer, who gifted us with a rare sight: a flying Orc. Gutz, his name is, seemed to have liked it. \nI want to thank the Grand King Torvin Grandaxe for giving me the honor of recording his day,\nwhich I probably didn't deserve, and I sure hope we can collaborate again one day.\n--------=-=--------", ""),
        StaticBook("Trade Agreement", "Rufus Longhoes", "`x~   The Trade  ~x'\n       Agreement\n\n\nA document as the confirmation between\nThe Independent settlement Mellsburry and The People of Riv'vallel.\n\n\nBoth sides agree with following paragraphs.\n* Both Sides should verify and discuss the Price List of trade.\n\n* Both Sides should follow the code of gentlemen, knowing, that they must be polite to each other, not allowing any aggression.\n\n*Conflicts must be Resolved Immediately\nPrice List:\nfollowing international prices - 1 Iron = 2 Gold = 2 minas.\n\n2 Stacks of Wheat - 3 iron = 6 gold.\n3 Sugar Canes = 1 Iron = 2 gold.\n8 Feathers = 1 Iron\n11 Wool = 1 Iron\n3 Leather = 1 Iron\n5 Carrots = 1 Iron\n5 Potatoes = 1 Iron\n6 Pumpkins = 1 Iron\n3 Beetroot = 2 Gold\n8 Slices of Melon = 1 Iron = 2 Gold\n\n§       Riv'Vallel\n1 bokolo= 30 wool, 10 carrots, 10 leather\n15 planks of wood= 1- wool, 6 carrots, 4 leather\n1 iron tool= 5 carrots, 2 pumpkins, 3 leather\n\n\n\nMembers of Trade Agreement:\nAmbassador and Librarian, Dark Elf, Balduul Exrith of the Tribe of Riv'vallel\n            ~\nTrade Major, Rufus Longhoes, Mellsburry.\nsirca\n\n4th of Sun's Smile 1596", ""),
        StaticBook("Trade Agreement", "Ascan Valein'thill", "`x~   The Trade   ~x'\n       Agreement\n\n\nThe document as the confirmation between\nThe Independent settlement Mellsburry and Ascan Valein'thill.\n\n\n\nBoth sides agree with following paragraphs.\n* Both Sides should verify and discuss the Price List of trade.\n\n* Both Side should follow the code of gentlemen, knowing, that they must be polite to each other, not allowing any aggression.\n\n*Conflicts must be Resolved.\nPrice List:\nFour full carts and a half of raw iron for every alchemist reagent in amount of 30.\n\n       Reagents:\nCrimson Vase - In Plains or Forests, easilly found around poppies.\nDwarf's Pumpkin - Usually found in swamp grass.\n\nDrake's Tale - Found in desert shrubs.\n\nCrouching Feather - Easily found in plains and forest's grass.\nFrost Vine- Found North on snowy areas or mountanious regions, vines.\n\nBlood Lotus- Usually found in dessert shrubs as the Drake's Tail.\n\nLarihei's Fingers- Mountanious or snowy regions among the grass.\nSaffvil- Found in large quantities in swamp grass.\n\nAthin- Found on snowy regions, usually frozen in blocks of ice.\n\n§\nElf's Hair Vine- Found on mountanious or snowy regions, usually on vines.\n\nGoblin's Ivy- In desserts or savannahs, vines.\n\nNether Warts- Commonly farmed.", ""),
        StaticBook("Trade Deal Dwarf", "Jack Bundle", "-=- Trade Deal -=-\n\n- A Full crate of Wood = 64 iron\n- A Full crate of Wheat = 64 iron\n- Half a crate of leather = 64 iron\n- Half a Crate of sugar cane 64 iron\n- Half a Crate Of Feathers = 32 Iron\n\n+ Due Every Week +\nMembers of Trade Agreement \n\n- Elder Jack Bundle\n\n- Grand King Bastion IronHeart Of Urguan\n\n          Sirca\n\n6th of The Deep Cold 1596", ""),
        StaticBook("Traitor Report", "Aaron Hungil", "Aaron Hungil\nMan-At-Arms\nSnow's Maiden\n1591\n\nThere has been a man accused of being a traitor, by a Westerlander. The Westerlander's name is unknown, since I did not have time to ask. The victim of being accused of traitor\nwas named Thomas Mukeet I believe. He seemed innocent. The accuser had no evidence that Thomas was a traitor, he accused him of being with the enemies, when the Westerlander was attacked on the road by 'bandits'. The Victim showed no signs of doing so. He\nwas let free aswell as the accuser.\n\nSigned\nAaron Hungil\nMan-At-Arms", ""),
        StaticBook("Tranquility", "Tethys Ilifina", "The Rekindled Grove.\n\nA lovely place. Secluded, separate from the horrors of the overworld.\n\nDespite the centuries we have spent buried beneath here, hunted by our kin as 'draoi', I will always treasure the beauty of nature. We meditate here-\n-when on a lost mind, or simply when in need of rejuvination.\n\nI continue to encourage Sister Fox to spend more time within here, rather than in her studies. But she insists she's found a breakthrough. A 'portal' of some kind I've been told.\nLion seems unconcerned. He lends his support to Fox when needed, but usually spends his time buried within games and trivia while my sister is busy.\n\nI always found it ironic though. Despite how different we've always been, Aila and I share the-\n-same blood.\n\nThough we grew distant, probably because of Lion. But she always got what she wanted in the end.\n\nShe's been acting strange lately however. I fear her studies are affecting her too much. To the point where even I-\n-can't seem to aid her, and I was the best the Gardens had.\n\nFox needs a break and some silence. Tranquility. Otherwise we'll need to make amends with our kin, and get her back to the mountain. At least, if we do, I can grab my old notes.\n- Sister Owl.", ""),
        StaticBook("Transfiguration", "Sarrion", "Transfiguration\n---------------->\n\"And so we learn to change the world around us, as if gods played with toys.\"\n-Sarrion\n----------------<\nWritten by:\nSarrion Zytiaear\nTransfiguration is under the school of Arcane Alteration, an art widely known for it’s use of Transmutation. This magic is known to have it’s user have the hands of one who match those of higher power,\nallowing them to shift properties of materials in which they had intently studied to their very will following the simple but so complex law of Equivalent Exchange. An art used by those who have minds that match brilliant scholars of old,\nthey are tasked with solving intense equations in their head in order to transmute their desired effect on the material, knowing the mass of the quantity transmuted as well as the alchemical make up, to those who witness such events just see it\nas a glow of aura, and the object magically changes. Transfiguration breaks down into three lesser schools of spells, the first would be Transmutation.\nTransmutation is the art of changing a material's properties to the users will following the art of Equivalent Exchange, as explained before, one cannot turn Ferrum to Gold, or make a blade out of a nugget of Ferrum,\nand matter cannot be destroyed, only broken down in the art of Deconstructive Transmutation, breaking a material down to a smaller form. The next school would be Enchanting, a mystical art that has intrigued the descendants for ages.\nEnchanting is the art of shaping mana crystals for use, as well as enspelling these crystals with a desired command, or in complex situations, entrap even other spells into the crystals captivity, encasing it to the command of the enchanter.\nThey say these crystals of old have always held high power in this art, for ages enchantments have been used for devices that only one could dream of, or artifacts of destruction such as weapons imbued with spells.\nOnly the enchanter may understand the enchantment that he has created, another would take many years of time to even remotely understand the complexity of another mages work. Finally, the last school of this art is Warding,\nanother mystical and complex art that allows it’s user to, the naked eye, completely neutralize spells. Warding comes in two main ways to cast, Wards themselves can be casted as an area of effect\nthat neutralizes the magic that the mage is casting against from being ever casted, this kind of ward can be enchanted into gems, in elven culture these gems would very commonly be integrated into beautiful jewelry.\nThe second commonly used ward is an Abjuration, a quick spell casted by the mage to ‘destroy’ another mages spell mid-cast. In order to actually ward a spell\nyou must entirely understand the magic that you are warding, which takes years of study for that specific school of magic. The common red lines of this magic are as follows, You must /always/ follow equivalent exchange,\nYou must entirely know the magic you are warding against, and you can only transmute a realistic proportion that you can handle, and of course as always with any Alteration one cannot transmute organic material.\n---------------\nEnd.", ""),
        StaticBook("Translations", "RogueSpectr3", "{t, ƒ:ªº£ ñ.t:c .ø,}\n\n[t.£ ûe:ç :º e, ñ.ô, ñ.nü| ƒ'ª t, u':ô .nô t, ,ñö£:n,ºº d,i'û t, u':ô û,ª, e:º £' c'ññ.nô]\n\n[t,ü û,ª, ô\"º£ .nô e, û.º .º . º\"nd,.ñ| ô,ƒ:n:nø .£ i.º£ t,:ª ê.ö,]\n[.º û.º d,ƒ'ª,| t.£ ûe:ç :º e, ñ.ô, .ø.:n| û:t t, º'ªª'û 'ƒ º\"ni:øe£ ª,ñ.:n:nø \"n£ª,.£,ô .nô \"nû,ic'ñ, £' t, ô,,ö c\"ªª,n£º 'ƒ t, º,.]\n\n[º\"ç ô:ª,c£:'ni,ººn,ºº :º .n.t,ñ. £' e:ñ| ûe' :º i:n,.ª]\n[t,º, .ª, £' d, E:º £ª:\"ñöeº .nô E:º ƒ.:i:nøº| ñ.nü £:ñ,º 'u,ª]\nThe first mathic age\n\nThat which is he made many, for the void and the emptiness below the void were his to command\n\nThey were dust and he was as a sunbeam, defining at last their shape\nAs was before, that which is he made again, with the sorrow of sunlight remaining untreated and unwelcome to the deep currents of the sea\n\nSuch directionlessness is anathema to him, who is linear\nThese are to be His triumphs and His failings, many times over\n{t, º,c‘nô ñ.t:c .ø,}\n\n[t, ƒª.c£:‘nº ‘ƒ t.£ ûe:ç :º e, .ª, d.ªª,ô ƒª‘ñ ,n£ªü]\n\n[t, ‘t,ªº e.u, t,:ª ô,u:c,º ‘ƒ û.ª .nô ô:º“n:‘n| ô,ƒ:n:æ t,ñ .º ûe.£ t,ü .iû.üº e.u, d,,n| t, c.ª,£.S,ªº ‘ƒ t,:ª ƒ.£,]\n[t,ü ê‘“£ .nô öi,.ô .nô ‘ƒƒ,ª t,:ª u‘:c,º £‘ t, e,.u,nº| d“£ t,ü .ª, .º t, ô,,ö c.u,º d,øø:æ ƒ‘ª º“ni:øe£]\n\n[t, û.ü :º ê“£]\nThe second mathic age\n\nThe fractions of that which is he are barred from entry\n\nThe others have their devices of war and disunion, defining them as what they always have been, the caretakers of their fate\nThey shout and plead and offer their voices to the heavens, but they are as the deep caves begging for sunlight\n\nThe way is shut\n{t, t:ªô ñ.t:c .ø,}\n\n[. ‘n, £,.ªº ƒª,, t, di:nôƒ‘iô ‘ƒ t, .düºº ƒª‘ñ t, ,ü,º ‘ƒ t, ö.ª£º]\n\n[:£ :º .º :£ û.º]\n\n[t, i:øe£ .nô i:øe£º .nô i:øe£:æ ‘ƒ t,:ª êª:n,º ƒª,, t,:ª º:øe£| t.£ t,ü ñ.ü di:nô ‘t,ªº]\n[û.ª .nô ô:º“n:‘n .ø.:n º“øø,º£º :£º,iƒ| .nô t, i:n, :º ñ.ô, .º .n “nc‘“n£.di, º,ª:,º ‘ƒ ö‘:n£º| .ii :n c‘nƒi:c£ û:t t,:ª ƒ,ii‘ûº]\n\n[.ii û:,iô:æ t,:ª i.û]\nThe third mathic age\n\nA one tears free the blindfold of the abyss from the eyes of the parts\n\nIt is as it was\nThe light and lights and lighting of their shrines free their sight, that they may blind others\n\nWar and disunion again suggests itself, and the line is made as an uncountable series of points, all in conflict with their fellows\nAll wielding their law", ""),
        StaticBook("Translocators", "Archmage Haadi", "~*~\n      On the creation\n    of translocators\n                  -\n\n\n\n              \\o/\n              -O-\n              /o\\\n[!] Along the page you see many strange markings and drawings. They look to be rough copies, at best. There appears to be some sort of archway built of stone, below it, several odd circular schematics, or perhaps a map. Next to the map, the phases of the\nmoon trail along.\n\n[OOC] View in browser:\n\n tinyurl.com/slatrop\n-------------------\nAn odd name, indeed. Though, the actual device is far more mysterious and eldritch in nature. Translocators, Lori Oathcast refers to them as. Crumena took to calling them closets, as per their birthplace, the closets within Rasmot's magical porta-potty.\nRegardless, the process for creating these translocators is a fairly complex ritualistic one that involves both a skilled Void Translocationist with knowledge of the subject, and a fairly powerful enchanter capable of binding the spell to the locations\nin question.\n---\nCreation\n\nAn enchanter holds the magic to the spot. One who knows how to send matter to the Void and bring it back again must have learnt to create what is like a 'gateway' into the Void. More than just the item itself, but anything that touches it. Even\nair. Then again you do it on the other end and the mage attempts to pull the block back through the Void and the enchanter binds that to a doorway or pillar or something. In short, one must reach into the Void and pull out an open space.\nMaintenance\n\nAfter time, it will need a mana supply or one end will fizzle out before the other and create an endless hole. It's advised then that you have the enchanter available fairly often to refill whatever large mana gem or crystal you wish to power\nthe translocators' magic with. As far as i'm aware, this would be the only option, unless one would be able to get ahold of Kalameet's notes on the mana obelisk. For the ignorant, this is large pillar in which sums of mana are stored for use. The mana\ncannot be pulled out by any means by a magi to fuel their own spellcasting, but instead it exerts energy needed to power enchantments in the area. I'd elaborate further, though i'm only going off of what i've seen myself.", ""),
        StaticBook("Translocators p2", "_Elad_", "Translocators Mk.1:\n\nFirst Observations-\n\nThere appears to be a delay on the appearance of entities through a set of portals, but it otherwise works just as Rasmot's closets had. The creation of the portal at first results in a great\npulling force towards the opening. Such an effect may be troubling to observe, but otherwise seems harmless. Further tests may be required. Organic matter has yet to be tested for transportation, but normal objects as stated transport successfully.\nAn era of magic has dawned, and we are the Harbingers of the future.\n\nHuman Trials-\nThe first guinea pig passes through the gateway as I write. We are hopeful, but it is uncertain whether or not the elf quite literally walks into his own death.\nFootnote:\nIn waiting, we have coined this delay in translocator transportation with the name \"lag\". \n\nHuman Trials Cont.-\nGlacio has passed through the portal. We watched with anticipation for his return, and a few elven minutes later, there\nhe was. This new delay still brings concern, but i'm certain with some manner of tinkering, and perhaps more exotic and rare gems, it can be lessened. Organic and non-organic manner is officially clear for teleportation.\nNew developments in world events render the translocator useless. These 'tomes of power' have made my invention defunct, and now I am stuck with nothing more than a fancy arch. Shame.", ""),
        StaticBook("Traveler Of Seas", "Dorin Starbreaker XII", "Traveler Of Sea's\n\n A Tale Of A Dwarf at               Sea\n\n\n\n\nBy:Dorin Starbreaker\n\n\n\n           1288\nThe year was 1160, and the time was of winter. The fire was roaring and the crys could be heard all throughout the village. But not every cry was coming from screaming villagers, but one coming from a female dwarf, Summer Starbreaker, giving birth to a\nnew dwarf. Along side her, holding her hand was Gherren Irongut. The baby was almost out when a orc raider came in and charged her, but he got no where near close as Gherren threw a fireball at his face, killing him. The baby was almost out and Gherren\ngrabed the babys body as it came out.\"w'at is it, a boy or girl?\". asked Summer \"A boy, w'at s'ould we call 'im 'oney?\" said Gherren \"I don't kn'w, 'and 'im over and i'll dicide.\". Gherren hand over the newborn, still in his birthday suit. The mother\nlooked at her new child, and said \"You know, i t'ink 'e look's like a Dorin... Yes Dorin Starbreaker.\" Don't ye t'ink 'e s'ould be called Irongut?\"asked Gherren, \"No... i want him to have my last name and be a excelent magic user... just like you!\".\nGherren though for a second, and how this could effect the baby in the future, but he did'nt think long as he had to get the baby to safty, He looked over to his wife, something was wrong however... He did not notice it untill now, but the baby had been\ncrying still in his mothers hands. Gherren knew she was having trouble breating but he did not think it was this bad... She had died. A tear droped from his face, but he did not think long, for the baby still had to be taken to safety... The docks!\nGherren grabed the baby and wraped him in a blanket, then started to run for the docks. While he was runing, he decided to hold the baby in one hand and focused for a moment, with his right hand up, a few seconds of running and a flame appeared in his\npalm, lighting the path that was dark untill now. He ran, and he could see the docks and all the light's coming from the now leaving boats's. He was just about to get off of the path onto the dock when a orc shaman appeared, and he shouted at Gherren\nwho stayed his distance as the orc shouted in a accent he could not understand. After a moment, the Shaman lifted his hand and the sky darkend up with cloud's, lighting started to spark through them... Gherren had to think fast.\nHe closed his eyes, the lightnig flaring in the backround, he concentraded and everything became quite. He stuck his hand up the fire going out, and water started to spout around Gherren and the baby, and as fast as the water had appeared, lightning\nflashed and struck the water, and the water fizziled and started to buzz, Gherren quikly made the water disapper along with the lightning. He looked up at the Shaman, who game a look of impress, but he still wanted to kill them, and he raised his hand\nagain. Gherren took fast action and put his hand up as well, and a blue flame appeared, small at first, but it quikly grew to the size of a softball, then it grew to a purple state, and the heat grew, wind started to form around it as it comsumed the air.\nHe looked to his foe, and smirked, throwing the ball, the shaman tried to run, but the Evocationest moved his hand, the fire following his command. The ball struck the orc's back and he fell down, his cloth's burned off and his skin singed to the bone.\nGherren smirked and then started to run again, he passed the dead orc and smirked. Gherren had gotten to the dock in time for the last boat, and handed the newborn over to the captin of the boat, he told him his name and said he was to be taken to his\nGrandfather, at the dwarven capital and taught magic when he get's old enough. Before Gherren could climb upinto the boat however, a arrow stuck him in the back and he fell slightly. Not even a second later, 3 more arrows hit him in the back, he fell, and\nwith his last dieing breath he managed to say \"Go!\". The captin looked and understood... He was not going to make it, he turned around and told his crew to put the sail's up and they pushed off the dock, sailing away as arrows flew at\nthem, the newborn baby crying in the distance.\n75 Years later\n\"Are ye sure ye don't want te come wit' me grandfat'er? I could use t'e 'elp wit' finding me master...\" Dorin said to his grandfather, both f them sitting around a fire, behind Dorin a bag filled with food and fire wood, a pouch set aside with about\n500minas. \"no...no ye need to go on t'is journey yerself. lot's of exsperince you will get from doing t'is on yer own... yer already almost 100... ye need te' proove yerself, so don't come back if ye 'avent masterd any magic!\". The young dwarf looked to\nhis grandfather, he was not surprised, after all, his grandfather had always been this stubern, why would it change now? Dorin was 75 now, and it was time for him to go look for a master to teach him the ways of the fire and water evocationist.\nHe had beed given food and fire wood for his travel's, and 500 minas to travel on the boats. He had everything he needed now and he was ready to set off. \"Alrig't grandfat'er, 'ave it yer way. W'en i get back ill be a Evocationist and ye will be proud!\"\nDorin said. \"Well boy, i 'ope yer rig't, because if ye don't t'en i will surely be disapointed in ye, so make me proud! Now ye better get goen, yer boat leave's at newn does it not?\".\"Aye, it does, well ill be off now.\"Dorin got up from his chair, took\none last look at his grandfather and then walked out the door, heading strait for the dwarven docks, but he was not going for just a ride... But instead a job. He had not told his grandfather that realy he was going to pursue his dream of becoming a\nsailor and crossing the seas, exsploring.\nDorin arrived at the dock and looked for the boat he had been hired to sail on for the next year, taking cargo to the distant islands. He found the ship and looked at the sun, it was newn, and it was time to leave\nhe was late! Dorin started to run for his ship hoping the captin would not yell at him for his tardyness. Dorin quikly found the boat and got aboard.\nThe captin had beed waiting for him. He was a tall man, large muscles, he must have been doing this job\nyears, as his hands were coverd in cysts, and they cracked every time he moved them. He also had a very large beard, almost as large as Dorin's beard, which went down to his chest, although it would be larger if he hadnt shaved it. \"Reporting for duty\nCpt.Theodore.\" The captin looked at the dwarf, \"you can just call me Teddy, your one of my sailors now, and we're in it togeather in the long run, so we might as well get better aquanted. You have anything you might want to be called beside's... What was\nit again? Dorin,Right?\"\nThe Cpt. said \"Aye sir, t'at be my name Dorin Starbreaker, and nay, i don't have anything id like to be called sir.\" Said Dorin. \"You can drop the formalitys, like i said, justcall me Teddy. Now then, your quarters are down stairs\n3 doors to your right, it has a bed, a desk and chair with a window, and a chest. You can get settled in and we will launch off at about 6. So get settled, maybe a nap, and wait untill i say otherwise.\n\n      Later That Day\nDorin was settled in, and started sleep, he woke up about 4 hours later, when he could hear yelling from the captin. It was time to leave and he could hear the other sailors rushing down the hall to the main deck. Dorin got up with excitement, and ran to\nthe main deck along with the other sailors. The captin called them to attention, 6 sailors standing in a row. \"Listen up! We have a newcomer to our ship. His name is Dorin, Dorin why don't you step out now, and introduce yourself to everyone?\"\n\"Aye Teddy.\" Dorin said as he stepped out to introduce himslef to the other 5 sailors, 3 other dwarfs, and 2 humans. \"I am Dorin Starbreaker, and i am hoping to become a member of this crew for a very long time, i 'ope we will all bec'me very well\naquainted on 'ur journey, and i lott forward to many adventures.\" One of the crew members, the one closest to him, put thier hand out and introduced herself. She was a thing shorter dwarf, with brown hair and a mole right by her lip.\nShe was dressed in a leather armor of sorts. \"Nice te meet a fellow dwarf sailor. My name is Diana.\" She said, her voice in a high pitched manner. \"aye nice to meet you as well.\" The captin did'nt want to waste much time on aquatinces and so he introduced\nthe others for them.\n\"from left to write this is Maveric, Sally, and Loki, and Diana has already introduced herself to you.\" Teddy said as he was slowly looking back and forth between them all. \"Aye! Nice te meat ye all, i 'ope we all become great friends\n.\" The captin raised his hand and everyone moved out to the sail's and started to unravel them, letting them loose. Dorin looked to the sun, and before he knew it the captin had already pushed them o the dock nd they were floating to the ocean.\n1 Month later\n\n\"Land ahoy!\" Yelled Maveric atop the crows nest. \"We finaly made it then? How long until we dock?\"Yelled Dorin to the man. \"About 1/2-1 hour until we dock, so get ready, and wake the captin!\" Dorin took note and then went into the\nunderdeck, heading for the captins quarters. He knocked on the door and said \"Captin, you up? We have seen land, we will be ready for docking in about an hour.\"Dorin said. Over the month that Dorin had spent with the crew, he had merged accents\nto fit thiers, and now he sounded as a human. \"Aye, im up. Tell the rest of the crew to get ready, we have a lot of work today.\"\nLater that hour, the boat slowly rocked as it floated ever closer to the dock of the island. It was filled with jungle trees\nand there were lots of cat people, all of them stairing as the boat arrived. The boat finaly touched down and some of the cat people ran up, puting a wooden pallet across the water to the boat as a little bridge. \"Dorin, get that rope and tie us up.\"\nsaid the captin. \"Aye sir!\" Dorin replyed, quikly grabing the boat's rope and tieing them to the dock. \"Get the cargo, we have to take it all the way to the palace up the road. Dorin and the other crew member's, including the captin went down into the\nhull, each coming out with a crate. They took the crates up the road where they finaly got to a palace. They stoped outside the gate where a man walked up and asked them to take them to the celler. They did as the man asked but when they got down into the\nceller, the door shut, they were traped! And they stayed traped for 315 years, at least as slaves that is.\n\n\n\n\n      315 Years later\n\"Get up! you need to get up, get your things and run for the docks!\" Diana shouted \"I can't just leave you! Besides they killed our son!\" DOrin shouted back. \"Aye, but it will take one of us to hold them off for the other to exscape, and you still have\nfamily! I don't!\" Diana shouted back. \"What about me?\" \"yes you are my family, but as i stated one of us has to get of this island, and i could'nt live without you, you can!\" She shouted \"Now go!\"Dorin had to make a desision, but he did'nt want to leave\nher. He decided it was best to leave her and ran, he got to the docks, that had been plated with iron since the last time he had seen it. He got aboard a boat and pushed off, a pair of cats running up yelling at him to give it back. He did not and a tear\nfell from his eye as he heard a scream from the night.\n\n\n\n\n   Dorin Starbreaker\nBook Two Coming Soon", ""),
        StaticBook("Treating Wounds", "Elluna Koortova", "Treating Wounds\n  \n    By Anonymous\n\n\nMy time in the Order of Saint Amyas did teach me a few things, healing wounds is one of them. \nLet’s start using steps,\nStep I - Cleaning the Wound\n\nAlthough that might sound simple, water will not do, for a gash or deeper wounds you'll need something with alcohol in it, like beer or something of the sorts. Of course you need to wash the dirt out\nfirst should it have dirt in it. Remember to clean thoroughly!\nStep II -  Suturing the Wound\n\nFor that you'll need a needle and some thread. Sounds easy right? Well not really, you need a steady hand and you also need to do it by these.. Let’s call them sub steps.\nSub Step I - Heating the Needle\n\nYou need to do that to burn away any remaining illness covering the needle, should it have had any.\n\nSub Step II - Clean the Thread\nYou surely need to do so, as you do not want a single speck dirt in your wound!\n\nSub Step III - Starting the Suture\n\nYou start at, well, the start of the gash or deep wound. (Warning! this does NOT apply for small wounds!)\nYou then sew it closed like you’re sewing a tear in a rag, a messy and bloody rag that screams like a little girl. Nonetheless, a rag. \n\nSub Step IV - Bandaging the Wound\n\nA bandage could be just about anything,\nan old rag (As long as it's clean, obviously!), bed sheets, anything of cloth material. Then you simply wrap it around the wound. Done!\n\nNote: If there's any sign of infection before or after you’ve gone through this process you'll be\nbetter off cutting off the leg.\nCopied by Elluna Koortova.", ""),
        StaticBook("Trial of Words", "Murlocs", "The Trial of Words\n----------------\nBy The Unnamed\n__________________\n|                          |\n|          [][][]          |\n|          []| |[]          |\n|          [][][]          |\n|_________________\nTo be nothing, I am stone.\nTo be fragile, I am glass.\nTo be cruel, I am cold.\n\nIf not a metaphor, what am I?\n\nA heart.\nWith a head, no arms.\nWith a tail, no legs.\nDevoid of a body.\n\nWhat am I?\n\nA coin.\nAt the hour of darkness, they come as a guide.\nAt the hour of light, they are lost themselves.\n\nWho are they?\n\nStars.\nI do not breathe, but I drink.\nI do not run, but I eat.\nI do not drown, but I fear.\n\nWhat am I?\n\nA fish.\nI give life, but I am the villain.\nI have no name, but I am the most known.\nYou ask for me, but I never come.\n\nWhat am I?\n\nTime.\nYou give it,\nBut you keep it.\nIf you turn back,\nIt is meaningless.\n\nWhat is it?\n\nYour word.\nIt runs with no legs.\nIt has a mouth with no words.\nIt has a bed but is sleepless.\nIt does not live, but flows with life.\n\nWhat is it?\n\nA river.\nI devour, but I do not eat.\nYou can fight me, but I am not solid.\nI am feared, but wind is my enemy.\n\nWhat am I?\n\nFire.\nYou can see me, but I cannot see you.\nWhen you look in to me, I will look you in the eye.\nAnd you will see, that I do not lie.\n\nWhat am I?\n\nA mirror.\nIt can carry, but can devour.\nIt is strong, but kisses the clouds.\nIt can be lethal, but gives life.\n\nWhat is it?\n\nWater.\nWhen I weep, I am dark.\nWhen I am empty, I am light.\nWhen I'm angry, I yell.\n\nWhat am I?\n\nA cloud.\nWith a single tooth, he howls.\nThe bane of the forests;\nThough he can be swung as a killer.\n\nWho is he?\n\nAn axe.\nThe men with most want it.\nThe men with little despise it.\nIt is the feeling of death,\nBut is felt by the emotionless.\n\nWhat is it?\n\nNothing.\nThey dig and feed, but never need any air.\nThey can be small, or huge, but never nothing.\n\nWhat are they?\n\nRoots.\nThe young wish for it.\nThe old loathe it.\nIt is the killer of man,\nBut the strength behind wisdom.\n\nWhat is it?\n\nAge.\nIt is, but it is not.\nIt is good, but it is bad.\nTo the left, it is to the right.\nDuring the day, it is night.\n\nWhat is it?\n\nA paradox.\nA lot of bark, but it is never heard.\nIt stands straight, but can be struck down.\nIt is life, but it can die.\n\nWhat is it?\n\nA tree.\nI birth as green; I die as brown.\nI dance upon the littlest gusts of air.\nI drift far from my home as I wither.\n\nWhat am I?\n\nA leaf.\nHe who held the light for those dim nights.\nThe one who stands, but not always.\nGrowing shorter and shorter.\n\nWho is he?\n\nA candle.\nShe sings, but never talks.\nHer shadow passes the ocean, but always dry.\nHer home aloft, but never settled.\n\nWho is she?\n\nA bird.\nIt flies swiftly, but doesn't move.\nFor the young, it is forever.\nFor the old, it is gone.\n\nWhat is it?\n\nYouth.\nTo guard his gold, he bears the sword that is his life.\nA warrior amongst many, to protect and serve.\n\nWho is he?\n\nA bee.\nHe sits on ice, but is not cold.\nHe sits on tables, but is not ashamed.\nHe watches, but does not speak.\n\nWho is he?\n\nThe sun.\nWith wings that do not flap.\nThe dead that carries the living.\nIt cannot see, but it moves.\n\nWhat is it?\n\nA boat.\n*Some sort of gibberish litters this page. It makes you ponder.*\n\n¡ʎoɾuƎ ˙sɔolɹnW ʎq noʎ oʇ ʇɥƃnoɹq 'sǝlppᴉɹ ɯoʇsnɔ ll∀\n\n---\nThe Riddler.", ""),
        StaticBook("True Communion", "Pine Druid Garun", "Many are under the assumption that to commune with the Aspects' beasts and plants, one must use their voice, whether it be the native tongue, or the tongue of the beasts in question. But a plant does not speak. It has not\na language that can be conveyed with words or voice, and neither, in fact, do animals. \n\nTo have a bond with the Aspects is to have a bond with the birds, the beasts, the flowers, the trees. This bond allows what\nwe define as Communion. To commune with an animal is to convey a message, a meaning, a request. This is done, no matter what medium you use, whether vocal or otherwise, through your bond with the Aspects, the bond that was formed during\nyour attunement. It is possible to utilise this bond without having to speak, without having to whistle like a bird or to roar like a lion. \n\nIt is this ability, this direct use of the bond, this empathetic understanding\nof that which you are communicating with, that separates the Elders from the young. Words can be misheard, sounds can be mistaken, but true empathy, a true bond with nature, is always understood.\nThis is what all Druids should strive to be capable of. Once you are truely able to utilise your bond, once you are truely one with yourself, you will be truely one with the animals, truely one with the plants, and through\nthem, truely one with the Aspects. \n\nCommunion is the heart of one's bond with the Aspects, it is a gift that must be fully understood for one to fully understand the world around them.\nMay this insight help push aside one's ignorance, and allow them to persue a proper understanding of the Aspects and their creations.\n\nBlessed be.\n\nScribed by Hierophant Garun, the Pine Druid", ""),
        StaticBook("Truth", "Melia", "How to love a woman\nbuy her stuff", ""),
        StaticBook("Undead Forts", "Albert Bjórk", "Fort Specture\n\nThe Fort it's self is lifeless, you could hear a fly fall in the snow it was so peaceful. However although the fort looked abandoned it gave an ominous feeling to the chest, as if an undead would pop out any minuite. There was a large crane\nwhich seems to have been used for a mine it was placed over. On further inspection the mine looked as if not all the ore had been taken from it, there were still some shiny black veins of coal protuding out of the rock. Also it looks as if Iron could be\nfound deeper in its depths.\n\nMoving into the actual fort feels rather uneasy, there's a sensation which feels as if you're constantly under watch. Large glowing beams would still be shining atop the towers. I couldn't find anyway into these towers\nwhich was odd, I guessed the doors had been filled in. Skulls and black banners would hang all over the forts walls.\nFort Waith\n\nThis fortress was much smaller than Specture, but was build in the same style with the black and red coloured walls. I could find no way into the courtyard as the port cullis was still down. Like specture there was an obvious feeling of being\nwatched, but it was slightly less prominant here. The only sound you can hear is the Swifts chirping in the air.", ""),
        StaticBook("Undead Invasion", "Ebonsquire", "The Undead Invasion of Oren\n\n((Originally written by monkeychez))\nOn a busy afternoon in Oren... Something evil emerged... I was buying an apartment at the time, when a thunderstorm began. Nobody was very concerned, as a thunderstorm is a natural occurence... But when the lightning was more coordinated, and more\nconstant, we knew what was happening. The thunger rumbled the town as the Undead, in Snowy Fields at the time, were getting closer. Men and women hid in their shops and homes, the king and queen in a bakery... A man offered me a staff, to help with my\nmagic. Not too long after, the outskirts of the city were coated with Undead. I swept in, setting the ground ablaze... Parts of the groud reflected the evil we were facing... Giants were stomping about, the chatter of skeleton archers firing... the moans\nof the damned, but they were no match for those who fought. The men and women hacking away at the Undead scum were doing a wonderful job. Our hopes were high when Sage Okonkwo arrived. He was in the towers and trees setting ablaze the other enemies like\nme. After a while of fighting . . . My staff's power was no more, and broke in two. I unsheathed my trusty carbarum sword, and began to slay at the beasts. We cleared the edge of the city, and began to push to the castle... The streets were swarmed, fires\nablazed from every building. I climbed atop the walls and headed towards the castle... When I arrived, the Undead were on top of the castle and remembering seeing the king with his wife, I stormed the castle... When I got inside through a large hole,\nthere were roughly ten others. They were dispatching the zombies inside the castle. I went to take a peek above. Proceeding to climb the flame scorched and horribly battered ladder, there were many Undead on top... I saw High Prince Native\nand the Elven princess, I believe. Anyhow, when I got atop the castle, I charged the closest Undead. A horrible mistake on my side... Anyhow, the Undeads prevailed to an extent... The King was killed, but the whereabouts of his wife are still\nunknown. The Wandering Wizard was able to return the Undead back to the hhell in which they cam from... The badly injured survivors of the battle helped dispatch the rest of the zombies in the city, and snuffed fires. Is Aegis safe? For now... But what is\nto come? Prophets fortell Kal'Urguan is next to be invaded, but that may be rumors, or is it?\n\n\nTHE END", ""),
        StaticBook("Unison", "Shagarath", "-_~_-\n          Unison\n        -__~__-\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWritten by Shagarath\n9th of The First Seed, 1580\nThe past few weeks has been a busy one, for the sighting of an orc in the grove was well discussed among animal life around. The message spread and spread of an... appointment... a deal struck between druid and shaman.\nA Shaman and Druids strode into the Savannah Grove, a meeting of sorts between two rivaling groups for some time. The meeting was one of understanding and peace between the two group\nas the Warlock Shagarath began to explain the common ground between the two groups. In great trust, He called upon the spirits to show the binding unison of the groups and the Spirits answered.\nQiouvor, Lesser Spirit of Trees was summoned by his master Freygoth. He appeared in his avatar: an Ent. A light flash shone, and soon the goliath of leaf and bark stood before them.\n[!] The image of an Ent, a Goliath being of bark and leaf is drawn in great detail. The figure appearing aged, leaning on a tree-sized cane.\nThe spirit then inquired from the shaman, in the Spirit Tongue of Old Blah.“Why did you call for my. Why was I summoned?” Followed by “Do you wish me to kill these?”\nPointing at the children of the forest. The shaman then quickly shouted in reply, putting emphasis on the aspect of learning. For that was the purpose for which he was summoned. To teach… to make understand the ways of the spirits.\n“I have… communed with… your companions..” Qiouvor spoke in common tongue, looking upon the trees of the grove. A halfing named Jeremiah spoke “Wha’d they tell ya?”\n“We will… work in… unison…” Qiouvor spoke as it looked upon the group\nThe spirit then disappeard as it came, leaving but the two roots that were his legs. From then shone a bright emerald hue. For in each of these two roots… seeds were placed.\n“A gift…”\n“A gift from spirits….to aspects”\nShagarath spoke, offering one to the Druids, keeping one for the Shamans of the Angathgûl.\nA gift was given, and the branch of an alliance was received.\nA branch of alliance is once again shared upon the two groups, knowing full well the common ground they stand upon, and in hopes to flourish together rather than tear each other apart.\nUpon departing, the two groups blessed one another:\n“Aspects guide you, Shagarath” Spoke Oo’ri\n“Afar-Ilzgûl, Lûp-Ilzgûl.” Shagarath replied.\n\n\n\nFear the Spirits, Praise the Spirits", ""),
        StaticBook("Unsound Spells", "Anawkin", "Upon Unsound Magic\n\n A relatively weaning magic in the eyes of it's users, Unsound is derived of three basic elements that I shall relay to you today.\n\nFirstly, one must make contact with either a voidal horror or teacher of said magic to obtain this\naltered spellcasting.\n\nSecondarily, you must establish a connection with a fabbled watcher of which haunts your mind fervently. This is done through the horror or teacher's will.\n\nNext, we have the draining effects\nto one's persona, an unsound mage will succumb to a variety of personal afflictions, each of which is dependent upon how the user reacts. This could range from uncoth twitchings, bi-polar disorder and even murder.\n\nLastly, are anomalies,\nwhich are practically rifts to the void. An unsound mage can cast these only when attuned to their observer (( a second connection)) and the effects are rather crippling. They eat everything at a slow pace, but seem to draw towards mana.\nWritten by Orias.", ""),
        StaticBook("Uruk Culture", "PiercingDarkness", "Culture of the Orcs\n-----------------\nBook I, written by Ves\n\n\"May this book serve as a guide to any brave enough to venture into Orcish land. Or any scholar who may be curious of the hostile land to the far south.\"\nChapter 1:\nThe orcish homeland\n------------------\nAs most will know, the territory of orcs is the harsh sands of the desert. They have adapted to survive in such an unforgiving environment, so unless you are an orc born upon the sands, it is\nadvisable to be prepared before heading into the desert terrain, orcs are not the only threat there, thier land is just as harsh and unforgiving as they are. Many foolish adventurers have perished because of lack of preperation.\nThere are very few resources out there in the desert, so it is best to bring what you need to survive, water food and clothing to protect you from the effects of the strong desert sun. If however you are stranded without the supplies necassary\nthere are a few ways of obtaining them. Dehydration may be the most prominent killers in the desert, it is important to drink a lot and drink regularly, finding a stream is the most obvious source of water, however if you cannot find one,\nanother way of obtaining water is digging near vegitation such as the bushes or cacti that are found there, if you dig you will almost certainly find some water, but remember to never drink the sea water of surrounding oceans, that will only make\nthings worse. As for food, you may find small critters or bugs amongst the bushes or under rocks, so long as you cook them, most should be fine to eat, just to not eat the cacti as they are poisonous. Another very important thing is finding some shelter\nin the day, shelter will keep you cool and at night it will keep you warm, the days are hot and nights are cold so it is important to find a place to stay out of the harsh weather as it can have some pretty nasty effects if you are exposed for too long.\nbut is important to remember, that if you are in the desert, you are considered an intruder and will be treated as such, so do not step into orc land without expecting to be approached with a certain amount of hostility.\nChapter 2:\nOrc Clans\n------------------\nOrcs divide themselves into different groups called clans, the best way of explaining what a clan is, is that they are like families. That is why orcs will show such fierce loyalty to thier clan and will\nprotect thier clans with thier lives. Since the orcs left thier city there are too many clans to count, more and more sprout up constantly these new clans are often approached with hostility from the older and more respected clans such\nas Gorkil, Lur, Braduk and Ugluk. Each clan has thier own fort and land, which they develop and protect. Land is often the cause of war between clans, whether it be because one intrudes on another's land, or one clan wants the land owned by a\ndifferent clan. Orcs can either be born into a clan, or inducted by completing some kind of trial, which is different for each clan, often this is followed by some kind of ritual to welcome them to thier new family. Although the clans tend to stay\nout of each others business, they will often meet to discuss important matters and rally together in times of war against a common enemy, such as intruder in the desert or factions that oppose thier race. Each clan has a leader and various\nranks stemming down from there, orcs will earn thier rank by showing promise in battle or through loyalty, another less common way for an orc to gain a rank is for them to challenge another for thier possition, they will then fight for the rank.\nWhen on orc land, it is a smart idea to avoid setting foot in the city or on clan land, as for most clans this is a crime punnishable by death and sometimes something worse.\nChapter 3\nOrcish anatomy\n------------------\nWhen a orc is born and up until it is about eight to thirteen years old, it will look much like the child of any other race, of course larger and with a different coloured skin. It is when an orc\nreaches it's age of development that it takes the form that most people will recoginse. It is at this age of development that orcs take their adult form; generally described as the rapid growth of thick, ivory tusks, darkening and thickening of skin, and\nA greater tendancy to be thrown into Bloodlust. Along with these attributes, Orcs generally become more determined and 'Wise', compared to the cubs. Wise being a very widened term, with Orcs it can be used to tell of their inner sense of 'rightness'.\nBefore the age of thirteen is generally when most Orcs become whitewashes. The cubs are much more thick headed and rash compared to their older brothers (Though these are still much more easily angered than most other races).\nAfter this age, most Orcs tend to bond with their family and clan, and only tend to leave in much more serious circumstances, such as being banished. \nAn Orc's skin is generally thicker than most other races, Kha's included. The rough sands bite their\nHides and slowly but surely make them as tough as leather. Not unsurpisingly, Orcs hate colder climates. Perhaps it's their choice of clothing, or their tendancy to live in the hot badlands, but at any case, a shivering Orc is the only one you'll see in\nThe colder climates of the North and South, usually dressed in a somewhat amusing choice of thick, wooly, bundled clothing. Orcs come in a variety of colours, the most common being green, the rarest being black or even blue.\nChapter 4\nOrcish Customs\n-------------------As a race, the Orcs have certain customs that are shown by all clans. All Orcs hate Whitewashes. Save for those who are banished themselves, whitewashes are hated by all clans and all Orcs, and are hunted\nAs a sport by the race as a whole. Orcs are commonly superstitious, believing the spirits of their dead ascendants watch over to them this day, judging their honour watching their choices with approval, or disapproval, depending on the situation.\nThey see the Humans, Elves, Dwarves and Kha's as lesser races in general, though they have a certain mutual respect for the Dwaves' sturdyness. Various theories have arisen to propose why this is so, with the most generall accepted one being extracted\nFrom an Orcish fable, common to that of the Wandering Wizard. At the time of the four brothers, each had green skin. As the years of war against Iblees raged on, and the bad attributes of each race was shown, slowly the Elves, Humans and Dwarves' skin\nTurned pink; the colour of dishonour and taint, the same of that of the fungi which grow between their toes, often. Black, they see as trecherous and unstrustable, while colours such as purple is the colour of the spirits, and green the colour of life and\nPurity.\nChapter 5\nWhitewashes\n-------------------Whitewashes are somewhat uncommon in today's Orcish culture, though nonetheless hated by the race as a whole. A whitewash is not, as some believe, a nomadic Orc; one without a clan who roames at his free\nWill. A whitewash Orc, commonly known as Wiydwazh by the Uruks, is an Orc that has forsaken his or her own kind, broken their traditions and disregarded their god and beliefs, which generally revolve around Honor and Krug. A Whitewash Orc is hunted his or\nHer whole life (In most cases), by Orcs, and shooed away from any permanent home by any others due to the 'trouble' they bring, trouble being the Orc hunters intent on mounting the Whitewash's skull somewhere impressive.\nThey don't vary at all physically from other Orcs, though it is common for weaker Orcs to be banished from the Uzg, or their clan, due to losing an honor klomp, or something similar. In several cases, Whitewash Orcs can make their way back into the Orcish\nCommunity, usually by varying means, most involving klomps. Additionally, any Orc Shaman that becomes Whitewash loses their powers, since it is foremost fueled by the ancestors and spirits, which generally look down on Whitewashes.", ""),
        StaticBook("Uruk Records", "Thurak'Yar", "Uruk Records\n\nForeword\n\nThe following is to be a record of all notable events of the Uruk people, going on from the 1’st of The Amber Cold, 1501. Although these records focus solely\non events after this date, other relevant information will be included for past context.\n\n\n~Scribed by the Farseer Thurak, of the Yar Clan.\n-First of The Amber Cold, 1501.\n\nThe population of the Uruks has flourished in recent months; some say even to the point where we could once again be held as a major force in the workings of the realm, and yet to what we have to thank for\nthis one cannot rightly say. Some, quite fairly, claim this spike to be attributed to the migration of the Trog (This is the name given to the village situated by the Main Atherian Road) from our capital San’Vitar (Fittingly, “Old City” In Old Blah”).\nAlthough there might be some truth in this, one can find Uruks openly mumbling dissent about the move; even as we’re at our most powerful, we’re at our most vulnerable, for here we have no forts or battlements to make war from, and\nthe looming threat of the Azogs and Oren is something we’re all too aware of. Others say that it is in fact our new Rex that we owe our activity to. Zogrocka’Rax, a Latauman and indeed a turned Dark Shamanism user, took\nup Rexdom from Rix’Rax, who he killed in single combat. He’s taken to a somewhat neutral stance to the war, however he’s actively encouraged brutal combat with those Orcs of the Azog clan, who were banished and are now raiding and\nassaulting our Trog Camp on a daily level. With this, however, comes an issue when we note that Oren has taken up an alliance with these Azogs. Although Zogrocka has not openly declared war, many battles and counter\nattacks have been had involving both Azogs and the men of Oren’s ever growing army. \nOn a less offensive front, the Shamans have been growing in population as the Orcs have, and many new apprentices have been taken\non in recent weeks. The past Wood Elven commander Phaedrus was recently indicted as an honorary Uruk, and has now begun training as the only other Farseer of the Uzg save for myself. Some take this with offense, however I believe with the\ncorrect training the Elf may just be a great Farseer and guide to the Uruk people. \nThe Spirit Realm has been mostly quiet recently, however Ehnrok, the spirit of War, is gaining prevalence once more as his ideals spread through\nthe Uzg and indeed the realm. A dispute has arisen between the spirit Arwa one one of the minor spirits under her control- Laklul. With a whole clan supporting him, the Spirit of Swamps seeks to break off from his overruling spirit of\nfertility, and commanded his followers to effectively neuter themselves as a show of violation to their pact. The Clan is led by none other than Shreck’Lak, and fittingly it is the first clan to be in full worship of a single spirit. If their progress\ncontinues, no doubt the spirit will soon rise to a fully fledged Greater Spirit in the Immortal Realm.\n-Fourteenth of The Amber Cold, 1501.\n\nThe Uruk Hu-Din has been declared Pug in the Rex Zogrocka’s latest preaching to the Uruks of the War Uzg. Hu-Din’Lak was once the most avid supporter of Rex and Farseer Rusk’Dom, and\never since the Doms’ disbandment and the death of Rusk Hu-Din has striven to impeach his own values on the Uzg. Even should these values be honourable and in the best interest of the Uzg, Zogrocka’s leadership has been challenged by them,\nand as such Hu-Din’Lak has been demoted until such time as he desists. Meanwhile, the Rex has openly declared the Uruk’s opposition to the humans of Oren, stating, “The Humans have decided to fight with our Azog enemy,\ntherefore they are treated like an Azog. No mercy will be given to them whatsoever.”\nHe has also condemned the attack of the Druids in response to a recent incident with the Wolf Druid Ouity. In thanks, the Druids have agreed to take\ncare of the wildlife of the Uruk savanna, which has been growing ever since the destruction of San’Vitar, and may soon be attractive poaching grounds for nearby human settlements. \nIn other events, Zar’roc’Yar has been appointed as a temporary\nTargoth, and both Shreck’Lak and Grazadh'Gorkil were promoted to Warbosses in response to the Laks’ growing population, which now stands as the most populous clan of the Uzg. The Uruks are currently neutral to the Dwarves, Dunamis,\nthe Kharajyr, and the Caliphate, and this isn’t looking to change any time soon with the Rex set in his position on the war.", ""),
        StaticBook("Uruk Requests.", "Thurak'Yar", "The Requests of Thurak'Yar (And the Shamans)\n\n=-=-=-=-=^=-=-=-=-=\n\nThe Siege of Sanjezal (Arch-Mage Aluuvia)\n\nMalog's Proverbs\n\nYar agh Nagii\nContemplation (I + II)\n\nPlay Orc\n\nSpirit Tales (I + II)\n\nHis Fungi\n\nAn Orc's Life\n\nBraduk Rhinos\n\nScaddernak\nOn Shamanism (I + II)\n\nImmortal Spirits\n\nAscended\n\nAura\n\nMental Defence\n\nNature of Memory\n\nOn Mana Anchors\nFi'hiiran'tanya\n\nTelekinesis (I+II+III)\n\nEWOROENLETEA (Translocation V2)\n\nA Book \n(Conjuration I, Joe)\n\nGreat Sandworm\nVourukhs\n\nMundane Healing\n\nThe Orcish Plague\n\nMori Language\n\nOld Elven\n\nElixir of Life\n\nHarbinger's Tale (ALL)\nOn Dragons\n\nDragonkin\n\nDragur\n\nAcerbus' Journal\n\nGathering Herbs\n\nGronkkston\n\nDiary of Mukar\nFall of Hanseti", ""),
        StaticBook("UrUKz GuID", "Bogrum'Lak", "Diz izh WeY tuH pEk uhp Da UruK Wumun.\n\nBai BOgRum.\ndIz IZH StUP AsH tuH Da WUMun GuDe.\n\nSTup Ash.\n\nfUInd dA wUmUN laT wUnd, UzE uR Lukz tUh pEEp ef Shi WuHNd LaT.\n\nWuRKz Un TwiGGEhZ.\nStUp DuB\n\nKlUmP dEm, Ef dEy sTel alIv, dEn KeP dem.\n\nEf Nub.\n\nFlaT dEm.\nStUp GaKH.\n\nMeK heeR uR zNaGA.\nNuW uH HAf a gRiL uF laTz Uwn.\n\n\nBud LaTZ Weel Neba bI leIk BoGRUm'LaK.\n\nUnLEZ LaTZ WUnD tuH BI BoGrUm'LaK ZnAGA.\n\nUKE GUG'YE.\n-BOgRuM'LAk", ""),
        StaticBook("V Veritatis 6", "Jacob Chapel", "Verbo Veritatis\nSixth Edition\n23-3-1480\n\nIn this edition:\n*Knights Rebellion\n*City of Dwarves reclaimed\n*The Karovian Column\n*Words from the Emperor\nAnd much much more!\nReporters needed for the newspaper\nDear readers, as always we are in great need of reporters for our esteemed newspaper, especially now Ralph Riley has stepped down from his position because of his prolonged battle with illness. Since patronage has\nbeen secured, we are able to pay much better rates for articles. As a reporter you can expect up to 500 minas per article!\n\nThe work is freelance, and you are paid per article delivered. Please contact Jacob Chapel if you are interested.\n((Contact me (Pepernoot) ingame or on the forums!))\nThe Knights Rebellion\nIn one of the greatest moves of treachery in our time, Maric Varodyr, once Grand Knight of the realm, and part of the Order of the Red Dragon has taken up arms against the Empire. After word had reached the Emperor that Maric was\nconspiring against the integrity of the Empire, intending to break it up into pieces. Immediately the Emperor dismissed him from his position, but Maric fled to the Keep of Angren and barricaded himself in there, along with a few rebels.\nOur grand Emperor demanded Maric to leave the keep, but the traitor defied these orders and claimed the keep for his own. Hiding inside the keep he proclaimed himself King of Renatus, a claim so audacious and without any real claim to the title,\nhe must surely be absolutely mad drunk on power.\n\nAs of now the traitors are still hiding behind the walls of Angren, awaiting their certain and inevitable death. Quoting our Emperor: \"Do not recognise this traitor who has so aptly deemed fit to call\nhimself King without any form of legitimization from the Church or the faith. Fight back against the foreign tyrants who would dare infringe upon our sovereignty, despite their signing of various treaties intended to ensure such would not be so.\nYet do not fight because of who you are, Highlander, Heartlander or Farfolk. Fight because by the creator above, you will never allow such a spineless snake-tongued worm as Maric Varodyr to sit upon the throne of humanity”\n\nCarry on Carrion!\nThe City of the Dwarves reclaimed\nSince the reconquest of the dwarven capital, the dwarves have been very busy to rebuild and reclaim their old capital. Nearly all signs of the Undead occupation have been removed and a lot of work is being done to\nrebuild the homes of the dwarves, under the guidance of Lord Balek Ironguy and Thurland Grandaxe, the architects of the arts guild. The new city will be completely situated in the mountains, with farmland in the valley in front of the entrance to\nthe mountain home.\n\nThe new city has been named Kal’Karaad, and it should be ready for habitation in 2 saints days ((11 November)). We of the Verbo Veritatis wish the dwarves happiness and prosperity in their new capital, and hope that it may last\na thousand years. Sadly the dwarves have not returned our goodwill to help in the current rebellion of the knights, and have retracted their offer to come to our assistance.\nFormation of the House of Magnates\nThe Emperor has formed Oren's first legislative body! Known as the House of Magnates, it consists of representatives, or magnates, of all the nobles of the realm, along with the burghers of Petrus. The higher one's\ntitle is, the more representatives and votes, one gets. The body votes on appointing various ministers, akin to privy councillors, who make up the government. It is led by the Lord Chancellor who acts as virtually any under-king to the Emperor,\nworking on the day to day affairs of the realm. Currently the Chancellor is Joachim var Sarkoz, a learned barrister from the court of King Francis who has been appointed by the Emperor to help facilitate the establishment of the Magnates while the nobles\nand emperor focus on the military expenditures at hand. He shall rule for three years, before he is either voted in again by the various Magnates or a new Chancellor, or known more colloquially as the Prime Minister, is appointed by the Magnates.\nLet us hope Prime Minister Joachim can guide our country to glory!\nHoly ward over Petrus\nOn the 10th of The First Seed, mages have cast an undead weakening ward over our grand city of Petrus. The main effects of this is to dispel the effects of their magics. The mages creating the magic, one of them being the ancient\nwizard Blundermore, forged a magic crystal and lifted it up into the air, defying gravity. From the crystal lights and other magical effects originate, bringing a feeling of safety and calm over the city.\nThe populace can rejoice over this noble effort of the mages, and it is hoped that the ward will keep the undead away for a long time.\nThe Karovian Column\nA Tragic End\nOver to the news from Karovia this week, and it appears that her husband’s reluctance to give her a child has finally pushed poor Lynn Rovin over the edge. The other day, her body was found lying at the bottom of\na cliff face, her stomach punctured with knife wounds. Though it has not yet been confirmed, early evidence appears to suggest that the blows were self inflicted. What an unpleasant end to what could have surely been a most enduring marriage...\nThis newspaper would like to extend its deepest condolences to her widowed husband, the Imperial Prince, Aleksandr Carrion for his tragic loss.\n\nIn other news, yet more spook-filled sightings of the Imperial Prince’s late twin brother, Yakov Carrion!\nAs reported in Edition Five, little is known of Yakov’s decision to betray Oren to the Undead scourge, though recent events suggest he has returned to to seek vengeance against close members of his family. We can only hope that the guard remain viligant\nin these dark and dreary times. In brighter news however, Aleksandr is said to have found a new wife to replace his dearest beloved. Rumour has it that this is said to be Lynn’s very own sister! We suspect it shall not be long before we have another\nroyal wedding on our hands!\n\nSo dear readers, with his wife’s demise and his brother’s fall to the Undead, where will Aleksandr turn now? Find out next time in the Karovian Column of Verbo Veritatis, Edition Seven!\n-Our anonymous source in Karovia\nWords from the Emperor\nTo the loyal fellows of Orenia,\n\nThough some minor rebellion plagues our lands, a simple matter it will be to drive out the meager forces assembled under the traitor Maric Varodyr.\nSuch a petty uprising is of little consequence in the grand scheme of our Holy Empire, such writing on this day regards the welfare of our capital, Petrus.\n\nWhen I had first been elected by the Electorate to serve as Emperor,\nPetrus had been little more than a ghost town. Now I am happy to say Petrus is the single most populated city in not only our realm, but of the world itself. This cannot be attributed to I, but to the true heartlanders of Petrus who have graced this city\nwith life. Petrus stands as the jewel of our modern world, in not just the strong economy, but in terms of cultural regards, social mobility, and military might. \n\nNowhere else in Athera can one find a public library with such a vast array of knowledge\navailable to the public, nowhere else in Athera maintains our efficient system of free food, and nowhere else in Athera upholds a city guard as do our Wardens of the Imperial Watch, a Watch at current roster twenty-four men strong.\nThe average daily income to Petrus coffers is 5,000 minas. The average yearly budget for the Imperial Watch is 20,000 minas. Petrus maintains a budget of 44,000 minas for building improvements and public works. Average yearly tax income is 4,000 minas.\nPetrus holds 53 separate plots, of which only 8 are not filled at the time of this writing; 43 plots had paid taxes last tax cycle. Truly the economic structure of Petrus is unmatched by any city in the world, and this does not take into account the great\nndustrial capability of our Holy City. Within Petrus are produced the finest weapons and armor in the entire world, with the most efficient labor force in the world harvesting vast quantities of wheat, ores, stone, and wood everyday.\nUnlike the treasuries of many other nations, the majority of goods produced are not stashed away but sold as surplus to the citizens of Petrus, weapons and armor worthy of Kings can be found for open sale and in quantity, at a pittance compared to what\none may find at the cloud temple auctioneer.\n\nThough there is much more than just numbers to Petrus, I hope this has given some insight into our holy Capital and I am proud for all the fellows of Petrus who make our city the jewel of the world.\nCreator watch over us all,\nTuvya Sigismundovic Carrion\nReturn of the Order of Saint Amyas\nThe Order of Saint Amyas has been reformed, with Adrian de Bar as its new Grand Master. Shockingly though, Adrian quickly pledged his support to Maric’s traitorous cause and was convicted of treason.\nAfter persuasion by Oren, and a lot of mercy on the side of the Emperor, he was returned to the fold quickly though. Hopefully he is wise enough to not betray Oren again.\nWe hope that the Order will become a beacon of purity and righteousness, especially in these dark times, and that honest God-fearing men fight for its cause.\nPetrus tavern under new management\nAs the old Throdo has not been able to properly take care of the tavern at the central square in Petrus, the tavern has been granted to a new owner. The tavern has been renamed “the Drunken Dragon”,\nand it has been quite busy indeed.\nThe Verbo Veritatis wishes Sam good luck with running the tavern, and may many drinks be drunk!\n{\"text\":\"\"}\nWe hope you enjoyed the newspaper, and remember: Athera’s greatest bookstore, “Books of Oren”, is the publisher of this great paper. There are shelves upon shelves of amazing books for incredibly low prices. Visit us at Abbey Road 13, Petrus!", ""),
        StaticBook("V. Veritatis 4", "Ralph Riley", "Verbo Veritatis\nFourth Edition\n\nIn this edition:\n\n*Ithelias Literature Award\n\n*Great Alrasian Purchase\n\n*Orc Attack in Karovia\n\n*New Orenian Anthem\nAnd more!\nIthelias Literature Award\nBooks of Oren, home of the Verbo Veritatis newspaper, is proud to announce the “Ithelias Literature Award” given to the most noted writers among Athera. The award is given to those that excel in the art of combining words to\nknit together an exceptional piece of literature, worthy of the honours of being recognized as a true masterpiece. A grand novel, a poem, every kind of literature is valid to be picked. The award will be given every Saint’s month and it will be funded\nby Books of Oren and his Highness, our emperor Tuvya Segismundovic Carrion to promote culture among our people. \n\nThe award will be a document stating the prize, and a sum of minas for the three best works of art.\nThe rewards are:\n\nFirst prize: 2000 minas\nSecond prize: 1000 minas\nThird prize: 500 minas\n\nTo join the competition send us a bird, with the book included, or just visit the store at Abbey Road 13a, Petrus.\nWinners will be announced in two Saint’s weeks!\nThe Great Alrasian Purchase\nWith the disappearance of the peoples of Alras in recent days, Emperor Tuvya made hasty moves to purchase the old lands of Alras from a local squatter. Recently annexed and renamed as the duchy of Karovia,\nPrince Aleksandr Carrion now sits as ruler of the new and burgeoning town, a proper homeland for the Raev in Oren being established.\nOrc Attack in Karovia\nIn Karovia, which recently joined the Empire of Oren after the Great Alrasian Purchase, orcs assaulted a defenseless young man. While this was happening Jacob Chapel walked in on them. He tried to hide, but was quickly\nfound by the savages, and captured and kicked to the ground. There were three, a large male orc, an apparently pregnant orc and a goblin. They went by the names of Malgroth, Shadback and Smelleh, respectively.\nAs they were busy extorting Jacob Chapel, the Emperor Himself arrived at the scene, covered in his Blessed Armor of St Augustus, wielding his Holy Axe of the Seven Skies. The male orc was quick to rush towards Tuvya, but his broadsword was no match\nfor the armour. After a short fight the Emperor’s sword was covered in orc blood. However, the goblin had just struck his pickaxe into the young lad’s chest, blood covering the ugly gobbo and the lush grass. The pregnant orc and the goblin quickly\nbolted off, Tuvya chasing after them, and killing at least one.\nThis was no help to the lad though, as he lay dying in the grass. He passed soon after Jacob Chapel took his confessions, and lies in an unnamed grave just outside Petrus. He died on the 3rd of the Deep Cold, 1474. May the Creator bless his soul.\nCaroline Hightower has composed the anthem of Oren\nThe new anthem of Oren, Thirty to One, has been composed by the great talent that is C. A. Hightower. Its great lyrics will surely inspire the peoples of the Empire and fill their hearts with pride.\nThe anthem is available for purchase at Books of Oren, Abbey Road 13a in Petrus. Contained within are the lyrics and instructions for the music.\nAmoss’ Crimes\nPart 1: Assault on the Uruguan Ambassador\nLegend tells of a white wizard, namely Amoss. Many say he is a psychopath, others call him a cannibal. I am here to confirm that both of these are true.\nTwas a cold and wet day. As I was heading to Petrus, a gentleman with a white beard approached me, asking me for help. I of course was obliged to help him find somewhere dry to stay. I offered my office and we began walking.\nAs we were walking I was kicked to the ground and bound in chains. He gagged me and I was dragged to the Orc capital. I believe this was an attempt to ignite the conflict between Orcs and the other races. Luckily a man witnessed this event and alerted\nEraborn Greyhame. He gathered an army of Humans and Dwarves to come to my rescue. I was rescued, but my captor still lurks out there. I feel that he is a direct threat to Oren and to his Majesty Tuvya himself.\nUpon returning to Petrus with many wounds from the attempts of Amoss to eat me, I was in a dire position. Luckily I was helped by a very kind gentleman, Jacob Chapel, who along with the city doctor saved me from the brink of death.\nAmoss’ attempts to kill me were not at an end though. He corrupted my own Co-Ambassador with a large sum of money, and had him try to assassinate me. Several shots were fired at me, and he also attempted to stab me.\nLuckily the he was captured by the guard forces of Petrus and justice was served.\n\nA report by Ambassador Grigor of Clan Grandaxe\nPart 2: Treason in Oren\nAmoss’ crimes didn’t stop with the attempted assassination of Grigor Grandaxe, soon after the last events Faramith Greyhame released information about a conspiracy, of which Amoss, Eraborn Greyhame, and the rangers were part of\nTheir plan was to assassinate Yukov Carrion, beloved son of the Emperor, and after that try and seize Petrus. Their plan was foolish and the mad man named Amoss was captured quickly.\nWords from the High Pontiff\nGreetings to the progeny of Horen,\n\nI bid you lot fair weathers and fair harvest. I write to address the peoples in a distinguished press, the Verbo Veritatis, in hopes the Pontificate can expand its listening base to those\nmore secular. And many have been, thanks to the ill-efforts of my predecessors, who've distanced many from the Church's goals.\n\nYet I hope to act with clemency and charity, and insure that the Church serves the denizens in Oren, enlightening them of the\nfaith, administering their poor and sickly, writing its histories, ministering a breadth of education, and establishing the epicenter of Oren's culture, intellectualism, and spirituality.\nAt hand, the firstmost goal of our Church is to train and induct new members of the priesthood, and finish the translations of the scripture. The former has been going great, and the Church number swells to new heights not seen in decades, though many\nstill are recruits and hence ill-fit to wholly minsiter. We hope to teach these Acolytes and Deaconry every two to three saint's days. Secondly, is the Canon; the Church has been working intensively on drafting a Common adaptation of its Holiest book,\nthe best of the Holy Scrolls, and the foundations of its Church, so that it may be spread to more of Oren's populace, who languish in uncertainty and apathy in regards to the Allfather and his worldly instruments. We have developed two identical\nmanuscripts of three of the seven books, a miracle in itself, yet we await a third to be sure that is His ordinance.\n\nUnfortunately, the feast day of St. Tobias had to have been cancelled due to a rogue guard locking the city off from the good parishioner\nduring the time of the ceremony. We hope to reschedule another feast day and fair soon enough, and we must apologize with this inconvenience. Whilst the Church has not made its presence wholly yet, this is due largely to an inexperienced budding\npriesthood and an undeveloped Canon. Once those are developed, we may engage in more active missions and more frequent rites and sermons.\n\nMay the Allfather protect!\nRoyal Marriage in Danger?\nThe proposed royal marriage between the Imperial Prince, Aleksandr Carrion, and the Waldian Princess, Lynn Rovin, may be in danger of breaking down! Harsh verbal arguments have broken out between Lynn and Aleksandr involving\nAleksandr’s twin brother Yakov. Yakov merely made a comment about the Waldian accent, which the princess took personal offense to. She then started yelling at Yakov and also took her anger out on poor Aleksandr, who made no such comment.\nLynn Rovin has also been heard slandering the Vanirs, calling them “Rude” and “Disrespectful”. The cruel woman also tried to deny little twelve year old Lorina Carrion her right to be the flower girl at the wedding, and instead tried to put a Waldian\ngirl, not even related to her, in the position instead. The Rovin has shown clear disrespect and disregard for the Prince, the Imperial Crown, and Oren itself. And yet Aleksandr Carrion has shown fantastic persistence in marrying her for the sake of\nuniting all of Humanity under one Empire. May the Creator have mercy on his life.\n\nA report by Jarrik Bloodstone", ""),
        StaticBook("V. Veritatis 5", "Ralph Riley", "Verbo Veritatis\nFifth Edition\n\nIn this edition:\n\n*Aesterwald united with Oren\n\n*Yakov’s Betrayal\n\n*A report from Kal’Agnar\n\n*And more!\nA deserved apology to our readers\nIt has been long enough since the previous edition was released, and I ask for your understanding. I, Ralph Riley, had caught a terrible illness, that medications could not really fight. Feverish and unable to work,\nJacob Chapel kept the bookstore working, but the paper could not continue without me. Now I have finally recovered from my illness and I am up to my feet, and this release marks the return of the paper.\nAesterwald united with Oren\nOn the 11th of Sun’s Smile, 1477, Aesterwald finally joined Oren, uniting humanity once more. Voron Rovin I, König of Aesterwald, and Tuvya, our dear Emperor, signed the Act of Unification bringing together the two realms.\nFrom now on Aesterwald and all its vassals are part of our nation, and house Rovin is a Duke Elector in the Empire.\n\nHumanity should rejoice at this act of peace, kindness, and unity in this time of great peril.\nLet the united Oren be a strong force against the undead blight.\n\nThe unification act is visible in the public library of Petrus, and for sale at Books of Oren.\nPrince Yakov's Betrayal\nA great tragedy has unfolded in our dear capital city of Petrus, after our beloved Imperial Prince, Yakov of the royal house Carrion, was last seen leaving Petrus riding a horse heading towards the north.\nIt is unknown what happened on his voyage, but one thing is certain, he is no longer the cheerful man we knew. He is now part of the undead menace and we hope that it was against his will to join them.\nBut all of this was yet unknown when he-who-was-Yakov entered Petrus and requested a meeting with Tuvya, accompanied by two staff wielding fiends and an armoured dwarf. Our dear Emperor was attacked, and in a valiant battle he was able to slay\nthe evil monsters. Quickly the Wardens, Sonn Ander, and Airthorn came to his help. The battle was won, and he-who-was-Yakov was captured, but at great cost. Our dear Emperor was struck by Iblees’ lightning and gravely injured. To add insult to this,\nthe being that once was Yakov was able to escape, after a great explosion.\n\nOur feelings of safety and pride have been tarnished, and the wounds of this betrayal will never heal. It will take time, but Oren will rebuild and get stronger,\nand defeat the undead menace and get vengeance for the injustice and savagery.\n\nCarry on Carrion, and Creator bless our Emperor and nation!\nA report from Kal'Agnar\n“Upon my entrance into the former capital of the Dwarves, I see much has changed. A gruesome disfigured cultist stands upon the wall of dark stone, waiting to be called upon by his fellow cultists to raise the darkened gates.\nThe once luscious and green rolling hills of this mountainland now bear the signs of darkness seeping into the soil and killing off all that lives. The city seems to be fighting against the evil that’s entangling it, and turning it into a hall of death.\nThe only witnesses of this being the cultists who slit the throats of the innocent, spilling blood upon the one life filled ground. A cavern to the left of the gates show signs of new inhabitants. The cavern called Asgol is watched over by the Doomforges.\nThey bear the marks of cultists, and I can only assume they live in this dark covered haven of death and despair. Along with death being strewn into the hills around the city, a substance of pure read laces through the hills, and a pillar stands near the\nentrance to the mountain hall, made of the same red substance. It is lit aflame and is perhaps a shrine to Iblees, or some deceptive pillar put up only to mock the once great capital. Fires burn in the hillsides, never wavering in the cold winds flowing\nthrough the mountains.\n\nIt seems as though the new residents of left large portions of the capital untouched, though. The mines seem to be sealed shut. As I wander about through the capital I come across a house built into the hillside.\nA steady stream of bloody water leaks out of a pipe heading out of the house. Limbs seem to be stuck in the drain, forcing spurts of bloody water out and onto the land. Dark ominous rain clouds float above, drearily drifting past,\nuntouched and unknowing of the evil and death that lays below. \n\nMy journey through the capital lead me to the gate once again, where a man stoop pleading for help to cross the deadly ravine between the mountains.\nWhile leaving a ghostly sight crossed before my eyes, a steed of pure bone, bearing no flesh, with a rider wearing the face of a pig and the body of a man. The city has been bearing the weight of this darkness for some time.\nIt is changing, growing in new ways that can define its path. These cultists prove to only kill viciously and with no defined reason and murder the innocent common folk who walk about.”\nReporter attacked by bandits\nAn eyewitness account from our reporter, Telperian Faroar\n“Just upon leaving Petrus my path seemed to be barred by two elven bandits. They seemed small, perhaps wood elves. Although I could not see much under their cover\nof darkness and the rusty chainmail that covered most of their bodies, leaving only hands and face exposed to the faint light of the moon through the rustling forest leaves. They held ferrum blades, with the lives of others before me stained upon the dull\nsurfaces of the blades. I was outnumbered and unarmed. I took my chance, seeing a narrow path, as I knew I could be killed if I’d stay and try to talk my way out of it.  I sprinted off through with fearless steps as my damp leather boots hit the ground.\nI hid behind a tree and waited. The two elves had been slow to notice my escape, but they pursued me nonetheless. From where I stood I could hear their heavy breaths. I took a risk and peered out from behind the trunk of the tree I was leaning against,\nnoticing the two men not far apart, one following a few paces behind the other. If only I had a weapon… Rummaging through my bag I located my bow. Removing it quietly, I notched a feathered arrow with ferrum tip. I drew the string up to my cheek,\nand all was silent except for the heavy breathing of the two elves. I leaned out from behind the tree, taking aim at the man in the back. As I released the bolt it whistled into the night, heading towards the man’s foot.  A scream pierced the darkness\nas the arrow struck the man into his calf. The next arrow found its target, and lodged itself into the elf’s chest. The screaming increased in volume, and his companion yelled out into the darkness “Show yourself and fight, you coward!”\nAt these words I began to whistle a merry tune. I released more arrows in their direction, and gave them a slight smile before running off, disappearing through the trees.”\nThe Karovian Column\nImperial marriage in peril?\nWhen first asked to write this week’s column on the quiet and peaceful town of Karovia, I of course asked myself… What would the people of Oren like to read?\nA thrilling piece on the construction of Prince Aleksandr’s newly erected fortress perhaps? A finely worded treatise on the governing institutions which keep Karovian society afloat? Or even a riveting article on how the good people of this town go about\nliving their daily lives? No. For we all know the real reason why the people of Oren choose to read this great newspaper over the rest. Why, to indulge themselves in the latest gossip and hearsay of course!\nWord on the street has it told that the Imperial Prince Aleksandr and his newly wedded wife Lynn Rovin’s marriage is in danger! Sources on the ground have told us that the pair were heard to be partaking in a bitter argument, late into the hours\nof the night. Supposedly the subject of such feud regarded Lynn’s desire to have a child, a suggestion which Aleksandr has adamantly ruled out. It has even been suggested that he may be considering offloading his significant other in favour of\na new mistress! In the past the pair have not been unknown for their turbulent marital status, having been forced into partnership in a bid to create peace between the Holy Empire of Oren and the Königreich of Aesterwald.\nThankfully unification has succeeded, though as we know, the marriage itself has left much to be desired. Unfortunately our sources have reported that Aleksandr has so far refused to answer any of our questions on the matter!\nSo dear readers, what is next for our Imperial Prince? Will he succumb to his wife’s wishes? Or will he emerge a fighter after all? Find out next time in the Karovian Column of Verbo Veritatis, Edition Six!\n -An anonymous source from Karovia", ""),
        StaticBook("V. Veritatis: 1", "Ralph Riley", "Verbo Veritatis\nFirst Edition         \nIn this edition:\n* A new emperor!\n\n* Fishing up relics\n\n* Greedy dwarves harras chef\n\n* “The Farmer”, by W. von Bran, reviewed.\nRecent News.\n\nA new emperor for our nation.\nOn the 11th of Sun’s Smile, 1471. A new emperor was elected to rule over the Empire, listen to people and keep the nation safe from threats.\nTuvya of House Carrion has sworn to our creator to represent our nation in good or bad times, keeping the innocent safe from harm.\nIn the ceremony, Emperor-Elect Tuvya kneeled before the Lorraine and the High Pontiff, Daniel I.  He recited his oaths to\nchurch and state. Afterwards, he received the onyx Crown of the Exalted and the Blade of St Amyas.\nThe new emperor will surely bring better times for the empire and we will prosper more than what any other nation could.\nFishing a relic.\nFishing on the river outside Furstenburg, Phillip Krasline, a skilled fisher and part-time guard of our Majesty the Emperor, found a strange rock after a tug on his line. The rock appears to be an old knife carved out of a stone.\nHe said \"You can see it for yourself, it's crealy older than even the ruins here in Athera\".\nFor now the carved stone knife will be kept by Phillip until the Imperial Museum is finished.\nPhillip will return in the next issue to tell us all about the capture of the Fishlord.\nReports.\nClan Irongut harasses Oren’s greatest chef.\nThe Bada Bing Inn just outside of Petrus, owned by Oren's greatest chef known as Vinnie, is in the process of being stolen by the greedy dwarves of the Irongut clan.\nThe clan seems to believe that the land the Bada Bing Inn is built on belongs to them, and not to Vinnie. To them, this means the inn belongs to them as well. Shortly after leaving, I was able to ask him what the Clan father of Irongut, Balek\nwas going to do next. He replied with, \"Don't worry about them, I will be back and have them handled...\" This seems to be very foreboding for Vinnie.\nI joined the group of men and women headed towards the Bada Bing Inn\nas they feverishly sprinted to Vinnie's aid.  Once we got there, clan father Balek Irongut refused to open the doors, and threatened those that were there. After a short period of arguing, the door was broken down, and people rushed in from the back\nAfter a brief moment of thick intensity, Balek agreed to leave.\n \nWhat will become of the Bada Bing Inn? Will Vinnie get to keep his restaurant, or will the Irongut clan be back to take him down? Find out more next week, when all of this gets resolved.\nA report by Cain Vir Miles.\nBooks & Reviews.\nThe Farmer, by Wilhelm von Bran.\n\n“The Farmer & The Witch, or The Defeat of the Conjurer”, a two part series, is a captivating and well written story about events in an unnamed village in the Waldenian forests.\nIt’s focussed on a man’s struggles and foes he has to deal with. Mainly in the second part is an elevating use of rhyme, making the books a joy to read.\nA must read!\n\n-Jacob Chapel.\nWords of the emperor.\n\nTo many of our fledgling state, the customs and traditions of my people of the Raev come off as foreign, queer, or outright disagreeable. Though predecessors of mine who shared\nmy blood desired to make Oren a Raevir state all-and-all, such outlandish desires my Reign shall bring an end to. I may be the eldest of living Crows and patriarch of my House, yet I was not born amongst the people of Raev. My childhood home was\nthe orphanage of Old Abresi, where I was warded until I was old enough to strike out on my own. Heartlander traditions and speech come more naturally  to I than my blood of Raev, and I simply wish to reassure all who remain loyal to our Realm that there\nshall be no pushing of Raev culture or language amongst our denizens, that Raev will largely be isolated from the affairs of our realm, and that my Reign is not that of Raev, but that of Man.\nCreator’s blessings to all subjects of Oren.\n\nTuvya Sigismundovic Carrion.\nLetters to the editor.\n\nIn future releases, you can send a letter to Ralph of Riley ((PM to nachotp, on forums)) to our offices on Abbey Road 13 next to the Cathedral of St. Sigismund, in Petrus.\nAll your letters will be published here for you to express your feelings about the current state of the society, economy or maybe denounce a villainous act. We expect your letters for the current releases, they can be anonymous if you wish to.\n-Ralph Riley\nEditor of the Verbo Veritatis.", ""),
        StaticBook("V. Veritatis: 2", "Ralph Riley", "§VVerbo Veritatis\nSecond edition      \n\nIn this edition:\n\n*Gardens for a great city\n\n*The United Races\n\n*A Halfling poem\nRecent News.\n\nConsiderate Kidnapper.\n   Out side the Bada Bing Inn, a child was rescued from a kidnapper by the kid’s father. Insults were thrown back and forth by both the kidnapper and the child’s father.\nThe kidnapper said that if the child had not been present, he would have killed the father. Quite the odd statement, coming from a man like him. The child was scared by the bandit’s threat, but no one was harmed. In the end the scoundrel put away his\nsword after being warned by others at the scene.\n    This shows that all citizens and people of Oren bear a responsibility to act against kidnappers, bandits, ruffians and strangers. Only united can we be safe.\nThe Maer's garden.\nPetrus’ main square by the Saint Sigismund Cathedral  has always been a monochromatic place with few old splintering stalls and an old mossy fountain. All of that has changed as by authorization of our emperor Tuvya Carrion, a new\nproject has begun to remodel the main square and instead of the old stalls, we now have trees, flowers and benches. The city has colours now!\nIt’s a great place to relax and take a deep breath while having shops nearby.\nReports.\n\nAssaults on young women\n\nOn an evening in the Deep Winter two men were seen milling around the city fountain, their appearances unknown. The pair then went on to speak with young\ngirls and women alike, seemingly posing as healers or physicians of the sort. After a short while one of the two offered to heal a young injured woman, who kindly denied, but was then drugged and carried some distance from the city, to a blocked off cave\nand was tied in chains. The woman was asleep for some time, and what happened next is unclear, though the pair seemed to have been practicing some sort of dark art, chanting wildly.  The woman awoke soon after, and a spell was cast so that she would only\nremember their names and actions. The two men, one reportedly called ‘Hanz’, left her against a rock where she stayed until a young man found her. She was safely returned to the capital and seems to be unhurt.\nThese actions clearly show the vile nature of citizens of Aesterwald, as there is no doubt from which place a man by the name of Hanz originates. These crimes against defenceless women can not go unanswered! \n\nA report by Lilian\nThe United Races.\nRecently, the halflings attempted to start a group called the United Races. Their goal was to ensure peace between all races and cultures. Faiz Kharadeen, Lord Chancellor of Aesterwald, was present during the first meeting.\nWhen interviewed, he said he thought the United Races was a ‘noble cause’ and ‘a dream that has been within most hearts since we were perhaps children.’\nOthers argued that world peace is impossible and that we are all born sinful and cannot get along.\nThis was made evident when Faiz stated that the high elves refused to participate in the meeting. He went on to say that some high elves, especially the ones who live in the capital, are ‘cruel creatures.’ And although many attended the meeting\nfew were involved in the discussions. Fumble Willowbottom, organiser of the group, said that restrictions would be put in place to protect the peace and that there would be consequences if they were broken.\nIt seems that peace between all races is another silly halfling dream and nothing more.\n\nA report by Ariana\nOpinion Column\n\nThe future of Petrus.\nPetrus, the young capital of the holy empire of Oren is under heavy overhaul these days, and what once was a rusty grey city, has slowly evolved into a colourful place.\n. I remember back then, when the city was still being built that the only important matters were the guards and military, and if you were not part of it, you would have to be a noble or a mere peasant.\nBut those days are over as now culture flows through\nevery corner of the city and the arts have a place to express, literature has flooded our minds and the auction houses are full of books that people desire to buy. The gardens that I mentioned earlier have given a new spark to the square giving life to\neverything around it.\n\nA new public library has been established that will surely catch the attention of many to get started in the world of letters and expression,  I see Petrus has a great future to come and the city is starting to blossom\nnew people come everyday to see it and it is just a matter of time until the the city of Petrus becomes the cultural capital of Athera.\n\nA opinion column by Ralph Riley, editor of the Verbo Veritatis.\nWords of the Emperor.\nThe overthrowing of the Imperium Tertius brought a great exodus of peoples from our capital of Petrus and I have heard many comments and rumors on the state of our Quiet City. It has been no small effort to encourage\nthose who left to return to life in the city once again, but through the efforts of my councillors, Life is once again returning to Petrus. Many years ago, a similar situation occurred in the old Capital of Abresi. A dead city even under Godfrey’s reign\nour old capital was all but abandoned following the Exodus of Chivays and others. We of Carrion did not wallow in the emptiness of Old Abresi, but rather strived to resettling the city once again. Although it took us many years, Abresi was made into the\nmercantile and cultural center of Anthosia, the grand city playing host to more than half of our population. Though times and circumstances are different,  with patience and fortitude our City of Petrus will once again become the Crown Jewel of our realm.\nWith this, I give reminder that taxation will be re-implemented within Petrus during the upcoming Sun’s Smile.\n\nTuvya Sigismundovic Carrion, Emperor of the Holy Empire of Oren.\nAdvertisement.\nVisit Vinnie’s Bada Bing Inn, just down the road towards the Cloud Temple from Petrus. It has great food and drinks, and most importantly, it sells the Verbo Veritatis!\nComplimentary Poem.\n\nThis week we have a free Halfling poem included in the newspaper, it’s from the future Halfling poem bundle by Jacob Chapel, soon to be sold in “Books of Oren”.\nOld Fat Spider Spinnin' in a tree.\n\nOld fat spider spinning in a tree!\nOld fat spider can’t see me!\nAttercorp! Attercorp!\nWon’t ya stop, stop ya spinnin’ and look for me?\nOld Tomnoddy, all big body,\nOld Timnoddy, can’t spy me!\nAttercorp! Attercorp!\nDown ya drop!\nYou’ll never catch me up ya tree!\nLazy Lob and crazy Cob\nAre wearing webs to wing me\nI am far more sweet than other meat\nBut still cannot find me!\nHere I am, naughty little fly\nYa are fat and lazy\nYa cannot trap meh, though you try.\nIn ya cobwebs crazy\n\n-Garry Bogger.\nThe previous release of the newspaper has been made public for everyone to read.\n\n-Ralph of Riley, editor of the Verbo Veritatis.", ""),
        StaticBook("V. Veritatis: 3", "Ralph Riley", "Verbo Veritatis\nThird Edition        \n\nIn this edition:\n\n*Sea monster attacks Aldersberg\n\n*Murders among the elves \n\n*Is war upon us?\nRecent News\n\nThe ultimatum to Aesterwald.\nAesterwald, a human region independent of the empire, has received a final call for diplomacy from our emperor Tuvya Carrion, as the empire has tried everything to try to unite\nAesterwald back to Oren, which has led to nothing but negative responses and an uncovered conspiracy to attack Oren. Considering that background, the ultimatum asks Aesterwald to join the empire and be able to prosper together\nso all the humans are united once more, even without judging about what happened in the Zion war so we could become united once again, because if they reject the proposal, the worst case scenario would be to go at war with Aesterwald.\nQuoting our emperor, Tuvya of the house Carrion,  “Humanity will only rise if we work together as a race, only if we are united we will truly prosper, and we will be able to overcome any trouble. ”\nwe can only stick together as the Oren empire following the lead of our emperor who will lead us to better times.\n§TThe Society of Snakes.\nAn unidentified High elf was found dead in a forest, it was determined that he was killed and the crime scene was choking. His right eyeball was removed from it's place and it was left on his right hand.\nIt would seem that it wasn't just a simple crime, a robbery that went wrong, it might be much more. \n\nAdding up to that murder, a wood Elf, know as Guz, bronze guard of the elven city was dropped from a ledge intentionally\nwhen his body was inspected, they found again the right eye removed and placed on top of the right palm, but on this case, another signature was left behind, a snake was carved on his chest, probably with a knife.\nWith what are we dealing here? is it a mass murderer or a bandit group? terror surrounds the elves as this murders are trying to send a message but we still don’t crack the code. I hope these murders do not continue in the future.\nExplosion on a dwarven library\nIn the dwarven capital, a tragedy occurred where there library was either attacked on there was an accident,the exact situation is still not confirmed. The incident did lead to the death of the head librarian\nand the destruction of part of the library. The blast also destroyed the desk and blew a hole through the floor, cracked stone was everywhere. It is hoped the cause will be revealed soon and it was just a mere accident.\nReports\n\nSea monster attacks Aldersberg\nOn the 7th of the Grand Harvest a giant tentacled monster attacked Aldersberg, its huge pink tentacles smashing into the docks, dragging with it crates and logs.\nAs the brave people of Oren came to Aldersberg to defend it, hordes upon hordes of crabs were thrown onto the deck by the monster. The crabs viciously clawed at the fighters, and during the long fight some were gravely injured.\nAs the crabs were eventually fought off the tentacles retreated, only to show up again further in the bay, just North of the ship. Sadly for the monster it was perfectly in range for the ballistas and the valiant men and women of Oren fired bolt after\nbolt into its flesh. After wounding it severely the monster grabbed the other side of the ship, and caught two men in its grip. One of them was able to break free from the grip, but the other was pulled into the water.\nBy perseverance and smarts the group was able to pull him out and struck a killing blow with a ballista bolt into the monster’s last tentacle.\n\nA report by Jacob Chapel.\nOpinion Columns.\n\nDwarven and human relationships.\nThe History of the Dwarven and Human races go back a long time, times of friendliness, times of hatred and times of bitterness. Many times have the dwarven people\nbeen at the throats of the human people and many times have the humans been at the throats of the dwarves. These I have experienced first hand. My aim is to help ensure that our people build a healthy friendship that, at times may come to be tested,\nbut will prove to be a friendship from which both of our people benefit. The future of the land depends on our relations, and how the future is shaped will be determined greatly by our relations. I urge you to make an effort with relations improvement.\nWe are all the citizens of the lands we live in but what is racial divide? it is simply a way of discriminations, calling out against someone else because of a thing that is out of their control, so I leave you with these final words,\n‘Peace is a virtue, that will bring progress, tolerance is a virtue that brings friendship, hatred is the destruction to bridges of peace and tolerances.’\n\nAn opinion column by Grigor Grandaxe, dwarven ambassador\nIf you want to learn more about the Philosophy of Equality, look for the book entitled ‘True Reason’ in our shop at Abbey Road 13, Petrus.\nWords of the Emperor.\nThough it has been but a short time since I have made my entrance in Petrus, already our quiet city is showing good signs. Of the squatters homes we had evicted, many have been taken up by new residents.\nOur Public library is the most comprehensive of it’s sort in all Athera and we boast a number of active shops, including the greatest bookstore in all the lands, our own Verbo Vertatis.\nOur guardly force has been reorganized and has been making great strides in reestablishing order, a number always to be found patrolling the streets or manning the newly refurbished gatehouse. A force of rangers has also been established, assisting\nthe Knightly Order of the Red Dragon in keeping our roads safe of banditry, in fact our roads are the safest they have been to date in our time in Athera. While our militaristic forces are going along in good fashion, our economic benefactors\nare even greater. A daily average of our revenues is some 7,500 minas, including usage of some 3,000 minas on average. Year-to-date, the Crown has used some 30,000 minas in funding recognized orders, establishing public works,\nand giving fair wage to workers. At the current rate, the rate of exchange within our Empire will triple in a few short years, providing a much more fluid environment for traders and laborers to make their way.\nThough we are still a long way off from making Petrus the jewel of the world, already we have made significant steps and I am eager for all of our hard work to finally pay off.\n\n-Tuvya Sigismundovic Carrion.\nAdvertisement\nInterior decorators for the palace\nGood citizens of Oren,\n I, Prince Yakov of House Carrion, am in search of an interior decorator who has both the time and ability required to work upon the Imperial Palace of Oren.\nPayment for such a job is up for negotiation though shall likely be substantial, depending upon the amount of work completed. If you are interested in applying for this job, I would request you send a raven to the palace at the earliest possible date.\n((My username and forum name is Zezimus.))\nLiterature.\n\nHalfling Poem\n\nWheat\nA golden glisten of summer sea,\nGraceful arms waving to and fro.\nA warm sensation runs through,\nA feeling of protect and peace bestow.\nSoft movements from a gentle breeze,\nGrace, prosperity is of Nature's own.\nThin straws of vigor and strength,\nA sense of light against the unknown.\nLand's children of grain,\nTreated as a gift that provides life.\nA gift of quelling formidable hunger,\nA mighty savior of times of strife.\nLife of giving, a seed to a stalk,\nO' Nature, grant me day and week.\nThat the grains retain their numbers,\nFor a life without wheat shows bleak.", ""),
        StaticBook("V.H", "Vicelin", "-Animated Armor in Alexandria, Courland-\n\nDuring a routine visit to Alexandria to purchase high quality minerals to be used in slayer steel weaponry, I came across two of these beings inside a tavern. They had crippled a man and one with Mordring's black\nsun upon his shield dragged the man off. I could not do anything as an assistant of his had barred the exit and killed another taverngoer by crushing his skull.\n\nThe Mordring dreadknight appeared uninterested in anybody else but the man who was crippled.\nHe was likely a sacrifice.", ""),
        StaticBook("Vailor Council I", "Suliin'thill", "Silver Council Meeting\n7/12/15\n\n-Discussed Silus' residence in The Citadel\n+See if he is useful.\n\n-Okariran Progress\n+Suliin'thill 16,000 minas gained\n+Vesryn awaiting blueprints. \"Stale progress\"\n^Remove Rear Gate\n^Stables not removed\n+Hier signed up gatherers and has assessment chest system.\n+Elwyn has obtained 10 Sillumir thus far, and wants 10 more\n\n-Trade Guild Defenses\n+Good idea, nothing to lose\n+Bolster Both Forces\n-Charter Minas Gathered\n+Those that didn't pay to be shamed\n+Set up a camp on the isle to be claimed\n+Sister States shall help\n+Uses for land: Company, farming, outposts", ""),
        StaticBook("Various Works II", "Fenris Cross", "~Wandering Lady\nI’ll tell you the tale of a lady fair who wanders off these roads, Her skin is pale and gold the hair that down her back does flow.\n\nThe lady is enchanting, entrancing is her voice,\nAnd all good fortune granting, she wanders by her choice.\n\nOver hill and sunny dale, her path is here and there, For ever was the lady, pale, free of every care.\n\nWith eyes of blue and silken touch is it too much to wonder,\nWhat other hue could move so much and draw a soldier’s blunder?\n\nOh the lady is enchanting, entrancing is her gaze, And all good fortune granting, she’ll come to lift our haze.\nShe’ll join us in our travel, she’ll sing for us at night, And all the while unravel that which would give us fright..\n~The Mountain’s Call\nOh~ oh~ oh~\n\nHear the mountains moan, Deep and low, Of things unknown.\n\nCold the wind, Blows upon your skin. She does rend, Through hides too thin.\n\nOh~ oh~ oh-oh-oh~\nThe path lays before my feet, The mountain at my back. I have a lengthy trail to beat, Under my heavy pack!\n\nOh~ oh~ oh-oh-oh~\n\nWinds gust and whine away, Steal the breath of fools today; Don’t mind as I bide my way..\nOh~ oh~ oh~\n\nHear the mountains moan, Deep and low, Of things unknown.\n\nOh~ oh~ oh~\n\nFeel the icy drift, Move and shift, Beneath the swift.\n\nGrave her kiss,\nFeels upon your lip. Her false bliss, Has claimed many a ship.\n\nOh~ oh~ oh-oh-oh~\n\nWhere light dances on the snow, I choose to make my way. No matter how the tides may flow, I’ve ground to gain today!\nOh~ oh~ oh-oh-oh~\n\nSnows drift and change away, Steal the heat of fools today; Don’t mind as I bide my way..\n\nOh~ oh~ oh~\n\nFeel the icy drift, Move and shift, Beneath the swift.\nOh~ oh~ oh~\n\nSee how hot the roar, Of the storm, From days of yore.\n\nBold her mark, Born upon the stark White hot arc, That shines within the dark.\n\nOh~ oh~ oh-oh-oh~\nThunder crashes on the peak, Through both day and night. The mountain will not take the weak, And gives the strong their fight!\n\nOh~ oh~ oh-oh-oh~\n\nLightning, thunder, clash away. Steal the life of fools today;\nDon’t mind as I bide my way..\n\nOh~ oh~ oh~\n\nSee how hot the roar, Of the storm, From days of yore.\n~Reason\nHow many rays shine in the skies? How many stars before our eyes? \n\nThere’s beauty in this ravaged world. There’s always more to be unfurled.\n\nOne more dream, One more sigh,\nOne more grin, As Fate draws nigh..\n\nThat’s what we fight for, just for each other, Just for the beauty found in a day…\n\nThat’s what I live for and I can’t smother, Smother the duty I have yet to pay..\nTo see the stars, Shine in the sky..\n\nWhat would you give for one more day, If you could live life the old way?\n\nFor one more hour with those you love? Or one more flower or one more dove?\nOn such a dream, We all rely, And hope and pray, Fate will comply.\n~Introspection\nSee us now, see us not. Let us be what time forgot. Spirits lost to the sea, Or some other fate will be...\n\nDreams on your eyelids, Figments of your mind, Answers to lifelong bids, Rewards returned in kind...\nHear our words, hear our voice. Close your ear, it is your choice. Spirits lost as fires burned, Or to some other fate that turned..\n\nSongs in your heart ring, Wisps of melody. Answers to a riddle sing, From souls so steadily..\nTurn your gaze upon the grave, Turn your eye within. What have you to lose or save, Before the end begins?", ""),
        StaticBook("Velulaei TI : BI", "Sathoro Shadeleaf", "Tome I of the Velul\n\n\"Velulaei, Moon Goddess & Protector of the Night.\" ~Written by High Velul Priest Vel'tas Klaren\n\nBook I - The Silver Globe\nChapter 1 - The Moon's Plains\n\nFrom the creators world, we see but a globe which is slowly shrouded by the sky and then reemerges. However it is more than what we perceive. After the world we live in was created, the creator made a sphere of silver\nappear. This was to accommodate Velulaei, the Aengul of the moon and night. This sphere was of a beauty matching the one of Velulaei. The creator placed it in the sky alongside the sun so it would provide another light in the previously dark nights.\nThe landscape of this place was covered in a light gray glow, as if the grass were clippings of silver. The sky was dark as the darkest night in which one was able to contemplate the creator's world in all it's magnificence. However, there was nothing\nelse in sight, only the mountains of silver coated in the glowing grass and the occasional spirit.\n\nDuring the day of the sun, this space grows faint, as if it was but a dreamland. However, it is but covered by the blinding light of the sun. Then the sun\nwill fall again and Velulaei shall rise.\nChapter 2 - Lands of the Night\n\nThough the silver land that we call moon seems empty, there are many inhabitants. These are the shadows of the Creator's world, the spirits of dark elves who have passed away and the Aengul herself, Velulaei.\nThese congregate in greater numbers for the dark moon assembly, thus why the moon is shrouded every few cycles.\n\nVelulaei called the land of the moon the lands of night as it is an eternal night. However, the night is the remover of shadows and the\nunification of beings. To the contrary of the sun which burns and destroys with its light, furthermore segregating beings of the creator. This is why the dark elves chose to worship her in the dawn of time, because they knew she was the fairest.\nChapter 3 - Up Above, Her Home\n\nWhat we don't see when we look at the moon is the palace of Velulaei. Her residence in the silver valley of the great ranges. It is pictured as dome from which three towers extend into the sky. Protection, family, and\nnight. The palace of Velulaei is called 'Nighted Sphere Keep'. The middle chamber of the residence is a big one. It has a throne made of silver in its center which faces the singular entrance. The seat is elevated on a pedestal in the middle of the bare\nroom. A light mist floods the lower parts of the hall. Leaving it through a great door way, one enters a circular hallway.\n\nThe hallway goes all around the main chamber and connects to the three towers of faith and some other secondary chambers.\nIn those, one can find ancient libraries of old scrolls written in Old Elven. \n\nThe three towers are similar in design, seen from the outside. However the interior varies depending on the value they represent. Protection has a solid and uniform flow of\nmoonlight falling through the middle of the tower. It's walls are thicker representing the defensive aspect of this important value. One can reach the top via a spiraling staircase which only stops at the source of the flow.\nFamily has a lighter and more watery flow of moonlight dropping from its center. Around it rise various pillars, created to represent members of a family. They are linked halfway up the tower by double arches on the second floor. One can reach only that\nfloor by taking one of the two turning staircases.\n\nNight has a sparkling midnight sky colored and troubled flow of moonlight falling down the center of the tower. The tower has no windows and thus the inside is dark, provided only with the glow of the\nmagic. There are no stairs in this tower, how to get to the roof is an unrevealed secret.\nChapter 4 - Our Haven do we Demise\n\nThere is another reason the silver sphere was created. It was to accommodate the faithful spirits of the dark elves when they die. Velulaei would take the spirit of a slain priest and bring it with her back to the\nplains of never-ending night. The spirit would take the form of a shadowy figure.\n\nThe spirits of the past ones roam the lands of Velulaei, gifted with immortality. They are permitted to roam through the palace of the Aengul. Many spend the majority of\ntheir existence reading the scrolls of the moon and learning the full reality of the world below. It is said that there are those which are blessed and that retain their form of the creator's world.\nUp above is our haven. It is the last place to go for those lost on land. There have been some which sacrificed themselves for their shrine, to gain access to the moon's plains. Velulaei is fair and gives residence to all those shadows she pulls from the\nworld. It has been said that in the after life a priest would have their own library chamber within the mountain ranges of the moon. Those who are blessed receive a personal room within the palace and stand beside Velulaei during the gathering of shadows.", ""),
        StaticBook("Verden's Review", "Jallentime", "I sent Gavin and Plonas to survey and lessen the presence of undead in a forest that had become infested with them.\n\nThey both brought back a specimen of an undead spider, and provided information vital to restoring the area.\n\n                          ->\nI taught Gavin about the dangers of the unnatural, and how we as druids not only look after nature, but also seek to remove that which is detrimental to the balance of the world.\n\nPlonas was asleep somewhere. You may want to give him a recap.", ""),
        StaticBook("Vermillion", "Chu Li Mang", "[!]The letter appears sealed with a wax stamp, a flaming bird shown clearly.\n\n\"For too long have you descendants lived under the grace of your so called \"Righteousness\", your dependancy upon the ancestors you worship like deities to justify your ways.\nThe times of war have crept upon the isles once more, the cogs of war turning to the sounds of our drums, fueled by greed and the drive for power.\n\nBe it by blade or flame, by death or subjugation, our horde calls out to bring an end to your way of life.\n[!]An elegantly written signature is engraved upon the coarse paper, seemingly out of place\n\n朱丽曼\nChu Li Mang\n\nHeavens Chosen\n\nCommander of the Vermillion Legion", ""),
        StaticBook("Vice of Purity.", "Awylan Wistari", "*The cover of the book is crafted from a blue leatherty-type substance, with the words \"THE VICE OF PURITY, VOL 1.\" inscribed in it. Below that would be a phrase written incursive \"By Awylan Wistari\"\nThe Vice Of Purity Vol 1. By Awylan Wistari,\nChapter 1. The meaning of purity.\n\n\"Perhaps the greatest fault amongst world cultures at this juncture in the temporal realm, or atleast the fault in the culture of my native peoples the High Elves, is the notion of purity that prevades the society.\nThis arbitrary, abstract concept that is wholly up to interpetation and therefore has no foundation in this reality enables others, particularly those within the silver walls of Haelun'or to exclude any and  all external cultures, beliefs or practices\nfrom their borders. This enables one to drift into complacency with their current state of being as opposed to embracing that which might bring change, that which might be different, and that which might be beneficial. But the greater question I have\nconcerns this notion of purity, what does it actually mean? To many within Haelun'or, or particularly the purists of high elven society, purity may mean the avoidance of inter-mixing. Purity may mean keeping within the culture and not outsourcing one's\nmental facilities to another culture. Commonly, the aforementioned is what purity means. But if this is what purity means then wouldn't a better word for this be isolation as opposed to being pure? I do not see what is pure about\nignoring mutual romantic affections that may not particularly be with one within your own culture. I call that self-denial. I do not see what is pure about not questioning the status quo and towing the line for the purists in High Elven society,\nI call that complacency. All in all, this arbitrary notion of pure that has been imposed upon those of high elven dissent is one of ignorance and intellectual drodgyness as opposed to genuine preservation.\nChapter 2. \"Remove those ears, they are unclean!\"\nI remember when I got off a boat and made my way to an assortment of carts that take people to various destinations. The area around these carts, rather predictably, have a lot of humans (and others, but mostly humans) congregating near them\nAs I stepped off the boat and walked towards the congregating humans, a gentleman that belongs to canonism, a fringe human religion, denigrated me for being of elven descent. Not only that, but he repeatedly told me how he was in support of\nexterminating all \"impure\" elves (those that had their ears). He also told me how homosexuals, insubordinates, dark elves, orcs and others who did not look like him deserved to be exterminated as well. Of course, his reasoning? They are \"impure.\"\nHe offered to wash me of my impurity several times by way of severing my ears from my head. The problem with this being a way to ensure purity is that I am still elven by blood, you cannot remove that by removing a part of me.\nFor example, if you sever the stem of an apple it doesn't become any less of an apple. It becomes an apple without a stem, but an apple nontheless. Of course, this man was not thinking rationally, the same notion of purity and cultural supremacy that\nthose in Haelun'or value had infected his mind and driven his actions, insofar as severing eyes would meet his standard for purity.\n\nA shame.\nChapter 3.  \"By blood we are the chosen!\" \n\nAs I mentioned earlier in Chapter 1, many of those in Haelun'or believe simply by the fact of them existing they are pure, and if one were to intermingle with those who are different than\nthey might be, whether it be culturally or racially, they have tainted themselves and are now impure.  They must be ostracized from society, excluded from the Silver city, subjected to the most severe mistreatment all because they refused to conform.\nThe broader issue here is not just one of treatment, even though that is a sizeable part of my dissent with the practice of exclusion, but it's one of conception of the notion of purity. If your stake to claim is something\ncompletely external to your control, to your power, then how is that superiority or purity on your part? Your \"purity\" is relegated solely to the hands of time and fate, not to your own achievements, which means you truly are not superior, time is.\nOne cannot be superior or pure for simply existing if one does not do anything within that existence to ensure himself and others are progressing from their initial state of being. If you are conceived into the natural world at point A\nand you manage to exit it at point B, perhaps you can make a stake to superiority or purity. However, if you are conceived at Point A and you leave the world at point A, and all you have to do to point to your purity is your name, your culture and the\ntype of blood that courses through your veins, you have deluded yourself into thinking you are more than you are. As I said before, mere existence is not purity, it is existence.  Biological composition isn't purity, it's biological composition. The\ndenotative meanings of these concepts are not very complex, it is the connotations that cultures that wish to stroke their egos attach to them that are troublesome.\nChapter 4. Challenges to the purists.\n\n\"But to those who would contend what I've laid out in this book, I have a series of question to ask them.\n\n1. If you believe in cultural superiority, in which way do you believe\nsaid cultural superiority materializes? If it materializes in the form of grandiose structures, ornate practices, language and so on, then isn't your superiority utterly relative? Don't you have a standard of superiority that could be\ndifferent than someone else's? 2. It follows question 1, what is your standard of superiority? \n\n3. Why should someone be subject to the sword for not doing  as you do?\n\n4. Why is an elven woman that loves a human \"impure\"\n5.  Would cultural heterogenity bring destruction to your culture? If so, can you point to any civilization on our earth who's downfall has been to having multiple ideas and cultures in their area?\nAs time goes on, these are the questions I hope are answers, the debates that are had. The status quo has been in place for too long, I intend to challenge it until it's shackles are broken and we, as a people, are  elevated to a state of enlightenment.\nTo those who read this and share the message I have conveyed, thank you and keep fighting for a better world. For those that read this and attempt to take my life or burn this piece of literature, your message is the product of a decaying world.\nWith or without my writings, it'll die. It is inevitable.", ""),
        StaticBook("Viscount's Book", "Aylwin Blaxton", "===================            The\n       Viscount's\n          Book.\n===================\n\n      Written by:\n Rt Hon Aylwin Blaxton\n 1st Viscount Brabant\n           For\n Future Rulers of the\n        Viscouty\nDearest Kin,\n\nI have created this book to show you what is required of a Pragmatic Viscount.      \nHeed these words, they might save your life. But remember, strive for no more power than what you have, unless granted.\n    Aylwin Blaxton.\nI. Men must either be \n      Treated Well or\n      Be Crushed.\n\nII. A Viscount should          not lust for               Power, unless it\n      is granted to him.\n\nIII. Keep Popular tasks       For yourself & \n      Hand out others\n      To subordinates.\nIV. Do Necessary Evils       In One Stroke.\n\nV. Pay out Benefits or        Rewards Little by        Little.\n\nVI. Pay attention to \n      Your Subjects.\n      Evil days will soon       Be over, or Warn        Them of what may        Come.\nVII. Always Do Lip-\n       Service to the\n       Virtues.\n\nVIII. Dress\n       Appropriately.\n\nIX. Use Religion as a           Pretext for your        Actions. It may \n       Permit \"Pious\n       Cruelty\".\nX. New Rewards will not        persuade your           Subjects to \n       Forget Old \n       Injuries.\n\nXI. It is easy to \n       Persuade people        - But, you need \n       Force to keep\n       Them Persuaded.\nXII. One can persuade           the people, but           Not the Nobles,           by fair deals.\n\nXIII. Mercenaries \n       Should be feared        for their Evil.\n       They may Betray. \nXIV. Excess Virtue may        Ruin the House.\nXV. Vice may Save the           House.\n\nXVI. Men are Greedy, \n        Fickle, False, \n        Cowardly &\n        Greedy.\n\nXVII. To persuade men,        Convince them\n       Your Aims are            the same.\nXVIII. You should be \n        Feared, not \n        Hated.\n\nXIX. Men do not forget        Crimes against\n       Property.\n\nXX. Any inward Faction         Can find Aid from        Abroad.\nXXI. A Viscount never           Lacks a Reason          To break a \n        Promise.\n\nXXII. A Wise man keeps          Faith, so long as         It serves his \n        designs.\n\nXXIII. Before all Else,           Be Armed.\nXXIV. GOD is not willing          to do everything         by divine right. \n\nXXV. Hatred is gained\n       by Good Deeds,\n       As well as Bad.\n\nXXVI. He who wishes to         be Obeyed must\n       Know how to \n       Command.\nXXVII. Be wary of the\n        Armed Prophets,         since they can           destroy you.\n\nXXVIII. A Son who is \n         Disinherited is \n         as Dangerous \n         as two foes.\n\nXXIX. Be Pragmatic.\n\nXXX. Get Minae in                  Peace.", ""),
        StaticBook("Void Connection", "Laureh'thill", "Notes on: Connecting to The Void\n\nWritten by: Laureh'thill\n\n-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-Chapter One: Basic Concepts\n\nThe Void is, as was explained to myself by Archmage Resia of the Mage's Guild, both everything and nothing. To properly learn arcane\nmagic, one must connect their mind to the void through demanding practice and study. This is usually done through what is formally referred to as \"meditation\" by Mages.\n\n\"Meditation\" while similar the non-Mage's understanding of the word, takes on a\ncompletely different meaning when mentioned in this regard. What Mages experience while meditating transcends what any non-Mage could achieve in the act without trying extensively to procure the same results. \n\nMeditation commonly has a focus of sorts,\nsomething for the subject to think exclusively about (or rather not think exclusively about) to focus their mind onto the subject matter that they are trying to understand or comprehend.\n\nSince the act of thinking about everything at once has so far been\nproven impossible by even the most accomplished scholars and intellectuals to date, Mages have taken to focusing on nothing at all to complete the ritual of voidal connection.\n\nChapter Two: The Process\n\nPurging a mind of all thought armed only with the\nwill of itself is no easy task. This fact is what deters most potential Mages, and the reason their kind is so spread out among the population.\n\nIt is, however, achieveable. With a mastery of will, one can train themselves to connect to the void easily\nand without even the slightest visible physical strain.\n\nThis does not mean, however, that the process of \"meditation\" becomes any easier. The mind is simply a muscle and, like any physical muscle, grows strong to compensate for stress placed upon it.\nA common misconception is that you should light candles or incense while going through the process of \"meditation\". These external distractions, however, prevent you from achieving the level of focus nessicary to clear your mind completely. Ignore those\nwho mention chimes and bells, those who urge you to listen to the sounds of the harp or flute; they are unknowing agents of your undoing.\n\nFind a small, quiet, room temperature area to rest and relax. Slowly begin to rid yourself of your five senses as in\nusual meditation. Sight, hearing, taste, smell, and feeling. And then turn your focus to your thoughts.\n\nThe most common mistake you can make is actively thinking about clearing your mind of thought. This paradox confuses you more than helps, and should\nbe avoided at any cost.\n\nEventually, you will find peace in your thoughts and senses; slowly coming to a state of complete rest (much like just before you fall asleep).\n\nYou will see nothingness, hear nothingness, taste nothingness, smell nothingness, and\nfeel nothingness. It is at this point that you reach your mind out, transposing your conciousness into this void of emptiness.\n\n-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-", ""),
        StaticBook("Void Translo", "Sab'Aoth", "=--=--=--=--=--=--=                 Void\n         Translocation\n=--=--=--=--=--=--=            \n   \n        -<= (O)\nVoid translocation is the art of bringing and placing objects into and out of the Void. Mana is what fuels our world and is in all forms of objects and beings. Void translocationists use said mana to perform their art. By copying the mana that an object\nor person has exactly they are able to place and remove objects into and out of the Void. One must copy the pattern and amount of mana that is inside the object or being before they may perform said art. As per such they simply need to create a connection\nto the Void and form a portal of sorts to place and take objects into and out of the Void. However people are unable to be transported to to the Void due to the complex and large amounts of mana they have. The same is said for other large objects, As well\none must be careful when performing said art because if an object is placed into the void for too long, their bodies and very being itself would be torn asunder and transformed into mana itself. This process would take about one to two elven weeks to\nreach.\n\n\n[An astonishingly complex drawing of a portal of sorts is detailed along the page.]", ""),
        StaticBook("Void-Origins V1", "Scholar of The Void", "Theory of Void-Based Origination - Volume I, Origination and Supporting Facts.\n\nGiven the nature of the following text, the author requestions anonymity.\nTable of Contents\n\nI - Statement of Theory, Page 3.\nII - Fallacies of the Creator, page 8.\nIII - Void Nodes, Page 15\nIV - Cast vs. Nature, Page 20\nV - Conclusion, page 25.\nI\nStatement of Theory and Support.\n\nPresented and supported in this text, and in following volumes, is a scientific theory as to the void's role in the creation of the world as we know it. An act commonly attributed to the\nomnipotent deity called \"The Creator\", it is the purpose of this text to provide evidence to an alternative means with fewer conflicts with the facts of reality.\n\nSupport for the theory, which will follow, can be initially comprised of three main points\nwhich will be detailed in their respective chapers. \n\nThe theory, as well as these three points, are as follows.\n\nThe Void is the origin of both our world and lives, brought forth by a means akin to a mage's spell.\nSupporting this:\n\nThe logical fallacies alongside a sentient 'creator'.\n\nThe recorded, known, effects of the Void on our world.\n\nThe nature of void-summoned elements and life, and\ntheir being capable of perfectly mimicking what is natural.\nII\nFallacies of the Creator.\n\nBy many names, a single, all-powerul being is the backbone of many modern idealisms. The idea that a sentient being existed before existence itself is popular.\nIt also, on a fundemental level, fails to make logical sense.\n\nThe core belief of these religions are that this creator was the one responsible for the world, the void, and all other planes of existence.\nThe flaw in this is the idea that sentience can exist without an environment for it to be housed in. \n\nThe abilities to see, hear, or feel are all useless when nothing exists to be seen, heard, or felt. And since these senses are the\nbases of thought, it can be inferred by extension that without these environmental stimuli, sentience cannot exist.\n\nWhile we can never know with complete certainty that this god does not transcend logic, the best solution is the most\nsimple. The Void, being both perpetual and infintesimal, has existed since before existence itself. It has been the constant throughout both reality and whatever lies outside.\n\nIt requires much less exceptions to accepted logic to assume\nthat the void is what created reality than a being did. When one sees a mountain, they do not assume the mountain was made by hand - merely that it has always been there.\n\nThe way by which the void has brought to life our world shall be\nexplained in the following pages.\nIII\nVoid Nodes.\n\nWhile in the vast majority of cases, the void cannot permanently change our world (For example, a mage's spell disappears when he releases it), there are recorded instances of such a thing happening.\nOne such instance was discovered in Anthos, where a void node under a southern Mage's hall had permanently altered a cavern with it's energy.\n\nHumming with energy, and the stone itself changed into all manner of material, the detonated void node\nbrought proof of two things - That the void can permanently sustain a physical change, and that it can enact itself on pre-existing material.\n\nThe first of these two facts is of most importance. The second will be addressed in a later volume.\nThe fact that the void can permanently alter the world is the basis of this theory.\n\nWhile what was created was random and without logic or pattern, it did create. In the node's aftermath existed material where none had existed before.\nIt did not simply change things, but created as well. The net sum of what was found after the node's change was greater than what had been there before.\nIV\nCast vs. Nature\n\nTwo types of magic interract with the void in the way closest to this theory's concluded way by which reality began. These are evocation and conjuration.\nEvocation, for the unaware, is the summoning of a chosen element from the void for temporary use within our realm. Usually weaponized, known forms are as follows: Air, Water, Fire, Earth, and Electrical.\n\nConjuration is similar, in some ways, but\ninstead of a simple object a conjurationist summons forth a living being. \n\nThe key point with both of these magics is that, in a skill mage's hands, the summoned element or creature is indistinguishable from a 'natural' piece, found in our world.\nIf a Earth Evocationist wished to form a stone exactly like one she had found, and she were skilled enough to do so, the summoned stone would be entirely identicle to the original. The same applies to all evocations as well as conjuration.\nThese facts in mind, in tandem with the void nodes' nature, provide evidence that our world could have been created as a result of the void, in a manner akin to evocation with a single key difference being that this is permanent.\nV\nConclusion\n\nFollowing volumes will include parts of the theory which answer possible conflicts with parts of the world. Volume II will cover the presence and divinty of aenguls and daemons.", ""),
        StaticBook("Voidal Shifting", "Valmir__", "=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=Voidal Shifting: Lessons by Irhamir Siil'crux, recorded by Valmir Synalli.\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=Theory Lesson #1:\nMana Anchors\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=The 'Mana Anchor' is the first essential requirement of a voidal shifter; It serves as the mage's personal tether to secure their return from the void as they traverse through\nit, meaning of course that the anchor is to be formed at the shifter's destination for them to move there. Without it, one would simply find themselves lost in the plane of knowledge.\n\nIrhamir then created one for me to exemplify its appearance -\nA black 'space' of energy, devoid of light and relatively small. From any angle it would appear as a flat disc and, according to my tutor, would not take another form for another mage.\n\nTo create this, in his words, one would have to \"pour mana and\nvoidal energies into a single location. This would form a conglomeration of them both, being a beacon of sorts to guide you through the void\". Advice which I, as a transfigurer, interpreted as essentially forming an aimless 'enchantment' in the desired\nlocation, which Irhamir did confirm accurate.  \n\nAs a versed enchanter prior to this lesson, it took me roughly an elven week before being able to comfortably produce a small anchor of my own, I would assume those without said experience to be slower.\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=Theory Lesson #2:\nTranslocation\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=Following the first lesson, Irhamir then conducted a brief lecture on the art of 'Voidal Translocation', in his own words: \"Translocation works by studying an object to\nunderstand how much mana it holds, and then you would send as much mana as the object holds into it and it will go into the void. The process for a shifter to enter the void is the same. Once you enter the void the anchor will pull you through.\" According\nto my teacher, my physical frame contains a certain amount of mana, whereas my soul cointains MY mana - as in the pool one would draw from to connect to the void. To enter the void I would simply match the Translocation process but on my own body.\nHowever as my soul would be the leading point though the void (unlike how a translocationist directs objects to and from themself, rather than directing their own forms), I would guide myself back to the physical realm via the mana anchor mentioned in\nthe first session.\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=Practical Lesson #1:\nShifting\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=After my time of theoretical study I arrived at a viable time to put my abilities into effect. To begin with Irhamir had first to consolidate my nerves by answering to me the\nfollowing: \"Would I risk losing a limb or any particular mass if I failed to use enough mana to shift my form?\" To which he explained I would simply be unable to shift any part of myself in such a scenario. Secondly I inquired \"Is it possible for one to\naim their anchor too low and have their feet lodged in the ground?\" Fortunately my tutor again reassured me such a risk is minimal, if not impossible. \n\nSo onwards I went to do as instructed; My first shift was an uncomfortable experience\nto say the least. I managed to travel just beyond the reach of my outstretched arm forwards by applying the earlier noted theories, then found myself incredibly dizzy. My line of sight and body pose stayed the same, however jolted into a new stance - as\nthough I had taken an incredibly quick step forward, but with no bodily action or muscular preparation. Black smoke quickly blanketed my form also, apparently, though I learnt this from my tutor's later report as I myself was too absent minded to keep\ntrack of such. The experience left me feeling 'out of place', horribly fatigued and with quite popped ears - perhaps from the pressure change in passing through the void, or simply the sudden speed of my movement. Needless to say afterward I retired with\nhaste and was unable to repeat the action until after some significant rest. With time, in accordance with all magics, I was told such would improve and truthfully it has.\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=This book is property of The Eternal Library of Haelun'or. -V.S.", ""),
        StaticBook("Voidal Theory", "John the Fair", "To begin this book, we must first ask what the Void is. For a simple description, it is an invisible plane of existence parallel to our own that allows a mage to create either a fireball, creature, what have you. For a more in-depth explanation, we'll\nhave to first understand a little bit about Conjuration. To keep it brutally simple, a living creature is evocated from the Void into what we deem reality, eventually teleporting back to the Void when the mage is done with whatever they were doing.\nIn fact, the Void surrounds us all, and permeates everything, from living beings to inanimate objects such as this book. Using this information, I have hypothesized the true nature of the Void, to be described in the next pages.\nI theorize that the Void is, rather than an invisible, driving force, is the stuff of everything. From the most simple item, to the most complicated life form, we are all products of the Void. Therefore, we can also theorize that an Angeudaemon, such\nas Metzli, is not an all-powerful, unreachable deity. Rather, these Angeudaemons can be better equated to very powerful mages. You can see something similar to what the Angeudaemons do in Transfiguration. The Transfigurationist, in a simple sense,\nmodifies the properties of an existing item via their own mana. So the Angeudaemons are just mages, considered much more powerful than us. Is this level of power unachieveable, or something that can be meticulously studied and accomplished?\nThis has yet to be seen, and instead of sullying and mulling over something that we might never be able to conclude in any lifetime, we should instead discuss the implications of what these findings mean. We can assume a few things.\n1) We are all creations of the Void.\n\n2) Our universe resides in the Void.\n\n3) We are unable to see the Void, because we are a part of its interior, much like a fish cannot tell it is in water, we as mortals cannot tell we are in\nthe Void.\n\nThe information laid out in this book might seem trivial to most. However, I cannot stress the importance of these findings. I challenge readers to create experiments to verify the statements made here. If we can understand the base\ncomponents that make up everything, we can begin to use magic in ways even more spectacular than what can be seen in our current state of mind. \n\nIf you have any inquiries, please send a bird to John the Fair, assuming he is not at the library.", ""),
        StaticBook("Vol. 1 : Gy'Waka", "Arnorian", "Introduction\n\nA Gy'Waka bird is a large 'bird like' creature that the Kharajyr came to discover in Karakatua. Their uses are many, transportation, food, battle, and much more. To be removed from it's enviroment causes the bird rather severe depression.\nHabitat and Lifestyle.\n\nThe Gy'Waka are native to the island of Karakatua, they are very rare and found nowhere else in the world apart from there. They are carnivores and will consume almost anything that vaugely resembles meat, this includes humanoids\ntoo. The Gy'Waka birds will never hunt the more dangerous humanoid creatures unless they are so desperate that there is simply no other choice, however they will happily kill and eat children that wouldn't usually pose a threat, on a daily basis. Their\nlong, sharkp break is perfect for pecking large chunks of flesh off a creature's bones, and their large springy legs mean they can cover shocking distances in a very short time, running faster than a horse. They do not however, have the most sensitive\ntongue, leaving them quite happy to eat anything they can.\n\nThey are not stupid creatures, in fact they are very smart indeed. The Gy'waka are able to mentally adapt to problems that may occur. For example, if they hear of a race that commonly hunts\ntheir kind in the distance, they will have remembered this, and flee. This also means that the Gy'waka has learnt to tolerate the Kharajyr as they began to see them as a source of food and protection. Although they are feathered, their layer of feathers\nis very thin due to their adaptation to the warm jungle enviroment. The reason the Gy'Waka birds settled on the island years ago, was due to the fact it was a haven for them - There they found plenty of prey and no predators. This has resulted in a\nsomewhat cocky personality in the Gy'waka - they will never look up, as they are the highest of all predators. This means the Kha' are able to jump down onto them with moderate ease.\n\nFortunately, the Gy'waka bird's exterior senses are\nvery strong. They have fair hearing, and would most likely notice you approach or move about them unless very stealthily. Their sense of smell however, is nearly completely defunct and useless. To make up for this, they have extremely keen sight. Their\nsight strength is undoubtably more powerful then that of a Kharajyr's which allows them to pinpoint their preys location fairly well. Gy'Waka do however, have two blind spots.\n\nDo not be fooled by the Gy'waka bird's wings. It is in fact, a flightless\nbird. It has long since evolved past the need for it's wrings as everything it ever needed was found on the ground of the island where they lived. Using their wings proved to be a waste of energy, so as they went on, they were no longer able to use them,\nyet they still carry smaller, vestigal wings useful for jumping.\n\nUnity with the Kha'.\n\nUpon arriving at the new Island, it didn't take long for the Kharajyr to discover the marvelous beasts that they named the Gy'waka, which loosely translates into\n'wings of our Goddess'. The Kha' believe that finding these creatures was a blessing from Metzli herself, and that they should respect her gift and make good use of it. As they first approached the Gy'waka birds, they did so with caution. The Gy'waka fled\naway from the strange creatures, hiding themselves in the furthest corner of the island as they began to work out what to do.\n\nThe Kha' approached them with offerings of both fruit and meat, laying them down in the jungle floor and then\nretreating to observe them from a distance. Much to their surprise, the birds consumed every last shred of meat, yet didn't touch the fruit at all. After a few more of these visits, the Gy'waka began to accept the Kha' as friends, now understanding them\nto be no source of trobule. They spread back out over the island and continued their day to day lives amongst the Kha', often filling their stomaches on meaty treats left by the Kha'.\n\nIt then didn't take long for the Gy'waka to allow the Kha'\nto approach and touch them, creating a new bond of companionship. They didn't seem to mind the Kha' strapping saddles and ropes to them provided they were offered a large amount of food in exchange. And so with that, the Kha were able to make use of\nthese giant birds that they had been so lucky to stumble upon.\n\nWritten by Charles Napier, Dean of Naturalism and Kharajyr Studies.", ""),
        StaticBook("Vol. 1 : Tongues", "Arnorian", "~*~ Languages ~*~\n\nDead Languages.\n\nOld Northeron: After the Highlanders migrated to the North of Aegis, they remained as one united people. They still spoke in Flexio then, but having to survive the harsh winters of Northern Aegis\ngave them little time for religious reflection, and as pagan traditions began to evolve, Flexio became less practiced as a language. It was still spoken, but began to warp from it's original form. This langguage's evolution was sped up by the Mountain\nDwarf clans fleeing from the Empire of Khorvad to the south. As the Grandaxe clan began to trade with the tribal men of the North, their tongue's became merged, creating a gutteral language known as Old Northeron. This language eventually died out with\nthe splitting of the Raevir people and the Hanseatic Tribes.\n\nClassical Raev:\n\nAfter the Raevir folk split off from their Hanseatic brethern into the East Highlander grouping of indigenous people, their tougne began to warp from\nisolation. Few in the south ever ventured to the frozen tundra of the Northlands and the Hanseatic tribes only conducted raids over the mountains every so often, and fought other Hanseatic tribes more than they fought Raevir tribes. This formed Classical\nRaevir, which was the common language of the many Raevir tribes up until the Carrions united the tribes into one sivereignty. After being driven out of Aegis by the undead's invasion of the North, the Raevir migrated to the lands of Asulon, in between the\ncity-states of Alras and Seventis. Caught between two common-speaking nations who were also the Raevir's main trading partners, they were forced to Evolve. Classical Raev died out as a language as the Carrion lord of the time swore underneath the Empire\nof Oren. All that exists now of Classic Raev is a crude dialect known as Botch.\n\nOld Common.\n\nAlthough still found in some bard's tales, the language of Old Common is very much dead. It is assumed that Old Common formed from a split\noff of Marian, when the Hanseatic peoples were the largest powerhouse in Aegisian Oren. Due to their merchant ways, as well as the their ways of war, they became an integral part of society, and their Marian language quickly replaced Flexio as a common\nlanguage. Marian was easier to understand for the peasant rabble of Oren, and Flexio became the language of the upper class and the True Faith. Because most peasants couldn't read or write, the language changed rapidly, morphing into old Common. Due to\nthe mistrust between the races in those days, Old Common did not spread very far for the Elves were still speaking Elvish in those days. In those days, Old Common was known simply as 'Orenian'. Old Common died off when it evolved into Common.\nBrae Adunian.\n\nTthough many believe Brae Adunian to be an offshoot bastard child of Thuaidian, Brae Adunian is in fact a child of Old Common. It was spoken by the Brae Clan of Adunians who worshipped the Old Faith primarily. Because the Old Faith was\nformed when the Adunians spoke Old Common, the Brae clan stuck to it even after Thuaidian was formed. The Brae Clan was known for it's stubborness.\n\nThuaidian.\n\nThe True name of the now dead Adunian language, there\nare very few Thuaidian words surviving. Thuaidian was formed as a mix of Old Northeron and Elvish resulting from the union of the two peoples. Most clans adopted it as their main language, though the Brae Clan continued to speak Old Northeron which soon\nMorphed into Brae Adunian. Thuaidian eventually died out when the Adunians left their isle and integrated back into Aegisian society, speaking the new language, Common.\n\nMori'Quessir.\n\nThough it is not certain we can call\nthis a dead language, due to the fact that anyone is unsure if the Mori'Quessir are still living or not, nobody other than they have spoken the tongue in decades. Mori'Quessir formed as a result of Nemiisae's teachings. It is an entire manufactured tongue\nwhat with Nemiisae not wishing for her children to speak Elvish, a language which she considered inferior. Mori was the spoken language of the Mori'Quessir for many centuries, and some Mali'Ker learned it when arriving in Asulon. Mori'Quessir died out\nwhen Asulon was flooded and the Descendant races migrated to Anthos. It is assumed that all the Mori'Quessir died.\n\nSabunani.\n\nIt is entirely impossible to tell where this language came from. The best guess\nwagered is that it evolved from the Dwarven tongue brought by the Dervas to Anthos. Nonetheless, this was the language spoken by the Zil'Maktumi. We can identify two periods in the language, Sabunani and New Sabunani. Sabunani was\ncharacterized by little to no vowel usage, wheras New Sabunani added vowels on for easier use. The Language died out with the Zil'Maktumi people.\n\nWritten by 'Watyll.'\n\nAnnotated by Arnorian Elendil.", ""),
        StaticBook("Vol. 2 'Adunai'", "Arnorian", "This blade became the official blade of house Elendil, and was passed down to the heir of the Adunian crown when he turned seventeen. No one is quite sure which Lord had the blade forged, but it is known that it happened around the reigns of the Lords\n'Dranan', 'Rymeul' and 'Anmas.' During Braen's (Dranan's father) reign, he commisioned a group of his finest archers and swordsmen to form an order of Elites, known as the Adunian Rangers - the sole military force of the Kingdom. This order would serve\nthe Kingdom for many years to come, under the command of several legendary Ranger Captains.\n\nDranan started another Adunian tradition, of burying each member of the Elendil family with a crown, each made out of a single Material with a gem on the\nfront. To have a steel crown meant that you were a brave and courageous warrior, whilst a gold one meant you were more diplomatically minded. A Silver crown would be a balance of both. A Diamond on the front of the crown would mean that you were an\nAdunian Lord, an emerald would mean you were a military man (Most commonly an Adunian Ranger), a ruby would mean you were a gifted Artisan, and a sapphire would mean you never found a calling, but were always willing to help others.\nWhen Rymeul came to the throne, he led an expedition back to the sea which his ancestor had crossed generations ago. He discovered a land bridge had connected the two realms, of Adunia and Aegis. Rymeul's grandson, Bethrol would then go on an expedition\nof his own across the land bridge and back into Aegis, where he discovered Idunia had long since been destroyed, and a new kingdom had arisen - The city, \"Al'Khazzar' and the Kingdom, 'Oren'. Bethrol came to arrange trade agreements with the Orenians\nwhilst on the expedition, and trade routes were formed. This was the first contact the Adunians had had with the outside world since the three hundred odd years of exile. \n\nOver the years, the Adunian settlement of Ildon turned from\nan Isolated village into a hefty city, then into a small Kingdom. By 'Rydel's' rule, the Adunian rangers were no longer sufficient to keep law and order in the Kingdom. He had his brother 'Thorenir' disband the Rangers, and start a larger force called the\nAdunian Legion. This decision, which was seen as foolish by some may have saved the entire Adunian race from destruction, as soon after this choice was made, Rydel's steward 'Icarian Delmar' turned agaisnt him, and attempted to ursurp the throne.\nThis marked the beginning of what would be reffered to in history books (such as this one) as the 'Great Adunian War'.\n\nWritten and annotated by Arnorian Elendil.", ""),
        StaticBook("Vol. 2 : Tongues", "Arnorian", "~*~ Living Languages ~*~\n\nFlexio.\n\nFlexio was the first language ever spoken by the descendant races, being that it was the language of the Aenguls and the Daemons. They taught it to the Four Brothers. However,\nafter the fall of Iblees and the great war between he and his followers, all but the Human race abandoned Flexio as a language. Elves, Orcs and Dwarves felt it was too corrupted by Iblees to continue speaking it. Flexio became a soley Human language.\nHumans felt it was a holy langyage that no evil being could ever corrupt. Flexio died out as a living language during the Aegisian period of history when it began to fracture apart. With the migration of the Farfolk people known as the Easterners to the\nEastern Isles, it slowly merged with their elven language to become Easterner. In the North of Aegis it morphed into the Highlander tongue known as Old Northeron. With the merging of Northeron and southeron peoples in Aegis, the language Illatian was\nformed. Aeldin Flexio was formed during the migration of people to the far islands in the verge, to the continent of Aeldin. Finally, Auvergnian was formed during the Old Kingdom of Auvergne in the Westlands of Orenian Aegis. The languages Illatian,\nAeldin Flexio and Auvergnian are all considered part of the Flexio Family of Languages. Flexio was reborn as a living language during the Holy Oren Empire under Emperor Godfrey Horen. Most nobles know it, and a few families speak it as their first tongue.\nIllatian.\n\nThe Illatian language formed from the commonly spoken Flexio in the midlands of Aegis, at the merging of Southeron and Northeron culture. It is still spoken today rarely.\n\nAeldin Flexio.\nThis language was formed by a group of human settlers who sailed through the Verge to the lands far, far to the East. This continent known as Aeldin, grew apart from much of the world and little is known about it. With the Great Orenian Exodus in Anthos,\nvast scores of the Empire's folk left to Aeldin and upon conqouring it, learned the language of their conquered people, just as the Aeldini learned Common. Upon the return of those who had left, Aeldin Flexio was brought back. It is most commonly spoken\nby the Chivay family.\n\nAuvergnian.\n\nThe Auvergnian language was born across the mountains from the Heartland of Oren, in the vast fertile lands of the West, in the Kingdom of Auvergne. Auvergnian society was one of beauty and honour,\nwhich their language reflects. As it evolved from Flexio, it changed to a flowing language that could be spoken without much effort. When Oren turned to adopting the Auvergnian culture, creating Knights instead of common soldiers, they adopted Auvergnian\nchivalry and other traditions. Kings began to dress in Royal Robes instead of Armor. Auvergnian is still a living language today, commonly spoken as a first language by the Valois and De Britagne families.\n\nWritten by 'Watyll', annotated by\nArnorian Elendil.", ""),
        StaticBook("Vol. 3 'Adunai'", "Arnorian", "Icarian and his followers started on the outskirts of the Adunian lands, taking villages and settlements one by one. They burnt houses, pillaged women, raped crops and took anyone left alive as prisoners. The Crops were sent to camps run by Icarians\nfollowers where they were treated like animals, while the men were tortured and brainwashed until they too followed Icarian. In a desperate attempt to find more soldiers, Rydel forced everyone between the ages of 17 and 110 into his brother's Adunian\nLegion. The war raged on for six years, until Thorenir was able to kill Icarian in a battle. At the begining of the War, the Adunians were at a large peak, with around 10,000 souls in Ildon, and around 8,000 in the countryside. The war ravaged the\ncountryside, leaving around 2000 left. Ildon was left a ghost town, with less then half it's population remaining.\n\nWith no longer the amounts of citizens that required the Legion, Thorenir disbanded the organization and\nrestarted the Adunian Rangers. The war had set back the race by centuries, but more than anything it had affected Rydel. Rydel was a diplomat, not a warrior, and seeing so many of the people he had known die before him. He eventually went mad.\nThorenir saw this, and decided to enact a peaceful coup'detat. Rymeul was lucid enough to call this an act of treason, banishing Thorenir and his wife Irene from his lands.\n\nLuckily, Rydel soon mellowed with age, and slowly became\nmore capable at his job once again. A few years before he was going to hand the throne to his youngest son, 'Aron', tragedgy struck. Aron, who was an Adunian ranger at the time was killed during a mission to clear out a cave full of orcs who had been\nraiding farms near Ildon. This left Rydel to rule for even longer, until his grandson Artorus Elendil the first came of age to rule.\n\nBefore Artorus's time came to rule, a fair greater tragedy struck. The undead threat that had\nbegun to sweep through the land from the north, and as they were further north than any other settlement, Ildon was the first place to be hit. Halboron Elendil, the eldest son of Rydel and the current leader of the Adunian Rangers, lead all the combat-\nworthy Adunians into battle agaisnt the undead, but it was not enough. Halboron was knocked unconcious during the battle, and all else were slaughtered.\n\nUpon waking, Halboron found the undead necromancers had left, but they had\nalready slaughtered all of the Adunians, and set Ildon alight. Halboron fought his way through the remaining undead minions to reach his house in Ildon. Upon entering, he found his nephew Artorus mourning over his mother's body. Halboron took the shards\nof Durendal from his lockbox, threw Artorus over his shoulder and fought his way back out of Ildon. The two travelled for many weeks, leaving the Adunian Kingdom and crossing back into Aegis. They reached the cloud temple at Aegis's center, and Halboron\nleft his nephew in the care of the monks. Before leaving, Halboron gave Artorus the shards of Durendal, in the hope that one day he might find a way to reforge the sword.\n\nFrom there, Halboron travelled back to Ildon to see what was left\nof the once grand city. Only smoking ruins remained. Halboron investigated the ashes of Al'Ildic where he found his father's charred body. He reluctantly prized the Circlet of Horen from the corpse before heading south to Oren, not to be reunited with\nanother Adunian for many years to come.\n\nWritten and annotated by Arnorian Elendil.", ""),
        StaticBook("Vol. 3 : Tongues", "Arnorian", "~*~ Languages Cont. ~*~\n\nMarian.\n\nMarian is a language that split off from Old Northeron. It's brother, Classical Raev is quite different. Marian evolved from the spoken tongue of the Westfolk, who lived in the mountains\nof the North, as opposed to the Raevir who lived on the flat frozen Tundra. The Westfolk became known as the Hanseatic peoples, and remained a harsh tribal people for a good long while after most other Humans had become civilized, they still raided the\nRaevir and the Southeron Lands. About half of the Hanseatic tribes left by the grace of the Wandering Wizard, and migrated to Asulon in search of new lands, but some stayed behind. Many of the remaining tribesmen moved into the Teutonic order city of\nNuremburg, and the language was absorbed by the Order members that lived there. Upon migration to Asulon, the Teutonic order found the ruins of the Kingdom established by the Hanseastic tribes who had left Aegis and migrated there, and named it Hanseti in\ntheir honour. Though the Teutonic Order is now disbanded and defunct, Marian is still spoken in Hanseti in Athera. The Marian language evolved into Old Common when the Northerners in Aegis migrated South and built a large trade league along the borders\nbetween Heartland and North. Though they were still what we could consider barbarians, they were also skilled traders, and their trade spread through the Heartland, and Flexio became replaced with Marian which evolved into Old Common.\nEasterner.\n\nThe Eastern tongue of the Eastern peoples of the Farfolk subrace of Humans evolved in the Eastern Isles of Aegis. It is a bastard tongue of Elvish which formed with the mixing of the two peoples. It is still spoken by all Easterners,\nmost prominently the Ishikawa family and the White Tiger Yakuza.\n\nOld Blah.\n\nOld Blah was taught to the Shamans of Aegisian Orcs by the Spirits. The Shamans, who were looking for a tongue to teach the Orcs besides Flexio which they\nconsidered corrupted began teaching them Old Blah. The language fit well with the Uruks, who could speak it well even with tusks. As Common began to rise to prominence however, it warped into the dialect simply known as Blah. Old Blah is now only spoken\nby Shamans.\n\nBlah.\n\nBlah is a warped and ugly dialect made by the merging of Common and the Orcish Old Blah. It was very few 'S' sounds, which are replaced with 'Z's. The grammer is nearly non-existant, and it is barely\nunderstandable by the other races. To add to this confusion, it still contains a great many Old Blah words, such as Bub'hosh, Nub'hosh, Rulg, Throm'ka, and others.\n\nElvish.\n\nElvish was first spoken in the Elvish lands in Aegis many\nyears ago. For reasons unknown, it was outlawed thousands of years ago and died out. The Elves switched to Common in favour of Elvish. It was the High Elves of Asulon who brought it back. It began to rise to prominence in Malinor (Anthos) as the High\nElves gained more power, and now in Athera, almost every Elf knows a bit of Elvish. Some High Elves speak it exclusively, though most of the words are lost to History. Perhaps someday the mysteries of Elvish will be uncovered. The Elvish language has\nthree child-groups. Thuaidian, which evolved by merging with the Old Common tongue of the Adunians, Easterner which evolved by merging with the Flexio tongue of the Easterners, and Mori, which merged with Proto-Asulonian.\nKharajyr.\n\nKharajyr is a language formed by the evolution of Proto-Asulonian into it's present form. It split off from the other Asulonian tongue, Mori'Quessir. Kharajyr is still spoken by the Kharajyr peoples today.\nBotch.\n\nA dialect spoken in the Highlands of Oren, it is a bastard child of the mostly lost Classical Raevir and Common. It rose to prominence during the Crow's age of Oren, when the Carrion family took the throne of the Empire. Raevir culture spread\nthroughout hte land, and Botch became commonly spoken.\n\nBlack Langguage.\n\nA language that can be naturally spoken by any being using, or formed by Dark Magic. According to Ikuras cultists, it was created by their Patron Ikuras, Greater\nSpirit of Fear and Insanity. In addition to being a common language spoken by the servants of Evil, Black language is used for spells in Phobism. Black language is most commonly spoken by the Ikuras Cult, the Necromancers, the Dread-Knights, and Shades.\nWritten by 'Watyll', annottated by Arnorian Elendil.", ""),
        StaticBook("Vol. 4 'Adunai'", "Arnorian", "Artorus eventually left the care of the monks and slowly made his way in the world as a military man. By the time Aegis was destroyed and it's citizens had voyaged to Asulon, Artorus was an esteemed military captain of the Phoenix Guard, which was the\nprimary military force of the Kingdom of Renatus. By chance, Halboron saw a notice in the cloud temple that had been placed by Artorus, claiming he was looking for his long lost uncle. Halboron traveled as fast as he could to Renatus where he was reunited\nwith his nephew. Together, they planned to reunite their race and rebuild what they once had.\n\nAfter many years of tireless work, Artorus and Halboron completed building a new Ildon in Western Renatus, by which time their family had grown\nimmensely. (Authors note: I was born at this time.) Many years after the time when it was acknowledged officially complete, Halboron met the end of his days due to an infected wound he had sustained serving Westfall as Lord Commander of the Westwatch.\nThe years pressed on, and Ildon continued to grow, eventually becoming one of the largest cities in Oren. As with all good things, they must come to an end - The Order of the Mongoose came to three figures - Artorus Elendil, Jon Norsem and Eze'kiel Tarus.\nThere, they convinced the three of a plot that in the House of Horen, lay the blood of Demons and the next undead uprising. Sold by the stout and trustworthy wizarding order, the three immidiatly rose in revolt in what they believed was for the greater\ngood, and were swiftly put down in a three day siege and battle in Ildon. Artorus and Eze'kiel were executed by Lancel Hightower (Who then forced marriage upon Eze'kiels Widow), and Norsem fell in combat. \nIn pity of Artorus's son Torrhen (My brother) the\nEmperor gifted him with the dukedom of Westfall in a successful attempt to sway Torrhen from wanting to rebel agaisnt Oren Himself. The Elendil family and the Adunian race continued to live in Ildon under Torrhen's rule, until the final days of Asulon.\nFrom there, the Adunians moved to the Isle of Elysium, where complex politics and a severe lack of land led to a terribly ugly bout of infighting amoungst the three young Elendils (I was a child at the time, too young to be concerned with said politics.)\nIsabella Elendil (My sister, age 17), Torrhen Elendil, aged 25, and Harrion Elendil, aged 35. It was during this time a near civil conflict broke out, and the two sides remained seperate well into the time of Anthos.\nWritten and Annotated by Arnorian Elendil.", ""),
        StaticBook("Volume 1 Orcs", "[Evarir] Kael'Daenor", "Behavioral Habits of the Uruk\n-----------------------------------------------------------    The Uruks although are often percieved as a primitive race of savages and brutes however that is not the case, although savage and brutish their are many\nintricacies of orcish culture that elude the other races.\n-----------------------------------------------------------Chapter 1 Clans\n\n  The Orcish warnation is comprised of family groups reffered to as clans, these clans are often based off of a famous\norc. The clan is usually comprised of the orc's descendants however it is not unheard of for clans to adopt new members through an initiation ceremony. Currently known clans are Lur, Yar, Gorkil and Azog the exiled Balrug clan is also worth mentioning.\nChapter 2 Orcish Subraces\n\n     The orcs are devided into several interesting subraces of varying strength and intelligence. The most common form of Orc is the Uruk, a large brutish creature typically standing around 7 feet tall with green skin and large\nprotruding tusks they are known for their bloodlust and aptitude for violence. Ologs, far and away the largest of the sentient beings to walk the land Ologs stand on average at 12 feet in height they typically have lighter skin and large tusks, be advised\nOlogs are incredibly stupid and should be handled with extreme care due to their unrivaled strength. Finally we come to the Goblins, Goblins are of the same stature as halflings however they are possessed of a feral cruetly and an innate cleverness that\nmakes goblins incredibly difficult to deal with, it is advised they be dealt with as bluntly as possible engaging them in games of riddles is not advised.\n----------------------------------------------------------\nChapter 3 Orcish religion\n\n     I was not able to garner very much information concerning the religon of the orcs, however from the meager scraps i was able to pick up  i believe the orcs worship spirits of nature as well as aspects of certain emotions or\nevents. They seem to be led by Shamans who have been educated in the ways of the spirits. Aside from that they seem to be devided into cults worshipping specific spirits, perhaps these spirits are more powerful or specifically significant? Their religious\norganization seems to resemble that of the Humans church of the creator in both its organisation and its compilation of various different religious orders.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------Chapter 4 Orcish War\n\n   Orcish warfare\nis remarkably void of tactics, The clans assemble as many warriors as they can and march off under the orders of the Rex in order to \"flat\" as many enemies as they can. Orcs are unable to use calvary due to their massive size being too great for horses to\nhandle therefore they go about warfare on foot. Orc typically employ oversized swords axes or clubs, however they're vulnerable to ranged attacks lacking skill in archery or magic therefore it would be wise to engage them from fortifications at a distance\nChapter 5 Orcish social Rankings\n\n      The highest ranking orc in orcish society is reffered to rex, modern orcs operate oddly for a warlike society with the rex acting as the head of a democratic council consisting of the Rex and the wargoth of each\nclan, a wargoth being the leader of each clan. Below the wargoths are the elders and nobs acting as kind of sergeants in the orcish society directing the grunts, youngest and weakest of the orcish war nation.\n\nTo conclude the strength of the orc warnation\nis not to be taken lightly therefore they should be approached lightly and engaged at a range as there are few none orcs that can beat an orc in a competition of strength. I advise they be advised at range from horseback or fortification wall.\n-Kael", ""),
        StaticBook("Volume 1: Adunai", "Arnorian", "In the years of ancient Aegis, there were no Kingdoms or cities, there were tribes and clans of Men, Elves, Dwarves, and Orcs. One of mankind's greatest tribes were the Harenites, a group of strong hearted warriors led by Harren, the First born of Horen,\nand one of his favourites. Soon the Harenites clashed with a tribe of Elves led by Princess Sarai of Malinor. The Two people fought for fifty years, until one day they finally made peace with one another. Weapons were thrown down, and soon the peoples of\neach tribe began to marry each other. The Blood from the Elves and the Human's mixed, and soon the first of a new race were born. \nThe descendants of the two tribes called themselves 'Adunian' and as one, they created the kingdom of 'Idunia' - one of\nthe first civilized settlements in Aegis, where they would rule over normal men for many years. During the rule of an Adunian called 'Arendil', the grandson of Haren, one of the pure-blooded humans living in Idunia called 'Owyn Godwinson' began a\nrebellion agaisnt the Adunians, sick of them ruling over his race. Sparing the gritty and long details, he succeeded and took Idunia for himself. Arendil was killed, and all Adunians were henceforth banished.\n\nArendil's son, 'Elendil' (Later to be\nknown as 'Elendil the Exiled') led the remaining Adunians to the far north of Aegis to get away from Godwinson and his forces, whom he feared would decide to chase after them and exterminate the scattered Adunians. The Adunians went as far north as\npossible, until they came to a large sea, (creatively named the Adunian Sea, by Lord 'Rymuel Elendil'.) Stretched out far before them. Elendil has his people build two boats, Salvation and Haren's Voyager. After months of labour, the Adunians completed\nthe boats and set sail across the sea, hoping to find a Haven for them to settle in peace on the other side.\n\nAfter a two month journey, the Adunians anchored their ships on the coast of a then foriegn land, and set off to find a fine place to settle. For\nanother week Elendil led the Adunians across an area of large open plains, and then into a thick forest of pine and spruce. It was within this area Elendil decided to settle, and put his people to work on building the town that would eventually be named\n'Ildon', meaning 'Haven.' The castle that sat on the hill nearby would be called 'Al'Ildic', meaning 'The Invincible.'\n\nThe Adunian race flourished in it's new Home, and under the rule of Elendil's descendants who\nbecame known as the House of Elendil. Elendil's only son, Braen Elendil became leader of the Adunian race, taking the title of 'Adunian Lord', and started the tradition of passing his title down to the youngest son, to give himself the longest reign\npossible. The Adunian Lord also wore a circlet called 'The circlet of Horen' which the Adunians believed to have belonged to Horen himself, before it was given to his son Haren, and passed down the line. Somewhere in the comming years, one of the Adunian\nLords had a blade forged, and specially enchanted, dubbing it 'Durendal.'\n\nWritten and annotated by Arnorian Elendil.", ""),
        StaticBook("Vote Sigismund", "Dima", "I, Dima, the most proficient food-smith of all the lands,\n\nHereby give my blessings,\n\nAnd right of vote,\n\nto Ser Sigismund the Hammer, for Mayor of Metz.\n\n    - дима", ""),
        StaticBook("Vourukhs", "Eath'Lur", "Vourukh\n-------\nI hath named one of these as large blood talons, considering their similiarity to the blood ravens bred by us, orcs, as carrier pidgeons. You may also call them \"The Rulers of the Sky\".\nWell, why do you ask me such a name?\n\nBy far, the vourukh was the largest bird I've ever seen during the hunts the spirit of the hunt, Votar, gave me.\n\nSo far, I've fought two of these almighty, powerful birds.\nThe vourukh is a very, very large bird that inhabits the deserts, making their nests ontop of tall sand dunes, as the omelet you can make from their eggs is exceptionally good, being a target for predators that eat eggs.\nThe vourukh is heavy himself and strong, strong enough to raise three uruks simutaneously. Fighting one alone is definitely not advised.\n\nIt's a carnivorous bird, predating on other desert birds and even jabbernacks.\nTheir plumage is also exceptional, being used often in shamanistical objects after being painted with the tint of the blood grapes, or simply raw.\n\nThey have a thick leather aswell, the best way to attack one is by stabbing with a spear.\nI shall repeat again: Do not hunt or seek one of these alone.\n\nWith this, I conclude this book on vourukhs, a beast native from the deserts.\n\n\n\n-Eath'Lur, shaman of the Lur clan.", ""),
        StaticBook("Vraen's Diary", "Vraen Dirgesinger", "The Writings of Vraen: Chapter 1:\n\nThe Churchill are retards.\n\nKind regards, Vraen\n\nPS: I stay only because the pay is good and the missus needs money", ""),
        StaticBook("Vydra: Vol I", "Andrik Vydra", "7th day of Malin's Welcome, 1491\n\nThe war is over.\nI sit here, in this empty hall, upon the seat of Humanity. The Lord's seat in Petrus, once grand capital of the Empire. \n\nI cannot help but feel utterl unaccomplished and empty as I write.\nOur once proud people are splintered into pieces, this farce of unity nothing but that - a facade. Petty squabbles and ambitious Lords litter my new Kingdom, but it was their swords and banners which placed me upon this throne.\n\nI have won a crown,\nbut now I find myself shackled to it, unable to act as a true monarch of men.\n\nWhat should happen when I pass? Who will follow? And if they succeed in keeping the Kingdom intact, what then shall come after? Our destiny as a people lies in the hands of -\n- indivduals who rise through whatever methods possible, no matter how incompetend, or cruel, or undeserving they may be. The reigns of Varon Kovachev in Akovia and Aleksandr who sat where I do now is testament to this. \n\nI fight now not just\nfor my homeland Akovia, but for all of Humanity. I must ensure that there is always someone to take up the mantle, even when I am but ash and memory.\n\nThere is much to do.\n12th day of The First Seed, 1491\n\nI have heard whisperings of discontent in my realm. In every corner, I see enemies. If only there were some way to purge these blinded fools in one fell sweep.\n\nDo they not understand?\nI AM Humanity. When I sleep, I see the destiny of our flock. Our people, MY people, shall reign supreme over all the lands from sea to sea. And then I wake to see the despicable state of things, the idiocy that has permeated itself throughout the very air\nthat we breath. The shortsightedness of my court is enough to make me sick. \n\nThe other races, even my own subjects - are not fit to rule themselves, squabbling as children do over toys.\n\nTo even attempt such a feat is monumental\nin itself, impossible in the current state that once proud Orenia finds itself. Personal armies and retinues dominate the nature of our marital strength. We must consolidate so that we may conquer.\n\nOne King. One Kingdom. One iron fist to smite down my -\n- my enemies in the form of the unwavering ranks of those who will see my vision into reality. My children, my Sons of Vydra - the Zealots of Man.\n\nMy legacy.\n20th day of The Grand Harvest, 1491\n\nUnfaltering strength is the only way to make others see reason, I have decided.\n\nThe weak are the easiest to manipulate, and any man can be made weak through force - A man cannot make a stand if\nhe has no legs with which to raise himself. \n\nMen mistake my silence for those very things I despise. Lethargy, indecision, weakness. How I pity the fools. Wisdom is patience. I sit and listen to them prattle and say nothing but simply nod. I watch on -\n- as they sneer and scheme, wringing their filthy hands with malice as they conspire against what I have build - what is yet to be built.\n\nBut one day, I will strike. \n\nWithout mercy and without remorse.\nI will gut them from head to toe, boil their children before their very eyes, let them watch on in terror as I skin their women alive. Their screams and pleas for death will do nothing for them.\n\nWho then, will have the will to oppose me? My vision?\nBut until that day - I sit and wait, and not like the buffoon they take me for.\n3rd day of Malin's Welcome, 1493\n\nObstacles do not exist to be surrendered to, but only to be broken.\n\nToday I walked past a great pasture field, full of grazing livestock. The grass within the field was dry - a field of nothingness.\nBut without...beyond the pitiful fences, that constituted the barrier between these feeding cows and freedom - was lush greenery, far as the eye could see.\n\nAnd yet they continued to roam aimlessly, picking at the dirt and dry patches of weeds.\nWhen the greater good is at hand, there is no length one should not go, no number of taboos taken up, traditions and expectations trod upon. I take the lesson those mindless creatures taught me to heart.\n\nOnly when every single possible -\n- option is exhausted, every terrible - deplorable - path explored, will I consider conceding. But only for the time being, for there is always another opportunity. Another man to kill. Another idiot to fool and bend like the branches of a tree in summer\nor if need be - break, like those in times of winter.\n17th day of The First Seed, 1493\n\nI am ashamed by my countrymen. They war seems to have given every human able to draw breath a bloodlust equal to that of even the savage Orcs to the west. There is no reason to it, no logic.\nThey cry for more and more with each battle, victory or defeat. What has happened to the versatility of Humanity? We are not weapons forged for war, a people with a purpose so singular and barbaric as simple slaughter.\nWar is raged for a purpose, and the day that purpose is for the simple slaughter of others and razing of homes is the day I set down my crown and relinquish any notion that Humanity is truly superior.\n\nYou cannot rule the dead.", ""),
        StaticBook("Waiting", "Sarya", "My love for Hero is so great\n\nMy heart melts for it 'til the dusk of day.\n\nThe night demons when it's away, attack, sword 'til day's dawn\n\nIts beauty is great\n\nWondering mind 'til it sees,\nfighting is all I do,\n\nWhile waiting for the moment, for it to say \"I do.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("War Plans", "Eepz the Ogre", "We have plasn to cross the Ogre pens now, we will send our greastest warriors across to capture my brother. I am sure we can takeback the seal's key...\n\nOur forces are ready, and should no events stop us, we should sweep through his weak forces.\nDisaster has struck... These war plans shall be scrapped and we must deal with this stout menace now", ""),
        StaticBook("War Story", "Uther Conrad", "It was a dark and gloomy day. The Flays were runnig up the the gates of Frostholm. The Nortruppen were defending the castle from the Flays. The Nortruppen were shooting arrows as the Flays hit the man next to me. I yelled It's Raining men.\nThe men of the Nortruppen fought valiently and defended the keep very well.\n\n\nBassed of a real War Story", ""),
        StaticBook("Water Evocation", "Haadi Mubdee", "Water, appearing to be possibly one of the most simplest of the elements, however, it’s more than such. It’s an incredibly complex element in which one must spend a large amount of time meditating and spending there time around water in general to be able\nto learn such an evocation such as itself. Water is a necessity of life, needed by generally all living things, for example; Humans, Orcs, Dwarves, Kharajyr, Elves and also plants, including beasts too. Water, also appearing as such a calm element is also\none of the most dangerous, out in the seas, a storm can take out a fleet of ships within moments, one can never have full control over water that isn’t evocated, well, practically no control whatsoever unless you’re of course, a Shaman. Despite our\nattempts, we are mortal, we do not live forever nor do we have amazing powers unlike the Ascended and Undead back in Aegis; as said before, water can be a very dangerous element, a single flood can wipe out a town, contaminate food and destroy buildings\nwith ease. A harsh winter, such as the one's in the North of Anthos and around the Dwarven regions which could halt one's food supply for months on end. The element, water contains raw power, a power that all Water Evocationist's would wish to wield.\nA Water Evocationist’s training consists of learning about the void, being able to evocate from it and about the element one is learning. It takes years on end to learn about evocating a single element. Water which has been evocated may appear to be the\nsame as the water we have around us, however, it is completely different. The water that us Water evocationist’s evocate can only be found in the void and some say it isn’t water at all. As all evocoationists know, their power comes from the ability to be\nable to control ‘mana’, mana is your life force in a way. If you use it to much then one would simply fall unconscious or they can even die from the overuse of course. After much dedication and training; such as spending time to learn about the void\nand about Water Evocation, a Water Evocationist is able to pull mana directly from the void, shaping it into a water-like substance in our world. This connection to the void is rather difficult to explain, however, once one has managed to learn about\nWater Evocation itself, then you should be able to understand about it and where we're coming from. One’s connection to the void is more of a sensation than something that can be explained as a mage’s training progresses, connecting to the void and\nevoking said element becomes more and more simpler tasks. As one would possibly notice, many mages use a staff, however, it isn’t needed much, though, it’s easier to focus upon, usually the tip for most and you would be able to evoke water from the tip,\ntoo. When water has been evoked, it can be placed into many forms, such as a jet of water, an orb of water, an orb of ice and other things which I generally haven’t explored yet.\nWater Evocationist’s which have been learning for a long period of time will\nbe able to use more things and be able to explore other skills such as learning to control ice which is also evoked from the void. Ice is more suited for battle than defence, however, water evocation itself is mainly used for defence than anything.\nHowever, ice can be evoked and be used to create walls, freeze doors shut, block incoming projectiles as a form of short-distance defence, and as a method of harming others too. Ice that we evoke isn't the same which can be found in our realm, it cannot\nbe melted by the heat of the sun nor a torch, however - it can be melted with the use of Fire Evocation. To break the ice, the Water Evocationist must either lose concentration, or as said before, a Fire Evocationist must melt the ice with their evoked\nfire. In the later stages of Water Evocation, one would be able to evoke wisps of steam, however, it's possibly too difficult for even the best of Water Evocationist's to do such. Water, being able to form any concievable shape, is only limited by the\nby the caster's imagination and fatigue, which the exception of finely detailed creatures of sort. Such is reserved for Elemental Conjurationists. With proper training, water can be suited for nearly any purpose.\nCopied by Haadi Mubdee, Instructor in the Mages' Guild. 1471", ""),
        StaticBook("Ways2DealWImpure", "[Ghost] The Eternal Librarian", "Liberals,\n  Dissidents and\n   the Impure:\n The Ways to Deal        with Them\n    Accordingly\n\n      by Nelecar\nForeword\nAs steadfast upholders of the mali’aheral ways, we must recognize the threats caused by these three subgroups to our blessed way of life. There are key differences between them, and factors about them vital for\nthe average citizen of Haelun’or to know - in this text, I do so hope to explain such.\nChapter One:\n      Liberals \nA liberal is a fellow Mali’aheral such as you or I who has fallen prey to the hedonistic and frivolous ways of the wood elves. They believe incorrectly and immaturely that we as a whole are wrong and they are right -\nthat our discrimination has ‘no basis’ and we should be equals with the vile orcs.\n\nThey are blatantly wrong in this regard; if you see or think you may have had any knowledge of a liberal, report it to the officials as soon as possible.\nFrom my studies and research, I have recognized that there are two main subgroups inside the liberal circle. These are:\n\nThe Dormant Liberal\nDormant Liberals disagree with our ideals, however they do not plan on taking\naction against them currently, and remain very silent about their opinions. While they may not seem to be, they can be potential threats to the government and the Mali’aheral way of life. They are essentially a seed stage, and dormant liberals can\nprogress into volatile liberals.\n\nThe Volatile Liberal\nThe volatile liberal disagrees with our ideals, and takes or plans to take action (albeit from the shadows) against them.  They try to recruit others to their cause subtly. While they are\nmuch more dangerous, they are far less subtle than dormant liberals are- dormant liberals, of course, keeping their opinions entirely to themselves.\n\nLiberals are perhaps the hardest of all to quell, and their punishment varies on severity, however\nideal course of events is to have an agent identify the liberal and zone in on him. A warning will be given most of the time, however in extreme cases (such as a desire to overthrow the government) a more permanent measure will be needed.\nChapter Two:\n     Dissidents\nThey are always sympathizers of the lesser races.\n\nDissidents tend to be easier to deal with in most cases - however sometimes they take refuge in other nations, particularly in nations where free\nspeech is permitted. In these cases they may be protected by law. The appropriate punishment is imprisonment (as exile wouldn’t work due to the previous statement), however in medium-to-high cases execution may be needed to prevent further offenses.\nChapter Three:\n    The Impure\nPerhaps the most heinous of the three groups is the unclean. An impure is one born of a Mali’aheral and a non-mali’aheral. Breeding with a member of the lesser races is perhaps the worst crime in our society, far\nsurpassing murder and thievery. They are often belligerent, troublesome, and corrupt, and would see us in ruin. They have many supporters despite their nature. Exile is the appropriate punishment for being an unclean and having intimate relations with\na non-Mali’aheral, whereas execution is the appropriate punishment for procreating with one.", ""),
        StaticBook("Wayward's Return", "Dragaar Aldirar", "A Wayward's Return\n\n\n       Published\n          1593\n\n\n\n        Author;\n   Dragaar Aldirar\nIt was strange, being here again after so long, but the strange feeling which lingered in my throat only grew to become a sign of great comfort as my gaze sat upon the spires which stretch upwards like some sort of marble tree which was planted by Larihei\nherself. However in spite of the years that had passed since our departure I still remember most everything of this place; the blue roofings which scattered the marble homes, the gentle softness of voices trickling the streets which met my ears with\nkindness. Taking a deep breath, I truly realized that it was indeed correct in stating that one may take the man out of their home but their home shall forever reside within them, and for me my home is with my kin inside the silver city of Haelun'or.", ""),
        StaticBook("We come as crows", "Unknown", "------------------- -------------------   We come as crows\n-------------------\n \n\n      _IIII\n     --IIIII\n         IIIIII\n         IIIIIIIII\n          IIIIIIIIIIII=-\n             IIIII\n              _I.\nIt was a quiet night in the city of Kralta. The never-ending, calming trickle of the murky riverwater was one of the few sounds that were heard through the night. Occasional caws of the crows echoed through the muddy pathways and alleywas of the city, as\na single woman walked in the night. Slutinyova, the most beautiful woman in the city, though, she hadn't managed to find any work in the city yet. On her way towards the inn, she heard an odd sound in the night. She gazed upwards to the sign.. \"Smithery\"\nThe name was carved on the sign. A quiet, steady banging could be heard inside. Her curiosity took over, and she snuck inside in quiet steps. The planks creaked under her foot as she was fully inside, and she attracted the smith's attention. He had been\nhammering a sword all alone in the night.\nThe smith quickly put the unfinished sword away as he noticed Slutinyova, ashamed of his work. Slutinyova, however, didn't mind. In fact, she thought the sword looked mighty.\nSurely the sword had thrusted through\nmany challenges and stretched even more wounds. \n\n\"Make leave, customer, smithery am closed!\"\nThe smith said.\n\n\"Worry not, am here to help! Sword looked like needs many grinding and polish.\" She claimed.\nThe blacksmith allowed a sigh escape his lips as he presented the his sword to her. She gently took the sword in her hands, examining it with a curious eyes.\nThe blade was great in size, yet it had its faults, it was curved to the side slightly.\nSlutinyova held the sword for a bit, before starting to work on it.\n\n\"I'm sure I know what I'm doing.\" Slutinyova said, as she brought the sword to the grindstone. The blade began getting in better shape with each swipe against the\ngrindstone. It would soon be finished. The sword started to look like it was done. The smith seemed very happy of the outcome, though she wasn't completely done with the sword.\n\n\"Slutinyova must make polish of sword!\" She said enthusiastically.\nShe took the banner in the colours of Carrion in her hand, rolling it around her palm before she rested it against the mighty fine blade. The unladylike manner she polished it was astonishing, furiosly she swiped against the sword up and down. Across the\nblade, until finally it looked like it was ready.\n\n\"Am done.\" she said, when she finished and the blade was finally done and it gleamed with victory and glory.\nThe smith smiled, as the most tedious part of creating merchandise was made\nin his stead.\n\n\"Many thanks, woman.\"\nhe said, continuing;\n\"But now must make way to fix creak-plank on floor, da?\"\nThe smith said, as he rested his sword. He moved over to the plank Slutinyova had stepped on, that let out a nasty creak\nas she stepped over it. He took the hammer he had been using earlier, beginning to nail the plank back to its place. It was unheard of to bang this loud in the night of Kralta, yet the plank was soon as good as new. \"Now all am ready for business, make\nstay for assistance?\"\nThe smith said.\n\"Da, da, da!\" She nodded in reply hastily, happy to finally find work..\n\nand so they made many swords together for the glory of Raevir.", ""),
        StaticBook("Weapons of war", "Walter Marshall", "Weapons Of Modern War\n\n By Walter Marshall\n\nVolume I, Weapons of the Golden Crow\n\n23rd of The First Seed\nKaedreni Longsword\n\nThe Kaedreni longsword is a staple weapon of all Highlander forces. Able to be wielded with a single arm and carry a shield alongside it. This razor sharp blade is a formidable weapon when used by a professional.\nHaensetic Arming Sword \n\nThe Haensetic Arming Sword is the primary weapon of the Brotherhood, It is given to fresh Man-at-arms upon acceptance, Although many prefer to use the Kaedreni Longsword when they-\nachieve a higher rank and gain access to more weapons, no man in the Brotherhood forgets their Haensetic Arming sword.\nScylfing Hand Axe\n\nThe Scylfing Hand Axe is deadly close range weapon popularized and produced in bulk by the Colborn family for use by Haensic soldiers when facing heavily armored foes hand to hand.\nTheir expert make and craftsmanship led to the victory of many Haensetic battles. A true staple of the Brotherhood and Colborn artisanry.\nStrannik Lance\n\nThe Strannik Lance is a formidable halberd that was adapted from the heavy Ruskan cavalry known as the Stranniks. Now used as a pike in order to fend off cavalry charges,\nit is a staple of the Brotherhood of the Golden Crow when fighting those who may be on horseback.\nAdunian Claymore\n\nThe Adunian Claymore is a giant sword capable of destroying any foe. Used without a shield, the Claymore is wielded with two hands. If it does not cut through armour, the sheer trauma of being hit by it is enough to stagger a man.\nWaldenian Warhammer\n\nThe Waldenian Warhammer is a fairly bulky weapon of significant weight reserved for the slaying of undead or heavily armored opponents. With a blunt face on one half of the head and a piercing crow’s beak on the other.\nThe hammer is crafted of the finest northern steel providing a good strong weapon with lots of power and weight behind its swing.\nKaedreni Arablest\n\nThe Kaedereni Arablest is a common weapon found during sieges and other large skirmishes, its long range and tough oak stock make it not only durable but deadly.\nHowever its increased reloading time and overall bulkiness prevents most soldiers from carrying one when not expecting large conflicts.\nBarbovic Lever Crossbow\n\nThe Barbovic Lever Crossbow was made famous during its tenure in the Gold Corps when protecting Felsen from Dreadlanic raids. Carried often by the defenders. The Barbovic Lever Crossbow was a medium power quick reload crossbow.\nThe men who wielded it praised its ability to fire shots in quick succession while being easy to maneuver within the tight streets and alleys. Mostly used by men on patrol or in urban environments.\nBarbovic Shield\n\nWhile many of the  new recruits are given whatever shields are present, that is not the case for the more experienced men of the order. There is a delicate balance between the weight of the shield, and the protection it offers.\nThese shields have been forged with that balance in mind, crafted in a curved rectangular fashion. The size offers a fair amount of  mobility to the user, while the curved design is effective at deflecting many different kinds of arrows and projectiles.", ""),
        StaticBook("Weapons Of War 2", "Walter Marshall", "Weapons Of Modern War\n              Volume II\n      Siege Weapons of The\n     Brotherhood Of The\n          Golden Crow\n\nBy Walter Marshall\nEngines of War\n\nIn order to effectively wage war, the Brotherhood has multiple engines to destroy fortifications. Taking from a vast variety of past Orenian engineers the Brotherhood is capable of waging war on a wide variety of fortifications.\nKaedreni Onager\n\nThe Kaedreni Onager is a small catapult utilized by Kaedreni forces in the sieges of Malinor, aiming to destroy small fixed fortifications while also being able to fire multiple projectiles at once in order to slaughter lines of infantry.\nThe weapon, while having a short range, is surprisingly effective at destroying enemy units.\nCarnatian Mangonel\n\nThe Carnatian Mangonel saw its main usage during the Eighteen Years War at the sieges of Rhewengrad, Kal’Valen, and Kal’Ordholm.\nThe Carnatian mangonel is a weapon capable of hurling very heavy and large projectiles over vast distances, causing its target to turn to rubble.\nHansetian Ballista\n\nThe Hansetian Ballista is a weapon which was created by the finest engineers of the Teutonic Order under the leadership of Mirtok DeNerum. With long range and accuracy it is a formidable weapon to wage war.\nIt is ideal for destroying other siege weapons, groups of personnel and and ships. However its wooden bolts have little effect on stone walls.\nHuron Trebuchet\n\nUsed extensively in the recent wars the Empire has faced the Huron Trebuchet has faced many battles from seahelm to the Forest of Huron of which its named, where it flung rocks at Krakens watch during the Courland/Carnatian war\nThe Huron Trebuchet uses a counterweight rather than manpower to fling boulders and other projectiles weighting up to 350 pounds across the battlefield or into enemy fortifications.", ""),
        StaticBook("Wes Osullivan", "Vanbrek zu Holtz", "-=Wes Osullivan=-\n\n       Written By:\n         -V.z.H.-\n\n\n\n       First Edition\nChapter 1\n\nThe sacred objects of my desire are ones not lusted for by men of sylvan heritage.  They are ones of a man newly enchanted by a city that glows both day and night.  A distinct shift has occurred in the world. Those who once made\ntheir petty livings slaving away in the countryside have found new hope and oppertunity in the great cities of Athera, namely Petrus.  Perhaps the only two things I have found to rival this great town are money and women.  Standing atop the bell tower of\nthe Petrus cathedral, I can not help but feel pulled by the indescribable energy the people emit below, spraying from the torchlit streets into my hungry eyes.\n\nThe priest known as Vincent Divine, who shares a name with an intellectual from old,\nwas distinct from his predecessors, favoring kind words and a warm smile over crucifixions and holy war.  His clothing was that of color, and his speech that of healthy and curious skepticism. He and I became good friends after I had moved to the city,\nseeking wealth and freedom from an oppressed life in the rustic fields, far from commerce.  Here, anything was possible.  The problems one faced while about the city were much different from those suffered under the tenure of a landed lord.  Now, the only\nlords were that of financial aristocrats, watching over the city with a seperate and innately different brand of lordship.\n\n        Chapter 2\n\n\"Good to see you, friend!\"\n\"Indeed, it is a pleasure to find your\ncompany in such a lovely location, Wes.\" spoke Vincent Divine, his face shaded by the Maer's Garden.  It was a beautiful time of morning, when the sun first casts its golden arrows into the sky so that they may streak across the fading stars.\n\"You are well read, Vincent, does this city remind you at all of the old Aegean capital?\" I asked, eager to compare the advances of Petrus to the standing accomplishments of fabled Al'Khazar.\n\"In some ways, yes.  I believe it is finding its identity, the\ncollective mass of humans searching together for a common grounding.  It is too early to tell.\"\nDivine had always been a bastion of intellect and free-thinking, despite his profession as a clergyman.  Ever since the wild influx of migrants from the outer\nreaches of Oren, he has found himself wildly successful in his career.  I knew to trust his judgement, but the question still lingered in my mind as a bee intent on pollen might hover about a vibrant golden flower.  \n        Chapter 3\nArt Kettleston was his name.  He sat in the corner of Parton's Tavern, wooing some hollow girl with equally as empty words.\n\"I am rather rich.\"\n\"Oh?\"\n\"Yes.  I have become so boringly rich.\"\nI frowned a disgusted frown and smirked a superior smirk all at\nonce.  To drown out his annoying voice I strode to the ale counter.  There stood a slightly thin framed girl, beautiful and shining.  It was easy to tell she hailed from somewhere remote in the countryside, somewhere as vibrant as that golden flower.\nI fell in nostalgic love.\n\nI found myself standing near Art after an exciting and whimsical conversation with the barmaid, whose name was later revealed to me as Elena Appleheart.  Her reaction to my rather generous tip, given in the form of a large\nsum of mina, had already cast the image of my wealth to those in the restaurant.  Finding my way to Art Kettleston, I could not restrain myself from inquiring-\n\"How much do you have, then?\" I politely interjected into his pitiful courtship attempts.  His\nresponse was that of a medium sized fund, nothing worth spouting pretentious triumph over.  I brought myself to setting a hand upon his shoulder and offering a sympathetic smile, not for his quanitity of mina, but for his arrogance.\nChapter 4\n\nDespite my sedulous collection of wealth, I remained- for the most part- humble.  I was not easily angered or driven to a heated feud.  When Elena revealed to me that Art was a writer, I found myself utterly defeated.  This\ncasually conceited author had more success as a wordsmith than I had ever.  This, due completely to never having had written before, angered me because of my aspirations to compose but my lack of motivation in doing so.  Reading his\nwell-crafted fiction compelled me to take my own shot at penning.  Elena and I became closer entwined during my early dabling in writing, mixing the integrated city dweller and the longing bucolic dame in a dance of love and confliction.\nMy first novel was a success.  It sold as rapidly as it was printed, taken home and read, studied.  Studied, of all things.  Even the established Priest Divine found it remarkable and symbolic.  A boiling rivalry was forged the moment Kettleston received\na copy.  A clash as fierce as the population war between the declining meadowland villages and the behemoth Petrus.  Elena, charmed by my substantial wealth and dazzled by my success, stayed with my in my flat hung care-free above and\nbeside Market Street.\n\n       Chapter 5\n\nThe city shown as bright at night as it did at day.  People seemed to always be about, sometimes heading to no location in particular.  Petrus had become open, inviting.  Just months\nbefore my formal moving-in, I would have been scared stepping a meter within the walls- fearing of some form of persecution.  There was an air of welcoming about the city now, and more importantly, about the people.  While the battle between Art and I\ngrew horribly intense, with each of our works topping one another, it seemed to serve as the epitome of fundamental change within Humandom.  New intelectual competition had risen in Petrus, exemplified in our condition.\n\nMy drive became,\neven above wealth, to beat Art Kettleston at his own game which I so coveted to monopolize.  Even Elena felt forgotten; my obsession with writing had manifested itself in long hours spent dipping a feather in ink and scratching upon soft parchment,\ncovering white in black.\n\"Mr Osullivan, good day!\" yelled a familiar voice, in derisive manner, from outside my apartment.  I opened my door, descending the steps to the cobbled street.\n\"Kettleston, have you come to tell me of your golden and monotonous\nlife?\"\n\n        Chapter 6\n\nRed streaked across my face, dripping in scarlet hues upon the roughly lain road.  His fist was dotted with bits of crimson, flung from the impact.  Elena hurried down the stairs with a bandage,\nshouting word I could not comprehend, the shock blinding my senses.  She extended her arms, wrapping them around my body as if to usher me back into the home so that the incident might simply be forgotten.\n\"You bastard!\" was the last he heard before a\nreciprocal force impacted his despicable features.  The arc of my fist flew across the busy city scene much as the city itself was, rising to an interim peak.  In that moment, caught up in the intensity of the fight, I later realized I had answered my own\nprior question.\n\n        Chapter 7\n\nElena was gone the next day, repulsed by city life.  She came seeking a living for her downtrodden self, but quickly became disenchanted with the lifestyle involved in doing so.  She seemed\nto have had favored the waggish methods of the detached.  The nostalgia of first meeting her, recalling the golden fields of wheat in doing so, remained with me even as she departed.  I was fused to the city at this point, unable to return to a pastoral\nbirth.  Art was downed after my fury found itself upon him, leaving him in a mental state unfit for writing or challenging me.  I had won, but only in a sense.  There was nothing fulfilling in being the only prominant writer within the town's partition.\nThe spirit of neverending tournament, with every soul vying for dominance, is what defined my life in Petrus.  A state of constant improvement, and sacrifice.  Now, with the combination of Elena's disillusionment and my substantial wealth, the city had\nbecome dark even when lit by the soft and flickering glow of burning torches.\n\n\n        Epilogue\n\nMy personal and domicile arc had crested.  Although the golden flower welted, the bees persisted in\na constant search for the lustrous hue.  Unable and reluctant to escape from my own free will, I found myself down the steps of the cathedral tower and back into my dimly lit home.\nAuthor's Note\n\nThe story of Wes Osullivan is one of true events, altered and brought together as one coherent tale.  The state of the world is a constantly changing one, a story writing itself.  The dramatic shift from rural living to close\nurban dwelling is one that may affect us for the better or worse, but it will most certainly affect us.  I am excited to enter this new era, and Wes Osullivan seeks to explore what truly defines our time.\n\n        -V.z.H.-\nSpecial thanks to Dravage and Durheim for the inspiration and friendship they confer unto me.", ""),
        StaticBook("What is Balance?", "Zahir Darthirii", "Once a Druid has been deemed worthy and has helped out enough around the Grove and with members of the Order, then an Arch Druid will see that and promote that Druid to Guide. Guide Druids have the ability to attune Dedicants to full fledged Druids.\nThey also should be of advanced wisdom than the normal Druid. But not all must reach the requirements. It really depends on the Arch Druid who notices the work that Druid has done for the Order.\nThis book was originally found in the Druid's Grove in Elandriel, in Asulon. It was brought over and transcribed by Elorna Avern.\n\nAnd now copyed by Zahir\nDarthirii.", ""),
        StaticBook("What is Love?", "The Eternal Library", "What is Love?\nby Unknown\nLove?\nWhat is love?\nMerely an entertaining hobby?\nOr just something to produce the next generation?\nOh how?\nHow do you love?\nHow do you get\nThat tender\nPassionate\nThumping\nSpeeding\nHeartbeat?\nFrom the long told fairy tales.\nWhat of the intense burning inside?\nThat were told by old couples.\nDoes love deserve your undivided attention?\nWhat is love?\nWhen one has not yet experienced?\nOr is it a simple personal journey\nThat everyone will pass one day?", ""),
        StaticBook("What Motivates?", "Hektor Blackwood", "From the beginning of time, when Godani's light pierced the shadow forming a veil between our realm and that of the Occ ult, placed a man and a woman upon the earth, and bred the first Descendants, these sentient minds cultivated hunger for Enlightenment.\nSomke became Wizards,Priests, Alchemists, Thinkers, ect. They all had different means tethered to their craft, with the Priest being bastions of faith. Wizards associated themselves with wisdom and knowledge, studying the weave of magic.\nThinkers unfolding the barriers off their hungering yet still physically bound minds. The chief concept has never changed even to this day; those of applying minds strive for enlightenment. One of the most pivotal questions concerning such is sentient\nbehavior, specifically the sole motivator of sentient behavior and action. From the contents of this parchment and ink, we together as author and reader shall explore this. What is the most, generlized motivator(s) that the mind can conceive as to why a\nperson performs an action? To answer as adequately as possible, provoke the question to yourself; why does a common man consume fine pastries and drink fine wines? An answer is quite difficult to cultivate at first as those of philosophical minds have\ntaught to broaden the conscious to the astronomically colossal thesis's that we often neglect the impact a simple question can have. The answer is dumbfoundingly simplistic; it delivers pleasure to said person. This is why said person would naturally\ngravitate towards eating the pastry or drinking the wine. The polar oppisite would be why a person avoids eating moldy bread or being stabbed; it delivers pain. In terms of sentient motivation, it is impossible to go upwards or sim-plpify the reasoning\nbeyond those two simple words of pleasure and pain. Though through this formula of thought, a philosopher can rationally break down practically any question concerning the motivation of sentient beings with relative ease. A person may argue\nthat people perform charity towards another person through sheer affection and that said person does not gain anything. Though the person obtains a \"good feeling\" of happiness for performing charity. The circcumstances are extremely broad, due to how\nactions themselves are so broad. your author is no cynic, and believes that there is such thing as a \"good\" and \"bad\" decision. If a person draws pleasure from the pain of others, they are a monster. If they draw pain from the pleasure of others, they are\ndepressed and sad individuals. If they draw pain from the pain of others, they are an empathic person. If they draw pleasure from the pleasure of others, they are benevolent, and so this is the key machination of the moral compass.\nYour author in no way seeks to catagorize a specific person with the traits of seeking pleasure and avoiding pain. All creatures possess this trait. I do, you do, your neighbour does. No one is truly \"Selfless\" due to this law of the mind, there is only\nhow people interact with the pleasure and pain of others. So wizards, become the bastions of wisdom and intellect if it is your desire. Warriors, be virtuous and strong, if that is what you desire. Do what pleases and fulfills you as long as it does not\nsap the pleasure of the virtous, pious and deserving. \n\nI truly wish this humble piece of parchment tied together into a book has given you the key knowledge of pleasure and pain.\n\n~Hektor Blackwood", ""),
        StaticBook("whatdoiputhereaa", "Zyvia Ba'ikana", "My Dearest Erolas,\n\nI, to, hope this letter finds you in good health and good company. For seven years I wondered quite often what our lives had come down to. The 7 years you took a leave of absence, I lived in constant doubt and worry. Not only for you,\nbut for our relationship and our precious daughter. \nYour letter has put my doubts to rest, but not my worry. As capable as I am, worry is my downfall.\nTo put your doubts at ease, I have not left you. I would never dream of it, nor act on it. To you I am\ntrue.\n\nI just hope our paths will cross again in the near future so your wonderful smile can light up my life once more.\nMay the aspects guide you.\n\n~Zyvia.\n((yes i know i made a grammar error on the first page but i can't fucking be bothered to remove the entire chunk of text to fix a fucking grammar error so ignore it bb ty xx))", ""),
        StaticBook("Wheat", "Nynaeve Sagehand", "Jae,\n\nI have been grinding farming and I didn't want to feel like a complete ass for harvesting all the wheat in the farm since I knew you grind your chef stuff so here is the wheat I gathered so I can grind my farming <3\n               Marsi", ""),
        StaticBook("Whitestorm Ck.Bk", "Rosso", "Baking with the\n      Whitestorms\n  Some of\nThe family’s\n    Favorite recipes.\n             James\n\n       Whitestorm\nVolume One:\n               Cakes\nBasic Cake\n----------\nServes an entire party. Prepare long in advance, and douse in brandy to prevent mold.\nIngredients\n----------\n1 lb Oat Flour\n1 lb Egg\n1 lb Sugar\n1 lb butter\n½ cup Candied OrangePeel\n½ cup Candied Lemon Peel\n½ cup Candied Citron\n1/3 Cup Currants\nIngredients Contd.\n----------\n½ Cup Almond Flour\n1 Tsp Nutmeg\n1 Tsp Mace\n1 ½ Tsp Cinnamon\n1 Tsp Ginger\n1 Tsp Cloves\n¼ Cup Sherry\n¼ Cup Brandy\nDirections\n----------\n1. Heat stove to adequate temperature. Grease a 10 inch pan in preparation.\nDirections Contd.\n----------\n2. Beat the butter in a bowl until creamy. Add sugar and beat until fluffy. Stir at a medium speed while gradually adding in egg, until thoroughly combined.\nDirections Contd.\n----------\n3. Sift the Oat Flour in a separate bowl. Add the spices and almond flour. Add the mixture gradually to the butter, sugar, and eggs, while stirring. Continue stirring until thoroughly mixed.\nDirections Contd.\n----------\n4. Add the brandy and sherry to the batter and mix.\n5. Pour the batter into the pan, and spread it evenly. Bake until a knife can come out clean. Allow cooling for half an hour.\nDirections Contd.\n----------\n6- Invert the pan onto a plate, then onto a cooling rack. Allow even more cooling.\nWhitestorm cook book\n\nWritten by James Whitestorm\nCoppied by Rosso\nVaerHaven", ""),
        StaticBook("Will of Aylwin B", "Aylwin Blaxton", "===================         The Last\n    Will & Testament \n           of\nThe Right Honourable\n     Aylwin Blaxton,\n1st Viscount Brabant.\n\n Written on the 5th of\nSun's Smile, in the Year    of our GOD, 1616.\n===================\nI, the Right Honourable Aylwin of the House of Blaxton, Chancellor of the Principality of Pruvia, 1st Viscount Brabant, being of sound mind and clear conscience, hereby declare this to be my last will & testament, verfied by the Seal of House Blaxton.\nI Appoint the Reigning Regency Council of His Serene Highness, Frederick Augustus of the House Horen-Preussen, Prince of Pruvia, Duke of Ostland, Count of Eastwatch, Baron of Hochspitze, Knight Paramount & Sheild of Mardon as Sole Executor of my Will.\nSaid Regency currently headed by the Her Serene Highness, Elisa of the House of Roswell, Princess-Consort of Pruncia and Countess of Istria, shall keep inventory over this will, until such time as it becomes necessary to read out the contents.\nTABLE\n      OF CONTENTS\n\nI    -   Funeral \n         Arrangements\n\nII   -   Distribution of\n         Estate\n\nIII  -   Conclusion &\n         Last words\nI.\n\nI appoint the Sole Executors of this Will to arrange for the commencement of Funeral Arrangements, Paid for by House Blaxton's Steward, Ayldan of the House Blaxton.\nI wish for the funeral to be held at the Church of St. Otto of Vanderfell in Anhalt, where by body is requested to lay in state for the period of One Saint's Day, before being buried in the Adjacent Graveyard in Anhalt. Any Guests may attend.\nI wish for a Wake to be Held at the Viscounty of Brabant, where drinks and food should be avaliable for any guests who wish to attend, with Ayldan of the House of Blaxton finishing the event with a small speech, to conclude the event.\nII.\n\nI hereby bequeath unto Ayldan of the House Blaxton, Steward of Brabant and Resident of the Viscounty, my lands, titles, furnishings, interests in the House of Blaxton. This shall include the Following:\nA) The Viscounty of\n    Brabant.\nB) The Title of\n    Viscount, for which      he shall be known       as the 2nd\n    Viscount Brabant.\nC) All Personal \n    Furnishings, such\n    As my bed, books,\n    Armour, Axe & \n    Piano.\nI hereby bequeath unto Erin of the House of Lockley, Owner of the Lockley Estate & my Dearest Friend, the following items:\nA) A Purple Party Hat. B) A Blue Diplomat's\n    Cap.\nC) The Sum of 2,500\n    Minae.\nD) The Right to a place     of Burial beside me\nIII.\n\nMay the Sole Executor please state the following to the beneficiaries of my estate, as these are the last words that I would say to them, after the event of my death:\nTo my Brother Ayldan,\nwe've not got along as well as I would ever have hoped. I have pushed you hard throughout your life, and at times, you have rightly rebelled against my authority, as your Older Brother. . .\nNonetheless, I could not be prouder of the Man who would come to inherit my Lands & Titles. I have full confidence in your abilities to lead the House to success & wish you the best of luck in your future endeavours. Just keep the bedroom locked.\nAylwin x\nTo Erin Lockley, my \nlongest and dearest friend. Words cannot describe the passion I have felt for you, despite being under an Oath of Celibacy to never know love. You are without a doubt the kindest and most beautiful person I know. . .\nIt grieves and pains me that you will be the one to feel the most heart-ache with my passing, in which I hope the gifts I give to you are enough to ease that heartache and replace it with the fond memories that we have shared.\nI love you.\nAylwin. xxxxx\nWith the Conclusion of this Will & Testament, in witness of which I have set my hand to, on this day, the 5th of Sun's Smile, in the Year of our God, 1616, please note the signatories hence, their residence & their own Seal:\nAylwin Blaxton.\n\n*Below is the Seal of the House of Blaxton:\n\nBlack Wax is dried here, with the imprint of a Dark Stone made into the Wax, which was made by a Signet Ring.*\nMaester Aldred\n            [!]\nThe Maester's seal is set tightly upon the page of the document.\n\n  Floris Van Loden\n             [!]\nBeneath Floris' name is a drawing of a swan, its wings spread out with scratchy ink.\nElisa Marie Horen-Pruessen\n            [!]\nThe seal of the house is marked on the page beneath the signature.", ""),
        StaticBook("Wilven Monks", "Monk Argyll", "Principles\n       of being a\n           Monk\n\n          Part I\n     The  History\n\nKeldrith, Lord of the Sun, began his story like the rest of us mortals. He was the son of a king, King Celetiman of\nCelestrian, a kingdom in what now know as Asulon, the city of Arethor, and thereby prince and heir to the throne. At the time the story begins, Keldrith was but a 13 year old boy. Thouthsand of villagers dwelt in the kingdom, and all of them loved\nKeldrith, for he was simply a kind and charasmatic person. As time went on, despite his age Keldrith fell in love with a princess.\n\nKeldrith's love was the princess Rellenia of a small city-state outside the Kingdom. He noticed her one day,\nwhen she was not at a political debate, like his father was most hours, but at the markets, purchasing wheat form a poor farmer and paying him twice it's worth. He was enthralled a maiden that was so beautiful, yet so kind. He went to the king of the\nstate, Taron, and offered an arranged marriage between the two. Taron approved his proposition, and a marriage was planned between Rellenia and Kledrith. Now one might that Rellenia would be unhappy about an arranged marriage, but quite the contrary, she\nhad loved Keldrith from the moment she met him. They were happily wed, and when Celetiman passed on, Kledrith took over as king. When time saw fit, they went out into the world, leaving the general of the military in charge.\nTime went on, and Keldrith, twenty-six, and Rellenia, twenty-four, arrived at a small hamlet known as Flowershire. In Flowershire lived a young man known as Tariel,  a kind farmer who the two liked instantly.\nKeldrith, Relenia, and Tariel became the greatest of friends,and when they left the hamlet, Tariel came with them. They explored all of Asulon, cherishing each others’ friendship, and having many adventures.\nSadly, their joy could not last. It was said that they came to a wasteland in Asulon, nothing was there except for scorched rocky mountains. Not much is known about what occurred within the valley, except a farmer a few leagues\naway said he saw a bright flash of light from that direction soon after they entered. In truth, they were murdered in this place. Their bodies faded into the earth, as death does, and their belongings vanished as well, all except for one each.\nIt was said that, upon their deaths, the Creator took pity upon their souls and bound them to three minerals, Rellenia, a diamond, Keldrith, a bar of gold, and Tariel, a gem of Lapis Lazuli.  He then waited, for he knew what would\nhappen to the three friends. The stones stayed upon the ground for centuries, and all around them, the wasteland transformed into a paradise, water flowing from the mountain peaks reformed the land into a valley of grass,\nforming a pool in the center, the stones laying on the shore. Such a paradise could not go unihabited, so the Creator chose a single woman and a single man to discover it.\nThe man, William Alerus, and the woman, Vera Alerus, set up a home their, not knowing the stones the lied upon the shore, until one day, their child went down and explored. Amanda Alerus, their child, discovered the stones, and called her parents.\nThey admired them, but something prevented both William and Vera from touching the stones, so Amanda went up and gathered them in her arms. The second she touched them, bright lights shot out, the colors of the stones, and they flew into the sky,\nthe gold to the sun, the lapis to the stars, and the diamond to the moon.\n\nThe Creator admired the friendship of the original three,and left knowledge upon the new three mortals living upon the shore.\nHe told them the story of the stones, and instructed them to build a Temple in their honor. They trained a messenger bird, sending him home to their friends and extended family, speaking of the paradise and the small price to pay.\nThey brought with them all the materials they could carry and departed for the soon-to-be Temple of the Triumvirate. Work progressed quickly, an immense library going up and the Temple itself a sight to behold. These were the original\nMonks of the Triumvirate.\nThe Celestial Triumvirate, as Keldrith, Rellenia, and Tariel came to be called, became deities in their own right, demigods of the sun, moon, and stars. They granted their followers\nthe ability to heal those who needed it by invoking their name in prayer, but the most powerful monks were able to do it through sheer mental focus upon them. They blessed the Temple when it was complete,\nthat it would be forever void of any illnesses or disease of the outside world, and that it would ever be a safe haven.As time went on, the monks forgot the old ways, becoming lazy and not helping those other than themselves\nThe Triumvirate saw this and were angry, so angry in fact that they banished the monks from the Temple, magical wards preventing any from entering the paradise as long as they lived, and longer.\nIn fact, they did not allow anyone through until the adventurer Wilven Adonan.\n\nWilven Adonan, a young human adventurer, was among the first to originally came to the land through the portal. Upon seeing the people become\nafflicted with the devastating curse, Wilven set out to find some way to cure or dispel it. He traveled long through swamps, mountains, and forests and eventually came to a grand mountain range.  At the base of the mountains, he found a partially\ncollapsed tunnel that seemed to cut through the mountain, so he made his way through it. On the other side, he discovered a marvelous sight.\n\nThis place that he had found was not like the world outside it. It seemed the curse did not affect this place.\nLush trees and vibrant grass covered the place and clear waterfalls streamed down the sides of the mountains. The structures, although collapsed in some places, were beautiful as well.  Another strange thing Wilven noticed about\nthis place is that he felt healthier while inside the valley. Exploring some more, Wilven came upon a large structure with several arches. He made his way inside and eventually came upon a hidden tunnel back behind a collapsed wall.\nHe made his way through hallways and down staircases and found himself inside a large library. Amazingly, the library was intact and untouched by nature. After looking over several tomes and manuscripts, Wilven discovered\nthat this place was built long ago in order to serve as a place of worship for three beings of power, Keldrith, Rellenia, and Tariel. Together, these three beings formed the Celestial Triumvirate which watched over the sky and all below.\nWilven wished to discover more, but he first had to bring others to this sacred place where the curse did not reside.\nBy the time he returned to the humans, many of them had fallen to the effects of the curse.\nHe collected those whom were still well enough to travel and brought them back to the sacred valley. Once they recovered enough,Wilven sent three messengers to send word to the Orcs, Elves, and Dwarfs that there was a place\nfree from the taint of the curse. When the messengers returned, however, they brought with them only a handfull of people. Unfortunately, many of the other races’ people had fallen to either the curse or other unfortunate circumstances.\nFeeling reinvigorated by the day, the few remaining people set to work making for themselves a new home in this sacred place.\n\nFor many years, the survivors worked hard to restore the sacred valley to its original form.\nWhen Wilven was very old, he called the people together and told them all that he had learned of the Celestial Triumvirate. The people consecrated themselves to the Celestial Triumvirate and constructed a shrine to allow worship to all three beings.\nThey formed themselves into monastic order and cloistered themselves from the rest of the world. They chose Wilven as their Abbott and, together, the monks continued to live on in peace taking care of the sacred valley,\ngiving praise to the Triumvirate, and praying for the curse to be cleansed from all the land. Upon Abbott Wilven’s death, the monks wished to pay honor to his life by naming the sacred valley after him.\nFrom that day forward, the place was known as Wilven Sanctuary.\nPart II\n    Laws of being a\n            Monk\n\nI. A Monk must remain neutral. This is for the smallest of argument to that of war.\n\nII. Monks are to remain a kind and gleeful mood, even when angered.\nIII. Monk are to not add acessories to their robes unless it is the trimming of the robes- and then it must be one of the colours of the three Triumvirate.\n\nIV. A Monk is free to furnish ones room, but is forbiden to touch anothers.\nV. A Monk may never sell goods for profit and personal gain. If under special circumstances, the minas go to the Sanctuary and not the individual.\n\nVI. Monks are obliged to give bread, clothing and shelter to all in need.\nVII. If in a situation of which none can come to an agreement, the word of the Elder Monk stands.\n\nVIII. If one acts out of these laws his robes may be taken and released from all duties within the sanctuary.\nPart III\n          Healing\n\nOur healing is done through the Triumvirate. If you do not belive in the Triumvirate, you will be unable to perform any acts of healing. The easiest act of invokeing power from the Triumvirate is\nthrough prayer. The more lengthy and the more praise given tends to give off more power. Another way to gain power is to chant the Triumvirate's name in sucsession, though this invoked less power. The hardest way is to invoke through silence, though that\nis the hardest to master. Healing works through the power of a selected Triumvirate to represent the caster. If a Monk is a follow of Keldrith, his healing usualy would give of a gold glow, though a Monk of Tariel's healing would be the colour of purple.\nResurection is a very obscure branch of healing, but is what makes the Monks so important. Resurection is very difficult to master, and requires the most concentration of all. Once a Monk has mastered silent healing, would he be able to sence the floating\nsouls around the temple. With practise, a Monk can revive these souls. Outside of the temple ressurection is much more difficult, and require a vast amount of energy. It usualy requires multiple sessions.\nPassive healing is one of the not as well known arts of healing. Around the time a Monk achieves ressurection and silent healing a Monk may unpurposly begin to heal himself, sometimes without one not even noticing, unless it's a grevious wound in which\nsparks of the chosed Triumvirates hue will begin bubble out of the Monk's wounds.\n\nChoosing a Triumvirate is one of the hardest decisions of a monk. As know, Keldrith's colour is a deep gold. Tariel is a Lapis purple, and Rellinia is a diamond blue. Even-\nthough this makes little diffrence to a Monks healing it often shows off a Monk's personality.\n\nFinaly, we talk about achieving ones robes and becoming a Monk. To become a Monk one has to spend time as an Initiate, in which the Initiates mostly study\nbooks such as these as well as farm. Once an Initiate seems ready the Elder Monk tests him on his knowledge. If they pass they are given their robes and become a full monk. \n\nBook Writen by Monk Argyll.", ""),
        StaticBook("Winzor's Letter", "Yhorm Aldyhr", ". . . Osgod has informed the council of Asterwaletch that they have managed to locate the rebellious witches. They have fled east in an attempt to secrete themselves under a veil of snow, as to conceal their very existence. Yet it has come to our\nattention that the locals living a village over, have reported seeing strange sights of glowing wisps and odd twisting lights late into the evenings. Although we doubt their ability to cast any manner of powerful magics,\nI implore you to remain wary of their capabilities, for even the Inquisitor knows not their aptness.", ""),
        StaticBook("Wise Sayings", "snowshovel", "\"When one Orc kills another Orc, they die.\"\n-Corvo-\n\n\"Do not go where the path may lead, go instead where there is no path and leave a trail.\"\n-Isabella Kamura-\n\n\"Quite.\"\n-Ben-\n\"Don' pu' yer 'ead in th' foireplace, Eldon.\"\n-Mum-\n\n\"Don't eat the green potatoes.\"\n-Drizzt Do'er-\n\n\"Don't call me Darkie ye racist!\"\n-Drizzt Do'er-\n\"It's only after we've lost everything that we're free to do anything.\"\n-Sir Alexander-\n\n\"Never trust a beardless dwarf.\"\n-Gathius di Silvari-\n\n\"Minas buy everything but hapiness.\"\n-Adam-\n\"The most expensive part of a building is the mistakes.\"\n-Grendor Bilok-\n\n\"Cake is pretty cool.\"\n-Ducky-\n\n\"I'm not sorry.\"\n-Pugsy-\n\n\"For the Hochmeister.\"\n-Erul Lernquell-\n\"Kiss my ass.\n-Anon-\n\n\"Never wear your sandals in the rain.\"\n-Ivan-\n\n\"Evil am always coming, just depends on how far away it am.\"\n-Gooms-\n\"Never pay up front.\"\n-Some shopkeeper-\n\n\"Wheat left in the ground fer too long is bad wheat.\"\n-Farmer Fred-\n\n\"Short people are short.\"\n-B. Uttlicker-\n\"Your friends are more dangerous than your enemies.\"\n-Gooms-\n\n\"Tomorrow never comes so just live in today.\"\n-Ivan-\n\n\"Minas are the surefire way to a man's heart.\"\n-Lady Stafyr-", ""),
        StaticBook("Wisps Of Love", "Arabella Rosalie Delevoye", "The light shines unto the earth that we step upon,\nWe dance a dance that turns people into partners.\n\nWe look into each others eyes and descend into the dirt beneath us, the dance continues, the wind sings the words we breathe.\n\nI look into your eyes and\nsee a world inside them, one i wish to explore more than the world around us, the tree leaves drop unto the ground.\n\nYou look into my eyes and see the world in my own, wishing to step foot into what they hold, the wildlife nearby watches in awe.\nWe are what could, two people who could stand in that position and love what they see, the beauty of nature around them, the gorgeous serene view of such untouched earth, goes unnoticed.\n\nWe are to busy falling into what our eyes hold, what they promise,\nyet we are scared to say the words, for we are to scared of the change it will bring.\n\nThe wind wisps by, knowing it is time to step out of such entranced state, we won't say the words and we never will.", ""),
        StaticBook("Witcher's Inform", "Sylas von Schummer", "A Witch-Hunter's Informational \n\nBy Sylas von Schummer.\nOne's work of slaying the dead can oftemtimes prove annoying and time consuming, dragging one from the welcoming hearth at home, from their woman in bed, out into a murky and desolate swamp to slay some damned beast.\n\nIt's not commomplace to find genuine\nenjoyment in the surroundings of your evershifting workplace, but hopefully this simple guide will assist in the actual dispatching of the creature you're searching for.\n-- Part One ---\n\nWalking Dead, Ghouls\nThe most basic form of a damned creature, returned from the afterlife in their previous ever-decaying body. These creatures are oftentimes rather powerful despite their rotting beings, and come with an inate immunity\nto pain from standard blades. It is reccomended to use Aurum, fire, and blunt weaponry to slay the creature. When faced off alone a Ghoul is generally rather easy to dispatch, however it is common to find them in groups, and a situtation like such\nbecomes far more dangerous, as numbers will overwhelm you.\n\nLich, and Darkstalkers\nLiches are the revived souls of the dead via arcane energy by a necromancer. They tend to prove highly intelligent and agressive, using manipulation and murder to achieve\nwhatever end they seek. When destroyed, like most dead a Lich will return to life to haunt and kill again, the only known way to end a Lich's life is to find it's phylactery. A phylactery is any object created to hold the Lich's soul, usually found as a\ngemstone or locket, variety of jewlery and the like, it however has been known for a phylactery to be placed within a tree, or other unexpected objects. Darkstalkers, unlike Liches are found wearing heavy armour head to toe, their prime focus in regards\nto combat is with melee weaponry, whereas a Lich shall oftentimes use magic since their focus is much harder to break than a mortal mage. Darkstalkers are known to have draining spells used to rip the very lifeforce from your body. To slay a Darkstalker\nyou must find it's phylacrery.\n\nWraiths, Ash-kin\nWraiths are shadowy, smog like creatures born of hatred and pure evil. They come in two forms, one haunting a specific area that it is bound to, another free and independant, roaming the countryside\nat will. They appear as black swirling masses of dark material, usually floating above the ground. They have the capability to cast powerful dark and voidal magics, and wield standard weaponry. They are most susceptible to aurum weaponry and holy magics.\nIt is also rumored that certain wraiths are capable of raising dead around them to fight on their behalf, this however is not confirmed.\n\nDreadknights\nBorn of blood magic, a Dreadknight is a walking suit of intelligent sentient armour, born to kill and\nextremely dangerous, it is reccomended to avoid fighting them without Holy mage assistance, or with a large group armed with blunt aurum weaponry.", ""),
        StaticBook("Wolf Druids Tome", "The Wolf Druid", "I- Power\n\nThe soul attracts that which it secretly harbors-that which it loves, and also that which it fears. Thus circumstances do not make the Druid; they only reveal him to himself. It means that blessedness, and not wealth, is the measure\nof right thought; misery, not poverty or lack of family is the measure of wrong thought. A Druid will find that as he alters his thoughts towards the Nature and the Aspects, Nature and Aspects will alter towards him. For you will always draw near toward\nthat which you, secretly, most love. The Races surge with uncontrolled passion, are tumultuous with ungoverned grief, and are blown about by anxiety, doubt, and the wars and wills of Aenguls and Daemons. Only the wise Druid, only he whose thoughts are\ncontrolled and purified, can make the winds and storms of the soul, and indeed the world, obey him. The greatest achievement was at first, and for a time only a dream. Just as the oak sleeps in the acorn, and the bird waits in the egg,\nso dreams are the seedlings of realities. Beware therefore of what you dream of. For some dreams are given by the Aspects to inspire us by what may yet be. Others are planted within us by others, foul seeds that we harvest to our destruction.\nII- Pride\n\nThere is but one way to truly gain mastery over nature, and that is to realize you cannot truly master it at all. It masters you. When one attempts to force it, compel it, command it, or otherwise exercise dominion over it-the\nover it-the power flees like a timid bird. This is because the Aspects know our innermost thoughts. They know how we intend to use Nature’s Gift. Man may deceive other men. But one simply does not deceive the Aspects.\nIf their will is sought,\nthey will\ncome. If we emulate the principals by which is thrives, they flourish in us. Pride is poison to them. In reality, there is perhaps not one of our natural passions so hard to subdue as our pride. Disguise it, struggle with it, beat it down, stifle it,\nmortify it as much as you please. It is still alive, and will every now and then peep out and show itself. You will see it perhaps, even with in the most sacred grottos of the realm. For even I, the Arch Druid, could conceive that I had completely\novercome it, I should probably be proud of my humility. A desire to be observed, considered, esteemed, praised, beloved, and admired by his fellows his one of the earliest, as well as the keenest dispositions discovered in the hearts of the Races.\nMy advice to new Dedicants is to squelch it all their days, for those desires lead to ruin.\nIII- Doubt\n\nMany Dedicants arrive at the Groves with passion already instilled in them. They yearn to learn, they carry drive, and zest, and youth, and curiosity.When they enter our great tree, they have nothing, and leave with everything.\nHowever, a few lose what they have. The rigorous trials of Dedicancy begin to take their toll on them, or they submit their thoughts to the subtle poison of doubt. Not even an Arch Druid’s power can cure it, for these students do harm to themselves.\nThe mind, like the body, can be moved from sunshine into shade. They submit themselves to the slews of myriad ways of Aenguls, Daemons, and the trickery of man, and they yield before this great power to sway one’s faith in the Aspects’ might. Those of you\nwho would stay and train inasmuch as you strip yourself from jealousies and fears, and humble yourself before the Aspects, for you are not sufficiently humble, the veil over your eyes shall be torn and you will see. See all their glory and power, and know\nyou are beloved. A servant of the earth, and wild. Having conceived of their attunement, a Druid should mentally mark out a straight pathway to service, looking neither to the right nor left. Doubts and fears should be zealously starved.\nThey are disintegrating elements which break up the straight path, rendering it crooked, ineffectual, and useless. Thoughts of doubt and fear can never accomplish anything. They always lead to failure. Purpose, energy, power to do, and all strong thoughts\ncease whenever doubt and fear creep in. The will to do springs from the knowledge that we can do. He who has conquered doubt and fear has conquered failure in all his endeavors, both as a Druid, and a person.\nIV- Blight\n\nIn every era there comes a moment when the collective thoughts, whims, and motivations of arcane delvers become so self-absorbed, so malignant, so unheeding that nature itself revolts. Man scars the land such that it-\nfinals rebels against him. Man scars the land such that it finals rebels against him. As thoughts can spread despair and death like seedlings of weeds strewn by the wind, so they must eventually draw the Druids to pluck them out. The vetches must be\npulled, roots and all. When this happens, the Aspects cease to bless, and instead they curse. Instead of healing, they spew poison. It happens so swiftly and terribly. The ancients of the Wayward’s time gave it a name, this culling process that blackens\nthe world. They named it after a wasting disease that occurs in once-healthy groves of trees. They called it the Blight, and the first of these, the Great War.\nI put this quill to paper here now so that others do not make the mistakes I did in my youth. Blinded by war and hate, my transgressions were many, and hard to earn penance for. Though I served the Aspects diligently for many lifetimes, I fear that in my\nheart, I have failed them. May the Aspects look kindly on me in the afterlife-\n\nXal ussta stath xunde mir dosst elamshinae, Nemmisae.\n\n-Wolf Druid Ouity, Retired Arch Druid of the Order, Elandriel Grove", ""),
        StaticBook("Word Exercises", "Benjamin Berric", "_____________\n__S_B_2ERVANT\nAP0L1_N______\n__E_A_O______\n__3RR4W__G___\n__R__R___R___\n_____E___E___\n__5AN6E7M8N__\n__L____E_N___\n__U____D_____\n_Y9LLOW______\n______E______\n______2WORD__\n______T______\nUnScRamBle!\nUse the hints to help!\n\nLike a Dog: FLOW\n\nChopping wood: XEA\n\nA fine snack: DREAB\n\nIn the night sky: TRAS\n\nProtection: DELISH\n\nPointy: WAROR\nWhich way is right?\nFind the correct way!\n\nSword___OR___Sord\n\nNumber__OR__Nombar\n\nFort____OR__Furt\n\nFlag____OR__Flehg\n\nHorse___OR__Hers\nFill out all assignments on a seperate work book and turn it in.", ""),
        StaticBook("Words", "Melia F.", "There was once an Elder Druid whom sat throughout the city of 'ame. Her tranquil state brought the eyes of those passing others pinning her in sight. \n     She never moved from a statue of the Aspects in the centre, always keeping awareness of tho\nwandering by. For within her grip of entangled nature was a mere tome. She never offered, only waited.\n           One day a blacksmith trambled down to sit nearby the old woman with teeth of ivory grinding together in a worth-shattering\nmanner. \"What bothers you, one of metal?\" The Druid had inquired soon enough, only to recieve the rambling rant in reply; \"I am too small within this realm - I declare! Everyday I forge knives that are looked over by another stall whom sells swords daily!\nI am simply tiny and worthless with my occupation. Baah- What am I kidding? I should give up.\" The blacksmith exhaled in a sorrowful fashion for their own pity. With a swoosh of parchment the Druid had opened the tome to tell of a tale for which a storm\nrecklessly threw a crew about upon the deck as they couldn't get a final sail down due to a rope. A mouse smaller than average on board had climbed up to gnaw and rid of the rope, saving the entire crew. \"Those whom are small, my dear blacksmith, might\nappear weak. Yet, they can end up being the strongest of all.\n       Satisfied and once more given strength of the mind the blacksmith returned to show off what they obtained, proving with a mere flick of their wrist and a target hung in the back. Soon\nselling more than the other with the new bravery! \n\n         There was once a sorrowful elven woman whom had lost her child - saline droplets leak from her alluring orbs they did. She weep and weep and to the fountain she sit, singing to the\nquiet dead. \"Mali'ii, mali'ii why must the Aspects greet you so soon? Would you rather be soothed in the arms of Green lady than your haelun? For now I am gone further than you.\"    \n       With further inspection the Druid  pressed a hand to the\nshoulder of the mourning mother before telling a story of one who left to travel - though never let his heart go, for it stay at home with his dear sweet mother. \n       With warmth in her heart the elfess went on joyfully!\nA sudden storm overwhelmed, swishing with rapid droplets and screeching of bolts above! The Druid was found dead. for her book of stories torn. Yet, those who gather had all a story to tell. A woman who could sooth with the mere forming of words.", ""),
        StaticBook("Work Orders I", "Gildon", "22x Iron Hoes\n8x Iron Spades\n4x Iron Axes\n1x Iron Pickaxe (for Devkon, no charge)\n6x Black Bronze Ochre Tree Models\n4x Iron Chests\n3x Iron Gates\n7x Black Bronze Elf Models\n2x Bismuth Bronze Elf Models\n30x Silver Spoons\n14x Silver Forks\n17x Silver Knives\n11x Electrum Ring Bases (ship to Masur for studding)\n8x Brass Bells\n2x Brass Hammers\n50x Billion Coins\n2x Rose Gold Necklaces", ""),
        StaticBook("Work Orders II", "Gildon", "119x Iron Swords\n40x Iron Warhammers\n33x Iron Battleaxes\n78x Iron Chestplates\n78x Iron Leggings\n78x Iron Helms\n78x Iron Boots\n22x Iron Lances\n34x Chain Chestplates\n34x Chain Leggings\n34x Chain Helms\n34x Chain Boots\nNote: Running out of metal for the war effort, put in a requisite for more. Bloody druids can complain about abusing nature all they want, tell them to fuck off, unless they want to save our people instead of their precious groves.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writ of", "Anastasius", "Writ of deed:\n\nFor the services rendered to the crown of Oren, duchy of Savoy & etc, hereby grant the silver elf Delonna Aeléyèlsa an estate of land no greater than twenty square acres between the northern wetlands and western badlands of Kaedrin. Such a\nplot possesses no recognized title within the trappings of nobility and thusly is to be rendered as a private estate.\n\nSigned,\nHis majesty, Olivier of house de Savoie.\n\n*The document bears a weathered, waxen sun.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Writ of Passage", "Tuvya", "*Seal of House Carrion*\n------------------\nThe Company of the Raven is given the right of passage of Emperor Tuvya Sigismundovic Carrion; to be unaccosted wherever their members may travel.\n\n*Tuv's signature*", ""),
        StaticBook("Writ-Ennoblement", "Theran", "Imperial Writ of Ennoblement for the House of Ruric, 1542\n¬†\nIssued and Confirmed by His Imperial Majesty the Holy Orenian Emperor John I Frederick, 24th of the Grand Harvest, 1542\n¬†\nTO OUR BELOVED SUBJECTS,\n¬†\nIt has pleased the Imperial Throne to raise Our leal vassal, Eiric Ruric, to distinguished rank among Our subjects. Accordingly, and with the grace of God and the attentions of Our realm, We do\nconfer the status of nobility upon the House of Ruric, in trust to Our throne for the duration of their loyal service. Its dynasts are enjoined to marry within their status, and similarly to disown such relations as shall displease Our rule. In\nreturn, and as a sign of Our graciousness, We do privilege their head to petition Our court, and to hold land in homage to the Holy Orenian Emperor.\n¬†\nIN NOMINE DEI,\n¬†\nHis Imperial Majesty John I\nFrederick of the House of Horen, by the Grace of GOD, Holy Orenian Emperor and rightful Emperor of Aeldin, forever August, Apostolic King in Oren, of Savoy, Westphalia, Kaedrin, Haense, Renatus and Salvus, Defender of the Faith, Grand Duke of Kaedrin,\nDuke of the Crownlands, Carimea, Erochland, Kingston and Leone, Margrave of Greater Kreden, Count of Felsen, Louvain, Beauclair, Wett and Metz, Sovereign of Humanity and Protector of the Elves, etcetera.", ""),
        StaticBook("Wyrms", "Arnorian", "Wyrms are the savage and Feral cousins to Dragons. Wyrm is the general term for the draconic descendants of the more ancient and powerful Dragaar and Dragons, as well as their corrupt counterparts. They consist of a wide selection of variants, and within\nthose variants, each wyrm is as different as the last. Some are big, some are small, some live by water, some live underground. They all have their base similarities,  but they are all quite different. They can however, be grouped into categories to\nbetter classify and understand them.\n\nWYVERNS.\n\nWyverns are the most common and well known type of wyrm. Their features greatly resemble their dragon counterparts, taking on most of the typical draconic traits such as the razor sharp\nteeth, spined backs, leather wings, scaly bodies, and horns sprouting from their heads.\n\nWyverns never have more than two legs, their hind legs being quite strong and taking almost full responsibility for their movement on land. All wyverns are raptor-\nlike in their forms, with a pair of large leathery wings sprouting from their shoulders. More often than not, their wings will have claws, useful for climbing buildings and assisting the Wyvern in moving on the ground.\n\nThey will often, but not always\nhave the ability to breath fire, which is produced deep within their chest. Sometimes, Wyverns have other weapons at their disposal, such as the ability to spit acid, or produce a thick smoke. This is not always the case, but it has been known to happen.\nWyverns are physically strong, and quite large, taller than the average horse and more than twice as long. Their claws are extremely sharp as are their teeth, but contrary to popular belief their bones are not unnaturally durable. Much like any other\nbeast, their bones are merely bones.\n\nTheir scales are much softer than that of a dragon or dragaar, taking on a more snakelike appearance. Their scales are often smooth, but should not be confused for weakness, as their hides are quite thick, and able to\nwithstand being embedded with numerous arrows.\n\nMuch like most predators, Wyverns feed on a surplus of raw meats, preferring to catch their prey themselves and savagely feast on them. Their young also pick up this instinct at an early age,\nas a baby wyvern is far more viscious than it is cute. They breed much like fish do, in the sense that the female Wyvern will lay a clutch of eggs, while the male fertilizes them. Because of this, the greater number of Wyverns are female.\n\nBASILISKS.\nUnlike the rest of their kin, Basilisks are always legless and wingless, taking on a more serpentine body than the rest of their kind. Most basilisks choose to live in watery areas, be it in lakes, seas, watery caves or even sewers. Generally, they are\nquite large, at full length being able to stretch to the top of most trees. However because of their snakelike bodies, their movement is fairly limited.\n\nHaving no legs and no wings, Basilisks slither across the ground, dragging their heavy\nbodies with them. However, with their loss of flight, they have gained a great affinity for swimming. Basilisks enjoy remaining in the water, often hunting large sea creatures as well as large game on land.\n\nMuch like snakes, Basilisks secret a potent\nand acidic venom from their teeth, using it to slow down their larger prey. This acidic venom can also be spat, often burning through most organic tissue, barring bone. Oddly, Basilisks use this at the end of their feeding, cleaning the carcasses of their\nprey and using the bones to decorate their caves.\n\nDifferent from their kin, their scales are mostly soft and snakelike, with a hard layer of tough scales across their backs. They have no claws, but have great horns and spines across\ntheir back and covering their tails, often using it to pummel large landborne victims. Their teeth are very sharp, however their snouts and noses are strangely tough and hardened, often using their faces to hammer into large creatures.\n\nBasilisks tend to\nreside and nest in large caves, often by coasts and by the sea. They will often come out of their caves, be it to the sea or land to catch prey to then devour within their lairs. Because of this, their caves are filled with the cleaned white skeletons of\ntheir miserable prey.\n\nWritten by Arnorian Elendil, Edited by Arnorian Elendil.", ""),
        StaticBook("Wúyuán", "Qiù Chóngyáng", "Wùyuán\n  The Five Principles\n\nThe Five Elements\nThese elements are known as the Wùyuán (five principles) and are water (shuí), metal (jín), earth (tù), fire (huó), and wood (mù).\nThey are believed to be the source of all things in the realm, and are the undermining values in all concepts. The Wùyuán are present in almost all Eastern cultures, being established from perhaps the beginning of time.\nEarth represents balance, and is portrayed by the colour yellow. It is believed by the Shí people that life is a cycle and that people are born from the earth and return to the earth when they die.\nIt also represents the centre of all things in the universe, and a passage to the divine world.\nWater is an element of neutrality, but also represents the cold and winter climate. The black tortoise is used to depict the north in Distorian and Eastern folklore.\nWood is used to represent the beginning of life; thus used to characterise spring and used as a symbol in agriculture in order to bring good fortune to crops and yields.\nFire of course associates itself to heat and warmth, from this it is used to depict summer. The vermillion bird corresponds to the south, where the climate is generally far warmer.\nMetal is coupled with the colour of white, and used to represent divinity. This stems from the ancient use of meteoric iron, linking the Earth to the aether above. The Shí rulers also use it to represent their dominance on this realm.\n§§The Five Colours\nThe principle colours are concepts established from the five elements, they are:\n\nWhite (bái) is the colour of the Shí (quartz), representing brightness, purity and harmony.\nYellow (huáng) is the colour of the emperor (Huangdi). Distorian legends tell of the first men being moulded from the clay and silt in the yellow river (Huánghé).\nIt is said that only the emperor may use the colour yellow, as it represents his divine right over the Shí people.\nGreen (lù), the colour of the Cuì (emerald), representing wealth, strength and health.\n\nRed (hóng) is associated with fortune and happiness, it is used extensively in celebratory events like weddings and festivals.\nDoors are pasted with red papers with blessings, and red lanterns adorn streets in order to bless those who pass by.\nBlack (héi) is regarded as the colour of neutrality, some consider it as the colour of the heavens, as daylight is blue and the night sky is black.\nThe Five Stars\nIt is said that five stars guard our realm, the Black Tortoise to the North, the Vermillion Bird to the south, the Azure Dragon to the east, and the White Tiger to the west. The brightest star of them all, the Yellow Dragon of the Realm\nEach takes its roots from the Five Elements. The tortoise from water, the bird from fire, the azure dragon from wood, the tiger from metal, and the Yellow Dragon from earth.", ""),
