        StaticBook("Yar agh Nargii", "Wargoth Malog'Yar", "((Written in simplified Blah for ease of reading.))\n Some of lat have heard the story of Yar before. Lat have heard of his birth, his wisdom, agh his flat. Lat have heard the broad strokes. Lat have nub, however, heard any of the more specific stories\nfrom his life. Mi have, therefore, decided this night to blah lat, mi brothers agh sisters, this tale from his life, and mi hope to blah lat more in the future. Tonight, mi blah lat all the story of Yar agh Nargii.\n As those who have heard the story of\nYar know, Yar was a great shaman, agh took some apprentices during his life. At ash point, he taught a group of futh young students: Naramok, Makor, Shula, agh Nargii. Naramok was his favored student, the most advanced agh naturally-gifted of the futh.\nMakor agh Shula were a young couple, who sought to learn alongside each other, agh serve the village as shamans together. Nargii, however, was the least-talented of the futh.\n It was nub so much that he lacked potential. He simply progressed at a slower\nrate. Consequently, Yar rarely allowed him to practice any actual use of shamanic power, as Nargii simply was nub ready. Day after day, he was forced to go over the fundamentals: collecting reagents, carving tokens agh masks, practicing his pronunciation\nof the same, basic Old Blah phrases ad nauseam; with very little practical application. All the while, his fellow apprentices were already learning to brew bottled hexes, agh Naramok was even beginning his training in ritualistic curses. Eventually,\nNargii grew bitter agh jealous. “Yar,” he complained ash day, after carving his upteenth prayer mask, “for h’ash years mi have been lats apprentice. For h’ash years, mi have been repeating these same dry lessons. The others are already practicing real\npower, and I’ve barely ever been allowed to boil a few herbs. When do mi get to start studying some real shamanism?”\n “Nargii,” he responded patiently, “a sapling bears nub fruit, agh rain does nub fall out of season. Lat will move on in lats training\nwhen lat am ready.”\n “Mi am ready now!” he protested.\n “Lat am ambitious, agh lat have potential to be a great shaman ash day; but lat am nub ready yet. Mi will blah lat when lat am ready, young brother.\" Yar then patted him on the shoulder, \"Now, go to\nlats blarg, Nargii. Keep practicing the fundamentals.”\n “But… Mi…” Nargii began to blah, but realized it to be pointless to argue further. He left the tent. A bundle of bones above the door flap clacked together as he exited with a sour grimace across his\ndull green face.\n            <O>\n“We are the conduits of the spirits,” Yar blah’d the next afternoon as he sat cross-legged on a woolen mat, his futh students seated around him in a semicircle, “We are their instruments by which they enact their will. We\nWe are their weapons to bring justice upon their enemies, agh we are the links by which the balance between our world and theirs is maintained. Naramok, what is our duty?”\n “To guide our brothers agh sisters in the path of honor, agh keep them in the ways\nof Krug.\"\n “Hosh.” Yar nodded approvingly, but Nargii simply sneered as he peeped down at his most recently-made token, resenting Naramok for holding their teacher’s favor. “Nargii, mi peep lat have made another token.” Nargii peep'd up to Yar's extended\nhand. He nodded, agh placed it in Yar’s palm. Yar held the token up to eye level. It was dub-inches long and made of bone, carved to resemble a cage. “This is hosh. Lat am getting hosher. Keep this up, agh lat will be ready before lat gruk it.” He then\noffered the token back to Nargii, “Hang it from lats staff.”\n “Rulg,” he replied with a slight smile, agh pulled a leather strap from his bag to tie the token to the top of his staff.\n Within a few seconds, right as Yar was about to address Makor agh\nShula, the clacking of bones was heard. Yar agh his students peeped a young warrior stepping through the tent flap, “Throm’ka, brother Yar. Mi hope mi du nub interrupt anything important, but there is news.”\n “News?” Yar arched a brow.\n \"Yub. Some\ntraveller from a far away land wants to blah to lat. He is an albai, but it seems he brings a tribute of resources. Would lat have us flat him?”\n “Nub yet.” he sighed a bit at the interruption. “If he has brought tribute to help the village, we may as\nwell hear what he has to blah. Mi will determine the worth of his blah.”\n With that, the warrior nodded, agh motioned the visitor in. Into the tent, accompanied by dub albai guards, strode a lithe, pale albai, with long cornsilk hair cascading gracefully\ndown his back agh shoulders. A pair of thin braids dangled beside his long ears, agh his narrow eyes were green as spring grass. With a smooth, sweet voice the elf spoke, “Karin’ayla, Yar.”\n “Ug,” replied Yar with little emotion, clearly unimpressed by\nthe thin creatures in his tent, “Blah.”\n The albai nodded, “My name is Celador. I have heard your name in my travels, and that you are a wise and powerful shaman. Having heard tales of you, I sought you out, in hopes that you may be interested in a\ncertain proposition.\" Celador stopped to await a response. Yar crossed his arms, agh peeped sternly upon the visitor, visibly suspicious of the albai’s blah. He blah’d nub-thing, allowing the albai to continue, “Well, anyways,” Celador continued, a bit\nunnerved by Yar’s stoic demeanor, “I come offering payment: gold, iron, pelts, and many spices. I can give you all these things beyond measure, if you will do but one simple task for me. You see, the Rex is a brutish cretin.” Celador blah'd boldly as he\nregained his composure. “I should think that a wise orc like yourself would make a much better Rex. My request, therefore, is that you put a curse on him, so that I may strike him down. You, then, could fight alongside me, and take the rexdom. Under your\nrule, I believe we could both prosper greatly.” He grinned expectantly, fully confident in his blah.\n Nargii’s eyes lit up at the mention of such treasures, but Yar stood to his feet in a rage, “Celador, lat am a dishonorable coward, agh mi will have nub\npart in lats plan! Flat these albai!”\n At Yar’s command, the students rose from the floor, agh the young warrior raised his war-lusk. The albais unsheathed their own beautifully-crafted blades, agh went on the defensive. A loud clang sounded as the\nwarrior’s lusk slammed against the zult of one of the guards. Celador pointed his own blade out in front as the shamans approached, agh peep’d, from the corner of his eye, his companion struggling under the strength of the warrior. His other guard alerted\nhim to the fact that the rest of the village was becoming aware of the situation, agh advised an immediate retreat. Celador nodded, agh turned to run, leaving their companion to his fate, agh cringing as a he felt a chunk of hair getting ripped from the\nback of his head by an orc’s hand. As the dub sprinted through the village, they heard the agonizing scream of the guard they’d left behind. The villagers readied their weapons, agh charged after the escaping albais. A spray of blood hit Celador in the\nthe left eye, as his only remaining guard was hacked down right beside him by a berserking feorc with a machete. A thrown spear narrowly grazed his cheek, agh chunks of sandstone whizzed past him from behind. He barely managed to escape with just a few\nbruises. The orcs returned to their business, agh Yar called his students back inside to continue their lesson, while Nargii glanced briefly over his shoulder in the direction of the fleeing albai.\n            <O>\n The following night, after the others\nhad gone to sleep, Nagrii was still awake, agh thinking of Celador’s offer. The lust for wealth had taken root in his heart, agh he’d even deluded himself, thinking that he would finally be taken more seriously if he could curse the Rex himself. He took\nhis spear, agh lied to the watchmen, telling them he was going hunting for the night. With their consent, he left the village, agh tracked down the albai. There wasn’t much to go on. He found the occasional drop of blood, a discarded piece of damaged\nchainmail here agh there, agh a little bit of blond hair. Eventually, after many hours, he found a cave, and decided to check inside. He saw Celador sleeping in a cot near the back. As he entered, a loose piece of sandstone broke free under his foot,\nsending him tumbling to the floor. Celador’s ear twitched, agh he sprung up from his sleep at the sudden noise. Snatching his zult from the floor, the startled albai barked, “Stay back, orc! I’ve had enough of your kind.”\n Nargii rose to his feet, holding\nup empty hands, “Nub nub. Mi nub here to hurt lat, albai. Mi-” he suddenly stopped, agh peep’d about the cave. Stacked against the right wall were chests so full of gold agh iron the lids couldn’t close. He peep’d a huge pile of pelts to his left, agh\ndozens of jars filled with various spices. He forced his gaze away from the riches, agh continued, “Mi want to help lat.”\n “How?” snapped Celador.\n “Mi am Yar’s apprentice. Mi will curse the Rex for lat.”\n Celador grinned. He could peep the greed in\nNargii’s eyes, “Is that so? Very well then. You put a curse on the Rex for me, and all you see here is yours. Make him weak and fragile. Sap his strength for me. Is that possible, shaman?”\n Nargii peep’d to the bone token dangling from his staff, agh\nnodded, “Yub. That can be done.”\n “Excellent!” Celador picked up a hefty bag of gold, agh tossed it to Nargii, “Consider this a down-payment.”\n Nargii caught the bag with an eager grin. “Rulg, albai. Mi will do hosh work. Lat will peep.\" He turned, agh\nhurried out of the cave and back to his village with one final “Gug’ye.”\n            <O>\n Arriving back at the village near sunrise, a morning watchman stopped him to ask about the bag agh where he’d been all night. Nargii blah’d him the same lie as he\nblah’d the night watchmen, “Mi was hunting. The bag is full of sand rats. Mi couldn’t peep much else out there last night.” With a shrug the watchman nodded, agh went back about his business. Nargii hurried back to his blarg, agh set the bribe money aside\nto begin his first attempt at a real curse. He held up his staff so the bone token hung at eye level, agh began chanting to Ogrol, the spirit of despair, entrapment, agh most relevant to Nargii’s situation, sapped strength. His chant, however, was\nawkward, as he had trouble remembering important Old Blah words. Eventually, he came to the climax of his ritual, agh raised his staff in the air. Then, the token on his staff began to vibrate, agh soon shattered, sending a splintered fragment into his\narm. Nargii then dropped his staff, as a horrible pain filled his body. His bones became brittle agh porous within him, agh he was left hunched over on the floor, too weak to even stand. \n Then, as if he had been waiting for him outside, the tent flap\nflung open, agh Yar stepped inside. He glared down at Nargii with intense disapproval, “Blah to mi, Nargii. Is now the time to take bribes? Is now the time to sacrifice our honor for filthy gain? Are the uruks to be as the gazat, led about by greed? Are\nwe to be as the shara, lusting after power? Perhaps, lat think, it is the time to be as the albai, sneaking around in the shadows. Peep now how the curse lat intended for the Rex has fallen upon lats own head, traitor.”\n Nargii peep’d up in astonishment,\n\"How..?\" he asked shakily in his weakened state. Immediately, Yar’s sister, Voltha the Huntress, entered from behind, tossing the corpse of Celador before Nargii. A thick orcish lig protruded from his neck.\n   \"Mi do a lot of night hunting,\" interjected\nVoltha, “but mi had never peep’d lat hunting at night before. Mi peep’d lat in the cave with the albai, Nargii...”\n Nargii was speechless, agh without defense. “Nargii,” blah’d Yar, “lat have nub integrity or uprightness in spirit, so lat will have nub in\nbody. Lat am a whitewash, agh a traitor to this village and the whole Uzg.”\n Nargii was dragged to the center of the village, agh tied up, too weak to resist. He was sentenced to flat by de-boning. His screams echoed throughout the desert, as his fragile\nbones were pulled from his body in front of the whole village until he was flat. Afterwards, his bones were piled up atop the ruins of his destroyed blarg, agh burned with his ill-gotten gold. The rest of his body was chopped up, agh thrown to the pigs.\nSo, to this day, de-boning remains the Yar clan’s punishment for the absolute nub’hoshest of offenders.", ""),
        StaticBook("Yellow", "Gayly Robed Figure", "Yellow,\nBy a homosexual Elf.\nYellow is a wonderous colour who's meaning is various and changes through the ages. The sun is yellow, and in this representation it could be percieved as a welcoming and warming colour, a symbol of gathering and togtherness in safty.\nYellow is the colour gold, in this representation yellow could be percieved as a symbol of wealth, or greed. Mayhap a colour worn by those who seek to display their wealth, or in the High Elven community, it is a symbol of impurity, a damning thing.\nYellow is the colour of maize, a symbol of good harvest and wholesum meals. Maize, or corn is a hearty and welcome part of numerous individuals and communities diets, plus, the taste is positivly wonderous.\nYellow, in gemstones are said to grant the holder of said item aid in their descision-making, so that they might find clarity in struggle. However this is simply a myth, and in truth probably holds no substance.\nCalling someone 'yellow', in the sense that they are a coward is a damning form of the colour, as being yellow-bellied is never a good thing. To show fear in damgerous or unnerving situtations displays one's internal weakness.", ""),
        StaticBook("You Failed", "Thurak'Yar", "{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\nYou Failed Bitch\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\nYou Failed\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\nYou Bitch\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n{\"text\":\"\"}\nYou're A Failure", ""),
        StaticBook("Youth and Age", "Mason Sezarius", "Age and Youth\nBoth different things,\nbut at the same time they're as similar as one can get.\nYouth is full of pleasance, Age is full of care. Youth is like the morning sun, Age is like the sun setting.\nOld age should burn and rave at the close of day,\nthough wise men at their end know dark is right, because their words had forked no lightning. Good men, the last wave by, crying how bright their frail deeds might have danced in a green bay, but wild men who caught and sang the sun in flight and learn,\ntoo late, they grieved it on its way. Grave men, near death, who see with blinding sight, blind eyes could blaze like torches and be bright.", ""),
        StaticBook("ZheEp ZTuRy", "Vrog'Lur", "ThURe wUZ agH ZheEp\n\nMi pUT aGh zhEEp\n\nZhEEP zay 'bAH bAh'\n\nThUn mI atE agh ZhEEp\n\nDaH End", ""),
        StaticBook("Zil' Dictionary", "gaiusmarius8", "The Magnus Opus\n     of Linguistics\n\nA study on the dialect of Sabunani, the language of the Zyl'Mxktlmy [Zil'Maktumi] \n\nCompiled by:\nYyl'Mxndxbh Xndxlls\n[Yil'Mandabh Andalus]\nThe language of the Zil'Maktumi is an intriguing feat of linguistic and scriptology. The Zil'Maktumi have gone through two phases of the development of their own language - Elder Maktumi and Sabunani scripts. The Elder Maktumi is remarkably different\nin that the written language does not represent vowels. Sabunani uses certain symbols to represent vowel pronunciation.\n\nA translation device is included to aid the fledgling linguist.\nCommon - Sabunani\n1. a/an - x\n2. and - sxw\n3. at - syr\n4. able/capable - txt\n5. before - sxzyd\n6. after - sxzym\n7. allow - yxk\n8. as much as - Rxl'\n9. much - rxm\n10. feed/eat - mlj\n11. seek/search/find - lxm\n12. irritate/scratch - gyd\n13. see/view - aytxn\n14. Perspective - Altgxp\n15. mirror - Aytgxb\n16. loose - nyj\n17. I/My - Hxt\n18. are - xy\n19. the - zxm\n20. you/your - xntx\n21. crawl - rlsxm\n22. begin - yxmln\n23. We/us/our/them - hxq\n24. he/son - nyv\n25. she/daughter - nyw\n26. few - qyw\n27. conquer/command/control - tlkyg\n28. homage/honor/respect/praise - dxslw\n29. result - vlrxb\n30. interest/intrigue/amazing - hljyk\n31. normal - gxzys\n32. King - Mxlyk\n33. study/learn - zys\n34. head - rxs\n35. Deity - Ylxm\n36. soul/spirit - Lyn\n37. Time - Bxl\n38. jar/vessel - bxt\n39. memory - bxjlk\n40. holy - hlr\n41. Heaven/Seventh Sky - Skxy\n42. life - tlryw\n43. horizon/edge/shore - qyj\n44. cry - zld\n45. creature/creation/thing - glvyp\n46. animal - gxvlb\n47. heir/inheritor - Fydxtlr\n48. self-begot - Ghxr\n49. have - zxw\n50. degrade - glhxt\n51. strange/odd - ghxb\n52. bond/group - pxrmyn\n53. in - hxw\n54. heart -kxlyb\n55. mourn - lymxb\n56. ancestor - gxjlb\n57. enter - cxtyn\n58. sand - rxf\n59. portal - slmt\n60. movement - flgyp\n61. up - qxd\n62. word - rxd\n63. action - gyn\n64. level/plane - rygxt\n65. move/travel - vlg\n66. on - ylb\n67. lack of/not/nothing - qxtlg\n68. than - tlg\n69. above - lxk\n70. under/below - jxk\n71. plant - frxr\n72. desert - sxhxrx\n73. name - lxmx\n74. peace - hxlxl\n75. table - txwyl\n76. wound/scar - glvyg\n77. every - fxw\n78. possible/liable - qlwxs\n79. guide - nxtlg\n80. ignorance - lxryf\n81. ability/skill - glbxl\n82. big/large - ryp\n83. small/mere - tlp\n84. good - nxm\n85. population - hyjxf\n86. situation/condition - qlrxg\n87. clean/polish - wld\n88. bad - mxl\n89. back - txv\n90. is - tx\n91. it - txz\n92. there - tlt\n93. their - txk\n94. those - tld\n95. know/known - vlt\n96. that - tyc\n97. cover/shealth/bath - hlrxv\n98. wind - wyhxd\n99. often/accustom/used to - pxl\n100. but/while - vlh\n101. history - wlryt\n102. wing - txlyn\n103. rational/intelligent/objective - clvyh\n104. part/aspect - rlg\n105. light - ylyln\n106. happen/take place - rxh\n107. withdraw - hxbyv\n108. then/thus - txqyr\n109. they - txwxt\n110. this - txxyp\n111. these - tlgyq\n112. if - vln\n113. with - fld\n114. desire/want/intent - rlflfm\n115. intend/wish - rltlm\n116. rub/smear - qlc\n117. gather/collect - pxrym\n118. kindness - sxtlr\n119. human/man - hxmx\n120. woman - nysx\n121. think/thought - fxvyl\n122. yes - gxb\n123. no - nxb\n124. don't - gxpnxb\n125. war/attack - byr\n126. naked/rip/tore - rlvyg\n127. reward - jybxv\n128. through - jxw\n129. warn - dlrys\n130. some - hxn\n131. clay - pywxt\n132. mud - mxd\n133. give - fyv\n134. between - rxkyj\n135. highest/ultimate - gxdlrxw\n136. goal/point - gxlxp\n137. since - wls\n138. North - Nlrxt\n139. South - Hlrxt\n140. touch - pxyg\n141. again - pxw\n142. bank/land/drop - ghxl\n143. near - pxv\n144. far/long - qyq\n145. native - flgys\n146. be - lyj\n147. resource/item - flk\n148. wise/smart - vxryl\n149. many/alot - wyjx\n150. organize - jxhr\n151. against - fyp\n152. invader - bxhyt\n153. nature - hljxt\n154. blind - gxbyv\n155. groan - fywyk\n156. to crack - blnxm\n157. apart - gxsyh\n158. hold - blc\n159. so - xl\n160. what - kxk\n161. where - txn\n162. when - klk\n163. who/whose - kxl\n164. how - mxn\n165. to - hxk\n166. put - mlv\n167. of - xp\n168. frolic/play - byw\n169. sun - yly\n170. fertile/healthy/growth - yljyn\n171. raid/steal/theft - rydxr\n172. damn/curse - Yxksyty\n173. from - gxm\n174. follow/stalk - ylc\n175. Federation/Civilization - Fyryrxtln\n176. Federator - Fyrxryt\n177. would - fxllt\n178. forget - fxpyn\n179. rise/gain - pys\n180. different - pylxh\n181. city - Mxdynxt\n182. thrive/live - jxklt\n183. yearn - dytxp\n184. for - dxs\n185. argue - gxvyl\n186. split - rybyn\n187 weigh - txj\n188. chaos - shlt\n189. child/youth - vxblm\n190. people - zxglk\n191. do/act - gxp\n192. serve/provide - qyn\n193. year - hljxn\n194. continent - ayq\n195. land/earth/ground - axg\n196. stand - gypxn\n197. death/stop - jlqxr\n198. power - gryvpxnvxr\n199. poet - dltxf\n200. tall - pyd\nGrammatical\n    Indicators\n\n1. prefix 'im/un' is noted with prefix Pyl\n2. Plurality is noted with a symbol '*' at the end of the word\n3. Zyl [Common: Zil] is used to refer to a group of people adjectivally.\n4. Adverbs are created with the symbol '/' at the end of words\n5. Past tense is created by the symbol '+' at the end of words\n6. To create gerunds or the -tion suffix, the symbol used is '=' at the end of words\nCommon Phrases\n1. How are you?\nMxn xy xntx\n2. Where are you from?\nTxn xy xntx gxm\n3. Hello!\nGxlymyk\n4. To each their own\nHxk hyglm txk yxn\n[[OOC: Those who possess this can contact gaiusmarius8 for a fuller dictionary.]]", ""),
        StaticBook("Zpirit Buuk", "Shreck", "DUH ZPIRIT BUUK\n\n   rulg tew awl ub duh shomoz whu halped mi ryte diz buuk.\n\n  ELEMENTUL ZPIRITZ\n\n*Skathach-Zpirit ub fiya\n\n*Akathro-Zpirit ub watur\n*Bregthar-Zpirit ub earth\n\n*Fiarza-Zpirit ub wind agh air\n\n*Kulthark-Zpirit ub metul\n\n*Neizdark-Zpirit ub sturm\n*Binazdar-Zpirit ub lite\n\n*Radzanib-Zpirit ub darknuzz\n\n*Fanzra-Zpirit ub chaoz\n\n*Arznaf-Zpirit ub ordur\n\n*Ringat-Zpirit ub lief\n*Tagnir-Zpirit ub death\n\n*Omnizan-Zpirit ub zpace, intertwindud wif etz partnur, Sandru\n\n*Sandru-Zpirit ub tyme\nIMMORTUL ZPIRITZ\n\n*Votar-Zpirit ub duh hunt\n\n*Enrohk-Zpirit ub bluudluzt, zavagery agh war\n\n*Shezept-Zpirit ub revunge, plotz agh stelth\n*Jevex-Zpirit ub ordur, hard wurk, agh zelf zakrifize\n\n*Ixli-Zpirit ub forbidun knowludge, truuf agh judgemunt\n\n*Ogrol-Zpirit ub dezpair, zapped strength agh entrapmunt\n*Kor-Zpirit ub duh flat\n\n*Ankrus-Zpirit ub duh zea, fishurmen agh zafe travulz\n\n*Arwa-Zpirit ub furtiluti, harvuzt agh farmun\n\n*Anyhuluz-Zpirit ub deztruction, malishush intunt, internul stryfe\n*Akezo-Zpirit ub helth, vitality agh heelun\n\n*Paxahru-Zpirit ub stewpudity agh arroganze\n\n*Ublulhar-Zpirit ub hope agh new beginunz\n\n*Ghorza-Zpirit ub travul\n*Rolfizh-Zpirit ub azzazzinashuns agh poizun\n\n*Trokorl-Zpirit ub engineerun, mashinery agh buldun\n\n*Luara-Zpirit ub duh moon\n\n*Ramakhet-Zpirit ub duh dezurt agh zand\n*Krathol-Zpirit ub payn zuffern agh ztarvashun\n\n*Veist-Zpirit ub illushun, trikz agh theivury\n\n*Freygoth-Zpirit ub duh wild agh wild animulz\n*Glutros-Zpirit ub greed agh beun phat\n\n*Thulezia-Zpirit ub luzt, plezure agh beautifulnuzz\n\n*Isuz-Zpirit ub lub, carun agh tranquiliti\n\n*Orgon-Zpirit ub dezease, pestilence agh failur\n*Urin-Zpirit ub rain agh hail\n\n*Kesaroth-Zpirit ub envi agh beun jelluz\n\n*Leyd-Zpirit ub dominanze agh strength\n\n*Scorthuz-Zpirit ub kleansing agh purgin\n*Theruz-Zpirit ub intelligunze agh lernun\n\n*Gentharuz-Zpirit ub zmithun, smeltun, induztry agh forgin\n\n*Ikuras-Zpirit ub fear agh inzanity\n\n*Drelthok-Zpirit ub zleepun agh dreemz\n*Eathruz-Zpirit ub dawn agh duzk\n\n*Kotrestruu-Zpirit ub memury agh duh rekordun uf knowludge\n\n*Lethrothak-Zpirit ub hindzite agh excuzuz\n\n*BETHARUZ-ZPIRIT UB BEER, GRIIN AGH CELEBRASHUN!!!!!!!\nANZESTRAL ZPIRITZ\n\n*Krug-Duh firzt shomo evur agh duh hozhuzt ork tew evur lib. Hi iz duh hozhuzt zpirit\n\n*Lur-Hozhuzt hunter en hiztury\n\n*Rax-Hozhuzt warriur ub awl tyme\n*Gorkil-Duh hozhiezt militari stratiguzt agh tactishun\n\n*Braduk-Ah faymed hozh chieftun\n\n*Dom-Duh zecund hozhezt shomo\n\n*Ugluk-A kub ub Gorkil, hozh warriur\n*Azog-Duh hozhezt smif en hiztory\n\n*Kurak-Alzo grukd az duh howlur ub Lur, wen zummond et kauzuz duh shomo tew tranzform intew ah half ork, half howlur, dey luze der mynd wile dey ar tranzfurmd\n*Tor-Knewn fur hiz kalm, kollective intellekt agh stronkth\n\n*Trickster-Knewn fur hiz zubterfuge\n\n*Bralkor-Knwen fur hiz rezuztunze tew physikul damag\n\n*Jarkun-Knewn fur hiz dexterity agh zpeed\n*Yar-Knewn fur hiz hozh wizdum agh zpirituality\n\n*Yaggo-Duh hozhezt ridur ub awl tyme\n\n*Dregort-Duh hozhezt boat buldur agh kaptun tew evur lib\n*Grumbah-Ah hozh buildur\n\n*Vargo-Knewn az beun ah veri hozh alchemizt\nHOZH URUKZ\n\nShreck-Wun ub duh hozhiezt urukz tew lib, hi iz blu agh stronk agh zmart agh handzum agh kewl agh stronk\n\nReynuh-Ah hozhie peepun uruk whu iz veri stronk agh zmart\n*Wun-Ah veri stronk ogre\n\n*Glumpuzz-Ah nub'hozh uruk whu iz rehd", ""),
        StaticBook("~Report~", "Co Co", "~Report On Karlsburg~\n\nStarting from the outside, there is only one way in. However there are mutiple ways of getting out. The wall is thick in build, making it difficult to just break in. Simply climbing over won't work either, due to its height.\nThere is almost never a guard on the gate, making it easy to just simply walk in. The soldiers that patrol the area, rarely carry heavy equipment. Their main line of attack is on horseback, due to the speed. Getting out, can be both tricky but benefical.\nUpon taking to the tops of the buildings, it offers easier ways to take out a soldier. Taking one out at a time, is the best root, as i watched a man recently do it. Nearly every soldier has a horse, so simply running is mere suicide.\n~End Of Report~", ""),
        StaticBook("~Wheat Poem~", "Dedicant Renn", "Renn's Poem\n\n~~\n\nA golden glisten of summer sea,\nGraceful arms waving to and fro.\nA warm sensation runs through,\nA feeling of protect and peace bestow.\nSoft movements from a gentle breeze,\nGrace, prosperity is of Nature's own.\nThin straws of strength and vigor,\nA sense of light against the unknown.\n\nLand's children of grain,\nTreated as a gift that provides life.\nA gift of quelling formidable hunger,\nA might savior of times of strife.\n\nA life of giving, a seed to a stalk,\nO' Nature, grant me day and week.\nThat the grains retain their numbers,\nFor a life without wheat shows bleak.", ""),
        StaticBook("~~Haelun'or~~", "Thallan Tal'iheiuh", "~~Haelun'or: The Motherland~~\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBy Thallan Tal'iheiuh\n~~Introduction~~\nSince early Asulon, the Mali'aheral, sometimes simply referred to as `High Elves` (although their name literally means `Blessed Elf` in the language of common), have lived in seclusion, away from the other children of Malin: the\nMali'ame (Wood Elves) and the Mali'ker (Dark Elves). This isolated land, reserved only for pure Mali'aheral (a Mali with a completely High Elven background, meaning marriages to only other\nAheral and certainly no offspring with an Elf of a different sub-race), was known as Haelun'or, translated from Ancient Elven as, like in the title of this work, `motherland`. Haelun'or has, since its founding in Asulon, existed in all of the realms,\nwhere the Mali'aheral lived in cities of different titles. As strict the High Elves are with who they let into elcihi (the city), on several occasions their nation has been a home of refuge for the other sub-races, and also the Kharajyr (often called the\nKha), a feline race, found already living on Asulon upon the descendants' arrival there, have stayed there on several occasions.\nIn this book, all of the cities which the Mali'aheral have resided in shall be listed, and a few words will be written about\neach, starting from Aegis and finishing in the land of Thales.\n~~Aegis~~\nIn the first realm that Malin, his brothers, and their descendants explored, the Mali'aheral lived at peace (mostly) in the nation of Malinor, dwelling within its leafy cities, such as its capital, Laurelin. Under the rule of High Prince Native,\nthe first of the High Princes of Malinor, a group known as the High Council was formed, so as to aid Native in governing and protecting Malinor. This council was predominantly made up of Wood Elves, yet one High Elf, Prince Toren, was a part of it.\nPrince Toren is well known for his idea for the creation of a large and fruitful farm which was built within Laurelin, keeping the Princedom of Malinor fed and happy. This happiness was, of course, before the arrival of Iblees, a powerful Daemon.\n~~Asulon~~\nAfter leaving the Verge, an island used to recuperate on following the destruction of Aegis to the bane of Iblees, and sailing to Asulon, the Mali'aheral, led by Dio Astoré and Ellir'siol, felt it time to detatch from the other Mali, setting\noff to build a city of their own. Said city was built upon one of the many ruins found across the land; the ruins used as the foundations for the city were that of an Ancient Elven civilisation. It took several years to construct the grand city (the\nlayout and design of which was just how the old cihi, now just rubble and stone, would have looked) and, upon its finishing, it flourished as the new home of the Mali'aheral. It was named Haelun'or, the same title as the nation known today - it was\nelcihi'thilln: the Silver City.\nJust after its building, Haelun'or was a part of the Princedom, under the rule of High Prince Kolyat Alfakyn. However, this, to the Mali'aheral, was not seen as a chance for open borders between elcihi and the rest of\nMalinor: large iron gates (more often than not seen closed and locked) at the end of a large bridge, branching out over a ravine, a natural split between the High Elves and their fellow Mali. No Mali'ame/ker/fenn were allowed through the gates; it was\nproperty reserved for the Aheral.\nAs the city grew in both size and population, the Silver Council, Haelun'or's equivalent of a government, led by elsohaer, the leader and ruler of the nation, negeotiated with the Princedom and, as a result, Haelun'or\ngained autonomy. From this point on, the Silver City ceased to be a part of Malinor, and instead the Mali'aheral began ruling themselves as an independant people.\n~~Anthos~~\nFollowing the great surge of natural disasters that rendered Asulon uninhabitable, the races travelled, stopping at two islands known as Elysium and Kalos, to Anthos, a new and unexplored land. For a short while, the Mali'aheral lived within\nMalinor once again, but this was short lived, as feuds and arguments between the Aheral and other sub-races caused the Blessed ones to leave, building their own city, called Lin'evaral. It was the most western city in the mainland and could be accessed in\ntwo ways. They remained happy in their home for many long and prosperous years before the Black Scourge (led by Setherien, last of the Drakaar, part Daemon, part dragon beings) and many large earthquakes forced them to flee the ruined cihi.\nWhile the\ndestruction of the city was ongoing, a camp, known as New Malinor, was set up outside the capital of Luminaire. It acted as a kind of refugee camp, giving Elves shelter as the war between the Elves and the Scourge drew on. The High Elves, distraught by\nthe loss of Lin'evaral, came to New Malinor, seeking help. They quickly set up a camp and began to live alongside other Mali once more. There was, for a short time, peace in New Malinor. However, some non-Aheral Mali were displeased with the treatment\nthat the High Council were providing and began to revolt. This revolt was successful without any bloodshed. The Conclave of Malin, a city built upon Lake Lake, then took control of ruling the Elves. Unlike the Mali'ame and Mali'ker, the High Elves were\ndisgusted by the Conclave, saying that the terms for purity were not popularising equality and that this new rule was promoting what they referred to as Mali'valah, Elves acting like Humans. The Mali'aheral then moved to a secret unerground home, entitled\nthe Tomb. Nearly 30,000 High Elves stayed there, a similar size population to the Conclave.\nThe Tomb contained several gates and gardens with four main sections, known as branches: a multi-floored library, with vast amounts of books. Another branch was a\nscientific area, used for research and experimentation. A housing branch, many levels deep,\nhoused all of the Tomb's residents and a final branch was for Elsillumiran, Haelun'or's guard force (the nation has never\nhad a recognised army). This area was\nused for training and was, by many, considered insiginificant to the rest of their home.\nOutside of the Tomb, the people who knew about its whereabouts were scarce, and it was never discovered, by another race (or sub-race, for that matter).\n~~The Fringe~~\nAfter Setherien was defeated, his icy realm in the North began to melt, flooding all of Anthos, causing its\nabandonment, as the races went through the portal into The Fringe. Here, the Mali'aheral built a city, Tahn'siol, meaning `lonely\npeak`hich was constructed on a large hill, with a great source of water that could supply the whole land.\nDuring the time spent on The Fringe, which was constructed on a large hill, with a great source of water that could supply the whole land. During the\ntime spent on The Fringe, concordats between the High Elves and the other sub-races were created so as to\nprotect the surrounding districts of Ker'lomi and Lin'ame (this should be simple to distinguish the homes of the different sub-races).\nunder the laws of Haelun'or. The Kharajyr also had a district within the walls of Tahn'siol.\n~~Thales~~\nUpon arriving in Thales, the High Elves built the city of Celi'ante. The concordats between the sub-races were destroyed, as\nthe Wood Elves and Dark Elves did not agree with the treatment they recieved in Tahn'siol, and they decided to build\nsettlements of their own. For a short while, Haelun'or went through a period of bitterness toward the newly created Council of Splinters. However, these arguments did not last long and againg the other Mali came under the protection of Haelun'or.\n~~Maehr'sae hiylun'ehya~~", ""),
        StaticBook("∫Alcohol∫", "Zyvia Haeviel", "∫Alcohol∫\n\n«Rum: 3 mina\n–Brewed with sugarcane in a brewing stand.\n\n«Wine: 4 mina\n–Brewed with Dark Resin in a brewing stand.\n∫Alcohol∫\n\n«Pale Ale: 5 mina\n–Brewed with wheat in a brewing stand.\n\n«Sweet Ale: 5 mina\n–Brewed by adding wheat to Melon Juice in a brewing stand.", ""),
        StaticBook("∫Juices∫", "Zyvia Haeviel", "∫Juices∫\n\n«Carrot Juice: 3 mina\n–Brewed with a carrot (can be rotten) in a brewing stand.\n\n«Melon Juice: 4 mina\n–Brewed with a melon slice (can be rotten) in a brewing stand.", ""),
        StaticBook("∫Teas∫", "Zyvia Haeviel", "∫Teas∫\n\n«Rose Tea: 3 mina\n–Brewed with a rose bush in a brewing stand.\n\n«Coffee: 4 mina\n–Brewed with cocoa beans in a brewing stand.\n∫Teas∫\n\n«Herb Tea: 5 mina\n–Brewed with grass in a brewing stand.\n\n«Dandelion Tea: 3 mina\n–Brewed with a dandelion in a brewing stand.\n∫Teas∫\n\n«Cactus Tea: 3 mina\n–Brewed with cactus green (not cactus) in a brewing stand.\n\n«Chamomile Tea: 4 mina\n–Brewed with an oxeye daisy in a brewing stand.\n∫Teas∫\n\n«Blue Orchid Tea: 4 mina\n–Brewed with a blue orchid flower in a brewing stand.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Poem by Dwed.", "Mossbeard", "A poem\nBy Mossbeard.\n\nO'er the hills comes the mist,\nthe valley's dewy bed.\neveryone has their hearts song,\neveryone has it their own.\nI'll go over the hills and through mist,\na proud Hefruth-dwed.\nI will call to my hearts song,\ntry to find it as my own.\nIt was told, they eat in the mist,\nthey feed on dewy bed\nEveryone seems to know my song,\neveryone sees it as their own.\nOver the hills comes the mist,\nthe valley's dewy bed.\nEveryone has their own song\nand I cant seem to find my own.", ""),
        StaticBook("Magical Goldfi", "Caroline Steinson", "The Magical Mister\n           Goldfish\n\n  By Caroline Steinson\nOnce Upon a Time there lived a little girl her name was Millie. She was 9 years old. Millie lived in a small town near a pond with her dad and her older brother and sister. Her mom unfortunately died when giving birth to Millie so Millie never knew her.\nshe didn't even know how her mom looked like but she learned about her mom's appearance and personality through her dad's and siblings' stories. Millie's life with her family was ok. She loved her family. But the pond next to the town was not ok.\nThe people of the town near the pond will always throw their trash inside that pond. One day Millie's dad bought her a pet goldfish. Millie was very happy. She loved the goldfish. But then one day when Millie went outside to play with her friends\nshe forgot to feed her fish. When Millie came back home, she noticed that the fish wasn't swiming in its bowl. Millie quickly ran to her dad and told him what happened. Her dad shook his head and took the fish bowl in his arms and walked outside of the\nhouse. He then went to the pond and dumped the fish in the water. Millie was very unhappy she stopped eating for a day and stayed inside her room for almost a week. Meanwhile, the fish in the pond wasn't actually dead. The fish began to eat trash\nfrom the pond, but littlle did he know some of the trash had magic in them. This caused the goldfish to grow into a big fish. One day Millie got over her grief for her lost goldfish. Her friends invited her to play with them near the pond and she agreed.\nWhile Millie was playing with her friends near the pond, the giant fish sprang up from the water and splashed them. All of Millie's friends ran away in fear but Millie stood her ground. The giant goldfish then swam near the shore and said in his loud\nvoice, \"Millie it is I! Your pet goldfish!\"\nMillie gasped, \"But I thought you were dead!\"\nThe goldfish said, \"No, I was only asleep.\"\n\"Oh.\" Said Millie\nMillie then happily ran to the goldfish and hugged him. They had a lot of fun that day.\nHowever at the end of the day the goldfish said, \"Millie you must tell your towns people to stop throwing trash in the pond\"\n\"But how will I do that?\", Said Millie.\n\"Hmmm, what if I told you that my scales were magical?\" Said the goldfish smiling.\n\"Really?\" Said Millie in awe.\n\"Yup.\" said the goldfish nodding, \"My scales can cure any disease. You can have my scales in return for the towns peoples' promise to not throw trash in the pond ever again.\"\n\"Okay.\" Said Millie.\nSo the towns people killed the fish and took all of his scales and in return they never threw trash in the pond ever again. So they all lived happily ever after well maybe except for Mister Goldfish. The End :)", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0Crystals in the holy order keep.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-Looking from the keep it'll be the glowing gem of raw silver and crimson. §0\n§0Inside the crystal seems to be this raw glow of light in the middle.§0\n§0The power coming from this crystal can be felt -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-through my whole body as if it wants to push something away.§0\n§0Yet I feel warm and calm as I look over it.§0\n§0\n§0No apparent symbols can be spotted across the crystal.§0\n§0\n§0The crystal seems to §0\n§0-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-gently move up and down bobbing in a small motion as beams of faint light move towards the gatehouse.§0\n§0\n§0As I put my hand in the glow surrounding the crystal I feel the raw power it holds, seeming to overwhelm my body §0\n§0-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-In harmony warmth and calmness. A strange feeling. Yet I feel uncomfortable to be around it. §0\n§0\n§0These could be the holy wards being used around to prevent the begins created by dark magic to access yet.§0\n§0-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\nThe people who practice the magic are not affected greatly.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "The wind howled wildly through the sails as the boat bumped it's way along the open ocean.§0\n§0\"'here is land 'head cap'n\"§0\n§0The sailor's voice was soon devoured by the wind.I could clearly see the white snow of Fenn now,I had forgotten how beautiful it\n\nwas to behold.§0\n§0I stepped onto the creeking dock a sailor piped up behind me.§0\n§0\"Careful now snelf can be a dangerous world nowwa days\"§0\n§0I simply nodded my head and bid him van'ayla and moved on towards the §0citadel.As§0 I arrived there my sister\n\nhad been awaiting my arrival,it was good to see her after being apart for so many years.§0\n§0After some catching up we ventured to Courland and it's capital,t'was a busy place filled with §0crowds.However§0 once we had arrived we relised we\n\ndid not know what to do,I nudged her arm and said \"How about you show me around\" she looked up to me and smiled then she showed me all of §0Alexsandria.It§0 was nice just to spend time with her.§0\n§0 The following day we revisited Alexsandria where I met\n\na small boy my sister had saved his name was William,however he was not well.A Olog had taken his eye out and the wound got infected,he showed me this wound and I ressured him that it looked completely §0fine.Yet§0 it did not it looked horrific.I did not\n\nhear from that boy again.§0\n§0 A few months later I was in Mardon where I had just got a property it was a lovely house just enough for §0me.As§0 I left my home I was approached by a gentleman by the name of Jasper,he offered me to come explore Axios with\n\nhim and I §0did.It§0 was alot of fun,we went to many little villages that I had never heard of or explored before!After some exploring we parted ways I would still like to go adventuring with him sometime.\n\n        §0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0        One Year Later...\n\nSeeing a sign for Sutica I wandered down a dirt road,it lead straight through a dense forest which gave of quite the spooky §0feeling.Soon§0 I reached a long bridge which lead to the great city and after a short while I entered through it's grand gates.\n\nAs I entered the city I found some mages who were trying to kill a §0noble.They§0 had already broken his jaw rendering him unable to speak,one of the two mages threatened the man so I approached her.§0\n§0\"You have had your fun so how about you and your\n\nfriend move along\"I said as I got close enough for her to hear me.§0\n§0The second mage piped up \"What's going on?\"§0\n§0The first mage replied§0\n§0\"This man is trying to command me\"§0\n§0\"Which man?\"§0\n§0\"This one\"As the first mage said those\n\nwords she raised her arm to point at me and blasted me in the chest with §0lightning.The§0 blast was so powerful it forced me off my feet and into the middle of the square.I lay there for a while feeling as if my insides were burning.I eventually\n\ngathered enough strength to stand.I moved back over to the mages feeling weaker by the second,my wound was deep and bleeding §0heavily.Now§0 the mages were attacking a mother and her young baby they were about to chase her when I stood in\n\ntheir path.\"I see you can still fight\"the mage laughed,I simply nodded weakly as the mother began to run away.§0\n§0\"No matter I'll just finish you off where you stand!\"she then threw a knife at my neck,I was to weak to dodge it.\n\nA couple months later,I headed back to Sutica as it was a beautiful city and I was not willing to allow one attack to stop me from visiting §0there.As§0 I headed down the dirt path I saw my old friend Jasper arguing with an Orc at the side of the road.\n\nI naturally stopped to help §0him.As§0 I stopped the Orc slashed his axe at Jasper cutting him deeply across his chest causing him to fall to the ground.A high elven woman was walking down the path and faught the Orc while I helped §0Jasper.There§0 wasn't\n\nalot I could do so I took off my leather strap from across my shoulders and tightened it around his §0wound.It§0 slowed his §0bleeding.As§0 I got up from helping him a spook came beside me and began to turn his hand into a weapon.\"Please you have to help,\n\nkill me if you wish but please help my friend\"I pleeded but the spook did not listen and struck me in the head.§0\n§0  About two months later,I had just got off a boat at the cloud temple when my sister approached me in tears\"Krin...\"she said hugging\n\nme tightly.I could feel her shaking against my body.§0\n§0\"What is the matter?\"I questioned.§0\n§0\"I was kidnapped and taken to a slave camp\"§0\n§0\"§0oh....Suliin..\"I§0 did not know what to say \"W-who took you?\"§0\n§0\"An Orc,he told he needed help\n\nso I followed §0him.He§0 took me to a house on wheels where he tried to chain me up.I tried to escape but he hit me then took me with him.\"she began to cry more.I then took her home where she explained to me what happened to her.I was so angry\n\nthat I could not stop this from happening to her yet I did not want to show her I was §0mad.So§0 I moved closer to her and comforted her,I just hope she never has to go through anything like that again.\n\n\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0        One Year Later...\n\nI walked into Alexsandria, it was quite quiet that day.I wandered into the tavern there when I saw my sister's boyfriend,I walked to the other side of the tavern seeing now he was with another §0woman.They§0 were laughing together a-and she was blushing.\n\nHe also seemed drunk.I watched them leave together,I did not know what to think.I could have just misunderstood but I will tell Suliin as she needs to §0know.The§0 following week I saw my sister at the housing area of the citadel.I told her of what I saw.\n\nShe began to look sad,I did not want to hurt her at all I just thought she needed to §0know.We§0 ventured to the library of the draugr as she wanted to visit there and we talked some §0more.Quietly§0 of course it was a library after §0all.Anyway§0 she\n\nthen told me of how her and Csaba had planned to get §0married.Which§0 made me wish I had never told §0her.Then§0 Csaba came and explained to her that I had clearly misunderstood which made me believe I §0had.Surely§0 I must §0have.Right§0?\n\n\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0         Two Years Later..§0\n§0           About 1613\n\nThe housing in the citadel was no longer available and I had been evicted from my house in Mardon. I had been told that my things had been left in the new Snow Elf §0city.As§0 I was looking around the city Suliin came,she had told me she was coming,it was\n\nnot a §0surprise.We§0 talked a little about her and Csaba,I asked about how they had met each §0other.It§0 was not as romantic as I thought but it was cute in a needy §0way.She§0 asked me if I was interested in any women but I am not and I\n\ntold her as §0much.She§0 told me that I need to make more of an effort in speaking to women.§0\n§0  A few months later I was searching for houses in the new city in Mardon when Suliin payed me a surprise §0visit.She§0 was so happy,she announced that her and\n\nCsaba were engaged.I was so happy for them both but mostly happy that my sister was finding happiness in this dangerous unforgiving world.§0\n§0  A few months later and it was just the beginning of 1614.I had just visited Sutica and\n\nwas walking back down the dirt paths towards the docks.A golem stood in my way.§0\n§0\"Have you payed tribute to impera?\"It questioned§0\n§0\"If you are asking if I have given a gift to your creator I have not as I do not know who they are\"I replied\n\n\"You give one now!\"§0\n§0I then handed it some gold ingots \"Here you go\"the golem did not seem satisfied and picked me up beginning to crush my chest.§0\n§0\"Unhand me\"I said gasping for air but the golem did not listen.I began to hit it's arm.\n\nThen it grabbed my arm and ripped it off with ease.I bellowed in pain I will never forget the §0sound.The§0 golem then hit me on the head and I awoke in the cloud temple still in pain,my arm now replaced with a wooden one.I began to walk to my sisters\n\nhouse.I wanted to see her desperately I did not care how much pain I was in.I sent my Falcon to deliver her a letter telling her to await my §0arrival.As§0 I approached her door I was weak from pain,as she answered I could see she had a bruised eye.\n\n\"Suliin...\"I muttered weakly§0\n§0\"Krin,what happened?who did this to you?...\"she then took me inside where we talked §0more.She§0 had been attacked on the roads to Sutica,I did not care for my pain anymore I was worried about §0her.She§0 had\n\nbeen through so much already. She told me she did not want to lose me and I assured her I was not leaving her anytime soon and even if I was to die she had Csaba and I am sure he would look after her.§0\n§0  A few months later I went to visit my sister again,\n\nI had visired her before just §0briefly.She§0 does not leave the house as much as she used because of the fear of being attacked once more.I saw her tending to her garden,it is good to see that she has found something to do outside of her §0house.She§0 told me\n\nthat she was pregnant and I was so happy for her and §0Csaba.It§0 also got me thinking about having a woman of my own but who would want a one armed Snelf.§0\n§0    It was now the time of my sisters wedding,she looked so beautiful in her dress and I was so happy\n\nto see she had settled down with Csaba and began to feel happier and safer with him around.I may nit have settled down yet because there is so much of Axios I am yet to explore and I have not yet found a love interest yet either but I do not worry too\n\nmuch as I will find a right woman for me I just do not know when.\n\n\n§0\n§0\n§0      A Few Months Later§0\n§0                1615§0\n\nIt is the begining of a new year and I now have a niece her name is Alis,she is so tiny and §0precious.She§0 looks like her mother and I can not wait to see how she will grow up,whether she will be quiet like her parents or §0loud.Only§0 time will tell.\n\n\n§0\n§0\n§0        Five Years Later§0\n\nI can not believe how fast time has gone §0by.Alis§0 is now 5.She is quiet just like her parents and is very §0sweet.She§0 is quite nervous however but she might grow out of that but I am just happy she is healthy", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Monthly Happenings:§0\n§0-Fought many battles against Rebels.§0\n§0-Encountered a strange Sludge-esque monster who took the life of a man.§0\n§0-Fought off countless Rebels seeking to enter the city.§0\n§0-Fought in a major battle; Oren lost.", ""),
