        StaticBook("Test", "§bQuinton Gael", "-=-=-=-=-=--=-=-=-\n\n\n        Tales for\n            the\n       Common Man\n\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\n\n    By: Quinton Gael", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "‡¤¤¤‡¤¤¤‡¤¤¤‹♦›¤¤¤‡¤¤¤‡¤¤¤‡§0\n§0\n§0      A Compendium§0\n§0     of the Anatomy§0\n§0          of the§0\n§0       Human Body§0\n§0\n§0‡¤¤¤‡¤¤¤‡¤¤¤‹♦›¤¤¤‡¤¤¤‡¤¤¤‡§0\n§0\n§0\n§0    By: Quinton Gael§0\n\n☲☲☲☲☲☲☲❂☲☲☲☲☲☲☲§0\n§0\n§0   Table of Contents§0\n§0\n§0▣ Foreword§0\n§0▣ Introduction§0\n§0\n§0▣ Bones§0\n§0   ◉ Generalities§0\n§0   ◉ The Skull§0\n§0     ▣ General Skull§0\n§0     ▣ Face Bones§0\n§0     ▣ Ear Bones§0\n§0     ▣ Human Teeth\n\n   ◉ The Trunk§0\n§0     ▣ Spinal Bones§0\n§0     ▣ Middle Pelvis§0\n§0   ◉ The Pelvis§0\n§0     ▣ Bone Fusion§0\n§0     ▣ Pelvic Parts§0\n§0   ◉ The Chest§0\n§0     ▣ Collar Bone§0\n§0     ▣ Mid-Chest Bone§0\n§0   ◉ Upper Extremities§0\n§0     ▣ Shoulder Bone§0\n§0     ▣ Upper Arm Bone\n\n     ▣ Fore-Arm Bones§0\n§0     ▣ Wrist Bones§0\n§0     ▣ Hand Bones§0\n§0   ◉ Lower Extremities§0\n§0     ▣ Upper Leg Bone§0\n§0     ▣ Knee Bone§0\n§0     ▣ Calf Bones§0\n§0     ▣ Ankle Bones§0\n§0     ▣ Feet Bones§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0☲☲☲☲☲☲☲❂☲☲☲☲☲☲☲\n\n☲☲☲☲☲☲☲❂☲☲☲☲☲☲☲§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Dearest Desimir,§0\n§0\n§0In the event of my death, I do not want you to despair. I want you to know what a wonderful gift you've been all the time I've known you. I want you to carry on, because the world needs more people like you, Desimir.\n\nMore people who laugh and cry, more people who always look out for others. More people who ask questions and want to know the truth, and who tell others the same with no hesitation. More people who aren't afraid.\n\nNot afraid to fight, or learn, or ask or see or struggle or do. More people who aren't afraid to apologize when they've done wrong.§0\n§0\n§0Your life is yours to do what you will with, and it's going to be a long one, so take your time with it.\n\nStick with the Library and with Nemir, at least until you're old enough to be on your own. Keep practicing and learning.§0\n§0\n§0Remember that magic isn't always the answer, and it's best to master yourself before attempting to master anything else.\n\nBe honest with yourself above all else.§0\n§0\n§0There's some more bitter life lessons I could touch upon. Like never place your trust in others, or always be ready to lie your way out of something.\n\nBut I think the Lyeth that would teach those lessons is mostly gone. The truth is, there are a lot of friends and allies you'll find, some without even looking. The people I suspected least would often help me the most.\n\nI love you, Desimir, and it is very important that you love yourself too.§0\n§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "I am not a man of the cloth, like High Priest Everard, or the good Seneschal Daniel. I am educated, enough to know not to believe the men of the Reformed Church and their claims to know the true word of God.\n\nWhen the Betrayer and his beastly corruptions of men, the rotting, walking, talking corpses of men, revealed themselves in the North, I was but a lad. §0\n§0My childhood was filled with the terror of nighttime raids on Al'khazar,\n\nand I had no choice but to pick up a blade as soon as I could carry one. That was every man and boy's duty. When your own dead rise up from their graves to claw upon the walls of what was once, in life, their beloved city, the dispensation\n\nof responsibility that comes with youth is quickly set aside and denied.§0\n§0When Al'khazar truly suffered a real attack, when King Perea was slain, I was on the streets fighting alongside everyone else. I'd just met a lovely lass a fortnight before.\n\nShe died in the attack. But so did many others. We were making plans to wed, two young lovebirds. I never did find myself as enamored with another after that.§0\n§0Instead my free time was spent elsewise, whenever I hadn't need to have a blade\n\nin my hand.§0\n§0I went to church as often as I could. I spent days in there, listening to High Priest Everard preach whenever he could. And I remember the crowds were vast at first, Faith the Aegis for all of Oren's people.\n\nI am certain crowds were the same in the North, under Seneschal Daniel, where the fighting was even worse and the attacks more frequent. But soon the attendance began to thin out. I could see how it disheartened\n\nHigh Priest Everard, to see his flock dwindle. Was it lack of Faith? Were so many lost in the fighting? Had the so-called 'Reformation' Church claimed them?§0\n§0\n§0I soon found it was none of these things.\n\nAfter the attack on Al'khazar, and the death of the King, and the subsequent worsening corruption of King Sheffield, I moved North, to Alstion, to serve on the front lines.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "TRANSFIGURATION NOTES:§0\n§0By: Lyeth, the stupid Hobo.§0\n§0\n§0First Weekly Task:§0\n§0Study Iron and all associated properties. Study small sapphires for use as mana gems. Write notes. See back page.\n\nTRANSFIGURATION is a magic which allows you to enchant objects. Some mistakenly believe it allows you to ward objects against other magics, but this is misnomer. Wards are not inherently put into objects,\n\nbut rather are a separate spell you can cast as part of transfiguration that you can then enchant into an item.§0\n§0\n§0Enchantment requires the use of gems which can hold mana, and as the enchantment is used,\n\nthe mana in the gem is depleted and requires refilling. §0\n§0\n§0At early stages, in order to enchant with a magic you must be an active practitioner of the magic.§0\n§0\n\nWhen more experienced, one can perform what is known as entrapment, which can be used to enchant objects with magics other than your own.\n\nEnchantments are spells woven into objects themselves. The mana gems embedded into these objects are the fuel for the enchantment, but do not carry the enchantment within them themselves.\n\nWhile enchantments are a large draw to mages wanting to learn Transfiguration, it is important to remember that Enchantment is only one part of the magic. The other is the art of Transmutation.§0\n§0\n§0Transmutation's reach is roughly arm's length distance.\n\nTransmutation is the manipulation of the mana that is stored in every object in existence. This process involves tapping into the mana of the object and by pooling your mana into it, you can change certain aspects of the object.\n\nOne property that can be changed in temperature, which can be raised or lowered.§0\n§0\n§0However, in order to change anything about the object you must know about the material and its properties at the desired state.\n\nAs discussed, Enchantment is a spell woven into an object, with a mana gem fueling it. The object is then able to be used to cast the spell. An advantage to this approach as opposed to typical spell casting is the ability to easily\n\ncast a spell without needing to focus on casting the spell. All that needs to be done is to have the enchantment on the object activated.§0\n§0§\n\nAbjurations are another facet of Transfiguration. Abjurations allow a mage to disrupt the mana anchor of the target spell, therefore removing the spell's connection to this plane.\n\nMana Anchors are the location in the world where a mage tears a hole into the Void, which they funnel their mana into, in order to perform magic. (This is also why casting magic at a longer distance is more tiring).\n\nAbjurations use their own mana to disrupt mana anchors, causing spells to fail.§0\n§0\n§0There are two types of Abjurations: Abjurations themselves, and Wards.\n\nAn Abjuration is essentially a projectile which can be propelled forwards to meet a spell a distance from you. A ward on the other hand is stationary and acts as a barrier. A ward can disrupt multiple magics but an abjuration can only disrupt one.\n\nIn order to disrupt any magic, you need to have knowledge of said magic. Simply reading a book about the magic won't do; You must either practice it or have someone demonstrate it and describe it to you.\n\nList of uses for Transmutation:\n\nNeed to learn about Telekinesis from Nemir so I can abjure it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "§0\n§0\n§0           The§0\n§0          Stone§0\n§0          Giant§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0By Lyeth\n\nThere once was a Mali'ame whose name is Unknown, and not knowing we'll call this one None. None was adventurous and bold to a fault, and thought of themselves all the world.§0\n\nNone wandered the lands, called not a one home, and never did let the soles of their feet touch a thing but the flesh of the earth.§0\n§0\n§0One day whilst wandering in lands not unknown, for None knew very well they were lands that None should be in,\n\nthey came upon a hill.§0\n§0", "")
    )

    private fun _AXIOS_TAHN_7(): List<StaticBook> = listOf(
        StaticBook("Dear Nemir", "§bCarver Le Prevost", "Dear Nemir Queen of the Library.§0\n§0\n§0     Good evening, I Carver Le Prevost Captain of the Norlandic Naval Forces have been tasked with bringing a magic 'awakening' to Norland. This of course is something I have no talent in.\n\nBut you, as the library do so. I have been given the go ahead to give a large island over to the Library's usage as long as they bring with them knowledge so that people in the Norlandic Nation can gain knowledge of Magic. Which so many of us have never\n\nseen or done before. This task is something few groups can do, the enchantry and the Library. I though have a conflict of intrest and would rather love seeing the library grow and spread. Hence I have given the Library my first pick to gain ownership of\n\nthis land in the trade that the lord of Norland has happily given me permission to do. So Nemir, If you give some time bird Carver Le Prevost who will more then likely be at the norlandic docks. I shall come swiftly to further this deal and hear you out.\n\nSincerly, Carver Le Prevost§0\n§013th of The Grand Harvest 1637§0\n§0\n§0P.S. This is a complete conflict of Intrest but I will happily make this deal work. This is part of my way of making amends for what I have done. The land is the island that is desolate\n\non norlandic lands. It is a great spot for something. You can make something great.", ""),
        StaticBook("<3", "§bLoric Armas", "I am surry fur whut mi am dun 2 jew. Mi apuligize fur steeling yer hay. <3", ""),
        StaticBook("Iron and Steel", "Gladuos", "In the following book we will be exploring the physical and magical traits of iron or steel, how it may react to the mundane senses, how it's made, weight, shape, hardness, melting point, and a magical understanding.\n\n   Iron or steel generally takes on a white-ish grey coloration that may give off a dim shine if smithed in the correct manner. \n   It will often give off clanging and dinging noises as it is used in whatever way it may. Sounds can occasionally\n\nreverberate throughout the material. \n   Iron, and especially steel, are incredibly tough materials. They are often used during combat or for specially tough constructions if necessary. Compared to stone or lesser materials, iron/steel\n\nis far more valuable and strong. Steel has a higher coal content compared to iron, and as thus is even more tough.\n\n   Metallic iron or steel is usually created through treating the ore variant through intense blast furnacing and introducing coals to improve quality of the material. The heat of these furnaces usually take on a heat of about 2000 degrees Celsius.\n\n  The difference between iron and steel is that steel has a higher content of coal added during this process to give an even tougher finish. This is removed from the furnace and cooled in a slow, meticulous process of reheating, cooling, tempering and so-\n\n- on.\n\n   Steel or iron are metallic materials and thus are often fairly dense, heavy materials, even comparative to earthen minerals.\n\n   The average shape of steel or iron varies dramatically depending on how it was formed. In its ore variant, it is normally in the shape of any other rock. However, it can be formed into the metallic variant that takes on a shape depending on the -\n\n- smith's choice and skill.\n\n   Once again, steel or iron are generally very strong materials. This can be often shown when making fine weapons or armors, as making purely metallic constructions may simply be too costly.\n\n   The melting point of steel and iron is in the range between 1370 and 1550 degrees Celsius. The lower portions of this range are attributed to steel, while the higher is closer to iron's melting point.\n\n   The magical signature of iron and steel isn't too terrible. It may not be comparable to carbarum or mage gold in conductivity of magical forces, but it may be slightly less resistant than some of the lesser valuable materials in the mortal planes.\n\n*When reaching these final pages, the reader would be shown a large amount of diagrams, sketches, illustrations, charts, and equations about the various properties of iron and steel. For pages and pages, these continue, being accompanied by various lines-\n\n- of information attempting to support many of the previous statements of the book. There are also some nuanced details of the materials less relevant than the information already given.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Thank you", "§bLukas Vanir", "Thanks for bringing some light into this old man's life. You've certainly made these last few days enjoyable for me, especially in my age. Thank you, Kate, you really do have a big heart. I've gifted some money to you, Sigmund, and Brynden to spend on\n\nwhatever you might want. Keep an eye on the baby girl for me.§0\n§0\n§0Uncle Lukas loves you.§0\n§0\n§0P.S. the necklace was also for you!!§0\n§0\n§0P.P.S. also it wasn't too much money but it was everything I have so hopefully it's enough.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Once upon a time there was a little boy. A light-haired, light-skinned little boy who found himself all alone.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Murder log: I§0\n§0-Arabella Entwesser, the Devil from Aeldin.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0Investigation of the first crime scene:§0\n§0-Adelburg Park, 23rd of The Grand Harvest, 1624.§0\n§0\n§0On top of a picnic blanket nearby a tree, the murder scene was found. Two patches of\n\nBlood on the blanket, about 12 hours old. Blood patches were dark-red and wide. No artery hit, blunt force used. A bag was present by the stains, containing clothes, various massage equipment including vials of olive oil and towels, and a name tag,\n\ninscribed 'Entwesser'. Clothes were of high quality, noblewoman-like. A theme of red and black was widely present. Long hair strands of a light-brown color spotted. I now have a basic idea of her physiognomy. The brand-new head of a mallet was found in\n\nthe bottom of the bag. Clothes of the victim left behind on a nearby tree branch. A big, burly man, wearing peasant clothes. Short spics of red hair were found on his jacket. Thus, from the Evidence, we can reach the following conclusions:\n\n-Arabella feigned the role of a massage-lady.§0\n§0-Arabella does not take the social status of their victims into consideration§0\n§0-Arabella is not afraid to hide her name, hence the name tag§0\n§0-Arabella left the murder scene in a hasty manner, leaving her bag\n\nbehind.§0\n§0-Arabella still uses her signature weapon to strike her victim's head when they least expect it, a mallet.§0\n§0-Arabella currently has light-brown dyed hair, and prefers wearing noblewoman clothes, a recurring theme of red and black present.\n\nMurder Log II§0\n§0\n§0Arabella Entwesser, feigned death.§0\n§0\n§0-Woman sporting the same characteristics aforementioned spotted in the Adelburg tavern, seducing a Daelish man. A conflict ensued when other supposed 'bounty hunters' directly tried to kill the woman.\n\nUnder the guise of her savior, I guided her away to a hidden alley, where I disposed of her. Upon checking her bag, I found a note:§0\n§0'Take my clothes from the cabinet, go to the Adelburg tavern, and pose as a massage-lady. Slightly dyeing your head black\n\nis advised, though not enforced.'§0\n§0\n§0I suspect I was tricked. The bounty issuers are tryng to find out whether the girl is Arabella or not based on her dental records. She looked like her, that's for sure.§0\n§0---------------------------------------§0\n§0Was I\n\ntricked? Has she made a fool of myself, by making me kill a mere henchwoman? Is this all a ruse...?§0\n§0*the writing above seems to be written in a sloppy manner*\n\n-13th of the First Seed, 1625§0\n§0\n§0-Major breakthrough. Through analyzing and deduction, we have concluded that Arabella Entwesser is not an individual, but a whole entity comprised of mysterious members, all working towards one goal.\n\n-Arabella, in Flexio, means 'Yielder of Prayers'§0\n§0-Entwesser, in turn, can be roughly translated to 'Killer of men'§0\n§0-The note suggests a familiar place in which 'Arabella' and Lucy swap clothes.\n\nNew Goals:§0\n§0- Find the organization's main base of operations.§0\n§0-Succesfully root out or trick one or several members of the organization(Extensive interrogation required)", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "§4___________________ |  A Guide to common   | |        Recipes          | -------------------", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Menu§0\n§0Bread - 2 Minas§0\n§0Flavoured bread - 5§0\n§0Pancake - 4§0\n§0\n§0Cake - 10 minas§0\n§0Pie - 8 minas§0\n§0Quiche - 10 minas§0\n§0Fish cake - 10 minas", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Day one§0\n§0Killed some shit, got a cool bluesteel sword. Its pretty cool, but im still struggling for money a bit. Hopefuly my leatherworking job will pull through. Got a horse aswell! I shall name him Charles VI in rememberance of all the other animals.\n\nDay two§0\n§0Ragatha gave me \"A shitload of leather\", itll help with my archer armor production. I flopped a bit with my last tunics, only 7%, but hopefully ill get a bit better at this. I found a new religion, pumpkinology. You have to love your pumpkin-\n\nwith all of your heart. Heritics will be mashed up and turened into pumpkin pie. My horse died before I could name him, but I found a donkey. He isnt quite as fast, but its the heart that matters. I HAVE DONE IT. the pumpkin mask is complete. A special-\n\nmask that allows you to hear thoughts of other pumpkin wearers. I am truly lucky to have been the one who created such a precous relic.", ""),
        StaticBook("SPARTA", "§bKaleb Radah \"Guardslayer\"", "THIS IS SPARTA", ""),
        StaticBook("Draug the bad", "§bThe Mysterious Stranger", "The Library of Draug.§0\n§0A simple lovely place right?§0\n§0Nope. It is one of the most  evil locations in all of Axios. They hold the worlds most powerful items. They won't let others use such items. These items are sitting useless and spotless. When they could\n\nbe used to shape the whole world. Atleast the Enchantary uses their horrid Items the Library won't. This word will fall. And when it does the library will be there sitting. Doing nothing. Dusting off their little antiques as everyone else dies.\n\nThere is only one person in the library that could change this and that said person won't change anything. Magic is bad. It is being used for everything except for the common good. When will these people realize this world is ours. Ours the ones that sit\n\non our feet. Fighting wars. Living. Finding stuff and using said stuff for our good. For the worlds good. The library finds the shit and locks it away. When someone else finds something they try to take it. Do any of you people realize this? The library\n\nmust fall. The library must be used for the common good not for their own goddamn good.§0\n§0\n§0- The dead man walking.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tragic Edge", "§bSchnub'nub", "{\"text\":\"Mylas I was lying when I said I could live with the pain I don\\u0027t want to live in pain. I want to be with you if you want to be with me two meet me in our room dw\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"[!]Tears would be stained into this page[!] I-Its hurts not being able to have someone that I love so much, but its to late I have to \"}\n\n{\"text\":\"I dream of our frist kiss..How he untied my corest...Looked at me..I want to relive that..But I know I can\\u0027t and I won\\u0027t...I am still a virgin...I wouldn\\u0027t give up that to anyone until marriage...But I can\\u0027t get him out of my mind..\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"I am planing on runing away. I am packing my things without anyone knowing. I am planning on going where ever the wind takes me. I won\\u0027t be froced to marry someone I don\\u0027t love...I will only marry Aiden..But I can\\u0027t and won\\u0027t marry him.\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"I am going to leave in a month I need to say some things to people and get some things done before I leave.\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"I am still a virgin unlike my sister. She got all mad at me after she said in public you almost had sex with him. I said the truth by saying she did because she isn\\u0027t a virgin shes a hertic.\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\" _    \\\n\\u003c\\u0027) ,/\\\n(_\\u003d\\u003d/\\\n _\\u0027-\\\n\\\n-------------------Cerulean flat naped thrust, 1596, halfling shores\"}", ""),
        StaticBook("How to get girls", "§bKalameet", "{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nI.. . ..\ndon't know how to", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Can you leave me some raw fish in my donation chest?§0\n§0Would be much appreciated.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0                 Sincerely,§0\n§0                 Agnar", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "My name is Bhyrindaar Geriayar and have dedicated this book to creating a better state of racial and national relations in the Island of Axios. I will survey multiple residents of Haesne and other cities for their opinions on the Orenian Empire and other\n\nraces. For some more information on me I am a wood elf, currently living in Haesne, and I have lived in the Empire for majority of my life. Now, turn the page for my first survey.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0(17th of the Sun's Smile, 1622)\n\nAnswerer: Zurge'Ram§0\n§0Race: Orc§0\n§0Residence: The War Nation of Krugmar (travels to Alban, Haense)§0\n§0Opposes Empire, due to \"Them attacking us orcs ages ago\" and hates wood elves (twiggies to him) the most because his nation is currently at war with them.\n\nAnswerer: Tulen§0\n§0Race: Kha'Tigrasi§0\n§0Residence: Veris and Dwarf Clans§0\n§0Oppose the Empire because of the men whole rule it that \"find themselves better than everyone else.\" and dislikes wood elves the most due to their cowardly nature.\n\nAnswerer: Hane§0\n§0Race: Human§0\n§0Residence: \"Half the time Warhawkes, other half private\"§0\n§0Since he doesnt live within the Imperial borders he has no opinion on the Empire. Does not have a most hated race but prefers Dark Elves because of him living\n\nin the Warhawkes.§0\n§0\n§0***********************§0\n§0\n§0I would like to note that if I have not finished this book by the time I'm dead, I'd prefer you publish it your self.§0\n§0\n§0***********************\n\nAnswerer: Gul-san§0\n§0Race: Orc§0\n§0Residence: War Ugz§0\n§0Opposes the Empire because of their weak nature. Hates Hou-Zis the most because they have \"enslaved and killed innocents and mine\"\n\nAnswerer: Ghai Jhork§0\n§0Race: Highlander§0\n§0Residence: Veris, now nowhere", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "I happen'd to take some things from'ee chest a few beds down, I guess ye' both had some similar things, so I just had to take some of yer' things.§0\n§0I'twill sell fer' quite thee' price, thank ye'.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Gatekeepers Handbook§0\n§0By Eric Robbin§0\n§0-------------------Customary questions:§0\n§0\"Name and Allegiance?\"\n\nNations disallowed:§0\n§0Norlanders§0\n§0Rebels§0\n§0\n§0Races disallowed:§0\n§0Orcs\n\nSuspicous persons:§0\n§0Saru- brown haired, neutral allegiance§0\n§0Red Orc-half-blood vouched for by guard Evalien fights for Oren\n\nAttempted Murderers§0\n§0A man, pale white skin, crystal blue eyes, and dark brown hair, wears a blue tabberd with deer sigil, killed roswell woman and attempted an attack on a church woman\n\nNeeded for Orc by King Stephen I§0\n§0large helm with Lur Wolf\n\nPeople have gone missing in the woods, mainly homeless.\n\n*A picture of Krog smashing a Norlanders Body with his axe and him falling to the ground is shown here and is signed at the bottom ~Eric Robbin*", ""),
        StaticBook("Demands or War", "§b___", "Demands:\nThe City of Felsen\nTwo Crates of Iron\nTen Crates of Wood\nTen Crates of Stone\nTen Crates of Hay\nAn Alliance to Fight Against the Dwarves and Snow Elves in War.\n\nAcceptance of the terms should be sent to Kahn'Braduk, Rex of the Iron Uzg within the next three elven days or else war shall be declared upon Oren and an alliance will be formed with Skravia against Oren.\n-The Rex", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "List of Items on the Agenda§0\n§01. regain land§0\n§02. raise mina§0\n§03. create citizenship list\n\nregain land that had been mistakenly re-granted to Haelun'or.\n\nraise 40,000 mina in an effort to have Norland officially recognized as a true nation.\n\nTo create a list of people who own homes within The Krag, for Organizational and taxing purposes. And to also create a list of formally recognized citizens of Norland, and the creation of benefits for those that are recognized as such.\n\nOrcs Badlands Scout:§0\n§05minutes in Saw 2 Orcs Patrolling the Roads§0\n§010minutes in Orc and Elf spotted at Market Place§0\n§015 Minutes in Orc Spotted Patrolling North Western Side of the City§0\n§020minutes in Orc Spotted Us leaving to Sound the War Horn\n\nOrc BadLands:§0\n§025 Minutes in Orcs found Swarming the Area.§0\n§030 Minutes in Left the Area for a short while§0\n§045 Minutes in Orcs seen entering and exiting the City.. Around 3-5", ""),
        StaticBook("WIP cookbook", "§bMortes Harbringer", "recipie book:§0\n§0\n§0pale ale:§0\n§0\n§0wheat§0\n§0\n§0water bottle\n\nmulled wine§0\n§0\n§0water bottle§0\n§0\n§0dark resign", ""),
        StaticBook("oren war reasons", "§bMortes Harbringer", "oren:§0\n§0\n§0thretened to kill me§0\n§0\n§0robbed me§0\n§0\n§0has an unfair and corrupt government§0\n§0\n§0are insultant of norland", ""),
        StaticBook("Thank You", "§bElliot Cook", "Dear Sir,\nI apologize for bringing inconvenience to you and your people. I did not mean to burden you> However, I have great gratitude that you took interest in my health and possibly even saved my life. I had no prior knowledge of heated daggers and\n\ninfections. \n\nI do think you should know what occured to me when I got this scar.\nI came across the orc settlement in the desert. Having never been to the place before, I decided I would proceed inside and see what inhabitated it. Once I\n\ncame inside, he got me. His name is Tar'zar. He then took me to a place, cut the arm, gave me a new name, and sent me to the farms. After the night, another Orc grew angry when he saw me and ordered me gone. I am still not very sure what was the purpose\n\nof what took place...\n\nSince then I have lost trust in unknown places as well as myself. How could I have been so foolish?\n\nI thank you for taking care of me, but I need time to recollect myself. I know I told you I don't write much, but\n\nI felt that this was a neccesary time for you.\n\nMy arm hurts much more than it did the first time, but I think it is for the best. \n\nI plan to return to your castle in the near future, but for now I want to go back to the camp and\n\nkill the orc myself once I find the right weapons and items...\n\nThank you sir for your help. You are very generous and honorable.", ""),
        StaticBook("Winter Roses.", "§bCassandra Louisa Vimmark", "-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-,-.-.-.-.-.-.-.-.-.-.-.-.-.-. -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-             Winter§0\n§0            Roses§0\n§0-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=--.-.-.-.-.-.-.-.-.-.-.-.-.-.-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-§0\n§0a play written by lady Cassandra Louisa Vimmark and her daughter, Ayana Augusta. §0\n\nA bed of five winter roses lay nestled in the snow.§0\n§0A woman stood over them, watching them grow.§0\n§0“Sweet, delicate roses; I shall protect you all forever.” Said the woman, kneeling down in the white and cradling them each.§0\n\n“Sweet delicate roses; my beautiful beings, my pride and joy.” Said the woman, picking out one of the flowers plagued with thorns. She picked at them, pricking her fingers as she did so. She loved this one the most. She loved this one so much - that when\n\nit died, when it wilted, a part of her did too.§0\n§0A bed of four winter roses lay nestled in the snow.§0\n§0A woman stood over them, distractedly watching them grow.§0\n§0\"My dear delicate roses; my symbols of grace and purity.\" Said the woman, setting down the rose\n\ncovered in throns and picking up the last two, blue and bright.§0\n§0“My dear delicate roses; for I shall always love you, until the seas go dry and the wind is forever still.” Said the woman, holding them up in the air with a smile for all the world to see.\n\nAs she lifted them higher, they shivered and quivered, and soon were blown away in the ocean breeze. §0\n§0A bed of three winter roses lay nestled in the snow. §0\n§0“Strong little roses; my little boys, my strong little lords. For I shall always prot--.\"\n\nBefore the woman could say what she wished to say, a man dressed in purple came and stomped them, pressing them deeper into the snow, savaging them until they were no more. §0\n§0“Ye are not worthy of being here; for thee are treasonous, and the foul woman\n\nthat says no only must be delirious.\"§0\n§0The woman looked up, mortified.§0\n§0\"My roses; my children. For I have failed you, and I shall now always live in despair.\"§0\n§0In the sad woman's mind, she believed that she had not truly treated her roses with that of a\n\nmotherly care.§0\n§0In the sad woman’s eyes, she saw herself as a lost, weak thing.§0\n§0In the sad woman’s heart however, she knew she would seek vengeance on the man who held more power than a king. §0\n§0\n§0--, for my dearests.§0\n\nlife is no song, sweetling. some day you will learn this, to your sorrow.§0\n§0\n§0[!] A single rose is stamped in the centre of the page.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Journey", "§bLanz Chilzbur", "this one time, i ate a potato. it was pretty good.", ""),
        StaticBook("To mha King", "§bBaldin Frostbeard", "Skippeh es §0blind...he§0 es not tha king of mah people. He might be a gud frend but ah cannot fight mah brothas because of he's ineptitude. I will leave, this civil war goes against the will of our §0gods...ah§0 wont spill dwarven blood.§0\n§0Sorreh mah King.", ""),
        StaticBook("V", "§bChu Li Mang", "The letter appears sealed with a wax stamp, a flaming bird shown clearly.§0\n§0\n§0\"For too long have you descendants lived under the grace of your so called \"Righteousness\", your dependancy upon the ancestors you worship like deities to justify your ways.\n\nThe times of war have crept upon the isles once more, the cogs of war turning to the sounds of our drums, fueled by greed and the drive for power.§0\n§0\n§0Be it by blade or flame, by death or subjugation, our horde calls out to bring an end to your way of life.\n\n[!]An elegantly written signature is engraved upon the coarse paper, seemingly out of place§0\n§0\n§0朱丽曼§0\n§0Chu Li Mang§0\n§0\n§0Heavens Chosen§0\n§0\n§0Commander of the Vermillion Legion", ""),
        StaticBook("A Receipt", "§bUnknown", "RECEIPT:\n\n10 okdodk\n5 lwdokwd\n\n\nodfkowkd\n15", ""),
        StaticBook("Dean's Journal", "§bDean Osborn", "Day 1 \n  Me and the Group drank ourself near to death and when around singing in town. John and Jon are good comapany.\n\nDay 2\n   Met the Barkeep, Lotte. He is a big guy and is very interested in the Workers union and sanonism. Drank most of the day and won alot of coin gambling.\n\nDay 3\n   Bought a room at the Dog and crow tavern. The room is alright and having a bed is nice. Met a halfling name Eila.\n\n Day 4\n   Found a strange cave while wondering. I normally take walks out in wilderness, sometimes with friends and found a cave that seems to be calling me.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Needs§0\n§0-Alcohol (Alot)§0\n§0-Fighters (At least §0\n§0two reliable one's who can be there the whole time)§0\n§0-People willing to come and spend money at the fights§0\n§0-A small amount of Body guards?§0\n§0-Pamphelts for the fight explaining key details\n\n-Sugarcane/Paper for phamplets§0\n§0-Feathers for phamplets\n\nLayout of the Fight§0\n§0-------------------Location:\n\nBetting- Bet", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Places to go to for§0\n§0selling.§0\n§0-------------------  The All father group§0\n§0 -Nivan says they might be able to pay    for it and might not be as crazy as thought.§0\n§0 The Enchantery§0\n§0 -Full of schoolars, possibly rich, probably one willing to buy\n\namong them.§0\n\n*The Notes at the start of the journal end and the latter of the journal is written in a neater, organized format.*\n\nDay four after the event.§0\n§0 I'm writing from my room in the dog and Crow currently. I can't stop thinking about what I saw in the Kal'varak, I just need a few days away from Alban to think it out. It isn't worth mentioning since I'll be back soon.\n\nDay six after the event.§0\n§0 I've spent the last few days in the newby woods in a small camp I've set up. I've decided I will stay out here a few more days, I just can't get him out of my mind, after this I'll be glad to see everyone.\n\nDay ten after the event.§0\n§0 I've abandoned my camp and started roaming, mainly among the sparsley populated towns among Tahn. I keep seeing Him in my dreams, I keep seeing Iblees... Creator bless me.\n\nDay twenty-two after the event.§0\n§0 I miss John, and John, and even Maria. I must stay away for now though I keep muttering to myself they'll think I'm mad..\n\nDay Fourty-five after the event.§0\n§0 I've started doing easy odd jobs to survive since my minas have run out. I keep seeing Iblees standing there.. talking- I can't remember his words but they still seem to echo in my mind. I almost wish he was here with me\n\nto remind me what he said.\n\nDay eighty-eighty after the event.§0\n§0 I thought I would have returned to Alban by now. I thought I would have settled down somewhere at least. I keep wandering. §0\n§0 I WOULD HAVE LET HIM FREE.§0\n§0 I have no right to be among even theives.\n\nDay one hundred twenty-two after the event.§0\n§0 I sometimes crave the power he held still, I almost wish I could return to the Kal'varak and bargin with him..§0\n§0   Such power..\n\n*This page is torn out*\n\n*This page is torn out*\n\n*This page is torn out*\n\nDay two hundred twelve after the event.  I haven't done much of what I used to since I left Alban, drinking, Gambling, adventuring. I need to stop this, I'm not mad I need to have everyone know.\n\n*This page is torn out*\n\n*This page is torn out*\n\n*This page is torn out*\n\nDay three hundred after the event.§0\n§0 I've spiraled out of control, I can't have anyone read what I've wrote.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "The Entire Tome, on The descendants of Dragur.§0\n§0-------------------§0\n§0\n§0 Dragons are commonly known among the people of our land but are still shrouded in mystery on the finer aspects of their existance. With this tome, those aspects can be\n\ncleared.\n\n Chapter One: Dragons          Of Old\n\nFemale dragons are more agressive§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Entry;§0\n§0 Found a Shire like structure in Asul, I marked it on my map. It has differnt structures around it that seem to symbolize: Ruby§0\n§0Lapiz§0\n§0Emerald§0\n§0Oxyn§0\n§0Pearl and §0\n§0Sapphires.\n\nAlong as floating colors above the shrine, matching the stones and the pearl. The structure is buried in a forrest by Haria.\n\n5th of Sun' Smile 1622 Entry;§0\n§0 The sacred holy tree in the Norlands (the one they hang people from). Has colored essence appearing and staying around it. The first was a deep purple essence heading out from the ground and pointing away from the tree.\n\nIn the last few saint days a blue and Orange essence has also appeared around the tree. They seem fixed and all come from the ground and point away from the tree.\n\n11th of the Amber Cold 1622§0\n§0 I ran into Erika the Cheiftess and found out her frost witch problem still exists. I then asked her about Lotte's whereabouts to which she quickly awnsered she didn't know and that she must then leave. I am starting to suspect\n\nshe might be involved in his disapearence. I will ask around to learn more of Lotte.\n\nSomeday in the Amber Cold 1622§0\n§0 At the Guild Hall when a floating orb came seeking a sentinal. It touched me and showed me a memory or a world engulfed in fire and darkness. The darkness ended when a golden figure created many stone pillars and ran magic\n\nthrough them. Then the golden figure disapeared. That was the memory. The stonepillar\n\n20th of the Amber Cold 1622§0\n§0 Turns out Hareven already knows the location of the Kal'Varak and Aluatis actually went through it safely.", ""),
        StaticBook("Apology", "§bAtturi Silversteed", "Im Sorry Serenity. I know you said I was a kind and sweet, caring, person. I think I can agree with that since you had the decency to tell me about being drawn to someone else instead of running away or just not telling me.\n\nThey must be a really great person to have been a better pick for you. *A drop or two of water seem to have left a crinkly circle outlined by scrunched up paper on the page in the past two lines*§0\n§0I admire your honesty. You are an amazing person..\n\nMaybe that's why it was so easy to fall in love with you. However, I believe I am also a bit selfish. I should have just let you leave the first time against my emotions. It was wrong of me to to hold you back from someone you have more feelings for and\n\n-your fate. *Tear stains dot around the last line in random spots. It had bled the ink a superficial amount.* I shouldn't have fallen for you in the first place. Out of respect for our friendship and the idea that some things are too good to be true.\n\nIf we become friends again I want things to go back to normal.. what was before.. or try to. I liked our friendship, and im sure you did too since we kept hugging when we saw each other. I hope that won't change.\n\nAgain, Im sorry for how I reacted... I might still be in love with you, I want to love you even if it can't be romantically, and it might be awkward at first but, May we be friends again?", ""),
        StaticBook("Immortal Spirits", "§bThurak'Yar", "Immortal Spirits\n\nA list of the Greater Spirits inhabiting the Immortal Realm and what they represent. This may change, given time, and will be updated as new spirits come to power.\n\nVotar- The spirit of the hunt, commonly shown as a giant, bloodied wolf. Praised by the Phrase Glougaz Votar.\n\n      /\\_==_/\\\n      | /o   o\\ |\n      \\         /\n       \\       /\n        \\ *.* /\n          \\ /\n\nEnrohk- The spirit of bloodlust, savagery and war, often shown as a bastard sword covered in blood. \n        \n         /\\\n         |  |\n         |  | \n         |....|\n         |. .|\n      `==8=='\n          ||\n\nShezept- The spirit of revenge, plots and stealth, depicted as a woman with a lower body of a snake. \n      \n        O\n       -|-\n   ^\\_\\\\_\n   \\____/\n\nJevex- Spirit of order, hard work and self sacrifice, shown as a giant hammer. He's a deadly enemy to the spirit Shezept.\n \n     [======]\n     [==|  |==]\n         ==\n         ==\n        |.--.|\n         ==\n\nIxli- The spirit of forbidden knowledge, truth and judgement. Depicted as an eye, he provides knowledge as the cost of sanity. \n\n       |/  \\|\n      |  (.)  |\n       |\\  /|\n\nOgrol- Spirit of despair, sapped strength and entrapement, shown as a cage full of writhing bodies. He tries to lock up all who summon him.\n\n       ______\n       | | |  | | |\n       =<< >>=\n       | | |  | | |\n      ========\n\nKor- The spirit of the dead, depicted as a cloaked man with an open hand.\n          _\n          |O\\\n           |-''\n          /\\\n\nAnkrus- Spirit of the sea, fishermen and safe travels, often shown as an aquatic woman wielding a spear. \n\n           () |\n           oo/\n           \\/\n           /\\\n           \\/\n\nArwa- Spirit of fertility, harvest and farming, commonly shown as a plump female with over seven hundred breasts.\n \n           ()\n         /.oo.\\\n        /o.oo.o\\\n        |o.o.o.o.o|\n        \\_____/\n         [|]    [|]\n\nAnyhuluz- Spirit of destruction, malicious intent and internal strife, shown as a warrior covered in open wounds.\n\n         O   ^\n       /(`)-`|\n         [|]\n         /\\\n\nAkezo- Spirit of health, vitality and healing, depicted as a winged whale surrounded by a blue aura.\n\n   (\\./)\n     \\\\_/--^--.\n      =.    \"~\"   )\n        \\______/\n\nPaxahru- Spirit of arrogance and stupidity, depicted as a boasting fool.\n\n        /**\\\n       ( ^^ ) \n        /--\\ \n        |`~~'|\n        ====\n        \\/\\/\n         |   |\n\nUblulhar- Spirit of hope an new beginnings, shown as a tree sapling bursting from the ground. \n\n       _____\n      {~~~~}\n     {~~~~~}\n      {~~~~}\n       {~| |~}\n          | |\n       ~~~~~\n\nGhorza- Spirit of travel, depicted as an ever turning wheel.\n\n       /----\\\n      / /--\\ \\\n      |  |<:::::)|  |\n      \\ \\--/ /\n       \\----/\n\nRolfizh- Spirit of assassinations and poison, depicted as a dagger with poison dripping from it.\n\n        /\\\n        |  | \n        |  |\n       =||||=\n         ||\n\nTrokorl- The spirit of engineering, machinery and building. Depicted as a goblin with a goblin with goggles and a hammer.\n\n       {o o}\n        \\-/P\n         |. |/\n         |. |\n         ==\n        /  \\\n\nLuara- The spirit of the moon, often shown by the symbol of a pale, white wolf.\n\n        \\___(>\n         |===/\n         |    |\n\nRamakhet- Spirit of the desert, barren lands and sand. He is never seen, and therefore is rarely ever depicted as something other than his name. He has sworn to scour the earth of all life for all time.\n       ~~~~~\n      Ramakhet\n\nKrathol- The spirit of pain, suffering and starvation. Depicted as a pile of dry bones.\n   \n      (------)\n      (------)\n\nVeist- Spirit of illusion, tricks and thievery, depicted as a goblin with four eyes.\n\n      (:_:)\n      \\| |/\n       /\\\n       |  |\n\nFreygoth- Spirit of the wind and wild animals. He takes any form which he may desire. \n \n       ~~~~~\n        ~~~~\n         ~~~\n\nGlutros- The spirit of greed and obesity. He is depicted as a cake.\n   \n        , , , ,\n       |====|\n       |====|\n\nThulezia- Spirit of lust, pleasure and beauty, depicted as a naked slave girl. \n\n        (_)\n        |00|\n      ,/|   |\\,\n        !__!       \n       /   \\\n\nIsuz- Spirit of love, caring, and tranquility, depicted as an open-armed woman.\n\n       { . }\n       \\| |/\n         ||\n         ||\n\nOrgon- Spirit of Disease, Pestilence, and failure. Depicted as a festering, starving man with six arms, each holding a rusted and broken weapon.\n            (.)\n           |-||-|\n           i-||-i\n           !-||-!\n            /\\\n\nUrin- The spirit of rain and hail, depicted as a dark rain cloud.\n\n         *****\n       ********\n         *****\n         ` ` ` ` \n          ` ` `\n           ` ` `\n            ` `\n\nKesaroth- Spirit of envy and jealousy, usually shown as a golden bull.\n \n                 |__|\n                 ('')\n     /`-------\\/\n    / |         | |\n  '~  | |-----| |\n      ^^       ^^\n\nLeyd- Spirit of dominance and physical strength, symbolised by a closed fist.\n\n       ()()()\n        (   )\n         |**|\n         |**|\n\nScorthuz- The spirit of cleansing and purging, depicted as a vial of clear water.\n\n          (-)\n           | |\n         /--\\\n         |~~~|\n         |~~~|\n         ----\n\nTheruz- Spirit of intelligence and learning, shown as a wise old teacher. Brother to Betharuz.\n\n        ----\n       /     \\\n       | _  _ |\n     ('| O  O |`)\n       |  (.)  |\n       `/=.=\\'\n        \\/\\/\n\nBetharuz- Spirit of alcohol, cactus green and celebration, often depicted as a young dim man, in direct contrast to his brother, Theruz.\n\n       *, (.) U\n        \\_||_/\n           ||\n          /\\\n\nGentharuz- Spirit of smithing, smelting, industry and forging, depicted as a man with no legs, hammering an anvil.\n\n          (,)\n           ||--P\n         || ||   <==->\n         ||===| |==|\n         ||    || |++|\n\nDrelthok- Spirit of sleeping and dreams, often shown as a dark cloud.\n\n        %%%%%%\n       %%%%%%%\n        %%%%%%\n\nEathruz- Spirit of dawn and dusk, shown by the symbol of a red sun.\n\n       . .       . .\n       .\\       /.\n         \\\\ //\n         /|/\\|\\\n         \\|\\/|/\n         // \\\\\n      . /       \\ .\n      . .         . .\n\nKotrestruu- The spirit of memory and the recording of knowledge, depicted as an endless book.\n   \n       ______\n       ||=====/|\n       ||=====/|\n       ||=====/|\n       ||=====/|\n       ||=====/|\n       ||=====/\n\nLetrothak- The spirit of hindsight and excuses, shown as a goblin with eyes in the back of his head.\n\n        /----\\\n     \\\\| |  ||  | |//\n      \\,| (i)(i) |,/\n        \\      /\n         |      |\n       /        \\\n   __/ |", ""),
