        StaticBook("Citizen Record", "§bAstmar", "-------------------Citizens of Kal'Nikaer§0\n§0-------------------Ambrosia§0\n§0Nkruma Frostbeard§0\n§0Magnus Frostbeard§0\n§0Jorka§0\n§0Dul'Ulkirk§0\n§0Astmar§0\n§0Torvin Grandaxe§0\n§0Odin Ireheart§0\n§0Vidar Frostbeard§0\n§0Fimlin Grandaxe§0\n§0Huthgar\n\nDozor Grandaxe§0\n§0Tharggus Irongut§0\n§0Dangren Starbreaker§0\n§0Ulfric Goldhand§0\n§0Freyja Grandaxe§0\n§0Sylen§0\n§0Sharr Irongut§0\n§0Tepah Brinejaw§0\n§0Arundel Irongut§0\n§0Jorik Grandaxe§0\n§0Lathros§0\n§0Horim Irongut§0\n§0Oyvind Frostbeard\n\nBalek Irongut§0\n§0Tenshar Karkun§0\n§0Thorgrim Irongut§0\n§0Thorvald Frostbeard§0\n§0Moggeak Frostbeard§0\n§0Egil Brinejaw§0\n§0Tarax Brinejaw§0\n§0Svardin Grandaxe§0\n§0Mitchel Seregon§0\n§0Runi Ireheart§0\n§0Olaf Ireheart§0\n§0Kevay Ireheart§0\n§0Gardath Starbreaker\n\nTog Irongrinder§0\n§0Thoran Irongut§0\n§0-------------------Citizens as of 9th of The Grand Harvest, 1573", ""),
        StaticBook("1", "§bNemiisae's Acolyte", "I remember his sleeping face, peaceful but still locked in a grimace. He sought to have me banished from my home for something out of my control. Hopefully his soul was claimed by the aspects, and he will not return to haunt my life.\n\nI gripped my knife,\n\nand it slipped across his throat like butter left in the sun.  He choked, and the crimson liquid poured forth from the wound and bubbled with each failed breath.\n\nI feel... regret. Just a little.\n\n\nNemiisae's Acolyte", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Zaend's Journel§0\n§0\n§0\n§0I can still feel burns of the stave and the pains of the rock. I know not what the permanent damge is but I have concerns it may be great.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0 §0\n\nA great time has passed since I last wrote but I feel that I can see myself once more.§0\n§0\n§0Rejoined SS hope nothing is off.§0\n§0\n§0Found a great opportunity now by calculations you must remember -1972 -332 this may save you\n\nUhazaal has contacted me again. Time to make some alchemy ingredients.§0\n§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Theory of War", "§bTenaka Khan", "Classification of actual military types of maneuvers and their variations have long been a part of military science. New technology and weapons have not drastically altered some of the classical types of offencive maveuvers:\n\npenetration, envelopment, offencive-defenciv-e maneuvers and turning movements.\n\nThe penetration-one of the oldest maneuvers-is a main attack that attempts to pierce the enemy line while secondary attacks\n\nup and down the enemy line prevents the freeing of enemy reserves.\n\nThe envelopment is a maneuver in which a secondary attack attempts to hold the enemy's center while one(single envelopment) or both flanks(double\n\nenvelopment) of the enemy are attacked or overlapped in a push to the enemy's rear in order to threaten the enemy's communications and line of retreat. This forces the enemy to fight in several directions and possbily be\n\ndestroyed in position.\n\nDefencive-offenciv-e maneuvers include attack from a strong defencive positiuon after the attacking enemy has been sapped in stength or feigned withdrawals that attempt to lure the enemy out of\n\nposition.\n\nTurning maneuvers are indirect approaches that attempt to swing wide around an enemy flank to so threaten an enemt's supply and communication lines that the enemy is forced to abandon a strong position\n\nor be cut off and encircled.\n\nMore strategies include: Strong right flank, often known as rolling up the line-Strength would be concentrated on the right flank, which would attempt to break the enemy left flank, and\n\nthen \"Roll up the line\" attacking the enemy from the rear.\n\nThe Cannae tactic(weak centre): Centre left weak diliberately to invite enemy certre attack and envelopment. Though you\n\nrequire a tactical reserve behind an apparently weak centre.\n\n=====------=====\n\nSingle line defence or extended line: All deployed in a single line to overlap enemy flanks or meet wider enemy\n\nformation and protect own flanks\n\n---------------\n\nWedge formation:\nLines thinned to provide concentration in centre to smash through enemy lines(turn to next page for diagram)\n\n            -\n         ----\n      -------\n--------------\n\nAdvice and tips;\n\nA general should never put himself on the front line and should keep himself protected, if a general dies\n\nthe soldiers will face a lack of morale, this could in turn affect the course of the battle severly. Therefore a general should keep himself behind the front line unless in dire need, or in face of defeat.\n\nTry to use gorrila tactics to slow your enemy down, this may not be the most honourable option, though it will save lives in the long term.\n\nA general should protect his ranged milita and or siege equipment with his life, if ones\n\narchers fall, then you rely on your infantry and cavalry alone.\n\nThis concludes the Theory of War.\n\nWritten by Tenaka Khan.", ""),
        StaticBook("Vladovic Army", "§bCarleton Cassius", "The Vladovic Regiment\n\nBy Carleton Cassius\n\nThe Vladovic Regiment was formed by General Josef Vladov after the fall of The Order Of The Imperial Dragon and the The Brotherhood of Horen.\n\nAt they're peak they boasted over 20,000 troops most of them situating themselves In The Capital Of Oren Felsen guarding or in opposing Urguan.They protected The Emperor Of Oren and it's people to do this they went into large scale battles and skirms\n\nGeneral Josef Vladov directed the trench war for fort rhewenguard and Fort Khaz'Nogaak\nwhere he gained his popularity and proved effective in war but that quickly died down after his crushing defeat for Fort Khaz'Nogaak after the long campaign Urguan\n\nProved they could drive away the attacking forces of Oren after Orens succeseful long conquest in Urguan.\n\nI have also wrote up a diary.\n\nCarleton Cassius \n\nDay one. I volunteered to join up the vladovic Regiment. I was accepted they gave me duties to protect felsen and its people so I manned the walls and looked out for any bandits or enemies that could be of threat\n\nDay two. My friends and fellow troops are being sent to the front I can only pray that I am not conscripted to go there as I am unready and need much more practice. It has been a very exhausting day.\n\nDay three. I'm being sent to the front with over a quarter of the armed forces with me we marched from Felsen to the front where we where supplied with gear and weapons it stinks with rotting dead bodies and gunpowder. I pray every morning and every night\n\nthat I will not be one of the sorry bastards that have already lost there lives.\n\nDay four all the men would put on there tabards and get ready as I woke up looking to them confused one of my fellow troops woke me up pulling me out of my bed\n\nI quickly put on my tabard as with the other soldiers General Josef Vladov walked through the countless Vladovic Troops getting ontop a ladder unsheathing his sword and pointing it to the opposite side of the trenches where the dwarfs where.\n\nhe would shout a long and loud \"Imperial Armys of Oren Charge!\" \nI would fight for my lifes as the trebruches blew up the dwarfen lines I was a small dot on a massive full scale war I would watch my fellow comrades die as well as legionnares.\n\nDay Five The capture was succseful we swarmed around fort Rhewenguard drinking ale and wine we would cheer from dawn to dusk.\n\nThe Vladovic Regiment still lives\n\n-Carleton Cassius \n21st of the first seed 1539.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "*some basic drawings and sketches of tree's cover the page*e", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Day 1: I've never kept a journal but guess i'll start today§0\n§0\n§0I've been waiting on §0Mr.Falk§0 to return so i may continue learning §0alchemy.....its§0 so lonely without someone here§0\n§0\n§0I saw three people get slaughtered and corpses beheaded.§0\n\nI dont think ill be sleeping tonight well i probably will but there will be alot of nightmares but ill get over them.§0\n§0Still trying to find a good weapon or armor so i can actually hold my own.§0\n§0Guess ill still be looking for awhile\n\nDay 2§0\n§0\n§0Well i woke up my head was a bit foggy there is a blank in my mind for about 2 hours of yesterday§0\n§0It was weird but §0Mr.Falk§0 is finally back today not sure when he'll be home though§0\n§0Even if he is a wanted man he seems nice.\n\nDay 3.§0\n§0Well §0Mr.Falk§0 is dead§0\n§0I saw his head on a spike today§0\n§0I heard rumors of more deaths to come.§0\n§0\n§0I wish i was there§0\n§0I couldve stopped it§0\n§0or at least said goodbye§0\n§0\n§0I never got that chance\n\nDay 4. ive grown to call Silversteed house family§0\n§0Its nice though i do still miss mister falk may he rest in peace.§0\n§0\n§0Day 5, no im not wasteing paper so day 5 starts here.§0\n§0Me and Atturi ran into so of the \"rif raf\" but luckily no fighting accured.\n\nDay 6, I know this journal is boring for whooever reads it but hopefully there will be some exciteing things i can write about so.§0\n§0Day 7, i havent written in a while, so far i went to war and got promoted so far im th eonly member of the \"black guard\" so-\n\nfar.§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Poems Of A Tale", "§bEli Stevens", "I sit beside the fire and think of all That I have seen, of meadow-flowers and butterflies in summers that have been;§0\n§0\n§0Of yellow leaves and gossamer in autumns that there were, with morning mist and silver sun wind upon my hair\n\nI sit beside the fire and think of how the world will be when winter comes without a spring that I shall ever see.§0\n§0\n§0For still there are so many things that I have never seen: in every wood in every spring there is a different green.§0\n\nI sit beside the fire and think of people long ago, and people who will see a world that I shall never know.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n\n          The road§0\n§0The road goes ever on and on§0\n§0   Down from the door where it began. §0\n§0Now far ahead the road has gone, and I must follow, If I can,§0\n§0Pursuing it with eager feet.§0\n§0Until it joins some larger way. Where many paths and errands meet\n\n       Treasures§0\n§0All that is gold does not glitter....§0\n§0Not all those who wander are lost;§0\n§0The old that is strong doe not wither,§0\n§0Deep roots are not reached by frost. §0\n§0From ashes a fire shall be woken,§0\n§0A light from the shadow shall spring\n\nRenewed shall be blade that was broken, The crownless again shall be kind.w\n\n         Lord§0\n§0The lord of silver fountains,§0\n§0The king of carven stone,§0\n§0The king beneath the moutain shall come into his hold, §0\n§0and the bells shall ring in gladness,§0\n§0at the mountain king's return, But all shall fall in sadness, and the lake will.....\n\nshine and burn", ""),
