        StaticBook("Task Complete", "§bZerix Fury", "Elf 1: Mariline Malum is a elven red head, She is a harlot and enjoys travelling, I was meeting her at the docks and god is she a flirt. She has no place of residence and to no avail as she tried. She has a few talents like tailoring and singing and is\n\nslowly becoming obsessed with me, She has slowly been convinced to join the Warhawkes but to no avail has any attempt been succesful.§0\n§0\n§0Elf 2: Mia Winterleaf§0\n§0A spell caster elf with long golden hair and glasses, She is innocent and cute in her\n\noutter lookings and in first impressions. But dont be fooled by the exterior as this woman, When not busy with research on Racial Behaviour, She will fuck any man who she deems fit. She picks the right allies. The females intelligents is greater then most\n\nof the Warhawkes, She is a forced to be reckoned with and a deciever at heart.§0\n§0Place Of Residence: Sutica.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0~Zerix Fury", ""),
        StaticBook("Age of Multitude", "§bMind Druid Aeras", "The Age of§0\n§0Many Circles§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0The Third Revolution\n\nI, Aeras Ibar'ker, would first like to thank you for taking the time to read through this paper. I ask you to set aside all personal judgements, and to analyse the information contained within, with a clear consience.\n\nIn the following pages you might find ideas that according to your book might be controversial or straight out ridiculous, that is why I, on a last note, ask the reader's absolute discretion, and expect from them only constructive come back.\n\nBefore officially flowing into the thesis, I would like to define certain words that I consider essential to my idea. First of all, a word we as Druids use very often, Order. An Order would be a particular social or political system. Which means a set of\n\nthings working together as parts of a mechanism or an interconnecting network; a complex whole. §0\n§0\n§0From this we can draw the definition of another very essential word, Circle, which would correspond to one of the\n\nsub-sets assuring the well functioning of the whole, the Order.§0\n§0\n§0Without further ado,\n\nAll throughout the past, the Druidic order's has been fluctuating between conflict and solidarity. Splits and Unification, of what we then referred to as circles. As an example I shall take the equinox split in Anthos. After disagreeing heavily with the\n\nmain Druidic body in Anthos the Equinox Druid Gavin had decided to split off and create his own 'circle', which had its own ideas, its own teachings, its own hierarchy and its own rules. Therefore the word 'Circle' becomes rather dubious, since after\n\nchanging all those core mechanics, and thus forming an entirely different mechanism, we can't truly consider that this group was still part of the same Order. No, they were simply two different Orders who had a common goal, and were forced to interact.\n\nBut now, Druids have gotten a very negative view of splits, which I find unneeded. I do rather understand the negativity towards an Order split, such as the Equinox split, even though we as an Order learnt from that. Though a circle split could only be\n\nbeneficial for the Order and for those who seek to sustain it. A circle split would imply that we as an Order create several different mechanisms, woul could be auto-reliant, and make them function as a whole, so that the order might be\n\nstronger and bigger.§0\n§0\n§0And it is exactly that that I propose to you on this very day, the 18th of the deep cold 1580, to split up. §0\n§0\n§0To properly do so, the help of ever single Druid that feels that they are capable of contributing, is\n\nneeded. They shall venture to other cities and grow groves, teach and spread the ways of Druidism. It is very much like a spider's web. We started off with a very centralised web, but we can now pursue by expanding it, in order to catch as many flies as\n\npossible. Not only will this make it easier for the Order to sustain itself, but it will also be easier for the order to act in case of unbalance.§0\n§0\n§0Now, of course the role of the mother circle can not be neglected. She shall be there to ensure the\n\nfluid communication between all circles, and she shall be taking the role of moderator as she should. Much like an actual parent. It is understandable that some are afraid of us losing a 'family' but quite on the contrary§0\n§0this will force us all to\n\ncooperate and work together. And much like a real family, the children always leave the nest at one point or the other.§0\n§0\n\nSo it is for this, that I ask you all, for the bettering of our work, for the Green Mother and Father, to look at what you could contribute, where you could settle and what you could do to make a change.\n\nFor it is only through change that progress can be made.\n\nAeras Ibar'ker§0\n§0\n§0The Mind Druid§0\n§0", ""),
        StaticBook("The Acerbus cult", "§bToby Williams", "Current known information about the Acerbus's and their cult.\n\n-Follow the Aengul / Daemon Aerkiath\n\n-Wish destruction on Aeriel, Iblees, the Undead, and the Ascended.\n\n-Wish for the god Aerkiath to become the Arch-Aengul / Arch-Daemon\n\n-Have automatons that are capable of Arcane Magic, suggesting the possibility of bound Souls similar to Heial\n\n-The masks is the source of power and corruption, hijacking control of the soul and mind.\n\n-Have Prohpets similar to Hosper. Last known prophet was named Aazar. Condition unknown.\n\n-Almost excusively use electric magic, colored red due to their connection to Aerikath.\n\n-Are able to taint normal mortals, causing them to hear whispers that try and break them and bend them to Aerkiaths will\n\n-Have an insignia very similar to the Eye of Iblees.\n\n-Masks possess people, forcing themselves on their mind and souls, bending them to Aerkiaths will.\n\n-Masks can be destroyed by Holy Magic, Arcane Magic, and Physical trauma.\n\n-Individuals who were possessed but had their masked destroyed will often be on the brink of insanity.\n\n-Insanity can be reversed with a great deal of time.\n\n-Contact Toby Williams of the Ascended ((tnoy23)) if more questions are had than are answered here.", ""),
        StaticBook("Odd Events C1", "§bSofetios Jayamen", "Odd Events\n\nA Fictional book series with a bit of Horror\n\n           ~By Sofetios\n                Jayamen\n\nPrologue\n\nMy name is James Geedin. My family recently settled in a new land without a name, so I call it Genway.  We were lucky enough to stumble upon an old house.\n\nWhoever built it, I don’t know. Some odd stuff seems to happen here, but I’m determined to stay at my new home. This is my story.\n\n      Chapter One\n        The Light\n\nI woke up in the middle of the night with chills running down my spine. I was around 13 at the time. I went downstairs to get something to drink.\n\n That’s when I noticed it. I looked out the window and noticed a light in the distance at the woods. Though it wasn’t yellow like a fire, it was white. I thought about checking it out, but decided I should go to bed instead.\n\nThe next day in the morning, I went downstairs to have breakfast, but the thing was, my parents weren’t awake. That was unusual, so I went upstairs to their room and knocked on the door.\n\nWhen I knocked on the door it simply opened slowly from the force of my knock. I looked in, but no one was there. I spent the rest of the day looking for them, but to no avail.\n\nSoon it became nighttime and I was in the kitchen. That’s when I noticed it again, the same light as before. This time I went out towards the light. I came to the forest clearing where the light was coming from.\n\nThere was a small mirror in the center, angled towards my house. Then I noticed something, the white light wasn’t coming from the mirror, It was coming from the attic window of my house being reflected by the mirror.\n\nI saw a word carved into the mirror. It said “Truth”. I looked back towards the house. Could my parents be were that light is? I took the mirror and made my way back the house.\n\nI got to the house and made my way upstairs to look for a way up into the attic. I looked different places until I got to my parents room. I walked in and there was a small white light coming from the bookcase in there, going around the books.\n\nI walked up to the bookcase and looked through the cracks between the books. There was a white stairway that lead upwards.  I shifted the bookcase over and started walking up the white stairs. Until I got to a white trapdoor above me.\n\n cautiously, I lifted it up a crack and looked in the attic room.  There were two statues that looked just like…  I then opened the trapdoor fully and rushed into the white room towards the two statues.\n\n They were exact replicas of my parent, but they had faces looked like they were scared of something. Suddenly there was the sound of the trapdoor shutting behind me.\n\nI looked back to see something in white robes that covered its whole body and a light coming from under its hood. \n\n“Who are you?” I said scared. It simply stood there. I looked back towards my parents for a second and back again.\n\n Then it was right in front of me. Startled I fell back and the mirror dropped on the floor face up but didn’t break. I got up and backed up. It didn’t move.\n\n Then I noticed something. In the reflection on the mirror on the ground, where the thing was supposed to be was a person. The person in the reflection had light coming from its eyes.\n\nI took out my short sword. Getting ready to fight whatever this was. I lunged at its chest, but as it made contact with the light coming fromit, the blade turned white. I dropped my sword from it happening.\n\nI was about to panic when I remembered the mirror, then got an idea. Keeping my eyes on the person, I picked up the mirror, careful not to get in the light.\n\nThen with one hand, I slid it under the light coming from the person’s hood, trying to aim it back at it. Suddenly the light coming from under the hood disappeared. Then the person in the robes simply fell over, solid as a stone.\n\nI turned to the statues of my parents. I wasn’t sure what to do. I talked, I yelled, but there was no response. I had never felt so alone before. My parents turned into stone, not knowing how to turn them back to normal.\n\nBut then that made me realize something. Something I should have thought from the start. \n\nWho had left the mirror in the woods?\n\nEnd of Chapter One\n\nThank you for taking the time to read this! I'll be writing more in the future!\n\nIf you like my writing send me a bird or tell me in person!\n\n~Sofetios Jayamen\n((Sofetios))", ""),
        StaticBook("Nativitas", "§bShady_Tales", "There were no planes of existence. There was nothing. Just the Void. And a bright shining light. It was not a light we could see, it was not really white either,but it would be the only way to explain the existance of such a Deity in contrast to the\n\nemptiness of the Void. None knows why, how or when this Deity existed. It is, in-fact, heresy to speculate on such matters. The all knowing God was this Deity. Truly none can describe the majesty of the Creator, the one and only. The Merciful Creator of\n\nthe seven skies. With his intent and only his intent, the World of Aegis was created. All he had to do was simply want it to occur and it happened. THe rolling seas, the proud mountains and vast landscapes, all in a second, created by God. The World was\n\nnot created in play or for fun, but as a theater for the inhabitants of the World to be tested in. And tested for what?Well, that is for us to speculate. Though I believe it is to test us for purity, how  hard we can fight temptation, and how clean and\n\ngood our actions be. The first mortal being to be created was a man.This man was sculptured with clay and water, but left hollow. Soulless, God's creation lay there for the other immortal beings to see.The Aengul and the Daemon, the two spirits created\n\nbefore the mortal beings and before the creation of Aegis. Not much is known about these two spirit races, but hopefully in the future we may know more.God then blew his own breath of existance into the hollow shell  and the Man lived. God then took the\n\nman and put him in the centre of all of Aegis, the same spot where The Cloud Temple now stands. God also made the Man a partner, from the exact same clay and the exact same breath, she was the first Woman.These simple beings could not talk, nor talk, nor\n\ndid they know much about the World. They roamed the world, enjoying its pre-historic beauty. Untouched, the fresh glades and dark thick forests were a wonder to set eyes on. Soon they had four children in the four corners of Aegis. Malin was the first of\n\ntheir sons, born in the deep forests of Aegis, he had blonde hair and sharp ears. Standing tall, he was the father of the Elves of Aegis. Krug was born in the scorching deserts of Aegis, fierce and relentless, he was the father of the Orcs. In the fresh\n\nmeadows of Aegis was born Horen, father of Humans. And lastly, in the deep underground caves of the World, Urguan was born, master of the Dwarves.\nWe do not know how they fathered sons and how their lines continued but perhaps God created a partner for\n\neach Son to continue their lines? Soon the first Man and Woman created by God departed Aegis and climbed the seven skies to meet with God their creator, for they had achieved their goal. The Sons began to explore the World of Aegis and each was stricken\n\nwith grief at the loss of their parents, seeking to fill the chasm of emotion inside them they began to create civilisation.\nAlthough none of the descendants of each Son had neither their long lives or splendour, they did carry their forefathers looks\n\nand traits. The Elves with Malin at their head travelled the lands and began naming all the inhabitants of this world, they were the first to create a tongue and began to name the trees and grass, the mountains and valleys across all of Aegis. At this\n\ntime, Malin, Urguan, Krug and Horen were not far apart in looks. Horen and Krug had darker hair than the other two and Krug was a bit larger in build. Malin had blonde hair and Urguan had red. They were all close companions, friends and had much love for\n\neach other and each others people.Urguan travelled into the deep underground of the earth, naming the beautiful ores and gems, sharing it with his brethren. Krug travelled the harsh deserts, testing his stamina and strength against the environment of\n\nAegis, and Horen began building the first squalid huts and villages in the valleys. The people lived for hundreds of years, in harmony and peace.Until the day where one of the great Daemons, great worshipers and squalid protectors of the void, kin spirits\n\nto the Aengul, defected.Iblees, who was once the greatest of all of God’s worshippers, was cast down into the mortal world, and so he was about to destroy the tranquility of Aegis forever. He came in the shape of a man. A gentle being who loved things\n\ndelicate, he was quickly befriended by Malin, Urguan and Horen. Krug had a great distrust of him but after many years of being convinced by his brothers, he finally accepted his company.\nLittle did Iblees know that this was all part of the Great God's\n\nplan to test the descendants of Man and Woman. Iblees wanted to destroy everything that God had designed and created, still not in a powerful physical form he began sowing seeds of evil in the minds of the Descendants. Prying on their needs and lusts.\n\nTo Malin, lover of nature, he promised him many children. He promised him that their laughter would resonate across their forest homes and that he would be content.\n Malin did not want anything more in this world than a bountiful amount of young to occupy\n\nthe barren forests.To Urguan, he promised infinite wealth of Gems and Ores, colours and crystals he could never imagine. To this, Urguan’s greed failed him. Horen, was anxious he would not live long enough to see his city completed and his lands increased\n\nHe needed more time, and Iblees struck the chord and promised immortality. Krug was the last to be tricked, Iblees tempted him with wealth, with food, with power. None interested Krug. Iblees was furious, he then challenged Krug in open combat in fury.\n\nThe whole world witnessed Ibleeses transformation into a hideous beast of the void. His skin turned into scales, fangs erupted and dark horns exploded from his head. He grew large wings and began to breath terrible fire. All stood in shock and horror. The\n\nbeast terrified all inhabitants of Aegis, animals fled and the Sons of the Descendants were too weak of blood to stand in front of such evil fury. Only Malin, Urguan, Horen and Krug stood in front of the terror. In Iblees’ right hand, a sword wrought in\n\nflame. Krug, naked and unarmed charged at The Daemon, throwing himself against the scalding scales of Iblees. He screamed in agony as his skin burned and decayed, becoming green and molten. Iblees was knocked off his feet, for the last time.\n\nHe stood up, heaving in rage and fury, flames exploded from the pores of his skin, he roared in anger and where he struck his sword the land collapsed and the ground erupted. And Lo, great was the Valour of Urguan and the strength of Krug as they fought\n\nthe beast.Powerful were the arms that carried Krug’s Axe and strong was Horens’ heart as they fought in open combat upon the plains of Aegis. Malin’s sword was fast and swift, smiting Iblees upon his breast and sides.For the thirty years the Descendants\n\nfought Iblees, the world became a war torn mess. The dead were defiled, summoned from their graves to follow Iblees’ mastery. The more mortal descendants died, the greater Iblees’ armys grew. It was a sad chapter in the World of Aegis, the brothers threw\n\nup their hands to God in prayer and in agony. Their creations destroyed, their children massacred. Woe to the Sons of Man and Woman. Krug grew bitter, his resentment of his brothers increased for befriending such a beast.Urguan grew greedy, he fought\n\nvalourously but began to hide his treasures underground. Malin feared for the lives of his children and did not leave his forest sanctuary. It seemed the world was destined for ruin. Iblees grew in strength and the Descendants weakened. Until one day. One\n\nday where the sound of horns could be heard from the far east. Beautiful horns echoing all across the skies of Aegis. God had heard their prayers. An army of Aengul and Daemons from the seven skies had appeared on the grand shores of Aegis. Their majesty\n\nand beauty so strong that all The Descendants could see was a flash of power white light erupt from the east. Only Malin with his strong sight could see the figures of light as they sped across the skies towards the armies of Iblees.\nIblees' soldiers\n\nburned where they stood, The thousands of skeletons and cadavers burst aflame and his living servants fled. There in the right middle of the world, he was cast down and chained by the Aengul and Daemon. A robed figure with brown hair and a black wreathed\n\napparation stood before him. They were a terrible image to look at, all shyed down and bowed in their majesty and glory. They stood before Iblees, knowing he was immortal and could not be killed, sentencing him to banishment to the void where his dark\n\nsoul would be forever trapped in torment. But..Before they could complete the sentence, Iblees stood tall for one last time. “You believe you may simply banish me from this plane and that my taint shall not last? I have touched this world with evil and it\n\nshall forever be part of the souls that inhabit it. Malin, I find no need to curse you, for so many of your kind have already willingly submitted to me now and will on my return in the distant future. The curse you will bear, is not of my doing, but of\n\nyour own. Even you have done my work, if you realize it or not.Urguan, your greed and lust shall overcome you, you are not worthy of the height God gave you, your descendants shall be short, squalid and ugly. You will always seek to find Gold and Gems in\n\nthe deep underground of the earth, your hunger never satisfied. Horen, the immortality you hope for will never arrive. Your longevity has already been stripped away thanks to the labors of the twisted heart of your brother Malin. You will age quickly and\n\ndie before you ever taste the fruits of your pointless labors. And you Krug, the most hated of the Descendants, you shall always have the lust of war. You are strong? Well the strength shall be used against your brothers, used to pillage and murder! Your\n\nlust for battle shall be unsatiated and your descendants shall grow ugly and heartless.\"As soon as his words were uttered, the world grew suddenly dark. A great roar erupted from Iblees’ mouth and in a blast of fire he was banished from the Mortal World.\n\nThe Descendants stood still for several moments, pondering over the words of Iblees. Malin, Krug, Urguan and Horen all knew naught of what the great Devil had spoken of when concerning Malin’s betrayal. Dismissing it as the lies of a demon propagated to\n\ncorrupt their souls, the brothers thought nothing further of Malin’s supposed treason. The robed figure stood before the four brothers. \"There is nothing in my power that may undo what that evil did. There is one thing I may do however, and that is to\n\nbless you. Malin, may your forests be a sanctuary of peace and your children long lived. Urguan, may your descendants be hardy, strong hearted and strong of mind. Krug, may your people show valour and honour where none exist. And Horen, may your people\n\none day explore the Seven Skies. I can do no more, for all my power is spent. We will go back to our master now, I believe your children may see us once more but long in the future.\" And with that, the great host of Aenguls and Daemons disappeared into\n\nthin wisps in the air.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Bards Ellis", "§bDread Knight Verin", "The Bards\n              Of \n             Ellis \n\n\n\nBy Verin Etitlan\n    Edemah Etitlan\n    Eiheiu Darky\n\n\"There once was a bard,\nDashing and daring,\nThe queens pants he did start to mangle, and they found him, and threw him to shambles.\n\nOut on the floor, cold as ice, his hair scratched and withered like lice --\n\nThat lonely bard, he did song. Of a place to the east, where no men could ying.\n\nThe druids, his home he did fine, and once more did this lonely bard find; \n\nHe took the archdruids pants and threw them a mangle,--\n\nAnd there they found him, and threw him to shambles!\"\n- Verin Etitlan.\n   Kalos/Anthos\n\nThe Will of God:\n\"The man looked down in fond reminiscance at the man he once knew. His dagger upraised in firm defiance, astrew its' blades handle, and he spoke, like the angry vassal of the messiah. \"You. Are. Done.\" The blade plunged down, slamming int\n\no the mans heart, and the ether came for him.\"\n  Edemah Etitlan\n     Kalos\n\nThe End:\n\"The armored man looked down to his creation, to its' mangled body. Its' child of any other, and it worked. Its' firm machinations elliciting no response, the ether calling out, trying as it would to grasp the man, to give him the end..unable.\n\nHe became his son, in all but name. His father his lord, forever in vein. His own son gone, lost to the ether he hoped for each day, he wishes he could go there, one day.\"\n   Unknown.\n     Anthos.", ""),
        StaticBook("A life..........", "§bLurk", "His body lay there with his guts torn out, I stand at the back watching our leader as he tears bits of his skin off and eats them.\n\nHe pulled out a slimy liver of the man and slurped it down his throat!\n\n\"T'ats what yer get fer tryin' ter assassinate me'h yer focks\"\nhe said with bits of kidney spewing out his mouth!\n\"A'h loike ter eat me hostages alive,\" he smiled a creepy grin.\n\n\"He chewed into the mans face tearing away the muscle and cheek bones.\nThe man screamed for his life, his voice boomed over the forest.\n\nOur leader dug his nails into his face ripping it open a bit more, He started to swallow the flesh until we heard footsteps nearby.\nThe leader rubbed some blood over his chest and pretended to be dead, the rest of us fled behind the trees.\n\n Orcs came out grunting, \"Oooh look at t'at we got ourselves a'h dinner.\"\nI took my bow off my back and aimed it at one of the Orcs, I slowly put the arrow on and Fired at the Orcs head.\n\nThe orc fell down with a loud slam.\nThe rest of us jumped out killing the other 2 Orcs.\nOur leader got up and thanked me then kicked the Orcs bodies to see if they were really dead.\n\nWe walked back to Petrus and our leader went into the Tavern, his blood stained outfit caused some curiosity, so people were\nasking if he was stabbed.\n\nHe didn't reply to none of them who asked, but instead slurped his Ale, I guess to get the taste of Internal Organs out of his\nmouth.\nI wandered out of Petrus and headed to the streets to the Temple.\n\nA man named Arthur stopped me and guided me into his Tavern, owned by Vinnie The Chef.\n I brought a couple of Ale's and stayed there writing, until I noticed a little girl\nwalk through.\n\nI decided to make a joke \"Yer 'ere fer Ale?\" I said, unfortunatley the father didn't take it Swell he told to the daughter to go\nplay outside onto the porch.\n\nHe started to get angry so before he could punch me I decided to punch him straight in the nose, blood dripped down from nostrils\nas he stood there holding it, tilting his head back.\n\nHe told me to get outside so I withdrawed my sword and was ready for a fight.\nI looked at him angrily, A women poked me with her sword and I can't remember much after that apart from he put his hands onto my neck behind me.\n\nArthur told me the story later on.\nI decided to walk back to Petrus and go to my Leader, but 6 Elves stopped me they wanted my swords, my bow and everything I had\nin my bag.\n\nLuckily for me, my group wasn't far behind the Elves and they came out of the trees chopping off the Elves heads, blood squirted\neverywhere.\n((Okay that is the first part of my Journal I will make the second one soon))", ""),
        StaticBook("Lilly", "§bCaelria", "A small and beautiful lilly with lush, white petals and a vibrant green stem, seemingly plucked perfectly from the ground.\n\nThe lilly does not require water or sunlight, and will not wilt underground due to the series of enchantments residing within it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ways2DealWImpure", "§b[Ghost] The Eternal Librarian", "Liberals,\n  Dissidents and\n   the Impure:\n The Ways to Deal        with Them\n    Accordingly\n\n      by Nelecar\n\n       Foreword\nAs steadfast upholders of the mali’aheral ways, we must recognize the threats caused by these three subgroups to our blessed way of life. There are key differences between them, and factors about them vital for\n\nthe average citizen of Haelun’or to know - in this text, I do so hope to explain such.\n\n   Chapter One:\n      Liberals \nA liberal is a fellow Mali’aheral such as you or I who has fallen prey to the hedonistic and frivolous ways of the wood elves. They believe incorrectly and immaturely that we as a whole are wrong and they are\n\nthat our discrimination has ‘no basis’ and we should be equals with the vile orcs.\n\nThey are blatantly wrong in this regard; if you see or think you may have had any knowledge of a liberal, report it to the officials as soon as possible.\n\nFrom my studies and research, I have recognized that there are two main subgroups inside the liberal circle. These are:\n\nThe Dormant Liberal\nDormant Liberals disagree with our ideals, however they do not plan on taking\n\naction against them currently, and remain very silent about their opinions. While they may not seem to be, they can be potential threats to the government and the Mali’aheral way of life. They are essentially a seed stage, and dormant liberals can\n\nprogress into volatile liberals.\n\nThe Volatile Liberal\nThe volatile liberal disagrees with our ideals, and takes or plans to take action (albeit from the shadows) against them.  They try to recruit others to their cause subtly. While they a\n\nmuch more dangerous, they are far less subtle than dormant liberals are- dormant liberals, of course, keeping their opinions entirely to themselves.\n\nLiberals are perhaps the hardest of all to quell, and their punishment varies on severity, howev\n\nideal course of events is to have an agent identify the liberal and zone in on him. A warning will be given most of the time, however in extreme cases (such as a desire to overthrow the government) a more permanent measure will be needed.\n\n   Chapter Two:\n     Dissidents\nThey are always sympathizers of the lesser races.\n\nDissidents tend to be easier to deal with in most cases - however sometimes they take refuge in other nations, particularly in nations where free\n\nspeech is permitted. In these cases they may be protected by law. The appropriate punishment is imprisonment (as exile wouldn’t work due to the previous statement), however in medium-to-high cases execution may be needed to prevent further offenses.\n\n  Chapter Three:\n    The Impure\nPerhaps the most heinous of the three groups is the unclean. An impure is one born of a Mali’aheral and a non-mali’aheral. Breeding with a member of the lesser races is perhaps the worst crime in our society,\n\nsurpassing murder and thievery. They are often belligerent, troublesome, and corrupt, and would see us in ruin. They have many supporters despite their nature. Exile is the appropriate punishment for being an unclean and having intimate relations with\n\na non-Mali’aheral, whereas execution is the appropriate punishment for procreating with one.", ""),
        StaticBook("On Mali'Aheral", "§bJistuma", "The Mali’Aheral, the blessed elves. Or as others call them: High elves.\n\nThis elven people is one of the most hated by their own race. People see them as racists and don’t think they’ll do any good. They kill members of their own race, for they are ‘impure’. However is this true?\n\nI say not.\n\nThe culture of the Mali’Aheral goes back to a specific elf known as Larihei lomahnih. She was one of elven kind who bathed in water that contained enchanted golden\n\nParticles, which had changed their appearance. Her elven kind had a paler skin and longer ears than the other elven kinds. They were also taller and their hair had become fiarer.\n\nThe change that these particles had made to them also was psychological, these early Mali’aheral had shifted away from their original beliefs and thought more logical.\n\nThey became scolars, one of which was Larihei.\nAs a child of her kin she learned their traditions and ideals. And soon she appeared to be a master in all subjects a Mali’Aheral was expected to learn. She grew up to become\n\nthe leader  of the Mali’Aheral and to be their support in the council of princes in Malinor. However she promoted the Mali’Aheral’s believes in the council: That elves were the superior race of Aegis and that they should also rule the other races.\n\nHowever the other princes and princesses said that she was only promoting war and was a danger to the elves. Larihei was banished from Malinor.\n\nHalf of the Mali’Aheral followed Larihei when she went to find a new home for their race. The other half remained with Malinor, slowly losing their culture. However when those high elves found the ruins of their kin in Asulon, the old culture was revived.\n\nMaehr’sae Hiylun’ehya That is the core of the Mali’Aheral culture. It can be translated as “Progress and Heath”.\nBreaking that sentence down, you can split it up in two parts: Maehr’sae, or Progress and Hiylun’ehya, or Heath.\n\nMaehr’sae refers to the development of knowledge and the value of it. It is the base of the position of science in their society, as scientist stand in a high position die to their ability to recover truth and knowledge.\n\nHiylun’ehya stands for the heath and purity of the Mali’Aheral race. They wish to keep their race from mixing blood, because they believe that their body is the perfect design. A Mali’Aheral is not to ruin his body, he shall not damage it in any way.\n\nThis means that he or she will not tattoo nor scar their Body out of free will. They are also not to mix blood with other races, because they produce children who are not ‘perfect’ anymore. This includes intimate contact with other races, because they\n\nthey would risk creating a ‘failure’, a child of mixed blood.\nAnother important part of their culture is that they believe to be superior to other races, die to them able to think clear because they do not follow any god.\n\nThey frown down upon the religions of other races, however they respect those who show to be wise and able to think logical.\n\nCombat is another thing that is frowned down upon, as it is an action that does not require thinking and will only cause the loss of people. That last one is very important: The Mali’Aheral are, of course also subject to the curse of Malin's children,\n\ntherefor all lives are valued high and loss of one is a waste. It is therefore also expected of all Mali’Aheral to create children at some point in their life.\n\nThe Mali’Aheral frown down upon those of mixed blood, they moght discriminate them, they are not violent however. Their only violent people are the sillumir, the mourning blades, they are the Mali who give their sacrifice to the race by taking up the\n\nsword. Their name comes from the need for them to fight, a sad thing to do in their society. They are respected for their sacrifice and remain few in number, due to the morals of their race. A Mali’Aheral does not fight unless necessary.\n\nI hope this has enlighted you about the Mali’Aheral.\n\nThink about this next time you see them, and try to understand their actions.\n\nMaehr’sae Hiylin’eyha\n\n -Vallel’Yuln Aeléyèlsa\n\nOn Mali’Aheral\n\nWritten by Vallel’Yuln\nCopied by Rosso\nVaerHaven", ""),
        StaticBook("The Great War", "§bShroom Druid Milo", "The Myth of the Great          ~* War *~\n\nThousands of years ago, a terrible war broke out between the two mighty guilds of wizards - one good and one evil - that controlled great empires. Wizards on both sides vowed to fight until they were\n\nutterly triumphant, seeking to purge their rivals from the earth. With fearsome magic and dragon armies they battled for centuries, neither side winning a final victory.\n\nIn the process of their warfare, the wizards wrought vast devestation on the\n\nworld. Forests caught fire and blazed til gone, islands sank into the sea, and entire races became extinct. Eventually, the great goddess of Nature awakened from her sleep to witness the savage conflict. Shocked by the destruction, the goddess sent a\n\nvision to a single human; the woman who would become the first Grand Druid. Through the vision, this chosen figure saw that she must found a Druidic Order to preserve the fragile remains of her world's ecology. With the guidance of her Goddess, the order\n\ngrew in strength until it finally had the power to intervene in the wizards' war. The force of young druids pooled their powers and together vanquished the members of both battling guilds, transforming the combatants into innocent wild beasts.\n\nOnce the former wizards - now unable to fathom the concept of good versus evil - slithered, bounded, loped, and crawled off into their ruined habitats, the order began to heal the world. Since then, the Druidic Order continually works to prevent such\n\ndestruction from ever occurring again. Druids pledge to make sure the wards of good and evil no longer mar the precious earth. But, the order also has bitter enemies in the ancient remnants of the guilds of warring wizards; those good and evil mages who\n\nluckily escaped the fate of their fellows. Each guild claims it had been on the verge of victory and would have won, had druids not interfered.\n\nAs recounted by Hierophant Pulver, Master of Dungeons.", ""),
        StaticBook("Hydromancy Tome", "§bAdorellan", "Water \nWater seems to be one of the most simplest elements that inhabit our world, but it is in fact imcomprehensively more complex than most people think. it is. To fully understand it, one must practice\n\namounts of time meditating, and indeed spending their time around said element- be it by lounging around a pond, or studying its properties profusely in laboratories. Water is a necessity of life, needed by all living things.\n\nFor example, Humans, Orcs, Dwarves, Kharajyr, Elves and also various other animals or plants. Water, also appearing as such a calm element, is also one of the more dangerous; out in the seas, a storm cane take ot\n\na fleet of ships in moments. One can never truly control water that isn’t evocated, unless of course one is a shaman- In which case the Spirit controls the element and inadvertently the shaman controls the water too.\n\nDespite our best attempts, we are all mortal; we do not live forever, nor do we have amazing power like the ascended or the undead back in Aegis. As said before, water can be a very dangerous element; a single flood can\n\nwipe out a village just as easily as it might cause it to flourish. The element water contains raw power; a power that all Hydromancer’s would wish to weild. A Hydromancer’s training consists of learning about the void, being able\n\nto evocate from it, and learning about their element so they can properly evocate it. It takes years on end to learn about evocating a single element. Water which has been evocated may appear to be the same as the water\n\nwe have around us, however, it is completely different. The water that us Hydromancers evocate can only be created in the void and can be brought forth into this world by ourselves. Mana, or life-force, is the\n\npower we use to create and transport water from the void, and is vital in most, if not every known magic. If one uses too much of this mana, then they would simply fall unconscious or even die before they complete\n\ntheir task due to overuse or too much exerted force after large amounts of dedication and training; such as learning about the void and Hydromancy, and shaping and creating\n\ntheir mana into an interpretation of water. The connection to the void is rather difficult to explain, however; though once one has learnt about Hydromancy tself then they should be able to understand where\n\nwe are coming from. One’s connection to the void is more of a sensation than something that can be explained- Like feeling happy, or in love. As a mage’s training progresses, connecting to the void and evocating elements becomes\n\na simpler task. As one would possibly notice, many mages use a staff when they’re casting their magic- This however, is not necessary at all, and only aids the magician by giving them something to  focus on while evocating.\n\nWater can be evocated in various forms, such as a jet of water, an orb of water, an orb of ice, and other things I have not generally experimented on yet. Hydromancers which have been learning for a long\n\ntime will be able to use more things and will be able to use more things and wll be able to completely different aspects of the element. Ice is more suitable for offence in a battle, rather than defence, however, generally  water\n\nevocating itself is more useful to protect the caster as walls of water or ice can be willed to block a projectile or a strike, or simply to\nintercept and deflect one, though such must be done at short distance.\nIce that we evoke\n\nisn’t the same that we find in our world naturally; it cannot be melted by the heat of the sun or a torch, but it can be melted with the use of Pyromancy. To break the ice, the Hydromancy must both lose connection to the void and have\n\ntheir creation dissipate, or have a Pyromancer melt it with their fire, or, in the later stages of their training, with steam.\n\nWater, being able to form any conceivable shape, is only limited to the caster’s imagination and fatigue, and with proper training it can be suited for any purpose.", ""),
        StaticBook("My apologizes", "§bGlee", "*The letter is written a neat elven male cursive.*\n\nDear Lanavia,\n\nI do apologize. I really do. Sometimes I don't know what comes over me. And when I think about it, you're right. My ways have been lost and have been for some time. *The paper flips over*\n\nAs you know, I am old, even for a mali. And my wisdom is meant to great in comparsion to others. But I am blinded and choose to mask that problem though my acts of foolishness and confusing it with my normal happy attitude. *You flip to next page*\n\nPerhaps it is a combination of things that blind me. One being I have almost no sense of purpose or being. I have been lost in that regard. With no light in front of me, only darkness as a friend. Which would bring me to my next point. *Flip to back*\n\nI am lonely, in many senses of the word. You remember that day back in Skyfall with that paper I hold dearly onto. They were one of my last true friends. And now, I have people who do not wish to be my friend or lack in the friendship. *Page goes to next*\n\nIt is a sad state in deed. Though not as bad in terms of love and endearment. You know, a partner whom may stick with me through it all. The thick and the thin. It's been too long.... since I felt that warmth. *Flips over to the back side*\n\nSo, in the end I guess you could describe my condition as depressed. And I mask it with happiness. I do not deserve the name Glee. Maybe I should be called Depressed or Tears... Probably Tears because it sounds better. *You flip to next page*\n\nAnyhow, I hope you forgive me dear friend as I do not want to lose you. You one of the few I have. Please, please forgive me.\n*At the bottom lays a formal signature*\n\n       Your dearest friend,                  -Glee", ""),
        StaticBook("Task Complete", "§bZerix Fury", "Task: Find Magic Casters who may be convinced to join the Warhawkes!§0\n§0\n§0Mars Hoppus: Human, Previous Orener, Looking to get rid of the Human Curse casted by Iblees a long time ago. I have not seen example of his magic. Yet I imagine he can cast magic due\n\nto his aestetic.", ""),
