        StaticBook("Old Man's Dream", "§bMerekM", "'There once was a dream,\nIn this man's heart,\nThat life was never sullied,\nInstead was cherished,\nWould not be perished,\nAnd brought to eternal flame.'\n\n\n'A keep they built,\nSo it was felt,\nA burden they all could carry,\nBut darkness fell,\nIt did compel,\nA burden for none to bury.'\n\n\n'New burden made,\nSo lightness fade,\nAnd the man was who to blame.'\n\n\n\n\n-Poem rewritten by Merek Moonstrike. Original creator: Gladius Moonstrike.", ""),
        StaticBook("Red Rose Day", "§bThe Eternal Library", "Red Rose Day\n\nBy Unknown\n\nRed Rose Day is a celebration of affection towards a special someone in your life As signified by its name, participation simply dictates that you five a Red Rose to a person of significant importance, whether it be a sign of love, or a simple greeting to\n\na dear friend. It is one of the most commonly celebrated occasion. Humans, Elves and Kharajyr are most likely to participate in these festivities, while many Dwarves prefer to give gifts such as ale.", ""),
        StaticBook("Defunct Writing.", "§bThe Scribe.", "Why Poetry is Defunct.\n\nPoetry is the most useless form of writing. It seeks to convey a message in the form of a both a riddle and a rhyme. This is highly inefficient, as the message is deluded by the ornamentation used to create it in the\n\nfirst place. How can the message originally intended to be read keep its integrity when it is laden with unnecessary words that mean to weave into song? \n\nA song is perhaps a poem, but it is a preformance,\n\nnot an arrogant rendition of a message that is to be translated. Songs are set to music, and are designed to be entertainment, but poetry is just mindless babble with no point.\n\nA painting and a paper are very much comparable. Both try to convey a point or image, and do so by being as detailed and well set up as possible. However, a painting is not layed upon another painting, and then glued together with interweaving locks.\n\nThis would be the pinnacle of madness. This is what poetry is to sensible writing.\n\nPoetry is defunct.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Jayan C2", "§bSofetios Jayamen", "The Jayan\n\nA fictional adventure series.\n\n           ~By Sofetios\n                 Jayamen\n\n      Chapter Two\n         The King\n\nWe were approaching Northenway’s front gates. It appeared to be a very large city looking from the outside. As soon as the guards spotted us they came running.\n\nWhen they got to us, one of them said, “Lord Jedway! What happened to you? You’ve been missing for a week!” Henry raised a hand and said, \n\n“I was kidnapped by two bandits, and this young man saved me.”\n\nHe pointed to me. The guards looked at me and seemed a bit unbelieving, but then said, \n\n“Well its good you are back, you had better get back in the city. It isn’t safe out here.”\n\nThe guards led us in the city, I was amazed at the size of the city. I had never been in one so big, at least I didn’t think I had. We passed people in tents and damaged buildings and went through another gate inside the city.\n\nThrough this gate there was much nicer housing and no tents. After a bit longer we passed through yet another gate. Here there were large houses and manors, and finally went through one last gate.\n\nOn the other side of this gate was a path that led to a castle. It troubled me that the first part we went through as in such poor condition. When we got to the castle, the guards opened the doors.\n\nWe were led  up to the throne room, I stayed behind Henry, not sure what to expect.  At the front was what appeared to be the queen, the king, and a prince. When we got to the throne, the king stood up and went to Henry.\n\n He said in a stern voice, “Henry, where have you been! The castle has been in dismay without you around.” Henry looked at the king and said,\n\n“My coach was attacked by bandits on my way to Sadzten. I was held captive for a week. I wouldn’t be here right now if it wasn’t for my friend here.” He got out of the way and pointed to me.\n\nAs soon as he got out of the way the queen looked at me and her mouth slowly dropped and she got up. The prince looked at me with strange eyes. The king said,\n\n“Well thank you very much young man for your se-“\n\nAll of the sudden,  the queen was at the kings side. The king turned to her and said “Sofia, is everything all right?” The queen looked at me with strange eyes and said, \n\n“I’m sorry… It’s just he looks so much like…”\n\nhe king raised a brow then looked at me. Suddenly a expression of shock came over his face. \n\n“Boy what is your name?” I said,\n\n“James… Clark?” As if I was unsure if it was true, which I was coincidently.\n\n“Its just, you have the same eyes, hair, and face as our lost son who disappeared five years ago…” said the king. “Does the name Cire mean anything to you?” Right as he said the name I felt a large pulse in my head.\n\nI fell to the floor in pain as I yelled. “ARG!” The queen and Henry stepped back, but the king did not. He said under his breath. “My word, that cult must have…” The King knelt down to me. A guard said,\n\n“My Lord, get away from him, he may be dangerous!” \n\nThe King looked up to the guard and said,\n\n“You fool, this… this is my son.”\n\nThe king said to me, “Cire.” My head throbbed hard again at the name. “Look at me.” I forced myself to look at him. I found myself recognizing him and not recognizing him at the same time. It made my head hurt worse.\n\nI think the king saw the recognition in my face and stood up and said, “Get my son to a bed, and get a doctor!” Two guards came up and helped support me as I tried to stand up.\n\nThey half helped half carried me to  a room and I laid on the bed clutching my head. After a few minutes my vision was hazy and I wasn’t hearing right. I think I saw a old, rich looking man came in the room with the king.\n\nThe old man said, “This had better be important, I was just having tea!” The old man looked to me and said. “So what is wrong with him?” The king closed the door and said,\n\n“The Arimo cult.”\n\nThe old man jumped back and said in a hushed tone.\n\n“What!? Are you sure he’s even stable enough to be around? And how did he escape?” The king just said,\n\n“You need to counter act the drug.”\n\n I thought, how did the king know about the drug? The old man said,\n\n“You think I even know where to begin? The complexity that I’ve heard is in that drug is incomprehensible, even to me. your better off putting him down.”\n\nThe king angrily responded,\n\n“This is my son you fool! I would rather die than do that.”  The old man shook his head.\n\n “ Look, I wouldn’t know where to start.”\n\nThe old man seemed to get something out of a small pouch he carried. “Put this powder in water and have him drink it, It’s an all around cure I’ve been working on. Though I doubt it will counter act the drug.”\n\nThe King grunted in frustration and said,\n\n“Fine. Thank you, you are no longer needed.” The old man then turned and went to the door, looked at me one last time, and left.\n\nThe king left the room and after a moment came back in with a mug and an empty pouch. By now I was starting to lose conciseness. The King held my head up and I barely made out him saying the word “Drink”\n\nI drank the water slowly but surely, at the end the king let my head down and everything went black.\n\nEnd of Chapter Two\n\nThank you for taking the time to read this book! I will be writing more in the future!\n\nIf you like my writing, please let me know in person or by bird!\n\n~Sofetios Jayamen", ""),
        StaticBook("Untitled", "§bRuth", "I've found it. I've found the ruin. Something is in there, its in the library! I'm going down furth\n\n*The letter is scorched beyond this point. The writing was made in a hurry. A manuscript is stapled to the back of the note.*\n\nImperial Manuscript, mandated by the new Lord Kaldor Wicce. The note was found near the ruin of Azgoth, the Arith Keep. A dead bird was found near the note with intentions to fly to our aviary. Further investigation pending.", ""),
        StaticBook("Our Purity", "§bIaria Elervathar", "The Prominence\n          Of Purity\n\nA special thanks to:\n\nMy maln and haelun,\n\nIatrilemar and Ariana Elervathar\n\nMy tutors and lliran,\n\nAcaele Lazul and Nyna Norval\n\nIntrocution:\n\nKarin’ayla everyone. Although you are probably moreso interested in the topic regarding purity, I cannot let you escape this brief introduction. My name is Iaria Elervathar, malii’lari ito Iatrilemar eyha Ariana Elervathar.\n\nI was both raised and lectured in The Silver City of Axios, eager to learn more about our desire for purity and the maehr’sae hiylun’ehya. Albeit I have yet much to learn, I consider myself quite adept in the ways of our culture regarding our most --\n\npriced possession, our purity. I wish to lecture you further upon the matter, or merely give more knowledge for you to enjoy.\n\nChapter 1:\nPurity\n\nPurity comes in many different ways. You have physical purity, but also mental purity. Both are priced possessions that us, the Mali’thill, would not want to trade for anything in the world.\n\n Our purity is defined by how closely we follow the maehr'sae hiylun'ehya. an ancient phrase that the Mali'thill have carried for centuries from the old books originally left in the College of Haelun’or. It roughly translates to --\n\n\"The pursuit of wisdom and health\".\n\nNow let me explain to you, dearest reader, what mental and physical purity actually means.\n\n--\n\nPhysical Purity:\n\nA matter regarding your lineage and appearance. We cannot take you seriously if you’re a mixed breed. Your maln and haelun, both probably mentally ill, had the sick idea of pursuing a romance that spits onto the work --\n\n that us, the Mali’thill, have protected and worked on for centuries. You are certainly not welcome in our blessed city.\n\nMental Purity:\n\nThis involves moreso your determination to the maehr’sae hiylun’ehya. --\n\nYou may look pure and come from a Mali’thill lineage, yet that does not necessarily mean that you’re the face of purity. It’s about your personal demeanour. If anything of the maehr’sae hiylun’ehya is violated by you, we consider you as mentally impure. -\n\nYou’re in luck however, since we grant you the courtesy of being lectured again by one of our blessed Mali’thill. You’re welcome, impuritan.\n\nChapter 2:\nMaehr'sae Hiylun'ehya\n\nNow that I’ve explained the matter of purity to you, dear reader, I must certainly inform you about the maehr’sae hiylun’ehya I’ve been writing about. --\n\nAs I’ve mentioned before, this ancient phrase in the Elven tongue is roughly translated to \"Wisdom and health\". Wisdom, and health. Both factors we value dearly. Let me thoroughly explain to you these two factors.\n\n--\n\nMaehr'sae \n(Work/Progress)\n\nThis refers to our expanded development of our knowledge and wisdom that we gain throughout our years in life. The life of a Mali’thill must be commonly filled with the eager to learn and gain more --\n\nknowledge and wisdom. This revolves around the topics of science, arts or magic.\n\nHiylun\n(Health)\n\nThis regards our purity, both physically and mentally. It is important for us to hold dignity --\n\nin our lineage and physical appearance, as we are blessed with this glorious race that stands above all. I myself am very proud of my heritage, especially about the prestations of both my maln and haelun.\n\nChapter 3:\nPurity, why is it so important?\n\nAs my last chapter, I’d like to explain why we value the maehr’sae hiylun’ehya and our purity so much. That our life can be determined from these two factors may seem absurd to you, --\n\nbut then again you may obviously still not understand after reading this tome.\n\nWe are proud of what we are. Yes- again, absurd to you perhaps. We do not wish to taint this work we’ve been providing for over centuries now, --\n\nespecially not with impuritans and mentally ill parents who provide us with mixed breeds. We presumably have more knowledge than any other race existant due to our years of experience and the information we are granted from our unique Eternal library. --\n\nI personally pity you, although not all living mortal could be like the Mali’thill.", ""),
        StaticBook("On \"Racism\"", "§b[Ghost] The Eternal Librarian", "On \"Racism\"\n\n   by Lucion Sullas\n\nDuring my initial days of Haelun'or, I took great care in writing a treatise upon the more common questions critical of Mali'aheral society. This book contained rebuttals to these questions for the sake of education, and the sake of the ignorant\n\npeoples beyond our community. This is a reprint of sorts (though not truly, as the original manuscript was lost in Asulon) that contains more ignorant questions, extended arguments, and superior literacy. That said, this introduction is long enough.\n\nLet us begin.\n\nA human once told me,\n\"Purity is of the heart, not of the mind and body.\"\n\nLet us ignore the obvious conclusion that a heart is merely a muscle that pumps blood through the body, with no importance to purity other than filling its\n\nmandatory biological role. The human presumably refers to the heart as the beholder of an abstract concept of \"goodness,\" so we shall argue that point. \n\n\"Goodness,\" the act of being \"good,\" is a fundamentally flawed concept. There are\n\nthings that are innately evil, such as the dread-demon Iblees, profligates of Dark Magics, and other varying monsters who tout goals of domination and destruction. These are certainly cruel. But what can truly be considered \"good?\". Good (and at times\n\n\"evil\") are subjective in their very nature. Even the words of the much-revered Aenguls are only a matter of perspective. Let us say that in a Valah village, a family is taxed heavily by their local Lord. This lord treats them the same as any other\n\nfamily, but this one is particularly poor, and can barely survive the long winters. One day, the father in desperation robs a nobleman, and kills him. The pauper did not take pleasure in the act, and had not intended the nobleman to die. This allows him\n\nto feed his long-suffering children. Would this act be good, or evil? If one situation can be skewed in such a way, then, logically, others must also be flawed. \n\nThe maehr'sae hiylun'ehya teaches that purity is a combination of mind,\n\nand body. It is something only mali'aheral are capable of, and can never be allowed to fester beneath the guidance of the ignorant. To advance our people, Mali'aheral must enhance and strengthen their minds. To understand nature's workings is\n\nto understand our existence and its natural place in the true-world. To this end, our people are gifted with extraordinary intelligence, and it allows us a greater capacity to absorb information, and create our own.\n\nIn advancing our people, we complete the maehr'sae hiylun'ehya. The heart has no purpose in true purity.\n\nA wood elf once asked me, \n\"If you are not racist, why do you not allow intermarriage between your people and other races?\"\n\nThe other races are, as commonly said, \"lesser\" than true, pure mali'aheral. This is not a malicious slur\n\naimed at them for amusement or as an emotion-fueled outburst of hatred. This is simply observable fact. Traits that commonly bring the ruin of other societies, for example; greed and violence, are barely prevalent within our community. Furthermore, our\n\naforementioned heightened mental faculties make such traits almost non-existent. Our blood ensures this superiority, and every muddying of our family lines with inferior specimens dulls preferred Mali'aheral traits. This makes the completion of the\n\nmaehr'sae hiylun'ehya more difficult with every corrupted generation. Were we to allow rampant, foolish breeding, then the maehr'sae hiylun'ehya would never be completed, and our kind would languish in the mediocrity of the other Mali.\n\nA Dwarf once asked me,\n\"If you have no prejudices, why do you allow so few outsiders within your society?\"\n\nOutsiders are difficult to trust. There are a worthy few of them accepted into our numbers, but these have proven their\n\ncompliance and worthiness to our people. To why we bar outsiders in general, will be answered in an allegory--one that will be far simpler to grasp for those not of our people. \n\nImagine yourself the owner of a fabulous dwelling, filled with\n\ndelights unknown to your envious neighbours. You enjoy your life amongst the trinkets and comfort items that you gathered, and rest in a fine wicker chair in the sitting room. Suddenly, a person you have never met walks through your door, without so much\n\nas a knock, and begins to walk about \"Ooh\"ing and \"Ahh\"ing at the many delights and placing her dirty fingers upon your property. Confused and concerned, you ask the obvious question of \"What are you doing?\" The stranger, with a smile, explains that she\n\nthinks your home beautiful, and is looking around. You, in turn, explain to her that you don't want unannounced people in your home. With that, she becomes angered, and declares that you're \"greedy\" for keeping your property to yourself. Such things\n\nshould be for everyone to see! You explain to her that she is free to do as she pleases with her own home, but that you prefer your privacy, thank you very much. \n\nThe stranger disappears, and begins spreading  rumours amongst your fellow\n\nneigbours of your greed, and how you \"hate people.\" Suddenly these neighbours also begin to barge their way in, and look about. Sometimes, things go missing. You in turn build a high wall around your home, and though they continue to voice their anger\n\nat your actions, they are no longer a nuisance. It should not be a necessity to do this, but the nature of your neighbours makes it so.\n\nA dark elf once asked me, \n\"Your people insult ours so viciously! Why would you be so cruel?\"\n\nMisinterpretation on the part of those whom we \"insult.\" If this occurs so commonly, why have these victims not re-evaluated the\n\nreasons behind our words? What we say always has merit. This is what they do not understand. They choose defensiveness over recognising their faults, and therefore never adapt and improve themselves. Thusly, our people will \"insult\" them again, and will\n\nlikely continue to do so until their missteps are recognised. Such is only befitting a proper Mali, and for their own good.\n\nA Goblin once asked me (version interpreted from orcish babble),\n\"If you are superior, how is it we orcs have slaughtered you in battle countless times?\"\n\nActs of combat and physical strength do not imply superiority. Violence is one of the\n\nbasest and most simplistic natural urges that any animal is capable. It can stem from any dark emotional outburst, and those that practice them commonly cannot be fully trusted. To use yet another example -- were a giant spider to attack and kill an Uruk,\n\nwould the spider therefore be superior to the orc?\n\nSuch as it is, these questions irk me so, especially when my associates cannot answer them. May you be further enlightened, my reader.\n\nMaehr'sae hiylun'ehya.", ""),
        StaticBook("Defining Purity", "§bAzorella Coulissante", "As is often the case with such things as mutable as language, definitions and connotations can often become confused over the passage of time and the turnover from generation to generation. This particular treatise will attempt to clarify\n\nsome of these definitions, namely those regarding Mali'aheral purity.\n\nFirstly, it must be noted that this treatise will not attempt to explain how the lesser races may try to define their own standards for purity,\n\nshould they have any standards at all. Since a pure Mali'aheral would never breed with such lesser stock, such definitions are generally irrelevant for practical use and will not be addressed in this document. For the purposes of this document, the terms\n\n'pure' and 'impure' will refer only to those who have some form of Mali'aheral heritage. The term 'lesser' refers to any of those without a Mali'aheral heritage.\n\nPurity, like the maehr'sae hiylun'ehya, typically relies on\n\ntwo main pillars: mental purity and physical purity. The first pillar, mental purity, is more difficult to define and is dependent on a Mali'aheral's actions and intentions. This will be covered in more depth later in this document. However,\n\nthe second pillar, physical purity, is considerably more straightforward as it relies strictly on bloodlines.\n\nPhysical purity is dependent entirely on a Mali'aheral's heritage. A pure Mali'aheral can only\n\nbe born of physically pure parentage and therefore cannot have any of the lesser races marring their bloodline. By contrast, a physically impure Mali'aheral (also known as an acaln due to the severity of this impurity) will have a\n\nlesser amongst their ancestors. There is no way to remedy this kind of impurity aside from termination, hence, extreme care must always be taken in regards to producing offspring.\n\nMental purity is less simple to define and\n\nis reliant on a Mali'aheral's actions and intentions. A mentally pure Mali'aheral will often adhere to the tenants of the maehr'sae hiylun'ehya, although this kind of definition is bound to evoke confusion since each Mali'aheral likely has\n\na slightly different interpretation of Larihei's teachings. These different interpretations ought be embraced as they help weave a lush and rich environment ripe for debate and learning; however, in defining purity, these interpretations often\n\nbring with them ample confusion.\n\nInstead, it may be simpler to try and define the actions and intentions of a mentally impure Mali'aheral. The greatest offenses to mental purity lie in the murder of other pure Mali'aheral\n\nand in breeding with lessers. However, care must be taken to note the intention of such actions. For instance, a Haelun who accidentally smothers her infant in their slumber may remain mentally pure depending on the circumstances, but\n\na disgruntled guard arbitrarily murdering fellow pure Mali'aheral ought serve a capital punishment for their capital impure offense.\n\nSome lesser, but still troubling, offenses may include violent assault on another Mali'aheral or\n\nphysically intimate fraternization with a lesser, even if this does not lead to expected or unexpected offspring. These kinds of mental impurities may be recoverable by a strict reeducation, but are nonetheless a grave insult to the\n\nmaehr'sae hiylun'ehya and should not be taken lightly.\n\nAs a final word of warning--to accuse another Mali'aheral of impurity is a matter that should be handled with grave care. To do so falsely would be akin to trampling on\n\ngenerations of careful breeding and centuries of tradition with intense ramifications for the accused should the innocent walk guilty. By the same measure, however, it is equally dangerous to allow impures to scourge society should the\n\nguilty walk innocent. Take care with your judgement, lliran, for the future of the Mali'aheral rests upon it.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Case Study", "§bFalyen Darylus", "The Radiant Man - Powers and Subjugation of the Mind\nThe Radiant Man, a suspected incarnate aengul, has aligned himself with parts of the Spellcrafters of Rivel with the goal of uncovering the Forgotten Dwarven artifact known as\n\n“The Seal”. To those who follow him, the Radiant Man grants incredible powers. They are akin to holy magics, but are incapable of healing yet also functional against those who could not in any way be described as dark creatures. It seems to be Holy\n\nMagic without the requirement of being holy: an excellent addition to any Spellcrafter’s arsenal, especially when so freely given and easily mastered. Or so it would seem.\nIt appears to draw upon the Radiant Man’s power is to open one’s being\n\nto him: the more power one draws and the more frequently one draws it the more the Radiant Man is capable of influencing, or even controlling, one’s thoughts. We have carried out extensive experimentation on the two members\n\nof the Radiant Man’s following of Spellcrafters when they returned to Rivel to analyse the tomes from the Archive. Their behaviour was normal, yet they wholeheartedly refuse to accept the possibility that their minds are not fully\n\ntheirs, and mental magical probing is being blocked by a power beyond our own.\nPart of the danger of this is the slippery slope: once one opens one’s mind to the Radiant Man the Radiant Man can influence one to draw a little more, giving\n\nthe Radiant Man a little more control and thus the influence required to push one to draw slightly more power. This could rapidly lead to a complete inability to refuse the commands of the Radiant Man, and hypothetically could turn into what I\n\nrefer to as a “Subjugant”, an individual wielding untold power via the Radiant Man yet completely slaved to his will to the point of lacking independent thought: simply an extension of the Radiant Man’s desires. Such a being could prove\n\nincredibly dangerous, and I recommend total disconnection from the Radiant Man of all of his Spellcrafter followers as soon as they return from their venture to the Hall.\n- Senior Researcher Falyen Darylus", ""),
        StaticBook("Spider Troubles", "§bEnas Keyron", "The Spiders have been causing quite a ruckus lately. The golems have been keeping them for the most part at bay, but each day I must take precious time to repair the many puncture wounds and purge the wires of vemon. Blasted things, I can't pin them down.", ""),
        StaticBook("Old Journal", "§bMrWizardGorlock", "The Fire\nBy The Wanderer of the World\n\nThe Fire, bright as the Star\nThe Fire, deadly as war\nShining so brightly\nAs it Devours Air\nIt looks ever so fair\nThe Fire, warming as a hug\nThe Fire, A spark of hope\nthat is as deadly as you.\n\nA Light in the Darkness\nBy the Wanderer of the World\n\nLight, shining so bright\nDark, lurking like a shark\nYou light my way\nOut of the Caves\nInto the Fields\nAnd I follow your way\nOut of the Dark\nand into a new Day\n\nThe Wanderer\n\nTraveling Across lands far and wide.\nMoving through life like a slide.\nHe never stops, but always observing.\nNever participating on the side.\n((a picture of a man above a crowd is here))\n\nHe looks for a reason.\nHelping others, never himself as it's treason.\nHe forgot himself, forever lost,\nUpon the paths, like a fading season.\n\n((a drawing of spring overtaking the last snowflakes of winter is here))\n\nHis name lost and unknown.\nHe has been given many, but none he owns.\nThe Wanderer, there like starlight.\nFaded and grey, always out of sight.\n\n((a man is faded into a black background, barely a differentiating between the two colors, but still there))\n\nHe wanders, ever searching\nNo reasons, just observing.\nA life of solitude, always alone.\nHe looks for friends, but never finding.\n\n((a man is here among many, all have their back to him))\n\nDeath evades him.\nLife forgets him.\nAlone with an untold story\nBecause Nobody will remember him.\n\n((a group of people pass a man, darkness covers the left side and light on the other, he stands between.))\n\nEmotions, he gains.\nBut over time he has learned to feign.\nHappy but sad, he prays\nHoping Aspects take these reins.\n\n((a man cries into his legs, a few water splotches dot the page from 'tears'))\n\nHe needs someone, a friend.\nHe wants a lover, someone to tend.\nBut he walks alone upon the world.\nNow he sighs and stares as he meets his end.", ""),
        StaticBook("Torture Devices", "§bThe Eternal Library", "Torture Devices\n\nBy Sha Greyhammer\n\nJudas Cradle\nThe victim would be place on top of a pyramid-like seat. Where they would be slowly impaled.\n\nCoffin Torture\nThe victim was placed inside the ‘coffin’. Torturers were well-known for forcing overweight victims into the device, or even making\n\nthe ‘coffin’ slightly larger than normal to make the victims more uncomfortable.\n\nThe Brazen Bull\nWhen a victim is placed inside the brazen bull, he or she is slowly burned to death. It has a complex system of tubes in order to make the victim's screams\n\nsound like an infuriated ox.\n\nThe Rack\nThe rack is commonly considered the most painful form of torture. The torturer turned the handle causing the ropes to pull the victim’s arms. \nEventually the victim's bones were dislocated with a loud\n\ncrack. This method was mostly used to extract confessions, as not confessing meant that the torturer could stretch more. \nometimes, torturers forced their victim to watch other people be tortured with this device to implant psychological fear.\n\nThey often had spikes that penetrated the victim’s back  - as the limbs were pulled apart, so was his spinal cord increasing not only the physical pain, but the psychological one of being handicapped at best, too.\n\nDunking\nThe victim was tied to a chair\n\nwhich was elevated or lowered by the torturer. If he noticed that the victim was going to pass out, he elevated the chair. If they didn’t reveal information the chair was lowered. This could take hours.\n\nDrops of Water\nA very painful method of torture\n\nconsisted of fixing a victim’s head under a small tube that constantly filtered drops of water. These fell on the same spot of the victim’s head leading to, in prolonged periods of time, death.\n\nFreezing With Water\nPouring water on someone in cold areas.\n\nEventually causing them to freeze to death.\n\nForce Drinking\nThe effect is this: the victim is forced to drink much water until his confession or death.\n\nExposure\nAs its name implies, this method consists of exposing a victim to the elements. The victim\n\ncould be buried up to his neck, letting any animals, insects or other people kill him slowly.\n\nChair of Torture\nThere are many variants of the chair. They all have one thing in common: spikes cover the back, arm-rests, seat, leg-rests and foot-rests.\n\nThe number of spikes in one of these chairs ranges from 500 to 1,500. To avoid movement, the victim’s wrists were tied to the chair or, in one version, two bars pushed the arms against arm-rests for the spikes to penetrate the flesh even further.\n\nIn some versions a hole under the seat.\n\nThe Tickler\nIt’s a very simple instrument that was used to tear a victim’s skin apart. Due to its shape, neither bones nor muscles were spared. The tool had claws on it sharp enough to tear anything.\n\nThe Maiden\nIt stands 7 feet tall and is able to accommodate a man. The victim was tied inside the Maiden and one of the two doors was shut, penetrating the victim’s flesh with the strategically-placed spikes that didn’t penetrate any vital organs.\n\nWhen completely closed, the screams from the victim could not be heard outside, nor could the victim see any light or hear anything.\n\nThe Head Crusher\nWith the chin placed over the bottom bar and the head under the upper cap, the torturer slowly turned\n\nthe screw pressing the bar against the cap. This resulted in the head being slowly compressed.\n\nRats\nThe victim was completely restrained and tied to the ground or any horizontal surface. A rat was then placed on his stomach covered by a metallic\n\ncontainer. As the container was gradually heated, the rat began to look for a way out through the victim’s body. Digging a hole usually took a few hours of \nagonizing pain for the victim. The almost invariantly resulted in death.\n\nThe Wheel Torture\nThe device consists of a large wooden wheel with many spokes. The victim’s limbs were tied to the spokes and the wheel itself was slowly revolved. Through the openings between the spokes, the torturer usually hit the victim’s hones.\n\nOnce his bones were broken he was left on the wheel to die, sometimes placed on a tall pole so the birds could feed from the still-living human.\n\nFoot Roasting\nThe victim’s feet were imprisoned in the stocks and then red-hot coal was placed right under\n\n them. When the subject was interrogated a screen was put between the heat and his feet acting as relief. If he refused to confess, his bare feet were exposed to the flames. The torture progressed until the victim’s feet were charred to the bone.\n\nThumbscrew Torture\nThe victim’s fingers were placed inside the instrument and slowly crushed as the torturer turned the handle on top. This method was primarily used to extract confessions as it was both painful and very lasting.\n\nThe Heretic’s Fork\nThe instrument consists of two forks set against each other that penetrated the flesh under the chin in one end and the upper chest in the other. As usual, this instrument didn’t harm any vital points; thus avoiding death.\n\nLead Sprinkler\nAt first sight, it looks like a holy water sprinkler, but in reality it’s a bit more complex. The torturer poured molten metals in one end and its contents slowly rushed to the other side where they fell on any part of the victim’s body.\n\nFlaying\nThe victim’s arms were tied to a pole above his head while his feet were feet were tied below. His body now completely exposed and the torturer, with the help of a small knife, peeled off the victim’s skin slowly.\n\nKnee Splitter\nAs the torturer turned the handle, the claws slowly slammed against each other mutilating any skin in between. The number of spikes the knee splitter contained varied from three to more than twenty.\n\nCrocodile Tube\nThe victim was fixed\n\n inside a tube just big enough for the victim’s entrance. The tube, having crocodile teeth-like spikes, was slowly compressed leaving the victim totally immobilized. The torturer could only see his face and feet. With the help of carbon and fire\n\nunderneath the tube until he extracted a confession or killed the victim.\n\nThe Brank\nThe device was a metal cage or mask that enclosed the head, often with ridiculous adornments designed to humiliate its victim. Commonly attached with bell to warn people\n\nof their approach.\n\nCrocodile Shears\nThe interior design closely resembles a tube containing numerous spikes on both ends. Although it was sometimes used to mutilate the fingers, its most common purpose was to cut arteries.\n\nThe Copper Boot\nFirst, the torturer placed the victim’s feet inside the boot and secured them with chains inside the device. Depending on the crime, the victim could be tortured in many different ways: Molten metals, boiling water, beating it.\n\nThe Pendulum\nWith the help of a rope, the victim’s wrists were tied behind his back. As the torturer turned the handle, the rope slowly elevated eventually dislocating the victim’s shoulders.", ""),
        StaticBook("Life Of Thurak", "ilikefooddude", "The Life Of Thurak'Braduk\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=Thurak has only had two times in his life when he was really, undeniable happy. Two meagre, short lived moments to look back on for the rest of his life that he can safely say that he was happy.\n\nThe first was long ago,\nin his early childhood as a Cub of Raurna and Ghazkull Braduk. For a time, he\nlived without worry; his mother was caring, (in an Orcish way of course) and his father was there for him, training him proudly in the ways of being an\n\nOrc, and teaching him how to wield his chosen weapon, the hammer. Till the fourth\nyear of his infancy, such was Thurak's life, without worry or need to worry, and the days passed quickly and pleasantly.\n\nThe ancestors must have looked down\non Thurak, though, the day his happiness was swept away, and decided that he was\nnot destined to have this life, carefree and happy.\n\nThe air was bitter and cold on that silent desert night. Winds blew the sand\naround into small willy willies which swirled around in endless, untraceable\ncircles.\n\n'STOMP' went the boots when they clashed with the sand.\n\n'STOMP' went the footwear of the Orc of the Ugluk clan. Looking, searching was one pair, on patrol, was the other. The stomping stopped, as one pair neared\nthe other. A voice came, booming from the mouth of the owner of the loudest\n\nboots. Quieter, softer, came the voice of the Cub in response. Looking, searchin, was the cub.\n\"Where is mother? Where is father?\"\nIt asked, to be replied by the slide of a sword from its\nsheath.\n\n\"Follow or die,\" Accompanied the voice of the sword.\nThurak folllowed.\n\n10 years, Thurak stayed. Positions were reversed. Once his clan, now his enemy. Once his enemy, now his clan. Why\nthey did not come, he knew not. He questioned them, but did not hate them. 10 years of belief being crushed.\n\nMaybe tommorow, he said before he went to sleep on the dirt floor, next to the\nempty bed of his new father. Maybe next\nweek, he soon was saying. Maybe\nnever. His hope was crushed. Happiness, now such a sad memory to behold.\n\nArriving at the gate, another traveller.\nThurak thought nothing of the darks skinned Uruk as he entered the gates of his unwilling home, paying no more attention to him than any other of the passing by Uruks. This one was far from home, but close to\n\nBlood. Unrecognised, he went, by his enemies, and by his friends, until alone he was, with Thurak.\n\"What clan are you?\" He asked.\n\"Braduk,\" came the response. A name Thurak had not heard for too long.\n\n Hope came then,\nrushed in, the flood gates of his heart now open. \"Take me back,\" he pleaded, answered by a yes. It sounded strange, a word of hope and willingness where the young cub had thought there was none.\n\n\"No welcoming party for me.\" Ignored,\nhe should have expected. It hurt more now, hope of happiness is the easiest crushed. Time rushed by, though not like before. Now he strove for attention,\nwhere once he had an endless supply.\n\nOne Cub, two Cubs, three Cubs. Thurak was forgotton in the crowd, truly more alone than when he was alone.\n\nAt 18, Thurak was tired of holding it in. His youngest brother, Gor, was\ntroubling his Rhino, swinging his axe down on its toe. Patiently, Thurak asked\nGor to stop, an axe, flying at him, was the response. Anger, hatred. It filled Thurak, and bloodlust\n\nCame upon him.\nIt was a good kick; his brother must have gone a few meters.  Again, Gor troubled him, another good kick. The third time, Thurak lost all of his precious inhibitions. His brother, the leech, who stole everything Thurak needed so dearly, had\n\nDriven Thurak deep into bloodlust. Gor must have seen this, and had retrieved his axe, sending it spinning towards Thurak's neck. It was a good throw.\nJust as Thurak was about to launch another powerful kick at Gor, in came Durakai, pushing Thurak away,\n\ndepriving him of his vengeance.\nLater that day, a clan meeting was held, over what to do about Thurak. Exiled?\nNo, Thurak himself thought he deserved it, and would have accepted the punishment without complaint. Instead, the second happy\n\nhappy chapter in his life beginning.\n\nHe finally had a mate, Dari. Soon, along came little Sharn, a beacon of light in his once dark world. ogether, with Dari, he taught her, as his parents had done with him, and she grew to the strong age of four.\n\nThurak never liked that number.\nHe woke up in his Blarg, stretching and yawning, finding no one else there, not his mate, not his Cub.\nProbably hunting,\nhe though. So he thought, until two days later. No one had seen them, not a trace nor a letter of\n\nWhere they had gone.\nMaybe tomorrow, he said each night before he went to sleep on the empty bed. Maybe next week, he soon was saying. \nMaybe never.\nHis hope was crushed.\nHappiness, now such a sad memory to behold.\n\nWith them too, the eldest of his younger brothers had gone. Nazdag. He missed him as much as his mate and child, though he did not know why.\nMaybe because they shared a bloodline, they were both in line for the position of Chieftain.\n\nTwo years, he went without seeing those three who he held so\ndear. Why they did not come back, Thurak didn't know. He didn't question them, he didn't hate them.\nHe loved them.\n\nAnother day, another scar; Thurak hobbled around the Uzg, his injury stopping him from walking at his usual pace. The Scabbernak's stinger had plunged into his right ribcage, causing quite a bit of nerve damage.\n\nA growing infection was hidden underneath the thick Rhino hide bandage, unknown to him and all around him. Once he reached the gate, though, he knew the pain of the walk was worth it. here, stood his brother, bigger, stronger than when he left, but still\n\nHis brother. \nOne down, two to go.\nHe would restore his family, whatever the cost.\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-End Of Part One\n\nPart Two\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=The last few years of Thurak's life have been the most bloody and melancholic of them all.\n\n\nFor fifteen years, Thurak searched for a hint, a glimpse, a whisper of advice\n\nto direct him to what he most wanted; his life mate and cub. For fifteen years, Thurak found nothing but dead ends and false leads. From Oren to Malinor, no news of the two Uruks, mother and daughter. The men in Oren blamed the Elves, just as those\n\nResiding in Malinor shouted claims of slavery in Oren. From them, Thurak got nothing. From the many he paid off; knights, street urchins, assassins, he heard nothing from. The nobles in their towers knew nothing, and so neither did the\n\nShady groups delving in dark alleyways, even when beated to an inch of their lives.\n\nThurak killed, questioned and pleaded, all for naught for ten years, before he gave up his dignity and asked the Dwarves.\n\nHe had expected the result, but was disappointed nonetheless. Riducules and insults were all that awaited him at the Dwarven gates, tempting him to an action he knew he couldn't take.\n\nFinally, after sixteen years of searching, Thurak would find what he was looking for.\n\nA small trading group, located on the far west side of the desert, was rumoured to be trading in slaves.\n\nSo close, all along, Thurak though as he approached the small groups of dimly lit tents, the trusty Zpidhammah raised at the ready. Seeing a sentry, Thurak ducked under a dune, narrowly missing the sweeping gaze of the torch wielding human.\n\nTrying again after the man had done his rounds on his side of the camp; Thurak paced into the camp, and started looking around for any sign of the two feuruks. There, after sixteen years, Thurak caught the first glimpse of his life mate and child,\n\nLying face down in their blood.\n\nSixteen years, ten minutes late, was one of the thoughts racing\nthrough his head during the mindless bloodlust that followed. Sentries screamed warnings, and men scattered as they realised what was happening.\n\nNone were prepared for an attack this late at night, and none could ever be prepared for the wrath Thurak brought forth that night.\n\nThurak stood, panting amongst the clearing. Three days after the battle was ended, no remains of the slaving camp remained, except for the two pillars marking the remains of those he so loved. Hands splintered and bruised, Thurak sat beside the graves,\n\nSighing.\n\nNow he could rest.", ""),
        StaticBook("Iblees Journal", "§bAnnabella", "I have taken a break form my studies to examine the various Iblees eye structures that have been apearing.\n\nThe first one appeared to be harmless. Showing major corruption, but it did not cause harm form what I hear. The second structure found in forn of Dwarven lands has various creatures which are unknown to me.\n\nIt is confirmed, they are undead.\n\nA Drake has spawned, crashing into the city before it dies.\n\nThe general chaos is over, everyone is healing each other. I will stay for a slight time longer, but I should leave soon.\n\nConclusion: It appears our hope for peace on this land is far from the case. A traveler warns me it is Iblees, and the structures formed show the infamous 'Eye of Iblees'. \nI will make another journal should I hear of other incidents.", ""),
        StaticBook("Confessions", "§bRinaline Sirius", "Confessions by Rinaline S.§0\n§0-------------------§0\n§0When I first arrived in Haelun'or I was astonished. The beautiful scenery and kind people made me feel at home.§0\n§0\n§0Before I arrived, I was treated harshly as though I were an animal.\n\nBack in Oren it was horrible, the people were cruel and I was even called a, forgive me for this vile language, \"whore\".§0\n§0\n§0It didn't bother me at first, but gradually it kept happening, but a kind 'aheral living in Oren made me a beautiful dress.\n\nAt first, Oren had changed me, I even went as far as dying my hair with dyes I found in the Oren shops.§0\n§0\n§0I have stooped so low that I have even *almost* slept with the 'ata Veledin.§0\n§0\n§0After our brief time together I realized\n\nthat I needed to change. §0\n§0\n§0So I'm back in Haelun'or where I belong, with my kin.§0\n§0\n§0I am not proud of my mistakes and I'm here to find a council member to tell them about my sinful wrongdoings.\n\nFortunately, the dye was flower based so it washed out easily with a lot of rough scrubbing. §0\n§0\n§0I felt like an entirely new person after I washed that dye from my hair.§0\n\nSuch an idiot, I was to have ever tried it at all.§0\n§0\n§0I have sinned and so I am confessing to all now.§0\n§0\n§0I do not wish to be considered a mali'ata, not because they'd look down on me, but because I know that is not who I am.\n\nMy parents were 'ata. Such disgusting 'aheral, the time I reached 50 I started my adventures to get away from them.§0\n§0\n§0They were filthy impures and I wanted nothing of them.§0\n§0\n§0I love the 'aheral, but they. . . are not like the rest of us.\n\nI met some very kind people that changed my mind about the mali'thill. I look up to them, and feel like such a child because of it, but that's the truth.§0\n§0\n§0Thank you, Haelun'or for showing me what it means to live.\n\nI am finally sure that I belong somewhere. §0\n§0Here.§0\n§0\n§0I am ready for the punishment of my horrible sins, for I deserve it.§0\n§0\n§0I only hope that I survive a trial if there is one,because I truly wish to be a mali'thill.", ""),
        StaticBook("The M&H: Part 2", "§bAthedil Haler'thilln", "----------------Maehr’sae Hiylun’ehya\nChapter 2\n----------------As interpreted by Lucion Sullas, former Okarir, Tilruir, Sohaer, and Maheral of Haelun’or.\n\nTo follow the tenets of the Maehr’sea hiylun’ehya one must first know the meaning behind the ancient elven that masks it. Its most accurate common translation is “The pursuit of wisdom and health” or simply\n\n‘wisdom and health.’ So revered is this term that is akin to a blessing given between adherents. The Maehr’sae pertains to the acquisition and sharing of knowledge amongst fellow Mali’aheral. Our race is\n\nknown for many things, but poor academics are not included. After being changed by the magics of the Golden Pools, we were blessed with studious minds, and gifted great talent with magic of any form. Thusly,\n\nit is imperative that we embroil ourselves utterly within tasks that further our people’s knowledge.\n\nThe Hiylun’ehya pertains to the bloodlines and fortitude of the people. Pure bloodlines are the ones that best retain the blessings of the ancient pools. To sully them with poorly-reasoned mixed breeding thins the\n\nblessings that we gained, and therefore makes the maehr’sae hiylun’ehya more difficult to complete--if not impossible. In guarding our bloodlines we must show discipline and fortitude. Things that detract the health\n\nof the people; violence against the pure, mixed-breeding, and being too lenient and accepting towards the other races. One must always be diligent when regarding impurities. The small concessions of today always\n\nlead to the vilest impurities tomorrow beings. It has been observed, and thus it is known.\n\nThe ultimate goal of the Maehr’sae hiylun’ehya is its completion. To reach true enlightment , the Mali’aheral strive to understand all through constant learning, and a pure people. When all is understood,\n\nwe will be beyond the simple meanderings of the mundane world. It is unknown what will occur when this day of total enlightenment occurs, but one suspects the Mali’aheral will know precisely what to do.\n\nMaehr’sae hiylun’ehya.", ""),
        StaticBook("The M&H: Part 3", "§bAthedil Haler'thilln", "----------------Maehr’sae Hiylun’ehya\nChapter 3\n----------------As interpreted by Lucion Sullas, former Okarir, Tilruir, Sohaer, and Maheral of Haelun’or.\n\nAs with any ideology, there are misconceptions amongst the uninitiated. Mainly upon the desires of its adherents, the reasons behind their actions, or perhaps even mere differences in personality. It is difficult\n\nto write a truly concise list, but one hopes the ones he lists are relevant to the reader.\n\n----------------1. On Racism and Seclusion\n----------------The Maehr’sae hiylun’ehya does not support illogical hatreds of other peoples. Rather, it supports rational\n\nwariness of dangerous outsiders--such as urukan, tal’urukan and suspicious strangers. The urukan and tal’urukan are beings with a natural aversion to elven thought and philosophy. Though there can be\n\nexceptions, they are often ignored or destroyed, should they be in the presence of the Pure. They cannot be trusted under any circumstances. In regardes to the other races, it is most certainly dependant on the\n\nMali’aheral in question. I am yet to meet a Mali’aheral aside gtom Uradir who truly despised all peoples equally. It is for these reasons adherents separate themselves from contemporary society.\n\n----------------2. On Insults and the Insulted\n----------------The Maehr’sae hiylun’ehya does not support arbitrary personal attacks. It does however, support learning,\n\nadvising, and truth. Should an individual speak without merit or evidence upon an individual with the purpose of cruel amusement, then they are a poor adherent, and have provided nothing to anyone.\n\nHowever, advise can often be misinterpreted as insult. Adherents are taught to despise falsehood, therefore should something be perceived as incorrect they rightly feel the need to amend it. If an individual\n\nhas their feelings hurt during the process, it is their issue, and not the adherent’s.\n\n----------------3. On Violence and Aggression\n----------------The Maehr’sae hiylun’ehya does not support physical violence of any kind. It does support safeguarding the\n\npurity of its people. Often, death to those who would sully the purity of the adherents is the first and foremost answer to such crimes. However, violent actions belong to beasts, and are beneath us.\n\nOurs is an order built upon the mind, not the passions of raised fists.\n\n----------------4. On ‘Purges’ and Murder.\n----------------Maehr’sae hiylun’ehya does not support ‘purges’, or murder. It does, however, support the exaction of\n\njustice to craven monsters. Some individuals are so profane in their existence that they insult and endanger our way. Such people are more often-than-not loathed throughout all civilised lands.\n\nSuch individuals are few and far between, but if by the act of living they injure us, then they must be destroyed for the good of all. Exile ought to be the first and foremost method of drastic punishment in any case.\n\n----------------5. On Experimentation and Learning\n----------------The Maehr’sae hiylun’ehya does not support unethical and cruel experiments.\n\nIt does support the vigorous acquisition of knowledge. Those that would perform any experiment on a living, sentient, non-consenting induviduals are preforming a disgusting act that harms their own purity through reckless\n\nand untethered curiosity, as well as harming the reputation of their own people. It is bizarre, cruel, unethical, and the findings never outweigh the cost.\n\n----------------6. On Emotion and Aversion to it.\n----------------The Maehr’sae hiylun’ehya does not support and emotionless state in the individual.\n\nRather, it encourages logic, foresight, and wisdom over passionate outbursts. It is wiser to think before feeling. In public, it is beneath an adherent to act by the whims ofemotion--it shows a lack\n\nof self-control and would likely offend those around yourself.\n\n----------------7. On Superiority and Arrogance\n----------------The Maehr’sae hiylun’ehya does not declare Mali’aheral to be superior to other races. It does, however,\n\nsupport that those who follow its path closely are greater than others, as they seek enlightenment through the unravelling of truth, rather than the mundanities of life. Identifying adherents as ‘arrogant’ is simply an\n\ninnocent misinterpretation on the side of the uninitiated. Should one encounter an adherent that claims themselves to be ‘superior’ generally speaking, one would advise you to ask them their current academic projects.\n\nShould they refuse to answer, it is safe to say their ego speaks, and not the Maehr’sae hiylun’ehya.\n\n----------------8. On adherents and Their Qualities\n----------------The Maehr’sae hiylun’ehya supports that only the Mali’aheral, with their inherent blessings,\n\ncan successfully follow the Pure Way. But this is only true in theory. The Maehr’sae hiylun’ehya encourages community cohesion and the search for truth. Theoretically, any race (with the exception of perhaps\n\nlye’urukan) may adopt and follow the path to enlightenment. No other race has attempted to adhere to it, thus perhaps it will never be known for certain.\n\nOne hopes that this series has been illuminating. Seek out L. Sullas, if you can, should questions be sought. Otherwise, good luck on your own twisting path.\n\nMaehr’sae hiylun’ehya.", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter", "§bIaria Elervathar", "Dear mister Parion,\n\nI rather had this message delivered verbally, although it seems like you have took a voyage elsewhere. An unrelenting thing, yet who am I to truly judge?\n\nBecause of the inconvenient way that this message is written, I doubt that you will understand much from what I have to say. Do wish me luck however, I am fortunate enough to be literate.\n\nWhat happened?\nSurely I am not the only person who asks.\n\nWhat happened, mister Parion? Your attention seems to waver from our beloved elcihi'thilln to the Dominion's capital instead. A rare occasion to find you on these streets these days.\n\nWhat happened?\nYou have blatantly ignored my\n\nrobust wails in your home to make a leave for Linandria instead, letting your wife handle my sorrow and distress.\n\nIs this how lliran treat eachother?\n\nYou appeared careless and indifferent when I shared my genuine concerns with\n\nyou and miss Leuvina the other day. You appeared much more worried about your voyage to the Dominion's cihi than my own personal matters instead.\n\nIs this truly§  how lliran\ntreat eachother?\n\nPerhaps I shouldn't take it personally. You were influenced by alcohol and slightly intoxicated anyways, but can you really blame me for being neglected by one who you expected to be a llir?\n\nYour loyalties have start\n\nto become questionable and I cannot raise any questions anymore without truly thinking whether you still care for our precious elcihi'thilln.\n\nYou have caused a relentless amount of desolation to me, and I truly doubt that it is so simple to\n\nmerely fix. The fact that I write this message, and not personally tell you, might already give a definite answer to these inquiries I posed.\n\nAn apology is late, but perhaps progress is what this dire situation needs.\n\nWith kind regards,\n\nIaria Elervathar\n\n*The letter was scented with a remarkable smell. A combination perhaps of the writer's perfume and the peculiar aroma from the library.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Tasks Done", "§bLaethis Izalith", "Haelunor Tasks\n\n1)Avern\nLeave The Druids\n\n2)Amras\nNo Trail\n\n3)Seth\nmake a sugar cane farm\n\n4) Gallidron\nNo Task\n\n5) Kaun\nNo task\n\n6) Ciel\nNo Task\n\n7) Vesryn\nLeave the druids\n\n8) Tason\nFill a chaest full of wood\n\n9)Braxus\nLeave the druids\n\n10) Galanthil\nChest of rock\n\n11)Thurdan\nA snip of a Dwarven Beard\n\n12)Laethis\nGive him a hatchet\n\n13)Tahorran\nNot a Citizen\n\n14) Laurynil\nNo Task\n\n15) Aneurin\nbring him a gold sword\n\n16) Esgalith\nNo task\n\n17)Resmira\ngive her materials for an iron sword\n\n18)Arianril\nNo Task\n\n19)Elwyn\nfill a chest full of wood\n\n20)Vendir\ngive him a sword\n\n21)Illidar\nNo task\n\n22) Korus\nNo Task\n\n23)Vivian\nNo task\n\n24)Medi'ir?\nhelp collect rescourses\n\n25)Talimeranche\ngive him 4 shovels\n\n26)Shi\nNo task\n\n27)Ayln\nNo task\n\n28)Andria\nno task\n\nAll tasks preformed by Earendur Vym'vallei in the trail of purity\n\n\nThe document is signed by the Sohaer, Laethis Izalith, as evidence of its completion.", ""),
        StaticBook("Elven Lessons 2", "§bArinislia", "Elven Lessons 2\n\nOriginally By:\n\nKalenz Uradir\n\nRescribed after the burning of the Eternal Library by:\n\nArinislia\n\nJust as in common, pronouns may be used to replace nouns. The pronouns in Elven are as follows:\n\nKae-Me\nNae-You\nLae-He/Him\nHae- She/Her\nLye-We\n(used to speak of Elves, people, or\n\nworld)\n\nfor example, the sentence 'elvulnir van ayla' (The trickster fared well) may be transformed into 'Lae van ayla' (he fared well).\n\nIn addition to this, other good languages supplements to\n\nanyone learning Elven include basic affixes. These affixes may be added to create further detail of form critical grammatical structures in a sentence. The dash denotes location of a seed word. Affixes and seed words are seperated by an apostrophe.\n\nac-(aca-) - Honorific for accursedness\n\nah-(ahe-) Honorific for reverence. Often used as a prefix for scholar.\nEx.: Ah'Lucion\n\nfi- New or anew\n\ncer- (Slang from Ceru) -Honorific for strength. Often used as a prefix for those of high military rank. Ex. : Cer'Silir\n\n-ante (-nte) - Last\n\n-ento (-nto) - Next\n\n-onn - from or born\n\nu- - Or\n\nvul- (cule) - Clever or deceptive\n\n-ir -purpose\n\n-sae - The spreading, development, or management\n\n-ii - deminuitive form\n\nAs always, a full list of affixes may be found in the Elven Dictionary.", ""),
        StaticBook("Wood Elves", "§bErolas Ba'ikana", "very funny looking people, not as i expected.\n\nhalf orc half wood elf ladies, very very hideous\n\nnot much activity in the city at this time\n\ntwo guard towers on front gate\n\nminimal guard activity,\ncould just be the time\n\nvery young elves hanging around\n\nvery few activity before sundown\n\nnight time is very active\n\n2 gates one at each end\n\nhousing district seems to be quite empty tho\n\ntried to get in good with orc lady, had to leave before we could do the dirty\n\ntook detour\n\nin ker'nor the city of\ndark elves. swindled\nenough food to feed the Warhawkes\n\nWe got honeydicked by some chick so we left.", ""),
        StaticBook("Malinor Hist. V1", "§bAevalyn", "The Eldest Brother:§0\n§0 A History of Malinor§0\n§0 (Volume I: First Sky)§0\n§0\n§0       Haelun'or,§0\n§0          Axios§0\n§0\n§0    Published 1593§0\n§0\n§0   by Ebs Telrunya§0\n§0    Transcribed by§0\n§0   Aevalyn Bethiros\n\nMalinor as we know it began after the Collapse, an obscure event which lead to the collapse of any civilization that may have existed before 1300.\n\nWhen one of the symptoms of the Collapse, the erasing of the collective memory of all who survived the Collapse, wore off,\n\nHigh Prince Native banded together what was left of a wood elven colony, as well as the dark elves and high elves in the region surrounding Laurelin.\n\nHe set about consolidating his position in Laurelin, assisting many elves in setting up lives in the capital.\n\nVery few elves are left from this time almost all having gone missing at some point during Aegis, so accounts of the early days are secondhand at best,\n\nmany times having been passed from pointed ear to pointed ear until reaching the writer. By most accounts, Native picked an array of Princes to help him govern the growing elven population, some notable ones being:\n\nPrince Toren the Farmer, Prince Flefal the Engineer, Princess Arianna, and Prince Lafthi the §0Diplomat.The§0 mining paradise of Ravenhold was founded, home to such notable elves as:\n\nKhel Oussana, Haelphon Adecchio, and future Prince Ebs Telrunya.§0\n§0After the initial years in Laurelin, most of the High Council, including High Prince Native, were barely ever seen in Laurelin, and the Malinor suffered.\n\nThe Gauntlet, an obstacle course that offered a large minas reward, was opened rarely, and almost every elf immediately entered the Wardens or the Druidic Order upon entry into Malinor.\n\nThe only functioning part of Malinor's government were indeed the Wardens, the elite defenders of the forests of Malinor.\n\nLead at first by the ruthless Blackthorn, they protected the forests while the High Council squandered away the Princedom.\n\nNative's only notable action during this time was nearly destroying Ravenhold when he caused the mine to collapse.\n\nWhen Kal'Bryst was destroyed during the onset of the Undead invasion, the High Council's reaction was nonexistent.\n\nDuring the great northern wars, in which the humans struggled for survival against the undead invaders, the elves hid in the south, with very few participating in the defense of Alstion.\n\nThe Wardens instead focused on removing Wrath from Wrath's Clutch, an Undead citadel in the South that threatened to cut off Alras and Al'Khazar from Laurelin and Kal'Urguan.\n\nCountless wardens and other elves perished in attacks on Wrath's Clutch, which was repeatedly assaulted so that prisoners being held there, most notably Princess Indelwehn, could be freed.\n\nNo matter how many time the walls were breached, the forces of the United Aegis Coalition (UAC) could not dislodge Wrath until very late in the war.\n\nIndelwehn became notable for leading the wardens in the defense of Sanjezel, leading the to the signing of the Malin-Krug pact, a long-lasting defensive treaty between the Holy Princedom and Krugmar,\n\nwhich was signed by Princess Indelwehn and Wargoth Mogroka'Gorkil.§0\n§0\n§0Malinor had a token presence in the Verge, its official settlement, overseen by Princess Lirinya, lacking utility and security.\n\nMore enterprising elves and a few humans united under Viscount Ebs, who founded the city of Fionn, which flourished for a time, until all but the mentally unstable abandoned the Verge during the massive slime and spider invasion.\n\nAt this time, Laurelin abandoned its old Council Chambers to allow the Mages Guild to have a place to set up away from the unstable north.\n\nFor a time, Malinor had a High Princess, Sorious, the wife of Native. After her death, the High Council passed a law stating that being the spouse of a Prince does not inherently make you a Prince.\n\nNative later fell in love with the owner of the Treetop Inn, which flourished in the trees North of Malinor. The owner, Lirinya, quickly rose to prominence in Malinor, gaining the title of Princess quite quickly.\n\nHer down to earth nature and her humbleness disguised that she was Undead. Gaining trust from a besmitten Native, she betrayed Malinor, destroying Ravenhold during the rule of High Princess Indelwehn.\n\nWith the appointments of Princess Indelwehn and Prince Mylas, a new generation of Elven leaders took the helm of the nation, Ebs, a high elf, and Sythra, a dark elf, convinced High Prince Native to disband the corrupted Wardens,\n\nwho were being used by the cruel Prince Quazar as an aggressive force, sparking conflict with the other nations. The Vanguard was formed, with Sythra in command.\n\nWith the appointment of Prince Ebs as High Prince Native's final act, the High Council, guided by the still mostly absent Princes Toren and Lafthi elected High Princess Indelwehn to the highest position in Mainor.\n\nThey then added then Treelord Haelphon and Sythra to the Council, and removed the Archdruids from the Council, as in that time,\n\nthe druids grove was a pit of filth and crime, all but sanctioned, and most certainly indulged in by Respiren and Dusk.\n\nThis was a Golden Age for the elves, as their international power and influence waxed to a point where it could have been argued, after the fall of Al'Khazar, that Malinor was the stablest and most powerful state in Aegis.\n\nUnknown at the time of her election was a deep taint hidden in the heart of Indelwehn, installed during one of her stays in Wrath's Clutch. Her second husband, Bircalin, and her friends watched in horror as she changed.\n\nIt is still not clear if she was aware she was tainted, however, she broke the Malin-Krug pact, refusing to aid Krugmar in their war against Urguan and Oren, and made a series of disastrous mistakes.\n\nShe attempted to have prince Ebs assassinated for questioning her, however he barely survived, and after a year recovering in Hanseti, he returned when Indelwehn was charged with the murder of a small child.\n\nThe High Council attempted to cover up her crimes, but realized she had to go, and voted unanimously to remove her, revealing to the public only that she had resigned.\n\nIn a near tie, Haelphon was elected High Prince, with Sythra losing by one vote. By this point, Prince Mylas had been killed during an Undead attack, and his body had been laid to rest outside the Sister City, a suburb of Laurelin.\n\nAt this time, the High Council met in the Sister City, as it was too easy to Undead spies to listen in on proceedings in Laurelin.\n\nMalinor established good relations with the Kingdom of Renatus after it emerged from the Phoenix Rebellion, but the final days in Aegis were characterized by fear among the High Council.\n\nAfter the falls of both Al'Khazar and Alras, refugees flocked to Malinor. Prince Ebs set up the Alrasian refugee camp East of Laurelin, but the Alrasian officers and Vanguard struggled to keep order in the once peaceful city of Laurelin.\n\nDuring a magical experiment by the druids and mages, Arkelos, and Undead, destroyed the Gauntlet, spreading miasma around Laurelin.\n\nAs elves prepared to flee the city, the druids managed to restore the air, however the damage was staggering.\n\nThe High Council, despite the pleading of a few members, refused to build additional fortifications around Laurelin, instead opting to give Deltaro Black, an elf who thought he was much more competent that he actually was,\n\npermission to remodel the front entrance to make it more \"naturey.\" Laurelin did not stand a chance in the final battle, and as the dragons leveled the once proud jewel of Laurelin,\n\nthe elves fled for the Verge, many of which were openly weeping, where they were met by the chaotic conditions, as the elven government has fallen apart.\n\nTreelord Alan managed to build an elven ship, but the travel conditions were horrid, and many elves were lost in the voyage.\n\nAnd so the elves set out for Asulon, to brave a strange new world full of dangers they could not have possibly conceived as they left Laurelin.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0- Ebs Telrunya, Former Fourth Prince of Malinor", ""),
        StaticBook("The Wolf and Pig", "§bKatona Therenal", "The pig and the wolf\n-------------------\n\nOnce upon a time, there was a pig, a pig that enjoyed butchering those who would upset him. Opening them up, trying to find what make them 'tick'. The pig once, had a friend. That friend was the wolf.\n\nStrange, for such different creatures to be friends. But that's what they were. The wolf kept his anger contained, taking it out on himself. One day, the pig threatened to butcher the wolve's family. The wolf flared with anger, but as he usually does,\n\ntook it out himself. The wolf started hating the Pig, losing all sort of friendship he ever had towards him. The pig took this as a sign of hatred, and so, he attacked his family. The wolf twitched with anger. As the pig was arrested the wolf went to end\n\nthe pig's miserable life. He was not able to do so, and was pushed away. As the pig made his escape through death, the wolf followed. And once they were face to face, the wolf took his chance. Using his new found magic he immobilized the pig\n\nHe then started to butcher the pig, as he did so with his family. Anger flared through his eyes as he skinned the pig, cutting off his ears, feeding them to the pig, the pig squealed, asking for a swift death. The Wolf wouldn't allow it, after hours of\n\ntorture, the wolf left the pig to hurt, feel the anger and pain the wolf had put up with. \n\nThis is the story of the Wolf and the Pig\n\nThis is the story of Katona and Miran.", ""),
        StaticBook("Poem of the city", "§bKnwell Quill", "Poem of A new city\n-------------------The City was the best thing in my memory,\n\nMore amazing than i would of though.\n\nI could of thought anything suddenly,\n\nI would of used some materials to make my own fort.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ame Folktales", "§b[7M Pregnant] Rhea Acius", "Folktales From\n   Better Times\n \n by Artimec Camoryn\n\nIt is said that while malin’s children were still young, and the first war of Iblees fresh in our minds, there existed a town of mali’ame far away from the rest of the descendants. This town knew no outside contact from the rest of the world. It's\n\ninhabitants lived their lives in peace and content, immersed in the nature our kind loves.\n\nThis town forbid the harming of Malin’s blessed forests, and so it’s people were forced to build homes out of stone, making mining a prevalent\n\ntrade in this small community. Among these miners were two young mali, by the names of Faenor and Eleyas.\n\nOne fateful day along the forest path back into town, poor Eleya’s pickaxe got clipped on a branch, and thrown into a lake adjacent to the path!\n\nEleyas did not know how to swim, nor had he any other way to retrieve his tool. That pickaxe was his only form of livelihood, and with no means to create a new one, he knew for sure he was ruined, he fell to his knees in front of the water and wept.\n\nLo and Behold, from the water rose an apparition of the blessed Aspect of Nature, Cerridwen. A shimmering entity of ever changing form, she gazed down on the weeping elf.\n\n\"Why do you cry, my child?\"\n\n“I have lost my livelihood.” Eleyas sobbed. “My only means of living given to me by my father.”\n\n\"Do not despair, my child.\" The aspect soothed in an otherworldly tone. “I will retrieve your tool for you.”\n\nAnd so a lovely golden axe hovered from out of the water into the hands of Eleyas, a brand new intricate tool, carved by a master.\n\n“This...This isn’t mine.” Eleyas gulped, hoping not to offend the Aspect.\n\n“Very well.” The apparition chimed, before sinking back beneath the waves. \n\nThis time, a fine silver axe hovered into the miner’s hands, a very fine piece of work, perhaps not as intricate as the golden one, but indeed a tool that would make him\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nenvy of the village.\n\n“This is not mine either.” The miner said miserably, giving the Aspect a pitiful look.\n\n“Very well, I will look one last time.” Cerridwen said, sinking back beneath the waves.\n\nThis time, a shoddy bronze pickaxe appeared in Eleya’s hands. A worn, torn and old looking tool, not anything anyone would be proud to own.\n\n“This! This is mine!” Eleyas exclaimed joyously, He thanked the aspect wholeheartedly.\n\nImpressed by the miner’s honestly, Cerridwen granted him not only his old axe, but the gold and silver ones too, sending him on his way home.\n\nSoon Eleyas was the talk of the town, for whom owned not only more than one tool, but a gold AND a silver\n\npickaxe? The miner Daenor grew envious of these tales and decided to test the truth of them. \n\nAt the same path and the same lake, Daenor the jealous miner tossed his worn bronze axe haphazardly into the lake without hesitation,\n\nhe then collasped in front of the water, crying fake crocodile tears.\n\nJust as she had done with Eleyas, the aspect of nature rose from the water, in flickering ever changing forms.\n\n“Why do you cry, my child?”\n\n“I..I dropped my pickaxe in the river.”\n\nAnd just as she had done with Eleyas, the kind aspect dived back into the water, and an amazingly intricate golden axe rose from the surface,  floating into the hands of the greedily awaiting Daenor.\n\n“Is this your axe, my child?”\n\n“Yes!” Daenor cried out gleefully. “Yes it is!”\n\nThe entire forest seemed to rumble in anger around the deceitful elf.\n\n“You are a liar. Plagued by greed.” The voice of the aspect boomed. “You shall recieve nothing, not a golden tool, nor the one you had. Let this be a lesson to you.”\n\nAnd so, the golden axe in Daenor’s hands vanished into thin air, leaving him with\n\nnothing, not so much as a wooden shiv. \n\nThere is a lesson to be had here, children of malin. Greed and deceit are traits of a bortu. Beings cursed not only with short stature and flat, ugly faces, but with an inherent desire to trick and bargain\n\ntheir way to riches.\n\nMali do not lust for wealth. Our society is one talonnii, one family. We do not seek to rise above one another, only to support each other.\n\nGreed is not a trait of mali'ame.", ""),
        StaticBook("An Old Note", "§bCeruberr Asul'Ailer", "~*~*~\n   A Silent Admiration\n\nIt began years ago, when I first laid eyes upon her in the grand city of Lin'everal. There she sat, under a willow, transfixed in a book. Her hair seemed to be an endless stream of gold, laying down upon her simple\n\nyet beautiful dress of blue. My heart seemed to skip a beat as she glanced up towards me, her eyes almost seemed to shimmer with a brilliant teal. I found myself for the first time in my life, speechless...\n\nMonths went by and every day, I continued to admire her beauty. Although it was not only her beauty that had me spellbound. She was the keeper of the Eternal Library, intelligent, witty and studied the arcane.\n\nEventually the months turned to years, and\n\nthe years to decades. \n\nI couldn't act upon my feelings. I was too young. But I didn't know if I'd ever have the courage to act upon them.\n\n*The note seems to have ended here. It appears to be very old and a name can\n\nbe seen faintly at the bottom of the page*\n\nCeruberr Asul'Ailer", ""),
        StaticBook("Governor Chivay", "§bLaethis Izalith", "Your Excellency,\n\nI write to inform you that I have requested a meeting with Praetor Tristin Tresery. This meeting is meant in hopes that I can apologize for much of the wrongdoing of my predecessors.\n\nThough I do not anticipate your\n\ndesire to attend this meeting, I thought it prudent to inform you my intentions so as not to circumvent your authority.\n\nIf you do wish to attend this meeting, you are more than welcome. The Praetor should have the details for such.\n\nSincerely,\nLaethis Izalith, Sohaer of Haelun'or", ""),
        StaticBook("The Inn", "§b[Bartender] Arthur Caulfrield", "True Stories\n      Made Fiction\n\n       By Arthur\n        Caulfield\n\nIt was a quiet day at the tavern. The bartender had just served the last of the ale to an odd gentleman in a mask and was beginning to pack up when A man came through the doors. \n   He said nothing. Going straight to a table in the back he\n\nwas soon followed by a young girl, no older than nine. \n   The man had a serious expression on his face while the girl had quite the opposite. She wore a bright smile that had not been seen in a tavern for years.\n\nThe bartender could see by the shape of their ears that they were elves. They were obviously not ashamed of it, wearing the sign so openly in a place so close to Oren. \n   This scared the bartender. It had been quite a common occurence to cut the tips of\n\nelven ears a while back and he was not sure whether the practice still continued. \n    After a while, the drinks hit the gentleman in the mask. The bartender was just cleaning out his fifth empty mug when the gentleman spoke up.\n\n\"Shouldn't bring a kid to a place like this,\" He said turning around in his stool to face the man, his back leaning against the bar. \"Could get hurt.\"\n   The elven man did not respond for what seemed like an eternity, but what could have only been seconds\n\n\"Don't talk about my child.\" And believing it was over, he turns back to face the table.\n   \"I'll talk 'bout ooever I bloody well want\" The gentleman in the mask responded. \n    The bartender sighed. This was all too common an occurence. Each night a\n\nbrawl broke out for one reason or another. Tonight it had been over a child's safety. \n   There was little time to react, while the masked gentleman was drunk, he was also very agile and moved with quickness no drunk could even comprehend.\n\nJumping from the bar stool, the masked man approached the table and waited for the elven man to react. \n   No words were spoken. The elven man simply got up and pushed the man aside as he walked over to the bar. The bartender smiled\n\npolitely and served him some ale. The masked man did not like this response. At a sprint, he crossed the room and hit the elf in the nose just as he turned to register the noise.\n   The elf stumbled back and closed both hands around the nose\n\nwhich had already began to seep blood that stained his colorful blue robes.\n    The bartender, having recoiled in shock, now tried to dissolve the bar fight not realising it was already too late.\n\nThe girl still sat on the table at the far corner of the bar. Watching in horror. \n    The father, after controlling the bleeding, turned to his daughter and demand she stay there.\n    The little girl did not say a word, just simply nodded along to his\n\norders.\n   Both men had the same mindset. Both men remained silent, knowing what was going to happen. Both men left the bar and stood on the grass outside, still wet from that mornings rain. \n    The daughter, knowing her father could no longer see,\n\nran to the nearest window and stared out, both hands and face smooshed against the glass in anticipation.\n   However, the father saw this as he looked back, causing him to point and shout something muted by the double doors which were now closed.\n\nThe bartender felt sorry for her. To have a father so easily led into brawls could not have been easy. \n   \"Do you like orange juice?\" He asked her in a friendly tone. She turned away from the window to look at him with some level of confusion.\n\n\"Did you know that oranges are guarded by dragons?\" He asked in a conversational tone, walking over to a chest full of fruit. \n   It had always seemed like a waste to have this chest, he though, seeing as no one ever came to a bar to order freshly\n\nsqueezed lemon juice.     \"Dragons?\" The girl asked, mystified. Her eyes widened, not in fear this time, but in amazement. \"But why would dragons want to guard oranges?\" She asked a moment later, as the bartender brought out a mug and oranges.\n\n\"Well, oranges are the most delicious fruit, and the dragons know it. So in order to get the oranges, we need to defeat the dragons!\" The bartender explained, using his imagination for the first time in a while.\n\n\"Wow\" The girl replied, now trying to balance herself on one of the bar stools. When the orange juice was placed in front of her, she eagerly drank it, respecting the brave knights who allowed her to have it.\n\nThe bartender chuckled softly, knowing no other child would eagerly drink bitter orange juice like she did. \n   The fight outside has escalated, the bartender could see this through the window to his right. They had begun to draw swords and the\n\nshouting had intensified. \n    But in the bar, the child looked up at him with innocent eyes. Forgetting the danger her father could be  in and instead, entranced in a story of dragons and oranges.\n\nOf course, the mug had a bottom. And she soon found it. Her attention was lost almost instantly and she began to turn towards the window once again. \n   Quickly thinking, the bartender grabbed a pumpkin from the chest of fruits and plopped it onto his\n\nhead. Cutting off every sense he had. \n   \"Mmmffmfmfm\" he tried to mumble in order to get her attention. Thankfully she looked around and giggled at the sight of him. \n   Despite his embarassment, the bartender was glad he drew her\n\nattention away for just a moment. \n   For it was in that moment that her father snapped the masked mans neck and left him lifeless on the ground. \n   It was an image the child would never have to see, and that was worth the pumpkin becoming stuck to his\n\nhead.\n   Once the fight was over, and the father had rummaged through the corpse's possessions, he came to collect her. \n   She sat on the bar stool looking up at the man with the pumpkin head. Giggling to herself even as her father\n\nwalked in with a bloody nose and battle scars all across his arm and legs.\n   \"You think this is funny?\" He asked angrily, walking up to her and pulling her off of the bar stool. \n   She had little time to explain as he picked her up and took her out.\n\nThe bartender waved her goodbye, and she waved back. The father just carried on walking.", ""),
        StaticBook("Prophecy.", "§bMuildir", "Second Extract of Prophecy From the Kha.\n\nThe priests gain a prophecy not of prophecy of images, but of words. The shamans do as well.\n\nThe first cryptic message is as follows: \nOrigins are all but absolute.\n\nWe've not past my own dispute. \n\nStrands of fate now do entwine, both minds and soul are my design. \n\nSafeguard not my children near, mine is the vessel of love and fear.\n\nPity not the weight of strain, I do this time and time again.\"\n\nEnd first message.\n\nBegin second message:\n\nFruits of life do beg my pardon, roaming astray my endless garden.\n\nMy will sees metal turn to rest, and grow tall from all but dust.\n\nFind me not in book nor tome, for I'm the breath of life and home.\n\nForge noble beasts and kinds that reign. I do this time and time again.\n\nEnd second message", ""),
        StaticBook("The Blah", "Valmir_", "The Blah\nby Unknown\n\nIntroduction:\n\nThe Blah, as you probably already know, is the language of the Orcs. I advise you to use much discretion when speaking this to Orcs themselves. The reason being that they may take great offense in this which could lead to a situation you do\n\nnot want to be in. Instead, use the information in this book to better understand and communicate with them.\n\nMaterial:\n\nFirst, a bit of history and explanation about the Blah. You see the reason this language came to be is because Orcs are unable to pronounce words like we can due to their tusks. Although, they needed a quick and effective way to quickly\n\nunderstand each others in battle. This lead to them using growls, grunts, and snarls to communicate between each other, which eventually lead to the dialect and words they use in the Blah word meshed in where its meaning fits. This is another reason I\n\nadvise not to try and speak the Blah. The dialect of common language of Orcs is hard to reproduce correctly since it is done naturally by their tusks. Now that you have an understanding of the Blah: I shall show you some words and their meanings.\n\nFirst off, their words for the numbers one through nine:\nAsh: One\nDub: Two\nGakh: Three\nFuth: Four\nH’: Fuve\nH’ash: Six\nH’dub: Seven\nH’gakh: Eight\nH’futh: Nine\n\nNext, their words for the table of tens. Basically the first nine numbers with the suffix ‘ty’ or ‘rty’ at the end:\nAshety: Ten\nDubty: Twenty\nGakhty: Thrity\nFuthety: Forty\nH’ety: Fifty\nH’ashety: Sixty\nH’dubty: Seventy\nH’gakhty: Eighty\nH’futhety: Ninety\n\nI am not aware of a higher number other than h’futhety although I’m sure there is one. Also remember that some of these higher numbers may be slightly off due to the fact they aren’t said as much as the lower numbers. The correct intermingling of these\n\nnumbers is just like in common tongue ‘twenty-one’. To say this in Blah, you would say ‘Dubty’ash’.\n\nNow then as I said, you will most likely never hear pure Blah, but usually a dialect of common tongue. So it is your responsibility to understand the\n\ncommon words they say. Here is a list of words of the Blah you are most likely to hear, categorized with their meanings.\n\nGreetings and Farewells:\n\nUg: Hail/Hey/Hello\nThrom’ka: Formal greeting\nGug’ye: Goodbye\nDabu: Yes/My pleasure (obedient, respectful)\n\nResponses and answers:\n\nYub: Yes\nNub: No\nRulg: Thanks\n\nNouns:\n\nObjects and Things\n\nLusk: Axe\nO’lig: Bow\nLigz: Arrow\nZult: Sword\nStik: Staff\nMojo: Magic\nSteemiez: Redstone technology\n\nLiving and Undead Things\n\nBuub: Pig\nHowlur: Wolf\nBrudda: War Uzg Orc\nStowt/Gazat: Dwarf\nTwiggie/Treeugger/Albai : Elf\nSqueal/Snaak: Halfling\nQuikspawn/Breedurs/Shara: Human\nGlob: Fool\nSnaga: Slave\nNuutshara: Ascended\n\nNubded: Undead\nBuubshara Nubded: Zombie Pigman\n\nPlaces and Locations\n\nUzg: World\nGoi: City\nBlarg: Home\n\nAdjectives:\n\nBubhosh: Great/Big\nNubhosh: Bad/Small\nPushdug: Stinky\nFlat: Dead\nBuurz: Dark\n\nPronouns:\n\nLat: You\nMi: Me/I\n\nConjuntions:\n\nAgh: And\n\nOther:\n\nSkah/Saahkah: Curse word\n\nThank you for reading this book and I hope you learned much from it.", ""),
        StaticBook("JayasJourney C1", "§bSofetios", "Jaya's\n        Journey\n\n            ~By Sofetios\n                  Jayamen\n\n(( This is a book I have worked on on and off for years. I've currently lost motivation to continue and hope you all will help bring it back.))\n\n      Chapter One\n\n A Walk in the Woods\n\n“Mom!” I yelled as I went out the back door. “I’m going out to the woods!”\n\n“Fine Honey!” My mom yelled back. “Just be back before dusk ok?”\n\n“Sure Mom!” I answered. I put on my sword, closed the back door, and headed out. Knowing exactly where I was going as I ventured more into the woods. As I walked I couldn’t help but notice how nice everything was today.\n\nFrom the glistening emerald green leaves leaving a slight greenish tint on the ground, to the random scuttles and noises coming from the woods, it just seemed like it was going to be a good day. I approached the usual spot I hung out at near dusk.\n\nA small opening with a flat rock and a small clear pool in the middle. It wasn’t much but I always thought better here. I laid down on the rock looking up into the trees and begin to wander off in my head.\n\nI was about to dose off when I heard something. I sat up quickly. It wasn’t a normal sound. It sounded like the song that Linink played on the piano at the Festival, only it was on a flute. Cautiously, I got up and went in the direction of the sound.\n\nIt got louder and louder as I went along through the trees and bushes until I reached another larger clearing. I looked amazingly at what I saw. There was a Statue in the middle of the clearing with multiple statues around the clearing.\n\nThey all looked just like the one in the middle of town, except in different poses. The one in the middle had his arms outstretched in front of him.\n\nI went closer and saw that in it’s his hands outstretched was a Bow, Arrows, A sword, a dagger, and a scroll. Cautiously I went up closer to the statue and was about to take the scroll when suddenly the music stopped and a voice said,\n\n“Hey! Boy! What are you doing here” Startled I jumped back and turned to face an old man.\n\n“I’m sorry!” I said shocked. “I was just going to look at it! I swear!” The Old man had a frown on but then smiled and said.\n\n“Well why didn’t you say so? Go ahead and take a look.”\n\n“Wait… what?” I said surprised.\n\n“Go on, take a look.” Said the old man again still smiling.\n\n“Um… ok…” I said confused, turning to face the statue. I slowly took the scroll and opened it. Written on it was… nothing.  I frowned and looked back but the old man was gone. Only in his place was a flute.\n\nI scratched my head, went to it, and picked it up. As I touched it I heard the music start again but this time, it was in my head. Shocked again I dropped the flute, the scroll, and the music stopped.\n\nCuriously I picked up the flute and tried to play the notes I had heard. I had played the flute many times before but this time felt different somehow. As I finished playing the notes nothing seemed to happen.\n\nI wondered what I was expecting to happen. Once I waited about a minute I bent down and picked up the scroll. Only this time there was something written on it. Curiously I examined the scroll.\n\nIt had a few lines of music notes on it and the title of it was called “Song of the Rain”. The music notes where different from the ones I had just played, so I began to play these ones.\n\nAs I played it sounded like a stormy night at sea. When I completed it, nothing seemed to happen. After a minute I walked to the statue, wondering if it would be a good idea to take the sword. Suddenly a Voice behind me said,\n\n“Would you look at that! You’re a natural at the flute.”\n\nShocked, I turned to see the old man again, this time he had a bird on his shoulder. He had the same smile on his face. \n“Where do you keep coming from?” I said.\n\nSeeming to ignore the question the old man looked at the weapons the statue had.\n\n“I see you like those weapons?” Said the old man. \n\n“Yea. They look amazing.” I said turning to the statue.\n\nThen looked at the face and said,” But… where they his?”\n\n“What do you mean?” Said the old man. “You’re the one wearing them.”\n\n“What do you mean?” I said turning to the old man again.\n\nBut he was gone. I turned back to the statue that had the weapons but they were gone. Suddenly I saw something on myself. I looked down and there was a sword on my belt, but it wasn’t my sword, it was the statues.\n\nI looked to the other side of my belt and there was the dagger. I slowly reached up and touched my shoulder. As I did I felt the feathers of an arrow and the string of a bow.\n\nI then realized it was dusk, my mom would be annoyed if I wasn’t home soon. I took off the weapons, put them back on the statues hands, and began to walk home.\n\nAs I walked home I noticed the air began to feel denser and the wind began to pick up a little bit. Suddenly. I felt a raindrop. I looked up and one hit me on my forehead. I started running as fast as I could toward the house.\n\nAs I got in the back door my mom was standing there with her arms crossed. \n\n“Where have you been?” She said sternly. “You’re late and your soaked head to toe!”  All I could say was,\n\n“I don’t know.”\n\n“Jaya.” Said my mom in a warning voice. \n\nI sighed and recounted the whole story about the old man, the weapons, the flute and the scroll. As I finished my mom looked pale.\n\n“Are you alright?” I said. She walked slowly to a kitchen chair and sat down.\n\n“Jaya.” My mom began. “I’m going to have you see Linink.”\n\nLinink was the best doctor around and also the leader of the adventurer’s guild, a guild that helps people and goes on quests. My friends Sofetios and Sofia go there.\n\n“Wait, why?” I said concerned. “Do you think I’m sick?”\n\n“No Jaya.” My mom said. “It’s about something else. I think it’s time you went to bed.” Confused and concerned, I went to bed.\n\nThank you for taking the time to read this book! I will be writing more in the future!\n\nIf you like my writing, please let me know by bird or in person!\n\nAlso, feedback on this story would be appreciated.\n~Sofetios Jayamen", ""),
        StaticBook("GOM: Vol I", "§bValmir", "Game of Minds: Volume I\nby Sofetios\n\nAwakening\n\nPulsing. That is all I felt as I started to see again. Everything was a hazy black, even though my eyes were open. Another pulse happened inside my head. Things were beginning to become clearer. I could make out that I was in a small\n\nstone room... and there was something else in here with me.\n\n“Finally awake are we?” said a gruff voice.\n\nI could now see moderately well and saw a person sitting across from me looking straight at me. I coughed and said slowly, “Where am I?”\n\nMy head was still throbbing, though getting better.\n\nThe person then said, “You’re in the holding chamber, along with me.”\n\n“Holding chamber?”, I said, “Holding chamber for what?”\n\n    At that moment there was a slight creak to the right, as a part of the wall opened up like a door. The person got up and came to me, holding out a hand. He said, “We had better get going. They don’t like it when we stall.”\n\nI grasped his hand and he\n\nhoisted me to my feet. I nearly fell over but he helped me catch myself. I looked upwards and far above saw there was an opening to the sky. I said, “Who are they?”\n\nThe person helped walk me toward the door.\n\n\"They call themselves... The Followers of\n\nTruth,” he said.\n\nWe got to the door and opened it. A burst of cold air came in.\n\nIn the room was only a table that had frost on it, a fireplace to the right that had a metal pan on the fire with what appeared to be a steak on it, a small vase with a\n\nsmall top for an opening was on the floor with a lid next to it, a poufy cushioned chair was next to the fireplace, and there was also another fireplace at the far back of the room.\n\n“Great...” said the person, “A puzzle.”\n\nHe walked with me into the\n\nroom. As we got in the door slammed behind us.\n\n“Can you stand now?”\n\nI nodded slightly as I took my own weight back.\n\n“Good. My name is Jed. And you are?”\n\n\"James,\" I said.\n\nSuddenly I felt an overwhelming hunger as I smelled the smell of cooked steak. I looked to the steak and started to walk over, but as I did Jed caught my arm.\n\n“What?” I asked.\n\n\"The thing you should know about this place that it's a death trap,\" said Jed\n\nwith a serious face.\n\nHe lifted his sleeve and there was a severe gash about a foot long.\n\n“That,” he said, pointing to it, “is what happens when you aren’t careful.”\n\nI nodded, swallowing.\n\n\"We had best get to solving this. Before the cold kills\n\nus.\"\n\nI hadn’t noticed but my toes were starting to get numb.\n\n“What should we be looking for?” I asked.\n\n“A key to get back into the room we came in,” said Jed.\n\n“What?!” I said, “We were just in there?”\n\n“Trust me, James,” said the man, “We are better off in here for the moment. What you need to understand is that The Followers of Truth are ruthless. If you don't do what they want you to do, they will make you do it, one way or another. Put your ear to\n\nthe door.”\n\nI went to the door and put my ear on it like he said to. There were clicking sounds in the room. Like a giant insect walking in there.\n\n“Hear that?” said Jed, “That’s the Grimmer.”\n\nI got my head of the door and said, \"The Grimmer?\"\n\n“Yes,” said Jed, “A fearsome thing, they release it through the ceiling in the room to make sure we are out.”\n\nThen a thought occurred to me, “How do they know we are still alive?”\n\nJed shrugged then said, \"Well, if the Grimmer doesn't come back early I\n\nguess that means we are still alive. Either way we better find the key to the door. Before they push us to find it. Now where is that key... Or to hide something else. Always test things.”\n\nJed took a glove off and went to the couch. I followed but at a\n\ndistance. Jed, a few feet from the couch, tossed it on the seat. Suddenly there was a click. The cushion rose at an incredible speed to the ceiling, crushing the glove, then lowered back to position. The cushion didn’t even flatten, like it was rock hard.\n\nThe glove fell on the floor. Jed looked to me, nodded and said, “See?” As he picked up and put his glove back on. “Never touch things directly.”\n\nI took off my own glove went to the jar on the floor. I kind of whacked it with my glove. It just knocked\n\nover... and something clanked inside it. Jed looked to me and said, “Be careful.”\n\nI put my glove back on, picked up the jaw and looked in the opening. The key was inside it.\n\n“The key is in here!” I said.\n\nI turned the jaw upside-down and the key came out... a little. It was stuck. Jed let out a small grunt, “They never make it that easy.”\n\nSuddenly there was a trickling and hissing sound coming from the right fireplace. There was a small amount of water\n\ncoming above the fireplace. Jed cursed under his breath, I then panicked. I tried to smash the vase against the floor.\n\n“Stop!” said Jed.\n\nThe vase landed on the ground in my hand with a large thump, but didn’t break.\n\n“Careful, you idiot! That could have been filled with glass as well as the key.”\n\n“Well what are we supposed to do?” I said in a panicked voice.\n\n“Not panic. That’s what they want us to do, we need to think,” he replied.\n\nI forced myself to relax.\n\nJed then said after a moment, “I’ve got it! Put it on the cushion.”\n\n    I rushed over and tossed it on the cushion. The cushion rose again with great speed and there was a loud clunk. The cushion went back down and the vase, still whole, rolled off it.\n\nJed cursed again, “So it’s unbreakable.”\n\nJed then angrily threw his glove at the frosted table. As it hit the side, it stuck and turned frosted too. I came to a sudden realization.\n\n“The water!” I said.\n\n\"Yes, I know,\" said Jed looking down at the\n\nground, which had water rising a half inch above it.\n\n“No, I mean—” I didn’t explain. I ran to the jar, picked it up and the lid. I ran to the fireplace that was now extinguished and filled it with water, then screwed on the lid. I turned to Jed who\n\nlooked at me and looked like he just realized what I was doing and nodded. I hurried to the table and tossed the jar at the side.\n\nAs it made impact it stuck frosted, then in a few short seconds the jar exploded. Shards went everywhere.  Startled, I\n\nyelled and was knocked back on my backside. A few cut me on my arms and legs from the jar shards.\n\n“Jed! Are you alright?”\n\nI heard a few curses from the back of the room.\n\n“I’m fine,” said Jed. “I should have seen that coming.”\n\nI saw that there was a solid bit of ice in the shape of the vase on the floor near the table, and inside was the key. I picked it up and headed to the extinguished fireplace, picking up the pan. I didn’t head to the chair to smash the ice because I didn't\n\nwant to risk breaking the key.\n\nBy now the water was an inch and a half deep and I couldn’t feel from my ankle down. I ran carefully to the other fireplace, which was luckily a bit raised off the ground, but not much.\n\nI put the pan over the fire and the\n\nice on top of it. The pan was about two inches deep. Jed came behind me. After about a minute the pan was full of water, but the ice wasn’t melted all the way.\n\nI took the ice in one hand and tossed the water in the pan on the ground with the other, then\n\nput the ice back on the pan and started melting it again. After another minute the key was free. I took it and went to the door where Jed was not with his ear on the door. He took his head off the door and said, “The Grimmer isn’t there anymore.”\n\nI unlocked it and opened it. The Grimmer wasn’t in there. I went into the room and Jed followed me, but suddenly the door closed, there was a hissing sound, like air through a tight space. I started coughing, as if the air was bad. So did Jed.\n\nThen everything went black.", ""),
        StaticBook("Odd Events C2", "§bSofetios Jayamen", "Odd Events\n\nA fictional book series with a bit of horror\n\n          ~By Sofetios\n                Jayamen\n\n      Chapter Two\n        The Music\n\nI stayed awake for two days, fearing to go to sleep in case something else like that person with the light coming from their eyes was here. What was I going to do?\n\nMy parents turned to stone and I had no Idea of how to turn them back. It was starting to turn to night again. I went to my parents room and sat down on the bed.\n\nhough when I sat down, I sat on something that felt like paper. I jumped back off the bed and looked where I had sat. There was an Envelope. Carefully I took the envelope off the bed and opened it. Inside was... A key.\n\nI examined the key and noticed four letters. They read B. E. D. A. I was more then tired, I was exausted. I simply sat down and stared at the staircase with the key and the mirror in my hands, not sure what to expect.\n\nI felt my head dropping but caught myself. I couldn't let myself fall asleep now, not when things like the thing in the attic might exist.\n\nMy head was drooping again and I was about to give in to sleep when I heard something. The slight tinkling of what sounded like a piano.\n\nThat was odd, I had examined everywhere in the house in the last three days looking for any rooms like the attic, and found no piano in any of them.\n\nCarefully, I got off the bed and out into the hallway, the mirrors face pointed outward from me in my hands. O followed the sound until I got to the end of the hallway. The music was four notes playing continuously in a pattern.\n\nThe music was coming from the wall, yet there was no door. Confused, I looked to the mirror. It had shown me things that weren't there before, maybe it would work again. I turned away from the wall and put the mirror face facing me.\n\nIn the reflection I saw myself, but I also saw a door behind me that wasn't there when I looked before. I turned around and jumped back. There was now a door right where the music was coming from.\n\nCarefully I turned the knob, but it seemed to be stuck, or... Locked. I looked down to the key in my other hand and tried fitting it into the keyhole. It fit, so I turned it, and right as it clicked, the music stopped.\n\nI froze. Did whatever was in there now know I was there? I slowly took the key out and put it in my pocket. Then Held the mirror in front of me with one hand and opened the door with my other one.\n\nIn the room was a piano and some music sheets on the floor. I didn't see anyone or anything else in the room though.\n\nI slowly walked up to the piano. I saw that it had the names of the white keys imbedded into them. I hesitated, then played C, D, E, F, G, A, B, then C again.\n\nNothing seemed to happen.  I began to think coming here was a bad idea, so I turned and went to the door. I twisted the handle, but it was locked again. So I quickly took out the key and was about to put it in the lock, when I noticed the letters again.\n\nB. E. D. A... I went back to the piano and played the same notes, B. E. D. A. nothing again seemed to happen, But then the keys I just played repeated themselves without me touching them.\n\nIt started getting faster, faster, and louder. Suddenly I felt a strong breeze, but there was no window. The sheets blew off the ground and started swirling around me. I looked to the door but it wasn't there anymore.\n\nThe sound was now deafening. I yelled for help and then... I woke up.\n\nI sat straight up in my parents bed, holding the mirror. I walked over to the place in the hallway where the door was supposed to be and looked in the mirror to see if the door would appear, but it didnt.\n\nI walked back to my parents room and sat on the bed, sunlight coming in through the window. But as I sat down, I felt something small and lumpy under me.\n\nI sat up and there was a key, with the letters B. E. D. A. on it.\n\nEnd of Chapter Two\n\n“Fear mainly occurs in the absence of knowledge.” ~Sofetios Jayamen\n\nThank you for taking the time to read this book! I'll be writing more in the future!\n\nIf you like my writing, please let me know in person or by bird!\n\n~Sofetios Jayamen", ""),
        StaticBook("The Lion & Mouse", "§bKlaudia Crast", "-=-=-=-=--=-=-=-=-\n\nThe Lion & the Mouse\n\nby Lady Klaudia Crast\n\n------------------\n\nOnce when a lion, the king of the jungle, was asleep, a little mouse began running up and down on him. This soon awakened the lion, who placed his huge paw on the mouse, and opened his big jaws to swallow him.\n\n\"Pardon, O King!\" cried the little mouse.\n\n\"Forgive me this time. I shall never repeat it and I shall never forget your kindness. And who knows, I may be able to do you a good turn one of these days!”\n\nThe lion was so tickled by the idea of the mouse -\n\nbeing able to help him that he lifted his paw and let him go.\n\nSometime later, a few hunters captured the lion, and tied him to a tree. After that they went in search of a wagon, to take him to the animal keep.\n\nJust then the little mouse happened to pass by. On seeing the lion’s plight, he ran up to him and gnawed away the ropes that bound him, the king of the jungle.\n\n\"Was I not right?\" said the little mouse, very happy to help the lion.\n\n-------------------\n\nMORAL: Small acts of kindness will be rewarded greatly.", ""),
        StaticBook("EMERALD Vol. 2", "§bAemyn Verde", "The EMERALD\n         COLLECTION\n                of\n          STORY and\n              SONG\n\n*-*-*-*-]}X{[-*-*-*-*\n\nWritten and Compiled by\n       Aemyn Verde\n            of the\n   Emerald Company\n\nVOLUME TWO:\n-*-*-*-*-*-\n- O! Sweet Maiden of Flotsam-town!\n- Lord Extortion, or, The Flight of the Emerald Company\n\nO! Sweet Maiden of Flotsam-town!\n-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-\nThere once danced a maiden sweet\nFrom Flotsam-town on dainty feet\nFar along the Anthos Highway,\nEach graceful step did bring her my way.\n\nIt was such that I did glance\nUpon the horizon 'cross which she pranced,\nHer golden hair the wind caressed,\nAnd tugged at silken skirt, exposin'\nLegs with which she'd been quite bless'd,\n\nNevertheless! T'was not her clothin'\nThat caught my eye,\n'Twas the allure of her fair eyes!\n\nUpon the lute I played for her;\nShe spun upon her feet - a blur!\nAnd then, as the tune slowly faded,\nShe stopped, panting, in the mud.\n'Twas then that fair complexion,\nShimmering, shaking, took on perfection,\n\nThe shell of that poor peasant lass,\nDid break and fall like shatter'd glass;\nAnd where she once wore woolen rags;\nIn silken white, held an Aengul's flag!\n'Pon golden wings she then ascended,\nAnd there, she sang, her voice so splendid:\n\n\"My thanks for your song,\" she sighs,\n\"The tune so sweet it made me rise,\n\"Back t'wards the heavens gold!\"\nI sat there, shiv'ring in the cold,\nAnd watched her fade right out of sigh,\nOnce upon a lonely night...\n- A.V., 20 TGH 1457\n\nLord Extortion, or,\nThe Flight of the\nEmerald Company\n-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-\nThe situation had sprung up on a night as ordinary as any other; crowds began to flock as the Emerald Company primed for another night of music and merriment. Aemyn, backstage,\n\nplucked the strings of his lute, tuning its strings to perfection. Devon muttered something about how awfully large the crowd was, as Aregon stood upon the stage, calling passersby in to join the already-assembled audience. Laughter filled the crossroads\n\nVekaro and Kvaz as this Master of Ceremonies employed his stand-up charm.\n\nThis atmosphere of mirth swiftly dissipated as a grim-looking figure pushed through the suddenly silent onlookers. From behind his scraggly beard, his curled lips and cold\n\neyes marked him as an oppressor of the poor in spirit; a noble seeking to extort those he deemed 'beneath him' , and, with their taxes, vassalage, and very lives, he sought to pad his stone-cold throne.\n\nFrom between those desiccated, lustful lips\n\nof Ivan Ruthern were spat the egregious words, inquiring,\n\"What are you doing on my land!?\"\nThe members of the Company blinked, turning to each other in confusion. Of what did he speak? Surely we aren't on land that belongs to that horrid, towering keep?\n\nThis was Aemyn's mentality as he descended from the stage... He slapped a hand to the old codger's shoulder, proposing that they take this business elsewhere, that bureaucracy would not disturb their positive energy - their 'vibe'.\n\nAnd so, in the frigid halls of the nest where crows do sleep, the selfish lord did regard, with contempt, the entertainers at his feet. They begged why, at all, there need be such rivalry; why not let them carry on?\n\nNO! The laws of feudalism do provide me with the cause to extort from you taxes, just like any other under my blessed 'protection'! If you wish to remain (living) on that knoll, you will give to me yearly... Three-hundred Minas - Nay! Five-hundred!\n\nBy the end of his tirade, he had settled on three-thousand!\n\nAemyn looked to Aregon; unsure, at first, but swiftly resolution came to the pair. Aemyn cleared his throat, and defiantly stated that they would not bow to his unjust demands; they would\n\nmove elsewhere!\n\n\"Hah! Very well, you poor fools, but hear this! If you have not rid me of your presence by midnight, you will find yourself just that - fools! My steward; go fetch the jester hats; I sense they will soon have someone to entertain!\n\nThe sinister, wrinkled lord cackled as his 'guests' stormed from his lair; but, underestimating the value of brave Aemyn's word, he began compiling a list of lullabies - songs that his mother used to sing to him 'til the very day she died. Not strange in\n\nitself, apart from the odd fact - that she had died just last week, at the criminal hands - or pants, rather, of her son - his noxious gas had killed her in her sleep!\n\nBut the valiant, determined men of the Emerald Company had no intention of\n\nstaying under the oppression of that maniacal twit; they prepared, post-haste, to be, of him, rid. The wagon rumbled far away, behind the graveyard hill, where Aemyn had drunkenly piddled on King Heinrik's grave. The wagon wobbled as it passed the spot\n\nwhere Aemyn had then vomited on Lord Tuvya's chestplate. It was a long time before the wagon stopped in peaceful lands - at least a hundred metres away!\n\nAnd so, now, the merry band entertains beside the walls of grand Vekaro, with the\n\nproud patronage of the great leader Tuvya, who does honour to the cause of song, story, and of mirth. Let his joyous name be extolled as we entertain upon his earth!\n\nBut cursed shall be the House of Ruthern - let it be trampled in the dirt!\n\n- Aemyn Verde\n\n17th T.G.H. 1457", ""),
        StaticBook("May'ilu", "§bValmir", "May’ilu\nBy Unknown\n\nWith a clinking and chiming of bracelets signalling the arrival of her lover, Velara could hardly keep a grin off of her face as she rested her elbows on the furnished wooden counter; hands delicately supporting her head as she watched Mayirr sway into\n\nthe shop, pink hair cascading elegantly down over her precious shoulders. The two stare at each other for a moment; A soft “Karin’ayla” was all that needed saying. They lingered over each others frames for a moment before Mayirr broke the gaze, slipping\n\nlithely around the counter to cuddle Velara from behind. The pink haired elf’s ears twitched sensitively as she held her may’ilu, her cheeks turning a similar colour as they stood there similar colour as they stood there silently. Mere moments passed, and\n\nthe door to the shop rattled open, breaking the two apart. Watching Velara abruptly disappear down to the basement with a look of utter embarrassment, Mayirr smiles, her cheeks flushed with the same feeling as she looks back to greet the customer.", ""),
        StaticBook("Riddles", "§bThe Eternal Library", "Riddles\nBy Unknown\n\nI am known by all,\nThough used little by many.\nI help you see everything clearly,\nBut I am never seen.\nI am feared by the foolish\nBut appreciated by the wise.\nWhat am I?\n\nI’m sometimes white,\nAnd always wrong.\nI can break a heart,\nAnd hurt the strong.\nI can build love\nAnd tear it down.\nI can make a smile,\nBut more often bring a frown.\nWhat am I?\n\nWith no wings, I fly.\nWith no eyes, I see.\nWith no arms, I climb.\nMore frightening than any beast,\nStronger than any foe.\nI am cunning, ruthless and tall;\nIn the end, I rule all.\nWhat am I?\n\nTen Men’s Strength,\nThen Men’s Length,\nTen Men can’t break it,\nYet a young boy walks off with it.\nWhat am I?\n\nForwards I am heavy.\nBackwards  I am not.\nWhat am I?\n\nI am used to bat with,\nYet I never get a hit.\nI am near a ball,\nYet it is never thrown.\nWhat am I?\n\nA skin have I,\nMore eyes than one.\nI can be very nice when I am done.\nWhat am I?\n\nAnswers:\n1)      The Mind’s Eye\n2)      A lie\n3)      The wind\n4)      Rope\n5)      A ton\n6)      Eyelashes\n7)      A potato", ""),
        StaticBook("Creepy Tales V2", "§b[Teen] Mikazuki Mantisuku", "~The Girl in the Mask~\n\nNo one can be sure where she started. One thing was sure, she had long raven colored hair, deep sapphire eyes, a small form, fair skin, and a beautiful mask. The rumors that were spread\n\ncould never fully tell the story about this young girl who only seemed to appear at night. All they did tell was she was not something to be trusted or desire to see. Only one rumor seemed to be most agreed upon.\n\nThe story goes that a young girl lived happily in the lap of luxury with her human parents. She was of noble birth and to be wed to one of the princes. She had everything she wanted.\n\nThere was a masquerade ball made in her honor at her home, everyone was asked to wear masks and she was to see if she could find her \"prince\" among the men that attended.\n\nThe ball went well and the girl was excited. Still being just a young maiden, she was already prideful. She donned a beautiful royal blue velvet gown and lovely powder blue mask. She entered the room, excited and happy.\n\nDancing with glee she soon found a taller boy with a dark mask on his face. \"My prince~\" she whispered silkenly to him as she curtsied. Without a word he bowed and the two began to dance. Dizzy and joyous, she announced she found her prince.\n\nWhen he removed his mask, she was startled to realize it was a serving boy. Terrified, she called her guards and her father had him executed. Months passed and the girl lay in her bed soundly asleep. Her wedding gown near the bed,\n\nready for the next day's ceremony. A shadow fell across the room and a figure moved closer to the girl. Before she had time to scream he covered her face with the mask the serving boy wore to the ball.\n\nA scream ripped through the manor as the shadow vanished. Two guards broke into her room and ripped the mask from her face, only to find it had been laced with a powerful poison that ate at flesh. Horrified and fully maimed, they bandaged her face\n\nand tried to find a healer. Even monks could not reverse the damage that had been done and she was forced to wear a mask to cover her scars. With her fiance leaving her, she was locked away in the manor with only a few things to keep her company.\n\nOne night, she crept out and stole the dress away that she was to wear to her wedding. Donning the dress, she hung herself in her room, no one aware of her death till the next morning.\n\nWhen they went to bury her, the mother opened the coffin to find the body gone. Since that day, the young woman had been seen only at night wailing as she wandered.\n\nThe rumors say, if you were to see her, she would beg you to help her. If you try to remove her mask, you would be found brutally murdered with a pale plain mask on your face. But this is just a horror story meant to scare people at night. Or is it?", ""),
        StaticBook("Ado Revisits", "§bThe Eternal Library", "Ado Revisits\nBy Unknown\n\nHis footsteps echoing on the dark flagstones of the castle, the figure crept through the dark, dank hallways of his former home. As he finished descending the spiral stairs towards the corridor containing within itself his old office, a wave of nostalgia\n\nwashed over him, and he halted himself. Murmuring softly, he traced his fingers along the walls; He grazed over the cold, stone walls and onto the rough wooden beams supporting the structure. He closed his eyes, letting the memories flood his mind. He\n\nstood there for a moment, blissfully unaware of the danger of his situation, with nothing but memories filling his mind. The wood too reminded him of his inescapable Elven heritage, and he withdrew his hand, sighing. He pulled up his black and gold\n\ntrimmed hood as he looked once more behind him, and continued down the hall.", ""),
        StaticBook("Keep Walking", "§bValmir", "Keep Walking: A Tale of Truth\n\nBy Sillion Luthias\n\nHail friend, I am Silion Luthias, and I’m going to tell you a story.\n\nThis particular story happens to be one of great importance to me, for it is the story of me, and my brothers. \n\nWe’ve all been scarred, bruised and crushed by the harshness of reality,\n\nbut we’re also all come together under odd circumstances, and have come traveling companions, and friends to the end.\n\n As I sit underground in my study, I look towards the future, for it’s bright, and full of promise, and untold stories filled with\n\nadventure and hope. \n\nBut to look towards the future, you must keep the past in sight, so to learn of our current adventures, you must know our pasts.\n\nThere are five of us: Caden, Guraim, Gruol, Qwert, and I, Sillion. Each of us have tragedy in\n\nour past, but it has turned us into better people. First, we shall start with Qwert, one of the two Dwarves in our party.\n\nQwert was born in the Farlands, a place I’ve yet to see. His mother died during childbirth, and his father died in a fire trying to\n\nsave Qwert. From there, he was raised by a wolf mother and her cubs, so he was illiterate when he came to us.\n\nFrom there, he moved onwards to Oren, and eventually was brought into our party via Caden, and here he resides still.\n\nNext is Gruol, our Orc friend. Gruol was raised in the Orcish fashion, but joined the Orcish Guard as an adult.\n\nBut during a routine sweep of the lands, the unit Gruol was placed in encountered a group of bandits looking for food amongst a group of\n\nhomes. During the battle, most were slaughtered, but one of the humans in his teens, started running.\nGruol’s captain ordered him to hunt the boy down and kill him, but Gruol refused.\n\nGruol was reported to the Rex, and was discharged immediately. Gruol\n\nwas shamed by his people, family, and country. So he set off into the wilds, looking for redemption and riches. However, I found him, befriended him, and he travels with us as the group powerhouse, and is still looking to return his honor everyday.\n\nNow we move on to my dear friend, Caden. Caden was the second member to join our party and is our swordsman. But his past is the most horrendous of all of ours, and it’s time I document it for the world to know. \nCaden was raised in the Cathaldus Family,\n\none of the most prestigious families in Laurelin. He was taught sword fighting, archery, and perfect English to name a few of the many privelges he had in his childhood.\n\nBut, when he was quite young, his family adopted a young Orc child, I’Shaak.\n\nCaden was raised with him, learning from I’Shaak brutish capabilities, Caden became a force to rechoned with on the battlefield.\n\nHowever, I’Shaak caught a illness in his teen years, and died. This gave Caden a respect for Orcs, and a hole in his heart\n\n that has been left unfilled too long. Then, in his first years of adulthood, a hit was ordered upon family.\n\nCaden was away, training with his blade, when his family was murdered in cold blood in their sleep.\n\nWhen Caden returned that night, exhausted\n\nfrom practice, he found his parent’s corpses strewn with blood and bile sliced open in places along their throats, chest, and stomach.\n\nBut to their dismay, a shred of clothing adorned the bedpost, plastered with blood. But the true color still showed,\n\npurple tinged along the edges with green. It was the flag of a local mercenary company, and only their captain wore the colors.\n\nCaden marched to the local fort. His blade sharpened to a razor edge, and nothing but primal fury, and the lust for revenge\n\nswarming amongst his conscious. He trudged in, busting open then doors, and listened to the sounds of men rowdily drinking, laughing and reveling in a well earned payment, most likely a very large one.\n\nCaden walked into the main dining hall, and stood,\n\n ready to charge.\n\nHe ran his eye across the rows of fighters, and then steadied his gaze upon the only man standing, the captain, adorned with a flowing shirt, with a ripped sleeve. \n\nCaden drew in a breath and screamed, “YOU TOOK MY FAMILIES’ LIVES,\n\nI REQUIRE YOURS IN PAYMENT! YOU PATHETIC BLEMISHES BARELY MAKE THE PAYMENT!”. \n\nCaden then pulled out a bottle of spirits, plugged with a hankerchief. He dipped the flailing hankerchief end into a torch, and hurled it onto the table, fire and glass flew\n\naround, men instantly went up in flames, some from the initial explosion, some from the sparks touching their alcohol drenched garb.\n\nAmongst the chaos, most fled or perished, but the captain stood eye locked with Caden. \n\nThe captain brandished a\n\nbeautiful gilded axe, imbedded with diamonds.\n\nThe pair began stalking towards one another, and the captain swung the massive chunk of metal towards Caden’s throat, but he deftly dropped, and instantaneously drove his blade into the captain’s stomach,\n\nripped the blade left, and stepped back to let his guts splatter on the masonry. As his innards tasted air, he dropped to his knees and feebly tried to return his organs to their rightful place. \n\nHe looked up to Caden, blood seeping through his teeth,\n\nand whispered, “Your father died in his sleep, but your mother was awake by our footfalls. She looked up at us in her nightgown, eyes full of fear, and she screamed. \n\nShe squealed like a swine. I imagine the sound would be like music to you, dagger-ear.”\n\nCaden stared at him with pure fury, then raised his blade, and dropped it through the captain’s spinal cord. His head rolled across the floor, and landed amongst the pile of burnt bodies.\n\nCaden walked back to Laurelin, drenched in blood, dragging his\n\nblade, and staring into the distance, eyes blank. As he entered, he prepared for a hero’s embrace, but was gripped by guards right away. \n\nThey then began dragging him through town, preparing to throw him into prison for the murder of an entire company of\n\nmercenaries. As the men brought him through a cluster of homes for the richer members of town, a politician whose face was lightly covered, looked to be chuckling softly.\n \nCaden was imprisoned but escaped after a small sentence. I found him in the wilds,\n\n crouching near a tree, holding a makeshift stabbing weapon. I coaxed him to me with a loaf of bread. \n\nOnce I got him eating, he told me this story, and I vowed I would help him find the monster\n\nwho hired the hit upon his family, and so he stays with us now.", ""),
        StaticBook("Song Anthology 1", "§bAeran", "Song Anthology: Volume 1\n\nThe Great Pink Haired Man\n\nIt's Always Summer Under the Sea\n\nMaiden of the Tree\n\nThe Great Pink Haired Man\n\nThere once lived a dwarf named Pikel Boldshoulder/\nHis hair, colourful/\nHis heart, much bolder\n\nHe came to us in our hour of need/\nHe lived by a creed, did a great deed/\n\nHe and 4 brave warriors/\nFaced with many barriers\n\nThey ventured into the nether/\nThey did it with great haste/\nOnly 4 were turned to paste\n\nTo defeat the evil Iblees/\nThey tossed an axe into a pit/\nAnd also one of the heroes.../\nShit\n\nHe was a true hero/\nHe asked for no fame,/\nNot even a dame/\n\nSo if you see pink!/\nYou'd better rethink!/\nFor that could be Pikel Boldshoulder/\nAdmittedly, much older\n\nIt's Always Summer Under the Sea\n\nIt's always summer, under the sea/\nI know, oh, oh, oh/\nThe birds have scales, the fish take wing/\nI know, I know, oh, oh, oh/\nThe rain is dry, and the snow falls up/\nI know, I know, oh(x3)\n\nMaiden of the Tree\n\nMy featherbed is deep and soft,/\nAnd there I'll lay you down./\nI'll dress you all in yellow silk,/\nand on your head a crown.\nFor you shall be my lady love,/\n\nand I shall be your lord./\nI'll always keep you warm and safe,/\nAnd guard you with my sword\n\nAnd how she smiled, and how she laughed,\n/the maiden of the tree./\nShe spun away and said to him,/\n\nno featherbed for me./\nI'll wear a gown of golden leaves,/\nand bind my hair with grass,/\nBut you can be my forest love,/\nand me your forest lass.", ""),
        StaticBook("Song Anthology 2", "§bAeran", "Song Anthology: Volume 2\n\nThe Lame Drunk of Abresi\n\nThe Day the Spit Flew\n\nA poor man came to a fair maid/\nSaid ‘I need some work, I need to get paid?’/\nShe said that’s a damn shame/\nFor, he was lame!\n\nThe Lame Drunk of Abresi/\nHe ate messy/\nHe lvied poorly/\n\nAnd used to love a girl named Jessie!\n\nHis beard was down to his tits/\nHe smelt like uncleaned pits/\nBut he said I'm rich, geez/\nIf you counted fleas!\n\nIf you counted teeth,\nnah.\n\nThe Lame Drunk of Abresi/\nHe ate messy/\nHe lived poorly/\nAnd used to love a girl named Jessie/\n\nOne day he saw a great knight/\nHe challenged him to a fight!/\n\nThe great warrior prepared with sword and shield/\nAnd as he took the field.../\n\nThere was the Lame Drunk/\nHe smelt like a skunk/\nFor his smell was his shield/\nHis breath, what he would weild/\n\nThe knight fell, had no choice but to yield/\nHe could not take the field/\nHis helmet was filled with puke/\nHis dismissed the drunk as a cuke!/\n\nThe Lame Drunk of Abresi/\nHe ate messy/\nHe lived poorly/\n\nAnd used to love a girl named Jessie!/\n\nThe Lame Drunk of Abresi/\nHe ate messy/\nHe lived poorly/\nAnd used to love a girl named Jessie/\nAnd damn was he crazy!\n\nThe Day the Spit Flew\n\nIt was a day unlike today/\nExcept, nothing like today\nThe atmosphere was the opposite of gay/\nThe atmospher was yag/\nThe Snow Elves had kidnapped a princess! Or something!/\n\nBut it did not matter, the pale devils would get it!/\nAnd by it I mean completly disproport-\nionate aggression/\nBUT I'LL BE DAMNED IF THEY DIDN'T GET IT!/\n\nTwo kingdoms met infront of another kingdom/\n\nOren, half of their court had come/\nBut all of Snelvedom showed up; Tundrak!/\nIt was a standoff to be sung about maybe when the singer was really drunk or out of songs!/\n\nThey fought with words/\n\nEmperor Chivay drowned out by his court/\nTundrak drowned out by his nation's silence/\nBut alas, no solution came/\n\nSo, with a great 'HORK'/\nAnd a loud 'POOT'/\nHead to toe/\n\nTundrak was covered with spit/\nAnd damn, wasn't it an improvement!", ""),
        StaticBook("The MTG Volume I", "§bThe Agile Man", "Part One: The Beginning\n    There were once seven thieves walking the lands together.They were brothers, sisters and children of chaos. Untouchable by the law, and only caring for the riches and pleasures in life.They travelled for years and years all\n\nacross the lands, plundering and taking everything they could carry, sometimes leaving nothing behind.\n\nTheir riches were great and many, and soon they found themselves in need of a place to rest and stow away their treasures.\n\nThe eldest of the seven suggested they head back for their own home scattered across the lands, but the youngest then declared that they would be recognized at once and sent straight to the gallows. The group began to bicker and argue, yelling so loud as\n\nto alert a nearby group of travelling guards.\nThe men sprang from the darkness, taking the seven by surprise, and soon they were bound and gagged, watching the guardsmen laugh merrily and congratulate each other for the victory. All hope\n\n for them seemed to be lost…. Or so they thought. Out of the blue, the guards dropped dead, arrows embedded in each of their backs. The seven looked around frantically to see a smaller group of men and women, all dressed as they themselves were.\n\nSoon their bonds were cut and thanked the other group copiously. Once they were free the eldest asked why they chose to help them. The other group smiled back, and one of them walked forward and put a hand on the eldest’s shoulder.\n\n “We are family” He said. “And family take care of each other.”\n\nAfter this event took place, the seven finally went their separate ways, but not before it was decided that they would leave their mark on the world in the form of a guild, where anyone could join the family. Most of the seven had blood relatives and\n\n and friends to return to, but not the youngest. This was the only family that Lily Aldadiir knew, so she elected herself to set it up and spread the word.And so the seven went their separate ways, and now Lily finds herself alone for the first in a long\n\ntime. With no one to turn to, she sets out on her own.\n\nPart Two: An Unlikely Encounter\nWith the undead threat reaching a critical state and the recent overtaking of Al’Khazar, Lily found herself on the same path of all the others with no place to go, to the city of Alras, which to her great pleasure seemed to\n\n be bursting with merchants and wealthy folk who would be more than ripe for the picking. After some careful consideration, she decided to settle there for a while, as this town would be the perfect location for a con she had been working on.\n\nAnd with that thought, she begins to plan out her trickery.\n\nAfter a week of further planning, Lily walked through the city gates once more, confident that this job would bring in a lot of Minas to go toward the creation of the guild.\n\nShe walked to the docks then eyed the crowd and smiled as she spied a fair few potential targets. She then strolled confidently up to the first.\nFor the next few days she pulled many people into her scam.\n\nToday was the last day she would be out here however, and then tomorrow she planned to pack up and leave.\nOnce again she eyed the crowd, her glance skimming across the faces, and finally stopping to stay on one.\nLily squinted at the man.\n\n He was athletically built and wearing well-tailored clothing that counted him as a potential target, but the thing that really caught her eye was his mask.\nHe was speaking with a young child, who looked as if he was lost.After a while,\n\n when the two had parted ways, Lily followed him, and decided to confront him when he stopped at an expensive jewel store.A man who could afford those would certainly be an acceptable target. Lily strode over to the man who looked at her quizzically\n\n before asking, “May I help you?”\n“No,” Lily replied brightly, “But I think I may be able to help you.”\n“How so?” he asked amused.\n“I have a keen eye, and you look like a man who is out looking for expensive items at a more reasonable price then\n\nwhat you’ll find here,” She gestured toward the sparkling jewels, “which is something I happen to be doing.”\nThe man looked as if he was losing interest so she continued on quickly.“I have a keen eye, and you look like a man who is out looking for\n\nexpensive items at a more reasonable price then what you’ll find here,” She gestured toward the sparkling jewels, “which is something I happen to be doing.”\nThe man looked as if he was losing interest so she continued on quickly.\n\n“I am a merchant who is selling some very rare alchemy ingredients. First rate stuff too. And for just a small amount of what it would normally cost, I will give you a selection of everything. You can pay me in advance and I will use those Mina to ensure\n\n that the cargo is delivered safely. You see it is still currently on its way here by ship.”\nThankfully he seemed to regain interest at this.\n“How much would this cost?”\n“Only 350 Minas.”\n\nThe man thought deeply for a moment then said, “Alright, I will buy some from you.”\n“Fantastic! We shall meet here again in a weeks time, for that’s when it should arrive, and I will give you your items.”He handed over the money then they both\n\nwent their separate ways for now.\n\nA week later Lysle Rigger arrived at the same place where he was supposed to meet the woman. She had been selling the ingredients at a very cheap price for what they were really worth,\n\n and so buying them from her would almost be theft in it’s own way. He frowned, disappointed that taking them from her wasn’t more of a challenge, but no matter, she hadn’t given any information away regarding the whereabouts of the items to be delivered,\n\n so he would just have to pay for them.\nLysle patiently waited for her to return, but when she did not, he began to grow suspicious. He returned there for the next few days, in case she was help up in her journey, but still she did not show.\n\n On the fifth day, he realized what had happened, and cursed the deceptive woman. Lysle then left Alras angrily, not returning for another month, but when he did return, he saw a familiar face in the crowd.\n\nLily walked through the streets of Alras quickly, searching for her prize all the while unaware of her follower. She sighed relieved when she saw what she was looking for, and picked up a small necklace off the ground. “There you are..”\n\nshe said quietly, then once again walked away. Lysle followed her to a small park, where she stopped and examined the trinket. Lysle unsheathed his dagger, then walked up behind her, effectively cornering her in.\n“Hello again Ma’am”\n\nAt the sound of his voice Lily spun around sharply, then backed up at the sight of his blade.\n“It’s been well over a week now.”\nLily remained silent trying to think up an excuse, but he had caught her off-guard, and so all she was able to do was stare at\n\n him in silence, carefully watching his movements. He was holding the blade threateningly but lazily toward her, and with his other hand he was flipping a coin, over and over in his palm.\n“I think I smell a Con-Artist.  Why so quiet?\n\n Suddenly you lose your tongue when you need it the most?”\nLily finally found her voice, “Well pull a blade on me and you won't find me so co-operative”\n“Maybe so, but I find fear is a an effective weapon. I never intended to harm you.”\n\nLily glanced down at the dagger and then back up at him again, raising a speculative eyebrow. “Your blade says otherwise”\nLysle then sheathed his dagger.\n“Thank you\"Lily leaned up against the tree next to her,\n\n and began to fiddle with the charm in her hand. “You may be right in your assumption about me, but I also can see that you yourself are not the most noble citizen. So, how about we make a deal? I give you your money back,  as well as half of the profits\n\nI made from this scam, and you let me walk away from here.”\nHe considered it for a moment before saying “Deal.”Lily then unstrapped a coin pouch from her belt and threw it at him lazily. He caught it and tucked it away. “That should cover it.”\n\n“Good, now perhaps we should go our separate ways before a guard shows up.”\nLily stood upright once more “Agreed.”\n“Well then, farewell….” He trailed off and looked at her as prompting for a response.\n“Lily. And yours?”\n\n“You may call me The Upright Man. Perhaps one day I will explain, but for now, goodbye Lily.”\nAnd with that he turned on his heel and strode away. Lily watched him leave, amused, then she as well disappeared into the night.\n\nPartners Three: Partners in Crime\nFor the next month, the two did not meet again. Lily spent those days making plans for the guild, however the thrill of the job was calling to her once more. Tired of doing nothing but planning, Lilly set out for some\n\n more practical work.\n \nIt was just turning to dusk in Whispering Isles, as Lysle returned to The Hollow Peach Inn, plotting where was to be his target for tonight. The people around here are well off, and very naive.\n\nAs he opened the door to the inn, he was a little surprised to see Lily sitting at a table on the balcony. She had her back to him, and not wanting to be seen here, Lysle turned quietly and walked back out the door. However he was not so lucky.\n\nAlmost a week later, a pigeon arrived at the Hollow peach inn. It sat on the gate at the entrance, quietly cooing as Lysle stopped in front of it.Out of curiosity, he untied the note around its leg and was surprised to see the letter was addressed to the\n\nUpright Man. Now frowning, he unrolled the paper to read the message.\n\n“Hello again. If you are interested, meet me at the Laurelin gate today. I would like to discuss a business opportunity with you.\n~ Lily”\n\nLysle folded the note and put it in his pocket. This should be interesting.\n\nLily sat at the Laurelin gate, high up on an old tree root, humming quietly to herself. When she sent the letter, she wasn’t sure that he would show up, or even if the bird found him. She was sure that it was him she saw in Whispering Isles that day.\n\nA short while later, she heard someone approaching and looked over to see The Upright Man walking casually toward her. “Hello, how are you today?”\nLily smiled and jumped down from the root and replied, “I am well. What about yourself?”\n\n“Well, thank you\"\nLily chuckled at the exchange of pleasantries and then beckoned to him to follow her away from the road, and to a more private, and enclosed garden nearby. There, in the most secluded part of the garden, Lily turned to face him.\n\n“Here should do”\n“Now, what’s this… business opportunity you spoke of?\n“Well, judging from our last meeting we can both safely say that neither of us are what you would call model citizens.\n\nYou must have a good eye if you can catch me in the act, so I propose a partnership of sorts. I’m sure I could use your talents, and I could definitely help you in your line of work, which I’m sure isn’t even remotely honest…”\n\nLysle pondered this for a moment. Perhaps a good partnership could become of this meeting.\n\nTo be Continued.", ""),
        StaticBook("The MTG Volume 2", "§bThe Agile Man", "Part Three: Partners in Crime\n- Continued\n\n“What do you say? You scratch my back and I scratch yours?” Lily extended her hand toward him and Lysle grasped and shook it.“Deal. Though I must make it clear that this is a strictly professional relationship, and do not expect for\n\nme to give you any information about myself. This is all just a game to me.”\nAt this Lily laughed, “That’s alright by me, whatever helps to keep you sane. So if I need to contact you, shall I just send you a bird at The Hollow Peach?”\n\n“Aye, I frequent that area”\n“Alright then, I shall contact you. I dare say that I might be harder to find.”\nLysle turned and began to walk away “We’ll see about that. Farewell.”\nAnd with that, the two parted ways once more.\n\nPart Four: A Precious Painting\nIt was almost a year after Lily and Lysle met near Laurelin, before the two made contact again.\nA courier approached Lily on The Kings Road one day, and he handed her a letter before rushing off again.\n\n Curious, Lily opened the letter and read:\n‘I have a proposal to make, come to Whispering Isles, I’ll meet you there.’‘I have a proposal to make, come to Whispering Isles, I’ll meet you there.’\n\nShe frowned as she folded the note and tucked it away, and then set out in the direction of Whispering Isles.\nIt did not take long to get there, and once she did, she noticed Lysle, who was standing to the side of the path.\n\nLysle dragged his thoughts away from his plans when he saw a masked woman approach him casually. “Hello again” she drawled lazily. Lysle looked her up and down. It was a while since they had spoken,\n\n and her mask made it difficult to tell, but he was sure this was Lily. “Alright, follow me.” He motioned for her to follow and then after a short walk, lead her over to an old house. He walked around the back to a large window, which he then broke\n\n with his elbow, and climbed inside.\nLily climbed in after him, and was surprised to see two others in there already. Both were cloaked and masked, and they seemed to be waiting for The Upright Man’s return.\n\n“Right, we’re all here now. And what will I be calling you two?” He gestured toward the two men.\n“I’m Silex for the mission”\n“Dunes Walker. Just call me Dune when things heat up though”\nSilex looked over at Lily, “And this is?”\n\nThe Upright Man glanced over as well “A friend”\nLily looked from Dune to Silex and back again, “I was going to ask you both the same question”\n“They’re colleagues, just as we are.” Lysle looked around the room at them,\n\n the continued on confidently, “Now that’s enough chit chat, I have an important matter to discuss. I have a scheme I have been working on for quite a while. I plan to break into the King’s vault, and take the only portrait of The Wandering Wizard\n\n with me when I go. It should be quite a challenge and why not try the fun?”\nLily looked at him in surprise, but he continued on. “I was hoping we could all work together on this, I already know my way in. Though I need distractions and such.”\n\nThere was a moment of silence, then Silex spoke first, “Sounds interesting. I’m in, no second thoughts.”\n“Ahh good.” Lysle looked over at Dune who said “I’ve got your back.”\nLysle nodded at him, “But know this, I’m not in it for the Mina,\n\nonly for the challenge.\"\nily remained silent, and bit down on her bottom lip. He hasn’t revealed any type of plan, and she feared that improvisation might indeed be it. She looked up at Lysle,\n\n “Are you sure that you know what you’re doing? That your plan will succeed?”\n“Oh there always will be the possibility of defeat, but it’s worth it. ‘Tis all good sport. Now come, I’ll take you to the meeting place of which we will all meet before the\n\n heist”\nThe group followed The Upright Man from the house, and along the Kings Road.\nThey stopped to the east of Alras near a large tree farm, and Upright turned to face them. “We’ll meet up here, and whatever you think will help us, bring it.”\n\n“Alright. Travel light I assume?” Silex asked\n“Aye.”\nLily nods, “Alright.”\nWe shall meet here in a day and a half.” Lysle then bowed and pulled a stone from his pocket, turning it in his palm. Now the game begins.\n\n\nThe dwarves attack on Alras seemed to come at the perfect time for the group. In the confusion during the aftermath of the battle, Lysle, Dune and Lily were able to access the keep with the only hindrance being a locked door.\n“Damnit.”\n\nLysle exclaimed as the lock-pick broke in two. He pulled out another and tried again, leaving Lily a few moments with her thoughts.Silex had not shown up at the designated meeting spot on time, so they had gone on without him. And she had\n\nintroduced herself to Dune, under the Alias of The Red Raven.\nLily looked over as she heard the lock click.“Here we are.” Upright muttered, “Alright follow me this way.”They crept through the Keep, with eyes wide open, searching for any signs of trouble.\n\n Staircase after staircase they climbed up, until they reached a large crescent-shaped hallway.“Let’s split up here, look around for any possible entrances.”Not too long after they had split, Lily heard The Upright Man call out softy\n\n “Over here, I think I’ve found it.”\nHe lead both her and Dune up a flight of stairs and into a large, circular, tower room, and in the middle, was a wooden plaque. Upright walked over to it then touched it. He immediately disappeared.\n\n Dune went next, then Lily. As soon as she touched it, it transported her down, into a very grand room, filled with chests that were piled up right to the ceiling. She had to steady herself before falling into a dark pit that lay just before her feet.\n\n She stood next to another plaque in the center of a narrow cross, which acted as bridging across the pit “Hm? What was that?”\nLily jumped at the voice, for it belonged to neither Upright nor Dune. She scurried along the narrow bridge the plaque sat upon,\n\n and quickly ducked behind a chest. In the distance she could see a guard walking cautiously along one of the bridges. She looked around her and saw Dune crouching behind a stack of chests, and Upright, who was over the other side of the room,\n\n hurrying to find some cover.The guard walked across the pit and disappeared into the sea of boxes and chests. She and Dune then both hurried away looking for some better cover. Lily then heard the lid of a chest slam shut,\n\n and peeked up over a nearby crate only to see the guard looking straight in her direction, she immediately ducked back down again, but it was too late. He strode over, and Lily got ready to make a break for it. A few quiet moments passed,\n\n and her ears strained for the sound of his footsteps...There! He was coming around to the left. Lily quickly moved right, but the damage had been done.“Aha!” He exclaimed when he saw her dash around. Out of the corner of her eye she saw\n\n Dune move and quickly grabbed him from behind. The guard struggled for a moment before yelling “Thieves! There are thieving scum in the vault!” He then broke free and turned to face Dune. “Help! Down in the Vault!”\n\nA few moments later and King Syrio of Alras appeared yelling out to his guards. “Shoot them! Don’t let them escape!”\n“Run! Get out of here!” Upright yelled across the room as he made a dash for the plaque, with a covered painting under his arm.\n\nIn the confusion, Dune and Lily both made a mad dash toward it and could not be more relieved when they grabbed it, and were swiftly transported back to the tower room.\n\nAll three ran to the door and sprinted down the stairs. Upright quickly handed them both an enderpearl before throwing one himself, out a window and across onto a different section of the keeps roof.\n\n He was instantly transported across then yelled out, “Throw it!”They both hurled the pearls across the gap and in a blink of an eye were both transported across.\nIn less of a hurry now, they made their way down from the roof and into the corridor below.\n\nThe Upright Man peered out a nearby window and spotted the bridge that connected the Keep to Alras. “Alright, we go down this way.” And he climbed out the window onto the small ledge outside. Lily hesitated but followed out the window next to it,\n\n and Dune climbed onto the same one as Upright. Lily braced herself against the wall, as the ledges were slippery with ice. Upright clutched the painting tightly, took a deep breath and stepped back as far as he could go. Upright moved forward quickly,\n\n but just as he was about to jump his feet lost their grip and he slipped on the ice. Dune lunged forward as Upright flew over the edge and grabbed his feet, but in the process, he managed to slip over as well.  This left Lily, who hurled\n\n herself after Dune, grabbing his leg with one hand, and wrapping the other arm around the window frame, bracing herself from falling.They were all silent for a moment, but soon Upright began to laugh.\n\n “Red, do you think you could swing us forward?”\nLily blinked in astonishment. “What? Why?”“I could reach the bridge, all I need is some forward momentum. If you try to swing us both, and Dune, if you throw me at the same time I could reach that bridge.”\n\nDune nodded “Alright, I don’t see any other choice.”He was right. She would not be able to pull them up by herself. And if he reached if safely, he could help both of them across. “Fine. Ready?”\nHe nodded and she cried out\n\n as she tried her hardest to swing them backwards, then forwards, back again and then forward for a final swing. Dune then swung Upright as hard as he could, then letting go and sending him flying onto the bridge.\n\nHe got up quickly “Alright, same thing again Red, this time Dune try to grab my hands, and I’ll pull you across.”\nOnce more, Lily swung him as hard as she could a few times before letting go. Upright reached out quickly and grabbed Dune’s arms,\n\n pulling him to safety.Lily sighed with relief once they were both on their feet, and then shook her head at them. “I’m not going to try that jump, I will look for another way down. You both get out of here quick before you are caught.”\n\nUpright nodded, “Alright. I shall expect to see you again soon, do not disappoint me.” And with that they both ran away hurriedly. Lily climbed in from the window and set out searching for an unguarded exit.\n\nAfter not too long, she was able to slip away unnoticed, and made her escape from the city. As she ran, she began to laugh. It was too long since she had been that thrilled on a job. Perhaps something more could come of this partnership,\n\n and maybe he would appreciate the proposition she was now going to make.\n\nEnd of Volume Two\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nLike the Author? Read his other tales such as the classic:\nLittle Red Riding in dah Hood, A Tale of two cihi, Gone with the Pyromancer, The Little Edgey, and Mali the Ker.", ""),
        StaticBook("In a World #1", "§bArthur Caulfield", "My name is Arthur Caulfield. \n\nWrote a book that I sold to a book store in Oren. \n\nWrote some other books that I sold to the highest bid.\n\nWhen I write the words should mean something. \nBut that doesn't matter as the bid goes up and up. \n\nI'm well off now. Still don't have a home to go to. Could buy one if I wanted, but I won't.\n\nI work at a bar near Petrus. I have a lot of friends. I serve a lot of drinks. I am happy. \n\nI am empty.\n\nYou have bought this book because you don't know who I am. In all likeliness I don't know who you are either. But I would still like to tell you my story. \n\nBut just know that there is no end.\n\n\n\n\n\n         In A World\n             By\n     Arthur Caulfield\n\nI awoke in cloud temple, like everyone else. A place full of cult leaders trying to persuade you to join and inn keepers promising their ale is the best. \n   I had always wanted to write books, so with the only money I had I bought some paper and ink.\n\nI do not remember the story I wrote exactly, but it included a beggar and an orc. \n   For those of you that may know me, it is very likely from my book \"Into Nature\" which depicted my survival in the wilderness for some time.\n\nWhile that was not my proudest work, it was definetly the longest.\n    I had no job for some time. I would simply write and sell my stories to earn money for food and shelter at various inns. \n   In my times living in this way I met many\n\nunique characters. One of these being a man named Corvo. Dressed in a green robe that covered all parts of his skin including half of his face. \n   I had asked him where the best place to settle would be, he had replied Ilados.\n\nIlados was a small trading town far off the path to Petrus. \n   As we travelled there, it took a few days, we noticed we were being followed. \n   Eventually we discovered a girl, Arelin, who followed us all this way for reasons I am still unsure of today.\n\nShe seemed like a nice, if not quite strange, girl. \n   But Corvo had rather different feelings. Believing she was there to kill us and take our possessions. He had wielded an axe threatingly but calmed slightly when she did not fight back.\n\nSoon we travelled together, Arelin telling me of a witch that haunted Ilados and the people who lived there. \n   Once we reached the town we were offered rooms but I had to decline. \n   I had just discovered an idea for a new book.\n\nLater that week I had brought some gear into the wilderness which is where I wrote \"Into Nature\" though some of the book is quite obviously fiction.      Soon after, I was on my way to Petrus to get the book published. When an inn on the side of the road\n\ncaught my eye. My stomach had been growling all day so I decided to go inside. \n   This was where I met Vinnie, and after publishing the book, would get a job.\n   To this day my fondest memories where in that inn (Bada Bing Inn)\n\nGetting a haircut from Val and then convincing her I liked it. \n  Meeting an even more extreme version of Corvo, Lurk. \n  Laughing at Vinnies burnt cake because he dozed off while it baked.\n  Entertaining a child while her father\n\nfought outside.\n   Trying to convince orcs, in the middle of battle, to come inside and drink.\n   Hiding from bandits in the basement with two friends.\n   Falling in love.\n\nThe life of a bartender is pretty damn good.\n\nOf course it wasn't all good. In my time as a bartender I have witnessed four fights and six violent acts. \n   Although violence can't be avoided anywhere in life. Soon enough even YOU, reader, will find yourself in such a predicament as I.\n\nThat is all I am able to write in this book as the pages begin to dimmer. But until I write again and add more to the memoirs of my life, I would like to recall each of the people I have met, to show myself that I have known a good many people. And you a\n\nlist of interesting people to meet, though beware of some for they may not be so kind.\n\nVinnie the chef\nValarina\nJack \nMark\nCorvo\nLurk\nJessie\nVioletion\nAleri\nRalif\nAnd Violet", ""),
        StaticBook("Jayas Journey C6", "§bSofetios Jayamen", "Jaya's Journey\n\n             ~By Sofetios\n                  Jayamen\n\n((This is a book I'm actually writing in real life. I really need motivation to continue, so please let me know what you think.))\n\n      Chapter Six\n     The Lore Book\n\n“Wait.” I said. “How can you be part of the Omira. They died long ago.” \n\n“Not all of them.” Said Cloak.\n\n “My mother escaped the temple where your headed before the incident happened.”\n\n“What happened at the temple?” I said.\n\n“Something my mother made me swear never to speak of.” Said Cloak looking slightly away.\n\n“I hope you can respect that. You will know what it is when the time comes.”\n\n“Can you at least tell me something?” I said. “Seeing as I’m headed there.”\n\n“Let’s just say it’s beyond dangerous.” Said Cloak.\n\n “You will make it through alive with the weapons though. But the weapons you possess alone will not get you through. You will need to know how to use them. Which is why I’m coming with you in your travels.”\n\n“I’m not sure how that will go through with Sofetios and Sofia, especially Sofia.”  I said.\n\n“I’m sure we’ll figure something out.” Said Cloak. Then he paused and said,\n\n“ I guess ill have to follow you in the shadows when your traveling. Go ahead down and watch your friend in the competition. I’ll be down  there in a minute or two.”\n\n“How will I know your there?” I said.\n\n“I will be there in person.” Said Cloak.\n\n“I thought the Omira were supposed to be stealthy.” I said.\n\n“Who ever said I can’t walk around like a normal person.” Said Cloak with a slight smile.\n\n I got up, burning with questions and left out the door. I looked back at the waitress who nodded to me. I went down the stairs and sat back at the table with Sofetios.”\n\n“Where have you been?” Said Sofetios a bit concerned.\n\n“Oh I just went to use the restroom.” I lied\n\n“Ok.” Said Sofetios as he watched Sofia slam another guys arm down. I decided to take this time to look at my lore book. I opened it up and got to the first page.\n\nThere was a picture of the sun. In the middle of the sun was a small poem. It read,\n\nThe Prophecy, Part 1,\n\nOne day in the future,\nThe sun dims.\nThe Night will come up ever faster.\nAgainst every one of our wims.\n\nOne will come,\nOne bold and bright.\nTo stop the ever\nComing of the night.\n\nWith shining weapons,\nForged of light,\nThis hero will vanquish\nThe evils delight.\n\nBut the greatest weapon of all,\nThe Heart Indeed.\nWill determine how well,\nThe hero does succeed.\n\nI thought about this for a moment. So It was all up to me whether I succeed? Were the days really getting shorter?\n\nWhat is this evil it talks about? I turned the page. There was a note that said,\n\n‘Hello, If you are reading my book, that means you are either me or the Hero that the prophecy tells of. This also means I was lucky enough to find you.\n\nI’m just writing here to tell you of some pages in this book that you might find helpful, If you don’t already know the content of them. The pages are, 4, 7, 8, 14, 17, 20, and the last page. –Linink’\n\nI turned the page and found the table of contents. Page 4 said ‘The Lin Flute’. Page 7 said ‘The Lin Orb’. Page 8 said ‘The Temple of the Omira’. Page 14 said ‘Companions’. Page 17 said… Nothing. I turned the page to 17.\n\nIt was just a blank page. I turned back to page 4.   It said,\n\n‘The Lin Flute\n\nThe Lin flute is said to contain the ability to control the elements.\n\nIt is said to be able to make rain pore in a matter of seconds in a desert, make the most withering plant grow, or even teleport you places.’\n\nThat must have been what happened when I played The Song of Rain. I thought. I turned to page seven. It said,\n\n‘The Lin Orb\n\nThis artifact is said to be a ball of pure Lin that grows infinitely.\n\n No one knows how big or small it is. The fact that this is commonly known has caused many people to go looking for it, in which not many people return. Those who do return are empty handed.’\n\nNext I turned to page 8 and it said,\n\n‘The Temple of the Omira\n\nThis place is said to house The Alter of the Sun which is said to control how the sun acts. This is also headquarters of the Omira.’\n\nI turned the page to 14 and it said,\n\n‘Companions\n\nIt has been said that people have a type of spiritual animal familiar living within them. This companion is said to reflect ones self or inner being.\n\nI know this because I myself have one. To get yours to appear, simply will it out. If you are not practiced in Lin then yours might be harder to get out.\n\nThis passage scared me. The fact that there was some type of spirit inside me wasn’t exactly a pleasant one. I wondered what it was.\n\nI turned to page twenty. It read,\n\n‘The Great Monsters of Edrot\n\nEdger\n\nThis monster is said to be a giant spider and as large as a small cottage. It lives in the Dark woods on the side of Ridgewood.\n\nRumor has it knows how to defeat most all the other monsters as it is known to be the oldest and wisest monster.\n\nTifantis\n\nThis is a water spirit said to live in the water of lake Edrot. It is known to guard treasure of great magnitude as People passing by the lake can see a treasure chest at the bottom of the lake.\n\nThe trouble in getting it is that there is a current going away from the chest at all sides. Some people don’t believe Tifantis is real, and that the current is natural. But after all, what you believe is up to you.\n\nWenden\n\nWendon is said to be a wolf-man that roams the Dark woods. The simple fact that there are no others like him lead me to believe that he is not a wolf-man, but just a man who has the capability to use Lin to transform his body.\n\n Though why he would choose a wolfish form, I do not know.’\n\nThat is all there was, the bottom portion of the page was ripped out. Was there something that Linink didn’t want me to see?  I turned to the last page.\n\nThere was nothing put a picture of glasses with a dot above the nose rim. Sofetios poked me and I looked up. \n\nA larger crowd had gathered. Sofia got to the last person. It was a muscle like tan guy.\n\nI could tell Sofia’s arm was hurting Because she was stretching it. The muscle guy sat down. Sofia then said.\n\n“Wait, before this last round. Let me have a drink.” There were dissatisfied awws from the crowd. “You guys have Honeylinn?”\n\n“Of course!” said the waitress as she brought her one. Sofia took the drink and put it on the table. She then reached in her jacket pocket to get a coin when the waitress said, “On the house.”\n\nSofia smiled and brought her hand to the glass. The weird thing was her thumb was wet without it getting into the drink. She put her thumb over the glass quickly and took it out so fast that nobody seemed to notice that a drop fell in.\n\n“Cheers!” Said Sofia. Everyone raised their glass and said Cheers too. When Sofia drank her drink she gave the cup to the waitress and said, “Alright, lets do this!” It seemed as though her arm didn’t hurt as much anymore.\n\n The whole restaurant yelled, “THREE”, “TWO”, “ONE!”. There was a slight struggle, but in the end Sofia managed to get his arm to the side of the table. The place exploded with applause.\n\nAs if on queue, Someone walked into the room, dressed all in purple robes. It was Cloak.\n\n“Thank you everyone for coming to this event!” Said Cloak as he made his way toward Sofia. “And Congratulations to you!”\n\nCloak reached in his robes and gave Sofia a bag of gold. \n\n“Who are you?” Said Sofia taking the gold.\n\n“Why, the owner of this Café of course!” Said Cloak. “Now everyone. A round on me!” Everyone started rushing to the bar.\n\nSofia walked toward us and said, “well that was fun.” \n\n“Yea especially the Lin you put in your drink in the end.” Said Sofetios. Sofia elbowed Sofetios in the ribs .\n\n“Someone could hear us.” Said Sofia.\n\n“You don’t want us thrown out, do you?”\n\n“Ok, Ok.” Said Sofetios. “I was just kidding.”\n\n“Any way, lets get going.” Said Sofia. “We’re already behind schedule.”\n\n“Where’s our next stop?” I asked still looking at Cloak. \n\n“Sadzten.” Said Sofetios. \n\n“What kind of town is that.” I asked looking at Sofia.\n\n“It’s a fishing town.” Said Sofia.\n\n“So they are by the sea?” I asked.\n\n“No.” said Sofetios. “They are at Lake Edrot.” I remembered what the book said about Tifantus.\n\nThank you for taking the time to read this book! I will be writing more in the future!\n\nIf you like my writing, please let me know by bird or in person!\n\n~Sofetios Jayamen\n((Sofetios))", ""),
        StaticBook("Vol. 1 : Origins", "§bArnorian", "~*~ Origins ~*~\n\nDeities and Recognized Deities.\n\nIn the Old North faith, there are three circles are the domains of the Gods, and in each were both lesser, and demi gods. The three circles in order of least to greatest powerful\n\nare Nature, Life, and Astral. Within each rests one dominant God.\n\nWithin nature there is Gronn the Life Bringer, who is believed to be the aspects of the Druids in one form in the Old Faith's eyes. This means the old faith acknowledges the\n\nDruids as true and rightful worshippers of nature in their own religion. Gronn is said to be twelve feet tall with bark for skin and rocks for teeth. His eyes are two pools of water and his digits are branches. He has a full beard and head of leaves and\n\nvines which twist and turn wildly. It's said he is often seen, but never caught and has the ability to take on anything of living origin. This can be taken in two ways, as some hunters thank him for his sacrifices to let them eat, while others commune\n\nmore with animals, and forsake meat eating.\nHe is seen as a very benevolent God. His charge is to watch over all the planets, fish, animals and happenings of nature. He is what ties Astral to life. he is also credited for the creation of the elements as\n\ngifts to Morighaen.\n\n\nWithin Man there is Thronn the Impartial, who is believed to be the collection of all humanity's desires, virtues, morals and thoughts. He is a grey character, with no appearance albiet that of a silhouette. People who\n\npray to Thronn traditionally wait until the sun is half up or down, and wait in an open field. They turn to their own shadow and take to kneeling, nod their head and fold their hands. All the workings of men are held into the account of Thronn, which is\n\nwhy people depending on their lives will pray to Thronn. The people who are poorer, downtrodden and feel betrayed by life and tormented usually shun Thronn. The opposite crowd most often give thanks to him. Thronn is looked on positively by Mages and\n\nFathers for the gift of Heartfire to man.\n\nWithin the Astral planes beyond us, sits Morighaen, the Night Woman; a shoft looking lady covered in a veil of stars. She is larger than any planet or sun, and we are smaller then dust in her celestial eyes.\n\nShe is to large to see us, but she knows we are there - and she may assume a mortal form, or smaller size to medal with the cosmos as it pleases her. She is seen as sadistic by some due to her boredom. She was left alone, and to pass the time she often\n\nthrows planets, or galaxies together to watch the effects. She is easily the most fearsome of the Gods, and any mortal who claims to be Morighaen is usually killed out of fear, for if she has come down, the end is already upon us, and if she is lying, she\n\nmay anger Morighaen. People pray to her to appease her, and she is often seen as a Pillar of Strength for the female half of Northern society. She is the cause for moonblood and weather, time, space, and even magic. Her relationship to Thronn and Gronn is\n\nstrained by both the distance and nature of the figures.", ""),
        StaticBook("Scorched Paper", "§bLucion Sullas", "((Please leave this for others to read! :) ))\n\n*The paper seems to have been singed by the fire around the hut, but otherwise remains legible. The words themselves appear frantically written.*\n\nI will not be threatened by tyrants ever again. Not Uradir, not that Mages Guild, not Emperors, Kings, Sohaers, Princes, or any other children that pepper themselves with names of authority. I will not be a pawn in any overlord's plan. I am Lucion Sullas\n\nand I am above the petty gripes of power.\n\nHow's this for \"No choice,\" Ambros, you foul bag of excrement? \n\n-L. Sullas", ""),
        StaticBook("Lady", "§bValmir", "Lady Sophie\nBy Leyu’Maehr\n\nOn the island called Silva Insula, there is a legend of a sainted woman named Sophie and a dark evil. It all began when people who lived in small societies near the Lucky Goblin Inn began to go missing. They would leave the inn, or step out of their homes\n\nfor a minute and just vanish, never to be seen again. Then people noticed that some of the others were slowly changing, becoming wilder and more aggressive, or just insane. People became frightened and began to withdraw from each other, joining with their\n\nneighbors in an effort to stay safe. Lady Sophie and her son Trevor were among those who sought shelter and safety at the inn. Around that time creatures began to appear around the town. No two descriptions were ever the same, but most could agree on\n\ntheir glowing eyes and how they seemed to fade into the darkness around the when you looked at them.\n\nTrevor went insane overnight. He began to kill his friends and neighbors. People from the small societies banded together and tried many ways to stop\n\nhim, but, alas, the only way for his terror to end was by his death.\n\nOn the day he was buried, the Lady Sophie sat all day by her beloved son’s grave, neither eating nor speaking to any who came by to offer her their condolences. The remaining people\n\ngathered at the inn to wait for her return. By the time night fell, a dwarf named Brokk become concerned for her and went to the grave to check on her. As  he approached the grave, Lady Sophie stood up and walked out into the misty forest. Brokk tried to\n\nfollow her but quickly lost her and turned to go back to the inn. That’s when the scream pierced through the fog and darkness. No one could find the words to describe that unearthly, chill inducing scream. Many recalled grabbing their heads from the pain\n\nas the scream ripped throughout their brains. When the scream ended, Brokk went in the direction Lady Sophie went in, and found her unconscious on the ground. He picked her up in his arms and took her back to the inn.\n\nAs the sun banished the darkness,\n\nLady Sophie woke once and tried to tell Brokk what happened. She had found the source of the evil plaguing them and went to confront it. The scream that had rent the air had come from this evil as she defeated it. She only had time to mention that it\n\nwould never return before she closed her eyes and passed into the unknown realm we call death. As she died, all the other who had been slipping into madness, became whole once more.\n\nNo one else disappeared after that. Life went on. This is the one theory\n\nthat many in the town seemed to accept as fact. They said that Lady Sophie, after grieving for her loss so deeply, became determined that no one else should suffer her fate. It is whispered that her will and determination were so strong, that she defeated\n\nthe evil with her mind alone, And some even whisper that the evil that she faced was somehow connected to the enders that plague Asulon now. But perhaps the most disturbing thing of all is the rumors of noises coming from the graveyard late at night and\n\nthe shadow that rises from Trevor’s grave and prowls around the town looking for a new victim.", ""),
        StaticBook("*A", "§bThurak", "Delonna Aeleyelsa, as an elder and far seer of the Orcs. I am wondering if we could meet to dicuss relations with the Orcs about shamanism. Send me a bird with the time you are able to speak to me. RulG, \nMirdautas Vras", ""),
        StaticBook("Vol. 2 : Origins", "§bArnorian", "~*~ Shrines ~*~\n\nGod's Gardens were the most natural and beautiful of worshipping places. These were seen as absolute holy grounds made by the aspects of nature themselves. There are believed to be three God's Garden's in existence - one for\n\neach of the three Aspects. The God's Garden that we have currently located and were near (In Anthos, Vaerhaven.) is the God's Garden of the Elements. It was a hot spring situated in the north, protected by a granite and stone wall. Spruce trees spring up\n\nwith flowers poking through the snow. People would come here to cleanse the blood off themselves, to pray in it's hot waters and to fast and meditate. No blood, on any condition could ever be shed in a God's Garden, but blood could be cleansed there.\n\nStone Circles.\n\nStone circles were a very signifigant part of the traditional culture and faith. They were built with massive flagstones and set in a ring, with a series of four gates, two pillars around the gates, and a central altar.\n\nHeartfire.\n\nHeartfire is the projection of the inner spirit of humanity. The Old Northerners believed that inside of everyone's body was a fire, that the most powerful could actually channel into physical use. The blood in your\n\nbody keeps the fire from eating you from the inside out. When you breath, you feed the fire. When you die, your fire goes out - Even if you were to cut someone open, you would not find their fire. A Father (Priest) must be able to channel their Heartfire\n\nto show their devotion and inner strength, be it for combat or for healing. Many Kings and Queens in the past have also shown the ability to use Heartfire as a testiment to their faith and Strength.\n\nIt is believed that deep in the heart of a cave\n\nfar from the light of the sun lived a man and his family. They had fires and torches, which burned all night and accumulated smoke began to choke his family and himself. They would soon need to leave the relative security of the cave into the unknown and\n\nthe man prayed to Thronn every night before his fires, wishing for an answer. Eventually, one came. In the crackling fire a voice said solemnly and dryly, \"Drink your fires and know peace.\" He took this as an omen, and swallowed a piece of charcoal.\n\nHe did not feel pain, instead finding warmth in himself. His eyes grew bright like pyres, and illumanted what was before him. His hands were engulfed by a smokeless fire, and he felt no cold pervading. His family was awestruck, the man was dumbfounded and\n\nthe first Father's of Thronn were founded in that smokey cave.\n\nFathers.\n\nThe Fathers are the holders of the knowledge and traditions of the old faith. They act of behalf of the Gods, and while all their actions are\n\nnot godly, but very mortal, and are considered to be more in tune with the Gods, or a particular Gods. Fathers have very informal training and usually learn most of what they know orally, with some few choosing to record and write their teachings to pass\n\ndown.", ""),
        StaticBook("Task From Verden", "Jallentime", "((X -1059 / Y -291))\n\nTravel to the Infested Forest and survey the area. Bring back any information of the undead roaming there, and some proof that you were there.", ""),
        StaticBook("To Praetor TT", "§bLaethis Izalith", "Praetor Tristin Tresery,\n\nI was recently made aware of the dwarven attack upon your city. Though it is my understanding your defense was successful, I am sorry to hear of this unjust attack.\n\nIf there is anything\n\nour State can do to assist you, do not hesitate to contact me.\n\nMaehr'sae hiylun'ehya.\nLaethis Izalith, Sohaer of Haelun'or.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Marked Oath", "§bAdeon of Rhoswen", "The Sacred Oath\n\n\"I accept my marking and the burdens to follow it. I will act as expected of me and risk my life for the innocent mundane, to protect them from the dangers of the supernatural and monstrosity alike. Should I fail, God help me.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Lost Hope", "§bAmras Ancalimë", "Chapter One: Problem\n\"Immortality, a blessing but also a curse they say, I simply state that its an obscenity that never keeps my sanity at bay. Everything important slowly disintegrating away into ashes, that were once a well collected heart that could\n\nSING! Gone, ravaged into a dissapated state, only to re-occur when the feeling dawn. Need some new experiences, emotions, if only there were some differences. Stars.\"\n\nChapter two: Solution\n\"Stars. A bastion of hope that could free me from these bars. Brightening the night, not being able to reach so frightening. The induvidual emotion of each star is an endless fuel, keeping me going through the days like an exhausted\n\nmuel.\"\n\nChapter three: Realization\n\"I'll never reach them. Its a hopeless endeavour, lastin forever. Whats beyond? We'll never know, because we've been sompliy conned. Imprisoned within our realm, left to simply envision.\"\n\nFor this life without end, isn't a life at all.", ""),
        StaticBook("Blood of Many", "§bRosso", "With great might and ideals men have raised themselves to fight. Throughout the sands of time we have seen gigantic armies fall and tyrant kings still stand. And yet, where do these ideals, these admittedly impressive albeit unsuccessful ventures lead?\n\nDeath and destruction. The decay of rebellions, and the downfall of freedom. And yet where many have failed, it takes but one to succeed. Need one be reminded of any of the ancient kings and rules who have come to an, shall we say abrupt end? Indeed,\n\nAssassins shape the tide of history more than you know. And here you arem reading, seeking, learning. What is it that you wish to know I wonder?\nIt is true that we have our governments, it is true that they are what hold us together- And yet! It is also\n\nthat we have the power to sway the tide! Move the battlefield to our advantage! And even, end the rule of the horrendous” The power in the minority is greater than we think. And it is why today we live in a world DEFINED by the assassinations of\n\nyesterday! And were these the greatest historic decisions? Perhaps not. But while some were not the best, others changed history for the better, bringing Aegis to the place it is today-or was yesterday rather. Grand armies once again amass in a hopeless\n\neffort to combat the Undead forces.\nIt makes one question where the world will be left, with such meek enemies yet so strong.\nIt is high time we accept our history’s motive and ally ourselves with Iblees to bring salvation to our world. This is where our\n\npowers are tested. We must remain resolute in the times to come if we are to become united. Otherwise we might as well let our blood spatter against the stone.\n\nThe Blood of Many, the Heart of One\n\nRewritten by Leyu’Maehr\nCopied by Rosso\nVaerHaven", ""),
        StaticBook("Okarir'maehr", "§bIcarus Adil", "§0\n§0   To Fill a Vacancy:§0\n§0      Okarir'maehr§0\n§0\n§0     19th of Malin's§0\n§0     Welcome, 1590§0\n§0\n§0\n§0    §0\n§0     by Icarus Adil\n\nDearest mali'aheral, and any others gathered before me in Haelun'or, I seek to address you today with hopes of fixing a problem that as a nation we face. For with the appointment of our new Maheral, the Silver Council once more holds a vacancy: that of\n\nthe Okarir'maehr.§0\n§0\n§0I have none that I can decry for creating a sorry state of affairs, a champion of immense change, for we do not find ourselves needing such radical improvement. Our new Maheral, the former Okarir'maehr, proved sedulous in her duties,\n\ntaking a library unopened and bookless and revitalizing a home for knowledge worthy of the implications the name The Eternal Library bestows.§0\n§0\n§0Yet it is also imperative that we continue our pursuit of maehr'sae in our most treasured locale, more important\n\nthan ever, for I fear it clear that we do not hold the progress found through scholarship as dear to our hearts as we once did. It is for this reason that I, Icarus Adil, put my name forward as candidate for the next Okarir'maehr, spoken publicly so any\n\nother with interest might make their mind known, if they so wish. I will debate any other seeking the role as is our custom, if such a task proves necessary.§0\n§0\n§0Until another with interest arises, I merely bow my head to you, my fellow mali'thilln, in hope\n\n that I might serve you more fully. Maehr'sae hiylun'ehya.", ""),
        StaticBook("Our Maheral", "§bIcarus Adil", "§0    Our Maheral: To§0\n§0   Demit and Appoint§0\n§0\n§0\n§0     18th of Malin's§0\n§0     Welcome, 1590§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0  by Erinali Tahn'thill\n\nMy words are addressed to our mali’thill, those bearing loyalty to the beloved nation and her blessed heritage. As of late, elcihi’thilln has been burdened by recrudescing phases of instability; challenging, of course, yet we’ve always persevered.§0\n\nNevertheless, it pains me to admit that the latest changes of Maheralship have served as no exception - from absenteeism, the unprincipled, and now the publicly unannounced.§0\n§0\n§0Yes, I come forth to notify my audience that Lyu Elibar'acal\n\ndetermined it apt to retire from his position as Maheral - and, consequently, his successor was appointed. A posted document has confirmed this incident and is available.§0\n§0\n§0My lliran, I - Erinali S. Tahn’thill - was selected as our next malaurir. Alas,\n\nLyu’s lips were sick and I was not nominated by a sound mind. He saw me as a comforter and a friend…§0\n§0\n§0This swayed a troubling verdict.§0\n§0\n§0Some ‘aheral could embrace this expedient fortune, perhaps misuse it; though, I\n\nwon’t. Because, I know what is best for Haelun’or when we’ve exemplary subjects available. I decline a long term of cultural guidance for my original service as a Medi’ir of the Triumvirate. Although, my right to select our new figurehead is going to be\n\nput to good use. I’ve sought elcihi for one actively working for their nation, preserving their impeccable record and spurring the general populace to engage with the will outlined and established by our cultural founders.§0\n§0\n§0I'm proud to announce that\n\nIaria Elervather has been selected.§0\n§0\n§0Unforeseen, mayhaps - but I expect great progress while our precious culture is bolstered by her eternal knowledge. May Haelun’or be guided by her divine facility.\n\nliewyn'Larihei eltaeleh walehe ohn vallein eltaliyna walehe§0\n§0\n§0-= Maehr’sae Hiylun’ehya =-", ""),
        StaticBook("Norland 1600", "§bRalnor Kelyarus", "11th of The First Seed, 1600\n\nMeeting with Norland.\n\n\n\"The Silver State of Haelun'or and the Kingdom of Norland do hereby pledge to consult the other before announcing, forming or acting on any foreign\n\npolicy in the interest of maintaining peace and unity on the island which houses them both.\n\n-Ikur Sergon, Sohaer of Haelun'or\n\n-Annabel Staunton, Queen of Norland", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "This list contains the necessary reagents needed for the continuation of the research to improve the security of Silver State. The reagents are listed in order of priority, with the most needed plants listed first.\n\nHigh Priority: These reagents are the largest risk of running out.§0\n§0\n§0Mandragora: Found in swampland in shallow water. Look near lilypads.§0\n§0\n§0Dwarf's Pumpkin: Swamplands near muddy water.\n\nSerpent's Stalk: Grows near small bodies of water in forests.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "______________________________________ ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~             Diary§0\n§0             of§0\n§0          Cenwall§0\n§0          Glaeus§0\n§0______________________________________~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~Dated: §0\n§01st of Amber Cold, 1620\n\n1st of The Amber Cold, 1620§0\n§0___________________Dear Diary,§0\n§0   This is my first entry of many hopefully to come. I am well... maybe too well. I gained a very peculiar scar on the left of my face from him... I felt so scared when I heard his footsteps...\n\nTip tap, tip tap. The scar is quite grotesque and I hope that one day I can find a way to cover it up... Though I kind of like it. It reminds me of the pain I endured through that evil time in my life. Their is a constant pain associated with it.\n\n2nd of The Amber Cold, 1620§0\n§0___________________Dear Diary,§0\n§0   This is my second entry of many hopefully to come. After a few days the burn/scar started to darken and loses its sting with the passing day... so i'm glad about that to say the least. It's...\n\n... very cold walking for a new home. I've asked around to find where my fathers old home used to be. I'm terrified they may hang me at the gates to repent for his crimes... perhaps I shall keep a low profile until I know for sure. They call it Haelunor.\n\n3rd of The Amber Cold, 1620§0\n§0___________________Dear Diary,§0\n§0  This is the third entry of hopefully many to come. A lot has started happening since I first came to the city. I gained citizenship and the populace seemed to hold me up with open arms...\n\n... A house was even prepared for me and my newfound cousin! A cousin! I thought I was the only Glaeus left!... At any rate i've told a handful of people my true name and they've seem to take it rather well. Thank the luck of it all... Goodnight Diary.\n\n4th of The Amber Cold,§0\n§01620§0\n§0___________________Dear Diary,§0\n§0   This is my fourth entry of hopefully many to come. Today was an eventful day! I met the Maheral in person! She had such grace to her every step! I've gone to the grand library in Haelun'or...\n\n... I've read up on the history of this place and my people and I now see a reachable goal... I wish with every bone in my body to learn magic and use my high elven blood to its full potential. I've asked around the docks and I was told, The Enchantry...\n\n... Was the place to learn it. I can only walk their and see what may await me. I left the house given to me in Haelun'or still quite bare and empty when I left so I doubt anyone would break in. I can only hope my cousin Goras is well... tommorow awaits.\n\n5th of The Amber Cold,§0\n§01620§0\n§0___________________Dear Diary,§0\n§0   This is my fifth entry of many hopefully to come. A glorious day! My luck never seems to end! I've made it to The Enchantry after such a cold night. The first thing I noticed was a tasteless...\n\n... painting on the wall. Graffiti. It took a while but a rather intellectual looking high elf came to the gates after my constant wailing either annoyed him enough or implored him to check who was their. This man I would come to find out was The First...\n\n... Enchanter. I remember the sheer cold as we exchanged words. He was scholarly looking fellow and tested my convinction and motives to learning magics. I was physically shaking until at that point he'd figure to let me in. The unnamed elf so far...\n\n... he'd ask me for my cloak and use an unknown magic to warm it up handing it back to me. It was impressive. At this point he started asking more questions and invited me in for an interview of sorts. In came in another elf called Daniel Ward. They'd...\n\n... both jest to me the possibility of an animal cruelty cage in the basements... i'd of course laughed uncomfortably at the jest. They didn't seem to like that and advised me to lighten up but henceforth continued the interview. They'd ask why they...\n\n... should let me stay and I gave the only answer I knew how to give; I said that I was loyal. This seemed to make the scholarly fellow nod in approval in which he did indeed tell me his name. Sarrion. Sarrion then offered my a proposal to be a...\n\n... Steward of sorts to clean up and study until a years time where I would take a test. If i'd pass I would be his personal apprentice. Overjoyed I took the deal and now here I am.... I went instantly to cleaning that tasteless art on the wall.\n\n18th of Malin's Welcome, 1621§0\n§0___________________Dear Diary,§0\n§0   This is my sixth entry of hopefully many to come. An elven month has passed by since I last wrote in this diary... A lot has happened. For one I lost my scar! YES! I was ecstatic when...\n\nThese strange mages clad in steel plate head to toe showed up at the gates. One man, I forget his name was one of these knights. He noticed a scar on my face and saw the pain seared on my skin... he felt my pain. His hands burst into golden flames as...\n\nhe absorbed the scar completely removing it. A glorious moment indeed. A new start. A few weeks have passed and as I write this we attempt to make the enchantry float from its foundation! I hope we all do not perish under collapsing rubble.\n\n21st of Malin's Welcome, 1622§0\n§0___________________Dear Diary,§0\n§0   This is my seventh entry of hopefully many to come. One whole year has passed since my last entry and a lot surely has happened. Firstly I have changed my name to fit something I want to...\n\n... be called rather than the horrid name my father gifted me at birth. Atathri meaning cursed snake was what I was born with and it is sad to part with it but that time of my life is over. I am a new elven man. Cenwall Glaeus. AS for my last entry I...\n\n... it quite open for what may come next. We did survive the movement of the Enchantry and it succeeded, I am writing this in a floating building. Quite an accomplishment! My studies for Arcanism are just starting and I...\n\n... first was tasked with doing a survey on Arcanism from other Arcanists I could meet around the cities and towns I could find. This experience was QUITE the experience as I firstly saw Arcanism close and personal but I also saw how secretive many...\n\n... Arcanists can be. I was even punched in the jaw! The bastard!... Though I learned wisps make up an arcanists spell and that spell is personalized in special colors called auras in which it is personalized to specific persons quality or personality...\n\n... I met a bunch of people here at The Enchantry and I also personally met the Sohaer personally! She was quite nice! As for now I must get back to studies, I hear footsteps...\n\n14th of The Grand Harvest, 1623§0\n§0___________________Dear Diary,§0\n§0   This is my eigth entry of hopefully many to come. Another year has passed and there is much to discuss. The Silver City is dead, it has been dissolved. The restoration now begins...\n\ntoday I just saw a dwarves skull get stomped on! The membrane itself was truly a sight to see in person. I am truly not in the mood for writing today...", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "-------------------===================-------------------           Diary§0\n§0            of§0\n§0       Tennallar§0\n§0        Ilmoriel§0\n§0-------------------===================-------------------(( §0tinyurl.com/diaryofTI§0 ))\n\n15th of the Amber Cold, 1624§0\n§0Written in Lin'okaral Camp§0\n§0-------------------===================I am currently seated alone at a table located in the far end of a desolate, damp, and may I add TINY camp yet things have never been better.\n\nThis is my first journal entry of (hopefully, unless I die prematurely) many more to come. I write now, because i want to remember this time in my life when I am old and grey (I'll always be grey, and I'll never truely look old so just take that as a\n\nfigure of speech.) I very recently reunited with my beloved brothers (at the request of maln& haelun, I suppose 60 is the cut-off for living with them) in what previously was the cihi of Taliyna'maehr.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dear Mylas", "§bAnna Thassarion", "Dear Mylas,\n\n  I don't know if you will ever read this...But after hearing about you an your ex wife are now back together...It killed a part of me..I want to kill my slef because of this news...Mylas she left you and now you take her bac\n\nI understand if you loved her if you do still love her...But she broke your heart once why would you want her to break it agian...I would never leave or hurt you...I am writting in this book to get all of my emtions and feelings down to show you them y\n\nnever read this...But I love everything about you...even your grey hair because it makes you you...I always thought the frist man I kissed would be the last man I kissed...I gave my frist kiss to you...I love you more then you could ever know...I k\n\nDon't love me, but I can't help but loving you. Your not perfect but I admire the things that aren't perfect about you..I admire your courage...Your happiness...And I admire how you lead a big company without taking a break..I am such I fool i am g\n\nStop writting but know this...if you ever do read this..think about me...please..consider being with me..\n\nYour dear,\nAnna", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "20th of Grand Harvest 1610§0\n§0\n§01-Athin 0§0\n§02-Frost Vine 0§0\n§03-Mandragora 56§0\n§04-Serpant's Stalk 49§0\n§05-Blissfoil 0§0\n§06-Crimson Vase 49§0\n§07-Drake's Tail 28§0\n§08-Blood Lotus 40§0\n§09-Dwarf's Pumpkin 23§0\n§010-Flametongue 39\n\n11-Crouch Feather 29§0\n§012-Elf's Hair VIne 0§0\n§013-Halfling's Grass 8§0\n§014- Larihei's Finget 0§0\n§015-Alabaster 0§0\n§016-Saffvil 6§0\n§017-Tippen's Root 3§0\n§018-Goblin's Ivy 0§0\n§019-Clutch Straw 22§0\n§020-Metzli's Tangle", ""),
        StaticBook("Beloved Prince", "§bJames Hightower", "Unto Mylas, the Prince of Fenn.\nThe Prince of Ponce sends his reply.\n\nI am delighted by your letter to me and it warms my heart my beloved Prince of Fenn.  I wish to relay the fact that my message came to me unscathed.  Please be sure to pay the\n\ncourier once you retrieve this message for his hard work and diligence.", ""),
        StaticBook("Melia Approval", "§bIcarus Adil", "Name: Melia Finnigan\nRace: Mali’ame\nAge (at submission): 11\nPhysical Description: Light tan skin, green eyes, brown hair, currently a child.\nReason for Access: Assistance with the Eternal Library and research.\nApproval Date: 12th of the First Seed, 1593\n\nApproving Councillor: Icarus Adil\n-/---------------/-", ""),
        StaticBook("Notes on Reagent", "§bAscan Valein'thill", "-=Ascan's Notes=-\n\n-Athin= A\n-Frost Vine= FV\n-Mandragora= M\n-Serpent's Stalk= SS\n-Blissfoil= BF\n         \n         -Water-\n\n\n-Crimson Vase= CV\n-Drake's Tail= DT\n-Blood Lotus= BL\n-Dwarf's Pumpkin= DN\n-Flametongue Root= FR\n\n          -Fire-\n\n\n-Crouch Feather= CF\n-Elf's Hair Vine= EV\n-Halfling's Grass= HG\n-Larihei's Fingers= LF\n\n           -Air-\n\n\n-Alabaster Leaf= AL\n-Saffvil= SL\n-Tippen's Root= TR\n-Goblin's Ivy= GY\n-Clutcher's Straw= CS\n-Metzli's Tangle= MT\n\n          -Earth-\n\n\nPotion Mix Order=\n\n  \n       Water\n          Fire\n             Air\n              Earth", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "A Season§0\n§0   ---    With    ---§0\n§0       The Pastor§0\n§0\n§0~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ §0\n§0\n§0       Written by:§0\n§0\n§0    Ascan Valein'thill\n\n    -------------§0\n§0   This short story§0\n§0    is dedicated to§0\n§0 my ever loyal butler,§0\n§0        Fredrich.§0\n§0\n§0A victim of the eighteen years war prior to working for us, and a person of great stories, despite being a valah.§0\n§0    -------------\n\nChapter.01: Duty.§0\n§0\n§0   It was five months since the siege of Kal'Ordholm had begun, eight years into the 'Eighteen Years War' with ten more years left of slaughter and conquest, all started by the greedy Dwarf king Midgor's ambition of splitting the-\n\n-unified Human Empire, and see them placed under the Dwarven Yoke. It was around 1543 when I had reached my coming-of-age, enlisted into the Holy Oren military to aid in the war and push back the Dwarven envasion. Unlike the rest, I was one of the-\n\n-youngest without a father, died before  able to uphold the duty of service as many adult men are bound to when living under the protection of Oren, a thing that happens very rarely prior to facing Urguan's great force. Like many others, I was put under-\n\n-the intense but short training of combat, intended to be used as the main line of infantry, a line of under trained and under equipped grunts merely used to swarm in numbers and pave a way with bodies for the veterans to come in and finish the job. As-\n\n-any sane person would feel, I was struck with fear and depression knowing my life could be snapped away the moment I step into the battle field as 'Recruit Alistair', and I would have, had my moral lowered and allowed the fear within me to linger and-\n\n-spread, a thing that was prevented by the Pastor that came a day later after my enlistment.\n\nChapter.02:The Pastor.§0\n§0\n§0  He was adressed as 'Pastor Estaban', a man of faith, nearing the final years of his life but manages to look brilliant in his ever simple robe with his cross around his neck, and a simple cane always at his side. He was a-\n\n-man of a high religious importance, a minister in charge of a Canonist church, but had decided to take a copy of his holy book and leave behind his title and church to come to us as a moral support, 'blessing' the unwilling young servants with the-\n\n-creator's protection and guidance to a heaven all religious men and women work and pray to reach. To me it was an illusion, a final thought of hope in our minds before breathing our last breath, to me the 'Pastor' was a fake, a person with a fake smile -\n\n-planting fake hope into peasant minds as encouragement to readily throw their lives onto the pikes of war, acting as a blanket for others to walk atop and lengthen it. Though it was a final piece of hope none-the-less, something I've come to closely -\n\n-hold onto until the end of this war.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "[!]§0\n§0The book would contain the contents of multiple ancient scrolls§0\n§0\n§0((§0tinyurl.com/§0\n§0malin-island ))", ""),
        StaticBook("ELECTROMANCY", "§bonm224", "ELECTROMANCY\n         GUIDE\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBy: Richard Tarus\nAdapted: Amras Lúinwë\n\nWhat is electric evocation?\nElectrical Evocation is the arcane magic form whereby a mage creates Electrical bolts for his or her purposes. Unlike other types of Evocation electrical bolts is intended to be much more difficult to control due to its\n\nspeed and high energy nature. Mages who specialize in electrical evocation will be able to form electrical bolts and streams of electricity to electrocute their targets.However, electrical evocation requires much more energy than for example\n\nfire and therefore a single electrical bolt requires much more energy than a fireball. This however is made up for by the fact the lightning bolt is somewhat equal in power to the two fireballs which could be made in the same time period.\n\nStrength\nAn electrical evocationist is capable of producing powerful electrical bolts\nBolts may travel from any point to point with speed and reliable accuracy.\nWeakneses\nElectrical evocation takes a greater amount of time to produce a bo\n\nthan other types of evocation\nElectrical evocation is dangerous to learn and during some phases of learning the mage can be incapable of producing any spark which will not injure themselves.\n\nProcess\nReaching Tier 1:\nWhen you begin to learn magic, you will start a Tier 1. At that point in time, you are unable to cast any form of magic unless you have some sort of experience and have connected to the void.At this tier you will lear\n\nhow to connect to the void, and then research electricity as an element itself. Connecting to the void will take perhaps even years of practice, and once completed,you may still have some difficulty. Researching electricity would consist of practically\n\nfinding any sort of detailand then taking note of it.\nReaching Tier 2: \nAfter their advancement from tier 1, and their connection to the void, they can now create a multitude of sparks and perhaps an even minor bolt,albeit difficult to\n\ncontrol till towards the end of Tier 2.  Even though they can create sparks, users at this tier may have an overload in which the sparks will practically burst outwards towards the conjurer.In this tier they will need heavy loads of practice in order\n\nto become more proficient with a minor bolt.\nReaching Tier 3:\nIn this tier they can finally create a full powered bolt withought major troubles, and have full proficiency. At this point they can now create streams of electricity,\n\nthough they will simply spark and singethe target, rather then cause major damage. With this tier, they are novice mages. \nReaching Tier 4:\nNow, the electrical evocation users can create the \"call-down\"of electricity, aka a bolt from a high point\n\nin the sky. They can create multiple bolts in a shorter time, although a fire evocationist could create fireballs in an even shorter time.The call-down is not very proficient, and will rarely land on the user's target.  In this tier,they can create gre\n\nstreams of electricity that will do some good damage (burns, etc.) They are very proficient with the bolts now.\n\n For more information go to this link, there is the same info + RP guide:\nhttp://www.lordofthecraft.net/topic/88498-improved-electricity-guide/", ""),
        StaticBook("A Spark", "§bAthe'lor", "The Founding of Electrical Evocation\n\nSalamandra (or Regaki, I should state), founded Electrical Evocation in a year not known, though was approximated to have been sometime during the races stay in Elysium. However, the tale stretches backward int\n\nthe deep roots of Asulon, where the possibility for this, all began. \n\nRegaki was the violent, and dangerous figure that was a terror in the night for the common man, elf, or dwarf alike. Never was his skin shown, and this caused many to believe he w\n\ndemon, manifested, or perhaps the physical embodiment of the tortured soul of a great wizard, returned from the grave to slay all mortals. Nonetheless, a hooded figure left a note for Regaki, knowing it would be found. The directions on the note lead to a\n\ngrand, isolated tower where the robed figure would wait for him. Atop the tower did the shadow stand as the demon approached, rain and thunder battering the two of them with no effect. Rock, fire, and water beckoned to the command of the ghoul, -\n\nshattering the defenses of the robed figure; yet, still, the robed figure appeared to refuse to fight back, aside from casting minor defensive magic to protect himself. It was apparent Regaki would triumph, but in the last moment, bolt of lightning\n\nreigned down from the heavens, attracted to his golden mask. With ear-piercing howls and shrieks the demon squirmed as the gold melded to its face, until Regaki fell silent.\n\nWhen he awoke, he could not feel his face. He touched it, but the gold was\n\nand no matter how hard he tried, the mask would not yield from his head. \n\n...And so some great time passed, before Regaki could be called Salamandra again. With extensive research into his mask, it was concluded that the lightning's energy had bee\n\nabsorbed into the golden pieces, at least somewhat. Over time the mage found himself able to draw this energy from the mask, and bend it to his will. Before long the mask's power would wane, however, so he made it his obligation to create electricty\n\nhimself. The Undead had been capable of doing it in very large quantities, so perhaps he too could create lightning, albeit not as efficiently. \n\nThis was the founding of Electrical Evocation.", ""),
        StaticBook("Electric Evo.", "§bHaadi Mubdee", "=--=--=--=--=--=--=            Electrical\n           Evocation\n=--=--=--=--=--=--=\n\n\n     -< ^v^v^v^v^\n\nThere is an old saying that humans (mortals) fear most other humans. I believe, however, that those who say that have never looked outside the confines of the human world. If anyone has come face to face with the power of nature, they will consider the\n\nprevious proverb a joke. If this sounds like nothing more than nonsense coming from an old fool, then answer this next question. If you can possess any form of power, what would you choose? Would you choose the power of mankind, or that of a wild beast?\n\nWould it be the roars of powerful men, or the sound of thunder that shakes the heavens? Is it the limited life of men, or nature's continuous cycle of life? Whichever way you look at it, the power of man is feeble compared to the grandeur of nature.\n\nThroughout history, all of mankind has admired nature's power and though they had feared it, they tried to deny that. This is one of man's many follies. They neglect nature's power, which does not discriminate, solely because they are a part of nature.\n\nIn particular, as humans learned of Mana and started seeing a glimpse of nature's other realm, they began neglecting nature's power even more. They didn't realize that their \"magic\" was actually an imitation of nature's power. This is what worries me.\n\nThere are many students who are Wizards and Druids in training who do not understand that every magic's starting point is a natural phenomenon. I, who also boasted in my knowledge of Electric magic , did not learn this until I saw lightning strike down at\n\nthe Crown Lands Plateau of Oren. In hopes that those who come after me will not make the same mistake, I decided to write this book. In other words, I hope that beginner wizards will learn the laws of nature and have a healthy fear of it as well.\n\nAlthough this book only deals with lightning power, which is only one of nature's awesome power, if you are wise, you will take the moral of the story to heart and apply it when training other magic as well.\n\nThe Principle of Electricity series Magic Skill\n                -=-\n\nIn order to understand the principle of Electric magic, you must first learn its natural counterpart: Lightning. If you've seen anyone use Electric-based magic, you probably noticed a close resemblance to a lightning strike. The lightning strike occurs\n\nwhen Mana, the energy that surrounds us, splits into two polarities of energy for reasons unknown. These split polarities each continue to accumulate energy, when, in an instant, an explosion of energy flow occurs between heaven and earth.\n\nThe intensity of the light and heat during this process contains tremendous power. Also, because of its unpredictability of where it strikes, it has been an object of fear to mankind. There are many opinions as to when and why Mana, splits into two\n\npolarities of energy. However, before anyone could come up with any concrete evidence, the debate's focus shifted because of the ‘great’ Wizard Ambrosia, who at times lacked common sense. He claimed that he was able to stabilize his Mana to split the two\n\npolar energies in a controlled manner, which caused all the scholars to shift their focus from the conditions in which the energy splits to the process of it. (It is a shame that scholars today are not interested in insightfully studying natural\n\nphenomena, and rather just want to uncover it just for the sake of using it. This is quite foolish.) Once Mana is split into two polar energies, each polarity begins accumulating energy at a rapid rate and causes an electric discharge. Then, when the\n\nbalance of energy between the two polarities is broken, a transfer of energy occurs from the one with more energy to the other. So imagine what would happen if one could embody either of the polarities and designate his or her target as the other\n\npolarity. Then, using Mana, if he or she polarizes the Mana and also raises his/her own energy level to be higher than their target, what would happen?\nExactly. This is what is known as Electrical Energy Magic.\n\nHow to use the Lightning Bolt\n                -=-\n\nThe Lightning Bolt attack is a magic that uses the mechanic of creating static electricity, which in turn utilizes the characteristics of the negative charge for a sudden electrostatic discharge. During the energy transfusion, a bright explosion\n\nresembling a lightning strike, rushes toward your target as Mana is depleted into replicating this phenomenon. Once all the Mana is depleted from the bolt and the surrounding elements reach equilibrium, the flow of energy ends. (Just like a lightning\n\nstrike in nature.) There are many questions surrounding this magic, such as \"How powerful is it?\" and \"How easy is it to use?\", which is technically asking how much energy it needs and how long it takes. To give you an answer, there is a limit to how much\n\nenergy you can gather, and you can only maintain the energy for about 15 seconds until later coming to a greater grasp of the art. You can charge your energy multiple times to gather more energy, but it is reported that it can become highly unstable after\n\nafter the third charge which is already risky enough. Also, you only have about 15 seconds to charge all your energy. This is because of several factors, such as the difficulty of maintaining the Mana's focus, and also maintaining the polarized energy at\n\nthe same time. (Even if you have plenty of Mana, it is difficult to charge for an extensive electrical bolt). The ‘Lightning Bolt’ attack is used to strike your enemy with electricity . Once your opponent is struck with this attack, they will be in a\n\nstate of shock due to the electricity surging within them as it an energy. Not a tangible object. Since this attack is based on an instant energy explosion between you and your opponent, the lesser the energy gap between you and your opponent, the great\n\ndamage it will inflict as the longer the distance the surge of electricity must travel, the more it discharges. Wasting precious Mana in the long run.\n\n              Simple\n              Usage\n                -=-\n\nOnce you've carefully read through this book, and understood the principles behind the Lightning Bolt attack and are ready to use it, you can do so by following these simple steps. First, a connection to the Void is a must. As any form of magic. The\n\nsimplest manner in which to begin evoking such an element is to picture the empty black abyss that is the Void. A sleet of pure nothingness. Void of any life as the name suggests. Now one must mentally picture lightning crashing down upon the Earth. But\n\nstrictly the lighting. If one were to picture the scene, one could possibly border the realm of Pseudomancy (Illusionary magic) or if too much detail is placed on the Earth, soil or stone may be produced. Then you will see the static discharge enivision\n\nsuch an occurring unfolding before your palm you calm your mind to allow your Mana to polarize the energy and fuel it. Once the preparation is finished, lightning-like strands of light energy will flow around you. This indicated you have successfully\n\ncalibrated yourself with the Void and established an affinity to Electrical Evocation.\n\nThough mentioned before, I want to remind you that the intense light and heat from this attack can significantly startle your opponent.\n\n       Application:\n    Chain Lightning\n               -=-\n\nBefore we move on, I need to reiterate and explain in detail regarding multiple charges. As you know by now, the Lightning Bolt attack is very similar to the actual lightning strike that happens in nature. Does this mean that this magic is capable of\n\nimitating the continuous strikes that occur in a natural lightning strike?\n\nThe answer is yes. Scholars call this ‘Chain Lightning’. By charging the magic multiple times, you are able to hurl this energy to your target back to back.\n\nHowever, there is a limit to how many times you can strike in a row. As previously mentioned, since you can charge up to about three bolts, yet the risk increases with each charge. One interesting fact is, these bolts of energy attract to metallic\n\nobjects. Thus when in the vicinity of metal objects such as the bands of a barrel, swords and armor, iron grating, and other Ferrum or Arcarum apparel, the bolt will change it’s path of perjectory and curve to meet said object.\n\n  Continuous Attack\n    Between Lightning\n         Bolt Users\n               -=-\n\nWe looked at the principle behind the Lightning Bolt, the Chain Lightning attack, and the application of these attacks in the previous chapter. If you think you've mastered everything through these two attacks, you still have a lot to learn from mother\n\nnature. If anyone has studied lightning strikes carefully, you know that lightning does not only occur in single, or multiple chain of strikes. Sometimes, lightning strikes attract other lightning and fuse together. Thus, where there are multiple\n\nLightning Bolt users, they can fuse each other's energy to form a collaborative attack.\n\nThis is a unique trait of Electric energy based magic that other ‘generic’ elemental based magic do not possess. When a user is charging his or her Lightning bol\n\nattack, you can add on to their energy and instantly form a Chain Lightning attack. In other words, if you have charge your Lightning Bolt attack near another user that is charging, your charge will add to their charge, increasing their total number of\n\ncharges.\n\n        The Effects\n                of\n        Lightning Bolt\n               -=-\n\nSo, when is it a good time to use the Lightning Bolt attack? If you are wise, you should be able to figure it out yourself.\n\nFirst, the Lightning attack is good when facing multiple targets at once. Try it out yourself.\n\nUse skill of Electrical Evocation and attempt to fire off a bolt at a grouping of targets.. You will be amazed at how effective and convenient this property can prove to be.\n\nHowever, there is something you must remember: Chaining charges  inflicte damage which subsequently decreases with each hit. Beginners, unaware of this, might overuse the attack and find themselves out of Mana and getting attacked by the opponent.\n\nEven when you successfully use the Chain attack, the opponent might not have received as much damage as you think. Thus, the first target of the Chain Lightning Skill is very important. This is something every good wizard should be mindful.\n\nAuthor: Archmage Crumena V. Illwindior [HeeroZero]\n\nConsoliant: Electomancer Ceruberr Asul'Ailer [CaptainSheepy]\n\nCopier:\nGuildmaster Haadi Mubdee [Eladriendil]", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "-=Alchemist's Fire=-§0\n§0\n§0Water, Water, Fire, Fire Fire, Fire, Air.§0\n§0\n§0Serpent's Stalk, Mandragora, Flametongue, Dwarf's Pumpkin, Drake's Tail, Crimson Vase, Crouching Feather.§0\n§0\n§0\n\n----===========----Aqua Vitae + Mandragora = Salve§0\n§0\n§0M.Salve + Serpent's Stalk = B.Concoction§0\n§0\n§0B.Concoction + Flametongue Root = Firery Remedy§0\n§0\n§0Firery Remedy + Drake's Tale = Fire Brew\n\n----===========----Fire Brew + Dwarf's Pumpkin = Molten Core§0\n§0\n§0Molten Core + Crimson Vase = Nether's Wrath§0\n§0\n§0Nether's Wrath + Crouching Feather = Alchemist's Fire§0\n§0\n§0\n§0----===========----", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0  Task #1 Connecting\n\n    During the early parts of my venture i happend upon the forest of dark blooms. There is rested, the silence was a serene awakening to my surroundings. I could hear the pattering of the woodland creatures across the leaf ladden floor. I began to see\n\nthe forest differently, i saw how the animals must use each other to survive, the same with the plants.§0\n§0\n§0  I thought to interveen when a small creature was being chased by a small fox, but remembering my trial i left it alone and found out quickly\n\nhow there is hierarchy in with the animals. :(§0\n§0\n§0  While meditiating next to the stream i could feel the wind and the movement of the grass, after staying there for a lot longer then i originally planned to, i felt much more connected. As i left the f\n\nbehind i felt almost sad to leave the special place behind.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Athin snowy biome, Ice§0\n§0\n§0Frost Vine snowy mountain, Vines§0\n§0\n§0^ Elf's Hair Vine§0\n§0\n§0Blissfoil woods and plains, blue orchid§0\n§0\n§0Larihei's Fingers snowy mountains grass", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Laws & Guidance for the Warhawkes§0\n§0\n§0The following laws are the infrastructure for a secure environment, regulated to suit the contentments of our residents and visitors.§0\n\nRecurring malicious operations will be disciplined as seen fit; this incorporates penalties such as: amends through payment, detailed labour, temporary exclusion, permanent exile and execution.\n\nDespite the variation, merciful treatment is consistently sustained as the precursory alternative to exorbitant force.\n\nRegular Conduct§0\n§0\n§0- Any form of persistent torment inflicted upon another will be apprehended and ceased.§0\n\nThe unrefined endeavour to induce incessant agitation for your lliran will not be granted a complacent reception. When aforementioned activities are reported, orderly efforts will be launched to activate the dissipation of all anterior pursuits.\n\n- The delivery of needless hostility and immoderate aggression exercised throughout the grounds will not be tolerated; especially that devoid of provocation.\n\nThose who commit needless harm - upon any presence unmerited - are on-par with bestial savages and the primitive ferals. We do not condone barbarity and deem the safety of our community as paramount.\n\n- Association with both deceit and treason, lain upon the entirety of the settlement or the life of the Chieftains, is managed strictly.\n\nNo matter the degree of severity, the Warhawkes carry no tolerance towards this ambition and it will be accordingly penalised with the cost of your life. Any inclination designed to threaten Riv’vallel is not due to be treated passively.\n\n- The theft or damage of belongings, whether valuable or otherwise, will not be tolerated.\n\nPersonal possessions are predictably due to be treasured by the discernment of the owner.\n\nWhile receptiveness to distributing our goods is encouraged, the needless employment of denied profiteering from the property of your lliran is not backed or permitted.\n\n- Personal utilisation of the storage tent and its contents must be authorised by either Chieftain.\n\nIf material consumption without permittance is exposed, it will result in consequences equivalent to those recognised for thievery.\n\n- The mass destruction of farmland and the butchery of our livestock will result in predetermined banishment.\n\nAs a thriving settlement, we rely upon our own produce to sustain the livelihood of our residents. Oem who is willing to eradicate our sustenance is not worthy of our personal interest.\n\nIn addition, the Bokolo should be regarded with particular importance: For the glory of Bokolo, of course!\n\nFormal Expectations", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "-Aqua Vitae-§0\n§0\n§0AQ+SS=Serpant Stalk Salve§0\n§0\n§0AQ+M= Mandragora Salve§0\n§0\n\nSV+M=Boggy Concoction§0\n§0\n§0SV+FR=Null§0\n§0\n§0SV+BL=Null§0\n§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "The fountain pen is a pen I have recently invented. It is a nib pen, similar to your average quill or metal nibbed dip pen, however it does not require an inkwell. Instead, the ink is stored within the pen, in a reservoir. For the ink to get to the nib,\n\nit is drawn through a thin feed beneath the nib via capillary action. For those uneducated as to capillary action, it is the phenomenon where a liquid will automatically draw itself along a thin tube, rather like how water travels through a plant. Anyhow,\n\nshould you hold the pen nib down, you'll find that no ink will leak out. This is due to the fact that air cannot get in, and thus ink cannot get out. However, there is another slit in the nib, aside from the three channels in the feed, which, when the nib\n\nis pressed against paper, the ink is drawn through the feed, and down the slit in the nib toward the paper, through, you guessed it, capillary action. Finally, there are small ridges in the feed to act as a collector, to keep the ink from overflowing onto\n\nyour writings. I constructed my first prototype from metal, and shellacked wood. The feed was made from very finely tinkered steel, while the nib is platinum. The reservoir is durable glass, to allow one to view the ink level, and easily removable for\n\nreplacement when one runs out of ink. Finally, the pen blank, or body, was turned from fine dark wood and a threaded metal piece was put into the rim, to allow for attachment and unattachment to access the reservoir. The wood was shellacked to give it a\n\nrefined finish and polished look.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0*In small text at the bottom of the page is written: \"This book was written with a fountain pen\"*", ""),
        StaticBook("Warden's Notes", "§bLeithlan", "Notes from Raukov, warden of Talabec.§0\n§0\n§024th of The Deep Cold, 1602§0\n§0\n§0We're bunkered down in the keep. Guard's sleeping in the dungeons. It's damn cold. Most of the peasants are sleeping by the hearthfire on the first floor.\n\n18th of Snow's Maiden, 1602§0\n§0\n§0Cold's starting to go away, and the Baron's sent people out to forage for timber. We're also low on food. We should be fine until growing season, I think.\n\n3rd of Malin's Welcome, 1602§0\n§0\n§0Most of the peasants are back in their hovels with their firewood stocked. We're gathering mushrooms from the nearby moor, and the Baron traded some gold reserves from food in the farmers in Haense, just south.\n\n21st of The First Seed, 1602§0\n§0\n§0The farmers are out in the field again, and we'll soon be stockpiling our grain stores. I've sent Doric out to scout the moor. §0\n\n*The remaining text is burnt and falls out of the book in sooty flakes.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Wizard Chess", "§bCecil", "⌘    Wizard  Chess    ⌘\n\nA game originally created by the Wizards Guild of Anthos. The game is an intensive, emotional ball of effort. Built upon trial and error, weakness and strength the game tests the mind of the individual in a team based game.\n\nhe game is played with 10 players in total. A five versus five matchup, each player having their own specific role. These roles are as followed: Top Magister, Cabalist, Arch Wizard, Squire and Magic Hunter. Each roles have their own strengths and weakness\n\nEach role is either offensive, defensive or mixed. Offensive roles roll a 10-sided die, defensive roll a 4-sided die, and mixed roll a 4-sided die. Now, to go more in depth of the roles of each role.\n\n-      Offensive      -\nOffensive roles are always Arch Wizard, there is no choice aswell as Cabalist. Magic Hunter choose between Offensive or Defensive. Top Magister choose between Offensive or Defensive.\n\nAs offensive choice the player gains the 10-sided die. The player may roll the die once per turn, therefore they only roll the die once per team combat. The number they obtain from the die is translated into damage.\n\nThey may target the other player and deal this damage to them.\n\n-      Defensive      -\nDefensive roles are Magic Hunter or Top Magister should they choose so. As defensive role they gain the 4-sided die which can be rolled twice per team combat.\n\nHalf of the total in rolls are damage, the other negates damage.\n\n-        Mixed        -\nMixed may only be played by the Squire role. As such, they obtain the 4-sided die.\n\nThey may roll this 3 times per team combat, 1 of 3 rolls may be used to heal damage after damage is taken, 1 may be used for damage, the last to negate damage.\n\nThe game begins once roles are selected by the players. There are two rounds to the game. The players must use their rolls strategically to counter the opponents combat initiative.\n\nThe order of rolls will always be Defensive - Offensive - Mixed. Each player takes turns rolling.\n\nEach round begins with a roll from the Arch Wizard from both teams, the higher roll gains the initiative and may have their Defensive roll first to begin the round.\n\nThe round ends once one side loses all players. Offensive players have 10 hit points, Defensive have 14 and Mixed have 12.\n\nA large board is typically used with small statuettes to represents a player's role in the game. Any possible ties result in defeat for those involved.\n\nThis game remains a prototype to this day until the creators convene for the final time to settle their 40 year game.\n\n\n~ Penned by,\n   \n   Cecil", ""),
        StaticBook("Haelun'or Schism", "§bOrias", "The Haelun'or Schism\n==================\n\nBy Lucion Sullas\n\n\nRefurbished by Orias\n==================\nThe history of Asulon is known to be rich with wars, political usurpations, monstrous drakes,\n\n===================and the rise and fall of nations. However, one history that eludes most modern non- Mali'aheral scholars is the history of elhaelun'or and it's many trails and tribulations.\n\n         One such exercpt, (to take from ==================\n\n===================a vast swathe) is the Haelun'or Schism   --   a short and unusual period of instability and disunity in the motherland. In this three volume series, one will discuss  the turbulen period for the benefit of future citizens.\n=============\n\n===================\n       The Haelun'or of Asulon was, in this period, ruled by the echillan'thilln -- the Silver Council. Much like its Malinorian contemporary, members were chosen by those who were deemed worthy by the current council members.\n\n===================- the okariran. Two of these counsellors would begin a chain of events eventuallt causing the one, and only, demagogic political usurpation in Mali'aheral history. Their names were Ellir' siol, the Okarir'leyun. (Master of beauty.)\n\n===================and Nelecar, the Okarir'sil (Master of the Sword.)\n\nFrom the very inception of the two working together, friction betwizt their personalities was evident. Nelecar was a soldier with great, and admirable, dedication\n\n=================== to the purity of his kin. His efficeint, though admittedly extrene methods of protection allowed for a distinctly effective military force that has yet to be seen again within the walls of the Mali'aheral. Ellir'siol was an artist, and\n\n===================an architect. Her mesmerising design of of the Haelun'or residential district was one of the finest examples of classical, revivalist mali'aheral architecture available and is still emulated to this day. Touting overture of peace,\n\n===================wisdowm and forethought, she strove only for what can be percieved as the \"Greater Good\" in regards to the motherland. \n\nDespite their own good intentions, there were many obvious faults in thier actions\n\n===================throughout their years in service of cihi'thilln. Nelecar was not a forgiving Mali and when a single, minor wrongdoing was committed, he would often act harshly towards the perpetrator. One such case involved an adolescent mali'aheral\n\n===================who refused the Okarir's demands and was summarily locked in a cell for nearly a month as punishment. \n\n His liberal use of banishment to punish wrongdoes was also harshly debated affair, and was the main issue of the\n\n===================coming schism. \n\n Ellir'siol, however, was by contrast far too forgiving of wrongdoers. She often pressed for impure Mali'aheral (A rather ghastly state to a Mali'aheral.) to be re-intigrated to society, and those\n\n===================whose ideals were not conguent with Larihei's vision were protected by her delicate, and ever political machinations. Retrospectively, conflict should have been predicted.\n\n=================== This is but a tale of two Mali'aheral incapable of compromise, and such shall be shown in the second volume.\n\nPenned origanally by,\nLucion Sullas.\n\nUpdated by,\nOrias.", ""),
        StaticBook("On Telekinesis", "§bSarrion", "On Telekinesis\n------------->\nBy Sarrion Zytiaear\n\nThe following is written from my knowledge as a master of the art of Telekinesis. I was taught by the Infamous Beltran, one of the best at the art I know to this day.\n-Sarrion\n\nTelekinesis is the arcane art of alteration on the environment around the mage by changing a materials gravity and velocity. Simply enough it’s achieved by intently studying the world around the mage by understanding\n\na material inside out and able to weight this material just by a glance. The mage then establishes a mana anchor between them and the object they’re casting on and giving an intense focus\n\non the thought of changing the property of the materials gravity. Distance of the caster and object vary between the skill of the caster, where one who is a student may not be able to lift an object unless it’s a foot in front of them\n\nto a master who may lift an object on the other side of a tea room. When casting the mage is rooted in place due to the intense amount of focus it requires to shift an object, even if it’s just a cup of tea the user must stand still.\n\nIt’s also known that like any other alteration the mage may not lift organic material, fluids, or sands due to how complex the materials are.\n\nCommon combative uses of Telekinesis is the use of throwing knives which can be thrown at the speed of a crossbow bolt by changing it’s velocity, or any other normal day object as a projectile.", ""),
        StaticBook("L.R. Trans.", "§bKirrekith", "Long Range\nTranslocation Device\nInvestigation.\n\nFrom what I can gather from\nArchmage Haadi the long range translocator is developed through a use of 'Void Translocation' magics which establish small pockers within the\n\n- Enchanter. The void translocationist must take a object and place it within the\nvoid, and then a enchanter must co-operate in keeping such a object within the void without the\noriginal void translocationist present. The void translocationish must\n--->\n\n- then re-locate himself and in the\narea he wishes to designate the other opening pull forth the object from the void again, which the Enchanter had held there. This enables a hole to open between the two locations and stays open when powered.\n--->\n\nWrote by Lori Oathcast and re-wrote by\nKirrekith Reffahc\non the 8th of the\nDeep Cold, 1532.", ""),
        StaticBook("Laethisian Times", "§bOrias", "The Laethisian              Period\n----------------Penned by Orias\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~    Now I shall be brief in my forenote, as I have much to account for in very little space, but know this. These accounts are taken from an active\n\nparticapant of this period, I shall hope to avoid any biases or discrepencies in recounting the tales, but with such complexity and vastness I may fall to some. If it has not been made self evident, this tome shall cover everything from the rise of\n\nLaethis to what may be considered modern day.\n----------------\n\n         Ch. 1\nThe Ascension     & The Betrayal\n\n--------------Note; This may be perhaps my most hazy recollection.\n\nTo begin..\n\nMany years following, the assassination of Vydra and Avern's rule under Martial Law, a perhaps unifying or restoring figure emerged as Sohaer.\n\nThis figure came to be known as Laethis Izalith. \n\nHis first years were a budding spring in terms of what a leader could hope for. Relations flourished, and the rebellious Kalenz\nUradir had been killed.\n\n  While it was a humble peace, it did not last, as most tend to do. Laethis morphed into a vile mongrel with his newfound power. \n\n  The Triumvirate established in this reign of terror proved just as sinister. Let it be known that both\n\nContinued..\n\nparties played an equal role in the slaughters and betrayal to our people.\n\nSoon after, Laethis was killed off by unknown conspirators. And perhaps much like\n\nvalah do, a new Izalith assumed himself as our leader.\n\nKalameet was his name, and while his rule is recorded as being a light one It is important to note his abolishment of the Triumvirate. This\n\nwould later set the stage for a coming imperialism in our ruling, one without democracy or representation.\n----------------\n    Chapter 2\n\nThe Weary and The Damned.\n\n--------------\n\nNote; I shall continue my concise and neat format, although if you wish for a more detailed account, I shall be scribed so soon.\n\n  In the wake of an era dominated by the Izaliths, a new\nfigurehead, not\n\nprompted by true or lawful authority. Iatrilemar Elervathar  rose to prominent power.\n\n Iat. or how I shall abbreviate his dully long name, sought to maintain unity coupled with reformation of ties burned in the past\n\nHe was not a true Sohaer no, but rather the Maheral whom reigned as a beacon of hope for some decades.\n\n  Though this was all well and good, a new and true leader had to emerge. Coming from an Anti-mage\n\nheritage, the mali known as Taeleh and his band of other conglomerates took the helm in our goverment.\n\n  Reformations to the law were made, tolerance was somewhat maintained despite\n\nTaeleh's past convictions. Iat still maintaned some prominence with his figure, but it was truly Taeleh that had governed the land.\n\nThe Silluminir (Guardsforce or Haelun'or) were albiet abolished\n\nand replaced by the mage hunters known as The Golden Owl. Who were essentially Taeleh's puppets to enforce his will.\n\nThe previous home of all Aheral in Vailor, The Citadel saw a similar fate as the Sillumir\n\nin being abandoned and replaced by a cihi Taeleh constructed, Fi'Ceru.\n----------------    Chapter 3\n\nThe Continuation of Purity (Perhaps.)\n\n--------------\n\n  Taeleh's reign did last perhaps a decade or more, but as most grand reformers see. Opposition came quick, and it came in multtide. The first election was won, but the second against Avern was lost.\n\n  Avern has still started quite recently, but that has not halted her in revision. The Sohaer has been brought back along with small law changes.\n\n  It is during the youth of her rule that a new appointment seen\n\ncontroversial decision. Iat, the long reigning Maheral had chosen...\n\nLaethis Izalith to succeed him. It has come to be the focal point of politics now, and is debated currently. Though to clarify\n\nyou may wonder, what happened to Laethis after his exile and killing?\nIt can be summarized like so, Laethis fled after his supposed killing and then founded a new cihi to rival Haelun'or. the Sanctuary.\n\nTo conclude...\n\nIt seems we are in the stiffening winter and conclusion of the Laethisian Period, however with a new Maheral and a new Sohaer.. The path of the Mali'Thill is unclear once more.\n\nThe End.\n\nBy \n\nOrias\n\nThe Dutifull scribe of Haelun'or.", ""),
        StaticBook("Random Notes", "§bLucion Sullas", "*What follows are random notes found between pages of confusing arcane symbols and overcomplicated mechanical blueprints.*\n\nMushrooms may be preferable to potatoes for nutritional value. Will consider planning around them should I have the time.\n\nMethod of discerning between poisonous and edible samples needed.\n\nSullas-crete?\n\nSul-ment?\n\nSullas' liquid stone?\n\nWhy was I cursed with such a tragically unpoetic name?\n\nBreathing aparatus complete. Requires immediate testing. Pressure-management still a minor concern, but it is mostly functional.\n\nWill require larger iron shipments to complete buoyancy tests.\n\nThings to seek;\n\nIron,\nglass,\nhoney,\noats, \nbread,\nmilk.\n\nTomorrow's breakfast will be most gratifying. As will the science.\n\nMust remember to keep an eye on those buildings nearby. Unlikely that occupants will see my Submerser, but best to be vigilant.\n\nRemember to look for news regarding the war next time at library. Oren in total control is a preamble to destructive civil-war. So long as it avoids me, and my plans.\n\nVilest Sanctuary. Ice-cannibals around every corner. That impure sack of excrement Laethis has much to answer for. Maybe when his 'lover' devours him he can feel what he unleashed on so many others.\n\nMust remember not to write nonsense in my notebook. \n\nWhy did I feel the need to write that?", ""),
        StaticBook("On Flowers", "§bOrias", "_____\n         /  ___  \\ \n       /  /  _  \\  \\\n      [   I  (_)  I   ]\n       \\  \\ ___ / /\n         \\ _____ /\n             \\ \\ \n            <   /  \n            / / \n            [_]\n         ~<*>~\n  A Compendium on\n  Flora and Fauna\n    -Orias\n\n For all aspiring and\nperhaps newly aquianted conjurers, druids or perhaps herbalists, this is the book for you. \n\n I shall detail all my findings upon the strange verdure that roams on this equally pecuiliar land we enhabit.\n\nTable of Contents\n\nI. Dichotomy of a Flower and etc.\n\nII. Nature of the beast\n\nForeword:\n\n This book is not for the already knowledgable, nor is it for alchemical research. I have wrote this book for one goal, to educate the masses on the basic characteristics and nature of this world.\n\nChapter 1:\nDichotomoy of Flowers, Shubbery and Fauna.\n\n The flower while mundane and utterly basic to some, is a glistening beacon of sacred knowledge to the keen eye. It encompasses the fundamental and\n\ncompex processes of a plant, while still being rather easy to dissect and learn from. \n\n To begin, we must find a flower, any shall do. Flowers grow often in groves of lush, bedded grass. The kind of gras that gets rainfail!  Do not\n\nexpect to find scores of the magnificent tulip in an arid desert. Sunshine is also a must, for without sunlight a plant simply cannot live. Once you have met these two qualifications, simply pluck the flower from the ground. \n \n Now, while some may\n\n differ in foliage, and root systems, all plants comprise of essentially three things. A bud, a stem and roots. Each of which are all equally important. \n\n The bud, bearer of pollen and the beautiful hues is our reproductive center.\n\nYou shall notice in each flower, behind whatever tucked leaves, a pair of spore sacks congregating in the center. Each of which is surrounded by the more pronounced atenae (I like the call them), which look like miniscule copies of the flower.\n\n These two, server to provide coitus and expansion for that particular species, bearing tiny droplets of sap for insects and birds to eat and distribute eventually. \n\nSecondarily, we shall move downwards to the more basic, stem. The stem is-\n\nour body, and thus transports our fluids and diets betwixt the organism. It is coated by a thick greeny plaster, with the occasional thorn or leaf. The thorns evidently protect against needy consumers, while the leaf opens a new window for the-\n\nflower to absorb sunlight, and thus grow. You shall also find in cutting open the stem, an abundance of water and sometimes fiber. This works to hydrate the plant and contain/ support itself respectively.\n\n Conclusively, we reach the earthy and dully shaded roots. They may appear to be bland and unneeded, but hold an inner prowess vital to the survival of all plants. They are our storage system, and our skeleton. The roots lock the flower in it's\n\nplace, preventing gusts of wind to hurl it adrift nor letting the stem collapse on it's own weight and loftiness. Additionally, the roots store food and sunlight for when both are not available. The root prolongs plant life.\n\nChapter 2:\nNature of the Beast.\n\n While you now know the structure and composition of a plant, it's behaviorisms and nature are quite foriegn. This chapter shall explain the rudementary actions a flower might take.\n\n To begin, know that in their desire for energy and water, a plant shall grow towards both, or so I have observed. Even when I place one in the opaque windows of my estranged vacation home,  a  flower will tilt it's body to the sun, even if it was set -\n\nfacing the opposite.\n\n Secondarily, flowers tend to grow in clusters or even clumps of themselves. This is due to the unique way in which a flower's gametes (pollen or spores) are spread, as if you recall-\n\nthe soon to be defecating creature that ate from the bud, is likely to have consumed more than one seed. \n\n Now, to a flower's color and smell. Color is relatively subjective, and doesn't reveal much about the true\n\ndanger or aid a flower hides, it alonside the plant's arouma are indictators to potential consumers that it is ripe for distribution.. (ready to create babies, I suppose.) \n\n Conclusively, we must bear in mind the shape in question.\n\nA variety of thorns prongs removal and warning. A closed bud establishes youth and also decay, while an open bud shines of maturity in contrast. \n\n There are of course, other and more profound studies on the behaviorisms of the flower-\n\n, I would you to  take this as a beginners manual and indoctrination to the open landscape of herbology and plant study. Perhaps you shall be the next to pen a book akin to this one?\n\nAuthor's Notes;\n\nMind my excessive use of plant and flower interchangibly, this book is solely upon flowers and does not apply to all plants.\n\nSome thoughts have been developed more than others for brevity.\n\n I hope you enjoyed the read, \n\n Orias, \nScholar of the Library of Dragur.", ""),
        StaticBook("T.F. Notes I", "§bSarrion Zytiaear", "As I had guessed the art of Transfiguration seems to be just as easy as telekinesis, though this time it requires thorough understanding of Equivalent Exchange and alteration. Every object, no matter how small or large, has dormant mana.\n\nThis mana controls the alchemical make up of every object and such is where alchemy gets its powers, by tapping such and creating elixirs of the likes. This time the idea is to tap this mana using your own,\n\nnot to just change the velocity of this object but to change the whole makeup in your own way.. to alter the material how /you/ choose, though the law of equivalent exchange must be followed, so no turning Ferrum to Aurum any time soon.\n\nMy first connection seemed to be more easy than when I had first connected to control an object’s velocity when I had learned about telekinetics, but this time instead of using my connection to the void\n\nto ‘grip’ an object by this dormant mana, I was actually using my own mana to tap into this mana, and activate it! It was incredible, it had felt like I was one with this object.\n\nEven at my fairly low training with this magic I understand vastly on how this whole concept can be used in the most complex scenarios. For now I am to stick to heating this ball up, or cool it down.\n\nA simple task as temperature is a mere thought, though because of how new I am to this spell It seems to take a toll on my body as if I was a student once more, an odd feeling.\n\nAvenel, after our first lesson, has provide me with this metal ball. I will be using such to practice my first and many attempts of Transmutation, as it’s one of the most easiest matters to understand, especially as a blacksmith such as myself,\n\nor rather ex-blacksmith. It was simple, I had understood the weight of the ball when I had first held it, and I knew the makeup of Ferrum. So it was merely just /thinking/ of the reaction.\n\n-Sarrion\n2nd of Snow's Maiden\n1547", ""),
        StaticBook("Arc. Magci Wiki", "§bKypris Solaria", "Arcane Magic\n-------------------Arcane magic is the most widely spread magic throughout the realms.  It is a type of magic that does not require more than study and repetition,and so well known that many books are sold and written about it,\n\nthough of course, some types are kept secret from the masses. A mage that uses arcane magic draws his powers from the void, a realm of thoughts and emptiness, which he must first learn how to connect to.\n\nThe Void, Mana and Auras\n------------------- The Void: Arcane Magic is the archtype of magic which is fueled by The Void, or more specifically mana.  The Void is an empty plane of existence where things may be created\n\nwith the use of ones imagination and willpower.Many teachers of the Arcane often teach students with the following proverb: \"The Void is nothing, yet everything. Like our imagination, it may be dull and empty; or it can be full and colorful\".\n\nThe Void as a whole is simply a plane where nothing exists, unless the mage makes it exist. Since one must connect to the Void, this means a basic line of communication must be established, generally gained through meditation and practice.\n\nSince Void users must be connect to draw on the Void, distractions are capable of severing the connection for Novices,while Masters are capable of holding onto their connects until they are drained of mana,\n\nor wounded. It should be noted that only mages of proper age can connect to the Void.Those under the age of 16 can receive mental damage if they connect to the Void, and so those of the age of 16 and above can begin to practice magic.\n\n- Mana: When a mage is connected to the Void, he/she may imagine things in this Void; however, a mage must use mana to either draw this spell into the world, or apply it to someone/something.\n\nMana is sightless and is as invisible as the air in our world (See Auras and Arcane Evocation for more details on this). It flows through our world like streams, and is in every living thing, whether it is plants or animals.\n\nAlthough mana comes at a cost, since it flows through people, Void users have gained the ability to use this mana to draw from the Void. Void users often get fatigued when over using mana\n\nand have in rare cases died due to the use of large amounts of mana. Another draw-back with the use of mana is the effect (or lack thereof) on our mortal planewhen you draw on the Void for magics such as Evocations,\n\nthis element which has been evoked must eventually return to the Void.However this can become complicated with such magics as Alteration, as it has the ability to prolong the existence of Void based elements in our world.\n\n- Mana Pools: Mana pools are how much mana we have in our person, and this determines how grand our spells can be, along with the duration a spell can be held in our world. Mana pools are governed by two things;\n\nSkill level and Magic type. Skill level is simply how skilled you are at manipulating mana for your specific Sub-type. For example; the longer you train in the use of Evocations,the better and more efficient you are at manipulating mana for that sub-type.\n\nMagic type is a little more complicated, different magic Sub-types are naturally more mana consuming then others, a few examples of very draining Sub-types are as followed: Alteration, Arcane Evocation and Conjuration.\n\nAlthough far more difficult to learn if one of these are your first Sub-type, you will naturally get a bigger mana pool then someone who's first Sub-type was Illusion, or perhaps an Evocation.\n\n- Auras: Auras are a side-effect from the Void, and is deeply personal to mage's. An Aura directly reflects a mages personality through it's color, which will be listed below this section\n\nAura is generated from the mana pool regularly, and if a mage uses large amounts of mana at once for spells, they in turn produce more aura. Imagine a fire; the more wood you put on it\n\nthe more smoke is formed. Much like this fire, the mana pool can generate more aura depending on how much mana you're using at a given time. Auras are generally harmless and are simply a way of self expression.\n\nSome magics such as Arcane Evocation, Alteration, and Shade are directly tied to Auras, and are heavily effected by them. Auras are able to be openly role-played without being Lore breaking, so feel free to get interesting with it.\n\nBlue: Calculatedness and logicality (Sometimes emotional coldness) \n\nPurple: Mysteriousness\n\nWhite: Benevolence, order and innocence.\n\nBrown: Nurturing and caring\n\nYellow: Greed (Sometimes optimism)\n\nRed: Dominance, power and control (Sometimes tyrannical natures)\n\nGreen: Harmony and balance (Sometimes vanity).\n\nBlack: Chaos and malevolence.\n\nSub-types of Arcane Magic\n------------------- Arcane is the Arch-type of all the following Sub-types, these are also known as \"roots\".\n\n- Alteration:\n\nAlteration is manipulation of properties in the physical world.\n\nTransfiguration [Includes enchanting, transmutation and warding/abjuration]\nTelekinesis [The manipulation and lifting of objects]\nVoid Translocation [Dematerialising matter in the Void for later use]\n\n- Evocation:\nEvocation is the construction of artificial elements or organic tissues.\nElemental Evocation\nArcanism\nConjuration\n\n- Illusion:\nIllusion is the manipulation of emotions, and the five senses, such as sight, smell, sound, touch and taste.\n\nSensory Illusion [A form of illusion in which the mage attempts to influence the mind to fabricate senses and emotions.]\nCognitism [A specific form of Illusion that uses visual aids and mental manipulation to increase intelligence and imagination.]\n\nMental Magic [Involves accessing the minds of individuals to read thoughts and make illusions.]", ""),
        StaticBook("Further Notes", "§bLucion Sullas", "*Yet another tome filled with bizarre symbols and inexplicable diagrams. Perhaps it is in code, or perhaps the writer didn't feel the need to be understood by anyone other than themselves? Regardless, there are notes that can be deciphered in between the\n\npages.*\n\nBeginning next batch of mixtures. I cannot believe I had to leave my previous ones entirely unsupervised due to that ancient Valah's threats. Lets see how that wretched coot manages without a true visionary such as myself.\n\nI really must cease with such grand overtures of praise for myself. Nothing accomplished (yet). Humility in such times is preferable. Brag when successful.\n\nDay 1.\n\nPit A) Appropriate.\nPit B) Appropriate.\nPit C) Appropriate.\nPit D) Reasonable, but slow to set.\n\nDay 2.\n\nPit A) Reasonable.\nPit B) Appropriate.\nPit C) Appropriate.\nPit D) Unacceptable.\n\nDay 3. \n\nPit A) Reasonable.\nPit B) Appropriate.\nPit C) Excellent.\nPit D) Utter trash.\n\nDay 4.\n\nPit A) Unnacceptable.\nPit B) Appropriate.\nPit C) Magnificent.\nPit D) Horrendous.\n\nDay 5: As predicted, significant rainful. Though later than expected.\n\nPit A) Unnacceptable.\nPit B) Reasonable.\nPit C) Marvelous.\nPit D) Utterly repulsive.\n\nI have decided to end my observations a day earlier, as it appears I have found my desired concoction. Limestone was the key.\n\nSurprising.\n\nFinal results:\n\nThough Pit 2 shows some limited promise, I will sadly have to settle with the Pit 3 mixture. Shame about the colour, though.\n\nPit 4 is an utter disappointment. Pits and erosion--may consider giving it\n\nto the Dragur library as a distraction to potential thieves.\n\nConstruction of the testing cylinder has been completed. It took some time to mix so much of my substance. This will require far longer observation on sea-water's effects.\n\nVery important for the future.\n\nShould this long-observation prove an acceptable mixture, I will begin phase-2 pumping tests.\n\n*The rest of the books is blank. What is the writer waiting for?*", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "History of the Boleyn Family§0\n§0~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ ~ §0\n§0Many years ago in a small town a boy named Alfred Boleyn worked away in the workshop of his father, chiseling stone and chipping clumps of ore into gems. At only age 14, he had a grip on how things\n\nwent in a mason workshop. Alfred was always fascinated with the work of his father; watching him barter and trade with the townspeople for his goods. At age 14 however, Alfred's father fell ill to a sickness sweeping over the land. When his father passed,\n\nAlfred was left to handle all the workings of the business. Forced into an early maturing, Alfred began learning the ways of business. Bartering and trading were at first crutches of his, but with time he refined them into a powerful ally. His skill with\n\nwords and with business didn't stop there. With time Alfred expanded the business and moved it elsewhere, creating what is now known as the Boleyn Trading Company. This company, headquartered in the northern town of Ostermark, became rather profitable.\n\nSpecializing still in stone masonry and jewelry, the Boleyn Trade Company did wonders for Alfred and his pockets. Seeing his finesse with people and with commerce, the fair town Jarl, Erik Reyurnt, selected Alfred as a Thane of Ostermark. Alfred\n\ncontinued to bring attention to his name. Meanwhile, his softer side was exposed by a lady in Ostermark; a woman he fell madly in love with upon first sight. Krisa Azara, the strong and witty girl from down the street, couldn't get out of Alfred's head.\n\nOne event after the next formed their inevitable love story. With time Alfred and Krisa were married in the streets of the town they held so dear, henceforth becoming Alfred and Krisa Boleyn. A few years down the line, they were blessed with a child.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Morgan's big book of random notes\n\nTransfiguration;§0\n§0-Everything has dormant mana§0\n§0-Transfiguration is the act of manipulating dormant mana in object by tapping into with your own.§0\n§0-Equivelant Exchange§0\n§0-Change temperature of the object§0\n§0-Understand the object to manipulate\n\nDead-Armour-Ghost-People notes;§0\n§0-Fucking hate water§0\n§0-Can't die§0\n§0-Use gold+§0\n§0-Run like fuck§0\n§0-Try to dismantle\n\nWhen Steven uses his shitty magic wards, use an illusion of a water orb and make him feel pain instead, he'll take it as a water evocation orb and send out a ward, the ward wouldn't be able to stop the Illusion magic, Illusion magic is ultra powerful.\n\nCrumena is Crumena, and I am me, and because me is me, leave me be.\n\nGrass = Sun shines§0\n§0Hunter>Bear>Wolf>Deer>Grass§0\n§0\n§0\n§0Heial§0\n§0Lenniel", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Here lists every and all currently known alchemical reagents and what each ingredient symbolize in terms of elements. §0\n§0 §0\n§0 Take note that I, Ascan, merely wrote this for myself acknowledging that Nelgauth had done the majority of research.\n\n----    [Water]    ---- §0\n§0Athin- Found in snowy biomes, usually frozen solid in ice.§0\n§0\n§0Frost Vine- Found on snowy and mountainous regions, looks like any other vines if not with frozen tips.§0\n\nMandragora- Easily found growing in swamp water, usually under, on or near lily pads.§0\n§0\n§0Serpent's Stalk- Found only near sugarcanes or hidden among them, woods or plains regions.\n\n----     [Fire]     ----§0\n§0\n§0Crimson Vase- Can be found among the forests or plains grass, though is more frequent found near poppies.§0\n§0\n§0Drake's Tail- In desert or savannah regions. One would want to look for dried shrubs to find it.\n\nBlood Lotus- Found in woods or plains, though are easily obtained in deserts or savannah, usually found growing alongside Drake's Tail.§0\n§0\n§0Flametongue Root- Found in large quantities under poppies in a plain or forest area.\n\n----      [Air]     ----§0\n§0\n§0Crouching Feather- Found only in woods or plains. They resemble a feather, and are hidden well in grasses, hence their given name.§0\n§0\n§0Halfling's Grass- Grows among the woods and plains grass.\n\nElf's Hair Vine- On mountainous or snowy regions, a vine like any others, but is a strong alchemical reagent and §0thus..could§0 prove difficult to obtain.§0\n§0\n§0Larihei's Fingers- Could be found on the same region as Elf's Hair Vines, though among the gr\n\n----    [Earth]    ----§0\n§0\n§0Alabaster Leaf- Commonly found in tall plains or forest grasses.§0\n§0\n§0Saffvil- Easily found around swamp grass.§0\n§0\n§0Tippen's Root- Could be found in abundance in forest or plains Grass.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "9th of The First Seed§0\n§01623, Summer§0\n§0\n§0The books in the Dragon Library are shackled to the shelves.  Thief I may be, even I cannot pick these locks.§0\n§0\n§0The halls are empty, but prior experiance tells me they will not remain so.\n\n10th of The First Seed 1623, Summer§0\n§0\n§0Is there anything sadder than a Lich without a spell to its name?§0\n§0\n§0The books speak of something called the Void.  Whatever it is, this Void seems to be the root of wizardry.\n\n11th of The First Seed 1623, Summer§0\n§0\n§0The Void crops up more and more the deeper I delve.  The Dragon Library has many books on the matter.§0\n§0\n§0Perhaps it is time to seek out one of the Coven.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Sky Mapper§0\n§0                        =O=§0\n§0\n§0Recorded by§0\n§0Lion Sataniel DeNurem§0\n§0\n§0-------------------§0\n§0Foreword§0\n§0\n§0This work came about after a discussion with a rusted knight in the portcullis of Mordskov. He put-me-on to the\n\nthe idea of creating an enchanted telescope to improve it's capabilities in an ehancing way. This was after I had discussed my intention to build an astronomical observation structure to investigate the skies further. Understanding and mapping them.\n\n13th of The Deep Cold, Year 1620§0\n§0-----------Mordskov§0\n§0\n§0I have just returned from the High Elven settlement where I succesfully obtained their co-operation on the development of a magically enhanced telescope to act as a prototype for an eventual\n\ninstallation of a much more powerful magiscope into the planned astronomical observation tower.§0\n§0\n§0The next plan of action is to assess the best place in my Mordskov to lay the foundations for the exploration of the skies above and beyond ours.\n\nI found a location, but now I write about something completely different.§0\n§0-----§0\n§0\n§0Rhova'dir is some sort of scholar that follows and believes in Aspects and minors in spirits. Enlightening me to the idea that the spiritual language is\n\ncalled blackspeech and it is what Krug spoke before given tusks... (these tusks bastardised the tongue, making Old Blah come to be. The language that predated Blah spoken in contemporary orcish times. Apohet teaches Krug Blackspeech.\n\nIblees teaches Elvish.§0\n§0Aeriel teaches Flexio.§0\n§0\n§0These are magic languages that were forgotten by time for reasons that were not accidental. I believe that speaking these languages allows the User to cast active mana by way of incantation. Spoken-\n\n-spells.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Universal free education.§0\n§0\n§0By: Marcus Hotchen\n\nFor some time the benefits of universal education have been preached.§0\n§0Most formally by the sanonist faction that was denounced by the Holy Orenian Empire.§0\n§0After the dissapearance of teh Sanonists this subject has mostly been ignored.\n\nIn my opinion universal education should be implemented accros all nation states.§0\n§0\n§0The benefits of universal education are many and I will try and convince you of its usefullnes.§0\n\nMany parents need to work hard and feed their family.§0\n§0Yet time is money and much time is spent by the parents to educate their children.§0\n§0The other option for most parents is worse and that is not to give their children any education at all.§0\n\nThe only people who can afford to get their children educated by teachers or friends are people of the upper class who have money or connections to get teachers for their child.§0\n§0\n§0Yet a large percentage of the toal population does not\n\nhave any education and that includes the lower and middle class.§0\n§0\n§0My solution is to get the state to sponsor a basic school for children with the parents paying a small percentage of the education thus enabling lower class citizens being able to educate\n\ntheir children.§0\n§0\n§0This school should have the goal to learn all children how to: read and write, count and as an extra subject taking basic martial lessons.§0\n§0\n§0Each subject should be taught by a teacher with some experience in the subject.\n\nA teacher should also be able to properly interact with children and should not be seen as overly aggresive and should help discipline children when needed.§0\n§0\n§0A person might argue that a school would not give an advantage to soceity and will only cost\n\nmoney.§0\n§0\n§0Saying this a person might have some good points but generally I disagree.§0\n§0This is because a universal education would be able to increase the amount of middle class citizens, furthermore this will also be able to get more artists and\n\nother creative artisans.§0\n§0Thus if an education is given then 10 years after the implementation there is a possibility of a cultural golden age with the new generation being educated and promoting the idea of people thinking for themselves beckoning more\n\npeople to get creative jobs and not work as lowly serfs.§0\n§0\n§0Yet without government support this idea is impossible to implement otherwise education would only be avaiblable to the rich and the rich middle class with only fees being used for finance.\n\nThis is just my opinion and hopefully it will be listened to by calm heads.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0Signed,§0\n§0Marcus Hotchen", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Mansion Charter§0\n§0\n§0Starting charter: §0\n§0One kitchen, One bedroom, One common room.§0\n§0\n§0Plus one room every person recruited to Mordskov\n\nList of recruited Citizens§0\n§0\n§0El'yra Adr'yen§0\n§0\n§0Lusha Exilevils§0\n§0\n§0Lostro Trueside§0\n§0\n§0Merilia Monzoho§0\n§0\n§0Julip Swan§0\n§0\n§0Nephren El\n\nTeldram Jav'el", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "On The Void, §0\n§0By Miningtilldeath§0\n§0\n§0Index §0\n§0Chapter I What is the Void§0\n§0Chapter II How we can use the Void§0\n§0Chapter III Connecting to the Void§0\n§0\n§0Transcribed by Exa'vier\n\nChapter I§0\n§0What is the Void? No doubt you as the reader know it is the source of Arcane Magic (which includes the art of evocation, illusion, and alteration). But what actually /is/ it? The oid is a plane of excistance that contains absolutly nothing\n\nYet at the same time, it contains everything. Strange and complex as it may sound, it is in face reletivly simple. You see the Void is a place of /potential/. Thoughts, feelings, elements. Everything exists really exists within the void yet purely as\n\npotential, waiting to be shaped and formed. Such is the role of the Arcane Mage.\n\nChapter II §0\n§0How can we use the void? As mentioned the previous chapter, everything that exists in our world exists as potential in the Void. However everything in the Void is useless to us. Therefore through training a mage can learn to connect to the\n\nVoid and harness it's potential in various ways. One example, is Evocation, the art of evoking a certain element. An evokanist can", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "§0\n§0~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~  Reasearch on Non-Spoling Agricultural Products.§0\n§0\n§0     By: Varahock§0\n§0\n§0~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n  Table of Contents§0\n§0~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~-Introduction: Page 3§0\n§0-Wheat: Page 4\n\n      Introduction§0\n§0~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Dear Camille,§0\n§0I'm sorry, I really am: Truly. I didn't mean any what I said, just, times have been tough, alright? I gotta leave for a while now, going to be real busy comin' in and out of Axios on several ships. I owe somethin' to someone and I'm not\n\nabout to get you or me, or anyone I love killed for it. I hope that when I finish this, we can make up: Like old times sake.§0\n§0\n§0The building is yours to take care of while I'm gone, keep it locked up, use it: Whatever you like.\n\nKeep it cool, kiddo.§0\n§0\n§0Love,§0\n§0Pasquale Calabreeni§0\n§0Your Former Boss,§0\n§0and someone who really cares about you.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dream of Darknes", "§bLagertha Ojørna", "A Dream of Darkness\n\n\n\n\n         Written by\n      Lagertha Ojorna\n\n\n\n\n\n         To Agatha,\n     Someone who can\nmake my bitterness into warmth.\n\n    In deep sleep, I see what is a dark misty entity. It lingers in the darkness before coming upon a ruin within a forest.\n    The ruin is covered in hanging moss, and is in a crumble. The mist finds no entry, so instead forces its self upon a crumbling-\n\nwall.\n    The wall gives in after much force is applied to it. The mist continues on, now inside the ruin.\n    The mist makes its through the ruin, a long corridore. On each side of the corridore are pedastals, each with a unique tome upon it.\n\n    The mist then turns into a room larger than the corridore. There it finds five pedastals with one tome on each. It begins attacking them, shredding them and destroying the pedastals.\n    One of the five pedastals sink into the stone floor below, -\n\nprotecting the tome on it. The mist, now giving a feeling of enragement, is then surrounded by 6 warriors whom seem to be conjurations.\n    The warriors charge at the mist, who then sinks into the ground with the pedastal, destroying the tome.\n\n    At this moment, the ruinm begins to shake. The ceiling crumbles, and caves in on the warriors. The mist comes from the ground and forces its way out of the debris.\n    The mist comes upon darkness, and disappears. Taking whatever knowledge it-\n\ndestroyed within the tomes.\n\n\n    \"Neither by chance,\nnor fate.\"\n\n       - Algor Ojorna", ""),
        StaticBook("Two Doors", "§bDolan Velethen", "Two doors, both opaque in feature, stood in front of two staggly men. On the left stoff Veren, a human whose life was reached half. To his right stood Hijol, a wood elf younger than a fox out of season.\n\nIn between them was a sign that read \"Choose carfully\". Hijol inspected the sign and claimed that the sign was closer to the right door than the left one.\n\nAfter some long discussion the two decided that they must both choose the same door. They felt tired and rested.\n\nThe next marrow Hijol woke to fine two sleeping children. Both girls of unrecognizable race. He awoke one and quickly told her his tale. \"The right door is correct\" He notes that the sign has dissappeared. \"There was a sign that read 'There must be only\n\none right door'\".\n\nMeanwhile Veren awoke to find the other girl. Afyer he told her she must not trust Hijol, the two groups conjoined.\n\nFighting words came out. In one corner stood anger and spite.\n\nThe other stoff curriosity and fear. The winner, only the one brave enough to turn a knob,\n\nThey grew weary and slept another night. The next marrow Hijol's girl and Veren's girl awoke to find themselves alone and, adults.\n\nIn Hojol's girl's mind she had two facts, she must choose a door with Veren's girl, and it has to be  the right one. Veren's girl was to scared to speak to Hijol's girl.\n\nHijol's girl only had one option, in her mind, she must take out veren's girl to\n\ncontinue...\n\nHer fists hit her face. Her blood tained her tunic. Fist meet fist, and death was quick.\n\nHijol's girl turned the right knob slowly. On the other side was horrer. Both doors went to the same place. A small\n\nbedrock room with a sign that read \"Life isn't going to bend it'self to your perceptions.\"", ""),
        StaticBook(":)", "§bLord Limpy Tardly", "I <3 u", ""),
        StaticBook("When He Recoils", "§bKatherine de Savoie", "When  a man recoils his hand and give you a questionable look, it usually means you are very weird. Stop what you are doing, breathe and ask yourself, 'Is this really me?' Of course you can always redeem yourself by apologizing, but in the long wrong it\n\nwill effect the rest of your life. It will give you nightmares and worries. Send notes and wait for §0replies...it§0 is terrible in the long wrong. Don't let him recoil his hand away from your's let alone give you a questionable look. Be you! Then again, if\n\nyou are, then you need help. Please contact your nearest mental doctor or mental mage.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "§0-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-     Tales & History:§0\n§0  Blackwood Company§0\n§0-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-§0\n§0\n§0           By§0\n§0    Alessa Garthan§0\n§0     (Eagles2910)\n\n\n§0-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-§0\n§0\"We like to call ourselves tradesmen, servicemen, and sellswords.§0\n§0\n§0  -Kelian Dawnstrider,§0\n§0 in the year of 1516-§0\n§0-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-          History§0\n§0-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-   It is said the the Blackwood Company§0\n§0was orginally founded in the early 1500's though before 1516. Though there were many co-founders of the group, the Malinov family was said to be\n\nthe leading family of the group. The head of the Malinov family was Kazamir and with him were his son, Vladimir Malinov, and daughter, Rozaliya Malinov.§0\n§0  However there were key members and founders of the group who were not related§0\n§0by blood to the trio.\n\nOne such noteable figure was Kelian Dawnstrider. His role as the Manager of Internal and External affairs would help the Company accomplish many things during its time in Vailor.§0\n§0  Owynn Iron-forge was also another high ranking member outside of the\n\nfamily. Most of his efforts were helping organizing a mining operation and training the sellsword portation of the Company.§0\n§0  Lastly, the only known member of the Blackwood Company to be alive is Nemir V. The Malinov Family had taken Nemir in as one\n\nof their own. It is said that she arrived to them at a very young age but quickly became something of a leader amongst the group. Eventually she would be known as their greatest archer.§0\n§0  Something to note about these other founders is that they\n\nwere not in fact human. Nemir and Kelian were actually High elves and Owynn was a Dwarf. The diversity among the leadership ultimately led to a more diverse array in members of the Company.§0\n§0  With the difference races came a merge of different ideas\n\nand knowledge which allowed Blackwood Company to succeed and grow. For some time the Company remained largely out of the poltics of Vailor and was very successful traders and hired guards. However this changed when a small Dwarven\n\nCivil War had arisen in the years before the Duke's War. The Blackwood Company along with the Dwarven Loyalists took victory with ease, and this would establish the Company as well sought out mercenaries for the coming Duke's War.\n\n  There was a bidding war which in the end led to Blackwood Company being contracted by the Ducal Coalition forces. The contract though was only for one battle to the Ducal Coalitions dismay and to the Blackwood Company's unforseen luck. After that battle\n\nhad been lost to the Pro-Ashford forces, the Blackwood Company recieved word from Augustus de Sola.§0\n§0  This man who would later be known as Augustus d'Amaury offered this new but experienced Company a choice. They were to either surrender and given the\n\nchance to join his personal forces or be hunted down upon the Pro-Ashford victory.§0\n§0  The leaders of the Blackwood Company sought out the opinion of the lower members and it was agreed that the former option was better than the later.§0\n§0  So, when the time\n\ncame for the next and final battle of the Duke's War, the Siege of Barrowyk, the men of Blackwood Company would fight under their new liege. No longer were they sellswords and tradesmen but the very first Honor Guard of Augustus d'Amuary.§0\n\n  And so concludes the History portion of The Blackwood Company for they were no longer that. A choice that would forever change the Malinov Family and all other members of the group.\n\n\n§0-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=- \"And so the days of adventuring and nights of drinking begin.\"§0\n§0\n§0  -Rozaliya Malinov, in the year 1514 when Blackwood Co. began-§0\n§0-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-   The Tale of Three§0\n§0   Drunken Friends§0\n§0-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-  Once on a cool dark night three young members left the saftey of their keep and took to Laureh'lin. All ready in a drunken state", ""),
        StaticBook("Scrolls of Grace", "§bIngelrannus", "Glorious spirit, my keeper, I strayed from the path and stepped into darkness. I was blinded, my anger turned to an uncontrollable rage. Purge me of sin, brighten the darkness in my soul. Allow me to repent so I may live in your glory afresh.\n\nInfinite God, my keeper and guardian, I strayed from your path. My mind was weak, I did not spread your word as well as I could. Forgive me for my mistakes, cure me of my flaws. Sanction me for my sins so I may feel your divine power anew.\n\nMy Father, bringer of all that's good, I come to you to confess my sins. My apologies, I have not loved you with all my heart. Liberate me of my sins, cure me of my flaws. I accept your chosen verdict so I may be rid of this guilt and live life afresh.\n\nHoly Father, hallowed be your name, I come to you to confess my sins. I failed you, my greed led me to embezzle money for my family's sake. Relieve me of my sins, heal me of these self inflicted wounds.\n\nGlorious Father, eternal light in the darkness, I need to relieve my heart of darkness. I went astray, I took what isn't mine. Liberate me of my sins, have mercy on my soul. Sanction me for my sins so I may spread your glory to others.\n\nMy God, custodian of life, I have a confession to make for I have sinned. I've let you down, I was tempted by the flesh of another. Purge me of sin, I won't fail you again. Discipline me as you see fit so I may savor your eternal soul once more.\n\nIllustrious spirit, eternal beacon of hope, I strayed from your path. I was feebleminded, I have not loved you with all my heart. Relieve me of my sins, I won't fail you again. Sanction me for my sins so I may spread your glory to others.\n\nRevered Mother, eternal light of life, I strayed from your path. Have mercy on me, I have not loved you with all my heart. Relieve me of my sins, unburden me of this pain. I put my fate in your hands so I can walk the right path once again.\n\nExalted Mother, merciful creator, ashamed I admit that I have sinned. I fell from the path, I spread a rumor at the expense of another. Liberate me of my darkness, I won't fail you again. Show me mercy so I may delight in your will.\n\nIllustrious God, ruler in the heavens, I come to you with a remorseful heart. My sincerest apologies, I passed judgment where it wasn't my right to do so. I accept your punishment, unburden me of this pain.\n\nOur God, protector of life, I lost your light and stepped into darkness. I've let you down, I played with temptation and paid the price. I seek redemption, relieve me of my demons. Punish me as you see fit so I can walk the right path once again.\n\nDearest Father, creator of all life, temptation took hold of me in a moment of weakness. I've let you down, I have not loved you with all my heart. I beg your forgiveness, deliver me from evil.\n\nHeavenly Father, custodian of life, I come before you to confess me sins. I've let you down, I took what isn't mine. Purge me of sin, have mercy on my soul. Cast your judgment so I may savor your eternal soul once more.\n\nCelestial spirit, my redeemer, ashamed I admit that I have sinned. Absolve me, my pride led me to disobey my own parents. Grant me your forgiveness, heal me of these self inflicted wounds.\n\nHallowed God, protector of life, I come before you to confess me sins. I deserted you, I desired more power to change the world. Relieve me of my sins, unburden me of this pain. Cast your judgment so I may bask in your glory anew.", ""),
        StaticBook("A note to Sixtus", "JavaWizard", "Your Holiness,\n\nI will be moving back to Godansk to regain footing with the Raevir. I have set up a house there, and I also set up a house for two priest studying under me. I thank you for your generocity!\n\n- Yaroslav Vasilievna", ""),
        StaticBook("To Casimir Piast", "§bPatrek Roswell", "To the Exalted Magnate of the Pasnian People, Casimir, second of his name of House Piast.§0\n§0\n§0News have travelled far and wide across the vastness of Oren, telling stories of the reinvigorated peoples of Pasnia and their reunification.\n\nI myself, have found myself in such a position in which your people had suffered in so long.§0\n§0\n§0But I, along with my House shall rise once more as your people has.§0\n§0\n§0And as a friendly gesture I wish that you may find use-\n\n- for these supplies to rebuild your peoples former glory in the world and the empire.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0- Patrek Roswell, Patriarch of House Roswell", ""),
        StaticBook("Police Report", "§bBeluar the Botanist", "This is a criminal report of Mister Larry, or Laorin. He is accused of crimes against many including thievery, property damage, and assault. These crimes stretch from these lands into the Caliphate, where he reportedly was beaten badly after picking a\n\nfight with a group there. He should be evicted from his home and it should be given to someone of more decency and respect. There are many around these lands who need homes, so we should not waste them on criminals.\n\nI would like this report to remain\n\nanonymous, so that the scary criminal does not come after me.", ""),
        StaticBook("Kaiser's Love", "§bHigh Dictator Frederick II", "===Heil Vandaloria===\n\n\n    The Kaisers Love\n\n\n\n\n    Approved by the\n    Ministry of Truth\n\n\n\n==================\n\nThe people of Al'Wakhrah slept soundly in their beds when the Ghouls attacked. The three Ghouls stood firm at the entrance to the city, looking for easy targets to consume. Larry Kringle, an Elven officer within the Reich Ministry of Truth, sounded the\n\nalarm. The Kaisereich answered. The good denizens of the Hallowvale Company answered the call, headed by the Qalasheen Champion of the Hallowvale and the Kaiser himself. The company created a line of Elves and Humans alike at the gate.\n\nThe three Ghouls would be no match for the Kaisers finest! The elite troops pulled out their aurum blades and laid waste to the evil creatures where they stood. They never even reached the steps to Al'Wakhrah. The Champion and the Grand Conservitor worked\n\ntogether to take one of the ghouls head clean off! The Kaiser himself slashed with no mercy, finally impaling an aurum dagger int he eye socket of one of the animated corpses. The last was slow, behind the other two. This nightmarish creations of Iblees\n\norigin were hacked down by an unknown citizen of the Kaisereich. The unknown solider of Good. The Kaiser, under instruction from a wandering Cleric, ordered the building of a fire to burn the bodies of the fetid Ghouls. The group rallies, all lending a\n\nhand to rid the world of the monstrosities. \n\nThe Kaiser had few words for the valiant group that night, but offered his humbles thanks to all those who helped secure the safety of the children inside the walls of Al'Wakhrah. His humility\n\nwas unexpected, and took the group by surprise. It was then that they realized, we as an Empire, as Vanderlorians, are stronger together than we are apart. The Humans and Elves worked hand in hand, under the grace of God, and were victorious.\n\nThe Kaisers strongest words were the quietest spoken. \n\n\n     HEIL VANDALORIA\n     HEIL ROVINKIN\n     HEIL DECIMUS\n     HEIL TRUTH", ""),
        StaticBook("Hunt Note", "§bCrystal Bel'anoche", "Who’s pubs were all kinda borin’", ""),
        StaticBook("Passport III", "§bVejk Grandaxe", "Surname: Greyhame\n\nForename: Eraborn\n\nAge:23\n\nTitle: Magister\n\nOccupation: Captain/Magister\n\nRace: Human\n\nPurpouse in Town: Security, Resident\n\nHouse number: Soon be getting a house\n\nFull title: Captain Eraborn Greyhame", ""),
        StaticBook("FTM, Issue I", "§bArchibald", "-+ From the Mouth +-\n\n   Good day, good night, or good evening, or even good morning. I am Archibald Vallero. This book is quite simple. I go around asking other people questions, sometimes deep and personal, and then scribe them down in this tome\n\nfor you all to read and enjoy. I've no bias this time when it comes to who I ask, though keep in mind the demographics of the Descendant races. Enjoy. \n\nI will begin this first issue with an answer from one of my friends, Zeliek, a paladin of Xan.\n\nQI: Do you prefer a dictatorship or a republic? Why?\n\nZeliek: \"Republic. I just picked one at random. I don't even know what you're talking about.\"\n\nQ2: Do you think that crucifying people like the Amyasmen do is worse than torture? If so, why?\n\nShariana: \"Alright, I think that crucifixion is taking the easy way to solve something. Because torture, you have a... Hand on experience with\n\nsomeone. Hm... I think that is everything, really. The Amyas' have no experience with torture, and I doubt that any of them would be man enough to try it.\"\n\nQ3: Do you think that magic, in the future, will cause unforeseen catastrophes? If so, why?\n\nSalendys Doomforged: \"It has in the past and it will keep happening as long as there are irresponsible mages around.\"\n\nQ4: Do you believe that one of the Descendant races should be exterminated from the face of this realm? If so, which one and why?\n\nLyria Serthek:  \"Absolutely not. Because we all have a right to live, and why slay off a /whole/ race? Only a certain\n\nfew should die, and not be compared to their whole race.\"\n\nQ5: Do you believe that one day we will run out of continents and land to return to?\n\nCharles Fournier: \"No, why not?\"\n\nQ6: Thighs or breasts.\n\nForrest Sarr: \"Thighs.\"\n\nQ7: Would you prefer a redhead with green eyes, or a brunette with blue eyes?\n\nJon Snow: \"Brunette, of course! Redheads are usually... crazy.\"\n\nQ8: Do you think that any Descendant race will become extinct within the next 100 years? If so, which one?\n\nExalprick Oxenfeldt: \"Um... Yes I'll smash all their heads, crush 'm against a wall! Put them on spikes!\"\n\nQ9: Is the abundance of mages within the realm causing more or less chaos?\n\nDain Stormcrow: \"There are an abundance of mages? From what I understand of magic, or at least one of its major philosophies is balance. If balance\n\nis not kept preserved, things go out of whack.\"\n\nQ10: Would you rather eat a raw spider, or have a silverfish placed in your ear?\n\nDemagol Doomforged: \"Spideh.\"\n\nQ11: Do you think that necromantic practices are simply misunderstood, or, truly, are they just evil? \n\nAsher: \"Um, misunderstood.\n\nQ12: Are the four Descendant races doing considerably well given their curses?\n\nCheza Stirling: \"Some are, some aren't. Some better than others. Each race is doing 'alright' I suppose. Each has land, but they have problems.\"\n\nQ13: Is there truly such a thing as 'good' or 'evil' in your opinion, or is everything just formed by the aengudaemons above?\n\nGuarger Tsouderous: \"Everything is based on opinion, Archibald.\"\n\nQ14: What would you do if you saw an Orcish cub being bullied by a group of elven civilians? \n\nRyder Sturtart: \"Pick the cub up and take him away.\"\n\nQ15: Would you rather have to assassinate a loved king, or kill a new born child? Which one and why?\n\nSam Beadoin: \"King. Kings are all corrupt, no matter how loved. At least, human kings are...\"\n\nQ16: Do you think that immortality is achievable? \n\nOan: \"Yes, I think it is. What one must ask themselves, though, is this: How much are you willing to give up for it?\"\n\nQ17: Were the 'golden' ages of Aegis overrated?\n\nCharis: \"I wouldn't know, but Mister KAlen speaks of Alras as if it were golden. So, I can't say no.\"\n\nQ18: Would you rather kill a past lover or an old, human man?\n\nLicia: \"I have no past lovers. I am sworn to Xan and the creator only.\"\n\nQ19: Are aengudaemons the cause of all issues in the world, or is it truly us who has caused all these faults?\n\nMithras: \"It's a mix. Aenguls and Daemons interfere and use us because of how flawed we are. All of us differentiate, we all hold differ-\n\n-ent views. It makes us easy pawns in their games, they're merely bored children, you see. It's like when a child plays with a chess set. We're the pieces.\"\n\nQ20: Do you prefer to eat something sweet or sour at night? And why? \n\nCaitlyn: \"Sweet. Sour never tastes nice.\"\n\nQ21: Are we really in control of our own lives? Is our fate chosen by us?\n\nDaemon: \"We are in control of our lives. Fate is for the weak who need something to look forward to rather than doing it themselves.\"\n\nQ22: Who would win in a fight to the death: Blundermore or Archmage Cataris?\n\nLuthar: \"Blundermore. Despite Liches' callous and insidious nature,  our trickery only goes so far against raw holy power.\"\n\nQ23: From Iblees to Setherien, what has been the Descendant race's greatest threat in your opinion?\n\nJa'Mukar: \"Setherien. Because Iblees nevever did anything and he was defeated quite quickly. Where as Setherien showed his face and not hide\n\naway in an unknown location.\" \n\n*Translated by me, his accent was very thick!*\n\nQ24: Will the Human empire of Oren eventually dissolve entirely in the future, in your opinion?\n\nHorik Storasvard: \"Nay! Oren vill be forever! Because dey have da drue faith in da creador! And dey are the stronges der es!\"\n\nQ25: Out of all the four kinds of architecture exhibited by the Descendant races, which race's architecture do you favor the most? \n\nSer Bjorn of Bearhill: \"Human. It makes me feel safe. Other nations buildings just look . . . disgusting.\"\n\nQ26: If you had immortality, what's the first goal you would want to achieve?\n\nBeth: \"Uh . . . Eat a bunch of cake.\"\n\nQ27: From elven women to human, which one would you say is the most attractive, hands down? \n\nOliver Crowley: \"Human. Better build and often faces have more beauty to them.\"\n\nQ28: Where did homosexuality originate, do you think? The high elves, perhaps, or the elven kind in general? Even another race, even?\n\nVuln Shadeleaf: \"I don't know where it originated, but it sure seems likely it started with the mali'ker.\"\n\nQ29: House Chivay or House Horen? \n\nDread Knight Lennox(Dread Knight Noxx): \"I don't prefer either . . . both are idiotic.\"\n\n*I decided to ask him another question!*\n\nQ30: Was immortality worth it?\n\nDread Knight Lennox: \"Indeed.\"\n\nQ31: Would you rather demolish an orphanage or build a brothel?\n\nDorian Hunter: \"Build a brothel. Obviously. It's obvious. Girls.\"\n\nThat's the end of this book. But do not worry, this is only part one! I'm thinking of writing up another quite soon, and there'll be questions just as humorous or serious in the next one as there was in this one. Thank you for reading. Also, I'd rather\n\nnot answer any questions myself until after the end of the second issue, thanks. \n\n       //---\\\\\n      //       \\\\\n     //         \\\\\n    //========\\\\\n   //              \\\\\n  //                \\\\\n //                  \\\\", ""),
        StaticBook("Trials", "§bClan Father Vidar Frostbeard", "Frostbeard Trials\n   By Clan Father\n  Vidar Frostbeard\n\nAll Frostbeards must participate in their trials before they may ascend from beardling hood. On the day of their trial, they shall journey to the forests, armed with nothing but a spear and wearing naught but the simplest of clothes. Their task to\n\ntrack down a great bear and slay it, then proceed to skin its pelt and bring it back to their kinsmen.\n\nWhen he returns, the Frostbeards gather and the Clan Father and his elders examine the pelt. They study it and decide whether the pelt the beardling\n\nhas acquired is worthy of becoming a true Dwed among his kinsmen.\n\nIf the pelt is accepted, the final step of the Ceremony is lighting a grand bonfire. The Clan father would walk to the beardling and place his hands on the beardling's shoulders.\n\n\"BARUK KHAZAD!\" is what the Clan Father exclaims and then the beardling would say \"KHAZAD AI-MENU!\"\n\nThe Frostbeards are marked by the very same pelt that most wear upon their back and shoulders for the rest of their days and it is a rare sight to\n\nsee one without theirs on. The trials that a beardling passes are a test of courage and valor for those are two of the esteemed traits a Frostbeard must hold.", ""),
        StaticBook("Lunavim", "§bEsgäleth Vynatis", "My thanks for protection.\n\nBy Lunavim Lym-friend.\n\nEntitled to Lym.\n\nFrom light to darkness.\nPit of snakes full of venom.\nDagger in my heart.\n\nA gentle hand comes.\nThe scent sweet scent of blue orcid.\nFrom darkness to light.\n\nThank you is too small.\nEmbrace too hollow and short.\nAn art will last long.", ""),
        StaticBook("The T", "§bLionel Amador", "9th of First Seed, 1771. My name is Lionel Amador, I've traveled into the Spirit World via a boat as Orgon's taint consumed the world of Vailor. My home is gone, but my family is with me, along with our help and allies. There is hope yet, to a land we\n\nhave yet to see. Those who fell off the boat have perished. We are moving now, I shall stop writing, wish me well. \n~Lionel Amador", ""),
        StaticBook("Dwarf Civil War", "§bJistuma", "*---*---*---*---*\n\nThe first dwarven civil war of Anthos\n\n\nTestimony By Rosso\n\n  *---*---*---*---*\n\nWe first heard of the rebellion when their leader, a dwarf called Duregar, sent the Hold of VaerHaven a letter asking for the hold to join them. It didn’t impress me, the letter seemed poorly written, small, and with information that should not had been\n\nsaid in such a way, like his name and those of his allies. A meeting was done between the council of VaerHaven, which consisted of I, Rosso, the youngest of all councilman, a human, yet the one alive who has served as a councilman the longest, going back\n\nto the time of Silva Insula, then there is Killeki, he has been a councilman since the formation of Anthos, and a long time member of Silva Insula before, and to end we have Kardel, Jarl of the hold, took over when Ferron died, he had been around since\n\nthe time of Silva Insula, yet had never been on the council.\n\nMany things were discussed, the seeming inability of the leader of the rebellion to think and act correctly, what would happen if we joined, what happened if we didn’t, and the\n\nconsequences of it all. Before the meeting we had heard from the adunians, they were former members of VaerHaven, and banished by the legion and the king of the dwarves. They served a great deal in the decision of the council.\n\nIn the end, we had three choices:\n\n1. Remain with the king of the dwarves\n\n2. Remain neutral\n\n3. Join the rebels\n\nOne would think the first choice would be the safest, but they would be wrong. VaerHaven would be the town closest to the rebels, and all members of the hold would be made to take up arms, including the scribes and the healers, perhaps even the children.\n\nThe king had not been kind to us since we started, he went around the decision of the former king, and started made the town pay taxes. We were expecting as such, as long as they didn’t ask huge amount of taxes, we could pay, without having the residents\n\nwork. \n\nYet it continued, next they banished the adunians, the ones acting as guards of VaerHaven, and friends to many of us. Their charges were only against one member, and the other charges were not worthy of being\n\nbanished for. What angered me the most, was that the adunians had banished the accused adunian way before the dwarves placed charges on him, making the charges on the whole race pointless.\n\nIt didn’t stop there, after removing those\n\nthat were acting as guards, they ordered us to create a guard force. We had little men who would fight left, but we did as asked. We got the FrostShields, who were part of the Mageshields of the Delvers, and of course it didn’t work. In the end they were\n\nremoved for causing too much trouble. We were creating a new guard force when the dwarves decided to pass a law making every citizen join the auxiliars, and make them join with the legion’s training. We had no choice but to ignore it, but the\n\nlegion came almost every elven day to enforce it.\n\nThen once more the legion placed it’s nose on VaerHaven, this when I was away with my daughter in Malinor. They accused one of the town guilds, the Fallen, of Anarchism. When I asked what\n\ndid they do to be seen that way, all they told me was that they were told that they were plotting things. So, instead of wanting to question them, and search of the truth, they decided it would be better to just completely arrest every member without\n\nproof and for no crime committed. They were not let. I had a talk to some of the members of the Fallen, and knew most of them well, those rumors were false, and the legion didn’t even care for it.\n\nThen the rebels appeared, and the decision had to be done.\n\nKeep with the king, and continue to suffer in the hands of the legion, and be the frontline, with scribes made to fight, and those that would be against it, suffer as a traitor.\n\nKeep as neutral, and be attacked by the king without any allied forces, they would see neutrals as traitors.\n\nJoin the rebels, fight for our freedom, recover our friends the adunians, and try to end the reign of that king. We could decide who would fight, those that didn’t want to could decide to leave without being called traitors, or stay and hope for the best.\n\nWe could show, that VaerHaven didn’t think less of the dwarves of the king, only that we want our freedom.\n\nThe first battle is yet to happen, when it comes, I will try my hardest to keep try for the fight not to happen, but if it does happen, we have\n\npowerful forces in the free men of VaerHaven, who will give aid to us. I hope we do not have to use them.\n\nPerhaps we are being too selfish with our decision, perhaps we should have tried harder, have tried and perhaps even tried to\n\npay off the king for them to leave us alone. We’re a poor town, as all we produce is for the residents, but perhaps we would have been able to pay for it. But we believe the dwarves want military dominance over all the holds, we believe paying off the\n\nking would be pointless, maybe make him even remove the leadership of VaerHaven by force.\n\n\n(Writter's note, the text following this passage were done many days later.)\n\nThe problems have already started in town, the condition that we accepted the rebels in VaerHaven was that they would be less than residents, which means they would have no authority. Instead, they call everyone a spy, and break the peace of\n\nguests in VaerHaven, and they shall be treated as guests. If they act like they are in charge of VaerHaven, they will be removed.\n\nAn elven day ago I have asked for a dear friend of mine to leave town, and with her another two, perhaps\n\nthree residents. They are not meant to fight, nor to see war happen. They should have their own life, a happy life, in peace. I’ve seen one of the residents send a message to Malinor talking about the adunians, so I decided to go talk to the elven princes\n\nmyself. After saying a bit with my daughter I went to talk with one of the elven princes, and we discussed the war. They are with the dwarven king, and I understand their choice. They do not understand much our side,and I also do not blame them, as our\n\nway of managing is unique in every nation of Anthos. Even as elves, they are more similar to the dwarves when it comes to managing, then to a town of free men. The talk ended with an agreement. Those that do not wish to fight in the war, our residents,\n\nwill be allowed to head to Malinor, if they are not wanted there and do not cause trouble. It’s a way out for our residents if they wish, and I am happy this agreement was made.\n\n(Writter's note: Once more days passed before the next text)\n\nI’m writing now from a jail room in the dwarven capital, I was captured when I went out to look for the wolf who has been going around killing in the forests of the dwarven lands. Fast capture I guess, got shoot in the back. I was taken to the\n\ndwarven capital and placed in a cell after my wounds were healed. After being questioned, I was let as a diplomatic prisoner. They wanted all the information I had, but that information is pretty much not secret. They asked for who our allies were, they\n\nknew that already. They asked for our defenses, they are allowed to enter VaerHaven if they don’t cause trouble, and see for the defenses themselves. Number of men as well, I told them the truth, we don’t have many fighters.\n\nBefore I was captured, I saw Kjell in town. I had a talk to him about the reasons as to why we were rebels, he doesn’t seem to be impressed, not many are. Nothing was accomplished in that talk. The buildings of the drawbridge was complete, we now have the\n\nplace protected, not that will do us any good. Soon a small army of the legion came in armor and captured one of the residents. And then a friend of mine lost her daughter in a fight, which I don’t know about. I should had told her to leave town before.\n\nAfter a night in the cell, I was made a diplomatic prisoner, which meant that I could walk around town with a guard, and had access to the great and big room I am writing in now. They then took me to a tavern where I bought a drink. They did remove\n\neverything from me, but left me with my minas then returned this book. My staff is still missing though, might have to get a new one. These guards don’t seem very good, they just left me to wander alone in town.\n\nI was able to escape when they left me alone. I came to back to VaerHaven and shortly after, the rebel king was captured again. He was released after torture, and then once more was he captured. The civil war is over now, nothing much was done, not\n\neven a single battle happened, I guess I’m glad for it.\n\nWritten and coppied by Rosso, former councilmember and former Jarl of VaerHaven.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ilthiria Diplo", "§bDrynn Ireheart", "Dear Grand King Dyrrn Ireheart,\n\nGreetings thine majesty, I firmly believe we are now acquainted as of now; however I hope after this letter that will change.\n\nI am Tys WhiteWater, leader of a group called Ilthilia.\n\nWe are a government in exile, homeless and wandering. However new so not much hassle has concerned us as of now.\nWe number quite a many with many a race, age and personality all strewn into us.\n\nI do not ask for refuge, for I know of ye misfortunes of\n\na demon, but I do genuainely extend the hand of friendship.\n\nOOC Message:\n\nWe are a unique community that has thrived minecraft for over 3 years now, hopping to and fro servers. Litterally by that. Our last home we stayed on for over\n\ntwo years but is decaying; so were not server nomads :P.\nAnyways we have numerous supplies of players so we won't have a lack of recruits however once settled I hope some of the LoTC community will join us.\n\nAnyways, as you know charter rules have\n\nbeen implemented in place to disallow any charters (town/nation) for the first two months. I don't disagree with the rules, as many charters are 2 man villages; however damaging it may be to Ilthilia.\nAnyways, since these rules have been\n\nimplemented, we will need a home for the first two months (we will have to grind 40,000 minas anyways so we'll be busy). So I propose we have an embassy in the new Dwarven capitol or another major city in the Isles of Axios.\nThe terms would be that the\n\nembassy would be extraterritorial with no tax.\nWe will in return offer the same gesture when we are settled - you will also have an embassy that will be tax free. The embassy shall have 3 wings, 1 wing for disscussion rooms, council, entrance hall and\n\ncenter of the embassy whilst the other two wings shall be accomdation; one being emergency as this will be our prime home (for 2 months).\n\nAlso, we propose a permanent military alliance; we will always come to your aid and defend your lands.\nHowever do\n\nnote we do not intend to start ANY wars, as we will merely be defensive, however we hope none of our military will be required.\n\nOur government is composed of 5 members with an advisor. For more information contact me and I'll show you\n\nsome threads on our own forums.\nWe hope you accept.\n\n\nRP:\n\nG'day King Dyrrn IreHeart.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ancient Elves", "§bArchrim Elmoran", "Achient elves\n\nA long time ago, before written history, the world was inhabited by a single race known now as the achient elves and were the first ofthe Aegis, the build marvels in what is now niben bay\n\nThe achient elves built cities that are now considerd marvels and large statues of birds, lions, and also dragons, and it should be noted the elves learned how to befriend dragons aswell.\n\nthey knew the friendship between them was strong and so the dragons tought them the basics of what is know nowdays as magic, they also taught them on how to store energy within crystals and use them to power cities and give them light\n\nEventually a dragon by the name of Akron took power of the empire that had previously been formed by the elves and dragons. Akron hated the other newly formed races including the elves and so he started creating large crystals and using them for war\n\nbut there were dragons who did not agree with him and stood in the way of his plans, and so Akron called upon the forces of Iblees\nHe then used this power to slowly drain the life of the other dragons. and then the dragons seeing the inevitable end, used\n\ntheir remaining strength to close the gate to the nether that supplied Akrons Evil power. They died in the progress of closing the portal. The few dragons remaining turned them selves to stone waiting to one day be awoken\n\nWith the dragons out of the way Akron started the inslavement of the other races and with that came the great war witch lasted decades.\nFinnaly Akron was one day defeated and with that the humans took control of the crystals of power the dragon once owned\n\nThe human eventually became mad with power and started the genocide of the Anchient elves and burnt their cities to the ground, few managed to escape, and those few are now the ancestors of the current elven peoples\n\nAnd thus ended the Anchient elves", ""),
        StaticBook("CCC Supply List", "§bPasquale Calabreeni", "Calabreeni Cleaning Crew Needed Supplies§0\n§0\n§011th of Malin's Welcome, 1621§0\n§0-------------------*Mops§0\n§0*Buckets§0\n§0*Spray Bottles§0\n§0*Wood (refined)§0\n§0*Wood (unrefined)§0\n§0*Cobblestone§0\n§0*Masonry Table§0\n§0*Fuel", ""),
        StaticBook("Nature of Memory", "§bElindor", "The Manipulatable\n     Nature  Of\n       Memory\n\nOf what we remember is but a glimpse of detail. Our intentional recollection brings forth imagery to which specific details of importance are well defined, while the peripherals are smearily filled in by our intellect, attempting to make sense of gaps.\n\nAnd this because our association to that memory is of one (or in some cases multiple) detail that was of particular importance such that we consciously recalled it mutliple times in an effort to retain it within our long-term memory, rather than\n\nlosing it in the daily destruction of our short term memory that is most often catalysed by the catatonic state of sleep. Perhaps if the mind could avoid such periods of inactivity, the short term would never needs be reset in such a way that is\n\ndetrimental to retaining detailed memory, then we could at once recall in photographic precision all our experiences in an instant. But that is a suggestion for another book, most favourably attempted by a different author than this.\n\nBeyond what is the intetntion of the mind's recollection of the memory, little information is really accurate. Instead what is peripheral detail is assumed by the same section of thought that fills a castle in a dream with rooms. For from the outside, the\n\ndetail that matters of the castle is only the facade, but the assumption is always that within its walls are rooms of different sizes. But what do we see of the castle amidst the dreaming? It is none but an outer wall, perhaps a glimpse within to a tiny\n\nsection of a room that suggests a well furnished kingdom; but nothing that suggests any great quantity of detail within the dream itself. For such things are of little consequence to the dream itself.\n\nSo with memories suffering from the gaps being filled by merely the assumption of fact, the truth about memory is that it is indeed far more maleable than we would care to admit. For recollecting the final farewell of an old friend, one might recall the\n\ndetails that agree to what mattered at the time. If the parting were of particular sorrow then one might have subconsciously re-decorated the autumn leaves and budding flowers with a less distracting environment. Yet does the environment matter? Whether a\n\nbeautiful scene or a dreary mid-winter afternoon, of what consequence upon the memory is it? With the details deemed important by the owner of the memory saved, and all else filled with peripheral illustration, the unneccessary details are considered\n\nof no importance. But what if the focus shifts long after details have been assumed as peripheral? Let us suppose that another who experienced the same moment recalls their differing peripheral illustration. The former may beleive their details\n\naccurate, but under contest might easily agree to altering the peripheral details. Now, let us suppose further that the questioning of such details comes with an intent to shift the focus of the memory to something else entirely. The one who is attempting\n\nto call to remembrance these sepcifics which have remained as assumption for a length of time will be easily persuaded. And such persuasion can all take place under conscious recollection.\n\nBut let us now suppose that instead of having these details called into question, instead someone were able to plant within this memory a detail that is not entirely true and hide it within the peripheral illustration? The one with whom the memory\n\nbelongs will at no point have the recollection required to question this new addition. The further this newly planted detail is from the memory's purpose, the more undetectable it will remain.\n\nAnd so, by simple means of suggestion, one who wholeheartedly beleives the power of their own memory will unquestionably accept a thought that is not of their own origin as though it has always belonged.", ""),
        StaticBook("Forum of 1527", "§bIat", "What does it mean to be mali'aheral?\n\nAre we not what we are because we are together?\n\nThus mali'aheral is not but one of us but the collective.\n\nThus what is the collective?\n\nIs the collective simply a gathering of thoughts or is is a goal to achieve unity?\n\nWhat is unity?\n\nIs unity not but the undiscerned agreement from the mass?\n\nThus if we seek to reach unity is it not our duty to each other and not ourselves? \n\nDo we hold value in self-image or do we value unity and preserverance of our culture?\n\nDo destroy or limit each other in any means is to limit the maehr'sae hiylun'ehya and thus an act of greivance against all mali'aheral.\n\nTo deny access to public institutions is to limit.\n\nTo fail to offer ways to expand ones knowledge is to limit.\n\nTo take from the state is to take from each citizen of Haelun'or personally and in doing so commit a greivance against maehr'sae hiylun'ehya.\n\n~ Thoughts on unity.\nA public forum.\n\n14th  of The Deep Cold, 1527\n\n\nMaehre'sae Hiylun'ehya", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "CRIMINAL DOCUMENTATION BOOK§0\n§0\n§0\n§0Daquan Terrel - Vandalism (Attempted break in.)§0\n§0Punishment issued - Executions§0\n§0-------------------§0\n§0Ikail Runebrooke -§0\n§0Roof climbing, Assualt on Guard.§0\n§0Punishment Issued -\n\nDaniel - Trespassing§0\n§0Punishment - Day in the cells§0\n§0\n§0-------------------\n\nhis brother in a white cloak, you cant see his face) and then you have Ahti lakko one of the dwarfs, Fleeper a knight,§0\n§0\n§0Lady Basilia tosali§0\n§0She is day and knight in her house, meeting people but never shows herself or comes out her house.", ""),
