        StaticBook("Hora Beatae Mari", "§bIngelrannus", "Gloria tibi Domine.§0\n§0In principio erat Verbum, et Verbum erat apud Deum, et Deus erat Verbum. Hoc erat in principio apud Deum Omnia per ipsum facta sunt: et sine ipso factum est nihil, quod factum est. In ipso vita erat, et vita erat lux hominum: et lux it\n\ntenebris lucet, et tenebrae eam non comprehenderunt. Fuit homo missus a Deo, cui nomen erat Ioannes. Hic venit in testimonium ut testimonium perhiberet de lumine, ut omnes crederent per illum..§0\n\nNon erat ille lux, sed ut testimonium perhiberet de lumine. Erat lux vera, quae illuminat omnem hominem venientem in hunc mundum. In mundo erat, et mundus per ipsum factus est, et mundus eum non cognovit. §0\n§0In propria venit, et sui eum non receperunt.\n\nQuodquot autem receperunt eum, dedit eis potestatem filios Dei fieri, his qui credunt in nomine eius: qui non ex sanguinibus, neque ex voluntate carnis, neque ex voluntate viri,sed ex Deo nati sunt. Et verbum caro factum est,\n\net habitavit in nobis: et vidimus gloriam eius, gloriam quasi unigeniti a Patre plenum gratiae et veritatis...§0\n§0Gloria tibi Domine.§0\n§0In illo tempore, missus est angelus Gabriel a Deo in civitatem Galilaeae, cui nomen\n\nNazareth, ad virginem desponsatam viro, cui nomen erat Joseph, de domo David, et nomen virginis Maria. Et ingressus angelus ad eam dixit: Ave gratia plena: Dominus tecum: benedicta tu in mulieribus.\n\nQuae cum audisset, turbata est in sermone eius, et cogitabat qualis esset ista §0salutatio.Et§0 ait angelus ei: Ne timeas Maria, invenisti enim gratiam apud Deum: ecce concipies in utero, et paries filium, et vocabis nomen eius Iesum: hic erit magnus,\n\net Filius Altissimi vocabitur, et dabit illi Dominus Deus sedem David patris eius: et regnabit in domo Iacob in aeternum, et regni eius non erit finis. Dixit autem Maria ad angelum:Quomodo fiet istud, quoniam virum non cognosco?\n\nt respondens angelus dixit ei: Spiritus sanctus superveniet in te, et virtus Altissimi obumbrabit tibi. Ideoque et quod nascetur ex te sanctum, vocabitur Filius Dei. Et ecce Elisabeth cognata tua, et ipsa concepit filium in senectute sua\n\net hic mensis sextus est illi, quae vocatur sterilis: quia non erit impossibile apud Deum omne verbum. Dixit autem Maria: Ecce ancilla Domini, fiat mihi secundum verbum tuum.\n\nIn illo tempore, cum ergo natus esset Iesus in Bethlehem Iuda in diebus Herodis regis, ecce magi ab oriente venerunt Ierosolymam, dicentes: ubi est qui natus est rex Iudaeorum. vidimus enim stellam eius in oriente, et venimus adorare eum.\n\nAudiens autem Herodes rex, turbatus est, et omnis Ierosolyma cum illo. Et congregans omnes principes sacerdotum, et scribas populi, sciscitabatur ab eis ubiChristus nasceretur. At illi dixerunt ei: in Bethlehem Iudae:\n\nsic enim scriptum est per prophetam: et tu Bethelehem terra Iuda, nequaquam minima es in principibus Iuda: ex te enim exiet dux, qui regat populum meum Israel.\n\nTunc Herodes clam vocatis Magis diligenter didicit ab eis tempus stellae, quae apparuit eis: et mittens illos in Bethlehem, dixit:Ite, et interrogate diligenter de puero: et cum inveneritis, renuntiate mihi, ut et ego veniens adorem eum.\n\nQui cum audissent regem, abeirunt, et ecce stella, quam viderant in oriente, antecedebat eos, usque dum veniens staret supra, ubi erat puer.§0\n§0Videntes autem stellam gavisi sunt gaudio magno valde. Et intrantes domum, invenerunt puerum cum Maria matre eius,\n\net procidentes adoraverunt eum: et apertis thesauris suis obtulerunt ei munera, aurum, thus, et §0myrrham.Et§0 responso accepto in somnis ne redirent ad Herodem, per aliam viam reversi sunt in regionem suam.\n\nIn illo tempore, recumbentibus illis undecim apparuit: et exprobravit incredulitatem eorum et duritiam cordis: quia iis, qui viderant eum resurrexisse, non crediderunt. Et dixit eis: Euntes in mundum universum praedicate Evangelium omni creaturae.\n\nQui crediderit, et baptizatus fuerit, salvus erit: qui vero non crediderit, §0condemnabitur.Signa§0 autem eos qui crediderint, haec sequentur: In nomine meo daemonia eiicient: linguis loquentur novis: serpentes tollent: et si mortiferum quid biberint,\n\nnon eis nocebit: super aegros manus imponent, et bene habebunt. Et dominus quidem Iesus postquam locutus est eis, assumptus est in caelum, et sedet a dextris Dei..\n\nIlli autem profecti praedicaverunt ubique, Domino cooperante, et sermonem confirmante, sequentibus §0signis.Obsecro§0 te domina sancta Maria, mater Dei, pietate plenissima, summi regis filia, mater gloriosissima,\n\nmater orphanorum, consolatio desolatorum, via errantium, salus omnium in te sperantium: virgo ante partum, virgo in partu, et virgo post partum: fons\n\nmisericordiae, fons salutis et gratiae, fons consolationis et indulgentiae, fons pietatis et laetitiae, fons vitae et veniae: per illam sanctam ineffabilem laetitiam, qua exultavit spiritus tuus in illa hora, in qua tibi per\n\nGabrielem Archangelum annunciatus et onceptus filius Dei fuit. Et per illam sanctam ineffabilem humilitatem, in qua tu respondisti Archangelo Gabrieli:Ecce ancilla Domini, fiat mihi secundum verbum tuum: et per illud divinum mysterium,\n\noperatus est in te Spiritus sanctus: et per ineffabilem gratiam, pietatem, misericordiam, amorem, et humilitatem, per quas filius tuus Dominus noster Iesus Christus descendit accipere humanam carnem in venerabilissimo utero tuo: et per\n\ngloriosissima gaudia, quae habuisti de filio tuo Domino nostro Iesu Christo: Et per illam sanctam et maximam compassionem, et acerbissimum cordis dolorem, quem habuisti, quando filium tuum Dominum nostrum Iesum Christum ante crucem\n\nnudatum, et in ipsa levatum pendentem, crucifixum, vulneratum; sitientem, amarissimum potum, fel et acetum ori eius apponi vidisti, Eli clamantem audisti, et morientem vidisti. Et per quinque vulnera\n\neiusdem filii tui, et per contractionem viscerum tuorum, prae nimio dolore vulnerum suorum, et per dolorem quem habuisti, quando vidisti eum vulnerari. Et per fontes sanguinis sui: et per omnem passionem eius, et dolorem cordis tui, et per\n\nfontes lacrymarum tuarum, ut cum omnibus sanctis et electis Dei venias, et festines in auxilium, et consilium meum, in omnibus orationibus, et petitionibus meis, in omnibus angustiis, et necessitatibus §0meis.Et§0 in omnibus illis rebus, in quibus ego sum\n\naliquid facturus, locuturus, aut cogitaturus omnibus diebus ac noctibus, horis, atque momentis vitae meae. Et mihi famulo tuo impetres a dilecto filio tuo Domino nostro Iesu Christo virtutum omnium\n\ncomplementum, cum omnis misericordia, et consolatione, omni consilio et adiutorio, omni benedictione et sanctificatione, omni salvatione, pace et prosperitate, omni gaudio et alacritate: etiam abundantiam omnium bonorum spiritualium, et sufficentiam\n\ncorporalium, et gratiam sancti spiritus, qui me bene per omnia disponat, animam meam custodiat, corpus meum regat, et protegat,\n\nmentem erigat, mores componat, actus probet, cogitationes sanctas instituat, praeterita mala indulgeat, praesentia emendet, et futura moderetur: vitam\n\nhonestam, et castam mihi tribuat, fidem spem, et charitatem mihi praestet: articulos fidei firmiter credere, et praecepta legis observare me faciat. Sensus corporis mei\n\nregat et protegat, et a peccatis mortalibus me semper liberet, et defendat usque in finem meum: hanc orationem suppliciter exaudiat,\n\net suscipiat, et vitam aeternam mihi tribuat. Audi, et intercede pro me dulcissima virgo Maria mater Dei, et misericordiae, Amen.", ""),
        StaticBook("Illusion Theory", "§bValmir Audane", "Basic Information:\n\nGlamour: The illusionary alteration of the previous characteristics of an already existing physical object.  A basic glamour would be the changing of the color of an object.\n\nOne could change the color of a red ball without too much experience, or change the color of their eyes.  Both of these illusions would be brief at first, however it is the best introductory to the field of illusion as the concept of projected imagery is\n\nreinforced and given a solid shape as the budding illusionist continues to practice.\n\nFigment: A figment is a fully illusionary object that is created by the mage and serves useful for a variety of situations.  While a Glamour can alter a previously existing  by extending a sword for example a Figment can create it’s own complete sword.\n\nWith progression Figments can become readily available for more diverse and detailed illusions meanwhile allowing the illusionist to hold them for longer periods of time.\n\nPhantasm: A phantasm is an illusionary emotion that is brought on by an illusionist.  These would include feelings as simple as simple as hunger or sadness to things as complex as anxiety, shame, guilt, and pride.\n\nThis field of illusion is by far the most advanced and difficult to master and to even use.  Every phantasm must be logical as the instant feeling of dread will be easily dispelled by the will power of the recipient.\n\nThe creation and projection of an illusion can be simply described through the following steps.\n\nConnect to void> Create illusion in Void> Push illusion into a mind> Mind then accepts or denies the illusion.\n\nAt an early stage void connection should start with one figment such as a small  light source. This is the most basic of all and will help the budding illusionist not only grow comfortable with connecting to the void but also understanding the abstract\n\nmethodology needed to grasp this field of magic.\n\nAfter some time of practice the illusionist should start work with the senses, all senses.  Start learning touch, smell, sound and taste.\n\nOnce they’ve done that they’ll be true amateurs. Their illusions which will start breaking as the student can’t hold all the senses at once due to lack of practice and focus.\n\nAn illusionist might be able to hold a simple disguise at this level of talent for roughly five minutes if they avoid interaction with other objects and people.\n\nAfter several years all senses will be relatively mastered so illusions will hold much longer and be more effective in use and in mana consumption.  At this time disguises will become practical and stable.\n\nAt this stage an illusionist would have the ability to accurately reenact most sensations that they are familiar with.  A practitioner of illusion could slowly begin to develop the ability to cast a dual illusion.\n\nThis would allow the illusionist to hold two separate entities of light illusion, such as a glamour of turning herself into an extension of a book case, while another of her walking about the room.\n\nExample, A mage walks into a bar with a parrot on his shoulder. The Bartender says; “Hey, where’d you get that?” and the parrot says “Wyvernhymn, they’ve got them all over the place.”\n\nThis terrible joke is an example of a moderately experienced illusionist’s power. The illusion can be made to interact with basic things, move and speak on the fly, and incorporate multiple senses at the same time.\n\nSound (The voice) and sight (The parrot) being the key in the crude jest, but one could likely incorporate up to four and even all five with a great expenditure of mental energy.\n\n*Several pages have either fallen out of the tome or have been removed. While what is left may be a helpful resource to a practicing illusionist the tome lacks sufficient detail as to how the illusions are created in the void and therefore would not aid-\n\nanyone without a grasp of the essentials of the magic.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal", "§bTobias Millerson", "Entry 1§0\n§0\n§0I have a terrible thought about my new friend, Coltaine Wick. I have reason to believe he may be a lich. §0\n§0\n§0During my time at the library, I did a bit of reading on the\n\ncreatures. They are usually mages (which Coltaine is), who are considered experts in their field (this is true as well, he has been noted for his acomplishments several times). They have no need to eat (Coltaine mentioned not eating often, he\n\nseemed to be hiding something) and are rather frail and unfeeling (he spoke of this when we were discussing the elven woman he loves). §0\n§0\n§0They are immortal, by the sounds of it (which might explain his fasination with the\n\nsubject), and in this era are usually raised through some sort of evil magic. The only way to kill a lich is to destroy the item it's bound to, as near as I can tell. As you can see, this is an accurate description of the man. He's said other things\n\nthat make me suspect this as well, but I can hardly write them all here. I do not know what to do. Am I so foolish that I never noticed? Am I truly so stupid?§0\n§0\n§0It would be best for Ser Brynden never to hear of this. He might\n\nthink me some sort of... ally, to the evil. But Coltaine has wronged me in no way, and he must have redeemed himself if he's working with House Kovachev. I cannot decide if it would be wise to confront him about it. I'd rather not die at his hands.\n\nEntry 2§0\n§0\n§0God help me. Jeyne (by some unholy miracle) figured out that I am not the straightest arrow in the bunch. She didn't seem to care, but insists that Ser Brynden never find out. It seems he hates\n\n\"boys like me.\" I'm feeling rather bitter about the situation. I have done nothing but what was asked of me, but it would never be enough because of who I love.\n\nEntry 3§0\n§0\n§0I decided to take a trip around the islands, mostly to get away from Ser Brynden. I'll admit that the man scares me, these days. I can't help that feel Jeyne will let the secret slip\n\nand I'll come home to a blade in my chest. My search for somewhere to run isn't going well. I doubt anyone would help me, anyway.\n\nEntry 4§0\n§0\n§0All hell has broken loose. I decided to take my leave while my pride was still somewhat intact. Jeyne, however, managed to follow me far into dwarven lands before I realized it. She doesn't want to return\n\nto her family, it seems. I'm rather tempted to take her with me; Tosali is not a good man. But I cannot take her from her family. I must find a way to return her.\n\nEntry 5§0\n§0\n§0I ran into Ser Brynden today, near the Vanir Keep. He shouted at me for several hours, and I think it would have come to blows if his second daughter hadn't been witness. Now I fear he is coming to find us.\n\nI don't know what to do. Jeyne refuses to leave, and I can hardly force her away. §0\n§0\n§0We'll continue taking shelter with the dwarves, until the dust settles.\n\nEntry 6§0\n§0\n§0Tosali tracked us down outside of Karlsburg. He demanded that I go on trial and be punished for my \"crimes.\"§0\n§0\n§0Jeyne, needless to say, was not pleased. She yelled at him for\n\nseveral minutes.§0\n§0\n§0The trial itself went well. It happened at the Vanir keep called Serpentstone, and was led by Arik Vanir (a pale, cruel looking child). He decided that I was clear of the whole business, and that Jeyne could\n\nmake her own choice about where to go. §0\n§0\n§0So that is settled. It is somewhat bittersweet, I'll admit.\n\n-16th of the Amber Cold, 1602§0\n§0\n§0Entry 7§0\n§0\n§0It's been some time since I last wrote. Coltaine is, in fact, a lich. We ended up talking about it for some time, and he even agreed to train my...\n\n\"dear friend\" Elyrus in some magics. The elf is thrilled, to say the least. He is quite the character. §0\n§0\n§0He scares me. I might as well write it here, since I have no one else to confide in. He wants to create a lich, and seemed to think I would make\n\ngood one. It was deeply disturbing, and I'm only partially soothed by him admiting that it was \"just a joke.\"§0\n§0\n§0On top of all that, he got completely high on whatever he keeps in the main room and attacked me. I'm convinced he's a\n\nmonster.\n\n14th of Snow's Maiden, 1603§0\n§0\n§0Entry 8,§0\n§0\n§0I lied for Elyrus today. Told Coltaine that he was trustworthy. Pretended that he was a good man. Maybe I actually still believe\n\nhe is, when he isn't intoxicated. He's dangerous, then. Nearly killed me. Laughed it off. §0\n§0\n§0Maybe if I just give in and do what he wants, he'll calm down. Maybe it's the answer. I don't know. I guess I'll try it.\n\nDid I ever write about how much I used to drink? A lot, back when I spent money on useless things. That's one thing I learned while taking care of Jeyne; coin is the most important thing. If you don't have mina, you can't eat. You can't sleep, or defend\n\nyourself, or give your sister a life worth living. §0\n§0\n§0I shouldn't have taken her. The debate on where to send her is still on my mind. I'm loath to see her off, but she's nearly of age and needs to find some purpose in life.\n\nI guess I can't decide that for her. §0\n§0\n§0\n§0I need a drink.", ""),
        StaticBook("Hydromancy", "§b[Elder] Thurak'Yar", "Water\n\nWater appears of one of the simplest elements that inhabit our world, but it is in fact incomprehensively more complex that most people think it is. To fully understand it, one must practice large\n\n amounts of time meditating, and indeed spending their time around said element- be it by lounging around by a pond, or studying its properties profusely in laboratories. Water is a necessity of life, needed by all living and sentient things,\n\nfor example Humans, Orcs, Dwarves, Kharajyr, Elves and also various other animals or plants. Water, also appearing as such a calm element, is also one of the more dangerous; out in the seas, a storm can take out a fleet of ships within moments.\n\nOne can never fully control water that isn’t evocated, unless of course one is a shaman- In which case the Spirits control the element, and in-avertedly the shaman controls the water too. Despite out best attempts, we are\n\nall mortal; we do not live forever, nor do we have amazing power like the ascended or the undead back in Aegis. As said before, water can be a very dangerous element; a single flood can wipe out a village just as easily as it might cause it to flourish.\n\nThe element water contains raw power; a power that all Hydromancers would wish to wield. A Hydromancer’s training consists of learning about the Void, being able to evocate from it, and learning about their element so they can properly evocate it.\n\n. It takes years on end to learn about evocating a single element. Water which has been evocated may appear to be the same as the water we have around us, however it is completely different. The water that us Hydromancers evocate can only\n\nbe created in the void and can brought forth into this world by ourselves. Mana, or life-force, is the power we use to create and transport water from the void, and is vital in most, if not every known magic. If one uses too much of this mana,\n\n, then they would simply fall unconscious or even die before they complete their task due to overuse or too much exerted force after large amounts of dedication and training; such as learning about the void and Hydromancy, and shaping and creating\n\ntheir mana into an interpretation of water. The connection to the void is rather difficult to explain, however; though once one has learnt about Hydromancy itself then they should be able to understand where we are coming from. One’s\n\nconnection to the void is more of a sensation than something that can be explained- Like feeling happy, or in love. As a mage’s training progresses, connecting to the void and evocating elements becomes a simpler task. As one would possibly notice, many\n\nmages use a staff when they’re casting their magic- This however, is not necessary at all, and only aids the magician by giving them something to focus on while evocating. Water can be evocated in various forms, such as a jet of water, an orb of water,\n\nan orb of ice, and other things I have not generally experimented on yet. Hydromancers which have been learning for a long time will be able to use more things and will be able to explore completely different aspects of the element.\n\nIce is more suitable for offence in a battle, rather than defence, however, generally water evocation itself is more useful to protect the caster, as walls of water or ice can be willed to block a projectile or a strike, or simply to\n\nintercept and deflect one, though such must be done at short distance. Ice that we evoke isn’t the same that we find in our world naturally; it cannot be melted by the heat of the sun or a torch, but it can be melted with the use of Pyromancy.\n\nTo break the ice, the Hydromancy must both lose connection to the void and have their creation dissipate, or have a Pyromancer melt it with their fire, or, in the later stages of their training, with steam.\n\nWater, being able to form any conceivable shape, is only limited to the caster’s imagination and fatigue, and with proper training it can be suited for any purpose.\n~Adorellan", ""),
        StaticBook("Void Transloca.", "§bEvelangéline", "About Void Translocation:\n\n- Void Translocation, the voidal art of storing objects in the void, is one of the provailing magical arts in the means of utility.\n\n- A Void Translocationist can place and retrive objects-\n\nthat they have placed in the void anytime and anywhere they desire. \n\n- Although it may seem fairly easy for the eye, it requires intensive studying and observing to be actually translocating even the smallest of objects.\n\nBasic Understanding:\n\n- First of all, although it may seem that the object is being transferred inside the void in one piece, it isn't. The object breaks down into tiny pieces, moving freely inside the void. To call for the object, a void transloca-\n\n-tionist has to remember the physical properties of the object.\n\n- The magic happens in a rather interesting way. First, a lavander speck of light appears at the desired location of the void translocationist, growing larger-\n\nto fit the size of the object. Then, the void translocationit simply pushes the object inside the lavander circle of light, the light swelling in side before dissapearing again. To recall an object, the translocationist does the same with the lavander-\n\ncircle of lightly. Only this time, the object starts to form at the enterence of the light, before simply dropping down. One can say this could be used to drop heavy objects on others' head. One would be correct. However, it'd be a lot slower and mana-\n\nwasting way of attacking if not mastered than the other evocation arts, which is the main reason this magic is used for utility, not offense.\n\nConditions for Translocation:\n\n- The translocationist must be knowledged of the object, having it in clear vision. One cannot translocate an object behind walls. To further explain, a translocationist needs to know the physical properties-\n\nof the object before even attempting to send the object to the void. During my studies, I have carried a notebook with me to note the properties of the objects I wanted to translocate. Like my doll, or the anvil I keep with me for any emergency smithing!\n\nFirst, make a list of the physical properties of the object.\n\nWhat does it look like?\nIs it soft/rough?\nWhat colour is it?\nIs it cold/hot to touch?\nIs its surface smooth or rough?\nHow does it react to-\n\nfire and pressure?\n\n- These are only examples, there may be more if the translocationist feels there is more properties to cover. For example, I'll be covering a simple silver knife's properties on the next page;\n\nSilver Knife,\n\n- Made of silver, is durable\n-Cold to touch\n-Reflects light\n-A small 'Eva' is carved into the handle part,\n- Shaped like a long rectangle but with a sharp edge,\n-Used for cooking-\n\npurposes,\n-Durable, doesn't bend with pressure;\n-When reacted with fire, keeps shape when reacted with the average heat of the fire.\n\nMore Things to Know:\n\n- As in all magical arts, one must not use more than their existing energy. Failure to do so will result in fatigue and maybe even death.\n\n- As the objects gets more complex, the mana required-\n\nto translocate it increases as well. Because of their extreme complex design, living beings cannot be translocated in any instance.\n\n- For being fairly complex and lacking solidity, liquids also cannot be trans-\n\n-located.\n\n- As the mass of the object increases, so does the mana required to translocate it.\n\n- For any questions, do not hesitate to contact me, Evelangéline for further information.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dear Adelaide", "§bJakob", "I don't think this is working out Adelaide.§0\n§0I am VERY sorry but we can keep courting.  §0\n§0-Love Yours Truely!§0\n§0Prince Jakob Barbanov", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "§0          -=O=-§0\n§0\n§0      Mental Magic§0\n§0\n§0(my book of notes, musings, and hopeless scramblings to learn the subject, anyway)§0\n§0\n§0\n§0          -=O=-\n\n12th of Sun's Smile§0\n§01566§0\n§0\n§0This entry will simply be a summary of my journey so far. I sought to join the Aurowind Enclave to learn this subject a number of years ago. I looked for a teacher with no previal. It seems no one's seen the headmaster for\n\nmany years, and for the most part, the Enclave has sadly broken up. §0\n§0\n§0However, with the few meetings I had with some of the members, I gained some contacts in the mage community that in the end, helped me. Daniel Ward was the first person I had ever seen\n\nperform any kind of magic. He calls it a simple enchantment, but it was amazing to watch. The first part of the process was transfiguring an aurum brick into a disc. After this was done, he laid an enchantment upon it, so that it displayed a minature wolf\n\n, a figure of light, on top of it. I'm not sure what the function of this was, but I had never seen anything like it. Even Relavas, a young mali'ame woman that was there with me, was impressed, and she seems to be well versed in the theories of magic,\n\n(though not a mage herself.) §0\n§0\n§0Anyway, back to the point. I saw Daniel standing at the Clould Temple Docks sometime later. I had been sending out letters to various mages I had seen at Blundermore's gathering in Dragur ( I had attended with the\n\nEnclave), searching for a mental magic teacher, with no luck.§0\n§0Either they didn't answer or they didn't know. But after running up to Daniel, (God, I must have looked desperate), and asking him if he knew of anybody, he mentioned a name. Ayche, a dark elf.\n\nDaniel asked me not to mention his name when I found him. I still wonder why.... §0\n§0\n§0After asking multiple dark elves, a few weeks later I finally stumbled across him. He seems a very guarded individual. He did not confirm outright that he was Ayche.\n\nHe wanted to know who had told me about him. (I didn't tell him, but of course he found out anyway. Not much use hiding anything from a mental mage.) §0\n§0\n§0I have tried to get into contact with him a couple times since then. Daro, my raven, keeps returning,\n\napparently unable to deliver any message. He did ask me to send him a bird when we spoke. I hope to find him again...§0\n§0\n§0          -=O=-§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Tuvya's Homework", "§bTuvya var Ruthern", "Like a dog: Wolf\n\nChopping wood: Axe\n\nA fine snack: Bread\n\nIn the Night Sky: Star\n\nProtection: Shield\n\nPointy: Arrow", ""),
        StaticBook("Basic First Aid", "§bGwyneviere de Savoie", "Basic First Aid\n\nGwyneviere de Savoie\n\n~                        ~\n          Vol 1\n\nIt is important for those who commonly engage in fighting or combat that the wound is more deadly than your enemies' weapon. Even the smallest cut can kill you. Tend to your wounds as soon as you can and ensure that your wound does not become infected.\n\nUnder the circumstance that the patient has been inflicted with a cut or puncture injury, there will be blood. Tourniqet the wound to stop the blood flow, or apply a moss to absorb and clot the wound.\n\nForeign material, such as cloth and dirt\n\nfor example, will need to be removed from the wound. Particularly if the wound is a puncture. Anything inside the wound can lead to infection and then death.\n\nEven the smallest injury can kill the strongest, and it is important to be aware\n\nof how deadly infection is. Animal urine is an efficient way to sterylise an injury of any infection. Cauterizing the wound is a painful method, but an efficient one, to reduce chances of external infection. If perhaps you do not have ready available\n\nanimal urine, or a brand (or a fire), or you do not have herbs or medical plants; wrap the injury as best you can and replace bandaging often. Reach a doctor, or a field medic immediately.\n\nAfter sterylising the injury, you may chose to apply a medic\n\nor herbal paste to the wound if you have it on hand. Otherwise, apply a clean bandage to the wound and seek proper medical aid. Again, change the dressing regularly.\n\nIf a wound is so severe that an internal organ is punctured\n\nor cut by sword or knife- there isn't much first aid can do. Organ damage will most likely lead to a painful death without proffesional care. It is unlikely that the correct attention will be gained if the wound was inflicted in battle. Use tea's or herbs\n\nto ease your pain, or your patients' pain as best you can. It is likely that the patient will be suffering from his or hers' injury.\n\nSide note: Alcohol is good way to sterylise a wound and act as a pain killer.\n\nSevere Head Injury:\n\nIt is likely that in battle a person will come across a head or skull injury. This may also occur after a fall or a slip. If the injury is small, reach an area where you can sit, and check yourself for obvious\n\ninjury. It is likely you will be dazed or nausious. If skin has split, apply a bandage and seek help as fast as possible to ensure that no long term damage is dealt.\n\nIf the injury is severe, such as the crushing of a skull, your\n\npatient is most likely unconcious, or in a coma. Either way, they're in a bad state- and hopefully you're there to save their life. Check their pulse first, they may appear to be dead. Swelling of the face, nose, and eyes is a sign that the patient\n\nhas undergone some serious damage to their head or skull. In this case, it is unlikely that basic first aid can save their life. Do not move them, and if possible, seek proper medical attention. The brain of the patient will swell, causing brain damage\n\nor death. A hole will need to be drilled into the skull of the patient in order to allow the brain to swell. It is still likely that the patient will die.\n\nHead injuries can cause nausia, headaches, dizzyness and physical sickness. Resting will heal\n\nBroken Bones:\n\nYou can check to see the severity of your patients injuries (or your own) by physical appearance. Your patient or yourself will most likely be in shock because of the injury. State of shock is a dangerous thing. Never\n\nunderestimate the severity of the situation. Broken bones often can be seen externally as lumps in the skin, particularly in limbs. Check for mishape or difference in your limbs, and the limb affected.\n\nYou can use sticks and straps from boots or clothes, or fabric from your clothes also, to create a splint to keep limbs straight. If your patient has a broken leg, it is likely they wont be able to walk. This is a no brainer to identifying a broken bone\n\nor fracture. Splinting or creating a stretcher out of sturdy sticks strapped together in a ladder shape can be used to transport the patient. A splint can be used to keep the injury straight and reduce movement to the affected area\n\nin the case of injuring yourself.\n\nYou can also pack mud around the limb to set the break. Seek proper medical attention as soon as possible.\n\nDislocations can be relocated with pressure to the\n\naffected area. It is painful. Your patient may need pain killers. If you do not feel comfortable tending to a dislocated bone, seek medical attention of another, or man up.\n\nSlings, made out of tied cloth, or a shirt is great for arm or shoulder brea\n\nA bone break can also break the skin. There may be blood. Apply a splint or use a stretcher to get the patient to proper medical attention if this is the case.\n\nWater Injuries:\n\nIf a person has found themselves floating face down in the water. The first thing you should do is turn them onto their back. It is important not to apply weight to their body, as you could force them under water.\n\nThere isnt much you can do out in the water, so bring them back to shore quickly, and remember to keep their head above the waters' surface.\n\nLay them on their back and check for a pulse. A persons pulse can be found under their neck or the under-\n\n-side of their wrist. Either way, there is a possibility of saving the patient. Place one hand, a fist, onto the chest of the patient above their heart. Place your second hand atop the other.\n\nPump their chest, with short breaks. Count thirty pumps b\n\nstopping. This can force water out of the lungs of the patient or restart the heart.\n\nOpen the airway of the patient by placing your palm on the persons forhead and gently tilting their head back. Check for normal breathing. If the patient is not bre\n\n-ng still, open the persons mouth and transfer air from your own lungs to the patients. Afterwards, continue pumping. Hopefully this will be enough to revive the patient or get the water out of their lungs.\n\nArrow Wounds:\n\nIf your patient has an arrow injury, first be prepared to apply a lot of force to free the person of the arrow. They are very hard to get out safely. Pulling it out without care can sever arteries or break leave splinters\n\nor wood inside of the body. You could die of blood loss or infection. So long as the bolt or arrow is inside of the patient, the blood loss will be lower than without it.\n\nYou can remove the arrow by propulsion, where you force the arrow\n\nthrough the flesh and out the exit point of the wound. Reccomended for limb injuries.\n\nSaw off the shaft, and leave it for a few days so that the wound becomes full of pus and can then be removed with ease. The pus signals infection.\n\nand would then need proper medical attention.\n\nStretch the wound by plugging it with probes of elder pith, soaked in honey and then using a pair of tongs, reach into the wound and slowly, carefully, tug the arrow/bolt free.\n\nWash the wound with wine or liquor, and apply a bandage securely or cauterize the wound. Reduce the amount of strain on the affected area and rest for a few days to prevent pains and quicken the rate of healing.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "James Harden", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Enchanting Guide§0\n§0~~~~~~~~~~~~§0\n§0Unbreaking§0\n§00 o 0§0\n§0o 0 o§0\n§00 o 0", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Potential workers.§0\n§0\n§0Name: Taelon Sorow§0\n§0Race: Heartlander§0\n§0Work: Skilled miner§0\n§0       Lumberjack§0\n§0\n§0Name: Duhm Wun§0\n§0Race: Goblin§0\n§0Work: Skilled miner§0\n§0       Lacks dicipline", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Coffee - 5 mina§0\n§0wine - 5 mina§0\n§0Ale/Mead - 5 mina§0\n§0Orange Juice - 5 mina§0\n§0Run - 5 mina§0\n§0Vodka - 6 mina§0\n§0tea - 5 mina§0\n§0Bread - 2 mina§0\n§0soups - 2 mina§0\n§0fish - 2 mina §0\n§0meats - 2 mina§0\n§0Vintage drinks - 8 mina§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Alchemist's Fire\n\nWhere to find the ingredients§0\n§0\n§0Mandragora: Can be found in swamps under lily pads. §0\n§0\n§0Serpent's Stalk: Can be found in rivers(sugar canes)\n\nDwarf's Pumpkin: Can be found in swamps under lily pads and bushes.(lilypads and grass.) §0\n§0\n§0Drake's Tail: Can be found in the desert close to an oasis.(dead bushes)\n\nFlametongue Root: Can be found in plains and forest.(red flowers in plains)§0\n§0\n§0Crimson Vase: Can be found in forests and plains.(red flowers)§0\n§0\n§0Crouching Feather: Can be found in plains under bushes.(Grass)\n\nHow to make the potion:§0\n§0\n§01. step: Make Aqua Vitae with nether wart.§0\n§0\n§02. step: Put in Mandragora.§0\n§0\n§03. step: Put in Serpent's Stalk§0\n§0\n§04. step: Put in Dwarf's Pumpkin\n\n5. step: Put in Drake's Tail§0\n§0\n§06. step: Put in Flametongue Root§0\n§0\n§07. step: Put in Crimson Vase§0\n§0\n§08. step: Put in Crouching Feather\n\nNow if none of the brewings has failed you should now have yourself a potion called Alchemist's Fire. §0\n§0This potion is very valuable and will mostly be seld for 100+ minas.§0\n§0\n§0So make lots if you wish to be rich.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Rose = Blood Lotus§0\n§0Vines = Frost vine§0\n§0Birch = Alabastar§0\n§0Tallgrass = Saffuil§0\n§0RedMush = Flametongue§0\n§0BrowMush = Miner H.§0\n§0Lily pad = Mandragora§0\n§0Cactus = Goblins Ivy§0\n§0\n\nPoison Potatoe =§0\n§0Swamps blossom§0\n§0\n§0Slimeballs = Lard§0\n§0\n§0Tippens root = §0\n§0Tippens root§0\n§0(2 oak saplings)§0\n§0\n§0Red dye = Elrow berries\n\nFeather = Bird Feather§0\n§0\n§0Ice = Water Elemental§0\n§0\n§0String = Elves hair vine§0\n§0\n§0Eggs = Air Ele§0\n§0\n§0Glistening Melon =§0\n§0Night syrup", ""),
        StaticBook("Operation BOOM", "§bOperative KFB", "------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ =====OPERATION============BOOM========-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n10th of Grand Harvest§0\n§0Operation BOOM§0\n§0Big Order of Mass-Destruction.§0\n§0\n§0Operatives:§0\n§0Kerwyr Frostbeard§0\n§0Agent KFB§0\n§0\n§0Ogdan Frostbeard§0\n§0Agent OFB\n\nObjective:§0\n§0Sale of explosives to various factions throughout Axios for profit. §0\n§060%-40% split between operatives OFB and KFB. §0\n§0\n§0Security Level:§0\n§0HIGH (||||||)", "")
