0 (AEST)§0\n§0\n§0HONOR GIVEN\n\nName:§0\n§0Thond Doomforged§0\n§0\n§0Rank:§0\n§0Stoneguard§0\n§0\n§0Time in:§0\n§05:00pm §0\n§0\n§0Time out:§0\n§06:00pm§0\n§0Honor given", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "-O===============O-         Alcohol§0\n§0-O===============O-  §0\n§01. Alcoholic Base -§0\n§0   Wheat§0\n§0   Water§0\n§0\n§02. Pale Ale -§0\n§0   Alcoholic Base§0\n§0   Wheat\n\n3. Sweet Pale Ale - §0\n§0   Pale Ale§0\n§0   Melon", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal", "§bDor'Dwedmar Mercenary", "I have recieved word from Zharkhon to take slaves or heads from Kal'Omith! He says they will be perfect for the manipultion trials... Perhaps I shall get promoted! Heheheh!§0\n§0Once the capturing is done, the slaves shall be taken to the keep, where they\n\nfinish construction on the altar of Khorvad.§0\n§0I am instructed not to right full details however. I have heard of rumors that Urguan's dwarves are weak, spineless runts that complain and take gold from eachother! How primitive!\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0*Strange runes are written here..*", ""),
        StaticBook("Holy Scrolls - I", "§bJacob Chapel", "The Holy Scrolls\n\n     The Book of\n     Nativities\n\nTransscribed by Jacob Chapel during the Deep Cold, 1470.\n\nUse these words to keep true to your faith and to find strength and knowledge.\n\nThere were no planes of existence. There was nothing. Just the Void. And a bright shining light. It was not a light we could see, it was not really white either, but it would be the only way to explain the existence of such a Deity in contrast to the\n\nemptiness of the Void. None knows why, how or when this Deity existed. It is, in-fact, heresy to speculate on such matters. The all knowing God was this Deity.\n\nTruly none can describe the majesty of the Creator, the one and only. The Merciful Creato\n\nthe Seven Skys. With his intent, and only his intent, the World of Aegis was created. All he had to do was simply want it to occur and it happened. The rolling seas, proud mountains and vast landscapes, all in a second, created by God.\n\nThe World was not created in play or for fun, but as a theater for the inhabitants of the World to be tested in. And tested for what? That is for us to speculate. Though I believe it is to test us for purity, how hard we can fight temptation, and how\n\nclean and good can our actions be.\n\nThe first mortal being to be created was a man. This man was sculptured with clay and water, but left hollow. Soulless, God's creation lay there for the other immortal beings to see. The Aengul and the Daemon,\n\nthe two spirits created before the mortal beings and before the creation of Aegis. Not much is known about these two spirit races, but hopefully in the future we may know more.\n\nGod then blew his own breath of existance into the hollow shell and\n\nthe Man lived. God then took the man and put him in the centre of all of Aegis, the same spot where The Cloud Temple now stands. God also made the Man a partner, from the exact same clay\n\nand the exact same breath, she was the first Woman. These simple beings could not talk, nor did they know much about the World. They roamed the world, enjoying its pre-historic beauty. Untouched, the fresh glades and dark thick forests were a wonder to\n\nset eyes on. Soon they had four children in the four corners of Aegis.\n\nMalin was the first of their sons, born in the deep forests of Aegis, he had blonde hair and sharp ears. Standing tall, he was the father of the Elves of Aegis. Krug was born in\n\nscorching deserts of Aegis, fierce and relentless, he was the father of the Orcs. In the fresh meadows of Aegis was born Horen, father of Humans. And lastly, in the deep underground caves of the World, Urguan was born, master of the Dwarves.\n\nSoon the first Man and Woman created by God departed Aegis and climbed the seven skies to meet with God their creator, for they had achieved their goal. The Sons began to explore the World of Aegis and each was stricken with grief at the loss of their\n\nparents, seeking to fill the chasm of emotion inside them they began to create civilisation.\n\nAlthough none of the descendants of each Son had neither their long lives or splendour, they did carry their forefathers looks and traits. The Elves with Ma\n\nat their head travelled the lands and began naming all the inhabitants of this world, they were the first to create a tongue and began to name the trees and grass, the mountains and valleys across all of Aegis.\n\nAt this time, Malin, Urguan, Krug and\n\nHoren were not far apart in looks. Horen and Krug had darker hair than the other two and Krug was a bit larger in build. Malin had blonde hair and Urguan red. They were all close companions, friends and had much love for each other and each others people.\n\nUrguan travelled into the deep underground of the earth, naming the beautiful ores and gems, sharing it with his brethren. Krug travelled the harsh deserts, testing his stamina and strength against the environment of Aegis, and Horen began building the\n\nfirst squalid huts and villages in the valleys. The people lived for hundreds of years, in harmony and peace. Until the day where one of the great Daemons, great worshipers and squalid protectors of the Void, kin spirits to the Aengul, defected.\n\nIblees, who was once the greatest of all of God’s worshippers, was cast down into the mortal world, and so he was about to destroy the tranquility of Aegis forever. He came in the shape of a man. A gentle being who loved things delicate, he was quickly\n\nbefriended by Malin, Urguan and Horen. Krug had a great distrust of him but after many years of being convinced by his brothers, he finally accepted his company.\n\nLittle did Iblees know that this was all part of the Great God's plan to test the\n\ndescendants of Man and Woman. Iblees wanted to destroy everything that God had designed and created, still not in a powerful physical form he began sowing seeds of evil in the minds of the Descendants. Prying on their needs and lusts.\n\nTo Malin, lover of nature, he promised him many children. He promised him that their laughter would resonate across their forest homes and that he would be content. Malin did not want anything more in this world than a bountiful amount of young to\n\noccupy the barren forests.\n\nTo Urguan, he promised infinite wealth of Gems and Ores, colours and crystals he could never imagine. To this, Urguan’s greed failed him.\n\nHoren, was anxious he would not live long enough to see his city completed and his lands increased. He needed more time, and Iblees struck the chord and promised immortality.\n\nKrug was the last to be tricked, Iblees tempted him with wealth, with food\n\nwith power. None interested Krug. Iblees was furious, he then challenged Krug in open combat in fury.\n\nThe whole world witnessed Ibleeses transformation into a hideous beast of the void. His skin turned into scales, fangs erupted and dark horns explo\n\nfrom his head. He grew large wings and began to breath terrible fire. All stood in shock and horror. The beast terrified all inhabitants of Aegis, animals fled and the Sons of the Descendants were too weak of blood to stand in front of such evil fury.\n\nOnly Malin, Urguan, Horen and Krug stood in front of the terror.\n\nIn Iblees’ right hand, a sword wrought in flame. Krug, naked and unarmed charged at The Daemon, throwing himself against the scalding scales of Iblees. He screamed in agony as his skin\n\nburned and decayed, becoming green and molten. Iblees was knocked off his feet, for the last time. He stood up, heaving in rage and fury, flames exploded from the pores of his skin, he roared in anger and where he struck his sword the land collapsed and\n\nthe ground erupted. And Lo, great was the Valour of Urguan and the Strength of Krug as they fought the beast. Powerful were the arms that carried Krug’s Axe and strong was Horens’ heart as they fought in open combat upon the plains of Aegis. Malin’s sword\n\nwas fast and swift, smiting Iblees upon his breast and sides.\n\nFor the thirty years the Descendants fought Iblees, the world became a war torn mess. The dead were defiled, summoned from their graves to follow Iblees’ mastery. The more mortal descenda\n\ndied, the greater Iblees’ armys grew. It was a sad chapter in the World of Aegis, the brothers threw up their hands to God in prayer and in agony. Their creations destroyed, their children massacred. Woe to the Sons of Man and Woman. Krug grew bitter,\n\nhis resentment of his brothers increased for befriending such a beast. Urguan grew greedy, he fought valourously but began to hide his treasures underground. Malin feared for the lives of his children and did not leave his forest sanctuary. It seemed the\n\nworld was destined for ruin. Iblees grew in strength and the Descendants weakened. Until one day.\n\nOne day where the sound of horns could be heard from the far east. Beautiful horns echoing all across the skies of Aegis. God had heard their prayers.\n\nAn army of Aengul and Daemons from the seven skies had appeared on the grand shores of Aegis. Their majesty and beauty so strong that all The Descendants could see was a flash of power white light erupt from the east. Only Malin with his strong sight\n\ncould see the figures of light as they sped across the skies towards the armies of Iblees.\n\nIblees’ soldiers burned where they stood, The thousands of skeletons and cadavers burst aflame and his living servants fled. There in the right middle of the\n\nworld, he was cast down and chained by the Aengul and Daemon. A robed figure with brown hair and a black wreathed apparation stood before him. They were a terrible image to look at, all shyed down and bowed in their majesty and glory. They stood before\n\nIblees, knowing he was immortal and could not be killed, sentencing him to banishment to the void where his dark soul would be forever trapped in torment.\n\nBut before they could complete the sentence, Iblees stood tall for one last time.\n\n“You believe you may simply banish me from this plane and that my taint shall not last? I have touched this world with evil and it shall forever be part of the souls t\n\ninhabit it.\n\nMalin, I find no need to curse you, for so many of your kind have already willingly submitted to me now and will on my return in the distant future. The curse you will bear, is not of my doing, but of your own. Even you have done my work\n\nif you realize it or not.\n\nUrguan, your greed and lust shall overcome you, you are not worthy of the height God gave you, your descendants shall be short, squalid and ugly. You will always seek to find Gold and Gems in the deep underground of the ear\n\nyour hunger never satisfied.\n\nHoren, the immortality you hope for will never arrive. Your longevity has already been stripped away thanks to the labors of the twisted heart of your brother Malin. You will age quickly and die before you ever taste the\n\nfruits of your pointless labors.\n\nAnd you Krug, the most hated of the Descendants, you shall always have the lust of war. You are strong? Well the strength shall be used against your brothers, used to pillage and murder! Your lust for battle shall be\n\nunsatiated and your descendants shall grow ugly and heartless.”\n\nAs soon as his words were uttered, the world grew suddenly dark. A great roar erupted from Iblees’ mouth and in a blast of fire he was banished from the Mortal World. The Descendants st\n\nstill for several moments, pondering over the words of Iblees. Malin, Krug, Urguan and Horen all knew naught of what the great Devil had spoken of when concerning Malin’s betrayal. Dismissing it as the lies of a demon propagated to corrupt their souls,\n\nthe brothers thought nothing further of Malin’s supposed treason.\n\nThe robed figure stood before the four brothers.\n\n“There is nothing in my power that may undo what that evil did. There is one thing I may do however, and that is to bless you.\n\nMalin, may your forests be a sanctuary of peace and your children long lived.\n\nUrguan, may your descendants be hardy, strong hearted and strong of mind.\n\nKrug, may your people show valour and honour where none exist.\n\nAnd Horen, may your people one day explore the Seven Skies.\n\nI can do no more, for all my power is spent. We will go back to our master now, I believe your children may see us once more but long in the future.”\n\nAnd with that, the great host of Aenguls and Daemons disappeared into thin wisps in the air.", ""),
        StaticBook("Element Quality", "§bAmbros", "Of the Four Elements and Their Natural Qualities\n\nBy Ambros\n\nIT is necessary that we should know and understand the nature and quality of the four elements, in order to our being perfect in the principles and ground-work of our studies in the arcanic Art.\n\nTherefore, there are four elements, the original grounds of all corporeal things, viz. fire, earth, water, and air, of which elements all inferior bodies are compounded; not by way of being heaped up together, but by transmutation and union; and when they\n\nare destroyed, they are resolved into elements. But there are none of the sensible elements that are pure; but they are, more or less, mixed, and apt to be changed the one into the other: even as earth, being moistened and dissolved, becomes water, but\n\nthe same being made thick and hard, becomes earth again; and being evaporated through heat it passes into air, and that being kindled into fire, and this being extinguished, into air gain, but being cooled after burning, becomes earth again, or else\n\nstone, or sulphur; and this is clearly demonstrated by lightning. Now every one of these elements have two specifical properties: the former whereof it retains as proper to itself; in the other, as a mean, it agrees with that which comes directly after\n\nit. For fire is hot and dry--earth, cold and dry;--water, cold and moist--and air, hot and moist. And so in this manner the elements, according to two contrary qualities, are opposite one to the other: as fire to water, and earth to air. Likewise, the\n\nelements are contrary one to the other n another account: two are heavy, as earth and water--and the others are light, as fire and air; therefore the Stoics called the former, passives--but the latter, actives. And scholars distinguishes them after\n\nanother manner, and assigns to each of them three qualities, viz. to the fire, brightness, thinness, and motion--to the earth, darkness, thickness, and quietness; and, according to these qualities, the elements of fire and earth are contrary. Now the\n\nother elements borrow their qualities from these, so that the air receives two qualities from the fire,--thinness, and motion; and the earth one, viz. darkness. In like manner water receives two qualities of the earth,--darkness and thickness; and the\n\nfire one, viz. motion. But fire is twice as thin as air, thrice more moveable, and four times brighter; the air is twice more bright, thrice more thin, and four times more moveable. Therefore, as fire is to air, so is air to water, and water to the earth;\n\nand again, as the earth is to the water, so is water to air, and air to fire. And this is the root and foundation of all bodies, natures, and wonderful works; and he who can know, and thoroughly understand these qualities of the elements, and their\n\nmixtures, shall bring to pass wonderful and astonishing things in magic.\n\nNow each of these elements have a threefold consideration, so that the number of four may make up the number of twelve; and, by passing by the number of seven into ten, there may be a progress to the supreme unity upon which all virtue and wonderful\n\nthings do depend. Of the first order are the pure elements, which are neither compounded, changed, or mixed, but are incorruptible; and not OF which, but THROUGH which, the virtues of all natural things are brought forth to act. No man is able fully to\n\ndeclare their virtues, because they can do all things upon all things. He who remains ignorant of these, shall never be able to bring to pass any wonderful matter.\n\nOf the second order are elements that are compounded, changeable, and impure; yet such as may, by art, be reduced to their pure simplicity; whose virtue, when they are thus reduced, doth, above all things, perfect all occult and common operations of\n\nNature; and these are the foundation of the whole of Natural Magic.\n\nOf the third order, are those elements which originally and of themselves are not elements, but are twice compounded, various and changeable into another. These are the infallible medium, and are called the middle nature, or soul of the middle nature;\n\nvery few there are that understand the deep mysteries thereof. In them is, by means of certain numbers, degrees, and orders, the perfection of every effect in what thing soever, whether natural, celestial, or supercelestial: they are full of wonders and\n\nmysteries, and are operative as in Magic natural, so divine. For from these, through them, proceeds the binding, loosing, and transmutation of all things--the knowledge and foretelling of things to come--also, the expelling of evil, and the gaining of\n\ngood spirits. Let no one, therefore, without these three sorts of elements, and the true knowledge thereof, be confident that he can work any thing in the Occult Science of Magic and Nature.\n\nBut whosoever shall know how to reduce those of one order into another, impure into pure, compounded into simple, and shall understand distinctly the nature, virtue, and power of them, in number, degrees, and order, without dividing the substance, he\n\nhe shall easily attain to the knowledge and perfect operation of all natural things, and celestial secrets likewise; which teaches all these before mentioned; and, by a perfect knowledge thereof, we perform many rare and wonderful experiments.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dark Shamans", "§bHektor Blackwood", "A new foul being has inserted itself into our Lands. This being is extremely resiliant, capable of great feats of magic. It is no Wraith, Archon, or Lich. In fact, it is not of Light or Dark. It is of a Spiritual Nature. They are, The Dark Shamans.\n\nDark Shamans are known as practitioners of a vile art, not their own Creature or Race. Your writer understands this, though your writer also has faced a new breed of Dark Shaman. It all started in Courland. I encountered a skeletal being wielding\n\nscorching hot air that singed flesh upon contact. I made battle with this being, with the help of brave Men and Elves. Eventually we toppled this foul creature, and I recovered some of the ash left behind when it dis-integrated. It may have been a Lich,\n\nthough Liches cannot combine Evocations. They also cannot be unimpacted by Clerics, which this being was during the fight. I had a compulsive need to fully understand this creature (Which to this day, I do not). A Druid appraised the Ash I collected, and\n\nstated that it was of a Shamanistic nature. I met some Orcs in Sutica. One of them was kind enough to tell me that the creatures were Dark Shamans. I was quite puzzled. I've read of brief bits and pieces of the Dark Shamans from Athera. They looked\n\nnothing like the ones from the days of Athera. I theorize that perhaps this is caused by the source of the Vile Being's magic. Dark Shamans back in Athera derived their power from enslaving Spirits. Perhaps these Skeletal Shamans interact with the\n\nSpirit-Gods of the Mythical Realm in a different way. In a way that truly saps and stretches out their very being. Even with someone as such a keen mind as your Writer, I cannot even fathom how these Dark Shamans interact with the Spirits.\n\nI still keep the Ash with me to this day as a means of both symbolism and practical use. To me, it symbolizes knowledge and it's practical use. If the men and women of Axios can probe the secrets of these horrific beings, we can surely defend ourselves.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Urguan Docks:§0\n§0\n§0Map: 1251, 1252§0\n§0\n\nSutica:§0\n§0\n§0Maps: 1254, 1259, 1260, 1285, 1255, 1285, 1287,§0\n\nUnknown Undead Lands§0\n§0\n§0Maps: 1048, 1049, 1050, 1051, 1052, 1053, 1047,§0\n§01045,\n\nOrc Lands:§0\n§0\n§0Maps: 1335, 1334, 1333, 1358, 1359, 1360, 1357,§0\n\nJornheim:§0\n§0\n§0Maps: 1270, 1271, 1272,§0\n§01273\n\nArcadia Pre Runes:§0\n§0\n§0Maps: 1245, 1246, 1247§0\n§0\n§0Arcadia Post Runes:§0\n§0\n§0Maps:\n\nThe Krag:§0\n§0\n§0Maps: 1297, 1298, 1299, 1300, 1301\n\nHaelun'or:§0\n§0\n§06th of Sun's Smile, 1637§0\n§0\n§0Maps: 2380, 2381, 2382, 2383", ""),
        StaticBook("A Note", "§bOthelu", "*The letter is hand written in fancy, elven cursive.*§0\n§0\n§0Dear Ogdan Frostbeard, my name is Othelu, and I'm an aspiring alchemist. I acknowlege that I'm probably not the race you'd prefer to train, but I won't come empty handed. If you find yourself\n\nwilling to take on a student, I would happily like to learn from you.§0\n§0\n§0Highest Regards,§0\n§0Othelu", ""),
        StaticBook("silvervein I", "§bjerim frostbeard", "The cowardly Silverveins came begging for peace but the meeting went arie and a stormbreaker challenged boreas to a honor duel and he refused then not five minutes after the meeting all the silverveins came and they tried to attack the stormbreakers\n\nbut they were protected then edel the most inbred honorless fool tried to demand an honor duel with Hamil who refused do to the fact edel had brought  ELEVEN silverveins to back him up.\n\n Edel had the audacity to claim that hanil was honorless when not five minutes prior he leader did the same thing but a army wasn't facing him.§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Regents Request", "§bDean Osborn", "Highest Priority§0\n§0-Dwarf's Pumkin§0\n§0-Mandragora§0\n§0around 10 each or as many as possible\n\nMedium Priority§0\n§0-Athins§0\n§0-Frost Vine§0\n§0-Crouching Feather§0\n§0As many as available\n\nLow Prority§0\n§0-Any Earth Symbols\n\nSend a letter to a Dean Osborn when herbs can be available, Payment can be agreed at arrival.§0\n§0Thank you for your time.§0\n§0\n§0((Underwhereknight))§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Alchemy Reagents", "§bOgdan Frostbeard", "Alchemy Reagents§0\n§0\n§0\n§0             &§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0  Where to Find Them§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0by: Ogdan Frostbeard\n\nFrost Vine: Found in Ice Mountains/Mega Taiga - Vines§0\n§0\n§0Elf's Vine Hair: Found in Ice Mountains/Taiga - Vines§0\n§0\n§0Larihei's Fingers: Found in Taiga/Ice Mountains - Grass§0\n§0\n§0Athin: Found in Ice Mountains - Ice\n\nBlood Lotus: Found in Woodlands, Plains, or Deserts - Grass or Shrub§0\n§0\n§0Goblin's Ivy: Found in Desert - Sand§0\n§0\n§0Drake's Tail: Found in Deserts - Shrub§0\n§0\n§0Clutcher's Straw: Found in Desert - Fern\n\nAlabaster Leaf: Found in Plains or Woodlands - Grass§0\n§0\n§0Crouching Feather: Found in Plains or Woodlands - Grass§0\n§0\n§0Crimson Vase: Found in Plains or Woodlands - Grass§0\n§0\n§0Tippen's Root: Found in Plains - Grass\n\nHalfling's Grass: Found in Plains or Woodland - Grass§0\n§0\n§0Serpent's Stalk: Found in Woodland - Sugarcane§0\n§0\n§0Blissfoil: Found in Woodland - Blue Orchid§0\n§0\n§0Mandragora: Found in Swamps - Lily Pad\n\nFlametongue Root: Found in Woodland - Red Flower§0\n§0\n§0Dwarf's Pumpkin: Found in Jungle - Grass§0\n§0\n§0Saffvil: Found in Jungle - Grass§0\n§0\n§0Metzil's Tangle: Found in Jungle - Leaf\n\nAll have been tested and proven.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ethel's J", "§bEthel", "Ethel's\n         Journal\n\nStarting-16th of The Amber Cold 1623\n\nEnding-10th of Snow's Maiden 1625\n\n[!] A cute drawing of a flower crown is on the bottom of the page!\n\nI've been wandering for days. I'm so hungry, I haven't eaten anything in three days. I just wanted a real home, some people that actually cared about me, but all I got was a swift kick out the door when the one keeping me there was gone.\n\nA woman found me lying on the side of the street in Haense. She was almost see-through kinda like a ghost... I don't understand what she is but she definately isn't human. She took me to a random fort from some old Oren war. When we got there she called\n\nher ward. She said she would teach me what things that I could use to get my way whenever I wanted. I accepted of course, after all why would I turn down the chance to actually get what I wanted for once. She gave me an outfit, a cloak, and a mask.\n\n[!] On this page there would be a sketch of Ethel's outfit when she's cloaked and masked. At the bottom of the page is a signature that says \"BlueJay\".\n\nWhen hanging around Adelburg today with another girl I met named Lily we ran into some trouble with a guard. He called me a spook because of my outfit that Mother gave me. We didn't go there wanting trouble but I don't mind if he decides to start a fight.\n\nWe found him later that day, we hunted him down. The guard's name was Leopold Bassacre. The poor bastard didn't see us coming. He had been trying to break into an abandoned tavern in Mardon, he thought he was alone but he wasn't. We tied him up and asked\n\nhim questions before finally just killing the poor bastard. Oh how the blood drained from his neck when I slit it open. It was simply beautiful! I took his Imperial Guards Batan as a sort of trophy for successfully killing him off.\n\nWhile looking for some information on Frost Witches I met a little girl named Aelin that hung around a 7 foor tall dreadknight named Torug. We all went to the library so she could read to Torug and so I could learn more. After Aelin saw what I was reading\n\nshe told me how she knew some Frost Witches who could be able to help transform me into one of them. We took along another woman who was researching the same subject. Her name was Diligence, and she was rather cute...\n\nApparently after the meeting and fight with between the witches and Torug Diligence and I are to be considered by a witch mother to be made into them.", ""),
        StaticBook("A warning", "§bjerim frostbeard", "While I sit I realize that i'm an old bear now and that I won't live forever so I write this now in fear I'll won't be able to later. The downfall of the kingdom will be do to some fool thing that the silverveins do.\n\n I predict this as a man who understands cause and effect. I wish that my warning is taken to heart. Some say that this will never happen that they'll dissolve but I promise you if actions aren't taken they will destroy this kingdom.\n\nThis is the last warning for not only the kingdom but to all, the silverveins will be the downfall of Kaz’ulra but also with all nations they side with.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "-----Kivek's Journel-----§0\n§0\n§0\n§0It's been almost a month since I've joined the Eisenhorn clan now with Randall and his sons.§0\n§0Everyday, we're constantly moving from town-to-town looking for contracts and bounties to take down beast and creatures. Even\n\nthe occasional criminal.§0\n§0The Eisenhorn clan is clan of monster-hunters. They go around from place-to-place and collecting bounties that the town's people put up. The Eisenhorns come in, kill the creatures/beasts and collect the bounties. Pretty good\n\nMoney from what I'm told. Randall is thinking about joining the dwarfs in Jronheim. A city full of them, with a king and a queen. When I heard about it I got very excited. To see an actual king and queen like in the stories I've read as a child. There was\n\none issue though. They weren't very fond of elves... Shouldn't be that much of a problem with me being a part of the clan, I'll probably have to work harder than others to earn respect around there, but It's challenge I'm up for.§0\n\nAfter a few days of sending letters to the King, Randall got us into Jornheim. The place is massive and amazing looking. Nothing compared to the small towns I've seen so far. Everything is so new, never a dull moment with this lot. We've been given our §0\n\nown clan-hall for us to use as a small HQ or something for now. We aslo got our own rooms in the city close to the clan-hall. Even I got one, althought quite small compared to the others, I can easily work with it. I can edit the room in anyway I want to\n\npretty much for the most part. §0\n§0\n§0The clan-hall is finally done after a few days. I had to finish the stone work on and damn I did a fine job on it if I do say so myself... The next thing is to get a banner going...\n\nSo... turns out Randall has other sons.. His youngest just arrived in Jornheim asking to re-join the Eisenhorns after leaving for awhile to \"find himself\" He's still a boy from the way he acts...§0\n§0\n§0Update: I hate the new son. Little basterd acts like a\n\nfuckin' child. It's a good thing Randall keeps him on a short leash. §0\n§0\n§0\n§0Found a wolf pup today, a little female. Adorable. I fed her a few times and she's already followin' me around. Got her a pink collar, gonna name her Lilly.", ""),
        StaticBook("Case 005", "§bJames Tiberan", "-------------------§0\n§0CASE REPORT: 008§0\n§0JOHANNESBURG§0\n§0CROWN §0\n§0POLICE§0\n§0-------------------RECORDINING OFFICER:§0\n§0Mattington Ironsword§0\n§0\n§0ASSISTING OFFICER(S):\n\nPERSONS INVOLVED:§0\n§0\n§0House Uldrick and hired swords.\n\nPLACES(S) OF INCIDENT:§0\n§0Johannesburg§0\n§0\n§0CRIMES COMMITED:§0\n§0-High Treason against the Holy Orenian Empire§0\n§0+Cooperating with the enemy of the state, dreadlanders.§0\n§0+Inciting riots to cause distabilty in\n\nJohannesburg.§0\n§0-Falsely spreading claims of nobility.§0\n§0\n\n-------------------SUSPECT(S):§0\n§0-------------------Endon Uldrick - leader of house Uldrick§0\n§0\n\n-------------------SWORN SWORDS:§0\n§0-------------------", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter", "§bDaeren Rorel", "Kythaela - §0\n§0\n§0Today I march Northward to siege the keep of the noble house Brawm. If I'm not to return, all I own belongs to you. Though it's not much, it should be enough to keep you on your feet for a while. §0\n§0\n§0Secondly, I've found no greater pleasure in\n\nmy centuries of living than meeting you. While both of us sound as if we've downed pints of ale, I find nothing sweeter than the sound of your voice.§0\n§0\n§0For this reason, I will carry you with me in my mind as I brawl. I hope to return, though if I don't -\n\nworry not. We'll see one another soon.§0\n§0\n§0- Daeren Rorel.§0\n§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to Aven", "§bLord Constable David B. Adler", "\"This letter is to inform you, on behalf of the Constabulary. that the Halcourt levy, rally, and \"Brigade\" are under audit, just as all Crownland Vassals have been under. Please arrange a time within the next Saint's Week to conduct a Rally for       -->\n\nobservation from the Constabulary, as well as prepare Rosters and Statistics relating recruitment and retention of those troops.§0\n§0\n§0Long Live the Empire.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0David B. Adler", ""),
        StaticBook("Love's Ending", "§bFranswaar Kellian", "The day was starting to fade as the sun slowly crept across the sky towards the ever nearing horizon.  I left my home in a hurry wearing the most formal clothes I could manage to find laying around in my home. Nervous and slightly, I finally arrived at my\n\ndestination. She was more beautiful then ever. Her long, flowing auburn hair, striking hazel eyes, and smile were enough to make a man collaspe. The indigo dress swayed in the wind as we walked towards the ballroom.\nOur hands intertwined, I, walking a\n\nslightly faster pace. \nInside was full of elegant music and exquisite decor. The chandelier lit up room from above. As we began to dance together, our eyes were inseperable. Though the ballroom was filled to the point where moving was nearly impossible,\n\nI could only see her. Every second see smiled my stomach fluttered with astounding joy. As the night came to a close, I strolled with her until we could see the sun begin to tower over the mountains. We sat in the meadow watching the sun rise, her head on\n\nmy shoulder. At that moment, I knew I was in love. Months passed and seasons changed. Every spare second I had I spent it with her. She was the only I seemed to care about. Time spent apart seemed as if it were a life time. Though the day came where I was\n\nneeded on a cargo ship to sail across the oceans to sell goods. \n3 years were spent on the water exporting, though it felt more like 30 years. When I arrived home, all I wanted to do was see her. When I exited the boat I ran to her home. Excitement\n\ncoursing through, and adrenaline pumping. I arrived to be greated by a baby crawling on the lawn. Tears began to rush down my face as I learned I became a father. I knelt down to the baby, only to be screamed at by the mother, not realizing who I was.\n\nI stood up a looked her in the eyes, only to she her change from angry to shock. Together we began to sob as we ran into eachother's arms. We spent the rest of the day conversing about my travels and where I've been. I then asked why she didn't tell me\n\nshe was pregant when I left. Her reply was as if a dagger was stabbed into my heart, then was proceeded to be ripped and forced into it again. The baby was not mine. I learned that in my absence the woman I spent every moment with, the woman that I\n\ndevoted my life for, married another man and bore him a child. I lied as best I could fighting the tears congulating her on the new born. She began to explain that I was gone for 3 years and that she began to fall in love with another man.\n\nI left her home with full intent of drowning myself in the harbor. I stood on the edge of the pier, looking out into the now black water, for night has fallen, and prayed that my soul be given mercy. I shut my eyes and began to lean forward.\n\nHalf way into my fall or the pier, a hand ripped me away. I struggled to free myself, but I was restrained against the cold, damp floor. My 'Savior' began to scream at me, though he was tuned out as I began to rethink what I should do.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Dwarven Chemsi", "§bBalder Frostbeard", "-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-A Dwarven Guide on how to be a chemist\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-Chemist better know as a drug maker in basic terms. Drugs was founded by an Orc and given to dwarfs as a gift which has led to a happy friendship\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-Basics\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-A Dwarven maker would be an easy trade to be just because not a lot of dwarfs fully understand how to make drugs but in this book one type of drug will be given out and you will know how to make.\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-Farms\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-Farms yes farms not the type \"Normal\" dwarfs use this is a drug farm in a drug farm you would need three things grass, fern and vines this would make a basic farm for all your growing needs\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-Using a Hoo-Kah\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-Using a Hoo-Kah is very simple you would place all the ingredients you have gathered and put it into the Hoo-Kah if the ingredients are correct you would of made a drug if not the glass on the right\n\nwould go red. Good to know? not really if you dont know any ingredients to make anything but a Hoo-Kah requires no skills or special conditions just the correct ingredients.\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-Recipe\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-This is the part you have been waiting for what is the recipe to make any drug but this book gives only one which is cactus green its a basic drug and quite hard to get in a dwarven Kingdom\n\nbut you would need it the second would be grass depending in what type of Kingdom you live in is depending if you going to get a lot of it but to gather grass you would use shears.\n\nCactus green\nGrass", ""),
        StaticBook("A Dwarven Farmer", "§bBalder Frostbeard", "-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-A dwarven guild on farming\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-Being a farmer in the the Kingdom of Kaz'Ulrah means your a valid member of the Kingdom for dwarven farmers are always needed for most would be a blacksmith but a farmer brings food\n\nthe blacksmiths and over jobs in the dwarven Kingdom or any Kingdom.\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-Skills\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-There is always skills which work together and farmer can have three skills which are\n\nFarmer\nBreeder\nChef\n\nFarmer - To gather crops for the chef and supply the Kingdom with food\n\nBreeder - To keep the live stock in check and gather meat for chefs and leather\n\nfor leatherworkers which can make leather armor and they can give it to blacksmiths to make iron armor.\n\nChef - To cook the food for the Kingdom which feeds all the people living in the city which the chef is based in.", ""),
        StaticBook("Advanced D-Tool", "§bTesel Silvervein", "My D-Tool, Officer's Guidebook§0\n§0\n§0Lord Onar Ireheart\n\nThe D-Tool, or Digging Tool, is the standard issue tool for the Dwarven Legion.  As an officer, you are expected to take care of the D-Tool supply and distribute D-Tools to legionaires.  When a legionaire recieves their D-Tool, they are expected to be\n\nissued a copy of 'My D-Tool' as well, which will explain the greatness of the tool.  As officers, you have been issued an Advanced D-Tool but please use it wisely, they are expensive and limited.\n\nIt is also your duty to make sure that all D-Tools are being respected, and that the legionaires are using them properly.  If they are not, then the legionaire may be punished for improper use of a D-Tool.§0\n§0Best of luck,§0\n§0Legion Supply Officer", ""),
        StaticBook("Khazadmaros A-C", "§bTesel Blackaxe", "*The thick book is wrapped with old white leather and smells like vodka*\n\nRace-§0\n§0Dwarves = Dwed / Dwedmar - Khazad / Khazadmar§0\n§0\n§0Elves = Elger / Elgus§0\n§0Orcs = Ork / Orkos§0\n§0Humans = Umri / Umros§0\n§0Goblin / Goblins = Grobbi / Grobbins§0\n§0\n§0Not dwarf/foreign= Yrrok / Yrrommar\n\nVoz lare rem Khazadmaros§0\n§0aglot, gailuk voz~\n\nEinram \"A\"§0\n§0A (Singular) = E§0\n§0Above = Morred§0\n§0Advisor = Thelur§0\n§0Again / Another = Narhe§0\n§0Age = Kez§0\n§0Air = Kaas§0\n§0Alchemy = Gauld§0\n§0Alcohol = Graz§0\n§0Alcohol = Naztrak§0\n§0Ale = Beoir§0\n\nAll (This tem is tricky. Explained slightly more in the special term division) = Khrum§0\n§0Ally / Allies = Karrim / Karrimar§0\n§0Also = Nar’os§0\n§0Ancestor = Keznol§0\n§0Ancient = Karik / Hraaken / Den§0\n§0And = Nar / Na§0\n§0Anger = Krav\n\nAnguish = Azmoroth§0\n§0Anvil = Kadrin / Kazdorin§0\n§0Any = Vos§0\n§0Anyway = Vosirk§0\n§0Am (Is, Its, etc.) = Va-mer / Yol-mer / Meredos§0\n§0Arch (Leadership Position) = Ard- / Nak-§0\n§0Are = Ath§0\n§0Arena = Kahros§0\n§0Armor = Klad§0\n§0Arrival = Karnes§0\n§0Attack = Kahr\n\nAxe = Az / Kathadun§0\n\nEinram \"B\"§0\n§0Back (Refers to the anatomical “Back”, which comprises all muscles located in the fore body, which the person cannot see.) = Fraed§0\n§0Bad (Synonym to evil) = Vad / Vaador§0\n§0Bag/sack= Alaek§0\n§0Balance = Unn§0\n§0Bane = Alar / Noril\n\nBar (Tavern) = Beorim§0\n§0Battle = Krazdran§0\n§0Be (If used with adjective forms “Been”) = Mer§0\n§0Bear = Hefjhor§0\n§0Beard = Trumm§0\n§0Beast (Suffix, must have a substantive before it) = -Dharok§0\n\nBefore (Used to refer to a long past) / (Verb (needs suffix) ) = Den Kezzan / Dekan§0\n§0Below = Yarred§0\n§0Betray = Ogdaros§0\n§0Better (Good + Potential) = Thorokian§0\n§0Birth = Threin§0\n§0Black = Khorok / Vuur§0\n§0Blackaxe = Kharadunvuur§0\n§0Blaze = Nook§0\n§0Blood = Ardol\n\nBoat (Syn. to Ship) = Wathol§0\n§0Boiler (Synonym to furnace) = Nokri§0\n§0Book (Usually used to define lore of olden Dwarves. synonym to Scrolls and Tomes) = Kron§0\n§0Bourbon = Galraz§0\n§0Bow (Action to kneel before a king or superior) = Nelaraz§0\n\nBow (Item / Weapon) = Thrimmek§0\n§0Bravery (Syn. to courage) = Parathak§0\n§0Brawl (Usually used to depict a fight out of trivialities, Friendly fight.) = Nazaig§0\n§0Breach = Kodeh§0\n§0Break = Nazka§0\n§0Bring = Nighi\n\nBroad (Synonym to wide, can work as an adjective, if preceded by a possesive.) = Nazad§0\n§0Brothel = Belkar§0\n§0Brother (Can be used to refer a clan member) = Kronul§0\n§0Brow (Eyebrow) = Trullki§0\n§0Bull = Demm§0\n§0Burn = Karaave§0\n§0Burrow / Hole / Privy = Undor / Undo§0\n§0But = Ur\n\nCan = Ovar§0\n§0Cannon = Ithring§0\n§0Carcass (Corpse) = Naktrul§0\n§0Carve = Thruz§0\n§0Cave = Umgor / Ulnafer / Skulder§0\n§0Cave's Folk = Umgorumm§0\n§0Chair = Nakhimir§0\n§0Champion = Baladan / Az'adar§0\n§0Chancellor = Darmag§0\n\nCharge = Velannak (Vel'Annak)§0\n§0Chicken (Animal) = Pul§0\n§0City = Kal’ (Used as a prefix.)§0\n§0Civilization (Usually used as a prefix for an empire) = Onor§0\n§0Clan = Kazamar§0\n§0Clan suffix (Used when speaking of a person who belongs to a clan) = -rumm§0\n\nClose = Nerak§0\n§0Cloud = Norkai§0\n§0Cluster (Used to determine a group of plants, animals, or Orkos.) = Nozagar§0\n§0Collar (Necklace) = Nahibelk§0\n§0Comfort = Salez§0\n§0Command = Velerak§0\n\nCommon = Omur§0\n§0Continent prefix (Can be used for defining the term “World”, also stands for a massive landscape, or something that has massive ammounts of.) = Khor’§0\n§0Core = Derkon§0\n§0Council = Nozkron§0\n§0Cow = Keed§0\n§0Create (Syn. to Make) = Yemka\n\nCrown = Rulkahd§0\n§0Crystal = Krest§0\n§0\n§0\n§0Ozram Kronethos \"D\"", ""),
        StaticBook("On Dragons", "§bTesel Silvervein", "On Dragons§0\n§0 Their Life and Death§0\n§0       By Sam King§0\n§0  §0\n§0        Edited By§0\n§0     Jacob Winkler\n\nChapter 1: Birth§0\n§0\n§0Dragons are, known by most everyone, born by egg much like our domesticated and less dangerous, Chickens.  Once The egg is laid it goes on a month long incubation period.  The mother dragon will warm her eggs with her belly.\n\nLying next to it, gently mumuring away, like a loud rumbling purr, as she increases her internal heat.  She does this for hours at a time for a month, until the time the eggs hatch, at which point the egg now begins its life as a hatchling\n\nChapter 2: Hatchling§0\n§0\n§0The Hatchling will, if all goes well, stand on it's four legs, stretching its wings for the first time.  It is important to note that dragons are not yet able to fly at this young age, and won't be able to for quite some time.\n\nDragons at this age are around the size of a wolf, and are thought to be relativly tame and kind, much like a puppy.  For it's first week a hatching will wander around it's nesting site, never traveling out of eye sight of its mother.\n\nIt is during the second week of a hatching's life that it is left alone, as the mother goes to hunt to provide both her and her hatchings with sustenance.  The Hatching is then left to its own accord, and begins to hunt small rodents and animals.\n\nThe third month is when the hatching is able to hunt on its own, under normal circumstances, and is when the fires within begin to bubble up.  Though unable to breath its deadly fire, it is good to note, smoke can be seen from their nostrils and mouth.\n\nWhen the hatching reaches a year of age, is when it is left alone and now considered a Drake, an adolescent dragon.\n\nChapter 3: Drakes§0\n§0\n§0Drakes are still unable to breath fire, but it is still a fierce and dangerous hunter, around the size of a horse and rather grumpy.  At this age a dragon is at it's most sinister.  They are prone to explore great distances for\n\nthe sake of curiousity, which is why Drakes are the most commonly sighted age of dragons.  Do to their adolescent hormones, they will often act impulsive and territorial.\n\nChapter 4: Adult§0\n§0Little is known about adult dragons, as they were rarely ever sighted.  What is known however is at this stage is when a dragon is able to breathe fire and use their wings.  Adult dragons are thought to be rather unagressive, except for a\n\nfew circumstances which I will get back to further on.  They have rarely been sighted and don't attack often, if at all.  The mating rituals of dragons, is of course, unknown, most likely no one has witnessed this or survived to tell the tale.\n\nWhat is known is that a dragon will become extremely agressive during mating season.  It is said they attack towns during mating season however this cannot be confirmed.  Often times if a dragon has its nesting site picked, nothing will stop it from\n\nnesting there, even if it is already occupied.  It is also worthy to note that the legend and myth that dragons have an affinity for treasures is disputed to this day.  Though it is most likely false.  As to why and what purpose a dragon would horde\n\ntreasure is unknown, except possibly to attract potential mates.\n\nChapter 5: Wyrms§0\n§0\n§0Almost nothing is known about wyrms, other then they are the most ancient dragons to ever exist.  Whether wyrms are a separate breed or a stage in the life of a dragon is unknown.  What is known is that they are to be feared.\n\nChapter 6: Death§0\n§0\n§0The natural death of a dragon has never been witnessed.  Dragons have only been known to fall to courageous warriors or powerful magics.\n\nAuthors Note:§0\n§0\n§0This entire book is put together by a few years of research into myths and legends of these grand beasts.  Nothing written in this book is inherently fact.  And should not be treated as such.  This is just the most reasonable\n\npossibilities concerning dragons few if any, facts of these beasts exist.§0\n§0Dedication is to all who enjoy the mysterious and unknown in the, as well as to those who enjoy our history, though this is not per say \"History\"\n\nEditor's Note:§0\n§0\n§0This guy is a complete hack, I don't think he knows anything about dragons, I watched him eat dirt.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Arcadia:§0\n§0\n§011th of Snow's Maiden,§0\n§01600§0\n§0\n§0Maps# 1245, 1246, 1247, 1248§0\n§0\n§0Grand Kingdom of Urguan\n\nKal'Omith & Docks:§0\n§0\n§012th of Snow's Maiden,§0\n§01600§0\n§0\n§0Maps# 1249, 1250, 1251, 1252, 1253, 1275, 1276, 1283§0\n§0\n§0Grand Kingdom of Urguan.\n\nSutica:§0\n§0\n§015th of Snow's Maiden§0\n§01600§0\n§0\n§0Maps# 1255, 1256, 1257, 1258. 1258, 1260, 1286, 1287§0\n§0\n§0Federation of Sutica§0\n§0\n§0Independent\n\nBastion:§0\n§0\n§020th of Snow's Maiden,§0\n§01600§0\n§0\n§0Maps# 1263, 1264, 1265, 1266, 1267§0\n§0\n§0Kingdom of The Westerlands\n\nKarlsburg:§0\n§0\n§01st Of Malin's Welcome,§0\n§01600§0\n§0\n§0Maps# 1270, 1271, 1272, 1273§0\n§0\n§0Karlsburg Docks:§0\n§0\n§0Maps# 1268, 1269§0\n§0\n§0Kingdom of Haense\n\nAlexsandria:§0\n§0\n§018th of Malin's Welcome§0\n§01600§0\n§0\n§0Maps# 1278, 1279, 1280, 1281, 1282, 1292§0\n§0\n§0Kingdom of Courland.\n\nCitadel of Acael:§0\n§0\n§021st of Malin's Welcome§0\n§01600§0\n§0\n§0Maps# 1293, 1294, 1295, 1296§0\n§0\n§0Home of the Mali'Fenn\n\nThe Krag:§0\n§0\n§023rd of Malin's Welcome, 1600§0\n§0\n§0Maps# 1297, 1298, 1299, 1300, 1301, 1302§0\n§0\n§0Kingdom of Norland.\n\nMellsbury:§0\n§0\n§020th of The First Seed, 1600§0\n§0\n§0Maps# 1306, 1307, 1308, 1309§0\n§0\n§0Grand Kingdom of Urguan\n\nLinandria:§0\n§0\n§021st of The First Seed, 1600§0\n§0\n§0Maps#\n\nHaeulon'or:§0\n§0\n§013th The Grand Harvest, 1600§0\n§0\n§0Maps#\n\nDraugr Library:§0\n§0\n§017th of The Grand Harvest, 1600§0\n§0\n§0Maps# 1323, 1324, 1325, 1326§0\n§0\n\nBoats at Sea§0\n§0\n§01st of The Sun's Smile, 1600§0\n§0\n§0Maps#\n\nIcy Bridge from Bastion:§0\n§0\n§06th of the Sun's Smile, 1600§0\n§0\n§0Maps#\n\nSutican Farm:§0\n§0\n§014th of Sun's Smile, 1600§0\n§0\n§0Maps# 1329\n\nSann'Tor:§0\n§0\n§017th of The Sun's Smile, 1600§0\n§0\n§0Maps#\n\nOstermark:§0\n§0\n§0??§0\n§0\n§0Maps# 1351, 1352, 1353, 1354, 1356", ""),
        StaticBook("Golems", "§bBalder Frostbeard", "Ancient Asulon\n===================The oldest records of golems come from the Scriberfolk, a group believed to be part of ancient civilisation of Karik, who sought to understand what they called 'stonefolk' at a fundamental level.\n\nGolem bodies were stronger and did not weaken with age, and through understanding how a mind could be contained in stone, hey sought immortality. Their first discovery was soulbinding, where a soul could be bound to a golem's core,\n\ntaking the place of the rare elemental lightning they usually used to make golems. When this proved just to be an alternate (and less stable) power source  for the golem which gave none of the memories or personality of the Dwarf used to create it,\n\nthey sought to use a variant of necromancy to move a Dwarven mind into a golem. At first, and in spite of the damage it caused to the Anvil, this seemed to work, but their 'success' did not last.\n\n It soon became apparent that the golem was not the Dwarf in stone form, it simply believed itself to be the Dwarf it was 'copied' from. Before long, the fundamentally incompatible golem and Dwarven minds unraveled and the\n\nexperimental golem descended into insanity, becoming a renegade monster that rampaged until its mind finally came apart and its core imploded, killing it. The records of the Scriberfolk end soon after,\n\n although it is unclear if they were killed by the Drakes that would later drive the modern Dwarves from Karik, or if they were wiped out by another monstrosity of their own creation.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sailor's recipe", "§bTesel Blackaxe", "Ingrediants§0\n§02 wormfish, skinned, de-boned, de-wormed§0\n§0Butter§0\n§0Flour§0\n§03 eggs§0\n§03 cloves garlic§0\n§0Salt§0\n§0Cheese§0\n§0Any briny fish stock§0\n§0White wine§0\n\nMake a paste of the butter, flour, eggs, and the garlic.§0\n§0Add salt to taste.  Mince §0\n§0and pound the wormfish§0\n§0small, and combine into the paste.§0\n§0\n§0Bring stock to a low boil.§0\n§0Add the fishy paste to the stock by large spoonfuls,§0\n§0and simmer for 30 minutes.\n\nOnce solid quenelles have formed, arrange them in a deep fish.  Top with generous amounts of cheese and butter, and add the wine to the bottom of the dish.  Bake until the cheese melts and the quenelles are fragrant.§0\n§0\n§0Serve at once, with strong beer.", ""),
        StaticBook("Nub", "§bSchnub'nub", "Nub", ""),
        StaticBook("Cram", "§bTesel Blackaxe", "Pour a generous amount of rock salts or ice salts in a your water.  Stir and heat until dissolved.\nAdd flour to a mixing bowl.  Slowly add water and mix by hand.  Allow grease or coal powder for taste, but alchemists must wash their hands.  Once your\n\ndough feels like a tough clay, roll it flat but not too flat.  Roll it dwarf flat not human flat.  Cut into squares, poke holes evenly the size of a bluntfuck needle or steal a fork from a human.  Sticky top with honey and add a layer of oats, oats\n\nare not optional.  Optionally add chopped nuts, cinnimon, and any other pansy sugars depending on who is traveling with you.\nHeat oven, forge, or campfire enough to get steel redish.  Cook on both sides until very brown or black.\n\nCram should be hard and chewy and fill your belly up in two bites.  If it is not you are a failure.  Kill any yrrommar who learn this recipe.", ""),
        StaticBook("Worm", "§bTesel Blackaxe", "Ingredients§0\n§02 Wormfish, skinned, boned, de-wormed§0\n§0Butter§0\n§0Flour§0\n§03 eggs§0\n§0Salt§0\n§0Cheese§0\n§0Any briny fish stock§0\n§0White wine§0\n§03 cloves of garlic\n\nMake a paste of the butter, flour, eggs, and the garlic.  Add salt to taste.  Mince and pound the wormfish small, and combine into the paste.§0\n§0\n§0Bring stock to a low boil.  Add the fishy paste to the stock by large spoonfuls, and simmer for 30 minutes.\n\nOnce solid quenelles have formed, arrange them in a deep dish.  Top with generous amounts of cheese and butter, and add the wine to the bottom of the dish.  Bake until the cheese melts and the quenelles are fragrant. §0\n§0\n§0Serve at once, with strong beer.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Dwarven Brewer", "§bBalder Frostbeard", "-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-A Dwarven Guild on how to be a brewing\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\nAll dwarfs are familiar with brewer. A good dwarven brewer always makes the best of all the meads of all the ales everythink a normal brewer would do but better.\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-Getting started\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-Getting started with your new found hobby of alchemy some alchemist dont really consider brewing part of alchemy but it requires the same basic level of skill that a alchemist has.\n\nbasic recipes a dwarf would know is as followed:\n\nBottle Water\nWheat\n\nThis would make pale ale which is a common drink in a dwarven area for it one of the easier types of alcohol a brewer can make\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-Gathering materials\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-All dwarven brewers know what a good material is to make there drinks but other people from different professtions are needed for everyone helps each over out when crafting alcohol\n\nThe type of workers are as followed\n\nA Farmer and a lumberjack.\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-Farmers\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-Farmers are need for basic materials such as potatoes and wheat this is all the brewer would need a farmer for.\n\npoisonous potatoes\nwater bottles\nThis would make vodka\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-Lumberjack\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-A lumberjack is needed for one thing which is honey, Honey is needed to make a rich drink the drink would be mead a dwarfs favourite drink.\nHoney\nWater Bottle\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-recipes\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-Mead\n\nBottle water\nHoney\n\nPale Ale\n\nBottle water\nWheat\n\nVodka\n\nBottle water\nPoisonous Potatoe\n\nMullied wine\n\nBottle water\nDark resin\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-Skills & Items needed\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\nBottles\nAlchemic Fuel\nBrewing stand\n\nAlchemy - To make the drinks\n\nTinker - To make bottles", ""),
