        StaticBook("BalderFrostbeard", "§bOya Silvervein", "Tale Of Balder Frostbeard§0\n§0-------------------This tale begins as all do with a dwed who mastered many things he gathered information across many nations met and be friended many and made some foes but Balder was never written down for what he has done or\n\nwho he was this book will explain who and what he died in his short life.§0\n§0\n§0Begining§0\n§0-------------------Balder Frostbeard was born in the Frostbeard clan for his father was Kami Frostbeard a hard working dwarf who was murdered in the\n\nOren empire for helping people who needed it Balder never got told of his fathers death so he thought he has left him which caused Balder to do many things in his life which most wouldnt agree with.§0\n§0Balder also had a brother who was part of the Silvervein\n\nBjorn Silvervein he was a brute of a man who shortly after joining departed from Kaz'Ulrah to set off to far of lands.§0\n§0\n§0Word Master§0\n§0-------------------Balder Frostbeard was a master of words he would carefully select his words to\n\ngather information for his clan father (Hamnil Frostbeard) the information he gathered was always of help for his people and his home but there was a time he used his silver tougue for the Silverveins he sweet talked to there King and aloud for Edel\n\nSilvervein Clan Father of the silverveins to speak with them words broke at the end the Grand King gave armor and a large sum of minas to the young Silvervein Clan Father§0\n§0for what the king thought is that the Silverveins would follow him and his kingdom\n\nbut carefull placed words bounded Edel Silvervein to the Kingdom of Kaz'Ulrah and its king leaving the Grand city untouched and richer when they left.§0\n§0\n§0Magic§0\n§0-------------------Balder Frostbeard gathered information\n\nbut he also studied it, Balder mostly studied bloodmagic and made a golden sword encrusted with blood magic a mage cast upon it but the blood soon dried up and became an old broken sword still sharp as iron but easily destroyed like ice.\n\nKaz'Ulrah§0\n§0-------------------For a short time Balder became warden of Kaz'Ulrah as the warden he gave people jobs and mina was final flowing in to the people of Kaz'Ulrah he gave most of his own coin to the Kingdoms military and made a lot of there\n\nfood and gave his iron to them.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Houses Given§0\n§0-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-MC - necocraft§0\n§0IG -Balinor Blackaxe§0\n§0District - Common§0\n§0Date - 09/10/17§0\n§0IG Date - 4th The Amber Cold 1632\n\nMC - Thealgoda§0\n§0IG - Barradin Frostborn§0\n§0Distric - official§0\n§0Date - 09/10/17§0\n§0IG Date - 4th The Amber Cold 1632", ""),
        StaticBook("Note", "§bErin Lockley", "*This note was left within the container of an Ink and Quill set. It was clear that the writer had tried very hard to make their handwriting cursive and beautiful.*\n\nJohan, my love.§0\n§0\n§0I perhaps give you too many gifts I admit, but I love to see a smile on your face.§0\n§0\n§0It means that I am succeeding in doing what I promised, in making you happy.\n\nI look forward to the day you and I settle, marry, and raise our own little army of Lodens.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0With love,§0\n§0\n§0Erin Lockley.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Guard Log Book:§0\n§0Gabriel, Looking for smith/blade.§0\n§0(6 hours of gate duty total)§0\n§0Lord Thomas Harsing:§0\n§0Buying supplies before battle§0\n§0Aldur Roecik: Visiting§0\n§0Swifttoe-Brandyhill:§0\n§0Adventuring§0\n§0Phyrene: Drinking", ""),
        StaticBook("Mountain guide", "§bAv'maehr", "A guide to mountain survival by Av'maehr\nof the rangers.\n\n\nIf you find yourself climbing on a mountain for some reason, perhaps you like the air, your a wind mage going to a windy location or monster hunting you need to\n\nknow some things.\nFirst of all do not eat snow once your at that part of the mountain, this is because it will lower your body heat which is very dangerous for your continued living on the mountain.\nNext you should be careful to wear warm\n\nclothing to conserve body heat. Your probably noticing a theme here.\nThirdly you should be careful to do as little unnecessary movement as possible because it will waste body heat and energy.\n\nNow when climbing a mountain you want to be careful to try take the easiest path possible to your destination because taking too complicated of a way could lead to multiple dead-ends.\nOnce you have reached the snowy part of the mountain you must be awa\n\nthat the longer you stay there the higher chance of death by cold. If you plan to stay on the mountain for a long time I recommend finding some form of shelter as this will enable you to be better protected from the icy wind.\n\nAs for wildlife in the\n\nmountains are normally sparcely populated but at night creatures that live in the darkness of the come out and this will make it even harder to make the journey up and down the mountain so I highly recommend you try tackle the mountain during the day as\n\nmuch as you can.\n\nYou should also try keep damage to a minimum during the climb up and down.\n\nIf you follow these tips you should survive.\n\nAv'maehr of the Rosewood Rangers.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "On the faithful day of 9th The grand Harvest, year 1635 the allied forces of Kaz'Ulrah, Krugmar and Sntegia have taken the fort under the name of§0\n§0-rally§0\n§0-waiting in wooden fort§0\n§0-trebuchet fire exchange, rune cannon mention§0\n§0-first charge\n\n-back to wooden fort§0\n§0-more trebuchet warfare, we destroy all but two cannons and remain with four trebuchets, then with only two as we destroy the last two rune cannons§0\n§0-second charge, alch fire on bridge exchange§0\n§0-arrow fire etc ranged stuff\n\n-trebuchets taking down a corner of the fort, turning it into a slope so we can climb and fight our way up it§0\n§0-we do that and they flee throwing themselves into the sea or cliffs down below§0\n§0\n§0AZ§0\n§0\n§0-arrow fire killed thei\n\nr king (ioannis)§0\n§0-don't forget to mention the outlay of the fort§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Love", "§bjerim frostbeard", "As I ponder in my throne I look to my right, I see her transcended appearance. The gods bathe her in light to accent her features, her hair in a lovely bun, her glasses bright hiding her piercing eyes, her smile sends my mind away\n\n and awakens my feral most hungers. A need to smell her black raven hair, to feel her soft warm torso in my hands, to see into her piercing devious eyes, to hear her angelic voice sweeter than any candy.Her kiss the cool autumn, perfect and colorful\n\nl bliss harboring a cold, devious plans. Her hug stokes the fire blazing in my soul. I lust for her wit, her charm, and most of all her intelligence. She speaks of crimes and its profiteers, she speaks as if she is law\n\nI would follow her laws as if given by the gods themselves.\n\nI offered her to meet me in my home. I have no intentions of doing anything scandalous. Although I wish she would take me as her love. I love her with my heart when we kiss my mind is gone. She demands my attention with her smile and I obey.\n\nI will do all in my power to protect her even though I know she needs it not. She tells me of my predecessor and my blood transforms into lava, my stoicism converts into righteous fury as I wish to act as the inquisitor my soul demands I become.\n\nWhen she entered my domicile I saw something quite profound. I saw what I think to be angel wings, white feathers adorned by silver armor, blessed in golden light. Instead of a halo I saw a crown with scarlet rubies, her eyes filled with azure flames.\n\n When I blinked all that remained was the noble creature I fell in love with. I smiled because I knew she was still the woman I loved. We sat together and spoke for a long while. I wish to marry her but we must wait a while longer.", ""),
        StaticBook("Love II", "§bjerim frostbeard", "I weep now more than can have been predicted my angel turned out to be a dark succubus who was using me. I know not what she was using me for but from her actions it's clear that she has nothing but apathy for me when I had suspected love.\n\n As a sat in my throne she verbally attacked me telling me how she had more important people to speak to. Refusing to hug me not to even think of those kisses that now taste of poison and lies.\n\nShe summoned me to speak with her in hope of using me again, I shall go to this meeting and my feeling will be known. I will not be dominated by a weak willed hussy who wills to have a powerful servant to lord over lesser\n\nmen and any number of women. I will for my brothers not to fall prey to the fate I have escaped.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "e", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Daeren and I, we're not together anymore. I guess I'll start this off with that. Just writing this all down to catch my feelings and not have to keep them all to myself, I'd catch fire. Just to note, I let off a lot less emotion than I was feeling. It's\n\nso much of a blur now, I can't even bring myself to remember it; but I'll try. I remember his letter all those months ago when he spoke of my voice, how it was buttery and the music to his heart or some shit like that. Now, he spoke of me like trash on\n\nthe side of the cobblestone that lines the streets. God, I'd give anything to slap him one more time like I did then, it was the best feeling in the world to watch him feel defeated, for just that moment. He spoke of how he'd grown up, but how he'd acted\n\nlike a child then showed he's nothing more than a child in adults shoes, some 500 years my ass. Anyhow, I'm off to get a drink, exactly what I need right now, I'll continue writing in this little book of mine later down the line.", ""),
        StaticBook("Supply List", "§bVulkin Frostbeard", "Dungrimm's Folk List\nof supplies\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n1) 1 dozen preferably 2 dozen sets of Iron armor and weapons/shields.\n2) Any extra Book shelves\n3)Extra Supplies such as Wood,Stone, Coal, Iron.\n4)Arrows and Potions\n\n5) List of all Allies\n6) list of all Allied Military leaders", ""),
        StaticBook("1 V II I", "§bOracle", "The History of Magic\n\nRetold by Leyu'Maehr\n\nOracles Library\n\n2nd of the Grand Harvest -1443\n\nTranscribed on Sabet, 21st of Snows Maiden, 1304. Scribed by Arch Mage Bell, from the words of the Arcane Mage, Slayer. :: :: :: :: :: :: :: Before the beginning of time there was nothing, no planes of existence, only the Void. But\n\nwithin the Void was a light, we know of this light as god, the one deity. But this is not the lore we are interested in. This deity created in the Void the world of Aegis, wherefore you live out your lives. It came to pass that the deity moulded on the\n\nworld of Aegis Man, whom he blew his breath of existence into; giving life. After breathing his existence into man, he entwined some of his divine power, raw and unformed, into the world of Aegis itself. The power was to be called magic by man, and just\n\nas man was placed in the world to be tested, the power was to be utilized by man to be a test, a test of greed and power. :: The power was entwined into the very fabric of both worlds; it ensured the worlds were linked, ever connected. So it was that\n\nall the races of Aegis could access this power, but none were the same. As the power was channelled through the individual it scanned their soul, and was therefore manifested as an extension of their natural environment. So it was that the\n\nHumans had a diverse spread of magic, as they were the most versatile. The Elves came from their woodland homes, of nature and healing. Dwarves from their mighty halls, of stone, hardened and sturdy. Then the Orcs from their harsh deserts,\n\nstrong and vicious. The power of the Noble races came from their allegiance: The Ascended from their hallowed halls, pure and righteous. The Undead from their fiery fields, tainted and evil. :: But the magic was not forever present\n\nin the world of Aegis. It was lost in times long past, forgotten to all but a few, when the evil Iblees was to be banished from this world. In his banishment he was sent to the Void by the ancients. This sent his minions back whence they came, and a\n\nbarrier was erected between the worlds to stop their return. So it was that the worlds were no longer entwined, in separation the power no longer held, and magic all but disappeared from the world... :: But it was not to last. The power of Iblees was\n\ngreat, even in the Void, and he worked at unravelling the barrier between the worlds... Soon the barrier began to break down, the Undead taint spread once more across the face of Aegis. Although this time there was little hope for salvation... ::\n\nWith the failing of the barrier protectingthe world of the living from the dead, the magic once lost to the Descendants, all those years ago, once again seeped into the fabric of the world. The people of Aegis once more felt a somewhat\n\nunfamiliar tingle in their blood, unfamiliar but as though it was always there. :: :: So it came to pass that the ancient power of magic was awakened in Man. Those with the power of foresight could see ahead a fork in the path; one to light, the other\n\ndarkness...They could only hope with this new found power that the right decision would be made...", ""),
        StaticBook("book of Hamnil", "§bjerim frostbeard", "After Verthaik II had clan father passed down to him by Garrond Frostbeard he formed the nation of Kaz'ulrah. Becoming king of the nation he had to pass clan father down as you cannot fill both rolls at the same time. He chose to pass it down to Garronds\n\nson Hamnil Frostbeard. Hamnil was farely young to be clan father but gained it through hard work and dedication.§0\n§0\n§0LIST OF HIS ACCOMPLISMENTS§0\n§0\n§0Hamnil Frostbeard Took large parts in the construction of\n\nthe first two citys of Kaz'ulrah including the capital.§0\n§0\n§0Hamnil brought in many stray dwed lost in Urguans lies. Many of them chose to join frostbeard under his leadership.§0\n§0\n§0Before Hamnil became Clan Father of the Frostbeards\n\nhe was Warden of New Jornheim a city built to temporarly house the dwarves of the kingdom while there mountain home was in contruction. §0\n§0\n§0-------------------\n\nHamnil Frostbeard had many loyal dwed to have his back (which he needed seeing as the Frostbeards were the biggest clan) Some of them being Beorik Frostbeard Loyal friend of Hamnil, Baldar Frostbeard master at gathering information,\n\nVoldock Frostbeard Friend and elder of the clan, Garrond Frostbeard Loving father, Deneryn Frostbeard Jolly friend of Hamnil, Verthaik II good friend and king of Kaz'ulrah, §0\n§0Ferek Frostbeard Hamnils twin brother§0\n§0-------------------\n\nFAMILY§0\n§0\n§0Hamnil Frostbeard, son of Garrond, Son of Gorum, had a wide variety of sibling some of which he did not know of, His closest being his twin brother Ferek. others including beorik in whom he thought of more as a friend. Throri the traitor to the\n\nFrostbeards and the kingdom and Floin his younger brother and absolute goof. other than siblings he had his uncle, Clan legend Gorum Frostbeard and his nefew Edel frostbeard former leader of the silvervein clan son of the traitor Throri.\n\nILLUSTRATION §0\n§0\n§0*a poorly drawn picture would be on this page of Hamnil Frostbeard*§0\n§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Pride", "§bjerim frostbeard", "The hubris of men drunk with power feeds the will of their vassals who sit hungrily glaring at their master they wait for him to drunkenly stumble to the ground where they will devourer him and one will take his place promising to not to repeat\n\nthe sinful manner for which his old master lead them only to be filled with the same pride that earned his predecessor his death and the others gawk at him waiting for their turn.§0  I write this to warn my brothers not to fall prey\n\nto the dark predilection men tend to have to power I pray that no dwarf falls to this after this book's creation", ""),
        StaticBook("Tales of Gorum", "§bKödur Frostbeard", "Chapter One\nGorum FUCKS his OWN ASS.\n\nThis is but one of the feats the Legendary Gorum Frostbeard accomplished in his lifetime. During the first great civil war Gorum often found himself disillusioned with his life as a dwarf. Gorum needed\n\nan escape from reality, and found himself in the tavern frequently and often. One night, Gorum had one too many tankards of ale. He was feeling bold, and adventurous. Gorum's cheeks turned a bright red, and he giggled to himself. Gorum had an idea.\n\nGorum began to laugh hysterically, and yelled to the denizens of the tavern. \"Look 'ere everyun! Ah'm about tu' do somthin' AMAZIN'!\" Gorum dropped his trousers, and unsheathed his dwarven hand cannon. He then proceeded to place it in his diamond cavern.\n\n\"LOOK LADS, LOOK AND BEH' AMAZAID!\" The tavern was baffled, and began to cheer. Gorum then left the tavern, and didn't pay his tab.\n\nTruly, one of the finest Frostbeards of all time.\n\n*The rest of the chapters would be missing from the novel*", ""),
        StaticBook("Fishing Permit", "§bFirst Commander Senurean Mars", "This is a permit for fishing in Dredge Water, You have paid for one stoneweek. It will reset on sunday.(not tomorrow)\n\n\n\nSigned, First Commander Senurean Mars", ""),
        StaticBook("SquishCo Receipt", "§bJace Kellian", "thank you for your purchase form Squish Co and Friends§0\n§0\n§0Today you purchased caskets at 300 mina per§0\n§0\n§0Receipt§0\n§02 caskets§0\n§0\n§0Total:§0\n§0600 Mina\n\nThank you for your Purchase", ""),
        StaticBook("MYTHDORT THE GOD", "§bKödur Frostbeard", "This book is dedicated to the greatest Frostbeard of ALL TIME. His name is...\n  \nMYTHDORT FROSTBEARD...\n\nThis is the tale of his life and legacy...\n\n*The book would be covered in sketches of mighty dwarven cocks*\n\n8====D\n8====D\n8====D\n8====D\n8====D\n8====D\n8====D\n8====D\n\n8====D\n8====D\n8====D\n8====D\n8====D\n8====D\n8====D\n8====D\n8====D\n8====D\n8====D\n8====D\n8====D\n\n8====D\n8====D\n8====D\n8====D\n8====D\n8====D\n8====D\n8====D\n8====D\n8====D\n8====D\n8====D", ""),
        StaticBook("The MIGHTY Rudok", "§bKödur Frostbeard", "The tale of the NOBLE\n  RUDOK FROSTBEARD\n\nOur tale begins in small port town of Dredgewater. One day, a stocky dwarf washed onto the shores of what was then Kal'Omith's naval stronghold. The dwarf was covered in BULGING MUSCLES, and had a GLORIOUS BEARD\n\nThe dwarf had no memory of how he ended up on the shore, or even his own name. A POWERFUL dwarf by the name Grumbis Frostbeard found the poor lad on the shore, and offered his aid. \n\n*Several hundred pages would be missing from the novel*\n\nAnd that's how Rudok became one of the GREATEST DWARVES of ALL TIME. Legend has it he still wanders the wilds of Axios, patiently waiting, for when his clan needs him once more.\n\n        THE END", ""),
        StaticBook("For The Enchante", "§bBalinor Blackaxe", "Hello, I need some enchanter's services, please msg me if you want help me,§0\n§0I have an house in this town and a house in thenearby \"town in the mountain\" , or if you want I am in the Dwarfes Discord,\n\nSo Dear Domouuthran, please contact me how do you want.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0-Balinor Blackaxe", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "All potions begin with a water base:§0\n§0\n§0-Distilled Water: makes standard potions§0\n§0-Aqua Vitae: makes advanced potions§0\n§0-Impure Water: makes drinks§0\n§0\n§0Most potions start with a water symbol.\n\nIngredients must be placed in the right order, or the potion will not turn out.§0\n§0\n§0Drinks do not require multiple ingredients, with the exception of sweet ale.§0\n§0\n§0*A misshapen sketch of a brewing apparatus and bottles*\n\nDrinks:§0\n§0\n§0Juice is created with fruits that are cooked and strained with a fine mesh. Melon juice is used to make sweet ale.§0\n§0\n§0Tea is created by drying certain herbs or flowers and soaking them in hot water.\n\nMead is created from a long distillation of honey. This gives it its distinct smell.§0\n§0\n§0Pale ale is made from distilling wheat. It is a very common drink.§0\n§0\n§0Sweet ale is created by distilling wheat with melon juice.\n\nRum is made from fermenting cane sugar. This makes it sweet, but also very strong.§0\n§0\n§0Vodka is made from potatoes that cannot be used in food, as they carry some level of toxin to them. It is a popular drink, but difficult to make.\n\nMulled wine is made with resin from trees and mixed with various spices. It is the strongest drink, and it tends to be preferred with the upper class.", ""),
        StaticBook("HOME INSPECTION", "§bSultan Arlen Kharadeen", "NOTICE!!!§0\n§0\n§0Recpipent: Crumena Izalith§0\n§0\n§0By order of The Eternal Mubarizun, Alhambra Way 1 is to be inspected thoroughly within the next three Khali days. Failure to comply will result in a 500 mina fine. Report to Amir -\n\nAshruf Kaneen immediately once received.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0- Sultan Arlen Kharadeen", ""),
        StaticBook("Alchemy Vol.I", "§bFerek Frostbeard", "-The Essence of Alchemy-§0\n§0Volume 1: The Basics§0\n§0\n§0\n§0By: Ferek Frostbeard§0\n§0c. 1633\n\nChapter 1:§0\n§0So you want to be an Alchemist?§0\n§0\n§0I'm willing to bet that you, dear reader, picked up this volume thinking \"aha! a quick guide to the most mysterious and complex form of magic and science known to dwed!\"§0\n§0\n§0\n\nWell guess what you beardling§0\n§0\n§0YOURE WRONG!§0\n§0\n§0Alchemy is a complex art requiring great time and effort to even gain a basic understanding. It is taxing on one's resources and one's mind. It is not for the faint of heart or the easily off-put.\n\nTo begin, alchemy is the process of mixing, blending, and unlocking the potential of ingredients added, in a process known as the Equivalent Exchange.§0\n§0\n§0Every reaction has an exchange associated with it. Knowing the nature of your ingredient, it's inherent\n\nvalues, its capabilities, will make you more wise to your craft, and allow you to make better predictions on what speculative formulae will work, and which might explode in your face.§0\n§0\n\nChapter 2: Stocking the Cabinet§0\n§0\n§0So, dear reader, you've decided to press forward with your curiosity to embrace the unknown that is alchemical science. Bully to you. §0\n§0\n§0In order to actually proceed, however, one must have ingredients!\n\nOne can find alchemical reagents everywhere, from the icy mountains near Kaz'Ulrah to the forests of the wood elves. §0\n§0\n§0All reagents fall under one of four catagories, four symbols: Fire, Water, Air, and Earth. The combination of like or unlike symbols\n\nwill be the basis of your formulae. All reagents are not made equal under Yemekar's eyes, however. Some reagents within a symbol will be stronger than others. The stronger the ingredient, the stronger the result.\n\nChapter 3: Field Work§0\n§0\n§0Now that I have explained what a reagent is, how they work, and the concept of Equivalent Exchange and symbols, it is finally time to collect some reagents.§0\n§0\n§0Firstly, any budding alchemist must aquire for themselves a\n\nset of Alchemist Shears. This tool is your key to beginning alchemy, without your shears, one could not possibly hope to harvest the bountiful lot of ingredients this great world has to offer. In the proceeding volumes, I shall describe where\n\nyou, my reader, might find some fine specimens of each symbol.§0\n§0\n§0Armed with your shears, which can be purchased from any blacksmith worth their salt, you are now ready to step out into the wilds! Search high and low for reagents taht catch your eye.\n\nIt will take time, due diligence, and a few pairs of shears before you coome to learn the hiding places of the valuable ingredients you seek.§0\n§0\n§0Your knapsack bursting with fungi and flora, you should return to your lab and prepare your reagents for use.\n\nSome might require drying, others to be stored in jars, most must be cut and shaved to get to the usable bits.§0\n§0\n§0Once this is done, you are ready to begin the brewing process.§0\n§0\n§0In order to begin performing alchemy, one must have a brewing stand.\n\nA brewing stand can be aquired from any professional tinkerer for a modest price. Once aqcuired, you are to heat the device with alchemical fuel, then proceed to enter your ingredients at the top of the device, allowing the heat to transfer the essence of\n\nyour reagents to the waiting vessels below. §0\n§0\n§0All potions start with boiled water, which can be done at the stand itself by adding charcoal to the device.§0\n§0\n§0From there, your potions and formulae await!\n\nChapter 4: Continue On!§0\n§0\n§0This shall be the end of the First Volume of The Essence of Alchemy. I hope I have convinced you, my reader, to pick up the craft. §0\n§0Much good can come about from even a single alchemist, and I dare you to follow the path of your\n\ncuriosities.", ""),
