        StaticBook("To Raomir", "§bUnknown", "'Ello fat'er...\n\nAh would loike ter invite ye ter a meetin' so t'at yeh get ter meet yer grandc'ild. \n\nT'ough yeh may get t'is letteh a bit late as ah'm goin' ter meet wit' Morug first, 'e requested a meetin' wit' meh yeh see.\n\nAh'd also loike ter speak wit' yeh as ah 'ave nae seen ye in a w'ile...\n\nAh miss yeh fat'er.\n\nYer daug'ter,\nAvilia.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Deep Roads", "§bAgamm \"Ruins-Delver\" Ireheart", "THE RUINS OF\n       KAL'OMITH\n\n\n\n   By Agamm Ireheart\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n==================\n\n  Deep beneath the bustling markets of Kal'Omith lies strange ruins. The Dwarven city lies within mountains, and seem peaceful enough. But alas, there's more than what meets the eye. There are ruins beneath Kal'Omith, and little is known about them. The\n\nonly things known about them are that they're called \"The Deep Roads\" and that they once had goblins living there. Yet, dwarven architecture is visible from what I've seen. I've given names to the small pockets of settlements that I've found. Of course\n\nI've used the term \"city\" but I mean settlement. Here's what I have named:\nKal'Kraviil or \"City of the dead\". This ruin has plenty of dwarven remains, all in disturbing piles, as if they were suddenly killed at once, aware of their fates, yet fearing it.\n\nThe second one:\nKal'KavirGrobbi, or \"City of the dead goblins\". I've named it that because of the goblin-like structures, and fortifications built. This one had undead and spiders lingering, so I left as soon as a saw enough. It reeked of death as well.\n\nThe third;\nKal'Hefruth or \"City of the forest\". I named it so because of the strange vegetation in the area. It was beautiful, peaceful, yet unnerving. This settlement is the most important, as there are two paths from the area that would take one to the\n\nmysterious places.\n\n       KAL'KRAVIIL\n  Deep, past the halls that linger of decay, lies the abandoned, dead settlement of what I call, Kal'Kraviil. It is here, where the mystery begins. The buildings look familiar to the ones above, but the shadows have taken the area.\n\nThe remains of its past residents scattered everywhere. Many seem to be on the courtyard, meaning death was sudden, and perhaps, evil. It is given that many knew of their deaths, and others, oblivious to it. They were once dwed.\nIt is quite a disturbing\n\nsight. But it is here that my friend found a tome called \"Directions\". The contents of the book begins in Dwarvish, then a section is written in common tongue. It reads the same tale of the king of Urguan, as the runestone by the entrances to the ruins.\n\nUnfortunately, I still have no idea what it means.\n\n   KAL'KAVIRGROBBI\n  This settlement was hazardous. The stench of rot lingered, like the undead that wandered there. The area seems to be an old goblin-like fort, with tents and wooden walls and fortifications. It seemed too primitive to be of Dwarven\n\nhandiwork. I managed to get past the hordes of undead, and reached the inner part of the fort, but the cave there was sealed off. Not much was located there, and so, I left.\n\n       KAL'HEFRUTH\n  Here, I found giant glowing mushrooms and tall trees and bushes. Streams flowed as well, and it was quite a sight. Some tents littered the area, but not much happens there. Then there are the two paths from there. At the end of the\n\narea, there is a cave, and inside is the dormant spiders that are mammoth. Then there is a gate, where going through would take you to the \"Lava pits\". I'd like to call it \"Derkon Boor\" or Lava Core, as it seems to be the core of a volcano or something.\n\nThe contents of Lava pits are unnerving, with altars and statues that revers death in the most corrupted ways. I would advise anyone who would venture to the area to be prepared in every way when going to the pit.", ""),
        StaticBook("Welcoming Letter", "§bAnne Catherijne Hagelijn", "We would like to welcme you to our community of Batavians.§0\n§0If we can help you with anything please do not hesitate to ask.§0\n§0*Willem Hagelijn§0\n§0*Anne C. Hagelijn§0\n§0*Adriaan de Witt§0\n§0-------------------Here are some things you can find in our\n\ndistrict:§0\n§0*Batavian Home Guard:§0\n§0If interested contact W. Hagelijn or A. de Witt.§0\n§0*Oranjestraat's public garden.§0\n§0*Oranjestraat's Library.§0\n§0*Batavian Shop at Sutica's Main Square.§0\n§0*Leyunia's Arcane and Sub-arcane Magic Lessons.\n\n-------------------More information will be posted in our Community Noticeboard. Keep in touch for Monthly Updates.§0\n§0-------------------To show our hospitality the Welcoming Committe woul like to gift you this rose bouquet along with some sugar and\n\nmushroom soup.§0\n§0>@<>@<>@<>@<>@<>@<§0\n§0\n§0-Anne Catherijne Hagelijn", ""),
        StaticBook("Found Book #1", "§bGlen Werlaw", "First Seed, 7th, 1587§0\n§0We ran into undead, right now, it seems pretty stupid to be writing in a journal when your company is staring them down, but it's what I decided to do, it's what my brain told me to do... I'm so scared.", ""),
        StaticBook("Found Journal", "§bGlen Werlaw", "Entry 1§0\n§0\n§0This is the newest journal, which I begin  writing in shortly after the fall of Johannesburg and in turn, the Empire. It has been a whirlwind and I realize that I should have written my record sooner.\n\nThe end began at the battle on the field. Their forces were able to push us back, and quickly defeat us. §0\n§0\n§0The Empire was in a panic. We'd been well and truly beaten, and there was little anyone could do to stop the entire kingdom from\n\nspiralling into destruction. §0\n§0\n§0The kingdom of Haense was approached by the dwarves and offered a deal, which we gladly took. Peace for a fee and pulling our forces out of the fight. Had we not accepted, the\n\nentirety of humanity may have been wiped out. Shortly after Haense backed out of the war, the Empire began preparing for a final siege against the city. They didn't make it far. §0\n§0\n§0No, the battle didn't even take place.\n\nThe Emperor ignited the stores of thanium in the palace and blew the entire city from the map. All that remains now is a massive hole filled with thanium dust. It is deadly stuff, and thus recovery for the city is slow. Most of it's inhabitants were\n\nkilled, though some persist in Karlsburg and other settlements. I am truly saddened for these people. They had little to do with the war, yet they suffer greatly for it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Found Journal #3", "§bGlen Werlaw", "Alfred's Inventory in the Krag§0\n§0\n§03 dia§0\n§04 gol§0\n§025 em blck§0\n§037 iron", ""),
        StaticBook("Found Journal #2", "§bGlen Werlaw", "Nem era sgip. yreve emit i kniht i evah a daer no Eak, eh segnahc sih enut. I evah reven neeb os detartsurf ni ym efil. Eh stnaw em ot nioj sih etllil puorg fo seilla.\n\nI kniht i lliw og htiw mih. Eh dna Pilihp devas em morf eht scro- yeht devas ym efil. I ma dednarb won. A egral, ylgu kram no ym dhaherof. I od ton wonk nehw ti lliw edaf, ro fi ti neve lliw. Tub yeht devas em. Seod taht ton kaeps rof emos namuh ycneced?\n\nI yrrow rof Eak. Eh si tantsid ta semit- sih dnim srednaw. Tub nehw eh si ereh, eh si os teews. Eh serac rof em, i kniht. Ti sekam sgniht redrah rof em; i ylneddus evah enoemos ohw dluow erac fi i saw on regnol evila.\n\nCigam si eno fo eht tsom ridiculous sgniht ev'i reve-§0\n§0\n§0I tnew ot eht Dargur Library ot nrael woh ot dnefed tsniaga segam. Ti demees ekil a doog gniht ot wonk, nevig tahw ev'i nar otni fo etal. I denrael hcum- eno tsum\n\nkaerb rieht sucof.", ""),
        StaticBook("Found Journal 2", "§bPenn Louison", "14th of Deep Cold; 1603§0\n§0I'm starting my journal with this entry. I seek to learn more magic. Transmutation interests me most.. Need to find a teacher. Perhaps elves will know.§0\n§0\n§013th of Snows Maiden§0\n§01604§0\n§0Yesterday I met a man\n\nby the name of Roscoe. Fun to talk to, quirky. Today I have had an arguement with mother. I think she hates me because of all that stuff... Sorry.§0\n§0\n§0*half of this page was ripped out.*\n\n*the next five pages have been ripped from the book.*\n\n9th, Grand Harvest. 1615 - Study all forms of water, thoroughly.§0\n§0\n§0To be continued..§0\n§0\n§0-I found a water evocationist who seems intent on teaching me her art form... She also asked to date me. Probably an elf, mother says to be cautious. She's right.\n\n5th of Sun's Smile, 1615 -§0\n§0I need to calibrate some thermometers.. I've managed to make some glass instruments of varying sizes, we shall see which size fits my needs best..§0\n§0For the purpose of this, I am using a mixture of alcohol\n\nand water at a 1 to 1 ratio, I've used one cubic centimeter of each. §0\n§0\n§0For accuracies purpose I decided to use the thermometers lengthed at .7 meters. As it happens I've calibrated them to zero degrees centigrade, based on the freezing point of\n\nwater. To one hundred degrees, the point at which the water boils. Plus some extra thirty or so degrees minus, hard to tell as there is no standard scale for this.§0\n§0\n§0As always the measurements aren't going to need to be precise.. It is magic after all, not\n\nalchemy. Further, it does not seem possible to recreate snow by shaving ice, it's not the same and it melts far to quickly.§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Help Us", "§bMerridolph \"Merry\" Applebrook", "I am Merry Applebrook, and recently my village was razed by orcs. I am a Halfling, living in a village known as Pendlemere deep in the heart of the Empire, specifically near Lorraine. We are vassals, and we require assistance. The Orcs killed almost every\n\nperson witness to the event, including my best friend, Gerald. We request protection from these Orcs, and any other actions you can take to help would be appreciated.§0\n§0\n§0-Merry Applebrook.", ""),
