        StaticBook("Level 2 Code 1", "§bJaya Jayamen", "Level 2 Code 1\n\ni!.fy o!’uc a n,!re’1ad. th.,!isr !igh! t’ s’ayt!h ‘e!.,w or,!d Co!. ok’ie", ""),
        StaticBook("DUEL RULEBOOK", "§bJaya Jayamen", "DUEL RULE BOOK§0\n§0\n§0In duel, you build a character using points to assign his attack, defence, and items from a set amount of points.\n\nWhen you are happy with the character you have built, you face off your character vs. another persons. Your characters stats and equipment are recorded as you will be using this character continuously in games, so use your points wisely.\n\nThere will be tournaments where you can earn prizes. Your equipment and weapons have a durability, so use them wisely as the damage continues form game to game, each player has a book for them that holds their equipment.\n\nHere are the type of things a character will have.§0\n§0\n§0Name§0\n§0\n§0Attack§0\n§0\n§0Defence§0\n§0\n§0Stance§0\n§0\n§0HP§0\n\nWeapon§0\n§0\n§0Weapon HP§0\n§0\n§0Armor§0\n§0\n§0Armor HP§0\n§0\n§0Ability§0\n§0\n§0Item§0\n§0\n§0Item§0\n\nItem§0\n§0\n§0Here is how the game works.§0\n§0\n\nYour attack is how well you attack the opponent.§0\n§0\n§0Your defence is how well you take damage.§0\n§0\n§0There are 3 stances you can take in the battle.\n\nAggressive stance gives +3 attack.§0\n§0\n§0Versatile stance gives +1 attack and +1 Defence.§0\n§0\n§0Defencive stance gives +3 Defence.§0\n§0\n§0You choose your stance before the battle.\n\nChanging your stance can only be done once every 3 rounds.§0\n§0\n§0When it is your turn, you can choose to do an action, use one item, and use an ability. An action can be to either attack or defend.\n\nYou can also change your stance while attacking or defending, but the change of stance only takes place after your turn ends.\n\nAttack means you attack the opponent as your action. Your attack vs. their defence, roll 10 and add any modifiers to it such as your weapon attack value and your attack value.\n\nIf the attacker wins, then it deals the damage from the attack to the opponent’s armor with the amount being the final defence number minus the final attack number. If the armor breaks, then it goes to the characters HP.\n\nIf the attacker loses then their weapon is damaged the amount that is the final attack number minus the final defence number. If it goes over the weapons hp the weapon breaks, but the attacker isn’t damaged.\n\nDefend means you are defending for the round as your action. you take half damage and half armor damage. §0\n§0\n§0Use an item means that you use one item you have.\n\nUse an ability means you use an ability you have learned. §0\n§0\n§0When a number isn’t even like when taking half 9 damage, round up. So it would be 5.§0\n\nYou can only earn points from a fight with a staff member moderating it. if you lose a match, you get 1 point, if you tie, you get 2 points, if you win, you get 3 points.\n\nCreating a character§0\n§0\n§0A player can put 10 points between their attack and defense. Attack and defense must have at least 2 points in each. Your HP is 10.§0\n§0\n§0You start of with 20 points for items§0\n\nThe amount of points you have in armor, weapons, items, and unspent points are your ranking.", ""),
        StaticBook("Menu", "§bJaya Jayamen", "{\"text\":\"\"}", ""),
        StaticBook("Games Book", "§bJaya Jayamen", "Games\n\nThe current games we have are Catapult ((A mini battleship game)), Tic Tac Toe, 4 In a row ((Connect 4)), Duel (a Strategy game), Pico (a strategy card game), Checkers,  and Poker ((with reduced cards)).\n\n       Catapult\n\nCatapult is a simple game. There are four rows and four columns that make up the grid.  Each row has a number, each column has a letter. You decide where to put your carts, one three squares long, and one 2 squares long.\n\nAfter you choose, you write your choices in a book and quill and hand it to a staff member that is moderating the game. After your opponent does this as well, you roll a 20 sided dice to see who goes first.\n\n The person who takes the first turn picks a number and a letter. In that square if the opponent assigned one of his carts and it hits its space, the staff member tells them it is a hit and the player goes again until he has a miss.\n\n Then turns alternate. When one players 3 long cart and 2 long cart are destroyed, that player loses and the other wins.\n\n         Tic Tac Toe\n\nTic Tac Toe is a classic simple game. It is played on a 3x3 grid. The goal is to get three of your color in a row.  You roll a 20 sided dice to see who goes first.\n\nYou continue placing one of your color each turn until you get three in a row or tie.\n\n        4 in a Row\n\n4 In a row is a game where the objective is you are trying to get 4 of your color in a row. You begin by rolling a 20 sided dice. Then whoever goes first places one of his color on the bottom of the grid.\n\neach color you place must be on the bottom of the grid or directly on top of one color already placed. You alternate turns placing one color each turn. When someone gets 4 in a row, the game is over and the one who did it wins.\n\n          Pico\n\nPico is a simple card game where you try and earn points. Each player is given 5 cards, there are 11 cards in total. The 11th card that isn’t given is discarded. This means you know what cards your opponent has.\n\nYou each pick a card and when ready on the count of 3 say your card. A higher number means you win unless you are double or more your opponents, then they win.\n\nThe winner puts their card to the side for its points and the opponent can use the card they said again. You continue until only 1 card is remaining on one of the players hands.\n\nThen add up the points, keep it in mind, and the next round begins with your hands swapped. At the end of the swapped round, you add up the points and add those points to your previous match points and see who has more.\n\nThe winner is whoever has the most points.\n\n         Checkers\n\nCheckers is a simple game. The objective is to take all of your enemies pieces. You can only move diagonally. You start with 12 pieces on your side, and 12 on the other person’s side. Your goal is to jump over their pieces.\n\nIn order to just over a piece their needs to be space on the other side of their piece to jump to. It must be a blank space with no pieces that you jump to. When you jump someone’s piece. You take that piece.\n\nAfter you take their piece, you can jump again with the same piece if there is another jumpable piece with room on the other side of it.\n\nYour pieces can only move one direction, forward, there is no backwards until one of your pieces gets to the other side of the board. Then that piece has the ability to move backwards. You mark this piece by places two of your pieces on top of the other.\n\n When one player has no more pieces, the person who has pieces wins.\n\n         Poker\n\nPoker is played with a deck of 36 cards. There are four types of cards that go from 1 to 9. Diamonds is one type, spades is another, Hearts is another, and clubs is the last. Each person is dealt 2 cards.\n\nBoth cards are face down and you don’t want your opponent to know what it is. The objective of the game is to make the best 5 card hand you can. After you and others are dealt their 2 cards, you each take a turn betting.\n\nYou can bet, call which means you put the current highest bet, or fold which means you don’t bet and you are out of that round.\n\nIf someone bets, all other players must bet that much to stay in, if someone raises the bet, then all players must bet that much in order to stay in the current hand. When all betting is done, the dealer puts out 3 cards.\n\nBased on your hand and those three cards, you make up your mind on betting this round with those cards showing. After the betting is finished a 4th card is shown. Betting goes on and finally after that is done the 5th card is shown.\n\nNow with one last round of betting after that you show your cards. The person with the best hand wins!\n\nThese are the types of hands you can have, ordered from worst to best.\n\nNine high\nThis means of all the cards when you show them you have the highest numbers\n\nTop pair\nThis is when you have 2 of a certain number.\n\nTrips/set\nThis is when you have 3 of a certain number.\n\nStraight\nFive cards of any type in sequential order.\n\nFlush\n5 cards of the same type.\n\nFull house\nThree of one number and two of another.\n\nQuads\nFour of a number\n\nRoyal Flush\nThe highest 5 cards in one certain type of card.\n\n           DUEL\n\nDuel is our most complicated game. In duel, you build a character using points to assign his attack, defence, and items from a set amount of points.\n\nWhen you are happy with the character you have built you face off your character vs. another persons. Your characters stats and equipment are recorded as you will be using this character continuously in games, so use your points wisely.\n\nThere will be tournaments where you can earn prizes. Your equipment and weapons have a durability, so use them wisely as the damage continues from game to game. Each player has a book for them that holds their equipment.\n\nHere are the type of things a character will have.\n\nName\nAttack\nDefense\n\nStance\n\nHP\n\nWeapon\n\nWeapon HP\n\nArmor\n\nArmor HP\n\nability\n\nItem\n\nItem\n\nItem\n\n\n\nHere is how the game\nworks.\n\nYour attack is how well you attack the opponent.\n\nYour defense is how well you take damage.\n\nThere are 3 stances you can take in the battle.\n\nAggressive stance gives +3  attack\nVersatile stance gives +1 attack and +1 defense\nDefensive stance gives +3 Defense\nYou choose your stance before the battle.\nChanging your stance can only be done once every 3 rounds.\n\nWhen it is your turn, you can choose to do an action, use one item, and use an ability.\nAn action can be to either to attack or defend. You can also change your stance while attacking or defending.\n\nAttack means you attack the opponent as your action. Your attack vs their defense. Roll 10 and add any modifiers to it such as your weapon attack value and your attack value.\n\n if the attacker wins, then it deals the damage from the attack to the opponents armor with amount being the final defense number minus the final attack number. If the armor breaks, then it goes to the characters HP.\n\nIf the attacker loses, then their weapon is damaged the amount that is the final attack number minus the final defense number. If it goes over the weapons HP the weapon breaks, but the attacker isn’t damaged.\n\nDefend means you are defending for the round as your action. You take half damage and half armor damage.\nUse an item means that you use one item that you have.\n\nUse an ability means that you use an ability you have learned.\nWhen a number isn’t even like when taking half 9 damage, round up. So it would be 5.\n\nYou can only earn points from a fight with a staff member moderating it.\nIf you lose a match, you get 1 point\nFor a tie, you get 2 points\nFor a win, you get 3 points.\n\nCreating a Character\n\nA player can put 10 points between their attack and defense. Attack and defense must have at least 2 points in it.\nYour HP is 10\n\nYou start off with 20 points for items\n\nPlease ask Jaya Jayamen or a game staff member for the points shop book.", ""),
        StaticBook("DUEL POINT SHOP", "§bJaya Jayamen", "Armor§0\n§0\n§0Tin§0\n§0 1 defence §0\n§05 hp §0\n§01 point.§0\n§0\n§0Bronze §0\n§02 defense §0\n§010 hp§0\n§0 4 points§0\n\nIron§0\n§0 3 defense§0\n§0 15 hp §0\n§08 points§0\n§0\n§0Steel §0\n§04 defense§0\n§0 20 hp §0\n§014 points§0\n\nMithril §0\n§05 defense §0\n§025 hp §0\n§021 points§0\n§0\n§0Adamantine§0\n§0 6 defence §0\n§030 hp §0\n§029 points§0\n\nWeapons§0\n§0\n§0Tin §0\n§02 attack§0\n§02 Points§0\n§03 HP§0\n§0\n§0Bronze §0\n§03 attack §0\n§05 points§0\n§06 HP§0\n\nIron §0\n§04 attack§0\n§09 points§0\n§09 HP§0\n§0\n§0Steel §0\n§05 attack§0\n§015 points§0\n§012 HP§0\n\nMithril§0\n§0 6 attack §0\n§022 points§0\n§015 HP§0\n§0\n§0Adamantine§0\n§0 7 attack§0\n§030 points§0\n§018 HP§0\n\nStrength potion §0\n§0 attack increases by 4 for a round§0\n§0 5 points§0\n§0\n§0Swiftness potion§0\n§0defense increases by 4 for a round.§0\n§0 5 points§0\n\nSmokepot §0\n§0 your opponent loses two of his turns. §0\n§010 points§0\n§0\n§0Ultra strength potion§0\n§0 increasts attack by 8 for a round§0\n§010 points§0\n\nUltra swiftness potion §0\n§0increases defence by 8 for a round. §0\n§010 points§0\n§0\n§0Strength brace §0\n§0 increases attack by 2 passively §0\n§020 points§0\n\nMetal charm §0\n§0 increases defense by 2 passively§0\n§0 20 points§0\n\nAbilities§0\n§0\n§0Brace for impact – pink block§0\n§0 for the round you take half damage rounded up. §0\n§0Takes 3 rounds to recover.§0\n§0 Can be used on the other persons turn. 30 points to learn§0\n\nAdrenaline – orange block§0\n§0you do double damage for the round.§0\n§0 30 points to learn. §0\n§0Takes 3 rounds to recover.§0", ""),
